__d(function(e,a,t,r,o,n,i){o.exports=[{id:"q001",text:"Gel, gel, ne olursan ol, yine gel. \u0130ster k\xe2fir, ister mecusi, ister puta tapan ol, yine gel. Bizim derg\xe2h\u0131m\u0131z \xfcmitsizlik derg\xe2h\u0131 de\u011fildir. Y\xfcz kere t\xf6vbeni bozmu\u015f olsan da, yine gel.",original:"\u0628\u06cc\u0627 \u0628\u06cc\u0627 \u0647\u0631 \u0622\u0646\u0686\u0647 \u0647\u0633\u062a\u06cc \u0628\u0627\u0632 \u0622",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"kabul",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Come, come, whoever you are. Wanderer, idolater, worshiper of fire, come even though you have broken your vows a thousand times. Ours is not a caravan of despair. Come, yet again, come.",categoryEn:"acceptance",textDe:"Komm, komm, wer du auch bist. Wanderer, G\xf6tzendiener, Feueranbeter, komm, auch wenn du deine Gel\xfcbde tausendmal gebrochen hast. Unsere ist keine Karawane der Verzweiflung. Komm, komm noch einmal.",categoryDe:"Annahme",textEs:"Ven, ven, quienquiera que seas. Errante, id\xf3latra, adorador del fuego, ven aunque hayas roto tus votos mil veces. La nuestra no es una caravana de desesperaci\xf3n. Ven, una vez m\xe1s, ven.",categoryEs:"aceptaci\xf3n",textPt:"Vem, vem, sejas quem fores. Errante, id\xf3latra, adorador do fogo, vem ainda que tenhas quebrado teus votos mil vezes. A nossa n\xe3o \xe9 uma caravana de desespero. Vem, mais uma vez, vem.",categoryPt:"aceita\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Viens, viens, qui que tu sois. Errant, idol\xe2tre, adorateur du feu, viens m\xeame si tu as rompu tes v\u0153ux mille fois. La n\xf4tre n'est pas une caravane du d\xe9sespoir. Viens, encore une fois, viens.",categoryFr:"acceptation",textJa:"\u304a\u3044\u3067\u3001\u304a\u3044\u3067\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u304c\u4f55\u8005\u3067\u3042\u308d\u3046\u3068\u3002\u3055\u3059\u3089\u3044\u4eba\u3067\u3082\u3001\u5076\u50cf\u3092\u62dd\u3080\u8005\u3067\u3082\u3001\u706b\u3092\u5d07\u3081\u308b\u8005\u3067\u3082\u3001\u304a\u3044\u3067\u3002\u5343\u5ea6\u8a93\u3044\u3092\u7834\u3063\u305f\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3082\u3001\u304a\u3044\u3067\u3002\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306e\u3082\u3068\u306f\u7d76\u671b\u306e\u968a\u5546\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u3055\u3042\u3001\u3082\u3046\u4e00\u5ea6\u3001\u304a\u3044\u3067\u3002",categoryJa:"\u53d7\u5bb9"},{id:"q002",text:"D\xfcn ak\u0131ll\u0131yd\u0131m, d\xfcnyay\u0131 de\u011fi\u015ftirmek istiyordum. Bug\xfcn bilgeyim, kendimi de\u011fi\u015ftiriyorum.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"degisim",rarity:"common",textEn:"Yesterday I was clever, so I wanted to change the world. Today I am wise, so I am changing myself.",categoryEn:"transformation",textDe:"Gestern war ich klug, darum wollte ich die Welt ver\xe4ndern. Heute bin ich weise, darum ver\xe4ndere ich mich selbst.",categoryDe:"Wandlung",textEs:"Ayer era inteligente, por eso quer\xeda cambiar el mundo. Hoy soy sabio, por eso me cambio a m\xed mismo.",categoryEs:"transformaci\xf3n",textPt:"Ontem eu era esperto, por isso queria mudar o mundo. Hoje sou s\xe1bio, por isso mudo a mim mesmo.",categoryPt:"transforma\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Hier j'\xe9tais intelligent, alors je voulais changer le monde. Aujourd'hui je suis sage, alors je me change moi-m\xeame.",categoryFr:"transformation",textJa:"\u6628\u65e5\u306e\u79c1\u306f\u8ce2\u304b\u3063\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3001\u4e16\u754c\u3092\u5909\u3048\u305f\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3063\u305f\u3002\u4eca\u65e5\u306e\u79c1\u306f\u667a\u6167\u3092\u5f97\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u81ea\u8eab\u3092\u5909\u3048\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5909\u5bb9"},{id:"q003",text:"Ate\u015fin i\xe7inde yanmayan \u015feyin hi\xe7bir de\u011feri yoktur.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"cesaret",rarity:"common",textEn:"Whatever does not burn in the fire has no worth.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"Was nicht im Feuer brennt, hat keinen Wert.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"Lo que no arde en el fuego no tiene valor.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"Aquilo que n\xe3o arde no fogo n\xe3o tem valor.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"Ce qui ne br\xfble pas dans le feu n'a aucune valeur.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u706b\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u71c3\u3048\u306a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u306b\u3001\u4fa1\u5024\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q004",text:"A\u015fk gelince b\xfct\xfcn eksiklikler gider. A\u015fk gelince utan\xe7 da gider, korku da.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"When love arrives, all imperfections fall away. When love arrives, shame departs, and fear with it.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Wenn die Liebe kommt, fallen alle Unvollkommenheiten ab. Wenn die Liebe kommt, weicht die Scham, und mit ihr die Furcht.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Cuando llega el amor, caen todas las imperfecciones. Cuando llega el amor, se va la verg\xfcenza, y con ella el miedo.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Quando o amor chega, caem todas as imperfei\xe7\xf5es. Quando o amor chega, a vergonha parte, e com ela o medo.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Quand l'amour arrive, toutes les imperfections tombent. Quand l'amour arrive, la honte s'en va, et la peur avec elle.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u304c\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u3068\u3001\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u6b20\u70b9\u306f\u843d\u3061\u3066\u3044\u304f\u3002\u611b\u304c\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u3068\u3001\u6065\u306f\u53bb\u308a\u3001\u6050\u308c\u3082\u3068\u3082\u306b\u53bb\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q005",text:"Sesin duyulmuyor diye a\u011flama. Belki de sesin tam \xe7\u0131kmayan yerden, sessizlikten \xe7\u0131k\u0131yor.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"sabir",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Do not weep because your voice goes unheard. Perhaps your true voice rises from the silence itself.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Weine nicht, weil deine Stimme ungeh\xf6rt bleibt. Vielleicht erhebt sich deine wahre Stimme gerade aus der Stille selbst.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"No llores porque tu voz no es escuchada. Quiz\xe1 tu verdadera voz se eleve del propio silencio.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"N\xe3o chores porque a tua voz n\xe3o \xe9 ouvida. Talvez a tua verdadeira voz se erga do pr\xf3prio sil\xeancio.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"Ne pleure pas parce que ta voix n'est pas entendue. Peut-\xeatre ta vraie voix s'\xe9l\xe8ve-t-elle du silence m\xeame.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u58f0\u304c\u5c4a\u304b\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3068\u6ce3\u304f\u306a\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u771f\u306e\u58f0\u306f\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6c88\u9ed9\u305d\u306e\u3082\u306e\u304b\u3089\u7acb\u3061\u306e\u307c\u308b\u306e\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q006",text:"Hakikat g\xfcne\u015f gibidir; perde \xe7ekersen g\xf6zden kaybolur ama g\xfcne\u015f yine de oradad\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hakikat",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Truth is like the sun; draw a veil over it and it disappears from sight, yet the sun remains where it always was.",categoryEn:"truth",textDe:"Die Wahrheit ist wie die Sonne; verh\xfclle sie, und sie verschwindet aus dem Blick, doch die Sonne bleibt, wo sie immer war.",categoryDe:"Wahrheit",textEs:"La verdad es como el sol; \xe9chale un velo y desaparece de la vista, pero el sol sigue donde siempre estuvo.",categoryEs:"verdad",textPt:"A verdade \xe9 como o sol; lan\xe7a-lhe um v\xe9u e ela desaparece da vista, mas o sol permanece onde sempre esteve.",categoryPt:"verdade",textFr:"La v\xe9rit\xe9 est comme le soleil ; jette un voile sur elle et elle dispara\xeet du regard, mais le soleil reste o\xf9 il a toujours \xe9t\xe9.",categoryFr:"v\xe9rit\xe9",textJa:"\u771f\u5b9f\u306f\u592a\u967d\u306e\u3088\u3046\u3060\u3002\u8986\u3044\u3092\u304b\u3051\u308c\u3070\u8996\u754c\u304b\u3089\u6d88\u3048\u308b\u304c\u3001\u592a\u967d\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u306e\u5834\u6240\u306b\u3068\u3069\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u771f\u5b9f"},{id:"q007",text:"Biz neredeyiz? Sevgilinin bulundu\u011fu yerde. Neyiz biz? Onun i\xe7inde bir damlac\u0131k.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ask",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Where are we? Wherever the Beloved is. What are we? A single droplet within Him.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Wo sind wir? Wo immer der Geliebte ist. Was sind wir? Ein einziger Tropfen in Ihm.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"\xbfD\xf3nde estamos? Donde est\xe9 el Amado. \xbfQu\xe9 somos? Una sola gota dentro de \xc9l.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Onde estamos? Onde quer que esteja o Amado. O que somos? Uma \xfanica gota dentro Dele.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"O\xf9 sommes-nous ? L\xe0 o\xf9 est l'Aim\xe9. Que sommes-nous ? Une seule goutte en Lui.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306f\u3069\u3053\u306b\u3044\u308b\uff1f\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306e\u3044\u308b\u3068\u3053\u308d\u306b\u3002\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u3068\u306f\u4f55\u304b\uff1f\u5f7c\u306e\u4e2d\u306e\u4e00\u6ef4\u306e\u96eb\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q008",text:"Kendini bilen, Rabbini bilir.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"nefis",rarity:"common",textEn:"Whoever knows themselves knows their Lord.",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Wer sich selbst erkennt, erkennt seinen Herrn.",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"Quien se conoce a s\xed mismo conoce a su Se\xf1or.",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"Quem conhece a si mesmo conhece o seu Senhor.",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"Qui se conna\xeet soi-m\xeame conna\xeet son Seigneur.",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u5df1\u3092\u77e5\u308b\u8005\u306f\u3001\u305d\u306e\u4e3b\u3092\u77e5\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q009",text:"Bir mum di\u011fer bir mumu tutu\u015fturmakla \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131ndan bir \u015fey yitirmez.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"c\xf6mertlik",rarity:"common",textEn:"A candle loses nothing of its light by lighting another candle.",categoryEn:"generosity",textDe:"Eine Kerze verliert nichts von ihrem Licht, wenn sie eine andere Kerze entz\xfcndet.",categoryDe:"Gro\xdfz\xfcgigkeit",textEs:"Una vela no pierde nada de su luz al encender otra vela.",categoryEs:"generosidad",textPt:"Uma vela nada perde da sua luz ao acender outra vela.",categoryPt:"generosidade",textFr:"Une bougie ne perd rien de sa lumi\xe8re en allumant une autre bougie.",categoryFr:"g\xe9n\xe9rosit\xe9",textJa:"\u308d\u3046\u305d\u304f\u306f\u3001\u5225\u306e\u308d\u3046\u305d\u304f\u306b\u706b\u3092\u706f\u3057\u3066\u3082\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5149\u3092\u5c11\u3057\u3082\u5931\u308f\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5bdb\u5927\u3055"},{id:"q010",text:"Kalp bir ayna gibidir. Onu pas tutmu\u015fsa, \u0131\u015f\u0131k yans\u0131maz. Ama cilalan\u0131nca her \u015feyi g\xf6sterir.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"kalp",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The heart is like a mirror. When rust covers it, no light reflects. But once polished, it reveals everything.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Das Herz ist wie ein Spiegel. Wenn Rost ihn bedeckt, spiegelt kein Licht. Doch einmal poliert, offenbart er alles.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"El coraz\xf3n es como un espejo. Cuando lo cubre el \xf3xido, ninguna luz se refleja. Pero una vez pulido, lo revela todo.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"O cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 como um espelho. Quando a ferrugem o cobre, nenhuma luz se reflete. Mas, uma vez polido, revela tudo.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Le c\u0153ur est comme un miroir. Quand la rouille le couvre, aucune lumi\xe8re ne s'y refl\xe8te. Mais une fois poli, il r\xe9v\xe8le tout.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u5fc3\u306f\u93e1\u306e\u3088\u3046\u3060\u3002\u9306\u304c\u8986\u3048\u3070\u5149\u306f\u6620\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3002\u3060\u304c\u4e00\u5ea6\u78e8\u304b\u308c\u308c\u3070\u3001\u3059\u3079\u3066\u3092\u6620\u3057\u51fa\u3059\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q011",text:"\u0130\xe7inde bir nehir var; onu bulmak i\xe7in \xe7\xf6le gitme.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"There is a river within you; do not go to the desert to find it.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"In dir ist ein Fluss; geh nicht in die W\xfcste, um ihn zu finden.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Hay un r\xedo dentro de ti; no vayas al desierto a buscarlo.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"H\xe1 um rio dentro de ti; n\xe3o v\xe1s ao deserto procur\xe1-lo.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Il y a une rivi\xe8re en toi ; ne va pas au d\xe9sert pour la trouver.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u5ddd\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3002\u305d\u308c\u3092\u63a2\u3057\u306b\u7802\u6f20\u3078\u884c\u304f\u306a\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q012",text:"Sab\u0131r ac\u0131d\u0131r ama meyvesi tatl\u0131d\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"sabir",rarity:"common",textEn:"Patience is bitter, but its fruit is sweet.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Geduld ist bitter, doch ihre Frucht ist s\xfc\xdf.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"La paciencia es amarga, pero su fruto es dulce.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"A paci\xeancia \xe9 amarga, mas o seu fruto \xe9 doce.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"La patience est am\xe8re, mais son fruit est doux.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u5fcd\u8010\u306f\u82e6\u3044\u304c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5b9f\u306f\u7518\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q013",text:"Ney, ayr\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 anlat\u0131r. Hepimiz birer neyiz, k\xf6k\xfczden kopar\u0131lm\u0131\u015f.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hasret",rarity:"rare",textEn:"The reed tells the tale of separation. We are all reeds, torn from our roots.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Das Rohr erz\xe4hlt die Geschichte der Trennung. Wir alle sind Rohre, aus unseren Wurzeln gerissen.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"La ca\xf1a cuenta la historia de la separaci\xf3n. Todos somos ca\xf1as, arrancadas de nuestras ra\xedces.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"A cana conta a hist\xf3ria da separa\xe7\xe3o. Somos todos canas, arrancadas de nossas ra\xedzes.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Le roseau raconte l'histoire de la s\xe9paration. Nous sommes tous des roseaux, arrach\xe9s \xe0 nos racines.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u8466\u306f\u5225\u96e2\u306e\u7269\u8a9e\u3092\u8a9e\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306f\u7686\u3001\u6839\u304b\u3089\u5f15\u304d\u88c2\u304b\u308c\u305f\u8466\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q014",text:"Susarsan lal olursun, konu\u015fursan kelam olursun. Se\xe7.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"irade",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"If you stay silent, you become mute; if you speak, you become the Word. Choose.",categoryEn:"will",textDe:"Bleibst du still, wirst du stumm; sprichst du, wirst du zum Wort. W\xe4hle.",categoryDe:"Wille",textEs:"Si callas, te vuelves mudo; si hablas, te vuelves la Palabra. Elige.",categoryEs:"voluntad",textPt:"Se ficares calado, tornas-te mudo; se falares, tornas-te a Palavra. Escolhe.",categoryPt:"vontade",textFr:"Si tu te tais, tu deviens muet ; si tu parles, tu deviens la Parole. Choisis.",categoryFr:"volont\xe9",textJa:"\u9ed9\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308c\u3070\u3001\u5516\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002\u8a9e\u308c\u3070\u3001\u8a00\u8449\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002\u9078\u3073\u306a\u3055\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u610f\u5fd7"},{id:"q015",text:"G\xf6nl\xfcn\xfc y\u0131ka, temizle; o Allah'\u0131n evi olacak.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"kalp",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Wash your heart, cleanse it; it shall become the house of God.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Wasche dein Herz, reinige es; es wird zum Haus Gottes werden.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"Lava tu coraz\xf3n, purif\xedcalo; se volver\xe1 la casa de Dios.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"Lava o teu cora\xe7\xe3o, purifica-o; ele se tornar\xe1 a casa de Deus.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Lave ton c\u0153ur, purifie-le ; il deviendra la maison de Dieu.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u5fc3\u3092\u6d17\u3044\u3001\u6e05\u3081\u3088\u3002\u305d\u308c\u306f\u795e\u306e\u5bb6\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q016",text:"K\xe2inat bir kitapt\u0131r. Her yapra\u011f\u0131nda bir s\u0131r gizlidir.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hikmet",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The universe is a book. On every page a secret is hidden.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Das Universum ist ein Buch. Auf jeder Seite ist ein Geheimnis verborgen.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"El universo es un libro. En cada p\xe1gina se oculta un secreto.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"O universo \xe9 um livro. Em cada p\xe1gina esconde-se um segredo.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"L'univers est un livre. Sur chaque page se cache un secret.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u5b87\u5b99\u306f\u4e00\u518a\u306e\u66f8\u3060\u3002\u3069\u306e\u9801\u306b\u3082\u79d8\u5bc6\u304c\u96a0\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q017",text:"A\u015fk ate\u015fiyle yanan, d\xfcnyay\u0131 de\u011fi\u015ftirir.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"Whoever burns with the fire of love transforms the world.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Wer im Feuer der Liebe brennt, verwandelt die Welt.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Quien arde con el fuego del amor transforma el mundo.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Quem arde com o fogo do amor transforma o mundo.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Celui qui br\xfble du feu de l'amour transforme le monde.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u306e\u706b\u306b\u71c3\u3048\u308b\u8005\u306f\u3001\u4e16\u754c\u3092\u5909\u3048\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q018",text:"Herkes g\xf6r\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfc gibi de\u011fildir; herkes g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfc kadar g\xf6rebilir.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hikmet",rarity:"common",textEn:"No one is as they appear; each can see only as much as they themselves see.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Niemand ist, wie er erscheint; jeder kann nur so viel sehen, wie er selbst sieht.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"Nadie es como parece; cada uno solo puede ver cuanto ve por s\xed mismo.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"Ningu\xe9m \xe9 como aparenta; cada um s\xf3 consegue ver tanto quanto v\xea por si.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Personne n'est tel qu'il para\xeet ; chacun ne peut voir qu'autant qu'il voit lui-m\xeame.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u8ab0\u3082\u898b\u304b\u3051\u901a\u308a\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u4eba\u306f\u305d\u308c\u305e\u308c\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u898b\u308b\u3060\u3051\u3057\u304b\u898b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q019",text:"Ya oldu\u011fun gibi g\xf6r\xfcn, ya g\xf6r\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfcn gibi ol.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfck",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Either appear as you are, or be as you appear.",categoryEn:"honesty",textDe:"Erscheine, wie du bist, oder sei, wie du erscheinst.",categoryDe:"Ehrlichkeit",textEs:"O mu\xe9strate como eres, o s\xe9 como te muestras.",categoryEs:"honestidad",textPt:"Ou mostra-te como \xe9s, ou s\xea como te mostras.",categoryPt:"honestidade",textFr:"Ou parais tel que tu es, ou sois tel que tu parais.",categoryFr:"honn\xeatet\xe9",textJa:"\u3042\u308a\u306e\u307e\u307e\u306b\u73fe\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u73fe\u308c\u308b\u901a\u308a\u3067\u3042\u308c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u8aa0\u5b9f\u3055"},{id:"q020",text:"Yolun ortas\u0131nda durma. Ortas\u0131 yoktur yolun; ya ileri ya geri.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"irade",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Do not stand still in the middle of the road. The road has no middle; either forward or back.",categoryEn:"will",textDe:"Bleib nicht in der Mitte des Weges stehen. Der Weg hat keine Mitte; entweder vorw\xe4rts oder zur\xfcck.",categoryDe:"Wille",textEs:"No te quedes parado en medio del camino. El camino no tiene medio; o adelante o atr\xe1s.",categoryEs:"voluntad",textPt:"N\xe3o fiques parado no meio do caminho. O caminho n\xe3o tem meio; ou para a frente ou para tr\xe1s.",categoryPt:"vontade",textFr:"Ne reste pas immobile au milieu du chemin. Le chemin n'a pas de milieu ; soit en avant, soit en arri\xe8re.",categoryFr:"volont\xe9",textJa:"\u9053\u306e\u771f\u3093\u4e2d\u3067\u7acb\u3061\u6b62\u307e\u308b\u306a\u3002\u9053\u306b\u771f\u3093\u4e2d\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u524d\u3078\u9032\u3080\u304b\u3001\u5f8c\u308d\u3078\u9000\u304f\u304b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u610f\u5fd7"},{id:"q021",text:"Birlik \u015farab\u0131n\u0131 i\xe7ince, ayr\u0131l\u0131k ac\u0131s\u0131 sona erer.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"birlik",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Once you drink the wine of unity, the pain of separation comes to an end.",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"Hast du einmal den Wein der Einheit getrunken, endet der Schmerz der Trennung.",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"Una vez que bebes el vino de la unidad, el dolor de la separaci\xf3n llega a su fin.",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"Uma vez que bebas o vinho da unidade, a dor da separa\xe7\xe3o chega ao fim.",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"Une fois que tu bois le vin de l'unit\xe9, la douleur de la s\xe9paration prend fin.",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u3072\u3068\u305f\u3073\u4e00\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306e\u9152\u3092\u98f2\u3081\u3070\u3001\u5225\u96e2\u306e\u75db\u307f\u306f\u7d42\u308f\u308a\u3092\u8fce\u3048\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q022",text:"Korktu\u011fun \u015feyin yan\u0131na git. Orada hazine bulursun.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"cesaret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Walk toward what you fear. There you will find treasure.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"Geh auf das zu, was du f\xfcrchtest. Dort wirst du den Schatz finden.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"Camina hacia lo que temes. All\xed encontrar\xe1s el tesoro.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"Caminha em dire\xe7\xe3o \xe0quilo que temes. Ali encontrar\xe1s o tesouro.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"Marche vers ce que tu crains. L\xe0 tu trouveras le tr\xe9sor.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u6050\u308c\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3078\u5411\u304b\u3063\u3066\u6b69\u3081\u3002\u305d\u3053\u306b\u5b9d\u3092\u898b\u3044\u3060\u3059\u3060\u308d\u3046\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q023",text:"Ger\xe7ek dost, seni oldu\u011fun gibi kabul eden de\u011fil, olabilece\u011fin en iyi hale do\u011fru \xe7ekendir.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"dostluk",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"A true friend is not one who accepts you as you are, but one who draws you toward the best you can become.",categoryEn:"friendship",textDe:"Ein wahrer Freund ist nicht der, der dich nimmt, wie du bist, sondern der dich zum Besten zieht, das du werden kannst.",categoryDe:"Freundschaft",textEs:"Un verdadero amigo no es quien te acepta como eres, sino quien te impulsa hacia lo mejor que puedes llegar a ser.",categoryEs:"amistad",textPt:"Um verdadeiro amigo n\xe3o \xe9 aquele que te aceita como \xe9s, mas aquele que te impulsiona ao melhor que podes vir a ser.",categoryPt:"amizade",textFr:"Un vrai ami n'est pas celui qui t'accepte tel que tu es, mais celui qui t'attire vers le meilleur que tu peux devenir.",categoryFr:"amiti\xe9",textJa:"\u771f\u306e\u53cb\u3068\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u3042\u308a\u306e\u307e\u307e\u53d7\u3051\u5165\u308c\u308b\u8005\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u304c\u306a\u308a\u3046\u308b\u6700\u5584\u3078\u3068\u5f15\u304d\u4e0a\u3052\u308b\u8005\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u53cb\u60c5"},{id:"q024",text:"G\xf6lgeni b\u0131rak, g\xfcne\u015fi takip et.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"degisim",rarity:"common",textEn:"Leave your shadow behind and follow the sun.",categoryEn:"transformation",textDe:"Lass deinen Schatten hinter dir und folge der Sonne.",categoryDe:"Wandlung",textEs:"Deja tu sombra atr\xe1s y sigue al sol.",categoryEs:"transformaci\xf3n",textPt:"Deixa a tua sombra para tr\xe1s e segue o sol.",categoryPt:"transforma\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Laisse ton ombre derri\xe8re toi et suis le soleil.",categoryFr:"transformation",textJa:"\u5f71\u3092\u5f8c\u306b\u3057\u3066\u3001\u592a\u967d\u306b\u5f93\u3048\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5909\u5bb9"},{id:"q025",text:"\u0130\xe7indeki denizi fark et. D\u0131\u015far\u0131da p\u0131nar arama.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Notice the sea within you. Do not seek a spring outside.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Beachte das Meer in dir. Suche keine Quelle drau\xdfen.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Advierte el mar que hay en ti. No busques un manantial afuera.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"Repara no mar que h\xe1 em ti. N\xe3o procures uma nascente l\xe1 fora.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Remarque la mer en toi. Ne cherche pas une source au-dehors.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u4e2d\u306e\u6d77\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u304d\u306a\u3055\u3044\u3002\u5916\u306b\u6cc9\u3092\u6c42\u3081\u308b\u306a\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q026",text:"Bir insan bir anda bile de\u011fi\u015febilir. Bu de\u011fi\u015fime kap\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7\u0131k tut.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"degisim",rarity:"common",textEn:"A person can change in a single moment. Keep your door open to that change.",categoryEn:"transformation",textDe:"Ein Mensch kann sich in einem einzigen Augenblick wandeln. Halte deine T\xfcr f\xfcr diesen Wandel offen.",categoryDe:"Wandlung",textEs:"Una persona puede cambiar en un solo instante. Mant\xe9n tu puerta abierta a ese cambio.",categoryEs:"transformaci\xf3n",textPt:"Uma pessoa pode mudar num \xfanico instante. Mant\xe9m a tua porta aberta a essa mudan\xe7a.",categoryPt:"transforma\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Une personne peut changer en un seul instant. Garde ta porte ouverte \xe0 ce changement.",categoryFr:"transformation",textJa:"\u4eba\u306f\u305f\u3060\u4e00\u77ac\u3067\u5909\u308f\u308a\u3046\u308b\u3002\u305d\u306e\u5909\u5316\u306b\u6249\u3092\u958b\u3051\u3066\u304a\u304d\u306a\u3055\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5909\u5bb9"},{id:"q027",text:"A\u015fk bir ate\u015ftir; ya yakar d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcr, ya da yok eder.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Love is a fire; it either burns and transforms you, or it destroys you.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Die Liebe ist ein Feuer; entweder brennt sie und verwandelt dich, oder sie zerst\xf6rt dich.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"El amor es un fuego; o te quema y te transforma, o te destruye.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O amor \xe9 um fogo; ou te queima e te transforma, ou te destr\xf3i.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"L'amour est un feu ; soit il te br\xfble et te transforme, soit il te d\xe9truit.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u306f\u706b\u3060\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u71c3\u3084\u3057\u3066\u5909\u3048\u308b\u304b\u3001\u6ec5\u307c\u3059\u304b\u306e\u3069\u3061\u3089\u304b\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q028",text:"Sessizlik bazen en derin konu\u015fmad\u0131r.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"hikmet",rarity:"common",textEn:"Silence is sometimes the deepest of all conversations.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Stille ist manchmal das tiefste aller Gespr\xe4che.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"El silencio es a veces la m\xe1s profunda de todas las conversaciones.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"O sil\xeancio \xe9, por vezes, a mais profunda de todas as conversas.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Le silence est parfois la plus profonde de toutes les conversations.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u6c88\u9ed9\u306f\u6642\u306b\u3001\u3042\u3089\u3086\u308b\u4f1a\u8a71\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u6700\u3082\u6df1\u3044\u3082\u306e\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q029",text:"Seni en iyi tan\u0131yan, sana en \xe7ok zorluk \xe7\u0131karand\u0131r. \xc7\xfcnk\xfc o seni d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcr.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"degisim",rarity:"rare",textEn:"The one who knows you best is the one who challenges you the most. For that one transforms you.",categoryEn:"transformation",textDe:"Der, der dich am besten kennt, ist der, der dich am meisten herausfordert. Denn er verwandelt dich.",categoryDe:"Wandlung",textEs:"Quien mejor te conoce es quien m\xe1s te desaf\xeda. Pues ese te transforma.",categoryEs:"transformaci\xf3n",textPt:"Quem melhor te conhece \xe9 quem mais te desafia. Pois esse te transforma.",categoryPt:"transforma\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Celui qui te conna\xeet le mieux est celui qui te met le plus \xe0 l'\xe9preuve. Car celui-l\xe0 te transforme.",categoryFr:"transformation",textJa:"\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u6700\u3082\u3088\u304f\u77e5\u308b\u8005\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u6700\u3082\u8a66\u3059\u8005\u3060\u3002\u305d\u306e\u8005\u304c\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u5909\u3048\u308b\u306e\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5909\u5bb9"},{id:"q030",text:"Nur, karanl\u0131\u011f\u0131n i\xe7inden gelir. Karanl\u0131ktan ka\xe7ma.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"cesaret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Light comes through the darkness. Do not flee the dark.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"Das Licht kommt durch die Dunkelheit. Fliehe nicht vor dem Dunkel.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"La luz llega a trav\xe9s de la oscuridad. No huyas de lo oscuro.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"A luz vem atrav\xe9s da escurid\xe3o. N\xe3o fujas do escuro.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"La lumi\xe8re vient \xe0 travers les t\xe9n\xe8bres. Ne fuis pas l'obscurit\xe9.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u5149\u306f\u95c7\u3092\u901a\u3057\u3066\u6765\u308b\u3002\u95c7\u304b\u3089\u9003\u3052\u308b\u306a\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q031",text:"Her nefes bir hediyedir; fark\u0131nda m\u0131s\u0131n?",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"s\xfck\xfcr",rarity:"common",textEn:"Each breath is a gift; are you aware of it?",categoryEn:"gratitude",textDe:"Jeder Atemzug ist ein Geschenk; bist du dir dessen bewusst?",categoryDe:"Dankbarkeit",textEs:"Cada aliento es un regalo; \xbferes consciente de ello?",categoryEs:"gratitud",textPt:"Cada respira\xe7\xe3o \xe9 um presente; est\xe1s ciente disso?",categoryPt:"gratid\xe3o",textFr:"Chaque souffle est un pr\xe9sent ; en es-tu conscient ?",categoryFr:"gratitude",textJa:"\u3072\u3068\u606f\u3072\u3068\u606f\u304c\u8d08\u308a\u7269\u3060\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u305d\u308c\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u304b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611f\u8b1d"},{id:"q032",text:"Kalbinde ne varsa, dilin onu konu\u015fur.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"kalp",rarity:"common",textEn:"Whatever is in your heart, your tongue will speak.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Was in deinem Herzen ist, wird deine Zunge sprechen.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"Lo que haya en tu coraz\xf3n, tu lengua lo hablar\xe1.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"O que houver no teu cora\xe7\xe3o, a tua l\xedngua falar\xe1.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Ce qui est dans ton c\u0153ur, ta langue le dira.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u5fc3\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3092\u3001\u820c\u306f\u8a9e\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q033",text:"Y\xfcz kere d\xfc\u015fsen de, y\xfcz bir kere kalk.",original:"",source:"\u015eems-i Tebrizi",category:"sabir",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Though you fall a hundred times, rise a hundred and one.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Auch wenn du hundertmal f\xe4llst, erhebe dich einhundertundeinmal.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"Aunque caigas cien veces, lev\xe1ntate ciento una.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"Ainda que caias cem vezes, ergue-te cento e uma.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"M\xeame si tu tombes cent fois, rel\xe8ve-toi cent une fois.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u767e\u5ea6\u5012\u308c\u3066\u3082\u3001\u767e\u4e00\u5ea6\u7acb\u3061\u4e0a\u304c\u308c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q034",text:"Ben Yunus'um, bu d\xfcnyaya bir kez gelirim. Sevgiyi b\u0131rakacak ne var ki geride?",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ask",rarity:"rare",textEn:"I am Yunus, I come to this world but once. What is there to leave behind but love?",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Ich bin Yunus, ich komme nur einmal in diese Welt. Was bleibt zu hinterlassen au\xdfer Liebe?",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Soy Yunus, vengo a este mundo una sola vez. \xbfQu\xe9 hay que dejar atr\xe1s sino amor?",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Sou Yunus, venho a este mundo apenas uma vez. O que h\xe1 para deixar sen\xe3o amor?",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Je suis Yunus, je ne viens qu'une fois en ce monde. Que reste-t-il \xe0 laisser sinon l'amour ?",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u30e6\u30cc\u30b9\u3001\u3053\u306e\u4e16\u306b\u6765\u308b\u306e\u306f\u305f\u3060\u4e00\u5ea6\u3002\u611b\u306e\u307b\u304b\u306b\u3001\u907a\u3059\u3082\u306e\u306a\u3069\u3042\u308d\u3046\u304b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q035",text:"Ben gelmedim dava i\xe7in, benim i\u015fim sevi i\xe7in. Dost'un evi g\xf6n\xfcllerdir, g\xf6n\xfcller yapmaya geldim.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ask",rarity:"rare",textEn:"I came not for quarrel; my work is love. The house of the Beloved is in hearts, and I came to build hearts.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Ich kam nicht zum Streit; mein Werk ist die Liebe. Das Haus des Geliebten ist in den Herzen, und ich kam, um Herzen zu bauen.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"No vine a re\xf1ir; mi labor es el amor. La casa del Amado est\xe1 en los corazones, y vine a construir corazones.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"N\xe3o vim para a briga; o meu trabalho \xe9 o amor. A casa do Amado est\xe1 nos cora\xe7\xf5es, e vim construir cora\xe7\xf5es.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Je ne suis pas venu pour la querelle ; mon \u0153uvre est l'amour. La maison de l'Aim\xe9 est dans les c\u0153urs, et je suis venu b\xe2tir des c\u0153urs.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4e89\u3044\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6765\u305f\u306e\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u4ed5\u4e8b\u306f\u611b\u3060\u3002\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306e\u5bb6\u306f\u5fc3\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u308a\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u7bc9\u304f\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6765\u305f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q036",text:"Sevelim sevilelim; bu d\xfcnya kimseye kalmaz.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"Let us love and be loved; this world is for no one to keep.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Lasst uns lieben und geliebt werden; diese Welt geh\xf6rt keinem f\xfcr immer.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Amemos y seamos amados; este mundo no es de nadie para conservarlo.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Amemos e sejamos amados; este mundo n\xe3o \xe9 de ningu\xe9m para guardar.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Aimons et soyons aim\xe9s ; ce monde n'est \xe0 personne pour le garder.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u3057\u3001\u611b\u3055\u308c\u3088\u3046\u3002\u3053\u306e\u4e16\u306f\u8ab0\u306e\u3082\u306e\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3068\u3069\u307e\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3067\u3082\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q037",text:"\u0130lim ilim bilmektir, ilim kendin bilmektir. Sen kendini bilmezsen, bu nice okumakt\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"nefis",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Knowledge is to know knowledge; knowledge is to know oneself. If you do not know yourself, what good is all this reading?",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Wissen ist, das Wissen zu kennen; Wissen ist, sich selbst zu kennen. Wenn du dich selbst nicht kennst, was n\xfctzt all das Lesen?",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"El conocimiento es conocer el conocimiento; el conocimiento es conocerse a uno mismo. Si no te conoces a ti, \xbfde qu\xe9 sirve tanta lectura?",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"O conhecimento \xe9 conhecer o conhecimento; o conhecimento \xe9 conhecer a si mesmo. Se n\xe3o te conheces, de que serve toda essa leitura?",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"Le savoir, c'est conna\xeetre le savoir ; le savoir, c'est se conna\xeetre soi-m\xeame. Si tu ne te connais pas, \xe0 quoi bon toutes ces lectures ?",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u77e5\u3068\u306f\u77e5\u3092\u77e5\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3002\u77e5\u3068\u306f\u5df1\u3092\u77e5\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3002\u5df1\u3092\u77e5\u3089\u306d\u3070\u3001\u3042\u308c\u307b\u3069\u306e\u8aad\u66f8\u304c\u4f55\u306e\u5f79\u306b\u7acb\u3068\u3046\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q038",text:"Bir kez g\xf6n\xfcl y\u0131kt\u0131ysan, k\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131n namaz de\u011fil. Yetmi\u015f iki millet bile etmez o g\xfcnah\u0131.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"kalp",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"If you break a heart even once, your prayers are not prayers. Not even seventy-two nations can absolve that sin.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Brichst du ein Herz auch nur einmal, sind deine Gebete keine Gebete. Nicht einmal zweiundsiebzig V\xf6lker k\xf6nnen diese S\xfcnde tilgen.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"Si rompes un coraz\xf3n aunque sea una vez, tus oraciones no son oraciones. Ni siquiera setenta y dos naciones pueden absolver ese pecado.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"Se partires um cora\xe7\xe3o ao menos uma vez, as tuas ora\xe7\xf5es n\xe3o s\xe3o ora\xe7\xf5es. Nem mesmo setenta e duas na\xe7\xf5es podem absolver esse pecado.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Si tu brises un c\u0153ur ne serait-ce qu'une fois, tes pri\xe8res ne sont pas des pri\xe8res. M\xeame soixante-douze nations ne peuvent absoudre ce p\xe9ch\xe9.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u305f\u3060\u4e00\u5ea6\u3067\u3082\u5fc3\u3092\u50b7\u3064\u3051\u308c\u3070\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u7948\u308a\u306f\u7948\u308a\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u4e03\u5341\u4e8c\u306e\u6c11\u65cf\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u3057\u3066\u3082\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7f6a\u306f\u8d66\u305b\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q039",text:"Cennet cennet dedikleri birka\xe7 k\xf6\u015fkle birka\xe7 huri. \u0130steyene ver sen an\u0131, bana seni gerek seni.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ask",rarity:"rare",textEn:"What they call paradise is a few mansions and a few houris. Give it to whoever wants it; what I want is You, only You.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Was sie Paradies nennen, sind ein paar Villen und ein paar Huris. Gib es, wem es begehrt; was ich will, bist Du, nur Du.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Lo que llaman para\xedso son unas mansiones y unas hur\xedes. D\xe1selo a quien lo quiera; lo que yo quiero eres T\xfa, solo T\xfa.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O que chamam de para\xedso s\xe3o algumas mans\xf5es e algumas h\xfaris. D\xe1-o a quem o quiser; o que eu quero \xe9s Tu, s\xf3 Tu.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Ce qu'ils appellent paradis n'est que quelques demeures et quelques houris. Donne-le \xe0 qui le veut ; ce que je veux, c'est Toi, rien que Toi.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u5f7c\u3089\u304c\u697d\u5712\u3068\u547c\u3076\u3082\u306e\u306f\u3001\u3044\u304f\u3064\u304b\u306e\u9928\u3068\u3044\u304f\u3064\u304b\u306e\u5929\u5973\u3002\u6b32\u3057\u3044\u8005\u306b\u3084\u308c\u3070\u3088\u3044\u3002\u79c1\u304c\u6b32\u3057\u3044\u306e\u306f\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3001\u305f\u3060\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3060\u3051\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q040",text:"Ete kemi\u011fe b\xfcr\xfcnd\xfcm, Yunus diye g\xf6r\xfcnd\xfcm.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"birlik",rarity:"rare",textEn:"I clothed myself in flesh and bone, and appeared as Yunus.",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"Ich kleidete mich in Fleisch und Bein und erschien als Yunus.",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"Me vest\xed de carne y hueso, y aparec\xed como Yunus.",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"Vesti-me de carne e osso, e apareci como Yunus.",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"Je me suis v\xeatu de chair et d'os, et je suis apparu sous le nom de Yunus.",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u8089\u3068\u9aa8\u3092\u307e\u3068\u3044\u3001\u30e6\u30cc\u30b9\u3068\u3057\u3066\u73fe\u308c\u305f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q041",text:"A\u015fk\u0131n ald\u0131 benden beni, bana seni gerek seni.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Your love has taken me from myself; what I need is You, only You.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Deine Liebe hat mich von mir selbst genommen; was ich brauche, bist Du, nur Du.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Tu amor me ha apartado de m\xed mismo; lo que necesito eres T\xfa, solo T\xfa.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O teu amor tirou-me de mim mesmo; o que preciso \xe9s Tu, s\xf3 Tu.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Ton amour m'a pris \xe0 moi-m\xeame ; ce dont j'ai besoin, c'est Toi, rien que Toi.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u611b\u304c\u79c1\u3092\u79c1\u81ea\u8eab\u304b\u3089\u596a\u3063\u305f\u3002\u79c1\u306b\u5fc5\u8981\u306a\u306e\u306f\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3001\u305f\u3060\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3060\u3051\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q042",text:"Dost elinden i\xe7tim \u015farap, bende kalmad\u0131 hesap.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"I drank wine from the hand of the Beloved; no reckoning remains in me.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Ich trank Wein aus der Hand des Geliebten; keine Rechenschaft bleibt mehr in mir.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Beb\xed vino de la mano del Amado; ya no queda cuenta alguna en m\xed.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Bebi vinho da m\xe3o do Amado; j\xe1 n\xe3o resta conta alguma em mim.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"J'ai bu le vin de la main de l'Aim\xe9 ; il ne reste plus en moi aucun compte \xe0 rendre.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306e\u624b\u304b\u3089\u9152\u3092\u98f2\u3093\u3060\u3002\u3082\u306f\u3084\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u52d8\u5b9a\u306f\u6b8b\u3063\u3066\u3044\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q043",text:"Benim ile \xfcn \xfc san\u0131m, g\xf6nl\xfcmdeki dost dostum.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"common",textEn:"My name and renown are with me; the friend in my heart is my truest friend.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Mein Name und mein Ruhm sind bei mir; der Freund in meinem Herzen ist mein wahrster Freund.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Mi nombre y mi fama est\xe1n conmigo; el amigo en mi coraz\xf3n es mi amigo m\xe1s verdadero.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"O meu nome e a minha fama est\xe3o comigo; o amigo no meu cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o meu amigo mais verdadeiro.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Mon nom et ma renomm\xe9e sont avec moi ; l'ami dans mon c\u0153ur est mon ami le plus vrai.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u540d\u3082\u8a89\u308c\u3082\u79c1\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306e\u4e2d\u306e\u53cb\u3053\u305d\u3001\u6700\u3082\u771f\u306e\u53cb\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q044",text:"Ad\u0131m ad\u0131m benden \xf6te, bana ta\u015f atan ki\u015finin. Her att\u0131\u011f\u0131 benim i\xe7in, g\xfcl demeye ba\u015flad\u0131m.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"sabir",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Step by step beyond myself I go. For each stone thrown at me, I have begun to say: a rose.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Schritt f\xfcr Schritt gehe ich \xfcber mich selbst hinaus. F\xfcr jeden Stein, der nach mir geworfen wird, habe ich begonnen zu sagen: eine Rose.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"Paso a paso m\xe1s all\xe1 de m\xed mismo voy. Por cada piedra que me arrojan, he empezado a decir: una rosa.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"Passo a passo, para al\xe9m de mim mesmo eu vou. Por cada pedra que me atiram, comecei a dizer: uma rosa.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"Pas \xe0 pas, je vais au-del\xe0 de moi-m\xeame. \xc0 chaque pierre qu'on me jette, j'ai commenc\xe9 \xe0 dire : une rose.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u4e00\u6b69\u305a\u3064\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u8d8a\u3048\u3066\u3044\u304f\u3002\u79c1\u306b\u6295\u3052\u3089\u308c\u308b\u77f3\u306e\u4e00\u3064\u3072\u3068\u3064\u306b\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u300c\u30d0\u30e9\u3060\u300d\u3068\u8a00\u3044\u59cb\u3081\u305f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q045",text:"Ne ararsan kendinde ara. Kud\xfcs'te Mekke'de de\u011fil.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"common",textEn:"Whatever you seek, seek within yourself. Not in Jerusalem, not in Mecca.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Was du auch suchst, suche es in dir selbst. Nicht in Jerusalem, nicht in Mekka.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Lo que busques, b\xfascalo dentro de ti. No en Jerusal\xe9n, ni en La Meca.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"O que quer que busques, busca-o dentro de ti. N\xe3o em Jerusal\xe9m, nem em Meca.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Quoi que tu cherches, cherche-le en toi-m\xeame. Ni \xe0 J\xe9rusalem, ni \xe0 La Mecque.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u4f55\u3092\u6c42\u3081\u308b\u306b\u305b\u3088\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u6c42\u3081\u3088\u3002\u30a8\u30eb\u30b5\u30ec\u30e0\u3067\u3082\u306a\u304f\u3001\u30e1\u30c3\u30ab\u3067\u3082\u306a\u304f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q046",text:"\u015eu d\xfcnya bir p\u0131nar gibidir, i\xe7enler doymaz.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"hikmet",rarity:"common",textEn:"This world is like a spring; those who drink are never satisfied.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Diese Welt ist wie eine Quelle; wer trinkt, wird niemals satt.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"Este mundo es como un manantial; quienes beben nunca quedan saciados.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"Este mundo \xe9 como uma nascente; quem bebe nunca se sacia.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Ce monde est comme une source ; ceux qui boivent ne sont jamais rassasi\xe9s.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u3053\u306e\u4e16\u306f\u6cc9\u306e\u3088\u3046\u3060\u3002\u98f2\u3080\u8005\u306f\u6c7a\u3057\u3066\u6e80\u305f\u3055\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q047",text:"G\xf6nl\xfcm bir b\xfclb\xfcl gibi, dost bah\xe7esinde \xf6ter.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"My heart is like a nightingale that sings in the Beloved's garden.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Mein Herz ist wie eine Nachtigall, die im Garten des Geliebten singt.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Mi coraz\xf3n es como un ruise\xf1or que canta en el jard\xedn del Amado.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O meu cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 como um rouxinol que canta no jardim do Amado.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Mon c\u0153ur est comme un rossignol qui chante dans le jardin de l'Aim\xe9.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u3001\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306e\u5ead\u3067\u3055\u3048\u305a\u308b\u30ca\u30a4\u30c1\u30f3\u30b2\u30fc\u30eb\u306e\u3088\u3046\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q048",text:"S\xf6z ola kese sava\u015f\u0131, s\xf6z ola kestire ba\u015f\u0131. S\xf6z ola a\u011fulu a\u015f\u0131, ya\u011f ile bal eyleye.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"hikmet",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"A word can end a war, a word can sever a head. A word can turn bitter poison into honey and oil.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Ein Wort kann einen Krieg beenden, ein Wort kann ein Haupt abtrennen. Ein Wort kann bitteres Gift in Honig und \xd6l verwandeln.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"Una palabra puede acabar una guerra, una palabra puede cortar una cabeza. Una palabra puede volver miel y aceite el veneno amargo.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"Uma palavra pode acabar uma guerra, uma palavra pode cortar uma cabe\xe7a. Uma palavra pode tornar mel e \xf3leo o veneno amargo.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Un mot peut mettre fin \xe0 une guerre, un mot peut trancher une t\xeate. Un mot peut changer un poison amer en miel et en huile.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u4e00\u8a00\u304c\u6226\u3092\u7d42\u308f\u3089\u305b\u3001\u4e00\u8a00\u304c\u9996\u3092\u843d\u3068\u3059\u3002\u4e00\u8a00\u304c\u82e6\u3044\u6bd2\u3092\u871c\u3068\u6cb9\u306b\u5909\u3048\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q049",text:"Bir ben vard\u0131r bende benden i\xe7eru.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"rare",textEn:"There is an I within me, deeper than myself.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"In mir ist ein Ich, tiefer als ich selbst.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Hay un yo dentro de m\xed, m\xe1s hondo que yo mismo.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"H\xe1 um eu dentro de mim, mais profundo do que eu mesmo.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Il y a un moi en moi, plus profond que moi-m\xeame.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3001\u79c1\u81ea\u8eab\u3088\u308a\u6df1\u3044\u300c\u79c1\u300d\u304c\u3044\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q050",text:"Hak'tan gelen \u015ferbeti i\xe7tik elhamd\xfclillah.",original:"",source:"Yunus Emre",category:"s\xfck\xfcr",rarity:"common",textEn:"We have drunk the sherbet that comes from the Truth, praise be to God.",categoryEn:"gratitude",textDe:"Wir haben den Sirup getrunken, der von der Wahrheit kommt, gelobt sei Gott.",categoryDe:"Dankbarkeit",textEs:"Hemos bebido el sorbete que viene de la Verdad, alabado sea Dios.",categoryEs:"gratitud",textPt:"Bebemos o xarope que vem da Verdade, louvado seja Deus.",categoryPt:"gratid\xe3o",textFr:"Nous avons bu le sirop qui vient de la V\xe9rit\xe9, louange \xe0 Dieu.",categoryFr:"gratitude",textJa:"\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306f\u771f\u5b9f\u304b\u3089\u6765\u308b\u7518\u9732\u3092\u98f2\u3093\u3060\u3002\u795e\u306b\u8b83\u3048\u3042\u308c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611f\u8b1d"},{id:"q051",text:"Hararet nardad\u0131r, sacda de\u011fil. Keramet ba\u015ftad\u0131r, ta\xe7ta de\u011fil.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"hikmet",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The heat is in the fire, not in the pan. The grace is in the head, not in the crown.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Die Hitze ist im Feuer, nicht in der Pfanne. Die Gnade ist im Haupt, nicht in der Krone.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"El calor est\xe1 en el fuego, no en la sart\xe9n. La gracia est\xe1 en la cabeza, no en la corona.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"O calor est\xe1 no fogo, n\xe3o na panela. A gra\xe7a est\xe1 na cabe\xe7a, n\xe3o na coroa.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"La chaleur est dans le feu, non dans la po\xeale. La gr\xe2ce est dans la t\xeate, non dans la couronne.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u71b1\u306f\u706b\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u308a\u3001\u934b\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u6075\u307f\u306f\u982d\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u308a\u3001\u51a0\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q052",text:"Eline, beline, diline sahip ol.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"nefis",rarity:"common",textEn:"Master your hand, your loins, and your tongue.",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Beherrsche deine Hand, deine Lenden und deine Zunge.",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"Domina tu mano, tus entra\xf1as y tu lengua.",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"Domina a tua m\xe3o, as tuas entranhas e a tua l\xedngua.",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"Ma\xeetrise ta main, tes reins et ta langue.",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u5df1\u306e\u624b\u3068\u3001\u8170\u3068\u3001\u820c\u3092\u6cbb\u3081\u3088\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q053",text:"Okunacak en b\xfcy\xfck kitap insand\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"nefis",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The greatest book to be read is the human being.",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Das gr\xf6\xdfte Buch, das es zu lesen gilt, ist der Mensch.",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"El mayor libro que se ha de leer es el ser humano.",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"O maior livro a ser lido \xe9 o ser humano.",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"Le plus grand livre \xe0 lire est l'\xeatre humain.",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u8aad\u3080\u3079\u304d\u6700\u3082\u5049\u5927\u306a\u66f8\u306f\u3001\u4eba\u9593\u305d\u306e\u3082\u306e\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q054",text:"Kad\u0131nlar\u0131 okutunuz. Bir milleti kurtarmak i\xe7in evvela analar\u0131n\u0131 irfanl\u0131 yeti\u015ftirmek laz\u0131md\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"bilgi",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Educate your women. To save a nation, one must first raise its mothers in wisdom.",categoryEn:"knowledge",textDe:"Bildet eure Frauen. Um ein Volk zu retten, muss man zuerst seine M\xfctter in Weisheit erziehen.",categoryDe:"Wissen",textEs:"Educa a tus mujeres. Para salvar a una naci\xf3n, primero hay que criar a sus madres en la sabidur\xeda.",categoryEs:"conocimiento",textPt:"Educa as tuas mulheres. Para salvar uma na\xe7\xe3o, \xe9 preciso primeiro criar as suas m\xe3es na sabedoria.",categoryPt:"conhecimento",textFr:"\xc9duque tes femmes. Pour sauver une nation, il faut d'abord \xe9lever ses m\xe8res dans la sagesse.",categoryFr:"savoir",textJa:"\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u5973\u6027\u305f\u3061\u3092\u6559\u80b2\u305b\u3088\u3002\u56fd\u3092\u6551\u3046\u306b\u306f\u3001\u307e\u305a\u305d\u306e\u6bcd\u305f\u3061\u3092\u667a\u6167\u306e\u3046\u3061\u306b\u80b2\u3066\u306d\u3070\u306a\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u8b58"},{id:"q055",text:"M\xfcr\u015fidin s\xf6z\xfc, suyun ta\u015f\u0131 yalamas\u0131 gibidir. Yava\u015f ama emin.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"sabir",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The word of the master is like water wearing away a stone. Slow, but sure.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Das Wort des Meisters ist wie Wasser, das einen Stein aush\xf6hlt. Langsam, doch gewiss.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"La palabra del maestro es como el agua que desgasta una piedra. Lenta, pero segura.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"A palavra do mestre \xe9 como a \xe1gua que desgasta a pedra. Lenta, mas certa.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"La parole du ma\xeetre est comme l'eau qui use une pierre. Lente, mais s\xfbre.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u5e2b\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u306f\u3001\u77f3\u3092\u3059\u308a\u6e1b\u3089\u3059\u6c34\u306e\u3088\u3046\u3060\u3002\u3086\u3063\u304f\u308a\u3068\u3001\u3057\u304b\u3057\u78ba\u304b\u306b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q056",text:"G\xf6n\xfcl \xc7alab'\u0131n taht\u0131, \xc7alab g\xf6n\xfcle bakt\u0131.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"kalp",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The heart is the throne of God; God looked upon the heart.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Das Herz ist der Thron Gottes; Gott blickte auf das Herz.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"El coraz\xf3n es el trono de Dios; Dios mir\xf3 al coraz\xf3n.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"O cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o trono de Deus; Deus olhou para o cora\xe7\xe3o.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Le c\u0153ur est le tr\xf4ne de Dieu ; Dieu a regard\xe9 le c\u0153ur.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u5fc3\u306f\u795e\u306e\u5fa1\u5ea7\u3002\u795e\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u3054\u89a7\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q057",text:"Her ne ararsan aray\u0131 aray\u0131. Kendinden ba\u015fka bir \u015fey bulamazs\u0131n.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"common",textEn:"Search and search for whatever you seek. You will find nothing but yourself.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Suche und suche, was du auch suchst. Du wirst nichts als dich selbst finden.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Busca y busca lo que busques. No hallar\xe1s m\xe1s que a ti mismo.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"Procura e procura o que quer que busques. Nada encontrar\xe1s sen\xe3o a ti mesmo.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Cherche et cherche encore ce que tu cherches. Tu ne trouveras rien d'autre que toi-m\xeame.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u4f55\u3092\u6c42\u3081\u3088\u3046\u3068\u3001\u63a2\u3057\u3066\u3001\u63a2\u3057\u7d9a\u3051\u3088\u3002\u5df1\u81ea\u8eab\u306e\u307b\u304b\u306b\u306f\u4f55\u3082\u898b\u3044\u3060\u3055\u306a\u3044\u3060\u308d\u3046\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q058",text:"D\xf6rt kap\u0131 k\u0131rk makam: \u015feriat, tarikat, marifet, hakikat.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"yol",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Four gates and forty stations: sharia, tariqa, marifa, haqiqa.",categoryEn:"path",textDe:"Vier Tore und vierzig Stufen: Scharia, Tariqa, Marifa, Haqiqa.",categoryDe:"Weg",textEs:"Cuatro puertas y cuarenta estaciones: sharia, tariqa, marifa, haqiqa.",categoryEs:"sendero",textPt:"Quatro portas e quarenta esta\xe7\xf5es: xaria, tariqa, marifa, haqiqa.",categoryPt:"caminho",textFr:"Quatre portes et quarante stations : charia, tariqa, marifa, haqiqa.",categoryFr:"voie",textJa:"\u56db\u3064\u306e\u9580\u3068\u56db\u5341\u306e\u968e\u68af\u2014\u2014\u30b7\u30e3\u30ea\u30fc\u30a2\u3001\u30bf\u30ea\u30fc\u30ab\u3001\u30de\u30a2\u30ea\u30d5\u30a1\u3001\u30cf\u30ad\u30fc\u30ab\u3002",categoryJa:"\u9053"},{id:"q059",text:"\u0130ncinsen de incitme.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"sabir",rarity:"common",textEn:"Though you be wounded, wound no one.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Auch wenn du verwundet bist, verwunde keinen.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"Aunque est\xe9s herido, no hieras a nadie.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"Ainda que estejas ferido, n\xe3o firas ningu\xe9m.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"M\xeame bless\xe9, ne blesse personne.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u305f\u3068\u3048\u50b7\u3064\u3044\u3066\u3082\u3001\u8ab0\u3082\u50b7\u3064\u3051\u308b\u306a\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q060",text:"D\xfcnya gam\u0131 \xe7ekmek, ahiret i\xe7in haz\u0131rlanmak de\u011fildir. \u015eimdi yap iyi olan\u0131.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"an",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"To bear the world's sorrow is not the same as preparing for the hereafter. Do the good now.",categoryEn:"present moment",textDe:"Den Kummer der Welt zu tragen ist nicht dasselbe wie sich auf das Jenseits vorzubereiten. Tu das Gute jetzt.",categoryDe:"Gegenwart",textEs:"Cargar con el dolor del mundo no es lo mismo que prepararse para el m\xe1s all\xe1. Haz el bien ahora.",categoryEs:"presente",textPt:"Carregar a tristeza do mundo n\xe3o \xe9 o mesmo que preparar-se para o al\xe9m. Faz o bem agora.",categoryPt:"presente",textFr:"Porter le chagrin du monde n'est pas la m\xeame chose que se pr\xe9parer \xe0 l'au-del\xe0. Fais le bien maintenant.",categoryFr:"pr\xe9sent",textJa:"\u4e16\u306e\u6182\u3044\u3092\u80cc\u8ca0\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u6765\u4e16\u306b\u5099\u3048\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3068\u540c\u3058\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u5584\u306f\u4eca\u3001\u884c\u3048\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4eca\u3053\u306e\u77ac\u9593"},{id:"q061",text:"Kul hatas\u0131n\u0131 bilirse, Hak affeder.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"tevbe",rarity:"common",textEn:"If the servant knows their fault, the Truth forgives.",categoryEn:"repentance",textDe:"Wenn der Diener seinen Fehler erkennt, vergibt die Wahrheit.",categoryDe:"Reue",textEs:"Si el siervo conoce su falta, la Verdad perdona.",categoryEs:"arrepentimiento",textPt:"Se o servo conhece a sua falta, a Verdade perdoa.",categoryPt:"arrependimento",textFr:"Si le serviteur conna\xeet sa faute, la V\xe9rit\xe9 pardonne.",categoryFr:"repentir",textJa:"\u50d5\u304c\u305d\u306e\u904e\u3061\u3092\u77e5\u308c\u3070\u3001\u771f\u5b9f\u306f\u8d66\u3057\u305f\u307e\u3046\u3002",categoryJa:"\u6094\u609f"},{id:"q062",text:"\u015eu d\xfcnya fanidir. Temelden in\u015fa etti\u011fin g\xf6nl\xfc yap.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"kalp",rarity:"common",textEn:"This world is fleeting. Build the heart you raise from its foundation.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Diese Welt ist verg\xe4nglich. Baue das Herz, das du errichtest, von Grund auf.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"Este mundo es fugaz. Construye desde sus cimientos el coraz\xf3n que levantas.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"Este mundo \xe9 passageiro. Constr\xf3i desde os alicerces o cora\xe7\xe3o que ergues.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Ce monde est \xe9ph\xe9m\xe8re. B\xe2tis d\xe8s ses fondations le c\u0153ur que tu \xe9l\xe8ves.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u3053\u306e\u4e16\u306f\u79fb\u308d\u3046\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u304c\u7bc9\u304d\u4e0a\u3052\u308b\u5fc3\u3092\u3001\u305d\u306e\u571f\u53f0\u304b\u3089\u5efa\u3066\u3088\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q063",text:"K\u0131rklar meclisinde i\xe7ilen \u015farap sevgi \u015farab\u0131d\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"ask",rarity:"rare",textEn:"The wine drunk in the gathering of the Forty is the wine of love.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Der Wein, der in der Versammlung der Vierzig getrunken wird, ist der Wein der Liebe.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"El vino que se bebe en la reuni\xf3n de los Cuarenta es el vino del amor.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O vinho que se bebe na reuni\xe3o dos Quarenta \xe9 o vinho do amor.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Le vin bu dans l'assembl\xe9e des Quarante est le vin de l'amour.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u56db\u5341\u4eba\u306e\u96c6\u3044\u3067\u98f2\u307e\u308c\u308b\u9152\u306f\u3001\u611b\u306e\u9152\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q064",text:"Alim olmak kolayd\u0131r, insan olmak zordur.",original:"",source:"Hac\u0131 Bekta\u015f Veli",category:"nefis",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"It is easy to be a scholar; it is hard to be a human being.",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Es ist leicht, ein Gelehrter zu sein; es ist schwer, ein Mensch zu sein.",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"Es f\xe1cil ser un erudito; es dif\xedcil ser un ser humano.",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"\xc9 f\xe1cil ser um erudito; \xe9 dif\xedcil ser um ser humano.",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"Il est facile d'\xeatre un savant ; il est difficile d'\xeatre un \xeatre humain.",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u5b66\u8005\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u305f\u3084\u3059\u3044\u3002\u4eba\u9593\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u96e3\u3057\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q065",text:"Pir Sultan'\u0131m Sivas'ta, ad\u0131n\u0131 bilmez bizi. \u015eah bizi and\u0131 m\u0131? And\u0131ysa, ne iyi.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"hasret",rarity:"rare",textEn:"I am Pir Sultan in Sivas; he knows not even our name. Has the Shah remembered us? If he has, how good.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Ich bin Pir Sultan in Sivas; er kennt nicht einmal unseren Namen. Hat der Schah unser gedacht? Wenn ja, wie sch\xf6n.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"Soy Pir Sultan en Sivas; ni siquiera conoce nuestro nombre. \xbfSe ha acordado el Sah de nosotros? Si lo ha hecho, qu\xe9 bien.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"Sou Pir Sultan em Sivas; ele nem sequer conhece o nosso nome. Ter\xe1 o X\xe1 se lembrado de n\xf3s? Se sim, que bom.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Je suis Pir Sultan \xe0 Sivas ; il ne conna\xeet m\xeame pas notre nom. Le Chah s'est-il souvenu de nous ? S'il l'a fait, comme c'est bon.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u30b9\u30a3\u30f4\u30a1\u30b9\u306e\u30d4\u30eb\u30fb\u30b9\u30eb\u30bf\u30f3\u3002\u5f7c\u306f\u6211\u3089\u306e\u540d\u3059\u3089\u77e5\u3089\u306c\u3002\u30b7\u30e3\u30fc\u306f\u6211\u3089\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u305f\u304b\u3002\u3082\u3057\u305d\u3046\u306a\u3089\u3001\u4f55\u3068\u5b09\u3057\u3044\u3053\u3068\u304b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q066",text:"Bize de sormazlar halden, ne \xe7ekeriz bilmezler.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"hasret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"No one asks us of our state; they do not know what we bear.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Niemand fragt nach unserem Zustand; sie wissen nicht, was wir tragen.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"Nadie nos pregunta por nuestro estado; no saben lo que cargamos.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"Ningu\xe9m nos pergunta pelo nosso estado; n\xe3o sabem o que carregamos.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Personne ne nous demande notre \xe9tat ; ils ne savent pas ce que nous portons.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u8ab0\u3082\u6211\u3089\u306e\u5883\u9047\u3092\u554f\u308f\u306c\u3002\u6211\u3089\u304c\u4f55\u3092\u80cc\u8ca0\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u304b\u3092\u3001\u5f7c\u3089\u306f\u77e5\u3089\u306c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q067",text:"Kul olay\u0131m kalem tutan eline. Yaz\u0131lan\u0131 silemezsek de yazar\u0131z.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"irade",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"May I be servant to the hand that holds the pen. Even if we cannot erase what is written, still we write.",categoryEn:"will",textDe:"Diener sei ich der Hand, die die Feder h\xe4lt. Auch wenn wir das Geschriebene nicht tilgen k\xf6nnen, schreiben wir dennoch.",categoryDe:"Wille",textEs:"Que sea siervo de la mano que sostiene la pluma. Aunque no podamos borrar lo escrito, aun as\xed escribimos.",categoryEs:"voluntad",textPt:"Que eu seja servo da m\xe3o que segura a pena. Ainda que n\xe3o possamos apagar o que est\xe1 escrito, mesmo assim escrevemos.",categoryPt:"vontade",textFr:"Que je sois serviteur de la main qui tient la plume. M\xeame si nous ne pouvons effacer ce qui est \xe9crit, nous \xe9crivons quand m\xeame.",categoryFr:"volont\xe9",textJa:"\u30da\u30f3\u3092\u63e1\u308b\u624b\u306e\u50d5\u3067\u3042\u308a\u305f\u3044\u3002\u66f8\u304b\u308c\u305f\u3082\u306e\u3092\u6d88\u305b\u305a\u3068\u3082\u3001\u305d\u308c\u3067\u3082\u306a\u304a\u6211\u3089\u306f\u66f8\u304f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u610f\u5fd7"},{id:"q068",text:"Hak yoluna gidenlerin, geri d\xf6nmek ay\u0131pt\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"yol",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"For those who walk the path of Truth, to turn back is shameful.",categoryEn:"path",textDe:"F\xfcr die, die den Weg der Wahrheit gehen, ist Umkehren eine Schande.",categoryDe:"Weg",textEs:"Para quienes recorren el camino de la Verdad, volver atr\xe1s es vergonzoso.",categoryEs:"sendero",textPt:"Para os que percorrem o caminho da Verdade, voltar atr\xe1s \xe9 vergonhoso.",categoryPt:"caminho",textFr:"Pour ceux qui marchent sur la voie de la V\xe9rit\xe9, faire demi-tour est une honte.",categoryFr:"voie",textJa:"\u771f\u5b9f\u306e\u9053\u3092\u6b69\u3080\u8005\u306b\u3068\u3063\u3066\u3001\u5f15\u304d\u8fd4\u3059\u3053\u3068\u306f\u6065\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u9053"},{id:"q069",text:"E\u011fer bir g\xfcn \xf6l\xfcm hakk\u0131nda d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcrsen, sevgi \xfczerine d\xfc\u015f\xfcn daha \xe7ok.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"If one day you think upon death, think more upon love.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Wenn du eines Tages an den Tod denkst, denke mehr an die Liebe.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Si un d\xeda piensas en la muerte, piensa m\xe1s en el amor.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Se um dia pensares na morte, pensa mais no amor.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Si un jour tu penses \xe0 la mort, pense davantage \xe0 l'amour.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u3044\u3064\u304b\u6b7b\u3092\u601d\u3046\u306a\u3089\u3001\u305d\u308c\u4ee5\u4e0a\u306b\u611b\u3092\u601d\u3048\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q070",text:"Da\u011flar ile ta\u015flar ile \xe7a\u011f\u0131ray\u0131m Mevlam seni.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"teslimiyet",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"With mountains and with stones, I will call upon You, my Lord.",categoryEn:"surrender",textDe:"Mit den Bergen und den Steinen werde ich Dich anrufen, mein Herr.",categoryDe:"Hingabe",textEs:"Con las monta\xf1as y con las piedras Te invocar\xe9, mi Se\xf1or.",categoryEs:"entrega",textPt:"Com as montanhas e com as pedras Te invocarei, meu Senhor.",categoryPt:"entrega",textFr:"Avec les montagnes et avec les pierres, je T'invoquerai, mon Seigneur.",categoryFr:"abandon",textJa:"\u5c71\u3005\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3001\u77f3\u3005\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u547c\u3073\u307e\u3059\u3001\u308f\u304c\u4e3b\u3088\u3002",categoryJa:"\u660e\u3051\u6e21\u3057"},{id:"q071",text:"Zul\xfcm ile baki kalmaz, er ge\xe7 hak yerini bulur.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"adalet",rarity:"common",textEn:"Tyranny does not endure; sooner or later truth finds its place.",categoryEn:"justice",textDe:"Tyrannei dauert nicht; fr\xfcher oder sp\xe4ter findet die Wahrheit ihren Platz.",categoryDe:"Gerechtigkeit",textEs:"La tiran\xeda no perdura; tarde o temprano la verdad halla su lugar.",categoryEs:"justicia",textPt:"A tirania n\xe3o perdura; mais cedo ou mais tarde a verdade encontra o seu lugar.",categoryPt:"justi\xe7a",textFr:"La tyrannie ne dure pas ; t\xf4t ou tard la v\xe9rit\xe9 trouve sa place.",categoryFr:"justice",textJa:"\u66b4\u653f\u306f\u7d9a\u304b\u306c\u3002\u9045\u304b\u308c\u65e9\u304b\u308c\u3001\u771f\u5b9f\u306f\u305d\u306e\u5834\u6240\u3092\u898b\u3044\u3060\u3059\u3002",categoryJa:"\u6b63\u7fa9"},{id:"q072",text:"G\xf6nl\xfcm d\xfc\u015ft\xfc bir derde, derman yok mu bilmezem.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"hasret",rarity:"common",textEn:"My heart has fallen into sorrow; I know not whether a cure exists.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Mein Herz ist in Kummer gefallen; ich wei\xdf nicht, ob es eine Heilung gibt.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"Mi coraz\xf3n ha ca\xeddo en la pena; no s\xe9 si existe cura.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"O meu cora\xe7\xe3o caiu na tristeza; n\xe3o sei se h\xe1 cura.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Mon c\u0153ur est tomb\xe9 dans le chagrin ; je ne sais s'il existe un rem\xe8de.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u306b\u6c88\u3093\u3060\u3002\u7652\u3057\u304c\u3042\u308b\u306e\u304b\u3069\u3046\u304b\u3001\u79c1\u306b\u306f\u5206\u304b\u3089\u306c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q073",text:"Allah bir, Muhammed hak, Ali arslan-\u0131 Huda.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"inanc",rarity:"common",textEn:"Allah is one, Muhammad is truth, Ali is the lion of God.",categoryEn:"faith",textDe:"Allah ist einer, Mohammed ist Wahrheit, Ali ist der L\xf6we Gottes.",categoryDe:"Glaube",textEs:"Al\xe1 es uno, Mahoma es verdad, Al\xed es el le\xf3n de Dios.",categoryEs:"fe",textPt:"Al\xe1 \xe9 um, Maom\xe9 \xe9 verdade, Ali \xe9 o le\xe3o de Deus.",categoryPt:"f\xe9",textFr:"Allah est un, Mahomet est v\xe9rit\xe9, Ali est le lion de Dieu.",categoryFr:"foi",textJa:"\u30a2\u30c3\u30e9\u30fc\u306f\u552f\u4e00\u3001\u30e0\u30cf\u30f3\u30de\u30c9\u306f\u771f\u5b9f\u3001\u30a2\u30ea\u30fc\u306f\u795e\u306e\u7345\u5b50\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4fe1\u4ef0"},{id:"q074",text:"M\xfcmin olan ikrar verir, s\xf6z\xfcnde durmak gerek.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfck",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The believer gives their word; one must stand by what one says.",categoryEn:"honesty",textDe:"Der Gl\xe4ubige gibt sein Wort; man muss zu dem stehen, was man sagt.",categoryDe:"Ehrlichkeit",textEs:"El creyente da su palabra; hay que cumplir lo que se dice.",categoryEs:"honestidad",textPt:"O crente d\xe1 a sua palavra; \xe9 preciso cumprir o que se diz.",categoryPt:"honestidade",textFr:"Le croyant donne sa parole ; il faut tenir ce qu'on dit.",categoryFr:"honn\xeatet\xe9",textJa:"\u4fe1\u305a\u308b\u8005\u306f\u8a00\u8449\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u308b\u3002\u8a00\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306b\u306f\u7acb\u305f\u306d\u3070\u306a\u3089\u306c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u8aa0\u5b9f\u3055"},{id:"q075",text:"Bah\xe7ende g\xfcl a\xe7ar m\u0131? A\xe7arsa getir bana.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"Does a rose bloom in your garden? If it does, bring it to me.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Bl\xfcht eine Rose in deinem Garten? Wenn ja, bring sie mir.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"\xbfFlorece una rosa en tu jard\xedn? Si florece, tr\xe1emela.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Floresce uma rosa no teu jardim? Se floresce, traz-ma.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Une rose fleurit-elle dans ton jardin ? Si oui, apporte-la-moi.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u5ead\u306b\u30d0\u30e9\u306f\u54b2\u304f\u304b\u3002\u54b2\u304f\u306a\u3089\u3001\u79c1\u306b\u6301\u3063\u3066\u304d\u3066\u304f\u308c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q076",text:"Hakk'a y\xfcr\xfcyen er olmak; g\xf6nl\xfcn\xfc temiz tutmak gerek.",original:"",source:"Pir Sultan Abdal",category:"kalp",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"To be one who walks unto the Truth, you must keep your heart clean.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Um einer zu sein, der zur Wahrheit schreitet, musst du dein Herz rein halten.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"Para ser de quienes caminan hacia la Verdad, debes mantener limpio tu coraz\xf3n.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"Para seres dos que caminham para a Verdade, deves manter o teu cora\xe7\xe3o limpo.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Pour \xeatre de ceux qui marchent vers la V\xe9rit\xe9, tu dois garder ton c\u0153ur pur.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u771f\u5b9f\u3078\u6b69\u3080\u8005\u306e\u4e00\u4eba\u3067\u3042\u308b\u306b\u306f\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u6e05\u304f\u4fdd\u305f\u306d\u3070\u306a\u3089\u306c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q077",text:"\u0130lk mektep anad\u0131r. \u0130yi ana, iyi \xfcmmet.",original:"",source:"Ahmed Yesevi",category:"bilgi",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The first school is the mother. A good mother makes a good people.",categoryEn:"knowledge",textDe:"Die erste Schule ist die Mutter. Eine gute Mutter macht ein gutes Volk.",categoryDe:"Wissen",textEs:"La primera escuela es la madre. Una buena madre hace un buen pueblo.",categoryEs:"conocimiento",textPt:"A primeira escola \xe9 a m\xe3e. Uma boa m\xe3e faz um bom povo.",categoryPt:"conhecimento",textFr:"La premi\xe8re \xe9cole est la m\xe8re. Une bonne m\xe8re fait un bon peuple.",categoryFr:"savoir",textJa:"\u6700\u521d\u306e\u5b66\u6821\u306f\u6bcd\u3060\u3002\u826f\u304d\u6bcd\u304c\u826f\u304d\u6c11\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u8b58"},{id:"q078",text:"Her kim Allah'\u0131 severse, halk\u0131 da sever.",original:"",source:"Ahmed Yesevi",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"Whoever loves God also loves the people.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Wer Gott liebt, liebt auch die Menschen.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Quien ama a Dios ama tambi\xe9n a las personas.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Quem ama a Deus ama tamb\xe9m as pessoas.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Qui aime Dieu aime aussi les hommes.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u795e\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306f\u3001\u4eba\u3005\u3092\u3082\u611b\u3059\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q079",text:"Yetmi\u015f ya\u015f\u0131nda yere girdim hicap ile, Allah yolunda \xf6lmek \u015feref.",original:"",source:"Ahmed Yesevi",category:"teslimiyet",rarity:"rare",textEn:"At seventy I entered the earth in humility; to die in the path of God is an honor.",categoryEn:"surrender",textDe:"Mit siebzig trat ich in Demut in die Erde; im Weg Gottes zu sterben ist eine Ehre.",categoryDe:"Hingabe",textEs:"A los setenta entr\xe9 en la tierra con humildad; morir en el camino de Dios es un honor.",categoryEs:"entrega",textPt:"Aos setenta entrei na terra com humildade; morrer no caminho de Deus \xe9 uma honra.",categoryPt:"entrega",textFr:"\xc0 soixante-dix ans je suis entr\xe9 en terre dans l'humilit\xe9 ; mourir dans la voie de Dieu est un honneur.",categoryFr:"abandon",textJa:"\u4e03\u5341\u306b\u3057\u3066\u8b19\u865a\u306b\u5927\u5730\u3078\u5165\u3063\u305f\u3002\u795e\u306e\u9053\u306b\u6b7b\u306c\u3053\u3068\u306f\u8a89\u308c\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u660e\u3051\u6e21\u3057"},{id:"q080",text:"Nefsi yenmek, da\u011f yenmekten b\xfcy\xfckt\xfcr.",original:"",source:"Ahmed Yesevi",category:"nefis",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"To conquer the self is greater than to conquer a mountain.",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Das Selbst zu erobern ist gr\xf6\xdfer, als einen Berg zu erobern.",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"Conquistar el yo es m\xe1s grande que conquistar una monta\xf1a.",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"Conquistar o eu \xe9 maior do que conquistar uma montanha.",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"Conqu\xe9rir le soi est plus grand que conqu\xe9rir une montagne.",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u5df1\u306b\u514b\u3064\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u5c71\u3092\u5f81\u3059\u308b\u3088\u308a\u5927\u304d\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q081",text:"Hak yoluna koyulanlar yorulmaz.",original:"",source:"Ahmed Yesevi",category:"irade",rarity:"common",textEn:"Those who set out on the path of the Truth do not grow weary.",categoryEn:"will",textDe:"Die sich auf den Weg der Wahrheit machen, werden nicht m\xfcde.",categoryDe:"Wille",textEs:"Quienes parten por el camino de la Verdad no se cansan.",categoryEs:"voluntad",textPt:"Os que partem pelo caminho da Verdade n\xe3o se cansam.",categoryPt:"vontade",textFr:"Ceux qui se mettent en route sur la voie de la V\xe9rit\xe9 ne se lassent pas.",categoryFr:"volont\xe9",textJa:"\u771f\u5b9f\u306e\u9053\u306b\u65c5\u7acb\u3064\u8005\u306f\u75b2\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u610f\u5fd7"},{id:"q082",text:"G\xf6nl\xfc geni\u015f ol. Dar g\xf6n\xfclde ilim durmaz.",original:"",source:"Ahmed Yesevi",category:"kalp",rarity:"common",textEn:"Be wide of heart. Knowledge cannot dwell in a narrow heart.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Sei weit im Herzen. Wissen kann nicht in einem engen Herzen wohnen.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"S\xe9 de coraz\xf3n amplio. El conocimiento no puede morar en un coraz\xf3n estrecho.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"S\xea de cora\xe7\xe3o amplo. O conhecimento n\xe3o pode morar num cora\xe7\xe3o estreito.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Sois large de c\u0153ur. Le savoir ne peut habiter un c\u0153ur \xe9troit.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u5fc3\u3092\u5e83\u304f\u6301\u3066\u3002\u77e5\u306f\u72ed\u3044\u5fc3\u306b\u306f\u5bbf\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q083",text:"Merd ol, yi\u011fit ol; s\xf6z\xfcnde dur.",original:"",source:"Ahmed Yesevi",category:"d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfck",rarity:"common",textEn:"Be upright, be brave; stand by your word.",categoryEn:"honesty",textDe:"Sei aufrecht, sei mutig; stehe zu deinem Wort.",categoryDe:"Ehrlichkeit",textEs:"S\xe9 recto, s\xe9 valiente; cumple tu palabra.",categoryEs:"honestidad",textPt:"S\xea reto, s\xea corajoso; cumpre a tua palavra.",categoryPt:"honestidade",textFr:"Sois droit, sois courageux ; tiens ta parole.",categoryFr:"honn\xeatet\xe9",textJa:"\u307e\u3063\u3059\u3050\u3067\u3042\u308c\u3001\u52c7\u6562\u3067\u3042\u308c\u3002\u5df1\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u306b\u7acb\u3066\u3002",categoryJa:"\u8aa0\u5b9f\u3055"},{id:"q084",text:"D\xfcnyay\u0131 seven Allah'\u0131 unutur; Allah'\u0131 seven d\xfcnyay\u0131.",original:"",source:"Ahmed Yesevi",category:"z\xfchd",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Whoever loves the world forgets God; whoever loves God forgets the world.",categoryEn:"detachment",textDe:"Wer die Welt liebt, vergisst Gott; wer Gott liebt, vergisst die Welt.",categoryDe:"Losl\xf6sung",textEs:"Quien ama el mundo olvida a Dios; quien ama a Dios olvida el mundo.",categoryEs:"desapego",textPt:"Quem ama o mundo esquece Deus; quem ama Deus esquece o mundo.",categoryPt:"desapego",textFr:"Qui aime le monde oublie Dieu ; qui aime Dieu oublie le monde.",categoryFr:"d\xe9tachement",textJa:"\u4e16\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306f\u795e\u3092\u5fd8\u308c\u3001\u795e\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306f\u4e16\u3092\u5fd8\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u96e2\u8131"},{id:"q085",text:"Hakikat \u015farab\u0131n\u0131 i\xe7meden ger\xe7ek \xe2\u015f\u0131k olunamaz.",original:"",source:"Ahmed Yesevi",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Without drinking the wine of truth, one cannot become a true lover.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Ohne den Wein der Wahrheit zu trinken, kann man kein wahrer Liebender werden.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Sin beber el vino de la verdad, no se puede llegar a ser un verdadero amante.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Sem beber o vinho da verdade, n\xe3o se pode tornar um verdadeiro amante.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Sans boire le vin de la v\xe9rit\xe9, on ne peut devenir un vrai amant.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u771f\u5b9f\u306e\u9152\u3092\u98f2\u307e\u305a\u306b\u3001\u771f\u306e\u604b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306b\u306f\u306a\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q086",text:"Ben Nesimiyem, hakikat eriyim. Deriyi y\xfczseler de i\xe7imi alamazlar.",original:"",source:"Nesimi",category:"cesaret",rarity:"rare",textEn:"I am Nesimi, a man of truth. Though they flay my skin, they cannot take what is within.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"Ich bin Nesimi, ein Mann der Wahrheit. Auch wenn sie mir die Haut abziehen, k\xf6nnen sie nicht nehmen, was darin ist.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"Soy Nesimi, hombre de verdad. Aunque me desuellen, no pueden quitarme lo que llevo dentro.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"Sou Nesimi, homem de verdade. Ainda que me esfolem a pele, n\xe3o podem levar o que h\xe1 dentro.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"Je suis Nesimi, homme de v\xe9rit\xe9. M\xeame s'ils m'\xe9corchent la peau, ils ne peuvent prendre ce qui est au-dedans.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u30cd\u30b9\u30a3\u30df\u3001\u771f\u5b9f\u306e\u4eba\u3002\u305f\u3068\u3048\u76ae\u3092\u525d\u304c\u308c\u3066\u3082\u3001\u5185\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306f\u596a\u3048\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q087",text:"\u0130\xe7imde Allah sakl\u0131d\u0131r, bulmak isteyen i\xe7ine baks\u0131n.",original:"",source:"Nesimi",category:"birlik",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Within me, God is hidden; let whoever wishes to find Him look within.",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"In mir ist Gott verborgen; wer Ihn finden will, schaue in sich hinein.",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"Dentro de m\xed est\xe1 oculto Dios; que quien desee hallarlo mire en su interior.",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"Dentro de mim est\xe1 oculto Deus; quem quiser encontr\xe1-Lo, olhe para dentro de si.",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"En moi Dieu est cach\xe9 ; que celui qui veut Le trouver regarde au-dedans.",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u795e\u306f\u96a0\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002\u898b\u3044\u3060\u3057\u305f\u3044\u8005\u306f\u3001\u5df1\u306e\u5185\u3092\u898b\u308b\u304c\u3088\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q088",text:"Ben bu isme lay\u0131k m\u0131y\u0131m? S\xf6yle y\xfcre\u011fim.",original:"",source:"Nesimi",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Am I worthy of this name? Tell me, my heart.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Bin ich dieses Namens w\xfcrdig? Sag es mir, mein Herz.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"\xbfSoy digno de este nombre? D\xedmelo, coraz\xf3n m\xedo.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"Sou digno deste nome? Diz-me, meu cora\xe7\xe3o.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Suis-je digne de ce nom ? Dis-le-moi, mon c\u0153ur.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u3053\u306e\u540d\u306b\u3075\u3055\u308f\u3057\u3044\u304b\u3002\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u3001\u308f\u304c\u5fc3\u3088\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q089",text:"Enel Hak s\u0131rr\u0131n\u0131 gizleme, s\xf6yle cesaretle.",original:"",source:"Nesimi",category:"cesaret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Do not hide the secret of 'I am the Truth'; speak it with courage.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"Verbirg nicht das Geheimnis von \u201aIch bin die Wahrheit\u2018; sprich es mit Mut.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"No ocultes el secreto de 'Yo soy la Verdad'; dilo con valor.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"N\xe3o escondas o segredo de 'Eu sou a Verdade'; di-lo com coragem.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"Ne cache pas le secret de \xab Je suis la V\xe9rit\xe9 \xbb ; dis-le avec courage.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u300c\u6211\u306f\u771f\u5b9f\u306a\u308a\u300d\u3068\u3044\u3046\u79d8\u5bc6\u3092\u96a0\u3059\u306a\u3002\u52c7\u6c17\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u8a9e\u308c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q090",text:"Yere g\xf6\u011fe s\u0131\u011fmam, bir m\xfcminin g\xf6nl\xfcne s\u0131\u011far\u0131m.",original:"",source:"Nesimi",category:"birlik",rarity:"rare",textEn:"I do not fit in earth or sky, but I fit within a believer's heart.",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"Ich passe nicht in Erde oder Himmel, doch ich passe in das Herz eines Gl\xe4ubigen.",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"No quepo en la tierra ni en el cielo, pero quepo en el coraz\xf3n de un creyente.",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"N\xe3o caibo na terra nem no c\xe9u, mas caibo no cora\xe7\xe3o de um crente.",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"Je ne tiens ni dans la terre ni dans le ciel, mais je tiens dans le c\u0153ur d'un croyant.",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5730\u306b\u3082\u5929\u306b\u3082\u53ce\u307e\u3089\u306c\u304c\u3001\u4fe1\u305a\u308b\u8005\u306e\u5fc3\u306b\u306f\u53ce\u307e\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q091",text:"G\xfczellik senin i\xe7inde; ayna \xe7atlasa da bu ger\xe7ek de\u011fi\u015fmez.",original:"",source:"Nesimi",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Beauty is within you; though the mirror crack, this truth does not change.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Die Sch\xf6nheit ist in dir; auch wenn der Spiegel zerspringt, \xe4ndert sich diese Wahrheit nicht.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"La belleza est\xe1 dentro de ti; aunque el espejo se quiebre, esta verdad no cambia.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"A beleza est\xe1 dentro de ti; ainda que o espelho se quebre, esta verdade n\xe3o muda.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"La beaut\xe9 est en toi ; m\xeame si le miroir se brise, cette v\xe9rit\xe9 ne change pas.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u7f8e\u306f\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3002\u93e1\u304c\u5272\u308c\u3066\u3082\u3001\u3053\u306e\u771f\u5b9f\u306f\u5909\u308f\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q092",text:"\xd6l\xfcmden korkan hayat\u0131 ya\u015fayamaz.",original:"",source:"Nesimi",category:"cesaret",rarity:"common",textEn:"Whoever fears death cannot truly live.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"Wer den Tod f\xfcrchtet, kann nicht wahrhaft leben.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"Quien teme a la muerte no puede vivir de verdad.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"Quem teme a morte n\xe3o pode viver de verdade.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"Qui craint la mort ne peut vraiment vivre.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u6b7b\u3092\u6050\u308c\u308b\u8005\u306f\u3001\u771f\u306b\u751f\u304d\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q093",text:"Tanr\u0131'y\u0131 insanda ara, ta\u015fta de\u011fil.",original:"",source:"Nesimi",category:"birlik",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Seek God in the human being, not in stone.",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"Suche Gott im Menschen, nicht im Stein.",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"Busca a Dios en el ser humano, no en la piedra.",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"Procura Deus no ser humano, n\xe3o na pedra.",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"Cherche Dieu dans l'\xeatre humain, non dans la pierre.",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u795e\u3092\u4eba\u9593\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u6c42\u3081\u3088\u3001\u77f3\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q094",text:"Derd-i a\u015fk devas\u0131 olmaz, ama derde de\u011fer.",original:"",source:"Nesimi",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"There is no cure for the sickness of love, yet the sickness is worth it.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Es gibt keine Heilung f\xfcr die Krankheit der Liebe, und doch ist die Krankheit es wert.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"No hay cura para la enfermedad del amor, y sin embargo la enfermedad vale la pena.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"N\xe3o h\xe1 cura para a doen\xe7a do amor, e ainda assim a doen\xe7a vale a pena.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Il n'y a pas de rem\xe8de \xe0 la maladie de l'amour, et pourtant la maladie en vaut la peine.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u3068\u3044\u3046\u75c5\u306b\u7652\u3057\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u305d\u308c\u3067\u3082\u3001\u305d\u306e\u75c5\u306f\u5024\u3059\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q095",text:"Kaygusuz abdal gezer da\u011fda bay\u0131rda. D\xfcnya ona dar, g\xf6n\xfcl ona geni\u015f.",original:"",source:"Kaygusuz Abdal",category:"z\xfchd",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Kaygusuz the dervish wanders over hills and dales. The world is too narrow for him, his heart is wide.",categoryEn:"detachment",textDe:"Kaygusuz der Derwisch wandert \xfcber H\xfcgel und T\xe4ler. Die Welt ist ihm zu eng, sein Herz ist weit.",categoryDe:"Losl\xf6sung",textEs:"Kaygusuz el derviche vaga por cerros y valles. El mundo le es demasiado estrecho, su coraz\xf3n es amplio.",categoryEs:"desapego",textPt:"Kaygusuz, o dervixe, vagueia por colinas e vales. O mundo \xe9 demasiado estreito para ele, o seu cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 amplo.",categoryPt:"desapego",textFr:"Kaygusuz le derviche erre par monts et par vaux. Le monde lui est trop \xe9troit, son c\u0153ur est vaste.",categoryFr:"d\xe9tachement",textJa:"\u6258\u9262\u50e7\u30ab\u30a4\u30b0\u30b9\u30ba\u306f\u4e18\u3084\u8c37\u3092\u3055\u3059\u3089\u3046\u3002\u4e16\u306f\u5f7c\u306b\u306f\u72ed\u3059\u304e\u308b\u3001\u5f7c\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u5e83\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u96e2\u8131"},{id:"q096",text:"Benim Hakk'\u0131m bende sakl\u0131, ne hac ne da\u011f ne deniz.",original:"",source:"Kaygusuz Abdal",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"My Truth is hidden within me; not in pilgrimage, mountain, or sea.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Meine Wahrheit ist in mir verborgen; nicht in Pilgerfahrt, Berg oder Meer.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Mi Verdad est\xe1 oculta dentro de m\xed; no en la peregrinaci\xf3n, la monta\xf1a ni el mar.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"A minha Verdade est\xe1 oculta dentro de mim; n\xe3o na peregrina\xe7\xe3o, na montanha ou no mar.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Ma V\xe9rit\xe9 est cach\xe9e en moi ; ni dans le p\xe8lerinage, ni dans la montagne, ni dans la mer.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u771f\u5b9f\u306f\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002\u5de1\u793c\u306b\u3082\u3001\u5c71\u306b\u3082\u3001\u6d77\u306b\u3082\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q097",text:"D\xfcnya tuza\u011f\u0131na d\xfc\u015fme, keklik gibi u\xe7up git.",original:"",source:"Kaygusuz Abdal",category:"z\xfchd",rarity:"common",textEn:"Do not fall into the world's snare; fly away like the partridge.",categoryEn:"detachment",textDe:"Falle nicht in die Falle der Welt; flieg davon wie das Rebhuhn.",categoryDe:"Losl\xf6sung",textEs:"No caigas en la trampa del mundo; vuela lejos como la perdiz.",categoryEs:"desapego",textPt:"N\xe3o caias na armadilha do mundo; voa para longe como a perdiz.",categoryPt:"desapego",textFr:"Ne tombe pas dans le pi\xe8ge du monde ; envole-toi comme la perdrix.",categoryFr:"d\xe9tachement",textJa:"\u4e16\u306e\u7f60\u306b\u843d\u3061\u308b\u306a\u3002\u30e4\u30de\u30a6\u30ba\u30e9\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u98db\u3073\u53bb\u308c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u96e2\u8131"},{id:"q098",text:"Allah a\u015fk\u0131n\u0131 i\xe7mi\u015fem, ne un ne ekmek isterem.",original:"",source:"Kaygusuz Abdal",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"I have drunk the love of God; I need neither flour nor bread.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Ich habe die Liebe Gottes getrunken; ich brauche weder Mehl noch Brot.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"He bebido el amor de Dios; no necesito harina ni pan.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Bebi o amor de Deus; n\xe3o preciso de farinha nem de p\xe3o.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"J'ai bu l'amour de Dieu ; je n'ai besoin ni de farine ni de pain.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u795e\u306e\u611b\u3092\u98f2\u3093\u3060\u3002\u7c89\u3082\u30d1\u30f3\u3082\u3044\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q099",text:"Ger\xe7ek fakr budur: ne varsa ver, ne yoksa isteme.",original:"",source:"Kaygusuz Abdal",category:"c\xf6mertlik",rarity:"rare",textEn:"True poverty is this: give whatever you have, and ask for nothing you do not.",categoryEn:"generosity",textDe:"Wahre Armut ist dies: gib, was du hast, und bitte um nichts, was du nicht hast.",categoryDe:"Gro\xdfz\xfcgigkeit",textEs:"La verdadera pobreza es esta: da cuanto tienes y no pidas nada de lo que no tienes.",categoryEs:"generosidad",textPt:"A verdadeira pobreza \xe9 esta: d\xe1 o que tiveres e nada pe\xe7as do que n\xe3o tens.",categoryPt:"generosidade",textFr:"La vraie pauvret\xe9 est celle-ci : donne tout ce que tu as, et ne demande rien que tu n'aies pas.",categoryFr:"g\xe9n\xe9rosit\xe9",textJa:"\u771f\u306e\u8ca7\u3057\u3055\u3068\u306f\u3053\u308c\u3060\u2014\u2014\u6301\u3066\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3092\u3059\u3079\u3066\u4e0e\u3048\u3001\u6301\u305f\u306c\u3082\u306e\u3092\u4f55\u3082\u6c42\u3081\u306c\u3053\u3068\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5bdb\u5927\u3055"},{id:"q100",text:"Dost ile dost ol, dosta d\xfc\u015fman olma.",original:"",source:"Kaygusuz Abdal",category:"dostluk",rarity:"common",textEn:"Be a friend to your friend; never be foe to a friend.",categoryEn:"friendship",textDe:"Sei deinem Freund ein Freund; sei niemals einem Freund ein Feind.",categoryDe:"Freundschaft",textEs:"S\xe9 amigo de tu amigo; nunca seas enemigo de un amigo.",categoryEs:"amistad",textPt:"S\xea amigo do teu amigo; nunca sejas inimigo de um amigo.",categoryPt:"amizade",textFr:"Sois un ami pour ton ami ; ne sois jamais l'ennemi d'un ami.",categoryFr:"amiti\xe9",textJa:"\u53cb\u306b\u306f\u53cb\u3067\u3042\u308c\u3002\u6c7a\u3057\u3066\u53cb\u306e\u6575\u3068\u306a\u308b\u306a\u3002",categoryJa:"\u53cb\u60c5"},{id:"q101",text:"G\xf6n\xfcl ev sahibini bilirse, ne gam ne keder.",original:"",source:"Niyazi M\u0131sri",category:"kalp",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"If the heart knows its master, there is neither grief nor sorrow.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Kennt das Herz seinen Herrn, gibt es weder Gram noch Kummer.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"Si el coraz\xf3n conoce a su se\xf1or, no hay ni pena ni dolor.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"Se o cora\xe7\xe3o conhece o seu senhor, n\xe3o h\xe1 nem m\xe1goa nem tristeza.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Si le c\u0153ur conna\xeet son ma\xeetre, il n'y a ni peine ni chagrin.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u5fc3\u304c\u305d\u306e\u4e3b\u3092\u77e5\u308c\u3070\u3001\u5606\u304d\u3082\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u3082\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q102",text:"Mevla'm bana yeter, ba\u015fka neye muhtac\u0131m?",original:"",source:"Niyazi M\u0131sri",category:"teslimiyet",rarity:"common",textEn:"My Lord is enough for me; what else could I need?",categoryEn:"surrender",textDe:"Mein Herr gen\xfcgt mir; was k\xf6nnte ich sonst noch brauchen?",categoryDe:"Hingabe",textEs:"Mi Se\xf1or me basta; \xbfqu\xe9 m\xe1s podr\xeda necesitar?",categoryEs:"entrega",textPt:"O meu Senhor me basta; de que mais eu precisaria?",categoryPt:"entrega",textFr:"Mon Seigneur me suffit ; de quoi d'autre aurais-je besoin ?",categoryFr:"abandon",textJa:"\u308f\u304c\u4e3b\u3067\u5341\u5206\u3060\u3002\u307b\u304b\u306b\u4f55\u304c\u5fc5\u8981\u3060\u308d\u3046\u3002",categoryJa:"\u660e\u3051\u6e21\u3057"},{id:"q103",text:"A\u015fk ate\u015fine yanmayan; sufi, arif, alim de\u011fildir.",original:"",source:"Niyazi M\u0131sri",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"One who has not burned in the fire of love is no Sufi, no sage, no scholar.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Wer nicht im Feuer der Liebe gebrannt hat, ist kein Sufi, kein Weiser, kein Gelehrter.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Quien no ha ardido en el fuego del amor no es suf\xed, ni sabio, ni erudito.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Quem n\xe3o ardeu no fogo do amor n\xe3o \xe9 sufi, nem s\xe1bio, nem erudito.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Celui qui n'a pas br\xfbl\xe9 du feu de l'amour n'est ni soufi, ni sage, ni savant.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u306e\u706b\u306b\u71c3\u3048\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306e\u306a\u3044\u8005\u306f\u3001\u30b9\u30fc\u30d5\u30a3\u30fc\u3067\u3082\u3001\u8ce2\u8005\u3067\u3082\u3001\u5b66\u8005\u3067\u3082\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q104",text:"Marifet bu de\u011fil mi: herkeste Hak'k\u0131 g\xf6rmek.",original:"",source:"Niyazi M\u0131sri",category:"birlik",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Is this not gnosis: to see the Truth in everyone?",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"Ist dies nicht Gnosis: die Wahrheit in jedem zu sehen?",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"\xbfNo es esto gnosis: ver la Verdad en todos?",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"N\xe3o \xe9 isto gnose: ver a Verdade em todos?",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"N'est-ce pas l\xe0 la gnose : voir la V\xe9rit\xe9 en chacun ?",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u3053\u308c\u3053\u305d\u53e1\u667a\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u304b\u2014\u2014\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u4eba\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u771f\u5b9f\u3092\u898b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q105",text:"G\xf6nl\xfcnde \u015f\xfcphe varsa, \xf6nce onu temizle.",original:"",source:"Niyazi M\u0131sri",category:"kalp",rarity:"common",textEn:"If there is doubt in your heart, cleanse that first.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Ist Zweifel in deinem Herzen, reinige zuerst diesen.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"Si hay duda en tu coraz\xf3n, limpia primero eso.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"Se h\xe1 d\xfavida no teu cora\xe7\xe3o, limpa primeiro isso.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"S'il y a du doute dans ton c\u0153ur, purifie d'abord cela.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u5fc3\u306b\u7591\u3044\u304c\u3042\u308b\u306a\u3089\u3001\u307e\u305a\u305d\u308c\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u3088\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q106",text:"Ney gibi inliyorum ayr\u0131l\u0131ktan. Ama bu ini\u015f beni Hakk'a g\xf6t\xfcr\xfcyor.",original:"",source:"Niyazi M\u0131sri",category:"hasret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Like the reed flute, I wail with separation. But this lament carries me toward the Truth.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Wie die Rohrfl\xf6te klage ich vor Trennung. Doch dieses Klagen tr\xe4gt mich zur Wahrheit.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"Como la flauta de ca\xf1a, gimo por la separaci\xf3n. Pero este lamento me lleva hacia la Verdad.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"Como a flauta de cana, gemo de separa\xe7\xe3o. Mas este lamento leva-me \xe0 Verdade.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Comme la fl\xfbte de roseau, je g\xe9mis de la s\xe9paration. Mais ce lament me porte vers la V\xe9rit\xe9.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u8466\u7b1b\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u5225\u96e2\u3092\u5606\u304f\u3002\u3060\u304c\u3053\u306e\u5606\u304d\u306f\u79c1\u3092\u771f\u5b9f\u3078\u3068\u904b\u3076\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q107",text:"Senden sana \xe7ok yak\u0131n bir yol var; git.",original:"",source:"Niyazi M\u0131sri",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"rare",textEn:"There is a path from you to you, very near; walk it.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Es gibt einen Weg von dir zu dir, ganz nah; geh ihn.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Hay un camino de ti hacia ti, muy cercano; rec\xf3rrelo.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"H\xe1 um caminho de ti para ti, muito perto; percorre-o.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Il existe un chemin de toi \xe0 toi, tout proche ; parcours-le.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u3042\u306a\u305f\u304b\u3089\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3078\u306e\u9053\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3001\u3054\u304f\u8fd1\u304f\u306b\u3002\u305d\u308c\u3092\u6b69\u3081\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q108",text:"Varl\u0131\u011f\u0131m yoklu\u011fumdan gelir. Yok olursam var olurum.",original:"",source:"Niyazi M\u0131sri",category:"birlik",rarity:"rare",textEn:"My being comes from my nothingness. If I become nothing, I truly am.",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"Mein Sein kommt aus meinem Nichts. Werde ich zu nichts, dann bin ich wahrhaft.",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"Mi ser viene de mi nada. Si me vuelvo nada, verdaderamente soy.",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"O meu ser vem do meu nada. Se me torno nada, verdadeiramente sou.",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"Mon \xeatre vient de mon n\xe9ant. Si je deviens rien, alors je suis vraiment.",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u5b58\u5728\u306f\u79c1\u306e\u7121\u304b\u3089\u6765\u308b\u3002\u7121\u3068\u306a\u308c\u3070\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u771f\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q109",text:"A\u015f\u0131k Veysel'im, ba\u011flar beni bu topra\u011fa. Bu toprak benim, ben bu topra\u011f\u0131m.",original:"",source:"A\u015f\u0131k Veysel",category:"toprak",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"I am A\u015f\u0131k Veysel, bound to this earth. This earth is mine, and I am this earth.",categoryEn:"earth",textDe:"Ich bin A\u015f\u0131k Veysel, an diese Erde gebunden. Diese Erde ist mein, und ich bin diese Erde.",categoryDe:"Erde",textEs:"Soy A\u015f\u0131k Veysel, ligado a esta tierra. Esta tierra es m\xeda, y yo soy esta tierra.",categoryEs:"tierra",textPt:"Sou A\u015f\u0131k Veysel, ligado a esta terra. Esta terra \xe9 minha, e eu sou esta terra.",categoryPt:"terra",textFr:"Je suis A\u015f\u0131k Veysel, li\xe9 \xe0 cette terre. Cette terre est mienne, et je suis cette terre.",categoryFr:"terre",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u30a2\u30fc\u30b7\u30e5\u30af\u30fb\u30f4\u30a7\u30a4\u30bb\u30eb\u3001\u3053\u306e\u5927\u5730\u306b\u7d50\u3070\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002\u3053\u306e\u5927\u5730\u306f\u79c1\u306e\u3082\u306e\u3001\u305d\u3057\u3066\u79c1\u306f\u3053\u306e\u5927\u5730\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5927\u5730"},{id:"q110",text:"G\xf6zlerim g\xf6rmese de g\xf6nl\xfcm g\xf6r\xfcr. Ger\xe7ek \u0131\u015f\u0131k i\xe7ten gelir.",original:"",source:"A\u015f\u0131k Veysel",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Though my eyes do not see, my heart sees. True light comes from within.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Auch wenn meine Augen nicht sehen, sieht mein Herz. Wahres Licht kommt von innen.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Aunque mis ojos no vean, mi coraz\xf3n ve. La verdadera luz viene de dentro.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"Ainda que os meus olhos n\xe3o vejam, o meu cora\xe7\xe3o v\xea. A verdadeira luz vem de dentro.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"M\xeame si mes yeux ne voient pas, mon c\u0153ur voit. La vraie lumi\xe8re vient de l'int\xe9rieur.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u76ee\u306f\u898b\u3048\u305a\u3068\u3082\u3001\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u898b\u308b\u3002\u771f\u306e\u5149\u306f\u5185\u304b\u3089\u6765\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q111",text:"Uzun ince bir yolday\u0131m, gidiyorum g\xfcnd\xfcz gece.",original:"",source:"A\u015f\u0131k Veysel",category:"yol",rarity:"common",textEn:"I walk a long and narrow road, going on by day and by night.",categoryEn:"path",textDe:"Ich gehe einen langen und schmalen Weg, bei Tag und bei Nacht.",categoryDe:"Weg",textEs:"Recorro un camino largo y estrecho, andando de d\xeda y de noche.",categoryEs:"sendero",textPt:"Percorro um caminho longo e estreito, seguindo de dia e de noite.",categoryPt:"caminho",textFr:"Je parcours un chemin long et \xe9troit, avan\xe7ant de jour et de nuit.",categoryFr:"voie",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u9577\u304f\u7d30\u3044\u9053\u3092\u6b69\u3080\u3001\u663c\u3082\u591c\u3082\u9032\u307f\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3002",categoryJa:"\u9053"},{id:"q112",text:"Bah\xe7emizde g\xfcl biter, b\xfclb\xfcller \xf6ter. G\xfczellik bitimsizdir.",original:"",source:"A\u015f\u0131k Veysel",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"Roses bloom in our garden, nightingales sing. Beauty has no end.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"In unserem Garten bl\xfchen Rosen, Nachtigallen singen. Die Sch\xf6nheit hat kein Ende.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"En nuestro jard\xedn florecen rosas, cantan los ruise\xf1ores. La belleza no tiene fin.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"No nosso jardim florescem rosas, cantam rouxin\xf3is. A beleza n\xe3o tem fim.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Dans notre jardin fleurissent les roses, chantent les rossignols. La beaut\xe9 n'a pas de fin.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306e\u5ead\u306b\u306f\u30d0\u30e9\u304c\u54b2\u304d\u3001\u30ca\u30a4\u30c1\u30f3\u30b2\u30fc\u30eb\u304c\u3055\u3048\u305a\u308b\u3002\u7f8e\u306b\u7d42\u308f\u308a\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q113",text:"En g\xfczel k\xf6y senin b\xfcy\xfcd\xfc\u011f\xfcn, en g\xfczel ana senin anan.",original:"",source:"A\u015f\u0131k Veysel",category:"toprak",rarity:"common",textEn:"The most beautiful village is the one where you grew up; the most beautiful mother is your own.",categoryEn:"earth",textDe:"Das sch\xf6nste Dorf ist das, in dem du aufgewachsen bist; die sch\xf6nste Mutter ist deine eigene.",categoryDe:"Erde",textEs:"El pueblo m\xe1s hermoso es aquel donde creciste; la madre m\xe1s hermosa es la tuya.",categoryEs:"tierra",textPt:"A aldeia mais bela \xe9 aquela onde cresceste; a m\xe3e mais bela \xe9 a tua pr\xf3pria.",categoryPt:"terra",textFr:"Le plus beau village est celui o\xf9 tu as grandi ; la plus belle m\xe8re est la tienne.",categoryFr:"terre",textJa:"\u6700\u3082\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u6751\u306f\u3042\u306a\u305f\u304c\u80b2\u3063\u305f\u6751\u3001\u6700\u3082\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u6bcd\u306f\u3042\u306a\u305f\u81ea\u8eab\u306e\u6bcd\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5927\u5730"},{id:"q114",text:"D\xfcnya bir misafirhanedir, misafir k\u0131namaz evi.",original:"",source:"A\u015f\u0131k Veysel",category:"hikmet",rarity:"common",textEn:"The world is a guesthouse; a guest does not find fault with the house.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Die Welt ist ein Gasthaus; ein Gast tadelt das Haus nicht.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"El mundo es una casa de hu\xe9spedes; un hu\xe9sped no le pone reparos a la casa.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"O mundo \xe9 uma hospedaria; um h\xf3spede n\xe3o acha defeitos na casa.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Le monde est une maison d'h\xf4tes ; un h\xf4te ne trouve pas \xe0 redire \xe0 la maison.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u4e16\u306f\u5bbf\u5c4b\u3060\u3002\u5ba2\u306f\u5bbf\u306b\u96e3\u7656\u3092\u3064\u3051\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q115",text:"Sevda da\u011flar\u0131 a\u015far, nehirleri ge\xe7er. Ama ilk ad\u0131m ayaktan de\u011fil, g\xf6n\xfclden at\u0131l\u0131r.",original:"",source:"A\u015f\u0131k Veysel",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Love crosses mountains and rivers. But the first step is taken not by the foot, but by the heart.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Die Liebe \xfcberquert Berge und Fl\xfcsse. Doch den ersten Schritt tut nicht der Fu\xdf, sondern das Herz.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"El amor cruza monta\xf1as y r\xedos. Pero el primer paso no lo da el pie, sino el coraz\xf3n.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O amor atravessa montanhas e rios. Mas o primeiro passo n\xe3o \xe9 dado pelo p\xe9, e sim pelo cora\xe7\xe3o.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"L'amour franchit montagnes et rivi\xe8res. Mais le premier pas n'est pas fait par le pied, mais par le c\u0153ur.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u306f\u5c71\u3084\u5ddd\u3092\u8d8a\u3048\u308b\u3002\u3060\u304c\u6700\u521d\u306e\u4e00\u6b69\u306f\u8db3\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u5fc3\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u8e0f\u307f\u51fa\u3055\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q116",text:"Dadalo\u011flu der ki: Er odur ki, s\xf6z\xfcnde durur.",original:"",source:"Dadalo\u011flu",category:"d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfck",rarity:"common",textEn:"Dadalo\u011flu says: A true man is one who stands by his word.",categoryEn:"honesty",textDe:"Dadalo\u011flu sagt: Ein wahrer Mann ist der, der zu seinem Wort steht.",categoryDe:"Ehrlichkeit",textEs:"Dadalo\u011flu dice: un hombre de verdad es aquel que cumple su palabra.",categoryEs:"honestidad",textPt:"Dadalo\u011flu diz: um homem de verdade \xe9 aquele que cumpre a sua palavra.",categoryPt:"honestidade",textFr:"Dadalo\u011flu dit : un vrai homme est celui qui tient sa parole.",categoryFr:"honn\xeatet\xe9",textJa:"\u30c0\u30c0\u30eb\u30aa\u30fc\u30eb\u306f\u8a00\u3046\u2014\u2014\u771f\u306e\u7537\u3068\u306f\u3001\u5df1\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u306b\u7acb\u3064\u8005\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u8aa0\u5b9f\u3055"},{id:"q117",text:"Ferman padi\u015fah\u0131n, da\u011flar bizimdir. Hi\xe7bir g\xfc\xe7 k\xf6kten s\xf6kelemez bizi.",original:"",source:"Dadalo\u011flu",category:"cesaret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The decree is the sultan's, but the mountains are ours. No force can uproot us.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"Der Erlass geh\xf6rt dem Sultan, doch die Berge sind unser. Keine Macht kann uns entwurzeln.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"El decreto es del sult\xe1n, pero las monta\xf1as son nuestras. Ninguna fuerza puede arrancarnos.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"O decreto \xe9 do sult\xe3o, mas as montanhas s\xe3o nossas. Nenhuma for\xe7a pode arrancar-nos.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"Le d\xe9cret est au sultan, mais les montagnes sont \xe0 nous. Aucune force ne peut nous d\xe9raciner.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u52c5\u4ee4\u306f\u30b9\u30eb\u30bf\u30f3\u306e\u3082\u306e\u3001\u3060\u304c\u5c71\u3005\u306f\u6211\u3089\u306e\u3082\u306e\u3002\u3044\u304b\u306a\u308b\u529b\u3082\u6211\u3089\u3092\u6839\u3053\u305d\u304e\u306b\u306f\u3067\u304d\u306c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q118",text:"Ele g\xfcne kar\u015f\u0131 \u015feref, ev i\xe7inde insanl\u0131k.",original:"",source:"Dadalo\u011flu",category:"nefis",rarity:"common",textEn:"Honor before the world, humanity within the home.",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Ehre vor der Welt, Menschlichkeit im Haus.",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"Honor ante el mundo, humanidad dentro del hogar.",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"Honra perante o mundo, humanidade dentro do lar.",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"Honneur devant le monde, humanit\xe9 au sein du foyer.",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u4e16\u306e\u524d\u3067\u306f\u8a89\u308c\u3092\u3001\u5bb6\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u306f\u4eba\u3068\u3057\u3066\u306e\u6e29\u304b\u3055\u3092\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q119",text:"Aslana yi\u011fitlik gerekmez, kuzuya gerekir.",original:"",source:"Dadalo\u011flu",category:"cesaret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The lion need not prove its courage; the lamb must.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"Der L\xf6we braucht seinen Mut nicht zu beweisen; das Lamm muss es.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"El le\xf3n no necesita probar su valor; el cordero s\xed.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"O le\xe3o n\xe3o precisa provar a sua coragem; o cordeiro precisa.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"Le lion n'a pas besoin de prouver son courage ; l'agneau le doit.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u7345\u5b50\u306f\u305d\u306e\u52c7\u6c17\u3092\u8a3c\u3059\u5fc5\u8981\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u8a3c\u3059\u3079\u304d\u306f\u5b50\u7f8a\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q120",text:"K\xf6ro\u011flu der ki: Meydan okumak yi\u011fitli\u011fin ba\u015f\u0131d\u0131r.",original:"",source:"K\xf6ro\u011flu",category:"cesaret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"K\xf6ro\u011flu says: To dare is the beginning of bravery.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"K\xf6ro\u011flu sagt: Zu wagen ist der Anfang der Tapferkeit.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"K\xf6ro\u011flu dice: atreverse es el principio de la valent\xeda.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"K\xf6ro\u011flu diz: ousar \xe9 o come\xe7o da bravura.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"K\xf6ro\u011flu dit : oser est le commencement de la bravoure.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u30ad\u30e7\u30eb\u30aa\u30fc\u30eb\u306f\u8a00\u3046\u2014\u2014\u6562\u3048\u3066\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3001\u52c7\u6562\u3055\u306e\u59cb\u307e\u308a\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q121",text:"At cinsinden belli olur, er yi\u011fitten.",original:"",source:"K\xf6ro\u011flu",category:"irade",rarity:"common",textEn:"A horse is known by its breed, a man by his valor.",categoryEn:"will",textDe:"Ein Pferd erkennt man an seiner Rasse, einen Mann an seiner Tapferkeit.",categoryDe:"Wille",textEs:"Al caballo se le conoce por su raza, al hombre por su valor.",categoryEs:"voluntad",textPt:"O cavalo conhece-se pela ra\xe7a, o homem pelo valor.",categoryPt:"vontade",textFr:"On conna\xeet le cheval \xe0 sa race, l'homme \xe0 sa vaillance.",categoryFr:"volont\xe9",textJa:"\u99ac\u306f\u305d\u306e\u8840\u7d71\u3067\u3001\u4eba\u306f\u305d\u306e\u6b66\u52c7\u3067\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u610f\u5fd7"},{id:"q122",text:"Da\u011f ba\u015f\u0131n\u0131 duman alm\u0131\u015f, ge\xe7ilmez diye \xe7ekilme. Duman da da\u011fd\u0131r, yol da.",original:"",source:"K\xf6ro\u011flu",category:"cesaret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Mist has covered the mountain's peak; do not turn back saying it cannot be crossed. The mist is part of the mountain, and so is the road.",categoryEn:"courage",textDe:"Nebel hat den Gipfel des Berges bedeckt; kehre nicht um mit den Worten, er sei nicht zu \xfcberqueren. Der Nebel geh\xf6rt zum Berg, und so auch der Weg.",categoryDe:"Mut",textEs:"La niebla ha cubierto la cima del monte; no te vuelvas diciendo que no se puede cruzar. La niebla es parte del monte, y tambi\xe9n lo es el camino.",categoryEs:"valent\xeda",textPt:"A n\xe9voa cobriu o cume da montanha; n\xe3o voltes atr\xe1s dizendo que n\xe3o d\xe1 para atravessar. A n\xe9voa \xe9 parte da montanha, e o caminho tamb\xe9m.",categoryPt:"coragem",textFr:"La brume a couvert le sommet de la montagne ; ne fais pas demi-tour en disant qu'on ne peut la franchir. La brume fait partie de la montagne, et le chemin aussi.",categoryFr:"courage",textJa:"\u9727\u304c\u5c71\u306e\u9802\u3092\u8986\u3063\u305f\u3002\u8d8a\u3048\u3089\u308c\u306c\u3068\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u5f15\u304d\u8fd4\u3059\u306a\u3002\u9727\u3082\u5c71\u306e\u4e00\u90e8\u3001\u305d\u3057\u3066\u9053\u3082\u307e\u305f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u52c7\u6c17"},{id:"q123",text:"Karac'o\u011flan der ki: G\xfczel seven g\xfczel olur.",original:"",source:"Karacao\u011flan",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"Karacao\u011flan says: One who loves the beautiful becomes beautiful.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Karacao\u011flan sagt: Wer das Sch\xf6ne liebt, wird sch\xf6n.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Karacao\u011flan dice: quien ama lo bello se vuelve bello.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Karacao\u011flan diz: quem ama o belo torna-se belo.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Karacao\u011flan dit : qui aime le beau devient beau.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u30ab\u30e9\u30b8\u30e3\u30aa\u30fc\u30eb\u306f\u8a00\u3046\u2014\u2014\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u3082\u306e\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306f\u3001\u7f8e\u3057\u304f\u306a\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q124",text:"Y\xfcksek yerde oturan, derin vadiye bakar. Bak da \xf6\u011fren.",original:"",source:"Karacao\u011flan",category:"hikmet",rarity:"common",textEn:"He who sits in the high place gazes upon the deep valley. Look and learn.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Wer am hohen Ort sitzt, blickt ins tiefe Tal. Schau und lerne.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"Quien se sienta en lo alto contempla el valle profundo. Mira y aprende.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"Quem se senta no alto contempla o vale profundo. Olha e aprende.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Celui qui si\xe8ge en haut contemple la vall\xe9e profonde. Regarde et apprends.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u9ad8\u304d\u5834\u6240\u306b\u5ea7\u3059\u8005\u306f\u3001\u6df1\u304d\u8c37\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3081\u308b\u3002\u898b\u3066\u3001\u5b66\u3079\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q125",text:"Sevda bu kadar m\u0131 g\xfczel? G\xfczellik bu kadar m\u0131 sevdaya yak\u0131n?",original:"",source:"Karacao\u011flan",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"Can love be this beautiful? Can beauty be this close to love?",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Kann die Liebe so sch\xf6n sein? Kann die Sch\xf6nheit der Liebe so nah sein?",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"\xbfPuede el amor ser tan hermoso? \xbfPuede la belleza estar tan cerca del amor?",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Pode o amor ser t\xe3o belo? Pode a beleza estar t\xe3o perto do amor?",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"L'amour peut-il \xeatre si beau ? La beaut\xe9 peut-elle \xeatre si proche de l'amour ?",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u306f\u3053\u308c\u307b\u3069\u7f8e\u3057\u304f\u3042\u308a\u3046\u308b\u306e\u304b\u3002\u7f8e\u306f\u611b\u306b\u3053\u308c\u307b\u3069\u8fd1\u304f\u3042\u308a\u3046\u308b\u306e\u304b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q126",text:"Su uyur d\xfc\u015fman uyumaz; sen de uyan\u0131k ol.",original:"",source:"Karacao\u011flan",category:"hikmet",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Water sleeps, but the enemy does not; you too must stay watchful.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Das Wasser schl\xe4ft, doch der Feind nicht; auch du musst wachsam bleiben.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"El agua duerme, pero el enemigo no; t\xfa tambi\xe9n debes permanecer alerta.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"A \xe1gua dorme, mas o inimigo n\xe3o; tu tamb\xe9m deves permanecer vigilante.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"L'eau dort, mais l'ennemi non ; toi aussi tu dois rester vigilant.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u6c34\u306f\u7720\u308b\u304c\u3001\u6575\u306f\u7720\u3089\u306c\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u307e\u305f\u3001\u8b66\u6212\u3092\u6020\u308b\u306a\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q127",text:"G\xf6n\xfcl sevdalara d\xfc\u015fmeden \xf6nce uyar\u0131r. Dinle onu.",original:"",source:"Karacao\u011flan",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The heart gives warning before falling into love. Listen to it.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Das Herz warnt, bevor es in die Liebe f\xe4llt. H\xf6re auf es.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"El coraz\xf3n avisa antes de caer en el amor. Esc\xfachalo.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"O cora\xe7\xe3o avisa antes de cair no amor. Escuta-o.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Le c\u0153ur avertit avant de tomber en amour. \xc9coute-le.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u5fc3\u306f\u611b\u306b\u843d\u3061\u308b\u524d\u306b\u544a\u3052\u308b\u3002\u305d\u308c\u306b\u8033\u3092\u50be\u3051\u3088\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q128",text:"Kul Himmet der ki: Hakikat kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7acak tek anahtar sevgidir.",original:"",source:"Kul Himmet",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Kul Himmet says: The only key that opens the door of truth is love.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Kul Himmet sagt: Der einzige Schl\xfcssel, der die T\xfcr der Wahrheit \xf6ffnet, ist die Liebe.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Kul Himmet dice: la \xfanica llave que abre la puerta de la verdad es el amor.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Kul Himmet diz: a \xfanica chave que abre a porta da verdade \xe9 o amor.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Kul Himmet dit : la seule cl\xe9 qui ouvre la porte de la v\xe9rit\xe9 est l'amour.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u30af\u30eb\u30fb\u30d2\u30f3\u30e1\u30c8\u306f\u8a00\u3046\u2014\u2014\u771f\u5b9f\u306e\u6249\u3092\u958b\u304f\u552f\u4e00\u306e\u9375\u306f\u611b\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q129",text:"Yol erinin ni\u015fan\u0131: s\xf6yledi\u011fi ile yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131 birdir.",original:"",source:"Kul Himmet",category:"d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfck",rarity:"common",textEn:"The mark of one upon the path: what they say and what they do are one.",categoryEn:"honesty",textDe:"Das Zeichen eines Menschen auf dem Weg: was er sagt und was er tut, sind eins.",categoryDe:"Ehrlichkeit",textEs:"La marca de quien va por el camino: lo que dice y lo que hace son una sola cosa.",categoryEs:"honestidad",textPt:"A marca de quem segue o caminho: o que diz e o que faz s\xe3o uma s\xf3 coisa.",categoryPt:"honestidade",textFr:"La marque de celui qui est sur la voie : ce qu'il dit et ce qu'il fait ne font qu'un.",categoryFr:"honn\xeatet\xe9",textJa:"\u9053\u3092\u884c\u304f\u8005\u306e\u5370\u2014\u2014\u305d\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u3068\u305d\u306e\u884c\u3044\u304c\u4e00\u3064\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3002",categoryJa:"\u8aa0\u5b9f\u3055"},{id:"q130",text:"Hakk'\u0131 seven zalim olmaz.",original:"",source:"Kul Himmet",category:"adalet",rarity:"common",textEn:"Whoever loves the Truth cannot be a tyrant.",categoryEn:"justice",textDe:"Wer die Wahrheit liebt, kann kein Tyrann sein.",categoryDe:"Gerechtigkeit",textEs:"Quien ama la Verdad no puede ser un tirano.",categoryEs:"justicia",textPt:"Quem ama a Verdade n\xe3o pode ser um tirano.",categoryPt:"justi\xe7a",textFr:"Qui aime la V\xe9rit\xe9 ne peut \xeatre un tyran.",categoryFr:"justice",textJa:"\u771f\u5b9f\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306f\u3001\u66b4\u541b\u306b\u306f\u306a\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u6b63\u7fa9"},{id:"q131",text:"A\u015fk bir bahr-i ummand\u0131r, i\xe7inde inci sakl\u0131d\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Kul Himmet",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Love is a boundless ocean; within it, pearls are hidden.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Die Liebe ist ein grenzenloser Ozean; in ihm sind Perlen verborgen.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"El amor es un oc\xe9ano sin l\xedmites; en \xe9l se ocultan las perlas.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O amor \xe9 um oceano sem limites; dentro dele escondem-se p\xe9rolas.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"L'amour est un oc\xe9an sans limites ; en lui sont cach\xe9es les perles.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u306f\u679c\u3066\u306a\u304d\u5927\u6d77\u3002\u305d\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u771f\u73e0\u304c\u96a0\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q132",text:"S\u0131r verme her yabanc\u0131ya, i\xe7in dolar d\u0131\u015fa ta\u015far.",original:"",source:"Kul Himmet",category:"hikmet",rarity:"common",textEn:"Do not share your secret with every stranger; what fills within will spill outside.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Teile dein Geheimnis nicht mit jedem Fremden; was sich innen f\xfcllt, l\xe4uft nach au\xdfen \xfcber.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"No compartas tu secreto con cualquier extra\xf1o; lo que se llena por dentro se derrama por fuera.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"N\xe3o partilhes o teu segredo com qualquer estranho; o que se enche por dentro transborda por fora.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Ne partage pas ton secret avec chaque \xe9tranger ; ce qui se remplit au-dedans d\xe9borde au-dehors.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u79d8\u5bc6\u3092\u3069\u3093\u306a\u898b\u77e5\u3089\u306c\u8005\u3068\u3082\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u306a\u3002\u5185\u306b\u6e80\u3061\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306f\u5916\u3078\u3042\u3075\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q133",text:"Mevlana sever, \u015eems sever, Yunus sever; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc a\u015fk tek bir nehirdir.",original:"",source:"Tasavvuf Gelene\u011fi",category:"ask",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Mevlana loves, \u015eems loves, Yunus loves; for love is a single river.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Mevlana liebt, \u015eems liebt, Yunus liebt; denn die Liebe ist ein einziger Fluss.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Mevlana ama, \u015eems ama, Yunus ama; pues el amor es un solo r\xedo.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"Mevlana ama, \u015eems ama, Yunus ama; pois o amor \xe9 um s\xf3 rio.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Mevlana aime, \u015eems aime, Yunus aime ; car l'amour est une seule rivi\xe8re.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u30e1\u30f4\u30e9\u30fc\u30ca\u306f\u611b\u3057\u3001\u30b7\u30a7\u30e0\u30b9\u306f\u611b\u3057\u3001\u30e6\u30cc\u30b9\u306f\u611b\u3059\u308b\u3002\u611b\u306f\u305f\u3060\u4e00\u7b4b\u306e\u5ddd\u306a\u306e\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q134",text:"Nefsi \xf6ld\xfcrmeden, ruh dirileemez.",original:"",source:"Tasavvuf Gelene\u011fi",category:"nefis",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Without slaying the ego, the soul cannot come alive.",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Ohne das Ego zu t\xf6ten, kann die Seele nicht lebendig werden.",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"Sin dar muerte al ego, el alma no puede cobrar vida.",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"Sem matar o ego, a alma n\xe3o pode ganhar vida.",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"Sans tuer l'ego, l'\xe2me ne peut prendre vie.",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u81ea\u6211\u3092\u6bba\u3055\u305a\u306b\u3001\u9b42\u306f\u751f\u304d\u751f\u304d\u3068\u306f\u306a\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q135",text:"Halvette olsan da halk i\xe7inde, halkta olsan da halvette.",original:"",source:"Tasavvuf Gelene\u011fi",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Be in solitude even amid the crowd, be among the crowd even in solitude.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Sei in der Einsamkeit selbst inmitten der Menge, sei unter der Menge selbst in der Einsamkeit.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"Est\xe1 en soledad aun en medio de la multitud, est\xe1 entre la multitud aun en la soledad.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"Est\xe1 na solid\xe3o mesmo no meio da multid\xe3o, est\xe1 entre a multid\xe3o mesmo na solid\xe3o.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Sois dans la solitude m\xeame au milieu de la foule, sois parmi la foule m\xeame dans la solitude.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u7fa4\u8846\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u3063\u3066\u3082\u5b64\u72ec\u306b\u3042\u308c\u3001\u5b64\u72ec\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u3063\u3066\u3082\u7fa4\u8846\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u308c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q136",text:"Dervi\u015f d\xfcnyaya iki eliyle sar\u0131lmaz.",original:"",source:"Tasavvuf Gelene\u011fi",category:"z\xfchd",rarity:"common",textEn:"A dervish does not embrace the world with both hands.",categoryEn:"detachment",textDe:"Ein Derwisch umarmt die Welt nicht mit beiden H\xe4nden.",categoryDe:"Losl\xf6sung",textEs:"Un derviche no abraza el mundo con ambas manos.",categoryEs:"desapego",textPt:"Um dervixe n\xe3o abra\xe7a o mundo com ambas as m\xe3os.",categoryPt:"desapego",textFr:"Un derviche n'embrasse pas le monde \xe0 deux mains.",categoryFr:"d\xe9tachement",textJa:"\u6258\u9262\u50e7\u306f\u4e21\u624b\u3067\u4e16\u754c\u3092\u62b1\u304d\u3057\u3081\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u96e2\u8131"},{id:"q137",text:"Sab\u0131r ile koruk helva olur.",original:"",source:"Tasavvuf Gelene\u011fi",category:"sabir",rarity:"common",textEn:"With patience, sour grapes become sweet halva.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Mit Geduld werden saure Trauben zu s\xfc\xdfer Halva.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"Con paciencia, las uvas agrias se vuelven dulce halva.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"Com paci\xeancia, as uvas azedas tornam-se doce halva.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"Avec la patience, les raisins acides deviennent un doux halva.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u5fcd\u8010\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u3059\u308c\u3070\u3001\u9178\u3044\u3076\u3069\u3046\u3082\u7518\u3044\u30cf\u30eb\u30f4\u30a1\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q138",text:"\u015e\xfck\xfcr kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7an, bolluk i\xe7inde ya\u015far.",original:"",source:"Tasavvuf Gelene\u011fi",category:"s\xfck\xfcr",rarity:"common",textEn:"Whoever opens the door of gratitude lives in abundance.",categoryEn:"gratitude",textDe:"Wer die T\xfcr der Dankbarkeit \xf6ffnet, lebt in F\xfclle.",categoryDe:"Dankbarkeit",textEs:"Quien abre la puerta de la gratitud vive en abundancia.",categoryEs:"gratitud",textPt:"Quem abre a porta da gratid\xe3o vive em abund\xe2ncia.",categoryPt:"gratid\xe3o",textFr:"Qui ouvre la porte de la gratitude vit dans l'abondance.",categoryFr:"gratitude",textJa:"\u611f\u8b1d\u306e\u6249\u3092\u958b\u304f\u8005\u306f\u3001\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u751f\u304d\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611f\u8b1d"},{id:"q139",text:"Her g\xfczelli\u011fin alt\u0131nda bir ac\u0131 yatar. Her olgunlu\u011fun alt\u0131nda bir yara.",original:"",source:"Tasavvuf Gelene\u011fi",category:"hikmet",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Beneath every beauty lies a sorrow. Beneath every ripeness, a wound.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Unter jeder Sch\xf6nheit liegt ein Kummer. Unter jeder Reife eine Wunde.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"Bajo cada belleza yace una pena. Bajo cada madurez, una herida.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"Sob cada beleza jaz uma tristeza. Sob cada maturidade, uma ferida.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Sous chaque beaut\xe9 repose un chagrin. Sous chaque maturit\xe9, une blessure.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u3069\u306e\u7f8e\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u3082\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u304c\u6a2a\u305f\u308f\u308b\u3002\u3069\u306e\u5186\u719f\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u3082\u50b7\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q140",text:"B\xfclb\xfcl\xfcn g\xfclden ayr\u0131 d\xfc\u015fmesi gibidir insan Hakk'tan.",original:"",source:"Tasavvuf Gelene\u011fi",category:"hasret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"As the nightingale is parted from the rose, so is the human from the Truth.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Wie die Nachtigall von der Rose getrennt ist, so ist der Mensch von der Wahrheit.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"Como el ruise\xf1or est\xe1 separado de la rosa, as\xed lo est\xe1 el ser humano de la Verdad.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"Como o rouxinol est\xe1 separado da rosa, assim est\xe1 o ser humano da Verdade.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Comme le rossignol est s\xe9par\xe9 de la rose, ainsi l'\xeatre humain l'est de la V\xe9rit\xe9.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u30ca\u30a4\u30c1\u30f3\u30b2\u30fc\u30eb\u304c\u30d0\u30e9\u304b\u3089\u5f15\u304d\u96e2\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u4eba\u9593\u306f\u771f\u5b9f\u304b\u3089\u5f15\u304d\u96e2\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q141",text:"Dinle, bu ney nas\u0131l \u015fik\xe2yet ediyor; ayr\u0131l\u0131klar\u0131 nas\u0131l anlat\u0131yor.",original:"\u0628\u0634\u0646\u0648 \u0627\u0632 \u0646\u06cc \u0686\u0648\u0646 \u062d\u06a9\u0627\u06cc\u062a \u0645\u06cc\u200c\u06a9\u0646\u062f / \u0627\u0632 \u062c\u062f\u0627\u06cc\u06cc\u200c\u0647\u0627 \u0634\u06a9\u0627\u06cc\u062a \u0645\u06cc\u200c\u06a9\u0646\u062f",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hasret",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Listen to the reed, how it tells a tale, complaining of separations.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"H\xf6re auf das Rohr, wie es eine Geschichte erz\xe4hlt und \xfcber die Trennungen klagt.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"Escucha a la ca\xf1a, c\xf3mo cuenta una historia, lament\xe1ndose de las separaciones.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"Escuta a cana, como conta uma hist\xf3ria, queixando-se das separa\xe7\xf5es.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"\xc9coute le roseau, comme il raconte une histoire, se plaignant des s\xe9parations.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u8466\u306b\u8033\u3092\u50be\u3051\u3088\u3001\u3044\u304b\u306b\u7269\u8a9e\u3092\u8a9e\u308a\u3001\u5225\u96e2\u3092\u5606\u304f\u304b\u3092\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q142",text:"Beni kam\u0131\u015fl\u0131ktan kestiklerinden beri, feryad\u0131mla erkek de kad\u0131n da inledi.",original:"\u06a9\u0632 \u0646\u06cc\u0633\u062a\u0627\u0646 \u062a\u0627 \u0645\u0631\u0627 \u0628\u0628\u0631\u06cc\u062f\u0647\u200c\u0627\u0646\u062f / \u0627\u0632 \u0646\u0641\u06cc\u0631\u0645 \u0645\u0631\u062f \u0648 \u0632\u0646 \u0646\u0627\u0644\u06cc\u062f\u0647\u200c\u0627\u0646\u062f",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hasret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Ever since they cut me from the reed bed, men and women have moaned at my lament.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Seit sie mich aus dem R\xf6hricht schnitten, haben M\xe4nner und Frauen bei meinem Klagen geseufzt.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"Desde que me cortaron del ca\xf1averal, hombres y mujeres han gemido ante mi lamento.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"Desde que me cortaram do canavial, homens e mulheres gemeram ante o meu lamento.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Depuis qu'on m'a coup\xe9 de la roseli\xe8re, hommes et femmes ont g\xe9mi \xe0 ma plainte.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u8466\u539f\u304b\u3089\u5207\u308a\u53d6\u3089\u308c\u3066\u4ee5\u6765\u3001\u7537\u3082\u5973\u3082\u79c1\u306e\u5606\u304d\u306b\u3046\u3081\u3044\u3066\u304d\u305f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q143",text:"Ayr\u0131l\u0131ktan par\xe7a par\xe7a olmu\u015f bir y\xfcrek isterim ki, ona \xf6zleyi\u015fin ac\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 anlatabileyim.",original:"\u0633\u06cc\u0646\u0647 \u062e\u0648\u0627\u0647\u0645 \u0634\u0631\u062d\u0647 \u0634\u0631\u062d\u0647 \u0627\u0632 \u0641\u0631\u0627\u0642 / \u062a\u0627 \u0628\u06af\u0648\u06cc\u0645 \u0634\u0631\u062d \u062f\u0631\u062f \u0627\u0634\u062a\u06cc\u0627\u0642",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hasret",rarity:"rare",textEn:"I want a heart torn to shreds by separation, that I may unfold to it the pain of longing.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Ich will ein Herz, von der Trennung zerrissen, damit ich ihm den Schmerz der Sehnsucht entfalten kann.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"Quiero un coraz\xf3n hecho jirones por la separaci\xf3n, para desplegarle el dolor de la a\xf1oranza.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"Quero um cora\xe7\xe3o feito em farrapos pela separa\xe7\xe3o, para lhe desdobrar a dor da saudade.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Je veux un c\u0153ur d\xe9chir\xe9 en lambeaux par la s\xe9paration, pour lui d\xe9ployer la douleur de la nostalgie.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5225\u96e2\u306b\u5f15\u304d\u88c2\u304b\u308c\u305f\u5fc3\u304c\u6b32\u3057\u3044\u3001\u305d\u3053\u306b\u61a7\u308c\u306e\u75db\u307f\u3092\u958b\u3044\u3066\u898b\u305b\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q144",text:"Asl\u0131ndan uzak d\xfc\u015fen ki\u015fi, yine birle\u015fece\u011fi zaman\u0131 arar durur.",original:"\u0647\u0631 \u06a9\u0633\u06cc \u06a9\u0648 \u062f\u0648\u0631 \u0645\u0627\u0646\u062f \u0627\u0632 \u0627\u0635\u0644 \u062e\u0648\u06cc\u0634 / \u0628\u0627\u0632 \u062c\u0648\u06cc\u062f \u0631\u0648\u0632\u06af\u0627\u0631 \u0648\u0635\u0644 \u062e\u0648\u06cc\u0634",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hasret",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Whoever is left far from their source seeks once more the time of reunion.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Wer fern von seiner Quelle blieb, sucht aufs Neue die Zeit der Wiedervereinigung.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"Quien queda lejos de su origen busca de nuevo el tiempo del reencuentro.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"Quem fica longe da sua origem busca de novo o tempo do reencontro.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Celui qui est rest\xe9 loin de sa source cherche de nouveau le temps des retrouvailles.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u5df1\u306e\u6e90\u304b\u3089\u9060\u304f\u96e2\u308c\u305f\u8005\u306f\u3001\u518d\u3073\u518d\u4f1a\u306e\u3068\u304d\u3092\u6c42\u3081\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q145",text:"Neyin sesi havadan de\u011fil ate\u015ftendir; kimde bu ate\u015f yoksa, yok olsun.",original:"\u0622\u062a\u0634 \u0627\u0633\u062a \u0627\u06cc\u0646 \u0628\u0627\u0646\u06af \u0646\u0627\u06cc \u0648 \u0646\u06cc\u0633\u062a \u0628\u0627\u062f / \u0647\u0631 \u06a9\u0647 \u0627\u06cc\u0646 \u0622\u062a\u0634 \u0646\u062f\u0627\u0631\u062f \u0646\u06cc\u0633\u062a \u0628\u0627\u062f",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ask",rarity:"rare",textEn:"The reed's cry is fire, not wind; whoever lacks this fire, let them be nothing.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Der Schrei des Rohrs ist Feuer, nicht Wind; wem dieses Feuer fehlt, der sei nichts.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"El llanto de la ca\xf1a es fuego, no viento; quien carezca de este fuego, que sea nada.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O choro da cana \xe9 fogo, n\xe3o vento; quem n\xe3o tiver este fogo, que seja nada.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Le cri du roseau est feu, non vent ; que celui qui manque de ce feu ne soit rien.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u8466\u306e\u53eb\u3073\u306f\u706b\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u98a8\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u3053\u306e\u706b\u3092\u6b20\u304f\u8005\u306f\u3001\u7121\u3067\u3042\u308c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q146",text:"A\u015fk\u0131n ate\u015fidir neye d\xfc\u015fen; a\u015fk\u0131n co\u015fkusudur \u015faraba d\xfc\u015fen.",original:"\u0622\u062a\u0634 \u0639\u0634\u0642 \u0627\u0633\u062a \u06a9\u0627\u0646\u062f\u0631 \u0646\u06cc \u0641\u062a\u0627\u062f / \u062c\u0648\u0634\u0634 \u0639\u0634\u0642 \u0627\u0633\u062a \u06a9\u0627\u0646\u062f\u0631 \u0645\u06cc \u0641\u062a\u0627\u062f",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"It is the fire of love that fell upon the reed; the ferment of love that fell upon the wine.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Es ist das Feuer der Liebe, das auf das Rohr fiel; der Rausch der Liebe, der auf den Wein fiel.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"Es el fuego del amor el que cay\xf3 sobre la ca\xf1a; el fermento del amor el que cay\xf3 sobre el vino.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"\xc9 o fogo do amor que caiu sobre a cana; o fermento do amor que caiu sobre o vinho.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"C'est le feu de l'amour qui est tomb\xe9 sur le roseau ; le ferment de l'amour qui est tomb\xe9 sur le vin.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u8466\u306b\u843d\u3061\u305f\u306e\u306f\u611b\u306e\u706b\u3001\u9152\u306b\u843d\u3061\u305f\u306e\u306f\u611b\u306e\u9175\u6bcd\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q147",text:"Hamd\u0131m, pi\u015ftim, yand\u0131m.",original:"\u062e\u0627\u0645 \u0628\u062f\u0645 \u067e\u062e\u062a\u0647 \u0634\u062f\u0645 \u0633\u0648\u062e\u062a\u0645",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"degisim",rarity:"rare",textEn:"I was raw, I became cooked, I was burned.",categoryEn:"transformation",textDe:"Ich war roh, ich wurde gekocht, ich wurde verbrannt.",categoryDe:"Wandlung",textEs:"Era crudo, me coc\xed, ard\xed.",categoryEs:"transformaci\xf3n",textPt:"Eu era cru, fiquei cozido, fui queimado.",categoryPt:"transforma\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"J'\xe9tais cru, je suis devenu cuit, j'ai \xe9t\xe9 br\xfbl\xe9.",categoryFr:"transformation",textJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u751f\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3001\u716e\u3048\u305f\u3001\u305d\u3057\u3066\u713c\u304b\u308c\u305f\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5909\u5bb9"},{id:"q148",text:"Sevgilinin geli\u015fiyle g\xf6n\xfclde bir geni\u015flik a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r; bu g\xf6n\xfcl, ba\u015fka bir kap\u0131d\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"kalp",rarity:"common",textEn:"With the Beloved's coming, a spaciousness opens in the heart; this heart is another door.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Mit dem Kommen des Geliebten \xf6ffnet sich eine Weite im Herzen; dieses Herz ist eine andere T\xfcr.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"Con la llegada del Amado se abre una amplitud en el coraz\xf3n; este coraz\xf3n es otra puerta.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"Com a chegada do Amado, abre-se uma amplid\xe3o no cora\xe7\xe3o; este cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 outra porta.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"\xc0 la venue de l'Aim\xe9, une ampleur s'ouvre dans le c\u0153ur ; ce c\u0153ur est une autre porte.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306e\u8a2a\u308c\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3001\u5fc3\u306b\u5e83\u304c\u308a\u304c\u958b\u304f\u3002\u3053\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u3001\u3082\u3046\u4e00\u3064\u306e\u6249\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q149",text:"Bu d\xfcnyaya, kals\u0131n diye gelmedik; bir kona\u011fa indik, yine yola \xe7\u0131kaca\u011f\u0131z.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"z\xfchd",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"We did not come to this world to remain; we have lodged at an inn and will set out again.",categoryEn:"detachment",textDe:"Wir kamen nicht in diese Welt, um zu bleiben; wir haben in einer Herberge Quartier genommen und werden wieder aufbrechen.",categoryDe:"Losl\xf6sung",textEs:"No vinimos a este mundo para quedarnos; nos hemos hospedado en una posada y partiremos de nuevo.",categoryEs:"desapego",textPt:"N\xe3o viemos a este mundo para ficar; hosped\xe1mo-nos numa estalagem e partiremos de novo.",categoryPt:"desapego",textFr:"Nous ne sommes pas venus en ce monde pour rester ; nous avons log\xe9 dans une auberge et repartirons.",categoryFr:"d\xe9tachement",textJa:"\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306f\u3068\u3069\u307e\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3053\u306e\u4e16\u3078\u6765\u305f\u306e\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u5bbf\u306b\u6cca\u307e\u308a\u3001\u307e\u305f\u65c5\u7acb\u3064\u306e\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u96e2\u8131"},{id:"q150",text:"Su kab\u0131n \u015feklini al\u0131r; g\xf6nl\xfcn rengini i\xe7ine konandan al\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hikmet",rarity:"common",textEn:"Water takes the shape of its vessel; the heart takes its color from what is placed within it.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Das Wasser nimmt die Form seines Gef\xe4\xdfes an; das Herz nimmt die Farbe dessen an, was man hineinlegt.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"El agua toma la forma de su recipiente; el coraz\xf3n toma el color de lo que se pone dentro.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"A \xe1gua toma a forma do seu recipiente; o cora\xe7\xe3o toma a cor daquilo que se coloca dentro.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"L'eau prend la forme de son r\xe9cipient ; le c\u0153ur prend la couleur de ce qu'on y d\xe9pose.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u6c34\u306f\u5668\u306e\u5f62\u3092\u3068\u308b\u3002\u5fc3\u306f\u305d\u3053\u306b\u7f6e\u304b\u308c\u305f\u3082\u306e\u306e\u8272\u3092\u3068\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q151",text:"Ba\u011f bozulunca \xfcz\xfcm \u015faraba d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr; sen de da\u011f\u0131l ki ba\u015fka bir \u015feye d\xf6n\xfc\u015fesin.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"degisim",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"When the vineyard is undone the grape becomes wine; you too must come apart, that you may become something else.",categoryEn:"transformation",textDe:"Wenn der Weinberg vergeht, wird die Traube zu Wein; auch du musst zerfallen, damit du etwas anderes wirst.",categoryDe:"Wandlung",textEs:"Cuando el vi\xf1edo se deshace, la uva se vuelve vino; t\xfa tambi\xe9n debes deshacerte para volverte otra cosa.",categoryEs:"transformaci\xf3n",textPt:"Quando o vinhedo se desfaz, a uva torna-se vinho; tu tamb\xe9m deves desfazer-te, para te tornares outra coisa.",categoryPt:"transforma\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Quand la vigne se d\xe9fait, le raisin devient vin ; toi aussi tu dois te d\xe9faire, pour devenir autre chose.",categoryFr:"transformation",textJa:"\u3076\u3069\u3046\u7551\u304c\u89e3\u3051\u308b\u3068\u304d\u3001\u3076\u3069\u3046\u306f\u9152\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u307e\u305f\u3001\u307b\u3069\u3051\u3066\u3053\u305d\u3001\u5225\u306e\u3082\u306e\u306b\u306a\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5909\u5bb9"},{id:"q152",text:"Sen d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceden ibaretsin; gerisi et ile kemiktir. G\xfcl d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcrsen g\xfcl bah\xe7esi olursun, diken d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcrsen dikenlik.",original:"\u0627\u06cc \u0628\u0631\u0627\u062f\u0631 \u062a\u0648 \u0647\u0645\u0647 \u0627\u0646\u062f\u06cc\u0634\u0647\u200c\u0627\u06cc / \u0645\u0627\u0628\u0642\u06cc \u062e\u0648\u062f \u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u0648\u0627\u0646 \u0648 \u0631\u06cc\u0634\u0647\u200c\u0627\u06cc",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"rare",textEn:"You are nothing but thought, brother; the rest is bone and sinew. Think a rose and you are a rose garden; think a thorn and you are thorn brush.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Du bist nichts als Gedanke, Bruder; der Rest ist Knochen und Sehne. Denk eine Rose, und du bist ein Rosengarten; denk einen Dorn, und du bist Dorngestr\xfcpp.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"No eres m\xe1s que pensamiento, hermano; el resto es hueso y tend\xf3n. Piensa una rosa y eres un jard\xedn de rosas; piensa una espina y eres un zarzal.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"N\xe3o \xe9s sen\xe3o pensamento, irm\xe3o; o resto \xe9 osso e tend\xe3o. Pensa uma rosa e \xe9s um roseiral; pensa um espinho e \xe9s um espinheiro.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"Tu n'es rien que pens\xe9e, mon fr\xe8re ; le reste est os et tendon. Pense une rose et tu es un jardin de roses ; pense une \xe9pine et tu es un buisson d'\xe9pines.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u5144\u5f1f\u3088\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u601d\u3044\u306b\u307b\u304b\u306a\u3089\u306c\u3002\u6b8b\u308a\u306f\u9aa8\u3068\u8171\u3060\u3002\u30d0\u30e9\u3092\u601d\u3048\u3070\u30d0\u30e9\u5712\u3068\u306a\u308a\u3001\u68d8\u3092\u601d\u3048\u3070\u68d8\u306e\u8302\u307f\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q153",text:"D\xfcn\xfcn ge\xe7ti, s\xf6z\xfc de onunla gitti; bug\xfcn yeni bir s\xf6z s\xf6ylemek gerek.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"an",rarity:"common",textEn:"Yesterday has passed, and its words passed with it; today one must speak a new word.",categoryEn:"present moment",textDe:"Gestern ist vergangen, und mit ihm seine Worte; heute muss man ein neues Wort sprechen.",categoryDe:"Gegenwart",textEs:"El ayer ha pasado, y con \xe9l pasaron sus palabras; hoy hay que decir una palabra nueva.",categoryEs:"presente",textPt:"O ontem passou, e com ele passaram as suas palavras; hoje \xe9 preciso dizer uma palavra nova.",categoryPt:"presente",textFr:"Hier est pass\xe9, et ses paroles avec lui ; aujourd'hui il faut dire une parole nouvelle.",categoryFr:"pr\xe9sent",textJa:"\u6628\u65e5\u306f\u904e\u304e\u3001\u305d\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u3082\u904e\u304e\u53bb\u3063\u305f\u3002\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u8a00\u8449\u3092\u8a9e\u3089\u306d\u3070\u306a\u3089\u306c\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4eca\u3053\u306e\u77ac\u9593"},{id:"q154",text:"D\xfcn ge\xe7ti, d\xfcnk\xfc s\xf6zler de ge\xe7ti; \u015fimdi yeni \u015feyler s\xf6ylemek gerek.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"an",rarity:"common",textEn:"Yesterday is gone, and yesterday's talk is gone; now it is time to speak of new things.",categoryEn:"present moment",textDe:"Das Gestern ist fort, und das Gerede von gestern ist fort; nun ist es Zeit, von Neuem zu sprechen.",categoryDe:"Gegenwart",textEs:"El ayer se ha ido, y la charla de ayer se ha ido; ahora es tiempo de hablar de cosas nuevas.",categoryEs:"presente",textPt:"O ontem foi-se, e a conversa de ontem foi-se; agora \xe9 tempo de falar de coisas novas.",categoryPt:"presente",textFr:"Hier s'en est all\xe9, et les propos d'hier s'en sont all\xe9s ; il est temps maintenant de parler de choses nouvelles.",categoryFr:"pr\xe9sent",textJa:"\u6628\u65e5\u306f\u53bb\u308a\u3001\u6628\u65e5\u306e\u8a71\u3082\u53bb\u3063\u305f\u3002\u4eca\u306f\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u3053\u3068\u3092\u8a9e\u308b\u3068\u304d\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4eca\u3053\u306e\u77ac\u9593"},{id:"q155",text:"Kuyunun dibinde gibiyiz; ipi salan, bizi yukar\u0131 \xe7ekendir. \u0130pi salan ele g\xfcven.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"teslimiyet",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"We are as if at the bottom of a well; the One who lets down the rope is the One who draws us up. Trust the hand that lowers the rope.",categoryEn:"surrender",textDe:"Wir sind wie am Grund eines Brunnens; der das Seil hinabl\xe4sst, ist der, der uns heraufzieht. Vertraue der Hand, die das Seil senkt.",categoryDe:"Hingabe",textEs:"Somos como si estuvi\xe9ramos en el fondo de un pozo; quien arroja la cuerda es quien nos saca. Conf\xeda en la mano que baja la cuerda.",categoryEs:"entrega",textPt:"Somos como que no fundo de um po\xe7o; quem desce a corda \xe9 quem nos puxa para cima. Confia na m\xe3o que baixa a corda.",categoryPt:"entrega",textFr:"Nous sommes comme au fond d'un puits ; celui qui descend la corde est celui qui nous remonte. Fais confiance \xe0 la main qui abaisse la corde.",categoryFr:"abandon",textJa:"\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306f\u4e95\u6238\u306e\u5e95\u306b\u3044\u308b\u304b\u306e\u3088\u3046\u3060\u3002\u7db1\u3092\u4e0b\u308d\u3059\u8005\u3053\u305d\u3001\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u3092\u5f15\u304d\u4e0a\u3052\u308b\u8005\u3002\u7db1\u3092\u4e0b\u308d\u3059\u624b\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u3088\u3002",categoryJa:"\u660e\u3051\u6e21\u3057"},{id:"q156",text:"Bir bah\xe7eye girersen, dikenleri de\u011fil g\xfclleri g\xf6r; g\xfcl\xfc g\xf6renin g\xf6nl\xfc g\xfcl olur.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hikmet",rarity:"common",textEn:"If you enter a garden, see the roses, not the thorns; whoever beholds the rose, their heart becomes a rose.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Trittst du in einen Garten, sieh die Rosen, nicht die Dornen; wer die Rose schaut, dessen Herz wird zur Rose.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"Si entras en un jard\xedn, mira las rosas, no las espinas; quien contempla la rosa, su coraz\xf3n se vuelve rosa.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"Se entrares num jardim, v\xea as rosas, n\xe3o os espinhos; quem contempla a rosa, o seu cora\xe7\xe3o torna-se rosa.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Si tu entres dans un jardin, vois les roses, non les \xe9pines ; qui contemple la rose, son c\u0153ur devient rose.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u5ead\u306b\u5165\u308b\u306a\u3089\u3001\u68d8\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u30d0\u30e9\u3092\u898b\u3088\u3002\u30d0\u30e9\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3081\u308b\u8005\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u3001\u30d0\u30e9\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q157",text:"K\xf6t\xfcl\xfc\u011fe iyilikle kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131k ver; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc k\xf6t\xfcl\xfck dumand\u0131r, iyilik \u0131\u015f\u0131kt\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"sabir",rarity:"common",textEn:"Answer evil with good; for evil is smoke and good is light.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Begegne dem B\xf6sen mit Gutem; denn das B\xf6se ist Rauch und das Gute ist Licht.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"Responde al mal con el bien; pues el mal es humo y el bien es luz.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"Responde ao mal com o bem; pois o mal \xe9 fumo e o bem \xe9 luz.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"R\xe9ponds au mal par le bien ; car le mal est fum\xe9e et le bien est lumi\xe8re.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u60aa\u306b\u306f\u5584\u3067\u5fdc\u3048\u3088\u3002\u60aa\u306f\u7159\u3001\u5584\u306f\u5149\u306a\u306e\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q158",text:"Sabret; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc sab\u0131r, s\u0131k\u0131nt\u0131dan ferahl\u0131\u011fa a\xe7\u0131lan anahtard\u0131r.",original:"\u0635\u0628\u0631 \u06a9\u0646 \u06a9\u0627\u0627\u0644\u0635\u0628\u0631 \u0645\u0641\u062a\u0627\u062d \u0627\u0644\u0641\u0631\u062c",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"sabir",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Be patient; for patience is the key that opens relief from distress.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Sei geduldig; denn die Geduld ist der Schl\xfcssel, der die Erleichterung aus der Not \xf6ffnet.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"S\xe9 paciente; pues la paciencia es la llave que abre el alivio en la angustia.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"S\xea paciente; pois a paci\xeancia \xe9 a chave que abre o al\xedvio na afli\xe7\xe3o.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"Sois patient ; car la patience est la cl\xe9 qui ouvre le soulagement dans la d\xe9tresse.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u5fcd\u8010\u305b\u3088\u3002\u5fcd\u8010\u306f\u82e6\u96e3\u304b\u3089\u306e\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u958b\u304f\u9375\u306a\u306e\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q159",text:"T\xf6vbe at\u0131na bin; bu at, bir anda uzun yollar\u0131 a\u015far.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"tevbe",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Mount the steed of repentance; this steed crosses long roads in a single moment.",categoryEn:"repentance",textDe:"Besteige das Ross der Reue; dieses Ross durchquert lange Wege in einem einzigen Augenblick.",categoryDe:"Reue",textEs:"Monta el corcel del arrepentimiento; este corcel cruza largos caminos en un solo instante.",categoryEs:"arrepentimiento",textPt:"Monta o corcel do arrependimento; este corcel atravessa longos caminhos num \xfanico instante.",categoryPt:"arrependimento",textFr:"Monte le coursier du repentir ; ce coursier franchit de longs chemins en un seul instant.",categoryFr:"repentir",textJa:"\u6094\u609f\u306e\u99ff\u99ac\u306b\u4e57\u308c\u3002\u3053\u306e\u99ac\u306f\u3001\u305f\u3060\u4e00\u77ac\u3067\u9577\u3044\u9053\u3092\u99c6\u3051\u629c\u3051\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u6094\u609f"},{id:"q160",text:"Kul, hatas\u0131n\u0131 anlad\u0131\u011f\u0131 an, derg\xe2h\u0131n kap\u0131s\u0131 ona a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"tevbe",rarity:"common",textEn:"The moment the servant understands their fault, the door of the lodge opens to them.",categoryEn:"repentance",textDe:"In dem Augenblick, da der Diener seinen Fehler versteht, \xf6ffnet sich ihm die T\xfcr der Loge.",categoryDe:"Reue",textEs:"En el momento en que el siervo comprende su falta, se le abre la puerta de la logia.",categoryEs:"arrepentimiento",textPt:"No momento em que o servo compreende a sua falta, abre-se-lhe a porta da loja.",categoryPt:"arrependimento",textFr:"\xc0 l'instant o\xf9 le serviteur comprend sa faute, la porte de la loge s'ouvre \xe0 lui.",categoryFr:"repentir",textJa:"\u50d5\u304c\u5df1\u306e\u904e\u3061\u3092\u609f\u308b\u305d\u306e\u77ac\u9593\u3001\u4fee\u9053\u5834\u306e\u6249\u304c\u5f7c\u306b\u958b\u304b\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u6094\u609f"},{id:"q161",text:"A\u015fk \xf6yle bir denizdir ki, g\xf6\u011f\xfcn \xfcst\xfcn\xfc k\xf6p\xfck kaplam\u0131\u015ft\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ask",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Love is such a sea that its foam has covered even the face of the heavens.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Die Liebe ist ein solches Meer, dass ihr Schaum selbst das Antlitz der Himmel bedeckt hat.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"El amor es un mar tan grande que su espuma ha cubierto hasta el rostro de los cielos.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O amor \xe9 um mar t\xe3o grande que a sua espuma cobriu at\xe9 a face dos c\xe9us.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"L'amour est une mer telle que son \xe9cume a couvert jusqu'au visage des cieux.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u306f\u305d\u306e\u6ce1\u304c\u5929\u306e\u9854\u3055\u3048\u8986\u3046\u307b\u3069\u306e\u6d77\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q162",text:"A\u015fk, a\u011f\u0131r y\xfckleri hafifletir; a\u015fkla her ac\u0131 tatl\u0131 olur.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ask",rarity:"common",textEn:"Love makes heavy burdens light; with love every pain turns sweet.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Die Liebe macht schwere Lasten leicht; mit der Liebe wird jeder Schmerz s\xfc\xdf.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"El amor hace ligeras las cargas pesadas; con amor todo dolor se vuelve dulce.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"O amor torna leves os fardos pesados; com amor toda dor se torna doce.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"L'amour rend l\xe9gers les lourds fardeaux ; avec l'amour toute douleur devient douce.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u306f\u91cd\u3044\u8377\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u3059\u308b\u3002\u611b\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3001\u3069\u3093\u306a\u75db\u307f\u3082\u7518\u304f\u306a\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q163",text:"Ak\u0131l topal e\u015fek \xfcst\xfcndeki yolcu gibidir; a\u015fk ise kanatla u\xe7ar.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Reason is like a traveler upon a lame donkey; love, by contrast, flies upon wings.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Der Verstand ist wie ein Reisender auf einem lahmen Esel; die Liebe dagegen fliegt auf Fl\xfcgeln.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"La raz\xf3n es como un viajero sobre un asno cojo; el amor, en cambio, vuela sobre alas.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"A raz\xe3o \xe9 como um viajante sobre um burro coxo; o amor, ao contr\xe1rio, voa sobre asas.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"La raison est comme un voyageur sur un \xe2ne boiteux ; l'amour, au contraire, vole sur des ailes.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u7406\u6027\u306f\u8db3\u306e\u4e0d\u81ea\u7531\u306a\u30ed\u30d0\u306b\u4e57\u308b\u65c5\u4eba\u306e\u3088\u3046\u3060\u3002\u4e00\u65b9\u3001\u611b\u306f\u7ffc\u3067\u98db\u3076\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q164",text:"C\xfczler k\xfcllerine do\u011fru \xe7ekilir; biz de asl\u0131m\u0131za, sevgiliye do\u011fru \xe7ekiliriz.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"birlik",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The parts are drawn toward their wholes; so are we drawn toward our origin, toward the Beloved.",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"Die Teile werden zu ihren Ganzen gezogen; so werden auch wir zu unserem Ursprung gezogen, zum Geliebten.",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"Las partes son atra\xeddas hacia sus todos; as\xed somos atra\xeddos hacia nuestro origen, hacia el Amado.",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"As partes s\xe3o atra\xeddas para os seus todos; assim somos atra\xeddos para a nossa origem, para o Amado.",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"Les parties sont attir\xe9es vers leurs touts ; ainsi sommes-nous attir\xe9s vers notre origine, vers l'Aim\xe9.",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u90e8\u5206\u306f\u305d\u306e\u5168\u4f53\u3078\u3068\u5f15\u304d\u5bc4\u305b\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3002\u305d\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u3082\u5df1\u306e\u6e90\u3078\u3001\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u3078\u3068\u5f15\u304d\u5bc4\u305b\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q165",text:"Damla, denize ula\u015f\u0131nca deniz olur; sen de benli\u011fini b\u0131rak ki ummana kar\u0131\u015fas\u0131n.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"birlik",rarity:"rare",textEn:"When the drop reaches the sea it becomes the sea; you too must let go of your self, that you may merge with the ocean.",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"Wenn der Tropfen das Meer erreicht, wird er zum Meer; auch du musst dein Selbst loslassen, damit du mit dem Ozean verschmilzt.",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"Cuando la gota llega al mar se vuelve mar; t\xfa tambi\xe9n debes soltar tu yo para fundirte con el oc\xe9ano.",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"Quando a gota chega ao mar torna-se mar; tu tamb\xe9m deves soltar o teu eu, para te fundires com o oceano.",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"Quand la goutte atteint la mer, elle devient la mer ; toi aussi tu dois l\xe2cher ton soi, pour te fondre dans l'oc\xe9an.",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u96eb\u304c\u6d77\u306b\u9054\u3059\u308c\u3070\u6d77\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u307e\u305f\u5df1\u3092\u624b\u653e\u3057\u3066\u3053\u305d\u3001\u5927\u6d77\u3068\u4e00\u3064\u306b\u306a\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q166",text:"\u0130nsan iki d\xfcnya aras\u0131nda bir k\xf6pr\xfcd\xfcr; \xfczerinde durma, ge\xe7.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"yol",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The human being is a bridge between two worlds; do not linger upon it, pass over.",categoryEn:"path",textDe:"Der Mensch ist eine Br\xfccke zwischen zwei Welten; verweile nicht auf ihr, geh hin\xfcber.",categoryDe:"Weg",textEs:"El ser humano es un puente entre dos mundos; no te demores en \xe9l, pasa al otro lado.",categoryEs:"sendero",textPt:"O ser humano \xe9 uma ponte entre dois mundos; n\xe3o te demores nela, passa para o outro lado.",categoryPt:"caminho",textFr:"L'\xeatre humain est un pont entre deux mondes ; ne t'attarde pas dessus, passe de l'autre c\xf4t\xe9.",categoryFr:"voie",textJa:"\u4eba\u9593\u306f\u4e8c\u3064\u306e\u4e16\u754c\u3092\u7d50\u3076\u6a4b\u3060\u3002\u305d\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u3068\u3069\u307e\u308b\u306a\u3001\u6e21\u308a\u8d8a\u3048\u3088\u3002",categoryJa:"\u9053"},{id:"q167",text:"Yol g\xf6steren \u0131\u015f\u0131k i\xe7eridedir; d\u0131\u015far\u0131da mum arayan, kendi g\xfcne\u015fini s\xf6nd\xfcrm\xfc\u015f demektir.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ic_ses",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The guiding light is within; whoever seeks a candle outside has put out their own sun.",categoryEn:"inner voice",textDe:"Das f\xfchrende Licht ist innen; wer drau\xdfen eine Kerze sucht, hat seine eigene Sonne ausgel\xf6scht.",categoryDe:"innere Stimme",textEs:"La luz que gu\xeda est\xe1 dentro; quien busca una vela afuera ha apagado su propio sol.",categoryEs:"voz interior",textPt:"A luz que guia est\xe1 dentro; quem procura uma vela l\xe1 fora apagou o seu pr\xf3prio sol.",categoryPt:"voz interior",textFr:"La lumi\xe8re qui guide est au-dedans ; qui cherche une bougie au-dehors a \xe9teint son propre soleil.",categoryFr:"voix int\xe9rieure",textJa:"\u5c0e\u304d\u306e\u5149\u306f\u5185\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3002\u5916\u306b\u308d\u3046\u305d\u304f\u3092\u6c42\u3081\u308b\u8005\u306f\u3001\u5df1\u306e\u592a\u967d\u3092\u6d88\u3057\u305f\u306e\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5185\u306a\u308b\u58f0"},{id:"q168",text:"C\xf6mert ol; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc toprak, tohumu c\xf6mert\xe7e al\u0131r ve kat kat geri verir.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"c\xf6mertlik",rarity:"common",textEn:"Be generous; for the earth receives the seed generously and returns it manifold.",categoryEn:"generosity",textDe:"Sei gro\xdfz\xfcgig; denn die Erde empf\xe4ngt den Samen gro\xdfz\xfcgig und gibt ihn vielfach zur\xfcck.",categoryDe:"Gro\xdfz\xfcgigkeit",textEs:"S\xe9 generoso; pues la tierra recibe la semilla con generosidad y la devuelve multiplicada.",categoryEs:"generosidad",textPt:"S\xea generoso; pois a terra recebe a semente com generosidade e devolve-a multiplicada.",categoryPt:"generosidade",textFr:"Sois g\xe9n\xe9reux ; car la terre re\xe7oit la graine avec g\xe9n\xe9rosit\xe9 et la rend au centuple.",categoryFr:"g\xe9n\xe9rosit\xe9",textJa:"\u5bdb\u5927\u3067\u3042\u308c\u3002\u5927\u5730\u306f\u7a2e\u3092\u5bdb\u5927\u306b\u53d7\u3051\u3001\u5e7e\u500d\u306b\u3082\u3057\u3066\u8fd4\u3059\u306e\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5bdb\u5927\u3055"},{id:"q169",text:"Veren el, alan elden \xfcst\xfcnd\xfcr; vererek azalmazs\u0131n, \xe7o\u011fal\u0131rs\u0131n.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"c\xf6mertlik",rarity:"common",textEn:"The giving hand is above the receiving hand; by giving you do not grow less, you grow more.",categoryEn:"generosity",textDe:"Die gebende Hand steht \xfcber der nehmenden; durch Geben wirst du nicht weniger, du wirst mehr.",categoryDe:"Gro\xdfz\xfcgigkeit",textEs:"La mano que da est\xe1 por encima de la que recibe; al dar no menguas, creces.",categoryEs:"generosidad",textPt:"A m\xe3o que d\xe1 est\xe1 acima da que recebe; ao dar n\xe3o diminuis, cresces.",categoryPt:"generosidade",textFr:"La main qui donne est au-dessus de celle qui re\xe7oit ; en donnant tu ne deviens pas moindre, tu deviens plus grand.",categoryFr:"g\xe9n\xe9rosit\xe9",textJa:"\u4e0e\u3048\u308b\u624b\u306f\u53d7\u3051\u53d6\u308b\u624b\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3002\u4e0e\u3048\u3066\u3082\u6e1b\u308b\u306e\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u5897\u3048\u308b\u306e\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5bdb\u5927\u3055"},{id:"q170",text:"\u015e\xfckret; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc \u015f\xfck\xfcr, nimetin ba\u011f\u0131d\u0131r, onu sana ba\u011flar.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"s\xfck\xfcr",rarity:"common",textEn:"Give thanks; for gratitude is the tether of blessing, binding it to you.",categoryEn:"gratitude",textDe:"Sei dankbar; denn die Dankbarkeit ist das Band des Segens, das ihn an dich bindet.",categoryDe:"Dankbarkeit",textEs:"Da gracias; pues la gratitud es la atadura de la bendici\xf3n, que la liga a ti.",categoryEs:"gratitud",textPt:"D\xe1 gra\xe7as; pois a gratid\xe3o \xe9 a amarra da b\xean\xe7\xe3o, que a prende a ti.",categoryPt:"gratid\xe3o",textFr:"Rends gr\xe2ce ; car la gratitude est l'attache de la b\xe9n\xe9diction, qui la lie \xe0 toi.",categoryFr:"gratitude",textJa:"\u611f\u8b1d\u305b\u3088\u3002\u611f\u8b1d\u306f\u6075\u307f\u3092\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306b\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u3051\u308b\u7db1\u306a\u306e\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611f\u8b1d"},{id:"q171",text:"Her sabah yeniden do\u011far\u0131z; d\xfcnk\xfc kayg\u0131lar\u0131 yata\u011f\u0131nda b\u0131rak.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"an",rarity:"common",textEn:"Each morning we are born anew; leave yesterday's worries in their bed.",categoryEn:"present moment",textDe:"Jeden Morgen werden wir neu geboren; lass die Sorgen von gestern in ihrem Bett.",categoryDe:"Gegenwart",textEs:"Cada ma\xf1ana nacemos de nuevo; deja las preocupaciones de ayer en su lecho.",categoryEs:"presente",textPt:"A cada manh\xe3 nascemos de novo; deixa as preocupa\xe7\xf5es de ontem no seu leito.",categoryPt:"presente",textFr:"Chaque matin nous naissons \xe0 nouveau ; laisse les soucis d'hier dans leur lit.",categoryFr:"pr\xe9sent",textJa:"\u6bce\u671d\u3001\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306f\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u751f\u307e\u308c\u308b\u3002\u6628\u65e5\u306e\u6182\u3044\u306f\u305d\u306e\u5bdd\u5e8a\u306b\u7f6e\u3044\u3066\u304a\u3051\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4eca\u3053\u306e\u77ac\u9593"},{id:"q172",text:"G\xf6n\xfcl aynas\u0131n\u0131 cilala; pas tutmu\u015f ayna, ne sureti g\xf6sterir ne nuru.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"kalp",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Polish the mirror of the heart; a rusted mirror shows neither form nor light.",categoryEn:"heart",textDe:"Poliere den Spiegel des Herzens; ein verrosteter Spiegel zeigt weder Gestalt noch Licht.",categoryDe:"Herz",textEs:"Pule el espejo del coraz\xf3n; un espejo oxidado no muestra ni forma ni luz.",categoryEs:"coraz\xf3n",textPt:"Pole o espelho do cora\xe7\xe3o; um espelho enferrujado n\xe3o mostra nem forma nem luz.",categoryPt:"cora\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Polis le miroir du c\u0153ur ; un miroir rouill\xe9 ne montre ni forme ni lumi\xe8re.",categoryFr:"c\u0153ur",textJa:"\u5fc3\u306e\u93e1\u3092\u78e8\u3051\u3002\u9306\u3073\u305f\u93e1\u306f\u3001\u59ff\u3082\u5149\u3082\u6620\u3055\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fc3"},{id:"q173",text:"Nefis, beslendik\xe7e azar; a\xe7 b\u0131rakt\u0131k\xe7a uysalla\u015f\u0131r.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"nefis",rarity:"common",textEn:"The ego grows insolent the more it is fed; the more you starve it, the gentler it becomes.",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Das Ego wird umso anma\xdfender, je mehr man es f\xfcttert; je mehr du es hungern l\xe4sst, desto sanfter wird es.",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"El ego se vuelve m\xe1s insolente cuanto m\xe1s se le alimenta; cuanto m\xe1s lo dejas en ayunas, m\xe1s manso se vuelve.",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"O ego torna-se mais insolente quanto mais o alimentas; quanto mais o deixas em jejum, mais manso se torna.",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"L'ego devient d'autant plus insolent qu'on le nourrit ; plus tu l'affames, plus il devient doux.",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u81ea\u6211\u306f\u990a\u3048\u3070\u990a\u3046\u307b\u3069\u50b2\u6162\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3002\u98e2\u3048\u3055\u305b\u308b\u307b\u3069\u3001\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q174",text:"Kendini arayan, sonunda kendinden ge\xe7meyi \xf6\u011frenir.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"nefis",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Whoever searches for the self in the end learns to pass beyond the self.",categoryEn:"self",textDe:"Wer nach dem Selbst sucht, lernt am Ende, \xfcber das Selbst hinauszugehen.",categoryDe:"Selbst",textEs:"Quien busca el yo aprende al fin a ir m\xe1s all\xe1 del yo.",categoryEs:"ser",textPt:"Quem procura o eu aprende, ao fim, a ir al\xe9m do eu.",categoryPt:"eu",textFr:"Qui cherche le soi apprend \xe0 la fin \xe0 d\xe9passer le soi.",categoryFr:"soi",textJa:"\u81ea\u5df1\u3092\u63a2\u3059\u8005\u306f\u3001\u3064\u3044\u306b\u306f\u81ea\u5df1\u3092\u8d8a\u3048\u3066\u3044\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3092\u5b66\u3076\u3002",categoryJa:"\u81ea\u5df1"},{id:"q175",text:"\xd6l\xfcm\xfcm\xfcn ard\u0131ndan mezar\u0131m\u0131 yerde arama; o, \xe2riflerin g\xf6nl\xfcndedir.",original:"\u0628\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0632 \u0648\u0641\u0627\u062a \u062a\u0631\u0628\u062a \u0645\u0627 \u062f\u0631 \u0632\u0645\u06cc\u0646 \u0645\u062c\u0648\u06cc / \u062f\u0631 \u0633\u06cc\u0646\u0647\u200c\u0647\u0627\u06cc \u0645\u0631\u062f\u0645 \u0639\u0627\u0631\u0641 \u0645\u0632\u0627\u0631 \u0645\u0627\u0633\u062a",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"birlik",rarity:"rare",textEn:"After my death, do not seek my grave in the ground; it is in the hearts of those who know.",categoryEn:"unity",textDe:"Such nach meinem Tod mein Grab nicht in der Erde; es ist in den Herzen derer, die wissen.",categoryDe:"Einheit",textEs:"Despu\xe9s de mi muerte, no busques mi tumba en la tierra; est\xe1 en los corazones de quienes saben.",categoryEs:"unidad",textPt:"Depois da minha morte, n\xe3o procures o meu t\xfamulo na terra; est\xe1 nos cora\xe7\xf5es dos que sabem.",categoryPt:"unidade",textFr:"Apr\xe8s ma mort, ne cherche pas ma tombe dans la terre ; elle est dans les c\u0153urs de ceux qui savent.",categoryFr:"unit\xe9",textJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u6b7b\u5f8c\u3001\u5730\u4e2d\u306b\u79c1\u306e\u5893\u3092\u63a2\u3059\u306a\u3002\u305d\u308c\u306f\u77e5\u308b\u8005\u305f\u3061\u306e\u5fc3\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u4e00\u4f53"},{id:"q176",text:"Bizim \xf6l\xfcm\xfcm\xfcz d\xfc\u011f\xfcn gecemizdir; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc ayr\u0131l\u0131k biter, kavu\u015fma ba\u015flar.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"teslimiyet",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Our death is our wedding night; for separation ends and reunion begins.",categoryEn:"surrender",textDe:"Unser Tod ist unsere Hochzeitsnacht; denn die Trennung endet und die Wiedervereinigung beginnt.",categoryDe:"Hingabe",textEs:"Nuestra muerte es nuestra noche de bodas; pues la separaci\xf3n termina y comienza el reencuentro.",categoryEs:"entrega",textPt:"A nossa morte \xe9 a nossa noite de n\xfapcias; pois a separa\xe7\xe3o termina e o reencontro come\xe7a.",categoryPt:"entrega",textFr:"Notre mort est notre nuit de noces ; car la s\xe9paration finit et les retrouvailles commencent.",categoryFr:"abandon",textJa:"\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306e\u6b7b\u306f\u3001\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306e\u5a5a\u793c\u306e\u591c\u3060\u3002\u5225\u96e2\u304c\u7d42\u308f\u308a\u3001\u518d\u4f1a\u304c\u59cb\u307e\u308b\u306e\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3002",categoryJa:"\u660e\u3051\u6e21\u3057"},{id:"q177",text:"Dost, g\xf6nl\xfcn hekimidir; derdini ondan saklama.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"dostluk",rarity:"common",textEn:"A friend is the physician of the heart; do not hide your sorrow from them.",categoryEn:"friendship",textDe:"Ein Freund ist der Arzt des Herzens; verbirg deinen Kummer nicht vor ihm.",categoryDe:"Freundschaft",textEs:"Un amigo es el m\xe9dico del coraz\xf3n; no le ocultes tu pena.",categoryEs:"amistad",textPt:"Um amigo \xe9 o m\xe9dico do cora\xe7\xe3o; n\xe3o lhe escondas a tua tristeza.",categoryPt:"amizade",textFr:"Un ami est le m\xe9decin du c\u0153ur ; ne lui cache pas ton chagrin.",categoryFr:"amiti\xe9",textJa:"\u53cb\u306f\u5fc3\u306e\u533b\u8005\u3060\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u3092\u5f7c\u304b\u3089\u96a0\u3059\u306a\u3002",categoryJa:"\u53cb\u60c5"},{id:"q178",text:"S\xf6z\xfcn g\xfcm\xfc\u015fse, susman alt\u0131nd\u0131r; ama yerinde s\xf6z, inci gibidir.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hikmet",rarity:"common",textEn:"If your speech is silver, your silence is gold; yet a word in its proper place is like a pearl.",categoryEn:"wisdom",textDe:"Ist deine Rede Silber, so ist dein Schweigen Gold; doch ein Wort am rechten Ort ist wie eine Perle.",categoryDe:"Weisheit",textEs:"Si tu palabra es plata, tu silencio es oro; pero una palabra en su justo lugar es como una perla.",categoryEs:"sabidur\xeda",textPt:"Se a tua fala \xe9 prata, o teu sil\xeancio \xe9 ouro; mas uma palavra no seu devido lugar \xe9 como uma p\xe9rola.",categoryPt:"sabedoria",textFr:"Si ta parole est d'argent, ton silence est d'or ; mais un mot \xe0 sa juste place est comme une perle.",categoryFr:"sagesse",textJa:"\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u304c\u9280\u306a\u3089\u3001\u6c88\u9ed9\u306f\u91d1\u3060\u3002\u3060\u304c\u3001\u3075\u3055\u308f\u3057\u3044\u5834\u6240\u306b\u7f6e\u304b\u308c\u305f\u4e00\u8a00\u306f\u771f\u73e0\u306e\u3088\u3046\u3060\u3002",categoryJa:"\u77e5\u6075"},{id:"q179",text:"Korkma; sana ula\u015fmas\u0131 gereken \u015fey, ba\u015fkas\u0131na gitmez.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"teslimiyet",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Do not fear; what is meant to reach you will not go to another.",categoryEn:"surrender",textDe:"F\xfcrchte dich nicht; was dich erreichen soll, geht nicht zu einem anderen.",categoryDe:"Hingabe",textEs:"No temas; lo que ha de llegarte no ir\xe1 a otro.",categoryEs:"entrega",textPt:"N\xe3o temas; o que te h\xe1 de chegar n\xe3o ir\xe1 para outro.",categoryPt:"entrega",textFr:"Ne crains pas ; ce qui doit te parvenir n'ira pas \xe0 un autre.",categoryFr:"abandon",textJa:"\u6050\u308c\u308b\u306a\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306b\u5c4a\u304f\u3079\u304d\u3082\u306e\u306f\u3001\u4ed6\u306e\u8005\u306e\u3068\u3053\u308d\u3078\u306f\u884c\u304b\u306a\u3044\u3002",categoryJa:"\u660e\u3051\u6e21\u3057"},{id:"q180",text:"Hak, kalpleri s\u0131nar; sabredenin kalbi alt\u0131n gibi parlar \xe7\u0131kar.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"sabir",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The Truth tests hearts; the heart of the patient one comes forth shining like gold.",categoryEn:"patience",textDe:"Die Wahrheit pr\xfcft die Herzen; das Herz des Geduldigen geht hervor und gl\xe4nzt wie Gold.",categoryDe:"Geduld",textEs:"La Verdad pone a prueba los corazones; el coraz\xf3n del paciente sale reluciente como el oro.",categoryEs:"paciencia",textPt:"A Verdade p\xf5e os cora\xe7\xf5es \xe0 prova; o cora\xe7\xe3o do paciente sai reluzente como o ouro.",categoryPt:"paci\xeancia",textFr:"La V\xe9rit\xe9 \xe9prouve les c\u0153urs ; le c\u0153ur du patient en ressort brillant comme l'or.",categoryFr:"patience",textJa:"\u771f\u5b9f\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u8a66\u3059\u3002\u5fcd\u8010\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u3001\u91d1\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u8f1d\u3044\u3066\u73fe\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u5fcd\u8010"},{id:"q181",text:"A\u015fk davas\u0131 kolay s\xf6ylenir; ama onun kan\u0131t\u0131, \xe7ekilen cefada belli olur.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"ask",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"The claim of love is easily spoken; but its proof appears in the hardship one endures.",categoryEn:"love",textDe:"Den Anspruch auf Liebe spricht man leicht aus; doch ihr Beweis zeigt sich in der H\xe4rte, die man ertr\xe4gt.",categoryDe:"Liebe",textEs:"La pretensi\xf3n del amor se dice con facilidad; pero su prueba aparece en la dureza que uno soporta.",categoryEs:"amor",textPt:"A pretens\xe3o do amor diz-se com facilidade; mas a sua prova aparece na dureza que se suporta.",categoryPt:"amor",textFr:"Pr\xe9tendre \xe0 l'amour se dit ais\xe9ment ; mais sa preuve appara\xeet dans l'\xe9preuve que l'on endure.",categoryFr:"amour",textJa:"\u611b\u3092\u4e3b\u5f35\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u305f\u3084\u3059\u3044\u3002\u3060\u304c\u305d\u306e\u8a3c\u306f\u3001\u8010\u3048\u5fcd\u3076\u82e6\u96e3\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u73fe\u308c\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u611b"},{id:"q182",text:"Susuzluk suyu arar; ama su da susuzlar\u0131 arar.",original:"\u0646\u0647 \u062a\u0646\u0647\u0627 \u062a\u0634\u0646\u0647 \u0631\u0627 \u0622\u0628 \u0622\u0631\u0632\u0648 \u0634\u062f / \u06a9\u0647 \u0622\u0628 \u0627\u0632 \u0648\u06cc \u0646\u0647\u0627\u0646 \u062c\u0648\u06cc\u0646\u062f\u0647 \u0627\u0648 \u0634\u062f",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"hasret",rarity:"rare",textEn:"Not only does the thirsty seek the water; the water too, unseen, seeks the thirsty.",categoryEn:"longing",textDe:"Nicht nur der Durstige sucht das Wasser; auch das Wasser sucht, ungesehen, den Durstigen.",categoryDe:"Sehnsucht",textEs:"No solo el sediento busca el agua; el agua tambi\xe9n, sin que se vea, busca al sediento.",categoryEs:"a\xf1oranza",textPt:"N\xe3o s\xf3 o sedento procura a \xe1gua; a \xe1gua tamb\xe9m, sem que se veja, procura o sedento.",categoryPt:"saudade",textFr:"Non seulement l'assoiff\xe9 cherche l'eau ; l'eau aussi, invisible, cherche l'assoiff\xe9.",categoryFr:"nostalgie",textJa:"\u6e07\u3044\u305f\u8005\u304c\u6c34\u3092\u6c42\u3081\u308b\u3060\u3051\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002\u6c34\u3082\u307e\u305f\u3001\u898b\u3048\u306c\u3068\u3053\u308d\u3067\u6e07\u3044\u305f\u8005\u3092\u6c42\u3081\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u61a7\u308c"},{id:"q183",text:"Bir kap\u0131 kapan\u0131r, ba\u015fkas\u0131 a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r; karanl\u0131\u011fa de\u011fil a\xe7\u0131lan kap\u0131ya bak.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"kabul",rarity:"common",textEn:"One door closes, another opens; look not at the darkness but at the opening door.",categoryEn:"acceptance",textDe:"Eine T\xfcr schlie\xdft sich, eine andere \xf6ffnet sich; schau nicht auf das Dunkel, sondern auf die sich \xf6ffnende T\xfcr.",categoryDe:"Annahme",textEs:"Una puerta se cierra, otra se abre; no mires la oscuridad, sino la puerta que se abre.",categoryEs:"aceptaci\xf3n",textPt:"Uma porta fecha-se, outra abre-se; n\xe3o olhes para a escurid\xe3o, mas para a porta que se abre.",categoryPt:"aceita\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Une porte se ferme, une autre s'ouvre ; ne regarde pas l'obscurit\xe9 mais la porte qui s'ouvre.",categoryFr:"acceptation",textJa:"\u4e00\u3064\u306e\u6249\u304c\u9589\u3058\u308c\u3070\u3001\u3082\u3046\u4e00\u3064\u304c\u958b\u304f\u3002\u95c7\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u958b\u304d\u3086\u304f\u6249\u3092\u898b\u3088\u3002",categoryJa:"\u53d7\u5bb9"},{id:"q184",text:"Geceyi su\xe7lama; y\u0131ld\u0131zlar ancak karanl\u0131kta g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr.",original:"",source:"Mevlana Rumi",category:"kabul",rarity:"uncommon",textEn:"Do not blame the night; the stars become visible only in the dark.",categoryEn:"acceptance",textDe:"Tadle nicht die Nacht; die Sterne werden nur im Dunkel sichtbar.",categoryDe:"Annahme",textEs:"No culpes a la noche; las estrellas solo se hacen visibles en lo oscuro.",categoryEs:"aceptaci\xf3n",textPt:"N\xe3o culpes a noite; as estrelas s\xf3 se tornam vis\xedveis no escuro.",categoryPt:"aceita\xe7\xe3o",textFr:"Ne bl\xe2me pas la nuit ; les \xe9toiles ne deviennent visibles que dans l'obscurit\xe9.",categoryFr:"acceptation",textJa:"\u591c\u3092\u8cac\u3081\u308b\u306a\u3002\u661f\u306f\u95c7\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u3053\u305d\u898b\u3048\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3002",categoryJa:"\u53d7\u5bb9"}]},730,[]);
__d(function(e,a,n,i,r,o,s){r.exports=[{id:"plant-001",emoji:"\ud83d\udc9c",color:"#7C6BAE",name:"Lavanta",nameEn:"Lavender",nameDe:"Lavendel",nameEs:"Lavanda",nameFr:"Lavande",nameJa:"\u30e9\u30d9\u30f3\u30c0\u30fc",namePt:"Lavanda",origin:"Akdeniz havzas\u0131",originEn:"Mediterranean basin",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Cuenca mediterr\xe1nea",originFr:"Bassin m\xe9diterran\xe9en",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u6cbf\u5cb8",originPt:"Bacia do Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["sakinle\u015ftirici","uyku getirici","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["calming","sleep-inducing","purifying"],propertiesDe:["beruhigend","schlaff\xf6rdernd","reinigend"],propertiesEs:["calmante","inductor del sue\xf1o","purificante"],propertiesFr:["apaisant","favorise le sommeil","purifiant"],propertiesJa:["\u93ae\u9759","\u5b89\u7720","\u6d44\u5316"],propertiesPt:["calmante","indutor do sono","purificante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn nefesini yava\u015flat ve omuzlar\u0131n\u0131 gev\u015fet. Lavanta sana aceleye gerek olmad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131, huzurun zaten i\xe7inde oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, slow your breath and let your shoulders soften. Lavender reminds you there is no need to rush; peace already lives within you.",dailyMessageDe:"Verlangsame heute deinen Atem und lass deine Schultern weich werden. Lavendel erinnert dich daran, dass keine Eile n\xf6tig ist; der Friede wohnt bereits in dir.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, calma tu respiraci\xf3n y deja que tus hombros se relajen. La lavanda te recuerda que no hay prisa; la paz ya vive en ti.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ralentis ton souffle et laisse tes \xe9paules se d\xe9tendre. La lavande te rappelle qu'il n'y a pas d'urgence ; la paix habite d\xe9j\xe0 en toi.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u547c\u5438\u3092\u3086\u308b\u3081\u3001\u80a9\u306e\u529b\u3092\u629c\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30e9\u30d9\u30f3\u30c0\u30fc\u306f\u3001\u6025\u3050\u5fc5\u8981\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u306f\u3059\u3067\u306b\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, desacelere a respira\xe7\xe3o e deixe os ombros relaxarem. A lavanda lembra voc\xea de que n\xe3o h\xe1 pressa; a paz j\xe1 vive dentro de voc\xea.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f \xe7i\xe7eklerini s\u0131cak suda demleyip uyumadan \xf6nce i\xe7 ya da birka\xe7 damla esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 yast\u0131\u011f\u0131na damlat. Banyo suyuna bir avu\xe7 \xe7i\xe7ek ekleyerek rahatla.",howToUseEn:"Brew the dried flowers in hot water before bed, or drip a few drops of essential oil onto your pillow. Add a handful of flowers to your bath to unwind.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die getrockneten Bl\xfcten vor dem Schlafen in hei\xdfem Wasser auf oder gib ein paar Tropfen \xe4therisches \xd6l auf dein Kissen. F\xfcge eine Handvoll Bl\xfcten ins Bad, um zu entspannen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las flores secas en agua caliente antes de dormir, o pon unas gotas de aceite esencial en tu almohada. A\xf1ade un pu\xf1ado de flores al ba\xf1o para relajarte.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fleurs s\xe9ch\xe9es dans de l'eau chaude avant le coucher, ou verse quelques gouttes d'huile essentielle sur ton oreiller. Ajoute une poign\xe9e de fleurs \xe0 ton bain pour te d\xe9tendre.",howToUseJa:"\u5c31\u5bdd\u524d\u306b\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u82b1\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u6795\u306b\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u6570\u6ef4\u5782\u3089\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u6e6f\u8239\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u308b\u3068\u304f\u3064\u308d\u3052\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores secas em \xe1gua quente antes de dormir, ou pingue algumas gotas de \xf3leo essencial no travesseiro. Adicione um punhado de flores ao banho para relaxar.",affirmation:"Huzur i\xe7inde nefes al\u0131yorum, sakinlik benim do\u011fal halim.",affirmationEn:"I breathe in peace; calm is my natural state.",affirmationDe:"Ich atme Frieden ein; Ruhe ist mein nat\xfcrlicher Zustand.",affirmationEs:"Respiro paz; la calma es mi estado natural.",affirmationFr:"J'inspire la paix ; le calme est mon \xe9tat naturel.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u5438\u3044\u8fbc\u3080\u3002\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u3055\u306f\u79c1\u306e\u81ea\u7136\u306a\u72b6\u614b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Eu respiro paz; a calma \xe9 o meu estado natural.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Single_lavender_flower02.jpg/330px-Single_lavender_flower02.jpg",myth:"Lavanta, s\xfck\xfbnetin mor nefesidir. Ad\u0131 Latince 'y\u0131kamak'tan gelir; antik \xe7a\u011fda hamamlarda ve \u015fifahanelerde ar\u0131nma i\xe7in kullan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Anadolu'nun g\xfcne\u015fli yama\xe7lar\u0131nda yeti\u015fen lavanta uykuyu \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131r, kayg\u0131y\u0131 dindirir, zihni berrakla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131r. Yast\u0131k alt\u0131na konan demeti huzurlu r\xfcyalar getirir; yak\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda mek\xe2n\u0131 k\xf6t\xfc enerjiden ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131r. Kokusu sinir sistemini yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131ran, g\xf6nl\xfc geni\u015fleten bir duad\u0131r. Kuruyunca bile kokusunu y\u0131llarca koruyan \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi, sabr\u0131n ve kal\u0131c\u0131 dinginli\u011fin dersidir.",mythEn:"Lavender is the violet breath of serenity. Its name comes from the Latin for 'to wash'; in antiquity it was used for purification in baths and houses of healing. Growing on Anatolia's sunlit slopes, lavender calls in sleep, soothes anxiety and clears the mind. A sprig placed under the pillow brings peaceful dreams; burned, it cleanses a space of ill energy. Its scent is a prayer that calms the nervous system and widens the heart. Its flower, keeping its fragrance for years even when dried, is the lesson of patience and lasting calm.",mythDe:"Lavendel ist der violette Atem der Gelassenheit. Sein Name kommt vom lateinischen 'waschen'; in der Antike diente er in B\xe4dern und Heilh\xe4usern zur Reinigung. An den sonnigen H\xe4ngen Anatoliens gewachsen, ruft Lavendel den Schlaf herbei, lindert Angst und kl\xe4rt den Geist. Ein unter das Kissen gelegtes Str\xe4u\xdfchen bringt friedliche Tr\xe4ume; verbrannt reinigt es einen Raum von schlechter Energie. Sein Duft ist ein Gebet, das das Nervensystem beruhigt und das Herz weitet. Seine Bl\xfcte, die selbst getrocknet jahrelang ihren Duft bewahrt, lehrt Geduld und dauerhafte Ruhe.",mythEs:"La lavanda es el aliento violeta de la serenidad. Su nombre viene del lat\xedn 'lavar'; en la antig\xfcedad se usaba para la purificaci\xf3n en ba\xf1os y casas de sanaci\xf3n. Crecida en las laderas soleadas de Anatolia, la lavanda llama al sue\xf1o, calma la ansiedad y aclara la mente. Un ramillete bajo la almohada trae sue\xf1os apacibles; quemada, limpia un espacio de mala energ\xeda. Su aroma es una oraci\xf3n que serena el sistema nervioso y ensancha el coraz\xf3n. Su flor, que conserva su fragancia durante a\xf1os aun seca, ense\xf1a la paciencia y la calma duradera.",mythFr:"La lavande est le souffle violet de la s\xe9r\xe9nit\xe9. Son nom vient du latin 'laver' ; dans l'Antiquit\xe9, elle servait \xe0 la purification dans les bains et les maisons de soin. Poussant sur les pentes ensoleill\xe9es de l'Anatolie, la lavande appelle le sommeil, apaise l'anxi\xe9t\xe9 et \xe9claircit l'esprit. Un brin gliss\xe9 sous l'oreiller apporte des r\xeaves paisibles ; br\xfbl\xe9e, elle purifie un lieu de l'\xe9nergie n\xe9faste. Son parfum est une pri\xe8re qui calme le syst\xe8me nerveux et \xe9largit le c\u0153ur. Sa fleur, qui garde son parfum des ann\xe9es m\xeame s\xe9ch\xe9e, enseigne la patience et le calme durable.",mythJa:"\u30e9\u30d9\u30f3\u30c0\u30fc\u306f\u9759\u3051\u3055\u306e\u7d2b\u306e\u606f\u5439\u3002\u305d\u306e\u540d\u306f\u30e9\u30c6\u30f3\u8a9e\u306e\u300c\u6d17\u3046\u300d\u306b\u7531\u6765\u3057\u3001\u53e4\u4ee3\u306b\u306f\u6d74\u5834\u3084\u7652\u3057\u306e\u9928\u3067\u6d44\u5316\u306b\u7528\u3044\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u967d\u3042\u305f\u308b\u659c\u9762\u306b\u80b2\u3064\u30e9\u30d9\u30f3\u30c0\u30fc\u306f\u3001\u7720\u308a\u3092\u62db\u304d\u3001\u4e0d\u5b89\u3092\u548c\u3089\u3052\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u6f84\u307e\u305b\u308b\u3002\u6795\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u7f6e\u3044\u305f\u4e00\u679d\u306f\u5b89\u3089\u304b\u306a\u5922\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3057\u3001\u711a\u3051\u3070\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u60aa\u3044\u6c17\u304b\u3089\u6e05\u3081\u308b\u3002\u305d\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306f\u795e\u7d4c\u3092\u93ae\u3081\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u5e83\u3052\u308b\u7948\u308a\u3002\u4e7e\u3044\u3066\u3082\u306a\u304a\u4f55\u5e74\u3082\u9999\u308a\u3092\u4fdd\u3064\u82b1\u306f\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u6c38\u304f\u7d9a\u304f\u9759\u3051\u3055\u306e\u6559\u3048\u3002",mythPt:"A lavanda \xe9 o sopro violeta da serenidade. O seu nome vem do latim 'lavar'; na antiguidade era usada para a purifica\xe7\xe3o em banhos e casas de cura. Crescida nas encostas soalheiras da Anat\xf3lia, a lavanda chama o sono, acalma a ansiedade e clareia a mente. Um raminho sob a almofada traz sonhos serenos; queimada, limpa um espa\xe7o da m\xe1 energia. O seu aroma \xe9 uma ora\xe7\xe3o que serena o sistema nervoso e alarga o cora\xe7\xe3o. A sua flor, que guarda o perfume por anos mesmo seca, ensina a paci\xeancia e a calma duradoura."},{id:"plant-002",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#8AA67B",name:"Ada\xe7ay\u0131",nameEn:"Sage",nameDe:"Salbei",nameEs:"Salvia",nameFr:"Sauge",nameJa:"\u30bb\u30fc\u30b8",namePt:"S\xe1lvia",origin:"Akdeniz",originEn:"Mediterranean",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u5730\u57df",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Lar\xedngeo",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","bilgelik","koruma"],propertiesEn:["purifying","wisdom","protection"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","Weisheit","Schutz"],propertiesEs:["purificante","sabidur\xeda","protecci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","sagesse","protection"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u77e5\u6075","\u5b88\u8b77"],propertiesPt:["purificante","sabedoria","prote\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn art\u0131k sana hizmet etmeyen d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceleri b\u0131rak. Ada\xe7ay\u0131 zihnini ve mek\xe2n\u0131n\u0131 temizler, yeni bir ba\u015flang\u0131ca alan a\xe7ar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, release the thoughts that no longer serve you. Sage cleanses your mind and space, making room for a fresh beginning.",dailyMessageDe:"Lass heute die Gedanken los, die dir nicht mehr dienen. Salbei reinigt deinen Geist und Raum und schafft Platz f\xfcr einen Neuanfang.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, suelta los pensamientos que ya no te sirven. La salvia limpia tu mente y tu espacio, dando lugar a un nuevo comienzo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, lib\xe8re les pens\xe9es qui ne te servent plus. La sauge purifie ton esprit et ton espace, faisant place \xe0 un nouveau d\xe9part.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3082\u3046\u5f79\u7acb\u305f\u306a\u3044\u601d\u3044\u3092\u624b\u653e\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30bb\u30fc\u30b8\u306f\u5fc3\u3068\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u3001\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u59cb\u307e\u308a\u3078\u306e\u4f59\u767d\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, solte os pensamentos que j\xe1 n\xe3o servem a voc\xea. A s\xe1lvia limpa sua mente e seu espa\xe7o, abrindo lugar para um novo come\xe7o.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f demetini t\xfcts\xfcleyerek odan\u0131 ar\u0131nd\u0131r ya da yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle. Bo\u011faz a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131nda \u0131l\u0131k suyla gargara yapabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Smudge the dried bundle to purify your room, or lightly brew the leaves as a tea. Gargle with the warm infusion for a sore throat.",howToUseDe:"R\xe4uchere das getrocknete B\xfcndel, um deinen Raum zu reinigen, oder br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter leicht als Tee. Gurgle bei Halsschmerzen mit dem warmen Aufguss.",howToUseEs:"Quema el manojo seco para purificar tu habitaci\xf3n, o prepara ligeramente las hojas como t\xe9. Haz g\xe1rgaras con la infusi\xf3n tibia para el dolor de garganta.",howToUseFr:"Fais br\xfbler le bouquet s\xe9ch\xe9 pour purifier ta pi\xe8ce, ou infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les feuilles en tisane. Gargarise avec l'infusion ti\xe8de en cas de mal de gorge.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u675f\u3092\u711a\u3044\u3066\u90e8\u5c4b\u3092\u6d44\u5316\u3059\u308b\u304b\u3001\u8449\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5589\u306e\u75db\u307f\u306b\u306f\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u714e\u3058\u6db2\u3067\u3046\u304c\u3044\u3092\u3002",howToUsePt:"Defume o ma\xe7o seco para purificar seu ambiente, ou prepare levemente as folhas como ch\xe1. Gargareje com a infus\xe3o morna para dor de garganta.",affirmation:"Ge\xe7mi\u015fi b\u0131rak\u0131yorum, i\xe7imdeki bilgeli\u011fe g\xfcveniyorum.",affirmationEn:"I release the past and trust the wisdom within me.",affirmationDe:"Ich lasse die Vergangenheit los und vertraue der Weisheit in mir.",affirmationEs:"Suelto el pasado y conf\xedo en la sabidur\xeda que hay en m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Je lib\xe8re le pass\xe9 et fais confiance \xe0 la sagesse en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u904e\u53bb\u3092\u624b\u653e\u3057\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u77e5\u6075\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3059\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Eu solto o passado e confio na sabedoria dentro de mim.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Salvia_officinalis0.jpg/330px-Salvia_officinalis0.jpg",myth:"Ada\xe7ay\u0131, ad\u0131n\u0131 Latince 'salvare' \u2014 kurtarmak, iyile\u015ftirmek \u2014 k\xf6k\xfcnden alan kutsal \u015fifa otudur. Anadolu'da y\xfczy\u0131llard\u0131r bo\u011faz a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131ndan zihinsel berrakl\u0131\u011fa dek her derde demlenir. Yak\u0131lan ada\xe7ay\u0131 duman\u0131 mek\xe2n\u0131 ve ki\u015fiyi k\xf6t\xfc enerjiden, nazardan ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131r \u2014 k\xf6y odalar\u0131ndan t\xfcrbelere dek s\xfcregelen bir gelenektir. Bilgeli\u011fin, uzun \xf6mr\xfcn ve koruyucu ar\u0131nman\u0131n otudur; 'ada\xe7ay\u0131 yeti\u015ftiren bah\xe7ede \xf6l\xfcm bar\u0131nmaz' denirdi. G\xfcm\xfc\u015fi yapra\u011f\u0131, s\xf6z\xfcn ve niyetin temizlenmesini hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",mythEn:"Sage is the sacred healing herb whose name comes from the Latin 'salvare' \u2014 to save, to heal. In Anatolia it has been brewed for centuries for everything from a sore throat to mental clarity. The smoke of burning sage cleanses a space and a person of ill energy and the evil eye \u2014 a tradition carried from village rooms to shrines. It is the herb of wisdom, long life and protective purification; it was said that 'death does not dwell in a garden where sage grows.' Its silvery leaf reminds us to cleanse our word and our intention.",mythDe:"Salbei ist das heilige Heilkraut, dessen Name vom lateinischen 'salvare' \u2014 retten, heilen \u2014 stammt. In Anatolien wird er seit Jahrhunderten f\xfcr alles aufgebr\xfcht, von Halsschmerzen bis zu geistiger Klarheit. Der Rauch brennenden Salbeis reinigt einen Raum und einen Menschen von schlechter Energie und dem b\xf6sen Blick \u2014 eine Tradition, die von Dorfstuben bis zu Schreinen reicht. Er ist das Kraut der Weisheit, des langen Lebens und der sch\xfctzenden Reinigung; man sagte: 'In einem Garten, in dem Salbei w\xe4chst, wohnt der Tod nicht.' Sein silbriges Blatt mahnt, unser Wort und unsere Absicht zu reinigen.",mythEs:"La salvia es la hierba sagrada de la sanaci\xf3n, cuyo nombre viene del lat\xedn 'salvare' \u2014 salvar, sanar. En Anatolia se ha preparado durante siglos para todo, desde el dolor de garganta hasta la claridad mental. El humo de la salvia quemada limpia un espacio y a la persona de la mala energ\xeda y el mal de ojo \u2014 una tradici\xf3n que va de las salas de aldea a los santuarios. Es la hierba de la sabidur\xeda, la larga vida y la purificaci\xf3n protectora; se dec\xeda que 'la muerte no habita en un jard\xedn donde crece la salvia.' Su hoja plateada nos recuerda purificar nuestra palabra y nuestra intenci\xf3n.",mythFr:"La sauge est l'herbe sacr\xe9e de la gu\xe9rison, dont le nom vient du latin 'salvare' \u2014 sauver, gu\xe9rir. En Anatolie, on l'infuse depuis des si\xe8cles pour tout, du mal de gorge \xe0 la clart\xe9 de l'esprit. La fum\xe9e de la sauge br\xfbl\xe9e purifie un lieu et une personne de l'\xe9nergie n\xe9faste et du mauvais \u0153il \u2014 tradition qui va des chambres villageoises aux sanctuaires. C'est l'herbe de la sagesse, de la longue vie et de la purification protectrice ; on disait que 'la mort n'habite pas un jardin o\xf9 pousse la sauge.' Sa feuille argent\xe9e nous rappelle de purifier notre parole et notre intention.",mythJa:"\u30bb\u30fc\u30b8\u306f\u300c\u6551\u3046\u30fb\u7652\u3059\u300d\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3059\u308b\u30e9\u30c6\u30f3\u8a9e salvare \u306b\u540d\u3092\u6301\u3064\u8056\u306a\u308b\u85ac\u8349\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u4f55\u4e16\u7d00\u3082\u306e\u9593\u3001\u5589\u306e\u75db\u307f\u304b\u3089\u5fc3\u306e\u660e\u6670\u3055\u307e\u3067\u3001\u3042\u3089\u3086\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6df9\u308c\u3089\u308c\u3066\u304d\u305f\u3002\u71c3\u3084\u3059\u30bb\u30fc\u30b8\u306e\u7159\u306f\u3001\u7a7a\u9593\u3068\u4eba\u3092\u60aa\u3044\u6c17\u3084\u90aa\u8996\u304b\u3089\u6e05\u3081\u308b\u2014\u2014\u6751\u306e\u90e8\u5c4b\u304b\u3089\u8056\u5edf\u307e\u3067\u53d7\u3051\u7d99\u304c\u308c\u308b\u7fd2\u308f\u3057\u3002\u53e1\u667a\u3068\u9577\u5bff\u3001\u5b88\u308a\u306e\u6d44\u5316\u306e\u8349\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u300c\u30bb\u30fc\u30b8\u306e\u80b2\u3064\u5ead\u306b\u6b7b\u306f\u5bbf\u3089\u306c\u300d\u3068\u8a00\u308f\u308c\u305f\u3002\u9280\u8272\u306e\u8449\u306f\u3001\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u3068\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u308b\u3002",mythPt:"A s\xe1lvia \xe9 a erva sagrada da cura, cujo nome vem do latim 'salvare' \u2014 salvar, curar. Na Anat\xf3lia, \xe9 preparada h\xe1 s\xe9culos para tudo, da dor de garganta \xe0 clareza mental. O fumo da s\xe1lvia queimada limpa um espa\xe7o e a pessoa da m\xe1 energia e do mau-olhado \u2014 uma tradi\xe7\xe3o que vai das salas de aldeia aos santu\xe1rios. \xc9 a erva da sabedoria, da longa vida e da purifica\xe7\xe3o protetora; dizia-se que 'a morte n\xe3o habita um jardim onde cresce a s\xe1lvia.' A sua folha prateada lembra-nos de purificar a nossa palavra e a nossa inten\xe7\xe3o."},{id:"plant-003",emoji:"\ud83c\udf31",color:"#5C8A4A",name:"Biberiye",nameEn:"Rosemary",nameDe:"Rosmarin",nameEs:"Romero",nameFr:"Romarin",nameJa:"\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30de\u30ea\u30fc",namePt:"Alecrim",origin:"Akdeniz k\u0131y\u0131lar\u0131",originEn:"Mediterranean coast",originDe:"Mittelmeerk\xfcste",originEs:"Costa mediterr\xe1nea",originFr:"C\xf4tes m\xe9diterran\xe9ennes",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u6cbf\u5cb8",originPt:"Costa do Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["haf\u0131za","odaklanma","canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["memory","focus","invigorating"],propertiesDe:["Ged\xe4chtnis","Konzentration","belebend"],propertiesEs:["memoria","concentraci\xf3n","vigorizante"],propertiesFr:["m\xe9moire","concentration","tonifiant"],propertiesJa:["\u8a18\u61b6","\u96c6\u4e2d","\u6d3b\u6027"],propertiesPt:["mem\xf3ria","foco","revigorante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn zihnini berrakla\u015ft\u0131r ve niyetini hat\u0131rla. Biberiye haf\u0131zan\u0131 bileyler, dikkatini \xf6nemli olana y\xf6neltmene yard\u0131m eder.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, clear your mind and remember your intention. Rosemary sharpens your memory and helps you turn your attention to what matters.",dailyMessageDe:"Kl\xe4re heute deinen Geist und erinnere dich an deine Absicht. Rosmarin sch\xe4rft dein Ged\xe4chtnis und hilft dir, deine Aufmerksamkeit auf das Wesentliche zu richten.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, aclara tu mente y recuerda tu intenci\xf3n. El romero agudiza tu memoria y te ayuda a dirigir tu atenci\xf3n a lo que importa.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, clarifie ton esprit et souviens-toi de ton intention. Le romarin aiguise ta m\xe9moire et t'aide \xe0 porter ton attention sur l'essentiel.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u6f84\u307e\u305b\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30de\u30ea\u30fc\u306f\u8a18\u61b6\u3092\u7814\u304e\u6f84\u307e\u3057\u3001\u5927\u5207\u306a\u3053\u3068\u306b\u6ce8\u610f\u3092\u5411\u3051\u308b\u624b\u52a9\u3051\u3092\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, clareie a mente e lembre-se da sua inten\xe7\xe3o. O alecrim agu\xe7a a mem\xf3ria e ajuda voc\xea a voltar a aten\xe7\xe3o para o que importa.",howToUse:"Taze dal\u0131n\u0131 \xe7al\u0131\u015fma masan\u0131n yan\u0131nda bulundur ya da \xe7ay\u0131n\u0131 demleyip i\xe7erek zihnini canland\u0131r. Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 \u015fakaklar\u0131na nazik\xe7e s\xfcr.",howToUseEn:"Keep a fresh sprig near your desk, or brew it as a tea to invigorate your mind. Gently massage the essential oil into your temples.",howToUseDe:"Halte einen frischen Zweig auf deinem Schreibtisch bereit oder br\xfche ihn als Tee, um deinen Geist zu beleben. Massiere das \xe4therische \xd6l sanft in deine Schl\xe4fen ein.",howToUseEs:"Ten una ramita fresca cerca de tu escritorio, o prep\xe1rala como t\xe9 para vigorizar tu mente. Masajea suavemente el aceite esencial en tus sienes.",howToUseFr:"Garde un brin frais pr\xe8s de ton bureau, ou infuse-le en tisane pour stimuler ton esprit. Masse doucement l'huile essentielle sur tes tempes.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u679d\u3092\u673a\u306e\u305d\u3070\u306b\u7f6e\u304f\u304b\u3001\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3066\u5fc3\u3092\u6d3b\u6027\u5316\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u3053\u3081\u304b\u307f\u306b\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5857\u308a\u8fbc\u307f\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Mantenha um raminho fresco perto da sua mesa, ou prepare-o como ch\xe1 para revigorar a mente. Massageie suavemente o \xf3leo essencial nas t\xeamporas.",affirmation:"Zihnim a\xe7\u0131k ve net, niyetimi hat\u0131rl\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"My mind is clear and sharp; I remember my intention.",affirmationDe:"Mein Geist ist klar und scharf; ich erinnere mich an meine Absicht.",affirmationEs:"Mi mente est\xe1 clara y aguda; recuerdo mi intenci\xf3n.",affirmationFr:"Mon esprit est clair et vif ; je me souviens de mon intention.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u6f84\u3093\u3067\u92ed\u3044\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3059\u3002",affirmationPt:"Minha mente est\xe1 clara e afiada; eu lembro da minha inten\xe7\xe3o.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Rosemary_in_bloom.JPG/330px-Rosemary_in_bloom.JPG",myth:"Biberiye, hat\u0131ran\u0131n ve sadakatin otudur. 'Biberiye unutmamak i\xe7indir' denir; Akdeniz'de hem d\xfc\u011f\xfcnlerde hem cenazelerde dal olarak ta\u015f\u0131n\u0131r \u2014 hat\u0131rlanman\u0131n simgesi. Antik \xe7a\u011fda Afrodit'in \xf6rt\xfcs\xfcnden do\u011fdu\u011funa inan\u0131l\u0131r; \xf6\u011frencilere haf\u0131zay\u0131 keskinle\u015ftirmesi i\xe7in tak\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Anadolu'da koruma ve ar\u0131nma i\xe7in yak\u0131l\u0131r; kokusu zihni uyand\u0131r\u0131r, niyeti g\xfc\xe7lendirir.",mythEn:"Rosemary is the herb of memory and faithfulness. 'Rosemary is for remembrance,' it is said; in the Mediterranean a sprig is carried at both weddings and funerals \u2014 an emblem of being remembered. In antiquity it was believed born of Aphrodite's mantle; students wore it to sharpen memory. In Anatolia it is burned for protection and purification; its scent wakes the mind and strengthens intention.",mythDe:"Rosmarin ist das Kraut der Erinnerung und Treue. 'Rosmarin ist zum Gedenken', hei\xdft es; im Mittelmeerraum tr\xe4gt man einen Zweig sowohl bei Hochzeiten als auch bei Begr\xe4bnissen \u2014 ein Sinnbild des Erinnertwerdens. In der Antike glaubte man, er sei aus dem Mantel der Aphrodite entstanden; Sch\xfcler trugen ihn, um das Ged\xe4chtnis zu sch\xe4rfen. In Anatolien wird er zum Schutz und zur Reinigung verbrannt; sein Duft weckt den Geist und st\xe4rkt die Absicht.",mythEs:"El romero es la hierba de la memoria y la fidelidad. 'El romero es para el recuerdo', se dice; en el Mediterr\xe1neo se lleva una ramita tanto en bodas como en funerales \u2014 emblema de ser recordado. En la antig\xfcedad se cre\xeda nacido del manto de Afrodita; los estudiantes lo llevaban para agudizar la memoria. En Anatolia se quema para la protecci\xf3n y la purificaci\xf3n; su aroma despierta la mente y fortalece la intenci\xf3n.",mythFr:"Le romarin est l'herbe de la m\xe9moire et de la fid\xe9lit\xe9. 'Le romarin est pour le souvenir', dit-on ; en M\xe9diterran\xe9e, on en porte un brin aux mariages comme aux fun\xe9railles \u2014 embl\xe8me d'\xeatre gard\xe9 en m\xe9moire. Dans l'Antiquit\xe9, on le croyait n\xe9 du manteau d'Aphrodite ; les \xe9tudiants en portaient pour aiguiser la m\xe9moire. En Anatolie, on le br\xfble pour la protection et la purification ; son parfum \xe9veille l'esprit et renforce l'intention.",mythJa:"\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30de\u30ea\u30fc\u306f\u8a18\u61b6\u3068\u8aa0\u306e\u8349\u3002\u300c\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30de\u30ea\u30fc\u306f\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u306e\u305f\u3081\u300d\u3068\u8a00\u308f\u308c\u3001\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u3067\u306f\u5a5a\u793c\u306b\u3082\u846c\u793c\u306b\u3082\u4e00\u679d\u304c\u643a\u3048\u3089\u308c\u308b\u2014\u2014\u8a18\u61b6\u3055\u308c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3002\u53e4\u4ee3\u306b\u306f\u30a2\u30d5\u30ed\u30c7\u30a3\u30fc\u30c6\u306e\u8863\u304b\u3089\u751f\u307e\u308c\u305f\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3001\u5b66\u5f92\u306f\u8a18\u61b6\u3092\u7814\u3050\u305f\u3081\u306b\u8eab\u306b\u3064\u3051\u305f\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u5b88\u308a\u3068\u6d44\u5316\u306e\u305f\u3081\u711a\u304b\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u3055\u305b\u3001\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u5f37\u3081\u308b\u3002",mythPt:"O alecrim \xe9 a erva da mem\xf3ria e da fidelidade. 'O alecrim \xe9 para a lembran\xe7a', diz-se; no Mediterr\xe2neo leva-se um raminho tanto em casamentos como em funerais \u2014 emblema de ser recordado. Na antiguidade cria-se nascido do manto de Afrodite; os estudantes usavam-no para agu\xe7ar a mem\xf3ria. Na Anat\xf3lia queima-se para a prote\xe7\xe3o e a purifica\xe7\xe3o; o seu aroma desperta a mente e fortalece a inten\xe7\xe3o."},{id:"plant-004",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3c",color:"#F2D680",name:"Papatya",nameEn:"Chamomile",nameDe:"Kamille",nameEs:"Manzanilla",nameFr:"Camomille",nameJa:"\u30ab\u30e2\u30df\u30fc\u30eb",namePt:"Camomila",origin:"Avrupa, Bat\u0131 Asya",originEn:"Europe, Western Asia",originDe:"Europa, Westasien",originEs:"Europa, Asia Occidental",originFr:"Europe, Asie occidentale",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u897f\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia Ocidental",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","\u015fefkat","huzur"],propertiesEn:["soothing","compassion","peace"],propertiesDe:["beruhigend","Mitgef\xfchl","Frieden"],propertiesEs:["calmante","compasi\xf3n","paz"],propertiesFr:["apaisant","compassion","paix"],propertiesJa:["\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b","\u6148\u3057\u307f","\u5b89\u3089\u304e"],propertiesPt:["suavizante","compaix\xe3o","paz"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kendine biraz \u015fefkat g\xf6ster. Papatya, sinirlerini yumu\u015fat\u0131r ve i\xe7indeki \xe7ocu\u011fa nazik\xe7e sar\u0131lman\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, offer yourself a little tenderness. Chamomile softens your nerves and reminds you to gently embrace your inner child.",dailyMessageDe:"Schenke dir heute ein wenig Z\xe4rtlichkeit. Kamille bes\xe4nftigt deine Nerven und erinnert dich daran, dein inneres Kind sanft zu umarmen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ofr\xe9cete un poco de ternura. La manzanilla suaviza tus nervios y te recuerda abrazar con dulzura a tu ni\xf1o interior.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, offre-toi un peu de tendresse. La camomille apaise tes nerfs et te rappelle d'embrasser doucement ton enfant int\xe9rieur.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u5c11\u3057\u306e\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055\u3092\u8d08\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ab\u30e2\u30df\u30fc\u30eb\u306f\u795e\u7d4c\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u5b50\u3069\u3082\u3092\u305d\u3063\u3068\u62b1\u304d\u3057\u3081\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, ofere\xe7a a voc\xea um pouco de ternura. A camomila suaviza seus nervos e lembra voc\xea de abra\xe7ar com carinho a sua crian\xe7a interior.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini s\u0131cak suda demleyip ak\u015fam \xe7ay\u0131 olarak yudumla. So\u011futulmu\u015f \xe7ay\u0131n\u0131 yorgun g\xf6zlere kompres olarak uygula.",howToUseEn:"Brew the flowers in hot water and sip as an evening tea. Apply the cooled infusion as a compress for tired eyes.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten in hei\xdfem Wasser und genie\xdfe sie als Abendtee. Lege den abgek\xfchlten Aufguss als Kompresse auf m\xfcde Augen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las flores en agua caliente y b\xe9bela como t\xe9 de la tarde. Aplica la infusi\xf3n fr\xeda como compresa para los ojos cansados.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fleurs dans de l'eau chaude et savoure-les en tisane du soir. Applique l'infusion refroidie en compresse sur les yeux fatigu\xe9s.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u591c\u306e\u304a\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u51b7\u307e\u3057\u305f\u714e\u3058\u6db2\u3092\u75b2\u308c\u305f\u76ee\u3078\u306e\u6e7f\u5e03\u3068\u3057\u3066\u4f7f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores em \xe1gua quente e tome como ch\xe1 da noite. Aplique a infus\xe3o fria como compressa para os olhos cansados.",affirmation:"Kendime nazik\xe7e davran\u0131yorum, hak etti\u011fim huzuru kucakl\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I treat myself gently and embrace the peace I deserve.",affirmationDe:"Ich behandle mich sanft und nehme den Frieden an, den ich verdiene.",affirmationEs:"Me trato con dulzura y abrazo la paz que merezco.",affirmationFr:"Je me traite avec douceur et accueille la paix que je m\xe9rite.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u6271\u3044\u3001\u3075\u3055\u308f\u3057\u3044\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u53d7\u3051\u5165\u308c\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Eu me trato com gentileza e acolho a paz que mere\xe7o.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Kamomillasaunio_%28Matricaria_recutita%29.JPG/330px-Kamomillasaunio_%28Matricaria_recutita%29.JPG",myth:"Papatya, masumiyetin ve \u015fefkatli \u015fifan\u0131n \xe7i\xe7e\u011fidir. Anadolu'da 'ana \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi' diye an\u0131l\u0131r; \xe7ay\u0131 y\xfczy\u0131llard\u0131r mideyi, sinirleri ve uykuyu yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131r. Antik M\u0131s\u0131r'da g\xfcne\u015f tanr\u0131s\u0131na adanm\u0131\u015f, k\xfc\xe7\xfck g\xfcne\u015fler gibi a\xe7an yapraklar\u0131 umudun simgesi olmu\u015ftur. \xc7i\u011fnense de yeniden biten \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi, g\xf6steri\u015fsiz ama diren\xe7li sevginin dersidir.",mythEn:"Chamomile is the flower of innocence and gentle healing. In Anatolia it is called the 'mother flower'; its tea has soothed the stomach, nerves and sleep for centuries. In ancient Egypt it was dedicated to the sun god, its petals opening like little suns, an emblem of hope. Trodden yet rising again, it teaches an unshowy but resilient love.",mythDe:"Kamille ist die Blume der Unschuld und der sanften Heilung. In Anatolien hei\xdft sie 'Mutterblume'; ihr Tee beruhigt seit Jahrhunderten Magen, Nerven und Schlaf. Im alten \xc4gypten dem Sonnengott geweiht, \xf6ffnen sich ihre Bl\xfctenbl\xe4tter wie kleine Sonnen, ein Sinnbild der Hoffnung. Zertreten und doch wieder aufstehend, lehrt sie eine unscheinbare, aber widerstandsf\xe4hige Liebe.",mythEs:"La manzanilla es la flor de la inocencia y la sanaci\xf3n suave. En Anatolia se la llama 'flor madre'; su infusi\xf3n calma el est\xf3mago, los nervios y el sue\xf1o desde hace siglos. En el antiguo Egipto, consagrada al dios sol, sus p\xe9talos se abren como peque\xf1os soles, emblema de esperanza. Pisada y de nuevo alz\xe1ndose, ense\xf1a un amor discreto pero resistente.",mythFr:"La camomille est la fleur de l'innocence et de la gu\xe9rison douce. En Anatolie on l'appelle 'fleur m\xe8re' ; sa tisane apaise depuis des si\xe8cles l'estomac, les nerfs et le sommeil. Dans l'\xc9gypte antique, consacr\xe9e au dieu solaire, ses p\xe9tales s'ouvrent comme de petits soleils, embl\xe8me d'espoir. Pi\xe9tin\xe9e et se relevant, elle enseigne un amour discret mais r\xe9silient.",mythJa:"\u30ab\u30e2\u30df\u30fc\u30eb\u306f\u7121\u57a2\u3068\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u7652\u3057\u306e\u82b1\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u300c\u6bcd\u306e\u82b1\u300d\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u8336\u306f\u4f55\u4e16\u7d00\u3082\u80c3\u3068\u795e\u7d4c\u3068\u7720\u308a\u3092\u548c\u3089\u3052\u3066\u304d\u305f\u3002\u53e4\u4ee3\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u3067\u306f\u592a\u967d\u795e\u306b\u6367\u3052\u3089\u308c\u3001\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u592a\u967d\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u958b\u304f\u82b1\u3073\u3089\u306f\u5e0c\u671b\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3002\u8e0f\u307e\u308c\u3066\u3082\u518d\u3073\u7acb\u3064\u305d\u306e\u82b1\u306f\u3001\u5730\u5473\u3067\u3082\u6298\u308c\u306a\u3044\u611b\u306e\u6559\u3048\u3002",mythPt:"A camomila \xe9 a flor da inoc\xeancia e da cura suave. Na Anat\xf3lia chama-se 'flor m\xe3e'; a sua infus\xe3o acalma o est\xf4mago, os nervos e o sono h\xe1 s\xe9culos. No antigo Egito, consagrada ao deus sol, as suas p\xe9talas abrem-se como pequenos s\xf3is, emblema de esperan\xe7a. Pisada e erguendo-se de novo, ensina um amor discreto mas resiliente."},{id:"plant-005",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#4FA67D",name:"Nane",nameEn:"Mint",nameDe:"Minze",nameEs:"Menta",nameFr:"Menthe",nameJa:"\u30df\u30f3\u30c8",namePt:"Hortel\xe3",origin:"Avrupa, Asya",originEn:"Europe, Asia",originDe:"Europa, Asien",originEs:"Europa, Asia",originFr:"Europe, Asie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["ferahlat\u0131c\u0131","canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","sindirim dostu"],propertiesEn:["refreshing","invigorating","digestive"],propertiesDe:["erfrischend","belebend","verdauungsf\xf6rdernd"],propertiesEs:["refrescante","vigorizante","digestiva"],propertiesFr:["rafra\xeechissant","tonifiant","digestif"],propertiesJa:["\u723d\u5feb","\u6d3b\u6027","\u6d88\u5316\u3092\u52a9\u3051\u308b"],propertiesPt:["refrescante","revigorante","digestiva"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn serin bir nefes al ve zihnini tazele. Nane a\u011f\u0131rla\u015fan d\xfc\u015f\xfcncelerini ferahlat\u0131r, sana yeni bir berrakl\u0131k getirir.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, take a cool breath and refresh your mind. Mint lightens your heavy thoughts and brings you new clarity.",dailyMessageDe:"Atme heute k\xfchl durch und erfrische deinen Geist. Minze erleichtert deine schweren Gedanken und schenkt dir neue Klarheit.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, respira fresco y refresca tu mente. La menta aligera tus pensamientos pesados y te trae una nueva claridad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, prends une respiration fra\xeeche et rafra\xeechis ton esprit. La menthe all\xe8ge tes pens\xe9es lourdes et t'apporte une nouvelle clart\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u6dbc\u3084\u304b\u306a\u606f\u3092\u5438\u3044\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30df\u30f3\u30c8\u306f\u91cd\u305f\u3044\u601d\u3044\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u3057\u3001\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u660e\u6670\u3055\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, respire fresco e renove a mente. A hortel\xe3 alivia seus pensamentos pesados e traz uma nova clareza.",howToUse:"Taze yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip i\xe7 ya da so\u011fuk suya ekleyerek serinle. Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 koklayarak ba\u015f a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 hafiflet.",howToUseEn:"Brew fresh leaves in hot water, or add them to cold water to cool down. Inhale the essential oil to ease a headache.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche frische Bl\xe4tter in hei\xdfem Wasser oder gib sie ins kalte Wasser zur Erfrischung. Atme das \xe4therische \xd6l ein, um Kopfschmerzen zu lindern.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona hojas frescas en agua caliente, o agr\xe9galas al agua fr\xeda para refrescarte. Inhala el aceite esencial para aliviar el dolor de cabeza.",howToUseFr:"Infuse des feuilles fra\xeeches dans de l'eau chaude, ou ajoute-les \xe0 de l'eau froide pour te rafra\xeechir. Inhale l'huile essentielle pour soulager un mal de t\xeate.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u8449\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u51b7\u6c34\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3066\u6dbc\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7cbe\u6cb9\u306e\u9999\u308a\u3092\u5438\u3063\u3066\u982d\u75db\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare folhas frescas em \xe1gua quente, ou adicione-as \xe0 \xe1gua fria para refrescar. Inale o \xf3leo essencial para aliviar a dor de cabe\xe7a.",affirmation:"Her nefeste tazelenir, yeniden ba\u015flar\u0131m.",affirmationEn:"With every breath I am refreshed and begin anew.",affirmationDe:"Mit jedem Atemzug erfrische ich mich und beginne neu.",affirmationEs:"Con cada respiraci\xf3n me refresco y vuelvo a empezar.",affirmationFr:"\xc0 chaque souffle, je me rafra\xeechis et recommence.",affirmationJa:"\u3072\u3068\u547c\u5438\u3054\u3068\u306b\u79c1\u306f\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u306a\u308a\u3001\u518d\u3073\u59cb\u3081\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"A cada respira\xe7\xe3o eu me renovo e come\xe7o de novo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Mentha_spicata-IMG_6186.jpg/330px-Mentha_spicata-IMG_6186.jpg",myth:"Nane, ferahl\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve misafirperverli\u011fin otudur. Anadolu sofras\u0131n\u0131n vazge\xe7ilmezi \u2014 \xe7ayda, ayranda, yemekte serinlik ve berrakl\u0131k verir. Yunan mitinde su perisi Minthe, k\u0131skan\xe7 tanr\u0131\xe7a taraf\u0131ndan nane bitkisine d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcl\xfcr; ezildik\xe7e daha g\xfczel kokmas\u0131 bu efsaneden gelir. Zihni a\xe7ar, mideyi yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131r; eve getirilen demeti tazelik ve bereket \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131r.",mythEn:"Mint is the herb of freshness and hospitality. It is indispensable to the Anatolian table \u2014 lending coolness and clarity to tea, ayran and food. In the Greek myth the water nymph Minthe is turned into the mint plant by a jealous goddess; that the more it is crushed the sweeter it smells comes from this tale. It clears the mind and settles the stomach; a sprig brought home calls in freshness and abundance.",mythDe:"Minze ist das Kraut der Frische und Gastfreundschaft. Auf der anatolischen Tafel unverzichtbar \u2014 sie gibt Tee, Ayran und Speisen K\xfchle und Klarheit. Im griechischen Mythos wird die Wassernymphe Minthe von einer eifers\xfcchtigen G\xf6ttin in die Minzpflanze verwandelt; dass sie umso s\xfc\xdfer duftet, je mehr man sie zerreibt, kommt aus dieser Sage. Sie kl\xe4rt den Geist und beruhigt den Magen; ein heimgebrachter Zweig ruft Frische und F\xfclle herbei.",mythEs:"La menta es la hierba de la frescura y la hospitalidad. Indispensable en la mesa anatolia \u2014 da frescor y claridad al t\xe9, al ayran y a la comida. En el mito griego, la ninfa del agua Mente es convertida en menta por una diosa celosa; que cuanto m\xe1s se la estruja m\xe1s dulce huele viene de esa leyenda. Despeja la mente y asienta el est\xf3mago; un ramillete en casa llama a la frescura y la abundancia.",mythFr:"La menthe est l'herbe de la fra\xeecheur et de l'hospitalit\xe9. Indispensable \xe0 la table anatolienne \u2014 elle donne fra\xeecheur et clart\xe9 au th\xe9, \xe0 l'ayran et aux plats. Dans le mythe grec, la nymphe des eaux Minth\xe9 est chang\xe9e en menthe par une d\xe9esse jalouse ; que plus on la froisse, plus elle embaume, vient de cette l\xe9gende. Elle \xe9claircit l'esprit et apaise l'estomac ; un brin rapport\xe9 \xe0 la maison appelle la fra\xeecheur et l'abondance.",mythJa:"\u30df\u30f3\u30c8\u306f\u6e05\u6dbc\u3068\u3082\u3066\u306a\u3057\u306e\u8349\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u98df\u5353\u306b\u6b20\u304b\u305b\u305a\u3001\u8336\u3084\u30a2\u30a4\u30e9\u30f3\u3001\u6599\u7406\u306b\u6dbc\u3084\u304b\u3055\u3068\u660e\u6670\u3055\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u308b\u3002\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u6c34\u306e\u5996\u7cbe\u30df\u30f3\u30c6\u304c\u3001\u5ac9\u59ac\u3059\u308b\u5973\u795e\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u30df\u30f3\u30c8\u306b\u5909\u3048\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3002\u63c9\u3080\u307b\u3069\u7518\u304f\u9999\u308b\u306e\u306f\u3053\u306e\u7269\u8a9e\u306b\u7531\u6765\u3059\u308b\u3002\u5fc3\u3092\u6674\u3089\u3057\u3001\u80c3\u3092\u843d\u3061\u7740\u304b\u305b\u3001\u5bb6\u306b\u6301\u3061\u5e30\u308b\u4e00\u679d\u306f\u723d\u3084\u304b\u3055\u3068\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u3092\u62db\u304f\u3002",mythPt:"A hortel\xe3 \xe9 a erva da frescura e da hospitalidade. Indispens\xe1vel \xe0 mesa anat\xf3lia \u2014 d\xe1 frescura e clareza ao ch\xe1, ao ayran e \xe0 comida. No mito grego, a ninfa das \xe1guas Mente \xe9 transformada em hortel\xe3 por uma deusa ciumenta; o facto de quanto mais se esmaga mais doce cheira vem dessa lenda. Clareia a mente e acalma o est\xf4mago; um raminho em casa chama a frescura e a abund\xe2ncia."},{id:"plant-006",emoji:"\ud83c\udf43",color:"#6FB28A",name:"Melisa",nameEn:"Lemon Balm",nameDe:"Zitronenmelisse",nameEs:"Melisa",nameFr:"M\xe9lisse",nameJa:"\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30d0\u30fc\u30e0",namePt:"Erva-cidreira",origin:"G\xfcney Avrupa, Akdeniz",originEn:"Southern Europe, Mediterranean",originDe:"S\xfcdeuropa, Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Sur de Europa, Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"Europe du Sud, M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u5357\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77",originPt:"Sul da Europa, Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["ne\u015felendirici","sakinle\u015ftirici","kayg\u0131 giderici"],propertiesEn:["uplifting","calming","anxiety-easing"],propertiesDe:["aufmunternd","beruhigend","angstlindernd"],propertiesEs:["alegrante","calmante","alivia la ansiedad"],propertiesFr:["r\xe9jouissant","apaisant","anti-anxi\xe9t\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u9ad8\u63da","\u93ae\u9759","\u4e0d\u5b89\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u308b"],propertiesPt:["alegrante","calmante","alivia a ansiedade"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kalbine g\xfcne\u015f gibi dokun. Melisa endi\u015feni da\u011f\u0131t\u0131r, ruhuna hafif bir ne\u015fe ve umut ta\u015f\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, let sunlight touch your heart. Lemon balm scatters your worry and carries a light joy and hope into your spirit.",dailyMessageDe:"Lass heute Sonnenlicht dein Herz ber\xfchren. Zitronenmelisse zerstreut deine Sorge und bringt eine leichte Freude und Hoffnung in deine Seele.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, deja que la luz del sol toque tu coraz\xf3n. La melisa dispersa tu preocupaci\xf3n y lleva una alegr\xeda ligera y esperanza a tu esp\xedritu.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, laisse la lumi\xe8re du soleil toucher ton c\u0153ur. La m\xe9lisse disperse ton souci et porte une joie l\xe9g\xe8re et de l'espoir \xe0 ton esprit.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u967d\u306e\u5149\u306b\u5fc3\u3092\u3075\u308c\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30d0\u30fc\u30e0\u306f\u4e0d\u5b89\u3092\u6563\u3089\u3057\u3001\u8efd\u3084\u304b\u306a\u559c\u3073\u3068\u5e0c\u671b\u3092\u9b42\u3078\u904b\u3073\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, deixe a luz do sol tocar seu cora\xe7\xe3o. A erva-cidreira dispersa a preocupa\xe7\xe3o e leva uma alegria leve e esperan\xe7a ao seu esp\xedrito.",howToUse:"Taze yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip g\xfcn boyu sakinlik i\xe7in i\xe7. Ak\u015fam banyosuna ekleyerek gerginli\u011fi \xe7\xf6z.",howToUseEn:"Brew fresh leaves in hot water and sip through the day for calm. Add it to your evening bath to dissolve tension.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche frische Bl\xe4tter in hei\xdfem Wasser und trinke sie \xfcber den Tag zur Beruhigung. Gib sie ins Abendbad, um Spannung zu l\xf6sen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona hojas frescas en agua caliente y bebe durante el d\xeda para calmarte. Agr\xe9gala a tu ba\xf1o nocturno para disolver la tensi\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Infuse des feuilles fra\xeeches dans de l'eau chaude et bois-en au cours de la journ\xe9e pour te calmer. Ajoute-la \xe0 ton bain du soir pour dissoudre la tension.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u8449\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u901a\u3057\u3066\u98f2\u3093\u3067\u843d\u3061\u7740\u304d\u3092\u3002\u591c\u306e\u5165\u6d74\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3066\u7dca\u5f35\u3092\u307b\u3069\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare folhas frescas em \xe1gua quente e tome ao longo do dia para se acalmar. Adicione ao banho da noite para dissolver a tens\xe3o.",affirmation:"Kalbim hafif, ruhum umutla dolu.",affirmationEn:"My heart is light and my spirit is full of hope.",affirmationDe:"Mein Herz ist leicht und meine Seele voller Hoffnung.",affirmationEs:"Mi coraz\xf3n es ligero y mi esp\xedritu est\xe1 lleno de esperanza.",affirmationFr:"Mon c\u0153ur est l\xe9ger et mon esprit plein d'espoir.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u8efd\u304f\u3001\u9b42\u306f\u5e0c\u671b\u306b\u6e80\u3061\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Meu cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 leve e meu esp\xedrito est\xe1 cheio de esperan\xe7a.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Lemon_balm_plant.jpg/330px-Lemon_balm_plant.jpg"},{id:"plant-007",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#7E9E5C",name:"Kekik",nameEn:"Thyme",nameDe:"Thymian",nameEs:"Tomillo",nameFr:"Thym",nameJa:"\u30bf\u30a4\u30e0",namePt:"Tomilho",origin:"Akdeniz havzas\u0131",originEn:"Mediterranean basin",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Cuenca mediterr\xe1nea",originFr:"Bassin m\xe9diterran\xe9en",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u6cbf\u5cb8",originPt:"Bacia do Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Lar\xedngeo",properties:["g\xfc\xe7 veren","koruyucu","cesaret"],propertiesEn:["strengthening","protective","courage"],propertiesDe:["st\xe4rkend","sch\xfctzend","Mut"],propertiesEs:["fortalecedor","protector","valor"],propertiesFr:["fortifiant","protecteur","courage"],propertiesJa:["\u5f37\u5316","\u5b88\u8b77","\u52c7\u6c17"],propertiesPt:["fortalecedor","protetor","coragem"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn cesaretini topla ve sesini duyur. Kekik sana i\xe7 g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc hat\u0131rlat\u0131r, zorluklar\u0131n kar\u015f\u0131s\u0131nda dik durman\u0131 destekler.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, gather your courage and let your voice be heard. Thyme reminds you of your inner strength and supports you in standing tall before challenges.",dailyMessageDe:"Sammle heute deinen Mut und lass deine Stimme h\xf6ren. Thymian erinnert dich an deine innere St\xe4rke und hilft dir, Herausforderungen aufrecht zu begegnen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, re\xfane tu valor y deja que tu voz se escuche. El tomillo te recuerda tu fuerza interior y te apoya a mantenerte firme ante los desaf\xedos.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, rassemble ton courage et fais entendre ta voix. Le thym te rappelle ta force int\xe9rieure et te soutient pour te tenir droit face aux d\xe9fis.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u52c7\u6c17\u3092\u96c6\u3081\u3001\u58f0\u3092\u3042\u3052\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30bf\u30a4\u30e0\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u529b\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u3001\u56f0\u96e3\u306e\u524d\u3067\u5802\u3005\u3068\u7acb\u3064\u3053\u3068\u3092\u652f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, re\xfana sua coragem e deixe sua voz ser ouvida. O tomilho lembra voc\xea da sua for\xe7a interior e o apoia a se manter firme diante dos desafios.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip bo\u011faz i\xe7in \u0131l\u0131k olarak i\xe7. Buhar banyosunda nefes a\xe7\u0131c\u0131 olarak kullan.",howToUseEn:"Brew the leaves in hot water and drink warm for the throat. Use it in a steam bath to open the breath.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter in hei\xdfem Wasser und trinke sie warm f\xfcr den Hals. Verwende ihn im Dampfbad, um den Atem zu \xf6ffnen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las hojas en agua caliente y bebe tibio para la garganta. \xdasalo en un ba\xf1o de vapor para abrir la respiraci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les feuilles dans de l'eau chaude et bois ti\xe8de pour la gorge. Utilise-le en bain de vapeur pour d\xe9gager la respiration.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u5589\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6e29\u304b\u304f\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u84b8\u6c17\u6d74\u3067\u547c\u5438\u3092\u958b\u304f\u306e\u306b\u4f7f\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as folhas em \xe1gua quente e beba morno para a garganta. Use em um banho de vapor para abrir a respira\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7 g\xfcc\xfcme g\xfcveniyorum, cesaretle ilerliyorum.",affirmationEn:"I trust my inner strength and move forward with courage.",affirmationDe:"Ich vertraue meiner inneren St\xe4rke und gehe mutig voran.",affirmationEs:"Conf\xedo en mi fuerza interior y avanzo con valor.",affirmationFr:"Je fais confiance \xe0 ma force int\xe9rieure et j'avance avec courage.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u529b\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3057\u3001\u52c7\u6c17\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u9032\u3080\u3002",affirmationPt:"Confio na minha for\xe7a interior e sigo em frente com coragem.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Thyme-Bundle.jpg/330px-Thyme-Bundle.jpg",myth:"Kekik, Anadolu da\u011flar\u0131n\u0131n cesaret ve ar\u0131nma otudur. Ad\u0131 Yunanca 'thymos' \u2014 y\xfcrek, cesaret \u2014 ile an\u0131l\u0131r; antik askerler y\u0131kanma suyuna kekik katar, sava\u015ftan \xf6nce g\xf6\u011fse s\xfcrerdi. G\xfc\xe7l\xfc antiseptik kokusu mek\xe2n\u0131 ve bedeni temizler. \xc7obanlar\u0131n ate\u015finde yak\u0131lan kekik, kurdu ve k\xf6t\xfcl\xfc\u011f\xfc uzak tutard\u0131. Y\xfcksek, \xe7orak yama\xe7larda inatla yeti\u015fen bu ot, zor ko\u015fulda bile dik durman\u0131n ve i\xe7teki g\xfcc\xfcn dersidir.",mythEn:"Thyme is the herb of courage and purification of the Anatolian mountains. Its name comes from the Greek 'thymos' \u2014 heart, courage; ancient soldiers added thyme to their bath water and rubbed it on the chest before battle. Its strong, antiseptic scent cleanses a space and the body. Burned on shepherds' fires, thyme kept wolf and evil at bay. Growing stubbornly on high, barren slopes, this herb is the lesson of standing tall in hard conditions and of inner strength.",mythDe:"Thymian ist das Kraut des Mutes und der Reinigung der anatolischen Berge. Sein Name kommt vom griechischen 'thymos' \u2014 Herz, Mut; antike Soldaten gaben Thymian ins Badewasser und rieben ihn vor der Schlacht auf die Brust. Sein starker, antiseptischer Duft reinigt Raum und K\xf6rper. Auf Hirtenfeuern verbrannt, hielt Thymian Wolf und B\xf6ses fern. Eigensinnig an hohen, kargen H\xe4ngen wachsend, lehrt dieses Kraut, unter harten Bedingungen aufrecht zu stehen, und die innere St\xe4rke.",mythEs:"El tomillo es la hierba del valor y la purificaci\xf3n de las monta\xf1as de Anatolia. Su nombre viene del griego 'thymos' \u2014 coraz\xf3n, valor; los antiguos soldados a\xf1ad\xedan tomillo al agua del ba\xf1o y se lo frotaban en el pecho antes de la batalla. Su aroma fuerte y antis\xe9ptico limpia un espacio y el cuerpo. Quemado en las hogueras de los pastores, el tomillo manten\xeda a raya al lobo y al mal. Creciendo tenaz en laderas altas y \xe1ridas, esta hierba ense\xf1a a mantenerse erguido en condiciones duras y la fuerza interior.",mythFr:"Le thym est l'herbe du courage et de la purification des montagnes d'Anatolie. Son nom vient du grec 'thymos' \u2014 c\u0153ur, courage ; les anciens soldats en ajoutaient \xe0 l'eau du bain et s'en frottaient la poitrine avant la bataille. Son parfum fort et antiseptique purifie un lieu et le corps. Br\xfbl\xe9 sur les feux des bergers, le thym tenait le loup et le mal \xe0 distance. Poussant avec t\xe9nacit\xe9 sur les pentes hautes et arides, cette herbe enseigne \xe0 se tenir droit dans les conditions rudes et la force int\xe9rieure.",mythJa:"\u30bf\u30a4\u30e0\u306f\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u5c71\u3005\u306e\u3001\u52c7\u6c17\u3068\u6d44\u5316\u306e\u8349\u3002\u305d\u306e\u540d\u306f\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u8a9e\u300c\u30c6\u30e5\u30fc\u30e2\u30b9\u300d\u2014\u2014\u5fc3\u3001\u52c7\u6c17\u2014\u2014\u306b\u7531\u6765\u3057\u3001\u53e4\u4ee3\u306e\u5175\u58eb\u306f\u6e6f\u306b\u30bf\u30a4\u30e0\u3092\u52a0\u3048\u3001\u6226\u306e\u524d\u306b\u80f8\u306b\u64e6\u308a\u8fbc\u3093\u3060\u3002\u5f37\u3044\u6bba\u83cc\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306f\u7a7a\u9593\u3068\u8eab\u4f53\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u308b\u3002\u7f8a\u98fc\u3044\u306e\u706b\u306b\u711a\u304b\u308c\u3001\u72fc\u3068\u707d\u3044\u3092\u9060\u3056\u3051\u305f\u3002\u9ad8\u304f\u75e9\u305b\u305f\u659c\u9762\u306b\u9811\u306a\u306b\u80b2\u3064\u3053\u306e\u8349\u306f\u3001\u53b3\u3057\u3044\u4e2d\u3067\u3082\u80cc\u7b4b\u3092\u4f38\u3070\u3059\u3053\u3068\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u5f37\u3055\u306e\u6559\u3048\u3002",mythPt:"O tomilho \xe9 a erva da coragem e da purifica\xe7\xe3o das montanhas da Anat\xf3lia. O seu nome vem do grego 'thymos' \u2014 cora\xe7\xe3o, coragem; os antigos soldados juntavam tomilho \xe0 \xe1gua do banho e esfregavam-no no peito antes da batalha. O seu aroma forte e antiss\xe9ptico limpa um espa\xe7o e o corpo. Queimado nas fogueiras dos pastores, o tomilho mantinha o lobo e o mal \xe0 dist\xe2ncia. Crescendo teimoso em encostas altas e \xe1ridas, esta erva ensina a manter-se ereto em condi\xe7\xf5es duras e a for\xe7a interior."},{id:"plant-008",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3e",color:"#C9B458",name:"Rezene",nameEn:"Fennel",nameDe:"Fenchel",nameEs:"Hinojo",nameFr:"Fenouil",nameJa:"\u30d5\u30a7\u30f3\u30cd\u30eb",namePt:"Funcho",origin:"Akdeniz",originEn:"Mediterranean",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u5730\u57df",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["sindirim dostu","rahatlat\u0131c\u0131","bolluk"],propertiesEn:["digestive","relaxing","abundance"],propertiesDe:["verdauungsf\xf6rdernd","entspannend","F\xfclle"],propertiesEs:["digestivo","relajante","abundancia"],propertiesFr:["digestif","relaxant","abondance"],propertiesJa:["\u6d88\u5316\u3092\u52a9\u3051\u308b","\u30ea\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30b9","\u8c4a\u304b\u3055"],propertiesPt:["digestivo","relaxante","abund\xe2ncia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131n ak\u0131\u015f\u0131na g\xfcven ve sindirebilece\u011finden fazlas\u0131n\u0131 y\xfcklenme. Rezene i\xe7sel dengeyi onar\u0131r, bollu\u011fa a\xe7\u0131k kalman\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, trust the flow of life and don't take on more than you can digest. Fennel restores inner balance and reminds you to stay open to abundance.",dailyMessageDe:"Vertraue heute dem Fluss des Lebens und nimm nicht mehr auf, als du verdauen kannst. Fenchel stellt das innere Gleichgewicht wieder her und erinnert dich, offen f\xfcr F\xfclle zu bleiben.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, conf\xeda en el fluir de la vida y no asumas m\xe1s de lo que puedes digerir. El hinojo restaura el equilibrio interior y te recuerda permanecer abierto a la abundancia.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, fais confiance au flux de la vie et ne prends pas plus que tu ne peux dig\xe9rer. Le fenouil r\xe9tablit l'\xe9quilibre int\xe9rieur et te rappelle de rester ouvert \xe0 l'abondance.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u306e\u6d41\u308c\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u3001\u6d88\u5316\u3067\u304d\u308b\u4ee5\u4e0a\u3092\u62b1\u3048\u8fbc\u307e\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d5\u30a7\u30f3\u30cd\u30eb\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u5747\u8861\u3092\u53d6\u308a\u623b\u3057\u3001\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306b\u958b\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, confie no fluxo da vida e n\xe3o assuma mais do que consegue digerir. O funcho restaura o equil\xedbrio interior e lembra voc\xea de permanecer aberto \xe0 abund\xe2ncia.",howToUse:"Tohumlar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip yemek sonras\u0131 i\xe7. \xc7i\u011fneyerek nefesini tazeleyebilir, sindirimini rahatlatabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Brew the seeds in hot water and drink after meals. You can chew them to freshen your breath and ease digestion.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Samen in hei\xdfem Wasser und trinke sie nach dem Essen. Du kannst sie kauen, um deinen Atem zu erfrischen und die Verdauung zu erleichtern.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las semillas en agua caliente y bebe despu\xe9s de las comidas. Puedes masticarlas para refrescar el aliento y aliviar la digesti\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les graines dans de l'eau chaude et bois apr\xe8s les repas. Tu peux les m\xe2cher pour rafra\xeechir ton haleine et faciliter la digestion.",howToUseJa:"\u7a2e\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u98df\u5f8c\u306b\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u565b\u3093\u3067\u606f\u3092\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306b\u3057\u3001\u6d88\u5316\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as sementes em \xe1gua quente e beba ap\xf3s as refei\xe7\xf5es. Voc\xea pode mastig\xe1-las para refrescar o h\xe1lito e facilitar a digest\xe3o.",affirmation:"Hayat\u0131n ak\u0131\u015f\u0131na g\xfcveniyorum, dengedeyim.",affirmationEn:"I trust the flow of life and I am in balance.",affirmationDe:"Ich vertraue dem Fluss des Lebens und bin im Gleichgewicht.",affirmationEs:"Conf\xedo en el fluir de la vida y estoy en equilibrio.",affirmationFr:"Je fais confiance au flux de la vie et je suis en \xe9quilibre.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u306e\u6d41\u308c\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3057\u3001\u5747\u8861\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Confio no fluxo da vida e estou em equil\xedbrio.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Foeniculum_July_2011-1a.jpg/330px-Foeniculum_July_2011-1a.jpg"},{id:"plant-009",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#D9B26A",name:"Ihlamur",nameEn:"Linden",nameDe:"Linde",nameEs:"Tilo",nameFr:"Tilleul",nameJa:"\u30ea\u30f3\u30c7\u30f3",namePt:"T\xedlia",origin:"Avrupa, Anadolu",originEn:"Europe, Anatolia",originDe:"Europa, Anatolien",originEs:"Europa, Anatolia",originFr:"Europe, Anatolie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, Anat\xf3lia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["\u015fefkat","rahatlat\u0131c\u0131","s\u0131cakl\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["compassion","soothing","warmth"],propertiesDe:["Mitgef\xfchl","beruhigend","W\xe4rme"],propertiesEs:["compasi\xf3n","calmante","calidez"],propertiesFr:["compassion","apaisant","chaleur"],propertiesJa:["\u6148\u3057\u307f","\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b","\u6e29\u3082\u308a"],propertiesPt:["compaix\xe3o","suavizante","aconchego"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kendine s\u0131cak bir kucak a\xe7. Ihlamur i\xe7indeki gerginli\u011fi yumu\u015fat\u0131r, sana evdeki gibi bir huzur hissi verir.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, open a warm embrace to yourself. Linden softens the tension within you and gives you a feeling of being at home.",dailyMessageDe:"\xd6ffne dir heute eine warme Umarmung. Die Linde mildert die Spannung in dir und schenkt dir das Gef\xfchl, zu Hause zu sein.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, \xe1brete un c\xe1lido abrazo. El tilo suaviza la tensi\xf3n en tu interior y te da la sensaci\xf3n de estar en casa.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, offre-toi une chaleureuse \xe9treinte. Le tilleul adoucit la tension en toi et te donne la sensation d'\xeatre chez toi.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u62b1\u64c1\u3092\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ea\u30f3\u30c7\u30f3\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u7dca\u5f35\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u3001\u308f\u304c\u5bb6\u306b\u3044\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306a\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, abra um abra\xe7o caloroso para voc\xea. A t\xedlia suaviza a tens\xe3o dentro de voc\xea e d\xe1 a sensa\xe7\xe3o de estar em casa.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini s\u0131cak suda demleyip so\u011fuk g\xfcnlerde s\u0131cak \xe7ay olarak i\xe7. Bal ekleyerek bo\u011faz\u0131n\u0131 yumu\u015fat.",howToUseEn:"Brew the flowers in hot water and drink as a warm tea on cold days. Add honey to soothe your throat.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten in hei\xdfem Wasser und trinke sie an kalten Tagen als warmen Tee. Gib Honig hinzu, um deinen Hals zu beruhigen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las flores en agua caliente y bebe como t\xe9 caliente en d\xedas fr\xedos. A\xf1ade miel para suavizar la garganta.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fleurs dans de l'eau chaude et bois en tisane chaude les jours froids. Ajoute du miel pour adoucir ta gorge.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u5bd2\u3044\u65e5\u306b\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u304a\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u8702\u871c\u3092\u52a0\u3048\u3066\u5589\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores em \xe1gua quente e beba como ch\xe1 quente nos dias frios. Adicione mel para suavizar a garganta.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7imde s\u0131cak bir yuva ta\u015f\u0131yorum, her yerde huzurluyum.",affirmationEn:"I carry a warm home within me; I am at peace anywhere.",affirmationDe:"Ich trage ein warmes Zuhause in mir; ich bin \xfcberall im Frieden.",affirmationEs:"Llevo un hogar c\xe1lido dentro de m\xed; estoy en paz en cualquier lugar.",affirmationFr:"Je porte un foyer chaleureux en moi ; je suis en paix partout.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5185\u306b\u6e29\u304b\u306a\u5bb6\u3092\u62b1\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002\u3069\u3053\u306b\u3044\u3066\u3082\u79c1\u306f\u5b89\u3089\u304b\u3060\u3002",affirmationPt:"Carrego um lar aconchegante dentro de mim; estou em paz em qualquer lugar.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kristinas_lind_2013.jpg/330px-Kristinas_lind_2013.jpg"},{id:"plant-010",emoji:"\ud83c\udf39",color:"#D45D7A",name:"G\xfcl",nameEn:"Rose",nameDe:"Rose",nameEs:"Rosa",nameFr:"Rose",nameJa:"\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba",namePt:"Rosa",origin:"Asya, Anadolu",originEn:"Asia, Anatolia",originDe:"Asien, Anatolien",originEs:"Asia, Anatolia",originFr:"Asie, Anatolie",originJa:"\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"\xc1sia, Anat\xf3lia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["sevgi","\xf6z \u015fefkat","a\xe7\u0131l\u0131m"],propertiesEn:["love","self-compassion","opening"],propertiesDe:["Liebe","Selbstmitgef\xfchl","\xd6ffnung"],propertiesEs:["amor","autocompasi\xf3n","apertura"],propertiesFr:["amour","auto-compassion","ouverture"],propertiesJa:["\u611b","\u81ea\u5df1\u3078\u306e\u6148\u3057\u307f","\u958b\u304d"],propertiesPt:["amor","autocompaix\xe3o","abertura"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kalbini bir g\xfcl gibi yava\u015f\xe7a a\xe7. G\xfcl sana sevginin \xf6nce kendine y\xf6nelmesi gerekti\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, open your heart slowly like a rose. The rose whispers that love must first be turned toward yourself.",dailyMessageDe:"\xd6ffne heute dein Herz langsam wie eine Rose. Die Rose fl\xfcstert, dass die Liebe sich zuerst dir selbst zuwenden muss.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, abre tu coraz\xf3n despacio como una rosa. La rosa susurra que el amor debe dirigirse primero hacia ti mismo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ouvre ton c\u0153ur doucement comme une rose. La rose murmure que l'amour doit d'abord se tourner vers toi-m\xeame.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u8594\u8587\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u5fc3\u3092\u3086\u3063\u304f\u308a\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u306f\u3001\u611b\u306f\u307e\u305a\u81ea\u5206\u81ea\u8eab\u3078\u5411\u3051\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3079\u304d\u3060\u3068\u3055\u3055\u3084\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, abra seu cora\xe7\xe3o devagar como uma rosa. A rosa sussurra que o amor deve primeiro se voltar para voc\xea mesmo.",howToUse:"Kuru goncalar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip kalp a\xe7\u0131c\u0131 \xe7ay olarak i\xe7. G\xfcl suyunu y\xfcz\xfcne serperek tazelen ya da banyona birka\xe7 yaprak ekle.",howToUseEn:"Brew dried buds in hot water as a heart-opening tea. Mist rose water on your face to refresh, or add a few petals to your bath.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche getrocknete Knospen in hei\xdfem Wasser als herz\xf6ffnenden Tee. Spr\xfche Rosenwasser ins Gesicht zur Erfrischung oder gib ein paar Bl\xfctenbl\xe4tter ins Bad.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona capullos secos en agua caliente como t\xe9 que abre el coraz\xf3n. Roc\xeda agua de rosas en tu rostro para refrescarte, o a\xf1ade unos p\xe9talos a tu ba\xf1o.",howToUseFr:"Infuse des boutons s\xe9ch\xe9s dans de l'eau chaude en tisane qui ouvre le c\u0153ur. Vaporise de l'eau de rose sur ton visage pour te rafra\xeechir, ou ajoute quelques p\xe9tales \xe0 ton bain.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u857e\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u958b\u304f\u304a\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30a6\u30a9\u30fc\u30bf\u30fc\u3092\u9854\u306b\u5439\u304d\u304b\u3051\u3066\u723d\u3084\u304b\u306b\u3001\u307e\u305f\u306f\u82b1\u3073\u3089\u3092\u6570\u679a\u304a\u98a8\u5442\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare bot\xf5es secos em \xe1gua quente como um ch\xe1 que abre o cora\xe7\xe3o. Borrife \xe1gua de rosas no rosto para refrescar, ou adicione algumas p\xe9talas ao banho.",affirmation:"\xd6nce kendimi seviyorum, kalbim sevgiyle a\xe7\u0131l\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I love myself first; my heart opens with love.",affirmationDe:"Ich liebe zuerst mich selbst; mein Herz \xf6ffnet sich mit Liebe.",affirmationEs:"Me amo primero a m\xed mismo; mi coraz\xf3n se abre con amor.",affirmationFr:"Je m'aime d'abord moi-m\xeame ; mon c\u0153ur s'ouvre avec amour.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u307e\u305a\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u611b\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u958b\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Eu me amo primeiro; meu cora\xe7\xe3o se abre com amor.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg",myth:"G\xfcl, Anadolu'nun kutsal \xe7i\xe7e\u011fidir. Isparta'n\u0131n g\xfcl bah\xe7elerinden dam\u0131t\u0131lan g\xfclsuyu ve g\xfclya\u011f\u0131 y\xfczy\u0131llard\u0131r \u015fifa ve ar\u0131nmada kullan\u0131l\u0131r. Tasavvufta g\xfcl ilahi a\u015fk\u0131n ve Hz. Muhammed'in simgesidir; 'g\xfcl' ile 'g\xf6n\xfcl' ayn\u0131 nefeste an\u0131l\u0131r. Yunus Emre ve Mevlana'n\u0131n dizelerinde dikeni \xe7ile, kokusu cennettir. T\xfcrbelerde, mevlitlerde ve d\xfc\u011f\xfcnlerde serpilen g\xfclsuyu bereket ve ba\u011f\u0131\u015flanma dile\u011fidir. Antik Frigya ve Lidya'da g\xfczellik tanr\u0131\xe7alar\u0131na adan\u0131rd\u0131.",mythEn:"The rose is Anatolia's sacred flower. Rosewater and rose oil distilled in the gardens of Isparta have been used for healing and purification for centuries. In Sufism the rose is the emblem of divine love and of the Prophet; in Turkish 'g\xfcl' (rose) and 'g\xf6n\xfcl' (heart) are spoken in one breath. In the verses of Yunus Emre and Rumi its thorn is hardship, its scent is paradise. Rosewater sprinkled at shrines, memorials and weddings is a wish for blessing and forgiveness. In ancient Phrygia and Lydia it was offered to goddesses of beauty.",mythDe:"Die Rose ist Anatoliens heilige Blume. Rosenwasser und Rosen\xf6l, in den G\xe4rten von Isparta destilliert, werden seit Jahrhunderten zur Heilung und Reinigung verwendet. Im Sufismus ist die Rose Sinnbild der g\xf6ttlichen Liebe und des Propheten; im T\xfcrkischen werden 'g\xfcl' (Rose) und 'g\xf6n\xfcl' (Herz) in einem Atemzug genannt. In den Versen von Yunus Emre und Rumi ist ihr Dorn die M\xfchsal, ihr Duft das Paradies. An Schreinen, Gedenkfeiern und Hochzeiten versprengtes Rosenwasser ist ein Wunsch nach Segen und Vergebung. Im alten Phrygien und Lydien wurde sie den G\xf6ttinnen der Sch\xf6nheit dargebracht.",mythEs:"La rosa es la flor sagrada de Anatolia. El agua y el aceite de rosa destilados en los jardines de Isparta se usan desde hace siglos para la sanaci\xf3n y la purificaci\xf3n. En el sufismo la rosa es emblema del amor divino y del Profeta; en turco 'g\xfcl' (rosa) y 'g\xf6n\xfcl' (coraz\xf3n) se pronuncian en un mismo aliento. En los versos de Yunus Emre y Rumi su espina es la prueba, su aroma el para\xedso. El agua de rosas rociada en santuarios, conmemoraciones y bodas es un deseo de bendici\xf3n y perd\xf3n. En la antigua Frigia y Lidia se ofrec\xeda a las diosas de la belleza.",mythFr:"La rose est la fleur sacr\xe9e de l'Anatolie. L'eau et l'huile de rose distill\xe9es dans les jardins d'Isparta servent depuis des si\xe8cles \xe0 la gu\xe9rison et \xe0 la purification. Dans le soufisme, la rose est l'embl\xe8me de l'amour divin et du Proph\xe8te ; en turc, 'g\xfcl' (rose) et 'g\xf6n\xfcl' (c\u0153ur) se disent d'un m\xeame souffle. Dans les vers de Yunus Emre et de Roumi, son \xe9pine est l'\xe9preuve, son parfum le paradis. L'eau de rose r\xe9pandue aux sanctuaires, aux comm\xe9morations et aux mariages est un v\u0153u de b\xe9n\xe9diction et de pardon. Dans l'antique Phrygie et Lydie, elle \xe9tait offerte aux d\xe9esses de la beaut\xe9.",mythJa:"\u30d0\u30e9\u306f\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u82b1\u3002\u30a4\u30b9\u30d1\u30eb\u30bf\u306e\u8594\u8587\u5712\u3067\u84b8\u7559\u3055\u308c\u308b\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30a6\u30a9\u30fc\u30bf\u30fc\u3068\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30aa\u30a4\u30eb\u306f\u3001\u4f55\u4e16\u7d00\u306b\u3082\u308f\u305f\u308a\u7652\u3057\u3068\u6d44\u5316\u306b\u7528\u3044\u3089\u308c\u3066\u304d\u305f\u3002\u30b9\u30fc\u30d5\u30a3\u30ba\u30e0\u3067\u306f\u795e\u8056\u306a\u611b\u3068\u9810\u8a00\u8005\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u30c8\u30eb\u30b3\u8a9e\u3067\u306f\u300cg\xfcl\uff08\u30d0\u30e9\uff09\u300d\u3068\u300cg\xf6n\xfcl\uff08\u5fc3\uff09\u300d\u304c\u3072\u3068\u606f\u306b\u8a9e\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3002\u30e6\u30cc\u30b9\u30fb\u30a8\u30e0\u30ec\u3084\u30eb\u30fc\u30df\u30fc\u306e\u8a69\u306b\u304a\u3044\u3066\u3001\u305d\u306e\u68d8\u306f\u8a66\u7df4\u3001\u305d\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306f\u697d\u5712\u3002\u8056\u5edf\u3084\u8ffd\u60bc\u3001\u5a5a\u793c\u3067\u307e\u304b\u308c\u308b\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30a6\u30a9\u30fc\u30bf\u30fc\u306f\u3001\u795d\u798f\u3068\u8d66\u3057\u306e\u9858\u3044\u3002\u53e4\u4ee3\u30d5\u30ea\u30ae\u30a2\u3084\u30ea\u30c7\u30a3\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u7f8e\u306e\u5973\u795e\u306b\u6367\u3052\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"A rosa \xe9 a flor sagrada da Anat\xf3lia. A \xe1gua e o \xf3leo de rosa destilados nos jardins de Isparta s\xe3o usados h\xe1 s\xe9culos para a cura e a purifica\xe7\xe3o. No sufismo, a rosa \xe9 o emblema do amor divino e do Profeta; em turco, 'g\xfcl' (rosa) e 'g\xf6n\xfcl' (cora\xe7\xe3o) dizem-se num mesmo f\xf4lego. Nos versos de Yunus Emre e Rumi, o seu espinho \xe9 a prova\xe7\xe3o, o seu aroma o para\xedso. A \xe1gua de rosas aspergida em santu\xe1rios, memoriais e casamentos \xe9 um desejo de b\xean\xe7\xe3o e perd\xe3o. Na antiga Fr\xedgia e L\xeddia, era oferecida \xe0s deusas da beleza."},{id:"plant-011",emoji:"\ud83e\udeb4",color:"#6BB58F",name:"Aloe Vera",nameEn:"Aloe Vera",nameDe:"Aloe Vera",nameEs:"Aloe Vera",nameFr:"Aloe Vera",nameJa:"\u30a2\u30ed\u30a8\u30d9\u30e9",namePt:"Babosa",origin:"Arap Yar\u0131madas\u0131",originEn:"Arabian Peninsula",originDe:"Arabische Halbinsel",originEs:"Pen\xednsula ar\xe1biga",originFr:"P\xe9ninsule arabique",originJa:"\u30a2\u30e9\u30d3\u30a2\u534a\u5cf6",originPt:"Pen\xednsula Ar\xe1bica",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["iyile\u015ftirici","koruyucu","serinletici"],propertiesEn:["healing","protective","cooling"],propertiesDe:["heilend","sch\xfctzend","k\xfchlend"],propertiesEs:["sanador","protector","refrescante"],propertiesFr:["gu\xe9risseur","protecteur","rafra\xeechissant"],propertiesJa:["\u7652\u3057","\u5b88\u8b77","\u51b7\u5374"],propertiesPt:["curativo","protetor","refrescante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn yaralar\u0131na nazik\xe7e dokun ve iyile\u015fmeye izin ver. Aloe vera sab\u0131rla onarman\u0131n ve kendine alan a\xe7man\u0131n g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, touch your wounds gently and allow healing. Aloe vera reminds you of the power of patient repair and making space for yourself.",dailyMessageDe:"Ber\xfchre heute deine Wunden sanft und erlaube die Heilung. Aloe Vera erinnert dich an die Kraft geduldiger Genesung und daran, dir Raum zu schaffen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, toca tus heridas con suavidad y permite la sanaci\xf3n. El aloe vera te recuerda el poder de la reparaci\xf3n paciente y de hacerte espacio.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, touche tes blessures avec douceur et permets la gu\xe9rison. L'aloe vera te rappelle le pouvoir d'une r\xe9paration patiente et de te faire de l'espace.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u50b7\u306b\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u3075\u308c\u3001\u7652\u3057\u3092\u8a31\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30a2\u30ed\u30a8\u30d9\u30e9\u306f\u3001\u8f9b\u62b1\u5f37\u3044\u4fee\u5fa9\u3068\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u4f59\u767d\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308b\u529b\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, toque suas feridas com suavidade e permita a cura. A babosa lembra voc\xea do poder do reparo paciente e de abrir espa\xe7o para si.",howToUse:"Yapra\u011f\u0131n\u0131n jelini g\xfcne\u015f yan\u0131\u011f\u0131 ya da kuru cilde nazik\xe7e s\xfcr. Sa\xe7 bak\u0131m\u0131nda ya da nemlendirici maske olarak kullanabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Gently apply the leaf gel to sunburn or dry skin. You can use it in hair care or as a moisturizing mask.",howToUseDe:"Trage das Blattgel sanft auf Sonnenbrand oder trockene Haut auf. Du kannst es in der Haarpflege oder als feuchtigkeitsspendende Maske verwenden.",howToUseEs:"Aplica suavemente el gel de la hoja sobre quemaduras solares o piel seca. Puedes usarlo en el cuidado del cabello o como mascarilla hidratante.",howToUseFr:"Applique doucement le gel de la feuille sur les coups de soleil ou la peau s\xe8che. Tu peux l'utiliser en soin capillaire ou en masque hydratant.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u306e\u30b8\u30a7\u30eb\u3092\u65e5\u713c\u3051\u3084\u4e7e\u3044\u305f\u808c\u306b\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5857\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d8\u30a2\u30b1\u30a2\u3084\u4fdd\u6e7f\u30de\u30b9\u30af\u3068\u3057\u3066\u4f7f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Aplique suavemente o gel da folha em queimaduras solares ou pele seca. Voc\xea pode us\xe1-lo no cuidado dos cabelos ou como m\xe1scara hidratante.",affirmation:"Kendime iyile\u015fmesi i\xe7in zaman ve \u015fefkat veriyorum.",affirmationEn:"I give myself time and compassion to heal.",affirmationDe:"Ich gebe mir Zeit und Mitgef\xfchl, um zu heilen.",affirmationEs:"Me doy tiempo y compasi\xf3n para sanar.",affirmationFr:"Je m'accorde du temps et de la compassion pour gu\xe9rir.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u7652\u3057\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306e\u6642\u9593\u3068\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Dou a mim mesmo tempo e compaix\xe3o para curar.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Aloe_vera_flower_inset.png/330px-Aloe_vera_flower_inset.png"},{id:"plant-012",emoji:"\ud83d\udda4",color:"#3C3A45",name:"\xc7\xf6rek Otu",nameEn:"Black Cumin",nameDe:"Schwarzk\xfcmmel",nameEs:"Comino negro",nameFr:"Cumin noir",nameJa:"\u30d6\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30af\u30df\u30f3",namePt:"Cominho-preto",origin:"G\xfcneybat\u0131 Asya",originEn:"Southwest Asia",originDe:"S\xfcdwestasien",originEs:"Suroeste de Asia",originFr:"Asie du Sud-Ouest",originJa:"\u5357\u897f\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Sudoeste da \xc1sia",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["g\xfc\xe7lendirici","koruyucu","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["strengthening","protective","resilience"],propertiesDe:["st\xe4rkend","sch\xfctzend","Widerstandskraft"],propertiesEs:["fortalecedor","protector","resiliencia"],propertiesFr:["fortifiant","protecteur","r\xe9silience"],propertiesJa:["\u5f37\u5316","\u5b88\u8b77","\u56de\u5fa9\u529b"],propertiesPt:["fortalecedor","protetor","resili\xeancia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn k\xf6klerine inan ve dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rla. \xc7\xf6rek otu k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir tohumun i\xe7inde b\xfcy\xfck bir g\xfc\xe7 ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, believe in your roots and remember your resilience. Black cumin whispers that a tiny seed carries great strength within.",dailyMessageDe:"Glaube heute an deine Wurzeln und erinnere dich an deine Widerstandskraft. Schwarzk\xfcmmel fl\xfcstert, dass ein winziges Samenkorn gro\xdfe Kraft in sich tr\xe4gt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, cree en tus ra\xedces y recuerda tu resiliencia. El comino negro susurra que una semilla diminuta lleva una gran fuerza dentro.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, crois en tes racines et souviens-toi de ta r\xe9silience. Le cumin noir murmure qu'une minuscule graine porte une grande force en elle.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u6839\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u3001\u56de\u5fa9\u529b\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d6\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30af\u30df\u30f3\u306f\u3001\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u7a2e\u304c\u5185\u306b\u5927\u304d\u306a\u529b\u3092\u79d8\u3081\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u3055\u3055\u3084\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, acredite nas suas ra\xedzes e lembre-se da sua resili\xeancia. O cominho-preto sussurra que uma pequena semente carrega uma grande for\xe7a dentro de si.",howToUse:"Tohumlar\u0131n\u0131 bala kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131rarak sabahlar\u0131 t\xfcket ya da ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 az miktarda kullan. \xc7orbaya ve ekme\u011fe serperek g\xfcnl\xfck rutinine kat.",howToUseEn:"Mix the seeds with honey in the morning, or use the oil sparingly. Sprinkle them over soup and bread to add to your daily routine.",howToUseDe:"Mische die Samen morgens mit Honig oder verwende das \xd6l sparsam. Streue sie \xfcber Suppe und Brot, um sie in deinen Alltag einzubauen.",howToUseEs:"Mezcla las semillas con miel por la ma\xf1ana, o usa el aceite con moderaci\xf3n. Esp\xe1rcelas sobre sopa y pan para sumarlas a tu rutina diaria.",howToUseFr:"M\xe9lange les graines avec du miel le matin, ou utilise l'huile avec mod\xe9ration. Pars\xe8mes-en sur la soupe et le pain pour les int\xe9grer \xe0 ta routine.",howToUseJa:"\u7a2e\u3092\u671d\u306b\u8702\u871c\u3068\u6df7\u305c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u6cb9\u3092\u5c11\u91cf\u4f7f\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b9\u30fc\u30d7\u3084\u30d1\u30f3\u306b\u632f\u308a\u304b\u3051\u3066\u65e5\u3005\u306e\u7fd2\u6163\u306b\u53d6\u308a\u5165\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Misture as sementes com mel pela manh\xe3, ou use o \xf3leo com modera\xe7\xe3o. Salpique-as sobre sopa e p\xe3o para incluir na rotina di\xe1ria.",affirmation:"K\xfc\xe7\xfck bir tohum gibi b\xfcy\xfck bir g\xfcc\xfc i\xe7imde ta\u015f\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"Like a tiny seed, I carry great strength within me.",affirmationDe:"Wie ein winziges Samenkorn trage ich gro\xdfe Kraft in mir.",affirmationEs:"Como una semilla diminuta, llevo una gran fuerza dentro de m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Comme une minuscule graine, je porte une grande force en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u7a2e\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u5927\u304d\u306a\u529b\u3092\u5185\u306b\u62b1\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Como uma pequena semente, carrego uma grande for\xe7a dentro de mim.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Nsativa001Wien.jpg/330px-Nsativa001Wien.jpg"},{id:"plant-013",emoji:"\ud83d\udfe1",color:"#E6A817",name:"Zerde\xe7al",nameEn:"Turmeric",nameDe:"Kurkuma",nameEs:"C\xfarcuma",nameFr:"Curcuma",nameJa:"\u30bf\u30fc\u30e1\u30ea\u30c3\u30af",namePt:"A\xe7afr\xe3o-da-terra",origin:"G\xfcney Asya, Hindistan",originEn:"South Asia, India",originDe:"S\xfcdasien, Indien",originEs:"Sur de Asia, India",originFr:"Asie du Sud, Inde",originJa:"\u5357\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9",originPt:"Sul da \xc1sia, \xcdndia",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","s\u0131cakl\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["invigorating","purifying","warmth"],propertiesDe:["belebend","reinigend","W\xe4rme"],propertiesEs:["vigorizante","purificante","calidez"],propertiesFr:["tonifiant","purifiant","chaleur"],propertiesJa:["\u6d3b\u6027","\u6d44\u5316","\u6e29\u3082\u308a"],propertiesPt:["revigorante","purificante","aconchego"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn i\xe7indeki ate\u015fi nazik\xe7e yak. Zerde\xe7al sana alt\u0131n renkli enerjini, g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc ve canl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, gently kindle the fire within. Turmeric reminds you of your golden energy, your power and vitality.",dailyMessageDe:"Entfache heute sanft das Feuer in dir. Kurkuma erinnert dich an deine goldene Energie, deine Kraft und Vitalit\xe4t.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, enciende con suavidad el fuego interior. La c\xfarcuma te recuerda tu energ\xeda dorada, tu poder y vitalidad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, allume doucement le feu int\xe9rieur. Le curcuma te rappelle ton \xe9nergie dor\xe9e, ta force et ta vitalit\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u706b\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u706f\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30bf\u30fc\u30e1\u30ea\u30c3\u30af\u306f\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc\u3001\u529b\u3001\u305d\u3057\u3066\u751f\u547d\u529b\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, acenda com suavidade o fogo interior. O a\xe7afr\xe3o-da-terra lembra voc\xea da sua energia dourada, do seu poder e vitalidade.",howToUse:"Bir tutam\u0131n\u0131 \u0131l\u0131k s\xfcte ve bala katarak alt\u0131n s\xfct olarak i\xe7. Yemeklerine ekleyerek g\xfcnl\xfck s\u0131cakl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 koru.",howToUseEn:"Stir a pinch into warm milk with honey for a golden latte. Add it to your meals to keep your daily warmth.",howToUseDe:"R\xfchre eine Prise in warme Milch mit Honig f\xfcr eine goldene Milch. Gib es in deine Mahlzeiten, um deine t\xe4gliche W\xe4rme zu bewahren.",howToUseEs:"Mezcla una pizca en leche tibia con miel para una leche dorada. A\xf1\xe1dela a tus comidas para conservar tu calidez diaria.",howToUseFr:"M\xe9lange une pinc\xe9e dans du lait chaud avec du miel pour un lait d'or. Ajoute-le \xe0 tes repas pour garder ta chaleur quotidienne.",howToUseJa:"\u3072\u3068\u3064\u307e\u307f\u3092\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u30df\u30eb\u30af\u3068\u8702\u871c\u306b\u6df7\u305c\u3066\u30b4\u30fc\u30eb\u30c7\u30f3\u30df\u30eb\u30af\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3066\u65e5\u3005\u306e\u6e29\u3082\u308a\u3092\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Misture uma pitada no leite morno com mel para um leite dourado. Adicione \xe0s refei\xe7\xf5es para manter o aconchego di\xe1rio.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7imdeki alt\u0131n \u0131\u015f\u0131k parl\u0131yor, canl\u0131l\u0131kla doluyum.",affirmationEn:"The golden light within me shines; I am full of vitality.",affirmationDe:"Das goldene Licht in mir leuchtet; ich bin voller Vitalit\xe4t.",affirmationEs:"La luz dorada en m\xed brilla; estoy lleno de vitalidad.",affirmationFr:"La lumi\xe8re dor\xe9e en moi brille ; je suis plein de vitalit\xe9.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306e\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u5149\u304c\u8f1d\u304f\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u751f\u547d\u529b\u306b\u6e80\u3061\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"A luz dourada dentro de mim brilha; estou cheio de vitalidade.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Turmeric_inflorescence.jpg/330px-Turmeric_inflorescence.jpg"},{id:"plant-014",emoji:"\ud83e\udeda",color:"#D8A45B",name:"Zencefil",nameEn:"Ginger",nameDe:"Ingwer",nameEs:"Jengibre",nameFr:"Gingembre",nameJa:"\u30b8\u30f3\u30b8\u30e3\u30fc",namePt:"Gengibre",origin:"G\xfcneydo\u011fu Asya",originEn:"Southeast Asia",originDe:"S\xfcdostasien",originEs:"Sudeste asi\xe1tico",originFr:"Asie du Sud-Est",originJa:"\u6771\u5357\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Sudeste Asi\xe1tico",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["\u0131s\u0131t\u0131c\u0131","canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","cesaret"],propertiesEn:["warming","invigorating","courage"],propertiesDe:["w\xe4rmend","belebend","Mut"],propertiesEs:["caliente","vigorizante","valor"],propertiesFr:["r\xe9chauffant","tonifiant","courage"],propertiesJa:["\u6e29\u3081","\u6d3b\u6027","\u52c7\u6c17"],propertiesPt:["aquecedor","revigorante","coragem"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn i\xe7indeki ate\u015fi harekete ge\xe7ir ve cesaretle harekete ge\xe7. Zencefil dura\u011fanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 da\u011f\u0131t\u0131r, seni canl\u0131 ve at\u0131lgan k\u0131lar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, stir the fire within and act with courage. Ginger scatters stagnation and makes you alive and bold.",dailyMessageDe:"Entfache heute das Feuer in dir und handle mit Mut. Ingwer zerstreut Stillstand und macht dich lebendig und k\xfchn.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, aviva el fuego interior y act\xfaa con valor. El jengibre dispersa el estancamiento y te vuelve vivo y audaz.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, attise le feu int\xe9rieur et agis avec courage. Le gingembre disperse la stagnation et te rend vivant et audacieux.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u706b\u3092\u304b\u304d\u7acb\u3066\u3001\u52c7\u6c17\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u52d5\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b8\u30f3\u30b8\u30e3\u30fc\u306f\u505c\u6ede\u3092\u6563\u3089\u3057\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u751f\u304d\u751f\u304d\u3068\u5927\u80c6\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, atice o fogo interior e aja com coragem. O gengibre dispersa a estagna\xe7\xe3o e torna voc\xea vivo e ousado.",howToUse:"Taze k\xf6k\xfcni rendeleyip s\u0131cak suda demle, bal ve limonla i\xe7. So\u011fuk g\xfcnlerde ba\u011f\u0131\u015f\u0131kl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ve s\u0131cakl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 destekle.",howToUseEn:"Grate the fresh root, brew it in hot water, and drink with honey and lemon. Support your warmth and immunity on cold days.",howToUseDe:"Reibe die frische Wurzel, br\xfche sie in hei\xdfem Wasser auf und trinke sie mit Honig und Zitrone. Unterst\xfctze an kalten Tagen deine W\xe4rme und Abwehr.",howToUseEs:"Ralla la ra\xedz fresca, inf\xfandela en agua caliente y b\xe9bela con miel y lim\xf3n. Apoya tu calidez e inmunidad en d\xedas fr\xedos.",howToUseFr:"R\xe2pe la racine fra\xeeche, infuse-la dans de l'eau chaude et bois avec du miel et du citron. Soutiens ta chaleur et ton immunit\xe9 les jours froids.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u6839\u3092\u3059\u308a\u304a\u308d\u3057\u3001\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u8702\u871c\u3068\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u3067\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5bd2\u3044\u65e5\u306b\u6e29\u3082\u308a\u3068\u514d\u75ab\u3092\u652f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Rale a raiz fresca, prepare-a em \xe1gua quente e beba com mel e lim\xe3o. Apoie seu aconchego e imunidade nos dias frios.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7imdeki ate\u015f canl\u0131, cesaretle harekete ge\xe7iyorum.",affirmationEn:"The fire within me is alive; I act with courage.",affirmationDe:"Das Feuer in mir ist lebendig; ich handle mit Mut.",affirmationEs:"El fuego en m\xed est\xe1 vivo; act\xfao con valor.",affirmationFr:"Le feu en moi est vivant ; j'agis avec courage.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306e\u706b\u306f\u751f\u304d\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u52c7\u6c17\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u52d5\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"O fogo dentro de mim est\xe1 vivo; eu ajo com coragem.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Koeh-146-no_text.jpg/330px-Koeh-146-no_text.jpg"},{id:"plant-015",emoji:"\ud83e\uddc4",color:"#E8E0CF",name:"Sar\u0131msak",nameEn:"Garlic",nameDe:"Knoblauch",nameEs:"Ajo",nameFr:"Ail",nameJa:"\u30ac\u30fc\u30ea\u30c3\u30af",namePt:"Alho",origin:"Orta Asya",originEn:"Central Asia",originDe:"Zentralasien",originEs:"Asia Central",originFr:"Asie centrale",originJa:"\u4e2d\u592e\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"\xc1sia Central",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["koruyucu","g\xfc\xe7lendirici","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["protective","strengthening","purifying"],propertiesDe:["sch\xfctzend","st\xe4rkend","reinigend"],propertiesEs:["protector","fortalecedor","purificante"],propertiesFr:["protecteur","fortifiant","purifiant"],propertiesJa:["\u5b88\u8b77","\u5f37\u5316","\u6d44\u5316"],propertiesPt:["protetor","fortalecedor","purificante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 koru ve kendine sahip \xe7\u0131k. Sar\u0131msak y\xfczy\u0131llard\u0131r koruma sembol\xfc olmu\u015ftur; sen de kendi alan\u0131n\u0131 savunabilirsin.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, guard your boundaries and stand up for yourself. Garlic has been a symbol of protection for centuries; you too can defend your space.",dailyMessageDe:"Sch\xfctze heute deine Grenzen und steh f\xfcr dich ein. Knoblauch ist seit Jahrhunderten ein Symbol des Schutzes; auch du kannst deinen Raum verteidigen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, protege tus l\xedmites y defi\xe9ndete. El ajo ha sido s\xedmbolo de protecci\xf3n durante siglos; t\xfa tambi\xe9n puedes defender tu espacio.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, prot\xe8ge tes limites et d\xe9fends-toi. L'ail est un symbole de protection depuis des si\xe8cles ; toi aussi tu peux d\xe9fendre ton espace.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5883\u754c\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u7acb\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ac\u30fc\u30ea\u30c3\u30af\u306f\u4f55\u4e16\u7d00\u3082\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u9818\u57df\u3092\u5b88\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, proteja seus limites e defenda-se. O alho \xe9 s\xedmbolo de prote\xe7\xe3o h\xe1 s\xe9culos; voc\xea tamb\xe9m pode defender o seu espa\xe7o.",howToUse:"\xc7i\u011f olarak az miktarda t\xfcket ya da yemeklerine ekle. So\u011fuk alg\u0131nl\u0131\u011f\u0131nda bal ile kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131rarak ba\u011f\u0131\u015f\u0131kl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 destekle.",howToUseEn:"Eat a small amount raw or add it to your meals. Mix it with honey during a cold to support your immunity.",howToUseDe:"Iss eine kleine Menge roh oder gib es in deine Mahlzeiten. Mische es bei einer Erk\xe4ltung mit Honig, um deine Abwehr zu unterst\xfctzen.",howToUseEs:"Come una peque\xf1a cantidad cruda o a\xf1\xe1delo a tus comidas. M\xe9zclalo con miel durante un resfriado para apoyar tu inmunidad.",howToUseFr:"Mange une petite quantit\xe9 crue ou ajoute-le \xe0 tes repas. M\xe9lange-le avec du miel en cas de rhume pour soutenir ton immunit\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u5c11\u91cf\u3092\u751f\u3067\u98df\u3079\u308b\u304b\u3001\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u98a8\u90aa\u306e\u3068\u304d\u306f\u8702\u871c\u3068\u6df7\u305c\u3066\u514d\u75ab\u3092\u652f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Coma uma pequena quantidade crua ou adicione \xe0s refei\xe7\xf5es. Misture com mel durante um resfriado para apoiar a imunidade.",affirmation:"S\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131m\u0131 koruyorum, kendi alan\u0131mda g\xfc\xe7l\xfcy\xfcm.",affirmationEn:"I protect my boundaries; I am strong in my own space.",affirmationDe:"Ich sch\xfctze meine Grenzen; ich bin stark in meinem eigenen Raum.",affirmationEs:"Protejo mis l\xedmites; soy fuerte en mi propio espacio.",affirmationFr:"Je prot\xe8ge mes limites ; je suis fort dans mon propre espace.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5883\u754c\u3092\u5b88\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u9818\u57df\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u5f37\u3044\u3002",affirmationPt:"Eu protejo meus limites; sou forte no meu pr\xf3prio espa\xe7o.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/39/Allium_sativum_Woodwill_1793.jpg"},{id:"plant-016",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#6E9A6B",name:"Ginkgo",nameEn:"Ginkgo",nameDe:"Ginkgo",nameEs:"Ginkgo",nameFr:"Ginkgo",nameJa:"\u30a4\u30c1\u30e7\u30a6",namePt:"Ginkgo",origin:"\xc7in",originEn:"China",originDe:"China",originEs:"China",originFr:"Chine",originJa:"\u4e2d\u56fd",originPt:"China",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["uzun \xf6m\xfcr","haf\u0131za","bilgelik"],propertiesEn:["longevity","memory","wisdom"],propertiesDe:["Langlebigkeit","Ged\xe4chtnis","Weisheit"],propertiesEs:["longevidad","memoria","sabidur\xeda"],propertiesFr:["long\xe9vit\xe9","m\xe9moire","sagesse"],propertiesJa:["\u9577\u5bff","\u8a18\u61b6","\u77e5\u6075"],propertiesPt:["longevidade","mem\xf3ria","sabedoria"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn zaman\u0131n ak\u0131\u015f\u0131na sayg\u0131 duy ve sab\u0131rla b\xfcy\xfc. Ginkgo milyonlarca y\u0131ld\u0131r var olan bir a\u011fa\xe7t\u0131r; sana dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve s\xfcreklili\u011fin g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, honor the flow of time and grow with patience. Ginkgo is a tree that has existed for millions of years; it reminds you of the power of endurance and continuity.",dailyMessageDe:"Ehre heute den Fluss der Zeit und wachse mit Geduld. Ginkgo ist ein Baum, der seit Millionen Jahren existiert; er erinnert dich an die Kraft von Ausdauer und Kontinuit\xe4t.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, honra el fluir del tiempo y crece con paciencia. El ginkgo es un \xe1rbol que existe desde hace millones de a\xf1os; te recuerda el poder de la resistencia y la continuidad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, honore le flux du temps et grandis avec patience. Le ginkgo est un arbre qui existe depuis des millions d'ann\xe9es ; il te rappelle le pouvoir de l'endurance et de la continuit\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u6642\u306e\u6d41\u308c\u3092\u656c\u3044\u3001\u8f9b\u62b1\u5f37\u304f\u80b2\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30a4\u30c1\u30e7\u30a6\u306f\u4f55\u767e\u4e07\u5e74\u3082\u5b58\u5728\u3057\u3066\u304d\u305f\u6728\u3067\u3059\u3002\u305d\u308c\u306f\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u7d99\u7d9a\u306e\u529b\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, honre o fluxo do tempo e cres\xe7a com paci\xeancia. O ginkgo \xe9 uma \xe1rvore que existe h\xe1 milh\xf5es de anos; ele lembra voc\xea do poder da resist\xeancia e da continuidade.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle. D\xfczenli kullan\u0131mda zihinsel berrakl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 desteklemek i\xe7in \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc t\xfcket.",howToUseEn:"Lightly brew the dried leaves as a tea. Use it in moderation to support your mental clarity over time.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die getrockneten Bl\xe4tter leicht als Tee. Verwende ihn in Ma\xdfen, um deine geistige Klarheit langfristig zu unterst\xfctzen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona ligeramente las hojas secas como t\xe9. \xdasalo con moderaci\xf3n para apoyar tu claridad mental con el tiempo.",howToUseFr:"Infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les feuilles s\xe9ch\xe9es en tisane. Utilise-le avec mod\xe9ration pour soutenir ta clart\xe9 mentale dans le temps.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u8449\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306b\u4f7f\u3044\u3001\u6642\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u7cbe\u795e\u306e\u660e\u6670\u3055\u3092\u652f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare levemente as folhas secas como ch\xe1. Use com modera\xe7\xe3o para apoiar sua clareza mental ao longo do tempo.",affirmation:"Sab\u0131rla b\xfcy\xfcyorum, zaman\u0131n bilgeli\u011fine g\xfcveniyorum.",affirmationEn:"I grow with patience and trust the wisdom of time.",affirmationDe:"Ich wachse mit Geduld und vertraue der Weisheit der Zeit.",affirmationEs:"Crezco con paciencia y conf\xedo en la sabidur\xeda del tiempo.",affirmationFr:"Je grandis avec patience et fais confiance \xe0 la sagesse du temps.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u8f9b\u62b1\u5f37\u304f\u80b2\u3061\u3001\u6642\u306e\u77e5\u6075\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3059\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Eu cres\xe7o com paci\xeancia e confio na sabedoria do tempo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/GINKGOBAUM-2.jpg/330px-GINKGOBAUM-2.jpg"},{id:"plant-017",emoji:"\ud83c\udf1f",color:"#E3C04B",name:"Sar\u0131 Kantaron",nameEn:"St John's Wort",nameDe:"Johanniskraut",nameEs:"Hierba de San Juan",nameFr:"Millepertuis",nameJa:"\u30bb\u30f3\u30c8\u30b8\u30e7\u30fc\u30f3\u30ba\u30ef\u30fc\u30c8",namePt:"Erva-de-s\xe3o-jo\xe3o",origin:"Avrupa, Anadolu",originEn:"Europe, Anatolia",originDe:"Europa, Anatolien",originEs:"Europa, Anatolia",originFr:"Europe, Anatolie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, Anat\xf3lia",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["g\xfcne\u015f \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131","umut","ayd\u0131nlat\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["sunlight","hope","brightening"],propertiesDe:["Sonnenlicht","Hoffnung","aufhellend"],propertiesEs:["luz solar","esperanza","iluminador"],propertiesFr:["lumi\xe8re solaire","espoir","\xe9claircissant"],propertiesJa:["\u967d\u5149","\u5e0c\u671b","\u660e\u308b\u304f\u3059\u308b"],propertiesPt:["luz solar","esperan\xe7a","iluminador"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn karanl\u0131k anlarda bile i\xe7indeki \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131 ara. Sar\u0131 kantaron g\xfcne\u015fin enerjisini ta\u015f\u0131r, ruhuna umut ve ayd\u0131nl\u0131k getirir.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, look for the light within even in dark moments. St John's wort carries the sun's energy, bringing hope and brightness to your spirit.",dailyMessageDe:"Suche heute auch in dunklen Momenten das Licht in dir. Johanniskraut tr\xe4gt die Energie der Sonne und bringt Hoffnung und Helligkeit in deine Seele.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, busca la luz interior incluso en los momentos oscuros. La hierba de San Juan lleva la energ\xeda del sol, trayendo esperanza y luz a tu esp\xedritu.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, cherche la lumi\xe8re en toi m\xeame dans les moments sombres. Le millepertuis porte l'\xe9nergie du soleil, apportant espoir et clart\xe9 \xe0 ton esprit.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u6697\u3044\u3068\u304d\u3067\u3082\u5185\u306a\u308b\u5149\u3092\u63a2\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30bb\u30f3\u30c8\u30b8\u30e7\u30fc\u30f3\u30ba\u30ef\u30fc\u30c8\u306f\u592a\u967d\u306e\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc\u3092\u5bbf\u3057\u3001\u9b42\u306b\u5e0c\u671b\u3068\u660e\u308b\u3055\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, procure a luz interior mesmo nos momentos escuros. A erva-de-s\xe3o-jo\xe3o carrega a energia do sol, trazendo esperan\xe7a e luz ao seu esp\xedrito.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle. Ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 cilt bak\u0131m\u0131nda kullanabilirsin; ila\xe7 kullan\u0131yorsan \xf6nce uzmana dan\u0131\u015f.",howToUseEn:"Lightly brew the flowers as a tea. You can use the oil in skin care; if you take medication, consult a professional first.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten leicht als Tee. Du kannst das \xd6l in der Hautpflege verwenden; wenn du Medikamente nimmst, frage zuerst eine Fachperson.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona ligeramente las flores como t\xe9. Puedes usar el aceite en el cuidado de la piel; si tomas medicaci\xf3n, consulta antes a un profesional.",howToUseFr:"Infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les fleurs en tisane. Tu peux utiliser l'huile en soin de la peau ; si tu prends des m\xe9dicaments, consulte d'abord un professionnel.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6cb9\u306f\u30b9\u30ad\u30f3\u30b1\u30a2\u306b\u4f7f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002\u85ac\u3092\u670d\u7528\u4e2d\u306a\u3089\u3001\u307e\u305a\u5c02\u9580\u5bb6\u306b\u76f8\u8ac7\u3092\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare levemente as flores como ch\xe1. Voc\xea pode usar o \xf3leo no cuidado da pele; se toma medica\xe7\xe3o, consulte um profissional antes.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7imde g\xfcne\u015f gibi bir \u0131\u015f\u0131k ta\u015f\u0131yorum, umut hep benimle.",affirmationEn:"I carry a sun-like light within me; hope is always with me.",affirmationDe:"Ich trage ein sonnengleiches Licht in mir; Hoffnung ist stets bei mir.",affirmationEs:"Llevo una luz solar dentro de m\xed; la esperanza siempre me acompa\xf1a.",affirmationFr:"Je porte une lumi\xe8re solaire en moi ; l'espoir est toujours avec moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u592a\u967d\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306a\u5149\u3092\u5185\u306b\u62b1\u304f\u3002\u5e0c\u671b\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u79c1\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Carrego uma luz solar dentro de mim; a esperan\xe7a est\xe1 sempre comigo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/%28MHNT%29_Hypericum_perforatum_flower_and_buttons.jpg/330px-%28MHNT%29_Hypericum_perforatum_flower_and_buttons.jpg"},{id:"plant-018",emoji:"\ud83c\udf38",color:"#D17AA8",name:"Ekinezya",nameEn:"Echinacea",nameDe:"Echinacea",nameEs:"Equin\xe1cea",nameFr:"\xc9chinac\xe9e",nameJa:"\u30a8\u30ad\u30ca\u30bb\u30a2",namePt:"Equin\xe1cea",origin:"Kuzey Amerika",originEn:"North America",originDe:"Nordamerika",originEs:"Am\xe9rica del Norte",originFr:"Am\xe9rique du Nord",originJa:"\u5317\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Am\xe9rica do Norte",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["g\xfc\xe7lendirici","koruyucu","diren\xe7"],propertiesEn:["strengthening","protective","resistance"],propertiesDe:["st\xe4rkend","sch\xfctzend","Widerstand"],propertiesEs:["fortalecedor","protector","resistencia"],propertiesFr:["fortifiant","protecteur","r\xe9sistance"],propertiesJa:["\u5f37\u5316","\u5b88\u8b77","\u62b5\u6297\u529b"],propertiesPt:["fortalecedor","protetor","resist\xeancia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kendi savunma g\xfcc\xfcne g\xfcven. Ekinezya i\xe7 direncini destekler, zorluklar kar\u015f\u0131s\u0131nda dayan\u0131kl\u0131 kalman\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, trust your own defenses. Echinacea supports your inner resistance and reminds you to stay resilient in the face of difficulty.",dailyMessageDe:"Vertraue heute deinen eigenen Abwehrkr\xe4ften. Echinacea unterst\xfctzt deinen inneren Widerstand und erinnert dich, in Schwierigkeiten widerstandsf\xe4hig zu bleiben.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, conf\xeda en tus propias defensas. La equin\xe1cea apoya tu resistencia interior y te recuerda mantenerte fuerte ante la dificultad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, fais confiance \xe0 tes propres d\xe9fenses. L'\xe9chinac\xe9e soutient ta r\xe9sistance int\xe9rieure et te rappelle de rester r\xe9silient face \xe0 la difficult\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u9632\u5fa1\u529b\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30a8\u30ad\u30ca\u30bb\u30a2\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u62b5\u6297\u529b\u3092\u652f\u3048\u3001\u56f0\u96e3\u306e\u524d\u3067\u3082\u5f37\u304f\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, confie nas suas pr\xf3prias defesas. A equin\xe1cea apoia sua resist\xeancia interior e lembra voc\xea de se manter resiliente diante da dificuldade.",howToUse:"K\xf6k\xfcn\xfc ya da \xe7i\xe7e\u011fini \xe7ay olarak demle, \xf6zellikle mevsim ge\xe7i\u015flerinde t\xfcket. Tent\xfcr\xfcn\xfc \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc kullanarak ba\u011f\u0131\u015f\u0131kl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 destekle.",howToUseEn:"Brew the root or flower as a tea, especially during seasonal changes. Use the tincture in moderation to support your immunity.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Wurzel oder Bl\xfcte als Tee, besonders bei Jahreszeitenwechseln. Verwende die Tinktur in Ma\xdfen, um deine Abwehr zu unterst\xfctzen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona la ra\xedz o la flor como t\xe9, sobre todo en los cambios de estaci\xf3n. Usa la tintura con moderaci\xf3n para apoyar tu inmunidad.",howToUseFr:"Infuse la racine ou la fleur en tisane, surtout lors des changements de saison. Utilise la teinture avec mod\xe9ration pour soutenir ton immunit\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u6839\u3084\u82b1\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u7279\u306b\u5b63\u7bc0\u306e\u5909\u308f\u308a\u76ee\u306b\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30c1\u30f3\u30ad\u306f\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306b\u4f7f\u3044\u3001\u514d\u75ab\u3092\u652f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare a raiz ou a flor como ch\xe1, especialmente nas mudan\xe7as de esta\xe7\xe3o. Use a tintura com modera\xe7\xe3o para apoiar a imunidade.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7 g\xfcc\xfcm beni koruyor, dayan\u0131kl\u0131 ve sa\u011flam\u0131m.",affirmationEn:"My inner strength protects me; I am resilient and sound.",affirmationDe:"Meine innere St\xe4rke sch\xfctzt mich; ich bin widerstandsf\xe4hig und gesund.",affirmationEs:"Mi fuerza interior me protege; soy resiliente y s\xf3lido.",affirmationFr:"Ma force int\xe9rieure me prot\xe8ge ; je suis r\xe9silient et solide.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u5185\u306a\u308b\u529b\u304c\u79c1\u3092\u5b88\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u5f37\u304f\u5065\u3084\u304b\u3060\u3002",affirmationPt:"Minha for\xe7a interior me protege; sou resiliente e firme.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/EchinaceaPurpureaMaxima1a.UME.JPG/330px-EchinaceaPurpureaMaxima1a.UME.JPG"},{id:"plant-019",emoji:"\ud83e\udd0d",color:"#EDEDE0",name:"Civanper\xe7emi",nameEn:"Yarrow",nameDe:"Schafgarbe",nameEs:"Milenrama",nameFr:"Achill\xe9e",nameJa:"\u30e4\u30ed\u30a6",namePt:"Mil-folhas",origin:"Avrupa, Asya",originEn:"Europe, Asia",originDe:"Europa, Asien",originEs:"Europa, Asia",originFr:"Europe, Asie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["koruyucu","s\u0131n\u0131r koyucu","iyile\u015ftirici"],propertiesEn:["protective","boundary-setting","healing"],propertiesDe:["sch\xfctzend","Grenzen setzend","heilend"],propertiesEs:["protector","establece l\xedmites","sanador"],propertiesFr:["protecteur","pose des limites","gu\xe9risseur"],propertiesJa:["\u5b88\u8b77","\u5883\u754c\u3092\u5f15\u304f","\u7652\u3057"],propertiesPt:["protetor","define limites","curativo"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn enerjini koru ve nazik\xe7e s\u0131n\u0131r \xe7iz. Civanper\xe7emi ba\u015fkalar\u0131n\u0131n y\xfck\xfcne kap\u0131lmadan \u015fefkatli kalman\u0131 destekler.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, protect your energy and set gentle boundaries. Yarrow supports you in staying compassionate without absorbing others' burdens.",dailyMessageDe:"Sch\xfctze heute deine Energie und setze sanfte Grenzen. Schafgarbe hilft dir, mitf\xfchlend zu bleiben, ohne die Lasten anderer aufzunehmen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, protege tu energ\xeda y pon l\xedmites suaves. La milenrama te ayuda a permanecer compasivo sin absorber las cargas de otros.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, prot\xe8ge ton \xe9nergie et pose des limites douces. L'achill\xe9e t'aide \xe0 rester compatissant sans absorber les fardeaux des autres.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3001\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5883\u754c\u3092\u5f15\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30e4\u30ed\u30a6\u306f\u3001\u4ed6\u8005\u306e\u91cd\u8377\u3092\u5438\u3044\u8fbc\u307e\u305a\u306b\u601d\u3044\u3084\u308a\u3092\u4fdd\u3064\u624b\u52a9\u3051\u3092\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, proteja sua energia e estabele\xe7a limites gentis. A mil-folhas ajuda voc\xea a permanecer compassivo sem absorver os fardos dos outros.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak demle ya da bir demetini koruma niyetiyle \xe7al\u0131\u015fma alan\u0131na as. Banyo suyuna ekleyerek ar\u0131nma rit\xfceli yap.",howToUseEn:"Brew the flowers as a tea, or hang a bundle in your workspace with an intention of protection. Add it to your bath for a cleansing ritual.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten als Tee oder h\xe4nge ein B\xfcndel mit Schutzabsicht in deinen Arbeitsbereich. Gib es ins Bad f\xfcr ein Reinigungsritual.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las flores como t\xe9, o cuelga un manojo en tu espacio de trabajo con intenci\xf3n de protecci\xf3n. A\xf1\xe1delo al ba\xf1o para un ritual de limpieza.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fleurs en tisane, ou suspends un bouquet dans ton espace de travail avec une intention de protection. Ajoute-le au bain pour un rituel de purification.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3067\u675f\u3092\u4f5c\u696d\u5834\u306b\u540a\u308b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5165\u6d74\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3066\u6d44\u5316\u306e\u5100\u5f0f\u3092\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores como ch\xe1, ou pendure um ma\xe7o no seu espa\xe7o de trabalho com a inten\xe7\xe3o de prote\xe7\xe3o. Adicione ao banho para um ritual de limpeza.",affirmation:"Sevecen kal\u0131rken kendi enerjimi koruyorum.",affirmationEn:"I stay loving while protecting my own energy.",affirmationDe:"Ich bleibe liebevoll und sch\xfctze zugleich meine eigene Energie.",affirmationEs:"Permanezco amoroso mientras protejo mi propia energ\xeda.",affirmationFr:"Je reste aimant tout en prot\xe9geant ma propre \xe9nergie.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u611b\u60c5\u6df1\u304f\u3042\u308a\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc\u3092\u5b88\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Permane\xe7o amoroso enquanto protejo a minha pr\xf3pria energia.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Achillea_millefolium_%28bright%29.jpg/330px-Achillea_millefolium_%28bright%29.jpg",myth:"Civanper\xe7emi, yaralar\u0131n ve s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n otudur. Bilimsel ad\u0131 'Achillea', kahraman Akhilleus'tan gelir; mitte Truva sava\u015f\u0131nda askerlerin yaralar\u0131n\u0131 bu otla sarar. Anadolu halk hekimli\u011finde kan\u0131 durdurmas\u0131, yaray\u0131 iyile\u015ftirmesiyle bilinir. Saplar\u0131 antik \xc7in'de I Ching kehanetinde kullan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131 \u2014 gelece\u011fe k\xf6pr\xfc. Koruyucu ve cesaret verici; s\u0131n\u0131r \xe7izmenin, kendini koruyarak \u015fefkatli kalman\u0131n dersidir.",mythEn:"Yarrow is the herb of wounds and boundaries. Its botanical name 'Achillea' comes from the hero Achilles; in the myth he binds his soldiers' wounds with it in the Trojan War. In Anatolian folk medicine it is known for staunching blood and healing wounds. Its stalks were used in the I Ching divination of ancient China \u2014 a bridge to what is to come. Protective and courage-giving, it is the lesson of drawing a boundary, of staying compassionate while keeping oneself safe.",mythDe:"Schafgarbe ist das Kraut der Wunden und Grenzen. Ihr botanischer Name 'Achillea' kommt vom Helden Achilles; im Mythos verbindet er damit im Trojanischen Krieg die Wunden seiner Soldaten. In der anatolischen Volksmedizin ist sie bekannt daf\xfcr, Blut zu stillen und Wunden zu heilen. Ihre St\xe4ngel dienten im alten China der I-Ging-Weissagung \u2014 eine Br\xfccke zum Kommenden. Sch\xfctzend und mutspendend, lehrt sie, eine Grenze zu ziehen und mitf\xfchlend zu bleiben, w\xe4hrend man sich selbst bewahrt.",mythEs:"La milenrama es la hierba de las heridas y los l\xedmites. Su nombre bot\xe1nico 'Achillea' viene del h\xe9roe Aquiles; en el mito venda con ella las heridas de sus soldados en la guerra de Troya. En la medicina popular de Anatolia se la conoce por detener la sangre y sanar heridas. Sus tallos se usaban en la adivinaci\xf3n del I Ching de la antigua China \u2014 un puente hacia lo por venir. Protectora y dadora de valor, ense\xf1a a trazar un l\xedmite, a permanecer compasivo mientras uno se cuida.",mythFr:"L'achill\xe9e est l'herbe des blessures et des limites. Son nom botanique 'Achillea' vient du h\xe9ros Achille ; dans le mythe, il en bande les plaies de ses soldats lors de la guerre de Troie. Dans la m\xe9decine populaire d'Anatolie, elle est connue pour arr\xeater le sang et gu\xe9rir les plaies. Ses tiges servaient \xe0 la divination du Yi King dans la Chine antique \u2014 un pont vers ce qui vient. Protectrice et donneuse de courage, elle enseigne \xe0 tracer une limite, \xe0 rester compatissant tout en se pr\xe9servant.",mythJa:"\u30ce\u30b3\u30ae\u30ea\u30bd\u30a6\u306f\u50b7\u3068\u5883\u754c\u306e\u8349\u3002\u5b66\u540d\u300c\u30a2\u30ad\u30ec\u30a2\u300d\u306f\u82f1\u96c4\u30a2\u30ad\u30ec\u30a6\u30b9\u306b\u7531\u6765\u3057\u3001\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u30c8\u30ed\u30a4\u30a2\u6226\u4e89\u3067\u5175\u58eb\u306e\u50b7\u3092\u3053\u306e\u8349\u3067\u5305\u3080\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u6c11\u9593\u533b\u7642\u3067\u306f\u6b62\u8840\u3068\u50b7\u306e\u6cbb\u7652\u3067\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3002\u305d\u306e\u830e\u306f\u53e4\u4ee3\u4e2d\u56fd\u306e\u6613\u7d4c\u306e\u5360\u3044\u306b\u7528\u3044\u3089\u308c\u305f\u2014\u2014\u6765\u305f\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3078\u306e\u6a4b\u3002\u5b88\u308a\u3068\u52c7\u6c17\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u3001\u81ea\u3089\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3064\u3064\u6148\u3057\u307f\u3092\u4fdd\u3061\u3001\u5883\u754c\u3092\u5f15\u304f\u6559\u3048\u3002",mythPt:"A milef\xf3lio \xe9 a erva das feridas e dos limites. O seu nome bot\xe2nico 'Achillea' vem do her\xf3i Aquiles; no mito, ele liga com ela as feridas dos seus soldados na guerra de Troia. Na medicina popular da Anat\xf3lia \xe9 conhecida por estancar o sangue e curar feridas. Os seus caules eram usados na adivinha\xe7\xe3o do I Ching da China antiga \u2014 uma ponte para o que est\xe1 para vir. Protetora e dadora de coragem, ensina a tra\xe7ar um limite, a permanecer compassivo enquanto se mant\xe9m a salvo."},{id:"plant-020",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3a",color:"#E8A6C0",name:"Hatmi",nameEn:"Marshmallow",nameDe:"Eibisch",nameEs:"Malvavisco",nameFr:"Guimauve",nameJa:"\u30de\u30b7\u30e5\u30de\u30ed\u30a6",namePt:"Malva\xedsco",origin:"Avrupa, Bat\u0131 Asya",originEn:"Europe, Western Asia",originDe:"Europa, Westasien",originEs:"Europa, Asia Occidental",originFr:"Europe, Asie occidentale",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u897f\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia Ocidental",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Lar\xedngeo",properties:["yumu\u015fat\u0131c\u0131","yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","\u015fefkat"],propertiesEn:["softening","soothing","compassion"],propertiesDe:["weichmachend","beruhigend","Mitgef\xfchl"],propertiesEs:["suavizante","calmante","compasi\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["adoucissant","apaisant","compassion"],propertiesJa:["\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u308b","\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b","\u6148\u3057\u307f"],propertiesPt:["suavizante","calmante","compaix\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kat\u0131 oldu\u011fun yerleri yumu\u015fat. Hatmi sertli\u011fin de\u011fil, naziklik ve esnekli\u011fin g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, soften the places where you've grown hard. Marshmallow reminds you of the power not of rigidity, but of gentleness and flexibility.",dailyMessageDe:"Erweiche heute die Stellen, an denen du hart geworden bist. Eibisch erinnert dich an die Kraft nicht der H\xe4rte, sondern der Sanftheit und Flexibilit\xe4t.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, suaviza los lugares donde te has endurecido. El malvavisco te recuerda el poder no de la rigidez, sino de la suavidad y la flexibilidad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, adoucis les endroits o\xf9 tu t'es endurci. La guimauve te rappelle le pouvoir non de la rigidit\xe9, mais de la douceur et de la souplesse.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u786c\u304f\u306a\u3063\u305f\u90e8\u5206\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30de\u30b7\u30e5\u30de\u30ed\u30a6\u306f\u3001\u786c\u3055\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055\u3068\u3057\u306a\u3084\u304b\u3055\u306e\u529b\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, suavize os lugares onde voc\xea endureceu. O malva\xedsco lembra voc\xea do poder n\xe3o da rigidez, mas da suavidade e da flexibilidade.",howToUse:"K\xf6k\xfcn\xfc so\u011fuk suda bekleterek yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131c\u0131 bir i\xe7ecek haz\u0131rla ya da \xe7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak demle. Bo\u011faz ve sindirim i\xe7in \u0131l\u0131k t\xfcket.",howToUseEn:"Steep the root in cold water for a soothing drink, or brew the flowers as a tea. Drink it warm for the throat and digestion.",howToUseDe:"Lass die Wurzel in kaltem Wasser ziehen f\xfcr ein beruhigendes Getr\xe4nk oder br\xfche die Bl\xfcten als Tee. Trinke es warm f\xfcr Hals und Verdauung.",howToUseEs:"Deja la ra\xedz en agua fr\xeda para una bebida calmante, o prepara las flores como t\xe9. B\xe9belo tibio para la garganta y la digesti\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Laisse mac\xe9rer la racine dans l'eau froide pour une boisson apaisante, ou infuse les fleurs en tisane. Bois-le ti\xe8de pour la gorge et la digestion.",howToUseJa:"\u6839\u3092\u51b7\u6c34\u306b\u6d78\u3057\u3066\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u306b\u3059\u308b\u304b\u3001\u82b1\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5589\u3068\u6d88\u5316\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6e29\u304b\u304f\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Deixe a raiz em \xe1gua fria para uma bebida calmante, ou prepare as flores como ch\xe1. Beba morno para a garganta e a digest\xe3o.",affirmation:"Yumu\u015fakl\u0131\u011f\u0131m g\xfcc\xfcmd\xfcr, nazik\xe7e esneyebilirim.",affirmationEn:"My softness is my strength; I can bend gently.",affirmationDe:"Meine Sanftheit ist meine St\xe4rke; ich kann mich sanft biegen.",affirmationEs:"Mi suavidad es mi fuerza; puedo doblarme con dulzura.",affirmationFr:"Ma douceur est ma force ; je peux plier avec douceur.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u3084\u308f\u3089\u304b\u3055\u306f\u79c1\u306e\u5f37\u3055\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u3057\u306a\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Minha suavidade \xe9 minha for\xe7a; posso me curvar com gentileza.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/White_Marshmallows.jpg/330px-White_Marshmallows.jpg"},{id:"plant-021",emoji:"\ud83c\udf37",color:"#B58BC4",name:"Kediotu",nameEn:"Valerian",nameDe:"Baldrian",nameEs:"Valeriana",nameFr:"Val\xe9riane",nameJa:"\u30d0\u30ec\u30ea\u30a2\u30f3",namePt:"Valeriana",origin:"Avrupa, Asya",originEn:"Europe, Asia",originDe:"Europa, Asien",originEs:"Europa, Asia",originFr:"Europe, Asie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["derin uyku","sakinle\u015ftirici","gev\u015fetici"],propertiesEn:["deep sleep","calming","relaxing"],propertiesDe:["tiefer Schlaf","beruhigend","entspannend"],propertiesEs:["sue\xf1o profundo","calmante","relajante"],propertiesFr:["sommeil profond","apaisant","relaxant"],propertiesJa:["\u6df1\u3044\u7720\u308a","\u93ae\u9759","\u30ea\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30b9"],propertiesPt:["sono profundo","calmante","relaxante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn dinlenmenin bir zay\u0131fl\u0131k de\u011fil, bir ihtiya\xe7 oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rla. Kediotu sinirlerini yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131r, derin ve onar\u0131c\u0131 bir uykuya davet eder.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that rest is not weakness but a need. Valerian calms your nerves and invites you into deep, restorative sleep.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass Ruhe keine Schw\xe4che, sondern ein Bed\xfcrfnis ist. Baldrian beruhigt deine Nerven und l\xe4dt dich zu tiefem, erholsamem Schlaf ein.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que descansar no es debilidad sino una necesidad. La valeriana calma tus nervios y te invita a un sue\xf1o profundo y reparador.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que le repos n'est pas une faiblesse mais un besoin. La val\xe9riane apaise tes nerfs et t'invite \xe0 un sommeil profond et r\xe9parateur.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4f11\u3080\u3053\u3068\u306f\u5f31\u3055\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u5fc5\u8981\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d0\u30ec\u30ea\u30a2\u30f3\u306f\u795e\u7d4c\u3092\u93ae\u3081\u3001\u6df1\u304f\u56de\u5fa9\u3059\u308b\u7720\u308a\u3078\u8a98\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que descansar n\xe3o \xe9 fraqueza, mas uma necessidade. A valeriana acalma seus nervos e convida voc\xea a um sono profundo e reparador.",howToUse:"K\xf6k\xfcn\xfc uyumadan bir saat \xf6nce \xe7ay olarak demle. Kokusu g\xfc\xe7l\xfcd\xfcr; bal ya da nane ekleyerek yumu\u015fatabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Brew the root as a tea about an hour before sleep. Its scent is strong; you can soften it with honey or mint.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Wurzel etwa eine Stunde vor dem Schlafen als Tee. Ihr Geruch ist stark; du kannst ihn mit Honig oder Minze mildern.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona la ra\xedz como t\xe9 una hora antes de dormir. Su olor es fuerte; puedes suavizarlo con miel o menta.",howToUseFr:"Infuse la racine en tisane environ une heure avant le coucher. Son odeur est forte ; tu peux l'adoucir avec du miel ou de la menthe.",howToUseJa:"\u5c31\u5bdd\u306e\u7d04\u4e00\u6642\u9593\u524d\u306b\u6839\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u9999\u308a\u304c\u5f37\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u8702\u871c\u3084\u30df\u30f3\u30c8\u3067\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare a raiz como ch\xe1 cerca de uma hora antes de dormir. Seu cheiro \xe9 forte; voc\xea pode suaviz\xe1-lo com mel ou hortel\xe3.",affirmation:"Dinlenmeye izin veriyorum, huzurla uykuya teslim oluyorum.",affirmationEn:"I allow myself to rest and surrender to sleep in peace.",affirmationDe:"Ich erlaube mir zu ruhen und \xfcberlasse mich friedlich dem Schlaf.",affirmationEs:"Me permito descansar y me entrego al sue\xf1o en paz.",affirmationFr:"Je m'autorise \xe0 me reposer et m'abandonne au sommeil en paix.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4f11\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3092\u8a31\u3057\u3001\u5b89\u3089\u304b\u306b\u7720\u308a\u3078\u8eab\u3092\u3086\u3060\u306d\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Permito-me descansar e me entrego ao sono em paz.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Valeriana_officinalis_inflorescence_-_Niitv%C3%A4lja.jpg/330px-Valeriana_officinalis_inflorescence_-_Niitv%C3%A4lja.jpg"},{id:"plant-022",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#4E7A4C",name:"Defne",nameEn:"Bay Laurel",nameDe:"Lorbeer",nameEs:"Laurel",nameFr:"Laurier",nameJa:"\u30ed\u30fc\u30ea\u30a8",namePt:"Louro",origin:"Akdeniz",originEn:"Mediterranean",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u5730\u57df",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["zafer","bilgelik","koruma"],propertiesEn:["victory","wisdom","protection"],propertiesDe:["Sieg","Weisheit","Schutz"],propertiesEs:["victoria","sabidur\xeda","protecci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["victoire","sagesse","protection"],propertiesJa:["\u52dd\u5229","\u77e5\u6075","\u5b88\u8b77"],propertiesPt:["vit\xf3ria","sabedoria","prote\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kendi ba\u015far\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131 onurland\u0131r. Defne kadim \xe7a\u011flardan beri zaferin tac\u0131 olmu\u015ftur; sen de kendi yolundaki zaferlerini kutla.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, honor your own achievements. Bay laurel has been the crown of victory since ancient times; celebrate the victories on your own path.",dailyMessageDe:"Ehre heute deine eigenen Erfolge. Der Lorbeer ist seit der Antike die Krone des Sieges; feiere die Siege auf deinem eigenen Weg.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, honra tus propios logros. El laurel ha sido la corona de la victoria desde la antig\xfcedad; celebra las victorias en tu propio camino.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, honore tes propres r\xe9ussites. Le laurier est la couronne de la victoire depuis l'Antiquit\xe9 ; c\xe9l\xe8bre les victoires sur ton propre chemin.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u9054\u6210\u3092\u8b83\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ed\u30fc\u30ea\u30a8\u306f\u53e4\u4ee3\u304b\u3089\u52dd\u5229\u306e\u51a0\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u9053\u3067\u306e\u52dd\u5229\u3092\u795d\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, honre as suas pr\xf3prias conquistas. O louro \xe9 a coroa da vit\xf3ria desde a antiguidade; celebre as vit\xf3rias no seu pr\xf3prio caminho.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 yemeklerine ekleyerek aromas\u0131ndan yararlan ya da bir yapra\u011f\u0131n \xfczerine niyetini yaz\u0131p g\xfcvenle yakarak rit\xfcel yap. \xc7ay\u0131n\u0131 hafif\xe7e demleyebilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Add the leaves to your dishes for their aroma, or write your intention on a leaf and safely burn it as a ritual. You can lightly brew it as a tea.",howToUseDe:"Gib die Bl\xe4tter f\xfcr ihr Aroma in deine Gerichte oder schreibe deine Absicht auf ein Blatt und verbrenne es sicher als Ritual. Du kannst ihn leicht als Tee br\xfchen.",howToUseEs:"A\xf1ade las hojas a tus platos por su aroma, o escribe tu intenci\xf3n en una hoja y qu\xe9mala con seguridad como ritual. Puedes prepararla ligeramente como t\xe9.",howToUseFr:"Ajoute les feuilles \xe0 tes plats pour leur ar\xf4me, ou \xe9cris ton intention sur une feuille et br\xfble-la en toute s\xe9curit\xe9 en rituel. Tu peux l'infuser l\xe9g\xe8rement en tisane.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3066\u9999\u308a\u3092\u697d\u3057\u3080\u304b\u3001\u8449\u306b\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u66f8\u3044\u3066\u5b89\u5168\u306b\u71c3\u3084\u3059\u5100\u5f0f\u3092\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Adicione as folhas aos pratos pelo aroma, ou escreva sua inten\xe7\xe3o em uma folha e queime-a com seguran\xe7a como ritual. Voc\xea pode prepar\xe1-la levemente como ch\xe1.",affirmation:"Kendi yolumdaki zaferleri onurland\u0131r\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I honor the victories along my own path.",affirmationDe:"Ich ehre die Siege auf meinem eigenen Weg.",affirmationEs:"Honro las victorias a lo largo de mi propio camino.",affirmationFr:"J'honore les victoires sur mon propre chemin.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u9053\u306b\u304a\u3051\u308b\u52dd\u5229\u3092\u8b83\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Honro as vit\xf3rias ao longo do meu pr\xf3prio caminho.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Starr-071024-0195-Laurus_nobilis-leaves-Enchanting_Floral_Gardens_of_Kula-Maui_%2824867859296%29.jpg/330px-Starr-071024-0195-Laurus_nobilis-leaves-Enchanting_Floral_Gardens_of_Kula-Maui_%2824867859296%29.jpg",myth:"Defne, zaferin ve \u015fiirin kutsal a\u011fac\u0131d\u0131r. Anadolu mitinde tanr\u0131 Apollon'un sevdi\u011fi Daphne, ondan ka\xe7arken defne a\u011fac\u0131na d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr; bu y\xfczden defne hem a\u015fk\u0131n hem d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn simgesidir. Galipler, kahramanlar ve \u015fairler defne tac\u0131yla onurland\u0131r\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Anadolu'da defne yapra\u011f\u0131 nazara ve k\xf6t\xfc enerjiye kar\u015f\u0131 yak\u0131l\u0131r, evlere bereket ve koruma i\xe7in as\u0131l\u0131r. Kokusu zihni a\xe7ar, niyeti g\xfc\xe7lendirir. K\u0131\u015f\u0131n bile ye\u015fil kalan yapra\u011f\u0131, s\u0131nanm\u0131\u015f ama y\u0131lmayan ruhun simgesidir.",mythEn:"Bay laurel is the sacred tree of victory and poetry. In the Anatolian myth, Daphne, beloved of the god Apollo, turns into a laurel tree as she flees him; thus the laurel is the emblem of both love and transformation. Victors, heroes and poets were honoured with a laurel crown. In Anatolia the bay leaf is burned against the evil eye and ill energy, and hung in homes for blessing and protection. Its scent clears the mind and strengthens intention. Its leaf, green even in winter, is the emblem of a spirit tested yet undaunted.",mythDe:"Der Lorbeer ist der heilige Baum des Sieges und der Dichtung. Im anatolischen Mythos verwandelt sich Daphne, die Geliebte des Gottes Apollon, auf der Flucht vor ihm in einen Lorbeerbaum; so ist der Lorbeer Sinnbild von Liebe und Wandlung zugleich. Sieger, Helden und Dichter wurden mit dem Lorbeerkranz geehrt. In Anatolien wird das Lorbeerblatt gegen den b\xf6sen Blick und schlechte Energie verbrannt und f\xfcr Segen und Schutz in den H\xe4usern aufgeh\xe4ngt. Sein Duft kl\xe4rt den Geist und st\xe4rkt die Absicht. Sein selbst im Winter gr\xfcnes Blatt ist Sinnbild eines gepr\xfcften, doch unbeugsamen Geistes.",mythEs:"El laurel es el \xe1rbol sagrado de la victoria y la poes\xeda. En el mito anatolio, Dafne, amada del dios Apolo, se transforma en laurel al huir de \xe9l; as\xed el laurel es emblema del amor y de la transformaci\xf3n a la vez. A vencedores, h\xe9roes y poetas se les honraba con una corona de laurel. En Anatolia la hoja de laurel se quema contra el mal de ojo y la mala energ\xeda, y se cuelga en los hogares para la bendici\xf3n y la protecci\xf3n. Su aroma despeja la mente y fortalece la intenci\xf3n. Su hoja, verde aun en invierno, es emblema de un esp\xedritu probado pero indomable.",mythFr:"Le laurier est l'arbre sacr\xe9 de la victoire et de la po\xe9sie. Dans le mythe anatolien, Daphn\xe9, aim\xe9e du dieu Apollon, se change en laurier en le fuyant ; ainsi le laurier est l'embl\xe8me de l'amour et de la transformation \xe0 la fois. Vainqueurs, h\xe9ros et po\xe8tes \xe9taient honor\xe9s d'une couronne de laurier. En Anatolie, la feuille de laurier se br\xfble contre le mauvais \u0153il et l'\xe9nergie n\xe9faste, et se suspend dans les maisons pour la b\xe9n\xe9diction et la protection. Son parfum \xe9claircit l'esprit et renforce l'intention. Sa feuille, verte m\xeame en hiver, est l'embl\xe8me d'un esprit \xe9prouv\xe9 mais indompt\xe9.",mythJa:"\u6708\u6842\u6a39\u306f\u52dd\u5229\u3068\u8a69\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u6a39\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u795e\u30a2\u30dd\u30ed\u30f3\u306b\u611b\u3055\u308c\u305f\u30c0\u30d5\u30cd\u304c\u3001\u5f7c\u304b\u3089\u9003\u308c\u308b\u9014\u4e2d\u3067\u6708\u6842\u6a39\u3078\u3068\u59ff\u3092\u5909\u3048\u308b\u3002\u3086\u3048\u306b\u6708\u6842\u306f\u611b\u3068\u5909\u5bb9\u306e\u53cc\u65b9\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3002\u52dd\u8005\u3001\u82f1\u96c4\u3001\u8a69\u4eba\u306f\u6708\u6842\u51a0\u3067\u8b83\u3048\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u6708\u6842\u306e\u8449\u306f\u90aa\u8996\u3084\u60aa\u3044\u6c17\u306b\u5bfe\u3057\u3066\u711a\u304b\u308c\u3001\u795d\u798f\u3068\u5b88\u308a\u306e\u305f\u3081\u5bb6\u306b\u540a\u308b\u3055\u308c\u308b\u3002\u305d\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u6674\u3089\u3057\u3001\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u5f37\u3081\u308b\u3002\u51ac\u306b\u3082\u7dd1\u3092\u4fdd\u3064\u8449\u306f\u3001\u8a66\u3055\u308c\u3066\u306a\u304a\u5c48\u3057\u306a\u3044\u9b42\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3002",mythPt:"O loureiro \xe9 a \xe1rvore sagrada da vit\xf3ria e da poesia. No mito anat\xf3lio, Dafne, amada do deus Apolo, transforma-se em loureiro ao fugir dele; assim o loureiro \xe9 emblema do amor e da transforma\xe7\xe3o ao mesmo tempo. Vencedores, her\xf3is e poetas eram honrados com uma coroa de louro. Na Anat\xf3lia, a folha de louro queima-se contra o mau-olhado e a m\xe1 energia, e pendura-se nas casas para a b\xean\xe7\xe3o e a prote\xe7\xe3o. O seu aroma clareia a mente e fortalece a inten\xe7\xe3o. A sua folha, verde mesmo no inverno, \xe9 emblema de um esp\xedrito provado mas indom\xe1vel."},{id:"plant-023",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#3E6B4F",name:"Mersin",nameEn:"Myrtle",nameDe:"Myrte",nameEs:"Mirto",nameFr:"Myrte",nameJa:"\u30df\u30eb\u30c6",namePt:"Murta",origin:"Akdeniz",originEn:"Mediterranean",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u5730\u57df",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["sevgi","ar\u0131nma","ferahl\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["love","purification","freshness"],propertiesDe:["Liebe","Reinigung","Frische"],propertiesEs:["amor","purificaci\xf3n","frescura"],propertiesFr:["amour","purification","fra\xeecheur"],propertiesJa:["\u611b","\u6d44\u5316","\u6e05\u6dbc"],propertiesPt:["amor","purifica\xe7\xe3o","frescor"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn sevgini saf ve ferah tut. Mersin kadim zamanlardan beri a\u015fk\u0131n ve bar\u0131\u015f\u0131n sembol\xfc olmu\u015ftur; kalbini temiz bir niyetle a\xe7.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, keep your love pure and fresh. Myrtle has been a symbol of love and peace since ancient times; open your heart with a clean intention.",dailyMessageDe:"Halte heute deine Liebe rein und frisch. Die Myrte ist seit der Antike ein Symbol von Liebe und Frieden; \xf6ffne dein Herz mit einer reinen Absicht.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, mant\xe9n tu amor puro y fresco. El mirto ha sido s\xedmbolo de amor y paz desde la antig\xfcedad; abre tu coraz\xf3n con una intenci\xf3n limpia.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, garde ton amour pur et frais. Le myrte est un symbole d'amour et de paix depuis l'Antiquit\xe9 ; ouvre ton c\u0153ur avec une intention pure.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u611b\u3092\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306b\u3001\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306b\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30df\u30eb\u30c6\u306f\u53e4\u4ee3\u304b\u3089\u611b\u3068\u5e73\u548c\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306a\u610f\u56f3\u3067\u5fc3\u3092\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, mantenha o seu amor puro e fresco. A murta \xe9 s\xedmbolo de amor e paz desde a antiguidade; abra o cora\xe7\xe3o com uma inten\xe7\xe3o limpa.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle ya da bir dal\u0131n\u0131 eve ferahl\u0131k i\xe7in yerle\u015ftir. Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 solunum i\xe7in buharda kullan.",howToUseEn:"Lightly brew the leaves as a tea, or place a sprig in your home for freshness. Use the essential oil in steam for the breath.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter leicht als Tee oder stelle einen Zweig f\xfcr Frische ins Haus. Verwende das \xe4therische \xd6l im Dampf f\xfcr die Atmung.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona ligeramente las hojas como t\xe9, o coloca una ramita en casa para dar frescura. Usa el aceite esencial en vapor para la respiraci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les feuilles en tisane, ou place un brin chez toi pour la fra\xeecheur. Utilise l'huile essentielle en inhalation pour la respiration.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u679d\u3092\u6e05\u6dbc\u306e\u305f\u3081\u5bb6\u306b\u7f6e\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u84b8\u6c17\u3067\u547c\u5438\u306b\u4f7f\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare levemente as folhas como ch\xe1, ou coloque um raminho em casa para frescor. Use o \xf3leo essencial no vapor para a respira\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Kalbim saf, sevgim ferah ve berrak.",affirmationEn:"My heart is pure; my love is fresh and clear.",affirmationDe:"Mein Herz ist rein; meine Liebe ist frisch und klar.",affirmationEs:"Mi coraz\xf3n es puro; mi amor es fresco y claro.",affirmationFr:"Mon c\u0153ur est pur ; mon amour est frais et clair.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u611b\u306f\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u3067\u6f84\u3093\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Meu cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 puro; meu amor \xe9 fresco e claro.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Mersin-tekneler.jpg/330px-Mersin-tekneler.jpg",myth:"Mersin, a\u015fk\u0131n ve sadakatin mis kokulu a\u011fac\u0131d\u0131r. Antik Anadolu'da g\xfczellik tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Afrodit'e adanm\u0131\u015ft\u0131; gelinler mersin dal\u0131ndan ta\xe7 takar, d\xfc\u011f\xfcnlerde d\xf6k\xfclmeyen yapra\u011f\u0131 ebedi ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 simgelerdi. Ad\u0131n\u0131 ona veren Mersin \u015fehrinde ve Akdeniz k\u0131y\u0131lar\u0131nda h\xe2l\xe2 kutsal say\u0131l\u0131r. Mersin yapra\u011f\u0131 ar\u0131nma i\xe7in yak\u0131l\u0131r, sevgiyi ve bar\u0131\u015f\u0131 \xe7a\u011f\u0131rmak i\xe7in eve getirilir. K\u0131\u015f\u0131n bile ye\u015feren, k\xfc\xe7\xfck beyaz \xe7i\xe7ekleri y\u0131ld\u0131z gibi a\xe7an a\u011fac\u0131, sebat\u0131n ve nazik sevginin dersidir.",mythEn:"The myrtle is the fragrant tree of love and faithfulness. In ancient Anatolia it was dedicated to Aphrodite, goddess of beauty; brides wore crowns of myrtle, and its ever-green leaf at weddings signified eternal devotion. It is still held sacred along the Mediterranean coast and in the city of Mersin that bears its name. Myrtle leaves are burned for purification and brought into the home to call in love and peace. Its tree, green even in winter, its little white flowers opening like stars, is the lesson of constancy and gentle love.",mythDe:"Die Myrte ist der duftende Baum der Liebe und Treue. Im alten Anatolien war sie der Sch\xf6nheitsg\xf6ttin Aphrodite geweiht; Br\xe4ute trugen Kr\xe4nze aus Myrte, und ihr immergr\xfcnes Blatt bei Hochzeiten bedeutete ewige Hingabe. An der Mittelmeerk\xfcste und in der nach ihr benannten Stadt Mersin gilt sie noch immer als heilig. Myrtenbl\xe4tter werden zur Reinigung verbrannt und ins Haus gebracht, um Liebe und Frieden herbeizurufen. Ihr selbst im Winter gr\xfcner Baum, dessen kleine wei\xdfe Bl\xfcten wie Sterne aufgehen, lehrt Best\xe4ndigkeit und sanfte Liebe.",mythEs:"El mirto es el \xe1rbol fragante del amor y la fidelidad. En la antigua Anatolia estaba consagrado a Afrodita, diosa de la belleza; las novias llevaban coronas de mirto, y su hoja siempre verde en las bodas significaba la devoci\xf3n eterna. A\xfan se considera sagrado en la costa mediterr\xe1nea y en la ciudad de Mersin que lleva su nombre. Las hojas de mirto se queman para la purificaci\xf3n y se llevan al hogar para llamar al amor y la paz. Su \xe1rbol, verde aun en invierno, con florecillas blancas que se abren como estrellas, ense\xf1a la constancia y el amor tierno.",mythFr:"Le myrte est l'arbre parfum\xe9 de l'amour et de la fid\xe9lit\xe9. Dans l'Anatolie antique, il \xe9tait consacr\xe9 \xe0 Aphrodite, d\xe9esse de la beaut\xe9 ; les mari\xe9es portaient des couronnes de myrte, et sa feuille toujours verte aux noces signifiait la d\xe9votion \xe9ternelle. Il est encore tenu pour sacr\xe9 sur la c\xf4te m\xe9diterran\xe9enne et dans la ville de Mersin qui porte son nom. Les feuilles de myrte se br\xfblent pour la purification et s'apportent \xe0 la maison pour appeler l'amour et la paix. Son arbre, vert m\xeame en hiver, aux petites fleurs blanches qui s'ouvrent comme des \xe9toiles, enseigne la constance et l'amour tendre.",mythJa:"\u30df\u30eb\u30c8\u30b9\u306f\u611b\u3068\u8aa0\u306e\u9999\u308a\u9ad8\u3044\u6a39\u3002\u53e4\u4ee3\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u7f8e\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30a2\u30d5\u30ed\u30c7\u30a3\u30fc\u30c6\u306b\u6367\u3052\u3089\u308c\u3001\u82b1\u5ac1\u306f\u30df\u30eb\u30c8\u30b9\u306e\u51a0\u3092\u304b\u3076\u308a\u3001\u5a5a\u793c\u3067\u306e\u5e38\u7dd1\u306e\u8449\u306f\u6c38\u9060\u306e\u732e\u8eab\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u6cbf\u5cb8\u3001\u305d\u3057\u3066\u305d\u306e\u540d\u3092\u51a0\u3059\u308b\u90fd\u5e02\u30e1\u30eb\u30b7\u30f3\u3067\u306f\u4eca\u3082\u8056\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3068\u3055\u308c\u308b\u3002\u30df\u30eb\u30c8\u30b9\u306e\u8449\u306f\u6d44\u5316\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u711a\u304b\u308c\u3001\u611b\u3068\u5e73\u548c\u3092\u62db\u304f\u305f\u3081\u5bb6\u306b\u6301\u3061\u8fbc\u307e\u308c\u308b\u3002\u51ac\u306b\u3082\u7dd1\u3092\u4fdd\u3061\u3001\u661f\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u767d\u3044\u5c0f\u82b1\u3092\u958b\u304f\u305d\u306e\u6a39\u306f\u3001\u5909\u308f\u3089\u306c\u5fc3\u3068\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u611b\u306e\u6559\u3048\u3002",mythPt:"A murta \xe9 a \xe1rvore perfumada do amor e da fidelidade. Na antiga Anat\xf3lia era consagrada a Afrodite, deusa da beleza; as noivas usavam coroas de murta, e a sua folha sempre verde nos casamentos significava a devo\xe7\xe3o eterna. Ainda \xe9 tida por sagrada ao longo da costa mediterr\xe2nica e na cidade de Mersin que tem o seu nome. As folhas de murta queimam-se para a purifica\xe7\xe3o e levam-se para casa para chamar o amor e a paz. A sua \xe1rvore, verde mesmo no inverno, com florzinhas brancas que se abrem como estrelas, ensina a const\xe2ncia e o amor terno."},{id:"plant-024",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5B8C6F",name:"Okalipt\xfcs",nameEn:"Eucalyptus",nameDe:"Eukalyptus",nameEs:"Eucalipto",nameFr:"Eucalyptus",nameJa:"\u30e6\u30fc\u30ab\u30ea",namePt:"Eucalipto",origin:"Avustralya",originEn:"Australia",originDe:"Australien",originEs:"Australia",originFr:"Australie",originJa:"\u30aa\u30fc\u30b9\u30c8\u30e9\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Austr\xe1lia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Lar\xedngeo",properties:["a\xe7\u0131c\u0131","ferahlat\u0131c\u0131","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["opening","refreshing","purifying"],propertiesDe:["\xf6ffnend","erfrischend","reinigend"],propertiesEs:["abridor","refrescante","purificante"],propertiesFr:["ouvrant","rafra\xeechissant","purifiant"],propertiesJa:["\u958b\u304f","\u723d\u5feb","\u6d44\u5316"],propertiesPt:["abridor","refrescante","purificante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn derin bir nefes al ve i\xe7indeki s\u0131k\u0131\u015fmay\u0131 serbest b\u0131rak. Okalipt\xfcs g\xf6\u011fs\xfcn\xfc ve zihnini a\xe7ar, sana yeni bir alan arma\u011fan eder.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, take a deep breath and release the tightness within. Eucalyptus opens your chest and mind, gifting you new space.",dailyMessageDe:"Atme heute tief durch und lass die Enge in dir los. Eukalyptus \xf6ffnet Brust und Geist und schenkt dir neuen Raum.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, respira hondo y suelta la opresi\xf3n interior. El eucalipto abre tu pecho y tu mente, regal\xe1ndote un nuevo espacio.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, respire profond\xe9ment et lib\xe8re la tension int\xe9rieure. L'eucalyptus ouvre ta poitrine et ton esprit, t'offrant un nouvel espace.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u6df1\u304f\u606f\u3092\u5438\u3044\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u8a70\u307e\u308a\u3092\u89e3\u304d\u653e\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30e6\u30fc\u30ab\u30ea\u306f\u80f8\u3068\u5fc3\u3092\u958b\u304d\u3001\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u4f59\u767d\u3092\u8d08\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, respire fundo e solte o aperto interior. O eucalipto abre o peito e a mente, presenteando voc\xea com um novo espa\xe7o.",howToUse:"Birka\xe7 damla esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suya damlat\u0131p buhar\u0131n\u0131 solu ya da du\u015f s\u0131ras\u0131nda dal\u0131n\u0131 asarak nefes a\xe7\u0131c\u0131 bir ortam yarat.",howToUseEn:"Drip a few drops of essential oil into hot water and inhale the steam, or hang a sprig in the shower for a breath-opening atmosphere.",howToUseDe:"Gib ein paar Tropfen \xe4therisches \xd6l in hei\xdfes Wasser und atme den Dampf ein, oder h\xe4nge einen Zweig in die Dusche f\xfcr eine atem\xf6ffnende Atmosph\xe4re.",howToUseEs:"Pon unas gotas de aceite esencial en agua caliente e inhala el vapor, o cuelga una ramita en la ducha para un ambiente que abra la respiraci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Verse quelques gouttes d'huile essentielle dans de l'eau chaude et inhale la vapeur, ou suspends un brin dans la douche pour une atmosph\xe8re qui d\xe9gage la respiration.",howToUseJa:"\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u6570\u6ef4\u6e6f\u306b\u5782\u3089\u3057\u3066\u84b8\u6c17\u3092\u5438\u3046\u304b\u3001\u679d\u3092\u30b7\u30e3\u30ef\u30fc\u306b\u540a\u308b\u3057\u3066\u547c\u5438\u304c\u958b\u304f\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",howToUsePt:"Pingue algumas gotas de \xf3leo essencial na \xe1gua quente e inale o vapor, ou pendure um raminho no chuveiro para um ambiente que abre a respira\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Derin nefes al\u0131yorum, i\xe7imde bolca alan var.",affirmationEn:"I breathe deeply; there is plenty of space within me.",affirmationDe:"Ich atme tief; in mir ist viel Raum.",affirmationEs:"Respiro profundamente; hay mucho espacio dentro de m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Je respire profond\xe9ment ; il y a beaucoup d'espace en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6df1\u304f\u547c\u5438\u3059\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u306f\u5341\u5206\u306a\u4f59\u767d\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Respiro profundamente; h\xe1 muito espa\xe7o dentro de mim.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Eucalyptus_tereticornis_flowers%2C_capsules%2C_buds_and_foliage.jpeg/330px-Eucalyptus_tereticornis_flowers%2C_capsules%2C_buds_and_foliage.jpeg"},{id:"plant-025",emoji:"\ud83e\udeb5",color:"#C49A6C",name:"Sandal A\u011fac\u0131",nameEn:"Sandalwood",nameDe:"Sandelholz",nameEs:"S\xe1ndalo",nameFr:"Santal",nameJa:"\u30b5\u30f3\u30c0\u30eb\u30a6\u30c3\u30c9",namePt:"S\xe2ndalo",origin:"Hindistan, G\xfcney Asya",originEn:"India, South Asia",originDe:"Indien, S\xfcdasien",originEs:"India, Sur de Asia",originFr:"Inde, Asie du Sud",originJa:"\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9\u30fb\u5357\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"\xcdndia, Sul da \xc1sia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["topraklay\u0131c\u0131","kutsal","meditatif"],propertiesEn:["grounding","sacred","meditative"],propertiesDe:["erdend","heilig","meditativ"],propertiesEs:["enraizante","sagrado","meditativo"],propertiesFr:["ancrant","sacr\xe9","m\xe9ditatif"],propertiesJa:["\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304f","\u8056\u306a\u308b","\u7791\u60f3\u7684"],propertiesPt:["enraizador","sagrado","meditativo"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn i\xe7sel bir sessizli\u011fe \xe7ekil ve kendinle ba\u015f ba\u015fa kal. Sandal a\u011fac\u0131 seni topraklar, meditasyon ve dua i\xe7in kutsal bir alan a\xe7ar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, withdraw into an inner silence and be alone with yourself. Sandalwood grounds you and opens a sacred space for meditation and prayer.",dailyMessageDe:"Ziehe dich heute in eine innere Stille zur\xfcck und sei allein mit dir. Sandelholz erdet dich und \xf6ffnet einen heiligen Raum f\xfcr Meditation und Gebet.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ret\xedrate a un silencio interior y qu\xe9date a solas contigo. El s\xe1ndalo te enra\xedza y abre un espacio sagrado para la meditaci\xf3n y la oraci\xf3n.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, retire-toi dans un silence int\xe9rieur et reste seul avec toi-m\xeame. Le santal t'ancre et ouvre un espace sacr\xe9 pour la m\xe9ditation et la pri\xe8re.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u9759\u3051\u3055\u306b\u9000\u304d\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u81ea\u8eab\u3068\u5411\u304d\u5408\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b5\u30f3\u30c0\u30eb\u30a6\u30c3\u30c9\u306f\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304b\u305b\u3001\u7791\u60f3\u3068\u7948\u308a\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, recolha-se em um sil\xeancio interior e fique a s\xf3s consigo. O s\xe2ndalo enra\xedza voc\xea e abre um espa\xe7o sagrado para a medita\xe7\xe3o e a ora\xe7\xe3o.",howToUse:"T\xfcts\xfc \xe7ubu\u011fu olarak yakarak meditasyon alan\u0131n\u0131 kutsa ya da esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 bileklerine s\xfcrerek topraklan. Derin nefeslerle kokusunu i\xe7ine \xe7ek.",howToUseEn:"Burn it as incense to bless your meditation space, or apply the essential oil to your wrists to ground yourself. Draw in its scent with deep breaths.",howToUseDe:"Verbrenne es als R\xe4ucherst\xe4bchen, um deinen Meditationsraum zu segnen, oder trage das \xe4therische \xd6l auf deine Handgelenke auf, um dich zu erden. Atme seinen Duft tief ein.",howToUseEs:"Qu\xe9malo como incienso para bendecir tu espacio de meditaci\xf3n, o aplica el aceite esencial en tus mu\xf1ecas para enraizarte. Inhala su aroma con respiraciones profundas.",howToUseFr:"Br\xfble-le en encens pour b\xe9nir ton espace de m\xe9ditation, ou applique l'huile essentielle sur tes poignets pour t'ancrer. Inspire son parfum par des respirations profondes.",howToUseJa:"\u304a\u9999\u3068\u3057\u3066\u711a\u3044\u3066\u7791\u60f3\u306e\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u308b\u304b\u3001\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u624b\u9996\u306b\u5857\u3063\u3066\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6df1\u3044\u547c\u5438\u3067\u305d\u306e\u9999\u308a\u3092\u53d6\u308a\u8fbc\u307f\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Queime-o como incenso para aben\xe7oar seu espa\xe7o de medita\xe7\xe3o, ou aplique o \xf3leo essencial nos pulsos para se enraizar. Inspire seu aroma com respira\xe7\xf5es profundas.",affirmation:"K\xf6kleniyorum ve kutsal bir sessizlikte huzur buluyorum.",affirmationEn:"I am grounded and find peace in a sacred silence.",affirmationDe:"Ich bin geerdet und finde Frieden in einer heiligen Stille.",affirmationEs:"Estoy enraizado y encuentro paz en un silencio sagrado.",affirmationFr:"Je suis ancr\xe9 et je trouve la paix dans un silence sacr\xe9.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304d\u3001\u8056\u306a\u308b\u9759\u3051\u3055\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u898b\u3044\u3060\u3059\u3002",affirmationPt:"Estou enraizado e encontro paz em um sil\xeancio sagrado.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Santalum_paniculatum_1326.jpg/330px-Santalum_paniculatum_1326.jpg",myth:"Sandal a\u011fac\u0131, meditasyonun ve adanm\u0131\u015fl\u0131\u011f\u0131n kutsal kokusudur. Hindistan tap\u0131naklar\u0131nda binlerce y\u0131ld\u0131r t\xfcts\xfc ve macun olarak yak\u0131l\u0131r; kokusu zihni durultur, ruhu yukar\u0131 \xe7eker. Odununun kalbi, kesildikten y\u0131llar sonra bile kokusunu korur \u2014 kal\u0131c\u0131 \xf6z\xfcn, d\u0131\u015f kabuk soyulunca a\xe7\u0131\u011fa \xe7\u0131kan i\xe7sel g\xfczelli\u011fin dersidir. Anadolu tekkelerinde de huzur ve dua i\xe7in kullan\u0131lm\u0131\u015f; s\u0131cak, tatl\u0131 kokusu kalbi yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131r.",mythEn:"Sandalwood is the sacred scent of meditation and devotion. For thousands of years it has been burned as incense and ground into paste in the temples of India; its fragrance stills the mind and draws the soul upward. Its heartwood keeps its scent for years even after being cut \u2014 the lesson of an enduring essence, of an inner beauty revealed once the outer husk is stripped away. In Anatolian dervish lodges too it was used for peace and prayer; its warm, sweet scent calms the heart.",mythDe:"Sandelholz ist der heilige Duft der Meditation und Hingabe. Seit Jahrtausenden wird es in den Tempeln Indiens als R\xe4ucherwerk verbrannt und zu Paste verrieben; sein Duft stillt den Geist und zieht die Seele empor. Sein Kernholz bewahrt seinen Duft noch Jahre nach dem Schnitt \u2014 die Lehre eines bleibenden Wesens, einer inneren Sch\xf6nheit, die sich zeigt, wenn die \xe4u\xdfere H\xfclle abf\xe4llt. Auch in anatolischen Derwischkonventen diente es Frieden und Gebet; sein warmer, s\xfc\xdfer Duft beruhigt das Herz.",mythEs:"El s\xe1ndalo es el aroma sagrado de la meditaci\xf3n y la devoci\xf3n. Durante milenios se ha quemado como incienso y molido en pasta en los templos de la India; su fragancia aquieta la mente y eleva el alma. Su madera de coraz\xf3n conserva el aroma a\xf1os despu\xe9s de ser cortada \u2014 la lecci\xf3n de una esencia perdurable, de una belleza interior que se revela al desprenderse la c\xe1scara externa. Tambi\xe9n en las tekkes de Anatolia se usaba para la paz y la oraci\xf3n; su aroma c\xe1lido y dulce serena el coraz\xf3n.",mythFr:"Le bois de santal est le parfum sacr\xe9 de la m\xe9ditation et de la d\xe9votion. Depuis des mill\xe9naires, on le br\xfble en encens et on le r\xe9duit en p\xe2te dans les temples de l'Inde ; son parfum apaise l'esprit et \xe9l\xe8ve l'\xe2me. Son bois de c\u0153ur garde son parfum des ann\xe9es apr\xe8s la coupe \u2014 la le\xe7on d'une essence durable, d'une beaut\xe9 int\xe9rieure r\xe9v\xe9l\xe9e une fois l'\xe9corce \xf4t\xe9e. Dans les tekk\xe9s d'Anatolie aussi, on l'employait pour la paix et la pri\xe8re ; son parfum chaud et doux calme le c\u0153ur.",mythJa:"\u767d\u6a80\u306f\u7791\u60f3\u3068\u732e\u8eab\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u9999\u308a\u3002\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9\u306e\u5bfa\u9662\u3067\u306f\u4f55\u5343\u5e74\u3082\u306e\u9593\u3001\u9999\u3068\u3057\u3066\u711a\u304b\u308c\u3001\u7df4\u308a\u9999\u306b\u3055\u308c\u3066\u304d\u305f\u3002\u305d\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u9759\u3081\u3001\u9b42\u3092\u4e0a\u3078\u3068\u5c0e\u304f\u3002\u82af\u6750\u306f\u5207\u3089\u308c\u305f\u5f8c\u3082\u4f55\u5e74\u3082\u9999\u308a\u3092\u4fdd\u3064\u2014\u2014\u673d\u3061\u306c\u672c\u8cea\u306e\u3001\u5916\u76ae\u3092\u5265\u304c\u308c\u3066\u9855\u308c\u308b\u5185\u306a\u308b\u7f8e\u306e\u6559\u3048\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u30c6\u30c3\u30b1\u3067\u3082\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3068\u7948\u308a\u306b\u7528\u3044\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3002\u6e29\u304b\u304f\u7518\u3044\u9999\u308a\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u93ae\u3081\u308b\u3002",mythPt:"O s\xe2ndalo \xe9 o aroma sagrado da medita\xe7\xe3o e da devo\xe7\xe3o. H\xe1 mil\xe9nios \xe9 queimado como incenso e mo\xeddo em pasta nos templos da \xcdndia; a sua fragr\xe2ncia aquieta a mente e eleva a alma. O seu cerne guarda o aroma anos depois de cortado \u2014 a li\xe7\xe3o de uma ess\xeancia duradoura, de uma beleza interior revelada ao despir-se a casca exterior. Tamb\xe9m nas tekkes da Anat\xf3lia se usava para a paz e a ora\xe7\xe3o; o seu aroma quente e doce serena o cora\xe7\xe3o."},{id:"plant-026",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#A8B79E",name:"G\xfcnl\xfck (Buhur A\u011fac\u0131)",nameEn:"Frankincense",nameDe:"Weihrauch",nameEs:"Incienso",nameFr:"Encens (Oliban)",nameJa:"\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3\u30ad\u30f3\u30bb\u30f3\u30b9",namePt:"Ol\xedbano",origin:"Arap Yar\u0131madas\u0131, Do\u011fu Afrika",originEn:"Arabian Peninsula, East Africa",originDe:"Arabische Halbinsel, Ostafrika",originEs:"Pen\xednsula ar\xe1biga, \xc1frica Oriental",originFr:"P\xe9ninsule arabique, Afrique de l'Est",originJa:"\u30a2\u30e9\u30d3\u30a2\u534a\u5cf6\u30fb\u6771\u30a2\u30d5\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Pen\xednsula Ar\xe1bica, \xc1frica Oriental",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["kutsal","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","y\xfckseltici"],propertiesEn:["sacred","purifying","elevating"],propertiesDe:["heilig","reinigend","erhebend"],propertiesEs:["sagrado","purificante","elevador"],propertiesFr:["sacr\xe9","purifiant","\xe9l\xe9vateur"],propertiesJa:["\u8056\u306a\u308b","\u6d44\u5316","\u9ad8\u3081\u308b"],propertiesPt:["sagrado","purificante","elevador"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn maddeden bir an i\xe7in y\xfcksel ve ruhuna yer a\xe7. G\xfcnl\xfck binlerce y\u0131ld\u0131r kutsal mek\xe2nlar\u0131n t\xfcts\xfcs\xfc olmu\u015ftur; sen de i\xe7sel tap\u0131na\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ar\u0131nd\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, rise for a moment beyond the material and make room for your spirit. Frankincense has been the incense of sacred places for thousands of years; purify your inner temple.",dailyMessageDe:"Erhebe dich heute einen Moment \xfcber das Materielle und schaffe Raum f\xfcr deine Seele. Weihrauch ist seit Jahrtausenden der R\xe4ucherduft heiliger St\xe4tten; reinige deinen inneren Tempel.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, el\xe9vate por un momento m\xe1s all\xe1 de lo material y haz espacio para tu esp\xedritu. El incienso ha sido el sahumerio de los lugares sagrados durante milenios; purifica tu templo interior.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, \xe9l\xe8ve-toi un instant au-del\xe0 du mat\xe9riel et fais de la place \xe0 ton esprit. L'encens est la fum\xe9e des lieux sacr\xe9s depuis des mill\xe9naires ; purifie ton temple int\xe9rieur.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4e00\u77ac\u3001\u7269\u8cea\u3092\u8d85\u3048\u3066\u6607\u308a\u3001\u9b42\u306b\u5834\u6240\u3092\u7a7a\u3051\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3\u30ad\u30f3\u30bb\u30f3\u30b9\u306f\u4f55\u5343\u5e74\u3082\u8056\u306a\u308b\u5834\u6240\u306e\u9999\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5185\u306a\u308b\u795e\u6bbf\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, eleve-se por um momento al\xe9m do material e abra espa\xe7o para o seu esp\xedrito. O ol\xedbano \xe9 o incenso dos lugares sagrados h\xe1 mil\xeanios; purifique o seu templo interior.",howToUse:"Re\xe7inesini bir t\xfcts\xfc k\xf6m\xfcr\xfcnde yakarak mek\xe2n\u0131n\u0131 kutsa. Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 meditasyon \xf6ncesi aln\u0131na nazik\xe7e s\xfcr.",howToUseEn:"Burn the resin on an incense charcoal to bless your space. Gently apply the essential oil to your forehead before meditation.",howToUseDe:"Verbrenne das Harz auf einer R\xe4ucherkohle, um deinen Raum zu segnen. Trage das \xe4therische \xd6l vor der Meditation sanft auf deine Stirn auf.",howToUseEs:"Quema la resina sobre un carb\xf3n de incienso para bendecir tu espacio. Aplica suavemente el aceite esencial en tu frente antes de meditar.",howToUseFr:"Br\xfble la r\xe9sine sur un charbon \xe0 encens pour b\xe9nir ton espace. Applique doucement l'huile essentielle sur ton front avant la m\xe9ditation.",howToUseJa:"\u6a39\u8102\u3092\u9999\u70ad\u3067\u711a\u3044\u3066\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7791\u60f3\u524d\u306b\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u984d\u306b\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5857\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Queime a resina em um carv\xe3o de incenso para aben\xe7oar seu espa\xe7o. Aplique suavemente o \xf3leo essencial na testa antes de meditar.",affirmation:"Ruhumu y\xfckseltiyorum, i\xe7imdeki kutsall\u0131\u011fa ba\u011flan\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I elevate my spirit and connect to the sacred within me.",affirmationDe:"Ich erhebe meine Seele und verbinde mich mit dem Heiligen in mir.",affirmationEs:"Elevo mi esp\xedritu y me conecto con lo sagrado en m\xed.",affirmationFr:"J'\xe9l\xe8ve mon esprit et me relie au sacr\xe9 en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u9b42\u3092\u9ad8\u3081\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u8056\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3068\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Elevo o meu esp\xedrito e me conecto ao sagrado dentro de mim.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Frankincense_2005-12-31.jpg/330px-Frankincense_2005-12-31.jpg"},{id:"plant-027",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#9C6B4A",name:"M\xfcr (Mirra)",nameEn:"Myrrh",nameDe:"Myrrhe",nameEs:"Mirra",nameFr:"Myrrhe",nameJa:"\u30df\u30eb\u30e9",namePt:"Mirra",origin:"Arap Yar\u0131madas\u0131, Kuzeydo\u011fu Afrika",originEn:"Arabian Peninsula, Northeast Africa",originDe:"Arabische Halbinsel, Nordostafrika",originEs:"Pen\xednsula ar\xe1biga, Nordeste de \xc1frica",originFr:"P\xe9ninsule arabique, Nord-Est de l'Afrique",originJa:"\u30a2\u30e9\u30d3\u30a2\u534a\u5cf6\u30fb\u5317\u6771\u30a2\u30d5\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Pen\xednsula Ar\xe1bica, Nordeste da \xc1frica",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["kutsal","topraklay\u0131c\u0131","\u015fifa"],propertiesEn:["sacred","grounding","healing"],propertiesDe:["heilig","erdend","heilend"],propertiesEs:["sagrado","enraizante","sanador"],propertiesFr:["sacr\xe9","ancrant","gu\xe9risseur"],propertiesJa:["\u8056\u306a\u308b","\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304f","\u7652\u3057"],propertiesPt:["sagrado","enraizador","curativo"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ge\xe7mi\u015f yaralar\u0131na sayg\u0131yla bak ve onlar\u0131n seni nas\u0131l olgunla\u015ft\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6r. M\xfcr kadim bir \u015fifa re\xe7inesidir; derin d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn kokusunu ta\u015f\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, look upon your past wounds with respect and see how they have ripened you. Myrrh is an ancient healing resin; it carries the scent of deep transformation.",dailyMessageDe:"Betrachte heute deine vergangenen Wunden mit Respekt und sieh, wie sie dich gereift haben. Myrrhe ist ein altes Heilharz; sie tr\xe4gt den Duft tiefer Verwandlung.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, mira tus heridas pasadas con respeto y ve c\xf3mo te han madurado. La mirra es una antigua resina sanadora; lleva el aroma de la transformaci\xf3n profunda.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, regarde tes blessures pass\xe9es avec respect et vois comme elles t'ont m\xfbri. La myrrhe est une ancienne r\xe9sine gu\xe9risseuse ; elle porte le parfum d'une transformation profonde.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u904e\u53bb\u306e\u50b7\u3092\u656c\u610f\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u898b\u3064\u3081\u3001\u305d\u308c\u304c\u3069\u3046\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u6210\u719f\u3055\u305b\u305f\u304b\u3092\u898b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30df\u30eb\u30e9\u306f\u53e4\u4ee3\u306e\u7652\u3057\u306e\u6a39\u8102\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u6df1\u3044\u5909\u5bb9\u306e\u9999\u308a\u3092\u5bbf\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, olhe para suas feridas passadas com respeito e veja como elas amadureceram voc\xea. A mirra \xe9 uma antiga resina curativa; carrega o aroma da transforma\xe7\xe3o profunda.",howToUse:"Re\xe7inesini t\xfcts\xfc olarak yakarak topraklay\u0131c\u0131 bir rit\xfcel olu\u015ftur. Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 badem ya\u011f\u0131yla seyreltip cilde nazik\xe7e uygula.",howToUseEn:"Burn the resin as incense to create a grounding ritual. Dilute the essential oil with almond oil and gently apply to the skin.",howToUseDe:"Verbrenne das Harz als R\xe4ucherwerk, um ein erdendes Ritual zu schaffen. Verd\xfcnne das \xe4therische \xd6l mit Mandel\xf6l und trage es sanft auf die Haut auf.",howToUseEs:"Quema la resina como incienso para crear un ritual enraizante. Diluye el aceite esencial con aceite de almendras y apl\xedcalo suavemente sobre la piel.",howToUseFr:"Br\xfble la r\xe9sine en encens pour cr\xe9er un rituel d'ancrage. Dilue l'huile essentielle avec de l'huile d'amande et applique-la doucement sur la peau.",howToUseJa:"\u6a39\u8102\u3092\u304a\u9999\u3068\u3057\u3066\u711a\u304d\u3001\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304f\u5100\u5f0f\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u30a2\u30fc\u30e2\u30f3\u30c9\u30aa\u30a4\u30eb\u3067\u8584\u3081\u3001\u808c\u306b\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5857\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Queime a resina como incenso para criar um ritual de enraizamento. Dilua o \xf3leo essencial com \xf3leo de am\xeandoas e aplique suavemente na pele.",affirmation:"Yaralar\u0131m beni olgunla\u015ft\u0131rd\u0131, derin bir huzurla k\xf6kleniyorum.",affirmationEn:"My wounds have ripened me; I root with a deep peace.",affirmationDe:"Meine Wunden haben mich gereift; ich wurzle in tiefem Frieden.",affirmationEs:"Mis heridas me han madurado; me enra\xedzo con una paz profunda.",affirmationFr:"Mes blessures m'ont m\xfbri ; je m'enracine dans une paix profonde.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u50b7\u306f\u79c1\u3092\u6210\u719f\u3055\u305b\u305f\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u6df1\u3044\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Minhas feridas me amadureceram; eu me enra\xedzo com uma paz profunda.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/Commiphora-myrrha-resin-myrrh.jpg"},{id:"plant-028",emoji:"\ud83e\udd0d",color:"#F4F0E6",name:"Yasemin",nameEn:"Jasmine",nameDe:"Jasmin",nameEs:"Jazm\xedn",nameFr:"Jasmin",nameJa:"\u30b8\u30e3\u30b9\u30df\u30f3",namePt:"Jasmim",origin:"G\xfcney Asya, \u0130ran",originEn:"South Asia, Persia",originDe:"S\xfcdasien, Persien",originEs:"Sur de Asia, Persia",originFr:"Asie du Sud, Perse",originJa:"\u5357\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u30da\u30eb\u30b7\u30a2",originPt:"Sul da \xc1sia, P\xe9rsia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u30b5\u30af\u30e9\u30eb\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacral",properties:["sezgi","duyusall\u0131k","huzur"],propertiesEn:["intuition","sensuality","serenity"],propertiesDe:["Intuition","Sinnlichkeit","Gelassenheit"],propertiesEs:["intuici\xf3n","sensualidad","serenidad"],propertiesFr:["intuition","sensualit\xe9","s\xe9r\xe9nit\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u76f4\u611f","\u5b98\u80fd","\u9759\u3051\u3055"],propertiesPt:["intui\xe7\xe3o","sensualidade","serenidade"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn geceyle dost ol ve duygular\u0131n\u0131 yumu\u015fak\xe7a hisset. Yasemin geceleri a\xe7an bir \xe7i\xe7ektir; sana sezginin karanl\u0131kta da \u0131\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, befriend the night and feel your emotions gently. Jasmine is a flower that blooms at night; it whispers that intuition shines even in the dark.",dailyMessageDe:"Freunde dich heute mit der Nacht an und f\xfchle deine Gef\xfchle sanft. Jasmin ist eine Blume, die nachts bl\xfcht; er fl\xfcstert, dass Intuition auch im Dunkeln leuchtet.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, hazte amigo de la noche y siente tus emociones con suavidad. El jazm\xedn es una flor que florece de noche; te susurra que la intuici\xf3n brilla incluso en la oscuridad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, lie-toi d'amiti\xe9 avec la nuit et ressens tes \xe9motions avec douceur. Le jasmin est une fleur qui s'\xe9panouit la nuit ; il murmure que l'intuition brille m\xeame dans l'obscurit\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u591c\u3068\u89aa\u3057\u304f\u306a\u308a\u3001\u611f\u60c5\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u611f\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b8\u30e3\u30b9\u30df\u30f3\u306f\u591c\u306b\u54b2\u304f\u82b1\u3002\u76f4\u611f\u306f\u6697\u95c7\u3067\u3082\u8f1d\u304f\u3068\u3055\u3055\u3084\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, fa\xe7a amizade com a noite e sinta suas emo\xe7\xf5es com suavidade. O jasmim \xe9 uma flor que floresce \xe0 noite; ele sussurra que a intui\xe7\xe3o brilha mesmo no escuro.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle ya da esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ak\u015fam rit\xfcellerinde kullan. Birka\xe7 damlay\u0131 yast\u0131\u011f\u0131na ekleyerek huzurlu bir uykuya haz\u0131rlan.",howToUseEn:"Lightly brew the flowers as a tea, or use the essential oil in evening rituals. Add a few drops to your pillow to prepare for peaceful sleep.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten leicht als Tee oder verwende das \xe4therische \xd6l in Abendritualen. Gib ein paar Tropfen auf dein Kissen, um dich auf einen friedlichen Schlaf vorzubereiten.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona ligeramente las flores como t\xe9, o usa el aceite esencial en rituales nocturnos. A\xf1ade unas gotas a tu almohada para preparar un sue\xf1o tranquilo.",howToUseFr:"Infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les fleurs en tisane, ou utilise l'huile essentielle dans tes rituels du soir. Ajoute quelques gouttes \xe0 ton oreiller pour pr\xe9parer un sommeil paisible.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u591c\u306e\u5100\u5f0f\u306b\u4f7f\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6570\u6ef4\u3092\u6795\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3001\u5b89\u3089\u304b\u306a\u7720\u308a\u306b\u5099\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare levemente as flores como ch\xe1, ou use o \xf3leo essencial em rituais noturnos. Adicione algumas gotas ao travesseiro para preparar um sono tranquilo.",affirmation:"Sezgime g\xfcveniyorum, karanl\u0131kta bile \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131 buluyorum.",affirmationEn:"I trust my intuition; I find the light even in the dark.",affirmationDe:"Ich vertraue meiner Intuition; ich finde das Licht auch im Dunkeln.",affirmationEs:"Conf\xedo en mi intuici\xf3n; encuentro la luz incluso en la oscuridad.",affirmationFr:"Je fais confiance \xe0 mon intuition ; je trouve la lumi\xe8re m\xeame dans l'obscurit\xe9.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u76f4\u611f\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3059\u308b\u3002\u6697\u95c7\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u3082\u5149\u3092\u898b\u3044\u3060\u3059\u3002",affirmationPt:"Confio na minha intui\xe7\xe3o; encontro a luz mesmo no escuro.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Common_Jasmine.jpg/330px-Common_Jasmine.jpg",myth:"Yasemin, gecenin kokusu, ilahi ve d\xfcnyevi a\u015fk\u0131n \xe7i\xe7e\u011fidir. Ad\u0131 Fars\xe7a 'y\xe2sem\xeen'den gelir; Osmanl\u0131 ve \u0130ran bah\xe7elerinde 'gecenin krali\xe7esi' diye an\u0131l\u0131r, kokusu karanl\u0131kta en yo\u011fun a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r. Sufi \u015fiirinde sevgilinin teninin kokusu, ruhun \xf6zlemidir. Beyaz \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi safl\u0131\u011f\u0131, yo\u011fun esans\u0131 tutkuyu simgeler; yast\u0131k yan\u0131na konan demeti tatl\u0131 r\xfcyalar ve sevgi \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131r.",mythEn:"Jasmine is the scent of night, the flower of love both divine and earthly. Its name comes from the Persian 'y\xe2sem\xeen'; in Ottoman and Persian gardens it is called the 'queen of the night,' its fragrance opening fullest in the dark. In Sufi poetry it is the scent of the beloved's skin, the longing of the soul. Its white flower signifies purity, its heavy essence passion; a sprig by the pillow calls in sweet dreams and love.",mythDe:"Jasmin ist der Duft der Nacht, die Blume der g\xf6ttlichen wie der irdischen Liebe. Sein Name kommt vom persischen 'y\xe2sem\xeen'; in osmanischen und persischen G\xe4rten hei\xdft er 'K\xf6nigin der Nacht', sein Duft entfaltet sich im Dunkeln am vollsten. In der Sufi-Dichtung ist er der Duft der Haut des Geliebten, die Sehnsucht der Seele. Seine wei\xdfe Bl\xfcte steht f\xfcr Reinheit, seine schwere Essenz f\xfcr Leidenschaft; ein Zweig am Kissen ruft s\xfc\xdfe Tr\xe4ume und Liebe herbei.",mythEs:"El jazm\xedn es el aroma de la noche, la flor del amor divino y terrenal. Su nombre viene del persa 'y\xe2sem\xeen'; en los jardines otomanos y persas se le llama 'reina de la noche', su fragancia se abre plena en la oscuridad. En la poes\xeda suf\xed es el aroma de la piel del amado, el anhelo del alma. Su flor blanca significa pureza, su esencia intensa la pasi\xf3n; una ramita junto a la almohada llama a los dulces sue\xf1os y al amor.",mythFr:"Le jasmin est le parfum de la nuit, la fleur de l'amour divin comme terrestre. Son nom vient du persan 'y\xe2sem\xeen' ; dans les jardins ottomans et persans, on l'appelle 'reine de la nuit', son parfum s'\xe9panouissant le plus dans l'obscurit\xe9. Dans la po\xe9sie soufie, il est le parfum de la peau du bien-aim\xe9, le d\xe9sir de l'\xe2me. Sa fleur blanche signifie la puret\xe9, son essence lourde la passion ; un brin pr\xe8s de l'oreiller appelle les doux r\xeaves et l'amour.",mythJa:"\u30b8\u30e3\u30b9\u30df\u30f3\u306f\u591c\u306e\u9999\u308a\u3001\u795e\u8056\u306b\u3082\u4e16\u4fd7\u306b\u3082\u611b\u306e\u82b1\u3002\u305d\u306e\u540d\u306f\u30da\u30eb\u30b7\u30e3\u8a9e\u300cy\xe2sem\xeen\u300d\u306b\u7531\u6765\u3057\u3001\u30aa\u30b9\u30de\u30f3\u3084\u30da\u30eb\u30b7\u30e3\u306e\u5ead\u3067\u300c\u591c\u306e\u5973\u738b\u300d\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306f\u95c7\u3067\u3082\u3063\u3068\u3082\u6fc3\u304f\u958b\u304f\u3002\u30b9\u30fc\u30d5\u30a3\u30fc\u306e\u8a69\u3067\u306f\u3001\u604b\u4eba\u306e\u808c\u306e\u9999\u308a\u3001\u9b42\u306e\u61a7\u308c\u3002\u767d\u3044\u82b1\u306f\u7d14\u7c8b\u3055\u3001\u6fc3\u3044\u9999\u308a\u306f\u60c5\u71b1\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3002\u6795\u8fba\u306e\u4e00\u679d\u306f\u7518\u3044\u5922\u3068\u611b\u3092\u62db\u304f\u3002",mythPt:"O jasmim \xe9 o aroma da noite, a flor do amor divino e terreno. O seu nome vem do persa 'y\xe2sem\xeen'; nos jardins otomanos e persas chama-se 'rainha da noite', a sua fragr\xe2ncia abrindo-se mais plena na escurid\xe3o. Na poesia sufi \xe9 o aroma da pele do amado, o anseio da alma. A sua flor branca significa pureza, a sua ess\xeancia intensa a paix\xe3o; um raminho junto \xe0 almofada chama os doces sonhos e o amor."},{id:"plant-029",emoji:"\ud83e\udeb7",color:"#E7A9C8",name:"Lotus",nameEn:"Lotus",nameDe:"Lotus",nameEs:"Loto",nameFr:"Lotus",nameJa:"\u84ee",namePt:"L\xf3tus",origin:"Asya, Hindistan",originEn:"Asia, India",originDe:"Asien, Indien",originEs:"Asia, India",originFr:"Asie, Inde",originJa:"\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9",originPt:"\xc1sia, \xcdndia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["ayd\u0131nlanma","safl\u0131k","y\xfckseli\u015f"],propertiesEn:["enlightenment","purity","rising"],propertiesDe:["Erleuchtung","Reinheit","Aufstieg"],propertiesEs:["iluminaci\xf3n","pureza","ascenso"],propertiesFr:["illumination","puret\xe9","\xe9l\xe9vation"],propertiesJa:["\u609f\u308a","\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u3055","\u4e0a\u6607"],propertiesPt:["ilumina\xe7\xe3o","pureza","ascens\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn i\xe7inde bulundu\u011fun \xe7amurun seni kirletmedi\u011fini hat\u0131rla. Lotus karanl\u0131k sulardan y\xfckselip saf bir \xe7i\xe7ek a\xe7ar; sen de zorluklardan g\xfczellikle \xe7\u0131kabilirsin.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that the mud you are in does not stain you. The lotus rises from dark waters and blooms pure; you too can emerge from hardship with beauty.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass der Schlamm, in dem du bist, dich nicht beschmutzt. Der Lotus erhebt sich aus dunklen Wassern und bl\xfcht rein; auch du kannst aus Schwierigkeiten in Sch\xf6nheit hervorgehen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que el lodo en el que est\xe1s no te ensucia. El loto se eleva desde aguas oscuras y florece puro; t\xfa tambi\xe9n puedes emerger de la dificultad con belleza.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que la boue dans laquelle tu es ne te souille pas. Le lotus s'\xe9l\xe8ve des eaux sombres et fleurit pur ; toi aussi tu peux \xe9merger des difficult\xe9s avec beaut\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u3044\u308b\u6ce5\u304c\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u6c5a\u3055\u306a\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u84ee\u306f\u6697\u3044\u6c34\u304b\u3089\u6607\u308a\u3001\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306b\u54b2\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u56f0\u96e3\u304b\u3089\u7f8e\u3057\u304f\u73fe\u308c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que a lama em que voc\xea est\xe1 n\xe3o o mancha. O l\xf3tus se ergue de \xe1guas escuras e floresce puro; voc\xea tamb\xe9m pode emergir das dificuldades com beleza.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7e\u011fini meditasyon imgesi olarak zihninde canland\u0131r ya da lotus \xe7ay\u0131n\u0131 hafif\xe7e demleyerek sakinle\u015f. Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 kalp hizas\u0131na s\xfcrerek a\xe7\u0131l\u0131m niyeti ta\u015f\u0131.",howToUseEn:"Visualize the flower as a meditation image, or lightly brew lotus tea to calm down. Apply the essential oil at heart level to carry an intention of opening.",howToUseDe:"Visualisiere die Blume als Meditationsbild oder br\xfche leicht Lotustee, um zur Ruhe zu kommen. Trage das \xe4therische \xd6l in Herzh\xf6he auf, um eine Absicht der \xd6ffnung zu tragen.",howToUseEs:"Visualiza la flor como imagen de meditaci\xf3n, o prepara ligeramente t\xe9 de loto para calmarte. Aplica el aceite esencial a la altura del coraz\xf3n para llevar una intenci\xf3n de apertura.",howToUseFr:"Visualise la fleur comme image de m\xe9ditation, ou infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement une tisane de lotus pour te calmer. Applique l'huile essentielle au niveau du c\u0153ur pour porter une intention d'ouverture.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u7791\u60f3\u306e\u30a4\u30e1\u30fc\u30b8\u3068\u3057\u3066\u601d\u3044\u63cf\u304f\u304b\u3001\u84ee\u8336\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u6df9\u308c\u3066\u843d\u3061\u7740\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u5fc3\u81d3\u306e\u9ad8\u3055\u306b\u5857\u308a\u3001\u958b\u304d\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u6301\u3061\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Visualize a flor como imagem de medita\xe7\xe3o, ou prepare levemente um ch\xe1 de l\xf3tus para se acalmar. Aplique o \xf3leo essencial na altura do cora\xe7\xe3o para carregar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de abertura.",affirmation:"\xc7amurdan y\xfckselip saf ve g\xfczel a\xe7\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I rise from the mud and bloom pure and beautiful.",affirmationDe:"Ich erhebe mich aus dem Schlamm und bl\xfche rein und sch\xf6n.",affirmationEs:"Me elevo del lodo y florezco puro y hermoso.",affirmationFr:"Je m'\xe9l\xe8ve de la boue et je fleuris pur et beau.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6ce5\u304b\u3089\u6607\u308a\u3001\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306b\u7f8e\u3057\u304f\u54b2\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Eu me ergo da lama e flores\xe7o puro e belo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg/330px-Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg",myth:"Lotus, \xe7amurdan y\xfckselip lekesiz a\xe7an safl\u0131\u011f\u0131n \xe7i\xe7e\u011fidir. M\u0131s\u0131r'da g\xfcne\u015fin do\u011fu\u015funu, Hindistan ve Tibet'te ayd\u0131nlanmay\u0131 simgeler; her yapra\u011f\u0131 bir \xe7akran\u0131n a\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131d\u0131r. Anadolu'da nil\xfcfer olarak bilinen su \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi, Sel\xe7uklu ve erken Osmanl\u0131 ta\u015f i\u015f\xe7ili\u011finde, \xe7ini ve hal\u0131 motiflerinde bereketin ve dirili\u015fin simgesi olarak i\u015flenmi\u015ftir. Antik Anadolu'da batakl\u0131ktan do\u011fan lotus, \xf6l\xfcmden sonra yeniden do\u011fu\u015fun m\xfcjdesiydi. Suyun \xfcst\xfcnde durup \u0131slanmayan yapra\u011f\u0131, d\xfcnyada olup d\xfcnyaya kap\u0131lmaman\u0131n dersidir.",mythEn:"The lotus is the flower of purity that rises from the mud and opens unstained. In Egypt it signified the rising sun, in India and Tibet enlightenment; each petal an opening of a chakra. Known in Anatolia as the water lily, it was worked into Seljuk and early Ottoman stone-carving, tiles and carpet motifs as a sign of abundance and resurrection. In ancient Anatolia the lotus born from the marsh heralded rebirth after death. Its leaf, resting on the water yet never soaked, is the lesson of being in the world without being caught by it.",mythDe:"Der Lotus ist die Blume der Reinheit, die aus dem Schlamm aufsteigt und makellos erbl\xfcht. In \xc4gypten stand er f\xfcr die aufgehende Sonne, in Indien und Tibet f\xfcr die Erleuchtung; jedes Bl\xfctenblatt das \xd6ffnen eines Chakras. In Anatolien als Seerose bekannt, wurde er in seldschukische und fr\xfchosmanische Steinmetzkunst, Fliesen und Teppichmuster als Zeichen von F\xfclle und Auferstehung eingearbeitet. Im alten Anatolien k\xfcndete der aus dem Sumpf geborene Lotus die Wiedergeburt nach dem Tod an. Sein Blatt, das auf dem Wasser ruht und doch nie durchn\xe4sst, lehrt, in der Welt zu sein, ohne von ihr ergriffen zu werden.",mythEs:"El loto es la flor de la pureza que se eleva del lodo y se abre sin mancha. En Egipto represent\xf3 el sol naciente, en India y T\xedbet la iluminaci\xf3n; cada p\xe9talo la apertura de un chakra. Conocido en Anatolia como nen\xfafar, fue labrado en la canter\xeda sely\xfacida y otomana temprana, en azulejos y motivos de alfombra como signo de abundancia y resurrecci\xf3n. En la antigua Anatolia, el loto nacido del pantano anunciaba el renacer tras la muerte. Su hoja, que descansa sobre el agua sin empaparse, ense\xf1a a estar en el mundo sin quedar atrapado en \xe9l.",mythFr:"Le lotus est la fleur de la puret\xe9 qui s'\xe9l\xe8ve de la boue et s'ouvre sans tache. En \xc9gypte il figurait le soleil levant, en Inde et au Tibet l'illumination ; chaque p\xe9tale l'ouverture d'un chakra. Connu en Anatolie sous le nom de n\xe9nuphar, il fut sculpt\xe9 dans la pierre seldjoukide et ottomane ancienne, sur les fa\xefences et les motifs de tapis, signe d'abondance et de r\xe9surrection. Dans l'Anatolie antique, le lotus n\xe9 du marais annon\xe7ait la renaissance apr\xe8s la mort. Sa feuille, pos\xe9e sur l'eau sans jamais s'imbiber, enseigne \xe0 \xeatre dans le monde sans s'y laisser prendre.",mythJa:"\u84ee\u306f\u6ce5\u306e\u4e2d\u304b\u3089\u7acb\u3061\u4e0a\u304c\u308a\u3001\u6c5a\u308c\u306a\u304f\u54b2\u304f\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u3055\u306e\u82b1\u3002\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u3067\u306f\u6607\u308b\u592a\u967d\u3092\u3001\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9\u3084\u30c1\u30d9\u30c3\u30c8\u3067\u306f\u609f\u308a\u3092\u8c61\u5fb4\u3057\u3001\u4e00\u679a\u4e00\u679a\u306e\u82b1\u5f01\u306f\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9\u306e\u958b\u82b1\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u7761\u84ee\u3068\u3057\u3066\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u3001\u30bb\u30eb\u30b8\u30e5\u30fc\u30af\u671d\u3084\u521d\u671f\u30aa\u30b9\u30de\u30f3\u671d\u306e\u77f3\u5f6b\u3001\u30bf\u30a4\u30eb\u3001\u7d68\u6bef\u306e\u6587\u69d8\u306b\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u5fa9\u6d3b\u306e\u3057\u308b\u3057\u3068\u3057\u3066\u523b\u307e\u308c\u305f\u3002\u53e4\u4ee3\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u3001\u6cbc\u304b\u3089\u751f\u307e\u308c\u308b\u84ee\u306f\u6b7b\u5f8c\u306e\u518d\u751f\u306e\u544a\u3052\u3067\u3042\u3063\u305f\u3002\u6c34\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u3042\u308a\u306a\u304c\u3089\u6fe1\u308c\u306a\u3044\u305d\u306e\u8449\u306f\u3001\u4e16\u306b\u3042\u308a\u3066\u4e16\u306b\u3068\u3089\u308f\u308c\u306c\u6559\u3048\u3002",mythPt:"O l\xf3tus \xe9 a flor da pureza que se ergue da lama e se abre sem m\xe1cula. No Egito representou o sol nascente, na \xcdndia e no Tibete a ilumina\xe7\xe3o; cada p\xe9tala a abertura de um chakra. Conhecido na Anat\xf3lia como nen\xfafar, foi lavrado na cantaria selj\xfacida e otomana primitiva, em azulejos e motivos de tapete, como sinal de abund\xe2ncia e ressurrei\xe7\xe3o. Na antiga Anat\xf3lia, o l\xf3tus nascido do p\xe2ntano anunciava o renascer ap\xf3s a morte. A sua folha, que repousa sobre a \xe1gua sem se ensopar, ensina a estar no mundo sem ser apanhado por ele."},{id:"plant-030",emoji:"\ud83e\udd0d",color:"#C9D6C0",name:"Beyaz Ada\xe7ay\u0131",nameEn:"White Sage",nameDe:"Wei\xdfer Salbei",nameEs:"Salvia Blanca",nameFr:"Sauge Blanche",nameJa:"\u30db\u30ef\u30a4\u30c8\u30bb\u30fc\u30b8",namePt:"S\xe1lvia Branca",origin:"Kuzey Amerika",originEn:"North America",originDe:"Nordamerika",originEs:"Am\xe9rica del Norte",originFr:"Am\xe9rique du Nord",originJa:"\u5317\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Am\xe9rica do Norte",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","kutsal","koruyucu"],propertiesEn:["purifying","sacred","protective"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","heilig","sch\xfctzend"],propertiesEs:["purificante","sagrado","protector"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","sacr\xe9","protecteur"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u8056\u306a\u308b","\u5b88\u8b77"],propertiesPt:["purificante","sagrado","protetor"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn etraf\u0131ndaki ve i\xe7indeki a\u011f\u0131r enerjiyi temizle. Beyaz ada\xe7ay\u0131 yerli geleneklerde kutsal bir ar\u0131nma bitkisidir; sayg\u0131yla ve niyetle kullan.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, clear the heavy energy around and within you. White sage is a sacred cleansing plant in Indigenous traditions; use it with respect and intention.",dailyMessageDe:"Reinige heute die schwere Energie um dich und in dir. Wei\xdfer Salbei ist in indigenen Traditionen eine heilige Reinigungspflanze; verwende ihn mit Respekt und Absicht.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, limpia la energ\xeda pesada a tu alrededor y en tu interior. La salvia blanca es una planta sagrada de limpieza en tradiciones ind\xedgenas; \xfasala con respeto e intenci\xf3n.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, purifie l'\xe9nergie lourde autour de toi et en toi. La sauge blanche est une plante de purification sacr\xe9e dans les traditions autochtones ; utilise-la avec respect et intention.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u5468\u308a\u3068\u5185\u306b\u3042\u308b\u91cd\u3044\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30db\u30ef\u30a4\u30c8\u30bb\u30fc\u30b8\u306f\u5148\u4f4f\u6c11\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71\u3067\u8056\u306a\u308b\u6d44\u5316\u306e\u690d\u7269\u3067\u3059\u3002\u656c\u610f\u3068\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u4f7f\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, limpe a energia pesada ao seu redor e dentro de voc\xea. A s\xe1lvia branca \xe9 uma planta sagrada de limpeza nas tradi\xe7\xf5es ind\xedgenas; use-a com respeito e inten\xe7\xe3o.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f demetini g\xfcvenle tutu\u015fturup duman\u0131n\u0131 mek\xe2nda gezdirerek ar\u0131nma yap. Niyetini s\xf6zlerle ifade et ve pencereyi a\xe7. Bitkiye sayg\u0131yla, \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc kullan.",howToUseEn:"Safely light the dried bundle and move the smoke through your space to cleanse. Speak your intention aloud and open a window. Use it respectfully and sparingly.",howToUseDe:"Entz\xfcnde das getrocknete B\xfcndel sicher und f\xfchre den Rauch durch deinen Raum zur Reinigung. Sprich deine Absicht aus und \xf6ffne ein Fenster. Verwende es respektvoll und sparsam.",howToUseEs:"Enciende con seguridad el manojo seco y pasa el humo por tu espacio para limpiarlo. Expresa tu intenci\xf3n en voz alta y abre una ventana. \xdasala con respeto y moderaci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Allume en toute s\xe9curit\xe9 le bouquet s\xe9ch\xe9 et fais circuler la fum\xe9e dans ton espace pour le purifier. Exprime ton intention \xe0 voix haute et ouvre une fen\xeatre. Utilise-la avec respect et mod\xe9ration.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u675f\u3092\u5b89\u5168\u306b\u711a\u304d\u3001\u7159\u3092\u7a7a\u9593\u306b\u5de1\u3089\u305b\u3066\u6d44\u5316\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u58f0\u306b\u51fa\u3057\u3001\u7a93\u3092\u958b\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002\u656c\u610f\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u63a7\u3048\u3081\u306b\u4f7f\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",howToUsePt:"Acenda com seguran\xe7a o ma\xe7o seco e passe a fuma\xe7a pelo seu espa\xe7o para limp\xe1-lo. Diga sua inten\xe7\xe3o em voz alta e abra uma janela. Use com respeito e modera\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Etraf\u0131m\u0131 ve i\xe7imi ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131yorum, saf bir niyetle duruyorum.",affirmationEn:"I cleanse my surroundings and my inner self; I stand in pure intention.",affirmationDe:"Ich reinige meine Umgebung und mein Inneres; ich stehe in reiner Absicht.",affirmationEs:"Limpio mi entorno y mi interior; permanezco en una intenci\xf3n pura.",affirmationFr:"Je purifie mon entourage et mon int\xe9rieur ; je me tiens dans une intention pure.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5468\u308a\u3068\u5185\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u3001\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306a\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u7acb\u3064\u3002",affirmationPt:"Eu limpo o meu entorno e o meu interior; permane\xe7o em uma inten\xe7\xe3o pura.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Salvia_apiana_1.jpg/330px-Salvia_apiana_1.jpg"},{id:"plant-031",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#A89B7C",name:"Palo Santo",nameEn:"Palo Santo",nameDe:"Palo Santo",nameEs:"Palo Santo",nameFr:"Palo Santo",nameJa:"\u30d1\u30ed\u30b5\u30f3\u30c8",namePt:"Palo Santo",origin:"G\xfcney Amerika",originEn:"South America",originDe:"S\xfcdamerika",originEs:"Am\xe9rica del Sur",originFr:"Am\xe9rique du Sud",originJa:"\u5357\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Am\xe9rica do Sul",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","huzur","kutsal"],propertiesEn:["purifying","peace","sacred"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","Frieden","heilig"],propertiesEs:["purificante","paz","sagrado"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","paix","sacr\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u5b89\u3089\u304e","\u8056\u306a\u308b"],propertiesPt:["purificante","paz","sagrado"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn tatl\u0131 bir huzuru i\xe7ine davet et. Palo Santo 'kutsal odun' demektir; duman\u0131 negatifi da\u011f\u0131t\u0131r, yerine s\u0131cak bir dinginlik b\u0131rak\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, invite a sweet peace within. Palo Santo means 'holy wood'; its smoke scatters the negative and leaves a warm stillness in its place.",dailyMessageDe:"Lade heute einen s\xfc\xdfen Frieden in dich ein. Palo Santo bedeutet 'heiliges Holz'; sein Rauch zerstreut das Negative und hinterl\xe4sst eine warme Stille.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, invita una dulce paz a tu interior. Palo Santo significa 'madera sagrada'; su humo dispersa lo negativo y deja en su lugar una c\xe1lida quietud.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, invite une douce paix en toi. Palo Santo signifie 'bois sacr\xe9' ; sa fum\xe9e disperse le n\xe9gatif et laisse \xe0 la place un calme chaleureux.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u7518\u3084\u304b\u306a\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u5185\u306b\u62db\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d1\u30ed\u30b5\u30f3\u30c8\u306f\u300c\u8056\u306a\u308b\u6728\u300d\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u305d\u306e\u7159\u306f\u8ca0\u3092\u6563\u3089\u3057\u3001\u6e29\u304b\u306a\u9759\u3051\u3055\u3092\u6b8b\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, convide uma doce paz para dentro de voc\xea. Palo Santo significa 'madeira sagrada'; sua fuma\xe7a dispersa o negativo e deixa em seu lugar uma quietude calorosa.",howToUse:"\xc7ubu\u011fun ucunu g\xfcvenle tutu\u015fturup alevi s\xf6nd\xfcr, duman\u0131n\u0131 mek\xe2nda ya da \xe7evrende gezdir. Etik kaynakl\u0131, d\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015f dallardan toplanm\u0131\u015f olan\u0131 tercih et.",howToUseEn:"Safely light the tip of the stick, blow out the flame, and move the smoke around your space or yourself. Choose ethically sourced wood gathered from fallen branches.",howToUseDe:"Entz\xfcnde die Spitze des St\xe4bchens sicher, l\xf6sche die Flamme und f\xfchre den Rauch durch deinen Raum oder um dich herum. W\xe4hle ethisch gewonnenes Holz aus heruntergefallenen \xc4sten.",howToUseEs:"Enciende con seguridad la punta del palo, apaga la llama y pasa el humo por tu espacio o por ti. Elige madera de origen \xe9tico, recogida de ramas ca\xeddas.",howToUseFr:"Allume en toute s\xe9curit\xe9 le bout du b\xe2ton, \xe9teins la flamme et fais circuler la fum\xe9e autour de ton espace ou de toi. Choisis du bois d'origine \xe9thique, ramass\xe9 sur des branches tomb\xe9es.",howToUseJa:"\u68d2\u306e\u5148\u3092\u5b89\u5168\u306b\u706f\u3057\u3001\u708e\u3092\u6d88\u3057\u3066\u3001\u7159\u3092\u7a7a\u9593\u3084\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u5468\u308a\u306b\u5de1\u3089\u305b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u502b\u7406\u7684\u306b\u63a1\u53d6\u3055\u308c\u305f\u3001\u843d\u679d\u304b\u3089\u96c6\u3081\u305f\u3082\u306e\u3092\u9078\u3073\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",howToUsePt:"Acenda com seguran\xe7a a ponta do bast\xe3o, apague a chama e passe a fuma\xe7a pelo seu espa\xe7o ou ao seu redor. Escolha madeira de origem \xe9tica, coletada de galhos ca\xeddos.",affirmation:"Tatl\u0131 bir huzuru i\xe7ime davet ediyorum, dinginlik benimle.",affirmationEn:"I invite a sweet peace within; stillness is with me.",affirmationDe:"Ich lade einen s\xfc\xdfen Frieden in mich ein; die Stille ist bei mir.",affirmationEs:"Invito una dulce paz a mi interior; la quietud est\xe1 conmigo.",affirmationFr:"J'invite une douce paix en moi ; le calme est avec moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u7518\u3084\u304b\u306a\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u5185\u306b\u62db\u304f\u3002\u9759\u3051\u3055\u304c\u79c1\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Eu convido uma doce paz para dentro de mim; a quietude est\xe1 comigo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Bursera_graveolens.jpg/330px-Bursera_graveolens.jpg"},{id:"plant-032",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3c",color:"#F0A93C",name:"Ayn\u0131sefa",nameEn:"Calendula",nameDe:"Ringelblume",nameEs:"Cal\xe9ndula",nameFr:"Calendula",nameJa:"\u30ab\u30ec\u30f3\u30c7\u30e5\u30e9",namePt:"Cal\xeandula",origin:"G\xfcney Avrupa",originEn:"Southern Europe",originDe:"S\xfcdeuropa",originEs:"Sur de Europa",originFr:"Europe du Sud",originJa:"\u5357\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1",originPt:"Sul da Europa",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["iyile\u015ftirici","ne\u015fe","g\xfcne\u015f enerjisi"],propertiesEn:["healing","joy","solar energy"],propertiesDe:["heilend","Freude","Sonnenenergie"],propertiesEs:["sanador","alegr\xeda","energ\xeda solar"],propertiesFr:["gu\xe9risseur","joie","\xe9nergie solaire"],propertiesJa:["\u7652\u3057","\u559c\u3073","\u592a\u967d\u306e\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc"],propertiesPt:["curativo","alegria","energia solar"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xfcne\u015fi takip eden bu \xe7i\xe7ek gibi, \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa y\xf6nel. Ayn\u0131sefa ne\u015feyi ve iyile\u015fmeyi ta\u015f\u0131r; sen de y\xfcz\xfcn\xfc ayd\u0131nl\u0131\u011fa \xe7evir.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, like this flower that follows the sun, turn toward the light. Calendula carries joy and healing; turn your face to the brightness too.",dailyMessageDe:"Wende dich heute wie diese sonnenfolgende Blume dem Licht zu. Ringelblume tr\xe4gt Freude und Heilung; richte auch du dein Gesicht zur Helligkeit.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, como esta flor que sigue al sol, vu\xe9lvete hacia la luz. La cal\xe9ndula lleva alegr\xeda y sanaci\xf3n; vuelve tambi\xe9n tu rostro a la claridad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, comme cette fleur qui suit le soleil, tourne-toi vers la lumi\xe8re. Le calendula porte joie et gu\xe9rison ; tourne aussi ton visage vers la clart\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u592a\u967d\u3092\u8ffd\u3046\u3053\u306e\u82b1\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u5149\u3078\u5411\u304b\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ab\u30ec\u30f3\u30c7\u30e5\u30e9\u306f\u559c\u3073\u3068\u7652\u3057\u3092\u5bbf\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u9854\u3092\u660e\u308b\u3055\u3078\u5411\u3051\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, como esta flor que segue o sol, volte-se para a luz. A cal\xeandula carrega alegria e cura; vire tamb\xe9m o seu rosto para a claridade.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak demle ya da ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 cilt bak\u0131m\u0131 i\xe7in kullan. Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 salatalara katarak g\xfcne\u015fin ne\u015fesini sofrana ta\u015f\u0131.",howToUseEn:"Brew the flowers as a tea, or use the oil for skin care. Add the petals to salads to bring the sun's joy to your table.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten als Tee oder verwende das \xd6l f\xfcr die Hautpflege. Gib die Bl\xfctenbl\xe4tter in Salate, um die Freude der Sonne auf deinen Tisch zu bringen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las flores como t\xe9, o usa el aceite para el cuidado de la piel. A\xf1ade los p\xe9talos a las ensaladas para llevar la alegr\xeda del sol a tu mesa.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fleurs en tisane, ou utilise l'huile pour le soin de la peau. Ajoute les p\xe9tales aux salades pour apporter la joie du soleil \xe0 ta table.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u6cb9\u3092\u30b9\u30ad\u30f3\u30b1\u30a2\u306b\u4f7f\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u82b1\u3073\u3089\u3092\u30b5\u30e9\u30c0\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3001\u592a\u967d\u306e\u559c\u3073\u3092\u98df\u5353\u3078\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores como ch\xe1, ou use o \xf3leo para o cuidado da pele. Adicione as p\xe9talas \xe0s saladas para levar a alegria do sol \xe0 sua mesa.",affirmation:"Y\xfcz\xfcm\xfc \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa \xe7eviriyorum, ne\u015feyle iyile\u015fiyorum.",affirmationEn:"I turn my face to the light and heal with joy.",affirmationDe:"Ich wende mein Gesicht dem Licht zu und heile mit Freude.",affirmationEs:"Vuelvo mi rostro a la luz y sano con alegr\xeda.",affirmationFr:"Je tourne mon visage vers la lumi\xe8re et je gu\xe9ris dans la joie.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u9854\u3092\u5149\u3078\u5411\u3051\u3001\u559c\u3073\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u7652\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Volto o meu rosto para a luz e me curo com alegria.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg/330px-Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg"},{id:"plant-033",emoji:"\ud83d\udc9c",color:"#9A6FB0",name:"\xc7uha \xc7i\xe7e\u011fi",nameEn:"Passionflower",nameDe:"Passionsblume",nameEs:"Pasiflora",nameFr:"Passiflore",nameJa:"\u30d1\u30c3\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u30d5\u30e9\u30ef\u30fc",namePt:"Maracuj\xe1 (flor)",origin:"Amerika k\u0131tas\u0131",originEn:"The Americas",originDe:"Amerikanischer Kontinent",originEs:"Continente americano",originFr:"Continent am\xe9ricain",originJa:"\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u5927\u9678",originPt:"Continente americano",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["sakinle\u015ftirici","zihni dindiren","uyku"],propertiesEn:["calming","mind-quieting","sleep"],propertiesDe:["beruhigend","geistberuhigend","Schlaf"],propertiesEs:["calmante","aquieta la mente","sue\xf1o"],propertiesFr:["apaisant","calme le mental","sommeil"],propertiesJa:["\u93ae\u9759","\u5fc3\u3092\u9759\u3081\u308b","\u7720\u308a"],propertiesPt:["calmante","aquieta a mente","sono"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn durup d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmeye ara ver ve zihnini dinlendir. \xc7uha \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi d\xf6n\xfcp duran d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceleri yava\u015flat\u0131r, sana i\xe7sel bir s\xfck\xfbnet sunar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, pause from overthinking and let your mind rest. Passionflower slows your spinning thoughts and offers you an inner stillness.",dailyMessageDe:"Mache heute eine Pause vom Gr\xfcbeln und lass deinen Geist ruhen. Passionsblume verlangsamt deine kreisenden Gedanken und schenkt dir innere Ruhe.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, haz una pausa del pensar en exceso y deja descansar tu mente. La pasiflora ralentiza tus pensamientos giratorios y te ofrece una quietud interior.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, fais une pause dans tes ruminations et laisse ton esprit se reposer. La passiflore ralentit tes pens\xe9es tourbillonnantes et t'offre un calme int\xe9rieur.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u8003\u3048\u3059\u304e\u3092\u4f11\u3081\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u4f11\u307e\u305b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d1\u30c3\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u30d5\u30e9\u30ef\u30fc\u306f\u3050\u308b\u3050\u308b\u56de\u308b\u601d\u8003\u3092\u3086\u308b\u3081\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u9759\u3051\u3055\u3092\u5dee\u3057\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, fa\xe7a uma pausa do excesso de pensamentos e deixe a mente descansar. O maracuj\xe1 em flor desacelera os pensamentos girat\xf3rios e oferece a voc\xea uma quietude interior.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7ek ve yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak demleyip ak\u015famlar\u0131 i\xe7. Zihnin yoruldu\u011fu g\xfcnlerde \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc kullanarak rahatla.",howToUseEn:"Brew the flowers and leaves as a tea and drink in the evenings. On mentally tiring days, use it in moderation to relax.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche Bl\xfcten und Bl\xe4tter als Tee und trinke ihn abends. An geistig anstrengenden Tagen verwende ihn in Ma\xdfen zum Entspannen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona flores y hojas como t\xe9 y bebe por las noches. En d\xedas mentalmente agotadores, \xfasala con moderaci\xf3n para relajarte.",howToUseFr:"Infuse fleurs et feuilles en tisane et bois le soir. Les jours mentalement fatigants, utilise-la avec mod\xe9ration pour te d\xe9tendre.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3068\u8449\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u591c\u306b\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u982d\u304c\u75b2\u308c\u305f\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306b\u4f7f\u3063\u3066\u304f\u3064\u308d\u304e\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores e folhas como ch\xe1 e beba \xe0 noite. Em dias mentalmente cansativos, use com modera\xe7\xe3o para relaxar.",affirmation:"Zihnimi dinlendirmeye izin veriyorum, i\xe7imde s\xfck\xfbnet var.",affirmationEn:"I allow my mind to rest; there is stillness within me.",affirmationDe:"Ich erlaube meinem Geist zu ruhen; in mir ist Stille.",affirmationEs:"Permito que mi mente descanse; hay quietud dentro de m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Je permets \xe0 mon esprit de se reposer ; il y a du calme en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5fc3\u304c\u4f11\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3092\u8a31\u3059\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u9759\u3051\u3055\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Permito que minha mente descanse; h\xe1 quietude dentro de mim.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/OQ_Passion_flower.jpg/330px-OQ_Passion_flower.jpg"},{id:"plant-034",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#7C9D6A",name:"Ada \xc7ay\u0131 Keki\u011fi (Mercank\xf6\u015fk)",nameEn:"Oregano",nameDe:"Oregano",nameEs:"Or\xe9gano",nameFr:"Origan",nameJa:"\u30aa\u30ec\u30ac\u30ce",namePt:"Or\xe9gano",origin:"Akdeniz, Avrasya",originEn:"Mediterranean, Eurasia",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum, Eurasien",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo, Eurasia",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e, Eurasie",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u30fb\u30e6\u30fc\u30e9\u30b7\u30a2",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo, Eur\xe1sia",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["g\xfc\xe7lendirici","ne\u015fe","koruyucu"],propertiesEn:["strengthening","joy","protective"],propertiesDe:["st\xe4rkend","Freude","sch\xfctzend"],propertiesEs:["fortalecedor","alegr\xeda","protector"],propertiesFr:["fortifiant","joie","protecteur"],propertiesJa:["\u5f37\u5316","\u559c\u3073","\u5b88\u8b77"],propertiesPt:["fortalecedor","alegria","protetor"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131n s\u0131radan anlar\u0131nda ne\u015feyi ara. Mercank\xf6\u015fk antik Yunan'da 'da\u011f\u0131n sevinci' anlam\u0131na gelirdi; sen de k\xfc\xe7\xfck \u015feylerde mutlulu\u011fu bul.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, look for joy in life's ordinary moments. Oregano meant 'joy of the mountain' in ancient Greece; find happiness in small things too.",dailyMessageDe:"Suche heute Freude in den gew\xf6hnlichen Momenten des Lebens. Oregano bedeutete im antiken Griechenland 'Freude des Berges'; finde auch du Gl\xfcck in kleinen Dingen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, busca la alegr\xeda en los momentos ordinarios de la vida. El or\xe9gano significaba 'alegr\xeda de la monta\xf1a' en la antigua Grecia; encuentra tambi\xe9n felicidad en las peque\xf1as cosas.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, cherche la joie dans les moments ordinaires de la vie. L'origan signifiait 'joie de la montagne' dans la Gr\xe8ce antique ; trouve aussi le bonheur dans les petites choses.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u306e\u3042\u308a\u3075\u308c\u305f\u77ac\u9593\u306b\u559c\u3073\u3092\u63a2\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30aa\u30ec\u30ac\u30ce\u306f\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u3067\u300c\u5c71\u306e\u559c\u3073\u300d\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u3053\u3068\u306b\u5e78\u305b\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, procure a alegria nos momentos comuns da vida. O or\xe9gano significava 'alegria da montanha' na Gr\xe9cia antiga; encontre felicidade tamb\xe9m nas pequenas coisas.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 yemeklerine ekle ya da \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle. Buhar banyosunda nefes a\xe7\u0131c\u0131 olarak kullanabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Add the dried leaves to your meals, or lightly brew as a tea. You can use it in a steam bath to open the breath.",howToUseDe:"Gib die getrockneten Bl\xe4tter in deine Mahlzeiten oder br\xfche sie leicht als Tee. Du kannst ihn im Dampfbad zum \xd6ffnen des Atems verwenden.",howToUseEs:"A\xf1ade las hojas secas a tus comidas, o prep\xe1ralas ligeramente como t\xe9. Puedes usarlo en un ba\xf1o de vapor para abrir la respiraci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Ajoute les feuilles s\xe9ch\xe9es \xe0 tes plats, ou infuse-les l\xe9g\xe8rement en tisane. Tu peux l'utiliser en bain de vapeur pour d\xe9gager la respiration.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u8449\u3092\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u308b\u304b\u3001\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u84b8\u6c17\u6d74\u3067\u547c\u5438\u3092\u958b\u304f\u306e\u306b\u4f7f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Adicione as folhas secas \xe0s refei\xe7\xf5es, ou prepare levemente como ch\xe1. Voc\xea pode us\xe1-lo em um banho de vapor para abrir a respira\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"K\xfc\xe7\xfck anlar\u0131n sevincini kucakl\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I embrace the joy of small moments.",affirmationDe:"Ich umarme die Freude der kleinen Momente.",affirmationEs:"Abrazo la alegr\xeda de los peque\xf1os momentos.",affirmationFr:"J'embrasse la joie des petits instants.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u77ac\u9593\u306e\u559c\u3073\u3092\u62b1\u304d\u3057\u3081\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Abra\xe7o a alegria dos pequenos momentos.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Origanum_vulgare_-_harilik_pune.jpg/330px-Origanum_vulgare_-_harilik_pune.jpg"},{id:"plant-035",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#88A86B",name:"Fesle\u011fen",nameEn:"Basil",nameDe:"Basilikum",nameEs:"Albahaca",nameFr:"Basilic",nameJa:"\u30d0\u30b8\u30eb",namePt:"Manjeric\xe3o",origin:"Hindistan, G\xfcneydo\u011fu Asya",originEn:"India, Southeast Asia",originDe:"Indien, S\xfcdostasien",originEs:"India, Sudeste asi\xe1tico",originFr:"Inde, Asie du Sud-Est",originJa:"\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9\u30fb\u6771\u5357\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"\xcdndia, Sudeste Asi\xe1tico",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["bolluk","koruma","ferahl\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["abundance","protection","freshness"],propertiesDe:["F\xfclle","Schutz","Frische"],propertiesEs:["abundancia","protecci\xf3n","frescura"],propertiesFr:["abondance","protection","fra\xeecheur"],propertiesJa:["\u8c4a\u304b\u3055","\u5b88\u8b77","\u6e05\u6dbc"],propertiesPt:["abund\xe2ncia","prote\xe7\xe3o","frescor"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn sahip olduklar\u0131na \u015f\xfckret ve bollu\u011fa a\xe7\u0131l. Fesle\u011fen bir\xe7ok k\xfclt\xfcrde u\u011fur ve bereket sembol\xfcd\xfcr; minnet kalbini a\xe7ar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, be grateful for what you have and open to abundance. Basil is a symbol of luck and plenty in many cultures; gratitude opens your heart.",dailyMessageDe:"Sei heute dankbar f\xfcr das, was du hast, und \xf6ffne dich der F\xfclle. Basilikum ist in vielen Kulturen ein Symbol f\xfcr Gl\xfcck und \xdcberfluss; Dankbarkeit \xf6ffnet dein Herz.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, agradece lo que tienes y \xe1brete a la abundancia. La albahaca es s\xedmbolo de suerte y abundancia en muchas culturas; la gratitud abre tu coraz\xf3n.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, sois reconnaissant pour ce que tu as et ouvre-toi \xe0 l'abondance. Le basilic est un symbole de chance et de prosp\xe9rit\xe9 dans de nombreuses cultures ; la gratitude ouvre ton c\u0153ur.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u6301\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306b\u611f\u8b1d\u3057\u3001\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306b\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d0\u30b8\u30eb\u306f\u591a\u304f\u306e\u6587\u5316\u3067\u5e78\u904b\u3068\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3059\u3002\u611f\u8b1d\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, seja grato pelo que tem e abra-se \xe0 abund\xe2ncia. O manjeric\xe3o \xe9 s\xedmbolo de sorte e fartura em muitas culturas; a gratid\xe3o abre o seu cora\xe7\xe3o.",howToUse:"Taze yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 yemeklerine ekle ya da \xe7ay olarak demle. Bir saks\u0131 fesle\u011feni evine koyarak ferah ve u\u011furlu bir enerji davet et.",howToUseEn:"Add fresh leaves to your meals, or brew as a tea. Place a pot of basil in your home to invite fresh, lucky energy.",howToUseDe:"Gib frische Bl\xe4tter in deine Mahlzeiten oder br\xfche sie als Tee. Stelle einen Topf Basilikum in dein Zuhause, um frische, gl\xfcckbringende Energie einzuladen.",howToUseEs:"A\xf1ade hojas frescas a tus comidas, o prep\xe1ralas como t\xe9. Coloca una maceta de albahaca en tu hogar para invitar energ\xeda fresca y afortunada.",howToUseFr:"Ajoute des feuilles fra\xeeches \xe0 tes plats, ou infuse-les en tisane. Place un pot de basilic chez toi pour inviter une \xe9nergie fra\xeeche et porte-bonheur.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u8449\u3092\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u308b\u304b\u3001\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d0\u30b8\u30eb\u306e\u9262\u3092\u5bb6\u306b\u7f6e\u304d\u3001\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u3067\u5e78\u904b\u306a\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc\u3092\u62db\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Adicione folhas frescas \xe0s refei\xe7\xf5es, ou prepare como ch\xe1. Coloque um vaso de manjeric\xe3o em casa para convidar uma energia fresca e de sorte.",affirmation:"Sahip olduklar\u0131ma \u015f\xfckrediyorum, bollu\u011fa a\xe7\u0131\u011f\u0131m.",affirmationEn:"I am grateful for what I have and open to abundance.",affirmationDe:"Ich bin dankbar f\xfcr das, was ich habe, und offen f\xfcr F\xfclle.",affirmationEs:"Agradezco lo que tengo y estoy abierto a la abundancia.",affirmationFr:"Je suis reconnaissant pour ce que j'ai et ouvert \xe0 l'abondance.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6301\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306b\u611f\u8b1d\u3057\u3001\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306b\u958b\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Sou grato pelo que tenho e estou aberto \xe0 abund\xe2ncia.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Ocimum_basilicum_8zz.jpg/330px-Ocimum_basilicum_8zz.jpg",myth:"Fesle\u011fen, sevginin, koruman\u0131n ve kraliyetin otudur. Ad\u0131 Yunanca 'basilikon' \u2014 krala ait \u2014 k\xf6k\xfcnden gelir. Hindistan'da kutsal tulsi olarak tap\u0131n\u0131l\u0131r; Anadolu'da pencere kenar\u0131na konan saks\u0131s\u0131 eve bereket \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131r, sine\u011fi ve k\xf6t\xfc g\xf6z\xfc uzak tutar. Halk inanc\u0131nda mezar ba\u015f\u0131nda ekilen fesle\u011fen, ruha huzur dilemenin i\u015faretidir. Kokusu zihni canland\u0131r\u0131r, g\xf6nl\xfc a\xe7ar; misafire sunulan dal\u0131 ho\u015f geldin demektir.",mythEn:"Basil is the herb of love, protection and royalty. Its name comes from the Greek 'basilikon' \u2014 belonging to the king. In India it is revered as the sacred tulsi; in Anatolia a pot on the windowsill calls abundance into the home and keeps flies and the evil eye away. In folk belief, basil planted at the graveside is a sign of wishing peace upon the soul. Its scent enlivens the mind and opens the heart; a sprig offered to a guest is a welcome.",mythDe:"Basilikum ist das Kraut der Liebe, des Schutzes und des K\xf6niglichen. Sein Name kommt vom griechischen 'basilikon' \u2014 dem K\xf6nig geh\xf6rend. In Indien wird es als heiliges Tulsi verehrt; in Anatolien ruft ein Topf auf der Fensterbank F\xfclle ins Haus und h\xe4lt Fliegen und den b\xf6sen Blick fern. Im Volksglauben ist am Grab gepflanztes Basilikum ein Zeichen, der Seele Frieden zu w\xfcnschen. Sein Duft belebt den Geist und \xf6ffnet das Herz; ein einem Gast gereichter Zweig ist ein Willkommen.",mythEs:"La albahaca es la hierba del amor, la protecci\xf3n y la realeza. Su nombre viene del griego 'basilikon' \u2014 perteneciente al rey. En la India se la venera como la sagrada tulsi; en Anatolia una maceta en el alf\xe9izar llama la abundancia al hogar y mantiene alejadas las moscas y el mal de ojo. En la creencia popular, la albahaca plantada junto a la tumba es se\xf1al de desear paz al alma. Su aroma aviva la mente y abre el coraz\xf3n; una ramita ofrecida a un hu\xe9sped es una bienvenida.",mythFr:"Le basilic est l'herbe de l'amour, de la protection et de la royaut\xe9. Son nom vient du grec 'basilikon' \u2014 qui appartient au roi. En Inde, il est v\xe9n\xe9r\xe9 comme le tulsi sacr\xe9 ; en Anatolie, un pot sur le rebord de la fen\xeatre appelle l'abondance dans la maison et tient \xe0 distance les mouches et le mauvais \u0153il. Dans la croyance populaire, le basilic plant\xe9 au bord de la tombe est un signe de v\u0153u de paix pour l'\xe2me. Son parfum ravive l'esprit et ouvre le c\u0153ur ; un brin offert \xe0 un h\xf4te est un accueil.",mythJa:"\u30d0\u30b8\u30eb\u306f\u611b\u3068\u5b88\u308a\u3068\u738b\u8005\u306e\u8349\u3002\u305d\u306e\u540d\u306f\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u8a9e\u300c\u30d0\u30b7\u30ea\u30b3\u30f3\u300d\u2014\u2014\u738b\u306b\u5c5e\u3059\u308b\u2014\u2014\u306b\u7531\u6765\u3059\u308b\u3002\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9\u3067\u306f\u8056\u306a\u308b\u30c8\u30a5\u30eb\u30b7\u30fc\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5d07\u3081\u3089\u308c\u3001\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u7a93\u8fba\u306e\u9262\u304c\u5bb6\u306b\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u3092\u62db\u304d\u3001\u877f\u3068\u90aa\u8996\u3092\u9060\u3056\u3051\u308b\u3002\u6c11\u9593\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5893\u8fba\u306b\u690d\u3048\u308b\u30d0\u30b8\u30eb\u306f\u9b42\u306b\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u9858\u3046\u3057\u308b\u3057\u3002\u305d\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u751f\u304d\u751f\u304d\u3068\u3055\u305b\u3001\u80f8\u3092\u958b\u304f\u3002\u5ba2\u306b\u5dee\u3057\u51fa\u3059\u4e00\u679d\u306f\u6b53\u8fce\u306e\u610f\u3002",mythPt:"O manjeric\xe3o \xe9 a erva do amor, da prote\xe7\xe3o e da realeza. O seu nome vem do grego 'basilikon' \u2014 pertencente ao rei. Na \xcdndia \xe9 venerado como o sagrado tulsi; na Anat\xf3lia um vaso no parapeito chama a abund\xe2ncia para casa e mant\xe9m afastadas as moscas e o mau-olhado. Na cren\xe7a popular, o manjeric\xe3o plantado \xe0 beira da campa \xe9 sinal de desejar paz \xe0 alma. O seu aroma avia a mente e abre o cora\xe7\xe3o; um raminho oferecido a um h\xf3spede \xe9 um acolhimento."},{id:"plant-036",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#6B8E5A",name:"Ki\u015fni\u015f",nameEn:"Coriander",nameDe:"Koriander",nameEs:"Cilantro",nameFr:"Coriandre",nameJa:"\u30b3\u30ea\u30a2\u30f3\u30c0\u30fc",namePt:"Coentro",origin:"G\xfcney Avrupa, Bat\u0131 Asya",originEn:"Southern Europe, Western Asia",originDe:"S\xfcdeuropa, Westasien",originEs:"Sur de Europa, Asia Occidental",originFr:"Europe du Sud, Asie occidentale",originJa:"\u5357\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u897f\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Sul da Europa, \xc1sia Ocidental",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","sindirim dostu","denge"],propertiesEn:["purifying","digestive","balance"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","verdauungsf\xf6rdernd","Gleichgewicht"],propertiesEs:["purificante","digestivo","equilibrio"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","digestif","\xe9quilibre"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u6d88\u5316\u3092\u52a9\u3051\u308b","\u5747\u8861"],propertiesPt:["purificante","digestivo","equil\xedbrio"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn biriktirdi\u011fin a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131klar\u0131 nazik\xe7e b\u0131rak. Ki\u015fni\u015f geleneksel olarak ar\u0131nma ile an\u0131l\u0131r; sen de gereksiz y\xfckleri sal\u0131ver ve hafifle.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, gently let go of the weight you've accumulated. Coriander is traditionally linked with cleansing; release what you don't need and lighten.",dailyMessageDe:"Lass heute sanft die Last los, die du angesammelt hast. Koriander wird traditionell mit Reinigung verbunden; gib \xdcberfl\xfcssiges frei und werde leichter.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, suelta con suavidad el peso que has acumulado. El cilantro se asocia tradicionalmente con la limpieza; libera lo que no necesitas y alig\xe9rate.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, lib\xe8re doucement le poids que tu as accumul\xe9. La coriandre est traditionnellement li\xe9e \xe0 la purification ; rel\xe2che ce dont tu n'as pas besoin et all\xe8ge-toi.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u6e9c\u3081\u8fbc\u3093\u3060\u91cd\u3055\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u624b\u653e\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b3\u30ea\u30a2\u30f3\u30c0\u30fc\u306f\u4f1d\u7d71\u7684\u306b\u6d44\u5316\u3068\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u8981\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u3092\u624b\u653e\u3057\u3001\u8efd\u304f\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, solte com suavidade o peso que voc\xea acumulou. O coentro est\xe1 tradicionalmente ligado \xe0 limpeza; libere o que n\xe3o precisa e fique mais leve.",howToUse:"Tohumlar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip sindirim i\xe7in i\xe7 ya da taze yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 yemeklerine ekle. Tohumlar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7i\u011fneyerek nefesini tazele.",howToUseEn:"Brew the seeds in hot water for digestion, or add fresh leaves to your meals. Chew the seeds to freshen your breath.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Samen in hei\xdfem Wasser f\xfcr die Verdauung oder gib frische Bl\xe4tter in deine Mahlzeiten. Kaue die Samen, um deinen Atem zu erfrischen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las semillas en agua caliente para la digesti\xf3n, o a\xf1ade hojas frescas a tus comidas. Mastica las semillas para refrescar el aliento.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les graines dans de l'eau chaude pour la digestion, ou ajoute des feuilles fra\xeeches \xe0 tes plats. M\xe2che les graines pour rafra\xeechir ton haleine.",howToUseJa:"\u7a2e\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3066\u6d88\u5316\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u98f2\u3080\u304b\u3001\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u8449\u3092\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7a2e\u3092\u565b\u3093\u3067\u606f\u3092\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306b\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as sementes em \xe1gua quente para a digest\xe3o, ou adicione folhas frescas \xe0s refei\xe7\xf5es. Mastigue as sementes para refrescar o h\xe1lito.",affirmation:"Gereksiz y\xfckleri b\u0131rak\u0131yorum, hafif ve dengedeyim.",affirmationEn:"I release unnecessary burdens; I am light and balanced.",affirmationDe:"Ich lasse unn\xf6tige Lasten los; ich bin leicht und im Gleichgewicht.",affirmationEs:"Suelto las cargas innecesarias; estoy ligero y en equilibrio.",affirmationFr:"Je lib\xe8re les fardeaux inutiles ; je suis l\xe9ger et \xe9quilibr\xe9.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4e0d\u8981\u306a\u91cd\u8377\u3092\u624b\u653e\u3059\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u8efd\u304f\u3001\u5747\u8861\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Solto os fardos desnecess\xe1rios; estou leve e equilibrado.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Coriandrum_sativum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-193.jpg/330px-Coriandrum_sativum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-193.jpg"},{id:"plant-037",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3e",color:"#C7A23E",name:"Anason",nameEn:"Anise",nameDe:"Anis",nameEs:"An\xeds",nameFr:"Anis",nameJa:"\u30a2\u30cb\u30b9",namePt:"Erva-doce",origin:"Do\u011fu Akdeniz, Bat\u0131 Asya",originEn:"Eastern Mediterranean, Western Asia",originDe:"\xd6stliches Mittelmeer, Westasien",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo oriental, Asia Occidental",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e orientale, Asie occidentale",originJa:"\u6771\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u30fb\u897f\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo Oriental, \xc1sia Ocidental",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Lar\xedngeo",properties:["rahatlat\u0131c\u0131","sindirim dostu","huzur"],propertiesEn:["soothing","digestive","peace"],propertiesDe:["beruhigend","verdauungsf\xf6rdernd","Frieden"],propertiesEs:["calmante","digestivo","paz"],propertiesFr:["apaisant","digestif","paix"],propertiesJa:["\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b","\u6d88\u5316\u3092\u52a9\u3051\u308b","\u5b89\u3089\u304e"],propertiesPt:["suavizante","digestivo","paz"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xfcn\xfcn\xfc tatl\u0131 ve sakin bir notayla kapat. Anason yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131c\u0131 bir bitkidir; i\xe7indeki gerginli\u011fi yumu\u015fat\u0131r, huzura davet eder.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, close your day on a sweet, calm note. Anise is a soothing plant; it softens the tension within you and invites peace.",dailyMessageDe:"Schlie\xdfe heute deinen Tag mit einer s\xfc\xdfen, ruhigen Note ab. Anis ist eine beruhigende Pflanze; er mildert die Spannung in dir und l\xe4dt zum Frieden ein.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, cierra tu d\xeda con una nota dulce y serena. El an\xeds es una planta calmante; suaviza la tensi\xf3n interior e invita a la paz.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, termine ta journ\xe9e sur une note douce et calme. L'anis est une plante apaisante ; il adoucit la tension en toi et invite \xe0 la paix.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u7518\u3084\u304b\u3067\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u97f3\u8272\u3067\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u7de0\u3081\u304f\u304f\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30a2\u30cb\u30b9\u306f\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b\u690d\u7269\u3002\u5185\u306a\u308b\u7dca\u5f35\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u3001\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3078\u8a98\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, encerre o seu dia em uma nota doce e tranquila. A erva-doce \xe9 uma planta calmante; suaviza a tens\xe3o interior e convida \xe0 paz.",howToUse:"Tohumlar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip yemek sonras\u0131 ya da yatmadan \xf6nce i\xe7. Bal ekleyerek tatland\u0131rabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Brew the seeds in hot water and drink after meals or before bed. You can sweeten it with honey.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Samen in hei\xdfem Wasser und trinke sie nach dem Essen oder vor dem Schlafen. Du kannst ihn mit Honig s\xfc\xdfen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las semillas en agua caliente y bebe despu\xe9s de las comidas o antes de dormir. Puedes endulzarlo con miel.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les graines dans de l'eau chaude et bois apr\xe8s les repas ou avant le coucher. Tu peux le sucrer avec du miel.",howToUseJa:"\u7a2e\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u98df\u5f8c\u3084\u5c31\u5bdd\u524d\u306b\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u8702\u871c\u3067\u7518\u304f\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as sementes em \xe1gua quente e beba ap\xf3s as refei\xe7\xf5es ou antes de dormir. Voc\xea pode ado\xe7ar com mel.",affirmation:"G\xfcn\xfcm\xfc huzurla kapat\u0131yorum, i\xe7im sakin.",affirmationEn:"I close my day in peace; my inner self is calm.",affirmationDe:"Ich schlie\xdfe meinen Tag in Frieden ab; mein Inneres ist ruhig.",affirmationEs:"Cierro mi d\xeda en paz; mi interior est\xe1 en calma.",affirmationFr:"Je termine ma journ\xe9e en paix ; mon int\xe9rieur est calme.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u9589\u3058\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u5185\u306f\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u3060\u3002",affirmationPt:"Encerro o meu dia em paz; o meu interior est\xe1 calmo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Koehler1887-PimpinellaAnisum.jpg/330px-Koehler1887-PimpinellaAnisum.jpg"},{id:"plant-038",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3c",color:"#E0C341",name:"S\u0131\u011f\u0131r Kuyru\u011fu",nameEn:"Mullein",nameDe:"K\xf6nigskerze",nameEs:"Gordolobo",nameFr:"Mol\xe8ne",nameJa:"\u30d3\u30ed\u30fc\u30c9\u30e2\u30a6\u30ba\u30a4\u30ab",namePt:"Verbasco",origin:"Avrupa, Asya",originEn:"Europe, Asia",originDe:"Europa, Asien",originEs:"Europa, Asia",originFr:"Europe, Asie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Lar\xedngeo",properties:["yumu\u015fat\u0131c\u0131","koruyucu","nefes a\xe7\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["softening","protective","breath-opening"],propertiesDe:["weichmachend","sch\xfctzend","atem\xf6ffnend"],propertiesEs:["suavizante","protector","abre la respiraci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["adoucissant","protecteur","ouvre la respiration"],propertiesJa:["\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u308b","\u5b88\u8b77","\u547c\u5438\u3092\u958b\u304f"],propertiesPt:["suavizante","protetor","abre a respira\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn nazik\xe7e nefes al ve i\xe7indeki yumu\u015fakl\u0131\u011f\u0131 koru. S\u0131\u011f\u0131r kuyru\u011fu dik durur ama yapraklar\u0131 kadifedir; g\xfc\xe7 ve \u015fefkat bir arada olabilir.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, breathe gently and protect the softness within. Mullein stands tall yet its leaves are velvet; strength and tenderness can coexist.",dailyMessageDe:"Atme heute sanft und bewahre die Weichheit in dir. Die K\xf6nigskerze steht aufrecht, doch ihre Bl\xe4tter sind samtig; St\xe4rke und Z\xe4rtlichkeit k\xf6nnen zugleich bestehen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, respira con suavidad y protege la suavidad interior. El gordolobo se yergue alto pero sus hojas son aterciopeladas; la fuerza y la ternura pueden coexistir.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, respire doucement et prot\xe8ge la douceur en toi. La mol\xe8ne se dresse haut mais ses feuilles sont de velours ; force et tendresse peuvent coexister.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u547c\u5438\u3057\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u3084\u308f\u3089\u304b\u3055\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d3\u30ed\u30fc\u30c9\u30e2\u30a6\u30ba\u30a4\u30ab\u306f\u9ad8\u304f\u305d\u3073\u3048\u306a\u304c\u3089\u8449\u306f\u30d3\u30ed\u30fc\u30c9\u306e\u3088\u3046\u3002\u5f37\u3055\u3068\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055\u306f\u5171\u306b\u3042\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, respire com suavidade e proteja a suavidade interior. O verbasco se ergue alto, mas suas folhas s\xe3o de veludo; for\xe7a e ternura podem coexistir.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7ek ve yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak demle, bo\u011faz ve nefes i\xe7in \u0131l\u0131k i\xe7. Demlemeyi s\xfczge\xe7ten ge\xe7irerek t\xfcylerinden ar\u0131nd\u0131r.",howToUseEn:"Brew the flowers and leaves as a tea and drink warm for the throat and breath. Strain the infusion to remove the fine hairs.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche Bl\xfcten und Bl\xe4tter als Tee und trinke ihn warm f\xfcr Hals und Atem. Siebe den Aufguss, um die feinen H\xe4rchen zu entfernen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona flores y hojas como t\xe9 y bebe tibio para la garganta y la respiraci\xf3n. Cuela la infusi\xf3n para retirar los pelillos finos.",howToUseFr:"Infuse fleurs et feuilles en tisane et bois ti\xe8de pour la gorge et la respiration. Filtre l'infusion pour retirer les petits poils.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3068\u8449\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u5589\u3068\u547c\u5438\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6e29\u304b\u304f\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u714e\u3058\u6db2\u3092\u6ffe\u3057\u3066\u7d30\u304b\u3044\u6bdb\u3092\u53d6\u308a\u9664\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores e folhas como ch\xe1 e beba morno para a garganta e a respira\xe7\xe3o. Coe a infus\xe3o para remover os pelinhos finos.",affirmation:"G\xfc\xe7l\xfc dururken yumu\u015fakl\u0131\u011f\u0131m\u0131 koruyorum.",affirmationEn:"I stand strong while protecting my softness.",affirmationDe:"Ich stehe stark und bewahre dabei meine Sanftheit.",affirmationEs:"Permanezco fuerte mientras protejo mi suavidad.",affirmationFr:"Je reste fort tout en prot\xe9geant ma douceur.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5f37\u304f\u7acb\u3061\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3001\u3084\u308f\u3089\u304b\u3055\u3092\u5b88\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Permane\xe7o forte enquanto protejo a minha suavidade.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Verbascum_sinuatum_August_2007-1.jpg/330px-Verbascum_sinuatum_August_2007-1.jpg"},{id:"plant-039",emoji:"\ud83d\udc9b",color:"#E8B23A",name:"Sar\u0131 Papatya (\xd6k\xfczg\xf6z\xfc)",nameEn:"Arnica",nameDe:"Arnika",nameEs:"\xc1rnica",nameFr:"Arnica",nameJa:"\u30a2\u30eb\u30cb\u30ab",namePt:"Arnica",origin:"Avrupa da\u011flar\u0131",originEn:"European mountains",originDe:"Europ\xe4ische Gebirge",originEs:"Monta\xf1as de Europa",originFr:"Montagnes d'Europe",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u306e\u5c71\u5cb3",originPt:"Montanhas da Europa",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["onar\u0131c\u0131","rahatlat\u0131c\u0131","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["restorative","soothing","resilience"],propertiesDe:["regenerierend","beruhigend","Widerstandskraft"],propertiesEs:["reparador","calmante","resiliencia"],propertiesFr:["r\xe9parateur","apaisant","r\xe9silience"],propertiesJa:["\u56de\u5fa9","\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b","\u56de\u5fa9\u529b"],propertiesPt:["restaurador","suavizante","resili\xeancia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn d\xfc\u015f\xfc\u015flerinden sonra kendine nazik\xe7e bak. Arnika morarmalar\u0131 yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131r; sen de incindi\u011fin yerlere \u015fefkatle dokun ve yeniden aya\u011fa kalk.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, look kindly upon yourself after your falls. Arnica soothes bruises; touch your bruised places with compassion and rise again.",dailyMessageDe:"Sieh heute nach deinen St\xfcrzen freundlich auf dich. Arnika beruhigt blaue Flecken; ber\xfchre deine verletzten Stellen mit Mitgef\xfchl und steh wieder auf.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, m\xedrate con bondad despu\xe9s de tus ca\xeddas. El \xe1rnica calma los moretones; toca con compasi\xf3n tus lugares heridos y lev\xe1ntate de nuevo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, regarde-toi avec bont\xe9 apr\xe8s tes chutes. L'arnica apaise les bleus ; touche tes zones meurtries avec compassion et rel\xe8ve-toi.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u8ee2\u3093\u3060\u3042\u3068\u306e\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u898b\u3064\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30a2\u30eb\u30cb\u30ab\u306f\u6253\u3061\u8eab\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u307e\u3059\u3002\u75db\u3093\u3060\u3068\u3053\u308d\u306b\u601d\u3044\u3084\u308a\u3067\u3075\u308c\u3001\u307e\u305f\u7acb\u3061\u4e0a\u304c\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, olhe com bondade para si depois das suas quedas. A arnica acalma os hematomas; toque com compaix\xe3o os seus pontos feridos e levante-se de novo.",howToUse:"Ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ya da kremini berelenmi\u015f cilde d\u0131\u015ftan nazik\xe7e uygula. Asla a\xe7\u0131k yaraya ya da i\xe7 kullan\u0131m i\xe7in uygulama; sadece harici kullan.",howToUseEn:"Gently apply the oil or cream externally to bruised skin. Never use on open wounds or internally; for external use only.",howToUseDe:"Trage das \xd6l oder die Creme \xe4u\xdferlich sanft auf verletzte Haut auf. Niemals auf offene Wunden oder innerlich anwenden; nur zur \xe4u\xdferen Anwendung.",howToUseEs:"Aplica suavemente el aceite o la crema de forma externa sobre la piel magullada. Nunca lo uses en heridas abiertas ni de forma interna; solo uso externo.",howToUseFr:"Applique doucement l'huile ou la cr\xe8me en externe sur la peau meurtrie. Ne jamais utiliser sur des plaies ouvertes ni en interne ; usage externe uniquement.",howToUseJa:"\u6cb9\u3084\u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30e0\u3092\u6253\u3061\u8eab\u306e\u808c\u306b\u5916\u7528\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5857\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u958b\u3044\u305f\u50b7\u3084\u5185\u670d\u306b\u306f\u6c7a\u3057\u3066\u4f7f\u308f\u305a\u3001\u5916\u7528\u306e\u307f\u3002",howToUsePt:"Aplique suavemente o \xf3leo ou creme externamente na pele machucada. Nunca use em feridas abertas ou internamente; somente uso externo.",affirmation:"D\xfc\u015fsem de incindi\u011fim yerlere \u015fefkatle dokunup aya\u011fa kalk\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"Even when I fall, I touch my wounds with compassion and rise.",affirmationDe:"Auch wenn ich falle, ber\xfchre ich meine Wunden mit Mitgef\xfchl und stehe auf.",affirmationEs:"Aunque caiga, toco mis heridas con compasi\xf3n y me levanto.",affirmationFr:"M\xeame quand je tombe, je touche mes blessures avec compassion et je me rel\xe8ve.",affirmationJa:"\u305f\u3068\u3048\u8ee2\u3093\u3067\u3082\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u50b7\u306b\u601d\u3044\u3084\u308a\u3067\u3075\u308c\u3001\u7acb\u3061\u4e0a\u304c\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Mesmo quando caio, toco minhas feridas com compaix\xe3o e me levanto.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Arnica_montana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-015.jpg/330px-Arnica_montana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-015.jpg"},{id:"plant-040",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5F8A6E",name:"Is\u0131rgan Otu",nameEn:"Nettle",nameDe:"Brennnessel",nameEs:"Ortiga",nameFr:"Ortie",nameJa:"\u30cd\u30c8\u30eb",namePt:"Urtiga",origin:"Avrupa, Asya, Kuzey Amerika",originEn:"Europe, Asia, North America",originDe:"Europa, Asien, Nordamerika",originEs:"Europa, Asia, Am\xe9rica del Norte",originFr:"Europe, Asie, Am\xe9rique du Nord",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u5317\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia, Am\xe9rica do Norte",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["g\xfc\xe7lendirici","canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","besleyici"],propertiesEn:["strengthening","invigorating","nourishing"],propertiesDe:["st\xe4rkend","belebend","n\xe4hrend"],propertiesEs:["fortalecedor","vigorizante","nutritivo"],propertiesFr:["fortifiant","tonifiant","nourrissant"],propertiesJa:["\u5f37\u5316","\u6d3b\u6027","\u6ecb\u990a"],propertiesPt:["fortalecedor","revigorante","nutritivo"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn d\u0131\u015f\u0131 dikenli g\xf6r\xfcnenin i\xe7inde besleyici bir hazine olabilece\u011fini hat\u0131rla. Is\u0131rgan zorluklar\u0131n alt\u0131nda sakl\u0131 g\xfcc\xfc temsil eder.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that what looks prickly on the outside can hold a nourishing treasure within. Nettle represents the strength hidden beneath hardship.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass das, was au\xdfen stachelig wirkt, innen einen n\xe4hrenden Schatz bergen kann. Die Brennnessel steht f\xfcr die Kraft, die unter Schwierigkeiten verborgen liegt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que lo que parece espinoso por fuera puede guardar un tesoro nutritivo dentro. La ortiga representa la fuerza oculta bajo la dificultad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que ce qui para\xeet piquant \xe0 l'ext\xe9rieur peut renfermer un tr\xe9sor nourrissant. L'ortie repr\xe9sente la force cach\xe9e sous la difficult\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5916\u304c\u3068\u3052\u3068\u3052\u3057\u304f\u898b\u3048\u308b\u3082\u306e\u304c\u3001\u5185\u306b\u6ecb\u990a\u306e\u5b9d\u3092\u79d8\u3081\u3046\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30cd\u30c8\u30eb\u306f\u56f0\u96e3\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u529b\u3092\u8868\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que o que parece espinhoso por fora pode guardar um tesouro nutritivo por dentro. A urtiga representa a for\xe7a escondida sob a dificuldade.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak demle, canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131 bir i\xe7ecek i\xe7in i\xe7. Taze toplarken eldiven kullan; pi\u015firince ya da kuruyunca dikenli\u011fi kaybolur.",howToUseEn:"Brew the dried leaves as a tea for an invigorating drink. Wear gloves when picking it fresh; its sting fades once cooked or dried.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die getrockneten Bl\xe4tter als Tee f\xfcr ein belebendes Getr\xe4nk. Trage Handschuhe beim frischen Pfl\xfccken; das Brennen verschwindet beim Kochen oder Trocknen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las hojas secas como t\xe9 para una bebida vigorizante. Usa guantes al recogerla fresca; su escozor desaparece al cocinarla o secarla.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les feuilles s\xe9ch\xe9es en tisane pour une boisson tonifiante. Porte des gants pour la cueillir fra\xeeche ; sa piq\xfbre dispara\xeet une fois cuite ou s\xe9ch\xe9e.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u8449\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u6d3b\u6027\u5316\u3059\u308b\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u751f\u3067\u6458\u3080\u3068\u304d\u306f\u624b\u888b\u3092\u3002\u52a0\u71b1\u3084\u4e7e\u71e5\u3067\u3068\u3052\u306f\u6d88\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as folhas secas como ch\xe1 para uma bebida revigorante. Use luvas ao colh\xea-la fresca; a ard\xeancia some quando cozida ou seca.",affirmation:"Zorluklar\u0131n alt\u0131ndaki g\xfcc\xfcm\xfc ve de\u011ferimi g\xf6r\xfcyorum.",affirmationEn:"I see the strength and worth hidden beneath hardship.",affirmationDe:"Ich sehe die Kraft und den Wert, die unter Schwierigkeiten verborgen sind.",affirmationEs:"Veo la fuerza y el valor ocultos bajo la dificultad.",affirmationFr:"Je vois la force et la valeur cach\xe9es sous la difficult\xe9.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u56f0\u96e3\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u529b\u3068\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u898b\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Vejo a for\xe7a e o valor escondidos sob a dificuldade.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Fen_nettle_%28Urtica_dioica_ssp._galeopsifolia%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5423125.jpg/330px-Fen_nettle_%28Urtica_dioica_ssp._galeopsifolia%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5423125.jpg"},{id:"plant-041",emoji:"\ud83c\udf38",color:"#E29ABF",name:"Ebeg\xfcmeci",nameEn:"Mallow",nameDe:"Malve",nameEs:"Malva",nameFr:"Mauve",nameJa:"\u30de\u30ed\u30a6",namePt:"Malva",origin:"Avrupa, Asya, Afrika",originEn:"Europe, Asia, Africa",originDe:"Europa, Asien, Afrika",originEs:"Europa, Asia, \xc1frica",originFr:"Europe, Asie, Afrique",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u30a2\u30d5\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia, \xc1frica",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Lar\xedngeo",properties:["yumu\u015fat\u0131c\u0131","yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","\u015fefkat"],propertiesEn:["softening","soothing","compassion"],propertiesDe:["weichmachend","beruhigend","Mitgef\xfchl"],propertiesEs:["suavizante","calmante","compasi\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["adoucissant","apaisant","compassion"],propertiesJa:["\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u308b","\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b","\u6148\u3057\u307f"],propertiesPt:["suavizante","calmante","compaix\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kendine ve ba\u015fkalar\u0131na yumu\u015fakl\u0131kla yakla\u015f. Ebeg\xfcmeci nazik\xe7e yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131ran bir bitkidir; sertli\u011fin yerine \u015fefkati se\xe7.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, approach yourself and others with softness. Mallow is a gently soothing plant; choose compassion over harshness.",dailyMessageDe:"Begegne heute dir selbst und anderen mit Sanftheit. Malve ist eine sanft beruhigende Pflanze; w\xe4hle Mitgef\xfchl statt H\xe4rte.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ac\xe9rcate a ti y a los dem\xe1s con suavidad. La malva es una planta que calma con dulzura; elige la compasi\xf3n en lugar de la dureza.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, approche-toi de toi-m\xeame et des autres avec douceur. La mauve est une plante qui apaise en douceur ; choisis la compassion plut\xf4t que la duret\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u3082\u4ed6\u8005\u306b\u3082\u3084\u308f\u3089\u304b\u304f\u63a5\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30de\u30ed\u30a6\u306f\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b\u690d\u7269\u3002\u786c\u3055\u306e\u4ee3\u308f\u308a\u306b\u601d\u3044\u3084\u308a\u3092\u9078\u3073\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, aproxime-se de si e dos outros com suavidade. A malva \xe9 uma planta que acalma com delicadeza; escolha a compaix\xe3o em vez da dureza.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7ek ve yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip bo\u011faz i\xe7in \u0131l\u0131k i\xe7. So\u011fuk demlemesi mavi-mor renk verir; rengiyle de g\xf6z\xfcn\xfc dinlendir.",howToUseEn:"Brew the flowers and leaves in hot water and drink warm for the throat. A cold infusion turns blue-violet; let its color rest your eyes too.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche Bl\xfcten und Bl\xe4tter in hei\xdfem Wasser und trinke sie warm f\xfcr den Hals. Ein Kaltaufguss wird blau-violett; lass auch seine Farbe deine Augen ruhen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona flores y hojas en agua caliente y bebe tibio para la garganta. Una infusi\xf3n fr\xeda se vuelve azul violeta; deja que su color tambi\xe9n descanse tus ojos.",howToUseFr:"Infuse fleurs et feuilles dans de l'eau chaude et bois ti\xe8de pour la gorge. Une infusion froide devient bleu-violet ; laisse aussi sa couleur reposer tes yeux.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3068\u8449\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u5589\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6e29\u304b\u304f\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6c34\u51fa\u3057\u306f\u9752\u7d2b\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u305d\u306e\u8272\u3067\u76ee\u3082\u4f11\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare flores e folhas em \xe1gua quente e beba morno para a garganta. Uma infus\xe3o fria fica azul-violeta; deixe a cor tamb\xe9m descansar os seus olhos.",affirmation:"Kendime ve ba\u015fkalar\u0131na yumu\u015fakl\u0131kla yakla\u015f\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I approach myself and others with softness.",affirmationDe:"Ich begegne mir und anderen mit Sanftheit.",affirmationEs:"Me acerco a m\xed y a los dem\xe1s con suavidad.",affirmationFr:"Je m'approche de moi-m\xeame et des autres avec douceur.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u3068\u4ed6\u8005\u306b\u3084\u308f\u3089\u304b\u304f\u63a5\u3059\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Aproximo-me de mim e dos outros com suavidade.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Mallow_January_2008-1.jpg/330px-Mallow_January_2008-1.jpg"},{id:"plant-042",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3a",color:"#E26D5A",name:"Hibiskus",nameEn:"Hibiscus",nameDe:"Hibiskus",nameEs:"Hibisco",nameFr:"Hibiscus",nameJa:"\u30cf\u30a4\u30d3\u30b9\u30ab\u30b9",namePt:"Hibisco",origin:"Tropikal b\xf6lgeler",originEn:"Tropical regions",originDe:"Tropische Regionen",originEs:"Regiones tropicales",originFr:"R\xe9gions tropicales",originJa:"\u71b1\u5e2f\u5730\u57df",originPt:"Regi\xf5es tropicais",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u30b5\u30af\u30e9\u30eb\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacral",properties:["canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","tutku","ne\u015fe"],propertiesEn:["invigorating","passion","joy"],propertiesDe:["belebend","Leidenschaft","Freude"],propertiesEs:["vigorizante","pasi\xf3n","alegr\xeda"],propertiesFr:["tonifiant","passion","joie"],propertiesJa:["\u6d3b\u6027","\u60c5\u71b1","\u559c\u3073"],propertiesPt:["revigorante","paix\xe3o","alegria"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn i\xe7indeki canl\u0131 renge izin ver. Hibiskus parlak ve cesur a\xe7ar; sen de tutkunu ve ya\u015fam sevincini g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr k\u0131l.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, allow the vivid color within you. Hibiscus blooms bright and bold; make your passion and joy of life visible too.",dailyMessageDe:"Lass heute die lebendige Farbe in dir zu. Hibiskus bl\xfcht hell und k\xfchn; mache auch deine Leidenschaft und Lebensfreude sichtbar.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, permite el color vivo en tu interior. El hibisco florece brillante y audaz; haz visible tambi\xe9n tu pasi\xf3n y tu alegr\xeda de vivir.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, laisse la couleur vive en toi s'exprimer. L'hibiscus fleurit \xe9clatant et audacieux ; rends aussi ta passion et ta joie de vivre visibles.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u9bae\u3084\u304b\u306a\u8272\u3092\u8a31\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30cf\u30a4\u30d3\u30b9\u30ab\u30b9\u306f\u660e\u308b\u304f\u5927\u80c6\u306b\u54b2\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u60c5\u71b1\u3068\u751f\u304d\u308b\u559c\u3073\u3082\u898b\u3048\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, permita a cor v\xedvida dentro de voc\xea. O hibisco floresce brilhante e ousado; torne tamb\xe9m a sua paix\xe3o e alegria de viver vis\xedveis.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f \xe7i\xe7eklerini s\u0131cak ya da so\u011fuk suda demleyip k\u0131rm\u0131z\u0131, ferahlat\u0131c\u0131 bir i\xe7ecek olarak i\xe7. Bal ya da limonla tatland\u0131r.",howToUseEn:"Brew the dried flowers in hot or cold water for a red, refreshing drink. Sweeten with honey or lemon.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die getrockneten Bl\xfcten in hei\xdfem oder kaltem Wasser f\xfcr ein rotes, erfrischendes Getr\xe4nk. S\xfc\xdfe mit Honig oder Zitrone.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las flores secas en agua caliente o fr\xeda para una bebida roja y refrescante. Endulza con miel o lim\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fleurs s\xe9ch\xe9es dans de l'eau chaude ou froide pour une boisson rouge et rafra\xeechissante. Sucre avec du miel ou du citron.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u82b1\u3092\u6e6f\u307e\u305f\u306f\u51b7\u6c34\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u8d64\u304f\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u8702\u871c\u3084\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u3067\u7518\u304f\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores secas em \xe1gua quente ou fria para uma bebida vermelha e refrescante. Adoce com mel ou lim\xe3o.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7imdeki canl\u0131 rengi ve ya\u015fam sevincimi g\xf6steriyorum.",affirmationEn:"I show the vivid color within me and my joy of life.",affirmationDe:"Ich zeige die lebendige Farbe in mir und meine Lebensfreude.",affirmationEs:"Muestro el color vivo en m\xed y mi alegr\xeda de vivir.",affirmationFr:"Je montre la couleur vive en moi et ma joie de vivre.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u9bae\u3084\u304b\u306a\u8272\u3068\u751f\u304d\u308b\u559c\u3073\u3092\u793a\u3059\u3002",affirmationPt:"Mostro a cor v\xedvida dentro de mim e a minha alegria de viver.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg/330px-Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg"},{id:"plant-043",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#7A9A52",name:"Limon Otu",nameEn:"Lemongrass",nameDe:"Zitronengras",nameEs:"Hierba de lim\xf3n",nameFr:"Citronnelle",nameJa:"\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30b0\u30e9\u30b9",namePt:"Capim-lim\xe3o",origin:"G\xfcney Asya, Tropikler",originEn:"South Asia, Tropics",originDe:"S\xfcdasien, Tropen",originEs:"Sur de Asia, Tr\xf3picos",originFr:"Asie du Sud, Tropiques",originJa:"\u5357\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u71b1\u5e2f",originPt:"Sul da \xc1sia, Tr\xf3picos",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["ferahlat\u0131c\u0131","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["refreshing","clarifying","invigorating"],propertiesDe:["erfrischend","kl\xe4rend","belebend"],propertiesEs:["refrescante","clarificador","vigorizante"],propertiesFr:["rafra\xeechissant","clarifiant","tonifiant"],propertiesJa:["\u723d\u5feb","\u660e\u6670","\u6d3b\u6027"],propertiesPt:["refrescante","clarificador","revigorante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn zihnini ve \xe7evreni ferahlat. Limon otu canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131 bir kokuya sahiptir; durgunlu\u011fu da\u011f\u0131t\u0131r, yeni bir tazelik getirir.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, refresh your mind and surroundings. Lemongrass has an invigorating scent; it scatters stagnation and brings new freshness.",dailyMessageDe:"Erfrische heute deinen Geist und deine Umgebung. Zitronengras hat einen belebenden Duft; es zerstreut Stillstand und bringt neue Frische.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, refresca tu mente y tu entorno. La hierba de lim\xf3n tiene un aroma vigorizante; dispersa el estancamiento y trae nueva frescura.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, rafra\xeechis ton esprit et ton environnement. La citronnelle a un parfum tonifiant ; elle disperse la stagnation et apporte une fra\xeecheur nouvelle.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5fc3\u3068\u5468\u308a\u3092\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30b0\u30e9\u30b9\u306f\u6d3b\u6027\u5316\u3059\u308b\u9999\u308a\u3092\u6301\u3061\u3001\u505c\u6ede\u3092\u6563\u3089\u3057\u3001\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u6e05\u3005\u3057\u3055\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, refresque a sua mente e o seu entorno. O capim-lim\xe3o tem um aroma revigorante; dispersa a estagna\xe7\xe3o e traz um novo frescor.",howToUse:"Saplar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip ferahlat\u0131c\u0131 bir \xe7ay olarak i\xe7. Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ortam kokusu olarak kullanarak alan\u0131n\u0131 canland\u0131r.",howToUseEn:"Brew the stalks in hot water for a refreshing tea. Use the essential oil as a room scent to enliven your space.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die St\xe4ngel in hei\xdfem Wasser f\xfcr einen erfrischenden Tee. Verwende das \xe4therische \xd6l als Raumduft, um deinen Raum zu beleben.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona los tallos en agua caliente para un t\xe9 refrescante. Usa el aceite esencial como aroma ambiental para animar tu espacio.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les tiges dans de l'eau chaude pour une tisane rafra\xeechissante. Utilise l'huile essentielle comme parfum d'ambiance pour animer ton espace.",howToUseJa:"\u830e\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u304a\u8336\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u30eb\u30fc\u30e0\u30d5\u30ec\u30b0\u30e9\u30f3\u30b9\u3068\u3057\u3066\u4f7f\u3044\u3001\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u751f\u304d\u751f\u304d\u3068\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare os talos em \xe1gua quente para um ch\xe1 refrescante. Use o \xf3leo essencial como aroma de ambiente para animar o seu espa\xe7o.",affirmation:"Zihnimi ve \xe7evremi tazeliyorum, canl\u0131 ve berrakt\u0131m.",affirmationEn:"I refresh my mind and surroundings; I am alive and clear.",affirmationDe:"Ich erfrische meinen Geist und meine Umgebung; ich bin lebendig und klar.",affirmationEs:"Refresco mi mente y mi entorno; estoy vivo y claro.",affirmationFr:"Je rafra\xeechis mon esprit et mon environnement ; je suis vivant et clair.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5fc3\u3068\u5468\u308a\u3092\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u3059\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u751f\u304d\u751f\u304d\u3068\u6f84\u3093\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Renovo a minha mente e o meu entorno; estou vivo e claro.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/YosriNov04Pokok_Serai.JPG/330px-YosriNov04Pokok_Serai.JPG"},{id:"plant-044",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#6E8F4E",name:"Pelin Otu",nameEn:"Wormwood",nameDe:"Wermut",nameEs:"Ajenjo",nameFr:"Absinthe",nameJa:"\u30cb\u30ac\u30e8\u30e2\u30ae",namePt:"Losna",origin:"Avrupa, Asya, Kuzey Afrika",originEn:"Europe, Asia, North Africa",originDe:"Europa, Asien, Nordafrika",originEs:"Europa, Asia, Norte de \xc1frica",originFr:"Europe, Asie, Afrique du Nord",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u5317\u30a2\u30d5\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia, Norte da \xc1frica",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","koruyucu","sezgi"],propertiesEn:["purifying","protective","intuition"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","sch\xfctzend","Intuition"],propertiesEs:["purificante","protector","intuici\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","protecteur","intuition"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u5b88\u8b77","\u76f4\u611f"],propertiesPt:["purificante","protetor","intui\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ac\u0131 ger\xe7eklerle bile d\xfcr\xfcst\xe7e y\xfczle\u015f. Pelin ac\u0131d\u0131r ama ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131r; sen de zor ama gerekli bir g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfc cesaretle kabullenebilirsin.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, face even bitter truths honestly. Wormwood is bitter yet purifying; you too can courageously accept a hard but necessary insight.",dailyMessageDe:"Stelle dich heute auch bitteren Wahrheiten ehrlich. Wermut ist bitter, doch reinigend; auch du kannst mutig eine harte, aber notwendige Einsicht annehmen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, enfrenta con honestidad incluso las verdades amargas. El ajenjo es amargo pero purificante; t\xfa tambi\xe9n puedes aceptar con valor una visi\xf3n dura pero necesaria.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, affronte honn\xeatement m\xeame les v\xe9rit\xe9s am\xe8res. L'absinthe est am\xe8re mais purifiante ; toi aussi tu peux accepter avec courage une prise de conscience dure mais n\xe9cessaire.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u82e6\u3044\u771f\u5b9f\u306b\u3082\u6b63\u76f4\u306b\u5411\u304d\u5408\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30cb\u30ac\u30e8\u30e2\u30ae\u306f\u82e6\u304f\u3082\u6d44\u5316\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u3001\u3064\u3089\u3044\u304c\u5fc5\u8981\u306a\u6c17\u3065\u304d\u3092\u52c7\u6c17\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u53d7\u3051\u5165\u308c\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, encare com honestidade at\xe9 as verdades amargas. A losna \xe9 amarga, mas purificante; voc\xea tamb\xe9m pode aceitar com coragem uma percep\xe7\xe3o dif\xedcil mas necess\xe1ria.",howToUse:"\xc7ok az miktarda, k\u0131sa s\xfcreli\u011fine \xe7ay olarak demlenir; ac\u0131d\u0131r ve dikkatli, \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc kullan\u0131lmal\u0131d\u0131r. Bir demetini koruma niyetiyle kap\u0131 yan\u0131na asabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Brew a very small amount as a tea only briefly; it is bitter and should be used carefully and sparingly. You can hang a bundle by the door with an intention of protection.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche nur eine sehr kleine Menge kurz als Tee; er ist bitter und sollte vorsichtig und sparsam verwendet werden. Du kannst ein B\xfcndel mit Schutzabsicht neben die T\xfcr h\xe4ngen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona una cantidad muy peque\xf1a como t\xe9 solo brevemente; es amargo y debe usarse con cuidado y moderaci\xf3n. Puedes colgar un manojo junto a la puerta con intenci\xf3n de protecci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Infuse une tr\xe8s petite quantit\xe9 en tisane bri\xe8vement ; elle est am\xe8re et doit \xeatre utilis\xe9e avec prudence et mod\xe9ration. Tu peux suspendre un bouquet pr\xe8s de la porte avec une intention de protection.",howToUseJa:"\u3054\u304f\u5c11\u91cf\u3092\u77ed\u6642\u9593\u3060\u3051\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u82e6\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u6ce8\u610f\u3057\u3066\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306b\u4f7f\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3067\u675f\u3092\u6238\u53e3\u306b\u540a\u308b\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare uma quantidade muito pequena como ch\xe1 por pouco tempo; \xe9 amarga e deve ser usada com cuidado e modera\xe7\xe3o. Voc\xea pode pendurar um ma\xe7o junto \xe0 porta com a inten\xe7\xe3o de prote\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Ac\u0131 ger\xe7eklerle bile d\xfcr\xfcst\xe7e y\xfczle\u015febilirim.",affirmationEn:"I can face even bitter truths with honesty.",affirmationDe:"Ich kann selbst bitteren Wahrheiten ehrlich begegnen.",affirmationEs:"Puedo enfrentar incluso las verdades amargas con honestidad.",affirmationFr:"Je peux affronter m\xeame les v\xe9rit\xe9s am\xe8res avec honn\xeatet\xe9.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u82e6\u3044\u771f\u5b9f\u306b\u3082\u6b63\u76f4\u306b\u5411\u304d\u5408\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Posso encarar at\xe9 as verdades amargas com honestidade.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Artemisia_absinthium_P1210748.jpg/330px-Artemisia_absinthium_P1210748.jpg"},{id:"plant-045",emoji:"\ud83c\udf38",color:"#D98FA8",name:"\u015eakay\u0131k",nameEn:"Peony",nameDe:"Pfingstrose",nameEs:"Peon\xeda",nameFr:"Pivoine",nameJa:"\u7261\u4e39",namePt:"Pe\xf4nia",origin:"Asya, Avrupa",originEn:"Asia, Europe",originDe:"Asien, Europa",originEs:"Asia, Europa",originFr:"Asie, Europe",originJa:"\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1",originPt:"\xc1sia, Europa",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["onur","zarafet","bolluk"],propertiesEn:["honor","grace","abundance"],propertiesDe:["Ehre","Anmut","F\xfclle"],propertiesEs:["honor","gracia","abundancia"],propertiesFr:["honneur","gr\xe2ce","abondance"],propertiesJa:["\u8a89\u308c","\u512a\u7f8e","\u8c4a\u304b\u3055"],propertiesPt:["honra","gra\xe7a","abund\xe2ncia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kendi de\u011ferini zarafetle ta\u015f\u0131. \u015eakay\u0131k bir\xe7ok k\xfclt\xfcrde onurun ve bollu\u011fun \xe7i\xe7e\u011fidir; sen de g\xfczelli\u011fini gururla a\xe7.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, carry your worth with grace. The peony is the flower of honor and abundance in many cultures; bloom your beauty with pride too.",dailyMessageDe:"Trage heute deinen Wert mit Anmut. Die Pfingstrose ist in vielen Kulturen die Blume der Ehre und F\xfclle; erbl\xfche auch du stolz in deiner Sch\xf6nheit.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, lleva tu valor con gracia. La peon\xeda es la flor del honor y la abundancia en muchas culturas; florece tambi\xe9n tu belleza con orgullo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, porte ta valeur avec gr\xe2ce. La pivoine est la fleur de l'honneur et de l'abondance dans de nombreuses cultures ; \xe9panouis aussi ta beaut\xe9 avec fiert\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u512a\u7f8e\u306b\u643a\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7261\u4e39\u306f\u591a\u304f\u306e\u6587\u5316\u3067\u8a89\u308c\u3068\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306e\u82b1\u3067\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u8a87\u308a\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u54b2\u304b\u305b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, carregue o seu valor com gra\xe7a. A pe\xf4nia \xe9 a flor da honra e da abund\xe2ncia em muitas culturas; flores\xe7a tamb\xe9m a sua beleza com orgulho.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7e\u011fini g\xfczellik ve onur niyetiyle bir vazoda bulundur ya da imgesini meditasyonda canland\u0131r. Bah\xe7ende yeti\u015ftirerek mevsimsel bir kutlama yarat.",howToUseEn:"Keep the flower in a vase with an intention of beauty and honor, or visualize its image in meditation. Grow it in your garden to create a seasonal celebration.",howToUseDe:"Stelle die Blume mit einer Absicht von Sch\xf6nheit und Ehre in eine Vase oder visualisiere ihr Bild in der Meditation. Ziehe sie im Garten, um eine jahreszeitliche Feier zu schaffen.",howToUseEs:"Coloca la flor en un jarr\xf3n con intenci\xf3n de belleza y honor, o visualiza su imagen en meditaci\xf3n. Cult\xedvala en tu jard\xedn para crear una celebraci\xf3n estacional.",howToUseFr:"Garde la fleur dans un vase avec une intention de beaut\xe9 et d'honneur, ou visualise son image en m\xe9ditation. Cultive-la dans ton jardin pour cr\xe9er une c\xe9l\xe9bration saisonni\xe8re.",howToUseJa:"\u7f8e\u3068\u8a89\u308c\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3067\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u306b\u98fe\u308b\u304b\u3001\u305d\u306e\u59ff\u3092\u7791\u60f3\u3067\u601d\u3044\u63cf\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5ead\u3067\u80b2\u3066\u3001\u5b63\u7bc0\u306e\u795d\u3044\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Mantenha a flor em um vaso com a inten\xe7\xe3o de beleza e honra, ou visualize a imagem dela na medita\xe7\xe3o. Cultive-a no seu jardim para criar uma celebra\xe7\xe3o sazonal.",affirmation:"De\u011ferimi zarafetle ta\u015f\u0131yorum, g\xfczelli\u011fimi gururla a\xe7\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I carry my worth with grace and bloom my beauty with pride.",affirmationDe:"Ich trage meinen Wert mit Anmut und erbl\xfche stolz in meiner Sch\xf6nheit.",affirmationEs:"Llevo mi valor con gracia y florezco mi belleza con orgullo.",affirmationFr:"Je porte ma valeur avec gr\xe2ce et j'\xe9panouis ma beaut\xe9 avec fiert\xe9.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u512a\u7f8e\u306b\u643a\u3048\u3001\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u8a87\u308a\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u54b2\u304b\u305b\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Carrego o meu valor com gra\xe7a e flores\xe7o a minha beleza com orgulho.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/PaeoniaSuffruticosa7.jpg/330px-PaeoniaSuffruticosa7.jpg",myth:"\u015eakay\u0131k, ad\u0131n\u0131 tanr\u0131lar\u0131n hekimi Paion'dan alan \u015fifa \xe7i\xe7e\u011fidir; mitte Paion, hocas\u0131n\u0131n k\u0131skan\xe7l\u0131\u011f\u0131ndan \u015fakay\u0131\u011fa d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfclerek korunur. G\xf6rkemli a\xe7\u0131\u015f\u0131yla bollu\u011fun, onurun ve utanga\xe7 g\xfczelli\u011fin simgesidir. Antik t\u0131pta k\xf6k\xfc sakinle\u015ftirici say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Do\u011fu'da '\xe7i\xe7eklerin kral\u0131', refah ve iyi talih m\xfcjdecisidir; dolgun ta\xe7 yapraklar\u0131 a\xe7\u0131lan kalbin ve c\xf6mert sevginin dersidir.",mythEn:"The peony is the healing flower named after Paeon, physician of the gods; in the myth Paeon is saved by being turned into a peony to escape his teacher's envy. With its magnificent bloom it is the emblem of abundance, honour and bashful beauty. In ancient medicine its root was held to be calming. In the East the 'king of flowers,' a herald of prosperity and good fortune; its full petals are the lesson of an opening heart and generous love.",mythDe:"Die Pfingstrose ist die Heilblume, benannt nach Paion, dem Arzt der G\xf6tter; im Mythos wird Paion gerettet, indem er in eine Pfingstrose verwandelt wird, um dem Neid seines Lehrers zu entkommen. Mit ihrer pr\xe4chtigen Bl\xfcte ist sie Sinnbild von F\xfclle, Ehre und scheuer Sch\xf6nheit. In der antiken Medizin galt ihre Wurzel als beruhigend. Im Osten der 'K\xf6nig der Blumen', ein Bote von Wohlstand und Gl\xfcck; ihre vollen Bl\xfctenbl\xe4tter lehren ein sich \xf6ffnendes Herz und gro\xdfz\xfcgige Liebe.",mythEs:"La peon\xeda es la flor sanadora que lleva el nombre de Pe\xf3n, m\xe9dico de los dioses; en el mito, Pe\xf3n se salva al ser convertido en peon\xeda para escapar de la envidia de su maestro. Con su magn\xedfica floraci\xf3n es emblema de abundancia, honor y belleza recatada. En la medicina antigua su ra\xedz se ten\xeda por calmante. En Oriente, el 'rey de las flores', heraldo de prosperidad y buena fortuna; sus p\xe9talos llenos ense\xf1an un coraz\xf3n que se abre y un amor generoso.",mythFr:"La pivoine est la fleur gu\xe9risseuse nomm\xe9e d'apr\xe8s P\xe9an, m\xe9decin des dieux ; dans le mythe, P\xe9an est sauv\xe9 en \xe9tant chang\xe9 en pivoine pour \xe9chapper \xe0 la jalousie de son ma\xeetre. Par sa floraison magnifique, elle est l'embl\xe8me de l'abondance, de l'honneur et de la beaut\xe9 pudique. Dans la m\xe9decine antique, sa racine passait pour apaisante. En Orient, le 'roi des fleurs', h\xe9raut de prosp\xe9rit\xe9 et de bonne fortune ; ses p\xe9tales pleins enseignent un c\u0153ur qui s'ouvre et un amour g\xe9n\xe9reux.",mythJa:"\u828d\u85ac\u306f\u3001\u795e\u3005\u306e\u533b\u5e2b\u30d1\u30a4\u30a8\u30aa\u30f3\u306b\u3061\u306a\u3080\u7652\u3057\u306e\u82b1\u3002\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5e2b\u306e\u5ac9\u59ac\u304b\u3089\u9003\u308c\u308b\u305f\u3081\u828d\u85ac\u306b\u5909\u3048\u3089\u308c\u3066\u6551\u308f\u308c\u308b\u3002\u8c6a\u5962\u306a\u958b\u82b1\u306f\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u8a89\u308c\u3001\u614e\u307e\u3057\u3044\u7f8e\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3002\u53e4\u4ee3\u533b\u5b66\u3067\u306f\u6839\u304c\u93ae\u9759\u306b\u3088\u3044\u3068\u3055\u308c\u305f\u3002\u6771\u6d0b\u3067\u306f\u300c\u82b1\u306e\u738b\u300d\u3001\u7e41\u6804\u3068\u5e78\u904b\u306e\u544a\u3052\u3002\u3075\u304f\u3088\u304b\u306a\u82b1\u3073\u3089\u306f\u3001\u958b\u304f\u5fc3\u3068\u60dc\u3057\u307f\u306a\u3044\u611b\u306e\u6559\u3048\u3002",mythPt:"A pe\xf4nia \xe9 a flor curativa que leva o nome de P\xe9on, m\xe9dico dos deuses; no mito, P\xe9on \xe9 salvo ao ser transformado em pe\xf4nia para escapar \xe0 inveja do seu mestre. Com a sua flora\xe7\xe3o magn\xedfica \xe9 emblema de abund\xe2ncia, honra e beleza recatada. Na medicina antiga, a sua raiz era tida por calmante. No Oriente, o 'rei das flores', arauto de prosperidade e boa fortuna; as suas p\xe9talas cheias ensinam um cora\xe7\xe3o que se abre e um amor generoso."},{id:"plant-046",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#7E9B6A",name:"Tulsi (Kutsal Fesle\u011fen)",nameEn:"Holy Basil (Tulsi)",nameDe:"Heiliges Basilikum (Tulsi)",nameEs:"Albahaca Sagrada (Tulsi)",nameFr:"Basilic Sacr\xe9 (Tulsi)",nameJa:"\u30db\u30fc\u30ea\u30fc\u30d0\u30b8\u30eb\uff08\u30c8\u30a5\u30eb\u30b7\u30fc\uff09",namePt:"Manjeric\xe3o Sagrado (Tulsi)",origin:"Hindistan",originEn:"India",originDe:"Indien",originEs:"India",originFr:"Inde",originJa:"\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9",originPt:"\xcdndia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["denge","kutsal","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["balance","sacred","resilience"],propertiesDe:["Gleichgewicht","heilig","Widerstandskraft"],propertiesEs:["equilibrio","sagrado","resiliencia"],propertiesFr:["\xe9quilibre","sacr\xe9","r\xe9silience"],propertiesJa:["\u5747\u8861","\u8056\u306a\u308b","\u56de\u5fa9\u529b"],propertiesPt:["equil\xedbrio","sagrado","resili\xeancia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn strese kar\u015f\u0131 k\xf6k\xfcnden dengeli kal. Tulsi Ayurveda'da kutsal say\u0131l\u0131r; sana hem d\xfcnyaya ba\u011fl\u0131 hem de ruhunla y\xfckseli\u015f g\xfcc\xfc verir.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, stay balanced at your roots in the face of stress. Tulsi is sacred in Ayurveda; it gives you the power to stay grounded yet rise in spirit.",dailyMessageDe:"Bleibe heute angesichts von Stress in deinen Wurzeln ausgeglichen. Tulsi ist im Ayurveda heilig; es schenkt dir die Kraft, geerdet zu bleiben und zugleich im Geist aufzusteigen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, mantente equilibrado desde tus ra\xedces frente al estr\xe9s. El tulsi es sagrado en el ayurveda; te da el poder de permanecer enraizado y a la vez elevarte en esp\xedritu.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, reste \xe9quilibr\xe9 \xe0 tes racines face au stress. Le tulsi est sacr\xe9 dans l'ayurveda ; il te donne la force de rester ancr\xe9 tout en t'\xe9levant en esprit.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u30b9\u30c8\u30ec\u30b9\u306b\u5bfe\u3057\u3001\u6839\u304b\u3089\u5747\u8861\u3092\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30c8\u30a5\u30eb\u30b7\u30fc\u306f\u30a2\u30fc\u30e6\u30eb\u30f4\u30a7\u30fc\u30c0\u3067\u8056\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3002\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304d\u306a\u304c\u3089\u9b42\u3067\u6607\u308b\u529b\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, mantenha-se equilibrado nas suas ra\xedzes diante do estresse. O tulsi \xe9 sagrado no Ayurveda; d\xe1 a voc\xea o poder de permanecer enraizado e ao mesmo tempo se elevar em esp\xedrito.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip g\xfcnl\xfck denge i\xe7in i\xe7. Bir saks\u0131 tulsi'yi evinde bulundurarak kutsal bir k\xf6\u015fe yarat.",howToUseEn:"Brew the leaves in hot water for daily balance. Keep a pot of tulsi in your home to create a sacred corner.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter in hei\xdfem Wasser f\xfcr t\xe4gliches Gleichgewicht. Halte einen Topf Tulsi in deinem Zuhause, um eine heilige Ecke zu schaffen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las hojas en agua caliente para el equilibrio diario. Ten una maceta de tulsi en casa para crear un rinc\xf3n sagrado.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les feuilles dans de l'eau chaude pour un \xe9quilibre quotidien. Garde un pot de tulsi chez toi pour cr\xe9er un coin sacr\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u65e5\u3005\u306e\u5747\u8861\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30c8\u30a5\u30eb\u30b7\u30fc\u306e\u9262\u3092\u5bb6\u306b\u7f6e\u304d\u3001\u8056\u306a\u308b\u4e00\u89d2\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as folhas em \xe1gua quente para o equil\xedbrio di\xe1rio. Mantenha um vaso de tulsi em casa para criar um canto sagrado.",affirmation:"K\xf6klerimde dengeliyim, ruhumda y\xfckseliyorum.",affirmationEn:"I am balanced at my roots and rising in my spirit.",affirmationDe:"Ich bin ausgeglichen in meinen Wurzeln und steige im Geist auf.",affirmationEs:"Estoy equilibrado en mis ra\xedces y me elevo en mi esp\xedritu.",affirmationFr:"Je suis \xe9quilibr\xe9 dans mes racines et je m'\xe9l\xe8ve en esprit.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6839\u306b\u304a\u3044\u3066\u5747\u8861\u3057\u3001\u9b42\u306b\u304a\u3044\u3066\u6607\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Estou equilibrado nas minhas ra\xedzes e me elevo no meu esp\xedrito.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Tulsi_or_Tulasi_Holy_basil.jpg/330px-Tulsi_or_Tulasi_Holy_basil.jpg"},{id:"plant-047",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#9CA86E",name:"A\u015fvaganda",nameEn:"Ashwagandha",nameDe:"Ashwagandha",nameEs:"Ashwagandha",nameFr:"Ashwagandha",nameJa:"\u30a2\u30b7\u30e5\u30ef\u30ac\u30f3\u30c0",namePt:"Ashwagandha",origin:"Hindistan, Kuzey Afrika",originEn:"India, North Africa",originDe:"Indien, Nordafrika",originEs:"India, Norte de \xc1frica",originFr:"Inde, Afrique du Nord",originJa:"\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9\u30fb\u5317\u30a2\u30d5\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"\xcdndia, Norte da \xc1frica",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["topraklay\u0131c\u0131","dinginlik","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["grounding","calm","resilience"],propertiesDe:["erdend","Ruhe","Widerstandskraft"],propertiesEs:["enraizante","calma","resiliencia"],propertiesFr:["ancrant","calme","r\xe9silience"],propertiesJa:["\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304f","\u9759\u3051\u3055","\u56de\u5fa9\u529b"],propertiesPt:["enraizador","calma","resili\xeancia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn tela\u015f\u0131n ortas\u0131nda bile sakin bir merkez bul. A\u015fvaganda 'at\u0131n g\xfcc\xfc' demektir; sana sars\u0131lmadan kalma dinginli\u011fini hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, find a calm center even amid the rush. Ashwagandha means 'strength of the horse'; it reminds you of the stillness of staying unshaken.",dailyMessageDe:"Finde heute selbst im Trubel ein ruhiges Zentrum. Ashwagandha bedeutet 'Kraft des Pferdes'; es erinnert dich an die Ruhe, unersch\xfcttert zu bleiben.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, encuentra un centro tranquilo incluso en medio del ajetreo. La ashwagandha significa 'fuerza del caballo'; te recuerda la quietud de permanecer firme.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, trouve un centre calme m\xeame au milieu de l'agitation. L'ashwagandha signifie 'force du cheval' ; elle te rappelle le calme de rester in\xe9branlable.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u614c\u305f\u3060\u3057\u3055\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u3082\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u4e2d\u5fc3\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30a2\u30b7\u30e5\u30ef\u30ac\u30f3\u30c0\u306f\u300c\u99ac\u306e\u529b\u300d\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u63fa\u308b\u304c\u305a\u306b\u3044\u308b\u9759\u3051\u3055\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, encontre um centro calmo mesmo em meio \xe0 correria. A ashwagandha significa 'for\xe7a do cavalo'; lembra voc\xea da quietude de permanecer inabal\xe1vel.",howToUse:"K\xf6k tozunu \u0131l\u0131k s\xfcte ve bala kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131rarak ak\u015famlar\u0131 t\xfcket. Az miktarda, d\xfczenli olarak kullan; ila\xe7 kullan\u0131yorsan \xf6nce uzmana dan\u0131\u015f.",howToUseEn:"Mix the root powder into warm milk with honey in the evenings. Use it in small, regular amounts; if you take medication, consult a professional first.",howToUseDe:"R\xfchre das Wurzelpulver abends in warme Milch mit Honig. Verwende es in kleinen, regelm\xe4\xdfigen Mengen; bei Medikamenteneinnahme frage zuerst eine Fachperson.",howToUseEs:"Mezcla el polvo de ra\xedz en leche tibia con miel por las noches. \xdasalo en cantidades peque\xf1as y regulares; si tomas medicaci\xf3n, consulta antes a un profesional.",howToUseFr:"M\xe9lange la poudre de racine dans du lait chaud avec du miel le soir. Utilise-la en petites quantit\xe9s r\xe9guli\xe8res ; si tu prends des m\xe9dicaments, consulte d'abord un professionnel.",howToUseJa:"\u6839\u306e\u7c89\u672b\u3092\u591c\u306b\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u30df\u30eb\u30af\u3068\u8702\u871c\u306b\u6df7\u305c\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5c11\u91cf\u3092\u5b9a\u671f\u7684\u306b\u3002\u85ac\u3092\u670d\u7528\u4e2d\u306a\u3089\u307e\u305a\u5c02\u9580\u5bb6\u306b\u76f8\u8ac7\u3092\u3002",howToUsePt:"Misture o p\xf3 da raiz no leite morno com mel \xe0 noite. Use em quantidades pequenas e regulares; se toma medica\xe7\xe3o, consulte um profissional antes.",affirmation:"Tela\u015f\u0131n ortas\u0131nda bile sakin merkezimde duruyorum.",affirmationEn:"Even amid the rush, I stand in my calm center.",affirmationDe:"Selbst im Trubel stehe ich in meinem ruhigen Zentrum.",affirmationEs:"Incluso en medio del ajetreo, permanezco en mi centro tranquilo.",affirmationFr:"M\xeame dans l'agitation, je me tiens dans mon centre calme.",affirmationJa:"\u614c\u305f\u3060\u3057\u3055\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u3082\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u4e2d\u5fc3\u306b\u7acb\u3064\u3002",affirmationPt:"Mesmo em meio \xe0 correria, permane\xe7o no meu centro calmo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/WithaniaFruit.jpg/330px-WithaniaFruit.jpg"},{id:"plant-048",emoji:"\ud83c\udf75",color:"#8BAE66",name:"Ye\u015fil \xc7ay",nameEn:"Green Tea",nameDe:"Gr\xfcner Tee",nameEs:"T\xe9 Verde",nameFr:"Th\xe9 Vert",nameJa:"\u7dd1\u8336",namePt:"Ch\xe1 Verde",origin:"\xc7in, Do\u011fu Asya",originEn:"China, East Asia",originDe:"China, Ostasien",originEs:"China, Asia Oriental",originFr:"Chine, Asie de l'Est",originJa:"\u4e2d\u56fd\u30fb\u6771\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"China, \xc1sia Oriental",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["dingin uyan\u0131kl\u0131k","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","fark\u0131ndal\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["calm alertness","purifying","mindfulness"],propertiesDe:["ruhige Wachheit","reinigend","Achtsamkeit"],propertiesEs:["alerta serena","purificante","atenci\xf3n plena"],propertiesFr:["vigilance sereine","purifiant","pleine conscience"],propertiesJa:["\u9759\u304b\u306a\u899a\u9192","\u6d44\u5316","\u6c17\u3065\u304d"],propertiesPt:["alerta calmo","purificante","aten\xe7\xe3o plena"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn bir fincan \xe7ay\u0131 bilin\xe7le yudumla ve anda kal. Ye\u015fil \xe7ay seni sakin ama uyan\u0131k tutar; tela\u015fs\u0131z bir berrakl\u0131\u011fa davet eder.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, sip a cup of tea mindfully and stay in the moment. Green tea keeps you calm yet alert; it invites a clarity without rush.",dailyMessageDe:"Trinke heute eine Tasse Tee achtsam und bleibe im Moment. Gr\xfcner Tee h\xe4lt dich ruhig und doch wach; er l\xe4dt zu einer Klarheit ohne Hast ein.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, bebe una taza de t\xe9 con atenci\xf3n y permanece en el momento. El t\xe9 verde te mantiene calmado pero alerta; invita a una claridad sin prisa.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, savoure une tasse de th\xe9 en pleine conscience et reste dans l'instant. Le th\xe9 vert te garde calme mais alerte ; il invite \xe0 une clart\xe9 sans h\xe2te.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4e00\u676f\u306e\u304a\u8336\u3092\u5fc3\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3044\u3001\u3044\u307e\u306b\u3068\u3069\u307e\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7dd1\u8336\u306f\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u3067\u3042\u308a\u306a\u304c\u3089\u899a\u3081\u305f\u72b6\u614b\u306b\u4fdd\u3061\u3001\u6025\u304c\u306a\u3044\u660e\u6670\u3055\u3078\u8a98\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, tome uma x\xedcara de ch\xe1 com aten\xe7\xe3o e permane\xe7a no momento. O ch\xe1 verde mant\xe9m voc\xea calmo mas alerta; convida a uma clareza sem pressa.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ok s\u0131cak olmayan suyla (yakla\u015f\u0131k 70-80\xb0C) demle, k\u0131sa s\xfcre beklet ve bilin\xe7li bir rit\xfcel olarak yudumla. Ac\u0131la\u015fmamas\u0131 i\xe7in fazla demlenme.",howToUseEn:"Brew the leaves with water that is not too hot (about 70-80\xb0C), steep briefly, and sip as a mindful ritual. Don't over-steep so it won't turn bitter.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter mit nicht zu hei\xdfem Wasser (etwa 70-80\xb0C), lass sie kurz ziehen und genie\xdfe achtsam als Ritual. Lass ihn nicht zu lange ziehen, damit er nicht bitter wird.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las hojas con agua no demasiado caliente (unos 70-80\xb0C), deja reposar poco y b\xe9belo como un ritual consciente. No lo dejes mucho para que no amargue.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les feuilles avec une eau pas trop chaude (environ 70-80\xb0C), laisse infuser bri\xe8vement et savoure en rituel conscient. N'infuse pas trop longtemps pour \xe9viter l'amertume.",howToUseJa:"\u3042\u307e\u308a\u71b1\u304f\u306a\u3044\u6e6f\uff08\u7d0470\u301c80\u2103\uff09\u3067\u8449\u3092\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u77ed\u304f\u84b8\u3089\u3057\u3001\u5fc3\u3042\u308b\u5100\u5f0f\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u82e6\u304f\u306a\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3046\u6df9\u308c\u3059\u304e\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as folhas com \xe1gua n\xe3o muito quente (cerca de 70-80\xb0C), deixe em infus\xe3o por pouco tempo e tome como um ritual consciente. N\xe3o deixe muito tempo para n\xe3o amargar.",affirmation:"Anda kal\u0131yorum, sakin ve uyan\u0131k bir berrakl\u0131ktay\u0131m.",affirmationEn:"I stay in the moment, in a calm and alert clarity.",affirmationDe:"Ich bleibe im Moment, in einer ruhigen und wachen Klarheit.",affirmationEs:"Permanezco en el momento, en una claridad serena y alerta.",affirmationFr:"Je reste dans l'instant, dans une clart\xe9 calme et alerte.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u3044\u307e\u306b\u3068\u3069\u307e\u308a\u3001\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u3067\u899a\u3081\u305f\u660e\u6670\u3055\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Permane\xe7o no momento, em uma clareza calma e alerta.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Green_tea_3_appearances.jpg/330px-Green_tea_3_appearances.jpg"},{id:"plant-049",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5C7E4E",name:"Mate",nameEn:"Yerba Mate",nameDe:"Mate",nameEs:"Yerba Mate",nameFr:"Yerba Mat\xe9",nameJa:"\u30de\u30c6",namePt:"Erva-mate",origin:"G\xfcney Amerika",originEn:"South America",originDe:"S\xfcdamerika",originEs:"Am\xe9rica del Sur",originFr:"Am\xe9rique du Sud",originJa:"\u5357\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Am\xe9rica do Sul",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","payla\u015f\u0131m","odak"],propertiesEn:["invigorating","sharing","focus"],propertiesDe:["belebend","Teilen","Fokus"],propertiesEs:["vigorizante","compartir","enfoque"],propertiesFr:["tonifiant","partage","concentration"],propertiesJa:["\u6d3b\u6027","\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3044","\u96c6\u4e2d"],propertiesPt:["revigorante","partilha","foco"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn canl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ba\u015fkalar\u0131yla payla\u015f. Mate G\xfcney Amerika'da payla\u015f\u0131lan bir dostluk i\xe7ece\u011fidir; enerjinin ba\u011f kurarak da yenilendi\u011fini hat\u0131rla.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, share your vitality with others. Mate is a friendship drink shared in South America; remember that your energy renews through connection too.",dailyMessageDe:"Teile heute deine Lebendigkeit mit anderen. Mate ist in S\xfcdamerika ein geteiltes Freundschaftsgetr\xe4nk; denk daran, dass sich deine Energie auch durch Verbindung erneuert.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, comparte tu vitalidad con los dem\xe1s. El mate es una bebida de amistad compartida en Sudam\xe9rica; recuerda que tu energ\xeda tambi\xe9n se renueva al conectar.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, partage ta vitalit\xe9 avec les autres. Le mat\xe9 est une boisson d'amiti\xe9 partag\xe9e en Am\xe9rique du Sud ; souviens-toi que ton \xe9nergie se renouvelle aussi par le lien.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u6d3b\u529b\u3092\u4ed6\u8005\u3068\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30de\u30c6\u306f\u5357\u7c73\u3067\u5206\u3051\u5408\u3046\u53cb\u60c5\u306e\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u3002\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc\u306f\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u3082\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, partilhe a sua vitalidade com os outros. O mate \xe9 uma bebida de amizade compartilhada na Am\xe9rica do Sul; lembre-se de que a sua energia tamb\xe9m se renova pela conex\xe3o.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 geleneksel bir kaba\u011fa (mate) koyup s\u0131cak suyla demle ve bombilla ile i\xe7. Sevdiklerinle payla\u015farak bir ba\u011f rit\xfceli yarat.",howToUseEn:"Place the leaves in a traditional gourd (mate), pour hot water, and drink through a bombilla. Share it with loved ones to create a bonding ritual.",howToUseDe:"Gib die Bl\xe4tter in eine traditionelle Kalebasse (Mate), \xfcbergie\xdfe sie mit hei\xdfem Wasser und trinke durch eine Bombilla. Teile es mit deinen Liebsten als Verbindungsritual.",howToUseEs:"Coloca las hojas en una calabaza tradicional (mate), vierte agua caliente y bebe con bombilla. Comp\xe1rtelo con tus seres queridos para crear un ritual de uni\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Place les feuilles dans une calebasse traditionnelle (mat\xe9), verse de l'eau chaude et bois \xe0 la bombilla. Partage-le avec tes proches pour cr\xe9er un rituel de lien.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u4f1d\u7d71\u7684\u306a\u3072\u3087\u3046\u305f\u3093\uff08\u30de\u30c6\uff09\u306b\u5165\u308c\u3001\u6e6f\u3092\u6ce8\u304e\u3001\u30dc\u30f3\u30d3\u30fc\u30b8\u30e3\u3067\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5927\u5207\u306a\u4eba\u3068\u5206\u3051\u5408\u3044\u3001\u7d46\u306e\u5100\u5f0f\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Coloque as folhas em uma cuia tradicional (mate), despeje \xe1gua quente e beba pela bomba. Partilhe com pessoas queridas para criar um ritual de conex\xe3o.",affirmation:"Canl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131m\u0131 payla\u015f\u0131yorum, ba\u011f kurarak yenileniyorum.",affirmationEn:"I share my vitality and renew through connection.",affirmationDe:"Ich teile meine Lebendigkeit und erneuere mich durch Verbindung.",affirmationEs:"Comparto mi vitalidad y me renuevo al conectar.",affirmationFr:"Je partage ma vitalit\xe9 et me renouvelle par le lien.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6d3b\u529b\u3092\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3044\u3001\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Partilho a minha vitalidade e me renovo pela conex\xe3o.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Ilex_paraguariensis_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-074.jpg/330px-Ilex_paraguariensis_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-074.jpg"},{id:"plant-050",emoji:"\ud83c\udf39",color:"#C25B4E",name:"Ku\u015fburnu",nameEn:"Rosehip",nameDe:"Hagebutte",nameEs:"Escaramujo",nameFr:"Cynorhodon",nameJa:"\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30d2\u30c3\u30d7",namePt:"Rosa Mosqueta",origin:"Avrupa, Asya",originEn:"Europe, Asia",originDe:"Europa, Asien",originEs:"Europa, Asia",originFr:"Europe, Asie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["g\xfc\xe7lendirici","besleyici","s\u0131cakl\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["strengthening","nourishing","warmth"],propertiesDe:["st\xe4rkend","n\xe4hrend","W\xe4rme"],propertiesEs:["fortalecedor","nutritivo","calidez"],propertiesFr:["fortifiant","nourrissant","chaleur"],propertiesJa:["\u5f37\u5316","\u6ecb\u990a","\u6e29\u3082\u308a"],propertiesPt:["fortalecedor","nutritivo","aconchego"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xfcl\xfcn dikenlerini geride b\u0131rak\u0131p meyvesinin tatl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6r. Ku\u015fburnu, g\xfczelli\u011fin ard\u0131ndan gelen besleyici arma\u011fan\u0131 temsil eder.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, leave the rose's thorns behind and see the sweetness of its fruit. Rosehip represents the nourishing gift that comes after the bloom.",dailyMessageDe:"Lass heute die Dornen der Rose hinter dir und sieh die S\xfc\xdfe ihrer Frucht. Hagebutte steht f\xfcr das n\xe4hrende Geschenk, das nach der Bl\xfcte kommt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, deja atr\xe1s las espinas de la rosa y mira la dulzura de su fruto. El escaramujo representa el regalo nutritivo que llega tras la floraci\xf3n.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, laisse derri\xe8re toi les \xe9pines de la rose et vois la douceur de son fruit. Le cynorhodon repr\xe9sente le don nourrissant qui vient apr\xe8s la floraison.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u8594\u8587\u306e\u3068\u3052\u3092\u5f8c\u306b\u3057\u3066\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5b9f\u306e\u7518\u3055\u3092\u898b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ed\u30fc\u30ba\u30d2\u30c3\u30d7\u306f\u3001\u82b1\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306b\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u6ecb\u990a\u306e\u8d08\u308a\u7269\u3092\u8868\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, deixe para tr\xe1s os espinhos da rosa e veja a do\xe7ura do seu fruto. A rosa mosqueta representa o presente nutritivo que vem ap\xf3s a flora\xe7\xe3o.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f meyvelerini s\u0131cak suda uzunca demleyip ek\u015fimsi, besleyici bir \xe7ay olarak i\xe7. Ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 cilt bak\u0131m\u0131nda nazik\xe7e kullanabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Brew the dried fruits in hot water for a longer time for a tangy, nourishing tea. You can gently use the oil in skin care.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die getrockneten Fr\xfcchte l\xe4nger in hei\xdfem Wasser f\xfcr einen s\xe4uerlichen, n\xe4hrenden Tee. Du kannst das \xd6l sanft in der Hautpflege verwenden.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona los frutos secos en agua caliente por m\xe1s tiempo para un t\xe9 \xe1cido y nutritivo. Puedes usar suavemente el aceite en el cuidado de la piel.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fruits s\xe9ch\xe9s plus longtemps dans de l'eau chaude pour une tisane acidul\xe9e et nourrissante. Tu peux utiliser doucement l'huile en soin de la peau.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u5b9f\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u9577\u3081\u306b\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u9178\u5473\u306e\u3042\u308b\u6ecb\u990a\u306e\u304a\u8336\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6cb9\u306f\u30b9\u30ad\u30f3\u30b1\u30a2\u306b\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u4f7f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare os frutos secos em \xe1gua quente por mais tempo para um ch\xe1 azedinho e nutritivo. Voc\xea pode usar suavemente o \xf3leo no cuidado da pele.",affirmation:"Dikenlerin ard\u0131ndan gelen tatl\u0131l\u0131\u011fa ve bereketine g\xfcveniyorum.",affirmationEn:"I trust the sweetness and bounty that come after the thorns.",affirmationDe:"Ich vertraue der S\xfc\xdfe und F\xfclle, die nach den Dornen kommen.",affirmationEs:"Conf\xedo en la dulzura y la abundancia que llegan tras las espinas.",affirmationFr:"Je fais confiance \xe0 la douceur et \xe0 l'abondance qui viennent apr\xe8s les \xe9pines.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u3068\u3052\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306b\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u7518\u3055\u3068\u6075\u307f\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3059\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Confio na do\xe7ura e na fartura que v\xeam depois dos espinhos.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Rose_hips.jpg/330px-Rose_hips.jpg"},{id:"plant-051",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#86A05E",name:"Tar\xe7\u0131n",nameEn:"Cinnamon",nameDe:"Zimt",nameEs:"Canela",nameFr:"Cannelle",nameJa:"\u30b7\u30ca\u30e2\u30f3",namePt:"Canela",origin:"Sri Lanka, G\xfcney Asya",originEn:"Sri Lanka, South Asia",originDe:"Sri Lanka, S\xfcdasien",originEs:"Sri Lanka, Sur de Asia",originFr:"Sri Lanka, Asie du Sud",originJa:"\u30b9\u30ea\u30e9\u30f3\u30ab\u30fb\u5357\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Sri Lanka, Sul da \xc1sia",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u30b5\u30af\u30e9\u30eb\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacral",properties:["\u0131s\u0131t\u0131c\u0131","bolluk","tutku"],propertiesEn:["warming","abundance","passion"],propertiesDe:["w\xe4rmend","F\xfclle","Leidenschaft"],propertiesEs:["caliente","abundancia","pasi\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["r\xe9chauffant","abondance","passion"],propertiesJa:["\u6e29\u3081","\u8c4a\u304b\u3055","\u60c5\u71b1"],propertiesPt:["aquecedor","abund\xe2ncia","paix\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131na biraz tatl\u0131l\u0131k ve s\u0131cakl\u0131k kat. Tar\xe7\u0131n bolluk ve tutku \xe7ekmekle ili\u015fkilendirilir; k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir baharat\u0131n bile g\xfcn\xfc d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrebildi\u011fini hat\u0131rla.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, add a little sweetness and warmth to your life. Cinnamon is linked with drawing abundance and passion; remember that even a small spice can transform the day.",dailyMessageDe:"F\xfcge heute deinem Leben etwas S\xfc\xdfe und W\xe4rme hinzu. Zimt wird damit verbunden, F\xfclle und Leidenschaft anzuziehen; denk daran, dass selbst ein kleines Gew\xfcrz den Tag verwandeln kann.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, a\xf1ade un poco de dulzura y calidez a tu vida. La canela se asocia con atraer abundancia y pasi\xf3n; recuerda que incluso una peque\xf1a especia puede transformar el d\xeda.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ajoute un peu de douceur et de chaleur \xe0 ta vie. La cannelle est associ\xe9e \xe0 l'attraction de l'abondance et de la passion ; souviens-toi qu'une petite \xe9pice peut transformer la journ\xe9e.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u66ae\u3089\u3057\u306b\u5c11\u3057\u306e\u7518\u3055\u3068\u6e29\u3082\u308a\u3092\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b7\u30ca\u30e2\u30f3\u306f\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u3068\u60c5\u71b1\u3092\u5f15\u304d\u5bc4\u305b\u308b\u3068\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u9999\u8f9b\u6599\u3067\u3082\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u5909\u3048\u3046\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, adicione um pouco de do\xe7ura e aconchego \xe0 sua vida. A canela est\xe1 ligada a atrair abund\xe2ncia e paix\xe3o; lembre-se de que at\xe9 uma pequena especiaria pode transformar o dia.",howToUse:"\xc7ubu\u011funu s\u0131cak s\xfct ya da \xe7aya katarak \u0131s\u0131t\u0131c\u0131 bir i\xe7ecek haz\u0131rla. Bir niyet rit\xfcelinde tar\xe7\u0131n tozunu e\u015fi\u011fe serperek bolluk davet edebilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Add a stick to warm milk or tea for a warming drink. In an intention ritual, you can sprinkle cinnamon powder on your threshold to invite abundance.",howToUseDe:"Gib eine Stange in warme Milch oder Tee f\xfcr ein w\xe4rmendes Getr\xe4nk. In einem Absichtsritual kannst du Zimtpulver auf deine Schwelle streuen, um F\xfclle einzuladen.",howToUseEs:"A\xf1ade una rama a leche tibia o t\xe9 para una bebida que reconforta. En un ritual de intenci\xf3n, puedes espolvorear canela en tu umbral para invitar abundancia.",howToUseFr:"Ajoute un b\xe2ton \xe0 du lait chaud ou du th\xe9 pour une boisson r\xe9chauffante. Dans un rituel d'intention, tu peux saupoudrer de la cannelle sur ton seuil pour inviter l'abondance.",howToUseJa:"\u30b9\u30c6\u30a3\u30c3\u30af\u3092\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u30df\u30eb\u30af\u3084\u304a\u8336\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3001\u6e29\u307e\u308b\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u5100\u5f0f\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30b7\u30ca\u30e2\u30f3\u306e\u7c89\u3092\u6577\u5c45\u306b\u307e\u3044\u3066\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u3092\u62db\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Adicione um pau ao leite morno ou ch\xe1 para uma bebida aquecedora. Em um ritual de inten\xe7\xe3o, voc\xea pode polvilhar canela na soleira para convidar a abund\xe2ncia.",affirmation:"Hayat\u0131ma tatl\u0131l\u0131k ve bolluk davet ediyorum.",affirmationEn:"I invite sweetness and abundance into my life.",affirmationDe:"Ich lade S\xfc\xdfe und F\xfclle in mein Leben ein.",affirmationEs:"Invito dulzura y abundancia a mi vida.",affirmationFr:"J'invite la douceur et l'abondance dans ma vie.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u306b\u7518\u3055\u3068\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u3092\u62db\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Convido do\xe7ura e abund\xe2ncia para a minha vida.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Cinnamomum_verum_spices.jpg/330px-Cinnamomum_verum_spices.jpg"},{id:"plant-052",emoji:"\ud83e\udd0e",color:"#8A6B4F",name:"Karanfil",nameEn:"Clove",nameDe:"Gew\xfcrznelke",nameEs:"Clavo de olor",nameFr:"Clou de girofle",nameJa:"\u30af\u30ed\u30fc\u30d6",namePt:"Cravo-da-\xedndia",origin:"Endonezya, Maluku Adalar\u0131",originEn:"Indonesia, Maluku Islands",originDe:"Indonesien, Molukken",originEs:"Indonesia, Islas Molucas",originFr:"Indon\xe9sie, \xeeles Moluques",originJa:"\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9\u30cd\u30b7\u30a2\u30fb\u30e2\u30eb\u30c3\u30ab\u8af8\u5cf6",originPt:"Indon\xe9sia, Ilhas Molucas",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["koruyucu","\u0131s\u0131t\u0131c\u0131","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["protective","warming","purifying"],propertiesDe:["sch\xfctzend","w\xe4rmend","reinigend"],propertiesEs:["protector","caliente","purificante"],propertiesFr:["protecteur","r\xe9chauffant","purifiant"],propertiesJa:["\u5b88\u8b77","\u6e29\u3081","\u6d44\u5316"],propertiesPt:["protetor","aquecedor","purificante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olan\u0131n de\u011ferini g\xf6r. Karanfil minik bir baharatt\u0131r ama yo\u011fun bir koruma ve s\u0131cakl\u0131k ta\u015f\u0131r; sen de g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc boyutunla \xf6l\xe7me.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, see the value of what is small yet powerful. Clove is a tiny spice that carries intense protection and warmth; don't measure your power by your size.",dailyMessageDe:"Erkenne heute den Wert dessen, was klein und doch kraftvoll ist. Die Gew\xfcrznelke ist ein winziges Gew\xfcrz mit intensivem Schutz und W\xe4rme; miss deine Kraft nicht an deiner Gr\xf6\xdfe.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ve el valor de lo peque\xf1o pero poderoso. El clavo es una especia diminuta que lleva una protecci\xf3n y calidez intensas; no midas tu poder por tu tama\xf1o.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, vois la valeur de ce qui est petit mais puissant. Le clou de girofle est une minuscule \xe9pice qui porte une protection et une chaleur intenses ; ne mesure pas ta force \xe0 ta taille.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5c0f\u3055\u304f\u3068\u3082\u529b\u5f37\u3044\u3082\u306e\u306e\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u898b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30af\u30ed\u30fc\u30d6\u306f\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u9999\u8f9b\u6599\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3001\u6fc3\u3044\u5b88\u8b77\u3068\u6e29\u3082\u308a\u3092\u5bbf\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u529b\u3092\u5927\u304d\u3055\u3067\u6e2c\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, veja o valor do que \xe9 pequeno mas poderoso. O cravo \xe9 uma especiaria min\xfascula que carrega uma prote\xe7\xe3o e um aconchego intensos; n\xe3o me\xe7a o seu poder pelo seu tamanho.",howToUse:"Birka\xe7 tanesini s\u0131cak \xe7aya ya da s\xfcte katarak \u0131s\u0131t\u0131c\u0131 bir i\xe7ecek haz\u0131rla. Bir portakala karanfil \xe7akarak do\u011fal, koruyucu bir koku objesi yap.",howToUseEn:"Add a few to hot tea or milk for a warming drink. Stud an orange with cloves to make a natural, protective scent object.",howToUseDe:"Gib einige in hei\xdfen Tee oder Milch f\xfcr ein w\xe4rmendes Getr\xe4nk. Spicke eine Orange mit Nelken, um ein nat\xfcrliches, sch\xfctzendes Duftobjekt zu machen.",howToUseEs:"A\xf1ade unos cuantos a t\xe9 o leche calientes para una bebida que reconforta. Clava clavos en una naranja para hacer un objeto arom\xe1tico natural y protector.",howToUseFr:"Ajoute-en quelques-uns \xe0 du th\xe9 ou du lait chaud pour une boisson r\xe9chauffante. Pique une orange de clous de girofle pour cr\xe9er un objet parfum\xe9 naturel et protecteur.",howToUseJa:"\u6570\u7c92\u3092\u71b1\u3044\u304a\u8336\u3084\u30df\u30eb\u30af\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3001\u6e29\u307e\u308b\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30aa\u30ec\u30f3\u30b8\u306b\u30af\u30ed\u30fc\u30d6\u3092\u523a\u3057\u3001\u81ea\u7136\u3067\u5b88\u8b77\u7684\u306a\u9999\u308a\u306e\u98fe\u308a\u3092\u4f5c\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Adicione alguns ao ch\xe1 ou leite quente para uma bebida aquecedora. Espete cravos em uma laranja para fazer um objeto arom\xe1tico natural e protetor.",affirmation:"K\xfc\xe7\xfck olsam da g\xfcc\xfcm yo\u011fun ve ger\xe7ek.",affirmationEn:"Though I am small, my power is intense and real.",affirmationDe:"Auch wenn ich klein bin, ist meine Kraft intensiv und echt.",affirmationEs:"Aunque sea peque\xf1o, mi poder es intenso y real.",affirmationFr:"Bien que je sois petit, ma force est intense et r\xe9elle.",affirmationJa:"\u5c0f\u3055\u304f\u3068\u3082\u3001\u79c1\u306e\u529b\u306f\u6fc3\u304f\u672c\u7269\u3060\u3002",affirmationPt:"Embora eu seja pequeno, o meu poder \xe9 intenso e real.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Syzygium_aromaticum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-030.jpg/330px-Syzygium_aromaticum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-030.jpg"},{id:"plant-053",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#7D9C5F",name:"Hindiba",nameEn:"Dandelion",nameDe:"L\xf6wenzahn",nameEs:"Diente de le\xf3n",nameFr:"Pissenlit",nameJa:"\u30c0\u30f3\u30c7\u30e9\u30a4\u30aa\u30f3",namePt:"Dente-de-le\xe3o",origin:"Avrupa, Asya",originEn:"Europe, Asia",originDe:"Europa, Asien",originEs:"Europa, Asia",originFr:"Europe, Asie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","\xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["purifying","freedom","resilience"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","Freiheit","Widerstandskraft"],propertiesEs:["purificante","libertad","resiliencia"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","libert\xe9","r\xe9silience"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u81ea\u7531","\u56de\u5fa9\u529b"],propertiesPt:["purificante","liberdade","resili\xeancia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn tutmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n \u015feyleri r\xfczg\xe2ra b\u0131rakmay\u0131 dene. Hindiba tohumlar\u0131 gibi, b\u0131rakman\u0131n da bir t\xfcr g\xfcven ve \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rla.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, try releasing what you've been gripping to the wind. Like dandelion seeds, remember that letting go is also a kind of trust and freedom.",dailyMessageDe:"Versuche heute, das, was du festh\xe4ltst, dem Wind zu \xfcberlassen. Wie L\xf6wenzahnsamen: Denk daran, dass Loslassen auch eine Art Vertrauen und Freiheit ist.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, intenta soltar al viento lo que has estado aferrando. Como las semillas del diente de le\xf3n, recuerda que soltar tambi\xe9n es una forma de confianza y libertad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, essaie de confier au vent ce que tu retiens. Comme les graines de pissenlit, souviens-toi que l\xe2cher prise est aussi une forme de confiance et de libert\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u63e1\u308a\u3057\u3081\u3066\u304d\u305f\u3082\u306e\u3092\u98a8\u306b\u653e\u3057\u3066\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30bf\u30f3\u30dd\u30dd\u306e\u7a2e\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u624b\u653e\u3059\u3053\u3068\u3082\u307e\u305f\u4fe1\u983c\u3068\u81ea\u7531\u306e\u304b\u305f\u3061\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, tente soltar ao vento o que voc\xea vem segurando. Como as sementes do dente-de-le\xe3o, lembre-se de que soltar tamb\xe9m \xe9 uma forma de confian\xe7a e liberdade.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 salataya ekle ya da k\xf6k\xfcn\xfc kavurup kahve benzeri bir i\xe7ecek haz\u0131rla. \xc7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak demleyerek ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131 bir tat dene.",howToUseEn:"Add the leaves to salads, or roast the root for a coffee-like drink. Brew the flowers as a tea for a purifying flavor.",howToUseDe:"Gib die Bl\xe4tter in Salate oder r\xf6ste die Wurzel f\xfcr ein kaffee\xe4hnliches Getr\xe4nk. Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten als Tee f\xfcr einen reinigenden Geschmack.",howToUseEs:"A\xf1ade las hojas a ensaladas, o tuesta la ra\xedz para una bebida parecida al caf\xe9. Infusiona las flores como t\xe9 para un sabor purificante.",howToUseFr:"Ajoute les feuilles aux salades, ou torr\xe9fie la racine pour une boisson proche du caf\xe9. Infuse les fleurs en tisane pour une saveur purifiante.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u30b5\u30e9\u30c0\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u308b\u304b\u3001\u6839\u3092\u7119\u714e\u3057\u3066\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306a\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u82b1\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u6d44\u5316\u306e\u98a8\u5473\u3092\u8a66\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Adicione as folhas a saladas, ou torre a raiz para uma bebida parecida com caf\xe9. Prepare as flores como ch\xe1 para um sabor purificante.",affirmation:"Tutmaktan \xe7ok b\u0131rakmaya g\xfcveniyorum, \xf6zg\xfcrce savruluyorum.",affirmationEn:"I trust letting go more than gripping; I drift freely.",affirmationDe:"Ich vertraue dem Loslassen mehr als dem Festhalten; ich treibe frei.",affirmationEs:"Conf\xedo m\xe1s en soltar que en aferrar; me dejo llevar con libertad.",affirmationFr:"Je fais davantage confiance au l\xe2cher-prise qu'\xe0 la prise ; je d\xe9rive librement.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u63e1\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3088\u308a\u624b\u653e\u3059\u3053\u3068\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3057\u3001\u81ea\u7531\u306b\u6f02\u3046\u3002",affirmationPt:"Confio mais em soltar do que em segurar; flutuo livremente.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/DandelionFlower.jpg/330px-DandelionFlower.jpg"},{id:"plant-054",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5E8C5A",name:"K\u0131rm\u0131z\u0131 Yonca",nameEn:"Red Clover",nameDe:"Rotklee",nameEs:"Tr\xe9bol rojo",nameFr:"Tr\xe8fle rouge",nameJa:"\u30ec\u30c3\u30c9\u30af\u30ed\u30fc\u30d0\u30fc",namePt:"Trevo-vermelho",origin:"Avrupa, Asya",originEn:"Europe, Asia",originDe:"Europa, Asien",originEs:"Europa, Asia",originFr:"Europe, Asie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["bolluk","\u015fans","besleyici"],propertiesEn:["abundance","luck","nourishing"],propertiesDe:["F\xfclle","Gl\xfcck","n\xe4hrend"],propertiesEs:["abundancia","suerte","nutritivo"],propertiesFr:["abondance","chance","nourrissant"],propertiesJa:["\u8c4a\u304b\u3055","\u5e78\u904b","\u6ecb\u990a"],propertiesPt:["abund\xe2ncia","sorte","nutritivo"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131ndaki sade bereketleri fark et. Yonca \u015fans ve bollu\u011fun sembol\xfcd\xfcr; en s\u0131radan tarlalarda bile sakl\u0131 bir hediye olabilir.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, notice the simple blessings in your life. Clover is a symbol of luck and abundance; even the most ordinary fields can hold a hidden gift.",dailyMessageDe:"Bemerke heute die einfachen Segnungen in deinem Leben. Klee ist ein Symbol f\xfcr Gl\xfcck und F\xfclle; selbst die gew\xf6hnlichsten Felder k\xf6nnen ein verborgenes Geschenk bergen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, nota las bendiciones simples en tu vida. El tr\xe9bol es s\xedmbolo de suerte y abundancia; incluso los campos m\xe1s comunes pueden guardar un regalo oculto.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, remarque les simples b\xe9n\xe9dictions de ta vie. Le tr\xe8fle est un symbole de chance et d'abondance ; m\xeame les champs les plus ordinaires peuvent cacher un cadeau.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u306e\u3055\u3055\u3084\u304b\u306a\u6075\u307f\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30af\u30ed\u30fc\u30d0\u30fc\u306f\u5e78\u904b\u3068\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3002\u3042\u308a\u3075\u308c\u305f\u91ce\u539f\u306b\u3082\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u8d08\u308a\u7269\u304c\u3042\u308b\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, perceba as b\xean\xe7\xe3os simples da sua vida. O trevo \xe9 s\xedmbolo de sorte e abund\xe2ncia; at\xe9 os campos mais comuns podem guardar um presente escondido.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak demleyip yumu\u015fak, besleyici bir i\xe7ecek olarak i\xe7. Bir \xe7i\xe7e\u011fini niyet rit\xfcelinde \u015fans sembol\xfc olarak yan\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131.",howToUseEn:"Brew the flowers as a tea for a soft, nourishing drink. Carry a flower with you in an intention ritual as a symbol of luck.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten als Tee f\xfcr ein sanftes, n\xe4hrendes Getr\xe4nk. Trage in einem Absichtsritual eine Bl\xfcte als Gl\xfcckssymbol bei dir.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las flores como t\xe9 para una bebida suave y nutritiva. Lleva una flor contigo en un ritual de intenci\xf3n como s\xedmbolo de suerte.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fleurs en tisane pour une boisson douce et nourrissante. Porte une fleur sur toi dans un rituel d'intention comme symbole de chance.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u3084\u308f\u3089\u304b\u304f\u6ecb\u990a\u306e\u3042\u308b\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u5100\u5f0f\u3067\u82b1\u3092\u4e00\u8f2a\u3001\u5e78\u904b\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3057\u3066\u643a\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores como ch\xe1 para uma bebida suave e nutritiva. Leve uma flor com voc\xea em um ritual de inten\xe7\xe3o como s\xedmbolo de sorte.",affirmation:"S\u0131radan g\xfcnlerdeki bereketi g\xf6r\xfcyorum, \u015f\xfckranla doluyum.",affirmationEn:"I see the blessings in ordinary days; I am full of gratitude.",affirmationDe:"Ich sehe die Segnungen gew\xf6hnlicher Tage; ich bin voller Dankbarkeit.",affirmationEs:"Veo las bendiciones de los d\xedas comunes; estoy lleno de gratitud.",affirmationFr:"Je vois les b\xe9n\xe9dictions des jours ordinaires ; je suis plein de gratitude.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u3042\u308a\u3075\u308c\u305f\u65e5\u3005\u306e\u6075\u307f\u3092\u898b\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u611f\u8b1d\u306b\u6e80\u3061\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Vejo as b\xean\xe7\xe3os dos dias comuns; estou cheio de gratid\xe3o.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Trifolium_pratense_-_Keila2.jpg/330px-Trifolium_pratense_-_Keila2.jpg"},{id:"plant-055",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#6F9462",name:"Limon Verbena",nameEn:"Lemon Verbena",nameDe:"Zitronenverbene",nameEs:"Hierba luisa",nameFr:"Verveine citronnelle",nameJa:"\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30d0\u30fc\u30d9\u30ca",namePt:"Verbena-lim\xe3o",origin:"G\xfcney Amerika",originEn:"South America",originDe:"S\xfcdamerika",originEs:"Am\xe9rica del Sur",originFr:"Am\xe9rique du Sud",originJa:"\u5357\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Am\xe9rica do Sul",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["ferahlat\u0131c\u0131","ne\u015felendirici","rahatlat\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["refreshing","uplifting","relaxing"],propertiesDe:["erfrischend","aufmunternd","entspannend"],propertiesEs:["refrescante","alegrante","relajante"],propertiesFr:["rafra\xeechissant","r\xe9jouissant","relaxant"],propertiesJa:["\u723d\u5feb","\u9ad8\u63da","\u30ea\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30b9"],propertiesPt:["refrescante","alegrante","relaxante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir koku bile ruh halini de\u011fi\u015ftirebilir. Limon verbena ferah ve ne\u015feli bir aromaya sahiptir; bir nefeste g\xfcl\xfcmsemeyi hat\u0131rla.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, even a small scent can shift your mood. Lemon verbena has a fresh, cheerful aroma; remember to smile in a single breath.",dailyMessageDe:"Heute kann selbst ein kleiner Duft deine Stimmung ver\xe4ndern. Zitronenverbene hat ein frisches, fr\xf6hliches Aroma; erinnere dich, in einem Atemzug zu l\xe4cheln.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, incluso un peque\xf1o aroma puede cambiar tu \xe1nimo. La hierba luisa tiene un aroma fresco y alegre; recuerda sonre\xedr en una sola respiraci\xf3n.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, m\xeame un l\xe9ger parfum peut changer ton humeur. La verveine citronnelle a un ar\xf4me frais et joyeux ; souviens-toi de sourire en une seule respiration.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u9999\u308a\u3067\u3082\u6c17\u5206\u3092\u5909\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30d0\u30fc\u30d9\u30ca\u306f\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u3067\u967d\u6c17\u306a\u9999\u308a\u3002\u3072\u3068\u547c\u5438\u3067\u307b\u307b\u3048\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, at\xe9 um pequeno aroma pode mudar o seu humor. A verbena-lim\xe3o tem um aroma fresco e alegre; lembre-se de sorrir em uma \xfanica respira\xe7\xe3o.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip ferahlat\u0131c\u0131 bir \xe7ay olarak i\xe7. Ak\u015fam yeme\u011fi sonras\u0131 rahatlamak i\xe7in bal ekleyebilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Brew the leaves in hot water for a refreshing tea. You can add honey to relax after dinner.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter in hei\xdfem Wasser f\xfcr einen erfrischenden Tee. Du kannst Honig hinzuf\xfcgen, um nach dem Abendessen zu entspannen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las hojas en agua caliente para un t\xe9 refrescante. Puedes a\xf1adir miel para relajarte despu\xe9s de cenar.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les feuilles dans de l'eau chaude pour une tisane rafra\xeechissante. Tu peux ajouter du miel pour te d\xe9tendre apr\xe8s le d\xeener.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u304a\u8336\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5915\u98df\u5f8c\u306b\u304f\u3064\u308d\u3050\u305f\u3081\u8702\u871c\u3092\u52a0\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as folhas em \xe1gua quente para um ch\xe1 refrescante. Voc\xea pode adicionar mel para relaxar ap\xf3s o jantar.",affirmation:"Bir nefeste tazelenip g\xfcl\xfcmsemeyi se\xe7iyorum.",affirmationEn:"In a single breath, I choose to refresh and smile.",affirmationDe:"In einem Atemzug w\xe4hle ich, mich zu erfrischen und zu l\xe4cheln.",affirmationEs:"En una sola respiraci\xf3n, elijo refrescarme y sonre\xedr.",affirmationFr:"En une seule respiration, je choisis de me rafra\xeechir et de sourire.",affirmationJa:"\u3072\u3068\u547c\u5438\u3067\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u306a\u308a\u3001\u307b\u307b\u3048\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3092\u9078\u3076\u3002",affirmationPt:"Em uma \xfanica respira\xe7\xe3o, escolho me renovar e sorrir.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Aloysia_citriodora_002.jpg/330px-Aloysia_citriodora_002.jpg"},{id:"plant-056",emoji:"\ud83d\udc9c",color:"#8E6FA8",name:"M\xfcrver \xc7i\xe7e\u011fi",nameEn:"Elderflower",nameDe:"Holunderbl\xfcte",nameEs:"Flor de sa\xfaco",nameFr:"Fleur de sureau",nameJa:"\u30a8\u30eb\u30c0\u30fc\u30d5\u30e9\u30ef\u30fc",namePt:"Flor de sabugueiro",origin:"Avrupa, Kuzey Afrika",originEn:"Europe, North Africa",originDe:"Europa, Nordafrika",originEs:"Europa, Norte de \xc1frica",originFr:"Europe, Afrique du Nord",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u5317\u30a2\u30d5\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Europa, Norte da \xc1frica",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["koruyucu","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm"],propertiesEn:["protective","purifying","transformation"],propertiesDe:["sch\xfctzend","reinigend","Verwandlung"],propertiesEs:["protector","purificante","transformaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["protecteur","purifiant","transformation"],propertiesJa:["\u5b88\u8b77","\u6d44\u5316","\u5909\u5bb9"],propertiesPt:["protetor","purificante","transforma\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ge\xe7i\u015flere ve e\u015fiklere sayg\u0131yla yakla\u015f. M\xfcrver halk geleneklerinde koruyucu bir e\u015fik bitkisidir; sen de yeni bir a\u015famaya nazik\xe7e ad\u0131m at.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, approach transitions and thresholds with respect. Elder is a protective threshold plant in folk traditions; step gently into a new phase too.",dailyMessageDe:"Begegne heute \xdcberg\xe4ngen und Schwellen mit Respekt. Der Holunder ist in volkst\xfcmlichen Traditionen eine sch\xfctzende Schwellenpflanze; tritt auch du sanft in eine neue Phase.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ac\xe9rcate a las transiciones y los umbrales con respeto. El sa\xfaco es una planta protectora de umbral en las tradiciones populares; entra tambi\xe9n con suavidad en una nueva etapa.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, approche les transitions et les seuils avec respect. Le sureau est une plante de seuil protectrice dans les traditions populaires ; entre aussi doucement dans une nouvelle phase.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u79fb\u308a\u5909\u308f\u308a\u3068\u5883\u76ee\u306b\u656c\u610f\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u8fd1\u3065\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30a8\u30eb\u30c0\u30fc\u306f\u6c11\u9593\u4f1d\u627f\u3067\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u5883\u754c\u306e\u690d\u7269\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u6bb5\u968e\u3078\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u8e0f\u307f\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, aproxime-se das transi\xe7\xf5es e dos limiares com respeito. O sabugueiro \xe9 uma planta protetora de limiar nas tradi\xe7\xf5es populares; entre tamb\xe9m com suavidade em uma nova fase.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini s\u0131cak suda demleyip ferahlat\u0131c\u0131 bir \xe7ay olarak i\xe7 ya da \u015furubunu haz\u0131rla. Olgun meyveleri \xe7i\u011f t\xfcketilmez; her zaman pi\u015firilmelidir.",howToUseEn:"Brew the flowers in hot water for a refreshing tea, or make a cordial. The ripe berries should not be eaten raw; always cook them.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten in hei\xdfem Wasser f\xfcr einen erfrischenden Tee oder mache einen Sirup. Die reifen Beeren sollten nicht roh gegessen werden; koche sie stets.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las flores en agua caliente para un t\xe9 refrescante, o prepara un jarabe. Las bayas maduras no se comen crudas; coc\xednalas siempre.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fleurs dans de l'eau chaude pour une tisane rafra\xeechissante, ou pr\xe9pare un sirop. Les baies m\xfbres ne se mangent pas crues ; cuis-les toujours.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3066\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u304a\u8336\u306b\u3059\u308b\u304b\u3001\u30b3\u30fc\u30c7\u30a3\u30a2\u30eb\u3092\u4f5c\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u719f\u3057\u305f\u5b9f\u306f\u751f\u3067\u98df\u3079\u305a\u3001\u5fc5\u305a\u52a0\u71b1\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores em \xe1gua quente para um ch\xe1 refrescante, ou fa\xe7a um xarope. As bagas maduras n\xe3o devem ser comidas cruas; cozinhe-as sempre.",affirmation:"E\u015fiklerden nazik\xe7e ge\xe7iyorum, d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcme a\xe7\u0131\u011f\u0131m.",affirmationEn:"I cross thresholds gently; I am open to transformation.",affirmationDe:"Ich \xfcberschreite Schwellen sanft; ich bin offen f\xfcr Verwandlung.",affirmationEs:"Cruzo los umbrales con suavidad; estoy abierto a la transformaci\xf3n.",affirmationFr:"Je franchis les seuils avec douceur ; je suis ouvert \xe0 la transformation.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5883\u76ee\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u8d8a\u3048\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u5909\u5bb9\u306b\u958b\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Atravesso os limiares com suavidade; estou aberto \xe0 transforma\xe7\xe3o.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Sambucus-berries.jpg/330px-Sambucus-berries.jpg"},{id:"plant-057",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#7B9657",name:"Misk Ada\xe7ay\u0131",nameEn:"Clary Sage",nameDe:"Muskatellersalbei",nameEs:"Salvia romana",nameFr:"Sauge sclar\xe9e",nameJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30ea\u30bb\u30fc\u30b8",namePt:"S\xe1lvia esclareia",origin:"Akdeniz",originEn:"Mediterranean",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u5730\u57df",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["sezgi","rahatlat\u0131c\u0131","netlik"],propertiesEn:["intuition","relaxing","clarity"],propertiesDe:["Intuition","entspannend","Klarheit"],propertiesEs:["intuici\xf3n","relajante","claridad"],propertiesFr:["intuition","relaxant","clart\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u76f4\u611f","\u30ea\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30b9","\u660e\u6670"],propertiesPt:["intui\xe7\xe3o","relaxante","clareza"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn zihnini yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r ve i\xe7sel g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfcne yer a\xe7. Misk ada\xe7ay\u0131n\u0131n ad\u0131 'berrakl\u0131k' anlam\u0131na gelir; g\xf6zlerini kapat\u0131p i\xe7ine bak.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, calm your mind and make room for your inner sight. Clary sage's name means 'clarity'; close your eyes and look within.",dailyMessageDe:"Beruhige heute deinen Geist und schaffe Raum f\xfcr deine innere Sicht. Der Name des Muskatellersalbeis bedeutet 'Klarheit'; schlie\xdfe die Augen und blicke nach innen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, calma tu mente y haz espacio para tu visi\xf3n interior. El nombre de la salvia romana significa 'claridad'; cierra los ojos y mira dentro.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, apaise ton esprit et fais de la place \xe0 ta vision int\xe9rieure. Le nom de la sauge sclar\xe9e signifie 'clart\xe9' ; ferme les yeux et regarde en toi.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u93ae\u3081\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u8996\u529b\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u4f59\u767d\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30af\u30e9\u30ea\u30bb\u30fc\u30b8\u306e\u540d\u306f\u300c\u660e\u6670\u3055\u300d\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u76ee\u3092\u9589\u3058\u3001\u5185\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, acalme a sua mente e abra espa\xe7o para a sua vis\xe3o interior. O nome da s\xe1lvia esclareia significa 'clareza'; feche os olhos e olhe para dentro.",howToUse:"Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 dif\xfcz\xf6rde kullanarak rahatlat\u0131c\u0131 bir ortam yarat ya da meditasyon \xf6ncesi avucuna bir damla koyup kokla. \xc7ay\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ok hafif demle.",howToUseEn:"Use the essential oil in a diffuser to create a relaxing atmosphere, or put a drop in your palm and inhale before meditation. Brew its tea very lightly.",howToUseDe:"Verwende das \xe4therische \xd6l im Diffuser, um eine entspannende Atmosph\xe4re zu schaffen, oder gib vor der Meditation einen Tropfen in die Handfl\xe4che und atme ihn ein. Br\xfche seinen Tee sehr leicht.",howToUseEs:"Usa el aceite esencial en un difusor para crear un ambiente relajante, o pon una gota en tu palma e inhala antes de meditar. Prepara su t\xe9 muy ligero.",howToUseFr:"Utilise l'huile essentielle dans un diffuseur pour cr\xe9er une atmosph\xe8re relaxante, ou mets une goutte dans ta paume et inhale avant la m\xe9ditation. Infuse sa tisane tr\xe8s l\xe9g\xe8rement.",howToUseJa:"\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u30c7\u30a3\u30d5\u30e5\u30fc\u30b6\u30fc\u3067\u4f7f\u3044\u3001\u30ea\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30b9\u3059\u308b\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308b\u304b\u3001\u7791\u60f3\u524d\u306b\u624b\u306e\u3072\u3089\u306b\u4e00\u6ef4\u5782\u3089\u3057\u3066\u9999\u308a\u3092\u5438\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u304a\u8336\u306f\u3054\u304f\u8efd\u304f\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Use o \xf3leo essencial em um difusor para criar um ambiente relaxante, ou pingue uma gota na palma e inale antes de meditar. Prepare o ch\xe1 bem leve.",affirmation:"Zihnimi yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131yorum, i\xe7sel g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfcm berrakla\u015f\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I calm my mind; my inner sight grows clear.",affirmationDe:"Ich beruhige meinen Geist; meine innere Sicht wird klar.",affirmationEs:"Calmo mi mente; mi visi\xf3n interior se aclara.",affirmationFr:"J'apaise mon esprit ; ma vision int\xe9rieure s'\xe9claircit.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u93ae\u3081\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u8996\u529b\u304c\u6f84\u3093\u3067\u3044\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Acalmo a minha mente; a minha vis\xe3o interior fica clara.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Salvia_sclarea3.jpg/330px-Salvia_sclarea3.jpg"},{id:"plant-058",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#6D8F58",name:"It\u0131r (Geranyum)",nameEn:"Geranium",nameDe:"Geranie",nameEs:"Geranio",nameFr:"G\xe9ranium",nameJa:"\u30bc\u30e9\u30cb\u30a6\u30e0",namePt:"Ger\xe2nio",origin:"G\xfcney Afrika",originEn:"South Africa",originDe:"S\xfcdafrika",originEs:"Sud\xe1frica",originFr:"Afrique du Sud",originJa:"\u5357\u30a2\u30d5\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"\xc1frica do Sul",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["denge","duygusal uyum","\u015fefkat"],propertiesEn:["balance","emotional harmony","compassion"],propertiesDe:["Gleichgewicht","emotionale Harmonie","Mitgef\xfchl"],propertiesEs:["equilibrio","armon\xeda emocional","compasi\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["\xe9quilibre","harmonie \xe9motionnelle","compassion"],propertiesJa:["\u5747\u8861","\u611f\u60c5\u306e\u8abf\u548c","\u6148\u3057\u307f"],propertiesPt:["equil\xedbrio","harmonia emocional","compaix\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn duygular\u0131n\u0131 ne bast\u0131r ne de ta\u015fmas\u0131na izin ver; dengede tut. Geranyum kalbinin ini\u015f \xe7\u0131k\u0131\u015flar\u0131n\u0131 yumu\u015fat\u0131r, i\xe7sel bir uyum getirir.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, neither suppress your emotions nor let them overflow; hold them in balance. Geranium softens the ups and downs of your heart and brings inner harmony.",dailyMessageDe:"Unterdr\xfccke heute deine Gef\xfchle weder, noch lass sie \xfcberlaufen; halte sie im Gleichgewicht. Geranie mildert die H\xf6hen und Tiefen deines Herzens und bringt innere Harmonie.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ni reprimas tus emociones ni dejes que desborden; mantenlas en equilibrio. El geranio suaviza los altibajos de tu coraz\xf3n y trae armon\xeda interior.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ne r\xe9prime pas tes \xe9motions et ne les laisse pas d\xe9border ; maintiens-les en \xe9quilibre. Le g\xe9ranium adoucit les hauts et les bas de ton c\u0153ur et apporte une harmonie int\xe9rieure.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u611f\u60c5\u3092\u6291\u3048\u8fbc\u307f\u3082\u305b\u305a\u3001\u3042\u3075\u308c\u3055\u305b\u3082\u305b\u305a\u3001\u5747\u8861\u306b\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30bc\u30e9\u30cb\u30a6\u30e0\u306f\u5fc3\u306e\u6d6e\u304d\u6c88\u307f\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u8abf\u548c\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, nem reprima as suas emo\xe7\xf5es nem deixe que transbordem; mantenha-as em equil\xedbrio. O ger\xe2nio suaviza os altos e baixos do seu cora\xe7\xe3o e traz harmonia interior.",howToUse:"Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 dif\xfcz\xf6rde kullanarak dengeleyici bir ortam yarat ya da ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131 ya\u011fla seyreltip cilde nazik\xe7e s\xfcr. Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 kokulu bir banyo i\xe7in suya ekle.",howToUseEn:"Use the essential oil in a diffuser to create a balancing atmosphere, or dilute it with a carrier oil and gently apply to the skin. Add the leaves to your bath for a scented soak.",howToUseDe:"Verwende das \xe4therische \xd6l im Diffuser, um eine ausgleichende Atmosph\xe4re zu schaffen, oder verd\xfcnne es mit einem Tr\xe4ger\xf6l und trage es sanft auf die Haut auf. Gib die Bl\xe4tter f\xfcr ein duftendes Bad ins Wasser.",howToUseEs:"Usa el aceite esencial en un difusor para crear un ambiente equilibrante, o dil\xfayelo con un aceite portador y apl\xedcalo suavemente sobre la piel. A\xf1ade las hojas al ba\xf1o para un remojo arom\xe1tico.",howToUseFr:"Utilise l'huile essentielle dans un diffuseur pour cr\xe9er une atmosph\xe8re \xe9quilibrante, ou dilue-la avec une huile v\xe9g\xe9tale et applique-la doucement sur la peau. Ajoute les feuilles au bain pour un trempage parfum\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u30c7\u30a3\u30d5\u30e5\u30fc\u30b6\u30fc\u3067\u4f7f\u3044\u3001\u5747\u8861\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308b\u304b\u3001\u30ad\u30e3\u30ea\u30a2\u30aa\u30a4\u30eb\u3067\u8584\u3081\u3066\u808c\u306b\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5857\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u8449\u3092\u6e6f\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3001\u9999\u308a\u306e\u5165\u6d74\u3092\u3002",howToUsePt:"Use o \xf3leo essencial em um difusor para criar um ambiente equilibrante, ou dilua-o com um \xf3leo carreador e aplique suavemente na pele. Adicione as folhas ao banho para uma imers\xe3o perfumada.",affirmation:"Duygular\u0131m\u0131 dengede tutuyorum, i\xe7sel uyum i\xe7indeyim.",affirmationEn:"I hold my emotions in balance; I am in inner harmony.",affirmationDe:"Ich halte meine Gef\xfchle im Gleichgewicht; ich bin in innerer Harmonie.",affirmationEs:"Mantengo mis emociones en equilibrio; estoy en armon\xeda interior.",affirmationFr:"Je maintiens mes \xe9motions en \xe9quilibre ; je suis en harmonie int\xe9rieure.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u611f\u60c5\u3092\u5747\u8861\u306b\u4fdd\u3061\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u8abf\u548c\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Mantenho as minhas emo\xe7\xf5es em equil\xedbrio; estou em harmonia interior.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg/330px-Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg"},{id:"plant-059",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3c",color:"#EBD25A",name:"\xd6lmez \xc7i\xe7ek (Helikrizum)",nameEn:"Helichrysum",nameDe:"Strohblume",nameEs:"Siempreviva",nameFr:"Immortelle",nameJa:"\u30d8\u30ea\u30af\u30ea\u30b5\u30e0",namePt:"Helicriso",origin:"Akdeniz",originEn:"Mediterranean",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u5730\u57df",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["onar\u0131c\u0131","kal\u0131c\u0131l\u0131k","iyile\u015ftirici"],propertiesEn:["restorative","everlasting","healing"],propertiesDe:["regenerierend","best\xe4ndig","heilend"],propertiesEs:["reparador","perdurable","sanador"],propertiesFr:["r\xe9parateur","\xe9ternel","gu\xe9risseur"],propertiesJa:["\u56de\u5fa9","\u6c38\u7d9a","\u7652\u3057"],propertiesPt:["restaurador","duradouro","curativo"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ge\xe7mi\u015f yaralar\u0131n\u0131n zamanla iyile\u015febilece\u011fine inan. Kantaron sar\u0131s\u0131 'solmayan \xe7i\xe7ek' olarak bilinir; sen de kal\u0131c\u0131 bir umut ta\u015f\u0131.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, believe that your past wounds can heal in time. Helichrysum is known as the 'everlasting flower'; carry a lasting hope too.",dailyMessageDe:"Glaube heute daran, dass deine vergangenen Wunden mit der Zeit heilen k\xf6nnen. Die Strohblume ist als 'unverg\xe4ngliche Blume' bekannt; trage auch du eine best\xe4ndige Hoffnung.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, cree que tus heridas pasadas pueden sanar con el tiempo. La siempreviva es conocida como la 'flor que no se marchita'; lleva tambi\xe9n una esperanza duradera.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, crois que tes blessures pass\xe9es peuvent gu\xe9rir avec le temps. L'immortelle est connue comme la 'fleur qui ne fane pas' ; porte aussi un espoir durable.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u904e\u53bb\u306e\u50b7\u304c\u6642\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u7652\u3048\u3046\u308b\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d8\u30ea\u30af\u30ea\u30b5\u30e0\u306f\u300c\u67af\u308c\u306a\u3044\u82b1\u300d\u3068\u3057\u3066\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u8272\u3042\u305b\u306c\u5e0c\u671b\u3092\u643a\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, acredite que as suas feridas passadas podem curar com o tempo. O helicriso \xe9 conhecido como a 'flor que n\xe3o murcha'; carregue tamb\xe9m uma esperan\xe7a duradoura.",howToUse:"Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131 ya\u011fla seyreltip yorgun cilde nazik\xe7e s\xfcr. Kurutulmu\u015f \xe7i\xe7eklerini solmayan bir buket olarak evinde umut sembol\xfc gibi sakla.",howToUseEn:"Dilute the essential oil with a carrier oil and gently apply to tired skin. Keep the dried flowers as an everlasting bouquet, a symbol of hope at home.",howToUseDe:"Verd\xfcnne das \xe4therische \xd6l mit einem Tr\xe4ger\xf6l und trage es sanft auf m\xfcde Haut auf. Bewahre die getrockneten Bl\xfcten als unverg\xe4nglichen Strau\xdf auf, ein Symbol der Hoffnung zu Hause.",howToUseEs:"Diluye el aceite esencial con un aceite portador y apl\xedcalo suavemente sobre la piel cansada. Guarda las flores secas como un ramo perdurable, s\xedmbolo de esperanza en casa.",howToUseFr:"Dilue l'huile essentielle avec une huile v\xe9g\xe9tale et applique-la doucement sur la peau fatigu\xe9e. Garde les fleurs s\xe9ch\xe9es comme un bouquet \xe9ternel, symbole d'espoir chez toi.",howToUseJa:"\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u30ad\u30e3\u30ea\u30a2\u30aa\u30a4\u30eb\u3067\u8584\u3081\u3001\u75b2\u308c\u305f\u808c\u306b\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5857\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u82b1\u3092\u67af\u308c\u306a\u3044\u82b1\u675f\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5bb6\u306b\u98fe\u308a\u3001\u5e0c\u671b\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u306b\u3002",howToUsePt:"Dilua o \xf3leo essencial com um \xf3leo carreador e aplique suavemente na pele cansada. Guarde as flores secas como um buqu\xea duradouro, s\xedmbolo de esperan\xe7a em casa.",affirmation:"Yaralar\u0131m zamanla iyile\u015fir, kal\u0131c\u0131 bir umut ta\u015f\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"My wounds heal in time; I carry a lasting hope.",affirmationDe:"Meine Wunden heilen mit der Zeit; ich trage eine best\xe4ndige Hoffnung.",affirmationEs:"Mis heridas sanan con el tiempo; llevo una esperanza duradera.",affirmationFr:"Mes blessures gu\xe9rissent avec le temps ; je porte un espoir durable.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u50b7\u306f\u6642\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u7652\u3048\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u8272\u3042\u305b\u306c\u5e0c\u671b\u3092\u643a\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Minhas feridas curam com o tempo; carrego uma esperan\xe7a duradoura.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Helichrysum_sanguineum.jpg/330px-Helichrysum_sanguineum.jpg"},{id:"plant-060",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5A8466",name:"\xc7ay A\u011fac\u0131",nameEn:"Tea Tree",nameDe:"Teebaum",nameEs:"\xc1rbol de t\xe9",nameFr:"Arbre \xe0 th\xe9",nameJa:"\u30c6\u30a3\u30fc\u30c4\u30ea\u30fc",namePt:"Melaleuca",origin:"Avustralya",originEn:"Australia",originDe:"Australien",originEs:"Australia",originFr:"Australie",originJa:"\u30aa\u30fc\u30b9\u30c8\u30e9\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Austr\xe1lia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Lar\xedngeo",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","koruyucu","temizleyici"],propertiesEn:["purifying","protective","cleansing"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","sch\xfctzend","kl\xe4rend"],propertiesEs:["purificante","protector","limpiador"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","protecteur","nettoyant"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u5b88\u8b77","\u6e05\u3081\u308b"],propertiesPt:["purificante","protetor","limpador"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn hem bedenini hem \xe7evreni tazele ve temiz tut. \xc7ay a\u011fac\u0131 g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131d\u0131r; sen de ihtiyac\u0131n olmayan\u0131 temizleyip yeni bir ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7 yap.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, refresh and keep both your body and surroundings clean. Tea tree is a strong purifier; clear away what you don't need and make a fresh start.",dailyMessageDe:"Erfrische heute deinen K\xf6rper und deine Umgebung und halte beide rein. Teebaum ist ein starker Reiniger; r\xe4ume weg, was du nicht brauchst, und beginne neu.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, refresca y mant\xe9n limpios tu cuerpo y tu entorno. El \xe1rbol de t\xe9 es un purificante fuerte; despeja lo que no necesitas y empieza de nuevo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, rafra\xeechis et garde propres ton corps et ton environnement. L'arbre \xe0 th\xe9 est un puissant purifiant ; d\xe9barrasse-toi du superflu et prends un nouveau d\xe9part.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4f53\u3082\u5468\u308a\u3082\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306b\u6e05\u6f54\u306b\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30c6\u30a3\u30fc\u30c4\u30ea\u30fc\u306f\u5f37\u529b\u306a\u6d44\u5316\u5264\u3002\u8981\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u3092\u53d6\u308a\u9664\u304d\u3001\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u59cb\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, refresque e mantenha limpos o seu corpo e o seu entorno. A melaleuca \xe9 um forte purificante; limpe o que n\xe3o precisa e fa\xe7a um recome\xe7o.",howToUse:"Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131 ya\u011fla seyreltip cilt i\xe7in noktasal kullan ya da temizlik suyuna birka\xe7 damla katarak do\u011fal bir temizleyici yap. \u0130\xe7ilmez; sadece harici kullan.",howToUseEn:"Dilute the essential oil with a carrier oil for spot use on skin, or add a few drops to cleaning water for a natural cleaner. Not for drinking; external use only.",howToUseDe:"Verd\xfcnne das \xe4therische \xd6l mit einem Tr\xe4ger\xf6l f\xfcr die punktuelle Anwendung auf der Haut oder gib ein paar Tropfen ins Putzwasser f\xfcr einen nat\xfcrlichen Reiniger. Nicht zum Trinken; nur \xe4u\xdferlich.",howToUseEs:"Diluye el aceite esencial con un aceite portador para uso puntual en la piel, o a\xf1ade unas gotas al agua de limpieza para un limpiador natural. No se bebe; solo uso externo.",howToUseFr:"Dilue l'huile essentielle avec une huile v\xe9g\xe9tale pour une application locale sur la peau, ou ajoute quelques gouttes \xe0 l'eau de nettoyage pour un nettoyant naturel. Ne pas boire ; usage externe uniquement.",howToUseJa:"\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u30ad\u30e3\u30ea\u30a2\u30aa\u30a4\u30eb\u3067\u8584\u3081\u3001\u808c\u306b\u90e8\u5206\u7684\u306b\u4f7f\u3046\u304b\u3001\u6383\u9664\u306e\u6c34\u306b\u6570\u6ef4\u52a0\u3048\u3066\u81ea\u7136\u306a\u6d17\u6d44\u5264\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u98f2\u7528\u4e0d\u53ef\u3001\u5916\u7528\u306e\u307f\u3002",howToUsePt:"Dilua o \xf3leo essencial com um \xf3leo carreador para uso pontual na pele, ou adicione algumas gotas \xe0 \xe1gua de limpeza para um limpador natural. N\xe3o ingerir; apenas uso externo.",affirmation:"Bedenimi ve \xe7evremi temizliyorum, taze bir ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7 yap\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I cleanse my body and surroundings and make a fresh start.",affirmationDe:"Ich reinige meinen K\xf6rper und meine Umgebung und beginne neu.",affirmationEs:"Limpio mi cuerpo y mi entorno y hago un nuevo comienzo.",affirmationFr:"Je purifie mon corps et mon environnement et prends un nouveau d\xe9part.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4f53\u3068\u5468\u308a\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u3001\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u59cb\u307e\u308a\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Limpo o meu corpo e o meu entorno e fa\xe7o um recome\xe7o.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Melaleuca_alternifolia_flowers.jpg/330px-Melaleuca_alternifolia_flowers.jpg"},{id:"plant-061",emoji:"\ud83d\udc9c",color:"#8A78B8",name:"Funda (S\xfcp\xfcrge \xc7al\u0131s\u0131)",nameEn:"Heather",nameDe:"Heidekraut",nameEs:"Brezo",nameFr:"Bruy\xe8re",nameJa:"\u30d8\u30b6\u30fc",namePt:"Urze",origin:"Avrupa, Kuzey Afrika",originEn:"Europe, North Africa",originDe:"Europa, Nordafrika",originEs:"Europa, Norte de \xc1frica",originFr:"Europe, Afrique du Nord",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u5317\u30a2\u30d5\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Europa, Norte da \xc1frica",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["koruyucu","huzur","sadelik"],propertiesEn:["protective","peace","simplicity"],propertiesDe:["sch\xfctzend","Frieden","Einfachheit"],propertiesEs:["protector","paz","sencillez"],propertiesFr:["protecteur","paix","simplicit\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u5b88\u8b77","\u5b89\u3089\u304e","\u7d20\u6734\u3055"],propertiesPt:["protetor","paz","simplicidade"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn sade ve m\xfctevaz\u0131 olan\u0131n g\xfczelli\u011fini g\xf6r. Funda \xe7\u0131plak k\u0131rlarda bile diren\xe7le a\xe7ar; sen de g\xf6steri\u015fsiz bir huzurun de\u011ferini hat\u0131rla.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, see the beauty of what is simple and humble. Heather blooms with resilience even on bare moors; remember the worth of an unassuming peace.",dailyMessageDe:"Erkenne heute die Sch\xf6nheit des Einfachen und Bescheidenen. Heidekraut bl\xfcht selbst auf kahlen Heiden widerstandsf\xe4hig; erinnere dich an den Wert eines unaufdringlichen Friedens.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ve la belleza de lo sencillo y humilde. El brezo florece con resiliencia incluso en p\xe1ramos desnudos; recuerda el valor de una paz sin pretensiones.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, vois la beaut\xe9 de ce qui est simple et humble. La bruy\xe8re fleurit avec r\xe9silience m\xeame sur les landes nues ; souviens-toi de la valeur d'une paix discr\xe8te.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u7d20\u6734\u3067\u614e\u307e\u3057\u3044\u3082\u306e\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u898b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d8\u30b6\u30fc\u306f\u8352\u308c\u305f\u91ce\u3067\u3082\u529b\u5f37\u304f\u54b2\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u63a7\u3048\u3081\u306a\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u306e\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, veja a beleza do que \xe9 simples e humilde. A urze floresce com resili\xeancia mesmo em charnecas nuas; lembre-se do valor de uma paz despretensiosa.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle ya da kurutulmu\u015f bir demetini huzur niyetiyle evinde bulundur. Banyo suyuna ekleyerek sade bir dinlenme rit\xfceli yap.",howToUseEn:"Lightly brew the flowers as a tea, or keep a dried bundle at home with an intention of peace. Add it to your bath for a simple resting ritual.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xfcten leicht als Tee oder bewahre ein getrocknetes B\xfcndel mit Friedensabsicht zu Hause auf. Gib es ins Bad f\xfcr ein einfaches Ruheritual.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona ligeramente las flores como t\xe9, o guarda un manojo seco en casa con intenci\xf3n de paz. A\xf1\xe1delo al ba\xf1o para un sencillo ritual de descanso.",howToUseFr:"Infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les fleurs en tisane, ou garde un bouquet s\xe9ch\xe9 chez toi avec une intention de paix. Ajoute-le au bain pour un simple rituel de repos.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u675f\u3092\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3067\u5bb6\u306b\u7f6e\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5165\u6d74\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3001\u7d20\u6734\u306a\u4f11\u606f\u306e\u5100\u5f0f\u3092\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare levemente as flores como ch\xe1, ou mantenha um ma\xe7o seco em casa com a inten\xe7\xe3o de paz. Adicione ao banho para um simples ritual de descanso.",affirmation:"Sade olan\u0131n g\xfczelli\u011fini g\xf6r\xfcyorum, m\xfctevaz\u0131 huzurla doluyum.",affirmationEn:"I see the beauty of simplicity; I am full of humble peace.",affirmationDe:"Ich sehe die Sch\xf6nheit des Einfachen; ich bin voller bescheidenem Frieden.",affirmationEs:"Veo la belleza de lo sencillo; estoy lleno de paz humilde.",affirmationFr:"Je vois la beaut\xe9 de la simplicit\xe9 ; je suis plein d'une paix humble.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u7d20\u6734\u3055\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u898b\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u614e\u307e\u3057\u3044\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u306b\u6e80\u3061\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Vejo a beleza da simplicidade; estou cheio de uma paz humilde.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/CallunaVulgaris.jpg/330px-CallunaVulgaris.jpg"},{id:"plant-062",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3e",color:"#C8A94B",name:"\xc7emen Otu",nameEn:"Fenugreek",nameDe:"Bockshornklee",nameEs:"Fenogreco",nameFr:"Fenugrec",nameJa:"\u30d5\u30a7\u30cc\u30b0\u30ea\u30fc\u30af",namePt:"Feno-grego",origin:"Bat\u0131 Asya, Akdeniz",originEn:"Western Asia, Mediterranean",originDe:"Westasien, Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Asia Occidental, Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"Asie occidentale, M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u897f\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77",originPt:"\xc1sia Ocidental, Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["besleyici","g\xfc\xe7lendirici","bolluk"],propertiesEn:["nourishing","strengthening","abundance"],propertiesDe:["n\xe4hrend","st\xe4rkend","F\xfclle"],propertiesEs:["nutritivo","fortalecedor","abundancia"],propertiesFr:["nourrissant","fortifiant","abondance"],propertiesJa:["\u6ecb\u990a","\u5f37\u5316","\u8c4a\u304b\u3055"],propertiesPt:["nutritivo","fortalecedor","abund\xe2ncia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kendini i\xe7ten besle, sadece bedenini de\u011fil ruhunu da. \xc7emen kadim bir kuvvet tohumudur; ger\xe7ek g\xfcc\xfcn derin bir bak\u0131mdan geldi\u011fini hat\u0131rla.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, nourish yourself from within, not only your body but your spirit. Fenugreek is an ancient seed of strength; remember that real power comes from deep care.",dailyMessageDe:"N\xe4hre dich heute von innen, nicht nur deinen K\xf6rper, sondern auch deine Seele. Bockshornklee ist ein altes Kraftkorn; denk daran, dass wahre Kraft aus tiefer F\xfcrsorge kommt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, n\xfatrete desde dentro, no solo tu cuerpo sino tu esp\xedritu. El fenogreco es una antigua semilla de fuerza; recuerda que el verdadero poder viene de un cuidado profundo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, nourris-toi de l'int\xe9rieur, pas seulement ton corps mais ton esprit. Le fenugrec est une ancienne graine de force ; souviens-toi que la vraie puissance vient d'un soin profond.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5185\u5074\u304b\u3089\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u990a\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u4f53\u3060\u3051\u3067\u306a\u304f\u9b42\u3082\u3002\u30d5\u30a7\u30cc\u30b0\u30ea\u30fc\u30af\u306f\u53e4\u4ee3\u306e\u529b\u306e\u7a2e\u3002\u771f\u306e\u529b\u306f\u6df1\u3044\u624b\u5f53\u3066\u304b\u3089\u6765\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, nutra-se por dentro, n\xe3o s\xf3 o corpo mas o esp\xedrito. O feno-grego \xe9 uma antiga semente de for\xe7a; lembre-se de que o verdadeiro poder vem de um cuidado profundo.",howToUse:"Tohumlar\u0131n\u0131 suda bekletip yumu\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \xe7ay olarak i\xe7 ya da filizlendirip salataya ekle. Az miktarda, d\xfczenli olarak kullan.",howToUseEn:"Soak the seeds in water and drink them as a tea once softened, or sprout them and add to salads. Use in small, regular amounts.",howToUseDe:"Weiche die Samen in Wasser ein und trinke sie als Tee, sobald sie weich sind, oder ziehe Sprossen und gib sie in Salate. Verwende kleine, regelm\xe4\xdfige Mengen.",howToUseEs:"Remoja las semillas en agua y b\xe9belas como t\xe9 cuando est\xe9n blandas, o germ\xednalas y a\xf1\xe1delas a ensaladas. \xdasalas en cantidades peque\xf1as y regulares.",howToUseFr:"Fais tremper les graines dans l'eau et bois-les en tisane une fois ramollies, ou fais-les germer et ajoute-les aux salades. Utilise de petites quantit\xe9s r\xe9guli\xe8res.",howToUseJa:"\u7a2e\u3092\u6c34\u306b\u6d78\u3057\u3001\u3084\u308f\u3089\u304b\u304f\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3089\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u98f2\u3080\u304b\u3001\u767a\u82bd\u3055\u305b\u3066\u30b5\u30e9\u30c0\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5c11\u91cf\u3092\u5b9a\u671f\u7684\u306b\u3002",howToUsePt:"Deixe as sementes de molho na \xe1gua e beba-as como ch\xe1 quando amolecerem, ou germine-as e adicione a saladas. Use em quantidades pequenas e regulares.",affirmation:"Kendimi i\xe7ten besliyorum, g\xfcc\xfcm derin bir bak\u0131mdan geliyor.",affirmationEn:"I nourish myself from within; my strength comes from deep care.",affirmationDe:"Ich n\xe4hre mich von innen; meine Kraft kommt aus tiefer F\xfcrsorge.",affirmationEs:"Me nutro desde dentro; mi fuerza viene de un cuidado profundo.",affirmationFr:"Je me nourris de l'int\xe9rieur ; ma force vient d'un soin profond.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5185\u5074\u304b\u3089\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u990a\u3046\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u529b\u306f\u6df1\u3044\u624b\u5f53\u3066\u304b\u3089\u6765\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Nutro-me por dentro; a minha for\xe7a vem de um cuidado profundo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Illustration_Trigonella_foenum-graecum0_clean.jpg/330px-Illustration_Trigonella_foenum-graecum0_clean.jpg"},{id:"plant-063",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#6E9456",name:"Mine \xc7i\xe7e\u011fi",nameEn:"Verbena",nameDe:"Eisenkraut",nameEs:"Verbena",nameFr:"Verveine",nameJa:"\u30d0\u30fc\u30d9\u30ca",namePt:"Verbena",origin:"Avrupa, Asya",originEn:"Europe, Asia",originDe:"Europa, Asien",originEs:"Europa, Asia",originFr:"Europe, Asie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["ar\u0131nma","ilham","koruyucu"],propertiesEn:["purification","inspiration","protective"],propertiesDe:["Reinigung","Inspiration","sch\xfctzend"],propertiesEs:["purificaci\xf3n","inspiraci\xf3n","protector"],propertiesFr:["purification","inspiration","protecteur"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u3072\u3089\u3081\u304d","\u5b88\u8b77"],propertiesPt:["purifica\xe7\xe3o","inspira\xe7\xe3o","protetor"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ilham\u0131n gelmesine alan a\xe7. Mine \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi eski \xe7a\u011flarda kutsal bir t\xf6ren bitkisiydi; sen de g\xfcn\xfc k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir kutsall\u0131k duygusuyla kar\u015f\u0131la.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, make space for inspiration to come. Verbena was a sacred ceremonial plant in ancient times; meet the day with a small sense of the sacred.",dailyMessageDe:"Schaffe heute Raum, damit Inspiration kommen kann. Eisenkraut war in der Antike eine heilige Zeremonienpflanze; begegne dem Tag mit einem kleinen Gef\xfchl des Heiligen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, haz espacio para que llegue la inspiraci\xf3n. La verbena fue una planta ceremonial sagrada en la antig\xfcedad; recibe el d\xeda con un peque\xf1o sentido de lo sagrado.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, fais de la place pour que l'inspiration vienne. La verveine \xe9tait une plante c\xe9r\xe9monielle sacr\xe9e dans l'Antiquit\xe9 ; accueille le jour avec un petit sentiment du sacr\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3072\u3089\u3081\u304d\u304c\u6765\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306e\u4f59\u767d\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d0\u30fc\u30d9\u30ca\u306f\u53e4\u4ee3\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u5100\u5f0f\u306e\u690d\u7269\u3002\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u795e\u8056\u3055\u306e\u611f\u899a\u3067\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u8fce\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, abra espa\xe7o para a inspira\xe7\xe3o chegar. A verbena foi uma planta cerimonial sagrada na antiguidade; receba o dia com um pequeno senso do sagrado.",howToUse:"Yaprak ve \xe7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak demleyip ak\u015famlar\u0131 sakinle\u015fmek i\xe7in i\xe7. Bir demetini ilham ve koruma niyetiyle \xe7al\u0131\u015fma alan\u0131na yerle\u015ftir.",howToUseEn:"Brew the leaves and flowers as a tea and drink in the evenings to calm down. Place a bundle in your workspace with an intention of inspiration and protection.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche Bl\xe4tter und Bl\xfcten als Tee und trinke ihn abends zur Beruhigung. Stelle ein B\xfcndel mit der Absicht von Inspiration und Schutz in deinen Arbeitsbereich.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona hojas y flores como t\xe9 y bebe por las noches para calmarte. Coloca un manojo en tu espacio de trabajo con intenci\xf3n de inspiraci\xf3n y protecci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Infuse feuilles et fleurs en tisane et bois le soir pour te calmer. Place un bouquet dans ton espace de travail avec une intention d'inspiration et de protection.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3068\u82b1\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u591c\u306b\u843d\u3061\u7740\u304f\u305f\u3081\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3072\u3089\u3081\u304d\u3068\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3067\u675f\u3092\u4f5c\u696d\u5834\u306b\u7f6e\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as folhas e flores como ch\xe1 e beba \xe0 noite para se acalmar. Coloque um ma\xe7o no seu espa\xe7o de trabalho com a inten\xe7\xe3o de inspira\xe7\xe3o e prote\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"\u0130lhama alan a\xe7\u0131yorum, g\xfcn\xfc kutsall\u0131kla kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I make space for inspiration and meet the day with reverence.",affirmationDe:"Ich schaffe Raum f\xfcr Inspiration und begegne dem Tag mit Ehrfurcht.",affirmationEs:"Hago espacio para la inspiraci\xf3n y recibo el d\xeda con reverencia.",affirmationFr:"Je fais place \xe0 l'inspiration et accueille le jour avec r\xe9v\xe9rence.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u3072\u3089\u3081\u304d\u306b\u4f59\u767d\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u3001\u754f\u656c\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u8fce\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Abro espa\xe7o para a inspira\xe7\xe3o e recebo o dia com rever\xeancia.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Eisenkraut%2C_Passau.JPG/330px-Eisenkraut%2C_Passau.JPG"},{id:"plant-064",emoji:"\ud83c\udf38",color:"#D98AB0",name:"Kiraz \xc7i\xe7e\u011fi",nameEn:"Cherry Blossom",nameDe:"Kirschbl\xfcte",nameEs:"Flor de cerezo",nameFr:"Fleur de cerisier",nameJa:"\u685c",namePt:"Flor de cerejeira",origin:"Do\u011fu Asya, Japonya",originEn:"East Asia, Japan",originDe:"Ostasien, Japan",originEs:"Asia Oriental, Jap\xf3n",originFr:"Asie de l'Est, Japon",originJa:"\u6771\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u65e5\u672c",originPt:"\xc1sia Oriental, Jap\xe3o",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["ge\xe7icilik fark\u0131ndal\u0131\u011f\u0131","g\xfczellik","yenilenme"],propertiesEn:["impermanence awareness","beauty","renewal"],propertiesDe:["Bewusstsein f\xfcr Verg\xe4nglichkeit","Sch\xf6nheit","Erneuerung"],propertiesEs:["conciencia de la impermanencia","belleza","renovaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["conscience de l'impermanence","beaut\xe9","renouveau"],propertiesJa:["\u7121\u5e38\u3078\u306e\u6c17\u3065\u304d","\u7f8e","\u518d\u751f"],propertiesPt:["consci\xeancia da imperman\xeancia","beleza","renova\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn an\u0131n g\xfczelli\u011fini, ge\xe7ici oldu\u011fu i\xe7in daha \xe7ok sev. Kiraz \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi k\u0131sa \xf6m\xfcrl\xfcd\xfcr ama tam da bu y\xfczden de\u011ferlidir; sen de \u015fu an\u0131 kucakla.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, love the beauty of the moment all the more because it passes. Cherry blossoms are short-lived yet precious for that very reason; embrace this moment too.",dailyMessageDe:"Liebe heute die Sch\xf6nheit des Augenblicks umso mehr, weil er vergeht. Kirschbl\xfcten sind kurzlebig, doch gerade deshalb kostbar; umarme auch diesen Moment.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ama la belleza del momento a\xfan m\xe1s porque pasa. La flor de cerezo es ef\xedmera pero, justo por eso, preciosa; abraza tambi\xe9n este instante.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, aime la beaut\xe9 de l'instant d'autant plus qu'il passe. La fleur de cerisier est \xe9ph\xe9m\xe8re mais pr\xe9cieuse pour cette raison m\xeame ; embrasse aussi ce moment.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u79fb\u308d\u3046\u304b\u3089\u3053\u305d\u3001\u77ac\u9593\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u3044\u3063\u305d\u3046\u611b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u685c\u306f\u77ed\u547d\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3053\u305d\u5c0a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002\u3053\u306e\u77ac\u9593\u3092\u62b1\u304d\u3057\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, ame a beleza do momento ainda mais porque ele passa. A flor de cerejeira \xe9 breve mas, justamente por isso, preciosa; abrace tamb\xe9m este instante.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini imgesel bir meditasyonda canland\u0131r ya da tuzlanm\u0131\u015f sakura \xe7i\xe7e\u011fini geleneksel bir \xe7ay olarak demle. Bahar mevsiminde bir a\u011fac\u0131n alt\u0131nda oturup fark\u0131ndal\u0131k yap.",howToUseEn:"Visualize the blossoms in an imagery meditation, or brew salt-preserved sakura flowers as a traditional tea. Sit beneath a tree in spring and practice mindfulness.",howToUseDe:"Visualisiere die Bl\xfcten in einer Bildmeditation oder br\xfche salzkonservierte Sakura-Bl\xfcten als traditionellen Tee. Sitze im Fr\xfchling unter einem Baum und \xfcbe Achtsamkeit.",howToUseEs:"Visualiza las flores en una meditaci\xf3n de im\xe1genes, o prepara flores de sakura conservadas en sal como un t\xe9 tradicional. Si\xe9ntate bajo un \xe1rbol en primavera y practica la atenci\xf3n plena.",howToUseFr:"Visualise les fleurs dans une m\xe9ditation d'images, ou infuse des fleurs de sakura conserv\xe9es au sel en tisane traditionnelle. Assieds-toi sous un arbre au printemps et pratique la pleine conscience.",howToUseJa:"\u30a4\u30e1\u30fc\u30b8\u7791\u60f3\u3067\u82b1\u3092\u601d\u3044\u63cf\u304f\u304b\u3001\u5869\u6f2c\u3051\u306e\u685c\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u4f1d\u7d71\u7684\u306a\u304a\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6625\u306b\u6728\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u5ea7\u308a\u3001\u6c17\u3065\u304d\u306e\u5b9f\u8df5\u3092\u3002",howToUsePt:"Visualize as flores em uma medita\xe7\xe3o de imagens, ou prepare flores de sakura conservadas em sal como um ch\xe1 tradicional. Sente-se sob uma \xe1rvore na primavera e pratique a aten\xe7\xe3o plena.",affirmation:"\u015eu an\u0131n ge\xe7ici g\xfczelli\u011fini t\xfcm kalbimle kucakl\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I embrace the fleeting beauty of this moment with all my heart.",affirmationDe:"Ich umarme die fl\xfcchtige Sch\xf6nheit dieses Augenblicks von ganzem Herzen.",affirmationEs:"Abrazo la belleza ef\xedmera de este momento con todo mi coraz\xf3n.",affirmationFr:"J'embrasse la beaut\xe9 \xe9ph\xe9m\xe8re de cet instant de tout mon c\u0153ur.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u3053\u306e\u77ac\u9593\u306e\u306f\u304b\u306a\u3044\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u5fc3\u304b\u3089\u62b1\u304d\u3057\u3081\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Abra\xe7o a beleza ef\xeamera deste momento com todo o meu cora\xe7\xe3o.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg/330px-Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg"},{id:"plant-065",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5F8A52",name:"Damiana",nameEn:"Damiana",nameDe:"Damiana",nameEs:"Damiana",nameFr:"Damiana",nameJa:"\u30c0\u30df\u30a2\u30ca",namePt:"Damiana",origin:"Orta Amerika, Meksika",originEn:"Central America, Mexico",originDe:"Mittelamerika, Mexiko",originEs:"Am\xe9rica Central, M\xe9xico",originFr:"Am\xe9rique centrale, Mexique",originJa:"\u4e2d\u592e\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u30fb\u30e1\u30ad\u30b7\u30b3",originPt:"Am\xe9rica Central, M\xe9xico",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u30b5\u30af\u30e9\u30eb\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacral",properties:["ne\u015felendirici","tutku","rahatlat\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["uplifting","passion","relaxing"],propertiesDe:["aufmunternd","Leidenschaft","entspannend"],propertiesEs:["alegrante","pasi\xf3n","relajante"],propertiesFr:["r\xe9jouissant","passion","relaxant"],propertiesJa:["\u9ad8\u63da","\u60c5\u71b1","\u30ea\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30b9"],propertiesPt:["alegrante","paix\xe3o","relaxante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ya\u015fama olan i\u015ftah\u0131n\u0131 yeniden hisset. Damiana geleneksel olarak ne\u015fe ve canl\u0131l\u0131kla an\u0131l\u0131r; k\xfc\xe7\xfck zevkleri kendine \xe7ok g\xf6rme.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, feel your appetite for life again. Damiana is traditionally linked with joy and vitality; don't deny yourself small pleasures.",dailyMessageDe:"Sp\xfcre heute wieder deinen Appetit auf das Leben. Damiana wird traditionell mit Freude und Lebenskraft verbunden; versage dir kleine Freuden nicht.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, vuelve a sentir tu apetito por la vida. La damiana se asocia tradicionalmente con la alegr\xeda y la vitalidad; no te niegues los peque\xf1os placeres.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ressens \xe0 nouveau ton app\xe9tit pour la vie. La damiana est traditionnellement li\xe9e \xe0 la joie et \xe0 la vitalit\xe9 ; ne te prive pas des petits plaisirs.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u3078\u306e\u610f\u6b32\u3092\u518d\u3073\u611f\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30c0\u30df\u30a2\u30ca\u306f\u4f1d\u7d71\u7684\u306b\u559c\u3073\u3068\u6d3b\u529b\u306b\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u697d\u3057\u307f\u3092\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u7981\u3058\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, sinta novamente o seu apetite pela vida. A damiana est\xe1 tradicionalmente ligada \xe0 alegria e \xe0 vitalidade; n\xe3o negue a si mesmo os pequenos prazeres.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle, ak\u015famlar\u0131 rahatlamak i\xe7in i\xe7. Az miktarda, \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc kullan; hamilelikte kullanma.",howToUseEn:"Lightly brew the leaves as a tea and drink in the evenings to relax. Use in small, moderate amounts; avoid during pregnancy.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter leicht als Tee und trinke ihn abends zum Entspannen. Verwende in kleinen, ma\xdfvollen Mengen; meide ihn in der Schwangerschaft.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona ligeramente las hojas como t\xe9 y bebe por las noches para relajarte. \xdasala en cantidades peque\xf1as y moderadas; ev\xedtala durante el embarazo.",howToUseFr:"Infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les feuilles en tisane et bois le soir pour te d\xe9tendre. Utilise de petites quantit\xe9s mod\xe9r\xe9es ; \xe9vite-la pendant la grossesse.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u591c\u306b\u304f\u3064\u308d\u3050\u305f\u3081\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5c11\u91cf\u3092\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306b\u3002\u598a\u5a20\u4e2d\u306f\u4f7f\u308f\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare levemente as folhas como ch\xe1 e beba \xe0 noite para relaxar. Use em quantidades pequenas e moderadas; evite durante a gravidez.",affirmation:"Ya\u015fama olan i\u015ftah\u0131m\u0131 kucakl\u0131yorum, k\xfc\xe7\xfck zevklere izin veriyorum.",affirmationEn:"I embrace my appetite for life and allow myself small pleasures.",affirmationDe:"Ich umarme meinen Appetit auf das Leben und g\xf6nne mir kleine Freuden.",affirmationEs:"Abrazo mi apetito por la vida y me permito peque\xf1os placeres.",affirmationFr:"J'embrasse mon app\xe9tit pour la vie et m'autorise de petits plaisirs.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u3078\u306e\u610f\u6b32\u3092\u62b1\u304d\u3057\u3081\u3001\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u697d\u3057\u307f\u3092\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u8a31\u3059\u3002",affirmationPt:"Abra\xe7o o meu apetite pela vida e permito a mim mesmo pequenos prazeres.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Turnera_diffusa_var._aphrodisiaca_002.JPG/330px-Turnera_diffusa_var._aphrodisiaca_002.JPG"},{id:"plant-066",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#6B8E5C",name:"Kava Kava",nameEn:"Kava",nameDe:"Kava",nameEs:"Kava",nameFr:"Kava",nameJa:"\u30ab\u30f4\u30a1",namePt:"Kava",origin:"Pasifik Adalar\u0131",originEn:"Pacific Islands",originDe:"Pazifische Inseln",originEs:"Islas del Pac\xedfico",originFr:"\xceles du Pacifique",originJa:"\u592a\u5e73\u6d0b\u8af8\u5cf6",originPt:"Ilhas do Pac\xedfico",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["rahatlat\u0131c\u0131","topluluk","huzur"],propertiesEn:["relaxing","community","peace"],propertiesDe:["entspannend","Gemeinschaft","Frieden"],propertiesEs:["relajante","comunidad","paz"],propertiesFr:["relaxant","communaut\xe9","paix"],propertiesJa:["\u30ea\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30b9","\u5171\u540c\u4f53","\u5b89\u3089\u304e"],propertiesPt:["relaxante","comunidade","paz"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn gerginli\u011fini bir kenara b\u0131rak ve toplulu\u011fun huzuruna ba\u011flan. Kava Pasifik k\xfclt\xfcrlerinde payla\u015f\u0131lan bir bar\u0131\u015f i\xe7ece\u011fidir; dinlenmeye izin ver.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, set your tension aside and connect to the peace of community. Kava is a shared drink of peace in Pacific cultures; allow yourself to rest.",dailyMessageDe:"Lege heute deine Anspannung beiseite und verbinde dich mit dem Frieden der Gemeinschaft. Kava ist in pazifischen Kulturen ein geteiltes Friedensgetr\xe4nk; erlaube dir zu ruhen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, deja a un lado tu tensi\xf3n y con\xe9ctate con la paz de la comunidad. La kava es una bebida de paz compartida en las culturas del Pac\xedfico; perm\xedtete descansar.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, mets ta tension de c\xf4t\xe9 et relie-toi \xe0 la paix de la communaut\xe9. Le kava est une boisson de paix partag\xe9e dans les cultures du Pacifique ; autorise-toi \xe0 te reposer.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u7dca\u5f35\u3092\u8107\u306b\u7f6e\u304d\u3001\u5171\u540c\u4f53\u306e\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u306b\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ab\u30f4\u30a1\u306f\u592a\u5e73\u6d0b\u306e\u6587\u5316\u3067\u5206\u3051\u5408\u3046\u5e73\u548c\u306e\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u3002\u4f11\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3092\u8a31\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, deixe a sua tens\xe3o de lado e conecte-se \xe0 paz da comunidade. A kava \xe9 uma bebida de paz compartilhada nas culturas do Pac\xedfico; permita-se descansar.",howToUse:"Geleneksel olarak k\xf6k\xfc ezilip suyla kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131l\u0131r ve payla\u015f\u0131lan bir i\xe7ecek olarak \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc t\xfcketilir. Az miktarda ve dikkatle kullan; uzun s\xfcreli a\u015f\u0131r\u0131 kullan\u0131mdan ka\xe7\u0131n.",howToUseEn:"Traditionally, the root is pounded, mixed with water, and consumed moderately as a shared drink. Use in small amounts and with care; avoid prolonged excessive use.",howToUseDe:"Traditionell wird die Wurzel zersto\xdfen, mit Wasser vermischt und ma\xdfvoll als geteiltes Getr\xe4nk genossen. Verwende kleine Mengen und mit Vorsicht; vermeide langen \xfcberm\xe4\xdfigen Gebrauch.",howToUseEs:"Tradicionalmente, la ra\xedz se machaca, se mezcla con agua y se consume con moderaci\xf3n como bebida compartida. \xdasala en peque\xf1as cantidades y con cuidado; evita el uso excesivo prolongado.",howToUseFr:"Traditionnellement, la racine est pil\xe9e, m\xe9lang\xe9e \xe0 de l'eau et consomm\xe9e mod\xe9r\xe9ment comme boisson partag\xe9e. Utilise de petites quantit\xe9s avec prudence ; \xe9vite un usage excessif prolong\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u4f1d\u7d71\u7684\u306b\u306f\u6839\u3092\u3064\u304d\u3001\u6c34\u3068\u6df7\u305c\u3001\u5206\u3051\u5408\u3046\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u3068\u3057\u3066\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306b\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5c11\u91cf\u3092\u614e\u91cd\u306b\u3002\u9577\u671f\u306e\u904e\u5270\u4f7f\u7528\u306f\u907f\u3051\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",howToUsePt:"Tradicionalmente, a raiz \xe9 socada, misturada com \xe1gua e consumida com modera\xe7\xe3o como bebida compartilhada. Use em pequenas quantidades e com cuidado; evite uso excessivo prolongado.",affirmation:"Gerginli\u011fimi b\u0131rak\u0131yorum, huzura ve birlikteli\u011fe ba\u011flan\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I release my tension and connect to peace and togetherness.",affirmationDe:"Ich lasse meine Anspannung los und verbinde mich mit Frieden und Gemeinschaft.",affirmationEs:"Suelto mi tensi\xf3n y me conecto con la paz y la uni\xf3n.",affirmationFr:"Je lib\xe8re ma tension et me relie \xe0 la paix et \xe0 la communion.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u7dca\u5f35\u3092\u624b\u653e\u3057\u3001\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3068\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a\u306b\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Solto a minha tens\xe3o e me conecto \xe0 paz e \xe0 uni\xe3o.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Starr_070515-7054_Piper_methysticum.jpg/330px-Starr_070515-7054_Piper_methysticum.jpg"},{id:"plant-067",emoji:"\ud83c\udf42",color:"#B5752E",name:"Sar\u0131 K\xf6k (Goldenseal)",nameEn:"Goldenseal",nameDe:"Goldsiegel",nameEs:"Sello de oro",nameFr:"Hydraste",nameJa:"\u30b4\u30fc\u30eb\u30c7\u30f3\u30b7\u30fc\u30eb",namePt:"Hidraste",origin:"Kuzey Amerika",originEn:"North America",originDe:"Nordamerika",originEs:"Am\xe9rica del Norte",originFr:"Am\xe9rique du Nord",originJa:"\u5317\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Am\xe9rica do Norte",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["koruyucu","ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","g\xfc\xe7lendirici"],propertiesEn:["protective","purifying","strengthening"],propertiesDe:["sch\xfctzend","reinigend","st\xe4rkend"],propertiesEs:["protector","purificante","fortalecedor"],propertiesFr:["protecteur","purifiant","fortifiant"],propertiesJa:["\u5b88\u8b77","\u6d44\u5316","\u5f37\u5316"],propertiesPt:["protetor","purificante","fortalecedor"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn do\u011fan\u0131n de\u011ferli ama k\u0131r\u0131lgan arma\u011fanlar\u0131na sayg\u0131 duy. Sar\u0131 k\xf6k nadir bir bitkidir; sen de kendi kaynaklar\u0131n\u0131 koruyarak ve \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc kullanarak de\u011fer ver.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, respect nature's precious but fragile gifts. Goldenseal is a rare plant; honor your own resources too by protecting them and using them with measure.",dailyMessageDe:"Achte heute die kostbaren, aber zerbrechlichen Geschenke der Natur. Goldsiegel ist eine seltene Pflanze; ehre auch deine eigenen Ressourcen, indem du sie sch\xfctzt und ma\xdfvoll nutzt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, respeta los dones preciosos pero fr\xe1giles de la naturaleza. El sello de oro es una planta rara; honra tambi\xe9n tus propios recursos protegi\xe9ndolos y us\xe1ndolos con mesura.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, respecte les dons pr\xe9cieux mais fragiles de la nature. L'hydraste est une plante rare ; honore aussi tes propres ressources en les prot\xe9geant et en les utilisant avec mesure.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u7136\u306e\u8cb4\u91cd\u3060\u304c\u3082\u308d\u3044\u8d08\u308a\u7269\u306b\u656c\u610f\u3092\u6255\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b4\u30fc\u30eb\u30c7\u30f3\u30b7\u30fc\u30eb\u306f\u5e0c\u5c11\u306a\u690d\u7269\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u8cc7\u6e90\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3001\u307b\u3069\u3088\u304f\u4f7f\u3063\u3066\u5927\u5207\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, respeite os dons preciosos mas fr\xe1geis da natureza. O hidraste \xe9 uma planta rara; honre tamb\xe9m os seus pr\xf3prios recursos protegendo-os e usando-os com medida.",howToUse:"Geleneksel olarak k\xf6k\xfc \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc ve k\u0131sa s\xfcreli kullan\u0131l\u0131r; bitki nadir oldu\u011fu i\xe7in etik kaynakl\u0131 tercih edilmelidir. Hamilelikte kullanma; kullanmadan \xf6nce uzmana dan\u0131\u015f.",howToUseEn:"Traditionally, the root is used sparingly and for short periods; because the plant is rare, choose ethically sourced ones. Avoid during pregnancy; consult a professional before use.",howToUseDe:"Traditionell wird die Wurzel sparsam und kurzzeitig verwendet; da die Pflanze selten ist, w\xe4hle ethisch gewonnene. Meide sie in der Schwangerschaft; frage vor der Anwendung eine Fachperson.",howToUseEs:"Tradicionalmente, la ra\xedz se usa con moderaci\xf3n y por periodos cortos; como la planta es rara, elige las de origen \xe9tico. Ev\xedtala durante el embarazo; consulta a un profesional antes de usarla.",howToUseFr:"Traditionnellement, la racine s'utilise avec parcimonie et sur de courtes p\xe9riodes ; comme la plante est rare, choisis une source \xe9thique. \xc9vite-la pendant la grossesse ; consulte un professionnel avant usage.",howToUseJa:"\u4f1d\u7d71\u7684\u306b\u6839\u306f\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306b\u3001\u77ed\u671f\u9593\u4f7f\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5e0c\u5c11\u306a\u690d\u7269\u306a\u306e\u3067\u3001\u502b\u7406\u7684\u306b\u63a1\u53d6\u3055\u308c\u305f\u3082\u306e\u3092\u9078\u3073\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u598a\u5a20\u4e2d\u306f\u4f7f\u308f\u305a\u3001\u4f7f\u7528\u524d\u306b\u5c02\u9580\u5bb6\u306b\u76f8\u8ac7\u3092\u3002",howToUsePt:"Tradicionalmente, a raiz \xe9 usada com modera\xe7\xe3o e por curtos per\xedodos; como a planta \xe9 rara, escolha as de origem \xe9tica. Evite durante a gravidez; consulte um profissional antes de usar.",affirmation:"De\u011ferli kaynaklar\u0131m\u0131 koruyor, onlar\u0131 sayg\u0131yla kullan\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I protect my precious resources and use them with respect.",affirmationDe:"Ich sch\xfctze meine kostbaren Ressourcen und nutze sie mit Respekt.",affirmationEs:"Protejo mis recursos preciosos y los uso con respeto.",affirmationFr:"Je prot\xe8ge mes ressources pr\xe9cieuses et les utilise avec respect.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u8cb4\u91cd\u306a\u8cc7\u6e90\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3001\u656c\u610f\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u4f7f\u3046\u3002",affirmationPt:"Protejo os meus recursos preciosos e os uso com respeito.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Hydrastis_canadensis.jpg/330px-Hydrastis_canadensis.jpg"},{id:"plant-068",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#7A9A5E",name:"Gotu Kola",nameEn:"Gotu Kola",nameDe:"Gotu Kola",nameEs:"Gotu Kola",nameFr:"Gotu Kola",nameJa:"\u30b4\u30c4\u30b3\u30e9",namePt:"Gotu Kola",origin:"Asya, sulak alanlar",originEn:"Asia, wetlands",originDe:"Asien, Feuchtgebiete",originEs:"Asia, humedales",originFr:"Asie, zones humides",originJa:"\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u30fb\u6e7f\u5730",originPt:"\xc1sia, \xe1reas \xfamidas",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["zihin a\xe7\u0131c\u0131","sakinle\u015ftirici","denge"],propertiesEn:["mind-clearing","calming","balance"],propertiesDe:["geistkl\xe4rend","beruhigend","Gleichgewicht"],propertiesEs:["aclara la mente","calmante","equilibrio"],propertiesFr:["clarifie l'esprit","apaisant","\xe9quilibre"],propertiesJa:["\u5fc3\u3092\u6f84\u307e\u3059","\u93ae\u9759","\u5747\u8861"],propertiesPt:["clareia a mente","calmante","equil\xedbrio"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn zihnini hem sakin hem berrak tut. Gotu kola Ayurveda ve meditasyon geleneklerinde 'd\xfc\u015f\xfcnce otu' olarak an\u0131l\u0131r; i\xe7 dengeni koru.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, keep your mind both calm and clear. Gotu kola is known as the 'herb of thought' in Ayurvedic and meditative traditions; keep your inner balance.",dailyMessageDe:"Halte heute deinen Geist ruhig und klar zugleich. Gotu Kola gilt in ayurvedischen und meditativen Traditionen als 'Kraut des Denkens'; bewahre dein inneres Gleichgewicht.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, mant\xe9n tu mente serena y clara a la vez. La gotu kola es conocida como la 'hierba del pensamiento' en las tradiciones ayurv\xe9dicas y meditativas; conserva tu equilibrio interior.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, garde ton esprit \xe0 la fois calme et clair. Le gotu kola est connu comme 'l'herbe de la pens\xe9e' dans les traditions ayurv\xe9diques et m\xe9ditatives ; pr\xe9serve ton \xe9quilibre int\xe9rieur.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5fc3\u3092\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u3067\u3042\u308a\u306a\u304c\u3089\u6f84\u307e\u305b\u3066\u304a\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b4\u30c4\u30b3\u30e9\u306f\u30a2\u30fc\u30e6\u30eb\u30f4\u30a7\u30fc\u30c0\u3084\u7791\u60f3\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71\u3067\u300c\u601d\u8003\u306e\u8349\u300d\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5185\u306a\u308b\u5747\u8861\u3092\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, mantenha a sua mente calma e clara ao mesmo tempo. A gotu kola \xe9 conhecida como a 'erva do pensamento' nas tradi\xe7\xf5es ayurv\xe9dicas e meditativas; preserve o seu equil\xedbrio interior.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle ya da taze yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 salataya ekle. D\xfczenli, \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc kullanarak zihinsel berrakl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 destekle.",howToUseEn:"Lightly brew the leaves as a tea, or add fresh leaves to salads. Support your mental clarity with regular, moderate use.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter leicht als Tee oder gib frische Bl\xe4tter in Salate. Unterst\xfctze deine geistige Klarheit durch regelm\xe4\xdfigen, ma\xdfvollen Gebrauch.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona ligeramente las hojas como t\xe9, o a\xf1ade hojas frescas a las ensaladas. Apoya tu claridad mental con un uso regular y moderado.",howToUseFr:"Infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les feuilles en tisane, ou ajoute des feuilles fra\xeeches aux salades. Soutiens ta clart\xe9 mentale par un usage r\xe9gulier et mod\xe9r\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u8449\u3092\u30b5\u30e9\u30c0\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5b9a\u671f\u7684\u3067\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306e\u4f7f\u7528\u3067\u7cbe\u795e\u306e\u660e\u6670\u3055\u3092\u652f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare levemente as folhas como ch\xe1, ou adicione folhas frescas a saladas. Apoie a sua clareza mental com uso regular e moderado.",affirmation:"Zihnim hem sakin hem berrak, i\xe7 dengemdeyim.",affirmationEn:"My mind is both calm and clear; I am in inner balance.",affirmationDe:"Mein Geist ist ruhig und klar zugleich; ich bin im inneren Gleichgewicht.",affirmationEs:"Mi mente est\xe1 serena y clara; estoy en equilibrio interior.",affirmationFr:"Mon esprit est \xe0 la fois calme et clair ; je suis en \xe9quilibre int\xe9rieur.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u3067\u6f84\u3093\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u5747\u8861\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Minha mente est\xe1 calma e clara; estou em equil\xedbrio interior.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Centella_asiatica_%28%E0%A6%A5%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%95%E0%A7%81%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%BF%29_%283%29.jpg/330px-Centella_asiatica_%28%E0%A6%A5%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%95%E0%A7%81%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%BF%29_%283%29.jpg"},{id:"plant-069",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3a",color:"#C76B92",name:"Mavi Lotus",nameEn:"Blue Lotus",nameDe:"Blauer Lotus",nameEs:"Loto Azul",nameFr:"Lotus Bleu",nameJa:"\u9752\u3044\u7761\u84ee",namePt:"L\xf3tus Azul",origin:"M\u0131s\u0131r, Nil Vadisi",originEn:"Egypt, Nile Valley",originDe:"\xc4gypten, Niltal",originEs:"Egipto, Valle del Nilo",originFr:"\xc9gypte, vall\xe9e du Nil",originJa:"\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u30fb\u30ca\u30a4\u30eb\u6e13\u8c37",originPt:"Egito, Vale do Nilo",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["sezgi","huzur","kutsal"],propertiesEn:["intuition","serenity","sacred"],propertiesDe:["Intuition","Gelassenheit","heilig"],propertiesEs:["intuici\xf3n","serenidad","sagrado"],propertiesFr:["intuition","s\xe9r\xe9nit\xe9","sacr\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u76f4\u611f","\u9759\u3051\u3055","\u8056\u306a\u308b"],propertiesPt:["intui\xe7\xe3o","serenidade","sagrado"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn i\xe7sel sezgine ve r\xfcyalar\u0131na sayg\u0131yla kulak ver. Mavi lotus antik M\u0131s\u0131r'da kutsal bir \xe7i\xe7ekti; sana sakin bir derinlik ve i\xe7sel uyan\u0131\u015f hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, listen with respect to your inner intuition and your dreams. Blue lotus was a sacred flower in ancient Egypt; it reminds you of a calm depth and an inner awakening.",dailyMessageDe:"H\xf6re heute respektvoll auf deine innere Intuition und deine Tr\xe4ume. Der blaue Lotus war im alten \xc4gypten eine heilige Blume; er erinnert dich an eine ruhige Tiefe und ein inneres Erwachen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, escucha con respeto tu intuici\xf3n interior y tus sue\xf1os. El loto azul era una flor sagrada en el antiguo Egipto; te recuerda una profundidad serena y un despertar interior.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, \xe9coute avec respect ton intuition int\xe9rieure et tes r\xeaves. Le lotus bleu \xe9tait une fleur sacr\xe9e dans l'\xc9gypte antique ; il te rappelle une profondeur calme et un \xe9veil int\xe9rieur.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5185\u306a\u308b\u76f4\u611f\u3068\u5922\u306b\u656c\u610f\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u8033\u3092\u50be\u3051\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u9752\u3044\u7761\u84ee\u306f\u53e4\u4ee3\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u82b1\u3002\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u6df1\u307f\u3068\u5185\u306a\u308b\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, escute com respeito a sua intui\xe7\xe3o interior e os seus sonhos. O l\xf3tus azul era uma flor sagrada no antigo Egito; lembra voc\xea de uma profundidade calma e de um despertar interior.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f \xe7i\xe7eklerini \xe7ay olarak \xe7ok hafif demle ya da imgesini meditasyonda canland\u0131r. Sakin bir ak\u015fam rit\xfceli olarak \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc kullan.",howToUseEn:"Brew the dried flowers very lightly as a tea, or visualize its image in meditation. Use it sparingly as a calm evening ritual.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die getrockneten Bl\xfcten sehr leicht als Tee oder visualisiere ihr Bild in der Meditation. Verwende ihn sparsam als ruhiges Abendritual.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las flores secas muy ligeramente como t\xe9, o visualiza su imagen en meditaci\xf3n. \xdasalo con moderaci\xf3n como un sereno ritual nocturno.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les fleurs s\xe9ch\xe9es tr\xe8s l\xe9g\xe8rement en tisane, ou visualise son image en m\xe9ditation. Utilise-le avec mod\xe9ration comme un rituel du soir apaisant.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u82b1\u3092\u3054\u304f\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u305d\u306e\u59ff\u3092\u7791\u60f3\u3067\u601d\u3044\u63cf\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u591c\u306e\u5100\u5f0f\u3068\u3057\u3066\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306b\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as flores secas bem levemente como ch\xe1, ou visualize a imagem dela na medita\xe7\xe3o. Use com modera\xe7\xe3o como um sereno ritual noturno.",affirmation:"Sezgime ve r\xfcyalar\u0131ma sayg\u0131yla kulak veriyorum.",affirmationEn:"I listen with respect to my intuition and my dreams.",affirmationDe:"Ich h\xf6re respektvoll auf meine Intuition und meine Tr\xe4ume.",affirmationEs:"Escucho con respeto mi intuici\xf3n y mis sue\xf1os.",affirmationFr:"J'\xe9coute avec respect mon intuition et mes r\xeaves.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u76f4\u611f\u3068\u5922\u306b\u656c\u610f\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u8033\u3092\u50be\u3051\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Escuto com respeito a minha intui\xe7\xe3o e os meus sonhos.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Nymphaea_caerulea_Flower.JPG/330px-Nymphaea_caerulea_Flower.JPG"},{id:"plant-070",emoji:"\ud83c\udf32",color:"#3F6B4E",name:"Ard\u0131\xe7",nameEn:"Juniper",nameDe:"Wacholder",nameEs:"Enebro",nameFr:"Gen\xe9vrier",nameJa:"\u30b8\u30e5\u30cb\u30d1\u30fc",namePt:"Zimbro",origin:"Kuzey Yar\u0131mk\xfcre",originEn:"Northern Hemisphere",originDe:"Nordhalbkugel",originEs:"Hemisferio norte",originFr:"H\xe9misph\xe8re nord",originJa:"\u5317\u534a\u7403",originPt:"Hemisf\xe9rio Norte",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","koruyucu","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["purifying","protective","resilience"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","sch\xfctzend","Widerstandskraft"],propertiesEs:["purificante","protector","resiliencia"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","protecteur","r\xe9silience"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u5b88\u8b77","\u56de\u5fa9\u529b"],propertiesPt:["purificante","protetor","resili\xeancia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn sert ko\u015fullarda bile dimdik durabilece\u011fini hat\u0131rla. Ard\u0131\xe7 \xe7orak da\u011flarda y\xfczy\u0131llarca ya\u015far; sen de zorlu zeminlerde k\xf6klerini sa\u011flam tut.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that you can stand tall even in harsh conditions. Juniper lives for centuries on barren mountains; keep your roots firm on difficult ground too.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass du selbst unter harten Bedingungen aufrecht stehen kannst. Wacholder lebt jahrhundertelang auf kargen Bergen; halte auch auf schwierigem Boden deine Wurzeln fest.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que puedes mantenerte firme incluso en condiciones duras. El enebro vive siglos en monta\xf1as \xe1ridas; mant\xe9n tambi\xe9n firmes tus ra\xedces en terreno dif\xedcil.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que tu peux te tenir droit m\xeame dans des conditions rudes. Le gen\xe9vrier vit des si\xe8cles sur des montagnes arides ; garde aussi tes racines solides sur un sol difficile.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u53b3\u3057\u3044\u72b6\u6cc1\u3067\u3082\u5802\u3005\u3068\u7acb\u3066\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b8\u30e5\u30cb\u30d1\u30fc\u306f\u4e0d\u6bdb\u306e\u5c71\u3067\u4f55\u4e16\u7d00\u3082\u751f\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u96e3\u3057\u3044\u5730\u9762\u3067\u6839\u3092\u3057\u3063\u304b\u308a\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que voc\xea pode se manter firme mesmo em condi\xe7\xf5es dif\xedceis. O zimbro vive s\xe9culos em montanhas \xe1ridas; mantenha tamb\xe9m as suas ra\xedzes firmes em terreno dif\xedcil.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f dallar\u0131n\u0131 t\xfcts\xfc olarak yakarak mek\xe2n\u0131n\u0131 ar\u0131nd\u0131r ya da meyvelerini \xe7ok az miktarda \xe7aya kat. Meyveleri g\xfc\xe7l\xfcd\xfcr; hamilelikte kullanma.",howToUseEn:"Burn the dried branches as incense to purify your space, or add a very small amount of the berries to tea. The berries are potent; avoid during pregnancy.",howToUseDe:"Verbrenne die getrockneten Zweige als R\xe4ucherwerk, um deinen Raum zu reinigen, oder gib eine sehr kleine Menge der Beeren in den Tee. Die Beeren sind kr\xe4ftig; meide sie in der Schwangerschaft.",howToUseEs:"Quema las ramas secas como incienso para purificar tu espacio, o a\xf1ade una cantidad muy peque\xf1a de las bayas al t\xe9. Las bayas son potentes; ev\xedtalas durante el embarazo.",howToUseFr:"Br\xfble les branches s\xe9ch\xe9es en encens pour purifier ton espace, ou ajoute une tr\xe8s petite quantit\xe9 de baies au th\xe9. Les baies sont puissantes ; \xe9vite-les pendant la grossesse.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u679d\u3092\u304a\u9999\u3068\u3057\u3066\u711a\u3044\u3066\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u6d44\u5316\u3059\u308b\u304b\u3001\u5b9f\u3092\u3054\u304f\u5c11\u91cf\u304a\u8336\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5b9f\u306f\u4f5c\u7528\u304c\u5f37\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u598a\u5a20\u4e2d\u306f\u4f7f\u308f\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3002",howToUsePt:"Queime os galhos secos como incenso para purificar o seu espa\xe7o, ou adicione uma quantidade muito pequena das bagas ao ch\xe1. As bagas s\xe3o potentes; evite durante a gravidez.",affirmation:"Zorlu zeminlerde bile k\xf6klerim sa\u011flam, dimdik duruyorum.",affirmationEn:"Even on difficult ground my roots are firm; I stand tall.",affirmationDe:"Selbst auf schwierigem Boden sind meine Wurzeln fest; ich stehe aufrecht.",affirmationEs:"Incluso en terreno dif\xedcil mis ra\xedces son firmes; me mantengo erguido.",affirmationFr:"M\xeame sur un sol difficile mes racines sont solides ; je me tiens droit.",affirmationJa:"\u96e3\u3057\u3044\u5730\u9762\u3067\u3082\u79c1\u306e\u6839\u306f\u56fa\u3044\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u5802\u3005\u3068\u7acb\u3064\u3002",affirmationPt:"Mesmo em terreno dif\xedcil minhas ra\xedzes s\xe3o firmes; mantenho-me ereto.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Juniperus_osteosperma_1.jpg/330px-Juniperus_osteosperma_1.jpg"},{id:"plant-071",emoji:"\ud83c\udf32",color:"#356B52",name:"K\xf6knar (\xc7am)",nameEn:"Pine",nameDe:"Kiefer",nameEs:"Pino",nameFr:"Pin",nameJa:"\u677e",namePt:"Pinheiro",origin:"Kuzey Yar\u0131mk\xfcre",originEn:"Northern Hemisphere",originDe:"Nordhalbkugel",originEs:"Hemisferio norte",originFr:"H\xe9misph\xe8re nord",originJa:"\u5317\u534a\u7403",originPt:"Hemisf\xe9rio Norte",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k","ferahl\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["purifying","endurance","freshness"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","Ausdauer","Frische"],propertiesEs:["purificante","resistencia","frescura"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","endurance","fra\xeecheur"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u8010\u4e45","\u6e05\u6dbc"],propertiesPt:["purificante","resist\xeancia","frescor"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn k\u0131\u015f\u0131n ortas\u0131nda bile ye\u015fil kalabilece\u011fini hat\u0131rla. \xc7am d\xf6rt mevsim canl\u0131d\u0131r; sen de zorluklar boyunca i\xe7sel canl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 koru.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that you can stay green even in the heart of winter. Pine is alive through all four seasons; keep your inner vitality through hardship too.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass du selbst im tiefsten Winter gr\xfcn bleiben kannst. Die Kiefer ist durch alle vier Jahreszeiten lebendig; bewahre auch in Schwierigkeiten deine innere Lebendigkeit.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que puedes seguir verde incluso en pleno invierno. El pino est\xe1 vivo en las cuatro estaciones; conserva tambi\xe9n tu vitalidad interior en la dificultad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que tu peux rester vert m\xeame au c\u0153ur de l'hiver. Le pin est vivant aux quatre saisons ; garde aussi ta vitalit\xe9 int\xe9rieure \xe0 travers les \xe9preuves.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u771f\u51ac\u3067\u3082\u7dd1\u3067\u3044\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u677e\u306f\u56db\u5b63\u3092\u901a\u3058\u3066\u751f\u304d\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u56f0\u96e3\u306e\u9593\u3082\u5185\u306a\u308b\u751f\u547d\u529b\u3092\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que voc\xea pode permanecer verde mesmo no auge do inverno. O pinheiro est\xe1 vivo nas quatro esta\xe7\xf5es; mantenha tamb\xe9m a sua vitalidade interior atrav\xe9s das dificuldades.",howToUse:"Taze i\u011fne yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 C vitamini a\xe7\u0131s\u0131ndan zengin bir \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle. Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ya da dallar\u0131n\u0131 ferahlat\u0131c\u0131 bir orman kokusu i\xe7in evinde kullan.",howToUseEn:"Lightly brew the fresh needles as a vitamin-C-rich tea. Use the essential oil or branches at home for a refreshing forest scent.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die frischen Nadeln leicht als vitamin-C-reichen Tee. Verwende das \xe4therische \xd6l oder die Zweige zu Hause f\xfcr einen erfrischenden Walddurft.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona ligeramente las agujas frescas como un t\xe9 rico en vitamina C. Usa el aceite esencial o las ramas en casa para un refrescante aroma a bosque.",howToUseFr:"Infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les aiguilles fra\xeeches en tisane riche en vitamine C. Utilise l'huile essentielle ou les branches chez toi pour un parfum de for\xeat rafra\xeechissant.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u91dd\u8449\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u30d3\u30bf\u30df\u30f3C\u8c4a\u5bcc\u306a\u304a\u8336\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3084\u679d\u3092\u5bb6\u3067\u4f7f\u3044\u3001\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u68ee\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306b\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare levemente as agulhas frescas como um ch\xe1 rico em vitamina C. Use o \xf3leo essencial ou os galhos em casa para um refrescante aroma de floresta.",affirmation:"Zorluklar boyunca i\xe7sel canl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131m\u0131 ye\u015fil tutuyorum.",affirmationEn:"I keep my inner vitality green through hardship.",affirmationDe:"Ich halte meine innere Lebendigkeit durch Schwierigkeiten gr\xfcn.",affirmationEs:"Mantengo verde mi vitalidad interior a trav\xe9s de la dificultad.",affirmationFr:"Je garde verte ma vitalit\xe9 int\xe9rieure \xe0 travers les \xe9preuves.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u56f0\u96e3\u306e\u9593\u3082\u5185\u306a\u308b\u751f\u547d\u529b\u3092\u7dd1\u306b\u4fdd\u3064\u3002",affirmationPt:"Mantenho verde a minha vitalidade interior atrav\xe9s das dificuldades.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Pinus_jeffreyi_at_Lassen_Volcanic_National_Park.jpg/330px-Pinus_jeffreyi_at_Lassen_Volcanic_National_Park.jpg"},{id:"plant-072",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#728F50",name:"Maydanoz",nameEn:"Parsley",nameDe:"Petersilie",nameEs:"Perejil",nameFr:"Persil",nameJa:"\u30d1\u30bb\u30ea",namePt:"Salsa",origin:"Akdeniz",originEn:"Mediterranean",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u5730\u57df",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","yenilenme"],propertiesEn:["purifying","invigorating","renewal"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","belebend","Erneuerung"],propertiesEs:["purificante","vigorizante","renovaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","tonifiant","renouveau"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u6d3b\u6027","\u518d\u751f"],propertiesPt:["purificante","revigorante","renova\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn s\u0131radan, al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfc olan\u0131n de\u011ferini g\xf6r. Maydanoz m\xfctevaz\u0131 bir bitkidir ama tazeli\u011fiyle her sofraya canl\u0131l\u0131k katar; sen de sade katk\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131 k\xfc\xe7\xfcmseme.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, see the value of the ordinary and humble. Parsley is a modest plant, yet its freshness brings life to every table; don't underestimate your simple contributions.",dailyMessageDe:"Erkenne heute den Wert des Gew\xf6hnlichen und Bescheidenen. Petersilie ist eine bescheidene Pflanze, doch ihre Frische bringt Leben auf jeden Tisch; untersch\xe4tze deine einfachen Beitr\xe4ge nicht.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ve el valor de lo ordinario y humilde. El perejil es una planta modesta, pero su frescura da vida a cada mesa; no subestimes tus aportes sencillos.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, vois la valeur de l'ordinaire et de l'humble. Le persil est une plante modeste, mais sa fra\xeecheur donne vie \xe0 chaque table ; ne sous-estime pas tes apports simples.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3042\u308a\u3075\u308c\u3066\u614e\u307e\u3057\u3044\u3082\u306e\u306e\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u898b\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d1\u30bb\u30ea\u306f\u63a7\u3048\u3081\u306a\u690d\u7269\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u65b0\u9bae\u3055\u304c\u3069\u306e\u98df\u5353\u306b\u3082\u6d3b\u6c17\u3092\u6dfb\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u7d20\u6734\u306a\u8ca2\u732e\u3092\u4fae\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, veja o valor do comum e do humilde. A salsa \xe9 uma planta modesta, mas o seu frescor d\xe1 vida a cada mesa; n\xe3o subestime as suas contribui\xe7\xf5es simples.",howToUse:"Taze yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 yemeklerine bolca ekleyerek tazeli\u011finden yararlan. Bir tutam\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak demleyip hafif, ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131 bir i\xe7ecek olarak i\xe7.",howToUseEn:"Add fresh leaves generously to your meals to enjoy their freshness. Brew a small handful as a tea for a light, purifying drink.",howToUseDe:"Gib frische Bl\xe4tter gro\xdfz\xfcgig in deine Mahlzeiten, um ihre Frische zu genie\xdfen. Br\xfche eine kleine Handvoll als Tee f\xfcr ein leichtes, reinigendes Getr\xe4nk.",howToUseEs:"A\xf1ade hojas frescas en abundancia a tus comidas para disfrutar su frescura. Infusiona un pu\xf1ado peque\xf1o como t\xe9 para una bebida ligera y purificante.",howToUseFr:"Ajoute g\xe9n\xe9reusement des feuilles fra\xeeches \xe0 tes plats pour profiter de leur fra\xeecheur. Infuse une petite poign\xe9e en tisane pour une boisson l\xe9g\xe8re et purifiante.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u8449\u3092\u305f\u3063\u3077\u308a\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3001\u305d\u306e\u65b0\u9bae\u3055\u3092\u697d\u3057\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u8efd\u304f\u6d44\u5316\u3059\u308b\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u306b\u3002",howToUsePt:"Adicione folhas frescas generosamente \xe0s refei\xe7\xf5es para aproveitar o frescor. Prepare um pequeno punhado como ch\xe1 para uma bebida leve e purificante.",affirmation:"Sade katk\u0131lar\u0131m\u0131n de\u011ferini g\xf6r\xfcyorum, tazeli\u011fimle \xe7evreme canl\u0131l\u0131k kat\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I see the value of my simple contributions; my freshness brings life to those around me.",affirmationDe:"Ich sehe den Wert meiner einfachen Beitr\xe4ge; meine Frische bringt Leben in meine Umgebung.",affirmationEs:"Veo el valor de mis aportes sencillos; mi frescura da vida a quienes me rodean.",affirmationFr:"Je vois la valeur de mes apports simples ; ma fra\xeecheur donne vie \xe0 mon entourage.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u7d20\u6734\u306a\u8ca2\u732e\u306e\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u898b\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u65b0\u9bae\u3055\u304c\u5468\u308a\u306b\u6d3b\u6c17\u3092\u6dfb\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Vejo o valor das minhas contribui\xe7\xf5es simples; o meu frescor d\xe1 vida a quem est\xe1 \xe0 minha volta.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Petroselinum.jpg/330px-Petroselinum.jpg"},{id:"plant-073",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#7C9A4E",name:"Limon Keki\u011fi",nameEn:"Lemon Thyme",nameDe:"Zitronenthymian",nameEs:"Tomillo limonero",nameFr:"Thym citron",nameJa:"\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30bf\u30a4\u30e0",namePt:"Tomilho-lim\xe3o",origin:"Akdeniz",originEn:"Mediterranean",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u5730\u57df",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Lar\xedngeo",properties:["ferahlat\u0131c\u0131","g\xfc\xe7 veren","ne\u015fe"],propertiesEn:["refreshing","strengthening","joy"],propertiesDe:["erfrischend","st\xe4rkend","Freude"],propertiesEs:["refrescante","fortalecedor","alegr\xeda"],propertiesFr:["rafra\xeechissant","fortifiant","joie"],propertiesJa:["\u723d\u5feb","\u5f37\u5316","\u559c\u3073"],propertiesPt:["refrescante","fortalecedor","alegria"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xfcc\xfcnle ne\u015feyi bir araya getir. Limon keki\u011fi hem keki\u011fin direncini hem limonun ferahl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131r; sen de hem sa\u011flam hem hafif olabilirsin.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, bring strength and joy together. Lemon thyme carries both thyme's resilience and lemon's freshness; you too can be both solid and light.",dailyMessageDe:"Bringe heute St\xe4rke und Freude zusammen. Zitronenthymian tr\xe4gt sowohl die Widerstandskraft des Thymians als auch die Frische der Zitrone; auch du kannst zugleich fest und leicht sein.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, une la fuerza y la alegr\xeda. El tomillo limonero lleva tanto la resiliencia del tomillo como la frescura del lim\xf3n; t\xfa tambi\xe9n puedes ser firme y ligero a la vez.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, r\xe9unis la force et la joie. Le thym citron porte \xe0 la fois la r\xe9silience du thym et la fra\xeecheur du citron ; toi aussi tu peux \xeatre \xe0 la fois solide et l\xe9ger.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u529b\u3068\u559c\u3073\u3092\u4e00\u3064\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30bf\u30a4\u30e0\u306f\u30bf\u30a4\u30e0\u306e\u56de\u5fa9\u529b\u3068\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u306e\u6e05\u6dbc\u3055\u3092\u4f75\u305b\u6301\u3061\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u5805\u5b9f\u3067\u3042\u308a\u306a\u304c\u3089\u8efd\u3084\u304b\u3067\u3044\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, una a for\xe7a e a alegria. O tomilho-lim\xe3o carrega tanto a resili\xeancia do tomilho quanto o frescor do lim\xe3o; voc\xea tamb\xe9m pode ser firme e leve ao mesmo tempo.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131cak suda demleyip ferahlat\u0131c\u0131 ve g\xfc\xe7 verici bir \xe7ay olarak i\xe7. Yemeklerine ekleyerek limonsu bir aroma kat.",howToUseEn:"Brew the leaves in hot water for a refreshing and strengthening tea. Add it to your meals for a lemony aroma.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter in hei\xdfem Wasser f\xfcr einen erfrischenden und st\xe4rkenden Tee. Gib sie f\xfcr ein zitroniges Aroma in deine Mahlzeiten.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las hojas en agua caliente para un t\xe9 refrescante y fortalecedor. A\xf1\xe1delo a tus comidas para un aroma alimonado.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les feuilles dans de l'eau chaude pour une tisane rafra\xeechissante et fortifiante. Ajoute-le \xe0 tes plats pour un ar\xf4me citronn\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u6e6f\u3067\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u3067\u529b\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u308b\u304a\u8336\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3066\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306a\u9999\u308a\u3092\u6dfb\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as folhas em \xe1gua quente para um ch\xe1 refrescante e fortalecedor. Adicione \xe0s refei\xe7\xf5es para um aroma c\xedtrico.",affirmation:"Hem sa\u011flam hem hafifim; g\xfcc\xfcm\xfc ne\u015feyle birle\u015ftiriyorum.",affirmationEn:"I am both solid and light; I unite my strength with joy.",affirmationDe:"Ich bin zugleich fest und leicht; ich vereine meine St\xe4rke mit Freude.",affirmationEs:"Soy firme y ligero a la vez; uno mi fuerza con la alegr\xeda.",affirmationFr:"Je suis \xe0 la fois solide et l\xe9ger ; j'unis ma force \xe0 la joie.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5805\u5b9f\u3067\u8efd\u3084\u304b\u3002\u529b\u3092\u559c\u3073\u3068\u7d50\u3076\u3002",affirmationPt:"Sou firme e leve ao mesmo tempo; uno a minha for\xe7a \xe0 alegria.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Starr_070906-8846_Thymus_citriodorus.jpg/330px-Starr_070906-8846_Thymus_citriodorus.jpg"},{id:"plant-074",emoji:"\ud83d\udc90",color:"#B97FB0",name:"Leylak",nameEn:"Lilac",nameDe:"Flieder",nameEs:"Lila",nameFr:"Lilas",nameJa:"\u30e9\u30a4\u30e9\u30c3\u30af",namePt:"Lil\xe1s",origin:"Balkanlar, Do\u011fu Avrupa",originEn:"Balkans, Eastern Europe",originDe:"Balkan, Osteuropa",originEs:"Balcanes, Europa del Este",originFr:"Balkans, Europe de l'Est",originJa:"\u30d0\u30eb\u30ab\u30f3\u30fb\u6771\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1",originPt:"B\xe1lc\xe3s, Europa Oriental",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["nostalji","masumiyet","yenilenme"],propertiesEn:["nostalgia","innocence","renewal"],propertiesDe:["Nostalgie","Unschuld","Erneuerung"],propertiesEs:["nostalgia","inocencia","renovaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["nostalgie","innocence","renouveau"],propertiesJa:["\u90f7\u6101","\u7121\u57a2","\u518d\u751f"],propertiesPt:["nostalgia","inoc\xeancia","renova\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ilk a\u015fklar\u0131n ve tatl\u0131 an\u0131lar\u0131n masumiyetini hat\u0131rla. Leylak ilkbahar\u0131n k\u0131sa ama unutulmaz kokusudur; sen de ge\xe7mi\u015fin g\xfczelli\u011fine \u015f\xfckranla bak.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, recall the innocence of first loves and sweet memories. Lilac is spring's brief yet unforgettable scent; look upon the beauty of the past with gratitude.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute an die Unschuld erster Lieben und s\xfc\xdfer Erinnerungen. Flieder ist der kurze, doch unvergessliche Duft des Fr\xfchlings; betrachte die Sch\xf6nheit der Vergangenheit mit Dankbarkeit.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda la inocencia de los primeros amores y los dulces recuerdos. La lila es el aroma breve pero inolvidable de la primavera; mira con gratitud la belleza del pasado.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, rappelle-toi l'innocence des premiers amours et des doux souvenirs. Le lilas est le parfum bref mais inoubliable du printemps ; regarde la beaut\xe9 du pass\xe9 avec gratitude.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u521d\u604b\u3084\u7518\u3044\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u306e\u7121\u57a2\u3055\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30e9\u30a4\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u306f\u6625\u306e\u77ed\u304f\u3082\u5fd8\u308c\u304c\u305f\u3044\u9999\u308a\u3002\u904e\u53bb\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u611f\u8b1d\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u898b\u3064\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, recorde a inoc\xeancia dos primeiros amores e das doces lembran\xe7as. O lil\xe1s \xe9 o aroma breve mas inesquec\xedvel da primavera; olhe para a beleza do passado com gratid\xe3o.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7eklerini bir vazoda bulundurarak mek\xe2n\u0131n\u0131 tatl\u0131 bir kokuyla doldur ya da kurutulmu\u015f \xe7i\xe7eklerini kokulu bir kese i\xe7inde sakla. \u0130mgesini an\u0131larla ba\u011f kurmak i\xe7in meditasyonda canland\u0131r.",howToUseEn:"Keep the flowers in a vase to fill your space with a sweet scent, or store dried flowers in a scented sachet. Visualize its image in meditation to connect with memories.",howToUseDe:"Stelle die Bl\xfcten in eine Vase, um deinen Raum mit s\xfc\xdfem Duft zu f\xfcllen, oder bewahre getrocknete Bl\xfcten in einem Dufts\xe4ckchen auf. Visualisiere ihr Bild in der Meditation, um dich mit Erinnerungen zu verbinden.",howToUseEs:"Coloca las flores en un jarr\xf3n para llenar tu espacio de un aroma dulce, o guarda flores secas en una bolsita perfumada. Visualiza su imagen en meditaci\xf3n para conectar con los recuerdos.",howToUseFr:"Garde les fleurs dans un vase pour emplir ton espace d'un doux parfum, ou conserve des fleurs s\xe9ch\xe9es dans un sachet parfum\xe9. Visualise son image en m\xe9ditation pour te relier aux souvenirs.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u306b\u98fe\u308a\u3001\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u7518\u3044\u9999\u308a\u3067\u6e80\u305f\u3059\u304b\u3001\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u82b1\u3092\u9999\u308a\u888b\u306b\u5165\u308c\u3066\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3068\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308b\u305f\u3081\u3001\u305d\u306e\u59ff\u3092\u7791\u60f3\u3067\u601d\u3044\u63cf\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Mantenha as flores em um vaso para encher o seu espa\xe7o com um aroma doce, ou guarde flores secas em um sach\xea perfumado. Visualize a imagem dela na medita\xe7\xe3o para se conectar com as lembran\xe7as.",affirmation:"Ge\xe7mi\u015fin g\xfczelli\u011fine \u015f\xfckranla bak\u0131yorum, masumiyetimi koruyorum.",affirmationEn:"I look upon the beauty of the past with gratitude and keep my innocence.",affirmationDe:"Ich betrachte die Sch\xf6nheit der Vergangenheit mit Dankbarkeit und bewahre meine Unschuld.",affirmationEs:"Miro la belleza del pasado con gratitud y conservo mi inocencia.",affirmationFr:"Je regarde la beaut\xe9 du pass\xe9 avec gratitude et garde mon innocence.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u904e\u53bb\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u611f\u8b1d\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u898b\u3064\u3081\u3001\u7121\u57a2\u3092\u4fdd\u3064\u3002",affirmationPt:"Olho para a beleza do passado com gratid\xe3o e mantenho a minha inoc\xeancia.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg"},{id:"plant-075",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3b",color:"#F2B705",name:"Ay\xe7i\xe7e\u011fi",nameEn:"Sunflower",nameDe:"Sonnenblume",nameEs:"Girasol",nameFr:"Tournesol",nameJa:"\u3072\u307e\u308f\u308a",namePt:"Girassol",origin:"Kuzey Amerika",originEn:"North America",originDe:"Nordamerika",originEs:"Am\xe9rica del Norte",originFr:"Am\xe9rique du Nord",originJa:"\u5317\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab",originPt:"Am\xe9rica do Norte",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"G\xfcne\u015f Sinir A\u011f\u0131 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u30bd\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30d7\u30ec\u30af\u30b5\u30b9\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["g\xfcne\u015f enerjisi","iyimserlik","\xf6zg\xfcven"],propertiesEn:["solar energy","optimism","confidence"],propertiesDe:["Sonnenenergie","Optimismus","Selbstvertrauen"],propertiesEs:["energ\xeda solar","optimismo","confianza"],propertiesFr:["\xe9nergie solaire","optimisme","confiance"],propertiesJa:["\u592a\u967d\u306e\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc","\u697d\u89b3","\u81ea\u4fe1"],propertiesPt:["energia solar","otimismo","confian\xe7a"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn, ay\xe7i\xe7e\u011fi gibi y\xfcz\xfcn\xfc \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa \xe7evir. Karanl\u0131\u011fa de\u011fil ayd\u0131nl\u0131\u011fa y\xf6nelmek bir se\xe7imdir; sen de bug\xfcn iyimserli\u011fi se\xe7.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, like a sunflower, turn your face to the light. Facing brightness rather than darkness is a choice; choose optimism today too.",dailyMessageDe:"Wende heute wie eine Sonnenblume dein Gesicht dem Licht zu. Sich der Helligkeit statt der Dunkelheit zuzuwenden ist eine Wahl; w\xe4hle auch heute den Optimismus.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, como un girasol, vuelve tu rostro hacia la luz. Orientarse a la claridad en vez de a la oscuridad es una elecci\xf3n; elige hoy tambi\xe9n el optimismo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, comme un tournesol, tourne ton visage vers la lumi\xe8re. Se tourner vers la clart\xe9 plut\xf4t que vers l'obscurit\xe9 est un choix ; choisis aussi l'optimisme aujourd'hui.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3072\u307e\u308f\u308a\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u9854\u3092\u5149\u3078\u5411\u3051\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6697\u95c7\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u660e\u308b\u3055\u3078\u5411\u304b\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306f\u9078\u629e\u3067\u3059\u3002\u4eca\u65e5\u3082\u697d\u89b3\u3092\u9078\u3073\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, como um girassol, vire o seu rosto para a luz. Voltar-se para a claridade em vez da escurid\xe3o \xe9 uma escolha; escolha tamb\xe9m o otimismo hoje.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7e\u011fini bir vazoda bulundurarak g\xfcn\xfc ne\u015feli bir enerjiyle kar\u015f\u0131la. \xc7ekirdeklerini besleyici bir at\u0131\u015ft\u0131rmal\u0131k olarak t\xfcket ya da tohumlar\u0131n\u0131 niyet rit\xfcelinde umut sembol\xfc olarak ek.",howToUseEn:"Keep the flower in a vase to greet the day with a cheerful energy. Eat the seeds as a nourishing snack, or plant the seeds as a symbol of hope in an intention ritual.",howToUseDe:"Stelle die Blume in eine Vase, um den Tag mit fr\xf6hlicher Energie zu begr\xfc\xdfen. Iss die Kerne als nahrhaften Snack oder pflanze die Samen in einem Absichtsritual als Symbol der Hoffnung.",howToUseEs:"Coloca la flor en un jarr\xf3n para recibir el d\xeda con una energ\xeda alegre. Come las semillas como un tentempi\xe9 nutritivo, o siembra las semillas como s\xedmbolo de esperanza en un ritual de intenci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Garde la fleur dans un vase pour accueillir le jour avec une \xe9nergie joyeuse. Mange les graines en collation nourrissante, ou plante les graines comme symbole d'espoir dans un rituel d'intention.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u306b\u98fe\u308a\u3001\u660e\u308b\u3044\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc\u3067\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u8fce\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7a2e\u3092\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u304a\u3084\u3064\u3068\u3057\u3066\u98df\u3079\u308b\u304b\u3001\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u5100\u5f0f\u3067\u5e0c\u671b\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3057\u3066\u7a2e\u3092\u307e\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Mantenha a flor em um vaso para receber o dia com uma energia alegre. Coma as sementes como um lanche nutritivo, ou plante as sementes como s\xedmbolo de esperan\xe7a em um ritual de inten\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Y\xfcz\xfcm\xfc \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa \xe7eviriyorum, iyimserli\u011fi se\xe7iyorum.",affirmationEn:"I turn my face to the light and choose optimism.",affirmationDe:"Ich wende mein Gesicht dem Licht zu und w\xe4hle den Optimismus.",affirmationEs:"Vuelvo mi rostro hacia la luz y elijo el optimismo.",affirmationFr:"Je tourne mon visage vers la lumi\xe8re et choisis l'optimisme.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u9854\u3092\u5149\u3078\u5411\u3051\u3001\u697d\u89b3\u3092\u9078\u3076\u3002",affirmationPt:"Volto o meu rosto para a luz e escolho o otimismo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Sunflower_sky_backdrop.jpg/330px-Sunflower_sky_backdrop.jpg"},{id:"plant-076",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5E8A56",name:"Betoni Otu",nameEn:"Wood Betony",nameDe:"Echte Betonie",nameEs:"Bet\xf3nica",nameFr:"B\xe9toine",nameJa:"\u30d9\u30c8\u30cb\u30fc",namePt:"Bet\xf4nica",origin:"Avrupa",originEn:"Europe",originDe:"Europa",originEs:"Europa",originFr:"Europe",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1",originPt:"Europa",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["topraklay\u0131c\u0131","koruyucu","netlik"],propertiesEn:["grounding","protective","clarity"],propertiesDe:["erdend","sch\xfctzend","Klarheit"],propertiesEs:["enraizante","protector","claridad"],propertiesFr:["ancrant","protecteur","clart\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304f","\u5b88\u8b77","\u660e\u6670"],propertiesPt:["enraizador","protetor","clareza"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn da\u011f\u0131lan d\xfc\u015f\xfcncelerini topla ve ayaklar\u0131n\u0131 yere bas. Betoni eski \xe7a\u011flarda koruyucu bir ot olarak biliniyordu; sen de zihnini toparlay\u0131p merkezine d\xf6n.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, gather your scattered thoughts and plant your feet on the ground. Betony was known as a protective herb in ancient times; gather your mind and return to your center.",dailyMessageDe:"Sammle heute deine zerstreuten Gedanken und setze deine F\xfc\xdfe fest auf den Boden. Betonie galt in der Antike als sch\xfctzendes Kraut; sammle deinen Geist und kehre in deine Mitte zur\xfcck.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, re\xfane tus pensamientos dispersos y planta los pies en el suelo. La bet\xf3nica se conoc\xeda como una hierba protectora en la antig\xfcedad; recoge tu mente y vuelve a tu centro.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, rassemble tes pens\xe9es \xe9parpill\xe9es et pose tes pieds sur le sol. La b\xe9toine \xe9tait connue comme une herbe protectrice dans l'Antiquit\xe9 ; rassemble ton esprit et reviens \xe0 ton centre.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u6563\u3089\u3070\u3063\u305f\u601d\u3044\u3092\u96c6\u3081\u3001\u8db3\u3092\u5730\u306b\u3064\u3051\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d9\u30c8\u30cb\u30fc\u306f\u53e4\u4ee3\u306b\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u8349\u3068\u3057\u3066\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5fc3\u3092\u307e\u3068\u3081\u3001\u4e2d\u5fc3\u3078\u623b\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, re\xfana os seus pensamentos dispersos e firme os p\xe9s no ch\xe3o. A bet\xf4nica era conhecida como uma erva protetora na antiguidade; re\xfana a sua mente e volte ao seu centro.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak hafif\xe7e demle, zihnini toparlamak i\xe7in \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc i\xe7. Bir demetini koruma niyetiyle \xe7al\u0131\u015fma alan\u0131na asabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"Lightly brew the leaves as a tea and drink moderately to gather your mind. You can hang a bundle in your workspace with an intention of protection.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter leicht als Tee und trinke ihn ma\xdfvoll, um deinen Geist zu sammeln. Du kannst ein B\xfcndel mit Schutzabsicht in deinen Arbeitsbereich h\xe4ngen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona ligeramente las hojas como t\xe9 y bebe con moderaci\xf3n para recoger tu mente. Puedes colgar un manojo en tu espacio de trabajo con intenci\xf3n de protecci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Infuse l\xe9g\xe8rement les feuilles en tisane et bois avec mod\xe9ration pour rassembler ton esprit. Tu peux suspendre un bouquet dans ton espace de travail avec une intention de protection.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u307e\u3068\u3081\u308b\u305f\u3081\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306b\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3067\u675f\u3092\u4f5c\u696d\u5834\u306b\u540a\u308b\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare levemente as folhas como ch\xe1 e beba com modera\xe7\xe3o para reunir a sua mente. Voc\xea pode pendurar um ma\xe7o no seu espa\xe7o de trabalho com a inten\xe7\xe3o de prote\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"D\xfc\u015f\xfcncelerimi topluyorum, merkezimde sa\u011flam duruyorum.",affirmationEn:"I gather my thoughts and stand firm at my center.",affirmationDe:"Ich sammle meine Gedanken und stehe fest in meiner Mitte.",affirmationEs:"Re\xfano mis pensamientos y permanezco firme en mi centro.",affirmationFr:"Je rassemble mes pens\xe9es et je me tiens ferme en mon centre.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u601d\u3044\u3092\u96c6\u3081\u3001\u4e2d\u5fc3\u306b\u3057\u3063\u304b\u308a\u7acb\u3064\u3002",affirmationPt:"Re\xfano os meus pensamentos e permane\xe7o firme no meu centro.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Betonica_officinalis_%287775493816%29.jpg/330px-Betonica_officinalis_%287775493816%29.jpg"},{id:"plant-077",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#6E9456",name:"Limon Reyhan\u0131",nameEn:"Lemon Basil",nameDe:"Zitronenbasilikum",nameEs:"Albahaca lim\xf3n",nameFr:"Basilic citron",nameJa:"\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30d0\u30b8\u30eb",namePt:"Manjeric\xe3o-lim\xe3o",origin:"G\xfcney Asya",originEn:"South Asia",originDe:"S\xfcdasien",originEs:"Sur de Asia",originFr:"Asie du Sud",originJa:"\u5357\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Sul da \xc1sia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["ferahlat\u0131c\u0131","ne\u015felendirici","a\xe7\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["refreshing","uplifting","opening"],propertiesDe:["erfrischend","aufmunternd","\xf6ffnend"],propertiesEs:["refrescante","alegrante","abridor"],propertiesFr:["rafra\xeechissant","r\xe9jouissant","ouvrant"],propertiesJa:["\u723d\u5feb","\u9ad8\u63da","\u958b\u304f"],propertiesPt:["refrescante","alegrante","abridor"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kalbini ferah bir ne\u015feyle a\xe7. Reyhan limonsu kokusuyla ruhu hafifletir; sen de g\xfcn\xfc hafif ve a\xe7\u0131k bir kalple kar\u015f\u0131la.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, open your heart with a fresh joy. Lemon basil lightens the spirit with its citrus scent; meet the day with a light and open heart.",dailyMessageDe:"\xd6ffne heute dein Herz mit einer frischen Freude. Zitronenbasilikum erleichtert die Seele mit seinem Zitrusduft; begegne dem Tag mit einem leichten und offenen Herzen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, abre tu coraz\xf3n con una alegr\xeda fresca. La albahaca lim\xf3n aligera el esp\xedritu con su aroma c\xedtrico; recibe el d\xeda con un coraz\xf3n ligero y abierto.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ouvre ton c\u0153ur avec une joie fra\xeeche. Le basilic citron all\xe8ge l'esprit avec son parfum d'agrumes ; accueille le jour avec un c\u0153ur l\xe9ger et ouvert.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u559c\u3073\u3067\u5fc3\u3092\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30ec\u30e2\u30f3\u30d0\u30b8\u30eb\u306f\u67d1\u6a58\u306e\u9999\u308a\u3067\u9b42\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u8efd\u3084\u304b\u3067\u958b\u3044\u305f\u5fc3\u3067\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u8fce\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, abra o seu cora\xe7\xe3o com uma alegria fresca. O manjeric\xe3o-lim\xe3o alivia o esp\xedrito com o seu aroma c\xedtrico; receba o dia com um cora\xe7\xe3o leve e aberto.",howToUse:"Taze yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak demle ya da yemeklerine ferah bir aroma i\xe7in ekle. Bir saks\u0131da yeti\u015ftirerek mutfa\u011f\u0131na ne\u015feli bir koku kat.",howToUseEn:"Brew fresh leaves as a tea, or add them to your meals for a fresh aroma. Grow it in a pot to bring a cheerful scent to your kitchen.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche frische Bl\xe4tter als Tee oder gib sie f\xfcr ein frisches Aroma in deine Mahlzeiten. Ziehe es im Topf, um deiner K\xfcche einen fr\xf6hlichen Duft zu verleihen.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona hojas frescas como t\xe9, o a\xf1\xe1delas a tus comidas para un aroma fresco. Cult\xedvala en una maceta para dar un aroma alegre a tu cocina.",howToUseFr:"Infuse des feuilles fra\xeeches en tisane, ou ajoute-les \xe0 tes plats pour un ar\xf4me frais. Cultive-le en pot pour apporter un parfum joyeux \xe0 ta cuisine.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u8449\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3001\u3055\u308f\u3084\u304b\u306a\u9999\u308a\u306e\u305f\u3081\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u9262\u3067\u80b2\u3066\u3001\u53f0\u6240\u306b\u967d\u6c17\u306a\u9999\u308a\u3092\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare folhas frescas como ch\xe1, ou adicione-as \xe0s refei\xe7\xf5es para um aroma fresco. Cultive em um vaso para dar um aroma alegre \xe0 sua cozinha.",affirmation:"G\xfcn\xfc hafif ve a\xe7\u0131k bir kalple kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I meet the day with a light and open heart.",affirmationDe:"Ich begegne dem Tag mit einem leichten und offenen Herzen.",affirmationEs:"Recibo el d\xeda con un coraz\xf3n ligero y abierto.",affirmationFr:"J'accueille le jour avec un c\u0153ur l\xe9ger et ouvert.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u8efd\u3084\u304b\u3067\u958b\u3044\u305f\u5fc3\u3067\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u8fce\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Recebo o dia com um cora\xe7\xe3o leve e aberto.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Kemangi.jpg/330px-Kemangi.jpg"},{id:"plant-078",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5C7E4A",name:"Yabani Mercank\xf6\u015fk",nameEn:"Wild Marjoram",nameDe:"Wilder Majoran",nameEs:"Mejorana silvestre",nameFr:"Marjolaine sauvage",nameJa:"\u30ef\u30a4\u30eb\u30c9\u30de\u30b8\u30e7\u30e9\u30e0",namePt:"Manjerona-silvestre",origin:"Akdeniz, Avrupa",originEn:"Mediterranean, Europe",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum, Europa",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo, Europa",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e, Europe",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u30fb\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo, Europa",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","huzur","rahatlat\u0131c\u0131"],propertiesEn:["soothing","peace","relaxing"],propertiesDe:["beruhigend","Frieden","entspannend"],propertiesEs:["calmante","paz","relajante"],propertiesFr:["apaisant","paix","relaxant"],propertiesJa:["\u306a\u3060\u3081\u308b","\u5b89\u3089\u304e","\u30ea\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u30b9"],propertiesPt:["suavizante","paz","relaxante"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn i\xe7ine huzur veren k\xfc\xe7\xfck rit\xfcellere zaman ay\u0131r. Mercank\xf6\u015fk geleneksel olarak mutluluk ve rahatlamayla an\u0131l\u0131r; sakinli\u011fe kendini b\u0131rak.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, make time for the small rituals that bring you peace. Marjoram is traditionally linked with happiness and ease; surrender to calm.",dailyMessageDe:"Nimm dir heute Zeit f\xfcr die kleinen Rituale, die dir Frieden schenken. Majoran wird traditionell mit Gl\xfcck und Gelassenheit verbunden; \xfcberlasse dich der Ruhe.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, dedica tiempo a los peque\xf1os rituales que te dan paz. La mejorana se asocia tradicionalmente con la felicidad y el sosiego; entr\xe9gate a la calma.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, prends le temps des petits rituels qui t'apportent la paix. La marjolaine est traditionnellement li\xe9e au bonheur et \xe0 la qui\xe9tude ; abandonne-toi au calme.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u5100\u5f0f\u306b\u6642\u9593\u3092\u3068\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30de\u30b8\u30e7\u30e9\u30e0\u306f\u4f1d\u7d71\u7684\u306b\u5e78\u798f\u3068\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u306b\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u3055\u306b\u8eab\u3092\u3086\u3060\u306d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, reserve tempo para os pequenos rituais que trazem paz. A manjerona est\xe1 tradicionalmente ligada \xe0 felicidade e \xe0 serenidade; entregue-se \xe0 calma.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ay olarak demleyip ak\u015fam rahatlamas\u0131 i\xe7in i\xe7 ya da yemeklerine ekle. Esans ya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 yast\u0131\u011f\u0131na bir damla koyarak huzurlu bir uykuya haz\u0131rlan.",howToUseEn:"Brew the leaves as a tea for evening relaxation, or add them to your meals. Put a drop of the essential oil on your pillow to prepare for peaceful sleep.",howToUseDe:"Br\xfche die Bl\xe4tter als Tee zur abendlichen Entspannung oder gib sie in deine Mahlzeiten. Gib einen Tropfen des \xe4therischen \xd6ls auf dein Kissen, um dich auf einen friedlichen Schlaf vorzubereiten.",howToUseEs:"Infusiona las hojas como t\xe9 para la relajaci\xf3n de la tarde, o a\xf1\xe1delas a tus comidas. Pon una gota del aceite esencial en tu almohada para preparar un sue\xf1o tranquilo.",howToUseFr:"Infuse les feuilles en tisane pour la d\xe9tente du soir, ou ajoute-les \xe0 tes plats. Mets une goutte d'huile essentielle sur ton oreiller pour pr\xe9parer un sommeil paisible.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u591c\u306e\u304f\u3064\u308d\u304e\u306b\u98f2\u3080\u304b\u3001\u6599\u7406\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u7cbe\u6cb9\u3092\u4e00\u6ef4\u6795\u306b\u5782\u3089\u3057\u3001\u5b89\u3089\u304b\u306a\u7720\u308a\u306b\u5099\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Prepare as folhas como ch\xe1 para o relaxamento da noite, ou adicione-as \xe0s refei\xe7\xf5es. Pingue uma gota do \xf3leo essencial no travesseiro para preparar um sono tranquilo.",affirmation:"Sakinli\u011fe kendimi b\u0131rak\u0131yorum, i\xe7imde huzur var.",affirmationEn:"I surrender to calm; there is peace within me.",affirmationDe:"Ich \xfcberlasse mich der Ruhe; in mir ist Frieden.",affirmationEs:"Me entrego a la calma; hay paz dentro de m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Je m'abandonne au calme ; il y a la paix en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u7a4f\u3084\u304b\u3055\u306b\u8eab\u3092\u3086\u3060\u306d\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Entrego-me \xe0 calma; h\xe1 paz dentro de mim.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Origanum_vulgare_-_harilik_pune.jpg/330px-Origanum_vulgare_-_harilik_pune.jpg"},{id:"plant-079",emoji:"\ud83c\udf42",color:"#9C6B3A",name:"P\u0131trak K\xf6k\xfc (Dulavratotu)",nameEn:"Burdock",nameDe:"Klette",nameEs:"Bardana",nameFr:"Bardane",nameJa:"\u30b4\u30dc\u30a6",namePt:"Bardana",origin:"Avrupa, Asya",originEn:"Europe, Asia",originDe:"Europa, Asien",originEs:"Europa, Asia",originFr:"Europe, Asie",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2",originPt:"Europa, \xc1sia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u571f",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["ar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","topraklay\u0131c\u0131","besleyici"],propertiesEn:["purifying","grounding","nourishing"],propertiesDe:["reinigend","erdend","n\xe4hrend"],propertiesEs:["purificante","enraizante","nutritivo"],propertiesFr:["purifiant","ancrant","nourrissant"],propertiesJa:["\u6d44\u5316","\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304f","\u6ecb\u990a"],propertiesPt:["purificante","enraizador","nutritivo"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn derine inmeye, k\xf6kten temizlenmeye de\u011fer ver. Dulavratotunun k\xf6k\xfc topra\u011f\u0131n derinine uzan\u0131r; sen de y\xfczeysel de\u011fil, k\xf6kl\xfc bir yenilenmeye y\xf6nel.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, value going deep and cleansing from the root. Burdock's root reaches deep into the soil; aim for a renewal that is rooted, not superficial.",dailyMessageDe:"Sch\xe4tze es heute, in die Tiefe zu gehen und von der Wurzel her zu reinigen. Die Wurzel der Klette reicht tief in die Erde; strebe eine verwurzelte, nicht oberfl\xe4chliche Erneuerung an.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, valora ir a lo profundo y limpiar desde la ra\xedz. La ra\xedz de la bardana se hunde profundo en la tierra; busca una renovaci\xf3n enraizada, no superficial.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, accorde de la valeur \xe0 aller en profondeur et \xe0 purifier depuis la racine. La racine de la bardane plonge profond\xe9ment dans le sol ; vise un renouveau enracin\xe9, et non superficiel.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u6df1\u304f\u3082\u3050\u308a\u3001\u6839\u304b\u3089\u6e05\u3081\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u5927\u5207\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b4\u30dc\u30a6\u306e\u6839\u306f\u571f\u306e\u6df1\u304f\u3078\u4f38\u3073\u307e\u3059\u3002\u8868\u9762\u7684\u3067\u306a\u304f\u3001\u6839\u3065\u3044\u305f\u518d\u751f\u3092\u76ee\u6307\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, valorize ir fundo e limpar desde a raiz. A raiz da bardana alcan\xe7a o fundo do solo; busque uma renova\xe7\xe3o enraizada, n\xe3o superficial.",howToUse:"K\xf6k\xfcn\xfc ince do\u011fray\u0131p suda kaynatarak topraklay\u0131c\u0131 bir \xe7ay haz\u0131rla ya da \xe7orbaya kat. D\xfczenli, \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc kullanarak ar\u0131nmay\u0131 destekle.",howToUseEn:"Slice the root thinly and simmer it in water for a grounding tea, or add it to soup. Support cleansing with regular, moderate use.",howToUseDe:"Schneide die Wurzel d\xfcnn und k\xf6chle sie in Wasser f\xfcr einen erdenden Tee oder gib sie in Suppe. Unterst\xfctze die Reinigung durch regelm\xe4\xdfigen, ma\xdfvollen Gebrauch.",howToUseEs:"Corta la ra\xedz en rodajas finas y hi\xe9rvela a fuego lento para un t\xe9 enraizante, o a\xf1\xe1dela a la sopa. Apoya la limpieza con un uso regular y moderado.",howToUseFr:"Coupe la racine finement et fais-la mijoter dans l'eau pour une tisane d'ancrage, ou ajoute-la \xe0 la soupe. Soutiens la purification par un usage r\xe9gulier et mod\xe9r\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u6839\u3092\u8584\u304f\u5207\u3063\u3066\u6c34\u3067\u716e\u51fa\u3057\u3001\u5730\u306b\u6839\u3065\u304f\u304a\u8336\u306b\u3059\u308b\u304b\u3001\u30b9\u30fc\u30d7\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5b9a\u671f\u7684\u3067\u307b\u3069\u307b\u3069\u306e\u4f7f\u7528\u3067\u6d44\u5316\u3092\u652f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Corte a raiz em fatias finas e cozinhe em fogo brando para um ch\xe1 enraizador, ou adicione \xe0 sopa. Apoie a limpeza com uso regular e moderado.",affirmation:"K\xf6kl\xfc bir yenilenmeye a\xe7\u0131\u011f\u0131m, derinden ar\u0131n\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I am open to a rooted renewal; I cleanse from deep within.",affirmationDe:"Ich bin offen f\xfcr eine verwurzelte Erneuerung; ich reinige mich von tief innen.",affirmationEs:"Estoy abierto a una renovaci\xf3n enraizada; me limpio desde lo profundo.",affirmationFr:"Je suis ouvert \xe0 un renouveau enracin\xe9 ; je me purifie de l'int\xe9rieur.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6839\u3065\u3044\u305f\u518d\u751f\u306b\u958b\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u6df1\u304f\u304b\u3089\u6e05\u307e\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Estou aberto a uma renova\xe7\xe3o enraizada; limpo-me a partir das profundezas.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Villtakjas_2008.jpg/330px-Villtakjas_2008.jpg"},{id:"plant-080",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#4E7A4A",name:"Kutsal Ot (Sweetgrass)",nameEn:"Sweetgrass",nameDe:"Mariengras",nameEs:"Hierba dulce",nameFr:"Herbe sacr\xe9e",nameJa:"\u30b9\u30a4\u30fc\u30c8\u30b0\u30e9\u30b9",namePt:"Capim-doce",origin:"Kuzey Amerika, Avrasya",originEn:"North America, Eurasia",originDe:"Nordamerika, Eurasien",originEs:"Am\xe9rica del Norte, Eurasia",originFr:"Am\xe9rique du Nord, Eurasie",originJa:"\u5317\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u30fb\u30e6\u30fc\u30e9\u30b7\u30a2",originPt:"Am\xe9rica do Norte, Eur\xe1sia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["\u015f\xfckran","kutsal","huzur"],propertiesEn:["gratitude","sacred","peace"],propertiesDe:["Dankbarkeit","heilig","Frieden"],propertiesEs:["gratitud","sagrado","paz"],propertiesFr:["gratitude","sacr\xe9","paix"],propertiesJa:["\u611f\u8b1d","\u8056\u306a\u308b","\u5b89\u3089\u304e"],propertiesPt:["gratid\xe3o","sagrado","paz"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn \u015f\xfckranla kalbini yumu\u015fat. Kutsal ot yerli geleneklerde olumlu enerji ve \u015f\xfckran \xe7a\u011f\u0131rmak i\xe7in \xf6r\xfcl\xfcr; sen de g\xfcn\xfc minnetle \xf6rerek tamamla.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, soften your heart with gratitude. Sweetgrass is braided in Indigenous traditions to call in positive energy and thanks; weave your day in gratitude too.",dailyMessageDe:"Erweiche heute dein Herz mit Dankbarkeit. Mariengras wird in indigenen Traditionen geflochten, um positive Energie und Dank herbeizurufen; webe auch deinen Tag in Dankbarkeit.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ablanda tu coraz\xf3n con gratitud. La hierba dulce se trenza en tradiciones ind\xedgenas para invocar energ\xeda positiva y agradecimiento; teje tambi\xe9n tu d\xeda con gratitud.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, adoucis ton c\u0153ur par la gratitude. L'herbe sacr\xe9e se tresse dans les traditions autochtones pour appeler l'\xe9nergie positive et la reconnaissance ; tisse aussi ta journ\xe9e dans la gratitude.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u611f\u8b1d\u3067\u5fc3\u3092\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3052\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b9\u30a4\u30fc\u30c8\u30b0\u30e9\u30b9\u306f\u5148\u4f4f\u6c11\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71\u3067\u3001\u3088\u3044\u30a8\u30cd\u30eb\u30ae\u30fc\u3068\u611f\u8b1d\u3092\u62db\u304f\u305f\u3081\u7de8\u307e\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3082\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u611f\u8b1d\u3067\u7de8\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, suavize o seu cora\xe7\xe3o com gratid\xe3o. O capim-doce \xe9 tran\xe7ado nas tradi\xe7\xf5es ind\xedgenas para invocar energia positiva e agradecimento; te\xe7a tamb\xe9m o seu dia em gratid\xe3o.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f \xf6rg\xfcs\xfcn\xfc sayg\u0131yla, \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc tutu\u015fturup duman\u0131yla \u015f\xfckran niyetiyle mek\xe2n\u0131n\u0131 kutsa. Etik kaynakl\u0131 tercih et ve gelene\u011fe sayg\u0131 g\xf6ster.",howToUseEn:"Respectfully and sparingly light the dried braid and bless your space with its smoke in an intention of gratitude. Choose ethically sourced and honor the tradition.",howToUseDe:"Entz\xfcnde den getrockneten Zopf respektvoll und sparsam und segne deinen Raum mit seinem Rauch in einer Absicht der Dankbarkeit. W\xe4hle ethisch gewonnenes und ehre die Tradition.",howToUseEs:"Con respeto y moderaci\xf3n, enciende la trenza seca y bendice tu espacio con su humo en una intenci\xf3n de gratitud. Elige de origen \xe9tico y honra la tradici\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Avec respect et mod\xe9ration, allume la tresse s\xe9ch\xe9e et b\xe9nis ton espace avec sa fum\xe9e dans une intention de gratitude. Choisis une source \xe9thique et honore la tradition.",howToUseJa:"\u656c\u610f\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u63a7\u3048\u3081\u306b\u3001\u4e7e\u71e5\u3057\u305f\u7de8\u307f\u3092\u711a\u304d\u3001\u611f\u8b1d\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3067\u305d\u306e\u7159\u306b\u3088\u308a\u7a7a\u9593\u3092\u6e05\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u502b\u7406\u7684\u306a\u5165\u624b\u3092\u9078\u3073\u3001\u4f1d\u7d71\u3092\u656c\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",howToUsePt:"Com respeito e modera\xe7\xe3o, acenda a tran\xe7a seca e aben\xe7oe o seu espa\xe7o com a fuma\xe7a em uma inten\xe7\xe3o de gratid\xe3o. Escolha de origem \xe9tica e honre a tradi\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"G\xfcn\xfcm\xfc minnetle \xf6r\xfcyorum, kalbim \u015f\xfckranla yumu\u015fuyor.",affirmationEn:"I weave my day in gratitude; my heart softens with thanks.",affirmationDe:"Ich webe meinen Tag in Dankbarkeit; mein Herz wird durch Dank weich.",affirmationEs:"Tejo mi d\xeda con gratitud; mi coraz\xf3n se ablanda con el agradecimiento.",affirmationFr:"Je tisse ma journ\xe9e dans la gratitude ; mon c\u0153ur s'adoucit de reconnaissance.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u611f\u8b1d\u3067\u7de8\u3080\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u611f\u8b1d\u3067\u3084\u308f\u3089\u3050\u3002",affirmationPt:"Te\xe7o o meu dia em gratid\xe3o; o meu cora\xe7\xe3o se suaviza com o agradecimento.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Hierochloe_odorata_%28USDA%29.jpg/330px-Hierochloe_odorata_%28USDA%29.jpg"},{id:"plant-081",emoji:"\ud83e\uddd9",color:"#5C6B4A",name:"Adamotu",nameEn:"Mandrake",nameDe:"Alraune",nameEs:"Mandr\xe1gora",nameFr:"Mandragore",nameJa:"\u30de\u30f3\u30c9\u30ec\u30a4\u30af",namePt:"Mandr\xe1gora",origin:"Antik Yunan, Roma & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Greece, Rome & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland, Rom & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Grecia, Roma y Anatolia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique, Rome et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30ed\u30fc\u30de\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga, Roma e Anat\xf3lia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["koruma","t\u0131ls\u0131m","bereket","gizem"],propertiesEn:["protection","talisman","fertility","mystery"],propertiesDe:["Schutz","Talisman","Fruchtbarkeit","Geheimnis"],propertiesEs:["protecci\xf3n","talism\xe1n","fertilidad","misterio"],propertiesFr:["protection","talisman","fertilit\xe9","myst\xe8re"],propertiesJa:["\u5b88\u8b77","\u8b77\u7b26","\u8c4a\u7a63","\u795e\u79d8"],propertiesPt:["prote\xe7\xe3o","talism\xe3","fertilidade","mist\xe9rio"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn k\xf6klerine in ve i\xe7indeki gizemli g\xfcc\xfc onurland\u0131r. Adamotu sana her \u015feyin y\xfczeyde g\xf6r\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfc gibi olmad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131, derinde sakl\u0131 bir bilgeli\u011fin bekledi\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, descend into your roots and honor the mysterious power within you. Mandrake whispers that not all is as it appears on the surface, and that a hidden wisdom awaits in the depths.",dailyMessageDe:"Steige heute zu deinen Wurzeln hinab und ehre die geheimnisvolle Kraft in dir. Die Alraune fl\xfcstert, dass nicht alles so ist, wie es an der Oberfl\xe4che scheint, und dass in der Tiefe eine verborgene Weisheit wartet.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, desciende a tus ra\xedces y honra el poder misterioso que hay en ti. La mandr\xe1gora susurra que no todo es como parece en la superficie, y que una sabidur\xeda oculta espera en las profundidades.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, descends vers tes racines et honore le pouvoir myst\xe9rieux en toi. La mandragore murmure que tout n'est pas tel qu'il para\xeet en surface, et qu'une sagesse cach\xe9e attend dans les profondeurs.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u6839\u3078\u3068\u964d\u308a\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u795e\u79d8\u306e\u529b\u3092\u656c\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30de\u30f3\u30c9\u30ec\u30a4\u30af\u306f\u3001\u3059\u3079\u3066\u304c\u8868\u9762\u306b\u898b\u3048\u308b\u3068\u304a\u308a\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u6df1\u307f\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u77e5\u6075\u304c\u5f85\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, des\xe7a \xe0s suas ra\xedzes e honre o poder misterioso dentro de voc\xea. A mandr\xe1gora sussurra que nem tudo \xe9 como parece na superf\xedcie, e que uma sabedoria oculta espera nas profundezas.",howToUse:"Yaln\u0131zca sembolik ve t\xf6rensel olarak kullan: k\xf6k\xfcn\xfc bir koruma t\u0131ls\u0131m\u0131 olarak evinde bulundurabilirsin. Zehirlidir; i\xe7sel kullan\u0131m \xf6nerilmez.",howToUseEn:"Use only symbolically and ceremonially: you may keep its root at home as a protective talisman. It is toxic; internal use is not recommended.",howToUseDe:"Verwende sie nur symbolisch und zeremoniell: Du kannst ihre Wurzel als Schutztalisman zu Hause aufbewahren. Sie ist giftig; innere Anwendung wird nicht empfohlen.",howToUseEs:"\xdasala solo de forma simb\xf3lica y ceremonial: puedes guardar su ra\xedz en casa como talism\xe1n protector. Es t\xf3xica; no se recomienda el uso interno.",howToUseFr:"Utilise-la seulement de fa\xe7on symbolique et c\xe9r\xe9monielle : tu peux garder sa racine chez toi comme talisman protecteur. Elle est toxique ; l'usage interne n'est pas recommand\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u30fb\u5100\u5f0f\u7684\u306b\u306e\u307f\u7528\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\uff1a\u305d\u306e\u6839\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u306e\u8b77\u7b26\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5bb6\u306b\u7f6e\u304f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u6709\u6bd2\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u4f53\u5185\u3078\u306e\u4f7f\u7528\u306f\u52e7\u3081\u3089\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",howToUsePt:"Use apenas de forma simb\xf3lica e cerimonial: voc\xea pode guardar sua raiz em casa como talism\xe3 protetor. \xc9 t\xf3xica; o uso interno n\xe3o \xe9 recomendado.",affirmation:"K\xf6klerimde sakl\u0131 g\xfcc\xfcme g\xfcveniyorum, derinli\u011fimi onurland\u0131r\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I trust the power hidden in my roots and honor my own depth.",affirmationDe:"Ich vertraue der in meinen Wurzeln verborgenen Kraft und ehre meine eigene Tiefe.",affirmationEs:"Conf\xedo en el poder oculto en mis ra\xedces y honro mi propia profundidad.",affirmationFr:"Je fais confiance au pouvoir cach\xe9 dans mes racines et j'honore ma propre profondeur.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6839\u306b\u79d8\u3081\u3089\u308c\u305f\u529b\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3057\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u6df1\u3055\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3002",affirmationPt:"Confio no poder oculto nas minhas ra\xedzes e honro a minha pr\xf3pria profundidade.",myth:"Adamotu, g\xf6vdesi ve uzuvlar\u0131yla bir insana benzedi\u011fi i\xe7in ad\u0131n\u0131 al\u0131r; eski \xe7a\u011flarda T\xfcrkler ona 'abd\xfcsselamotu' demi\u015f, topra\u011fa s\u0131k\u0131ca ba\u011fl\u0131 bu k\xf6k\xfc s\xf6kmek i\xe7in \xf6k\xfczler ba\u011flan\u0131rm\u0131\u015f. S\xf6ke s\xf6ke kopar\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda ac\u0131yla \xe7\u0131\u011fl\u0131k att\u0131\u011f\u0131na ve onu ay\u0131ran ki\u015fiye \xf6l\xfcm getirdi\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131r, bu y\xfczden k\xf6peklere s\xf6kt\xfcr\xfcl\xfcrm\xfc\u015f. Yunan ve Roma'da b\xfcy\xfclerde aranan bir bitki olmu\u015f; a\u015fk, dilek ve bereket i\xe7in kullan\u0131lm\u0131\u015f, 'a\u015fk elmas\u0131' diye an\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r.",mythEn:"Mandrake takes its name from a root shaped like a human body with limbs; in old times the Turks called it 'abd\xfcsselamotu' and tied oxen to wrench the deeply rooted plant from the earth. It was said to scream in pain when pulled and to bring death to whoever uprooted it, so dogs were made to do the task. In Greece and Rome it was sought for spells, used for love, wishes and fertility, and was called the 'love apple'.",mythDe:"Die Alraune verdankt ihren Namen einer Wurzel, die wie ein menschlicher K\xf6rper mit Gliedern geformt ist; einst nannten die T\xfcrken sie 'abd\xfcsselamotu' und banden Ochsen an, um die tief verwurzelte Pflanze aus der Erde zu rei\xdfen. Man sagte, sie schreie vor Schmerz, wenn man sie zieht, und bringe dem Tod, der sie ausgr\xe4bt, weshalb man Hunde die Aufgabe verrichten lie\xdf. In Griechenland und Rom war sie f\xfcr Zauber begehrt, wurde f\xfcr Liebe, W\xfcnsche und Fruchtbarkeit verwendet und 'Liebesapfel' genannt.",mythEs:"La mandr\xe1gora toma su nombre de una ra\xedz con forma de cuerpo humano con miembros; antiguamente los turcos la llamaban 'abd\xfcsselamotu' y ataban bueyes para arrancar de la tierra la planta tan arraigada. Se dec\xeda que gritaba de dolor al ser arrancada y que tra\xeda la muerte a quien la desenterraba, por lo que hac\xedan que la sacaran los perros. En Grecia y Roma se buscaba para hechizos, se usaba para el amor, los deseos y la fertilidad, y se la llamaba 'manzana del amor'.",mythFr:"La mandragore tire son nom d'une racine en forme de corps humain avec des membres ; jadis les Turcs l'appelaient 'abd\xfcsselamotu' et attelaient des b\u0153ufs pour arracher de la terre cette plante profond\xe9ment enracin\xe9e. On disait qu'elle criait de douleur lorsqu'on l'arrachait et qu'elle apportait la mort \xe0 celui qui la d\xe9terrait, c'est pourquoi on faisait faire la t\xe2che par des chiens. En Gr\xe8ce et \xe0 Rome, elle \xe9tait recherch\xe9e pour les sortil\xe8ges, utilis\xe9e pour l'amour, les v\u0153ux et la fertilit\xe9, et appel\xe9e 'pomme d'amour'.",mythJa:"\u30de\u30f3\u30c9\u30ec\u30a4\u30af\u306f\u3001\u624b\u8db3\u306e\u3042\u308b\u4eba\u4f53\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306a\u6839\u306e\u5f62\u304b\u3089\u305d\u306e\u540d\u3092\u5f97\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u53e4\u3044\u6642\u4ee3\u3001\u30c8\u30eb\u30b3\u306e\u4eba\u3005\u306f\u3053\u308c\u3092\u300c\u30a2\u30d6\u30c7\u30e5\u30c3\u30bb\u30e9\u30e2\u30c8\u30a5\u300d\u3068\u547c\u3073\u3001\u6df1\u304f\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u308b\u3053\u306e\u690d\u7269\u3092\u5730\u304b\u3089\u5f15\u304d\u629c\u304f\u305f\u3081\u306b\u725b\u3092\u3064\u306a\u3044\u3060\u3068\u3044\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5f15\u304d\u629c\u304b\u308c\u308b\u3068\u82e6\u75db\u306e\u53eb\u3073\u3092\u3042\u3052\u3001\u6398\u308a\u51fa\u3057\u305f\u8005\u306b\u6b7b\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5f79\u306f\u72ac\u306b\u3055\u305b\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u3084\u30ed\u30fc\u30de\u3067\u306f\u546a\u8853\u306b\u6c42\u3081\u3089\u308c\u3001\u611b\u3084\u9858\u3044\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u7528\u3044\u3089\u308c\u3001\u300c\u611b\u306e\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u300d\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"A mandr\xe1gora recebe o nome de uma raiz com forma de corpo humano com membros; antigamente os turcos a chamavam de 'abd\xfcsselamotu' e atavam bois para arrancar da terra a planta t\xe3o enraizada. Dizia-se que ela gritava de dor ao ser arrancada e que trazia a morte a quem a desenterrasse, por isso faziam os c\xe3es realizarem a tarefa. Na Gr\xe9cia e em Roma era procurada para feiti\xe7os, usada para o amor, os desejos e a fertilidade, e era chamada de 'ma\xe7\xe3 do amor'.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Mandragoras_454_Dodoens_1583.png/330px-Mandragoras_454_Dodoens_1583.png"},{id:"plant-082",emoji:"\ud83c\udf38",color:"#C8D6B9",name:"Akdiken",nameEn:"Hawthorn",nameDe:"Wei\xdfdorn",nameEs:"Espino albar",nameFr:"Aub\xe9pine",nameJa:"\u30b5\u30f3\u30b6\u30b7",namePt:"Espinheiro-alvar",origin:"Antik Roma & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Rome & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Rom & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Roma y Anatolia",originFr:"Rome antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ed\u30fc\u30de\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Roma Antiga e Anat\xf3lia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["koruma","kalp dengesi","ar\u0131nma","s\u0131n\u0131r"],propertiesEn:["protection","heart balance","cleansing","boundary"],propertiesDe:["Schutz","Herzgleichgewicht","Reinigung","Grenze"],propertiesEs:["protecci\xf3n","equilibrio del coraz\xf3n","purificaci\xf3n","l\xedmite"],propertiesFr:["protection","\xe9quilibre du c\u0153ur","purification","limite"],propertiesJa:["\u5b88\u8b77","\u5fc3\u306e\u30d0\u30e9\u30f3\u30b9","\u6d44\u5316","\u5883\u754c"],propertiesPt:["prote\xe7\xe3o","equil\xedbrio do cora\xe7\xe3o","purifica\xe7\xe3o","limite"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 nazik\xe7e koru ve kalbini g\xfcvende tut. Akdiken sana k\xf6t\xfc niyetli olan\u0131 uzakta tutarken sevgiye a\xe7\u0131k kalman\u0131n m\xfcmk\xfcn oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, gently guard your boundaries and keep your heart safe. Hawthorn reminds you that you can keep ill will at bay while staying open to love.",dailyMessageDe:"H\xfcte heute sanft deine Grenzen und bewahre dein Herz in Sicherheit. Der Wei\xdfdorn erinnert dich daran, dass du b\xf6se Absichten fernhalten und doch offen f\xfcr Liebe bleiben kannst.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, guarda con suavidad tus l\xedmites y mant\xe9n tu coraz\xf3n a salvo. El espino te recuerda que puedes mantener alejada la mala intenci\xf3n mientras permaneces abierto al amor.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, prot\xe8ge doucement tes limites et garde ton c\u0153ur en s\xfbret\xe9. L'aub\xe9pine te rappelle que tu peux tenir la malveillance \xe0 distance tout en restant ouvert \xe0 l'amour.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5883\u754c\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u5b89\u5168\u306b\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30b5\u30f3\u30b6\u30b7\u306f\u3001\u60aa\u610f\u3092\u9060\u3056\u3051\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3082\u611b\u306b\u958b\u3044\u3066\u3044\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, guarde com gentileza os seus limites e mantenha o cora\xe7\xe3o seguro. O espinheiro lembra voc\xea de que pode manter a m\xe1 inten\xe7\xe3o \xe0 dist\xe2ncia enquanto permanece aberto ao amor.",howToUse:"\xc7i\xe7ek ve meyvelerini kalbi destekleyen yumu\u015fak bir \xe7ay olarak demleyebilirsin. Bir dal\u0131n\u0131 e\u015fi\u011fe asarak sembolik koruma niyeti ta\u015f\u0131yabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"You may brew its flowers and berries as a gentle heart-supporting tea. Hang a sprig at your threshold to carry a symbolic intention of protection.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst seine Bl\xfcten und Beeren als sanften, herzst\xe4rkenden Tee aufbr\xfchen. H\xe4nge einen Zweig an die Schwelle, um eine symbolische Schutzabsicht zu tragen.",howToUseEs:"Puedes preparar sus flores y frutos como un t\xe9 suave que apoya el coraz\xf3n. Cuelga una ramita en el umbral para llevar una intenci\xf3n simb\xf3lica de protecci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux infuser ses fleurs et ses baies en une douce tisane qui soutient le c\u0153ur. Suspends un brin sur le seuil pour porter une intention symbolique de protection.",howToUseJa:"\u82b1\u3068\u5b9f\u3092\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u652f\u3048\u308b\u304a\u8336\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5c0f\u679d\u3092\u6238\u53e3\u306b\u639b\u3051\u3001\u5b88\u308a\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u306a\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u8fbc\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode preparar suas flores e frutos como um ch\xe1 suave que apoia o cora\xe7\xe3o. Pendure um raminho na soleira para carregar uma inten\xe7\xe3o simb\xf3lica de prote\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"S\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131m\u0131 korurken kalbimi sevgiye a\xe7\u0131k tutuyorum.",affirmationEn:"I guard my boundaries while keeping my heart open to love.",affirmationDe:"Ich h\xfcte meine Grenzen und halte mein Herz doch offen f\xfcr die Liebe.",affirmationEs:"Guardo mis l\xedmites mientras mantengo mi coraz\xf3n abierto al amor.",affirmationFr:"Je prot\xe8ge mes limites tout en gardant mon c\u0153ur ouvert \xe0 l'amour.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5883\u754c\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3001\u5fc3\u3092\u611b\u306b\u958b\u3044\u3066\u304a\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Guardo os meus limites enquanto mantenho o cora\xe7\xe3o aberto ao amor.",myth:"Roma'n\u0131n kuruldu\u011fu Tiberis k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131ndaki kutsal ormanda ya\u015fayan nympha Cama, bakire kalmaya ant i\xe7mi\u015fti; g\xf6ren herkesi pe\u015finden \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131p ormanda kaybolurdu. \xc7ift y\xfczl\xfc tanr\u0131 \u0130anus ona a\u015f\u0131k olunca, saklanan Cama'y\u0131 g\xf6r\xfcp yakalad\u0131. Ald\u0131\u011f\u0131 \u015feyin kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \u0130anus ona kap\u0131 mente\u015felerine h\xfckmetme g\xfcc\xfc ve \xe7i\xe7ekli bir akdiken dal\u0131 verdi. Bu dalla Cama, yeni do\u011fanlar\u0131n kan\u0131n\u0131 emen ku\u015f g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcml\xfc Striga'lar\u0131 evlerden uzak tuttu.",mythEn:"Cama, a nympha living in the sacred forest by the Tiber where Rome would rise, had vowed to remain a maiden; she lured all who beheld her and vanished into the woods. When the two-faced god Ianus fell in love with her, he saw the hidden Cama and caught her. In return for what he took, Ianus gave her power over the hinges of doors and a flowering branch of hawthorn. With this branch Cama kept the bird-like Strigae, who drank the blood of newborns, away from homes.",mythDe:"Cama, eine Nympha im heiligen Wald am Tiber, wo Rom entstehen sollte, hatte gelobt, Jungfrau zu bleiben; sie lockte alle, die sie erblickten, und verschwand im Wald. Als der zweigesichtige Gott Ianus sich in sie verliebte, erblickte er die verborgene Cama und ergriff sie. Als Ausgleich f\xfcr das Genommene gab Ianus ihr Macht \xfcber die T\xfcrangeln und einen bl\xfchenden Wei\xdfdornzweig. Mit diesem Zweig hielt Cama die vogelartigen Strigae, die das Blut Neugeborener tranken, von den H\xe4usern fern.",mythEs:"Cama, una nympha que viv\xeda en el bosque sagrado junto al T\xedber donde se alzar\xeda Roma, hab\xeda jurado permanecer virgen; atra\xeda a cuantos la ve\xedan y se desvanec\xeda en el bosque. Cuando el dios de dos rostros Ianus se enamor\xf3 de ella, vio a la oculta Cama y la atrap\xf3. A cambio de lo que tom\xf3, Ianus le dio poder sobre los goznes de las puertas y una rama florecida de espino. Con esa rama Cama manten\xeda alejadas de los hogares a las Strigas con forma de ave, que beb\xedan la sangre de los reci\xe9n nacidos.",mythFr:"Cama, une nympha vivant dans la for\xeat sacr\xe9e au bord du Tibre o\xf9 Rome allait na\xeetre, avait jur\xe9 de rester vierge ; elle attirait tous ceux qui la voyaient et disparaissait dans les bois. Lorsque le dieu \xe0 deux visages Ianus tomba amoureux d'elle, il vit la Cama cach\xe9e et la saisit. En \xe9change de ce qu'il avait pris, Ianus lui donna pouvoir sur les gonds des portes et une branche fleurie d'aub\xe9pine. Avec cette branche, Cama tenait \xe9loign\xe9es des foyers les Strigae \xe0 l'apparence d'oiseau, qui buvaient le sang des nouveau-n\xe9s.",mythJa:"\u30ed\u30fc\u30de\u304c\u751f\u307e\u308c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306b\u306a\u308b\u30c6\u30a3\u30d9\u30ea\u30b9\u5ddd\u306e\u307b\u3068\u308a\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u68ee\u306b\u4f4f\u3080\u30cb\u30f3\u30d5\u3001\u30ab\u30de\u306f\u3001\u51e6\u5973\u306e\u307e\u307e\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3068\u8a93\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5f7c\u5973\u3092\u898b\u305f\u8005\u3092\u7686\u304a\u3073\u304d\u5bc4\u305b\u3001\u68ee\u306e\u4e2d\u3078\u59ff\u3092\u6d88\u3057\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002\u4e8c\u3064\u306e\u9854\u3092\u6301\u3064\u795e\u30e4\u30cc\u30b9\u304c\u604b\u306b\u843d\u3061\u308b\u3068\u3001\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u30ab\u30de\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u3066\u6355\u3089\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u596a\u3063\u305f\u3082\u306e\u306e\u4ee3\u308f\u308a\u306b\u3001\u30e4\u30cc\u30b9\u306f\u6249\u306e\u8776\u756a\u3092\u53f8\u308b\u529b\u3068\u3001\u82b1\u306e\u54b2\u3044\u305f\u30b5\u30f3\u30b6\u30b7\u306e\u679d\u3092\u5f7c\u5973\u306b\u4e0e\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3053\u306e\u679d\u3067\u30ab\u30de\u306f\u3001\u65b0\u751f\u5150\u306e\u8840\u3092\u5438\u3046\u9ce5\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306a\u59ff\u306e\u30b9\u30c8\u30ea\u30ac\u3092\u5bb6\u3005\u304b\u3089\u9060\u3056\u3051\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Cama, uma nympha que vivia na floresta sagrada \xe0s margens do Tibre onde Roma se ergueria, havia jurado permanecer virgem; atra\xeda todos os que a viam e desaparecia na mata. Quando o deus de dois rostos Ianus se apaixonou por ela, viu a Cama escondida e a apanhou. Em troca do que tomou, Ianus deu a ela poder sobre as dobradi\xe7as das portas e um ramo florido de espinheiro. Com esse ramo, Cama mantinha longe dos lares as Strigas com forma de ave, que bebiam o sangue dos rec\xe9m-nascidos.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Crataegus%2C_various_species%2C_fruit.jpg/330px-Crataegus%2C_various_species%2C_fruit.jpg"},{id:"plant-083",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3e",color:"#D8C56A",name:"Arpa",nameEn:"Barley",nameDe:"Gerste",nameEs:"Cebada",nameFr:"Orge",nameJa:"\u5927\u9ea6",namePt:"Cevada",origin:"Antik Yunan & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y Anatolia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e Anat\xf3lia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["bereket","besleyici","sab\u0131r","yenilenme"],propertiesEn:["abundance","nourishing","patience","renewal"],propertiesDe:["F\xfclle","n\xe4hrend","Geduld","Erneuerung"],propertiesEs:["abundancia","nutritivo","paciencia","renovaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["abondance","nourrissant","patience","renouveau"],propertiesJa:["\u8c4a\u7a63","\u6ecb\u990a","\u5fcd\u8010","\u518d\u751f"],propertiesPt:["abund\xe2ncia","nutritivo","paci\xeancia","renova\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn kendine ve topra\u011fa sab\u0131rla g\xfcven; her tohum kendi zaman\u0131nda olgunla\u015f\u0131r. Arpa sana kaybetti\u011fin ne\u015fenin de mevsimi gelince geri d\xf6nece\u011fini hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, trust yourself and the earth with patience; every seed ripens in its own time. Barley reminds you that the joy you have lost will return when its season comes.",dailyMessageDe:"Vertraue heute dir selbst und der Erde mit Geduld; jeder Same reift zu seiner Zeit. Die Gerste erinnert dich daran, dass die Freude, die du verloren hast, zur\xfcckkehrt, wenn ihre Zeit kommt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, conf\xeda en ti y en la tierra con paciencia; cada semilla madura a su tiempo. La cebada te recuerda que la alegr\xeda que has perdido volver\xe1 cuando llegue su estaci\xf3n.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, fais confiance \xe0 toi-m\xeame et \xe0 la terre avec patience ; chaque graine m\xfbrit en son temps. L'orge te rappelle que la joie que tu as perdue reviendra quand sa saison viendra.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u5fcd\u8010\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u81ea\u5206\u3068\u5927\u5730\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3069\u306e\u7a2e\u3082\u305d\u308c\u305e\u308c\u306e\u6642\u306b\u5b9f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5927\u9ea6\u306f\u3001\u5931\u3063\u305f\u559c\u3073\u3082\u305d\u306e\u5b63\u7bc0\u304c\u6765\u308c\u3070\u623b\u3063\u3066\u304f\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, confie em voc\xea e na terra com paci\xeancia; cada semente amadurece no seu tempo. A cevada lembra voc\xea de que a alegria que perdeu voltar\xe1 quando chegar a sua esta\xe7\xe3o.",howToUse:"Tanelerini suda kaynat\u0131p besleyici bir lapa ya da arpa suyu olarak i\xe7ebilirsin. Bir avu\xe7 taneyi bereket niyetiyle topra\u011fa serpmek de eski bir gelenektir.",howToUseEn:"You may boil the grains in water and take them as a nourishing porridge or barley water. Scattering a handful onto the soil with an intention of abundance is also an old custom.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die K\xf6rner in Wasser kochen und als n\xe4hrenden Brei oder Gerstenwasser zu dir nehmen. Eine Handvoll mit der Absicht der F\xfclle auf die Erde zu streuen, ist ebenfalls ein alter Brauch.",howToUseEs:"Puedes hervir los granos en agua y tomarlos como gachas nutritivas o agua de cebada. Esparcir un pu\xf1ado sobre la tierra con intenci\xf3n de abundancia es tambi\xe9n una vieja costumbre.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux faire bouillir les grains dans l'eau et les prendre en bouillie nourrissante ou en eau d'orge. R\xe9pandre une poign\xe9e sur la terre avec une intention d'abondance est aussi une vieille coutume.",howToUseJa:"\u7c92\u3092\u6c34\u3067\u716e\u3066\u3001\u6ecb\u990a\u306e\u3042\u308b\u7ca5\u3084\u5927\u9ea6\u6e6f\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3060\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u3092\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u571f\u306b\u307e\u304f\u306e\u3082\u3001\u53e4\u304f\u304b\u3089\u306e\u7fd2\u308f\u3057\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode ferver os gr\xe3os em \xe1gua e tom\xe1-los como um mingau nutritivo ou \xe1gua de cevada. Espalhar um punhado sobre a terra com inten\xe7\xe3o de abund\xe2ncia tamb\xe9m \xe9 um costume antigo.",affirmation:"Sab\u0131rla ekiyorum, bereketin kendi zaman\u0131nda gelece\u011fine g\xfcveniyorum.",affirmationEn:"I sow with patience, trusting that abundance will come in its own time.",affirmationDe:"Ich s\xe4e mit Geduld und vertraue darauf, dass die F\xfclle zu ihrer Zeit kommt.",affirmationEs:"Siembro con paciencia, confiando en que la abundancia llegar\xe1 a su tiempo.",affirmationFr:"Je s\xe8me avec patience, confiant que l'abondance viendra en son temps.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5fcd\u8010\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u8494\u304d\u3001\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u304c\u305d\u306e\u6642\u306b\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Semeio com paci\xeancia, confiando que a abund\xe2ncia vir\xe1 no seu tempo.",myth:"Ekinlerin tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Demeter'in biricik k\u0131z\u0131 Persephone, \xf6l\xfcler \xfclkesinin tanr\u0131s\u0131 Hades taraf\u0131ndan yeralt\u0131na ka\xe7\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131. K\u0131z\u0131n\u0131 her yerde arayan Demeter kederinden g\xf6revini b\u0131rak\u0131nca toprak kurudu ve hi\xe7bir ekin bitmedi. Eleusis'te dad\u0131 Baubo, tanr\u0131\xe7ay\u0131 ne\u015felendirmek i\xe7in ona arpa suyu ikram etti; bu i\xe7ecek kederli tanr\u0131\xe7aya bir an ferahl\u0131k verdi. B\xf6ylece arpa, Demeter'in yas ve yeniden do\u011fu\u015f d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfcn, topra\u011f\u0131n bereketinin simgesi oldu.",mythEn:"Persephone, the only daughter of Demeter, goddess of the harvest, was carried off into the underworld by Hades, god of the dead. As the grieving Demeter searched everywhere and abandoned her duties, the earth dried up and no crop would grow. At Eleusis the nurse Baubo offered the goddess barley water to lift her spirits, and the drink gave the sorrowful goddess a moment of ease. So barley became the emblem of Demeter's cycle of mourning and rebirth, of the fertility of the earth.",mythDe:"Persephone, die einzige Tochter Demeters, der G\xf6ttin der Ernte, wurde von Hades, dem Gott der Toten, in die Unterwelt entf\xfchrt. W\xe4hrend die trauernde Demeter \xfcberall suchte und ihre Pflichten aufgab, vertrocknete die Erde und kein Korn wuchs. In Eleusis reichte die Amme Baubo der G\xf6ttin Gerstenwasser, um sie aufzuheitern, und der Trank schenkte der bek\xfcmmerten G\xf6ttin einen Augenblick der Erleichterung. So wurde die Gerste zum Sinnbild von Demeters Kreislauf aus Trauer und Wiedergeburt, der Fruchtbarkeit der Erde.",mythEs:"Pers\xe9fone, la \xfanica hija de Dem\xe9ter, diosa de la cosecha, fue arrebatada al inframundo por Hades, dios de los muertos. Mientras la afligida Dem\xe9ter buscaba por todas partes y abandonaba sus deberes, la tierra se sec\xf3 y ning\xfan cultivo crec\xeda. En Eleusis la nodriza Baubo ofreci\xf3 a la diosa agua de cebada para animarla, y la bebida dio a la doliente diosa un momento de alivio. As\xed la cebada se volvi\xf3 emblema del ciclo de duelo y renacimiento de Dem\xe9ter, de la fertilidad de la tierra.",mythFr:"Pers\xe9phone, l'unique fille de D\xe9m\xe9ter, d\xe9esse de la moisson, fut emport\xe9e aux enfers par Had\xe8s, dieu des morts. Tandis que D\xe9m\xe9ter afflig\xe9e cherchait partout et d\xe9laissait ses devoirs, la terre se dess\xe9cha et aucune r\xe9colte ne poussait. \xc0 \xc9leusis, la nourrice Baubo offrit \xe0 la d\xe9esse de l'eau d'orge pour la r\xe9jouir, et la boisson donna \xe0 la d\xe9esse en peine un instant de soulagement. Ainsi l'orge devint l'embl\xe8me du cycle de deuil et de renaissance de D\xe9m\xe9ter, de la fertilit\xe9 de la terre.",mythJa:"\u53ce\u7a6b\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30c7\u30e1\u30c6\u30eb\u306e\u4e00\u4eba\u5a18\u30da\u30eb\u30bb\u30dd\u30cd\u306f\u3001\u6b7b\u8005\u306e\u56fd\u306e\u795e\u30cf\u30c7\u30b9\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u5730\u4e0b\u3078\u9023\u308c\u53bb\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5606\u304d\u60b2\u3057\u3080\u30c7\u30e1\u30c6\u30eb\u304c\u5404\u5730\u3092\u63a2\u3057\u3001\u52d9\u3081\u3092\u653e\u68c4\u3059\u308b\u3068\u3001\u5927\u5730\u306f\u67af\u308c\u3001\u4f5c\u7269\u306f\u4f55\u3082\u80b2\u3061\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30a8\u30ec\u30a6\u30b7\u30b9\u3067\u4e73\u6bcd\u30d0\u30a6\u30dc\u306f\u5973\u795e\u3092\u5143\u6c17\u3065\u3051\u3088\u3046\u3068\u5927\u9ea6\u6e6f\u3092\u5dee\u3057\u51fa\u3057\u3001\u305d\u306e\u98f2\u307f\u7269\u306f\u60b2\u3057\u3080\u5973\u795e\u306b\u3072\u3068\u3068\u304d\u306e\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u5927\u9ea6\u306f\u3001\u30c7\u30e1\u30c6\u30eb\u306e\u54c0\u60bc\u3068\u518d\u751f\u306e\u5faa\u74b0\u3001\u5927\u5730\u306e\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u306a\u3063\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Pers\xe9fone, a \xfanica filha de Dem\xe9ter, deusa da colheita, foi levada ao submundo por Hades, deus dos mortos. Enquanto a aflita Dem\xe9ter procurava por toda parte e abandonava seus deveres, a terra secou e nenhuma colheita brotava. Em El\xeausis, a ama Baubo ofereceu \xe0 deusa \xe1gua de cevada para anim\xe1-la, e a bebida deu \xe0 deusa pesarosa um momento de al\xedvio. Assim a cevada tornou-se o emblema do ciclo de luto e renascimento de Dem\xe9ter, da fertilidade da terra.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Barley_%28Hordeum_vulgare%29_-_United_States_National_Arboretum_-_24_May_2009.jpg/330px-Barley_%28Hordeum_vulgare%29_-_United_States_National_Arboretum_-_24_May_2009.jpg"},{id:"plant-084",emoji:"\ud83c\udf47",color:"#6E4B8B",name:"Asma (\xdcz\xfcm)",nameEn:"Grapevine",nameDe:"Weinrebe",nameEs:"Vid",nameFr:"Vigne",nameJa:"\u3076\u3069\u3046\u306e\u6728",namePt:"Videira",origin:"Anadolu & Antik Yak\u0131n Do\u011fu",originEn:"Anatolia & Ancient Near East",originDe:"Anatolien & Alter Naher Osten",originEs:"Anatolia y Antiguo Cercano Oriente",originFr:"Anatolie et Proche-Orient ancien",originJa:"\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u30fb\u53e4\u4ee3\u8fd1\u6771",originPt:"Anat\xf3lia e Antigo Oriente Pr\xf3ximo",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u30bb\u30a4\u30af\u30e9\u30eb\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacro",properties:["ne\u015fe","bolluk","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","kutlama"],propertiesEn:["joy","abundance","transformation","celebration"],propertiesDe:["Freude","F\xfclle","Verwandlung","Feier"],propertiesEs:["alegr\xeda","abundancia","transformaci\xf3n","celebraci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["joie","abondance","transformation","c\xe9l\xe9bration"],propertiesJa:["\u559c\u3073","\u8c4a\u304b\u3055","\u5909\u5bb9","\u795d\u796d"],propertiesPt:["alegria","abund\xe2ncia","transforma\xe7\xe3o","celebra\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131n tatl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131na izin ver ve ne\u015feyi payla\u015f. Asma sana sab\u0131rla olgunla\u015fan her \u015feyin sonunda ta\u015fk\u0131n bir bollukla meyve verdi\u011fini hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, allow the sweetness of life and share your joy. The grapevine reminds you that all that ripens with patience finally bears fruit in overflowing abundance.",dailyMessageDe:"Lass heute die S\xfc\xdfe des Lebens zu und teile deine Freude. Die Weinrebe erinnert dich daran, dass alles, was mit Geduld reift, schlie\xdflich in \xfcberflie\xdfender F\xfclle Frucht tr\xe4gt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, permite la dulzura de la vida y comparte tu alegr\xeda. La vid te recuerda que todo lo que madura con paciencia da fruto al fin en abundancia desbordante.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, laisse venir la douceur de la vie et partage ta joie. La vigne te rappelle que tout ce qui m\xfbrit avec patience finit par porter du fruit dans une abondance d\xe9bordante.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u306e\u7518\u3055\u3092\u53d7\u3051\u5165\u308c\u3001\u559c\u3073\u3092\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3076\u3069\u3046\u306e\u6728\u306f\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u719f\u3059\u3082\u306e\u306f\u3084\u304c\u3066\u3042\u3075\u308c\u308b\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u3067\u5b9f\u3092\u7d50\u3076\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, permita a do\xe7ura da vida e compartilhe a sua alegria. A videira lembra voc\xea de que tudo o que amadurece com paci\xeancia por fim d\xe1 fruto em abund\xe2ncia transbordante.",howToUse:"Taze meyvelerini ya da kurusunu besleyici bir ikram olarak tadabilir, yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 yemeklerde kullanabilirsin. Bir salk\u0131m\u0131 payla\u015fmak, bollu\u011fu kutlaman\u0131n eski bir yoludur.",howToUseEn:"You may savor its fresh or dried fruit as a nourishing treat and use its leaves in cooking. Sharing a bunch is an old way to celebrate abundance.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst seine frischen oder getrockneten Fr\xfcchte als nahrhafte K\xf6stlichkeit genie\xdfen und die Bl\xe4tter beim Kochen verwenden. Eine Traube zu teilen ist ein alter Weg, F\xfclle zu feiern.",howToUseEs:"Puedes saborear su fruto fresco o seco como un manjar nutritivo y usar sus hojas en la cocina. Compartir un racimo es una vieja manera de celebrar la abundancia.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux savourer son fruit frais ou sec comme une gourmandise nourrissante et utiliser ses feuilles en cuisine. Partager une grappe est une vieille fa\xe7on de c\xe9l\xe9brer l'abondance.",howToUseJa:"\u751f\u306e\u307e\u305f\u306f\u5e72\u3057\u305f\u5b9f\u3092\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u304a\u3084\u3064\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3044\u3001\u8449\u3092\u6599\u7406\u306b\u4f7f\u3046\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u623f\u3092\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u306e\u306f\u3001\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u3092\u795d\u3046\u53e4\u304f\u304b\u3089\u306e\u3084\u308a\u65b9\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode saborear seu fruto fresco ou seco como uma guloseima nutritiva e usar suas folhas na cozinha. Partilhar um cacho \xe9 uma maneira antiga de celebrar a abund\xe2ncia.",affirmation:"Hayat\u0131n tatl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131na a\xe7\u0131\u011f\u0131m, ne\u015femi c\xf6mert\xe7e payla\u015f\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I am open to the sweetness of life and share my joy generously.",affirmationDe:"Ich bin offen f\xfcr die S\xfc\xdfe des Lebens und teile meine Freude gro\xdfz\xfcgig.",affirmationEs:"Estoy abierto a la dulzura de la vida y comparto mi alegr\xeda con generosidad.",affirmationFr:"Je suis ouvert \xe0 la douceur de la vie et je partage ma joie avec g\xe9n\xe9rosit\xe9.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u306e\u7518\u3055\u306b\u958b\u304b\u308c\u3001\u559c\u3073\u3092\u60dc\u3057\u307f\u306a\u304f\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u3002",affirmationPt:"Estou aberto \xe0 do\xe7ura da vida e compartilho a minha alegria com generosidade.",myth:"Tufan sonras\u0131nda karaya oturan gemiden inen hayvanlar yiyecek ararken, bir ke\xe7i asman\u0131n meyvelerinden yedikten sonra ne\u015feyle s\u0131\xe7ramaya ba\u015flad\u0131. Onu izleyen Nuh b\xf6ylece \xfcz\xfcm\xfc ve \u015farab\u0131n verdi\u011fi ne\u015feyi ke\u015ffetti. Nuh'un sevincini k\u0131skanan \u015feytan, kavurucu nefesiyle asmalar\u0131 kuruttu; pi\u015fman olunca da onlar\u0131 diriltmek i\xe7in diplerine yedi hayvan\u0131n kan\u0131n\u0131 d\xf6kt\xfc. B\xf6ylece bir y\u0131l sonra asmalar yeniden ye\u015ferip \xfcr\xfcn verdi.",mythEn:"After the flood, as the animals left the grounded ark to search for food, a goat began to leap about merrily after eating the fruit of the vine. Watching it, Noah thus discovered the grape and the joy that wine brings. Envious of Noah's gladness, the devil withered the vines with his scorching breath; then, repenting, he poured the blood of seven animals at their roots to revive them. So a year later the vines grew green again and bore fruit.",mythDe:"Nach der Flut, als die Tiere die gestrandete Arche verlie\xdfen, um Nahrung zu suchen, begann eine Ziege fr\xf6hlich umherzuspringen, nachdem sie die Frucht der Rebe gefressen hatte. Als Noah sie beobachtete, entdeckte er so die Traube und die Freude, die der Wein bringt. Neidisch auf Noahs Fr\xf6hlichkeit lie\xdf der Teufel die Reben mit seinem sengenden Atem verdorren; dann, voller Reue, goss er das Blut von sieben Tieren an ihre Wurzeln, um sie wiederzubeleben. So ergr\xfcnten die Reben ein Jahr sp\xe4ter erneut und trugen Frucht.",mythEs:"Tras el diluvio, mientras los animales dejaban el arca encallada para buscar alimento, una cabra comenz\xf3 a brincar alegremente despu\xe9s de comer el fruto de la vid. Al observarla, No\xe9 descubri\xf3 as\xed la uva y la alegr\xeda que da el vino. Envidioso de la dicha de No\xe9, el diablo marchit\xf3 las vides con su aliento abrasador; luego, arrepentido, verti\xf3 la sangre de siete animales en sus ra\xedces para revivirlas. As\xed, un a\xf1o despu\xe9s, las vides reverdecieron y dieron fruto.",mythFr:"Apr\xe8s le d\xe9luge, tandis que les animaux quittaient l'arche \xe9chou\xe9e pour chercher de la nourriture, une ch\xe8vre se mit \xe0 bondir joyeusement apr\xe8s avoir mang\xe9 le fruit de la vigne. En l'observant, No\xe9 d\xe9couvrit ainsi le raisin et la joie que donne le vin. Jaloux de la joie de No\xe9, le diable dess\xe9cha les vignes de son souffle br\xfblant ; puis, repentant, il versa le sang de sept animaux \xe0 leurs racines pour les ranimer. Ainsi, un an plus tard, les vignes reverdirent et port\xe8rent du fruit.",mythJa:"\u5927\u6d2a\u6c34\u306e\u3042\u3068\u3001\u5ea7\u7901\u3057\u305f\u65b9\u821f\u3092\u51fa\u305f\u52d5\u7269\u305f\u3061\u304c\u98df\u3079\u7269\u3092\u63a2\u3059\u3046\u3061\u3001\u4e00\u982d\u306e\u5c71\u7f8a\u304c\u3076\u3069\u3046\u306e\u5b9f\u3092\u98df\u3079\u3066\u967d\u6c17\u306b\u8df3\u306d\u56de\u308a\u59cb\u3081\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u305d\u308c\u3092\u898b\u305f\u30ce\u30a2\u306f\u3001\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u3076\u3069\u3046\u3068\u3001\u30ef\u30a4\u30f3\u304c\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u559c\u3073\u3092\u77e5\u3063\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30ce\u30a2\u306e\u559c\u3073\u3092\u306d\u305f\u3093\u3060\u60aa\u9b54\u306f\u3001\u713c\u3051\u3064\u304f\u606f\u3067\u3076\u3069\u3046\u306e\u6728\u3092\u67af\u3089\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u5f8c\u6094\u3057\u3066\u4e03\u3064\u306e\u52d5\u7269\u306e\u8840\u3092\u305d\u306e\u6839\u306b\u6ce8\u304e\u3001\u3088\u307f\u304c\u3048\u3089\u305b\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u4e00\u5e74\u5f8c\u3001\u3076\u3069\u3046\u306e\u6728\u306f\u518d\u3073\u7dd1\u3065\u304d\u5b9f\u3092\u7d50\u3073\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Ap\xf3s o dil\xfavio, enquanto os animais deixavam a arca encalhada em busca de alimento, uma cabra come\xe7ou a saltitar alegremente depois de comer o fruto da videira. Ao observ\xe1-la, No\xe9 descobriu assim a uva e a alegria que o vinho traz. Invejoso da alegria de No\xe9, o diabo murchou as videiras com seu sopro abrasador; depois, arrependido, derramou o sangue de sete animais em suas ra\xedzes para reviv\xea-las. Assim, um ano depois, as videiras reverdeceram e deram fruto.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Vitis_californica_with_grapes.jpg/330px-Vitis_californica_with_grapes.jpg"},{id:"plant-085",emoji:"\ud83c\udf50",color:"#C9C45E",name:"Ayva",nameEn:"Quince",nameDe:"Quitte",nameEs:"Membrillo",nameFr:"Coing",nameJa:"\u30de\u30eb\u30e1\u30ed",namePt:"Marmelo",origin:"Antik Yunan & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y Anatolia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e Anat\xf3lia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["a\u015fk","ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k","s\xf6z","tatl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["love","devotion","vow","sweetness"],propertiesDe:["Liebe","Hingabe","Gel\xfcbde","S\xfc\xdfe"],propertiesEs:["amor","devoci\xf3n","voto","dulzura"],propertiesFr:["amour","d\xe9votion","serment","douceur"],propertiesJa:["\u611b","\u732e\u8eab","\u8a93\u3044","\u7518\u3084\u304b\u3055"],propertiesPt:["amor","devo\xe7\xe3o","voto","do\xe7ura"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn s\xf6zlerinin ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131 g\xfcce dikkat et; bir niyet, kalpten s\xf6ylendi\u011finde ger\xe7e\u011fe d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr. Ayva sana sevgiyle verilen s\xf6z\xfcn zamanla olgunla\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, notice the power your words carry; an intention, spoken from the heart, turns into reality. Quince reminds you that a promise given with love ripens in time.",dailyMessageDe:"Achte heute auf die Kraft, die deine Worte tragen; eine Absicht, von Herzen ausgesprochen, wird zur Wirklichkeit. Die Quitte erinnert dich daran, dass ein mit Liebe gegebenes Versprechen mit der Zeit reift.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, advierte el poder que llevan tus palabras; una intenci\xf3n, dicha desde el coraz\xf3n, se vuelve realidad. El membrillo te recuerda que una promesa dada con amor madura con el tiempo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, remarque le pouvoir que portent tes mots ; une intention, dite du c\u0153ur, devient r\xe9alit\xe9. Le coing te rappelle qu'une promesse donn\xe9e avec amour m\xfbrit avec le temps.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u304c\u6301\u3064\u529b\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5fc3\u304b\u3089\u8a9e\u3089\u308c\u305f\u610f\u56f3\u306f\u73fe\u5b9f\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30de\u30eb\u30e1\u30ed\u306f\u3001\u611b\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u4ea4\u308f\u3057\u305f\u7d04\u675f\u306f\u6642\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u719f\u3059\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, perceba o poder que as suas palavras carregam; uma inten\xe7\xe3o, dita do cora\xe7\xe3o, torna-se realidade. O marmelo lembra voc\xea de que uma promessa dada com amor amadurece com o tempo.",howToUse:"Olgun meyvesini bal ya da \u015fekerle pi\u015firip tatl\u0131 bir re\xe7el ya da ho\u015faf olarak tadabilirsin. Bir ayvay\u0131 sevgiyle payla\u015fmak, ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may cook the ripe fruit with honey or sugar into a sweet jam or compote. Sharing a quince with love is a gentle gesture that honors an intention of devotion.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die reife Frucht mit Honig oder Zucker zu einer s\xfc\xdfen Marmelade oder einem Kompott kochen. Eine Quitte mit Liebe zu teilen ist eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht der Hingabe ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes cocinar el fruto maduro con miel o az\xfacar en una dulce mermelada o compota. Compartir un membrillo con amor es un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de devoci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux cuire le fruit m\xfbr avec du miel ou du sucre en une douce confiture ou compote. Partager un coing avec amour est un geste tendre qui honore une intention de d\xe9votion.",howToUseJa:"\u719f\u3057\u305f\u5b9f\u3092\u8702\u871c\u3084\u7802\u7cd6\u3067\u716e\u3066\u3001\u7518\u3044\u30b8\u30e3\u30e0\u3084\u30b3\u30f3\u30dd\u30fc\u30c8\u306b\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30de\u30eb\u30e1\u30ed\u3092\u611b\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u732e\u8eab\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode cozinhar o fruto maduro com mel ou a\xe7\xfacar em uma doce geleia ou compota. Partilhar um marmelo com amor \xe9 um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de devo\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"S\xf6zlerimin g\xfcc\xfcne sayg\u0131 duyuyorum, sevgiyle verdi\u011fim s\xf6z\xfc onurland\u0131r\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I respect the power of my words and honor the promise I give with love.",affirmationDe:"Ich achte die Kraft meiner Worte und ehre das Versprechen, das ich mit Liebe gebe.",affirmationEs:"Respeto el poder de mis palabras y honro la promesa que doy con amor.",affirmationFr:"Je respecte le pouvoir de mes mots et j'honore la promesse que je donne avec amour.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u306e\u529b\u3092\u5c0a\u3073\u3001\u611b\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u4ea4\u308f\u3057\u305f\u7d04\u675f\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3002",affirmationPt:"Respeito o poder das minhas palavras e honro a promessa que dou com amor.",myth:"Gen\xe7 Akontios, Delos \u015fenliklerinde g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfc g\xfczel Kydippe'ye a\u015f\u0131k oldu. Bir ayvan\u0131n \xfczerine 'Akontios ile evlenece\u011fime Artemis tap\u0131na\u011f\u0131 \xfczerine yemin ederim' diye kaz\u0131y\u0131p k\u0131z\u0131n \xf6n\xfcne att\u0131. Kydippe, yaz\u0131y\u0131 fark\u0131nda olmadan y\xfcksek sesle okuyunca, tanr\u0131\xe7an\u0131n \xf6n\xfcnde bir ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k yemini etmi\u015f oldu. Bu y\xfczden ayva, antik \xe7a\u011fdan beri a\u015fk\u0131n ve evlilik s\xf6z\xfcn\xfcn simgesi say\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r.",mythEn:"Young Akontios fell in love with the beautiful Kydippe whom he saw at the festival of Delos. He carved on a quince, 'I swear by the temple of Artemis that I will marry Akontios,' and tossed it before her. When Kydippe unknowingly read the words aloud, she had sworn a vow of devotion before the goddess. For this reason the quince has, since antiquity, been seen as the emblem of love and the marriage vow.",mythDe:"Der junge Akontios verliebte sich in die sch\xf6ne Kydippe, die er beim Fest von Delos sah. Er ritzte in eine Quitte: 'Ich schw\xf6re beim Tempel der Artemis, dass ich Akontios heiraten werde', und warf sie ihr vor die F\xfc\xdfe. Als Kydippe die Worte unwissentlich laut vorlas, hatte sie vor der G\xf6ttin ein Gel\xfcbde der Hingabe abgelegt. Darum gilt die Quitte seit der Antike als Sinnbild der Liebe und des Ehegel\xfcbdes.",mythEs:"El joven Akontios se enamor\xf3 de la bella Kydippe, a quien vio en la fiesta de Delos. Grab\xf3 en un membrillo: 'Juro por el templo de Artemisa que me casar\xe9 con Akontios', y lo arroj\xf3 ante ella. Cuando Kydippe, sin saberlo, ley\xf3 las palabras en voz alta, hab\xeda hecho un voto de devoci\xf3n ante la diosa. Por ello el membrillo ha sido, desde la antig\xfcedad, emblema del amor y del voto matrimonial.",mythFr:"Le jeune Akontios tomba amoureux de la belle Kydippe qu'il vit \xe0 la f\xeate de D\xe9los. Il grava sur un coing : 'Je jure par le temple d'Art\xe9mis que j'\xe9pouserai Akontios', et le lan\xe7a devant elle. Quand Kydippe, \xe0 son insu, lut les mots \xe0 voix haute, elle avait prononc\xe9 un serment de d\xe9votion devant la d\xe9esse. C'est pourquoi le coing est, depuis l'Antiquit\xe9, l'embl\xe8me de l'amour et du serment de mariage.",mythJa:"\u82e5\u304d\u30a2\u30b3\u30f3\u30c6\u30a3\u30aa\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u30c7\u30ed\u30b9\u306e\u796d\u308a\u3067\u898b\u305f\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u30ad\u30e5\u30c7\u30a3\u30c3\u30da\u306b\u604b\u3092\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5f7c\u306f\u30de\u30eb\u30e1\u30ed\u306b\u300c\u30a2\u30eb\u30c6\u30df\u30b9\u306e\u795e\u6bbf\u306b\u304b\u3051\u3066\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u30a2\u30b3\u30f3\u30c6\u30a3\u30aa\u30b9\u3068\u7d50\u5a5a\u3059\u308b\u3068\u8a93\u3046\u300d\u3068\u523b\u307f\u3001\u5f7c\u5973\u306e\u524d\u306b\u6295\u3052\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30ad\u30e5\u30c7\u30a3\u30c3\u30da\u304c\u77e5\u3089\u305a\u306b\u305d\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u3092\u58f0\u306b\u51fa\u3057\u3066\u8aad\u3080\u3068\u3001\u5973\u795e\u306e\u524d\u3067\u732e\u8eab\u306e\u8a93\u3044\u3092\u7acb\u3066\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002\u305d\u306e\u305f\u3081\u30de\u30eb\u30e1\u30ed\u306f\u3001\u53e4\u4ee3\u3088\u308a\u611b\u3068\u7d50\u5a5a\u306e\u8a93\u3044\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3066\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"O jovem Akontios apaixonou-se pela bela Kydippe que viu na festa de Delos. Ele gravou num marmelo: 'Juro pelo templo de \xc1rtemis que me casarei com Akontios', e o lan\xe7ou diante dela. Quando Kydippe, sem saber, leu as palavras em voz alta, havia feito um voto de devo\xe7\xe3o diante da deusa. Por isso o marmelo tem sido, desde a antiguidade, o emblema do amor e do voto de casamento.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Pancrace_Bessa00.jpg/330px-Pancrace_Bessa00.jpg"},{id:"plant-086",emoji:"\ud83e\uded8",color:"#9CA86B",name:"Bakla",nameEn:"Broad Bean",nameDe:"Dicke Bohne",nameEs:"Haba",nameFr:"F\xe8ve",nameJa:"\u30bd\u30e9\u30de\u30e1",namePt:"Fava",origin:"Antik Roma & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Rome & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Rom & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Roma y Anatolia",originFr:"Rome antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ed\u30fc\u30de\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Roma Antiga e Anat\xf3lia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["koruma","ar\u0131nma","atalara sayg\u0131","besleyici"],propertiesEn:["protection","cleansing","honoring ancestors","nourishing"],propertiesDe:["Schutz","Reinigung","Ahnenehrung","n\xe4hrend"],propertiesEs:["protecci\xf3n","purificaci\xf3n","honra a los ancestros","nutritivo"],propertiesFr:["protection","purification","honorer les anc\xeatres","nourrissant"],propertiesJa:["\u5b88\u8b77","\u6d44\u5316","\u5148\u7956\u3092\u656c\u3046","\u6ecb\u990a"],propertiesPt:["prote\xe7\xe3o","purifica\xe7\xe3o","honrar os ancestrais","nutritivo"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ge\xe7mi\u015fine ve ge\xe7ip gidenlere sayg\u0131yla bir an ay\u0131r, sonra y\xfcz\xfcn\xfc hafif\xe7e gelece\u011fe d\xf6n. Bakla sana huzurun, eskiyi onurland\u0131r\u0131p nazik\xe7e b\u0131rakmaktan ge\xe7ti\u011fini hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, take a moment to honor your past and those who have passed, then turn your face gently toward the future. The broad bean reminds you that peace comes from honoring the old and gently letting it go.",dailyMessageDe:"Nimm dir heute einen Moment, um deine Vergangenheit und die Verstorbenen zu ehren, und wende dann dein Gesicht sanft der Zukunft zu. Die dicke Bohne erinnert dich daran, dass Frieden daraus entsteht, das Alte zu ehren und es sanft loszulassen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, t\xf3mate un momento para honrar tu pasado y a quienes partieron, y luego vuelve el rostro con suavidad hacia el futuro. El haba te recuerda que la paz nace de honrar lo antiguo y soltarlo con dulzura.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, prends un instant pour honorer ton pass\xe9 et ceux qui sont partis, puis tourne doucement ton visage vers l'avenir. La f\xe8ve te rappelle que la paix na\xeet d'honorer l'ancien et de le laisser partir avec douceur.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u904e\u53bb\u3068\u65c5\u7acb\u3063\u305f\u4eba\u3005\u3092\u656c\u3046\u6642\u3092\u3072\u3068\u3068\u304d\u6301\u3061\u3001\u305d\u308c\u304b\u3089\u305d\u3063\u3068\u9854\u3092\u672a\u6765\u3078\u5411\u3051\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30bd\u30e9\u30de\u30e1\u306f\u3001\u53e4\u3044\u3082\u306e\u3092\u656c\u3044\u3001\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u624b\u653e\u3059\u3053\u3068\u304b\u3089\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u304c\u751f\u307e\u308c\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, reserve um momento para honrar o seu passado e os que partiram, e depois volte o rosto com gentileza para o futuro. A fava lembra voc\xea de que a paz nasce de honrar o antigo e solt\xe1-lo com delicadeza.",howToUse:"Tanelerini suda pi\u015firip besleyici bir yemek olarak tadabilirsin. Atalar\u0131n\u0131 anmak i\xe7in bir avu\xe7 baklay\u0131 sembolik bir sayg\u0131 jesti olarak bir kenara koyabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"You may cook the beans in water and enjoy them as a nourishing dish. To remember your ancestors, you may set aside a handful of beans as a symbolic gesture of respect.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die Bohnen in Wasser kochen und als nahrhaftes Gericht genie\xdfen. Um deiner Ahnen zu gedenken, kannst du eine Handvoll Bohnen als symbolische Geste des Respekts beiseitelegen.",howToUseEs:"Puedes cocinar las habas en agua y disfrutarlas como un plato nutritivo. Para recordar a tus ancestros, puedes apartar un pu\xf1ado de habas como gesto simb\xf3lico de respeto.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux cuire les f\xe8ves dans l'eau et les d\xe9guster en plat nourrissant. Pour te souvenir de tes anc\xeatres, tu peux mettre de c\xf4t\xe9 une poign\xe9e de f\xe8ves en geste symbolique de respect.",howToUseJa:"\u8c46\u3092\u6c34\u3067\u716e\u3066\u3001\u6ecb\u990a\u306e\u3042\u308b\u6599\u7406\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5148\u7956\u3092\u5072\u3076\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3001\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u306e\u8c46\u3092\u656c\u610f\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3057\u3066\u8107\u306b\u7f6e\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode cozinhar as favas em \xe1gua e apreci\xe1-las como um prato nutritivo. Para lembrar os seus ancestrais, pode reservar um punhado de favas como gesto simb\xf3lico de respeito.",affirmation:"Ge\xe7mi\u015fi sayg\u0131yla onurland\u0131r\u0131yorum, huzurla bug\xfcne d\xf6n\xfcyorum.",affirmationEn:"I honor the past with respect and return to the present in peace.",affirmationDe:"Ich ehre die Vergangenheit mit Respekt und kehre in Frieden in die Gegenwart zur\xfcck.",affirmationEs:"Honro el pasado con respeto y vuelvo al presente en paz.",affirmationFr:"J'honore le pass\xe9 avec respect et je reviens au pr\xe9sent en paix.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u904e\u53bb\u3092\u656c\u610f\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u79f0\u3048\u3001\u5b89\u3089\u304b\u306b\u4eca\u3078\u3068\u623b\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Honro o passado com respeito e volto ao presente em paz.",myth:"Roma'da \xf6l\xfclerin hayaletlerine 'Lemurlar' denirdi; onlar\u0131 y\u0131l boyunca uzak tutmak i\xe7in her May\u0131s Lemuria bayram\u0131 kutlan\u0131rd\u0131. Evin reisi ellerini y\u0131kay\u0131p \xe7\u0131plak ayakla y\xfcr\xfcr, ard\u0131na bakmadan yola bakla taneleri b\u0131rak\u0131r ve dokuz kez 'bu baklalarla kendimin ve ailemin zekat\u0131n\u0131 \xf6d\xfcyorum' derdi. Lemurlar\u0131n bu baklalar\u0131 toplay\u0131p bir y\u0131l boyunca evi rahats\u0131z etmeyece\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Ekinler tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Demeter, bakla yeti\u015ftiricili\u011finin \xf6\u011freticisi say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131.",mythEn:"In Rome the ghosts of the dead were called 'Lemures'; to keep them at bay all year, the festival of Lemuria was held each May. The head of the household washed his hands and walked barefoot, dropping broad beans along the path without looking back, repeating nine times, 'with these beans I pay the dues of myself and my family.' It was believed the Lemures would gather these beans and not trouble the home for a year. Demeter, goddess of the harvest, was held to be the teacher of bean-growing.",mythDe:"In Rom nannte man die Geister der Toten 'Lemures'; um sie das ganze Jahr fernzuhalten, wurde jeden Mai das Lemuria-Fest gefeiert. Das Familienoberhaupt wusch sich die H\xe4nde und ging barfu\xdf, lie\xdf ohne zur\xfcckzublicken Bohnen auf den Weg fallen und wiederholte neunmal: 'Mit diesen Bohnen begleiche ich die Schuld meiner selbst und meiner Familie.' Man glaubte, die Lemures w\xfcrden diese Bohnen sammeln und das Haus ein Jahr lang nicht st\xf6ren. Demeter, die G\xf6ttin der Ernte, galt als Lehrerin des Bohnenanbaus.",mythEs:"En Roma a los esp\xedritus de los muertos se les llamaba 'Lemures'; para mantenerlos alejados todo el a\xf1o, cada mayo se celebraba la fiesta de Lemuria. El cabeza de familia se lavaba las manos y caminaba descalzo, dejando habas por el camino sin mirar atr\xe1s, repitiendo nueve veces: 'con estas habas pago la deuda de m\xed mismo y de mi familia.' Se cre\xeda que los Lemures recoger\xedan esas habas y no molestar\xedan el hogar durante un a\xf1o. Dem\xe9ter, diosa de la cosecha, era tenida por la maestra del cultivo del haba.",mythFr:"\xc0 Rome, on appelait 'L\xe9mures' les esprits des morts ; pour les tenir \xe0 distance toute l'ann\xe9e, on c\xe9l\xe9brait chaque mai la f\xeate des Lemuria. Le chef de famille se lavait les mains et marchait pieds nus, laissant tomber des f\xe8ves le long du chemin sans regarder en arri\xe8re, r\xe9p\xe9tant neuf fois : 'avec ces f\xe8ves, j'acquitte la dette de moi-m\xeame et de ma famille.' On croyait que les L\xe9mures ramasseraient ces f\xe8ves et ne troubleraient pas la maison pendant un an. D\xe9m\xe9ter, d\xe9esse de la moisson, \xe9tait tenue pour la ma\xeetresse de la culture de la f\xe8ve.",mythJa:"\u30ed\u30fc\u30de\u3067\u306f\u6b7b\u8005\u306e\u970a\u3092\u300c\u30ec\u30e0\u30ec\u30b9\u300d\u3068\u547c\u3073\u3001\u4e00\u5e74\u4e2d\u305d\u308c\u3089\u3092\u9060\u3056\u3051\u308b\u305f\u3081\u3001\u6bce\u5e74\u4e94\u6708\u306b\u30ec\u30e0\u30ea\u30a2\u796d\u304c\u884c\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5bb6\u9577\u306f\u624b\u3092\u6d17\u3044\u3001\u88f8\u8db3\u3067\u6b69\u304d\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3001\u632f\u308a\u8fd4\u3089\u305a\u306b\u9053\u306b\u30bd\u30e9\u30de\u30e1\u3092\u307e\u304d\u3001\u300c\u3053\u306e\u8c46\u3067\u79c1\u3068\u5bb6\u65cf\u306e\u8ca0\u50b5\u3092\u652f\u6255\u3046\u300d\u3068\u4e5d\u5ea6\u7e70\u308a\u8fd4\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30ec\u30e0\u30ec\u30b9\u306f\u3053\u306e\u8c46\u3092\u62fe\u3044\u3001\u4e00\u5e74\u9593\u5bb6\u3092\u7169\u308f\u305b\u306a\u3044\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u53ce\u7a6b\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30c7\u30e1\u30c6\u30eb\u306f\u3001\u30bd\u30e9\u30de\u30e1\u683d\u57f9\u306e\u5e2b\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Em Roma, os esp\xedritos dos mortos eram chamados 'L\xeamures'; para mant\xea-los afastados o ano todo, todo m\xeas de maio celebrava-se a festa de Lem\xfaria. O chefe da fam\xedlia lavava as m\xe3os e caminhava descal\xe7o, deixando cair favas pelo caminho sem olhar para tr\xe1s, repetindo nove vezes: 'com estas favas pago a d\xedvida de mim e da minha fam\xedlia.' Acreditava-se que os L\xeamures recolheriam essas favas e n\xe3o perturbariam o lar por um ano. Dem\xe9ter, deusa da colheita, era tida como a mestra do cultivo da fava.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Illustration_Vicia_faba1.jpg/330px-Illustration_Vicia_faba1.jpg"},{id:"plant-087",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3e",color:"#E0C964",name:"Bu\u011fday",nameEn:"Wheat",nameDe:"Weizen",nameEs:"Trigo",nameFr:"Bl\xe9",nameJa:"\u5c0f\u9ea6",namePt:"Trigo",origin:"Antik Yunan & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y Anatolia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e Anat\xf3lia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["bereket","ya\u015fam d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc","besleyici","kutsall\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["abundance","life cycle","nourishing","sacredness"],propertiesDe:["F\xfclle","Lebenszyklus","n\xe4hrend","Heiligkeit"],propertiesEs:["abundancia","ciclo de la vida","nutritivo","sacralidad"],propertiesFr:["abondance","cycle de la vie","nourrissant","sacralit\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u8c4a\u7a63","\u751f\u547d\u306e\u5faa\u74b0","\u6ecb\u990a","\u795e\u8056"],propertiesPt:["abund\xe2ncia","ciclo da vida","nutritivo","sacralidade"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ya\u015fam\u0131n do\u011fum, olgunla\u015fma ve yeniden ba\u015flama d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcne g\xfcven. Bu\u011fday sana her sonun yeni bir ekim, her hasad\u0131n bir arma\u011fan oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, trust the cycle of life: birth, ripening and beginning anew. Wheat reminds you that every ending is a new sowing and every harvest a gift.",dailyMessageDe:"Vertraue heute dem Kreislauf des Lebens: Geburt, Reifung und Neubeginn. Der Weizen erinnert dich daran, dass jedes Ende eine neue Aussaat und jede Ernte ein Geschenk ist.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, conf\xeda en el ciclo de la vida: nacimiento, madurez y nuevo comienzo. El trigo te recuerda que cada final es una nueva siembra y cada cosecha un regalo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, fais confiance au cycle de la vie : naissance, maturation et renouveau. Le bl\xe9 te rappelle que chaque fin est un nouveau semis et chaque r\xe9colte un don.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u8a95\u751f\u30fb\u6210\u719f\u30fb\u518d\u51fa\u767a\u3068\u3044\u3046\u751f\u547d\u306e\u5faa\u74b0\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5c0f\u9ea6\u306f\u3001\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u7d42\u308f\u308a\u304c\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u7a2e\u307e\u304d\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u53ce\u7a6b\u304c\u8d08\u308a\u7269\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, confie no ciclo da vida: nascimento, amadurecimento e recome\xe7o. O trigo lembra voc\xea de que todo fim \xe9 uma nova semeadura e toda colheita um presente.",howToUse:"Tanelerini \xf6\u011f\xfct\xfcp ekmek ya da lapa olarak besleyici bi\xe7imde t\xfcketebilirsin. Bir demet ba\u015fa\u011f\u0131 evinde bulundurmak, bereket ve \u015f\xfckran niyetini ta\u015f\u0131yan eski bir gelenektir.",howToUseEn:"You may grind the grains and eat them nourishingly as bread or porridge. Keeping a sheaf of ears at home is an old custom carrying an intention of abundance and gratitude.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die K\xf6rner mahlen und sie als Brot oder Brei n\xe4hrend verzehren. Eine Garbe \xc4hren zu Hause aufzubewahren ist ein alter Brauch, der eine Absicht der F\xfclle und Dankbarkeit tr\xe4gt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes moler los granos y comerlos de forma nutritiva como pan o gachas. Tener un manojo de espigas en casa es una vieja costumbre que lleva una intenci\xf3n de abundancia y gratitud.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux moudre les grains et les consommer de fa\xe7on nourrissante en pain ou en bouillie. Garder une gerbe d'\xe9pis chez toi est une vieille coutume portant une intention d'abondance et de gratitude.",howToUseJa:"\u7c92\u3092\u633d\u3044\u3066\u3001\u30d1\u30f3\u3084\u7ca5\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6ecb\u990a\u8c4a\u304b\u306b\u98df\u3079\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u9ea6\u306e\u7a42\u306e\u675f\u3092\u5bb6\u306b\u7f6e\u304f\u306e\u306f\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u611f\u8b1d\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u8fbc\u3081\u305f\u53e4\u304f\u304b\u3089\u306e\u7fd2\u308f\u3057\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode moer os gr\xe3os e consumi-los de forma nutritiva como p\xe3o ou mingau. Manter um feixe de espigas em casa \xe9 um costume antigo que carrega uma inten\xe7\xe3o de abund\xe2ncia e gratid\xe3o.",affirmation:"Ya\u015fam\u0131n d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcne g\xfcveniyorum, her hasad\u0131 \u015f\xfckranla kucakl\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I trust the cycle of life and embrace every harvest with gratitude.",affirmationDe:"Ich vertraue dem Kreislauf des Lebens und nehme jede Ernte mit Dankbarkeit an.",affirmationEs:"Conf\xedo en el ciclo de la vida y abrazo cada cosecha con gratitud.",affirmationFr:"Je fais confiance au cycle de la vie et j'accueille chaque r\xe9colte avec gratitude.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u751f\u547d\u306e\u5faa\u74b0\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3057\u3001\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u53ce\u7a6b\u3092\u611f\u8b1d\u3067\u8fce\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Confio no ciclo da vida e acolho cada colheita com gratid\xe3o.",myth:"Eski Yunan'da bu\u011fday ba\u015fa\u011f\u0131 topra\u011f\u0131n rahmini simgeler; ekimi, b\xfcy\xfcmesi ve hasad\u0131yla do\u011fumu, \xf6l\xfcm\xfc ve dirili\u015fi temsil eder. Ekili topra\u011f\u0131n koruyucusu Demeter ayn\u0131 zamanda bu\u011fday tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r ve tasvirlerinde elinde bu\u011fday ba\u015fa\u011f\u0131yla g\xf6sterilir. Tanr\u0131\xe7a bu ba\u015fak arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla insanlara hayat\u0131n s\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011fretmi\u015ftir. Rahipler bir kurban sunmadan \xf6nce kurban\u0131n ba\u015f\u0131na bu\u011fday ya da un serperek onu kutsarlard\u0131.",mythEn:"In ancient Greece the ear of wheat symbolized the womb of the earth; through its sowing, growth and harvest it represented birth, death and resurrection. Demeter, guardian of the tilled soil, is also the goddess of wheat and is depicted holding an ear of grain. Through this ear the goddess taught humankind the mysteries of life. Before offering a sacrifice, priests would consecrate the victim by sprinkling wheat or flour upon its head.",mythDe:"Im antiken Griechenland war die Weizen\xe4hre Sinnbild des Scho\xdfes der Erde; durch Aussaat, Wachstum und Ernte stand sie f\xfcr Geburt, Tod und Auferstehung. Demeter, H\xfcterin des bestellten Bodens, ist auch die G\xf6ttin des Weizens und wird mit einer \xc4hre in der Hand dargestellt. Durch diese \xc4hre lehrte die G\xf6ttin die Menschen die Geheimnisse des Lebens. Vor einem Opfer weihten die Priester das Opfertier, indem sie Weizen oder Mehl auf seinen Kopf streuten.",mythEs:"En la antigua Grecia la espiga de trigo simbolizaba el vientre de la tierra; por su siembra, crecimiento y cosecha representaba el nacimiento, la muerte y la resurrecci\xf3n. Dem\xe9ter, guardiana del suelo cultivado, es tambi\xe9n la diosa del trigo y se la representa sosteniendo una espiga. Mediante esa espiga la diosa ense\xf1\xf3 a los humanos los misterios de la vida. Antes de ofrecer un sacrificio, los sacerdotes consagraban a la v\xedctima esparciendo trigo o harina sobre su cabeza.",mythFr:"Dans la Gr\xe8ce antique, l'\xe9pi de bl\xe9 symbolisait le ventre de la terre ; par son semis, sa croissance et sa moisson, il repr\xe9sentait la naissance, la mort et la r\xe9surrection. D\xe9m\xe9ter, gardienne du sol cultiv\xe9, est aussi la d\xe9esse du bl\xe9 et on la repr\xe9sente tenant un \xe9pi. Par cet \xe9pi, la d\xe9esse enseignait aux hommes les myst\xe8res de la vie. Avant d'offrir un sacrifice, les pr\xeatres consacraient la victime en r\xe9pandant du bl\xe9 ou de la farine sur sa t\xeate.",mythJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5c0f\u9ea6\u306e\u7a42\u306f\u5927\u5730\u306e\u80ce\u3092\u8c61\u5fb4\u3057\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7a2e\u307e\u304d\u30fb\u6210\u9577\u30fb\u53ce\u7a6b\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u8a95\u751f\u30fb\u6b7b\u30fb\u5fa9\u6d3b\u3092\u8868\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u8015\u3055\u308c\u305f\u571f\u5730\u3092\u5b88\u308b\u30c7\u30e1\u30c6\u30eb\u306f\u5c0f\u9ea6\u306e\u5973\u795e\u3067\u3082\u3042\u308a\u3001\u7a42\u3092\u624b\u306b\u3057\u305f\u59ff\u3067\u63cf\u304b\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5973\u795e\u306f\u3053\u306e\u7a42\u3092\u901a\u3057\u3066\u4eba\u3005\u306b\u751f\u547d\u306e\u795e\u79d8\u3092\u6559\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u53f8\u796d\u306f\u4f9b\u7269\u3092\u6367\u3052\u308b\u524d\u306b\u3001\u305d\u306e\u982d\u306b\u5c0f\u9ea6\u3084\u7c89\u3092\u3075\u308a\u304b\u3051\u3066\u6e05\u3081\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na Gr\xe9cia antiga, a espiga de trigo simbolizava o ventre da terra; por sua semeadura, crescimento e colheita representava o nascimento, a morte e a ressurrei\xe7\xe3o. Dem\xe9ter, guardi\xe3 do solo cultivado, \xe9 tamb\xe9m a deusa do trigo e \xe9 retratada segurando uma espiga. Por meio dessa espiga, a deusa ensinou aos humanos os mist\xe9rios da vida. Antes de oferecer um sacrif\xedcio, os sacerdotes consagravam a v\xedtima espalhando trigo ou farinha sobre sua cabe\xe7a.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Vehn%C3%A4pelto_6.jpg/330px-Vehn%C3%A4pelto_6.jpg"},{id:"plant-088",emoji:"\ud83c\udf37",color:"#B06FA8",name:"\xc7i\u011fdem",nameEn:"Crocus",nameDe:"Krokus",nameEs:"Azafr\xe1n silvestre",nameFr:"Crocus",nameJa:"\u30af\u30ed\u30c3\u30ab\u30b9",namePt:"A\xe7afr\xe3o-bravo",origin:"Antik Yunan & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y Anatolia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e Anat\xf3lia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["yeniden do\u011fu\u015f","umut","yenilenme","bahar m\xfcjdesi"],propertiesEn:["rebirth","hope","renewal","herald of spring"],propertiesDe:["Wiedergeburt","Hoffnung","Erneuerung","Fr\xfchlingsbote"],propertiesEs:["renacimiento","esperanza","renovaci\xf3n","heraldo de la primavera"],propertiesFr:["renaissance","espoir","renouveau","messager du printemps"],propertiesJa:["\u518d\u751f","\u5e0c\u671b","\u5237\u65b0","\u6625\u306e\u4fbf\u308a"],propertiesPt:["renascimento","esperan\xe7a","renova\xe7\xe3o","arauto da primavera"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn karlar\u0131n alt\u0131ndan \xe7\u0131kan ilk \xe7i\xe7ek gibi cesur ol; en zorlu k\u0131\u015ftan sonra bile yeniden a\xe7abilirsin. \xc7i\u011fdem sana umudun her zaman topra\u011f\u0131n alt\u0131nda bekledi\u011fini hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, be brave like the first flower that pushes up through the snow; even after the harshest winter you can bloom again. Crocus reminds you that hope is always waiting beneath the soil.",dailyMessageDe:"Sei heute mutig wie die erste Blume, die sich durch den Schnee schiebt; selbst nach dem h\xe4rtesten Winter kannst du wieder erbl\xfchen. Der Krokus erinnert dich daran, dass die Hoffnung stets unter der Erde wartet.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, s\xe9 valiente como la primera flor que asoma entre la nieve; incluso tras el invierno m\xe1s duro puedes volver a florecer. El azafr\xe1n silvestre te recuerda que la esperanza siempre aguarda bajo la tierra.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, sois courageux comme la premi\xe8re fleur qui perce la neige ; m\xeame apr\xe8s l'hiver le plus rude, tu peux refleurir. Le crocus te rappelle que l'espoir attend toujours sous la terre.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u96ea\u3092\u62bc\u3057\u306e\u3051\u3066\u9854\u3092\u51fa\u3059\u6700\u521d\u306e\u82b1\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u52c7\u6562\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3069\u3093\u306a\u306b\u53b3\u3057\u3044\u51ac\u306e\u3042\u3068\u3067\u3082\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u307e\u305f\u54b2\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30af\u30ed\u30c3\u30ab\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u5e0c\u671b\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u571f\u306e\u4e0b\u3067\u5f85\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, seja corajoso como a primeira flor que rompe a neve; mesmo ap\xf3s o inverno mais rigoroso voc\xea pode florescer de novo. O a\xe7afr\xe3o-bravo lembra voc\xea de que a esperan\xe7a sempre espera sob a terra.",howToUse:"\u0130lkbaharda a\xe7an \xe7i\xe7eklerini bah\xe7ende ya da saks\u0131da yeti\u015ftirip yenilenme niyetiyle seyredebilirsin. Bir \xe7i\u011fdem so\u011fan\u0131n\u0131 topra\u011fa g\xf6mmek, umudun simgesel bir ekimidir.",howToUseEn:"You may grow its spring-blooming flowers in your garden or a pot and behold them with an intention of renewal. Planting a crocus bulb in the soil is a symbolic sowing of hope.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst seine im Fr\xfchling bl\xfchenden Bl\xfcten im Garten oder Topf ziehen und sie mit einer Absicht der Erneuerung betrachten. Eine Krokuszwiebel in die Erde zu setzen ist eine symbolische Aussaat der Hoffnung.",howToUseEs:"Puedes cultivar sus flores de primavera en el jard\xedn o en una maceta y contemplarlas con una intenci\xf3n de renovaci\xf3n. Plantar un bulbo de azafr\xe1n silvestre en la tierra es una siembra simb\xf3lica de esperanza.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux cultiver ses fleurs printani\xe8res au jardin ou en pot et les contempler avec une intention de renouveau. Planter un bulbe de crocus dans la terre est un semis symbolique d'espoir.",howToUseJa:"\u6625\u306b\u54b2\u304f\u82b1\u3092\u5ead\u3084\u9262\u3067\u80b2\u3066\u3001\u5237\u65b0\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u773a\u3081\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30af\u30ed\u30c3\u30ab\u30b9\u306e\u7403\u6839\u3092\u571f\u306b\u690d\u3048\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u5e0c\u671b\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u306a\u7a2e\u307e\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode cultivar suas flores que desabrocham na primavera no jardim ou em um vaso e contempl\xe1-las com uma inten\xe7\xe3o de renova\xe7\xe3o. Plantar um bulbo de a\xe7afr\xe3o-bravo na terra \xe9 uma semeadura simb\xf3lica de esperan\xe7a.",affirmation:"En zorlu k\u0131\u015ftan sonra yeniden a\xe7\u0131yorum, umut hep i\xe7imde.",affirmationEn:"After the harshest winter I bloom again; hope is always within me.",affirmationDe:"Nach dem h\xe4rtesten Winter erbl\xfche ich wieder; die Hoffnung ist stets in mir.",affirmationEs:"Tras el invierno m\xe1s duro vuelvo a florecer; la esperanza siempre est\xe1 en m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Apr\xe8s l'hiver le plus rude, je refleuris ; l'espoir est toujours en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u6700\u3082\u53b3\u3057\u3044\u51ac\u306e\u3042\u3068\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u518d\u3073\u54b2\u304f\u3002\u5e0c\u671b\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u79c1\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Ap\xf3s o inverno mais rigoroso, eu flores\xe7o de novo; a esperan\xe7a est\xe1 sempre em mim.",myth:"Latince ad\u0131 crocus olan \xe7i\u011fdem, ad\u0131n\u0131 tanr\u0131 Hermes'in yak\u0131n dostu, \xf6l\xfcml\xfc kahraman Krokos'tan al\u0131r. Krokos bir g\xfc\xe7 yar\u0131\u015f\u0131nda yaralan\u0131p d\xfc\u015ft\xfc\u011f\xfc yerde can verince, akan kan\u0131n\u0131n \u0131slatt\u0131\u011f\u0131 topraktan birbirinden g\xfczel bahar \xe7i\xe7ekleri a\xe7t\u0131 ve bunlara onun ad\u0131 verildi. \xc7i\u011fdem do\u011furganl\u0131kla ili\u015fkilendirilirdi; Gaia, o\u011flu Zeus ile Hera'n\u0131n gerdek yata\u011f\u0131na \xe7i\u011fdem serpmi\u015f, bu \xe7i\xe7ek a\u015fk\u0131n ve yeni ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7lar\u0131n simgesi olmu\u015ftu.",mythEn:"The crocus, whose Latin name is crocus, takes its name from Krokos, a mortal hero and close friend of the god Hermes. When Krokos, wounded in a contest of strength, fell and died, beautiful spring flowers sprang from the soil his flowing blood had moistened, and they were given his name. The crocus was linked to fertility; Gaia scattered crocus on the wedding bed of her son Zeus and Hera, and the flower became an emblem of love and new beginnings.",mythDe:"Der Krokus, dessen lateinischer Name crocus lautet, tr\xe4gt seinen Namen nach Krokos, einem sterblichen Helden und engen Freund des Gottes Hermes. Als Krokos, in einem Kr\xe4ftewettstreit verwundet, fiel und starb, sprossen aus der Erde, die sein flie\xdfendes Blut benetzt hatte, wundersch\xf6ne Fr\xfchlingsblumen, denen man seinen Namen gab. Der Krokus war mit der Fruchtbarkeit verbunden; Gaia streute Krokus auf das Hochzeitsbett ihres Sohnes Zeus und Heras, und die Blume wurde zum Sinnbild der Liebe und neuer Anf\xe4nge.",mythEs:"El azafr\xe1n silvestre, cuyo nombre latino es crocus, toma su nombre de Krokos, h\xe9roe mortal y amigo cercano del dios Hermes. Cuando Krokos, herido en una contienda de fuerza, cay\xf3 y muri\xf3, de la tierra que su sangre derramada hab\xeda humedecido brotaron hermosas flores primaverales, a las que se dio su nombre. El azafr\xe1n silvestre se vinculaba a la fertilidad; Gaia esparci\xf3 estas flores sobre el lecho nupcial de su hijo Zeus y Hera, y la flor se volvi\xf3 emblema del amor y de los nuevos comienzos.",mythFr:"Le crocus, dont le nom latin est crocus, tient son nom de Krokos, h\xe9ros mortel et ami proche du dieu Herm\xe8s. Lorsque Krokos, bless\xe9 dans un concours de force, tomba et mourut, de la terre que son sang r\xe9pandu avait humect\xe9e jaillirent de belles fleurs printani\xe8res, auxquelles on donna son nom. Le crocus \xe9tait li\xe9 \xe0 la fertilit\xe9 ; Gaia r\xe9pandit des crocus sur le lit nuptial de son fils Zeus et d'H\xe9ra, et la fleur devint l'embl\xe8me de l'amour et des nouveaux commencements.",mythJa:"\u30e9\u30c6\u30f3\u540d\u3092\u30af\u30ed\u30af\u30b9\u3068\u3044\u3046\u30af\u30ed\u30c3\u30ab\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u795e\u30d8\u30eb\u30e1\u30b9\u306e\u89aa\u3057\u3044\u53cb\u3067\u3042\u3063\u305f\u4eba\u9593\u306e\u82f1\u96c4\u30af\u30ed\u30b3\u30b9\u306b\u305d\u306e\u540d\u3092\u8ca0\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u529b\u6bd4\u3079\u3067\u50b7\u3064\u3044\u3066\u5012\u308c\u305f\u30af\u30ed\u30b3\u30b9\u304c\u606f\u7d76\u3048\u305f\u3068\u304d\u3001\u6d41\u308c\u305f\u8840\u304c\u3057\u3081\u3089\u305b\u305f\u571f\u304b\u3089\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u6625\u306e\u82b1\u3005\u304c\u54b2\u304d\u3001\u305d\u308c\u3089\u306b\u5f7c\u306e\u540d\u304c\u4e0e\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30af\u30ed\u30c3\u30ab\u30b9\u306f\u591a\u7523\u3068\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u304d\u3001\u30ac\u30a4\u30a2\u306f\u606f\u5b50\u30bc\u30a6\u30b9\u3068\u30d8\u30e9\u306e\u5a5a\u793c\u306e\u5e8a\u306b\u30af\u30ed\u30c3\u30ab\u30b9\u3092\u307e\u304d\u3001\u3053\u306e\u82b1\u306f\u611b\u3068\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u59cb\u307e\u308a\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"O a\xe7afr\xe3o-bravo, cujo nome latino \xe9 crocus, recebe o nome de Krokos, her\xf3i mortal e amigo pr\xf3ximo do deus Hermes. Quando Krokos, ferido numa disputa de for\xe7a, caiu e morreu, da terra que seu sangue derramado havia umedecido brotaram belas flores primaveris, \xe0s quais se deu o seu nome. O a\xe7afr\xe3o-bravo era ligado \xe0 fertilidade; Gaia espalhou essas flores sobre o leito nupcial de seu filho Zeus e de Hera, e a flor tornou-se emblema do amor e dos novos come\xe7os.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg/330px-860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg"},{id:"plant-089",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#7A8B5C",name:"\xc7\u0131nar",nameEn:"Plane Tree",nameDe:"Platane",nameEs:"Pl\xe1tano",nameFr:"Platane",nameJa:"\u30d7\u30e9\u30bf\u30ca\u30b9",namePt:"Pl\xe1tano",origin:"Antik Yunan & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y Anatolia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e Anat\xf3lia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["k\xf6k salma","uzun \xf6m\xfcr","g\xf6lge","bilgelik"],propertiesEn:["rootedness","longevity","shade","wisdom"],propertiesDe:["Verwurzelung","Langlebigkeit","Schatten","Weisheit"],propertiesEs:["arraigo","longevidad","sombra","sabidur\xeda"],propertiesFr:["enracinement","long\xe9vit\xe9","ombre","sagesse"],propertiesJa:["\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u308b\u3053\u3068","\u9577\u5bff","\u6728\u9670","\u77e5\u6075"],propertiesPt:["enraizamento","longevidade","sombra","sabedoria"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn y\xfczy\u0131llar g\xf6ren bir \xe7\u0131nar gibi sab\u0131rla k\xf6k sal ve g\xf6lgenle \xe7evrene huzur ver. \xc7\u0131nar sana ger\xe7ek g\xfcc\xfcn acele etmeden, derinden b\xfcy\xfcmekte oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, root yourself with patience like a plane tree that has watched over centuries, and offer peace to those around you with your shade. The plane tree reminds you that true strength grows deeply, without haste.",dailyMessageDe:"Wurzle dich heute mit Geduld wie eine Platane, die Jahrhunderte \xfcberdauert hat, und schenke mit deinem Schatten Frieden um dich her. Die Platane erinnert dich daran, dass wahre St\xe4rke tief und ohne Eile w\xe4chst.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, arr\xe1igate con paciencia como un pl\xe1tano que ha visto siglos, y ofrece paz a tu alrededor con tu sombra. El pl\xe1tano te recuerda que la verdadera fuerza crece en lo hondo, sin prisa.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, enracine-toi avec patience comme un platane qui a travers\xe9 les si\xe8cles, et offre la paix autour de toi par ton ombre. Le platane te rappelle que la vraie force pousse en profondeur, sans h\xe2te.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u4f55\u4e16\u7d00\u3082\u898b\u5b88\u3063\u3066\u304d\u305f\u30d7\u30e9\u30bf\u30ca\u30b9\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u308a\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6728\u9670\u3067\u5468\u308a\u306b\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u30d7\u30e9\u30bf\u30ca\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u771f\u306e\u5f37\u3055\u306f\u6025\u304c\u305a\u6df1\u304f\u80b2\u3064\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, enra\xedze-se com paci\xeancia como um pl\xe1tano que viu s\xe9culos, e ofere\xe7a paz ao seu redor com a sua sombra. O pl\xe1tano lembra voc\xea de que a verdadeira for\xe7a cresce em profundidade, sem pressa.",howToUse:"Ya\u015fl\u0131 bir \xe7\u0131nar\u0131n g\xf6lgesine oturup s\u0131rt\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6vdesine yaslayarak k\xf6klenme niyetini hissedebilirsin. D\xfc\u015fen geni\u015f yapraklar\u0131ndan birini, sab\u0131r ve s\xfcreklilik hat\u0131rlat\u0131c\u0131s\u0131 olarak saklayabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"You may sit in the shade of an old plane tree, lean your back against its trunk, and feel an intention of grounding. You may keep one of its broad fallen leaves as a reminder of patience and continuity.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst dich in den Schatten einer alten Platane setzen, deinen R\xfccken an ihren Stamm lehnen und eine Absicht der Erdung sp\xfcren. Eines ihrer breiten heruntergefallenen Bl\xe4tter kannst du als Erinnerung an Geduld und Best\xe4ndigkeit aufbewahren.",howToUseEs:"Puedes sentarte a la sombra de un viejo pl\xe1tano, apoyar la espalda en su tronco y sentir una intenci\xf3n de arraigo. Puedes guardar una de sus anchas hojas ca\xeddas como recordatorio de paciencia y continuidad.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux t'asseoir \xe0 l'ombre d'un vieux platane, appuyer ton dos contre son tronc et ressentir une intention d'ancrage. Tu peux garder une de ses larges feuilles tomb\xe9es comme rappel de patience et de continuit\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u53e4\u3044\u30d7\u30e9\u30bf\u30ca\u30b9\u306e\u6728\u9670\u306b\u5ea7\u308a\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5e79\u306b\u80cc\u3092\u3042\u305a\u3051\u3066\u3001\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u308b\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u611f\u3058\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u843d\u3061\u305f\u5e45\u5e83\u306e\u8449\u3092\u4e00\u679a\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u7d99\u7d9a\u306e\u3057\u308b\u3057\u3068\u3057\u3066\u53d6\u3063\u3066\u304a\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode sentar-se \xe0 sombra de um velho pl\xe1tano, encostar as costas em seu tronco e sentir uma inten\xe7\xe3o de enraizamento. Pode guardar uma de suas largas folhas ca\xeddas como lembrete de paci\xeancia e continuidade.",affirmation:"Sab\u0131rla k\xf6k sal\u0131yorum, g\xf6lgemle \xe7evreme huzur veriyorum.",affirmationEn:"I root myself with patience and offer peace around me with my shade.",affirmationDe:"Ich wurzle mich mit Geduld und schenke mit meinem Schatten Frieden um mich her.",affirmationEs:"Me arraigo con paciencia y ofrezco paz a mi alrededor con mi sombra.",affirmationFr:"Je m'enracine avec patience et j'offre la paix autour de moi par mon ombre.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u308a\u3001\u6728\u9670\u3067\u5468\u308a\u306b\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u3092\u4e0e\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Enra\xedzo-me com paci\xeancia e ofere\xe7o paz ao meu redor com a minha sombra.",myth:"\xc7\u0131nar, Anadolu ve Antik Yunan'da k\xf6k sald\u0131\u011f\u0131 yere y\xfczy\u0131llarca g\xf6lge veren kutsal bir a\u011fa\xe7 say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131; geni\u015f g\xf6vdesinin alt\u0131nda halk toplan\u0131r, kararlar burada al\u0131n\u0131rd\u0131. Efsaneye g\xf6re Girit'te Zeus, bo\u011fa k\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131nda ka\xe7\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131 Europa ile asla yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 d\xf6kmeyen bir \xe7\u0131nar\u0131n alt\u0131nda birle\u015fmi\u015f ve a\u011faca \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck bah\u015fetmi\u015ftir. Pers kral\u0131 Kserkses de bir \xe7\u0131nara \xf6yle hayran kalm\u0131\u015ft\u0131 ki onu alt\u0131n tak\u0131larla s\xfcsleyip yan\u0131na bir muhaf\u0131z b\u0131rakm\u0131\u015ft\u0131.",mythEn:"The plane tree was held sacred in Anatolia and ancient Greece, casting its shade for centuries over the place it took root; people gathered beneath its broad trunk, and decisions were made there. According to legend, on Crete Zeus, in the guise of a bull, united with Europa, whom he had carried off, beneath a plane tree that would never shed its leaves, and granted the tree immortality. The Persian king Xerxes too so admired a plane tree that he adorned it with golden ornaments and left a guard beside it.",mythDe:"Die Platane galt in Anatolien und im antiken Griechenland als heilig und warf jahrhundertelang ihren Schatten \xfcber den Ort, an dem sie Wurzeln schlug; unter ihrem breiten Stamm versammelte sich das Volk, und dort wurden Entscheidungen getroffen. Der Legende nach vereinigte sich auf Kreta Zeus in Gestalt eines Stiers mit der entf\xfchrten Europa unter einer Platane, die niemals ihre Bl\xe4tter verlor, und verlieh dem Baum Unsterblichkeit. Auch der Perserk\xf6nig Xerxes bewunderte eine Platane so sehr, dass er sie mit goldenem Schmuck beh\xe4ngte und eine Wache neben ihr zur\xfccklie\xdf.",mythEs:"El pl\xe1tano era tenido por sagrado en Anatolia y la antigua Grecia, dando su sombra durante siglos al lugar donde echaba ra\xedces; bajo su ancho tronco se reun\xeda la gente y all\xed se tomaban decisiones. Seg\xfan la leyenda, en Creta Zeus, en figura de toro, se uni\xf3 con Europa, a quien hab\xeda raptado, bajo un pl\xe1tano que nunca perder\xeda sus hojas, y concedi\xf3 al \xe1rbol la inmortalidad. Tambi\xe9n el rey persa Jerjes admir\xf3 tanto un pl\xe1tano que lo adorn\xf3 con joyas de oro y dej\xf3 un guardi\xe1n junto a \xe9l.",mythFr:"Le platane \xe9tait tenu pour sacr\xe9 en Anatolie et dans la Gr\xe8ce antique, offrant son ombre pendant des si\xe8cles au lieu o\xf9 il s'enracinait ; sous son large tronc le peuple se rassemblait, et c'est l\xe0 que se prenaient les d\xe9cisions. Selon la l\xe9gende, en Cr\xe8te, Zeus, sous la forme d'un taureau, s'unit \xe0 Europe qu'il avait enlev\xe9e, sous un platane qui ne perdrait jamais ses feuilles, et accorda l'immortalit\xe9 \xe0 l'arbre. Le roi perse Xerx\xe8s admira lui aussi tant un platane qu'il le para de parures d'or et laissa une garde aupr\xe8s de lui.",mythJa:"\u30d7\u30e9\u30bf\u30ca\u30b9\u306f\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3084\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u3067\u795e\u8056\u306a\u6728\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3001\u6839\u3092\u4e0b\u308d\u3057\u305f\u5834\u6240\u306b\u4f55\u4e16\u7d00\u3082\u6728\u9670\u3092\u843d\u3068\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u305d\u306e\u5e83\u3044\u5e79\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u4eba\u3005\u306f\u96c6\u3044\u3001\u305d\u3053\u3067\u6c7a\u5b9a\u304c\u4e0b\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u4f1d\u8aac\u306b\u3088\u308c\u3070\u3001\u30af\u30ec\u30bf\u5cf6\u3067\u30bc\u30a6\u30b9\u306f\u7261\u725b\u306e\u59ff\u3067\u3055\u3089\u3063\u3066\u304d\u305f\u30a8\u30a6\u30ed\u30d1\u3068\u3001\u6c7a\u3057\u3066\u8449\u3092\u843d\u3068\u3055\u306a\u3044\u30d7\u30e9\u30bf\u30ca\u30b9\u306e\u4e0b\u3067\u7d50\u3070\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6728\u306b\u4e0d\u6b7b\u3092\u6388\u3051\u305f\u3068\u3044\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30da\u30eb\u30b7\u30e3\u738b\u30af\u30bb\u30eb\u30af\u30bb\u30b9\u3082\u307e\u305f\u3001\u3042\u308b\u30d7\u30e9\u30bf\u30ca\u30b9\u3092\u3072\u3069\u304f\u611b\u3067\u3001\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u98fe\u308a\u3067\u5f69\u308a\u3001\u305d\u306e\u305d\u3070\u306b\u756a\u5175\u3092\u6b8b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"O pl\xe1tano era tido como sagrado na Anat\xf3lia e na Gr\xe9cia antiga, lan\xe7ando sua sombra por s\xe9culos sobre o lugar onde criava ra\xedzes; sob seu largo tronco o povo se reunia, e ali as decis\xf5es eram tomadas. Segundo a lenda, em Creta, Zeus, em forma de touro, uniu-se a Europa, que havia raptado, sob um pl\xe1tano que nunca perderia as folhas, e concedeu a imortalidade \xe0 \xe1rvore. Tamb\xe9m o rei persa Xerxes admirou tanto um pl\xe1tano que o adornou com joias de ouro e deixou um guarda ao seu lado.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Platanus_orientalis_fruits%2C_Thasos.jpg/330px-Platanus_orientalis_fruits%2C_Thasos.jpg"},{id:"plant-090",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#8E9A6C",name:"Di\u015fbudak",nameEn:"Ash Tree",nameDe:"Esche",nameEs:"Fresno",nameFr:"Fr\xeane",nameJa:"\u30c8\u30cd\u30ea\u30b3",namePt:"Freixo",origin:"Yunan & \u0130skandinav mitolojisi",originEn:"Greek & Norse mythology",originDe:"Griechische & nordische Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda griega y n\xf3rdica",originFr:"Mythologie grecque et nordique",originJa:"\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u5317\u6b27\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia grega e n\xf3rdica",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["ya\u015fam a\u011fac\u0131","ba\u011flant\u0131","koruma","d\xfcnyalar aras\u0131 k\xf6pr\xfc"],propertiesEn:["tree of life","connection","protection","bridge between worlds"],propertiesDe:["Lebensbaum","Verbindung","Schutz","Br\xfccke zwischen Welten"],propertiesEs:["\xe1rbol de la vida","conexi\xf3n","protecci\xf3n","puente entre mundos"],propertiesFr:["arbre de vie","connexion","protection","pont entre les mondes"],propertiesJa:["\u751f\u547d\u306e\u6728","\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a","\u5b88\u8b77","\u4e16\u754c\u3092\u3064\u306a\u3050\u6a4b"],propertiesPt:["\xe1rvore da vida","conex\xe3o","prote\xe7\xe3o","ponte entre mundos"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn k\xf6k\xfcnden tepesine kadar uzanan g\xf6r\xfcnmez ba\u011flar\u0131n\u0131 hisset; sen yer ile g\xf6k aras\u0131nda bir k\xf6pr\xfcs\xfcn. Di\u015fbudak sana hem derinlere k\xf6k sal\u0131p hem y\xfckseklere uzanabilece\u011fini hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, feel the invisible threads reaching from your roots to your crown; you are a bridge between earth and sky. The ash tree reminds you that you can root deep and reach high at once.",dailyMessageDe:"Sp\xfcre heute die unsichtbaren F\xe4den, die von deinen Wurzeln bis zu deiner Krone reichen; du bist eine Br\xfccke zwischen Erde und Himmel. Die Esche erinnert dich daran, dass du zugleich tief wurzeln und hoch hinausreichen kannst.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, siente los hilos invisibles que van de tus ra\xedces a tu copa; eres un puente entre la tierra y el cielo. El fresno te recuerda que puedes arraigar hondo y alcanzar lo alto a la vez.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ressens les fils invisibles qui vont de tes racines \xe0 ta cime ; tu es un pont entre la terre et le ciel. Le fr\xeane te rappelle que tu peux t'enraciner profond\xe9ment et t'\xe9lever en m\xeame temps.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u6839\u304b\u3089\u68a2\u307e\u3067\u4f38\u3073\u308b\u898b\u3048\u306a\u3044\u7cf8\u3092\u611f\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u5730\u3068\u5929\u3092\u3064\u306a\u3050\u6a4b\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30c8\u30cd\u30ea\u30b3\u306f\u3001\u6df1\u304f\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u308a\u306a\u304c\u3089\u540c\u6642\u306b\u9ad8\u304f\u4f38\u3073\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, sinta os fios invis\xedveis que v\xe3o das suas ra\xedzes at\xe9 a copa; voc\xea \xe9 uma ponte entre a terra e o c\xe9u. O freixo lembra voc\xea de que pode enraizar fundo e alcan\xe7ar o alto ao mesmo tempo.",howToUse:"Bir di\u015fbudak dal\u0131n\u0131 ba\u011flant\u0131 ve koruma niyetinin simgesi olarak \xe7al\u0131\u015fma alan\u0131nda bulundurabilirsin. G\xf6vdesine dokunup yer ile g\xf6k aras\u0131ndaki o k\xf6pr\xfc hissini sessizce hayal edebilirsin.",howToUseEn:"You may keep an ash branch in your space as a symbol of an intention of connection and protection. Touching its trunk, you can quietly imagine that feeling of a bridge between earth and sky.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst einen Eschenzweig in deinem Raum als Symbol einer Absicht von Verbindung und Schutz aufbewahren. Wenn du ihren Stamm ber\xfchrst, kannst du dir still jenes Gef\xfchl einer Br\xfccke zwischen Erde und Himmel vorstellen.",howToUseEs:"Puedes tener una rama de fresno en tu espacio como s\xedmbolo de una intenci\xf3n de conexi\xf3n y protecci\xf3n. Al tocar su tronco, puedes imaginar en silencio esa sensaci\xf3n de puente entre la tierra y el cielo.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux garder une branche de fr\xeane dans ton espace comme symbole d'une intention de connexion et de protection. En touchant son tronc, tu peux imaginer en silence cette sensation de pont entre la terre et le ciel.",howToUseJa:"\u30c8\u30cd\u30ea\u30b3\u306e\u679d\u3092\u3001\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a\u3068\u5b88\u308a\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3057\u3066\u7a7a\u9593\u306b\u7f6e\u304f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u305d\u306e\u5e79\u306b\u89e6\u308c\u3001\u5730\u3068\u5929\u3092\u3064\u306a\u3050\u6a4b\u306e\u611f\u899a\u3092\u9759\u304b\u306b\u601d\u3044\u63cf\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode manter um ramo de freixo em seu espa\xe7o como s\xedmbolo de uma inten\xe7\xe3o de conex\xe3o e prote\xe7\xe3o. Ao tocar seu tronco, pode imaginar em sil\xeancio aquela sensa\xe7\xe3o de ponte entre a terra e o c\xe9u.",affirmation:"Yer ile g\xf6k aras\u0131nda bir k\xf6pr\xfcy\xfcm, hem k\xf6kl\xfcy\xfcm hem \xf6zg\xfcr\xfcm.",affirmationEn:"I am a bridge between earth and sky; I am both rooted and free.",affirmationDe:"Ich bin eine Br\xfccke zwischen Erde und Himmel; ich bin zugleich verwurzelt und frei.",affirmationEs:"Soy un puente entre la tierra y el cielo; soy a la vez arraigado y libre.",affirmationFr:"Je suis un pont entre la terre et le ciel ; je suis \xe0 la fois enracin\xe9 et libre.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5730\u3068\u5929\u3092\u3064\u306a\u3050\u6a4b\u3002\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u308a\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3082\u81ea\u7531\u3060\u3002",affirmationPt:"Sou uma ponte entre a terra e o c\xe9u; sou ao mesmo tempo enraizado e livre.",myth:"Yunan mitolojisinde di\u015fbudak a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n nymphalar\u0131 Meliadlar, Kronos'un babas\u0131 Ouranos'u had\u0131m etti\u011fi yerden, akan kandan do\u011fmu\u015flard\u0131r; bu y\xfczden \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcc\xfc m\u0131zraklar ta\u015f\u0131r, m\u0131zraklar\u0131n\u0131n sap\u0131 di\u015fbudaktan yap\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. \u0130skandinav mitolojisinde ise tanr\u0131lar iki a\u011faca ya\u015fam \xfcfleyerek ilk insanlar\u0131 yaratt\u0131: erkek Ask bir di\u015fbudaktan do\u011fdu. Di\u015fbudak b\xf6ylece d\xfcnyalar\u0131 birbirine ba\u011flayan ya\u015fam a\u011fac\u0131 olarak g\xf6r\xfcld\xfc.",mythEn:"In Greek myth the Meliads, nymphs of the ash tree, were born from the blood that flowed where Kronos castrated his father Ouranos; for this reason they bore deadly spears whose shafts were made of ash. In Norse myth the gods breathed life into two trees to create the first humans: the man Ask was born from an ash. Thus the ash tree came to be seen as the tree of life that binds the worlds together.",mythDe:"In der griechischen Mythologie wurden die Meliaden, die Nymphen der Esche, aus dem Blut geboren, das floss, als Kronos seinen Vater Ouranos entmannte; deshalb trugen sie t\xf6dliche Speere, deren Sch\xe4fte aus Eschenholz waren. In der nordischen Mythologie hauchten die G\xf6tter zwei B\xe4umen Leben ein, um die ersten Menschen zu erschaffen: der Mann Ask wurde aus einer Esche geboren. So galt die Esche als der Lebensbaum, der die Welten miteinander verbindet.",mythEs:"En la mitolog\xeda griega las Mel\xedades, ninfas del fresno, nacieron de la sangre que brot\xf3 donde Crono castr\xf3 a su padre Urano; por ello portaban lanzas mortales cuyas astas eran de fresno. En la mitolog\xeda n\xf3rdica los dioses insuflaron vida a dos \xe1rboles para crear a los primeros humanos: el var\xf3n Ask naci\xf3 de un fresno. As\xed el fresno lleg\xf3 a verse como el \xe1rbol de la vida que une los mundos entre s\xed.",mythFr:"Dans la mythologie grecque, les M\xe9liades, nymphes du fr\xeane, naquirent du sang qui coula l\xe0 o\xf9 Cronos castra son p\xe8re Ouranos ; c'est pourquoi elles portaient des lances mortelles dont les hampes \xe9taient en fr\xeane. Dans la mythologie nordique, les dieux insuffl\xe8rent la vie \xe0 deux arbres pour cr\xe9er les premiers humains : l'homme Ask naquit d'un fr\xeane. Ainsi le fr\xeane en vint \xe0 \xeatre vu comme l'arbre de vie qui relie les mondes.",mythJa:"\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30c8\u30cd\u30ea\u30b3\u306e\u30cb\u30f3\u30d5\u3067\u3042\u308b\u30e1\u30ea\u30a2\u30b9\u305f\u3061\u306f\u3001\u30af\u30ed\u30ce\u30b9\u304c\u7236\u30a6\u30e9\u30ce\u30b9\u3092\u53bb\u52e2\u3057\u305f\u5834\u6240\u306b\u6d41\u308c\u305f\u8840\u304b\u3089\u751f\u307e\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u305d\u306e\u305f\u3081\u5f7c\u5973\u305f\u3061\u306f\u6b7b\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u69cd\u3092\u6301\u3061\u3001\u305d\u306e\u67c4\u306f\u30c8\u30cd\u30ea\u30b3\u3067\u3064\u304f\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5317\u6b27\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u795e\u3005\u304c\u4e8c\u672c\u306e\u6728\u306b\u547d\u3092\u5439\u304d\u8fbc\u3093\u3067\u6700\u521d\u306e\u4eba\u9593\u3092\u5275\u308a\u3001\u7537\u30a2\u30b9\u30af\u306f\u30c8\u30cd\u30ea\u30b3\u304b\u3089\u751f\u307e\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u30c8\u30cd\u30ea\u30b3\u306f\u3001\u4e16\u754c\u3092\u3064\u306a\u3050\u751f\u547d\u306e\u6728\u3068\u307f\u306a\u3055\u308c\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na mitologia grega, as Mel\xedades, ninfas do freixo, nasceram do sangue que correu onde Cronos castrou seu pai Urano; por isso portavam lan\xe7as mortais cujas hastes eram de freixo. Na mitologia n\xf3rdica, os deuses sopraram vida em duas \xe1rvores para criar os primeiros humanos: o homem Ask nasceu de um freixo. Assim o freixo passou a ser visto como a \xe1rvore da vida que une os mundos entre si.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Fraxinus_ornus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-062.jpg/330px-Fraxinus_ornus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-062.jpg"},{id:"plant-091",emoji:"\ud83c\udf47",color:"#5B2C3E",name:"Dut",nameEn:"Mulberry",nameDe:"Maulbeere",nameEs:"Morera",nameFr:"M\xfbrier",nameJa:"\u6851",namePt:"Amoreira",origin:"Antik Babil & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Babylon & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Babylon & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Babilonia y Anatolia",originFr:"Babylone antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30d0\u30d3\u30ed\u30f3\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Antiga Babil\xf4nia e Anat\xf3lia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k","tutku","anma","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm"],propertiesEn:["devotion","passion","remembrance","transformation"],propertiesDe:["Hingabe","Leidenschaft","Erinnerung","Verwandlung"],propertiesEs:["devoci\xf3n","pasi\xf3n","memoria","transformaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["d\xe9votion","passion","souvenir","transformation"],propertiesJa:["\u732e\u8eab","\u60c5\u71b1","\u8ffd\u61b6","\u5909\u5bb9"],propertiesPt:["devo\xe7\xe3o","paix\xe3o","mem\xf3ria","transforma\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn sevgiyi acele ettirmeden, kalbinle ta\u015f\u0131; ger\xe7ek ba\u011f tela\u015fa de\u011fil sabra ihtiya\xe7 duyar. Dut sana b\xfcy\xfck duygular\u0131n bizi d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc, iz b\u0131rakt\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 nazik\xe7e hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, carry love with your heart without rushing it; a true bond needs patience, not haste. The mulberry gently reminds you that great feelings transform us and leave their mark.",dailyMessageDe:"Trage heute die Liebe mit deinem Herzen, ohne sie zu \xfcberst\xfcrzen; eine wahre Bindung braucht Geduld, nicht Eile. Die Maulbeere erinnert dich sanft daran, dass gro\xdfe Gef\xfchle uns verwandeln und ihre Spur hinterlassen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, lleva el amor con tu coraz\xf3n sin apresurarlo; un v\xednculo verdadero necesita paciencia, no prisa. La morera te recuerda con dulzura que los grandes sentimientos nos transforman y dejan su huella.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, porte l'amour avec ton c\u0153ur sans le pr\xe9cipiter ; un lien v\xe9ritable a besoin de patience, non de h\xe2te. Le m\xfbrier te rappelle avec douceur que les grands sentiments nous transforment et laissent leur empreinte.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u611b\u3092\u6025\u304c\u305a\u5fc3\u3067\u904b\u3073\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u771f\u306e\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a\u306b\u306f\u7126\u308a\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u5fcd\u8010\u304c\u8981\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u6851\u306f\u3001\u5927\u304d\u306a\u611f\u60c5\u304c\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u3092\u5909\u3048\u3001\u8de1\u3092\u6b8b\u3059\u3068\u3001\u305d\u3063\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, carregue o amor com o seu cora\xe7\xe3o sem apress\xe1-lo; um v\xednculo verdadeiro precisa de paci\xeancia, n\xe3o de pressa. A amoreira lembra voc\xea com delicadeza de que os grandes sentimentos nos transformam e deixam sua marca.",howToUse:"Olgun meyvelerini taze ya da kurutulmu\u015f olarak tatl\u0131 bir ikram olarak tadabilir, pekmezini yapabilirsin. Bir avu\xe7 dutu sevdi\u011finle payla\u015fmak, ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may enjoy the ripe fruit fresh or dried as a sweet treat and make molasses from it. Sharing a handful of mulberries with someone you love is a gentle gesture honoring an intention of devotion.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die reifen Fr\xfcchte frisch oder getrocknet als s\xfc\xdfe K\xf6stlichkeit genie\xdfen und Sirup daraus machen. Eine Handvoll Maulbeeren mit einem geliebten Menschen zu teilen ist eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht der Hingabe ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes disfrutar el fruto maduro fresco o seco como un dulce manjar y hacer melaza con \xe9l. Compartir un pu\xf1ado de moras con alguien a quien amas es un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de devoci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux savourer le fruit m\xfbr frais ou s\xe9ch\xe9 comme une douceur et en faire de la m\xe9lasse. Partager une poign\xe9e de m\xfbres avec un \xeatre aim\xe9 est un geste tendre qui honore une intention de d\xe9votion.",howToUseJa:"\u719f\u3057\u305f\u5b9f\u3092\u751f\u306e\u307e\u307e\u3001\u307e\u305f\u306f\u5e72\u3057\u3066\u7518\u3044\u304a\u3084\u3064\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3044\u3001\u7cd6\u871c\u3092\u4f5c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u306e\u6851\u306e\u5b9f\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u4eba\u3068\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u732e\u8eab\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode apreciar o fruto maduro fresco ou seco como uma guloseima doce e fazer mela\xe7o com ele. Partilhar um punhado de amoras com algu\xe9m que voc\xea ama \xe9 um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de devo\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Sevgiyi sab\u0131rla ta\u015f\u0131yorum, duygular\u0131m beni nazik\xe7e d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcyor.",affirmationEn:"I carry love with patience, and my feelings transform me gently.",affirmationDe:"Ich trage die Liebe mit Geduld, und meine Gef\xfchle verwandeln mich sanft.",affirmationEs:"Llevo el amor con paciencia, y mis sentimientos me transforman con dulzura.",affirmationFr:"Je porte l'amour avec patience, et mes sentiments me transforment avec douceur.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u611b\u3092\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u904b\u3073\u3001\u611f\u60c5\u306f\u79c1\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u5909\u3048\u3066\u3086\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Carrego o amor com paci\xeancia, e meus sentimentos me transformam com delicadeza.",myth:"Bir zamanlar Babil'de aileleri y\xfcz\xfcnden gizlice bulu\u015fan iki \xe2\u015f\u0131k, Thisbe ile Pyramos vard\u0131. Bir gece \u015fehir d\u0131\u015f\u0131nda bir dut a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n alt\u0131nda bulu\u015facaklarken, Thisbe a\u011fz\u0131 kanl\u0131 bir aslandan ka\xe7arken e\u015farb\u0131n\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcrd\xfc. Sevgilisinin par\xe7alanm\u0131\u015f e\u015farb\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6ren Pyramos onu \xf6ld\xfc san\u0131p can\u0131na k\u0131yd\u0131; geri d\xf6nen Thisbe de ayn\u0131 b\u0131\xe7akla kendini \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc. \u0130ki \xe2\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131n akan kan\u0131yla, o g\xfcne dek bembeyaz olan dutun meyveleri k\u0131pk\u0131rm\u0131z\u0131ya d\xf6nd\xfc; karadut i\u015fte b\xf6yle do\u011fdu.",mythEn:"Once in Babylon there were two lovers, Thisbe and Pyramus, who met in secret because of their families. One night, as they were to meet beneath a mulberry tree outside the city, Thisbe dropped her veil while fleeing a lion with a bloodied mouth. Seeing his beloved's torn veil, Pyramus believed her dead and took his own life; returning, Thisbe killed herself with the same blade. With the flowing blood of the two lovers, the mulberry's fruit, white until that day, turned deep red; thus the black mulberry was born.",mythDe:"Einst gab es in Babylon zwei Liebende, Thisbe und Pyramus, die sich wegen ihrer Familien heimlich trafen. Eines Nachts, als sie sich unter einem Maulbeerbaum vor der Stadt treffen wollten, verlor Thisbe ihren Schleier, w\xe4hrend sie vor einem L\xf6wen mit blutigem Maul floh. Beim Anblick des zerrissenen Schleiers seiner Geliebten hielt Pyramus sie f\xfcr tot und nahm sich das Leben; als Thisbe zur\xfcckkehrte, t\xf6tete sie sich mit derselben Klinge. Mit dem flie\xdfenden Blut der beiden Liebenden f\xe4rbte sich die bis dahin wei\xdfe Frucht der Maulbeere tiefrot; so entstand die schwarze Maulbeere.",mythEs:"Hubo una vez en Babilonia dos amantes, Tisbe y P\xedramo, que se encontraban en secreto a causa de sus familias. Una noche, cuando iban a encontrarse bajo una morera a las afueras de la ciudad, Tisbe dej\xf3 caer su velo al huir de un le\xf3n de boca ensangrentada. Al ver el velo desgarrado de su amada, P\xedramo la crey\xf3 muerta y se quit\xf3 la vida; al volver, Tisbe se mat\xf3 con la misma hoja. Con la sangre derramada de los dos amantes, el fruto de la morera, blanco hasta aquel d\xeda, se volvi\xf3 rojo intenso; as\xed naci\xf3 la mora negra.",mythFr:"Il \xe9tait une fois \xe0 Babylone deux amants, Thisb\xe9 et Pyrame, qui se rencontraient en secret \xe0 cause de leurs familles. Une nuit, alors qu'ils devaient se retrouver sous un m\xfbrier hors de la ville, Thisb\xe9 laissa tomber son voile en fuyant un lion \xe0 la gueule ensanglant\xe9e. Voyant le voile d\xe9chir\xe9 de sa bien-aim\xe9e, Pyrame la crut morte et se donna la mort ; \xe0 son retour, Thisb\xe9 se tua de la m\xeame lame. Avec le sang vers\xe9 des deux amants, le fruit du m\xfbrier, blanc jusque-l\xe0, devint d'un rouge profond ; ainsi naquit la m\xfbre noire.",mythJa:"\u3080\u304b\u3057\u30d0\u30d3\u30ed\u30f3\u306b\u3001\u5bb6\u3069\u3046\u3057\u306e\u4e0d\u548c\u3086\u3048\u306b\u3072\u305d\u304b\u306b\u4f1a\u3063\u3066\u3044\u305f\u4e8c\u4eba\u306e\u604b\u4eba\u3001\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u30d9\u3068\u30d4\u30e5\u30e9\u30e2\u30b9\u304c\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3042\u308b\u591c\u3001\u753a\u5916\u308c\u306e\u6851\u306e\u6728\u306e\u4e0b\u3067\u4f1a\u304a\u3046\u3068\u3057\u305f\u3068\u304d\u3001\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u30d9\u306f\u53e3\u3092\u8840\u306b\u67d3\u3081\u305f\u7345\u5b50\u304b\u3089\u9003\u3052\u308b\u9014\u4e2d\u3067\u30f4\u30a7\u30fc\u30eb\u3092\u843d\u3068\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5f15\u304d\u88c2\u304b\u308c\u305f\u604b\u4eba\u306e\u30f4\u30a7\u30fc\u30eb\u3092\u898b\u305f\u30d4\u30e5\u30e9\u30e2\u30b9\u306f\u5f7c\u5973\u304c\u6b7b\u3093\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3044\u8fbc\u307f\u3001\u81ea\u3089\u547d\u3092\u7d76\u3061\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u623b\u3063\u3066\u304d\u305f\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u30d9\u3082\u540c\u3058\u5203\u3067\u81ea\u5bb3\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u4e8c\u4eba\u306e\u604b\u4eba\u306e\u6d41\u308c\u305f\u8840\u3067\u3001\u305d\u308c\u307e\u3067\u771f\u3063\u767d\u3060\u3063\u305f\u6851\u306e\u5b9f\u306f\u6df1\u7d05\u306b\u67d3\u307e\u308a\u3001\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u9ed2\u3044\u6851\u304c\u751f\u307e\u308c\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Era uma vez na Babil\xf4nia dois amantes, Tisbe e P\xedramo, que se encontravam em segredo por causa de suas fam\xedlias. Numa noite, quando iam se encontrar sob uma amoreira fora da cidade, Tisbe deixou cair o v\xe9u ao fugir de um le\xe3o de boca ensanguentada. Ao ver o v\xe9u rasgado da amada, P\xedramo a julgou morta e tirou a pr\xf3pria vida; ao voltar, Tisbe matou-se com a mesma l\xe2mina. Com o sangue derramado dos dois amantes, o fruto da amoreira, branco at\xe9 aquele dia, tornou-se vermelho intenso; assim nasceu a amora-preta.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Morus_alba_FrJPG.jpg/330px-Morus_alba_FrJPG.jpg"},{id:"plant-092",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5F7A4A",name:"E\u011freltiotu",nameEn:"Fern",nameDe:"Farn",nameEs:"Helecho",nameFr:"Foug\xe8re",nameJa:"\u30b7\u30c0",namePt:"Samambaia",origin:"Avrupa & Hitit Anadolusu",originEn:"Europe & Hittite Anatolia",originDe:"Europa & hethitisches Anatolien",originEs:"Europa y Anatolia hitita",originFr:"Europe et Anatolie hittite",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u30fb\u30d2\u30c3\u30bf\u30a4\u30c8\u306e\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Europa e Anat\xf3lia hitita",element:"eter",elementEn:"ether",elementDe:"\xc4ther",elementEs:"\xe9ter",elementFr:"\xe9ther",elementJa:"\u30a8\u30fc\u30c6\u30eb",elementPt:"\xe9ter",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["gizem","g\xf6r\xfcnmezlik","\u015fans","sakl\u0131 hazine"],propertiesEn:["mystery","invisibility","luck","hidden treasure"],propertiesDe:["Geheimnis","Unsichtbarkeit","Gl\xfcck","verborgener Schatz"],propertiesEs:["misterio","invisibilidad","suerte","tesoro oculto"],propertiesFr:["myst\xe8re","invisibilit\xe9","chance","tr\xe9sor cach\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u795e\u79d8","\u900f\u660e","\u5e78\u904b","\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u5b9d"],propertiesPt:["mist\xe9rio","invisibilidade","sorte","tesouro oculto"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xf6zle g\xf6r\xfcnmeyene g\xfcven; en de\u011ferli \u015feyler \xe7o\u011fu zaman g\xf6lgede, sessizce b\xfcy\xfcr. E\u011freltiotu sana i\xe7indeki sakl\u0131 hazinenin t\u0131pk\u0131 onun \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi gibi sab\u0131rla aranmay\u0131 bekledi\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, trust what the eye cannot see; the most precious things often grow quietly, in the shade. The fern whispers that the hidden treasure within you, like its flower, waits to be sought with patience.",dailyMessageDe:"Vertraue heute dem, was das Auge nicht sieht; das Kostbarste w\xe4chst oft still, im Schatten. Der Farn fl\xfcstert, dass der verborgene Schatz in dir, wie seine Bl\xfcte, darauf wartet, mit Geduld gesucht zu werden.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, conf\xeda en lo que el ojo no ve; lo m\xe1s valioso suele crecer en silencio, en la sombra. El helecho susurra que el tesoro oculto en ti, como su flor, espera ser buscado con paciencia.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, fais confiance \xe0 ce que l'\u0153il ne voit pas ; le plus pr\xe9cieux pousse souvent en silence, dans l'ombre. La foug\xe8re murmure que le tr\xe9sor cach\xe9 en toi, comme sa fleur, attend d'\xeatre cherch\xe9 avec patience.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u76ee\u306b\u898b\u3048\u306a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6700\u3082\u5c0a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u306f\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u3001\u6728\u9670\u3067\u9759\u304b\u306b\u80b2\u3061\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b7\u30c0\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u5185\u306a\u308b\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u5b9d\u304c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u82b1\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u63a2\u3055\u308c\u308b\u306e\u3092\u5f85\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, confie no que os olhos n\xe3o veem; as coisas mais preciosas muitas vezes crescem em sil\xeancio, na sombra. A samambaia sussurra que o tesouro oculto em voc\xea, como sua flor, espera ser buscado com paci\xeancia.",howToUse:"Yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6lgeli bir k\xf6\u015fede yeti\u015ftirip mek\xe2n\u0131na dinginlik ve gizem katabilirsin. Bir e\u011freltiotu yapra\u011f\u0131n\u0131, sakl\u0131 potansiyelini hat\u0131rlatan sembolik bir t\u0131ls\u0131m olarak yan\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131yabilirsin.",howToUseEn:"You may grow its fronds in a shady corner to bring stillness and mystery to your space. You may carry a fern frond with you as a symbolic charm that reminds you of your hidden potential.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst seine Wedel in einer schattigen Ecke ziehen, um Stille und Geheimnis in deinen Raum zu bringen. Einen Farnwedel kannst du als symbolischen Talisman bei dir tragen, der dich an dein verborgenes Potenzial erinnert.",howToUseEs:"Puedes cultivar sus frondas en un rinc\xf3n sombr\xedo para dar quietud y misterio a tu espacio. Puedes llevar una fronda de helecho contigo como amuleto simb\xf3lico que te recuerde tu potencial oculto.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux cultiver ses frondes dans un coin ombrag\xe9 pour apporter calme et myst\xe8re \xe0 ton espace. Tu peux porter une fronde de foug\xe8re sur toi comme amulette symbolique qui te rappelle ton potentiel cach\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u8449\u3092\u65e5\u9670\u306e\u7247\u9685\u3067\u80b2\u3066\u3001\u7a7a\u9593\u306b\u9759\u3051\u3055\u3068\u795e\u79d8\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b7\u30c0\u306e\u8449\u3092\u3001\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u53ef\u80fd\u6027\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u308b\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u306a\u304a\u5b88\u308a\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6301\u3061\u6b69\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode cultivar suas frondes em um canto sombreado para trazer quietude e mist\xe9rio ao seu espa\xe7o. Pode carregar uma fronde de samambaia consigo como amuleto simb\xf3lico que lembra o seu potencial oculto.",affirmation:"G\xf6r\xfcnmeyene g\xfcveniyorum, i\xe7imdeki sakl\u0131 hazineyi sab\u0131rla onurland\u0131r\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I trust the unseen and honor the hidden treasure within me with patience.",affirmationDe:"Ich vertraue dem Unsichtbaren und ehre den verborgenen Schatz in mir mit Geduld.",affirmationEs:"Conf\xedo en lo invisible y honro con paciencia el tesoro oculto en m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Je fais confiance \xe0 l'invisible et j'honore avec patience le tr\xe9sor cach\xe9 en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u76ee\u306b\u898b\u3048\u306c\u3082\u306e\u3092\u4fe1\u983c\u3057\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u5b9d\u3092\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u656c\u3046\u3002",affirmationPt:"Confio no invis\xedvel e honro com paci\xeancia o tesouro oculto dentro de mim.",myth:"Halk inanc\u0131na g\xf6re e\u011freltiotu, yaln\u0131zca yaz d\xf6n\xfcm\xfc gecesinde alt\u0131n gibi parlayan b\xfcy\xfcl\xfc bir \xe7i\xe7ek a\xe7ar; bu \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi elde eden ki\u015fi g\xf6r\xfcnmez olur, hayvanlar\u0131n dilini anlar ve yer alt\u0131ndaki t\xfcm hazineleri mavi bir \u0131\u015f\u0131k gibi g\xf6r\xfcrm\xfc\u015f. Bir efsanede avc\u0131 yaz d\xf6n\xfcm\xfcnde g\xfcne\u015fe ok at\u0131nca damlayan \xfc\xe7 damla kandan bu sihirli tohum do\u011fmu\u015ftur. Hitit mitolojisinde ise bereket tanr\u0131s\u0131 Telepinu \xf6fkelenip kaybolunca topraklar kurumu\u015f; e\u011freltiotu da onun geri d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcyle ye\u015feren do\u011fan\u0131n gizemine ba\u011flan\u0131r.",mythEn:"According to folk belief, the fern blooms a magical, golden-glowing flower only on the night of the summer solstice; whoever obtains this flower becomes invisible, understands the speech of animals, and sees all the treasures underground as a blue light. In one legend, a hunter shot an arrow at the sun on the solstice, and from the three drops of blood that fell, this magical seed was born. In Hittite myth, when the fertility god Telepinu grew angry and vanished, the land dried up; the fern, too, is bound to the mystery of nature greening again with his return.",mythDe:"Dem Volksglauben nach bringt der Farn nur in der Nacht der Sommersonnenwende eine magische, golden leuchtende Bl\xfcte hervor; wer diese Bl\xfcte erlangt, wird unsichtbar, versteht die Sprache der Tiere und sieht alle Sch\xe4tze unter der Erde als ein blaues Licht. In einer Legende schoss ein J\xe4ger zur Sonnenwende einen Pfeil auf die Sonne, und aus den drei Tropfen Blut, die fielen, wurde dieser magische Same geboren. In der hethitischen Mythologie vertrocknete das Land, als der Fruchtbarkeitsgott Telepinu z\xfcrnte und verschwand; auch der Farn ist mit dem Geheimnis der Natur verbunden, die mit seiner R\xfcckkehr wieder ergr\xfcnt.",mythEs:"Seg\xfan la creencia popular, el helecho florece una flor m\xe1gica de brillo dorado solo en la noche del solsticio de verano; quien obtiene esa flor se vuelve invisible, entiende el habla de los animales y ve todos los tesoros bajo tierra como una luz azul. En una leyenda, un cazador dispar\xf3 una flecha al sol en el solsticio, y de las tres gotas de sangre que cayeron naci\xf3 esta semilla m\xe1gica. En la mitolog\xeda hitita, cuando el dios de la fertilidad Telepinu se enoj\xf3 y desapareci\xf3, la tierra se sec\xf3; el helecho tambi\xe9n se vincula al misterio de la naturaleza que reverdece con su regreso.",mythFr:"Selon la croyance populaire, la foug\xe8re ne produit une fleur magique au rayonnement dor\xe9 que la nuit du solstice d'\xe9t\xe9 ; celui qui obtient cette fleur devient invisible, comprend le langage des animaux et voit tous les tr\xe9sors sous terre comme une lumi\xe8re bleue. Dans une l\xe9gende, un chasseur d\xe9cocha une fl\xe8che vers le soleil au solstice, et des trois gouttes de sang qui tomb\xe8rent naquit cette graine magique. Dans la mythologie hittite, lorsque le dieu de la fertilit\xe9 Telepinu se mit en col\xe8re et disparut, la terre se dess\xe9cha ; la foug\xe8re est aussi li\xe9e au myst\xe8re de la nature qui reverdit \xe0 son retour.",mythJa:"\u6c11\u9593\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u306b\u3088\u308c\u3070\u3001\u30b7\u30c0\u306f\u590f\u81f3\u306e\u591c\u306b\u3060\u3051\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u8f1d\u304f\u9b54\u6cd5\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u54b2\u304b\u305b\u3001\u305d\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u5f97\u305f\u8005\u306f\u59ff\u3092\u6d88\u3057\u3001\u52d5\u7269\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u3092\u89e3\u3057\u3001\u5730\u4e0b\u306e\u3042\u3089\u3086\u308b\u5b9d\u3092\u9752\u3044\u5149\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u898b\u308b\u3068\u3044\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u308b\u4f1d\u8aac\u3067\u306f\u3001\u72e9\u4eba\u304c\u590f\u81f3\u306b\u592a\u967d\u3078\u77e2\u3092\u653e\u3064\u3068\u3001\u6ef4\u308a\u843d\u3061\u305f\u4e09\u6ef4\u306e\u8840\u304b\u3089\u3053\u306e\u9b54\u6cd5\u306e\u7a2e\u304c\u751f\u307e\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30d2\u30c3\u30bf\u30a4\u30c8\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u795e\u30c6\u30ec\u30d4\u30cc\u304c\u6012\u3063\u3066\u59ff\u3092\u6d88\u3059\u3068\u5927\u5730\u306f\u67af\u308c\u679c\u3066\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30b7\u30c0\u3082\u307e\u305f\u3001\u5f7c\u306e\u5e30\u9084\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u7dd1\u3065\u304f\u81ea\u7136\u306e\u795e\u79d8\u306b\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u3051\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Segundo a cren\xe7a popular, a samambaia floresce uma flor m\xe1gica de brilho dourado apenas na noite do solst\xedcio de ver\xe3o; quem obt\xe9m essa flor torna-se invis\xedvel, entende a fala dos animais e v\xea todos os tesouros sob a terra como uma luz azul. Numa lenda, um ca\xe7ador atirou uma flecha ao sol no solst\xedcio, e das tr\xeas gotas de sangue que ca\xedram nasceu esta semente m\xe1gica. Na mitologia hitita, quando o deus da fertilidade Telepinu se irritou e desapareceu, a terra secou; a samambaia tamb\xe9m se liga ao mist\xe9rio da natureza que reverdece com o seu retorno.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg"},{id:"plant-093",emoji:"\ud83c\udf4e",color:"#C0392B",name:"Elma",nameEn:"Apple",nameDe:"Apfel",nameEs:"Manzana",nameFr:"Pomme",nameJa:"\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4",namePt:"Ma\xe7\xe3",origin:"Antik Yunan & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y Anatolia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e Anat\xf3lia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["a\u015fk","bereket","\xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck","bilgi","cazibe"],propertiesEn:["love","abundance","immortality","knowledge","allure"],propertiesDe:["Liebe","F\xfclle","Unsterblichkeit","Wissen","Anziehung"],propertiesEs:["amor","abundancia","inmortalidad","conocimiento","atracci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["amour","abondance","immortalit\xe9","savoir","attrait"],propertiesJa:["\u611b","\u8c4a\u7a63","\u4e0d\u6b7b","\u77e5\u8b58","\u9b45\u529b"],propertiesPt:["amor","abund\xe2ncia","imortalidade","conhecimento","atra\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn bir \u015feyin cazibesine kap\u0131l\u0131rken, ger\xe7ekten neyin pe\u015finde oldu\u011funu kendine sor; her parlak elma seni hedefinden sapt\u0131rmamal\u0131. Elma sana arzunun tatl\u0131, ama y\xf6n\xfcn\xfc bilmenin de\u011ferli oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, as you are drawn by something's allure, ask yourself what you are truly after; not every shining apple should pull you from your aim. The apple reminds you that desire is sweet, yet knowing your direction is precious.",dailyMessageDe:"Wenn dich heute der Reiz von etwas lockt, frage dich, wonach du wirklich strebst; nicht jeder gl\xe4nzende Apfel sollte dich von deinem Ziel abbringen. Der Apfel erinnert dich daran, dass Verlangen s\xfc\xdf ist, doch deine Richtung zu kennen kostbar.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, mientras te atrae el encanto de algo, preg\xfantate qu\xe9 buscas de verdad; no toda manzana reluciente debe apartarte de tu meta. La manzana te recuerda que el deseo es dulce, pero conocer tu rumbo es valioso.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, alors que l'attrait de quelque chose te s\xe9duit, demande-toi ce que tu cherches vraiment ; toute pomme brillante ne doit pas t'\xe9carter de ton but. La pomme te rappelle que le d\xe9sir est doux, mais que conna\xeetre ta direction est pr\xe9cieux.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u3001\u4f55\u304b\u306e\u9b45\u529b\u306b\u60f9\u304b\u308c\u308b\u3068\u304d\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u6c42\u3081\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3092\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u554f\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u8f1d\u304f\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u306e\u3059\u3079\u3066\u304c\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u76ee\u6a19\u304b\u3089\u9038\u3089\u3059\u3079\u304d\u3067\u306f\u3042\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u306f\u3001\u6b32\u671b\u306f\u7518\u304f\u3001\u3057\u304b\u3057\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u9032\u3080\u65b9\u5411\u3092\u77e5\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3053\u305d\u5c0a\u3044\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, ao ser atra\xeddo pelo encanto de algo, pergunte a voc\xea mesmo o que realmente busca; nem toda ma\xe7\xe3 reluzente deve afastar voc\xea do seu objetivo. A ma\xe7\xe3 lembra voc\xea de que o desejo \xe9 doce, mas conhecer a sua dire\xe7\xe3o \xe9 precioso.",howToUse:"Olgun bir elmay\u0131 taze yiyebilir, ortadan enine kesti\u011finde i\xe7indeki be\u015f k\xf6\u015feli y\u0131ld\u0131z\u0131 bir niyet sembol\xfc olarak g\xf6zlemleyebilirsin. Bir elmay\u0131 sevdi\u011finle payla\u015fmak, a\u015fk ve bereket niyetini onurland\u0131ran eski bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may eat a ripe apple fresh, and when you cut it crosswise, observe the five-pointed star inside as a symbol of intention. Sharing an apple with someone you love is an ancient gesture honoring an intention of love and abundance.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst einen reifen Apfel frisch essen und, wenn du ihn quer durchschneidest, den f\xfcnfzackigen Stern darin als Symbol der Absicht betrachten. Einen Apfel mit einem geliebten Menschen zu teilen ist eine alte Geste, die eine Absicht von Liebe und F\xfclle ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes comer una manzana madura fresca y, al cortarla transversalmente, observar la estrella de cinco puntas en su interior como s\xedmbolo de intenci\xf3n. Compartir una manzana con alguien a quien amas es un gesto antiguo que honra una intenci\xf3n de amor y abundancia.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux manger une pomme m\xfbre fra\xeeche et, en la coupant en travers, observer l'\xe9toile \xe0 cinq branches \xe0 l'int\xe9rieur comme symbole d'intention. Partager une pomme avec un \xeatre aim\xe9 est un geste ancien qui honore une intention d'amour et d'abondance.",howToUseJa:"\u719f\u3057\u305f\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3092\u751f\u306e\u307e\u307e\u98df\u3079\u3001\u6a2a\u306b\u5207\u3063\u305f\u3068\u304d\u306b\u73fe\u308c\u308b\u4e94\u8292\u661f\u3092\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3057\u3066\u773a\u3081\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u4eba\u3068\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u611b\u3068\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u53e4\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode comer uma ma\xe7\xe3 madura fresca e, ao cort\xe1-la transversalmente, observar a estrela de cinco pontas em seu interior como s\xedmbolo de inten\xe7\xe3o. Partilhar uma ma\xe7\xe3 com algu\xe9m que voc\xea ama \xe9 um gesto antigo que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de amor e abund\xe2ncia.",affirmation:"Arzular\u0131m\u0131 bilgelikle ta\u015f\u0131yorum, neyi ger\xe7ekten istedi\u011fimi biliyorum.",affirmationEn:"I carry my desires with wisdom, and I know what I truly want.",affirmationDe:"Ich trage meine W\xfcnsche mit Weisheit und wei\xdf, was ich wahrhaft will.",affirmationEs:"Llevo mis deseos con sabidur\xeda y s\xe9 lo que de verdad quiero.",affirmationFr:"Je porte mes d\xe9sirs avec sagesse et je sais ce que je veux vraiment.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6b32\u671b\u3092\u667a\u6167\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u904b\u3073\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u671b\u3080\u3082\u306e\u3092\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Carrego meus desejos com sabedoria e sei o que realmente quero.",myth:"Yunan mitolojisinde h\u0131zl\u0131 ko\u015fucu Atalante, kendisini ge\xe7emeyen taliplerini reddederdi. Hippomenes, Aphrodite'nin verdi\u011fi alt\u0131n elmalar\u0131 yar\u0131\u015f s\u0131ras\u0131nda bir bir yere b\u0131rak\u0131nca, onlar\u0131 toplamak i\xe7in duraklayan Atalante yar\u0131\u015f\u0131 kaybetti ve evlenmeye raz\u0131 oldu. Bir ba\u015fka mitte nifak tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Eris, \xfc\xe7 tanr\u0131\xe7a aras\u0131na 'en g\xfczele' yaz\u0131l\u0131 alt\u0131n bir elma at\u0131nca, Paris'in Aphrodite'yi se\xe7mesi Troya Sava\u015f\u0131'n\u0131n k\u0131v\u0131lc\u0131m\u0131 oldu. \u0130skandinav mitolojisinde gen\xe7lik tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 \u0130dun'un alt\u0131n elmalar\u0131 tanr\u0131lara sonsuz gen\xe7lik ba\u011f\u0131\u015flard\u0131.",mythEn:"In Greek myth, the swift runner Atalanta rejected suitors who could not outrun her. When Hippomenes dropped the golden apples given by Aphrodite one by one during their race, Atalanta paused to gather them, lost the race, and agreed to marry him. In another myth, when Eris, goddess of discord, threw among three goddesses a golden apple inscribed 'to the fairest,' Paris's choice of Aphrodite became the spark of the Trojan War. In Norse myth, the golden apples of Idun, goddess of youth, granted the gods eternal youth.",mythDe:"In der griechischen Mythologie wies die schnelle L\xe4uferin Atalante Freier zur\xfcck, die sie nicht \xfcberholen konnten. Als Hippomenes beim Wettlauf die von Aphrodite geschenkten goldenen \xc4pfel einen nach dem anderen fallen lie\xdf, hielt Atalante an, um sie aufzusammeln, verlor das Rennen und willigte in die Heirat ein. In einem anderen Mythos warf Eris, die G\xf6ttin der Zwietracht, einen goldenen Apfel mit der Aufschrift 'der Sch\xf6nsten' unter drei G\xf6ttinnen, und Paris' Wahl der Aphrodite wurde zum Funken des Trojanischen Krieges. In der nordischen Mythologie schenkten die goldenen \xc4pfel der Jugendg\xf6ttin Idun den G\xf6ttern ewige Jugend.",mythEs:"En la mitolog\xeda griega, la veloz corredora Atalanta rechazaba a los pretendientes que no lograban superarla. Cuando Hip\xf3menes dej\xf3 caer una a una las manzanas de oro dadas por Afrodita durante la carrera, Atalanta se detuvo a recogerlas, perdi\xf3 la carrera y acept\xf3 casarse. En otro mito, cuando Eris, diosa de la discordia, arroj\xf3 entre tres diosas una manzana de oro con la inscripci\xf3n 'a la m\xe1s bella', la elecci\xf3n de Afrodita por Paris fue la chispa de la Guerra de Troya. En la mitolog\xeda n\xf3rdica, las manzanas de oro de Idun, diosa de la juventud, otorgaban a los dioses la juventud eterna.",mythFr:"Dans la mythologie grecque, la rapide coureuse Atalante repoussait les pr\xe9tendants incapables de la d\xe9passer. Lorsque Hippom\xe8ne laissa tomber une \xe0 une les pommes d'or offertes par Aphrodite pendant la course, Atalante s'arr\xeata pour les ramasser, perdit la course et consentit au mariage. Dans un autre mythe, lorsque \xc9ris, d\xe9esse de la discorde, jeta entre trois d\xe9esses une pomme d'or portant l'inscription '\xe0 la plus belle', le choix d'Aphrodite par P\xe2ris devint l'\xe9tincelle de la guerre de Troie. Dans la mythologie nordique, les pommes d'or d'Idun, d\xe9esse de la jeunesse, accordaient aux dieux la jeunesse \xe9ternelle.",mythJa:"\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u4fca\u8db3\u306e\u8d70\u8005\u30a2\u30bf\u30e9\u30f3\u30c6\u306f\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u8ffd\u3044\u8d8a\u305b\u306a\u3044\u6c42\u5a5a\u8005\u3092\u9000\u3051\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u7af6\u8d70\u306e\u6700\u4e2d\u3001\u30d2\u30c3\u30dd\u30e1\u30cd\u30b9\u304c\u30a2\u30d5\u30ed\u30c7\u30a3\u30fc\u30c6\u304b\u3089\u6388\u304b\u3063\u305f\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3092\u4e00\u3064\u305a\u3064\u843d\u3068\u3059\u3068\u3001\u30a2\u30bf\u30e9\u30f3\u30c6\u306f\u305d\u308c\u3092\u62fe\u3046\u305f\u3081\u306b\u7acb\u3061\u6b62\u307e\u308a\u3001\u7af6\u8d70\u306b\u8ca0\u3051\u3066\u7d50\u5a5a\u306b\u5fdc\u3058\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5225\u306e\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u4e0d\u548c\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30a8\u30ea\u30b9\u304c\u4e09\u5973\u795e\u306e\u9593\u306b\u300e\u6700\u3082\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u8005\u3078\u300f\u3068\u8a18\u3055\u308c\u305f\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3092\u6295\u3052\u5165\u308c\u3001\u30d1\u30ea\u30b9\u304c\u30a2\u30d5\u30ed\u30c7\u30a3\u30fc\u30c6\u3092\u9078\u3093\u3060\u3053\u3068\u304c\u30c8\u30ed\u30a4\u30a2\u6226\u4e89\u306e\u706b\u7a2e\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5317\u6b27\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u82e5\u3055\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30a4\u30ba\u30f3\u306e\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u304c\u795e\u3005\u306b\u6c38\u9060\u306e\u82e5\u3055\u3092\u6388\u3051\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Na mitologia grega, a veloz corredora Atalanta rejeitava os pretendentes que n\xe3o conseguiam ultrapass\xe1-la. Quando Hip\xf3menes deixou cair uma a uma as ma\xe7\xe3s de ouro dadas por Afrodite durante a corrida, Atalanta parou para recolh\xea-las, perdeu a corrida e aceitou casar-se. Em outro mito, quando \xc9ris, deusa da disc\xf3rdia, lan\xe7ou entre tr\xeas deusas uma ma\xe7\xe3 de ouro com a inscri\xe7\xe3o 'para a mais bela', a escolha de Afrodite por P\xe1ris tornou-se a fa\xedsca da Guerra de Troia. Na mitologia n\xf3rdica, as ma\xe7\xe3s de ouro de Idun, deusa da juventude, concediam aos deuses a juventude eterna.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg"},{id:"plant-094",emoji:"\ud83e\uded8",color:"#6B8E4E",name:"Fasulye",nameEn:"Bean",nameDe:"Bohne",nameEs:"Frijol",nameFr:"Haricot",nameJa:"\u8c46",namePt:"Feij\xe3o",origin:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r & Antik Yunan",originEn:"Ancient Egypt & Ancient Greece",originDe:"Altes \xc4gypten & antikes Griechenland",originEs:"Antiguo Egipto y Antigua Grecia",originFr:"\xc9gypte ancienne et Gr\xe8ce antique",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u30fb\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3",originPt:"Antigo Egito e Gr\xe9cia Antiga",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["yeniden do\u011fu\u015f","ruh","bereket","gizem"],propertiesEn:["rebirth","soul","abundance","mystery"],propertiesDe:["Wiedergeburt","Seele","F\xfclle","Geheimnis"],propertiesEs:["renacimiento","alma","abundancia","misterio"],propertiesFr:["renaissance","\xe2me","abondance","myst\xe8re"],propertiesJa:["\u518d\u751f","\u9b42","\u8c4a\u7a63","\u795e\u79d8"],propertiesPt:["renascimento","alma","abund\xe2ncia","mist\xe9rio"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn karanl\u0131kta sab\u0131rla bekleyen bir tohum gibi, g\xf6r\xfcnmeyen bir d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn i\xe7inde olabilirsin; her bekleyi\u015f bir filize gebedir. Fasulye sana sessiz topra\u011f\u0131n alt\u0131nda bile ya\u015fam\u0131n yeniden do\u011fmaya haz\u0131rland\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, like a seed waiting patiently in the dark, you may be within an unseen transformation; every waiting is pregnant with a sprout. The bean reminds you that even beneath the silent earth, life is preparing to be reborn.",dailyMessageDe:"Heute bist du vielleicht, wie ein Samen, der geduldig im Dunkeln wartet, mitten in einer unsichtbaren Verwandlung; jedes Warten tr\xe4gt einen Keim in sich. Die Bohne erinnert dich daran, dass sich selbst unter der stillen Erde das Leben darauf vorbereitet, neu geboren zu werden.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, como una semilla que espera con paciencia en la oscuridad, puedes estar dentro de una transformaci\xf3n invisible; toda espera est\xe1 pre\xf1ada de un brote. El frijol te recuerda que, incluso bajo la tierra silenciosa, la vida se prepara para renacer.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, telle une graine qui attend patiemment dans l'obscurit\xe9, tu es peut-\xeatre au c\u0153ur d'une transformation invisible ; toute attente porte en elle un germe. Le haricot te rappelle que, m\xeame sous la terre silencieuse, la vie se pr\xe9pare \xe0 rena\xeetre.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u3001\u6697\u95c7\u3067\u8f9b\u62b1\u3065\u3088\u304f\u5f85\u3064\u7a2e\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u76ee\u306b\u898b\u3048\u306a\u3044\u5909\u5bb9\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3044\u308b\u306e\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u5f85\u3061\u306f\u82bd\u3092\u5b55\u3093\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u8c46\u306f\u3001\u9759\u304b\u306a\u571f\u306e\u4e0b\u3067\u3055\u3048\u3001\u751f\u547d\u304c\u518d\u3073\u751f\u307e\u308c\u308b\u6e96\u5099\u3092\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, como uma semente que espera com paci\xeancia na escurid\xe3o, voc\xea pode estar dentro de uma transforma\xe7\xe3o invis\xedvel; toda espera est\xe1 prenhe de um broto. O feij\xe3o lembra voc\xea de que, mesmo sob a terra silenciosa, a vida se prepara para renascer.",howToUse:"Kuru fasulyeleri \u0131slat\u0131p karanl\u0131k bir kapta filizlendirerek yeniden do\u011fu\u015fun mucizesini g\xf6zlemleyebilirsin. Bir avu\xe7 fasulye tanesini bir kavanozda saklamak, bereket ve yeni ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7 niyetini onurland\u0131ran sembolik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may soak dried beans and sprout them in a dark vessel to observe the miracle of rebirth. Keeping a handful of bean seeds in a jar is a symbolic gesture honoring an intention of abundance and new beginnings.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst getrocknete Bohnen einweichen und in einem dunklen Gef\xe4\xdf keimen lassen, um das Wunder der Wiedergeburt zu beobachten. Eine Handvoll Bohnenkerne in einem Glas aufzubewahren ist eine symbolische Geste, die eine Absicht von F\xfclle und Neuanfang ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes remojar frijoles secos y germinarlos en un recipiente oscuro para observar el milagro del renacimiento. Guardar un pu\xf1ado de semillas de frijol en un frasco es un gesto simb\xf3lico que honra una intenci\xf3n de abundancia y nuevos comienzos.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux faire tremper des haricots secs et les faire germer dans un r\xe9cipient sombre pour observer le miracle de la renaissance. Garder une poign\xe9e de graines de haricot dans un bocal est un geste symbolique qui honore une intention d'abondance et de renouveau.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u3044\u305f\u8c46\u3092\u6c34\u306b\u6d78\u3057\u3001\u6697\u3044\u5bb9\u5668\u3067\u767a\u82bd\u3055\u305b\u3066\u518d\u751f\u306e\u5947\u8de1\u3092\u89b3\u5bdf\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u306e\u8c46\u306e\u7a2e\u3092\u74f6\u306b\u4fdd\u7ba1\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u59cb\u307e\u308a\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u306a\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode deixar feij\xf5es secos de molho e faz\xea-los brotar em um recipiente escuro para observar o milagre do renascimento. Guardar um punhado de sementes de feij\xe3o em um frasco \xe9 um gesto simb\xf3lico que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de abund\xe2ncia e novos come\xe7os.",affirmation:"Karanl\u0131kta sab\u0131rla bekliyorum, i\xe7imde yeni bir ya\u015fam filizleniyor.",affirmationEn:"I wait patiently in the dark, and a new life sprouts within me.",affirmationDe:"Ich warte geduldig im Dunkeln, und ein neues Leben keimt in mir.",affirmationEs:"Espero con paciencia en la oscuridad, y una nueva vida germina en m\xed.",affirmationFr:"J'attends patiemment dans l'obscurit\xe9, et une nouvelle vie germe en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6697\u95c7\u3067\u8f9b\u62b1\u3065\u3088\u304f\u5f85\u3061\u3001\u5185\u306b\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u751f\u547d\u304c\u82bd\u5439\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Espero com paci\xeancia na escurid\xe3o, e uma nova vida germina em mim.",myth:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da \u0131slat\u0131lan fasulyenin karanl\u0131kta filizlenmesi yeniden ya\u015fam inanc\u0131yla ili\u015fkilendirilir; M\u0131s\u0131rl\u0131lar fasulyenin i\xe7inde bir ruhun canland\u0131\u011f\u0131na inan\u0131r, iyi fasulyeleri mezarlara sunu olarak b\u0131rak\u0131rlard\u0131. Filozof Pythagoras, ruhlar\u0131n bedenden bedene g\xf6\xe7t\xfc\u011f\xfc \xf6\u011fretisini bu M\u0131s\u0131r inanc\u0131ndan esinlenerek geli\u015ftirmi\u015f, fasulyeyi ruhlarla bir tuttu\u011fu i\xe7in tarikat\u0131nda yemeyi yasaklam\u0131\u015ft\u0131. Yunan mitolojisinde ekin tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Demeter de fasulyeyi \xf6l\xfcler ve hayaletlerle \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirerek bir s\xfcre insanlara fasulye ekmeyi yasaklam\u0131\u015ft\u0131.",mythEn:"In ancient Egypt, the sprouting of soaked beans in the dark was linked to the belief in renewed life; the Egyptians believed a soul came alive within the bean and left good beans as offerings in tombs. The philosopher Pythagoras developed his teaching of souls migrating from body to body inspired by this Egyptian belief, and because he identified the bean with souls, he forbade eating it in his order. In Greek myth, Demeter, goddess of grain, also identified the bean with the dead and ghosts and for a time forbade people to plant beans.",mythDe:"Im alten \xc4gypten wurde das Keimen eingeweichter Bohnen im Dunkeln mit dem Glauben an erneuertes Leben verbunden; die \xc4gypter glaubten, in der Bohne erwache eine Seele, und legten gute Bohnen als Opfergaben in die Gr\xe4ber. Der Philosoph Pythagoras entwickelte seine Lehre von der Seelenwanderung von K\xf6rper zu K\xf6rper, inspiriert von diesem \xe4gyptischen Glauben, und weil er die Bohne mit Seelen gleichsetzte, verbot er in seinem Orden, sie zu essen. In der griechischen Mythologie setzte auch Demeter, die G\xf6ttin des Getreides, die Bohne mit den Toten und Geistern gleich und verbot den Menschen eine Zeit lang, Bohnen zu pflanzen.",mythEs:"En el antiguo Egipto, la germinaci\xf3n de frijoles remojados en la oscuridad se vinculaba a la creencia en la vida renovada; los egipcios cre\xedan que un alma cobraba vida dentro del frijol y dejaban buenos frijoles como ofrenda en las tumbas. El fil\xf3sofo Pit\xe1goras desarroll\xf3 su ense\xf1anza de las almas que migran de cuerpo en cuerpo inspirado por esta creencia egipcia, y como identificaba el frijol con las almas, prohibi\xf3 comerlo en su orden. En la mitolog\xeda griega, Dem\xe9ter, diosa del grano, tambi\xe9n identificaba el frijol con los muertos y los fantasmas y por un tiempo prohibi\xf3 a la gente sembrar frijoles.",mythFr:"Dans l'\xc9gypte ancienne, la germination des haricots tremp\xe9s dans l'obscurit\xe9 \xe9tait li\xe9e \xe0 la croyance en une vie renouvel\xe9e ; les \xc9gyptiens croyaient qu'une \xe2me s'\xe9veillait dans le haricot et d\xe9posaient de bons haricots en offrande dans les tombes. Le philosophe Pythagore \xe9labora sa doctrine des \xe2mes migrant de corps en corps inspir\xe9 par cette croyance \xe9gyptienne, et parce qu'il identifiait le haricot aux \xe2mes, il en interdit la consommation dans son ordre. Dans la mythologie grecque, D\xe9m\xe9ter, d\xe9esse du grain, identifiait aussi le haricot aux morts et aux fant\xf4mes et interdit un temps aux hommes de semer des haricots.",mythJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u3067\u306f\u3001\u6c34\u306b\u6d78\u3057\u305f\u8c46\u304c\u6697\u95c7\u3067\u82bd\u5439\u304f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u751f\u547d\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3068\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u3051\u3089\u308c\u3001\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u4eba\u306f\u8c46\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u9b42\u304c\u5bbf\u308b\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3001\u826f\u3044\u8c46\u3092\u5893\u3078\u306e\u4f9b\u7269\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6b8b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u54f2\u5b66\u8005\u30d4\u30bf\u30b4\u30e9\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u9b42\u304c\u4f53\u304b\u3089\u4f53\u3078\u79fb\u308a\u4f4f\u3080\u3068\u3044\u3046\u6559\u3048\u3092\u3053\u306e\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u306b\u7740\u60f3\u3092\u5f97\u3066\u767a\u5c55\u3055\u305b\u3001\u8c46\u3092\u9b42\u3068\u540c\u4e00\u8996\u3057\u305f\u305f\u3081\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6559\u56e3\u3067\u98df\u3079\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u7981\u3058\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u7a40\u7269\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30c7\u30e1\u30c6\u30eb\u3082\u307e\u305f\u8c46\u3092\u6b7b\u8005\u3084\u4ea1\u970a\u3068\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u3051\u3001\u4e00\u6642\u671f\u3001\u4eba\u3005\u306b\u8c46\u3092\u690d\u3048\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u7981\u3058\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"No antigo Egito, o brotar de feij\xf5es de molho na escurid\xe3o era ligado \xe0 cren\xe7a na vida renovada; os eg\xedpcios acreditavam que uma alma ganhava vida dentro do feij\xe3o e deixavam bons feij\xf5es como oferenda nos t\xfamulos. O fil\xf3sofo Pit\xe1goras desenvolveu seu ensinamento das almas que migram de corpo em corpo inspirado por essa cren\xe7a eg\xedpcia e, como identificava o feij\xe3o com as almas, proibiu com\xea-lo em sua ordem. Na mitologia grega, Dem\xe9ter, deusa do gr\xe3o, tamb\xe9m identificava o feij\xe3o com os mortos e os fantasmas e por um tempo proibiu as pessoas de plantar feij\xf5es.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/French_beans_J1.JPG/330px-French_beans_J1.JPG"},{id:"plant-095",emoji:"\ud83c\udf30",color:"#8B5A2B",name:"F\u0131nd\u0131k",nameEn:"Hazelnut",nameDe:"Haselnuss",nameEs:"Avellana",nameFr:"Noisette",nameJa:"\u30d8\u30fc\u30bc\u30eb\u30ca\u30c3\u30c4",namePt:"Avel\xe3",origin:"Gal & Kelt Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Welsh & Celtic Tradition",originDe:"Walisische & keltische Tradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n galesa y celta",originFr:"Tradition galloise et celtique",originJa:"\u30a6\u30a7\u30fc\u30eb\u30ba\u30fb\u30b1\u30eb\u30c8\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o galesa e celta",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["bilgelik","koruma","\xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck","ilham"],propertiesEn:["wisdom","protection","immortality","inspiration"],propertiesDe:["Weisheit","Schutz","Unsterblichkeit","Inspiration"],propertiesEs:["sabidur\xeda","protecci\xf3n","inmortalidad","inspiraci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["sagesse","protection","immortalit\xe9","inspiration"],propertiesJa:["\u53e1\u667a","\u5b88\u8b77","\u4e0d\u6b7b","\u970a\u611f"],propertiesPt:["sabedoria","prote\xe7\xe3o","imortalidade","inspira\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn d\u0131\u015f kabu\u011fun sertli\u011fine aldanma; en de\u011ferli bilgelik \xe7o\u011fu zaman korunakl\u0131 bir sabr\u0131n i\xe7inde olgunla\u015f\u0131r. F\u0131nd\u0131k sana sa\u011flam bir kabu\u011fun ard\u0131nda sakl\u0131 \xf6z\xfcn\xfc koruyabilece\u011fini hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, do not be fooled by the hardness of the outer shell; the most precious wisdom often ripens within a sheltered patience. The hazelnut reminds you that you can protect your hidden essence behind a sturdy shell.",dailyMessageDe:"Lass dich heute nicht von der H\xe4rte der \xe4u\xdferen Schale t\xe4uschen; die kostbarste Weisheit reift oft in einer gesch\xfctzten Geduld. Die Haselnuss erinnert dich daran, dass du dein verborgenes Wesen hinter einer festen Schale sch\xfctzen kannst.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, no te dejes enga\xf1ar por la dureza de la c\xe1scara exterior; la sabidur\xeda m\xe1s preciosa suele madurar en una paciencia resguardada. La avellana te recuerda que puedes proteger tu esencia oculta tras una c\xe1scara firme.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ne te laisse pas tromper par la duret\xe9 de la coque ext\xe9rieure ; la sagesse la plus pr\xe9cieuse m\xfbrit souvent dans une patience prot\xe9g\xe9e. La noisette te rappelle que tu peux prot\xe9ger ton essence cach\xe9e derri\xe8re une coque solide.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u3001\u5916\u6bbb\u306e\u786c\u3055\u306b\u60d1\u308f\u3055\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002\u6700\u3082\u5c0a\u3044\u53e1\u667a\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u5b88\u3089\u308c\u305f\u5fcd\u8010\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u719f\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30d8\u30fc\u30bc\u30eb\u30ca\u30c3\u30c4\u306f\u3001\u5805\u3044\u6bbb\u306e\u5965\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u672c\u8cea\u3092\u5b88\u308c\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, n\xe3o se deixe enganar pela dureza da casca externa; a sabedoria mais preciosa muitas vezes amadurece dentro de uma paci\xeancia resguardada. A avel\xe3 lembra voc\xea de que pode proteger a sua ess\xeancia oculta atr\xe1s de uma casca firme.",howToUse:"F\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131 kabu\u011fundan \xe7\u0131kar\u0131p \xe7i\u011f ya da kavrularak besleyici bir at\u0131\u015ft\u0131rmal\u0131k olarak tadabilirsin. Bir avu\xe7 f\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131 bir k\xe2seye koyup masan\u0131n \xfczerinde tutmak, bilgelik ve koruma niyetini onurland\u0131ran sade bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may shell the hazelnut and enjoy it raw or roasted as a nourishing snack. Placing a handful of hazelnuts in a bowl on your table is a simple gesture honoring an intention of wisdom and protection.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die Haselnuss sch\xe4len und roh oder ger\xf6stet als n\xe4hrenden Snack genie\xdfen. Eine Handvoll Haseln\xfcsse in einer Schale auf dem Tisch ist eine schlichte Geste, die eine Absicht von Weisheit und Schutz ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes pelar la avellana y disfrutarla cruda o tostada como un tentempi\xe9 nutritivo. Colocar un pu\xf1ado de avellanas en un cuenco sobre la mesa es un gesto sencillo que honra una intenci\xf3n de sabidur\xeda y protecci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux d\xe9cortiquer la noisette et la savourer crue ou grill\xe9e comme un en-cas nourrissant. Placer une poign\xe9e de noisettes dans un bol sur ta table est un geste simple qui honore une intention de sagesse et de protection.",howToUseJa:"\u30d8\u30fc\u30bc\u30eb\u30ca\u30c3\u30c4\u3092\u6bbb\u304b\u3089\u53d6\u308a\u51fa\u3057\u3001\u751f\u306e\u307e\u307e\u3001\u307e\u305f\u306f\u7092\u3063\u3066\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u8efd\u98df\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u306e\u30d8\u30fc\u30bc\u30eb\u30ca\u30c3\u30c4\u3092\u5668\u306b\u5165\u308c\u3066\u673a\u306b\u7f6e\u304f\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u53e1\u667a\u3068\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3064\u3064\u307e\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode descascar a avel\xe3 e apreci\xe1-la crua ou torrada como um petisco nutritivo. Colocar um punhado de avel\xe3s em uma tigela sobre a mesa \xe9 um gesto simples que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de sabedoria e prote\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Sa\u011flam kabu\u011fumun ard\u0131nda \xf6z\xfcm\xfc koruyorum, bilgelik i\xe7imde olgunla\u015f\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"Behind my sturdy shell I protect my essence, and wisdom ripens within me.",affirmationDe:"Hinter meiner festen Schale sch\xfctze ich mein Wesen, und Weisheit reift in mir.",affirmationEs:"Tras mi c\xe1scara firme protejo mi esencia, y la sabidur\xeda madura en m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Derri\xe8re ma coque solide je prot\xe8ge mon essence, et la sagesse m\xfbrit en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5805\u3044\u6bbb\u306e\u5965\u306b\u672c\u8cea\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3001\u53e1\u667a\u304c\u5185\u306b\u719f\u3057\u3066\u3086\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Atr\xe1s da minha casca firme protejo a minha ess\xeancia, e a sabedoria amadurece em mim.",myth:"Gal mitolojisinde f\u0131nd\u0131k, t\u0131pk\u0131 elma gibi \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck meyvelerinden say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Bir efsanede g\xfcneyden gelen esrarengiz bir yolcu, Aziz Patrick'e \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfc\u011f\xfcn meyvesi olarak bir kucak dolusu f\u0131nd\u0131k getirmi\u015ftir. \u0130sve\xe7 halk inan\u0131\u015f\u0131nda ise f\u0131nd\u0131k, y\u0131lana kar\u015f\u0131 en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc koruyucu kabul edilir; tehlikeli bir y\u0131lana bir f\u0131nd\u0131k dal\u0131yla dokunman\u0131n, onun t\xfcm zehrini ak\u0131tmaya yetece\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131.",mythEn:"In Welsh myth, the hazelnut, like the apple, was counted among the fruits of immortality. In one legend, a mysterious traveler from the south brought Saint Patrick an armful of hazelnuts as the fruit of immortality. In Swedish folk belief, the hazel was considered the strongest protection against snakes; it was believed that touching a dangerous snake with a hazel branch was enough to make it pour out all its venom.",mythDe:"In der walisischen Mythologie z\xe4hlte die Haselnuss, wie der Apfel, zu den Fr\xfcchten der Unsterblichkeit. In einer Legende brachte ein geheimnisvoller Reisender aus dem S\xfcden dem heiligen Patrick eine Armvoll Haseln\xfcsse als Frucht der Unsterblichkeit. Im schwedischen Volksglauben galt die Hasel als st\xe4rkster Schutz gegen Schlangen; man glaubte, eine gef\xe4hrliche Schlange mit einem Haselzweig zu ber\xfchren gen\xfcge, um sie ihr ganzes Gift verstr\xf6men zu lassen.",mythEs:"En la mitolog\xeda galesa, la avellana, como la manzana, se contaba entre los frutos de la inmortalidad. En una leyenda, un misterioso viajero del sur trajo a san Patricio un brazado de avellanas como fruto de la inmortalidad. En la creencia popular sueca, el avellano se consideraba la protecci\xf3n m\xe1s fuerte contra las serpientes; se cre\xeda que tocar a una serpiente peligrosa con una rama de avellano bastaba para hacerle derramar todo su veneno.",mythFr:"Dans la mythologie galloise, la noisette, comme la pomme, comptait parmi les fruits de l'immortalit\xe9. Dans une l\xe9gende, un myst\xe9rieux voyageur venu du sud apporta \xe0 saint Patrick une brass\xe9e de noisettes comme fruit de l'immortalit\xe9. Dans la croyance populaire su\xe9doise, le noisetier \xe9tait consid\xe9r\xe9 comme la plus forte protection contre les serpents ; on croyait que toucher un serpent dangereux avec une branche de noisetier suffisait \xe0 lui faire r\xe9pandre tout son venin.",mythJa:"\u30a6\u30a7\u30fc\u30eb\u30ba\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30d8\u30fc\u30bc\u30eb\u30ca\u30c3\u30c4\u306f\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3068\u540c\u3058\u304f\u4e0d\u6b7b\u306e\u679c\u5b9f\u306e\u3072\u3068\u3064\u306b\u6570\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3042\u308b\u4f1d\u8aac\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5357\u304b\u3089\u6765\u305f\u8b0e\u3081\u3044\u305f\u65c5\u4eba\u304c\u3001\u4e0d\u6b7b\u306e\u679c\u5b9f\u3068\u3057\u3066\u4e00\u62b1\u3048\u306e\u30d8\u30fc\u30bc\u30eb\u30ca\u30c3\u30c4\u3092\u8056\u30d1\u30c8\u30ea\u30c3\u30af\u306b\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30b9\u30a6\u30a7\u30fc\u30c7\u30f3\u306e\u6c11\u9593\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30cf\u30b7\u30d0\u30df\u306f\u86c7\u306b\u5bfe\u3059\u308b\u6700\u3082\u5f37\u3044\u5b88\u308a\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3001\u5371\u967a\u306a\u86c7\u3092\u30cf\u30b7\u30d0\u30df\u306e\u679d\u3067\u89e6\u308c\u308b\u3060\u3051\u3067\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6bd2\u3092\u3059\u3079\u3066\u6d41\u3057\u51fa\u3055\u305b\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Na mitologia galesa, a avel\xe3, assim como a ma\xe7\xe3, era contada entre os frutos da imortalidade. Numa lenda, um misterioso viajante do sul trouxe a S\xe3o Patr\xedcio uma bra\xe7ada de avel\xe3s como fruto da imortalidade. Na cren\xe7a popular sueca, a aveleira era considerada a mais forte prote\xe7\xe3o contra serpentes; acreditava-se que tocar uma serpente perigosa com um ramo de aveleira bastava para faz\xea-la derramar todo o seu veneno.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg/330px-Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg"},{id:"plant-096",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3a",color:"#E63946",name:"Gelincik",nameEn:"Poppy",nameDe:"Mohn",nameEs:"Amapola",nameFr:"Coquelicot",nameJa:"\u30d2\u30ca\u30b2\u30b7",namePt:"Papoula",origin:"Antik Yunan",originEn:"Ancient Greece",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland",originEs:"Antigua Grecia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["uyku","r\xfcya","dirili\u015f","huzur","unutu\u015f"],propertiesEn:["sleep","dream","resurrection","peace","oblivion"],propertiesDe:["Schlaf","Traum","Auferstehung","Frieden","Vergessen"],propertiesEs:["sue\xf1o","ensue\xf1o","resurrecci\xf3n","paz","olvido"],propertiesFr:["sommeil","r\xeave","r\xe9surrection","paix","oubli"],propertiesJa:["\u7720\u308a","\u5922","\u5fa9\u6d3b","\u5b89\u3089\u304e","\u5fd8\u5374"],propertiesPt:["sono","sonho","ressurrei\xe7\xe3o","paz","esquecimento"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn dinlenmeye izin ver; her uyku k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir \xf6l\xfcm, her uyan\u0131\u015f k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir dirili\u015ftir. Gelincik sana yorgun ruhun, k\u0131\u015f\u0131n ard\u0131ndan gelen bahar gibi, dinlendikten sonra yeniden a\xe7aca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, allow yourself to rest; every sleep is a small death, every waking a small resurrection. The poppy whispers that your weary soul, like spring after winter, will bloom again once it has rested.",dailyMessageDe:"Erlaube dir heute, zu ruhen; jeder Schlaf ist ein kleiner Tod, jedes Erwachen eine kleine Auferstehung. Der Mohn fl\xfcstert, dass deine m\xfcde Seele, wie der Fr\xfchling nach dem Winter, wieder erbl\xfchen wird, sobald sie geruht hat.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, perm\xedtete descansar; todo sue\xf1o es una peque\xf1a muerte, todo despertar una peque\xf1a resurrecci\xf3n. La amapola susurra que tu alma cansada, como la primavera tras el invierno, volver\xe1 a florecer una vez que haya descansado.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, accorde-toi le repos ; tout sommeil est une petite mort, tout r\xe9veil une petite r\xe9surrection. Le coquelicot murmure que ton \xe2me lasse, comme le printemps apr\xe8s l'hiver, refleurira une fois qu'elle se sera repos\xe9e.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u4f11\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3092\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u8a31\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u7720\u308a\u306f\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u6b7b\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u306f\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u5fa9\u6d3b\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30d2\u30ca\u30b2\u30b7\u306f\u3001\u75b2\u308c\u305f\u9b42\u304c\u3001\u51ac\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306e\u6625\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u4f11\u3093\u3060\u306e\u3061\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u54b2\u304f\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, permita-se descansar; todo sono \xe9 uma pequena morte, todo despertar uma pequena ressurrei\xe7\xe3o. A papoula sussurra que a sua alma cansada, como a primavera depois do inverno, voltar\xe1 a florescer assim que tiver descansado.",howToUse:"Gelinci\u011fin k\u0131rm\u0131z\u0131 \xe7i\xe7eklerini bir vazoda seyrederek anma ve dinginlik niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. \xc7i\xe7e\u011fi uyku verici afyon kayna\u011f\u0131 oldu\u011fundan, kullan\u0131m\u0131 yaln\u0131zca sembolik ve t\xf6renseldir; i\xe7sel kullan\u0131m \xf6nerilmez.",howToUseEn:"You may keep the poppy's red flowers in a vase to accompany an intention of remembrance and stillness. Since the flower is a source of sleep-inducing opium, its use is symbolic and ceremonial only; inner use is not advised.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die roten Mohnbl\xfcten in einer Vase betrachten, um eine Absicht des Gedenkens und der Stille zu begleiten. Da die Bl\xfcte eine Quelle schlafbringenden Opiums ist, ist ihr Gebrauch nur symbolisch und zeremoniell; innere Anwendung wird nicht empfohlen.",howToUseEs:"Puedes contemplar las flores rojas de la amapola en un jarr\xf3n para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de memoria y quietud. Como la flor es fuente del opio que induce el sue\xf1o, su uso es solo simb\xf3lico y ceremonial; no se aconseja el uso interno.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux contempler les fleurs rouges du coquelicot dans un vase pour accompagner une intention de souvenir et de calme. Comme la fleur est source de l'opium qui induit le sommeil, son usage est seulement symbolique et c\xe9r\xe9moniel ; l'usage interne n'est pas conseill\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u30d2\u30ca\u30b2\u30b7\u306e\u8d64\u3044\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u3067\u773a\u3081\u3001\u8ffd\u61b6\u3068\u9759\u3051\u3055\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3053\u306e\u82b1\u306f\u7720\u308a\u3092\u8a98\u3046\u963f\u7247\u306e\u6e90\u3067\u3042\u308b\u305f\u3081\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7528\u3044\u65b9\u306f\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u30fb\u5100\u793c\u7684\u306a\u3082\u306e\u306b\u9650\u3089\u308c\u3001\u5185\u670d\u306f\u52e7\u3081\u3089\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode contemplar as flores vermelhas da papoula em um vaso para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de mem\xf3ria e quietude. Como a flor \xe9 fonte do \xf3pio que induz o sono, seu uso \xe9 apenas simb\xf3lico e cerimonial; o uso interno n\xe3o \xe9 aconselhado.",affirmation:"Dinlenmeye izin veriyorum, ruhum her uyan\u0131\u015fta yeniden diriliyor.",affirmationEn:"I allow myself to rest, and my soul is reborn with every waking.",affirmationDe:"Ich erlaube mir zu ruhen, und meine Seele wird mit jedem Erwachen neu geboren.",affirmationEs:"Me permito descansar, y mi alma renace con cada despertar.",affirmationFr:"Je m'autorise au repos, et mon \xe2me rena\xeet \xe0 chaque r\xe9veil.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4f11\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3092\u8a31\u3057\u3001\u9b42\u306f\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u308b\u305f\u3073\u306b\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u751f\u307e\u308c\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Permito-me descansar, e a minha alma renasce a cada despertar.",myth:"Gelincik, ekili topraklarda yeti\u015fti\u011fi i\xe7in ekin tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Demeter'le ili\u015fkilendirilmi\u015ftir; tanr\u0131\xe7a \xe7o\u011fu zaman ba\u015f\u0131nda ya da elinde gelinciklerle tasvir edilir. Demeter'in k\u0131z\u0131 Persephone k\u0131rda \xe7i\xe7ek toplarken yeralt\u0131 tanr\u0131s\u0131 Hades taraf\u0131ndan ka\xe7\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda, toplad\u0131\u011f\u0131 \xe7i\xe7eklerin gelincik oldu\u011fu s\xf6ylenir; \xe7i\xe7e\u011fin k\u0131rm\u0131z\u0131s\u0131 \xf6l\xfcmden sonraki dirili\u015fi, uyku verici etkisiyse Persephone'nin yeralt\u0131na indi\u011fi k\u0131\u015f\u0131 simgeler. Yunan mitolojisinde r\xfcya tanr\u0131s\u0131 Morpheus'un yata\u011f\u0131n\u0131n \xe7evresi de gelinciklerle sar\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r; morfin de bu bitkinin afyonundan elde edilir.",mythEn:"Because the poppy grows in cultivated fields, it was associated with Demeter, the goddess of grain; she is often depicted with poppies on her head or in her hand. When Demeter's daughter Persephone was abducted by Hades, god of the underworld, while gathering flowers in the meadow, the flowers she was gathering are said to have been poppies; the flower's red symbolizes resurrection after death, and its sleep-inducing power the winter when Persephone descended below. In Greek myth, the bed of Morpheus, god of dreams, is also ringed with poppies; morphine, too, is derived from this plant's opium.",mythDe:"Weil der Mohn auf bestelltem Land w\xe4chst, wurde er mit Demeter, der G\xf6ttin des Getreides, verbunden; sie wird oft mit Mohnbl\xfcten auf dem Haupt oder in der Hand dargestellt. Als Demeters Tochter Persephone beim Blumenpfl\xfccken auf der Wiese von Hades, dem Gott der Unterwelt, entf\xfchrt wurde, sollen die Blumen, die sie pfl\xfcckte, Mohnbl\xfcten gewesen sein; das Rot der Bl\xfcte versinnbildlicht die Auferstehung nach dem Tod, ihre schlafbringende Kraft den Winter, in dem Persephone hinabstieg. In der griechischen Mythologie ist auch das Lager des Morpheus, des Gottes der Tr\xe4ume, von Mohn umgeben; auch Morphin wird aus dem Opium dieser Pflanze gewonnen.",mythEs:"Como la amapola crece en campos cultivados, se asoci\xf3 con Dem\xe9ter, la diosa del grano; a menudo se la representa con amapolas en la cabeza o en la mano. Cuando la hija de Dem\xe9ter, Pers\xe9fone, fue raptada por Hades, dios del inframundo, mientras recog\xeda flores en el prado, se dice que las flores que recog\xeda eran amapolas; el rojo de la flor simboliza la resurrecci\xf3n tras la muerte, y su poder somn\xedfero el invierno en que Pers\xe9fone descendi\xf3. En la mitolog\xeda griega, el lecho de Morfeo, dios de los sue\xf1os, tambi\xe9n est\xe1 rodeado de amapolas; la morfina, adem\xe1s, se obtiene del opio de esta planta.",mythFr:"Parce que le coquelicot pousse dans les champs cultiv\xe9s, il fut associ\xe9 \xe0 D\xe9m\xe9ter, d\xe9esse du grain ; on la repr\xe9sente souvent avec des coquelicots sur la t\xeate ou \xe0 la main. Lorsque Pers\xe9phone, fille de D\xe9m\xe9ter, fut enlev\xe9e par Had\xe8s, dieu des enfers, alors qu'elle cueillait des fleurs dans le pr\xe9, on dit que les fleurs qu'elle cueillait \xe9taient des coquelicots ; le rouge de la fleur symbolise la r\xe9surrection apr\xe8s la mort, et son pouvoir soporifique l'hiver o\xf9 Pers\xe9phone descendit. Dans la mythologie grecque, la couche de Morph\xe9e, dieu des r\xeaves, est aussi entour\xe9e de coquelicots ; la morphine, elle aussi, est tir\xe9e de l'opium de cette plante.",mythJa:"\u30d2\u30ca\u30b2\u30b7\u306f\u8015\u3055\u308c\u305f\u7551\u306b\u80b2\u3064\u305f\u3081\u3001\u7a40\u7269\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30c7\u30e1\u30c6\u30eb\u3068\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u3051\u3089\u308c\u3001\u5973\u795e\u306f\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u982d\u3084\u624b\u306b\u30d2\u30ca\u30b2\u30b7\u3092\u3042\u3057\u3089\u3063\u3066\u63cf\u304b\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30c7\u30e1\u30c6\u30eb\u306e\u5a18\u30da\u30eb\u30bb\u30dd\u30cd\u304c\u91ce\u3067\u82b1\u3092\u6458\u3093\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3068\u304d\u3001\u51a5\u754c\u306e\u795e\u30cf\u30c7\u30b9\u306b\u3055\u3089\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u5f7c\u5973\u304c\u6458\u3093\u3067\u3044\u305f\u82b1\u306f\u30d2\u30ca\u30b2\u30b7\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3068\u3044\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u82b1\u306e\u8d64\u306f\u6b7b\u5f8c\u306e\u5fa9\u6d3b\u3092\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7720\u308a\u3092\u8a98\u3046\u529b\u306f\u30da\u30eb\u30bb\u30dd\u30cd\u304c\u5730\u4e0b\u3078\u964d\u308a\u305f\u51ac\u3092\u8c61\u5fb4\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5922\u306e\u795e\u30e2\u30eb\u30da\u30a6\u30b9\u306e\u5bdd\u5e8a\u3082\u30d2\u30ca\u30b2\u30b7\u306b\u56f2\u307e\u308c\u3066\u304a\u308a\u3001\u30e2\u30eb\u30d2\u30cd\u3082\u3053\u306e\u690d\u7269\u306e\u963f\u7247\u304b\u3089\u5f97\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Como a papoula cresce em campos cultivados, foi associada a Dem\xe9ter, a deusa do gr\xe3o; ela \xe9 muitas vezes representada com papoulas na cabe\xe7a ou na m\xe3o. Quando a filha de Dem\xe9ter, Pers\xe9fone, foi raptada por Hades, deus do submundo, enquanto colhia flores no prado, diz-se que as flores que ela colhia eram papoulas; o vermelho da flor simboliza a ressurrei\xe7\xe3o ap\xf3s a morte, e seu poder de induzir o sono o inverno em que Pers\xe9fone desceu. Na mitologia grega, o leito de Morfeu, deus dos sonhos, tamb\xe9m \xe9 cercado de papoulas; a morfina, igualmente, \xe9 obtida do \xf3pio desta planta.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Poppies_in_the_Sunset_on_Lake_Geneva.jpg/330px-Poppies_in_the_Sunset_on_Lake_Geneva.jpg"},{id:"plant-097",emoji:"\ud83e\udeb4",color:"#9C7A3C",name:"Ginseng",nameEn:"Ginseng",nameDe:"Ginseng",nameEs:"Ginseng",nameFr:"Ginseng",nameJa:"\u9ad8\u9e97\u4eba\u53c2",namePt:"Ginseng",origin:"\xc7in & Kore Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Chinese & Korean Tradition",originDe:"Chinesische & koreanische Tradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n china y coreana",originFr:"Tradition chinoise et cor\xe9enne",originJa:"\u4e2d\u56fd\u30fb\u671d\u9bae\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o chinesa e coreana",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["\u015fifa","canl\u0131l\u0131k","uzun \xf6m\xfcr","g\xfc\xe7"],propertiesEn:["healing","vitality","longevity","strength"],propertiesDe:["Heilung","Vitalit\xe4t","Langlebigkeit","Kraft"],propertiesEs:["sanaci\xf3n","vitalidad","longevidad","fuerza"],propertiesFr:["gu\xe9rison","vitalit\xe9","long\xe9vit\xe9","force"],propertiesJa:["\u7652\u3057","\u6d3b\u529b","\u9577\u5bff","\u529b"],propertiesPt:["cura","vitalidade","longevidade","for\xe7a"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc d\u0131\u015far\u0131da de\u011fil, derin k\xf6klerinde ara; ger\xe7ek canl\u0131l\u0131k yava\u015f ve sab\u0131rla biriken bir hazinedir. Ginseng sana y\u0131llar i\xe7inde sessizce olgunla\u015fan bir k\xf6k\xfcn, en zorlu anda seni aya\u011fa kald\u0131racak g\xfcc\xfc ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, seek your strength not outside but in your deep roots; true vitality is a treasure gathered slowly and with patience. Ginseng reminds you that a root quietly maturing over years carries the strength to lift you up in your hardest moment.",dailyMessageDe:"Suche heute deine Kraft nicht au\xdfen, sondern in deinen tiefen Wurzeln; wahre Vitalit\xe4t ist ein Schatz, der langsam und geduldig w\xe4chst. Ginseng erinnert dich daran, dass eine \xfcber Jahre still reifende Wurzel die Kraft tr\xe4gt, dich im schwersten Augenblick aufzurichten.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, busca tu fuerza no afuera sino en tus ra\xedces profundas; la verdadera vitalidad es un tesoro que se re\xfane lento y con paciencia. El ginseng te recuerda que una ra\xedz que madura en silencio durante a\xf1os lleva la fuerza para levantarte en tu momento m\xe1s dif\xedcil.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, cherche ta force non au-dehors mais dans tes racines profondes ; la vraie vitalit\xe9 est un tr\xe9sor amass\xe9 lentement et avec patience. Le ginseng te rappelle qu'une racine qui m\xfbrit en silence pendant des ann\xe9es porte la force de te relever dans ton instant le plus dur.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u529b\u3092\u5916\u306b\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u6df1\u3044\u6839\u306b\u6c42\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u771f\u306e\u6d3b\u529b\u306f\u3001\u3086\u3063\u304f\u308a\u3068\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u84c4\u3048\u3089\u308c\u308b\u5b9d\u3067\u3059\u3002\u9ad8\u9e97\u4eba\u53c2\u306f\u3001\u9577\u3044\u5e74\u6708\u3092\u304b\u3051\u3066\u9759\u304b\u306b\u719f\u3059\u6839\u304c\u3001\u6700\u3082\u82e6\u3057\u3044\u3068\u304d\u306b\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u8d77\u304d\u4e0a\u304c\u3089\u305b\u308b\u529b\u3092\u5bbf\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, busque a sua for\xe7a n\xe3o fora, mas nas suas ra\xedzes profundas; a verdadeira vitalidade \xe9 um tesouro reunido devagar e com paci\xeancia. O ginseng lembra voc\xea de que uma raiz que amadurece em sil\xeancio por anos carrega a for\xe7a para erguer voc\xea no seu momento mais dif\xedcil.",howToUse:"Kurutulmu\u015f ginseng k\xf6k\xfcnden \u0131l\u0131k bir \xe7ay demleyerek canl\u0131l\u0131k ve \u015fifa niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. K\xfc\xe7\xfck bir par\xe7a k\xf6k\xfc yan\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131mak da g\xfc\xe7 ve dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k niyetini onurland\u0131ran sembolik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may brew a warm tea from dried ginseng root to accompany an intention of vitality and healing. Carrying a small piece of root with you is also a symbolic gesture honoring an intention of strength and endurance.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst aus getrockneter Ginsengwurzel einen warmen Tee aufbr\xfchen, um eine Absicht von Vitalit\xe4t und Heilung zu begleiten. Ein kleines St\xfcck Wurzel bei dir zu tragen ist ebenfalls eine symbolische Geste, die eine Absicht von Kraft und Ausdauer ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes preparar un t\xe9 tibio con ra\xedz de ginseng seca para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de vitalidad y sanaci\xf3n. Llevar un trocito de ra\xedz contigo es tambi\xe9n un gesto simb\xf3lico que honra una intenci\xf3n de fuerza y resistencia.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux infuser un th\xe9 ti\xe8de \xe0 partir de racine de ginseng s\xe9ch\xe9e pour accompagner une intention de vitalit\xe9 et de gu\xe9rison. Porter un petit morceau de racine sur toi est aussi un geste symbolique qui honore une intention de force et d'endurance.",howToUseJa:"\u4e7e\u3044\u305f\u9ad8\u9e97\u4eba\u53c2\u306e\u6839\u304b\u3089\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u304a\u8336\u3092\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u6d3b\u529b\u3068\u7652\u3057\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u6839\u306e\u304b\u3051\u3089\u3092\u6301\u3061\u6b69\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u529b\u3068\u5fcd\u8010\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u306a\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode preparar um ch\xe1 morno a partir de raiz de ginseng seca para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de vitalidade e cura. Carregar um pequeno peda\xe7o de raiz consigo \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto simb\xf3lico que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de for\xe7a e resist\xeancia.",affirmation:"G\xfcc\xfcm\xfc derin k\xf6klerimden al\u0131yorum, canl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131m sab\u0131rla olgunla\u015f\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I draw my strength from my deep roots, and my vitality ripens with patience.",affirmationDe:"Ich sch\xf6pfe meine Kraft aus meinen tiefen Wurzeln, und meine Vitalit\xe4t reift mit Geduld.",affirmationEs:"Tomo mi fuerza de mis ra\xedces profundas, y mi vitalidad madura con paciencia.",affirmationFr:"Je puise ma force dans mes racines profondes, et ma vitalit\xe9 m\xfbrit avec patience.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6df1\u3044\u6839\u304b\u3089\u529b\u3092\u5f97\u3066\u3001\u6d3b\u529b\u304c\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u719f\u3057\u3066\u3086\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Tiro a minha for\xe7a das minhas ra\xedzes profundas, e a minha vitalidade amadurece com paci\xeancia.",myth:"Ginsengin Latince ad\u0131 'panax', Yunanca 'tam iyile\u015fme' anlam\u0131na gelen 'panacea'dan t\xfcremi\u015ftir ve bitkinin kutsal bir adada yeti\u015fti\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131r. Kore mitolojisinde fakir ve hasta bir adam\u0131n k\xfc\xe7\xfck o\u011flu da\u011flar\u0131n ruhuna dua eder; o gece ruh \xe7ocu\u011fun r\xfcyas\u0131na girip babas\u0131n\u0131n \u015fifas\u0131n\u0131n ginsengde oldu\u011funu ve onu nerede bulaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 s\xf6yler. \xc7ocuk k\xf6k\xfc bulup kaynat\u0131r, babas\u0131na i\xe7irir ve adam iyile\u015fip sa\u011fl\u0131\u011f\u0131na kavu\u015fur. Bir ba\u015fka anlat\u0131da zindana at\u0131lan bir adam \xf6fkeyle ginseng k\xf6k\xfcn\xfc yutunca \xf6yle bir g\xfc\xe7 bulur ki demir parmakl\u0131klar\u0131 b\xfckerek d\u0131\u015far\u0131 \xe7\u0131kar.",mythEn:"Ginseng's Latin name 'panax' derives from the Greek 'panacea,' meaning 'complete healing,' and the plant is believed to grow on a sacred island. In Korean myth, the little son of a poor, sick man prays to the spirit of the mountains; that night the spirit appears in the boy's dream and tells him his father's cure lies in ginseng and where to find it. The boy finds the root, boils it, gives it to his father, and the man recovers his health. In another tale, a man cast into a dungeon swallows a ginseng root in anger and finds such strength that he bends the iron bars and walks out.",mythDe:"Der lateinische Name des Ginsengs, 'panax', leitet sich vom griechischen 'panacea' ab, was 'vollst\xe4ndige Heilung' bedeutet, und man glaubt, die Pflanze wachse auf einer heiligen Insel. In der koreanischen Mythologie betet der kleine Sohn eines armen, kranken Mannes zum Geist der Berge; in jener Nacht erscheint der Geist im Traum des Jungen und sagt ihm, die Heilung seines Vaters liege im Ginseng und wo er ihn finde. Der Junge findet die Wurzel, kocht sie, gibt sie dem Vater, und der Mann gewinnt seine Gesundheit zur\xfcck. In einer anderen Erz\xe4hlung verschlingt ein in den Kerker geworfener Mann zornig eine Ginsengwurzel und findet solche Kraft, dass er die Eisengitter verbiegt und hinausgeht.",mythEs:"El nombre latino del ginseng, 'panax', deriva del griego 'panacea', que significa 'curaci\xf3n completa', y se cree que la planta crece en una isla sagrada. En la mitolog\xeda coreana, el peque\xf1o hijo de un hombre pobre y enfermo reza al esp\xedritu de las monta\xf1as; esa noche el esp\xedritu aparece en el sue\xf1o del ni\xf1o y le dice que la cura de su padre est\xe1 en el ginseng y d\xf3nde encontrarlo. El ni\xf1o halla la ra\xedz, la hierve, se la da a su padre, y el hombre recupera la salud. En otro relato, un hombre arrojado a un calabozo traga una ra\xedz de ginseng con ira y halla tal fuerza que dobla los barrotes de hierro y sale.",mythFr:"Le nom latin du ginseng, 'panax', d\xe9rive du grec 'panac\xe9e', qui signifie 'gu\xe9rison compl\xe8te', et l'on croit que la plante pousse sur une \xeele sacr\xe9e. Dans la mythologie cor\xe9enne, le petit fils d'un homme pauvre et malade prie l'esprit des montagnes ; cette nuit-l\xe0, l'esprit appara\xeet dans le r\xeave de l'enfant et lui dit que la gu\xe9rison de son p\xe8re r\xe9side dans le ginseng et o\xf9 le trouver. L'enfant trouve la racine, la fait bouillir, la donne \xe0 son p\xe8re, et l'homme recouvre la sant\xe9. Dans un autre r\xe9cit, un homme jet\xe9 dans un cachot avale une racine de ginseng de col\xe8re et trouve une telle force qu'il tord les barreaux de fer et sort.",mythJa:"\u9ad8\u9e97\u4eba\u53c2\u306e\u30e9\u30c6\u30f3\u540d\u300e\u30d1\u30ca\u30af\u30b9\u300f\u306f\u3001\u300e\u5b8c\u5168\u306a\u7652\u3057\u300f\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3059\u308b\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u8a9e\u300e\u30d1\u30ca\u30b1\u30a2\u300f\u306b\u7531\u6765\u3057\u3001\u3053\u306e\u690d\u7269\u306f\u8056\u306a\u308b\u5cf6\u306b\u80b2\u3064\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u671d\u9bae\u306e\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u8ca7\u3057\u304f\u75c5\u3093\u3060\u7537\u306e\u5e7c\u3044\u606f\u5b50\u304c\u5c71\u306e\u7cbe\u970a\u306b\u7948\u308b\u3068\u3001\u305d\u306e\u591c\u3001\u7cbe\u970a\u304c\u5c11\u5e74\u306e\u5922\u306b\u73fe\u308c\u3001\u7236\u306e\u6cbb\u7652\u306f\u9ad8\u9e97\u4eba\u53c2\u306b\u3042\u308a\u3001\u305d\u308c\u304c\u3069\u3053\u306b\u3042\u308b\u304b\u3092\u544a\u3052\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5c11\u5e74\u306f\u6839\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u3001\u716e\u3066\u7236\u306b\u98f2\u307e\u305b\u3001\u7537\u306f\u5065\u5eb7\u3092\u53d6\u308a\u623b\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5225\u306e\u7269\u8a9e\u3067\u306f\u3001\u7262\u306b\u6295\u3052\u8fbc\u307e\u308c\u305f\u7537\u304c\u6012\u308a\u306e\u307e\u307e\u9ad8\u9e97\u4eba\u53c2\u306e\u6839\u3092\u5451\u307f\u8fbc\u3080\u3068\u3001\u9244\u683c\u5b50\u3092\u66f2\u3052\u3066\u5916\u3078\u51fa\u308b\u307b\u3069\u306e\u529b\u3092\u5f97\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"O nome latino do ginseng, 'panax', deriva do grego 'panaceia', que significa 'cura completa', e acredita-se que a planta cres\xe7a em uma ilha sagrada. Na mitologia coreana, o pequeno filho de um homem pobre e doente reza ao esp\xedrito das montanhas; naquela noite o esp\xedrito aparece no sonho do menino e lhe diz que a cura de seu pai est\xe1 no ginseng e onde encontr\xe1-lo. O menino acha a raiz, ferve-a, d\xe1-a ao pai, e o homem recupera a sa\xfade. Em outro relato, um homem lan\xe7ado numa masmorra engole uma raiz de ginseng com raiva e encontra tamanha for\xe7a que entorta as grades de ferro e sai.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Insam_%28ginseng%29.jpg/330px-Insam_%28ginseng%29.jpg"},{id:"plant-098",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#3E6B4C",name:"Hayat A\u011fac\u0131",nameEn:"Tree of Life",nameDe:"Lebensbaum",nameEs:"\xc1rbol de la Vida",nameFr:"Arbre de Vie",nameJa:"\u751f\u547d\u306e\u6a39",namePt:"\xc1rvore da Vida",origin:"T\xfcrk & Mezopotamya Mitolojisi",originEn:"Turkic & Mesopotamian Mythology",originDe:"T\xfcrkische & mesopotamische Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda t\xfarquica y mesopot\xe1mica",originFr:"Mythologie turque et m\xe9sopotamienne",originJa:"\u30c6\u30e5\u30eb\u30af\u30fb\u30e1\u30bd\u30dd\u30bf\u30df\u30a2\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia t\xfarquica e mesopot\xe2mica",element:"eter",elementEn:"ether",elementDe:"\xc4ther",elementEs:"\xe9ter",elementFr:"\xe9ther",elementJa:"\u30a8\u30fc\u30c6\u30eb",elementPt:"\xe9ter",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["ya\u015fam","b\xfct\xfcnl\xfck","ba\u011flant\u0131","sonsuzluk","k\xf6k"],propertiesEn:["life","wholeness","connection","eternity","roots"],propertiesDe:["Leben","Ganzheit","Verbindung","Ewigkeit","Wurzeln"],propertiesEs:["vida","totalidad","conexi\xf3n","eternidad","ra\xedces"],propertiesFr:["vie","pl\xe9nitude","connexion","\xe9ternit\xe9","racines"],propertiesJa:["\u751f\u547d","\u5168\u4f53\u6027","\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a","\u6c38\u9060","\u6839"],propertiesPt:["vida","totalidade","conex\xe3o","eternidade","ra\xedzes"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn hem k\xf6klerini hem dallar\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rla; ger\xe7ek b\xfct\xfcnl\xfck, derinlerle g\xf6\u011f\xfc ayn\u0131 anda ta\u015f\u0131yabilmektir. Hayat A\u011fac\u0131 sana yerden beslenip g\xf6\u011fe uzanan bir varl\u0131k oldu\u011funu, her \u015feyle g\xf6r\xfcnmez bir ba\u011f i\xe7inde durdu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember both your roots and your branches; true wholeness is to hold the depths and the sky at once. The Tree of Life whispers that you are a being nourished by the earth and reaching toward the sky, standing in an invisible bond with all things.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute sowohl an deine Wurzeln als auch an deine \xc4ste; wahre Ganzheit ist es, die Tiefe und den Himmel zugleich zu tragen. Der Lebensbaum fl\xfcstert, dass du ein Wesen bist, von der Erde gen\xe4hrt und zum Himmel strebend, das in einer unsichtbaren Verbindung mit allem steht.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda tanto tus ra\xedces como tus ramas; la verdadera totalidad es sostener las profundidades y el cielo a la vez. El \xc1rbol de la Vida susurra que eres un ser nutrido por la tierra y que se extiende hacia el cielo, en un v\xednculo invisible con todas las cosas.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi de tes racines comme de tes branches ; la vraie pl\xe9nitude, c'est de porter les profondeurs et le ciel \xe0 la fois. L'Arbre de Vie murmure que tu es un \xeatre nourri par la terre et tendu vers le ciel, en lien invisible avec toute chose.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u6839\u3068\u679d\u306e\u4e21\u65b9\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u771f\u306e\u5168\u4f53\u6027\u3068\u306f\u3001\u6df1\u307f\u3068\u7a7a\u3092\u540c\u6642\u306b\u62b1\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3002\u751f\u547d\u306e\u6a39\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u304c\u5927\u5730\u306b\u990a\u308f\u308c\u5929\u3078\u3068\u4f38\u3073\u308b\u5b58\u5728\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u3059\u3079\u3066\u3068\u76ee\u306b\u898b\u3048\u306a\u3044\u7d46\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u7acb\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se tanto das suas ra\xedzes quanto dos seus galhos; a verdadeira totalidade \xe9 sustentar as profundezas e o c\xe9u ao mesmo tempo. A \xc1rvore da Vida sussurra que voc\xea \xe9 um ser nutrido pela terra e que se estende rumo ao c\xe9u, em um v\xednculo invis\xedvel com todas as coisas.",howToUse:"Sevdi\u011fin bir a\u011fac\u0131n g\xf6vdesine elini koyup nefesini onun ritmiyle e\u015fle\u015ftirerek ya\u015famla ba\u011f kurabilirsin. Bir hayat a\u011fac\u0131 sembol\xfcn\xfc \xe7izmek ya da yan\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131mak da b\xfct\xfcnl\xfck ve ba\u011flant\u0131 niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may place your hand on the trunk of a tree you love and match your breath to its rhythm to connect with life. Drawing a tree-of-life symbol or carrying one with you is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of wholeness and connection.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst deine Hand auf den Stamm eines Baumes legen, den du liebst, und deinen Atem seinem Rhythmus angleichen, um dich mit dem Leben zu verbinden. Ein Lebensbaum-Symbol zu zeichnen oder bei dir zu tragen ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Ganzheit und Verbindung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes poner la mano sobre el tronco de un \xe1rbol que ames y acompasar tu respiraci\xf3n a su ritmo para conectar con la vida. Dibujar un s\xedmbolo del \xe1rbol de la vida o llevarlo contigo es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de totalidad y conexi\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux poser la main sur le tronc d'un arbre que tu aimes et accorder ton souffle \xe0 son rythme pour te relier \xe0 la vie. Dessiner un symbole d'arbre de vie ou le porter sur toi est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de pl\xe9nitude et de connexion.",howToUseJa:"\u611b\u3059\u308b\u6728\u306e\u5e79\u306b\u624b\u3092\u7f6e\u304d\u3001\u547c\u5438\u3092\u305d\u306e\u5f8b\u52d5\u306b\u5408\u308f\u305b\u3066\u751f\u547d\u3068\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u751f\u547d\u306e\u6a39\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3092\u63cf\u3044\u305f\u308a\u6301\u3061\u6b69\u3044\u305f\u308a\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u5168\u4f53\u6027\u3068\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode pousar a m\xe3o no tronco de uma \xe1rvore que ama e ajustar a sua respira\xe7\xe3o ao ritmo dela para se conectar com a vida. Desenhar um s\xedmbolo da \xe1rvore da vida ou carreg\xe1-lo consigo \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de totalidade e conex\xe3o.",affirmation:"K\xf6klerimle beslenip dallar\u0131mla g\xf6\u011fe uzan\u0131yorum, her \u015feyle ba\u011f i\xe7indeyim.",affirmationEn:"Nourished by my roots, I reach toward the sky with my branches, in bond with all things.",affirmationDe:"Von meinen Wurzeln gen\xe4hrt, strebe ich mit meinen \xc4sten zum Himmel, in Verbindung mit allem.",affirmationEs:"Nutrido por mis ra\xedces, me extiendo hacia el cielo con mis ramas, en v\xednculo con todo.",affirmationFr:"Nourri par mes racines, je m'\xe9l\xe8ve vers le ciel par mes branches, en lien avec tout.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6839\u306b\u990a\u308f\u308c\u3001\u679d\u3067\u5929\u306b\u4f38\u3073\u3001\u3059\u3079\u3066\u3068\u3064\u306a\u304c\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Nutrido pelas minhas ra\xedzes, estendo-me ao c\xe9u com os meus galhos, em v\xednculo com tudo.",myth:"Do\u011fa dinlerinden tek tanr\u0131l\u0131 inan\xe7lara dek pek \xe7ok k\xfclt\xfcrde hayat a\u011fac\u0131, ya\u015fam\u0131n ve var olma bilincinin sembol\xfcd\xfcr. \u0130skandinav mitolojisinde d\xfcnyan\u0131n merkezinde duran kader a\u011fac\u0131 Yggdrasil'in \xfc\xe7 k\xf6k\xfc cehenneme, devlerin \xfclkesine ve insanlar\u0131n topraklar\u0131na uzan\u0131r; bu a\u011fa\xe7 ilk insan\u0131n do\u011fdu\u011fu a\u011fa\xe7 olarak da bilinir. T\xfcrk mitolojisinde g\xf6vdesi som g\xfcm\xfc\u015ften, g\xf6\u011fe kadar y\xfckselen Bay Terek, g\xf6k ile yeri birbirine ba\u011flar; \xf6len insanlar\u0131n ruhu ku\u015f olup onun dallar\u0131na konar, yeni canlar ise g\xf6vdesinden inerek yery\xfcz\xfcne ula\u015f\u0131r. Mezopotamya'da bu inan\xe7, g\xf6k ile yeri birle\u015ftiren kutsal zigurat da\u011flar\u0131nda yank\u0131 bulur.",mythEn:"From nature religions to monotheistic faiths, in many cultures the tree of life is the symbol of life and of the awareness of being. In Norse myth, the three roots of Yggdrasil, the tree of fate standing at the center of the world, reach to the underworld, to the land of giants, and to the lands of humankind; this tree is also known as the one from which the first human was born. In Turkic myth, Bay Terek, with a trunk of pure silver rising to the sky, binds heaven and earth; the souls of the dead become birds and alight on its branches, while new souls descend through its trunk to reach the earth. In Mesopotamia, this belief echoes in the sacred ziggurat mountains that join heaven and earth.",mythDe:"Von den Naturreligionen bis zu den monotheistischen Glauben ist der Lebensbaum in vielen Kulturen das Symbol des Lebens und des Bewusstseins des Seins. In der nordischen Mythologie reichen die drei Wurzeln Yggdrasils, des Schicksalsbaums im Zentrum der Welt, in die Unterwelt, in das Land der Riesen und in die L\xe4nder der Menschen; dieser Baum ist auch als jener bekannt, aus dem der erste Mensch geboren wurde. In der t\xfcrkischen Mythologie verbindet Bay Terek, mit einem Stamm aus reinem Silber, der bis zum Himmel ragt, Himmel und Erde; die Seelen der Toten werden zu V\xf6geln und lassen sich auf seinen \xc4sten nieder, w\xe4hrend neue Seelen durch seinen Stamm hinabsteigen, um die Erde zu erreichen. In Mesopotamien hallt dieser Glaube in den heiligen Zikkurat-Bergen wider, die Himmel und Erde verbinden.",mythEs:"Desde las religiones de la naturaleza hasta las fes monote\xedstas, en muchas culturas el \xe1rbol de la vida es el s\xedmbolo de la vida y de la conciencia del ser. En la mitolog\xeda n\xf3rdica, las tres ra\xedces de Yggdrasil, el \xe1rbol del destino que se alza en el centro del mundo, llegan al inframundo, a la tierra de los gigantes y a las tierras de los humanos; este \xe1rbol tambi\xe9n es conocido como aquel del que naci\xf3 el primer ser humano. En la mitolog\xeda t\xfarquica, Bay Terek, con un tronco de plata pura que se eleva al cielo, une cielo y tierra; las almas de los muertos se vuelven p\xe1jaros y se posan en sus ramas, mientras las almas nuevas descienden por su tronco para llegar a la tierra. En Mesopotamia, esta creencia resuena en las monta\xf1as sagradas de los zigurats que unen cielo y tierra.",mythFr:"Des religions de la nature aux fois monoth\xe9istes, dans bien des cultures l'arbre de vie est le symbole de la vie et de la conscience d'\xeatre. Dans la mythologie nordique, les trois racines d'Yggdrasil, l'arbre du destin dress\xe9 au centre du monde, atteignent les enfers, le pays des g\xe9ants et les terres des hommes ; cet arbre est aussi connu comme celui dont naquit le premier humain. Dans la mythologie turque, Bay Terek, au tronc d'argent pur s'\xe9levant jusqu'au ciel, unit le ciel et la terre ; les \xe2mes des morts deviennent oiseaux et se posent sur ses branches, tandis que les \xe2mes nouvelles descendent par son tronc pour atteindre la terre. En M\xe9sopotamie, cette croyance r\xe9sonne dans les montagnes sacr\xe9es des ziggourats qui joignent le ciel et la terre.",mythJa:"\u81ea\u7136\u5d07\u62dd\u306e\u5b97\u6559\u304b\u3089\u4e00\u795e\u6559\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u307e\u3067\u3001\u591a\u304f\u306e\u6587\u5316\u3067\u751f\u547d\u306e\u6a39\u306f\u751f\u547d\u3068\u5b58\u5728\u306e\u610f\u8b58\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3059\u3002\u5317\u6b27\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u4e16\u754c\u306e\u4e2d\u5fc3\u306b\u7acb\u3064\u904b\u547d\u306e\u6a39\u30e6\u30b0\u30c9\u30e9\u30b7\u30eb\u306e\u4e09\u3064\u306e\u6839\u304c\u3001\u51a5\u754c\u3001\u5de8\u4eba\u306e\u56fd\u3001\u4eba\u9593\u306e\u5730\u3078\u3068\u4f38\u3073\u3001\u3053\u306e\u6a39\u306f\u6700\u521d\u306e\u4eba\u9593\u304c\u751f\u307e\u308c\u305f\u6a39\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3082\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30c6\u30e5\u30eb\u30af\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u7d14\u9280\u306e\u5e79\u3092\u6301\u3061\u5929\u307e\u3067\u4f38\u3073\u308b\u30d0\u30a4\u30fb\u30c6\u30ec\u30af\u304c\u5929\u3068\u5730\u3092\u7d50\u3073\u3001\u6b7b\u8005\u306e\u9b42\u306f\u9ce5\u3068\u306a\u3063\u3066\u305d\u306e\u679d\u306b\u6b62\u307e\u308a\u3001\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u9b42\u306f\u305d\u306e\u5e79\u3092\u4f1d\u3063\u3066\u5730\u4e0a\u3078\u964d\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30e1\u30bd\u30dd\u30bf\u30df\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u3001\u3053\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u306f\u5929\u3068\u5730\u3092\u7d50\u3076\u8056\u306a\u308b\u30b8\u30c3\u30b0\u30e9\u30c8\u306e\u5c71\u3005\u306b\u97ff\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Das religi\xf5es da natureza \xe0s f\xe9s monote\xedstas, em muitas culturas a \xe1rvore da vida \xe9 o s\xedmbolo da vida e da consci\xeancia de existir. Na mitologia n\xf3rdica, as tr\xeas ra\xedzes de Yggdrasil, a \xe1rvore do destino que se ergue no centro do mundo, alcan\xe7am o submundo, a terra dos gigantes e as terras dos humanos; essa \xe1rvore tamb\xe9m \xe9 conhecida como aquela da qual nasceu o primeiro ser humano. Na mitologia t\xfarquica, Bay Terek, com um tronco de prata pura que se eleva ao c\xe9u, une c\xe9u e terra; as almas dos mortos tornam-se p\xe1ssaros e pousam em seus galhos, enquanto as almas novas descem pelo seu tronco para alcan\xe7ar a terra. Na Mesopot\xe2mia, essa cren\xe7a ecoa nas montanhas sagradas dos zigurates que unem c\xe9u e terra.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Yggdrasil.jpg/330px-Yggdrasil.jpg"},{id:"plant-099",emoji:"\ud83e\udd52",color:"#5A8F3C",name:"H\u0131yar",nameEn:"Cucumber",nameDe:"Gurke",nameEs:"Pepino",nameFr:"Concombre",nameJa:"\u30ad\u30e5\u30a6\u30ea",namePt:"Pepino",origin:"Mezopotamya (S\xfcmer)",originEn:"Mesopotamia (Sumer)",originDe:"Mesopotamien (Sumer)",originEs:"Mesopotamia (Sumeria)",originFr:"M\xe9sopotamie (Sumer)",originJa:"\u30e1\u30bd\u30dd\u30bf\u30df\u30a2\uff08\u30b7\u30e5\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\uff09",originPt:"Mesopot\xe2mia (Sum\xe9ria)",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u4ed9\u9aa8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacral",properties:["tazelik","serinlik","bereket","ar\u0131nma"],propertiesEn:["freshness","coolness","abundance","cleansing"],propertiesDe:["Frische","K\xfchle","F\xfclle","Reinigung"],propertiesEs:["frescura","frescor","abundancia","purificaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["fra\xeecheur","fra\xeecheur","abondance","purification"],propertiesJa:["\u65b0\u9bae\u3055","\u6dbc\u3084\u304b\u3055","\u8c4a\u7a63","\u6d44\u5316"],propertiesPt:["frescor","frescura","abund\xe2ncia","purifica\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn serinkanl\u0131 kal; sular nas\u0131l topra\u011f\u0131 bereketle dolduruyorsa, sab\u0131r da tela\u015fl\u0131 y\xfcre\u011fini yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131r. H\u0131yar sana tatl\u0131 suyun de\u011fdi\u011fi yerde ya\u015fam\u0131n ye\u015ferdi\u011fini, sakinli\u011fin bir bereket kayna\u011f\u0131 oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, stay cool-headed; just as waters fill the earth with abundance, patience soothes your hurried heart. The cucumber reminds you that where sweet water touches, life grows green, and calm is a source of abundance.",dailyMessageDe:"Bleibe heute k\xfchlen Kopfes; so wie Wasser die Erde mit F\xfclle f\xfcllt, bes\xe4nftigt Geduld dein hastiges Herz. Die Gurke erinnert dich daran, dass dort, wo s\xfc\xdfes Wasser ber\xfchrt, das Leben ergr\xfcnt und Ruhe eine Quelle der F\xfclle ist.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, mant\xe9n la cabeza fr\xeda; as\xed como las aguas llenan la tierra de abundancia, la paciencia calma tu coraz\xf3n apresurado. El pepino te recuerda que donde el agua dulce toca, la vida reverdece, y la calma es una fuente de abundancia.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, garde la t\xeate froide ; tout comme les eaux emplissent la terre d'abondance, la patience apaise ton c\u0153ur press\xe9. Le concombre te rappelle que l\xe0 o\xf9 l'eau douce touche, la vie reverdit, et que le calme est une source d'abondance.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u51b7\u9759\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6c34\u304c\u5927\u5730\u3092\u8c4a\u7a63\u3067\u6e80\u305f\u3059\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u304c\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u6025\u304f\u5fc3\u3092\u93ae\u3081\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ad\u30e5\u30a6\u30ea\u306f\u3001\u7518\u3044\u6c34\u304c\u89e6\u308c\u308b\u3068\u3053\u308d\u3067\u751f\u547d\u304c\u7dd1\u3065\u304d\u3001\u9759\u3051\u3055\u304c\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u6e90\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, mantenha a cabe\xe7a fria; assim como as \xe1guas enchem a terra de abund\xe2ncia, a paci\xeancia acalma o seu cora\xe7\xe3o apressado. O pepino lembra voc\xea de que onde a \xe1gua doce toca, a vida reverdece, e a calma \xe9 uma fonte de abund\xe2ncia.",howToUse:"Taze h\u0131yar\u0131 dilimleyip suya ya da salataya katarak serinletici bir tazelik niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bir dilim h\u0131yar\u0131 aln\u0131na ya da g\xf6zlerine koyup birka\xe7 dakika dinlenmek, ar\u0131nma ve s\xfck\xfbnet niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may slice fresh cucumber into water or a salad to accompany an intention of cooling freshness. Resting for a few minutes with a slice of cucumber on your forehead or eyes is a gentle gesture honoring an intention of cleansing and calm.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst frische Gurke in Wasser oder Salat schneiden, um eine Absicht k\xfchlender Frische zu begleiten. Ein paar Minuten mit einer Gurkenscheibe auf der Stirn oder den Augen zu ruhen ist eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Reinigung und Ruhe ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes cortar pepino fresco en agua o en una ensalada para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de frescura refrescante. Descansar unos minutos con una rodaja de pepino en la frente o los ojos es un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de purificaci\xf3n y calma.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux couper du concombre frais dans de l'eau ou une salade pour accompagner une intention de fra\xeecheur rafra\xeechissante. Te reposer quelques minutes avec une rondelle de concombre sur le front ou les yeux est un geste tendre qui honore une intention de purification et de calme.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u30ad\u30e5\u30a6\u30ea\u3092\u8584\u5207\u308a\u306b\u3057\u3066\u6c34\u3084\u30b5\u30e9\u30c0\u306b\u52a0\u3048\u3001\u6dbc\u3084\u304b\u306a\u65b0\u9bae\u3055\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ad\u30e5\u30a6\u30ea\u306e\u8584\u5207\u308a\u3092\u984d\u3084\u76ee\u306b\u7f6e\u3044\u3066\u6570\u5206\u4f11\u3080\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u6d44\u5316\u3068\u9759\u3051\u3055\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode fatiar pepino fresco na \xe1gua ou em uma salada para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de frescor refrescante. Descansar por alguns minutos com uma fatia de pepino na testa ou nos olhos \xe9 um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de purifica\xe7\xe3o e calma.",affirmation:"Serinkanl\u0131 kal\u0131yorum, sakinli\u011fim i\xe7imde bereketi besliyor.",affirmationEn:"I stay cool-headed, and my calm nourishes abundance within me.",affirmationDe:"Ich bleibe k\xfchlen Kopfes, und meine Ruhe n\xe4hrt die F\xfclle in mir.",affirmationEs:"Mantengo la cabeza fr\xeda, y mi calma nutre la abundancia en m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Je garde la t\xeate froide, et mon calme nourrit l'abondance en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u51b7\u9759\u3067\u3044\u3066\u3001\u9759\u3051\u3055\u304c\u5185\u306b\u8c4a\u7a63\u3092\u990a\u3046\u3002",affirmationPt:"Mantenho a cabe\xe7a fria, e a minha calma nutre a abund\xe2ncia dentro de mim.",myth:"S\xfcmer mitolojisinde tatl\u0131 sular\u0131n bilge tanr\u0131s\u0131 Enki, kusursuz \xfclke Dilmun'da ya\u015fard\u0131; \xfclkenin tek eksi\u011fi tatl\u0131 sudu. G\xfcne\u015f tanr\u0131 Utu Dilmun'a tatl\u0131 su getirince her yan bereketli tar\u0131m alanlar\u0131na d\xf6nd\xfc. Enki, bitki tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Uttu'yu istedi\u011finde Uttu ona h\u0131yar, \xfcz\xfcm ve elma getirmeden kendisini d\xf6llemeyece\u011fini s\xf6yler; Enki bah\xe7\u0131vana co\u015fkun sular ak\u0131t\u0131p kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131nda bu meyveleri al\u0131r ve Uttu'ya getirir. H\u0131yar b\xf6ylece Mezopotamya'n\u0131n en eski bereket ve ya\u015fam suyu mitlerine ba\u011flan\u0131r.",mythEn:"In Sumerian myth, Enki, the wise god of the sweet waters, lived in the perfect land of Dilmun; the land's only lack was fresh water. When the sun god Utu brought fresh water to Dilmun, everywhere turned into fertile farmland. When Enki desired Uttu, the goddess of plants, Uttu said she would not let him beget upon her unless he brought her cucumber, grapes, and apples; Enki sent gushing waters to the gardener and in return received these fruits, which he brought to Uttu. Thus the cucumber is bound to Mesopotamia's oldest myths of abundance and the water of life.",mythDe:"In der sumerischen Mythologie lebte Enki, der weise Gott der s\xfc\xdfen Wasser, im vollkommenen Land Dilmun; das einzige Manko des Landes war S\xfc\xdfwasser. Als der Sonnengott Utu S\xfc\xdfwasser nach Dilmun brachte, verwandelte sich alles in fruchtbares Ackerland. Als Enki Uttu, die G\xf6ttin der Pflanzen, begehrte, sagte Uttu, sie lasse sich nicht von ihm schw\xe4ngern, es sei denn, er bringe ihr Gurke, Trauben und \xc4pfel; Enki schickte sprudelnde Wasser zum G\xe4rtner und erhielt daf\xfcr diese Fr\xfcchte, die er Uttu brachte. So ist die Gurke mit Mesopotamiens \xe4ltesten Mythen von F\xfclle und dem Wasser des Lebens verbunden.",mythEs:"En la mitolog\xeda sumeria, Enki, el sabio dios de las aguas dulces, viv\xeda en la tierra perfecta de Dilmun; la \xfanica carencia de la tierra era el agua dulce. Cuando el dios sol Utu trajo agua dulce a Dilmun, todo se convirti\xf3 en tierras de cultivo f\xe9rtiles. Cuando Enki dese\xf3 a Uttu, la diosa de las plantas, Uttu dijo que no dejar\xeda que la fecundara a menos que le trajera pepino, uvas y manzanas; Enki envi\xf3 aguas caudalosas al jardinero y a cambio recibi\xf3 estos frutos, que llev\xf3 a Uttu. As\xed, el pepino se vincula a los mitos m\xe1s antiguos de Mesopotamia sobre la abundancia y el agua de la vida.",mythFr:"Dans la mythologie sum\xe9rienne, Enki, le sage dieu des eaux douces, vivait dans la terre parfaite de Dilmun ; le seul manque de la terre \xe9tait l'eau douce. Lorsque le dieu soleil Utu apporta de l'eau douce \xe0 Dilmun, tout se changea en terres fertiles. Quand Enki d\xe9sira Uttu, d\xe9esse des plantes, Uttu dit qu'elle ne le laisserait pas la f\xe9conder \xe0 moins qu'il ne lui apporte concombre, raisins et pommes ; Enki envoya des eaux jaillissantes au jardinier et re\xe7ut en retour ces fruits, qu'il porta \xe0 Uttu. Ainsi le concombre se rattache aux plus anciens mythes de M\xe9sopotamie sur l'abondance et l'eau de la vie.",mythJa:"\u30b7\u30e5\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u7518\u3044\u6c34\u306e\u8ce2\u795e\u30a8\u30f3\u30ad\u304c\u5b8c\u74a7\u306a\u56fd\u30c7\u30a3\u30eb\u30e0\u30f3\u306b\u4f4f\u3093\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u305d\u306e\u56fd\u306e\u552f\u4e00\u306e\u6b20\u3051\u306f\u771f\u6c34\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002\u592a\u967d\u795e\u30a6\u30c8\u30a5\u304c\u30c7\u30a3\u30eb\u30e0\u30f3\u306b\u771f\u6c34\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u3068\u3001\u3042\u305f\u308a\u4e00\u9762\u304c\u80a5\u6c83\u306a\u8fb2\u5730\u306b\u5909\u308f\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30a8\u30f3\u30ad\u304c\u690d\u7269\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30a6\u30c3\u30c8\u30a5\u3092\u6c42\u3081\u308b\u3068\u3001\u30a6\u30c3\u30c8\u30a5\u306f\u30ad\u30e5\u30a6\u30ea\u3001\u30d6\u30c9\u30a6\u3001\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3092\u6301\u3063\u3066\u3053\u306a\u3051\u308c\u3070\u8eab\u3054\u3082\u3089\u305b\u306f\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3068\u8a00\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30a8\u30f3\u30ad\u306f\u5ead\u5e2b\u306b\u6ea2\u308c\u308b\u6c34\u3092\u9001\u308a\u3001\u305d\u306e\u8fd4\u793c\u306b\u3053\u308c\u3089\u306e\u679c\u5b9f\u3092\u5f97\u3066\u3001\u30a6\u30c3\u30c8\u30a5\u306e\u3082\u3068\u3078\u6301\u3063\u3066\u3044\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u30ad\u30e5\u30a6\u30ea\u306f\u30e1\u30bd\u30dd\u30bf\u30df\u30a2\u6700\u53e4\u306e\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u751f\u547d\u306e\u6c34\u306e\u795e\u8a71\u306b\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u3051\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na mitologia sum\xe9ria, Enki, o s\xe1bio deus das \xe1guas doces, vivia na terra perfeita de Dilmun; a \xfanica falta da terra era \xe1gua doce. Quando o deus sol Utu trouxe \xe1gua doce a Dilmun, tudo se tornou terra f\xe9rtil de cultivo. Quando Enki desejou Uttu, a deusa das plantas, Uttu disse que n\xe3o o deixaria fecund\xe1-la a menos que ele lhe trouxesse pepino, uvas e ma\xe7\xe3s; Enki enviou \xe1guas caudalosas ao jardineiro e em troca recebeu esses frutos, que levou a Uttu. Assim o pepino liga-se aos mais antigos mitos da Mesopot\xe2mia sobre a abund\xe2ncia e a \xe1gua da vida.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/ARS_cucumber.jpg/330px-ARS_cucumber.jpg"},{id:"plant-100",emoji:"\ud83c\udf34",color:"#A0682B",name:"Hurma",nameEn:"Date Palm",nameDe:"Dattelpalme",nameEs:"D\xe1til",nameFr:"Datte",nameJa:"\u30ca\u30c4\u30e1\u30e4\u30b7",namePt:"T\xe2mara",origin:"Arap Yar\u0131madas\u0131 & \u0130slam Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Arabian Peninsula & Islamic Tradition",originDe:"Arabische Halbinsel & islamische Tradition",originEs:"Pen\xednsula ar\xe1biga y tradici\xf3n isl\xe1mica",originFr:"P\xe9ninsule arabique et tradition islamique",originJa:"\u30a2\u30e9\u30d3\u30a2\u534a\u5cf6\u30fb\u30a4\u30b9\u30e9\u30e0\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Pen\xednsula Ar\xe1bica e tradi\xe7\xe3o isl\xe2mica",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Solar Pleksus \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u592a\u967d\u795e\u7d4c\u53e2\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["bereket","kutsall\u0131k","besin","\u015f\xfck\xfcr"],propertiesEn:["abundance","sacredness","nourishment","gratitude"],propertiesDe:["F\xfclle","Heiligkeit","Nahrung","Dankbarkeit"],propertiesEs:["abundancia","sacralidad","alimento","gratitud"],propertiesFr:["abondance","sacralit\xe9","nourriture","gratitude"],propertiesJa:["\u8c4a\u7a63","\u8056\u6027","\u7ce7","\u611f\u8b1d"],propertiesPt:["abund\xe2ncia","sacralidade","alimento","gratid\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn en \xe7etin an\u0131nda bile dayanaca\u011f\u0131n bir dal oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rla; sanc\u0131 ge\xe7er, ard\u0131ndan tatl\u0131 bir bereket d\xfc\u015fer. Hurma sana sab\u0131rla bekleyenin elinin bo\u015f kalmayaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131, zorluktan sonra besleyici bir tatl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n geldi\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that even in your hardest moment there is a branch to lean on; the pang passes, and a sweet abundance falls after it. The date palm whispers that the one who waits with patience will not be left empty-handed, and that a nourishing sweetness comes after hardship.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass es selbst in deinem schwersten Augenblick einen Zweig gibt, an den du dich lehnen kannst; der Schmerz vergeht, und danach f\xe4llt eine s\xfc\xdfe F\xfclle herab. Die Dattelpalme fl\xfcstert, dass der geduldig Wartende nicht mit leeren H\xe4nden bleibt und dass nach der H\xe4rte eine n\xe4hrende S\xfc\xdfe kommt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que incluso en tu momento m\xe1s duro hay una rama en la que apoyarte; el dolor pasa, y tras \xe9l cae una dulce abundancia. El d\xe1til susurra que quien espera con paciencia no quedar\xe1 con las manos vac\xedas, y que tras la dureza llega una dulzura nutritiva.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que m\xeame dans ton instant le plus dur il y a une branche o\xf9 t'appuyer ; la douleur passe, et apr\xe8s elle tombe une douce abondance. La datte murmure que celui qui attend avec patience ne restera pas les mains vides, et qu'apr\xe8s l'\xe9preuve vient une douceur nourrissante.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u6700\u3082\u82e6\u3057\u3044\u3068\u304d\u3067\u3082\u5bc4\u308a\u304b\u304b\u308b\u679d\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u75db\u307f\u306f\u904e\u304e\u3001\u305d\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306b\u7518\u3044\u8c4a\u7a63\u304c\u964d\u308a\u6ce8\u304e\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ca\u30c4\u30e1\u30e4\u30b7\u306f\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u5f85\u3064\u8005\u306e\u624b\u304c\u7a7a\u306e\u307e\u307e\u306b\u306f\u306a\u3089\u305a\u3001\u82e6\u96e3\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306b\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u7518\u3055\u304c\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que mesmo no seu momento mais dif\xedcil h\xe1 um galho para se apoiar; a dor passa, e depois dela cai uma doce abund\xe2ncia. A t\xe2mara sussurra que quem espera com paci\xeancia n\xe3o ficar\xe1 de m\xe3os vazias, e que depois da dificuldade vem uma do\xe7ura nutritiva.",howToUse:"Olgun hurmay\u0131 taze ya da kuru olarak tadabilir, onunla orucunu ya da g\xfcn\xfcn\xfc tatl\u0131 bir \u015f\xfck\xfcrle a\xe7abilirsin. Bir avu\xe7 hurmay\u0131 bir k\xe2seye koyup payla\u015fmak, bereket ve \u015f\xfckran niyetini onurland\u0131ran eski bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may enjoy ripe dates fresh or dried, breaking your fast or your day with a sweet gratitude. Placing a handful of dates in a bowl to share is an ancient gesture honoring an intention of abundance and gratitude.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst reife Datteln frisch oder getrocknet genie\xdfen und dein Fasten oder deinen Tag mit s\xfc\xdfer Dankbarkeit beginnen. Eine Handvoll Datteln in einer Schale zum Teilen anzubieten ist eine alte Geste, die eine Absicht von F\xfclle und Dankbarkeit ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes disfrutar los d\xe1tiles maduros frescos o secos, rompiendo tu ayuno o tu d\xeda con una dulce gratitud. Poner un pu\xf1ado de d\xe1tiles en un cuenco para compartir es un gesto antiguo que honra una intenci\xf3n de abundancia y gratitud.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux savourer les dattes m\xfbres fra\xeeches ou s\xe9ch\xe9es, rompant ton je\xfbne ou ta journ\xe9e avec une douce gratitude. Disposer une poign\xe9e de dattes dans un bol \xe0 partager est un geste ancien qui honore une intention d'abondance et de gratitude.",howToUseJa:"\u719f\u3057\u305f\u30ca\u30c4\u30e1\u30e4\u30b7\u3092\u751f\u306e\u307e\u307e\u3001\u307e\u305f\u306f\u5e72\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3044\u3001\u7518\u3044\u611f\u8b1d\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u65ad\u98df\u3084\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u59cb\u3081\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u306e\u30ca\u30c4\u30e1\u30e4\u30b7\u3092\u5668\u306b\u5165\u308c\u3066\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u611f\u8b1d\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u53e4\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode apreciar t\xe2maras maduras frescas ou secas, quebrando o seu jejum ou o seu dia com uma doce gratid\xe3o. Colocar um punhado de t\xe2maras em uma tigela para partilhar \xe9 um gesto antigo que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de abund\xe2ncia e gratid\xe3o.",affirmation:"Zorluk an\u0131nda dayanacak bir dal\u0131m var, sabr\u0131m\u0131n ard\u0131ndan tatl\u0131 bir bereket geliyor.",affirmationEn:"In hardship I have a branch to lean on, and after my patience a sweet abundance comes.",affirmationDe:"In der Not habe ich einen Zweig zum Anlehnen, und nach meiner Geduld kommt eine s\xfc\xdfe F\xfclle.",affirmationEs:"En la dificultad tengo una rama donde apoyarme, y tras mi paciencia llega una dulce abundancia.",affirmationFr:"Dans l'\xe9preuve j'ai une branche o\xf9 m'appuyer, et apr\xe8s ma patience vient une douce abondance.",affirmationJa:"\u82e6\u96e3\u306e\u3068\u304d\u3001\u79c1\u306b\u306f\u5bc4\u308a\u304b\u304b\u308b\u679d\u304c\u3042\u308a\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306b\u7518\u3044\u8c4a\u7a63\u304c\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Na dificuldade tenho um galho para me apoiar, e depois da minha paci\xeancia vem uma doce abund\xe2ncia.",myth:"Hurma, Arap yar\u0131madas\u0131nda en bol yeti\u015fen a\u011fa\xe7lardan biridir ve \xf6zellikle \u0130slam d\xfcnyas\u0131nda kutsal say\u0131l\u0131r. Kuran'\u0131n Meryem suresinde, Meryem do\u011fum sanc\u0131s\u0131yla bir hurma a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n dal\u0131na tutunur; ona 'hurma dal\u0131n\u0131 kendine do\u011fru silkele ki \xfczerine taze, olgun hurma d\xf6k\xfcls\xfcn' diye seslenilir ve bu, \u0130sa'n\u0131n do\u011fumunda ilahi bir i\u015faret say\u0131l\u0131r. Bir \xc7in s\xf6ylencesinde rahip Chih, bir ma\u011farada \xf6l\xfcms\xfczlerin satranc\u0131n\u0131 izlerken kendisine verilen bir hurma \xe7ekirde\u011fini emer; bu tatl\u0131 \xe7ekirdek onun bir as\u0131r boyunca a\xe7l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ve susuzlu\u011funu giderir, hurma da \xc7in'de kutsal kabul edilir.",mythEn:"The date palm is one of the most abundant trees of the Arabian Peninsula and is held sacred especially in the Islamic world. In the Quran's chapter of Maryam, Mary, in the pangs of birth, grasps the branch of a date palm; she is told, 'Shake the trunk of the palm toward you, and fresh, ripe dates will fall upon you,' and this is taken as a divine sign at the birth of Jesus. In a Chinese tale, the monk Chih, watching the immortals' game of chess in a cave, sucks on a date pit given to him; this sweet pit stays his hunger and thirst for a whole century, and the date is held sacred in China.",mythDe:"Die Dattelpalme ist einer der ergiebigsten B\xe4ume der Arabischen Halbinsel und gilt besonders in der islamischen Welt als heilig. In der Sure Maryam des Korans ergreift Maria in den Geburtswehen den Zweig einer Dattelpalme; ihr wird gesagt: 'Sch\xfcttle den Stamm der Palme zu dir hin, so fallen frische, reife Datteln auf dich herab', und dies wird als g\xf6ttliches Zeichen bei der Geburt Jesu gedeutet. In einer chinesischen Erz\xe4hlung lutscht der M\xf6nch Chih, der in einer H\xf6hle dem Schachspiel der Unsterblichen zusieht, an einem ihm gereichten Dattelkern; dieser s\xfc\xdfe Kern stillt seinen Hunger und Durst ein ganzes Jahrhundert lang, und die Dattel gilt in China als heilig.",mythEs:"La palmera datilera es uno de los \xe1rboles m\xe1s abundantes de la pen\xednsula ar\xe1biga y se tiene por sagrada especialmente en el mundo isl\xe1mico. En el cap\xedtulo de Maryam del Cor\xe1n, Mar\xeda, con los dolores del parto, se aferra a la rama de una palmera datilera; se le dice: 'Sacude hacia ti el tronco de la palmera, y caer\xe1n sobre ti d\xe1tiles frescos y maduros', y esto se toma como una se\xf1al divina en el nacimiento de Jes\xfas. En un relato chino, el monje Chih, mirando la partida de ajedrez de los inmortales en una cueva, chupa un hueso de d\xe1til que le dan; este dulce hueso calma su hambre y su sed durante todo un siglo, y el d\xe1til se tiene por sagrado en China.",mythFr:"Le palmier-dattier est l'un des arbres les plus abondants de la p\xe9ninsule arabique et tenu pour sacr\xe9 surtout dans le monde islamique. Dans la sourate de Maryam du Coran, Marie, dans les douleurs de l'enfantement, s'agrippe \xe0 la branche d'un palmier-dattier ; on lui dit : 'Secoue vers toi le tronc du palmier, et il fera tomber sur toi des dattes fra\xeeches et m\xfbres', et cela est tenu pour un signe divin \xe0 la naissance de J\xe9sus. Dans un r\xe9cit chinois, le moine Chih, regardant la partie d'\xe9checs des immortels dans une grotte, suce un noyau de datte qu'on lui tend ; ce doux noyau apaise sa faim et sa soif durant tout un si\xe8cle, et la datte est tenue pour sacr\xe9e en Chine.",mythJa:"\u30ca\u30c4\u30e1\u30e4\u30b7\u306f\u30a2\u30e9\u30d3\u30a2\u534a\u5cf6\u3067\u6700\u3082\u8c4a\u304b\u306b\u80b2\u3064\u6728\u306e\u3072\u3068\u3064\u3067\u3001\u3068\u304f\u306b\u30a4\u30b9\u30e9\u30e0\u4e16\u754c\u3067\u8056\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3068\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b3\u30fc\u30e9\u30f3\u306e\u30de\u30ea\u30e4\u30e0\u7ae0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30de\u30ea\u30a2\u304c\u7523\u307f\u306e\u82e6\u3057\u307f\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u30ca\u30c4\u30e1\u30e4\u30b7\u306e\u679d\u306b\u3064\u304b\u307e\u308a\u3001\u300e\u68d5\u6ada\u306e\u5e79\u3092\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u307b\u3046\u306b\u63fa\u3059\u308c\u3070\u3001\u65b0\u9bae\u3067\u719f\u3057\u305f\u30ca\u30c4\u30e1\u30e4\u30b7\u304c\u843d\u3061\u3066\u304f\u308b\u300f\u3068\u544a\u3052\u3089\u308c\u3001\u3053\u308c\u306f\u30a4\u30a8\u30b9\u8a95\u751f\u306e\u795e\u306e\u5fb4\u3068\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u308b\u4e2d\u56fd\u306e\u7269\u8a9e\u3067\u306f\u3001\u50e7\u4fb6\u30c1\u30fc\u304c\u6d1e\u7a9f\u3067\u4e0d\u6b7b\u8005\u305f\u3061\u306e\u5c06\u68cb\u3092\u898b\u306a\u304c\u3089\u5dee\u3057\u51fa\u3055\u308c\u305f\u30ca\u30c4\u30e1\u30e4\u30b7\u306e\u7a2e\u3092\u3057\u3083\u3076\u308b\u3068\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7518\u3044\u7a2e\u304c\u4e00\u4e16\u7d00\u3082\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u5f7c\u306e\u98e2\u3048\u3068\u6e07\u304d\u3092\u7652\u3057\u3001\u30ca\u30c4\u30e1\u30e4\u30b7\u306f\u4e2d\u56fd\u3067\u8056\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3068\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"A tamareira \xe9 uma das \xe1rvores mais abundantes da pen\xednsula ar\xe1bica e \xe9 tida como sagrada especialmente no mundo isl\xe2mico. No cap\xedtulo de Maryam do Alcor\xe3o, Maria, nas dores do parto, agarra-se ao galho de uma tamareira; \xe9-lhe dito: 'Sacode em tua dire\xe7\xe3o o tronco da palmeira, e cair\xe3o sobre ti t\xe2maras frescas e maduras', e isto \xe9 tido como um sinal divino no nascimento de Jesus. Num relato chin\xeas, o monge Chih, assistindo \xe0 partida de xadrez dos imortais numa caverna, chupa um caro\xe7o de t\xe2mara que lhe \xe9 dado; esse doce caro\xe7o acalma a sua fome e a sua sede por um s\xe9culo inteiro, e a t\xe2mara \xe9 tida como sagrada na China.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Dates005.jpg/330px-Dates005.jpg"},{id:"plant-101",emoji:"\ud83c\udf38",color:"#C94C7C",name:"H\xfcsn\xfcyusuf",nameEn:"Sweet William",nameDe:"Bartnelke",nameEs:"Clavel del Poeta",nameFr:"\u0152illet de Po\xe8te",nameJa:"\u30d3\u30b8\u30e7\u30ca\u30c7\u30b7\u30b3",namePt:"Cravina-de-Poeta",origin:"\u0130slam & Anadolu Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Islamic & Anatolian Tradition",originDe:"Islamische & anatolische Tradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n isl\xe1mica y anatolia",originFr:"Tradition islamique et anatolienne",originJa:"\u30a4\u30b9\u30e9\u30e0\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o isl\xe2mica e anat\xf3lia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["g\xfczellik","sab\u0131r","masumiyet","ba\u011f\u0131\u015flama"],propertiesEn:["beauty","patience","innocence","forgiveness"],propertiesDe:["Sch\xf6nheit","Geduld","Unschuld","Vergebung"],propertiesEs:["belleza","paciencia","inocencia","perd\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["beaut\xe9","patience","innocence","pardon"],propertiesJa:["\u7f8e","\u5fcd\u8010","\u7121\u57a2","\u8d66\u3057"],propertiesPt:["beleza","paci\xeancia","inoc\xeancia","perd\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn sana haks\u0131zl\u0131k eden bir kuyuya d\xfc\u015fsen bile, i\xe7indeki g\xfczelli\u011fi koru; sab\u0131r eninde sonunda en karanl\u0131k \xe7ukuru bir tahta \xe7evirir. H\xfcsn\xfcyusuf sana iftiraya ve ayr\u0131l\u0131\u011fa ra\u011fmen temiz kalman\u0131n, sonunda ba\u011f\u0131\u015flamayla ta\xe7lanaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, even if you fall into a well dug by those who wronged you, keep the beauty within you; patience turns the darkest pit into a throne in the end. Sweet William whispers that staying pure despite slander and separation is, in the end, crowned with forgiveness.",dailyMessageDe:"Selbst wenn du heute in einen Brunnen f\xe4llst, den dir Unrechte gegraben haben, bewahre die Sch\xf6nheit in dir; Geduld verwandelt am Ende die dunkelste Grube in einen Thron. Die Bartnelke fl\xfcstert, dass rein zu bleiben trotz Verleumdung und Trennung am Ende mit Vergebung gekr\xf6nt wird.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, aunque caigas en un pozo cavado por quienes te hicieron mal, guarda la belleza que llevas dentro; la paciencia convierte al fin el pozo m\xe1s oscuro en un trono. El clavel del poeta susurra que mantenerte puro pese a la calumnia y la separaci\xf3n se corona, al final, con el perd\xf3n.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, m\xeame si tu tombes dans un puits creus\xe9 par ceux qui t'ont fait du tort, garde la beaut\xe9 en toi ; la patience finit par changer le puits le plus sombre en tr\xf4ne. L'\u0153illet de po\xe8te murmure que rester pur malgr\xe9 la calomnie et la s\xe9paration se couronne, \xe0 la fin, de pardon.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306b\u4e0d\u6b63\u3092\u50cd\u3044\u305f\u8005\u304c\u6398\u3063\u305f\u4e95\u6238\u306b\u843d\u3061\u3066\u3082\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u7f8e\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5fcd\u8010\u306f\u3001\u3064\u3044\u306b\u306f\u6700\u3082\u6697\u3044\u7a74\u3092\u7389\u5ea7\u306b\u5909\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30d3\u30b8\u30e7\u30ca\u30c7\u30b7\u30b3\u306f\u3001\u4e2d\u50b7\u3068\u5225\u96e2\u306b\u3082\u304b\u304b\u308f\u3089\u305a\u6e05\u304f\u3042\u308a\u7d9a\u3051\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3001\u6700\u5f8c\u306b\u306f\u8d66\u3057\u3067\u6234\u304b\u308c\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, mesmo que voc\xea caia num po\xe7o cavado por quem lhe fez mal, guarde a beleza que h\xe1 em voc\xea; a paci\xeancia transforma, no fim, o po\xe7o mais escuro em um trono. A cravina-de-poeta sussurra que permanecer puro apesar da cal\xfania e da separa\xe7\xe3o \xe9, no fim, coroado com o perd\xe3o.",howToUse:"H\xfcsn\xfcyusufun renkli \xe7i\xe7eklerini bir bah\xe7ede ya da saks\u0131da yeti\u015ftirerek g\xfczellik ve sab\u0131r niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bir demet h\xfcsn\xfcyusufu sevdi\u011fine sunmak, masumiyeti ve ba\u011f\u0131\u015flamay\u0131 onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may grow Sweet William's colorful flowers in a garden or pot to accompany an intention of beauty and patience. Offering a bunch of Sweet William to someone you love is a gentle gesture honoring innocence and forgiveness.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die bunten Bl\xfcten der Bartnelke im Garten oder Topf ziehen, um eine Absicht von Sch\xf6nheit und Geduld zu begleiten. Einen Strau\xdf Bartnelken einem geliebten Menschen zu schenken ist eine zarte Geste, die Unschuld und Vergebung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes cultivar las coloridas flores del clavel del poeta en un jard\xedn o maceta para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de belleza y paciencia. Ofrecer un ramo de clavel del poeta a alguien a quien amas es un gesto tierno que honra la inocencia y el perd\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux cultiver les fleurs color\xe9es de l'\u0153illet de po\xe8te au jardin ou en pot pour accompagner une intention de beaut\xe9 et de patience. Offrir un bouquet d'\u0153illets de po\xe8te \xe0 un \xeatre aim\xe9 est un geste tendre qui honore l'innocence et le pardon.",howToUseJa:"\u30d3\u30b8\u30e7\u30ca\u30c7\u30b7\u30b3\u306e\u8272\u3068\u308a\u3069\u308a\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u5ead\u3084\u9262\u3067\u80b2\u3066\u3001\u7f8e\u3068\u5fcd\u8010\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30d3\u30b8\u30e7\u30ca\u30c7\u30b7\u30b3\u306e\u82b1\u675f\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u4eba\u306b\u8d08\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u7121\u57a2\u3068\u8d66\u3057\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode cultivar as flores coloridas da cravina-de-poeta em um jardim ou vaso para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de beleza e paci\xeancia. Oferecer um buqu\xea de cravina-de-poeta a algu\xe9m que voc\xea ama \xe9 um gesto terno que honra a inoc\xeancia e o perd\xe3o.",affirmation:"\u0130ftiraya ve ayr\u0131l\u0131\u011fa ra\u011fmen g\xfczelli\u011fimi koruyorum, sabr\u0131m ba\u011f\u0131\u015flamayla ta\xe7lan\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"Despite slander and separation I keep my beauty, and my patience is crowned with forgiveness.",affirmationDe:"Trotz Verleumdung und Trennung bewahre ich meine Sch\xf6nheit, und meine Geduld wird mit Vergebung gekr\xf6nt.",affirmationEs:"Pese a la calumnia y la separaci\xf3n guardo mi belleza, y mi paciencia se corona con el perd\xf3n.",affirmationFr:"Malgr\xe9 la calomnie et la s\xe9paration je garde ma beaut\xe9, et ma patience se couronne de pardon.",affirmationJa:"\u4e2d\u50b7\u3068\u5225\u96e2\u306b\u3082\u304b\u304b\u308f\u3089\u305a\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u7f8e\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u306f\u8d66\u3057\u3067\u6234\u304b\u308c\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Apesar da cal\xfania e da separa\xe7\xe3o guardo a minha beleza, e a minha paci\xeancia \xe9 coroada com o perd\xe3o.",myth:"H\xfcsn\xfcyusuf \xe7i\xe7e\u011finin ad\u0131 'Yusuf'un g\xfczelli\u011fi' anlam\u0131na gelir; s\xf6ylenceye g\xf6re Yusuf peygambere d\xfcnyadaki g\xfczelli\u011fin yar\u0131s\u0131 verilmi\u015fti. Babas\u0131 Yakup'un en sevdi\u011fi o\u011flu oldu\u011fu i\xe7in k\u0131skanan karde\u015fleri Yusuf'u bir kuyuya att\u0131; bir kervan onu kurtard\u0131, M\u0131s\u0131r'a sat\u0131ld\u0131, azizin kar\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n iftiras\u0131yla zindana d\xfc\u015ft\xfc ama r\xfcya yorumlama bilgeli\u011fiyle sonunda M\u0131s\u0131r'a ba\u015f m\xfcste\u015far oldu. K\u0131tl\u0131k g\xfcnlerinde kendisine s\u0131\u011f\u0131nan karde\u015flerini ba\u011f\u0131\u015flay\u0131p ba\u011fr\u0131na bast\u0131. Yusuf'un \xf6l\xfcm\xfcnden sonra topraktan bir \xe7i\xe7ek do\u011fdu; onun cemalinin bu \xe7i\xe7e\u011fe yans\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131na ve b\xf6ylece g\xfczel y\xfcz\xfcn\xfcn \xf6l\xfcmden sonra yery\xfcz\xfcne d\xf6nd\xfc\u011f\xfcne inan\u0131ld\u0131.",mythEn:"The name of the Sweet William flower means 'the beauty of Joseph'; legend holds that half the world's beauty was given to the prophet Joseph (Yusuf). Because he was the favorite son of his father Jacob, his jealous brothers threw him into a well; a caravan rescued him, he was sold in Egypt, fell into a dungeon through the slander of the nobleman's wife, but through his wisdom in interpreting dreams he finally became chief minister of Egypt. In the days of famine he forgave the brothers who came to him and embraced them. After Joseph's death a flower sprang from the earth; it was believed that his beauty was reflected in this flower, and so his fair face returned to the world after death.",mythDe:"Der Name der Bartnelken-Blume bedeutet 'die Sch\xf6nheit Josephs'; der Legende nach wurde dem Propheten Joseph (Yusuf) die H\xe4lfte der Sch\xf6nheit der Welt verliehen. Weil er der Lieblingssohn seines Vaters Jakob war, warfen ihn seine eifers\xfcchtigen Br\xfcder in einen Brunnen; eine Karawane rettete ihn, er wurde in \xc4gypten verkauft, geriet durch die Verleumdung der Frau des Edelmanns in den Kerker, wurde aber durch seine Weisheit im Deuten von Tr\xe4umen schlie\xdflich oberster Minister \xc4gyptens. In den Tagen der Hungersnot vergab er den Br\xfcdern, die zu ihm kamen, und schloss sie in die Arme. Nach Josephs Tod entsprang der Erde eine Blume; man glaubte, seine Sch\xf6nheit spiegele sich in dieser Blume, und so kehre sein sch\xf6nes Antlitz nach dem Tod auf die Erde zur\xfcck.",mythEs:"El nombre de la flor del clavel del poeta significa 'la belleza de Jos\xe9'; la leyenda sostiene que al profeta Jos\xe9 (Yusuf) se le dio la mitad de la belleza del mundo. Por ser el hijo favorito de su padre Jacob, sus hermanos celosos lo arrojaron a un pozo; una caravana lo rescat\xf3, fue vendido en Egipto, cay\xf3 en un calabozo por la calumnia de la esposa del noble, pero por su sabidur\xeda al interpretar sue\xf1os lleg\xf3 al fin a ser ministro principal de Egipto. En los d\xedas del hambre perdon\xf3 a los hermanos que acudieron a \xe9l y los abraz\xf3. Tras la muerte de Jos\xe9 brot\xf3 una flor de la tierra; se crey\xf3 que su belleza se reflejaba en esta flor, y as\xed su hermoso rostro volv\xeda al mundo tras la muerte.",mythFr:"Le nom de la fleur d'\u0153illet de po\xe8te signifie 'la beaut\xe9 de Joseph' ; la l\xe9gende veut que la moiti\xe9 de la beaut\xe9 du monde ait \xe9t\xe9 donn\xe9e au proph\xe8te Joseph (Yusuf). Parce qu'il \xe9tait le fils pr\xe9f\xe9r\xe9 de son p\xe8re Jacob, ses fr\xe8res jaloux le jet\xe8rent dans un puits ; une caravane le sauva, il fut vendu en \xc9gypte, tomba dans un cachot par la calomnie de la femme du notable, mais par sa sagesse \xe0 interpr\xe9ter les songes il devint enfin premier ministre d'\xc9gypte. Aux jours de la famine il pardonna aux fr\xe8res venus \xe0 lui et les embrassa. Apr\xe8s la mort de Joseph une fleur jaillit de la terre ; on crut que sa beaut\xe9 se refl\xe9tait dans cette fleur, et qu'ainsi son beau visage revenait au monde apr\xe8s la mort.",mythJa:"\u30d3\u30b8\u30e7\u30ca\u30c7\u30b7\u30b3\u306e\u82b1\u306e\u540d\u306f\u300e\u30e8\u30bb\u30d5\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u300f\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4f1d\u8aac\u306b\u3088\u308c\u3070\u3001\u9810\u8a00\u8005\u30e8\u30bb\u30d5\uff08\u30e6\u30b9\u30d5\uff09\u306b\u306f\u4e16\u754c\u306e\u7f8e\u306e\u534a\u5206\u304c\u4e0e\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u7236\u30e4\u30b3\u30d6\u306e\u3044\u3061\u3070\u3093\u306e\u611b\u3057\u5b50\u3067\u3042\u3063\u305f\u305f\u3081\u3001\u5ac9\u59ac\u3057\u305f\u5144\u5f1f\u305f\u3061\u306f\u5f7c\u3092\u4e95\u6238\u306b\u6295\u3052\u8fbc\u307f\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u968a\u5546\u304c\u5f7c\u3092\u6551\u3044\u3001\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u3067\u58f2\u3089\u308c\u3001\u8cb4\u4eba\u306e\u59bb\u306e\u4e2d\u50b7\u3067\u7262\u306b\u843d\u3068\u3055\u308c\u305f\u3082\u306e\u306e\u3001\u5922\u3092\u89e3\u304f\u53e1\u667a\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u3064\u3044\u306b\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u306e\u5bb0\u76f8\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u98e2\u9949\u306e\u65e5\u3005\u3001\u5f7c\u306f\u8a2a\u306d\u3066\u304d\u305f\u5144\u5f1f\u305f\u3061\u3092\u8d66\u3057\u3001\u62b1\u304d\u3057\u3081\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30e8\u30bb\u30d5\u306e\u6b7b\u5f8c\u3001\u5927\u5730\u304b\u3089\u4e00\u8f2a\u306e\u82b1\u304c\u751f\u307e\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u304c\u3053\u306e\u82b1\u306b\u6620\u3063\u305f\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3001\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u5f7c\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u9854\u304c\u6b7b\u5f8c\u306b\u5730\u4e0a\u3078\u623b\u3063\u305f\u3068\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"O nome da flor cravina-de-poeta significa 'a beleza de Jos\xe9'; a lenda sustenta que ao profeta Jos\xe9 (Yusuf) foi dada metade da beleza do mundo. Por ser o filho favorito de seu pai Jac\xf3, seus irm\xe3os invejosos o lan\xe7aram num po\xe7o; uma caravana o resgatou, ele foi vendido no Egito, caiu numa masmorra pela cal\xfania da esposa do nobre, mas por sua sabedoria em interpretar sonhos tornou-se enfim ministro-chefe do Egito. Nos dias da fome, ele perdoou os irm\xe3os que vieram a ele e os abra\xe7ou. Ap\xf3s a morte de Jos\xe9, uma flor brotou da terra; acreditou-se que sua beleza se refletia nesta flor, e assim seu belo rosto voltava ao mundo depois da morte.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Dianthus_barbatus_flowers_01.jpg/330px-Dianthus_barbatus_flowers_01.jpg"},{id:"plant-102",emoji:"\ud83c\udf48",color:"#7C5BA6",name:"\u0130ncir",nameEn:"Fig",nameDe:"Feige",nameEs:"Higo",nameFr:"Figue",nameJa:"\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af",namePt:"Figo",origin:"Akdeniz & Antik Yunan",originEn:"Mediterranean & Ancient Greece",originDe:"Mittelmeerraum & antikes Griechenland",originEs:"Mediterr\xe1neo y Antigua Grecia",originFr:"M\xe9diterran\xe9e et Gr\xe8ce antique",originJa:"\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u30fb\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3",originPt:"Mediterr\xe2neo e Gr\xe9cia Antiga",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u4ed9\u9aa8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacral",properties:["bereket","do\u011furganl\u0131k","koruma","ayd\u0131nlanma","bar\u0131\u015f"],propertiesEn:["abundance","fertility","protection","enlightenment","peace"],propertiesDe:["F\xfclle","Fruchtbarkeit","Schutz","Erleuchtung","Frieden"],propertiesEs:["abundancia","fertilidad","protecci\xf3n","iluminaci\xf3n","paz"],propertiesFr:["abondance","fertilit\xe9","protection","illumination","paix"],propertiesJa:["\u8c4a\u7a63","\u591a\u7523","\u5b88\u8b77","\u609f\u308a","\u5e73\u548c"],propertiesPt:["abund\xe2ncia","fertilidade","prote\xe7\xe3o","ilumina\xe7\xe3o","paz"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn seni koruyacak bir g\xf6lge ara; bazen en b\xfcy\xfck f\u0131rt\u0131nada, k\xf6kleri derin bir a\u011fac\u0131n alt\u0131nda huzur bulunur. \u0130ncir sana hem bereketin hem korunman\u0131n ayn\u0131 dalda bulu\u015ftu\u011funu, sab\u0131rla beklenenin tatl\u0131 bir meyveye d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc hat\u0131rlat\u0131r.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, seek a shade that will shelter you; sometimes, in the greatest storm, peace is found beneath a deep-rooted tree. The fig reminds you that abundance and protection meet on the same branch, and that what is awaited with patience ripens into a sweet fruit.",dailyMessageDe:"Suche heute einen Schatten, der dich birgt; manchmal findet man im gr\xf6\xdften Sturm Frieden unter einem tief verwurzelten Baum. Die Feige erinnert dich daran, dass F\xfclle und Schutz sich am selben Zweig treffen und dass, was mit Geduld erwartet wird, zu einer s\xfc\xdfen Frucht reift.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, busca una sombra que te resguarde; a veces, en la mayor tormenta, se halla paz bajo un \xe1rbol de ra\xedces profundas. El higo te recuerda que la abundancia y la protecci\xf3n se encuentran en la misma rama, y que lo esperado con paciencia madura en un dulce fruto.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, cherche une ombre qui t'abrite ; parfois, dans la plus grande temp\xeate, on trouve la paix sous un arbre aux racines profondes. La figue te rappelle que l'abondance et la protection se rejoignent sur la m\xeame branche, et que ce qui s'attend avec patience m\xfbrit en un doux fruit.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u5b88\u308b\u6728\u9670\u3092\u63a2\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3068\u304d\u306b\u3001\u6700\u3082\u5927\u304d\u306a\u5d50\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u3082\u3001\u6df1\u304f\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u3063\u305f\u6728\u306e\u4e0b\u3067\u5b89\u3089\u304e\u304c\u898b\u3064\u304b\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af\u306f\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u5b88\u8b77\u304c\u540c\u3058\u679d\u3067\u51fa\u4f1a\u3044\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u5f85\u305f\u308c\u305f\u3082\u306e\u304c\u7518\u3044\u679c\u5b9f\u3078\u3068\u719f\u3059\u3068\u6559\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, busque uma sombra que abrigue voc\xea; \xe0s vezes, na maior tempestade, encontra-se paz sob uma \xe1rvore de ra\xedzes profundas. O figo lembra voc\xea de que a abund\xe2ncia e a prote\xe7\xe3o se encontram no mesmo galho, e que o que se espera com paci\xeancia amadurece em um doce fruto.",howToUse:"Olgun inciri taze ya da kuru olarak besleyici bir ikram olarak tadabilirsin. Bir incir a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n ya da yapra\u011f\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6lgesinde birka\xe7 dakika dinlenmek, koruma ve bereket niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may enjoy ripe figs fresh or dried as a nourishing treat. Resting for a few minutes in the shade of a fig tree or its leaf is a gentle gesture honoring an intention of protection and abundance.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst reife Feigen frisch oder getrocknet als n\xe4hrende K\xf6stlichkeit genie\xdfen. Ein paar Minuten im Schatten eines Feigenbaums oder seines Blattes zu ruhen ist eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Schutz und F\xfclle ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes disfrutar los higos maduros frescos o secos como un manjar nutritivo. Descansar unos minutos a la sombra de una higuera o de su hoja es un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de protecci\xf3n y abundancia.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux savourer les figues m\xfbres fra\xeeches ou s\xe9ch\xe9es comme une douceur nourrissante. Te reposer quelques minutes \xe0 l'ombre d'un figuier ou de sa feuille est un geste tendre qui honore une intention de protection et d'abondance.",howToUseJa:"\u719f\u3057\u305f\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af\u3092\u751f\u306e\u307e\u307e\u3001\u307e\u305f\u306f\u5e72\u3057\u3066\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u304a\u3084\u3064\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af\u306e\u6728\u3084\u305d\u306e\u8449\u306e\u9670\u3067\u6570\u5206\u4f11\u3080\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u5b88\u8b77\u3068\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode apreciar figos maduros frescos ou secos como uma guloseima nutritiva. Descansar por alguns minutos \xe0 sombra de uma figueira ou de sua folha \xe9 um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de prote\xe7\xe3o e abund\xe2ncia.",affirmation:"Beni koruyan bir g\xf6lge buluyorum, sabr\u0131m tatl\u0131 bir bereketle ta\xe7lan\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I find a shade that shelters me, and my patience is crowned with a sweet abundance.",affirmationDe:"Ich finde einen Schatten, der mich birgt, und meine Geduld wird mit s\xfc\xdfer F\xfclle gekr\xf6nt.",affirmationEs:"Encuentro una sombra que me resguarda, y mi paciencia se corona con una dulce abundancia.",affirmationFr:"Je trouve une ombre qui m'abrite, et ma patience se couronne d'une douce abondance.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5b88\u3063\u3066\u304f\u308c\u308b\u6728\u9670\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u304c\u7518\u3044\u8c4a\u7a63\u3067\u6234\u304b\u308c\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Encontro uma sombra que me abriga, e a minha paci\xeancia \xe9 coroada com uma doce abund\xe2ncia.",myth:"\u0130ncir neredeyse evrensel bir bereket ve do\u011furganl\u0131k sembol\xfcd\xfcr. Yunan mitolojisinde Gaia, Zeus'un y\u0131ld\u0131r\u0131mlar\u0131ndan, o\u011flu Titan Sykeus'un yerden \xe7\u0131kard\u0131\u011f\u0131 bir incir a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n alt\u0131na saklanarak korunur; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc incir y\u0131ld\u0131r\u0131m\u0131n y\xf6n\xfcn\xfc sapt\u0131ran bir a\u011fa\xe7 say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Tanr\u0131\xe7a Demeter, k\u0131z\u0131 Persephone'yi ararken kendisini a\u011f\u0131rlayan kahraman Phylatos'a bir incir fidan\u0131 arma\u011fan etmi\u015ftir. Yahudi inanc\u0131nda ise Adem ile Havva yasak meyveyi yedikten sonra \xe7\u0131plakl\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131 incir yapraklar\u0131yla \xf6rtm\xfc\u015f; Budizm'de Buda, incir a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6lgesinde yedi hafta d\xfc\u015f\xfcnerek ayd\u0131nlanmaya ermi\u015ftir.",mythEn:"The fig is an almost universal symbol of abundance and fertility. In Greek myth, Gaia is protected from Zeus's thunderbolts by hiding beneath a fig tree that her son, the Titan Sykeus, raised from the ground; for the fig was held to be a tree that deflects lightning. The goddess Demeter, while searching for her daughter Persephone, gave a fig sapling to the hero Phylatos who hosted her. In Jewish belief, after Adam and Eve ate the forbidden fruit, they covered their nakedness with fig leaves; in Buddhism, the Buddha attained enlightenment by meditating for seven weeks in the shade of a fig tree.",mythDe:"Die Feige ist ein nahezu universelles Symbol von F\xfclle und Fruchtbarkeit. In der griechischen Mythologie wird Gaia vor Zeus' Blitzen gesch\xfctzt, indem sie sich unter einem Feigenbaum verbirgt, den ihr Sohn, der Titan Sykeus, aus der Erde hervorbrachte; denn die Feige galt als Baum, der den Blitz ablenkt. Die G\xf6ttin Demeter schenkte dem Helden Phylatos, der sie bewirtete, w\xe4hrend der Suche nach ihrer Tochter Persephone einen jungen Feigenbaum. Im j\xfcdischen Glauben bedeckten Adam und Eva, nachdem sie die verbotene Frucht gegessen hatten, ihre Bl\xf6\xdfe mit Feigenbl\xe4ttern; im Buddhismus erlangte der Buddha die Erleuchtung, indem er sieben Wochen im Schatten eines Feigenbaums meditierte.",mythEs:"El higo es un s\xedmbolo casi universal de abundancia y fertilidad. En la mitolog\xeda griega, Gea se protege de los rayos de Zeus ocult\xe1ndose bajo una higuera que su hijo, el tit\xe1n Sikeo, hizo brotar de la tierra; pues el higo se ten\xeda por un \xe1rbol que desv\xeda el rayo. La diosa Dem\xe9ter, mientras buscaba a su hija Pers\xe9fone, regal\xf3 un plant\xf3n de higuera al h\xe9roe Filato que la hosped\xf3. En la creencia jud\xeda, tras comer Ad\xe1n y Eva el fruto prohibido, cubrieron su desnudez con hojas de higuera; en el budismo, el Buda alcanz\xf3 la iluminaci\xf3n meditando siete semanas a la sombra de una higuera.",mythFr:"La figue est un symbole presque universel d'abondance et de fertilit\xe9. Dans la mythologie grecque, Ga\xefa est prot\xe9g\xe9e des foudres de Zeus en se cachant sous un figuier que son fils, le Titan Sykeus, fit surgir du sol ; car la figue \xe9tait tenue pour un arbre qui d\xe9tourne la foudre. La d\xe9esse D\xe9m\xe9ter, cherchant sa fille Pers\xe9phone, offrit un plant de figuier au h\xe9ros Phylatos qui l'avait accueillie. Dans la croyance juive, apr\xe8s qu'Adam et \xc8ve eurent mang\xe9 le fruit d\xe9fendu, ils couvrirent leur nudit\xe9 de feuilles de figuier ; dans le bouddhisme, le Bouddha atteignit l'illumination en m\xe9ditant sept semaines \xe0 l'ombre d'un figuier.",mythJa:"\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af\u306f\u307b\u307c\u666e\u904d\u7684\u306a\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u591a\u7523\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30ac\u30a4\u30a2\u306f\u606f\u5b50\u306e\u30c6\u30a3\u30bf\u30f3\u795e\u30b7\u30e5\u30b1\u30a6\u30b9\u304c\u5730\u304b\u3089\u751f\u3084\u3057\u305f\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af\u306e\u6728\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u8eab\u3092\u96a0\u3057\u3066\u3001\u30bc\u30a6\u30b9\u306e\u96f7\u304b\u3089\u5b88\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af\u306f\u96f7\u306e\u5411\u304d\u3092\u9038\u3089\u3059\u6728\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3044\u305f\u304b\u3089\u3067\u3059\u3002\u5973\u795e\u30c7\u30e1\u30c6\u30eb\u306f\u3001\u5a18\u30da\u30eb\u30bb\u30dd\u30cd\u3092\u63a2\u3059\u9014\u4e0a\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u3082\u3066\u306a\u3057\u305f\u82f1\u96c4\u30d4\u30e5\u30e9\u30c8\u30b9\u306b\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af\u306e\u82d7\u3092\u8d08\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30e6\u30c0\u30e4\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30a2\u30c0\u30e0\u3068\u30a4\u30f4\u306f\u7981\u65ad\u306e\u679c\u5b9f\u3092\u98df\u3079\u305f\u306e\u3061\u3001\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af\u306e\u8449\u3067\u88f8\u3092\u8986\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u4ecf\u6559\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30d6\u30c3\u30c0\u306f\u30a4\u30c1\u30b8\u30af\u306e\u6728\u9670\u3067\u4e03\u9031\u9593\u7791\u60f3\u3057\u3066\u609f\u308a\u306b\u81f3\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"O figo \xe9 um s\xedmbolo quase universal de abund\xe2ncia e fertilidade. Na mitologia grega, Gaia \xe9 protegida dos raios de Zeus ao esconder-se sob uma figueira que seu filho, o tit\xe3 Sykeus, fez brotar da terra; pois o figo era tido como uma \xe1rvore que desvia o raio. A deusa Dem\xe9ter, ao procurar sua filha Pers\xe9fone, presenteou com uma muda de figueira o her\xf3i Phylatos que a hospedou. Na cren\xe7a judaica, depois que Ad\xe3o e Eva comeram o fruto proibido, cobriram a sua nudez com folhas de figueira; no budismo, o Buda alcan\xe7ou a ilumina\xe7\xe3o meditando sete semanas \xe0 sombra de uma figueira.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Ficus_carica_L%2C_1771.jpg/330px-Ficus_carica_L%2C_1771.jpg"},{id:"plant-103",emoji:"\ud83c\udf83",color:"#E08A2B",name:"Kabak",nameEn:"Gourd",nameDe:"K\xfcrbis",nameEs:"Calabaza",nameFr:"Courge",nameJa:"\u30d2\u30e7\u30a6\u30bf\u30f3",namePt:"Ab\xf3bora",origin:"\u0130slam Gelene\u011fi & Mezopotamya",originEn:"Islamic Tradition & Mesopotamia",originDe:"Islamische Tradition & Mesopotamien",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n isl\xe1mica y Mesopotamia",originFr:"Tradition islamique et M\xe9sopotamie",originJa:"\u30a4\u30b9\u30e9\u30e0\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71\u30fb\u30e1\u30bd\u30dd\u30bf\u30df\u30a2",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o isl\xe2mica e Mesopot\xe2mia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["\u015fefkat","\u015fifa","korunma","yeniden do\u011fu\u015f"],propertiesEn:["compassion","healing","shelter","rebirth"],propertiesDe:["Mitgef\xfchl","Heilung","Schutz","Wiedergeburt"],propertiesEs:["compasi\xf3n","sanaci\xf3n","amparo","renacimiento"],propertiesFr:["compassion","gu\xe9rison","abri","renaissance"],propertiesJa:["\u6148\u3057\u307f","\u7652\u3057","\u5e87\u8b77","\u518d\u751f"],propertiesPt:["compaix\xe3o","cura","abrigo","renascimento"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn en g\xfc\xe7s\xfcz, en bitkin an\u0131nda bile \xfcst\xfcne bir g\xf6lgenin d\xfc\u015fece\u011fine g\xfcven; \u015fefkat \xe7o\u011fu zaman tam yere y\u0131\u011f\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda gelir. Kabak sana \xe7aresizli\u011fin ard\u0131ndan nazik bir korunman\u0131n ve \u015fifan\u0131n gelece\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, trust that even in your weakest, most exhausted moment a shade will fall over you; compassion often comes just as you collapse. The gourd whispers that after helplessness a gentle shelter and healing will come.",dailyMessageDe:"Vertraue heute darauf, dass selbst in deinem schw\xe4chsten, ersch\xf6pftesten Augenblick ein Schatten auf dich f\xe4llt; Mitgef\xfchl kommt oft gerade dann, wenn du zusammenbrichst. Der K\xfcrbis fl\xfcstert, dass nach der Hilflosigkeit ein sanfter Schutz und Heilung kommen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, conf\xeda en que incluso en tu momento m\xe1s d\xe9bil y agotado caer\xe1 una sombra sobre ti; la compasi\xf3n suele llegar justo cuando te derrumbas. La calabaza susurra que tras el desamparo llegar\xe1n un amparo tierno y la sanaci\xf3n.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, aie confiance que m\xeame dans ton instant le plus faible et le plus \xe9puis\xe9 une ombre tombera sur toi ; la compassion vient souvent au moment o\xf9 tu t'effondres. La courge murmure qu'apr\xe8s le d\xe9sarroi viendront un abri tendre et la gu\xe9rison.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u6700\u3082\u5f31\u304f\u3001\u6700\u3082\u75b2\u308c\u679c\u3066\u305f\u3068\u304d\u3067\u3082\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u9670\u304c\u843d\u3061\u308b\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6148\u3057\u307f\u306f\u3001\u5d29\u308c\u843d\u3061\u308b\u305d\u306e\u3068\u304d\u306b\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u591a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30d2\u30e7\u30a6\u30bf\u30f3\u306f\u3001\u7121\u529b\u3055\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306b\u3001\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u5e87\u8b77\u3068\u7652\u3057\u304c\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, confie que mesmo no seu momento mais fraco e exausto uma sombra cair\xe1 sobre voc\xea; a compaix\xe3o muitas vezes chega justo quando voc\xea desaba. A ab\xf3bora sussurra que depois do desamparo vir\xe3o um abrigo terno e a cura.",howToUse:"Kaba\u011f\u0131 pi\u015firip besleyici bir yemek olarak haz\u0131rlayabilir, geni\u015f yapraklar\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6lgesinde bir an dinlenebilirsin. Kurutulmu\u015f bir su kaba\u011f\u0131n\u0131 k\xe2se ya da kap olarak kullanmak da \u015fifa ve korunma niyetini onurland\u0131ran sade bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may cook the gourd into a nourishing dish and rest a moment in the shade of its broad leaves. Using a dried gourd as a bowl or vessel is also a simple gesture honoring an intention of healing and shelter.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst den K\xfcrbis zu einem n\xe4hrenden Gericht kochen und einen Augenblick im Schatten seiner breiten Bl\xe4tter ruhen. Einen getrockneten K\xfcrbis als Schale oder Gef\xe4\xdf zu verwenden ist ebenfalls eine schlichte Geste, die eine Absicht von Heilung und Schutz ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes cocinar la calabaza en un plato nutritivo y descansar un momento a la sombra de sus anchas hojas. Usar una calabaza seca como cuenco o recipiente es tambi\xe9n un gesto sencillo que honra una intenci\xf3n de sanaci\xf3n y amparo.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux cuisiner la courge en un plat nourrissant et te reposer un instant \xe0 l'ombre de ses larges feuilles. Utiliser une courge s\xe9ch\xe9e comme bol ou r\xe9cipient est aussi un geste simple qui honore une intention de gu\xe9rison et d'abri.",howToUseJa:"\u30d2\u30e7\u30a6\u30bf\u30f3\u3092\u716e\u3066\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u6599\u7406\u306b\u3057\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5e83\u3044\u8449\u306e\u9670\u3067\u3072\u3068\u3068\u304d\u4f11\u3081\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e7e\u3044\u305f\u30d2\u30e7\u30a6\u30bf\u30f3\u3092\u5668\u3084\u5bb9\u308c\u7269\u3068\u3057\u3066\u4f7f\u3046\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u7652\u3057\u3068\u5e87\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3064\u3064\u307e\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode cozinhar a ab\xf3bora num prato nutritivo e descansar um instante \xe0 sombra de suas folhas largas. Usar uma ab\xf3bora seca como tigela ou recipiente \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto simples que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de cura e abrigo.",affirmation:"En \xe7aresiz an\u0131mda bile \xfcst\xfcme bir g\xf6lge d\xfc\u015f\xfcyor, \u015fefkat beni iyile\u015ftiriyor.",affirmationEn:"Even in my most helpless moment a shade falls over me, and compassion heals me.",affirmationDe:"Selbst in meinem hilflosesten Augenblick f\xe4llt ein Schatten auf mich, und Mitgef\xfchl heilt mich.",affirmationEs:"Incluso en mi momento m\xe1s desvalido cae una sombra sobre m\xed, y la compasi\xf3n me sana.",affirmationFr:"M\xeame dans mon instant le plus d\xe9muni une ombre tombe sur moi, et la compassion me gu\xe9rit.",affirmationJa:"\u6700\u3082\u7121\u529b\u306a\u3068\u304d\u3067\u3082\u3001\u79c1\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u9670\u304c\u843d\u3061\u3001\u6148\u3057\u307f\u304c\u79c1\u3092\u7652\u3059\u3002",affirmationPt:"Mesmo no meu momento mais desamparado uma sombra cai sobre mim, e a compaix\xe3o me cura.",myth:"\u0130slam s\xf6ylencesine g\xf6re Yunus peygamber, halk\u0131na k\xfcs\xfcp bindi\u011fi gemi f\u0131rt\u0131nada durunca, u\u011fursuzlu\u011fun kendisinde oldu\u011funu d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcp denize atlar ve Allah'\u0131n g\xf6nderdi\u011fi bir bal\u0131k onu yutarak kurtar\u0131r. K\u0131rk g\xfcn bal\u0131\u011f\u0131n karn\u0131nda durmadan t\xf6vbe eden Yunus, sonunda bitkin ve cans\u0131z bir halde k\u0131y\u0131ya b\u0131rak\u0131l\u0131r. Allah topraktan bir kabak bitkisi filizlendirir; dev yapraklar\u0131 Yunus'a g\xf6lgelik olur, kabaktan damlayan s\xfct ise onu doyurup aya\u011fa kald\u0131r\u0131r. Maya mitolojisinde ise \xf6ld\xfcr\xfclen ikiz Hun Hunahpu'nun ba\u015f\u0131 bir a\u011faca as\u0131l\u0131nca a\u011fac\u0131n meyveleri su kaba\u011f\u0131 bi\xe7imini al\u0131r; ilk su kabaklar\u0131 b\xf6yle do\u011fmu\u015ftur.",mythEn:"According to Islamic legend, when the prophet Jonah (Yunus), having turned away from his people, found the ship he had boarded stalled in a storm, he believed the ill omen was upon him and leapt into the sea, and a fish sent by God swallowed and saved him. Repenting ceaselessly for forty days in the fish's belly, Jonah was at last cast ashore, exhausted and lifeless. God caused a gourd plant to sprout from the earth; its huge leaves gave Jonah shade, and the milk dripping from the gourd nourished him and raised him to his feet. In Mayan myth, when the head of the slain twin Hun Hunahpu was hung on a tree, the tree's fruit took the shape of a gourd; thus the first gourds were born.",mythDe:"Der islamischen Legende nach glaubte der Prophet Jona (Yunus), der sich von seinem Volk abgewandt hatte, als das Schiff, das er bestiegen hatte, in einem Sturm liegenblieb, das b\xf6se Omen liege auf ihm, und sprang ins Meer, und ein von Gott gesandter Fisch verschlang und rettete ihn. Vierzig Tage lang ohne Unterlass im Bauch des Fisches bereuend, wurde Jona schlie\xdflich ersch\xf6pft und leblos ans Ufer geworfen. Gott lie\xdf eine K\xfcrbispflanze aus der Erde sprie\xdfen; ihre riesigen Bl\xe4tter gaben Jona Schatten, und die aus dem K\xfcrbis tropfende Milch n\xe4hrte ihn und richtete ihn auf. In der Maya-Mythologie nahm, als der Kopf des get\xf6teten Zwillings Hun Hunahpu an einen Baum geh\xe4ngt wurde, die Frucht des Baumes die Gestalt eines K\xfcrbisses an; so wurden die ersten K\xfcrbisse geboren.",mythEs:"Seg\xfan la leyenda isl\xe1mica, cuando el profeta Jon\xe1s (Yunus), tras apartarse de su pueblo, hall\xf3 detenido en una tormenta el barco que hab\xeda abordado, crey\xf3 que el mal augurio reca\xeda sobre \xe9l y se lanz\xf3 al mar, y un pez enviado por Dios lo trag\xf3 y lo salv\xf3. Arrepinti\xe9ndose sin cesar durante cuarenta d\xedas en el vientre del pez, Jon\xe1s fue al fin arrojado a la orilla, exhausto y sin vida. Dios hizo brotar de la tierra una planta de calabaza; sus enormes hojas dieron sombra a Jon\xe1s, y la leche que goteaba de la calabaza lo nutri\xf3 y lo puso en pie. En la mitolog\xeda maya, cuando la cabeza del gemelo asesinado Hun Hunahpu fue colgada de un \xe1rbol, el fruto del \xe1rbol tom\xf3 la forma de una calabaza; as\xed nacieron las primeras calabazas.",mythFr:"Selon la l\xe9gende islamique, lorsque le proph\xe8te Jonas (Yunus), s'\xe9tant d\xe9tourn\xe9 de son peuple, vit s'immobiliser dans une temp\xeate le navire o\xf9 il \xe9tait mont\xe9, il crut le mauvais pr\xe9sage sur lui et se jeta \xe0 la mer, et un poisson envoy\xe9 par Dieu l'engloutit et le sauva. Se repentant sans cesse durant quarante jours dans le ventre du poisson, Jonas fut enfin rejet\xe9 sur le rivage, \xe9puis\xe9 et sans vie. Dieu fit germer de la terre un plant de courge ; ses immenses feuilles donn\xe8rent de l'ombre \xe0 Jonas, et le lait qui gouttait de la courge le nourrit et le remit debout. Dans la mythologie maya, lorsque la t\xeate du jumeau tu\xe9 Hun Hunahpu fut suspendue \xe0 un arbre, le fruit de l'arbre prit la forme d'une courge ; ainsi naquirent les premi\xe8res courges.",mythJa:"\u30a4\u30b9\u30e9\u30e0\u306e\u4f1d\u8aac\u306b\u3088\u308c\u3070\u3001\u6c11\u306b\u80cc\u3092\u5411\u3051\u305f\u9810\u8a00\u8005\u30e8\u30ca\uff08\u30e6\u30cc\u30b9\uff09\u306f\u3001\u4e57\u3063\u305f\u8239\u304c\u5d50\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u52d5\u304b\u306a\u304f\u306a\u308b\u3068\u3001\u4e0d\u5409\u306e\u5fb4\u304c\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3063\u3066\u6d77\u306b\u8eab\u3092\u6295\u3052\u3001\u795e\u304c\u9063\u308f\u3057\u305f\u9b5a\u306b\u5451\u307f\u8fbc\u307e\u308c\u3066\u6551\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u9b5a\u306e\u8179\u3067\u56db\u5341\u65e5\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u7d76\u3048\u9593\u306a\u304f\u6094\u3044\u6539\u3081\u305f\u30e8\u30ca\u306f\u3001\u3064\u3044\u306b\u75b2\u308c\u679c\u3066\u3001\u606f\u3082\u7d76\u3048\u7d76\u3048\u306b\u5cb8\u3078\u6253\u3061\u4e0a\u3052\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u795e\u306f\u5927\u5730\u304b\u3089\u30d2\u30e7\u30a6\u30bf\u30f3\u306e\u8349\u3092\u82bd\u751f\u3048\u3055\u305b\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5de8\u5927\u306a\u8449\u304c\u30e8\u30ca\u306b\u9670\u3092\u3064\u304f\u308a\u3001\u30d2\u30e7\u30a6\u30bf\u30f3\u304b\u3089\u6ef4\u308b\u4e73\u304c\u5f7c\u3092\u990a\u3044\u3001\u7acb\u3061\u4e0a\u304c\u3089\u305b\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30de\u30e4\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u6bba\u3055\u308c\u305f\u53cc\u5b50\u30d5\u30f3\u30fb\u30d5\u30ca\u30d5\u30d7\u30a5\u306e\u9996\u304c\u6728\u306b\u639b\u3051\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u3001\u6728\u306e\u5b9f\u306f\u30d2\u30e7\u30a6\u30bf\u30f3\u306e\u5f62\u3092\u3068\u308a\u3001\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u6700\u521d\u306e\u30d2\u30e7\u30a6\u30bf\u30f3\u304c\u751f\u307e\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Segundo a lenda isl\xe2mica, quando o profeta Jonas (Yunus), tendo se afastado do seu povo, viu parar numa tempestade o navio em que embarcara, acreditou que o mau agouro reca\xeda sobre ele e atirou-se ao mar, e um peixe enviado por Deus o engoliu e o salvou. Arrependendo-se sem cessar por quarenta dias no ventre do peixe, Jonas foi enfim lan\xe7ado \xe0 margem, exausto e sem vida. Deus fez brotar da terra uma planta de ab\xf3bora; suas enormes folhas deram sombra a Jonas, e o leite que pingava da ab\xf3bora o nutriu e o ergueu de p\xe9. Na mitologia maia, quando a cabe\xe7a do g\xeameo morto Hun Hunahpu foi pendurada numa \xe1rvore, o fruto da \xe1rvore tomou a forma de uma ab\xf3bora; assim nasceram as primeiras ab\xf3boras.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/%D4%B4%D5%A4%D5%B4%D5%A5%D5%B2%D5%A7%D5%B6.jpg/330px-%D4%B4%D5%A4%D5%B4%D5%A5%D5%B2%D5%A7%D5%B6.jpg"},{id:"plant-104",emoji:"\u2615",color:"#5B3A29",name:"Kahve",nameEn:"Coffee",nameDe:"Kaffee",nameEs:"Caf\xe9",nameFr:"Caf\xe9",nameJa:"\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc",namePt:"Caf\xe9",origin:"Etiyopya & Yemen (\u0130slam Gelene\u011fi)",originEn:"Ethiopia & Yemen (Islamic Tradition)",originDe:"\xc4thiopien & Jemen (islamische Tradition)",originEs:"Etiop\xeda y Yemen (tradici\xf3n isl\xe1mica)",originFr:"\xc9thiopie et Y\xe9men (tradition islamique)",originJa:"\u30a8\u30c1\u30aa\u30d4\u30a2\u30fb\u30a4\u30a8\u30e1\u30f3\uff08\u30a4\u30b9\u30e9\u30e0\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71\uff09",originPt:"Eti\xf3pia e I\xeamen (tradi\xe7\xe3o isl\xe2mica)",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Solar Pleksus \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u592a\u967d\u795e\u7d4c\u53e2\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["uyan\u0131kl\u0131k","canl\u0131l\u0131k","\u015fifa","payla\u015f\u0131m"],propertiesEn:["wakefulness","vitality","healing","sharing"],propertiesDe:["Wachheit","Vitalit\xe4t","Heilung","Teilen"],propertiesEs:["vigilia","vitalidad","sanaci\xf3n","compartir"],propertiesFr:["\xe9veil","vitalit\xe9","gu\xe9rison","partage"],propertiesJa:["\u899a\u9192","\u6d3b\u529b","\u7652\u3057","\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3044"],propertiesPt:["vig\xedlia","vitalidade","cura","partilha"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xf6zlerini ve kalbini ger\xe7ekten a\xe7; uyan\u0131k olmak, hayat\u0131n k\xfc\xe7\xfck lezzetlerini ve \xf6n\xfcne \xe7\u0131kan \u015fifay\u0131 fark edebilmektir. Kahve sana s\xfcrg\xfcn gibi g\xf6r\xfcnen yerlerde bile bir nimetin sakl\u0131 olabilece\u011fini, payla\u015f\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \xe7o\u011fald\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, truly open your eyes and your heart; to be awake is to notice the small delights of life and the healing that comes your way. Coffee whispers that even in places that feel like exile a blessing may be hidden, and that it multiplies when shared.",dailyMessageDe:"\xd6ffne heute wahrhaft deine Augen und dein Herz; wach zu sein hei\xdft, die kleinen Freuden des Lebens und die Heilung zu bemerken, die dir begegnet. Der Kaffee fl\xfcstert, dass selbst an Orten, die wie Verbannung wirken, ein Segen verborgen sein kann und dass er sich vermehrt, wenn man ihn teilt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, abre de verdad tus ojos y tu coraz\xf3n; estar despierto es notar los peque\xf1os deleites de la vida y la sanaci\xf3n que se cruza en tu camino. El caf\xe9 susurra que incluso en lugares que parecen un destierro puede ocultarse una bendici\xf3n, y que se multiplica al compartirla.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ouvre vraiment tes yeux et ton c\u0153ur ; \xeatre \xe9veill\xe9, c'est remarquer les petits d\xe9lices de la vie et la gu\xe9rison qui croise ton chemin. Le caf\xe9 murmure que m\xeame dans des lieux qui ressemblent \xe0 l'exil une b\xe9n\xe9diction peut se cacher, et qu'elle se multiplie quand on la partage.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u76ee\u3068\u5fc3\u3092\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u306f\u3001\u4eba\u751f\u306e\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u559c\u3073\u3068\u3001\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u7652\u3057\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u306f\u3001\u8ffd\u653e\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u898b\u3048\u308b\u5834\u6240\u306b\u3055\u3048\u6075\u307f\u304c\u96a0\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3001\u305d\u3057\u3066\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u3068\u305d\u308c\u304c\u5897\u3048\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, abra de verdade os seus olhos e o seu cora\xe7\xe3o; estar desperto \xe9 notar os pequenos deleites da vida e a cura que cruza o seu caminho. O caf\xe9 sussurra que mesmo em lugares que parecem um ex\xedlio pode esconder-se uma b\xean\xe7\xe3o, e que ela se multiplica quando partilhada.",howToUse:"Kahve \xe7ekirdeklerini \xf6\u011f\xfct\xfcp a\u011f\u0131r a\u011f\u0131r demleyerek, ilk yudumu bir uyan\u0131\u015f ve \u015f\xfck\xfcr an\u0131na \xe7evirebilirsin. Bir fincan kahveyi sevdi\u011fin biriyle payla\u015fmak, canl\u0131l\u0131k ve dostluk niyetini onurland\u0131ran s\u0131cak bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may grind coffee beans and brew them slowly, turning the first sip into a moment of waking and gratitude. Sharing a cup of coffee with someone you love is a warm gesture honoring an intention of vitality and friendship.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst Kaffeebohnen mahlen und langsam aufbr\xfchen und den ersten Schluck in einen Augenblick des Erwachens und der Dankbarkeit verwandeln. Eine Tasse Kaffee mit einem geliebten Menschen zu teilen ist eine warme Geste, die eine Absicht von Vitalit\xe4t und Freundschaft ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes moler granos de caf\xe9 y prepararlos despacio, convirtiendo el primer sorbo en un momento de despertar y gratitud. Compartir una taza de caf\xe9 con alguien a quien amas es un gesto c\xe1lido que honra una intenci\xf3n de vitalidad y amistad.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux moudre des grains de caf\xe9 et les infuser lentement, faisant de la premi\xe8re gorg\xe9e un instant d'\xe9veil et de gratitude. Partager une tasse de caf\xe9 avec un \xeatre aim\xe9 est un geste chaleureux qui honore une intention de vitalit\xe9 et d'amiti\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u8c46\u3092\u633d\u3044\u3066\u3086\u3063\u304f\u308a\u3068\u6df9\u308c\u3001\u6700\u521d\u306e\u3072\u3068\u53e3\u3092\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u3068\u611f\u8b1d\u306e\u3072\u3068\u3068\u304d\u306b\u5909\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e00\u676f\u306e\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u4eba\u3068\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u6d3b\u529b\u3068\u53cb\u60c5\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u6e29\u304b\u306a\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode moer gr\xe3os de caf\xe9 e prepar\xe1-los devagar, transformando o primeiro gole num momento de despertar e gratid\xe3o. Partilhar uma x\xedcara de caf\xe9 com algu\xe9m que voc\xea ama \xe9 um gesto caloroso que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de vitalidade e amizade.",affirmation:"G\xf6zlerimi ve kalbimi a\xe7\u0131yorum, uyan\u0131kl\u0131\u011f\u0131m payla\u015ft\u0131k\xe7a \xe7o\u011fal\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I open my eyes and my heart, and my wakefulness multiplies as I share it.",affirmationDe:"Ich \xf6ffne meine Augen und mein Herz, und meine Wachheit vermehrt sich, indem ich sie teile.",affirmationEs:"Abro mis ojos y mi coraz\xf3n, y mi vigilia se multiplica al compartirla.",affirmationFr:"J'ouvre mes yeux et mon c\u0153ur, et mon \xe9veil se multiplie \xe0 mesure que je le partage.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u76ee\u3068\u5fc3\u3092\u958b\u304d\u3001\u899a\u9192\u306f\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u307b\u3069\u306b\u5897\u3048\u3066\u3086\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Abro os meus olhos e o meu cora\xe7\xe3o, e a minha vig\xedlia se multiplica \xe0 medida que a partilho.",myth:"Bir \u0130slam s\xf6ylencesinde \u015eeyh \u015eazali, hac yolunda \xf6lece\u011fini \xf6nceden bilir; \xf6ld\xfckten sonra y\xfcz\xfc \xf6rt\xfcl\xfc biri gelip m\xfcridi \u015eeyh \xd6mer'e yol g\xf6sterir ve giderken ona bir a\u011fa\xe7tan kopard\u0131\u011f\u0131 yuvarlak bir meyve verir. S\xfcrg\xfcne g\xf6nderilen \u015eeyh \xd6mer ve m\xfcritleri yiyecek bulamay\u0131nca bu meyveyi bir \xe7\xf6mlekte kaynat\u0131p suyunu i\xe7erler; i\u015fte i\xe7tikleri bu \u015fey kahveydi. \u015eeyh \xd6mer kahveyle hastalar\u0131 iyile\u015ftirince kahvecilerin piri olarak an\u0131l\u0131r. Etiyopya s\xf6ylencesinde ise bir ke\xe7i \xe7oban\u0131, bir \xe7al\u0131n\u0131n meyvesini yiyen ke\xe7isinin uzun s\xfcre uyan\u0131k ve ne\u015feli kald\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 fark eder ve bu \xe7ekirdekleri halk\u0131yla payla\u015f\u0131r.",mythEn:"In an Islamic legend, Sheikh Shazali foreknows that he will die on the pilgrimage road; after his death a veiled figure comes to guide his disciple Sheikh Omar and, on departing, gives him a round fruit plucked from a tree. When Sheikh Omar, sent into exile, and his disciples can find no food, they boil this fruit in a pot and drink its liquid; this thing they drank was coffee. When Sheikh Omar heals the sick with coffee, he is remembered as the patron of coffee makers. In an Ethiopian legend, a goatherd notices that his goat, having eaten the fruit of a shrub, stays awake and lively for a long time, and he shares these beans with his people.",mythDe:"In einer islamischen Legende wei\xdf Scheich Schazali im Voraus, dass er auf dem Pilgerweg sterben wird; nach seinem Tod kommt eine verschleierte Gestalt, um seinen Sch\xfcler Scheich Omar zu f\xfchren, und gibt ihm beim Abschied eine runde, von einem Baum gepfl\xfcckte Frucht. Als Scheich Omar, in die Verbannung geschickt, mit seinen Sch\xfclern keine Nahrung findet, kochen sie diese Frucht in einem Topf und trinken ihren Sud; dieses, was sie tranken, war Kaffee. Als Scheich Omar mit Kaffee die Kranken heilt, wird er als Schutzpatron der Kaffeebereiter in Erinnerung behalten. In einer \xe4thiopischen Legende bemerkt ein Ziegenhirt, dass seine Ziege, nachdem sie die Frucht eines Strauchs gefressen hat, lange wach und munter bleibt, und er teilt diese Bohnen mit seinem Volk.",mythEs:"En una leyenda isl\xe1mica, el jeque Shazali sabe de antemano que morir\xe1 en el camino de la peregrinaci\xf3n; tras su muerte, una figura velada viene a guiar a su disc\xedpulo el jeque Omar y, al partir, le da un fruto redondo arrancado de un \xe1rbol. Cuando el jeque Omar, enviado al destierro, y sus disc\xedpulos no hallan alimento, hierven este fruto en una olla y beben su l\xedquido; aquello que bebieron era caf\xe9. Cuando el jeque Omar sana a los enfermos con caf\xe9, se le recuerda como patr\xf3n de los cafeteros. En una leyenda et\xedope, un cabrero nota que su cabra, tras comer el fruto de un arbusto, permanece despierta y alegre largo tiempo, y comparte estos granos con su pueblo.",mythFr:"Dans une l\xe9gende islamique, le cheikh Shazali sait d'avance qu'il mourra sur la route du p\xe8lerinage ; apr\xe8s sa mort, une figure voil\xe9e vient guider son disciple le cheikh Omar et, en partant, lui donne un fruit rond cueilli sur un arbre. Lorsque le cheikh Omar, envoy\xe9 en exil, et ses disciples ne trouvent aucune nourriture, ils font bouillir ce fruit dans une marmite et en boivent le liquide ; ce qu'ils burent \xe9tait du caf\xe9. Quand le cheikh Omar gu\xe9rit les malades avec du caf\xe9, on le garde en m\xe9moire comme le patron des pr\xe9parateurs de caf\xe9. Dans une l\xe9gende \xe9thiopienne, un chevrier remarque que sa ch\xe8vre, ayant mang\xe9 le fruit d'un arbuste, reste longtemps \xe9veill\xe9e et joyeuse, et il partage ces grains avec son peuple.",mythJa:"\u3042\u308b\u30a4\u30b9\u30e9\u30e0\u306e\u4f1d\u8aac\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30b7\u30a7\u30a4\u30d5\u30fb\u30b7\u30e3\u30b6\u30fc\u30ea\u306f\u5de1\u793c\u306e\u9053\u3067\u6b7b\u306c\u3053\u3068\u3092\u3042\u3089\u304b\u3058\u3081\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u304a\u308a\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6b7b\u5f8c\u3001\u9854\u3092\u8986\u3063\u305f\u8005\u304c\u73fe\u308c\u3066\u5f1f\u5b50\u30b7\u30a7\u30a4\u30d5\u30fb\u30aa\u30de\u30eb\u3092\u5c0e\u304d\u3001\u53bb\u308a\u969b\u306b\u6728\u304b\u3089\u3082\u3044\u3060\u4e38\u3044\u679c\u5b9f\u3092\u5f7c\u306b\u6e21\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u8ffd\u653e\u3055\u308c\u305f\u30b7\u30a7\u30a4\u30d5\u30fb\u30aa\u30de\u30eb\u3068\u5f1f\u5b50\u305f\u3061\u306f\u98df\u3079\u7269\u304c\u898b\u3064\u304b\u3089\u305a\u3001\u3053\u306e\u679c\u5b9f\u3092\u934b\u3067\u716e\u3066\u305d\u306e\u6c41\u3092\u98f2\u307f\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5f7c\u3089\u304c\u98f2\u3093\u3060\u305d\u308c\u304c\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30b7\u30a7\u30a4\u30d5\u30fb\u30aa\u30de\u30eb\u304c\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u3067\u75c5\u4eba\u3092\u7652\u3059\u3068\u3001\u5f7c\u306f\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u3092\u6df9\u308c\u308b\u8005\u305f\u3061\u306e\u7956\u3068\u3057\u3066\u8a18\u61b6\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a8\u30c1\u30aa\u30d4\u30a2\u306e\u4f1d\u8aac\u3067\u306f\u3001\u3042\u308b\u5c71\u7f8a\u98fc\u3044\u304c\u3001\u4f4e\u6728\u306e\u5b9f\u3092\u98df\u3079\u305f\u5c71\u7f8a\u304c\u9577\u3044\u3042\u3044\u3060\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u3066\u5feb\u6d3b\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u304d\u3001\u305d\u306e\u8c46\u3092\u6c11\u3068\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Numa lenda isl\xe2mica, o xeique Shazali sabe de antem\xe3o que morrer\xe1 no caminho da peregrina\xe7\xe3o; ap\xf3s a sua morte, uma figura velada vem guiar o seu disc\xedpulo o xeique Omar e, ao partir, d\xe1-lhe um fruto redondo colhido de uma \xe1rvore. Quando o xeique Omar, enviado ao ex\xedlio, e seus disc\xedpulos n\xe3o encontram alimento, fervem este fruto numa panela e bebem o seu l\xedquido; aquilo que beberam era caf\xe9. Quando o xeique Omar cura os doentes com caf\xe9, \xe9 lembrado como o patrono dos preparadores de caf\xe9. Numa lenda et\xedope, um cabreiro nota que a sua cabra, depois de comer o fruto de um arbusto, permanece desperta e alegre por muito tempo, e partilha esses gr\xe3os com o seu povo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg"},{id:"plant-105",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3e",color:"#A89B5C",name:"Kam\u0131\u015f",nameEn:"Reed",nameDe:"Schilf",nameEs:"Ca\xf1a",nameFr:"Roseau",nameJa:"\u8466",namePt:"Junco",origin:"Antik Yunan",originEn:"Ancient Greece",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland",originEs:"Antigua Grecia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra de la Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra da Garganta",properties:["m\xfczik","esneklik","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","\xf6zlem"],propertiesEn:["music","flexibility","transformation","longing"],propertiesDe:["Musik","Biegsamkeit","Verwandlung","Sehnsucht"],propertiesEs:["m\xfasica","flexibilidad","transformaci\xf3n","anhelo"],propertiesFr:["musique","souplesse","transformation","nostalgie"],propertiesJa:["\u97f3\u697d","\u3057\u306a\u3084\u304b\u3055","\u5909\u5bb9","\u61a7\u308c"],propertiesPt:["m\xfasica","flexibilidade","transforma\xe7\xe3o","saudade"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn r\xfczg\xe2r seni e\u011fdi\u011finde k\u0131r\u0131lma, e\u011fil; en g\xfczel ezgiler \xe7o\u011fu zaman bir kayb\u0131n ard\u0131ndan, esnek bir y\xfcrekten do\u011far. Kam\u0131\u015f sana \xf6zlemini bir m\xfczi\u011fe \xe7evirebilece\u011fini, e\u011filmenin de bir t\xfcr g\xfc\xe7 oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, when the wind bends you, do not break, bend; the loveliest melodies are often born from a flexible heart, after a loss. The reed whispers that you can turn your longing into music, and that bending, too, is a kind of strength.",dailyMessageDe:"Wenn dich heute der Wind beugt, zerbrich nicht, beuge dich; die sch\xf6nsten Melodien entstehen oft aus einem biegsamen Herzen, nach einem Verlust. Das Schilf fl\xfcstert, dass du deine Sehnsucht in Musik verwandeln kannst und dass sich zu beugen auch eine Art St\xe4rke ist.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, cuando el viento te doble, no te rompas, d\xf3blate; las melod\xedas m\xe1s bellas suelen nacer de un coraz\xf3n flexible, tras una p\xe9rdida. La ca\xf1a susurra que puedes convertir tu anhelo en m\xfasica, y que doblarse es tambi\xe9n una forma de fuerza.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, quand le vent te courbe, ne romps pas, ploie ; les plus belles m\xe9lodies naissent souvent d'un c\u0153ur souple, apr\xe8s une perte. Le roseau murmure que tu peux changer ta nostalgie en musique, et que ployer est aussi une forme de force.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u3001\u98a8\u304c\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u6493\u3081\u308b\u3068\u304d\u3001\u6298\u308c\u305a\u306b\u3057\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6700\u3082\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u8abf\u3079\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u55aa\u5931\u306e\u3042\u3068\u3001\u3057\u306a\u3084\u304b\u306a\u5fc3\u304b\u3089\u751f\u307e\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u8466\u306f\u3001\u61a7\u308c\u3092\u97f3\u697d\u306b\u5909\u3048\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3001\u3057\u306a\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u307e\u305f\u4e00\u7a2e\u306e\u5f37\u3055\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, quando o vento curvar voc\xea, n\xe3o se quebre, curve-se; as melodias mais belas muitas vezes nascem de um cora\xe7\xe3o flex\xedvel, depois de uma perda. O junco sussurra que voc\xea pode transformar a sua saudade em m\xfasica, e que curvar-se \xe9 tamb\xe9m uma forma de for\xe7a.",howToUse:"Bir kam\u0131\u015f fl\xfct\xfc ya da basit bir d\xfcd\xfck \xe7alarak nefesini bir ezgiye d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrebilirsin. R\xfczg\xe2rda sallanan kam\u0131\u015flar\u0131n sesini dinlemek de esneklik ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir and\u0131r.",howToUseEn:"You may play a reed flute or a simple whistle, turning your breath into a melody. Listening to the sound of reeds swaying in the wind is also a gentle moment honoring an intention of flexibility and transformation.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst eine Rohrfl\xf6te oder eine einfache Pfeife spielen und deinen Atem in eine Melodie verwandeln. Dem Klang der im Wind wiegenden Schilfrohre zu lauschen ist ebenfalls ein zarter Augenblick, der eine Absicht von Biegsamkeit und Verwandlung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes tocar una flauta de ca\xf1a o un silbato sencillo, convirtiendo tu aliento en una melod\xeda. Escuchar el sonido de las ca\xf1as meci\xe9ndose al viento es tambi\xe9n un momento tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de flexibilidad y transformaci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux jouer d'une fl\xfbte de roseau ou d'un simple sifflet, changeant ton souffle en m\xe9lodie. \xc9couter le son des roseaux qui se balancent au vent est aussi un instant tendre qui honore une intention de souplesse et de transformation.",howToUseJa:"\u8466\u7b1b\u3084\u7d20\u6734\u306a\u7b1b\u3092\u5439\u3044\u3066\u3001\u606f\u3092\u65cb\u5f8b\u306b\u5909\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u98a8\u306b\u63fa\u308c\u308b\u8466\u306e\u97f3\u306b\u8033\u3092\u6f84\u307e\u3059\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u3057\u306a\u3084\u304b\u3055\u3068\u5909\u5bb9\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u3072\u3068\u3068\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode tocar uma flauta de junco ou um apito simples, transformando o seu sopro numa melodia. Ouvir o som dos juncos balan\xe7ando ao vento \xe9 tamb\xe9m um momento terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de flexibilidade e transforma\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"R\xfczg\xe2rda e\u011filiyorum ama k\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131yorum, \xf6zlemim bir m\xfczi\u011fe d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcyor.",affirmationEn:"I bend in the wind but do not break, and my longing turns into music.",affirmationDe:"Ich beuge mich im Wind, doch ich zerbreche nicht, und meine Sehnsucht wird zu Musik.",affirmationEs:"Me doblo con el viento pero no me rompo, y mi anhelo se vuelve m\xfasica.",affirmationFr:"Je ploie dans le vent mais ne romps pas, et ma nostalgie devient musique.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u98a8\u306b\u3057\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3082\u6298\u308c\u305a\u3001\u61a7\u308c\u306f\u97f3\u697d\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Curvo-me ao vento mas n\xe3o me quebro, e a minha saudade se transforma em m\xfasica.",myth:"Yunan mitolojisinde ke\xe7i ayakl\u0131 tanr\u0131 Pan, a\u011fa\xe7 nymphas\u0131 Syrinks'e tutkundu. Pan'dan ka\xe7an Syrinks, Ladon \u0131rma\u011f\u0131 k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131nda kam\u0131\u015fa d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc; Pan sevdi\u011fine kavu\u015famadan kam\u0131\u015flar\u0131n i\xe7inde kalakald\u0131. R\xfczg\xe2rda birbirine s\xfcrt\xfcnen kam\u0131\u015flar\u0131n ho\u015f bir ezgi \xe7\u0131kard\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 duyunca, de\u011fi\u015fik boylarda kesti\u011fi kam\u0131\u015flar\u0131 balmumuyla birle\u015ftirip bir m\xfczik aleti yapt\u0131 ve ona Syrinks'in ad\u0131n\u0131 verdi; bu \xfcflemeli alet Pan fl\xfct\xfc olarak bilinir. Bir ba\u015fka mitte Phrygial\u0131 Kalamos, yar\u0131\u015f\u0131rken bo\u011fulan sevdi\u011fi Karpos'un ac\u0131s\u0131yla yava\u015f yava\u015f kuruyup \u0131rmak kenar\u0131nda bir kam\u0131\u015fa d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr.",mythEn:"In Greek myth, the goat-footed god Pan was enamored of the tree nymph Syrinx. Fleeing from Pan, Syrinx turned into a reed on the bank of the river Ladon; Pan, unable to reach his beloved, stood lost among the reeds. Hearing the reeds rubbing together in the wind make a sweet melody, he cut reeds of different lengths, joined them with beeswax, and made a musical instrument, naming it after Syrinx; this wind instrument is known as the panpipe. In another myth, the Phrygian Kalamos, in grief for his beloved Karpos who drowned while they raced, slowly withers and turns into a reed on the riverbank.",mythDe:"In der griechischen Mythologie war der ziegenf\xfc\xdfige Gott Pan in die Baumnymphe Syrinx verliebt. Auf der Flucht vor Pan verwandelte sich Syrinx am Ufer des Flusses Ladon in ein Schilfrohr; Pan, der seine Geliebte nicht erreichen konnte, stand verloren zwischen dem Schilf. Als er h\xf6rte, wie das im Wind aneinander reibende Schilf eine s\xfc\xdfe Melodie hervorbrachte, schnitt er Rohre verschiedener L\xe4nge, f\xfcgte sie mit Bienenwachs zusammen und machte ein Musikinstrument, das er nach Syrinx benannte; dieses Blasinstrument ist als Panfl\xf6te bekannt. In einem anderen Mythos verdorrt der Phrygier Kalamos im Schmerz um seinen Geliebten Karpos, der beim Wettschwimmen ertrank, langsam und wird am Flussufer zu einem Schilfrohr.",mythEs:"En la mitolog\xeda griega, el dios de pies de cabra Pan estaba enamorado de la ninfa arb\xf3rea Siringa. Huyendo de Pan, Siringa se convirti\xf3 en ca\xf1a en la orilla del r\xedo Lad\xf3n; Pan, sin poder alcanzar a su amada, qued\xf3 perdido entre las ca\xf1as. Al o\xedr que las ca\xf1as, roz\xe1ndose al viento, produc\xedan una dulce melod\xeda, cort\xf3 ca\xf1as de distintas longitudes, las uni\xf3 con cera de abeja e hizo un instrumento musical, d\xe1ndole el nombre de Siringa; este instrumento de viento se conoce como flauta de Pan. En otro mito, el frigio K\xe1lamos, por el dolor de su amado Karpos, ahogado mientras compet\xedan nadando, se seca poco a poco y se convierte en ca\xf1a a la orilla del r\xedo.",mythFr:"Dans la mythologie grecque, le dieu aux pieds de bouc Pan \xe9tait \xe9pris de la nymphe des arbres Syrinx. Fuyant Pan, Syrinx se changea en roseau sur la rive du fleuve Ladon ; Pan, ne pouvant atteindre sa bien-aim\xe9e, resta perdu parmi les roseaux. Entendant les roseaux se frotter au vent en une douce m\xe9lodie, il coupa des roseaux de longueurs diff\xe9rentes, les assembla \xe0 la cire d'abeille et fit un instrument de musique, le nommant d'apr\xe8s Syrinx ; cet instrument \xe0 vent est connu sous le nom de fl\xfbte de Pan. Dans un autre mythe, le Phrygien Kalamos, dans la douleur de son aim\xe9 Karpos noy\xe9 pendant qu'ils faisaient la course, se dess\xe8che peu \xe0 peu et se change en roseau au bord du fleuve.",mythJa:"\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5c71\u7f8a\u306e\u8db3\u3092\u6301\u3064\u795e\u30d1\u30f3\u304c\u6728\u306e\u30cb\u30f3\u30d5\u3001\u30b7\u30e5\u30ea\u30f3\u30af\u30b9\u306b\u604b\u3044\u7126\u304c\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30d1\u30f3\u304b\u3089\u9003\u3052\u308b\u30b7\u30e5\u30ea\u30f3\u30af\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u30e9\u30c9\u30f3\u5ddd\u306e\u307b\u3068\u308a\u3067\u8466\u306b\u59ff\u3092\u5909\u3048\u3001\u30d1\u30f3\u306f\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u306b\u5c4a\u304b\u306c\u307e\u307e\u8466\u306e\u9593\u306b\u7acb\u3061\u3064\u304f\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u98a8\u306b\u64e6\u308c\u5408\u3046\u8466\u304c\u7518\u3044\u8abf\u3079\u3092\u594f\u3067\u308b\u306e\u3092\u805e\u3044\u305f\u5f7c\u306f\u3001\u3055\u307e\u3056\u307e\u306a\u9577\u3055\u306b\u5207\u3063\u305f\u8466\u3092\u871c\u874b\u3067\u7d99\u304e\u5408\u308f\u305b\u3066\u697d\u5668\u3092\u4f5c\u308a\u3001\u305d\u308c\u3092\u30b7\u30e5\u30ea\u30f3\u30af\u30b9\u306b\u3061\u306a\u3093\u3067\u540d\u3065\u3051\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3053\u306e\u5439\u594f\u697d\u5668\u306f\u30d1\u30f3\u306e\u7b1b\u3068\u3057\u3066\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5225\u306e\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30d5\u30ea\u30e5\u30ae\u30a2\u306e\u30ab\u30e9\u30e2\u30b9\u304c\u3001\u7af6\u6cf3\u4e2d\u306b\u6eba\u308c\u305f\u611b\u3059\u308b\u30ab\u30eb\u30dd\u30b9\u306e\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u3067\u5c11\u3057\u305a\u3064\u67af\u308c\u3001\u5ddd\u8fba\u306e\u8466\u306b\u5909\u308f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na mitologia grega, o deus de p\xe9s de bode P\xe3 estava apaixonado pela ninfa das \xe1rvores Siringe. Fugindo de P\xe3, Siringe transformou-se em junco na margem do rio Lad\xe3o; P\xe3, sem poder alcan\xe7ar a sua amada, ficou perdido entre os juncos. Ao ouvir os juncos, ro\xe7ando ao vento, produzirem uma doce melodia, cortou juncos de comprimentos diferentes, uniu-os com cera de abelha e fez um instrumento musical, dando-lhe o nome de Siringe; este instrumento de sopro \xe9 conhecido como flauta de P\xe3. Em outro mito, o fr\xedgio Kalamos, na dor pelo seu amado Karpos, afogado enquanto competiam a nadar, seca aos poucos e se transforma em junco \xe0 beira do rio.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Phragmites_australis_-_NASA_Tracks_an_Environmental_Invader_%2848049936657%29.jpg/330px-Phragmites_australis_-_NASA_Tracks_an_Environmental_Invader_%2848049936657%29.jpg"},{id:"plant-106",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3c",color:"#F2C849",name:"Kat\u0131rt\u0131rna\u011f\u0131",nameEn:"Broom",nameDe:"Ginster",nameEs:"Retama",nameFr:"Gen\xeat",nameJa:"\u30a8\u30cb\u30b7\u30c0",namePt:"Giesta",origin:"Galler & Kelt Mitolojisi",originEn:"Welsh & Celtic Mythology",originDe:"Walisische & keltische Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda galesa y celta",originFr:"Mythologie galloise et celtique",originJa:"\u30a6\u30a7\u30fc\u30eb\u30ba\u30fb\u30b1\u30eb\u30c8\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia galesa e celta",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Solar Pleksus \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u592a\u967d\u795e\u7d4c\u53e2\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["g\xfczellik","ar\u0131nma","\xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck","yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131rma"],propertiesEn:["beauty","cleansing","freedom","soothing"],propertiesDe:["Sch\xf6nheit","Reinigung","Freiheit","Bes\xe4nftigung"],propertiesEs:["belleza","purificaci\xf3n","libertad","sosiego"],propertiesFr:["beaut\xe9","purification","libert\xe9","apaisement"],propertiesJa:["\u7f8e","\u6d44\u5316","\u81ea\u7531","\u548c\u3089\u3052"],propertiesPt:["beleza","purifica\xe7\xe3o","liberdade","apaziguamento"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131n senin i\xe7in bi\xe7ti\u011fi bir kaderin esiri olma; \xe7i\xe7ekten yarat\u0131lm\u0131\u015f olsan bile kendi kalbinin sesini dinleme hakk\u0131n var. Kat\u0131rt\u0131rna\u011f\u0131 sana g\xfczelli\u011fin ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131n elinde de\u011fil, kendi \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcnde \xe7i\xe7ek a\xe7t\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, do not be a captive of a fate someone else cut out for you; even if you were made from flowers, you have the right to heed your own heart. Broom whispers that beauty blossoms not in another's hand but in your own freedom.",dailyMessageDe:"Sei heute nicht Gefangener eines Schicksals, das ein anderer dir zugeschnitten hat; selbst wenn du aus Blumen gemacht w\xe4rst, hast du das Recht, auf dein eigenes Herz zu h\xf6ren. Der Ginster fl\xfcstert, dass Sch\xf6nheit nicht in fremder Hand, sondern in deiner eigenen Freiheit erbl\xfcht.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, no seas cautivo de un destino que otro recort\xf3 para ti; aunque hubieras sido hecho de flores, tienes derecho a escuchar tu propio coraz\xf3n. La retama susurra que la belleza florece no en la mano de otro, sino en tu propia libertad.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ne sois pas captif d'un destin qu'un autre a taill\xe9 pour toi ; m\xeame si tu \xe9tais fait de fleurs, tu as le droit d'\xe9couter ton propre c\u0153ur. Le gen\xeat murmure que la beaut\xe9 s'\xe9panouit non dans la main d'autrui, mais dans ta propre libert\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u4ed6\u4eba\u304c\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u88c1\u65ad\u3057\u305f\u904b\u547d\u306e\u56da\u308f\u308c\u4eba\u306b\u306a\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002\u305f\u3068\u3048\u82b1\u304b\u3089\u9020\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u3066\u3082\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u5fc3\u306e\u58f0\u306b\u5f93\u3046\u6a29\u5229\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a8\u30cb\u30b7\u30c0\u306f\u3001\u7f8e\u306f\u4ed6\u8005\u306e\u624b\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u81ea\u8eab\u306e\u81ea\u7531\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u54b2\u304f\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, n\xe3o seja cativo de um destino que outro recortou para voc\xea; mesmo que voc\xea tivesse sido feito de flores, tem o direito de escutar o seu pr\xf3prio cora\xe7\xe3o. A giesta sussurra que a beleza floresce n\xe3o na m\xe3o de outro, mas na sua pr\xf3pria liberdade.",howToUse:"Kat\u0131rt\u0131rna\u011f\u0131n\u0131n alt\u0131n sar\u0131s\u0131 \xe7i\xe7eklerini bir vazoda seyrederek g\xfczellik ve \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bah\xe7ende ya da bir saks\u0131da yeti\u015ftirmek de ar\u0131nma ve yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131rma niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may contemplate broom's golden-yellow flowers in a vase to accompany an intention of beauty and freedom. Growing it in your garden or a pot is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of cleansing and soothing.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die goldgelben Bl\xfcten des Ginsters in einer Vase betrachten, um eine Absicht von Sch\xf6nheit und Freiheit zu begleiten. Ihn im Garten oder Topf zu ziehen ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Reinigung und Bes\xe4nftigung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes contemplar las flores amarillo doradas de la retama en un jarr\xf3n para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de belleza y libertad. Cultivarla en tu jard\xedn o en una maceta es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de purificaci\xf3n y sosiego.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux contempler les fleurs jaune dor\xe9 du gen\xeat dans un vase pour accompagner une intention de beaut\xe9 et de libert\xe9. Le cultiver dans ton jardin ou en pot est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de purification et d'apaisement.",howToUseJa:"\u30a8\u30cb\u30b7\u30c0\u306e\u9ec4\u91d1\u8272\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u3067\u773a\u3081\u3001\u7f8e\u3068\u81ea\u7531\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5ead\u3084\u9262\u3067\u80b2\u3066\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u6d44\u5316\u3068\u548c\u3089\u3052\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode contemplar as flores amarelo-douradas da giesta em um vaso para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de beleza e liberdade. Cultiv\xe1-la no seu jardim ou em um vaso \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de purifica\xe7\xe3o e apaziguamento.",affirmation:"Ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131n bi\xe7ti\u011fi kaderin esiri de\u011filim, g\xfczelli\u011fim \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcmde \xe7i\xe7ek a\xe7\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I am no captive of a fate cut by another, and my beauty blossoms in my freedom.",affirmationDe:"Ich bin kein Gefangener eines von anderen zugeschnittenen Schicksals, und meine Sch\xf6nheit erbl\xfcht in meiner Freiheit.",affirmationEs:"No soy cautivo de un destino recortado por otro, y mi belleza florece en mi libertad.",affirmationFr:"Je ne suis captif d'aucun destin taill\xe9 par autrui, et ma beaut\xe9 s'\xe9panouit dans ma libert\xe9.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4ed6\u8005\u304c\u88c1\u65ad\u3057\u305f\u904b\u547d\u306e\u56da\u308f\u308c\u4eba\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u7f8e\u306f\u79c1\u306e\u81ea\u7531\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u54b2\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"N\xe3o sou cativo de um destino recortado por outro, e a minha beleza floresce na minha liberdade.",myth:"Galler k\xf6kenli bir efsaneye g\xf6re Llev ad\u0131ndaki adam, annesinin lanetiyle insan soyundan bir e\u015fe sahip olamayacakt\u0131. Bunun \xe7\xf6z\xfcm\xfcn\xfc d\xfc\u015f\xfcnen amcas\u0131 Gwydion ve Kral Math, kat\u0131rt\u0131rna\u011f\u0131, \xe7ay\u0131rg\xfczeli ve me\u015fe \xe7i\xe7eklerinden Blodeuwedd ('\xe7i\xe7eky\xfcz') ad\u0131nda bir kad\u0131n yaratt\u0131lar. \xc7i\xe7eklerden do\u011fan bu kad\u0131n Llev'e e\u015f oldu; ama kalbi ba\u015fka birine aitti ve \xe2\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131yla birlikte kocas\u0131n\u0131 \xf6ld\xfcrmenin yolunu arad\u0131. Sonunda Gwydion, ye\u011fenini bir kartala, \xe7i\xe7ekten yaratt\u0131\u011f\u0131 kad\u0131n\u0131 ise bir bayku\u015fa d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc ve y\xfcz\xfcn\xfcn bir daha g\xfcne\u015f g\xf6rmeyece\u011fine h\xfckmetti.",mythEn:"According to a Welsh legend, a man named Lleu was cursed by his mother never to have a wife of human kind. Pondering a remedy, his uncle Gwydion and King Math created from the flowers of broom, meadowsweet, and oak a woman named Blodeuwedd ('flower-face'). This woman born of flowers became Lleu's wife; but her heart belonged to another, and together with her lover she sought a way to kill her husband. In the end Gwydion turned his nephew into an eagle, and the woman he had made from flowers into an owl, decreeing that her face would never again see the sun.",mythDe:"Einer walisischen Legende nach wurde ein Mann namens Lleu von seiner Mutter verflucht, niemals eine Frau menschlicher Art zu haben. Auf der Suche nach Abhilfe schufen sein Onkel Gwydion und K\xf6nig Math aus den Bl\xfcten von Ginster, M\xe4des\xfc\xdf und Eiche eine Frau namens Blodeuwedd ('Blumengesicht'). Diese aus Blumen geborene Frau wurde Lleus Gemahlin; doch ihr Herz geh\xf6rte einem anderen, und gemeinsam mit ihrem Geliebten suchte sie einen Weg, ihren Mann zu t\xf6ten. Am Ende verwandelte Gwydion seinen Neffen in einen Adler und die Frau, die er aus Blumen gemacht hatte, in eine Eule und verf\xfcgte, dass ihr Gesicht nie wieder die Sonne sehen werde.",mythEs:"Seg\xfan una leyenda galesa, un hombre llamado Lleu fue maldecido por su madre a no tener nunca una esposa de estirpe humana. Buscando un remedio, su t\xedo Gwydion y el rey Math crearon, con las flores de la retama, la reina de los prados y el roble, una mujer llamada Blodeuwedd ('rostro de flor'). Esta mujer nacida de flores fue esposa de Lleu; pero su coraz\xf3n pertenec\xeda a otro, y junto con su amante busc\xf3 la manera de matar a su marido. Al final, Gwydion convirti\xf3 a su sobrino en \xe1guila, y a la mujer que hab\xeda hecho de flores en lechuza, decretando que su rostro nunca volver\xeda a ver el sol.",mythFr:"Selon une l\xe9gende galloise, un homme nomm\xe9 Lleu fut maudit par sa m\xe8re de n'avoir jamais d'\xe9pouse de race humaine. Cherchant un rem\xe8de, son oncle Gwydion et le roi Math cr\xe9\xe8rent, \xe0 partir des fleurs de gen\xeat, de reine-des-pr\xe9s et de ch\xeane, une femme nomm\xe9e Blodeuwedd ('visage de fleur'). Cette femme n\xe9e des fleurs devint l'\xe9pouse de Lleu ; mais son c\u0153ur appartenait \xe0 un autre, et avec son amant elle chercha un moyen de tuer son mari. \xc0 la fin, Gwydion changea son neveu en aigle, et la femme qu'il avait faite de fleurs en chouette, d\xe9cr\xe9tant que son visage ne reverrait jamais le soleil.",mythJa:"\u30a6\u30a7\u30fc\u30eb\u30ba\u306e\u4f1d\u8aac\u306b\u3088\u308c\u3070\u3001\u30b9\u30ec\u30a6\u3068\u3044\u3046\u540d\u306e\u7537\u306f\u3001\u6bcd\u306e\u546a\u3044\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u4eba\u9593\u306e\u59bb\u3092\u6c7a\u3057\u3066\u6301\u3066\u306a\u3044\u3068\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u305d\u306e\u89e3\u6c7a\u3092\u8003\u3048\u305f\u53d4\u7236\u30b0\u30a6\u30a3\u30c7\u30a3\u30aa\u30f3\u3068\u738b\u30de\u30fc\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u30a8\u30cb\u30b7\u30c0\u3001\u30b7\u30e2\u30c4\u30b1\u30bd\u30a6\u3001\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306e\u82b1\u304b\u3089\u3001\u30d6\u30ed\u30c0\u30a4\u30a6\u30a7\u30c3\u30ba\uff08\u300e\u82b1\u306e\u9854\u300f\uff09\u3068\u3044\u3046\u540d\u306e\u5973\u3092\u9020\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u82b1\u304b\u3089\u751f\u307e\u308c\u305f\u3053\u306e\u5973\u306f\u30b9\u30ec\u30a6\u306e\u59bb\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5fc3\u306f\u5225\u306e\u8005\u306e\u3082\u306e\u3067\u3001\u611b\u4eba\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u592b\u3092\u6bba\u3059\u65b9\u6cd5\u3092\u63a2\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3064\u3044\u306b\u30b0\u30a6\u30a3\u30c7\u30a3\u30aa\u30f3\u306f\u7525\u3092\u9df2\u306b\u3001\u82b1\u304b\u3089\u9020\u3063\u305f\u5973\u3092\u689f\u306b\u5909\u3048\u3001\u305d\u306e\u9854\u304c\u4e8c\u5ea6\u3068\u967d\u306e\u76ee\u3092\u898b\u306a\u3044\u3068\u5b9a\u3081\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Segundo uma lenda galesa, um homem chamado Lleu foi amaldi\xe7oado pela m\xe3e a nunca ter uma esposa de estirpe humana. Buscando um rem\xe9dio, seu tio Gwydion e o rei Math criaram, com as flores da giesta, da rainha-dos-prados e do carvalho, uma mulher chamada Blodeuwedd ('rosto de flor'). Essa mulher nascida das flores tornou-se esposa de Lleu; mas o seu cora\xe7\xe3o pertencia a outro, e junto com o seu amante buscou um modo de matar o marido. No fim, Gwydion transformou o sobrinho numa \xe1guia, e a mulher que fizera de flores numa coruja, decretando que o seu rosto nunca mais veria o sol.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/BroomsforSale.jpg/330px-BroomsforSale.jpg"},{id:"plant-107",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#9BB07A",name:"Kavak",nameEn:"Poplar",nameDe:"Pappel",nameEs:"\xc1lamo",nameFr:"Peuplier",nameJa:"\u30dd\u30d7\u30e9",namePt:"Choupo",origin:"Antik Yunan & T\xfcrk Mitolojisi",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Turkic Mythology",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & t\xfcrkische Mythologie",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y mitolog\xeda t\xfarquica",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et mythologie turque",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30c6\u30e5\u30eb\u30af\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e mitologia t\xfarquica",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["y\xfckseli\u015f","ba\u011flant\u0131","yas","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","diren\xe7"],propertiesEn:["ascension","connection","mourning","transformation","resilience"],propertiesDe:["Aufstieg","Verbindung","Trauer","Verwandlung","Widerstandskraft"],propertiesEs:["ascenso","conexi\xf3n","duelo","transformaci\xf3n","resiliencia"],propertiesFr:["\xe9l\xe9vation","connexion","deuil","transformation","r\xe9silience"],propertiesJa:["\u4e0a\u6607","\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a","\u54c0\u60bc","\u5909\u5bb9","\u3057\u306a\u3084\u304b\u306a\u5f37\u3055"],propertiesPt:["ascens\xe3o","conex\xe3o","luto","transforma\xe7\xe3o","resili\xeancia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn ba\u015f\u0131n\u0131 dik tut ve g\xf6\u011fe uzan; en derin yas bile, k\xf6kleri sa\u011flam bir y\xfcrekte, bir g\xfcn yeni bir y\xfckseli\u015fe d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr. Kavak sana yeri ve g\xf6\u011f\xfc ayn\u0131 anda ta\u015f\u0131yabilece\u011fini, kayb\u0131n ard\u0131ndan d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmenin m\xfcmk\xfcn oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, hold your head high and reach for the sky; even the deepest grief, in a heart with firm roots, one day turns into a new ascent. The poplar whispers that you can hold earth and sky at once, and that transformation after loss is possible.",dailyMessageDe:"Halte heute den Kopf hoch und strecke dich zum Himmel; selbst die tiefste Trauer verwandelt sich in einem Herzen mit festen Wurzeln eines Tages in einen neuen Aufstieg. Die Pappel fl\xfcstert, dass du Erde und Himmel zugleich tragen kannst und dass Verwandlung nach dem Verlust m\xf6glich ist.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, mant\xe9n la cabeza alta y exti\xe9ndete hacia el cielo; incluso el duelo m\xe1s hondo, en un coraz\xf3n de ra\xedces firmes, un d\xeda se convierte en un nuevo ascenso. El \xe1lamo susurra que puedes sostener la tierra y el cielo a la vez, y que la transformaci\xf3n tras la p\xe9rdida es posible.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, garde la t\xeate haute et tends-toi vers le ciel ; m\xeame le deuil le plus profond, dans un c\u0153ur aux racines fermes, se change un jour en une nouvelle \xe9l\xe9vation. Le peuplier murmure que tu peux porter la terre et le ciel \xe0 la fois, et que la transformation apr\xe8s la perte est possible.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u982d\u3092\u9ad8\u304f\u4e0a\u3052\u3001\u7a7a\u3078\u4f38\u3073\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6700\u3082\u6df1\u3044\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u3055\u3048\u3001\u6839\u306e\u3057\u3063\u304b\u308a\u3057\u305f\u5fc3\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u306f\u3001\u3044\u3064\u304b\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u4e0a\u6607\u3078\u3068\u5909\u308f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30dd\u30d7\u30e9\u306f\u3001\u5730\u3068\u5929\u3092\u540c\u6642\u306b\u62b1\u3051\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3001\u55aa\u5931\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306e\u5909\u5bb9\u304c\u53ef\u80fd\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, mantenha a cabe\xe7a erguida e estenda-se rumo ao c\xe9u; mesmo o luto mais profundo, num cora\xe7\xe3o de ra\xedzes firmes, um dia se transforma em uma nova ascens\xe3o. O choupo sussurra que voc\xea pode sustentar a terra e o c\xe9u ao mesmo tempo, e que a transforma\xe7\xe3o ap\xf3s a perda \xe9 poss\xedvel.",howToUse:"Bir kavak a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n alt\u0131nda durup yapraklar\u0131n\u0131n r\xfczg\xe2rdaki f\u0131s\u0131lt\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 dinleyerek y\xfckseli\u015f ve ba\u011flant\u0131 niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. D\xfc\u015fen bir kavak yapra\u011f\u0131n\u0131 bir niyet sembol\xfc olarak yan\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131mak da yas ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may stand beneath a poplar and listen to the whisper of its leaves in the wind to accompany an intention of ascension and connection. Carrying a fallen poplar leaf as a symbol of intention is also a gentle gesture honoring mourning and transformation.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst unter einer Pappel stehen und dem Fl\xfcstern ihrer Bl\xe4tter im Wind lauschen, um eine Absicht von Aufstieg und Verbindung zu begleiten. Ein gefallenes Pappelblatt als Symbol der Absicht bei dir zu tragen ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die Trauer und Verwandlung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes detenerte bajo un \xe1lamo y escuchar el susurro de sus hojas al viento para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de ascenso y conexi\xf3n. Llevar una hoja de \xe1lamo ca\xedda como s\xedmbolo de intenci\xf3n es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra el duelo y la transformaci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux te tenir sous un peuplier et \xe9couter le murmure de ses feuilles dans le vent pour accompagner une intention d'\xe9l\xe9vation et de connexion. Porter une feuille de peuplier tomb\xe9e comme symbole d'intention est aussi un geste tendre qui honore le deuil et la transformation.",howToUseJa:"\u30dd\u30d7\u30e9\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u4f47\u307f\u3001\u98a8\u306b\u305d\u3088\u3050\u8449\u306e\u3055\u3055\u3084\u304d\u306b\u8033\u3092\u6f84\u307e\u305b\u3066\u3001\u4e0a\u6607\u3068\u3064\u306a\u304c\u308a\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u843d\u3061\u305f\u30dd\u30d7\u30e9\u306e\u8449\u3092\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6301\u3061\u6b69\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u54c0\u60bc\u3068\u5909\u5bb9\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode parar sob um choupo e ouvir o sussurro de suas folhas ao vento para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de ascens\xe3o e conex\xe3o. Carregar uma folha de choupo ca\xedda como s\xedmbolo de inten\xe7\xe3o \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra o luto e a transforma\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Ba\u015f\u0131m\u0131 dik tutup g\xf6\u011fe uzan\u0131yorum, kayb\u0131n ard\u0131ndan yeniden y\xfckseliyorum.",affirmationEn:"I hold my head high and reach for the sky, and after loss I rise anew.",affirmationDe:"Ich halte den Kopf hoch und strecke mich zum Himmel, und nach dem Verlust erhebe ich mich aufs Neue.",affirmationEs:"Mantengo la cabeza alta y me extiendo hacia el cielo, y tras la p\xe9rdida me elevo de nuevo.",affirmationFr:"Je garde la t\xeate haute et me tends vers le ciel, et apr\xe8s la perte je m'\xe9l\xe8ve de nouveau.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u982d\u3092\u9ad8\u304f\u4e0a\u3052\u3066\u7a7a\u3078\u4f38\u3073\u3001\u55aa\u5931\u306e\u3042\u3068\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u7acb\u3061\u4e0a\u304c\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Mantenho a cabe\xe7a erguida e me estendo rumo ao c\xe9u, e depois da perda me elevo de novo.",myth:"Yunan mitolojisinde \xf6l\xfcler \xfclkesinin tanr\u0131s\u0131 Hades, ad\u0131 'beyaz' anlam\u0131na gelen nympha Leuke'ye \xe2\u015f\u0131kt\u0131; onu yeralt\u0131na ka\xe7\u0131rd\u0131 ama \xf6l\xfcml\xfc Leuke orada \xf6ld\xfc. Hades sevdi\u011fini \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz k\u0131lmak i\xe7in onu ad\u0131yla uyumlu akkavak a\u011fac\u0131na d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc. Bir ba\u015fka mitte g\xfcne\u015f tanr\u0131 Helios'un o\u011flu Phaeton, babas\u0131n\u0131n g\xfcne\u015f arabas\u0131n\u0131 kullanamay\u0131p d\xfc\u015f\xfcnce, ona a\u011flayan k\u0131z karde\u015fleri durmadan g\xf6zya\u015f\u0131 d\xf6kt\xfc ve sonunda kavak a\u011fa\xe7lar\u0131na d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcld\xfcler; akan damlalar\u0131 da amber tanesi oldu. T\xfcrk mitolojisinde ise kavak (Bay Terek), yeri g\xf6\u011f\xfc birle\u015ftiren ve oyma\u011f\u0131 bir araya getiren kutsal bir 'direk' olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr.",mythEn:"In Greek myth, Hades, god of the underworld, loved the nymph Leuke, whose name means 'white'; he carried her down to the underworld, but the mortal Leuke died there. To make his beloved immortal, Hades turned her into the white poplar, in keeping with her name. In another myth, when Phaeton, son of the sun god Helios, could not drive his father's solar chariot and fell, his sisters who wept for him shed tears without end and were at last turned into poplars; the falling drops became beads of amber. In Turkic myth, the poplar (Bay Terek) is seen as a sacred 'pillar' that joins earth and sky and gathers the clan together.",mythDe:"In der griechischen Mythologie liebte Hades, der Gott der Unterwelt, die Nymphe Leuke, deren Name 'wei\xdf' bedeutet; er entf\xfchrte sie in die Unterwelt, doch die sterbliche Leuke starb dort. Um seine Geliebte unsterblich zu machen, verwandelte Hades sie in die Wei\xdfpappel, ihrem Namen entsprechend. In einem anderen Mythos vergossen, als Phaeton, der Sohn des Sonnengottes Helios, den Sonnenwagen seines Vaters nicht lenken konnte und st\xfcrzte, seine um ihn weinenden Schwestern unaufh\xf6rlich Tr\xe4nen und wurden schlie\xdflich in Pappeln verwandelt; die fallenden Tropfen wurden zu Bernsteinperlen. In der t\xfcrkischen Mythologie gilt die Pappel (Bay Terek) als heilige 'S\xe4ule', die Erde und Himmel verbindet und den Stamm zusammenf\xfchrt.",mythEs:"En la mitolog\xeda griega, Hades, dios del inframundo, amaba a la ninfa Leuce, cuyo nombre significa 'blanca'; la llev\xf3 al inframundo, pero la mortal Leuce muri\xf3 all\xed. Para hacer inmortal a su amada, Hades la convirti\xf3 en el \xe1lamo blanco, en armon\xeda con su nombre. En otro mito, cuando Faet\xf3n, hijo del dios sol Helios, no pudo conducir el carro solar de su padre y cay\xf3, sus hermanas, que lloraban por \xe9l, derramaron l\xe1grimas sin fin y al fin fueron convertidas en \xe1lamos; las gotas que ca\xedan se volvieron cuentas de \xe1mbar. En la mitolog\xeda t\xfarquica, el \xe1lamo (Bay Terek) se ve como un 'pilar' sagrado que une la tierra y el cielo y re\xfane al clan.",mythFr:"Dans la mythologie grecque, Had\xe8s, dieu des enfers, aimait la nymphe Leuk\xe9, dont le nom signifie 'blanche' ; il l'emmena aux enfers, mais la mortelle Leuk\xe9 y mourut. Pour rendre sa bien-aim\xe9e immortelle, Had\xe8s la changea en peuplier blanc, en accord avec son nom. Dans un autre mythe, lorsque Pha\xe9ton, fils du dieu soleil H\xe9lios, ne put conduire le char solaire de son p\xe8re et tomba, ses s\u0153urs qui le pleuraient vers\xe8rent des larmes sans fin et furent enfin chang\xe9es en peupliers ; les gouttes qui tombaient devinrent des perles d'ambre. Dans la mythologie turque, le peuplier (Bay Terek) est vu comme un 'pilier' sacr\xe9 qui unit la terre et le ciel et rassemble le clan.",mythJa:"\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u51a5\u754c\u306e\u795e\u30cf\u30c7\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u540d\u304c\u300e\u767d\u300f\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3059\u308b\u30cb\u30f3\u30d5\u3001\u30ec\u30a6\u30b1\u306b\u604b\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5f7c\u306f\u5f7c\u5973\u3092\u51a5\u754c\u3078\u9023\u308c\u53bb\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u4eba\u9593\u306e\u30ec\u30a6\u30b1\u306f\u305d\u3053\u3067\u6b7b\u3093\u3067\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u611b\u3059\u308b\u8005\u3092\u4e0d\u6b7b\u306b\u3059\u308b\u305f\u3081\u3001\u30cf\u30c7\u30b9\u306f\u5f7c\u5973\u3092\u540d\u306b\u3075\u3055\u308f\u3057\u304f\u767d\u30dd\u30d7\u30e9\u306b\u5909\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5225\u306e\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u592a\u967d\u795e\u30d8\u30ea\u30aa\u30b9\u306e\u5b50\u30d1\u30a8\u30c8\u30fc\u30f3\u304c\u7236\u306e\u592a\u967d\u306e\u99ac\u8eca\u3092\u5fa1\u305b\u305a\u306b\u843d\u3061\u308b\u3068\u3001\u5f7c\u3092\u60bc\u3080\u59c9\u59b9\u305f\u3061\u306f\u6d99\u3092\u6d41\u3057\u3064\u3065\u3051\u3001\u3064\u3044\u306b\u30dd\u30d7\u30e9\u306b\u5909\u3048\u3089\u308c\u3001\u843d\u3061\u308b\u6ef4\u306f\u7425\u73c0\u306e\u7c92\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30c6\u30e5\u30eb\u30af\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30dd\u30d7\u30e9\uff08\u30d0\u30a4\u30fb\u30c6\u30ec\u30af\uff09\u306f\u5730\u3068\u5929\u3092\u7d50\u3073\u3001\u6c0f\u65cf\u3092\u4e00\u3064\u306b\u96c6\u3081\u308b\u8056\u306a\u308b\u300e\u67f1\u300f\u3068\u307f\u306a\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na mitologia grega, Hades, deus do submundo, amava a ninfa Leuke, cujo nome significa 'branca'; ele a levou ao submundo, mas a mortal Leuke morreu ali. Para tornar a sua amada imortal, Hades a transformou no choupo-branco, em harmonia com o seu nome. Em outro mito, quando Faetonte, filho do deus sol H\xe9lio, n\xe3o conseguiu conduzir o carro solar de seu pai e caiu, suas irm\xe3s que choravam por ele derramaram l\xe1grimas sem fim e foram enfim transformadas em choupos; as gotas que ca\xedam tornaram-se contas de \xe2mbar. Na mitologia t\xfarquica, o choupo (Bay Terek) \xe9 visto como um 'pilar' sagrado que une a terra e o c\xe9u e re\xfane o cl\xe3.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Lapo_gyslos.jpeg/330px-Lapo_gyslos.jpeg"},{id:"plant-108",emoji:"\ud83c\udf32",color:"#7E8C6B",name:"Kay\u0131n",nameEn:"Birch",nameDe:"Birke",nameEs:"Abedul",nameFr:"Bouleau",nameJa:"\u30ab\u30d0",namePt:"B\xe9tula",origin:"T\xfcrk & \u015eaman Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Turkic & Shamanic Tradition",originDe:"T\xfcrkische & schamanische Tradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n t\xfarquica y cham\xe1nica",originFr:"Tradition turque et chamanique",originJa:"\u30c6\u30e5\u30eb\u30af\u30fb\u30b7\u30e3\u30fc\u30de\u30f3\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o t\xfarquica e xam\xe2nica",element:"eter",elementEn:"ether",elementDe:"\xc4ther",elementEs:"\xe9ter",elementFr:"\xe9ther",elementJa:"\u30a8\u30fc\u30c6\u30eb",elementPt:"\xe9ter",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["kutsall\u0131k","koruma","g\xf6kle ba\u011f","ar\u0131nma","safl\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["sacredness","protection","sky-bond","cleansing","purity"],propertiesDe:["Heiligkeit","Schutz","Himmelsband","Reinigung","Reinheit"],propertiesEs:["sacralidad","protecci\xf3n","v\xednculo celeste","purificaci\xf3n","pureza"],propertiesFr:["sacralit\xe9","protection","lien c\xe9leste","purification","puret\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u8056\u6027","\u5b88\u8b77","\u5929\u3068\u306e\u7d46","\u6d44\u5316","\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u3055"],propertiesPt:["sacralidade","prote\xe7\xe3o","v\xednculo celeste","purifica\xe7\xe3o","pureza"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xf6\u011fe a\xe7\u0131lan bir kap\u0131n\u0131n \xf6n\xfcnde durdu\u011funu hayal et; en y\xfcksek dualar, ayaklar\u0131 yere sa\u011flam basan bir kalpten y\xfckselir. Kay\u0131n sana saf bir niyetin, d\xfcnya ile g\xf6k aras\u0131nda bir k\xf6pr\xfc kurabilece\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, imagine that you stand before a door that opens to the sky; the highest prayers rise from a heart whose feet are firmly on the ground. The birch whispers that a pure intention can build a bridge between earth and sky.",dailyMessageDe:"Stelle dir heute vor, du st\xfcndest vor einer T\xfcr, die sich zum Himmel \xf6ffnet; die h\xf6chsten Gebete steigen aus einem Herzen auf, dessen F\xfc\xdfe fest auf dem Boden stehen. Die Birke fl\xfcstert, dass eine reine Absicht eine Br\xfccke zwischen Erde und Himmel bauen kann.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, imagina que est\xe1s ante una puerta que se abre al cielo; las oraciones m\xe1s altas se elevan de un coraz\xf3n con los pies firmes en la tierra. El abedul susurra que una intenci\xf3n pura puede tender un puente entre la tierra y el cielo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, imagine que tu te tiens devant une porte qui s'ouvre sur le ciel ; les plus hautes pri\xe8res s'\xe9l\xe8vent d'un c\u0153ur dont les pieds sont fermement sur le sol. Le bouleau murmure qu'une intention pure peut b\xe2tir un pont entre la terre et le ciel.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u5929\u3078\u958b\u304f\u6249\u306e\u524d\u306b\u7acb\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u60f3\u50cf\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6700\u3082\u9ad8\u304d\u7948\u308a\u306f\u3001\u8db3\u3092\u3057\u3063\u304b\u308a\u5730\u306b\u3064\u3051\u305f\u5fc3\u304b\u3089\u7acb\u3061\u306e\u307c\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ab\u30d0\u306f\u3001\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306a\u610f\u56f3\u304c\u5730\u3068\u5929\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u306b\u6a4b\u3092\u67b6\u3051\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, imagine que voc\xea est\xe1 diante de uma porta que se abre para o c\xe9u; as ora\xe7\xf5es mais altas se elevam de um cora\xe7\xe3o com os p\xe9s firmes na terra. A b\xe9tula sussurra que uma inten\xe7\xe3o pura pode erguer uma ponte entre a terra e o c\xe9u.",howToUse:"Bir kay\u0131n a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6vdesine elini koyup sessizce niyetini f\u0131s\u0131ldayarak g\xf6kle ba\u011f kurabilirsin. Bir kay\u0131n dal\u0131n\u0131 ya da kabu\u011funu temiz bir k\xf6\u015fede saklamak da kutsall\u0131k ve koruma niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may place your hand on a birch trunk and quietly whisper your intention to forge a bond with the sky. Keeping a birch branch or bark in a clean corner is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of sacredness and protection.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst deine Hand auf einen Birkenstamm legen und still deine Absicht fl\xfcstern, um eine Verbindung zum Himmel zu kn\xfcpfen. Einen Birkenzweig oder Rinde in einer reinen Ecke aufzubewahren ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Heiligkeit und Schutz ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes poner la mano sobre el tronco de un abedul y susurrar en silencio tu intenci\xf3n para forjar un v\xednculo con el cielo. Guardar una rama o corteza de abedul en un rinc\xf3n limpio es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de sacralidad y protecci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux poser la main sur un tronc de bouleau et murmurer en silence ton intention pour tisser un lien avec le ciel. Garder une branche ou une \xe9corce de bouleau dans un coin propre est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de sacralit\xe9 et de protection.",howToUseJa:"\u30ab\u30d0\u306e\u5e79\u306b\u624b\u3092\u7f6e\u304d\u3001\u9759\u304b\u306b\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u3055\u3055\u3084\u3044\u3066\u5929\u3068\u306e\u7d46\u3092\u7d50\u3076\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ab\u30d0\u306e\u679d\u3084\u6a39\u76ae\u3092\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306a\u7247\u9685\u306b\u4fdd\u3064\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u8056\u6027\u3068\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode pousar a m\xe3o no tronco de uma b\xe9tula e sussurrar em sil\xeancio a sua inten\xe7\xe3o para forjar um v\xednculo com o c\xe9u. Guardar um ramo ou casca de b\xe9tula em um canto limpo \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de sacralidade e prote\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Ayaklar\u0131m yere sa\u011flam bas\u0131yor, niyetim g\xf6kle bir k\xf6pr\xfc kuruyor.",affirmationEn:"My feet are firmly on the ground, and my intention builds a bridge with the sky.",affirmationDe:"Meine F\xfc\xdfe stehen fest auf dem Boden, und meine Absicht baut eine Br\xfccke zum Himmel.",affirmationEs:"Mis pies est\xe1n firmes en la tierra, y mi intenci\xf3n tiende un puente con el cielo.",affirmationFr:"Mes pieds sont fermement sur le sol, et mon intention b\xe2tit un pont avec le ciel.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u8db3\u306f\u5730\u306b\u3057\u3063\u304b\u308a\u3068\u3064\u304d\u3001\u610f\u56f3\u304c\u5929\u3068\u306e\u6a4b\u3092\u67b6\u3051\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Meus p\xe9s est\xe3o firmes na terra, e a minha inten\xe7\xe3o ergue uma ponte com o c\xe9u.",myth:"T\xfcrk ve \u015eaman k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde kay\u0131n kutsal bir a\u011fa\xe7t\u0131r; koruyucu ana Umay ile g\xf6ksel ata \xdclgen taraf\u0131ndan yere indirildi\u011fine ve ona y\u0131ld\u0131r\u0131m\u0131n i\u015flemedi\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131r. \u015eamanlar\u0131n ayinlerinde mutlaka bir kay\u0131n bulunur; yurdun i\xe7ine dikilen kay\u0131na 'kap\u0131n\u0131n bek\xe7isi' denir, \xe7\xfcnk\xfc g\xf6\u011f\xfcn kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 \u015famana a\xe7an odur. \u015eaman a\u011fac\u0131n tepesine t\u0131rman\u0131p duman deli\u011finden \xe7\u0131kar, g\xf6\u011f\xfcn dokuz kat\u0131n\u0131 temsilen dokuz \xe7entik atar ve tanr\u0131lara seslenerek onlar\u0131 yard\u0131ma \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131r. Yakut inan\u0131\u015f\u0131nda kay\u0131nda beyaz sa\xe7l\u0131, ya\u015fl\u0131 bir kad\u0131n bi\xe7iminde bir yer iyesi ya\u015far; bu y\xfczden kay\u0131n\u0131 korur, dallar\u0131na \xe7aputlar asar ve kay\u0131ndan yap\u0131lan e\u015fyalar\u0131 sihirli sayarlard\u0131.",mythEn:"In Turkic and shamanic culture, the birch is a sacred tree; it is believed to have been lowered to earth by the protective mother Umay and the celestial ancestor \xdclgen, and that lightning does not strike it. A birch is always present in the shamans' rites; the birch planted inside the yurt is called 'the door's keeper,' for it is the one that opens the gate of heaven to the shaman. The shaman climbs to the top of the tree, emerges through the smoke hole, cuts nine notches representing the nine layers of heaven, and calls upon the gods for aid. In Yakut belief, a land spirit in the form of a white-haired old woman lives in the birch; for this reason they protected the birch, hung cloths on its branches, and held objects made of birch to be magical.",mythDe:"In der t\xfcrkischen und schamanischen Kultur ist die Birke ein heiliger Baum; man glaubt, sie sei von der sch\xfctzenden Mutter Umay und dem himmlischen Ahn \xdclgen zur Erde herabgelassen worden und dass der Blitz sie nicht trifft. Bei den Riten der Schamanen ist stets eine Birke zugegen; die im Inneren der Jurte gepflanzte Birke wird 'H\xfcter der T\xfcr' genannt, denn sie ist es, die dem Schamanen das Tor des Himmels \xf6ffnet. Der Schamane klettert zur Spitze des Baumes, tritt durch das Rauchloch hervor, schneidet neun Kerben, die die neun Schichten des Himmels darstellen, und ruft die G\xf6tter um Hilfe an. Im jakutischen Glauben lebt in der Birke ein Landgeist in Gestalt einer wei\xdfhaarigen alten Frau; deshalb sch\xfctzten sie die Birke, h\xe4ngten T\xfccher an ihre Zweige und hielten aus Birke gefertigte Gegenst\xe4nde f\xfcr magisch.",mythEs:"En la cultura t\xfarquica y cham\xe1nica, el abedul es un \xe1rbol sagrado; se cree que fue bajado a la tierra por la madre protectora Umay y el ancestro celeste \xdclgen, y que el rayo no lo alcanza. En los ritos de los chamanes siempre hay un abedul; al abedul plantado dentro de la yurta se le llama 'el guardi\xe1n de la puerta', pues es el que abre al cham\xe1n la puerta del cielo. El cham\xe1n sube a la copa del \xe1rbol, sale por el agujero del humo, hace nueve muescas que representan las nueve capas del cielo, e invoca la ayuda de los dioses. En la creencia yakut, en el abedul vive un esp\xedritu de la tierra con forma de anciana de cabellos blancos; por eso proteg\xedan el abedul, colgaban telas de sus ramas y ten\xedan por m\xe1gicos los objetos hechos de abedul.",mythFr:"Dans la culture turque et chamanique, le bouleau est un arbre sacr\xe9 ; on croit qu'il a \xe9t\xe9 abaiss\xe9 sur terre par la m\xe8re protectrice Umay et l'anc\xeatre c\xe9leste \xdclgen, et que la foudre ne le frappe pas. Un bouleau est toujours pr\xe9sent dans les rites des chamanes ; le bouleau plant\xe9 \xe0 l'int\xe9rieur de la yourte est appel\xe9 'le gardien de la porte', car c'est lui qui ouvre au chamane la porte du ciel. Le chamane grimpe \xe0 la cime de l'arbre, sort par le trou de fum\xe9e, taille neuf entailles repr\xe9sentant les neuf couches du ciel et invoque l'aide des dieux. Dans la croyance iakoute, un esprit de la terre en forme de vieille femme aux cheveux blancs habite le bouleau ; c'est pourquoi ils prot\xe9geaient le bouleau, suspendaient des \xe9toffes \xe0 ses branches et tenaient pour magiques les objets faits de bouleau.",mythJa:"\u30c6\u30e5\u30eb\u30af\u3068\u30b7\u30e3\u30fc\u30de\u30f3\u306e\u6587\u5316\u306b\u304a\u3044\u3066\u3001\u30ab\u30d0\u306f\u8056\u306a\u308b\u6728\u3067\u3059\u3002\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u6bcd\u30a6\u30de\u30a4\u3068\u5929\u306e\u7956\u30e6\u30eb\u30b2\u30f3\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u5730\u4e0a\u306b\u964d\u308d\u3055\u308c\u305f\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3001\u96f7\u304c\u843d\u3061\u306a\u3044\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b7\u30e3\u30fc\u30de\u30f3\u306e\u5100\u5f0f\u306b\u306f\u5fc5\u305a\u30ab\u30d0\u304c\u3042\u308a\u3001\u30e6\u30eb\u30c8\uff08\u5929\u5e55\uff09\u306e\u5185\u306b\u7acb\u3066\u3089\u308c\u305f\u30ab\u30d0\u306f\u300e\u6249\u306e\u756a\u4eba\u300f\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b7\u30e3\u30fc\u30de\u30f3\u306b\u5929\u306e\u9580\u3092\u958b\u304f\u306e\u304c\u305d\u308c\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30b7\u30e3\u30fc\u30de\u30f3\u306f\u6728\u306e\u9802\u306b\u767b\u308a\u3001\u7159\u51fa\u3057\u306e\u7a74\u304b\u3089\u73fe\u308c\u3001\u5929\u306e\u4e5d\u5c64\u3092\u8868\u3059\u4e5d\u3064\u306e\u523b\u307f\u3092\u5165\u308c\u3001\u795e\u3005\u306b\u52a9\u3051\u3092\u547c\u3073\u304b\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30e4\u30af\u30fc\u30c8\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u767d\u9aea\u306e\u8001\u5973\u306e\u59ff\u3092\u3057\u305f\u571f\u5730\u306e\u7cbe\u304c\u30ab\u30d0\u306b\u4f4f\u3080\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u305f\u3081\u30ab\u30d0\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3001\u679d\u306b\u5e03\u3092\u639b\u3051\u3001\u30ab\u30d0\u3067\u4f5c\u3063\u305f\u9053\u5177\u3092\u9b54\u529b\u3042\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3068\u307f\u306a\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Na cultura t\xfarquica e xam\xe2nica, a b\xe9tula \xe9 uma \xe1rvore sagrada; acredita-se que foi descida \xe0 terra pela m\xe3e protetora Umay e pelo ancestral celeste \xdclgen, e que o raio n\xe3o a atinge. Uma b\xe9tula est\xe1 sempre presente nos ritos dos xam\xe3s; a b\xe9tula plantada dentro da iurta \xe9 chamada 'a guardi\xe3 da porta', pois \xe9 ela que abre ao xam\xe3 o port\xe3o do c\xe9u. O xam\xe3 sobe ao topo da \xe1rvore, sai pelo buraco da fuma\xe7a, faz nove entalhes representando as nove camadas do c\xe9u e invoca a ajuda dos deuses. Na cren\xe7a iacuta, um esp\xedrito da terra em forma de velha de cabelos brancos vive na b\xe9tula; por isso protegiam a b\xe9tula, penduravam panos em seus ramos e tinham por m\xe1gicos os objetos feitos de b\xe9tula.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Betula_pendula_001.jpg/330px-Betula_pendula_001.jpg"},{id:"plant-109",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#5C8A3A",name:"Kenevir",nameEn:"Hemp",nameDe:"Hanf",nameEs:"C\xe1\xf1amo",nameFr:"Chanvre",nameJa:"\u30a2\u30b5",namePt:"C\xe2nhamo",origin:"\xc7in & \u0130ran Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Chinese & Persian Tradition",originDe:"Chinesische & persische Tradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n china y persa",originFr:"Tradition chinoise et perse",originJa:"\u4e2d\u56fd\u30fb\u30da\u30eb\u30b7\u30e3\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o chinesa e persa",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["vizyon","r\xfcya","gev\u015feme","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm"],propertiesEn:["vision","dream","relaxation","transformation"],propertiesDe:["Vision","Traum","Entspannung","Wandlung"],propertiesEs:["visi\xf3n","sue\xf1o","relajaci\xf3n","transformaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["vision","r\xeave","d\xe9tente","transformation"],propertiesJa:["\u5e7b\u8996","\u5922","\u304f\u3064\u308d\u304e","\u5909\u5bb9"],propertiesPt:["vis\xe3o","sonho","relaxamento","transforma\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn zihninin s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 nazik\xe7e gev\u015fet ve i\xe7indeki sessiz hayal g\xfcc\xfcne kulak ver; bazen zaman, derin bir dal\u0131\u015f an\u0131nda bamba\u015fka akar. Kenevir sana i\xe7 d\xfcnyan\u0131n enginli\u011fine sayg\u0131yla, \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc bir merakla yakla\u015fman\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, gently loosen the borders of your mind and listen to the quiet imagination within you; sometimes, in a moment of deep immersion, time flows altogether differently. Hemp whispers that you should approach the vastness of your inner world with respect and measured curiosity.",dailyMessageDe:"Lockere heute sanft die Grenzen deines Geistes und lausche der stillen Vorstellungskraft in dir; manchmal flie\xdft in einem Augenblick tiefen Eintauchens die Zeit ganz anders. Der Hanf fl\xfcstert, dass du dich der Weite deiner inneren Welt mit Achtung und ma\xdfvoller Neugier n\xe4hern sollst.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, afloja con suavidad los l\xedmites de tu mente y escucha la imaginaci\xf3n silenciosa que llevas dentro; a veces, en un momento de inmersi\xf3n profunda, el tiempo fluye de un modo muy distinto. El c\xe1\xf1amo te susurra que te acerques a la inmensidad de tu mundo interior con respeto y una curiosidad mesurada.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, rel\xe2che doucement les fronti\xe8res de ton esprit et \xe9coute l'imagination silencieuse en toi ; parfois, dans un instant d'immersion profonde, le temps s'\xe9coule tout autrement. Le chanvre te murmure d'approcher l'immensit\xe9 de ton monde int\xe9rieur avec respect et une curiosit\xe9 mesur\xe9e.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u5fc3\u306e\u5883\u754c\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u3086\u308b\u3081\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u9759\u304b\u306a\u60f3\u50cf\u529b\u306b\u8033\u3092\u6f84\u307e\u305b\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002\u3068\u304d\u306b\u3001\u6df1\u304f\u6c88\u307f\u3053\u3080\u3072\u3068\u3068\u304d\u306b\u306f\u3001\u6642\u9593\u304c\u307e\u308b\u3067\u9055\u3063\u3066\u6d41\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a2\u30b5\u306f\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u4e16\u754c\u306e\u5e83\u5927\u3055\u306b\u3001\u656c\u610f\u3068\u7bc0\u5ea6\u3042\u308b\u597d\u5947\u5fc3\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u8fd1\u3065\u304f\u3088\u3046\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, afrouxe com suavidade os limites da sua mente e escute a imagina\xe7\xe3o silenciosa dentro de voc\xea; \xe0s vezes, num momento de imers\xe3o profunda, o tempo flui de um modo bem diferente. O c\xe2nhamo sussurra que voc\xea se aproxime da imensid\xe3o do seu mundo interior com respeito e uma curiosidade comedida.",howToUse:"Kenevir liflerinden dokunmu\u015f sa\u011flam bir kuma\u015f\u0131 ya da ipi g\xfcnl\xfck ya\u015fam\u0131nda kullanarak bu kadim bitkinin eme\u011fini onurland\u0131rabilirsin. Bir tutam kenevir tohumunu bir kavanozda saklamak, vizyon ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm niyetini onurland\u0131ran sembolik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may honor the labor of this ancient plant by using sturdy cloth or rope woven from hemp fibers in daily life. Keeping a pinch of hemp seeds in a jar is a symbolic gesture honoring an intention of vision and transformation.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die M\xfche dieser uralten Pflanze ehren, indem du im Alltag festen Stoff oder Seil aus Hanffasern verwendest. Eine Prise Hanfsamen in einem Glas aufzubewahren ist eine symbolische Geste, die eine Absicht von Vision und Wandlung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes honrar el trabajo de esta planta antigua usando en la vida diaria tela o cuerda resistente tejida con fibras de c\xe1\xf1amo. Guardar una pizca de semillas de c\xe1\xf1amo en un frasco es un gesto simb\xf3lico que honra una intenci\xf3n de visi\xf3n y transformaci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux honorer le labeur de cette plante ancienne en utilisant au quotidien un tissu ou une corde solide tiss\xe9s de fibres de chanvre. Garder une pinc\xe9e de graines de chanvre dans un bocal est un geste symbolique qui honore une intention de vision et de transformation.",howToUseJa:"\u9ebb\u306e\u7e4a\u7dad\u3067\u7e54\u3089\u308c\u305f\u4e08\u592b\u306a\u5e03\u3084\u7e04\u3092\u65e5\u3005\u306e\u66ae\u3089\u3057\u3067\u4f7f\u3044\u3001\u3053\u306e\u53e4\u6765\u306e\u690d\u7269\u306e\u52b4\u3092\u305f\u305f\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u307e\u307f\u306e\u9ebb\u306e\u7a2e\u3092\u74f6\u306b\u4fdd\u3064\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u5e7b\u8996\u3068\u5909\u5bb9\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u306a\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode honrar o trabalho desta planta antiga usando no dia a dia tecido ou corda resistente tecidos com fibras de c\xe2nhamo. Guardar uma pitada de sementes de c\xe2nhamo em um frasco \xe9 um gesto simb\xf3lico que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de vis\xe3o e transforma\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Zihnimin s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 nazik\xe7e gev\u015fetiyorum, i\xe7 d\xfcnyam\u0131n enginli\u011fine sayg\u0131yla yakla\u015f\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I gently loosen the borders of my mind and approach the vastness of my inner world with respect.",affirmationDe:"Ich lockere sanft die Grenzen meines Geistes und n\xe4here mich der Weite meiner inneren Welt mit Achtung.",affirmationEs:"Aflojo con suavidad los l\xedmites de mi mente y me acerco con respeto a la inmensidad de mi mundo interior.",affirmationFr:"Je rel\xe2che doucement les fronti\xe8res de mon esprit et j'approche avec respect l'immensit\xe9 de mon monde int\xe9rieur.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5fc3\u306e\u5883\u754c\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u3086\u308b\u3081\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u4e16\u754c\u306e\u5e83\u5927\u3055\u306b\u656c\u610f\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u8fd1\u3065\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Afrouxo com suavidade os limites da minha mente e me aproximo com respeito da imensid\xe3o do meu mundo interior.",myth:"Kenevir, \xc7in ve \u0130ran'da \xe7ok eski \xe7a\u011flardan beri yeti\u015ftirilen bir bitkidir; tohumundan elde edilen bir kar\u0131\u015f\u0131m\u0131n \xf6mr\xfc uzatt\u0131\u011f\u0131na ve zihinde yaratt\u0131\u011f\u0131 ho\u015flukla birlikte ki\u015fiye kehanet yetene\u011fi verdi\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. \xc7in'de anlat\u0131lan bir s\xf6ylencede da\u011fda y\xfcr\xfcy\xfc\u015fe \xe7\u0131kan iki adam\u0131n kar\u015f\u0131s\u0131na \xe7al\u0131l\u0131klar aras\u0131ndan iki gen\xe7 k\u0131z \xe7\u0131kar; k\u0131zlar onlar\u0131 ya\u015fad\u0131klar\u0131 yere g\xf6t\xfcr\xfcp kenevirden haz\u0131rlad\u0131klar\u0131 bir yiyecekle besler. Adamlar hayal\xee bir d\xfcnyada harika bir zaman ge\xe7irip kendilerini kaybeder; oysa da\u011fda ge\xe7irdikleri o s\xfcrenin tam yedi nesillik bir zaman oldu\u011fu anlat\u0131l\u0131r. Esrar\u0131n \xe7ok daha eskiden, S\xfcmerler zaman\u0131nda da g\xfcndelik ya\u015fam\u0131n bir par\xe7as\u0131 oldu\u011fu bilinir.",mythEn:"Hemp is a plant cultivated since very ancient times in China and Persia; a preparation made from its seed was believed to lengthen life and, along with the pleasantness it created in the mind, to grant a person the gift of prophecy. In a Chinese tale, two men out walking in the mountains are met by two young women emerging from the bushes; the women take them to where they live and feed them a food prepared from hemp. The men spend a wonderful time lost in an imaginary world; yet it is told that the time they spent in the mountains was in fact a span of seven generations. It is known that cannabis was a part of daily life much earlier still, in the time of the Sumerians.",mythDe:"Hanf ist eine Pflanze, die seit sehr alter Zeit in China und Persien angebaut wird; man glaubte, eine aus ihrem Samen bereitete Zubereitung verl\xe4ngere das Leben und verleihe einem Menschen, samt der Annehmlichkeit, die sie im Geist erzeugt, die Gabe der Weissagung. In einer chinesischen Erz\xe4hlung begegnen zwei M\xe4nnern, die in den Bergen spazieren gehen, zwei junge Frauen, die aus dem Geb\xfcsch treten; die Frauen f\xfchren sie zu ihrem Wohnort und speisen sie mit einem aus Hanf bereiteten Gericht. Die M\xe4nner verbringen eine wunderbare Zeit, verloren in einer eingebildeten Welt; doch wird erz\xe4hlt, dass die Zeit, die sie in den Bergen verbrachten, in Wahrheit eine Spanne von sieben Generationen war. Es ist bekannt, dass Cannabis schon viel fr\xfcher, zur Zeit der Sumerer, Teil des t\xe4glichen Lebens war.",mythEs:"El c\xe1\xf1amo es una planta cultivada desde tiempos muy antiguos en China y Persia; se cre\xeda que una preparaci\xf3n hecha con su semilla alargaba la vida y, junto con la placidez que creaba en la mente, otorgaba a la persona el don de la profec\xeda. En un relato chino, a dos hombres que pasean por las monta\xf1as les salen al encuentro dos j\xf3venes que surgen de los matorrales; las muchachas los llevan a donde viven y los alimentan con una comida preparada con c\xe1\xf1amo. Los hombres pasan un tiempo maravilloso perdidos en un mundo imaginario; sin embargo, se cuenta que el tiempo que pasaron en las monta\xf1as fue en realidad un lapso de siete generaciones. Se sabe que el cannabis fue parte de la vida cotidiana mucho antes a\xfan, en tiempos de los sumerios.",mythFr:"Le chanvre est une plante cultiv\xe9e depuis des temps tr\xe8s anciens en Chine et en Perse ; on croyait qu'une pr\xe9paration faite de sa graine prolongeait la vie et, avec l'agr\xe9ment qu'elle cr\xe9ait dans l'esprit, conf\xe9rait \xe0 la personne le don de proph\xe9tie. Dans un r\xe9cit chinois, deux hommes se promenant dans les montagnes rencontrent deux jeunes filles surgies des buissons ; les filles les emm\xe8nent l\xe0 o\xf9 elles vivent et les nourrissent d'un mets pr\xe9par\xe9 avec du chanvre. Les hommes passent un temps merveilleux, perdus dans un monde imaginaire ; or il est dit que le temps qu'ils pass\xe8rent dans les montagnes fut en r\xe9alit\xe9 une dur\xe9e de sept g\xe9n\xe9rations. On sait que le cannabis faisait partie de la vie quotidienne bien plus t\xf4t encore, du temps des Sum\xe9riens.",mythJa:"\u30a2\u30b5\u306f\u4e2d\u56fd\u3068\u30da\u30eb\u30b7\u30e3\u3067\u975e\u5e38\u306b\u53e4\u304f\u304b\u3089\u683d\u57f9\u3055\u308c\u3066\u304d\u305f\u690d\u7269\u3067\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7a2e\u304b\u3089\u4f5c\u308b\u8abf\u5408\u7269\u306f\u5bff\u547d\u3092\u5ef6\u3070\u3057\u3001\u5fc3\u306b\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u5fc3\u5730\u3088\u3055\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3001\u305d\u306e\u4eba\u306b\u4e88\u8a00\u306e\u529b\u3092\u6388\u3051\u308b\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3042\u308b\u4e2d\u56fd\u306e\u7269\u8a9e\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5c71\u3092\u6b69\u304f\u4e8c\u4eba\u306e\u7537\u306e\u524d\u306b\u3001\u8302\u307f\u304b\u3089\u4e8c\u4eba\u306e\u82e5\u3044\u5a18\u304c\u73fe\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5a18\u305f\u3061\u306f\u5f7c\u3089\u3092\u4f4f\u307e\u3044\u3078\u9023\u308c\u3066\u884c\u304d\u3001\u30a2\u30b5\u3067\u4f5c\u3063\u305f\u98df\u3079\u7269\u3067\u3082\u3066\u306a\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u7537\u305f\u3061\u306f\u5e7b\u306e\u4e16\u754c\u306b\u6211\u3092\u5fd8\u308c\u3066\u7d20\u6674\u3089\u3057\u3044\u3068\u304d\u3092\u904e\u3054\u3057\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u5f7c\u3089\u304c\u5c71\u3067\u904e\u3054\u3057\u305f\u305d\u306e\u6642\u9593\u306f\u3001\u5b9f\u306b\u4e03\u4e16\u4ee3\u5206\u306e\u9577\u3055\u3067\u3042\u3063\u305f\u3068\u4f1d\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5927\u9ebb\u306f\u3055\u3089\u306b\u305a\u3063\u3068\u6614\u3001\u30b7\u30e5\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\u4eba\u306e\u6642\u4ee3\u306b\u3059\u3067\u306b\u65e5\u3005\u306e\u66ae\u3089\u3057\u306e\u4e00\u90e8\u3067\u3042\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"O c\xe2nhamo \xe9 uma planta cultivada desde tempos muito antigos na China e na P\xe9rsia; acreditava-se que um preparo feito da sua semente prolongava a vida e, junto com a placidez que criava na mente, concedia \xe0 pessoa o dom da profecia. Num relato chin\xeas, dois homens que passeiam pelas montanhas s\xe3o surpreendidos por duas jovens que surgem do mato; as mo\xe7as os levam ao lugar onde vivem e os alimentam com uma comida preparada com c\xe2nhamo. Os homens passam um tempo maravilhoso, perdidos num mundo imagin\xe1rio; por\xe9m, conta-se que o tempo que passaram nas montanhas foi, na verdade, um per\xedodo de sete gera\xe7\xf5es. Sabe-se que o cannabis fazia parte da vida cotidiana muito antes ainda, no tempo dos sum\xe9rios.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/La_Roche_Jagu_chanvre_1.JPG/330px-La_Roche_Jagu_chanvre_1.JPG"},{id:"plant-110",emoji:"\ud83c\udf52",color:"#C8285A",name:"Kiraz",nameEn:"Cherry",nameDe:"Kirsche",nameEs:"Cereza",nameFr:"Cerise",nameJa:"\u30b5\u30af\u30e9\u30f3\u30dc",namePt:"Cereja",origin:"Japonya & \xc7in Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Japanese & Chinese Tradition",originDe:"Japanische & chinesische Tradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n japonesa y china",originFr:"Tradition japonaise et chinoise",originJa:"\u65e5\u672c\u30fb\u4e2d\u56fd\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o japonesa e chinesa",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["g\xfczellik","ge\xe7icilik","al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfcl\xfck","\xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck","tazelik"],propertiesEn:["beauty","transience","humility","immortality","freshness"],propertiesDe:["Sch\xf6nheit","Verg\xe4nglichkeit","Demut","Unsterblichkeit","Frische"],propertiesEs:["belleza","transitoriedad","humildad","inmortalidad","frescura"],propertiesFr:["beaut\xe9","\xe9ph\xe9m\xe8re","humilit\xe9","immortalit\xe9","fra\xeecheur"],propertiesJa:["\u7f8e","\u511a\u3055","\u8b19\u865a","\u4e0d\u6b7b","\u307f\u305a\u307f\u305a\u3057\u3055"],propertiesPt:["beleza","transitoriedade","humildade","imortalidade","frescor"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn an\u0131n g\xfczelli\u011fini, k\u0131sa \xf6m\xfcrl\xfc oldu\u011fu i\xe7in daha \xe7ok sev; kiraz \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi gibi, en g\xfczel anlar \xe7abuk ge\xe7ti\u011fi i\xe7in k\u0131ymetlidir. Kiraz sana ge\xe7icili\u011fin bir kay\u0131p de\u011fil, dolu dolu ya\u015famak i\xe7in bir davet oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, love the beauty of the moment all the more because it is fleeting; like the cherry blossom, the loveliest moments are precious because they pass quickly. The cherry whispers that transience is not a loss but an invitation to live fully.",dailyMessageDe:"Liebe heute die Sch\xf6nheit des Augenblicks umso mehr, weil sie fl\xfcchtig ist; wie die Kirschbl\xfcte sind die sch\xf6nsten Augenblicke kostbar, weil sie schnell vergehen. Die Kirsche fl\xfcstert, dass Verg\xe4nglichkeit kein Verlust ist, sondern eine Einladung, voll zu leben.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ama la belleza del instante a\xfan m\xe1s porque es fugaz; como la flor del cerezo, los momentos m\xe1s bellos son preciosos porque pasan r\xe1pido. La cereza susurra que la transitoriedad no es una p\xe9rdida, sino una invitaci\xf3n a vivir plenamente.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, aime la beaut\xe9 de l'instant d'autant plus qu'elle est fugace ; comme la fleur de cerisier, les plus beaux instants sont pr\xe9cieux parce qu'ils passent vite. La cerise murmure que l'\xe9ph\xe9m\xe8re n'est pas une perte mais une invitation \xe0 vivre pleinement.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u511a\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3053\u305d\u3001\u305d\u306e\u77ac\u9593\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u3044\u3063\u305d\u3046\u611b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u685c\u306e\u82b1\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u6700\u3082\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u77ac\u9593\u306f\u3001\u3059\u3050\u306b\u904e\u304e\u53bb\u308b\u304b\u3089\u3053\u305d\u5c0a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30b5\u30af\u30e9\u30f3\u30dc\u306f\u3001\u511a\u3055\u306f\u55aa\u5931\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u6e80\u3061\u8db3\u308a\u3066\u751f\u304d\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306e\u62db\u304d\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, ame a beleza do instante ainda mais por ela ser passageira; como a flor da cerejeira, os momentos mais belos s\xe3o preciosos porque passam depressa. A cereja sussurra que a transitoriedade n\xe3o \xe9 uma perda, mas um convite a viver plenamente.",howToUse:"Olgun kirazlar\u0131 taze yiyebilir, \xe7i\xe7ek a\xe7t\u0131\u011f\u0131 baharda bir kiraz a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n alt\u0131nda durup ge\xe7icili\u011fin g\xfczelli\u011fini seyredebilirsin. Bir dal kiraz \xe7i\xe7e\u011fini bir vazoda tutmak da g\xfczellik ve al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfcl\xfck niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may eat ripe cherries fresh, and in the spring when it blossoms, stand beneath a cherry tree and contemplate the beauty of transience. Keeping a sprig of cherry blossom in a vase is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of beauty and humility.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst reife Kirschen frisch essen und im Fr\xfchling, wenn er bl\xfcht, unter einem Kirschbaum stehen und die Sch\xf6nheit der Verg\xe4nglichkeit betrachten. Einen Zweig Kirschbl\xfcten in einer Vase aufzubewahren ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Sch\xf6nheit und Demut ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes comer cerezas maduras frescas y, en la primavera cuando florece, detenerte bajo un cerezo y contemplar la belleza de lo fugaz. Guardar una ramita de flor de cerezo en un jarr\xf3n es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de belleza y humildad.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux manger des cerises m\xfbres fra\xeeches et, au printemps quand il fleurit, te tenir sous un cerisier et contempler la beaut\xe9 de l'\xe9ph\xe9m\xe8re. Garder un rameau de fleur de cerisier dans un vase est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de beaut\xe9 et d'humilit\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u719f\u3057\u305f\u30b5\u30af\u30e9\u30f3\u30dc\u3092\u751f\u306e\u307e\u307e\u98df\u3079\u3001\u82b1\u54b2\u304f\u6625\u306b\u306f\u685c\u306e\u6728\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u4f47\u3093\u3067\u511a\u3055\u306e\u7f8e\u3092\u773a\u3081\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e00\u679d\u306e\u685c\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u306b\u633f\u3057\u3066\u304a\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u7f8e\u3068\u8b19\u865a\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode comer cerejas maduras frescas e, na primavera quando floresce, parar sob uma cerejeira e contemplar a beleza do que \xe9 passageiro. Manter um raminho de flor de cerejeira em um vaso \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de beleza e humildade.",affirmation:"Ge\xe7ici olan\u0131n g\xfczelli\u011fini seviyorum, her an\u0131 dolu dolu ya\u015f\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I love the beauty of the fleeting, and I live each moment fully.",affirmationDe:"Ich liebe die Sch\xf6nheit des Fl\xfcchtigen und lebe jeden Augenblick ganz.",affirmationEs:"Amo la belleza de lo fugaz, y vivo cada instante plenamente.",affirmationFr:"J'aime la beaut\xe9 de l'\xe9ph\xe9m\xe8re, et je vis chaque instant pleinement.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u511a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u306e\u7f8e\u3092\u611b\u3057\u3001\u4e00\u77ac\u4e00\u77ac\u3092\u6e80\u3061\u8db3\u308a\u3066\u751f\u304d\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Amo a beleza do que \xe9 passageiro, e vivo cada instante plenamente.",myth:"Kiraz \xe7i\xe7ekleriyle donanan Japonya'da kiraz; g\xfczelli\u011fin, nezaketin ve al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfcl\xfc\u011f\xfcn sembol\xfcd\xfcr, \xe7i\xe7e\u011finin k\u0131sa \xf6mr\xfc gen\xe7li\u011fin ge\xe7ici tatl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 anlat\u0131r. \xc7in'de ise kiraz \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfc\u011f\xfc simgeler; bir mitte tanr\u0131\xe7a Xi Wang Mu her bin y\u0131lda bir kiraz bah\xe7elerinde \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck biriktirirdi. Kiraz a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n k\xf6t\xfc ruhlara ge\xe7it vermedi\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131r; bu y\xfczden \xc7in'de yeni y\u0131lda evlerin kap\u0131s\u0131na kiraz dallar\u0131 as\u0131l\u0131r, \xf6nlerine kiraz a\u011fac\u0131ndan heykeller konulurdu. A\u011fac\u0131n yapraklanmadan \xf6nce \xe7i\xe7ek a\xe7mas\u0131, insan\u0131n d\xfcnyaya \xe7\u0131plak geli\u015fini temsil eder.",mythEn:"In Japan, adorned with cherry blossoms, the cherry is a symbol of beauty, gentleness, and humility, and the brief life of its blossom tells of the fleeting sweetness of youth. In China, the cherry symbolizes immortality; in one myth, the goddess Xi Wang Mu stored up immortality in her cherry orchards once every thousand years. The cherry tree was believed to bar passage to evil spirits; therefore in China cherry branches were hung on house doors at the new year, and statues made of cherry wood were placed before them. That the tree blossoms before it leafs represents the human being's naked arrival into the world.",mythDe:"In Japan, geschm\xfcckt mit Kirschbl\xfcten, ist die Kirsche ein Sinnbild der Sch\xf6nheit, der Sanftheit und der Demut, und das kurze Leben ihrer Bl\xfcte erz\xe4hlt von der fl\xfcchtigen S\xfc\xdfe der Jugend. In China versinnbildlicht die Kirsche die Unsterblichkeit; in einem Mythos sammelte die G\xf6ttin Xi Wang Mu einmal in tausend Jahren Unsterblichkeit in ihren Kirschg\xe4rten. Man glaubte, der Kirschbaum verwehre b\xf6sen Geistern den Durchgang; darum h\xe4ngte man in China zum Neujahr Kirschzweige an die Haust\xfcren und stellte aus Kirschholz gefertigte Statuen davor. Dass der Baum bl\xfcht, ehe er Bl\xe4tter tr\xe4gt, stellt die nackte Ankunft des Menschen in der Welt dar.",mythEs:"En Jap\xf3n, adornado con flores de cerezo, el cerezo es s\xedmbolo de belleza, gentileza y humildad, y la breve vida de su flor habla de la dulzura fugaz de la juventud. En China, la cereza simboliza la inmortalidad; en un mito, la diosa Xi Wang Mu acumulaba inmortalidad en sus huertos de cerezos una vez cada mil a\xf1os. Se cre\xeda que el cerezo imped\xeda el paso a los malos esp\xedritus; por ello en China se colgaban ramas de cerezo en las puertas de las casas en el a\xf1o nuevo, y se colocaban ante ellas estatuas hechas de madera de cerezo. Que el \xe1rbol florezca antes de echar hojas representa la llegada desnuda del ser humano al mundo.",mythFr:"Au Japon, par\xe9 de fleurs de cerisier, le cerisier est un symbole de beaut\xe9, de douceur et d'humilit\xe9, et la br\xe8ve vie de sa fleur dit la douceur \xe9ph\xe9m\xe8re de la jeunesse. En Chine, la cerise symbolise l'immortalit\xe9 ; dans un mythe, la d\xe9esse Xi Wang Mu emmagasinait l'immortalit\xe9 dans ses vergers de cerisiers une fois tous les mille ans. On croyait que le cerisier barrait le passage aux mauvais esprits ; c'est pourquoi en Chine on suspendait des branches de cerisier aux portes des maisons au nouvel an, et l'on pla\xe7ait devant elles des statues faites de bois de cerisier. Que l'arbre fleurisse avant de se couvrir de feuilles repr\xe9sente l'arriv\xe9e nue de l'\xeatre humain au monde.",mythJa:"\u685c\u306e\u82b1\u306b\u5f69\u3089\u308c\u308b\u65e5\u672c\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30b5\u30af\u30e9\u30f3\u30dc\uff08\u685c\uff09\u306f\u7f8e\u3068\u512a\u3057\u3055\u3068\u8b19\u865a\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u305d\u306e\u82b1\u306e\u77ed\u3044\u547d\u306f\u9752\u6625\u306e\u511a\u3044\u7518\u3055\u3092\u8a9e\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e2d\u56fd\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30b5\u30af\u30e9\u30f3\u30dc\u306f\u4e0d\u6b7b\u3092\u8c61\u5fb4\u3057\u3001\u3042\u308b\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u5973\u795e\u897f\u738b\u6bcd\u304c\u5343\u5e74\u306b\u4e00\u5ea6\u3001\u685c\u306e\u5712\u306b\u4e0d\u6b7b\u3092\u84c4\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u685c\u306e\u6728\u306f\u60aa\u970a\u306e\u901a\u884c\u3092\u963b\u3080\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u305f\u3081\u4e2d\u56fd\u3067\u306f\u65b0\u5e74\u306b\u5bb6\u306e\u6238\u53e3\u306b\u685c\u306e\u679d\u3092\u639b\u3051\u3001\u305d\u306e\u524d\u306b\u685c\u306e\u6728\u3067\u4f5c\u3063\u305f\u50cf\u3092\u7f6e\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u6728\u304c\u8449\u306b\u5148\u7acb\u3063\u3066\u82b1\u3092\u54b2\u304b\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u4eba\u304c\u88f8\u3067\u3053\u306e\u4e16\u306b\u751f\u307e\u308c\u51fa\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u8868\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"No Jap\xe3o, adornada com flores de cerejeira, a cereja \xe9 s\xedmbolo de beleza, gentileza e humildade, e a breve vida de sua flor fala da do\xe7ura passageira da juventude. Na China, a cereja simboliza a imortalidade; num mito, a deusa Xi Wang Mu acumulava imortalidade em seus pomares de cerejeira uma vez a cada mil anos. Acreditava-se que a cerejeira barrava a passagem aos maus esp\xedritos; por isso, na China, penduravam-se ramos de cerejeira nas portas das casas no ano-novo, e colocavam-se diante delas est\xe1tuas feitas de madeira de cerejeira. Que a \xe1rvore flores\xe7a antes de criar folhas representa a chegada nua do ser humano ao mundo.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg"},{id:"plant-111",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3c",color:"#F4D35E",name:"Koyung\xf6z\xfc",nameEn:"Daisy",nameDe:"G\xe4nsebl\xfcmchen",nameEs:"Margarita",nameFr:"P\xe2querette",nameJa:"\u30d2\u30ca\u30ae\u30af",namePt:"Margarida",origin:"Roma Mitolojisi",originEn:"Roman Mythology",originDe:"R\xf6mische Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda romana",originFr:"Mythologie romaine",originJa:"\u30ed\u30fc\u30de\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia romana",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["masumiyet","safl\u0131k","yeni ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7","umut"],propertiesEn:["innocence","purity","new beginning","hope"],propertiesDe:["Unschuld","Reinheit","Neuanfang","Hoffnung"],propertiesEs:["inocencia","pureza","nuevo comienzo","esperanza"],propertiesFr:["innocence","puret\xe9","nouveau d\xe9part","espoir"],propertiesJa:["\u7121\u57a2","\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u3055","\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u59cb\u307e\u308a","\u5e0c\u671b"],propertiesPt:["inoc\xeancia","pureza","novo come\xe7o","esperan\xe7a"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn sade ve saf bir kalple g\xfcne ba\u015fla; en k\xfc\xe7\xfck \xe7i\xe7ek bile her sabah g\xfcne\u015fe yeniden a\xe7\u0131lmay\u0131 bilir. Koyung\xf6z\xfc sana masumiyetin bir zay\u0131fl\u0131k de\u011fil, her g\xfcn yeniden ba\u015flama cesareti oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, begin the day with a simple, pure heart; even the smallest flower knows how to open to the sun anew each morning. The daisy whispers that innocence is not a weakness but the courage to begin again every day.",dailyMessageDe:"Beginne den Tag heute mit einem schlichten, reinen Herzen; selbst die kleinste Blume wei\xdf, sich jeden Morgen der Sonne aufs Neue zu \xf6ffnen. Das G\xe4nsebl\xfcmchen fl\xfcstert, dass Unschuld keine Schw\xe4che ist, sondern der Mut, jeden Tag neu zu beginnen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, comienza el d\xeda con un coraz\xf3n sencillo y puro; hasta la flor m\xe1s peque\xf1a sabe abrirse al sol de nuevo cada ma\xf1ana. La margarita susurra que la inocencia no es una debilidad, sino el valor de empezar de nuevo cada d\xeda.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, commence la journ\xe9e avec un c\u0153ur simple et pur ; m\xeame la plus petite fleur sait s'ouvrir au soleil \xe0 nouveau chaque matin. La p\xe2querette murmure que l'innocence n'est pas une faiblesse mais le courage de recommencer chaque jour.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u7d20\u6734\u3067\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306a\u5fc3\u3067\u4e00\u65e5\u3092\u59cb\u3081\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6700\u3082\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u82b1\u3067\u3055\u3048\u3001\u6bce\u671d\u3042\u3089\u305f\u306b\u592a\u967d\u3078\u5411\u304b\u3063\u3066\u958b\u304f\u3059\u3079\u3092\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30d2\u30ca\u30ae\u30af\u306f\u3001\u7121\u57a2\u306f\u5f31\u3055\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u6bce\u65e5\u3084\u308a\u76f4\u3059\u52c7\u6c17\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, comece o dia com um cora\xe7\xe3o simples e puro; at\xe9 a menor flor sabe abrir-se ao sol de novo a cada manh\xe3. A margarida sussurra que a inoc\xeancia n\xe3o \xe9 uma fraqueza, mas a coragem de recome\xe7ar todos os dias.",howToUse:"Bir avu\xe7 koyung\xf6z\xfcn\xfc toplay\u0131p k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir buket yaparak ya da zincir \xf6rerek masumiyet ve yeni ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7 niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. \xc7i\xe7e\u011fi bir vazoda tutmak da safl\u0131k ve umut niyetini onurland\u0131ran sade bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may gather a handful of daisies and make a small bouquet or weave a chain to accompany an intention of innocence and new beginnings. Keeping the flower in a vase is also a simple gesture honoring an intention of purity and hope.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst eine Handvoll G\xe4nsebl\xfcmchen pfl\xfccken und einen kleinen Strau\xdf binden oder eine Kette flechten, um eine Absicht von Unschuld und Neuanfang zu begleiten. Die Blume in einer Vase aufzubewahren ist ebenfalls eine schlichte Geste, die eine Absicht von Reinheit und Hoffnung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes recoger un pu\xf1ado de margaritas y hacer un peque\xf1o ramo o tejer una cadena para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de inocencia y nuevos comienzos. Guardar la flor en un jarr\xf3n es tambi\xe9n un gesto sencillo que honra una intenci\xf3n de pureza y esperanza.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux cueillir une poign\xe9e de p\xe2querettes et faire un petit bouquet ou tresser une cha\xeene pour accompagner une intention d'innocence et de renouveau. Garder la fleur dans un vase est aussi un geste simple qui honore une intention de puret\xe9 et d'espoir.",howToUseJa:"\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u306e\u30d2\u30ca\u30ae\u30af\u3092\u6458\u3093\u3067\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u82b1\u675f\u306b\u3057\u305f\u308a\u3001\u82b1\u306e\u9396\u3092\u7de8\u3093\u3060\u308a\u3057\u3066\u3001\u7121\u57a2\u3068\u65b0\u305f\u306a\u59cb\u307e\u308a\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u306b\u633f\u3057\u3066\u304a\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u3055\u3068\u5e0c\u671b\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3064\u3064\u307e\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode colher um punhado de margaridas e fazer um pequeno buqu\xea ou tecer uma corrente para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de inoc\xeancia e novos come\xe7os. Manter a flor em um vaso \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto simples que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de pureza e esperan\xe7a.",affirmation:"Sade ve saf bir kalple her g\xfcn yeniden ba\u015fl\u0131yorum, masumiyetim benim cesaretim.",affirmationEn:"With a simple, pure heart I begin again each day, and my innocence is my courage.",affirmationDe:"Mit einem schlichten, reinen Herzen beginne ich jeden Tag neu, und meine Unschuld ist mein Mut.",affirmationEs:"Con un coraz\xf3n sencillo y puro empiezo de nuevo cada d\xeda, y mi inocencia es mi valor.",affirmationFr:"Avec un c\u0153ur simple et pur je recommence chaque jour, et mon innocence est mon courage.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u7d20\u6734\u3067\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306a\u5fc3\u3067\u6bce\u65e5\u3084\u308a\u76f4\u3057\u3001\u7121\u57a2\u3053\u305d\u304c\u79c1\u306e\u52c7\u6c17\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Com um cora\xe7\xe3o simples e puro recome\xe7o a cada dia, e a minha inoc\xeancia \xe9 a minha coragem.",myth:"Bahar\u0131n m\xfcjdecisi olarak bilinen koyung\xf6z\xfc, g\xfcnd\xfcz \xe7i\xe7eklerini a\xe7\u0131p gece kapat\u0131r; e\u011fer dokuz koyung\xf6z\xfc bir ad\u0131mla ezilebiliyorsa ilkbahar\u0131n geldi\u011fi s\xf6ylenir. Roma mitolojisinde nympha Belides, meyve bah\xe7elerinin tanr\u0131s\u0131 Vertumnus'un a\u015fk\u0131ndan ka\xe7mak i\xe7in kendini koyung\xf6z\xfc \xe7i\xe7e\u011fine d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrm\xfc\u015ft\xfcr; bu y\xfczden \xe7i\xe7ek bekaretin ve masumiyetin simgesi say\u0131l\u0131r. Koyung\xf6z\xfc, Ven\xfcs, Aphrodite ve kuzeyin a\u015fk ile bahar nymphas\u0131 Freyja gibi a\u015fk ve g\xfczellik fig\xfcrleriyle de ili\u015fkilendirilmi\u015ftir.",mythEn:"Known as the herald of spring, the daisy opens its flowers by day and closes them at night; it is said that when nine daisies can be trodden under one step, spring has come. In Roman myth, the nymph Belides, fleeing the love of Vertumnus, god of orchards, turned herself into a daisy; for this reason the flower is held to be a symbol of virginity and innocence. The daisy has also been associated with figures of love and beauty such as Venus, Aphrodite, and Freyja, the love and spring nymph of the north.",mythDe:"Als Vorbotin des Fr\xfchlings \xf6ffnet das G\xe4nsebl\xfcmchen seine Bl\xfcten am Tag und schlie\xdft sie in der Nacht; man sagt, wenn neun G\xe4nsebl\xfcmchen mit einem Schritt niedergetreten werden k\xf6nnen, sei der Fr\xfchling gekommen. In der r\xf6mischen Mythologie verwandelte sich die Nymphe Belides auf der Flucht vor der Liebe des Vertumnus, des Gottes der Obstg\xe4rten, in ein G\xe4nsebl\xfcmchen; deshalb gilt die Blume als Sinnbild der Jungfr\xe4ulichkeit und Unschuld. Das G\xe4nsebl\xfcmchen wurde auch mit Gestalten der Liebe und Sch\xf6nheit wie Venus, Aphrodite und Freyja, der Liebes- und Fr\xfchlingsnymphe des Nordens, verbunden.",mythEs:"Conocida como heraldo de la primavera, la margarita abre sus flores de d\xeda y las cierra de noche; se dice que cuando nueve margaritas pueden pisarse de un paso, ha llegado la primavera. En la mitolog\xeda romana, la ninfa Belides, huyendo del amor de Vertumno, dios de los huertos, se convirti\xf3 en margarita; por ello la flor se tiene por s\xedmbolo de virginidad e inocencia. La margarita tambi\xe9n se ha asociado con figuras de amor y belleza como Venus, Afrodita y Freyja, la ninfa del amor y la primavera del norte.",mythFr:"Connue comme l'h\xe9raut du printemps, la p\xe2querette ouvre ses fleurs le jour et les ferme la nuit ; on dit que lorsque neuf p\xe2querettes peuvent \xeatre foul\xe9es d'un seul pas, le printemps est venu. Dans la mythologie romaine, la nymphe B\xe9lides, fuyant l'amour de Vertumne, dieu des vergers, se changea en p\xe2querette ; c'est pourquoi la fleur est tenue pour un symbole de virginit\xe9 et d'innocence. La p\xe2querette a aussi \xe9t\xe9 associ\xe9e \xe0 des figures d'amour et de beaut\xe9 comme V\xe9nus, Aphrodite et Freyja, la nymphe de l'amour et du printemps du nord.",mythJa:"\u6625\u306e\u4f7f\u8005\u3068\u3057\u3066\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u308b\u30d2\u30ca\u30ae\u30af\u306f\u3001\u663c\u306b\u82b1\u3092\u958b\u304d\u3001\u591c\u306b\u9589\u3058\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30d2\u30ca\u30ae\u30af\u4e5d\u8f2a\u3092\u4e00\u6b69\u3067\u8e0f\u3081\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u306a\u308c\u3070\u3001\u6625\u304c\u6765\u305f\u3068\u3044\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ed\u30fc\u30de\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30cb\u30f3\u30d5\u306e\u30d9\u30ea\u30c7\u30b9\u304c\u679c\u6a39\u5712\u306e\u795e\u30a6\u30a7\u30eb\u30c8\u30a5\u30e0\u30cc\u30b9\u306e\u611b\u304b\u3089\u9003\u308c\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3001\u81ea\u3089\u3092\u30d2\u30ca\u30ae\u30af\u306b\u5909\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u305d\u306e\u305f\u3081\u3001\u3053\u306e\u82b1\u306f\u51e6\u5973\u6027\u3068\u7121\u57a2\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30d2\u30ca\u30ae\u30af\u306f\u307e\u305f\u3001\u30a6\u30a7\u30cc\u30b9\u3001\u30a2\u30d5\u30ed\u30c7\u30a3\u30fc\u30c6\u3001\u305d\u3057\u3066\u5317\u65b9\u306e\u611b\u3068\u6625\u306e\u30cb\u30f3\u30d5\u3001\u30d5\u30ec\u30a4\u30e4\u3068\u3044\u3063\u305f\u611b\u3068\u7f8e\u306e\u5b58\u5728\u3068\u3082\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u3051\u3089\u308c\u3066\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Conhecida como arauto da primavera, a margarida abre suas flores de dia e as fecha de noite; diz-se que quando nove margaridas podem ser pisadas num s\xf3 passo, chegou a primavera. Na mitologia romana, a ninfa B\xe9lides, fugindo do amor de Vertumno, deus dos pomares, transformou-se numa margarida; por isso a flor \xe9 tida como s\xedmbolo de virgindade e inoc\xeancia. A margarida tamb\xe9m foi associada a figuras de amor e beleza como V\xeanus, Afrodite e Freyja, a ninfa do amor e da primavera do norte.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Bellis_perennis_sl1.jpg/330px-Bellis_perennis_sl1.jpg"},{id:"plant-112",emoji:"\ud83c\udf31",color:"#6FA45C",name:"Ku\u015fkonmaz",nameEn:"Asparagus",nameDe:"Spargel",nameEs:"Esp\xe1rrago",nameFr:"Asperge",nameJa:"\u30a2\u30b9\u30d1\u30e9\u30ac\u30b9",namePt:"Aspargo",origin:"Antik Yunan",originEn:"Ancient Greece",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland",originEs:"Antigua Grecia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["s\u0131\u011f\u0131nak","s\xfcreklilik","koruma","minnet"],propertiesEn:["refuge","continuity","protection","gratitude"],propertiesDe:["Zuflucht","Best\xe4ndigkeit","Schutz","Dankbarkeit"],propertiesEs:["refugio","continuidad","protecci\xf3n","gratitud"],propertiesFr:["refuge","continuit\xe9","protection","gratitude"],propertiesJa:["\u907f\u96e3\u6240","\u7d99\u7d9a","\u5b88\u8b77","\u611f\u8b1d"],propertiesPt:["ref\xfagio","continuidade","prote\xe7\xe3o","gratid\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn seni en korkulu an\u0131nda saklayan o sessiz s\u0131\u011f\u0131na\u011fa minnet duy; bazen bir tarla, bir k\xf6\u015fe, b\xfct\xfcn bir soyun ba\u015flang\u0131c\u0131 olur. Ku\u015fkonmaz sana ka\xe7t\u0131\u011f\u0131n yerin bile bir g\xfcn kutsal bir k\xf6k olabilece\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, feel gratitude for the silent refuge that hid you in your most fearful moment; sometimes a field, a corner, becomes the beginning of a whole lineage. Asparagus whispers that even the place you fled to may one day become a sacred root.",dailyMessageDe:"Empfinde heute Dankbarkeit f\xfcr die stille Zuflucht, die dich in deinem \xe4ngstlichsten Augenblick verbarg; manchmal wird ein Feld, eine Ecke, zum Anfang eines ganzen Geschlechts. Der Spargel fl\xfcstert, dass selbst der Ort, zu dem du flohst, eines Tages zu einer heiligen Wurzel werden kann.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, siente gratitud por el refugio silencioso que te ocult\xf3 en tu momento m\xe1s temeroso; a veces un campo, un rinc\xf3n, se convierte en el comienzo de todo un linaje. El esp\xe1rrago susurra que hasta el lugar al que huiste puede un d\xeda volverse una ra\xedz sagrada.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, \xe9prouve de la gratitude pour le refuge silencieux qui t'a cach\xe9 dans ton instant le plus craintif ; parfois un champ, un coin, devient le commencement de toute une lign\xe9e. L'asperge murmure que m\xeame le lieu o\xf9 tu t'es enfui peut un jour devenir une racine sacr\xe9e.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u6700\u3082\u6050\u308c\u305f\u3068\u304d\u306b\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u96a0\u3057\u3066\u304f\u308c\u305f\u9759\u304b\u306a\u907f\u96e3\u6240\u306b\u611f\u8b1d\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3068\u304d\u306b\u4e00\u679a\u306e\u7551\u3001\u3072\u3068\u3064\u306e\u7247\u9685\u304c\u3001\u3072\u3068\u3064\u306e\u8840\u7b4b\u306e\u59cb\u307e\u308a\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a2\u30b9\u30d1\u30e9\u30ac\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u304c\u9003\u3052\u8fbc\u3093\u3060\u5834\u6240\u3055\u3048\u3001\u3044\u3064\u304b\u8056\u306a\u308b\u6839\u306b\u306a\u308a\u3046\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, sinta gratid\xe3o pelo ref\xfagio silencioso que escondeu voc\xea no seu momento mais temeroso; \xe0s vezes um campo, um canto, torna-se o come\xe7o de toda uma linhagem. O aspargo sussurra que at\xe9 o lugar para onde voc\xea fugiu pode um dia tornar-se uma raiz sagrada.",howToUse:"Taze ku\u015fkonmaz filizlerini hafif\xe7e pi\u015firip besleyici bir yemek olarak tadabilirsin. Bir demet ku\u015fkonmaz\u0131 bir k\xe2seye koyup masanda tutmak da s\u0131\u011f\u0131nak ve minnet niyetini onurland\u0131ran sade bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may lightly cook fresh asparagus spears and enjoy them as a nourishing dish. Placing a bundle of asparagus in a bowl on your table is also a simple gesture honoring an intention of refuge and gratitude.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst frische Spargelstangen leicht garen und als n\xe4hrendes Gericht genie\xdfen. Ein Bund Spargel in einer Schale auf deinem Tisch ist ebenfalls eine schlichte Geste, die eine Absicht von Zuflucht und Dankbarkeit ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes cocer ligeramente esp\xe1rragos frescos y disfrutarlos como un plato nutritivo. Colocar un manojo de esp\xe1rragos en un cuenco sobre la mesa es tambi\xe9n un gesto sencillo que honra una intenci\xf3n de refugio y gratitud.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux cuire l\xe9g\xe8rement des asperges fra\xeeches et les savourer comme un plat nourrissant. Placer une botte d'asperges dans un bol sur ta table est aussi un geste simple qui honore une intention de refuge et de gratitude.",howToUseJa:"\u65b0\u9bae\u306a\u30a2\u30b9\u30d1\u30e9\u30ac\u30b9\u306e\u82bd\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u8abf\u7406\u3057\u3066\u3001\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u6599\u7406\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a2\u30b9\u30d1\u30e9\u30ac\u30b9\u306e\u675f\u3092\u5668\u306b\u5165\u308c\u3066\u673a\u306b\u7f6e\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u907f\u96e3\u6240\u3068\u611f\u8b1d\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3064\u3064\u307e\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode cozinhar levemente os brotos de aspargo fresco e apreci\xe1-los como um prato nutritivo. Colocar um molho de aspargos em uma tigela sobre a mesa \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto simples que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de ref\xfagio e gratid\xe3o.",affirmation:"Beni saklayan s\u0131\u011f\u0131na\u011fa minnet duyuyorum, ka\xe7t\u0131\u011f\u0131m yer kutsal bir k\xf6ke d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcyor.",affirmationEn:"I feel gratitude for the refuge that hid me, and the place I fled to becomes a sacred root.",affirmationDe:"Ich empfinde Dankbarkeit f\xfcr die Zuflucht, die mich verbarg, und der Ort, zu dem ich floh, wird zu einer heiligen Wurzel.",affirmationEs:"Siento gratitud por el refugio que me ocult\xf3, y el lugar al que hu\xed se vuelve una ra\xedz sagrada.",affirmationFr:"J'\xe9prouve de la gratitude pour le refuge qui m'a cach\xe9, et le lieu o\xf9 je me suis enfui devient une racine sacr\xe9e.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u3092\u96a0\u3057\u305f\u907f\u96e3\u6240\u306b\u611f\u8b1d\u3057\u3001\u9003\u3052\u8fbc\u3093\u3060\u5834\u6240\u306f\u8056\u306a\u308b\u6839\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Sinto gratid\xe3o pelo ref\xfagio que me escondeu, e o lugar para onde fugi torna-se uma raiz sagrada.",myth:"Yunan mitolojisinde Attike kahraman\u0131 Theseus, insanlar\u0131n yolunu kesen Poseidon'un o\u011flu dev Sinis'i yenip \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc. Babas\u0131n\u0131n \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcl\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfc g\xf6ren Sinis'in k\u0131z\u0131 Perigoune korkup ka\xe7t\u0131 ve bir ku\u015fkonmaz tarlas\u0131na sakland\u0131. Kader bu ya, \xe7ok sonra Perigoune ile Theseus bir araya geldi ve Perigoune ona Melanippos adl\u0131 bir evlat verdi. Melanippos'un o\u011flu \u0130oksos ve ondan gelen soy, atalar\u0131n\u0131n bu tarlada saklan\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131 bildikleri i\xe7in ku\u015fkonmaza \xf6zel bir sayg\u0131 geli\u015ftirdi; varl\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131 ve soylar\u0131n\u0131n devam\u0131n\u0131 bu bitkiye bor\xe7lu olduklar\u0131n\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcrlerdi.",mythEn:"In Greek myth, Theseus, the hero of Attica, defeated and killed the giant Sinis, son of Poseidon, who waylaid travelers. Seeing her father slain, Sinis's daughter Perigoune fled in fear and hid in a field of asparagus. As fate would have it, much later Perigoune and Theseus came together, and Perigoune bore him a son named Melanippos. Melanippos's son Ioxos and the lineage descended from him, knowing how their ancestor had hidden in that field, developed a special reverence for asparagus; they believed they owed their existence and the continuance of their line to this plant.",mythDe:"In der griechischen Mythologie besiegte und t\xf6tete Theseus, der Held von Attika, den Riesen Sinis, den Sohn Poseidons, der Reisende \xfcberfiel. Als sie ihren Vater erschlagen sah, floh Sinis' Tochter Perigoune voller Furcht und verbarg sich in einem Spargelfeld. Wie es das Schicksal wollte, kamen Perigoune und Theseus viel sp\xe4ter zusammen, und Perigoune gebar ihm einen Sohn namens Melanippos. Melanippos' Sohn Ioxos und das von ihm abstammende Geschlecht entwickelten, da sie wussten, wie ihr Ahn sich in jenem Feld verborgen hatte, eine besondere Ehrfurcht vor dem Spargel; sie glaubten, ihr Dasein und der Fortbestand ihres Geschlechts seien dieser Pflanze zu verdanken.",mythEs:"En la mitolog\xeda griega, Teseo, el h\xe9roe del \xc1tica, venci\xf3 y mat\xf3 al gigante Sinis, hijo de Poseid\xf3n, que asaltaba a los viajeros. Al ver muerto a su padre, la hija de Sinis, Perigune, huy\xf3 atemorizada y se ocult\xf3 en un campo de esp\xe1rragos. Quiso el destino que, mucho despu\xe9s, Perigune y Teseo se unieran, y Perigune le dio un hijo llamado Melanipo. El hijo de Melanipo, Ioxo, y el linaje que de \xe9l descendi\xf3, sabiendo c\xf3mo su antepasada se hab\xeda ocultado en aquel campo, desarrollaron un respeto especial por el esp\xe1rrago; cre\xedan deber su existencia y la continuaci\xf3n de su estirpe a esta planta.",mythFr:"Dans la mythologie grecque, Th\xe9s\xe9e, le h\xe9ros de l'Attique, vainquit et tua le g\xe9ant Sinis, fils de Pos\xe9idon, qui d\xe9troussait les voyageurs. Voyant son p\xe8re tu\xe9, la fille de Sinis, P\xe9rigoun\xe9, s'enfuit de peur et se cacha dans un champ d'asperges. Le destin voulut que, bien plus tard, P\xe9rigoun\xe9 et Th\xe9s\xe9e s'unissent, et P\xe9rigoun\xe9 lui donna un fils nomm\xe9 M\xe9lanippos. Le fils de M\xe9lanippos, Ioxos, et la lign\xe9e qui en descendit, sachant comment leur a\xefeule s'\xe9tait cach\xe9e dans ce champ, d\xe9velopp\xe8rent un respect particulier pour l'asperge ; ils croyaient devoir leur existence et la continuation de leur lign\xe9e \xe0 cette plante.",mythJa:"\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30a2\u30c3\u30c6\u30a3\u30ab\u306e\u82f1\u96c4\u30c6\u30bb\u30a6\u30b9\u304c\u3001\u65c5\u4eba\u3092\u8972\u3046\u30dd\u30bb\u30a4\u30c9\u30f3\u306e\u5b50\u3001\u5de8\u4eba\u30b7\u30cb\u30b9\u3092\u8a0e\u3061\u5012\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u7236\u304c\u6bba\u3055\u308c\u308b\u306e\u3092\u898b\u305f\u30b7\u30cb\u30b9\u306e\u5a18\u30da\u30ea\u30b4\u30a6\u30cd\u306f\u3001\u6050\u308c\u3066\u9003\u3052\u3001\u30a2\u30b9\u30d1\u30e9\u30ac\u30b9\u306e\u7551\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u904b\u547d\u306e\u3044\u305f\u305a\u3089\u304b\u3001\u305a\u3063\u3068\u306e\u3061\u306b\u30da\u30ea\u30b4\u30a6\u30cd\u3068\u30c6\u30bb\u30a6\u30b9\u306f\u7d50\u3070\u308c\u3001\u30da\u30ea\u30b4\u30a6\u30cd\u306f\u30e1\u30e9\u30cb\u30c3\u30dd\u30b9\u3068\u3044\u3046\u5b50\u3092\u7523\u307f\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30e1\u30e9\u30cb\u30c3\u30dd\u30b9\u306e\u5b50\u30a4\u30aa\u30af\u30bd\u30b9\u3068\u305d\u306e\u8840\u3092\u5f15\u304f\u4e00\u65cf\u306f\u3001\u5148\u7956\u304c\u305d\u306e\u7551\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u305f\u3053\u3068\u3092\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u3044\u305f\u305f\u3081\u3001\u30a2\u30b9\u30d1\u30e9\u30ac\u30b9\u306b\u7279\u5225\u306a\u656c\u610f\u3092\u62b1\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u81ea\u5206\u305f\u3061\u306e\u5b58\u5728\u3068\u8840\u7b4b\u306e\u5b58\u7d9a\u3092\u3053\u306e\u690d\u7269\u306b\u8ca0\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u8003\u3048\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na mitologia grega, Teseu, o her\xf3i da \xc1tica, venceu e matou o gigante Sinis, filho de Poseidon, que assaltava os viajantes. Ao ver o pai morto, a filha de Sinis, Perigune, fugiu com medo e escondeu-se num campo de aspargos. Quis o destino que, muito depois, Perigune e Teseu se unissem, e Perigune lhe deu um filho chamado Melanipo. O filho de Melanipo, Ioxo, e a linhagem dele descendente, sabendo como a sua antepassada se escondera naquele campo, desenvolveram um respeito especial pelo aspargo; acreditavam dever a sua exist\xeancia e a continua\xe7\xe3o da sua linhagem a esta planta."},{id:"plant-113",emoji:"\ud83c\udf38",color:"#7B4FA3",name:"Menek\u015fe",nameEn:"Violet",nameDe:"Veilchen",nameEs:"Violeta",nameFr:"Violette",nameJa:"\u30b9\u30df\u30ec",namePt:"Violeta",origin:"Antik Yunan (Anadolu)",originEn:"Ancient Greece (Anatolia)",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland (Anatolien)",originEs:"Antigua Grecia (Anatolia)",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique (Anatolie)",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\uff08\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\uff09",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga (Anat\xf3lia)",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfcl\xfck","anma","incelik","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","sadakat"],propertiesEn:["humility","remembrance","tenderness","transformation","devotion"],propertiesDe:["Demut","Erinnerung","Zartheit","Verwandlung","Treue"],propertiesEs:["humildad","memoria","ternura","transformaci\xf3n","devoci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["humilit\xe9","souvenir","tendresse","transformation","d\xe9votion"],propertiesJa:["\u8b19\u865a","\u8ffd\u61b6","\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055","\u5909\u5bb9","\u8aa0\u5b9f"],propertiesPt:["humildade","mem\xf3ria","ternura","transforma\xe7\xe3o","devo\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xf6steri\u015fsiz bir incelikle var ol; en derin sevgi \xe7o\u011fu zaman gizlice, al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfc bir k\xf6\u015fede a\xe7ar. Menek\u015fe sana b\xfcy\xfck bir ac\u0131n\u0131n ard\u0131ndan bile, topra\u011f\u0131n nazik bir g\xfczelli\u011fe can verebilece\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, be present with an unshowy tenderness; the deepest love often blooms quietly, in a humble corner. The violet whispers that even after a great grief, the earth can give birth to a gentle beauty.",dailyMessageDe:"Sei heute mit einer schlichten Zartheit gegenw\xe4rtig; die tiefste Liebe bl\xfcht oft still, in einer dem\xfctigen Ecke. Das Veilchen fl\xfcstert, dass die Erde selbst nach gro\xdfem Leid eine sanfte Sch\xf6nheit hervorbringen kann.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, est\xe1 presente con una ternura sin alardes; el amor m\xe1s hondo suele florecer en silencio, en un rinc\xf3n humilde. La violeta susurra que, aun tras un gran dolor, la tierra puede dar vida a una belleza tierna.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, sois pr\xe9sent avec une tendresse sans \xe9clat ; l'amour le plus profond fleurit souvent en silence, dans un coin humble. La violette murmure que, m\xeame apr\xe8s un grand chagrin, la terre peut donner naissance \xe0 une douce beaut\xe9.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u98fe\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3042\u3063\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002\u6700\u3082\u6df1\u3044\u611b\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u614e\u307e\u3057\u3044\u7247\u9685\u3067\u9759\u304b\u306b\u54b2\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b9\u30df\u30ec\u306f\u3001\u5927\u304d\u306a\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u306e\u3042\u3068\u3067\u3055\u3048\u3001\u5927\u5730\u304c\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u7f8e\u3092\u751f\u307f\u51fa\u305b\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, esteja presente com uma ternura sem alarde; o amor mais profundo muitas vezes floresce em sil\xeancio, num canto humilde. A violeta sussurra que, mesmo depois de um grande pesar, a terra pode dar \xe0 luz uma beleza terna.",howToUse:"Menek\u015fenin mor \xe7i\xe7eklerini bir vazoda seyrederek anma ve incelik niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bah\xe7ende ya da bir saks\u0131da yeti\u015ftirmek de al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfcl\xfck ve sadakat niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may contemplate the violet's purple flowers in a vase to accompany an intention of remembrance and tenderness. Growing it in your garden or a pot is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of humility and devotion.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die violetten Bl\xfcten des Veilchens in einer Vase betrachten, um eine Absicht von Erinnerung und Zartheit zu begleiten. Es im Garten oder Topf zu ziehen ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Demut und Treue ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes contemplar las flores moradas de la violeta en un jarr\xf3n para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de memoria y ternura. Cultivarla en tu jard\xedn o en una maceta es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de humildad y devoci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux contempler les fleurs violettes de la violette dans un vase pour accompagner une intention de souvenir et de tendresse. La cultiver dans ton jardin ou en pot est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention d'humilit\xe9 et de d\xe9votion.",howToUseJa:"\u30b9\u30df\u30ec\u306e\u7d2b\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u3067\u773a\u3081\u3001\u8ffd\u61b6\u3068\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5ead\u3084\u9262\u3067\u80b2\u3066\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u8b19\u865a\u3068\u8aa0\u5b9f\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode contemplar as flores roxas da violeta em um vaso para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de mem\xf3ria e ternura. Cultiv\xe1-la no seu jardim ou em um vaso \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de humildade e devo\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"G\xf6steri\u015fsiz bir incelikle var oluyorum, ac\u0131n\u0131n ard\u0131ndan nazik bir g\xfczellik a\xe7\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I am present with an unshowy tenderness, and after grief a gentle beauty blooms.",affirmationDe:"Ich bin mit einer schlichten Zartheit gegenw\xe4rtig, und nach dem Leid erbl\xfcht eine sanfte Sch\xf6nheit.",affirmationEs:"Estoy presente con una ternura sin alardes, y tras el dolor florece una belleza tierna.",affirmationFr:"Je suis pr\xe9sent avec une tendresse sans \xe9clat, et apr\xe8s le chagrin une douce beaut\xe9 s'\xe9panouit.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u98fe\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3042\u308a\u3001\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306b\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u7f8e\u304c\u54b2\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Estou presente com uma ternura sem alarde, e depois do pesar floresce uma beleza terna.",myth:"Yunan mitolojisinde ad\u0131 'yak\u0131\u015f\u0131kl\u0131' anlam\u0131na gelen gen\xe7 Attis, hermafrodit Agdistis ile tanr\u0131\xe7a Kybele aras\u0131nda payla\u015f\u0131lamad\u0131. Agdistis Attis'i delirtti; \xe7\u0131lg\u0131na d\xf6nen Attis bir \xe7am alt\u0131nda erkeklik organ\u0131n\u0131 kesip kan kayb\u0131ndan \xf6ld\xfc ve kan\u0131n\u0131n sulad\u0131\u011f\u0131 topraktan menek\u015feler a\xe7t\u0131. Attis'le evlendirilecek olan Midas'\u0131n k\u0131z\u0131 da onun \xf6l\xfcm\xfcne dayanamay\u0131p can\u0131na k\u0131yd\u0131; onun kan\u0131n\u0131n akt\u0131\u011f\u0131 yerlerden de menek\u015feler \xe7\u0131kt\u0131. Roma'da \xf6l\xfclerin ruhlar\u0131 i\xe7in d\xfczenlenen Violaria bayram\u0131nda mezarlar\u0131n \xfczerine menek\u015feler b\u0131rak\u0131larak ruhlar\u0131n ho\u015f tutulmas\u0131na \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131.",mythEn:"In Greek myth, the young Attis, whose name means 'handsome,' could not be shared between the hermaphrodite Agdistis and the goddess Cybele. Agdistis drove Attis mad; in his frenzy Attis cut off his manhood beneath a pine and died of loss of blood, and from the earth his blood had watered violets bloomed. The daughter of Midas, who was to be wed to Attis, could not bear his death and took her own life; from the places her blood flowed, violets sprang as well. In Rome, at the festival of Violaria held for the souls of the dead, violets were laid on graves in an effort to please the spirits.",mythDe:"In der griechischen Mythologie konnte der junge Attis, dessen Name 'sch\xf6n' bedeutet, zwischen dem Hermaphroditen Agdistis und der G\xf6ttin Kybele nicht geteilt werden. Agdistis machte Attis wahnsinnig; in seiner Raserei schnitt Attis unter einer Kiefer seine M\xe4nnlichkeit ab und starb am Blutverlust, und aus der Erde, die sein Blut getr\xe4nkt hatte, erbl\xfchten Veilchen. Die Tochter des Midas, die mit Attis verm\xe4hlt werden sollte, ertrug seinen Tod nicht und nahm sich das Leben; an den Stellen, wo ihr Blut floss, sprossen ebenfalls Veilchen. In Rom legte man beim Fest Violaria, das f\xfcr die Seelen der Toten abgehalten wurde, Veilchen auf die Gr\xe4ber, um die Geister zu bes\xe4nftigen.",mythEs:"En la mitolog\xeda griega, el joven Atis, cuyo nombre significa 'apuesto', no pudo ser compartido entre el hermafrodita Agdistis y la diosa Cibeles. Agdistis enloqueci\xf3 a Atis; en su frenes\xed Atis se cort\xf3 la virilidad bajo un pino y muri\xf3 por p\xe9rdida de sangre, y de la tierra que su sangre hab\xeda regado brotaron violetas. La hija de Midas, que iba a casarse con Atis, no soport\xf3 su muerte y se quit\xf3 la vida; de los lugares por donde corri\xf3 su sangre brotaron tambi\xe9n violetas. En Roma, en la fiesta de las Violaria celebrada por las almas de los muertos, se dejaban violetas sobre las tumbas para complacer a los esp\xedritus.",mythFr:"Dans la mythologie grecque, le jeune Attis, dont le nom signifie 'beau', ne put \xeatre partag\xe9 entre l'hermaphrodite Agdistis et la d\xe9esse Cyb\xe8le. Agdistis rendit Attis fou ; dans sa fr\xe9n\xe9sie, Attis se trancha la virilit\xe9 sous un pin et mourut de la perte de son sang, et de la terre que son sang avait arros\xe9e s'\xe9panouirent des violettes. La fille de Midas, qui devait \xe9pouser Attis, ne supporta pas sa mort et se donna la mort ; aux endroits o\xf9 coula son sang jaillirent aussi des violettes. \xc0 Rome, lors de la f\xeate des Violaria c\xe9l\xe9br\xe9e pour les \xe2mes des morts, on d\xe9posait des violettes sur les tombes pour apaiser les esprits.",mythJa:"\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u540d\u304c\u300e\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u300f\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3059\u308b\u82e5\u8005\u30a2\u30c3\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u4e21\u6027\u5177\u6709\u306e\u30a2\u30b0\u30c7\u30a3\u30b9\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u3068\u5973\u795e\u30ad\u30e5\u30d9\u30ec\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u3067\u5206\u3051\u5408\u3046\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30a2\u30b0\u30c7\u30a3\u30b9\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u306f\u30a2\u30c3\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u3092\u72c2\u6c17\u306b\u9665\u308c\u3001\u932f\u4e71\u3057\u305f\u30a2\u30c3\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u306f\u677e\u306e\u4e0b\u3067\u7537\u6839\u3092\u5207\u308a\u843d\u3068\u3057\u3001\u5931\u8840\u3057\u3066\u6b7b\u306b\u3001\u305d\u306e\u8840\u304c\u6f64\u3057\u305f\u5927\u5730\u304b\u3089\u30b9\u30df\u30ec\u304c\u54b2\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30a2\u30c3\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u3068\u7d50\u3070\u308c\u308b\u306f\u305a\u3060\u3063\u305f\u30df\u30c0\u30b9\u306e\u5a18\u3082\u3001\u5f7c\u306e\u6b7b\u306b\u8010\u3048\u3089\u308c\u305a\u81ea\u5bb3\u3057\u3001\u5f7c\u5973\u306e\u8840\u304c\u6d41\u308c\u305f\u5834\u6240\u304b\u3089\u3082\u30b9\u30df\u30ec\u304c\u751f\u307e\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30ed\u30fc\u30de\u3067\u306f\u3001\u6b7b\u8005\u306e\u9b42\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u50ac\u3055\u308c\u308b\u30a6\u30a3\u30aa\u30e9\u30ea\u30a2\u796d\u3067\u3001\u970a\u3092\u6170\u3081\u3088\u3046\u3068\u5893\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u30b9\u30df\u30ec\u304c\u4f9b\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Na mitologia grega, o jovem \xc1tis, cujo nome significa 'belo', n\xe3o p\xf4de ser partilhado entre o hermafrodita Agd\xedstis e a deusa Cibele. Agd\xedstis enlouqueceu \xc1tis; em seu frenesi, \xc1tis cortou a pr\xf3pria virilidade sob um pinheiro e morreu por perda de sangue, e da terra que o seu sangue regara brotaram violetas. A filha de Midas, que se casaria com \xc1tis, n\xe3o suportou a morte dele e tirou a pr\xf3pria vida; dos lugares por onde correu o seu sangue brotaram tamb\xe9m violetas. Em Roma, na festa das Violaria celebrada pelas almas dos mortos, deixavam-se violetas sobre os t\xfamulos para agradar aos esp\xedritos.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Viola_reichenbachiana_LC0128.jpg/330px-Viola_reichenbachiana_LC0128.jpg"},{id:"plant-114",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#6B5B3E",name:"Me\u015fe",nameEn:"Oak",nameDe:"Eiche",nameEs:"Roble",nameFr:"Ch\xeane",nameJa:"\u30aa\u30fc\u30af",namePt:"Carvalho",origin:"Antik Yunan & Kelt Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Celtic Tradition",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & keltische Tradition",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y tradici\xf3n celta",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et tradition celtique",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30b1\u30eb\u30c8\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e tradi\xe7\xe3o celta",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["g\xfc\xe7","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k","kutsall\u0131k","koruma","bilgelik"],propertiesEn:["strength","endurance","sacredness","protection","wisdom"],propertiesDe:["St\xe4rke","Ausdauer","Heiligkeit","Schutz","Weisheit"],propertiesEs:["fuerza","resistencia","sacralidad","protecci\xf3n","sabidur\xeda"],propertiesFr:["force","endurance","sacralit\xe9","protection","sagesse"],propertiesJa:["\u529b","\u5fcd\u8010","\u8056\u6027","\u5b88\u8b77","\u53e1\u667a"],propertiesPt:["for\xe7a","resist\xeancia","sacralidade","prote\xe7\xe3o","sabedoria"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn f\u0131rt\u0131nalara me\u015fe gibi g\xf6\u011f\xfcs ger; ger\xe7ek g\xfc\xe7, e\u011filmeden ve tela\u015fa kap\u0131lmadan sab\u0131rla yerinde durabilmektir. Me\u015fe sana y\u0131llar s\xfcren sabr\u0131n, g\xf6lgesinde nesilleri bar\u0131nd\u0131ran ulu bir varl\u0131\u011fa d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, face the storms like an oak; true strength is to stand patiently in place, without bending or being seized by haste. The oak whispers that years of patience turn into a mighty being that shelters generations in its shade.",dailyMessageDe:"Stelle dich heute den St\xfcrmen wie eine Eiche; wahre St\xe4rke ist es, geduldig am Platz zu stehen, ohne sich zu beugen oder von Hast ergriffen zu werden. Die Eiche fl\xfcstert, dass jahrelange Geduld zu einem m\xe4chtigen Wesen wird, das Generationen in seinem Schatten birgt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, enfrenta las tormentas como un roble; la verdadera fuerza es permanecer con paciencia en tu sitio, sin doblarte ni dejarte llevar por la prisa. El roble susurra que a\xf1os de paciencia se convierten en un ser poderoso que cobija generaciones a su sombra.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, affronte les temp\xeates comme un ch\xeane ; la vraie force, c'est de tenir patiemment en place, sans ployer ni te laisser saisir par la h\xe2te. Le ch\xeane murmure que des ann\xe9es de patience deviennent un \xeatre puissant qui abrite des g\xe9n\xe9rations \xe0 son ombre.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u5d50\u306b\u7acb\u3061\u5411\u304b\u3044\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u771f\u306e\u5f37\u3055\u3068\u306f\u3001\u305f\u308f\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3082\u7126\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u306a\u304f\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u305d\u306e\u5834\u306b\u7acb\u3061\u3064\u3065\u3051\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306f\u3001\u9577\u5e74\u306e\u5fcd\u8010\u304c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u9670\u306b\u5e7e\u4e16\u4ee3\u3092\u3082\u5bbf\u3059\u96c4\u5927\u306a\u5b58\u5728\u3078\u3068\u5909\u308f\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, enfrente as tempestades como um carvalho; a verdadeira for\xe7a \xe9 permanecer com paci\xeancia no seu lugar, sem se curvar nem se deixar levar pela pressa. O carvalho sussurra que anos de paci\xeancia se tornam um ser poderoso que abriga gera\xe7\xf5es \xe0 sua sombra.",howToUse:"Bir me\u015fe a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6vdesine elini koyup g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc ve dinginli\u011fini hissederek dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k ve koruma niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bir me\u015fe palamudunu bir niyet sembol\xfc olarak yan\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131mak da kutsall\u0131k ve bilgelik niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may place your hand on an oak's trunk and feel its strength and stillness to accompany an intention of endurance and protection. Carrying an acorn as a symbol of intention is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of sacredness and wisdom.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst deine Hand auf den Stamm einer Eiche legen und ihre Kraft und Stille sp\xfcren, um eine Absicht von Ausdauer und Schutz zu begleiten. Eine Eichel als Symbol der Absicht bei dir zu tragen ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Heiligkeit und Weisheit ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes poner la mano sobre el tronco de un roble y sentir su fuerza y su quietud para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de resistencia y protecci\xf3n. Llevar una bellota como s\xedmbolo de intenci\xf3n es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de sacralidad y sabidur\xeda.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux poser la main sur le tronc d'un ch\xeane et sentir sa force et son calme pour accompagner une intention d'endurance et de protection. Porter un gland comme symbole d'intention est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de sacralit\xe9 et de sagesse.",howToUseJa:"\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306e\u5e79\u306b\u624b\u3092\u7f6e\u304d\u3001\u305d\u306e\u529b\u3068\u9759\u3051\u3055\u3092\u611f\u3058\u3066\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3069\u3093\u3050\u308a\u3092\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3057\u3066\u6301\u3061\u6b69\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u8056\u6027\u3068\u53e1\u667a\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode pousar a m\xe3o no tronco de um carvalho e sentir a sua for\xe7a e a sua quietude para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de resist\xeancia e prote\xe7\xe3o. Carregar uma bolota como s\xedmbolo de inten\xe7\xe3o \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de sacralidade e sabedoria.",affirmation:"F\u0131rt\u0131nalara me\u015fe gibi g\xf6\u011f\xfcs geriyorum, sabr\u0131m nesilleri bar\u0131nd\u0131ran bir g\xfcce d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcyor.",affirmationEn:"I face the storms like an oak, and my patience turns into a strength that shelters generations.",affirmationDe:"Ich stelle mich den St\xfcrmen wie eine Eiche, und meine Geduld wird zu einer St\xe4rke, die Generationen birgt.",affirmationEs:"Enfrento las tormentas como un roble, y mi paciencia se vuelve una fuerza que cobija generaciones.",affirmationFr:"J'affronte les temp\xeates comme un ch\xeane, et ma patience devient une force qui abrite des g\xe9n\xe9rations.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u5d50\u306b\u7acb\u3061\u5411\u304b\u3044\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u306f\u5e7e\u4e16\u4ee3\u3092\u3082\u5bbf\u3059\u529b\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Enfrento as tempestades como um carvalho, e a minha paci\xeancia se torna uma for\xe7a que abriga gera\xe7\xf5es.",myth:"Yunan mitolojisinde me\u015fe, ba\u015f tanr\u0131 Zeus'un kutsal a\u011fac\u0131d\u0131r; Arkadya'da kurakl\u0131k oldu\u011funda Zeus rahibi, kutsal bir me\u015fe dal\u0131n\u0131 kayna\u011fa dald\u0131rarak ya\u011fmuru \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131rd\u0131. Hamadryad ve Dryad denen a\u011fa\xe7 nymphalar\u0131 me\u015felerle birlikte do\u011far ve onlar\u0131n \xf6l\xfcm\xfcyle \xf6l\xfcrd\xfc; a\u011faca zarar verenleri cezaland\u0131rd\u0131klar\u0131, koruyanlara ise dilek bah\u015fettikleri anlat\u0131l\u0131r. Kelt rahipleri Druidler me\u015fe ormanlar\u0131nda ya\u015far, kutsal \xf6kseotunu alt\u0131n bir orakla me\u015fe g\xf6vdesinden toplarlard\u0131; 'Druid' ad\u0131 'me\u015feyi bilen' anlam\u0131na gelir. \u0130skandinav mitolojisinde ise me\u015fe, \u0131\u015f\u0131k ve masumiyet tanr\u0131s\u0131 Balder'in sembol\xfcd\xfcr.",mythEn:"In Greek myth, the oak is the sacred tree of Zeus, king of the gods; when drought struck Arcadia, the priest of Zeus would dip a sacred oak branch into a spring to summon rain. The tree nymphs called Hamadryads and Dryads were born together with oaks and died with their death; it is told that they punished those who harmed the trees and granted wishes to those who protected them. The Celtic priests, the Druids, lived in oak forests and gathered the sacred mistletoe from the oak trunk with a golden sickle; the name 'Druid' means 'one who knows the oak.' In Norse myth, the oak is the symbol of Balder, god of light and innocence.",mythDe:"In der griechischen Mythologie ist die Eiche der heilige Baum des Zeus, des K\xf6nigs der G\xf6tter; als D\xfcrre Arkadien heimsuchte, tauchte der Priester des Zeus einen heiligen Eichenzweig in eine Quelle, um Regen herbeizurufen. Die Baumnymphen, Hamadryaden und Dryaden genannt, wurden mit den Eichen geboren und starben mit deren Tod; es hei\xdft, sie bestraften jene, die den B\xe4umen schadeten, und gew\xe4hrten jenen, die sie sch\xfctzten, W\xfcnsche. Die keltischen Priester, die Druiden, lebten in Eichenw\xe4ldern und sammelten die heilige Mistel mit einer goldenen Sichel vom Eichenstamm; der Name 'Druide' bedeutet 'einer, der die Eiche kennt'. In der nordischen Mythologie ist die Eiche das Symbol Balders, des Gottes des Lichts und der Unschuld.",mythEs:"En la mitolog\xeda griega, el roble es el \xe1rbol sagrado de Zeus, rey de los dioses; cuando la sequ\xeda asolaba la Arcadia, el sacerdote de Zeus sumerg\xeda una rama de roble sagrada en un manantial para invocar la lluvia. Las ninfas de los \xe1rboles llamadas hamadr\xedades y dr\xedades nac\xedan con los robles y mor\xedan con su muerte; se cuenta que castigaban a quienes da\xf1aban los \xe1rboles y conced\xedan deseos a quienes los proteg\xedan. Los sacerdotes celtas, los druidas, viv\xedan en bosques de robles y recog\xedan el mu\xe9rdago sagrado del tronco del roble con una hoz de oro; el nombre 'druida' significa 'el que conoce el roble'. En la mitolog\xeda n\xf3rdica, el roble es el s\xedmbolo de Balder, dios de la luz y la inocencia.",mythFr:"Dans la mythologie grecque, le ch\xeane est l'arbre sacr\xe9 de Zeus, roi des dieux ; lorsque la s\xe9cheresse frappait l'Arcadie, le pr\xeatre de Zeus plongeait une branche de ch\xeane sacr\xe9e dans une source pour appeler la pluie. Les nymphes des arbres appel\xe9es hamadryades et dryades naissaient avec les ch\xeanes et mouraient avec leur mort ; on raconte qu'elles punissaient ceux qui nuisaient aux arbres et accordaient des v\u0153ux \xe0 ceux qui les prot\xe9geaient. Les pr\xeatres celtes, les druides, vivaient dans les for\xeats de ch\xeanes et r\xe9coltaient le gui sacr\xe9 sur le tronc du ch\xeane avec une faucille d'or ; le nom 'druide' signifie 'celui qui conna\xeet le ch\xeane'. Dans la mythologie nordique, le ch\xeane est le symbole de Balder, dieu de la lumi\xe8re et de l'innocence.",mythJa:"\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306f\u795e\u3005\u306e\u738b\u30bc\u30a6\u30b9\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u6728\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30a2\u30eb\u30ab\u30c7\u30a3\u30a2\u306b\u5e72\u3070\u3064\u304c\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u3068\u3001\u30bc\u30a6\u30b9\u306e\u796d\u53f8\u306f\u8056\u306a\u308b\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306e\u679d\u3092\u6cc9\u306b\u6d78\u3057\u3066\u96e8\u3092\u547c\u3073\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30cf\u30de\u30c9\u30ea\u30e5\u30a2\u30b9\u3084\u30c9\u30ea\u30e5\u30a2\u30b9\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u308b\u6728\u306e\u30cb\u30f3\u30d5\u306f\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u751f\u307e\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6b7b\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u6b7b\u306b\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u6728\u3092\u50b7\u3064\u3051\u308b\u8005\u3092\u7f70\u3057\u3001\u5b88\u308b\u8005\u306b\u306f\u9858\u3044\u3092\u6388\u3051\u305f\u3068\u8a9e\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b1\u30eb\u30c8\u306e\u796d\u53f8\u30c9\u30eb\u30a4\u30c9\u306f\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306e\u68ee\u306b\u4f4f\u307f\u3001\u8056\u306a\u308b\u30e4\u30c9\u30ea\u30ae\u3092\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u938c\u3067\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306e\u5e79\u304b\u3089\u63a1\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u300e\u30c9\u30eb\u30a4\u30c9\u300f\u306e\u540d\u306f\u300e\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u3092\u77e5\u308b\u8005\u300f\u3092\u610f\u5473\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5317\u6b27\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306f\u5149\u3068\u7121\u57a2\u306e\u795e\u30d0\u30eb\u30c9\u30eb\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na mitologia grega, o carvalho \xe9 a \xe1rvore sagrada de Zeus, rei dos deuses; quando a seca assolava a Arc\xe1dia, o sacerdote de Zeus mergulhava um ramo de carvalho sagrado numa fonte para invocar a chuva. As ninfas das \xe1rvores chamadas hamadr\xedades e dr\xedades nasciam com os carvalhos e morriam com a morte deles; conta-se que castigavam os que prejudicavam as \xe1rvores e concediam desejos aos que as protegiam. Os sacerdotes celtas, os druidas, viviam em florestas de carvalhos e colhiam o visco sagrado do tronco do carvalho com uma foice de ouro; o nome 'druida' significa 'aquele que conhece o carvalho'. Na mitologia n\xf3rdica, o carvalho \xe9 o s\xedmbolo de Balder, deus da luz e da inoc\xeancia.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Quercus_robur.jpg/330px-Quercus_robur.jpg"},{id:"plant-115",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3d",color:"#E3B23C",name:"M\u0131s\u0131r",nameEn:"Corn",nameDe:"Mais",nameEs:"Ma\xedz",nameFr:"Ma\xefs",nameJa:"\u30c8\u30a6\u30e2\u30ed\u30b3\u30b7",namePt:"Milho",origin:"K\u0131z\u0131lderili & Aztek Mitolojisi",originEn:"Native American & Aztec Mythology",originDe:"Indianische & aztekische Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda amerindia y azteca",originFr:"Mythologie am\xe9rindienne et azt\xe8que",originJa:"\u30cd\u30a4\u30c6\u30a3\u30d6\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u30f3\u30fb\u30a2\u30b9\u30c6\u30ab\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia amer\xedndia e asteca",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"Solar Pleksus \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u592a\u967d\u795e\u7d4c\u53e2\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["bereket","fedak\xe2rl\u0131k","besin","s\xfcreklilik","\u015f\xfck\xfcr"],propertiesEn:["abundance","sacrifice","nourishment","continuity","gratitude"],propertiesDe:["F\xfclle","Opfer","Nahrung","Best\xe4ndigkeit","Dankbarkeit"],propertiesEs:["abundancia","sacrificio","alimento","continuidad","gratitud"],propertiesFr:["abondance","sacrifice","nourriture","continuit\xe9","gratitude"],propertiesJa:["\u8c4a\u7a63","\u6367\u3052\u3082\u306e","\u7ce7","\u7d99\u7d9a","\u611f\u8b1d"],propertiesPt:["abund\xe2ncia","sacrif\xedcio","alimento","continuidade","gratid\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn sana verilen her nimetin ard\u0131nda bir emek, bir fedak\xe2rl\u0131k oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rla; bolluk \xe7o\u011fu zaman birinin sevgiyle verdi\u011finden do\u011far. M\u0131s\u0131r sana topra\u011fa g\xf6m\xfclen bir tohumun, nesilleri besleyen bir berekete d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that behind every blessing given to you there is labor, a sacrifice; abundance often springs from what someone gave with love. Corn whispers that a seed buried in the earth turns into an abundance that nourishes generations.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass hinter jedem Segen, der dir geschenkt wird, M\xfche steht, ein Opfer; F\xfclle entspringt oft dem, was jemand mit Liebe gab. Der Mais fl\xfcstert, dass ein in die Erde gelegtes Korn zu einer F\xfclle wird, die Generationen n\xe4hrt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que tras cada bendici\xf3n que se te da hay un esfuerzo, un sacrificio; la abundancia suele brotar de lo que alguien dio con amor. El ma\xedz susurra que una semilla enterrada en la tierra se convierte en una abundancia que alimenta generaciones.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que derri\xe8re chaque bienfait qui t'est donn\xe9 il y a un labeur, un sacrifice ; l'abondance jaillit souvent de ce que quelqu'un a donn\xe9 avec amour. Le ma\xefs murmure qu'une graine enfouie dans la terre se change en une abondance qui nourrit des g\xe9n\xe9rations.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306b\u4e0e\u3048\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3042\u3089\u3086\u308b\u6075\u307f\u306e\u9670\u306b\u3001\u52b4\u82e6\u3084\u6367\u3052\u3082\u306e\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u8ab0\u304b\u304c\u611b\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u4e0e\u3048\u305f\u3082\u306e\u304b\u3089\u751f\u307e\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30c8\u30a6\u30e2\u30ed\u30b3\u30b7\u306f\u3001\u571f\u306b\u57cb\u3081\u3089\u308c\u305f\u4e00\u7c92\u306e\u7a2e\u304c\u3001\u5e7e\u4e16\u4ee3\u3092\u3082\u990a\u3046\u8c4a\u7a63\u306b\u5909\u308f\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que por tr\xe1s de cada b\xean\xe7\xe3o que lhe \xe9 dada h\xe1 um trabalho, um sacrif\xedcio; a abund\xe2ncia muitas vezes brota do que algu\xe9m deu com amor. O milho sussurra que uma semente enterrada na terra se transforma em uma abund\xe2ncia que alimenta gera\xe7\xf5es.",howToUse:"M\u0131s\u0131r\u0131 ha\u015flay\u0131p ya da pi\u015firip besleyici bir ikram olarak tadabilir, tanelerini bir kavanozda saklayabilirsin. Bir ko\xe7an m\u0131s\u0131r\u0131 bir k\xe2seye koyup masanda tutmak da bereket ve \u015f\xfck\xfcr niyetini onurland\u0131ran sade bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may boil or cook corn and enjoy it as a nourishing treat, and keep its kernels in a jar. Placing an ear of corn in a bowl on your table is also a simple gesture honoring an intention of abundance and gratitude.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst Mais kochen oder garen und als n\xe4hrende K\xf6stlichkeit genie\xdfen und seine K\xf6rner in einem Glas aufbewahren. Einen Maiskolben in einer Schale auf deinem Tisch ist ebenfalls eine schlichte Geste, die eine Absicht von F\xfclle und Dankbarkeit ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes hervir o cocinar el ma\xedz y disfrutarlo como un manjar nutritivo, y guardar sus granos en un frasco. Colocar una mazorca de ma\xedz en un cuenco sobre la mesa es tambi\xe9n un gesto sencillo que honra una intenci\xf3n de abundancia y gratitud.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux faire bouillir ou cuire le ma\xefs et le savourer comme une douceur nourrissante, et garder ses grains dans un bocal. Placer un \xe9pi de ma\xefs dans un bol sur ta table est aussi un geste simple qui honore une intention d'abondance et de gratitude.",howToUseJa:"\u30c8\u30a6\u30e2\u30ed\u30b3\u30b7\u3092\u8339\u3067\u305f\u308a\u716e\u305f\u308a\u3057\u3066\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u304a\u3084\u3064\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3044\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7c92\u3092\u74f6\u306b\u4fdd\u7ba1\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30c8\u30a6\u30e2\u30ed\u30b3\u30b7\u306e\u7a42\u3092\u5668\u306b\u5165\u308c\u3066\u673a\u306b\u7f6e\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u611f\u8b1d\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3064\u3064\u307e\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode ferver ou cozinhar o milho e apreci\xe1-lo como uma guloseima nutritiva, e guardar seus gr\xe3os em um frasco. Colocar uma espiga de milho em uma tigela sobre a mesa \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto simples que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de abund\xe2ncia e gratid\xe3o.",affirmation:"Bana verilen her nimetin ard\u0131ndaki sevgiyi g\xf6r\xfcyorum, \u015f\xfck\xfcrle besleniyorum.",affirmationEn:"I see the love behind every blessing given to me, and I am nourished with gratitude.",affirmationDe:"Ich sehe die Liebe hinter jedem Segen, der mir geschenkt wird, und ich werde mit Dankbarkeit gen\xe4hrt.",affirmationEs:"Veo el amor tras cada bendici\xf3n que se me da, y me alimento con gratitud.",affirmationFr:"Je vois l'amour derri\xe8re chaque bienfait qui m'est donn\xe9, et je me nourris avec gratitude.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4e0e\u3048\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3042\u3089\u3086\u308b\u6075\u307f\u306e\u9670\u306b\u3042\u308b\u611b\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3081\u3001\u611f\u8b1d\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u990a\u308f\u308c\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Vejo o amor por tr\xe1s de cada b\xean\xe7\xe3o que me \xe9 dada, e me nutro com gratid\xe3o.",myth:"Bir K\u0131z\u0131lderili (\u015eayen) s\xf6ylencesinde, kocalar\u0131 avdan d\xf6nmeyen yoksul bir anne ile zay\u0131f o\u011flu, k\u0131tl\u0131k i\xe7inde yaln\u0131zca yaban domatesleriyle hayatta kalmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r. Bir g\xfcn \xe7ad\u0131r\u0131n kap\u0131s\u0131nda \u015fi\u015fman bir \xe7ocuk belirir ve 'beni yiyebilirsin' diye \u015fark\u0131 s\xf6yler; anne ile o\u011ful bir plan kurar ve zay\u0131f \xe7ocuk, saklad\u0131\u011f\u0131 b\u0131\xe7a\u011f\u0131 \u015fi\u015fman \xe7ocu\u011fun karn\u0131na saplay\u0131nca ondan oday\u0131 dolduracak kadar m\u0131s\u0131r tanesi d\xf6k\xfcl\xfcr. Bu taneleri tadan ana o\u011ful g\xfc\xe7 kazan\u0131r ve m\u0131s\u0131r\u0131 halklar\u0131yla payla\u015f\u0131r. Aztek mitolojisinde ise tanr\u0131 Quetzalcouatl, k\u0131rm\u0131z\u0131 bir kar\u0131ncan\u0131n yard\u0131m\u0131yla yiyecek da\u011f\u0131nda gizli m\u0131s\u0131r\u0131 bulup ilk insanlara getirir.",mythEn:"In a Native American (Cheyenne) tale, a poor mother whose husband never returns from the hunt and her frail son try to survive a famine on wild tomatoes alone. One day a plump child appears at the tent door and sings, 'You may eat me'; the mother and son devise a plan, and when the frail boy plunges a hidden knife into the plump child's belly, corn kernels spill from him enough to fill the room. Tasting these kernels, mother and son gain strength and share the corn with their people. In Aztec myth, the god Quetzalcoatl, with the help of a red ant, finds the corn hidden in the mountain of food and brings it to the first humans.",mythDe:"In einer indianischen (Cheyenne-)Erz\xe4hlung versuchen eine arme Mutter, deren Mann nie von der Jagd zur\xfcckkehrt, und ihr schw\xe4chlicher Sohn, eine Hungersnot allein mit wilden Tomaten zu \xfcberleben. Eines Tages erscheint ein rundliches Kind an der Zelt\xf6ffnung und singt: 'Du darfst mich essen'; Mutter und Sohn ersinnen einen Plan, und als der schwache Junge ein verborgenes Messer in den Bauch des rundlichen Kindes st\xf6\xdft, ergie\xdfen sich Maisk\xf6rner aus ihm, genug, um den Raum zu f\xfcllen. Als Mutter und Sohn diese K\xf6rner kosten, gewinnen sie Kraft und teilen den Mais mit ihrem Volk. In der aztekischen Mythologie findet der Gott Quetzalcoatl mit Hilfe einer roten Ameise den im Berg der Nahrung verborgenen Mais und bringt ihn den ersten Menschen.",mythEs:"En un relato amerindio (cheyene), una madre pobre cuyo esposo nunca vuelve de la caza y su hijo d\xe9bil intentan sobrevivir a una hambruna solo con tomates silvestres. Un d\xeda un ni\xf1o regordete aparece en la entrada de la tienda y canta: 'Puedes comerme'; la madre y el hijo traman un plan, y cuando el ni\xf1o d\xe9bil clava un cuchillo oculto en el vientre del ni\xf1o regordete, de \xe9l se derraman granos de ma\xedz suficientes para llenar la estancia. Al probar esos granos, madre e hijo cobran fuerza y comparten el ma\xedz con su pueblo. En la mitolog\xeda azteca, el dios Quetzalc\xf3atl, con la ayuda de una hormiga roja, halla el ma\xedz oculto en la monta\xf1a del alimento y lo lleva a los primeros humanos.",mythFr:"Dans un r\xe9cit am\xe9rindien (cheyenne), une m\xe8re pauvre dont le mari ne revient jamais de la chasse et son fils fragile tentent de survivre \xe0 une famine avec les seules tomates sauvages. Un jour un enfant grassouillet para\xeet \xe0 l'entr\xe9e de la tente et chante : 'Tu peux me manger' ; la m\xe8re et le fils ourdissent un plan, et lorsque le fils fragile plonge un couteau cach\xe9 dans le ventre de l'enfant grassouillet, des grains de ma\xefs s'en d\xe9versent, assez pour emplir la pi\xe8ce. En go\xfbtant ces grains, la m\xe8re et le fils reprennent des forces et partagent le ma\xefs avec leur peuple. Dans la mythologie azt\xe8que, le dieu Quetzalcoatl, aid\xe9 d'une fourmi rouge, trouve le ma\xefs cach\xe9 dans la montagne de nourriture et l'apporte aux premiers humains.",mythJa:"\u3042\u308b\u30cd\u30a4\u30c6\u30a3\u30d6\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u30f3\uff08\u30b7\u30e3\u30a4\u30a2\u30f3\uff09\u306e\u7269\u8a9e\u3067\u306f\u3001\u592b\u304c\u72e9\u308a\u304b\u3089\u623b\u3089\u306a\u3044\u8ca7\u3057\u3044\u6bcd\u3068\u3072\u5f31\u306a\u606f\u5b50\u304c\u3001\u91ce\u751f\u306e\u30c8\u30de\u30c8\u3060\u3051\u3067\u98e2\u9949\u3092\u751f\u304d\u5ef6\u3073\u3088\u3046\u3068\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u308b\u65e5\u3001\u4e38\u3005\u3068\u3057\u305f\u5b50\u3069\u3082\u304c\u5929\u5e55\u306e\u5165\u53e3\u306b\u73fe\u308c\u3001\u300e\u79c1\u3092\u98df\u3079\u3066\u3082\u3088\u3044\u300f\u3068\u6b4c\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u6bcd\u3068\u606f\u5b50\u306f\u7b56\u3092\u7df4\u308a\u3001\u3072\u5f31\u306a\u5c11\u5e74\u304c\u96a0\u3057\u6301\u3063\u305f\u5203\u3092\u4e38\u3005\u3068\u3057\u305f\u5b50\u3069\u3082\u306e\u8179\u306b\u7a81\u304d\u523a\u3059\u3068\u3001\u90e8\u5c4b\u3092\u6e80\u305f\u3059\u307b\u3069\u306e\u30c8\u30a6\u30e2\u30ed\u30b3\u30b7\u306e\u7c92\u304c\u3053\u307c\u308c\u51fa\u307e\u3059\u3002\u305d\u306e\u7c92\u3092\u5473\u308f\u3063\u305f\u6bcd\u3068\u606f\u5b50\u306f\u529b\u3092\u5f97\u3066\u3001\u30c8\u30a6\u30e2\u30ed\u30b3\u30b7\u3092\u6c11\u3068\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a2\u30b9\u30c6\u30ab\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u795e\u30b1\u30c4\u30a1\u30eb\u30b3\u30a2\u30c8\u30eb\u304c\u8d64\u3044\u87fb\u306e\u52a9\u3051\u3092\u501f\u308a\u3066\u3001\u98df\u7269\u306e\u5c71\u306b\u96a0\u3055\u308c\u305f\u30c8\u30a6\u30e2\u30ed\u30b3\u30b7\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u3001\u6700\u521d\u306e\u4eba\u9593\u305f\u3061\u306b\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Num relato amer\xedndio (cheyenne), uma m\xe3e pobre cujo marido nunca volta da ca\xe7a e o seu filho fr\xe1gil tentam sobreviver a uma fome apenas com tomates silvestres. Um dia, uma crian\xe7a rechonchuda surge \xe0 entrada da tenda e canta: 'Voc\xea pode me comer'; a m\xe3e e o filho arquitetam um plano, e quando o menino fr\xe1gil crava uma faca escondida no ventre da crian\xe7a rechonchuda, dela se derramam gr\xe3os de milho suficientes para encher o aposento. Ao provar esses gr\xe3os, m\xe3e e filho ganham for\xe7a e partilham o milho com o seu povo. Na mitologia asteca, o deus Quetzalcoatl, com a ajuda de uma formiga vermelha, encontra o milho escondido na montanha do alimento e o leva aos primeiros humanos.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Zea_mays_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-283.jpg/330px-Zea_mays_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-283.jpg"},{id:"plant-116",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3a",color:"#A52A3C",name:"Nar",nameEn:"Pomegranate",nameDe:"Granatapfel",nameEs:"Granada",nameFr:"Grenade",nameJa:"\u30b6\u30af\u30ed",namePt:"Rom\xe3",origin:"Antik Yunan & Anadolu",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Anatolia",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & Anatolien",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y Anatolia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et Anatolie",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e Anat\xf3lia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u4ed9\u9aa8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacral",properties:["bereket","do\u011furganl\u0131k","yeniden do\u011fu\u015f","d\xf6ng\xfc","ba\u011f"],propertiesEn:["abundance","fertility","rebirth","cycle","bond"],propertiesDe:["F\xfclle","Fruchtbarkeit","Wiedergeburt","Kreislauf","Bindung"],propertiesEs:["abundancia","fertilidad","renacimiento","ciclo","v\xednculo"],propertiesFr:["abondance","fertilit\xe9","renaissance","cycle","lien"],propertiesJa:["\u8c4a\u7a63","\u591a\u7523","\u518d\u751f","\u5faa\u74b0","\u7d46"],propertiesPt:["abund\xe2ncia","fertilidade","renascimento","ciclo","v\xednculo"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131n k\u0131\u015f\u0131 ve bahar\u0131 bir arada ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rla; bir mevsim seni yeralt\u0131na \xe7ekse de, bir ba\u015fkas\u0131 seni mutlaka yeniden \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa \xe7\u0131kar\u0131r. Nar sana i\xe7indeki say\u0131s\u0131z tanenin, her d\xf6ng\xfcde yenilenen bir bereket ve ba\u011f s\xf6z\xfc oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that life carries its winter and its spring together; though one season pulls you underground, another will surely draw you back into the light. The pomegranate whispers that its countless seeds are a promise of abundance and bonds renewed with every cycle.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass das Leben seinen Winter und seinen Fr\xfchling zugleich tr\xe4gt; auch wenn dich eine Jahreszeit unter die Erde zieht, wird dich eine andere gewiss wieder ans Licht holen. Der Granatapfel fl\xfcstert, dass seine unz\xe4hligen Kerne ein Versprechen von F\xfclle und mit jedem Kreislauf erneuerten Bindungen sind.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que la vida lleva juntos su invierno y su primavera; aunque una estaci\xf3n te arrastre bajo tierra, otra te devolver\xe1 sin falta a la luz. La granada susurra que sus innumerables granos son una promesa de abundancia y de v\xednculos renovados en cada ciclo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que la vie porte ensemble son hiver et son printemps ; m\xeame si une saison t'entra\xeene sous terre, une autre te ram\xe8nera s\xfbrement \xe0 la lumi\xe8re. La grenade murmure que ses innombrables graines sont une promesse d'abondance et de liens renouvel\xe9s \xe0 chaque cycle.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u4eba\u751f\u304c\u51ac\u3068\u6625\u3092\u3068\u3082\u306b\u62b1\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3042\u308b\u5b63\u7bc0\u304c\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u5730\u306e\u4e0b\u3078\u5f15\u304d\u5165\u308c\u3066\u3082\u3001\u5225\u306e\u5b63\u7bc0\u304c\u304d\u3063\u3068\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u5149\u3078\u3068\u9023\u308c\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b6\u30af\u30ed\u306f\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7121\u6570\u306e\u7c92\u304c\u3001\u3081\u3050\u308b\u305f\u3073\u306b\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u306a\u308b\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u7d46\u306e\u7d04\u675f\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que a vida carrega o seu inverno e a sua primavera juntos; embora uma esta\xe7\xe3o puxe voc\xea para baixo da terra, outra certamente o trar\xe1 de volta \xe0 luz. A rom\xe3 sussurra que as suas in\xfameras sementes s\xe3o uma promessa de abund\xe2ncia e de v\xednculos renovados a cada ciclo.",howToUse:"Olgun bir nar\u0131 a\xe7\u0131p tanelerini tek tek tadarak bereket ve d\xf6ng\xfc niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bir nar\u0131 bir k\xe2seye koyup masanda tutmak ya da kurutulmu\u015f kabu\u011funu saklamak da do\u011furganl\u0131k ve yeniden do\u011fu\u015f niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may open a ripe pomegranate and taste its seeds one by one to accompany an intention of abundance and cycle. Placing a pomegranate in a bowl on your table or keeping its dried rind is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of fertility and rebirth.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst einen reifen Granatapfel \xf6ffnen und seine Kerne einen nach dem anderen kosten, um eine Absicht von F\xfclle und Kreislauf zu begleiten. Einen Granatapfel in einer Schale auf deinem Tisch aufzubewahren oder seine getrocknete Schale zu behalten ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Fruchtbarkeit und Wiedergeburt ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes abrir una granada madura y degustar sus granos uno a uno para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de abundancia y ciclo. Colocar una granada en un cuenco sobre la mesa o guardar su c\xe1scara seca es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de fertilidad y renacimiento.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux ouvrir une grenade m\xfbre et d\xe9guster ses graines une \xe0 une pour accompagner une intention d'abondance et de cycle. Placer une grenade dans un bol sur ta table ou garder son \xe9corce s\xe9ch\xe9e est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de fertilit\xe9 et de renaissance.",howToUseJa:"\u719f\u3057\u305f\u30b6\u30af\u30ed\u3092\u5272\u308a\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7c92\u3092\u4e00\u3064\u305a\u3064\u5473\u308f\u3063\u3066\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u5faa\u74b0\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b6\u30af\u30ed\u3092\u5668\u306b\u5165\u308c\u3066\u673a\u306b\u7f6e\u3044\u305f\u308a\u3001\u4e7e\u3044\u305f\u76ae\u3092\u4fdd\u7ba1\u3057\u305f\u308a\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u591a\u7523\u3068\u518d\u751f\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode abrir uma rom\xe3 madura e degustar suas sementes uma a uma para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de abund\xe2ncia e ciclo. Colocar uma rom\xe3 em uma tigela sobre a mesa ou guardar a sua casca seca \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de fertilidade e renascimento.",affirmation:"Hayat\u0131n k\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131 ve bahar\u0131n\u0131 bir arada ta\u015f\u0131yorum, her d\xf6ng\xfcde yeniden bereketleniyorum.",affirmationEn:"I carry life's winter and spring together, and with every cycle I am renewed in abundance.",affirmationDe:"Ich trage Winter und Fr\xfchling des Lebens zugleich, und mit jedem Kreislauf erneuere ich mich in F\xfclle.",affirmationEs:"Llevo juntos el invierno y la primavera de la vida, y con cada ciclo me renuevo en abundancia.",affirmationFr:"Je porte ensemble l'hiver et le printemps de la vie, et \xe0 chaque cycle je me renouvelle dans l'abondance.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u4eba\u751f\u306e\u51ac\u3068\u6625\u3092\u3068\u3082\u306b\u62b1\u304d\u3001\u3081\u3050\u308b\u305f\u3073\u306b\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306e\u3046\u3061\u306b\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Carrego juntos o inverno e a primavera da vida, e a cada ciclo me renovo em abund\xe2ncia.",myth:"Nar, bin tanesiyle bereketin, bollu\u011fun ve birli\u011fin meyvesidir. Anadolu'da yeni y\u0131l ve d\xfc\u011f\xfcnlerde yere \xe7al\u0131nan nar, ne kadar \xe7ok tane sa\xe7\u0131l\u0131rsa o kadar bolluk getirece\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131r. Antik Frigya'da ana tanr\u0131\xe7a Kibele'nin kutsal meyvesiydi; Persephone mitinde \xf6l\xfcm ile dirim aras\u0131ndaki ba\u011f\u0131 temsil eder \u2014 k\u0131\u015f\u0131n alt\u0131 tane, bahar\u0131n alt\u0131 tane. Kabu\u011funun sertli\u011fi koruma, i\xe7inin k\u0131z\u0131l bollu\u011fu ya\u015fam sevincidir. Sel\xe7uklu \xe7inilerinde nar motifi cennetin ve sonsuz bereketin simgesidir.",mythEn:"The pomegranate, with its thousand seeds, is the fruit of fertility, abundance and unity. In Anatolia, smashed on the ground at New Year and weddings, the more seeds it scatters the more abundance it is believed to bring. In ancient Phrygia it was the sacred fruit of the mother goddess Cybele; in the myth of Persephone it embodies the bond between death and life \u2014 six seeds for winter, six for spring. The hardness of its rind is protection, the red abundance within is the joy of life. In Seljuk tiles the pomegranate motif is the sign of paradise and endless plenty.",mythDe:"Der Granatapfel ist mit seinen tausend Kernen die Frucht der Fruchtbarkeit, der F\xfclle und der Einheit. In Anatolien wird er zu Neujahr und bei Hochzeiten auf den Boden geworfen \u2014 je mehr Kerne er verstreut, desto mehr F\xfclle soll er bringen. Im alten Phrygien war er die heilige Frucht der Mutterg\xf6ttin Kybele; im Mythos der Persephone verk\xf6rpert er das Band zwischen Tod und Leben \u2014 sechs Kerne f\xfcr den Winter, sechs f\xfcr den Fr\xfchling. Die H\xe4rte der Schale ist Schutz, die rote F\xfclle im Inneren die Lebensfreude. Auf seldschukischen Fliesen ist das Granatapfelmotiv das Zeichen des Paradieses und endloser F\xfclle.",mythEs:"La granada, con sus mil semillas, es el fruto de la fertilidad, la abundancia y la unidad. En Anatolia, estrellada contra el suelo en A\xf1o Nuevo y en las bodas, cuantas m\xe1s semillas esparce, m\xe1s abundancia se cree que trae. En la antigua Frigia era el fruto sagrado de la diosa madre Cibeles; en el mito de Pers\xe9fone encarna el v\xednculo entre la muerte y la vida \u2014 seis semillas para el invierno, seis para la primavera. La dureza de su corteza es protecci\xf3n, la roja abundancia interior es la alegr\xeda de vivir. En los azulejos sely\xfacidas, el motivo de la granada es signo del para\xedso y de la plenitud sin fin.",mythFr:"La grenade, avec ses mille graines, est le fruit de la f\xe9condit\xe9, de l'abondance et de l'unit\xe9. En Anatolie, bris\xe9e au sol au Nouvel An et aux mariages, plus elle disperse de graines, plus elle est cens\xe9e apporter d'abondance. Dans l'antique Phrygie, elle \xe9tait le fruit sacr\xe9 de la d\xe9esse m\xe8re Cyb\xe8le ; dans le mythe de Pers\xe9phone, elle incarne le lien entre la mort et la vie \u2014 six graines pour l'hiver, six pour le printemps. La duret\xe9 de son \xe9corce est protection, la rouge abondance int\xe9rieure la joie de vivre. Sur les fa\xefences seldjoukides, le motif de la grenade est signe du paradis et d'une pl\xe9nitude sans fin.",mythJa:"\u30b6\u30af\u30ed\u306f\u5343\u306e\u7a2e\u3092\u3082\u3064\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u5145\u6ea2\u3068\u4e00\u4f53\u306e\u679c\u5b9f\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u65b0\u5e74\u3084\u5a5a\u793c\u306b\u5730\u306b\u6253\u3061\u3064\u3051\u3001\u7a2e\u304c\u591a\u304f\u98db\u3073\u6563\u308b\u307b\u3069\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3002\u53e4\u4ee3\u30d5\u30ea\u30ae\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u6bcd\u306a\u308b\u5973\u795e\u30ad\u30e5\u30d9\u30ec\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u679c\u5b9f\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u30da\u30eb\u30bb\u30dd\u30cd\u306e\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u6b7b\u3068\u751f\u306e\u7d46\u3092\u4f53\u73fe\u3059\u308b\u2014\u2014\u51ac\u306b\u516d\u7c92\u3001\u6625\u306b\u516d\u7c92\u3002\u56fa\u3044\u76ae\u306f\u5b88\u308a\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u7d05\u306e\u5145\u6ea2\u306f\u751f\u304d\u308b\u559c\u3073\u3002\u30bb\u30eb\u30b8\u30e5\u30fc\u30af\u671d\u306e\u30bf\u30a4\u30eb\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30b6\u30af\u30ed\u306e\u6587\u69d8\u306f\u697d\u5712\u3068\u5c3d\u304d\u305b\u306c\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u3057\u308b\u3057\u3002",mythPt:"A rom\xe3, com as suas mil sementes, \xe9 o fruto da fertilidade, da abund\xe2ncia e da uni\xe3o. Na Anat\xf3lia, atirada ao ch\xe3o no Ano Novo e nos casamentos, quantas mais sementes espalha, mais abund\xe2ncia se cr\xea que traz. Na antiga Fr\xedgia era o fruto sagrado da deusa-m\xe3e Cibele; no mito de Pers\xe9fone encarna o la\xe7o entre a morte e a vida \u2014 seis sementes para o inverno, seis para a primavera. A dureza da casca \xe9 prote\xe7\xe3o, a vermelha abund\xe2ncia interior \xe9 a alegria de viver. Nos azulejos selj\xfacidas, o motivo da rom\xe3 \xe9 sinal do para\xedso e da fartura sem fim.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Pomegranate_Juice_%282019%29.jpg/330px-Pomegranate_Juice_%282019%29.jpg"},{id:"plant-117",emoji:"\ud83e\udeb7",color:"#E27BA0",name:"Nil\xfcfer",nameEn:"Lotus",nameDe:"Lotus",nameEs:"Loto",nameFr:"Lotus",nameJa:"\u84ee",namePt:"L\xf3tus",origin:"Hint & M\u0131s\u0131r Mitolojisi",originEn:"Indian & Egyptian Mythology",originDe:"Indische & \xe4gyptische Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda india y egipcia",originFr:"Mythologie indienne et \xe9gyptienne",originJa:"\u30a4\u30f3\u30c9\u30fb\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia indiana e eg\xedpcia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Ta\xe7 \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Crown Chakra",chakraDe:"Kronenchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Corona",chakraFr:"Chakra Couronne",chakraJa:"\u30af\u30e9\u30a6\u30f3\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Coroa",properties:["safl\u0131k","ayd\u0131nlanma","yeniden do\u011fu\u015f","bereket","y\xfckseli\u015f"],propertiesEn:["purity","enlightenment","rebirth","abundance","ascension"],propertiesDe:["Reinheit","Erleuchtung","Wiedergeburt","F\xfclle","Aufstieg"],propertiesEs:["pureza","iluminaci\xf3n","renacimiento","abundancia","ascenso"],propertiesFr:["puret\xe9","illumination","renaissance","abondance","\xe9l\xe9vation"],propertiesJa:["\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u3055","\u609f\u308a","\u518d\u751f","\u8c4a\u7a63","\u4e0a\u6607"],propertiesPt:["pureza","ilumina\xe7\xe3o","renascimento","abund\xe2ncia","ascens\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn i\xe7inde bulundu\u011fun \xe7amurun seni tan\u0131mlamas\u0131na izin verme; en saf g\xfczellik \xe7o\u011fu zaman en bulan\u0131k sulardan y\xfckselir. Nil\xfcfer sana karanl\u0131k bir yerden do\u011fsan bile, \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa do\u011fru a\xe7\u0131lma g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, do not let the mud you find yourself in define you; the purest beauty often rises from the murkiest waters. The lotus whispers that even if you are born from a dark place, you carry the power to open toward the light.",dailyMessageDe:"Lass dich heute nicht von dem Schlamm bestimmen, in dem du dich befindest; die reinste Sch\xf6nheit steigt oft aus den tr\xfcbsten Wassern empor. Der Lotus fl\xfcstert, dass du, selbst wenn du aus einem dunklen Ort geboren wirst, die Kraft tr\xe4gst, dich zum Licht hin zu \xf6ffnen.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, no dejes que el lodo en que te encuentras te defina; la belleza m\xe1s pura suele alzarse de las aguas m\xe1s turbias. El loto susurra que, aunque nazcas de un lugar oscuro, llevas el poder de abrirte hacia la luz.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ne laisse pas la boue o\xf9 tu te trouves te d\xe9finir ; la beaut\xe9 la plus pure s'\xe9l\xe8ve souvent des eaux les plus troubles. Le lotus murmure que, m\xeame si tu nais d'un lieu obscur, tu portes le pouvoir de t'ouvrir vers la lumi\xe8re.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u3044\u308b\u6ce5\u306b\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u5b9a\u7fa9\u3055\u305b\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002\u6700\u3082\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306a\u7f8e\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u6700\u3082\u6fc1\u3063\u305f\u6c34\u304b\u3089\u7acb\u3061\u306e\u307c\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u84ee\u306f\u3001\u6697\u3044\u5834\u6240\u304b\u3089\u751f\u307e\u308c\u3066\u3082\u3001\u5149\u3078\u3068\u958b\u304f\u529b\u3092\u5bbf\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, n\xe3o deixe que a lama em que voc\xea se encontra o defina; a beleza mais pura muitas vezes se ergue das \xe1guas mais turvas. O l\xf3tus sussurra que, mesmo que voc\xea nas\xe7a de um lugar escuro, carrega o poder de se abrir rumo \xe0 luz.",howToUse:"Bir g\xf6let ya da kapta yeti\u015fen bir nil\xfcferi seyrederek safl\u0131k ve ayd\u0131nlanma niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bir nil\xfcfer \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi \xfczerine sessizce meditasyon yapmak da yeniden do\u011fu\u015f ve y\xfckseli\u015f niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir and\u0131r.",howToUseEn:"You may contemplate a lotus growing in a pond or vessel to accompany an intention of purity and enlightenment. Meditating quietly upon a lotus flower is also a gentle moment honoring an intention of rebirth and ascension.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst einen in einem Teich oder Gef\xe4\xdf wachsenden Lotus betrachten, um eine Absicht von Reinheit und Erleuchtung zu begleiten. Still \xfcber eine Lotusbl\xfcte zu meditieren ist ebenfalls ein zarter Augenblick, der eine Absicht von Wiedergeburt und Aufstieg ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes contemplar un loto que crece en un estanque o recipiente para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de pureza e iluminaci\xf3n. Meditar en silencio sobre una flor de loto es tambi\xe9n un momento tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de renacimiento y ascenso.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux contempler un lotus poussant dans un bassin ou un r\xe9cipient pour accompagner une intention de puret\xe9 et d'illumination. M\xe9diter en silence sur une fleur de lotus est aussi un instant tendre qui honore une intention de renaissance et d'\xe9l\xe9vation.",howToUseJa:"\u6c60\u3084\u5668\u3067\u80b2\u3064\u84ee\u3092\u773a\u3081\u3066\u3001\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u3055\u3068\u609f\u308a\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u84ee\u306e\u82b1\u306e\u4e0a\u3067\u9759\u304b\u306b\u7791\u60f3\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u518d\u751f\u3068\u4e0a\u6607\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u3072\u3068\u3068\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode contemplar um l\xf3tus que cresce em um lago ou recipiente para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de pureza e ilumina\xe7\xe3o. Meditar em sil\xeancio sobre uma flor de l\xf3tus \xe9 tamb\xe9m um momento terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de renascimento e ascens\xe3o.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7inde bulundu\u011fum \xe7amur beni tan\u0131mlam\u0131yor, \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa do\u011fru saf bir g\xfczellikle a\xe7\u0131l\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"The mud I am in does not define me, and I open toward the light with a pure beauty.",affirmationDe:"Der Schlamm, in dem ich bin, bestimmt mich nicht, und ich \xf6ffne mich mit reiner Sch\xf6nheit zum Licht.",affirmationEs:"El lodo en que estoy no me define, y me abro hacia la luz con una belleza pura.",affirmationFr:"La boue o\xf9 je suis ne me d\xe9finit pas, et je m'ouvre vers la lumi\xe8re avec une beaut\xe9 pure.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u3044\u308b\u6ce5\u306f\u79c1\u3092\u5b9a\u7fa9\u305b\u305a\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306a\u7f8e\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u5149\u3078\u3068\u958b\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"A lama em que estou n\xe3o me define, e me abro rumo \xe0 luz com uma beleza pura.",myth:"Nil\xfcfer, su ile ya\u015fam\u0131 \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftiren b\xfcy\xfck nehir k\xfclt\xfcrlerinde kutsal say\u0131l\u0131r. Hindu inanc\u0131nda kozmik sularda bin yaprakl\u0131, alt\u0131ndan dev bir nil\xfcfer a\xe7ar; bu nil\xfcfer evrenin yarat\u0131c\u0131 rahmidir. Yeniden do\u011fu\u015fun tanr\u0131s\u0131 Vi\u015fnu'nun g\xf6be\u011finden bir nil\xfcfer \xe7\u0131kar, e\u015fi bereket tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Lak\u015fmi ise daima bir nil\xfcferin \xfczerinde tasvir edilir. Budist inanc\u0131nda \xe7amurlu sulardan y\xfckselip lekesiz a\xe7an nil\xfcfer, ruhsal ayd\u0131nlanman\u0131n simgesidir; gelece\u011fin Budas\u0131 Prens Siddharta do\u011fdu\u011funda ayaklar\u0131n\u0131n alt\u0131ndan nil\xfcfer \xe7i\xe7eklerinin \xe7\u0131kt\u0131\u011f\u0131 anlat\u0131l\u0131r. M\u0131s\u0131r yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f mitinde ise ilksel sulardan a\xe7an dev bir nil\xfcferin ortas\u0131ndan ilk sabah g\xfcne\u015fi do\u011fmu\u015ftur.",mythEn:"The lotus is held sacred in the great river cultures that identify water with life. In Hindu belief, a giant thousand-petaled golden lotus opens upon the cosmic waters; this lotus is the creative womb of the universe. From the navel of Vishnu, god of rebirth, a lotus springs, and his consort Lakshmi, goddess of abundance, is always depicted upon a lotus. In Buddhist belief, the lotus that rises from muddy waters and opens unstained is the symbol of spiritual enlightenment; it is told that when the future Buddha, Prince Siddhartha, was born, lotus flowers sprang up beneath his feet. In the Egyptian creation myth, the first morning sun rose from the heart of a giant lotus that opened upon the primeval waters.",mythDe:"Der Lotus gilt in den gro\xdfen Flusskulturen, die das Wasser mit dem Leben gleichsetzen, als heilig. Im hinduistischen Glauben \xf6ffnet sich auf den kosmischen Wassern ein riesiger, tausendbl\xe4ttriger goldener Lotus; dieser Lotus ist der sch\xf6pferische Scho\xdf des Universums. Aus dem Nabel Vishnus, des Gottes der Wiedergeburt, entspringt ein Lotus, und seine Gemahlin Lakshmi, die G\xf6ttin der F\xfclle, wird stets auf einem Lotus dargestellt. Im buddhistischen Glauben ist der Lotus, der aus tr\xfcbem Wasser emporsteigt und makellos erbl\xfcht, das Sinnbild der geistigen Erleuchtung; es hei\xdft, dass bei der Geburt des k\xfcnftigen Buddha, des Prinzen Siddhartha, unter seinen F\xfc\xdfen Lotusbl\xfcten emporsprossen. Im \xe4gyptischen Sch\xf6pfungsmythos stieg die erste Morgensonne aus dem Herzen eines riesigen Lotus, der sich auf den Urwassern \xf6ffnete.",mythEs:"El loto se tiene por sagrado en las grandes culturas fluviales que identifican el agua con la vida. En la creencia hind\xfa, sobre las aguas c\xf3smicas se abre un loto dorado gigante de mil p\xe9talos; este loto es el vientre creador del universo. Del ombligo de Vishnu, dios del renacimiento, brota un loto, y su consorte Lakshmi, diosa de la abundancia, siempre se representa sobre un loto. En la creencia budista, el loto que se alza de las aguas turbias y florece sin mancha es el s\xedmbolo de la iluminaci\xf3n espiritual; se cuenta que, al nacer el futuro Buda, el pr\xedncipe Siddhartha, brotaron flores de loto bajo sus pies. En el mito egipcio de la creaci\xf3n, el primer sol de la ma\xf1ana surgi\xf3 del coraz\xf3n de un loto gigante que se abri\xf3 sobre las aguas primordiales.",mythFr:"Le lotus est tenu pour sacr\xe9 dans les grandes cultures fluviales qui identifient l'eau \xe0 la vie. Dans la croyance hindoue, un lotus d'or g\xe9ant aux mille p\xe9tales s'ouvre sur les eaux cosmiques ; ce lotus est la matrice cr\xe9atrice de l'univers. Du nombril de Vishnou, dieu de la renaissance, jaillit un lotus, et son \xe9pouse Lakshmi, d\xe9esse de l'abondance, est toujours repr\xe9sent\xe9e sur un lotus. Dans la croyance bouddhiste, le lotus qui s'\xe9l\xe8ve des eaux troubles et s'\xe9panouit sans tache est le symbole de l'illumination spirituelle ; on raconte qu'\xe0 la naissance du futur Bouddha, le prince Siddhartha, des fleurs de lotus jaillirent sous ses pieds. Dans le mythe \xe9gyptien de la cr\xe9ation, le premier soleil du matin surgit du c\u0153ur d'un lotus g\xe9ant qui s'ouvrit sur les eaux primordiales.",mythJa:"\u84ee\u306f\u3001\u6c34\u3092\u751f\u547d\u3068\u540c\u4e00\u8996\u3059\u308b\u5927\u6cb3\u306e\u6587\u5316\u306b\u304a\u3044\u3066\u8056\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3068\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30d2\u30f3\u30c9\u30a5\u30fc\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5b87\u5b99\u306e\u6c34\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u5343\u5f01\u306e\u5de8\u5927\u306a\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u84ee\u304c\u958b\u304d\u3001\u3053\u306e\u84ee\u306f\u5b87\u5b99\u306e\u5275\u9020\u306e\u6bcd\u80ce\u3067\u3059\u3002\u518d\u751f\u306e\u795e\u30f4\u30a3\u30b7\u30e5\u30cc\u306e\u81cd\u304b\u3089\u84ee\u304c\u751f\u3048\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5983\u3067\u3042\u308b\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30e9\u30af\u30b7\u30e5\u30df\u30fc\u306f\u5e38\u306b\u84ee\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u63cf\u304b\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4ecf\u6559\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u6fc1\u3063\u305f\u6c34\u304b\u3089\u7acb\u3061\u306e\u307c\u308a\u3001\u6c5a\u308c\u306a\u304f\u54b2\u304f\u84ee\u306f\u970a\u7684\u306a\u609f\u308a\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3059\u3002\u672a\u6765\u306e\u4ecf\u3067\u3042\u308b\u738b\u5b50\u30b7\u30c3\u30c0\u30fc\u30eb\u30bf\u304c\u751f\u307e\u308c\u305f\u3068\u304d\u3001\u305d\u306e\u8db3\u3082\u3068\u304b\u3089\u84ee\u306e\u82b1\u304c\u54b2\u304d\u51fa\u305f\u3068\u8a9e\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a8\u30b8\u30d7\u30c8\u306e\u5275\u4e16\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u539f\u521d\u306e\u6c34\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u958b\u3044\u305f\u5de8\u5927\u306a\u84ee\u306e\u4e2d\u5fc3\u304b\u3089\u3001\u6700\u521d\u306e\u671d\u306e\u592a\u967d\u304c\u6607\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"O l\xf3tus \xe9 tido como sagrado nas grandes culturas fluviais que identificam a \xe1gua com a vida. Na cren\xe7a hindu, sobre as \xe1guas c\xf3smicas abre-se um l\xf3tus dourado gigante de mil p\xe9talas; este l\xf3tus \xe9 o ventre criador do universo. Do umbigo de Vishnu, deus do renascimento, brota um l\xf3tus, e a sua consorte Lakshmi, deusa da abund\xe2ncia, \xe9 sempre representada sobre um l\xf3tus. Na cren\xe7a budista, o l\xf3tus que se ergue das \xe1guas turvas e floresce sem m\xe1cula \xe9 o s\xedmbolo da ilumina\xe7\xe3o espiritual; conta-se que, ao nascer o futuro Buda, o pr\xedncipe Sidarta, brotaram flores de l\xf3tus sob os seus p\xe9s. No mito eg\xedpcio da cria\xe7\xe3o, o primeiro sol da manh\xe3 surgiu do cora\xe7\xe3o de um l\xf3tus gigante que se abriu sobre as \xe1guas primordiais.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg/330px-Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg"},{id:"plant-118",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#B7C98C",name:"\xd6kseotu",nameEn:"Mistletoe",nameDe:"Mistel",nameEs:"Mu\xe9rdago",nameFr:"Gui",nameJa:"\u30e4\u30c9\u30ea\u30ae",namePt:"Visco",origin:"Kelt & \u0130skandinav Mitolojisi",originEn:"Celtic & Norse Mythology",originDe:"Keltische & nordische Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda celta y n\xf3rdica",originFr:"Mythologie celtique et nordique",originJa:"\u30b1\u30eb\u30c8\u30fb\u5317\u6b27\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia celta e n\xf3rdica",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc G\xf6z \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Third Eye Chakra",chakraDe:"Stirnchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Tercer Ojo",chakraFr:"Chakra du Troisi\xe8me \u0152il",chakraJa:"\u7b2c\u4e09\u306e\u76ee\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Terceiro Olho",properties:["kutsall\u0131k","koruma","ya\u015fam g\xfcc\xfc","s\u0131r","k\u0131r\u0131lganl\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["sacredness","protection","life-force","mystery","fragility"],propertiesDe:["Heiligkeit","Schutz","Lebenskraft","Geheimnis","Zerbrechlichkeit"],propertiesEs:["sacralidad","protecci\xf3n","fuerza vital","misterio","fragilidad"],propertiesFr:["sacralit\xe9","protection","force vitale","myst\xe8re","fragilit\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u8056\u6027","\u5b88\u8b77","\u751f\u547d\u529b","\u79d8\u3081\u3054\u3068","\u8106\u3055"],propertiesPt:["sacralidade","prote\xe7\xe3o","for\xe7a vital","mist\xe9rio","fragilidade"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn en k\xfc\xe7\xfck, en hafife al\u0131nan \u015feyin bile b\xfcy\xfck bir g\xfc\xe7 ta\u015f\u0131yabilece\u011fini hat\u0131rla; \xe7\u0131plak bir a\u011fac\u0131n \xfczerinde ye\u015feren tek dal, o a\u011fac\u0131n h\xe2l\xe2 ya\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n kan\u0131t\u0131d\u0131r. \xd6kseotu sana g\xf6r\xfcn\xfc\u015fte zay\u0131f olan\u0131n bile kutsal bir ya\u015fam g\xfcc\xfc saklayabilece\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that even the smallest, most underestimated thing can carry great power; the single green branch on a bare tree is proof that the tree still lives. Mistletoe whispers that even what seems weak may hide a sacred life-force.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass selbst das Kleinste, am meisten Untersch\xe4tzte gro\xdfe Kraft tragen kann; der einzige gr\xfcne Zweig an einem kahlen Baum ist der Beweis, dass der Baum noch lebt. Die Mistel fl\xfcstert, dass selbst das, was schwach erscheint, eine heilige Lebenskraft bergen kann.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que incluso lo m\xe1s peque\xf1o y menospreciado puede llevar un gran poder; la \xfanica rama verde de un \xe1rbol desnudo es la prueba de que el \xe1rbol a\xfan vive. El mu\xe9rdago susurra que hasta lo que parece d\xe9bil puede ocultar una fuerza vital sagrada.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que m\xeame la plus petite chose, la plus sous-estim\xe9e, peut porter une grande puissance ; l'unique rameau vert sur un arbre d\xe9nud\xe9 est la preuve que l'arbre vit encore. Le gui murmure que m\xeame ce qui para\xeet faible peut cacher une force vitale sacr\xe9e.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u6700\u3082\u5c0f\u3055\u304f\u3001\u6700\u3082\u8efd\u3093\u3058\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3067\u3055\u3048\u3001\u5927\u304d\u306a\u529b\u3092\u5bbf\u3057\u3046\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u88f8\u306e\u6728\u306b\u82bd\u5439\u304f\u305f\u3060\u4e00\u672c\u306e\u7dd1\u306e\u679d\u306f\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6728\u304c\u307e\u3060\u751f\u304d\u3066\u3044\u308b\u8a3c\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30e4\u30c9\u30ea\u30ae\u306f\u3001\u5f31\u304f\u898b\u3048\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3055\u3048\u3001\u8056\u306a\u308b\u751f\u547d\u529b\u3092\u79d8\u3081\u3046\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que at\xe9 a coisa mais pequena e menosprezada pode carregar um grande poder; o \xfanico ramo verde numa \xe1rvore nua \xe9 a prova de que a \xe1rvore ainda vive. O visco sussurra que at\xe9 o que parece fr\xe1gil pode esconder uma for\xe7a vital sagrada.",howToUse:"K\u0131\u015f aylar\u0131nda bir a\u011fac\u0131n \xfczerinde ye\u015feren \xf6kseotunu uzaktan seyrederek ya\u015fam g\xfcc\xfc ve koruma niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bitki zehirli oldu\u011fundan kullan\u0131m\u0131 yaln\u0131zca sembolik ve t\xf6renseldir; i\xe7sel kullan\u0131m \xf6nerilmez.",howToUseEn:"You may observe from afar the mistletoe greening upon a tree in the winter months to accompany an intention of life-force and protection. Since the plant is toxic, its use is symbolic and ceremonial only; inner use is not advised.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die in den Wintermonaten auf einem Baum ergr\xfcnende Mistel aus der Ferne betrachten, um eine Absicht von Lebenskraft und Schutz zu begleiten. Da die Pflanze giftig ist, ist ihr Gebrauch nur symbolisch und zeremoniell; innere Anwendung wird nicht empfohlen.",howToUseEs:"Puedes observar de lejos el mu\xe9rdago que reverdece sobre un \xe1rbol en los meses de invierno para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de fuerza vital y protecci\xf3n. Como la planta es t\xf3xica, su uso es solo simb\xf3lico y ceremonial; no se aconseja el uso interno.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux observer de loin le gui qui verdit sur un arbre durant les mois d'hiver pour accompagner une intention de force vitale et de protection. Comme la plante est toxique, son usage est seulement symbolique et c\xe9r\xe9moniel ; l'usage interne n'est pas conseill\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u51ac\u306e\u6708\u3005\u306b\u6728\u306e\u4e0a\u3067\u7dd1\u3065\u304f\u30e4\u30c9\u30ea\u30ae\u3092\u9060\u304f\u304b\u3089\u773a\u3081\u3066\u3001\u751f\u547d\u529b\u3068\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3053\u306e\u690d\u7269\u306f\u6709\u6bd2\u3067\u3042\u308b\u305f\u3081\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7528\u3044\u65b9\u306f\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u30fb\u5100\u793c\u7684\u306a\u3082\u306e\u306b\u9650\u3089\u308c\u3001\u5185\u670d\u306f\u52e7\u3081\u3089\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode observar de longe o visco que reverdece sobre uma \xe1rvore nos meses de inverno para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de for\xe7a vital e prote\xe7\xe3o. Como a planta \xe9 t\xf3xica, seu uso \xe9 apenas simb\xf3lico e cerimonial; o uso interno n\xe3o \xe9 aconselhado.",affirmation:"G\xf6r\xfcn\xfc\u015fte zay\u0131f olan\u0131n g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc tan\u0131yorum, i\xe7imde kutsal bir ya\u015fam g\xfcc\xfc ta\u015f\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"I recognize the power of what seems weak, and I carry a sacred life-force within me.",affirmationDe:"Ich erkenne die Kraft dessen, was schwach erscheint, und ich trage eine heilige Lebenskraft in mir.",affirmationEs:"Reconozco el poder de lo que parece d\xe9bil, y llevo una fuerza vital sagrada dentro de m\xed.",affirmationFr:"Je reconnais la puissance de ce qui para\xeet faible, et je porte une force vitale sacr\xe9e en moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5f31\u304f\u898b\u3048\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306e\u529b\u3092\u8a8d\u3081\u3001\u5185\u306b\u8056\u306a\u308b\u751f\u547d\u529b\u3092\u5bbf\u3059\u3002",affirmationPt:"Reconhe\xe7o o poder do que parece fr\xe1gil, e carrego uma for\xe7a vital sagrada dentro de mim.",myth:"Mitolojide hazinelerin kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7an 'alt\u0131n dal'\u0131n \xf6kseotu oldu\u011fu d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcl\xfcr. Kelt rahipleri Druidler i\xe7in \xf6kseotu kutsald\u0131; yapra\u011f\u0131n\u0131 d\xf6ken me\u015fenin \xfczerinde k\u0131\u015f\u0131n yemye\u015fil durmas\u0131, a\u011fac\u0131n ya\u015fayan ruhunun g\xf6stergesi say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131 ve ona 'me\u015fe suyu' denirdi. Yaz d\xf6n\xfcm\xfcnde \xf6zel bir ayinle, beyaz bir kuma\u015fla tutulup alt\u0131n bir orakla kesilirdi. \u0130skandinav mitolojisinde ise iyi ve sevilen tanr\u0131 Balder'i annesi Frigg her \u015feyden korumak i\xe7in yemin ettirmi\u015f, ama zarars\u0131z sand\u0131\u011f\u0131 \xf6kseotunu unutmu\u015ftu; k\xf6t\xfc Loki bunu \xf6\u011frenip \xf6kseotundan bir ok yapt\u0131rd\u0131 ve k\xf6r tanr\u0131 H\xf6dur'un eliyle Balder bu okla vurularak \xf6ld\xfc.",mythEn:"In myth, the 'golden bough' that opens the door to treasures is thought to be the mistletoe. To the Celtic priests, the Druids, mistletoe was sacred; that it stayed green through winter upon the oak which shed its leaves was held to be the sign of the tree's living soul, and it was called 'oak water.' At the summer solstice it was cut in a special rite, held with a white cloth and severed with a golden sickle. In Norse myth, the good and beloved god Balder was made safe when his mother Frigg had all things swear not to harm him, but she had overlooked the mistletoe, thinking it harmless; the evil Loki learned of this and had an arrow made of mistletoe, and by the hand of the blind god H\xf6d, Balder was struck with it and died.",mythDe:"Im Mythos gilt der 'goldene Zweig', der die T\xfcr zu Sch\xe4tzen \xf6ffnet, als die Mistel. Den keltischen Priestern, den Druiden, war die Mistel heilig; dass sie auf der Eiche, die ihre Bl\xe4tter abwarf, durch den Winter gr\xfcn blieb, galt als Zeichen der lebendigen Seele des Baumes, und man nannte sie 'Eichenwasser'. Zur Sommersonnenwende wurde sie in einem besonderen Ritus geschnitten, mit einem wei\xdfen Tuch gehalten und mit einer goldenen Sichel abgetrennt. In der nordischen Mythologie wurde der gute und geliebte Gott Balder gesch\xfctzt, als seine Mutter Frigg alle Dinge schw\xf6ren lie\xdf, ihm nicht zu schaden, doch sie hatte die Mistel \xfcbersehen, da sie sie f\xfcr harmlos hielt; der b\xf6se Loki erfuhr davon und lie\xdf einen Pfeil aus Mistel fertigen, und durch die Hand des blinden Gottes H\xf6d wurde Balder davon getroffen und starb.",mythEs:"En el mito, se piensa que la 'rama dorada' que abre la puerta a los tesoros es el mu\xe9rdago. Para los sacerdotes celtas, los druidas, el mu\xe9rdago era sagrado; que permaneciera verde durante el invierno sobre el roble que perd\xeda sus hojas se ten\xeda por se\xf1al del alma viviente del \xe1rbol, y se le llamaba 'agua de roble'. En el solsticio de verano se cortaba en un rito especial, sostenido con un pa\xf1o blanco y separado con una hoz de oro. En la mitolog\xeda n\xf3rdica, el bueno y amado dios Balder qued\xf3 a salvo cuando su madre Frigg hizo jurar a todas las cosas no da\xf1arlo, pero hab\xeda pasado por alto el mu\xe9rdago, crey\xe9ndolo inofensivo; el malvado Loki lo supo e hizo fabricar una flecha de mu\xe9rdago, y por la mano del dios ciego H\xf6d, Balder fue herido con ella y muri\xf3.",mythFr:"Dans le mythe, on pense que le 'rameau d'or' qui ouvre la porte des tr\xe9sors est le gui. Pour les pr\xeatres celtes, les druides, le gui \xe9tait sacr\xe9 ; qu'il rest\xe2t vert tout l'hiver sur le ch\xeane d\xe9pouill\xe9 de ses feuilles \xe9tait tenu pour le signe de l'\xe2me vivante de l'arbre, et on l'appelait 'eau de ch\xeane'. Au solstice d'\xe9t\xe9, il \xe9tait coup\xe9 lors d'un rite sp\xe9cial, tenu dans un linge blanc et tranch\xe9 d'une faucille d'or. Dans la mythologie nordique, le bon et aim\xe9 dieu Balder fut mis \xe0 l'abri lorsque sa m\xe8re Frigg fit jurer \xe0 toutes choses de ne pas lui nuire, mais elle avait n\xe9glig\xe9 le gui, le croyant inoffensif ; le mauvais Loki l'apprit et fit fabriquer une fl\xe8che de gui, et par la main du dieu aveugle H\xf6d, Balder en fut frapp\xe9 et mourut.",mythJa:"\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5b9d\u5eab\u306e\u6249\u3092\u958b\u304f\u300e\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u679d\u300f\u306f\u30e4\u30c9\u30ea\u30ae\u3060\u3068\u8003\u3048\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b1\u30eb\u30c8\u306e\u796d\u53f8\u30c9\u30eb\u30a4\u30c9\u306b\u3068\u3063\u3066\u30e4\u30c9\u30ea\u30ae\u306f\u8056\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002\u8449\u3092\u843d\u3068\u3059\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306e\u4e0a\u3067\u51ac\u3058\u3085\u3046\u7dd1\u306e\u307e\u307e\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6728\u306e\u751f\u304d\u305f\u9b42\u306e\u3057\u308b\u3057\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3001\u300e\u30aa\u30fc\u30af\u306e\u6c34\u300f\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u590f\u81f3\u306b\u306f\u7279\u5225\u306a\u5100\u5f0f\u3067\u3001\u767d\u3044\u5e03\u3067\u53d7\u3051\u3068\u3081\u3001\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u938c\u3067\u5207\u308a\u53d6\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5317\u6b27\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u5584\u826f\u3067\u611b\u3055\u308c\u305f\u795e\u30d0\u30eb\u30c9\u30eb\u3092\u3001\u6bcd\u30d5\u30ea\u30c3\u30b0\u304c\u3042\u3089\u3086\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306b\u5bb3\u3055\u306c\u3088\u3046\u8a93\u308f\u305b\u3066\u5b88\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u7121\u5bb3\u3068\u601d\u3063\u305f\u30e4\u30c9\u30ea\u30ae\u3060\u3051\u3092\u898b\u843d\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u90aa\u60aa\u306a\u30ed\u30ad\u306f\u3053\u308c\u3092\u77e5\u308a\u3001\u30e4\u30c9\u30ea\u30ae\u3067\u77e2\u3092\u4f5c\u3089\u305b\u3001\u76f2\u76ee\u306e\u795e\u30d8\u30ba\u306e\u624b\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u30d0\u30eb\u30c9\u30eb\u306f\u305d\u306e\u77e2\u306b\u5c04\u3089\u308c\u3066\u6b7b\u306b\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"No mito, pensa-se que o 'ramo de ouro' que abre a porta dos tesouros \xe9 o visco. Para os sacerdotes celtas, os druidas, o visco era sagrado; o fato de permanecer verde durante o inverno sobre o carvalho que perdia as folhas era tido como o sinal da alma viva da \xe1rvore, e era chamado '\xe1gua de carvalho'. No solst\xedcio de ver\xe3o, era cortado num rito especial, segurado com um pano branco e separado com uma foice de ouro. Na mitologia n\xf3rdica, o bom e amado deus Balder ficou a salvo quando a sua m\xe3e Frigg fez todas as coisas jurarem n\xe3o o ferir, mas tinha esquecido o visco, julgando-o inofensivo; o malvado Loki soube disso e mandou fazer uma flecha de visco, e pela m\xe3o do deus cego H\xf6d, Balder foi atingido por ela e morreu.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Viscum_album_2026_G1.jpg/330px-Viscum_album_2026_G1.jpg"},{id:"plant-119",emoji:"\ud83e\udd54",color:"#A67C52",name:"Patates",nameEn:"Potato",nameDe:"Kartoffel",nameEs:"Patata",nameFr:"Pomme de terre",nameJa:"\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2",namePt:"Batata",origin:"Maori Mitolojisi",originEn:"Maori Mythology",originDe:"Maori-Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda maor\xed",originFr:"Mythologie maorie",originJa:"\u30de\u30aa\u30ea\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia maori",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["besin","c\xf6mertlik","sebat","toprak g\xfcc\xfc"],propertiesEn:["nourishment","generosity","perseverance","earth-strength"],propertiesDe:["Nahrung","Gro\xdfz\xfcgigkeit","Beharrlichkeit","Erdkraft"],propertiesEs:["alimento","generosidad","perseverancia","fuerza de la tierra"],propertiesFr:["nourriture","g\xe9n\xe9rosit\xe9","pers\xe9v\xe9rance","force de la terre"],propertiesJa:["\u7ce7","\u5bdb\u5927\u3055","\u7c98\u308a\u5f37\u3055","\u5927\u5730\u306e\u529b"],propertiesPt:["alimento","generosidade","perseveran\xe7a","for\xe7a da terra"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xf6steri\u015fe de\u011fil, topra\u011f\u0131n alt\u0131ndaki sa\u011flam bir k\xf6k gibi sessiz de\u011ferine g\xfcven; ger\xe7ek bolluk \xe7o\u011fu zaman g\xf6z \xf6n\xfcnde olmayan emekte sakl\u0131d\u0131r. Patates sana payla\u015f\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \xe7o\u011falan bir c\xf6mertli\u011fin, herkese yeten bir besin oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, trust not in show but in your quiet worth, like a firm root beneath the soil; true abundance often hides in unseen labor. The potato whispers that a generosity which multiplies when shared is a nourishment enough for all.",dailyMessageDe:"Vertraue heute nicht auf den Schein, sondern auf deinen stillen Wert, wie eine feste Wurzel unter der Erde; wahre F\xfclle verbirgt sich oft in ungesehener M\xfche. Die Kartoffel fl\xfcstert, dass eine Gro\xdfz\xfcgigkeit, die sich beim Teilen vermehrt, eine Nahrung ist, die f\xfcr alle reicht.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, conf\xeda no en la apariencia, sino en tu valor silencioso, como una ra\xedz firme bajo la tierra; la verdadera abundancia suele ocultarse en el esfuerzo invisible. La patata susurra que una generosidad que se multiplica al compartirla es un alimento que alcanza para todos.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, fie-toi non \xe0 l'apparence mais \xe0 ta valeur silencieuse, comme une racine ferme sous la terre ; la vraie abondance se cache souvent dans le labeur invisible. La pomme de terre murmure qu'une g\xe9n\xe9rosit\xe9 qui se multiplie quand on la partage est une nourriture suffisante pour tous.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u898b\u304b\u3051\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u571f\u306e\u4e0b\u306e\u5805\u3044\u6839\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306a\u9759\u304b\u306a\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u771f\u306e\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u4eba\u76ee\u306b\u3064\u304b\u306c\u52b4\u82e6\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2\u306f\u3001\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u307b\u3069\u306b\u5897\u3048\u308b\u5bdb\u5927\u3055\u304c\u3001\u307f\u306a\u306b\u8db3\u308a\u308b\u7ce7\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, confie n\xe3o na apar\xeancia, mas no seu valor silencioso, como uma raiz firme sob o solo; a verdadeira abund\xe2ncia muitas vezes se esconde no trabalho invis\xedvel. A batata sussurra que uma generosidade que se multiplica quando partilhada \xe9 um alimento que basta para todos.",howToUse:"Patatesi ha\u015flay\u0131p ya da pi\u015firip besleyici ve payla\u015f\u0131lan bir yemek olarak haz\u0131rlayabilirsin. Bir patatesi karanl\u0131k bir k\xf6\u015fede filizlendirip topra\u011fa dikmek de sebat ve toprak g\xfcc\xfc niyetini onurland\u0131ran sade bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may boil or cook the potato into a nourishing dish to share. Sprouting a potato in a dark corner and planting it in the soil is also a simple gesture honoring an intention of perseverance and earth-strength.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die Kartoffel zu einem n\xe4hrenden Gericht zum Teilen kochen oder garen. Eine Kartoffel in einer dunklen Ecke keimen zu lassen und in die Erde zu setzen ist ebenfalls eine schlichte Geste, die eine Absicht von Beharrlichkeit und Erdkraft ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes hervir o cocinar la patata en un plato nutritivo para compartir. Hacer brotar una patata en un rinc\xf3n oscuro y plantarla en la tierra es tambi\xe9n un gesto sencillo que honra una intenci\xf3n de perseverancia y fuerza de la tierra.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux faire bouillir ou cuire la pomme de terre en un plat nourrissant \xe0 partager. Faire germer une pomme de terre dans un coin sombre et la planter dans la terre est aussi un geste simple qui honore une intention de pers\xe9v\xe9rance et de force de la terre.",howToUseJa:"\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2\u3092\u8339\u3067\u305f\u308a\u716e\u305f\u308a\u3057\u3066\u3001\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u6599\u7406\u306b\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2\u3092\u6697\u3044\u7247\u9685\u3067\u767a\u82bd\u3055\u305b\u3066\u571f\u306b\u690d\u3048\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u7c98\u308a\u5f37\u3055\u3068\u5927\u5730\u306e\u529b\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3064\u3064\u307e\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode ferver ou cozinhar a batata num prato nutritivo para partilhar. Fazer uma batata brotar em um canto escuro e plant\xe1-la na terra \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto simples que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de perseveran\xe7a e for\xe7a da terra.",affirmation:"Sessiz de\u011ferime g\xfcveniyorum, c\xf6mertli\u011fim payla\u015ft\u0131k\xe7a \xe7o\u011fal\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I trust my quiet worth, and my generosity multiplies as I share it.",affirmationDe:"Ich vertraue meinem stillen Wert, und meine Gro\xdfz\xfcgigkeit vermehrt sich, indem ich sie teile.",affirmationEs:"Conf\xedo en mi valor silencioso, y mi generosidad se multiplica al compartirla.",affirmationFr:"Je me fie \xe0 ma valeur silencieuse, et ma g\xe9n\xe9rosit\xe9 se multiplie \xe0 mesure que je la partage.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u9759\u304b\u306a\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u3001\u5bdb\u5927\u3055\u306f\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u307b\u3069\u306b\u5897\u3048\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Confio no meu valor silencioso, e a minha generosidade se multiplica \xe0 medida que a partilho.",myth:"Yeni Zelanda'da ya\u015fayan Maorilerin mitolojik kahraman\u0131 Rongo-Maui, patatesi tanr\u0131lardan \xe7alarak insanlara verdi. G\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcnde ya\u015fayan karde\u015fi Whanaui patatesi yaln\u0131zca kendisi i\xe7in sakl\u0131yordu; Maui gizlice g\xf6\u011fe \xe7\u0131k\u0131p karde\u015finin saklad\u0131\u011f\u0131 patatesi \xe7ald\u0131 ve bu patatesle kar\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 d\xf6lledi. Bir s\xfcre sonra kad\u0131n suyun ak\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131na do\u011fum yapt\u0131; bu suyun sulad\u0131\u011f\u0131 topraklar boylu boyunca patates tarlas\u0131na d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc. B\xf6ylece Maui sayesinde patates, insanlar\u0131n yararland\u0131\u011f\u0131 \xf6nemli bir besin oldu.",mythEn:"Rongo-Maui, the mythological hero of the Maori of New Zealand, stole the potato from the gods and gave it to humankind. His brother Whanaui, who dwelt in the sky, kept the potato only for himself; Maui secretly climbed to the heavens, stole the potato his brother had hidden, and with this potato made his wife conceive. In time the woman gave birth into the flowing water; the lands this water watered became, along their whole length, fields of potatoes. Thus, through Maui, the potato became an important food that humankind could enjoy.",mythDe:"Rongo-Maui, der mythologische Held der Maori Neuseelands, stahl die Kartoffel von den G\xf6ttern und gab sie der Menschheit. Sein Bruder Whanaui, der im Himmel wohnte, behielt die Kartoffel nur f\xfcr sich; Maui stieg heimlich in den Himmel, stahl die Kartoffel, die sein Bruder verborgen hatte, und lie\xdf mit dieser Kartoffel seine Frau empfangen. Nach einiger Zeit gebar die Frau in das flie\xdfende Wasser hinein; die L\xe4nder, die dieses Wasser tr\xe4nkte, wurden auf ihrer ganzen L\xe4nge zu Kartoffelfeldern. So wurde durch Maui die Kartoffel zu einer wichtigen Nahrung, die die Menschheit genie\xdfen konnte.",mythEs:"Rongo-Maui, el h\xe9roe mitol\xf3gico de los maor\xedes de Nueva Zelanda, rob\xf3 la patata a los dioses y la dio a la humanidad. Su hermano Whanaui, que moraba en el cielo, guardaba la patata solo para s\xed; Maui subi\xf3 a escondidas a los cielos, rob\xf3 la patata que su hermano hab\xeda escondido y con esta patata hizo concebir a su esposa. Con el tiempo la mujer dio a luz en la corriente del agua; las tierras que esta agua reg\xf3 se volvieron, a todo lo largo, campos de patatas. As\xed, por medio de Maui, la patata se convirti\xf3 en un alimento importante del que la humanidad pudo disfrutar.",mythFr:"Rongo-Maui, le h\xe9ros mythologique des Maoris de Nouvelle-Z\xe9lande, d\xe9roba la pomme de terre aux dieux et la donna \xe0 l'humanit\xe9. Son fr\xe8re Whanaui, qui demeurait dans le ciel, gardait la pomme de terre pour lui seul ; Maui monta en secret aux cieux, d\xe9roba la pomme de terre que son fr\xe8re avait cach\xe9e et, avec cette pomme de terre, fit concevoir sa femme. Avec le temps, la femme enfanta dans le courant de l'eau ; les terres que cette eau arrosa devinrent, sur toute leur longueur, des champs de pommes de terre. Ainsi, gr\xe2ce \xe0 Maui, la pomme de terre devint une nourriture importante dont l'humanit\xe9 put profiter.",mythJa:"\u30cb\u30e5\u30fc\u30b8\u30fc\u30e9\u30f3\u30c9\u306e\u30de\u30aa\u30ea\u306e\u795e\u8a71\u7684\u82f1\u96c4\u30ed\u30f3\u30b4\uff1d\u30de\u30a6\u30a4\u306f\u3001\u795e\u3005\u304b\u3089\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2\u3092\u76d7\u3093\u3067\u4eba\u3005\u306b\u4e0e\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u5929\u306b\u4f4f\u3080\u5144\u30ef\u30ca\u30a6\u30a4\u306f\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2\u3092\u81ea\u5206\u3060\u3051\u306e\u3082\u306e\u3068\u3057\u3066\u96a0\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30de\u30a6\u30a4\u306f\u3072\u305d\u304b\u306b\u5929\u306b\u4e0a\u308a\u3001\u5144\u304c\u96a0\u3057\u305f\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2\u3092\u76d7\u307f\u3001\u305d\u306e\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2\u3067\u59bb\u3092\u8eab\u3054\u3082\u3089\u305b\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3084\u304c\u3066\u5973\u306f\u6d41\u308c\u308b\u6c34\u306e\u4e2d\u3078\u7523\u307f\u843d\u3068\u3057\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6c34\u304c\u6f64\u3057\u305f\u571f\u5730\u306f\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5168\u9577\u306b\u308f\u305f\u3063\u3066\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2\u7551\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u30de\u30a6\u30a4\u306e\u304a\u304b\u3052\u3067\u3001\u30b8\u30e3\u30ac\u30a4\u30e2\u306f\u4eba\u3005\u304c\u4eab\u53d7\u3059\u308b\u5927\u5207\u306a\u7ce7\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Rongo-Maui, o her\xf3i mitol\xf3gico dos maoris da Nova Zel\xe2ndia, roubou a batata dos deuses e a deu \xe0 humanidade. Seu irm\xe3o Whanaui, que morava no c\xe9u, guardava a batata s\xf3 para si; Maui subiu \xe0s escondidas aos c\xe9us, roubou a batata que o irm\xe3o havia escondido e, com esta batata, fez a sua esposa conceber. Com o tempo, a mulher deu \xe0 luz na corrente da \xe1gua; as terras que essa \xe1gua regou tornaram-se, em todo o seu comprimento, campos de batatas. Assim, por meio de Maui, a batata tornou-se um alimento importante de que a humanidade p\xf4de desfrutar.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Patates.jpg/330px-Patates.jpg"},{id:"plant-120",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3e",color:"#D8C77A",name:"Pirin\xe7",nameEn:"Rice",nameDe:"Reis",nameEs:"Arroz",nameFr:"Riz",nameJa:"\u7c73",namePt:"Arroz",origin:"Japon \u015einto Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Japanese Shinto Tradition",originDe:"Japanische Shinto-Tradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n sinto\xedsta japonesa",originFr:"Tradition shinto japonaise",originJa:"\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u795e\u9053\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o xinto\xedsta japonesa",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Solar Pleksus \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u592a\u967d\u795e\u7d4c\u53e2\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["bereket","besin","sab\u0131r","kutsall\u0131k","s\xfck\xfbnet"],propertiesEn:["abundance","nourishment","patience","sacredness","serenity"],propertiesDe:["F\xfclle","Nahrung","Geduld","Heiligkeit","Gelassenheit"],propertiesEs:["abundancia","alimento","paciencia","sacralidad","serenidad"],propertiesFr:["abondance","nourriture","patience","sacralit\xe9","s\xe9r\xe9nit\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u8c4a\u7a63","\u7ce7","\u5fcd\u8010","\u8056\u6027","\u9759\u3051\u3055"],propertiesPt:["abund\xe2ncia","alimento","paci\xeancia","sacralidade","serenidade"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn \xf6fkeye so\u011fukkanl\u0131l\u0131kla kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131k ver; bereket \xe7o\u011fu zaman sabreden ve s\xfck\xfbnetini koruyan kalbin tarlas\u0131nda ye\u015ferir. Pirin\xe7 sana her tanenin sessiz bir emekle olgunla\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131, sabr\u0131n en bol hasad\u0131 getirdi\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, meet anger with composure; abundance often grows in the field of a heart that is patient and keeps its calm. Rice whispers that each grain ripens through quiet labor, and that patience brings the most plentiful harvest.",dailyMessageDe:"Begegne heute dem Zorn mit Gelassenheit; F\xfclle w\xe4chst oft auf dem Feld eines Herzens, das geduldig ist und seine Ruhe bewahrt. Der Reis fl\xfcstert, dass jedes Korn durch stille M\xfche reift und dass Geduld die reichste Ernte bringt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, responde a la ira con serenidad; la abundancia suele crecer en el campo de un coraz\xf3n paciente que conserva su calma. El arroz susurra que cada grano madura con un esfuerzo silencioso, y que la paciencia trae la cosecha m\xe1s abundante.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, r\xe9ponds \xe0 la col\xe8re par le calme ; l'abondance pousse souvent dans le champ d'un c\u0153ur patient qui garde son sang-froid. Le riz murmure que chaque grain m\xfbrit par un labeur silencieux, et que la patience apporte la plus abondante des moissons.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u6012\u308a\u306b\u51b7\u9759\u3055\u3067\u5fdc\u3048\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u5fcd\u8010\u3065\u3088\u304f\u843d\u3061\u7740\u304d\u3092\u4fdd\u3064\u5fc3\u306e\u7530\u3067\u5b9f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u7c73\u306f\u3001\u4e00\u7c92\u3072\u3068\u3064\u3076\u304c\u9759\u304b\u306a\u52b4\u82e6\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u719f\u3057\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3053\u305d\u304c\u6700\u3082\u8c4a\u304b\u306a\u5b9f\u308a\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, responda \xe0 raiva com serenidade; a abund\xe2ncia muitas vezes cresce no campo de um cora\xe7\xe3o paciente que mant\xe9m a sua calma. O arroz sussurra que cada gr\xe3o amadurece por um trabalho silencioso, e que a paci\xeancia traz a colheita mais farta.",howToUse:"Pirinci sab\u0131rla pi\u015firip besleyici ve payla\u015f\u0131lan bir yemek olarak haz\u0131rlayabilirsin. Bir avu\xe7 pirinci bir k\xe2seye koyup masanda tutmak ya da bir niyetle topra\u011fa serpmek de bereket ve s\xfck\xfbnet niyetini onurland\u0131ran sade bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may cook rice with patience into a nourishing dish to share. Placing a handful of rice in a bowl on your table or scattering it on the earth with an intention is also a simple gesture honoring an intention of abundance and serenity.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst Reis geduldig zu einem n\xe4hrenden Gericht zum Teilen kochen. Eine Handvoll Reis in einer Schale auf deinem Tisch oder mit einer Absicht auf die Erde zu streuen ist ebenfalls eine schlichte Geste, die eine Absicht von F\xfclle und Gelassenheit ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes cocinar el arroz con paciencia en un plato nutritivo para compartir. Colocar un pu\xf1ado de arroz en un cuenco sobre la mesa o esparcirlo en la tierra con una intenci\xf3n es tambi\xe9n un gesto sencillo que honra una intenci\xf3n de abundancia y serenidad.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux cuire le riz avec patience en un plat nourrissant \xe0 partager. Placer une poign\xe9e de riz dans un bol sur ta table ou le r\xe9pandre sur la terre avec une intention est aussi un geste simple qui honore une intention d'abondance et de s\xe9r\xe9nit\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u7c73\u3092\u8f9b\u62b1\u3065\u3088\u304f\u708a\u3044\u3066\u3001\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u6599\u7406\u306b\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u306e\u7c73\u3092\u5668\u306b\u5165\u308c\u3066\u673a\u306b\u7f6e\u3044\u305f\u308a\u3001\u610f\u56f3\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u571f\u306b\u6492\u3044\u305f\u308a\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u9759\u3051\u3055\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3064\u3064\u307e\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode cozinhar o arroz com paci\xeancia num prato nutritivo para partilhar. Colocar um punhado de arroz em uma tigela sobre a mesa ou espalh\xe1-lo na terra com uma inten\xe7\xe3o \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto simples que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de abund\xe2ncia e serenidade.",affirmation:"\xd6fkeye so\u011fukkanl\u0131l\u0131kla kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131k veriyorum, sabr\u0131m bol bir bereket getiriyor.",affirmationEn:"I meet anger with composure, and my patience brings a plentiful abundance.",affirmationDe:"Ich begegne dem Zorn mit Gelassenheit, und meine Geduld bringt eine reiche F\xfclle.",affirmationEs:"Respondo a la ira con serenidad, y mi paciencia trae una abundancia copiosa.",affirmationFr:"Je r\xe9ponds \xe0 la col\xe8re par le calme, et ma patience apporte une abondance copieuse.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6012\u308a\u306b\u51b7\u9759\u3055\u3067\u5fdc\u3048\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u304c\u8c4a\u304b\u306a\u5b9f\u308a\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u3002",affirmationPt:"Respondo \xe0 raiva com serenidade, e a minha paci\xeancia traz uma abund\xe2ncia farta.",myth:"Japon \u015einto inanc\u0131nda pirin\xe7 tanr\u0131s\u0131 \u0130nari, bereketin ve bollu\u011fun simgesidir; haberci tilkileri arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla insanlarla ileti\u015fim kurar ve pirin\xe7 ekimi s\u0131ras\u0131nda ondan bereket istenir. Bir ba\u015fka anlat\u0131da g\xfcne\u015f tanr\u0131\xe7a Amaterasu, k\xf6t\xfc huylu karde\u015fi tarlalar\u0131n\u0131 talan etti\u011finde bile so\u011fukkanl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 korur; karde\u015fi en sonunda haddini a\u015f\u0131nca tanr\u0131\xe7a bir kaya ma\u011faras\u0131na kapan\u0131r ve d\xfcnyadan g\xfcne\u015f \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131 \xe7ekilir. Tanr\u0131lar m\xfczik ve \u015fenlikle onu ma\u011faradan \xe7\u0131kar\u0131nca ya\u015fam yeniden canlan\u0131r ve Amaterasu'nun yaratt\u0131\u011f\u0131 pirin\xe7 tarlalar\u0131, onun ba\u011f\u0131\u015flad\u0131\u011f\u0131 bereketle insanlar\u0131 doyurmaya devam eder.",mythEn:"In Japanese Shinto belief, the rice god Inari is the symbol of fertility and abundance; he communicates with people through his messenger foxes, and his blessing is asked at the planting of rice. In another tale, the sun goddess Amaterasu keeps her composure even when her ill-tempered brother lays waste to her fields; when her brother at last goes too far, the goddess shuts herself in a rock cave, and sunlight is withdrawn from the world. When the gods draw her from the cave with music and festivity, life revives, and the rice fields Amaterasu created continue to feed the people with the abundance she bestows.",mythDe:"Im japanischen Shinto-Glauben ist der Reisgott Inari das Sinnbild von Fruchtbarkeit und F\xfclle; er verst\xe4ndigt sich mit den Menschen durch seine Botenf\xfcchse, und beim Pflanzen des Reises wird um seinen Segen gebeten. In einer anderen Erz\xe4hlung bewahrt die Sonneng\xf6ttin Amaterasu ihre Gelassenheit, selbst als ihr \xfcbellauniger Bruder ihre Felder verw\xfcstet; als ihr Bruder schlie\xdflich zu weit geht, schlie\xdft sich die G\xf6ttin in eine Felsh\xf6hle ein, und das Sonnenlicht wird der Welt entzogen. Als die G\xf6tter sie mit Musik und Festlichkeit aus der H\xf6hle locken, erwacht das Leben wieder, und die Reisfelder, die Amaterasu schuf, n\xe4hren die Menschen weiter mit der F\xfclle, die sie schenkt.",mythEs:"En la creencia sinto\xedsta japonesa, el dios del arroz Inari es el s\xedmbolo de la fertilidad y la abundancia; se comunica con la gente mediante sus zorros mensajeros, y se le pide su bendici\xf3n al sembrar el arroz. En otro relato, la diosa del sol Amaterasu conserva su serenidad aun cuando su hermano de mal genio asola sus campos; cuando el hermano al fin se excede, la diosa se encierra en una cueva de roca, y la luz del sol se retira del mundo. Cuando los dioses la sacan de la cueva con m\xfasica y fiesta, la vida revive, y los campos de arroz que Amaterasu cre\xf3 siguen alimentando a la gente con la abundancia que ella concede.",mythFr:"Dans la croyance shinto japonaise, le dieu du riz Inari est le symbole de la fertilit\xe9 et de l'abondance ; il communique avec les humains par ses renards messagers, et l'on demande sa b\xe9n\xe9diction lors du repiquage du riz. Dans un autre r\xe9cit, la d\xe9esse du soleil Amaterasu garde son calme m\xeame lorsque son fr\xe8re de mauvaise humeur ravage ses champs ; quand le fr\xe8re finit par aller trop loin, la d\xe9esse s'enferme dans une grotte de roche, et la lumi\xe8re du soleil se retire du monde. Lorsque les dieux la tirent de la grotte par la musique et la f\xeate, la vie rena\xeet, et les rizi\xe8res cr\xe9\xe9es par Amaterasu continuent de nourrir les humains de l'abondance qu'elle accorde.",mythJa:"\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u795e\u9053\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u7a32\u306e\u795e\u30a4\u30ca\u30ea\u306f\u591a\u7523\u3068\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3001\u4f7f\u3044\u306e\u72d0\u3092\u901a\u3057\u3066\u4eba\u3005\u3068\u901a\u3058\u3001\u7a32\u3092\u690d\u3048\u308b\u3068\u304d\u306b\u305d\u306e\u6075\u307f\u304c\u4e5e\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5225\u306e\u7269\u8a9e\u3067\u306f\u3001\u592a\u967d\u306e\u5973\u795e\u30a2\u30de\u30c6\u30e9\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u6c17\u6027\u306e\u8352\u3044\u5f1f\u304c\u7530\u3092\u8352\u3089\u3057\u3066\u3082\u306a\u304a\u51b7\u9759\u3055\u3092\u4fdd\u3061\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5f1f\u304c\u3064\u3044\u306b\u5ea6\u3092\u8d8a\u3059\u3068\u3001\u5973\u795e\u306f\u5ca9\u5c4b\u306b\u9589\u3058\u3053\u3082\u308a\u3001\u4e16\u754c\u304b\u3089\u592a\u967d\u306e\u5149\u304c\u6d88\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002\u795e\u3005\u304c\u97f3\u697d\u3068\u796d\u308a\u3067\u5973\u795e\u3092\u5ca9\u5c4b\u304b\u3089\u8a98\u3044\u51fa\u3059\u3068\u3001\u751f\u547d\u304c\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u3088\u307f\u304c\u3048\u308a\u3001\u30a2\u30de\u30c6\u30e9\u30b9\u304c\u5275\u3063\u305f\u7a32\u7530\u306f\u3001\u5f7c\u5973\u304c\u6388\u3051\u308b\u8c4a\u7a63\u3067\u4eba\u3005\u3092\u990a\u3044\u3064\u3065\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na cren\xe7a xinto\xedsta japonesa, o deus do arroz Inari \xe9 o s\xedmbolo da fertilidade e da abund\xe2ncia; ele se comunica com as pessoas por meio das suas raposas mensageiras, e a sua b\xean\xe7\xe3o \xe9 pedida no plantio do arroz. Em outro relato, a deusa do sol Amaterasu mant\xe9m a sua serenidade mesmo quando o seu irm\xe3o de mau g\xeanio devasta os seus campos; quando o irm\xe3o enfim passa dos limites, a deusa se fecha numa caverna de rocha, e a luz do sol se retira do mundo. Quando os deuses a tiram da caverna com m\xfasica e festa, a vida revive, e os campos de arroz que Amaterasu criou continuam a alimentar as pessoas com a abund\xe2ncia que ela concede.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/20201102.Hengnan.Hybrid_rice_Sanyou-1.6.jpg/330px-20201102.Hengnan.Hybrid_rice_Sanyou-1.6.jpg"},{id:"plant-121",emoji:"\ud83c\udf4a",color:"#F39237",name:"Portakal",nameEn:"Orange",nameDe:"Orange",nameEs:"Naranja",nameFr:"Orange",nameJa:"\u30aa\u30ec\u30f3\u30b8",namePt:"Laranja",origin:"Japon Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Japanese Tradition",originDe:"Japanische Tradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n japonesa",originFr:"Tradition japonaise",originJa:"\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o japonesa",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u4ed9\u9aa8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacral",properties:["ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k","ne\u015fe","bolluk","\xf6zveri","tatl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["devotion","joy","abundance","dedication","sweetness"],propertiesDe:["Hingabe","Freude","F\xfclle","Aufopferung","S\xfc\xdfe"],propertiesEs:["devoci\xf3n","alegr\xeda","abundancia","entrega","dulzura"],propertiesFr:["d\xe9votion","joie","abondance","d\xe9vouement","douceur"],propertiesJa:["\u732e\u8eab","\u559c\u3073","\u8c4a\u304b\u3055","\u732e\u8eab\u7684\u52aa\u529b","\u7518\u3055"],propertiesPt:["devo\xe7\xe3o","alegria","abund\xe2ncia","dedica\xe7\xe3o","do\xe7ura"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn sevdi\u011fin bir \u015fey i\xe7in g\xf6sterdi\u011fin eme\u011fin asla bo\u015fa gitmedi\u011fini hat\u0131rla; bazen meyveni ge\xe7 teslim etsen de, o \xf6zveri bir koku gibi geride kal\u0131r. Portakal sana sadakatle ta\u015f\u0131nan bir niyetin, parlak ve tatl\u0131 bir arma\u011fana d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, remember that the effort you give for something you love is never wasted; even if you deliver your fruit late, that devotion lingers like a fragrance. The orange whispers that an intention carried with loyalty turns into a bright and sweet gift.",dailyMessageDe:"Erinnere dich heute daran, dass die M\xfche, die du f\xfcr etwas gibst, das du liebst, niemals vergebens ist; selbst wenn du deine Frucht sp\xe4t lieferst, bleibt diese Hingabe wie ein Duft zur\xfcck. Die Orange fl\xfcstert, dass eine mit Treue getragene Absicht zu einem hellen und s\xfc\xdfen Geschenk wird.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, recuerda que el esfuerzo que das por algo que amas nunca se pierde; aunque entregues tu fruto tarde, esa entrega permanece como una fragancia. La naranja susurra que una intenci\xf3n llevada con lealtad se convierte en un regalo brillante y dulce.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, souviens-toi que l'effort que tu donnes pour ce que tu aimes n'est jamais vain ; m\xeame si tu livres ton fruit tard, ce d\xe9vouement demeure comme un parfum. L'orange murmure qu'une intention port\xe9e avec loyaut\xe9 se change en un pr\xe9sent \xe9clatant et doux.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u611b\u3059\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6ce8\u3050\u52aa\u529b\u304c\u6c7a\u3057\u3066\u7121\u99c4\u306b\u306a\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u305f\u3068\u3048\u5b9f\u3092\u9045\u304f\u5c4a\u3051\u3066\u3082\u3001\u305d\u306e\u732e\u8eab\u306f\u9999\u308a\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u6b8b\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30aa\u30ec\u30f3\u30b8\u306f\u3001\u8aa0\u5b9f\u306b\u904b\u3070\u308c\u305f\u610f\u56f3\u304c\u3001\u660e\u308b\u304f\u7518\u3044\u8d08\u308a\u3082\u306e\u306b\u5909\u308f\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, lembre-se de que o esfor\xe7o que voc\xea d\xe1 por algo que ama nunca \xe9 em v\xe3o; mesmo que entregue o seu fruto tarde, essa dedica\xe7\xe3o permanece como uma fragr\xe2ncia. A laranja sussurra que uma inten\xe7\xe3o carregada com lealdade se transforma em um presente brilhante e doce.",howToUse:"Olgun bir portakal\u0131 taze yiyebilir ya da suyunu s\u0131k\u0131p ne\u015fe ve bolluk niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Kabu\u011funu kurutup mek\xe2n\u0131na tatl\u0131 bir koku katmak da ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k ve sevin\xe7 niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may eat a ripe orange fresh or squeeze its juice to accompany an intention of joy and abundance. Drying its peel to bring a sweet fragrance to your space is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of devotion and gladness.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst eine reife Orange frisch essen oder ihren Saft pressen, um eine Absicht von Freude und F\xfclle zu begleiten. Ihre Schale zu trocknen, um deinem Raum einen s\xfc\xdfen Duft zu verleihen, ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Hingabe und Freude ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes comer una naranja madura fresca o exprimir su zumo para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de alegr\xeda y abundancia. Secar su c\xe1scara para dar a tu espacio una dulce fragancia es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de devoci\xf3n y gozo.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux manger une orange m\xfbre fra\xeeche ou presser son jus pour accompagner une intention de joie et d'abondance. Faire s\xe9cher son \xe9corce pour donner \xe0 ton espace un doux parfum est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de d\xe9votion et de joie.",howToUseJa:"\u719f\u3057\u305f\u30aa\u30ec\u30f3\u30b8\u3092\u751f\u306e\u307e\u307e\u98df\u3079\u305f\u308a\u3001\u679c\u6c41\u3092\u7d5e\u3063\u305f\u308a\u3057\u3066\u3001\u559c\u3073\u3068\u8c4a\u304b\u3055\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u76ae\u3092\u5e72\u3057\u3066\u7a7a\u9593\u306b\u7518\u3044\u9999\u308a\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u732e\u8eab\u3068\u559c\u3073\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode comer uma laranja madura fresca ou espremer o seu suco para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de alegria e abund\xe2ncia. Secar a sua casca para trazer uma fragr\xe2ncia doce ao seu espa\xe7o \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de devo\xe7\xe3o e alegria.",affirmation:"Sevdi\u011fim i\xe7in verdi\u011fim emek bo\u015fa gitmiyor, sadakatim tatl\u0131 bir arma\u011fana d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcyor.",affirmationEn:"The effort I give for what I love is never wasted, and my loyalty turns into a sweet gift.",affirmationDe:"Die M\xfche, die ich f\xfcr das gebe, was ich liebe, ist nie vergebens, und meine Treue wird zu einem s\xfc\xdfen Geschenk.",affirmationEs:"El esfuerzo que doy por lo que amo nunca se pierde, y mi lealtad se vuelve un regalo dulce.",affirmationFr:"L'effort que je donne pour ce que j'aime n'est jamais vain, et ma loyaut\xe9 devient un doux pr\xe9sent.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u304c\u611b\u3059\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6ce8\u3050\u52aa\u529b\u306f\u6c7a\u3057\u3066\u7121\u99c4\u306b\u306a\u3089\u305a\u3001\u8aa0\u5b9f\u3055\u306f\u7518\u3044\u8d08\u308a\u3082\u306e\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"O esfor\xe7o que dou por aquilo que amo nunca \xe9 em v\xe3o, e a minha lealdade se torna um presente doce.",myth:"Japon s\xf6ylencesinde efsanevi kral Sui-nin, b\xfcy\xfck kahraman Tajima-mori'yi yan\u0131na \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131p ondan 'Ebedi Ho\u015f Kokulu A\u011fa\xe7'\u0131 bulup kutsal meyvesini getirmesini ister. Tajima-mori uzun bir aray\u0131\u015ftan sonra a\u011fac\u0131 bulup meyvesini kopar\u0131r ve \xfclkesine d\xf6ner; ne var ki kral o s\u0131rada \xf6lm\xfc\u015ft\xfcr. Kahraman meyveyi ikiye b\xf6ler, bir par\xe7as\u0131n\u0131 imparatori\xe7eye sunar, kalan\u0131n\u0131 kral\u0131n mezar\u0131na g\xf6t\xfcr\xfcr ve meyveyi zaman\u0131nda kral\u0131na yeti\u015ftiremedi\u011fi i\xe7in kederinden, mezar\u0131n ba\u015f\u0131nda yas tutarak \xf6l\xfcr. Bu 'Ebedi Ho\u015f Kokulu A\u011fa\xe7' portakal a\u011fac\u0131, kral\u0131n istedi\u011fi meyve ise bug\xfcn t\xfcm d\xfcnyan\u0131n bildi\u011fi portakald\u0131r.",mythEn:"In a Japanese legend, the legendary king Sui-nin summons the great hero Tajima-mori and bids him find the 'Tree of Everlasting Fragrance' and bring back its sacred fruit. After a long search, Tajima-mori finds the tree, plucks its fruit, and returns to his land; but the king has died in the meantime. The hero splits the fruit in two, offers one part to the empress, and carries the rest to the king's tomb; and because he could not bring the fruit to his king in time, he dies of grief, mourning at the graveside. This 'Tree of Everlasting Fragrance' is the orange tree, and the fruit the king desired is the orange known to all the world today.",mythDe:"In einer japanischen Legende ruft der sagenhafte K\xf6nig Sui-nin den gro\xdfen Helden Tajima-mori zu sich und tr\xe4gt ihm auf, den 'Baum des ewigen Wohlgeruchs' zu finden und seine heilige Frucht zu bringen. Nach langer Suche findet Tajima-mori den Baum, pfl\xfcckt seine Frucht und kehrt in sein Land zur\xfcck; doch der K\xf6nig ist inzwischen gestorben. Der Held teilt die Frucht in zwei, bietet einen Teil der Kaiserin dar und bringt den Rest zum Grab des K\xf6nigs; und weil er die Frucht seinem K\xf6nig nicht rechtzeitig bringen konnte, stirbt er aus Kummer, w\xe4hrend er am Grab trauert. Dieser 'Baum des ewigen Wohlgeruchs' ist der Orangenbaum, und die Frucht, die der K\xf6nig begehrte, ist die heute der ganzen Welt bekannte Orange.",mythEs:"En una leyenda japonesa, el legendario rey Sui-nin convoca al gran h\xe9roe Tajima-mori y le encarga hallar el '\xc1rbol de la Fragancia Eterna' y traer su fruto sagrado. Tras una larga b\xfasqueda, Tajima-mori encuentra el \xe1rbol, arranca su fruto y vuelve a su tierra; pero el rey ha muerto entretanto. El h\xe9roe parte el fruto en dos, ofrece una parte a la emperatriz y lleva el resto a la tumba del rey; y porque no pudo llevar el fruto a su rey a tiempo, muere de pena, llorando junto a la tumba. Este '\xc1rbol de la Fragancia Eterna' es el naranjo, y el fruto que el rey deseaba es la naranja que hoy conoce todo el mundo.",mythFr:"Dans une l\xe9gende japonaise, le l\xe9gendaire roi Sui-nin convoque le grand h\xe9ros Tajima-mori et lui ordonne de trouver l'\xab Arbre de l'\xc9ternel Parfum \xbb et d'en rapporter le fruit sacr\xe9. Apr\xe8s une longue qu\xeate, Tajima-mori trouve l'arbre, en cueille le fruit et revient dans son pays ; mais le roi est mort entre-temps. Le h\xe9ros partage le fruit en deux, en offre une part \xe0 l'imp\xe9ratrice et porte le reste au tombeau du roi ; et parce qu'il n'a pu apporter le fruit \xe0 son roi \xe0 temps, il meurt de chagrin, en deuil au bord de la tombe. Cet \xab Arbre de l'\xc9ternel Parfum \xbb est l'oranger, et le fruit que le roi d\xe9sirait est l'orange que conna\xeet aujourd'hui le monde entier.",mythJa:"\u3042\u308b\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u4f1d\u8aac\u3067\u306f\u3001\u4f1d\u8aac\u306e\u738b\u30b9\u30a4\u30cb\u30f3\u304c\u5927\u3044\u306a\u308b\u82f1\u96c4\u30bf\u30b8\u30de\u30e2\u30ea\u3092\u547c\u3073\u5bc4\u305b\u3001\u300e\u6c38\u9060\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306e\u6728\u300f\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u3066\u305d\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u5b9f\u3092\u6301\u3061\u5e30\u308b\u3088\u3046\u547d\u3058\u307e\u3059\u3002\u9577\u3044\u63a2\u6c42\u306e\u672b\u3001\u30bf\u30b8\u30de\u30e2\u30ea\u306f\u6728\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5b9f\u3092\u3082\u3044\u3067\u56fd\u3078\u5e30\u308a\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u9593\u306b\u738b\u306f\u4ea1\u304f\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u82f1\u96c4\u306f\u5b9f\u3092\u4e8c\u3064\u306b\u5206\u3051\u3001\u4e00\u65b9\u3092\u7687\u540e\u306b\u6367\u3052\u3001\u6b8b\u308a\u3092\u738b\u306e\u5893\u3078\u904b\u3073\u3001\u5b9f\u3092\u9593\u306b\u5408\u308f\u305b\u3066\u738b\u306b\u5c4a\u3051\u3089\u308c\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u5606\u304d\u306e\u3042\u307e\u308a\u3001\u5893\u306e\u304b\u305f\u308f\u3089\u3067\u55aa\u306b\u670d\u3057\u306a\u304c\u3089\u6b7b\u306b\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3053\u306e\u300e\u6c38\u9060\u306e\u9999\u308a\u306e\u6728\u300f\u306f\u30aa\u30ec\u30f3\u30b8\u306e\u6728\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u738b\u304c\u671b\u3093\u3060\u5b9f\u306f\u3001\u4eca\u65e5\u3067\u306f\u4e16\u754c\u3058\u3085\u3046\u304c\u77e5\u308b\u30aa\u30ec\u30f3\u30b8\u3067\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Numa lenda japonesa, o lend\xe1rio rei Sui-nin convoca o grande her\xf3i Tajima-mori e lhe ordena encontrar a '\xc1rvore da Fragr\xe2ncia Eterna' e trazer o seu fruto sagrado. Ap\xf3s uma longa busca, Tajima-mori encontra a \xe1rvore, colhe o seu fruto e volta \xe0 sua terra; mas o rei morreu nesse meio-tempo. O her\xf3i parte o fruto em dois, oferece uma parte \xe0 imperatriz e leva o resto ao t\xfamulo do rei; e porque n\xe3o p\xf4de levar o fruto ao seu rei a tempo, morre de pesar, de luto \xe0 beira do t\xfamulo. Esta '\xc1rvore da Fragr\xe2ncia Eterna' \xe9 a laranjeira, e o fruto que o rei desejava \xe9 a laranja que hoje todo o mundo conhece.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/OrangeBloss_wb.jpg/330px-OrangeBloss_wb.jpg"},{id:"plant-122",emoji:"\ud83c\udf38",color:"#D4A017",name:"Safran",nameEn:"Saffron",nameDe:"Safran",nameEs:"Azafr\xe1n",nameFr:"Safran",nameJa:"\u30b5\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3",namePt:"A\xe7afr\xe3o",origin:"Antik Yunan & Anadolu (Lidya)",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Anatolia (Lydia)",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & Anatolien (Lydien)",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y Anatolia (Lidia)",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et Anatolie (Lydie)",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\uff08\u30ea\u30c7\u30a3\u30a2\uff09",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e Anat\xf3lia (L\xeddia)",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Solar Pleksus \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Solar Plexus Chakra",chakraDe:"Solarplexuschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Plexo Solar",chakraFr:"Chakra du Plexus Solaire",chakraJa:"\u592a\u967d\u795e\u7d4c\u53e2\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra do Plexo Solar",properties:["de\u011fer","dirili\u015f","\u0131\u015f\u0131k","tutku","k\u0131ymet"],propertiesEn:["worth","resurrection","light","passion","preciousness"],propertiesDe:["Wert","Auferstehung","Licht","Leidenschaft","Kostbarkeit"],propertiesEs:["valor","resurrecci\xf3n","luz","pasi\xf3n","preciosidad"],propertiesFr:["valeur","r\xe9surrection","lumi\xe8re","passion","pr\xe9ciosit\xe9"],propertiesJa:["\u4fa1\u5024","\u5fa9\u6d3b","\u5149","\u60c5\u71b1","\u5c0a\u3055"],propertiesPt:["valor","ressurrei\xe7\xe3o","luz","paix\xe3o","preciosidade"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama de\u011ferli olan\u0131n k\u0131ymetini bil; en parlak g\xfczellik \xe7o\u011fu zaman ince, narin bir telde sakl\u0131d\u0131r. Safran sana en uzun k\u0131\u015f\u0131n ard\u0131ndan gelen bahar\u0131n, seni \xf6l\xfcm uykusundan uyand\u0131ran bir \u0131\u015f\u0131k ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, know the worth of what is small yet precious; the brightest beauty often hides in a fine, delicate thread. Saffron whispers that the spring which comes after the longest winter carries a light that wakes you from the sleep of death.",dailyMessageDe:"Erkenne heute den Wert dessen, was klein, doch kostbar ist; die strahlendste Sch\xf6nheit verbirgt sich oft in einem feinen, zarten Faden. Der Safran fl\xfcstert, dass der Fr\xfchling, der nach dem l\xe4ngsten Winter kommt, ein Licht tr\xe4gt, das dich aus dem Schlaf des Todes weckt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, conoce el valor de lo que es peque\xf1o pero precioso; la belleza m\xe1s brillante suele ocultarse en un hilo fino y delicado. El azafr\xe1n susurra que la primavera que llega tras el invierno m\xe1s largo trae una luz que te despierta del sue\xf1o de la muerte.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, connais la valeur de ce qui est petit mais pr\xe9cieux ; la beaut\xe9 la plus \xe9clatante se cache souvent dans un fil fin et d\xe9licat. Le safran murmure que le printemps qui vient apr\xe8s le plus long hiver porte une lumi\xe8re qui te r\xe9veille du sommeil de la mort.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u5c0f\u3055\u304f\u3068\u3082\u5c0a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u306e\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u77e5\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6700\u3082\u8f1d\u304b\u3057\u3044\u7f8e\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u7d30\u304f\u7e4a\u7d30\u306a\u4e00\u672c\u306e\u7cf8\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30b5\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3\u306f\u3001\u6700\u3082\u9577\u3044\u51ac\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306b\u8a2a\u308c\u308b\u6625\u304c\u3001\u6b7b\u306e\u7720\u308a\u304b\u3089\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u3055\u305b\u308b\u5149\u3092\u5bbf\u3059\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, conhe\xe7a o valor do que \xe9 pequeno mas precioso; a beleza mais brilhante muitas vezes se esconde num fio fino e delicado. O a\xe7afr\xe3o sussurra que a primavera que vem depois do inverno mais longo traz uma luz que desperta voc\xea do sono da morte.",howToUse:"Birka\xe7 tel safran\u0131 \u0131l\u0131k suda ya da yeme\u011finde demleyerek alt\u0131n rengini ve kokusunu bir niyet \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131 olarak kullanabilirsin. Bir tutam safran\u0131 k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir kapta saklamak da de\u011fer ve dirili\u015f niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may steep a few threads of saffron in warm water or in your food, using its golden color and fragrance as a light of intention. Keeping a pinch of saffron in a small vessel is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of worth and resurrection.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst einige Safranf\xe4den in warmem Wasser oder in deinem Essen ziehen lassen und seine goldene Farbe und seinen Duft als ein Licht der Absicht nutzen. Eine Prise Safran in einem kleinen Gef\xe4\xdf aufzubewahren ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Wert und Auferstehung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes infusionar unas hebras de azafr\xe1n en agua tibia o en tu comida, usando su color dorado y su fragancia como una luz de intenci\xf3n. Guardar una pizca de azafr\xe1n en un peque\xf1o recipiente es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de valor y resurrecci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux infuser quelques filaments de safran dans de l'eau ti\xe8de ou dans ton plat, en usant de sa couleur dor\xe9e et de son parfum comme d'une lumi\xe8re d'intention. Garder une pinc\xe9e de safran dans un petit r\xe9cipient est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de valeur et de r\xe9surrection.",howToUseJa:"\u6570\u672c\u306e\u30b5\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3\u3092\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u6e6f\u3084\u6599\u7406\u306b\u6d78\u3057\u3001\u305d\u306e\u91d1\u8272\u3068\u9999\u308a\u3092\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u5149\u3068\u3057\u3066\u7528\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u307e\u307f\u306e\u30b5\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3\u3092\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u5bb9\u308c\u7269\u306b\u4fdd\u7ba1\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u4fa1\u5024\u3068\u5fa9\u6d3b\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode deixar alguns fios de a\xe7afr\xe3o em \xe1gua morna ou na sua comida, usando a sua cor dourada e a sua fragr\xe2ncia como uma luz de inten\xe7\xe3o. Guardar uma pitada de a\xe7afr\xe3o em um pequeno recipiente \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de valor e ressurrei\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"K\xfc\xe7\xfck ama de\u011ferli olan\u0131n k\u0131ymetini biliyorum, i\xe7imdeki \u0131\u015f\u0131k beni yeniden uyand\u0131r\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I know the worth of what is small yet precious, and the light within me wakes me anew.",affirmationDe:"Ich kenne den Wert dessen, was klein, doch kostbar ist, und das Licht in mir weckt mich aufs Neue.",affirmationEs:"Conozco el valor de lo peque\xf1o pero precioso, y la luz en m\xed me despierta de nuevo.",affirmationFr:"Je connais la valeur de ce qui est petit mais pr\xe9cieux, et la lumi\xe8re en moi me r\xe9veille \xe0 nouveau.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5c0f\u3055\u304f\u3068\u3082\u5c0a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u306e\u4fa1\u5024\u3092\u77e5\u308a\u3001\u5185\u306a\u308b\u5149\u304c\u79c1\u3092\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u3055\u305b\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Conhe\xe7o o valor do que \xe9 pequeno mas precioso, e a luz dentro de mim me desperta de novo.",myth:"Safran \xe7ok eski \xe7a\u011flardan beri bilinir; Hititler ona 'A-zupiru' der, ila\xe7 olarak kullan\u0131rd\u0131. Latince ad\u0131 Crocus Sativus, mitolojideki Krokos'tan gelir: bir Yunan mitinde nympha Smilaks ile gen\xe7 Krokos b\xfcy\xfck bir a\u015fk ya\u015far, ama kaderleri k\xf6t\xfc bir son haz\u0131rlar ve Krokos safrana, Smilaks ise kendi ad\u0131yla an\u0131lan bir bitkiye d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr. Anadolu'da Lidya'da ise k\u0131\u015f\u0131n bir y\u0131lan\u0131n soktu\u011fu kahraman Til, ilkbaharda a\xe7an safran \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi koklat\u0131l\u0131nca \xf6l\xfcm uykusundan uyan\u0131r; bu y\xfczden safran bahar\u0131n ve dirili\u015fin m\xfcjdecisi say\u0131l\u0131r ve Lidya'da kutlanan bahar bayram\u0131na 'alt\u0131n \xe7i\xe7ek' bayram\u0131 denir.",mythEn:"Saffron has been known since the most ancient times; the Hittites called it 'A-zupiru' and used it as medicine. Its Latin name, Crocus Sativus, comes from the mythological Crocus: in a Greek myth, the nymph Smilax and the youth Crocus share a great love, but their fate prepares a sad end, and Crocus is turned into saffron, Smilax into a plant that bears her name. In Lydia in Anatolia, the hero Til, bitten by a snake in winter, wakes from the sleep of death when made to smell the saffron flower that blooms in spring; for this reason saffron is held to be the herald of spring and resurrection, and the spring festival celebrated in Lydia is called the 'golden flower' festival.",mythDe:"Safran ist seit den \xe4ltesten Zeiten bekannt; die Hethiter nannten ihn 'A-zupiru' und nutzten ihn als Heilmittel. Sein lateinischer Name, Crocus Sativus, stammt vom mythologischen Krokus: In einem griechischen Mythos teilen die Nymphe Smilax und der J\xfcngling Krokus eine gro\xdfe Liebe, doch ihr Schicksal bereitet ein trauriges Ende, und Krokus wird in Safran verwandelt, Smilax in eine Pflanze, die ihren Namen tr\xe4gt. In Lydien in Anatolien erwacht der Held Til, den im Winter eine Schlange biss, aus dem Schlaf des Todes, als man ihn an der im Fr\xfchling bl\xfchenden Safranbl\xfcte riechen l\xe4sst; deshalb gilt der Safran als Vorbote des Fr\xfchlings und der Auferstehung, und das in Lydien gefeierte Fr\xfchlingsfest hei\xdft das Fest der 'goldenen Blume'.",mythEs:"El azafr\xe1n se conoce desde los tiempos m\xe1s antiguos; los hititas lo llamaban 'A-zupiru' y lo usaban como medicina. Su nombre latino, Crocus Sativus, viene del mitol\xf3gico Croco: en un mito griego, la ninfa Esm\xedlax y el joven Croco comparten un gran amor, pero su destino prepara un final triste, y Croco se convierte en azafr\xe1n, y Esm\xedlax en una planta que lleva su nombre. En Lidia, en Anatolia, el h\xe9roe Til, mordido por una serpiente en invierno, despierta del sue\xf1o de la muerte cuando le hacen oler la flor de azafr\xe1n que florece en primavera; por ello el azafr\xe1n se tiene por heraldo de la primavera y la resurrecci\xf3n, y la fiesta primaveral celebrada en Lidia se llama la fiesta de la 'flor de oro'.",mythFr:"Le safran est connu depuis les temps les plus anciens ; les Hittites l'appelaient \xab A-zupiru \xbb et l'employaient comme rem\xe8de. Son nom latin, Crocus Sativus, vient du Crocus mythologique : dans un mythe grec, la nymphe Smilax et le jeune Crocus partagent un grand amour, mais leur destin pr\xe9pare une triste fin, et Crocus est chang\xe9 en safran, Smilax en une plante qui porte son nom. En Lydie, en Anatolie, le h\xe9ros Til, mordu par un serpent en hiver, s'\xe9veille du sommeil de la mort lorsqu'on lui fait sentir la fleur de safran qui \xe9cl\xf4t au printemps ; c'est pourquoi le safran est tenu pour le h\xe9raut du printemps et de la r\xe9surrection, et la f\xeate printani\xe8re c\xe9l\xe9br\xe9e en Lydie est appel\xe9e la f\xeate de la \xab fleur d'or \xbb.",mythJa:"\u30b5\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3\u306f\u6700\u53e4\u306e\u6642\u4ee3\u304b\u3089\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u3001\u30d2\u30c3\u30bf\u30a4\u30c8\u4eba\u306f\u3053\u308c\u3092\u300e\u30a2\u30ba\u30d4\u30eb\u300f\u3068\u547c\u3073\u3001\u85ac\u3068\u3057\u3066\u7528\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30e9\u30c6\u30f3\u540d\u30af\u30ed\u30af\u30b9\u30fb\u30b5\u30c6\u30a3\u30a6\u30b9\u306f\u3001\u795e\u8a71\u306e\u30af\u30ed\u30b3\u30b9\u306b\u7531\u6765\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u308b\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30cb\u30f3\u30d5\u306e\u30b9\u30df\u30e9\u30af\u30b9\u3068\u82e5\u8005\u30af\u30ed\u30b3\u30b9\u304c\u5927\u304d\u306a\u611b\u3092\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u904b\u547d\u306f\u60b2\u3057\u3044\u7d50\u672b\u3092\u7528\u610f\u3057\u3001\u30af\u30ed\u30b3\u30b9\u306f\u30b5\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3\u306b\u3001\u30b9\u30df\u30e9\u30af\u30b9\u306f\u81ea\u3089\u306e\u540d\u3067\u547c\u3070\u308c\u308b\u690d\u7269\u306b\u5909\u308f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u30ea\u30c7\u30a3\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u3001\u51ac\u306b\u86c7\u306b\u54ac\u307e\u308c\u305f\u82f1\u96c4\u30c6\u30a3\u30eb\u304c\u3001\u6625\u306b\u54b2\u304f\u30b5\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u55c5\u304c\u3055\u308c\u308b\u3068\u6b7b\u306e\u7720\u308a\u304b\u3089\u76ee\u899a\u3081\u307e\u3059\u3002\u305d\u306e\u305f\u3081\u30b5\u30d5\u30e9\u30f3\u306f\u6625\u3068\u5fa9\u6d3b\u306e\u4f7f\u8005\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3001\u30ea\u30c7\u30a3\u30a2\u3067\u795d\u308f\u308c\u308b\u6625\u796d\u308a\u306f\u300e\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u82b1\u300f\u306e\u796d\u308a\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"O a\xe7afr\xe3o \xe9 conhecido desde os tempos mais antigos; os hititas o chamavam 'A-zupiru' e o usavam como rem\xe9dio. Seu nome latino, Crocus Sativus, vem do mitol\xf3gico Croco: num mito grego, a ninfa Smilax e o jovem Croco partilham um grande amor, mas o seu destino prepara um fim triste, e Croco transforma-se em a\xe7afr\xe3o, e Smilax numa planta que leva o seu nome. Na L\xeddia, na Anat\xf3lia, o her\xf3i Til, picado por uma serpente no inverno, desperta do sono da morte quando o fazem cheirar a flor de a\xe7afr\xe3o que floresce na primavera; por isso o a\xe7afr\xe3o \xe9 tido como arauto da primavera e da ressurrei\xe7\xe3o, e a festa primaveril celebrada na L\xeddia \xe9 chamada a festa da 'flor de ouro'.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Saffron_-_premium_spice.jpg/330px-Saffron_-_premium_spice.jpg"},{id:"plant-123",emoji:"\ud83c\udf32",color:"#4A6B52",name:"Sedir",nameEn:"Cedar",nameDe:"Zeder",nameEs:"Cedro",nameFr:"C\xe8dre",nameJa:"\u6749",namePt:"Cedro",origin:"Mezopotamya (S\xfcmer) & Anadolu",originEn:"Mesopotamia (Sumer) & Anatolia",originDe:"Mesopotamien (Sumer) & Anatolien",originEs:"Mesopotamia (Sumeria) y Anatolia",originFr:"M\xe9sopotamie (Sumer) et Anatolie",originJa:"\u30e1\u30bd\u30dd\u30bf\u30df\u30a2\uff08\u30b7\u30e5\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\uff09\u30fb\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2",originPt:"Mesopot\xe2mia (Sum\xe9ria) e Anat\xf3lia",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["g\xfc\xe7","kutsall\u0131k","koruma","cesaret","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["strength","sacredness","protection","courage","endurance"],propertiesDe:["St\xe4rke","Heiligkeit","Schutz","Mut","Ausdauer"],propertiesEs:["fuerza","sacralidad","protecci\xf3n","valor","resistencia"],propertiesFr:["force","sacralit\xe9","protection","courage","endurance"],propertiesJa:["\u529b","\u8056\u6027","\u5b88\u8b77","\u52c7\u6c17","\u5fcd\u8010"],propertiesPt:["for\xe7a","sacralidade","prote\xe7\xe3o","coragem","resist\xeancia"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn korkunun bek\xe7ilik etti\u011fi bir kap\u0131n\u0131n \xf6n\xfcnde durabilirsin; ama cesaret, en heybetli engelin bile ge\xe7ilebilece\u011fini bilmektir. Sedir sana k\xf6kl\xfc bir g\xfcc\xfcn g\xf6lgesinde, kendini koruyan ve koruyan bir varl\u0131k olabilece\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, you may stand before a door guarded by fear; but courage is to know that even the most imposing obstacle can be passed. The cedar whispers that, in the shade of a deep-rooted strength, you can be a being who protects itself and others.",dailyMessageDe:"Heute stehst du vielleicht vor einer T\xfcr, die von Furcht bewacht wird; doch Mut hei\xdft zu wissen, dass selbst das gewaltigste Hindernis \xfcberwunden werden kann. Die Zeder fl\xfcstert, dass du im Schatten einer tief verwurzelten Kraft ein Wesen sein kannst, das sich selbst und andere sch\xfctzt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, puedes estar ante una puerta custodiada por el miedo; pero el valor es saber que aun el obst\xe1culo m\xe1s imponente puede superarse. El cedro susurra que, a la sombra de una fuerza de ra\xedces profundas, puedes ser un ser que se protege y protege a otros.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, tu te tiens peut-\xeatre devant une porte gard\xe9e par la peur ; mais le courage, c'est de savoir que m\xeame l'obstacle le plus imposant peut \xeatre franchi. Le c\xe8dre murmure qu'\xe0 l'ombre d'une force aux racines profondes, tu peux \xeatre un \xeatre qui se prot\xe8ge et prot\xe8ge les autres.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u6050\u308c\u304c\u756a\u3092\u3059\u308b\u6249\u306e\u524d\u306b\u7acb\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002\u3051\u308c\u3069\u52c7\u6c17\u3068\u306f\u3001\u6700\u3082\u5a01\u5727\u7684\u306a\u969c\u5bb3\u3055\u3048\u8d8a\u3048\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u77e5\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3002\u6749\u306f\u3001\u6df1\u304f\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u3063\u305f\u529b\u306e\u9670\u3067\u3001\u81ea\u3089\u3068\u4ed6\u8005\u3092\u5b88\u308b\u5b58\u5728\u306b\u306a\u308c\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, voc\xea pode estar diante de uma porta guardada pelo medo; mas a coragem \xe9 saber que at\xe9 o obst\xe1culo mais imponente pode ser ultrapassado. O cedro sussurra que, \xe0 sombra de uma for\xe7a de ra\xedzes profundas, voc\xea pode ser um ser que protege a si mesmo e aos outros.",howToUse:"Bir sedir dal\u0131n\u0131n ya da kozala\u011f\u0131n\u0131n kokusunu i\xe7ine \xe7ekerek g\xfc\xe7 ve koruma niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bir par\xe7a sedir odununu temiz bir k\xf6\u015fede saklamak ya da kokusunu mek\xe2n\u0131na katmak da cesaret ve kutsall\u0131k niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may breathe in the scent of a cedar branch or cone to accompany an intention of strength and protection. Keeping a piece of cedar wood in a clean corner or bringing its scent into your space is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of courage and sacredness.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst den Duft eines Zedernzweigs oder -zapfens einatmen, um eine Absicht von St\xe4rke und Schutz zu begleiten. Ein St\xfcck Zedernholz in einer reinen Ecke aufzubewahren oder seinen Duft in deinen Raum zu bringen ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Mut und Heiligkeit ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes inhalar el aroma de una rama o pi\xf1a de cedro para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de fuerza y protecci\xf3n. Guardar un trozo de madera de cedro en un rinc\xf3n limpio o llevar su aroma a tu espacio es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de valor y sacralidad.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux respirer le parfum d'une branche ou d'une pomme de c\xe8dre pour accompagner une intention de force et de protection. Garder un morceau de bois de c\xe8dre dans un coin propre ou apporter son parfum \xe0 ton espace est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de courage et de sacralit\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u6749\u306e\u679d\u3084\u7403\u679c\u306e\u9999\u308a\u3092\u5438\u3044\u8fbc\u3093\u3067\u3001\u529b\u3068\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u6749\u6750\u306e\u304b\u3051\u3089\u3092\u6e05\u3089\u304b\u306a\u7247\u9685\u306b\u4fdd\u3063\u305f\u308a\u3001\u305d\u306e\u9999\u308a\u3092\u7a7a\u9593\u306b\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3057\u305f\u308a\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u52c7\u6c17\u3068\u8056\u6027\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode inspirar o aroma de um ramo ou cone de cedro para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de for\xe7a e prote\xe7\xe3o. Guardar um peda\xe7o de madeira de cedro em um canto limpo ou trazer o seu aroma ao seu espa\xe7o \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de coragem e sacralidade.",affirmation:"Korkunun bek\xe7ilik etti\u011fi kap\u0131lar\u0131 cesaretle ge\xe7iyorum, k\xf6kl\xfc bir g\xfc\xe7 beni koruyor.",affirmationEn:"I pass with courage through doors guarded by fear, and a deep-rooted strength protects me.",affirmationDe:"Ich durchschreite mit Mut die von Furcht bewachten T\xfcren, und eine tief verwurzelte Kraft sch\xfctzt mich.",affirmationEs:"Cruzo con valor las puertas custodiadas por el miedo, y una fuerza de ra\xedces profundas me protege.",affirmationFr:"Je franchis avec courage les portes gard\xe9es par la peur, et une force aux racines profondes me prot\xe8ge.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u6050\u308c\u304c\u756a\u3092\u3059\u308b\u6249\u3092\u52c7\u6c17\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u8d8a\u3048\u3001\u6df1\u304f\u6839\u3092\u5f35\u3063\u305f\u529b\u304c\u79c1\u3092\u5b88\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Atravesso com coragem as portas guardadas pelo medo, e uma for\xe7a de ra\xedzes profundas me protege.",myth:"Sedir, da\u011flar\u0131n \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz a\u011fac\u0131d\u0131r; Toros ve L\xfcbnan zirvelerinde bin y\u0131l ya\u015far. Antik d\xfcnyada \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfc\u011f\xfcn, g\xfcc\xfcn ve kutsall\u0131\u011f\u0131n simgesiydi \u2014 S\xfcleyman Mabedi onun odunundan yap\u0131ld\u0131, G\u0131lgam\u0131\u015f destan\u0131nda kahraman kutsal sedir orman\u0131na girer. Re\xe7inesi mumyalamada ve ar\u0131nmada kullan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Anadolu'da koruyucu, dik ve kokusuyla zihni a\xe7an a\u011fa\xe7; k\xf6k\xfc derinde, ba\u015f\u0131 g\xf6kte \u2014 yere ba\u011fl\u0131 kalarak y\xfckselmenin dersidir.",mythEn:"The cedar is the immortal tree of the mountains; on the peaks of the Taurus and Lebanon it lives a thousand years. In the ancient world it was the emblem of immortality, strength and the sacred \u2014 the Temple of Solomon was built of its wood, and in the Epic of Gilgamesh the hero enters the sacred cedar forest. Its resin was used in embalming and purification. In Anatolia a protective tree, upright, its scent clearing the mind; root deep, crown in the sky \u2014 the lesson of rising while staying bound to the earth.",mythDe:"Die Zeder ist der unsterbliche Baum der Berge; auf den Gipfeln des Taurus und des Libanon lebt sie tausend Jahre. In der antiken Welt war sie Sinnbild von Unsterblichkeit, St\xe4rke und Heiligkeit \u2014 der Tempel Salomos wurde aus ihrem Holz erbaut, und im Gilgamesch-Epos betritt der Held den heiligen Zedernwald. Ihr Harz diente der Einbalsamierung und Reinigung. In Anatolien ein sch\xfctzender, aufrechter Baum, dessen Duft den Geist kl\xe4rt; Wurzel tief, Krone im Himmel \u2014 die Lehre, zu wachsen und doch der Erde verbunden zu bleiben.",mythEs:"El cedro es el \xe1rbol inmortal de las monta\xf1as; en las cumbres del Tauro y del L\xedbano vive mil a\xf1os. En el mundo antiguo era emblema de inmortalidad, fuerza y lo sagrado \u2014 el Templo de Salom\xf3n se construy\xf3 con su madera, y en la Epopeya de Gilgamesh el h\xe9roe entra en el bosque sagrado de cedros. Su resina se usaba en el embalsamamiento y la purificaci\xf3n. En Anatolia, \xe1rbol protector, erguido, cuyo aroma despeja la mente; ra\xedz profunda, copa en el cielo \u2014 la lecci\xf3n de elevarse permaneciendo unido a la tierra.",mythFr:"Le c\xe8dre est l'arbre immortel des montagnes ; sur les cimes du Taurus et du Liban, il vit mille ans. Dans le monde antique, il \xe9tait l'embl\xe8me de l'immortalit\xe9, de la force et du sacr\xe9 \u2014 le Temple de Salomon fut b\xe2ti de son bois, et dans l'\xc9pop\xe9e de Gilgamesh le h\xe9ros p\xe9n\xe8tre la for\xeat sacr\xe9e de c\xe8dres. Sa r\xe9sine servait \xe0 l'embaumement et \xe0 la purification. En Anatolie, arbre protecteur, droit, dont le parfum \xe9claircit l'esprit ; racine profonde, cime dans le ciel \u2014 la le\xe7on de s'\xe9lever en restant li\xe9 \xe0 la terre.",mythJa:"\u6749\uff08\u30b7\u30c0\u30fc\uff09\u306f\u5c71\u3005\u306e\u4e0d\u6b7b\u306e\u6a39\u3002\u30bf\u30a6\u30ed\u30b9\u3084\u30ec\u30d0\u30ce\u30f3\u306e\u5cf0\u3067\u5343\u5e74\u3092\u751f\u304d\u308b\u3002\u53e4\u4ee3\u4e16\u754c\u3067\u306f\u4e0d\u6b7b\u3068\u529b\u3068\u8056\u6027\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u2014\u2014\u30bd\u30ed\u30e2\u30f3\u306e\u795e\u6bbf\u306f\u305d\u306e\u6728\u3067\u5efa\u3066\u3089\u308c\u3001\u30ae\u30eb\u30ac\u30e1\u30b7\u30e5\u53d9\u4e8b\u8a69\u3067\u306f\u82f1\u96c4\u304c\u8056\u306a\u308b\u6749\u306e\u68ee\u3078\u5206\u3051\u5165\u308b\u3002\u305d\u306e\u6a39\u8102\u306f\u9632\u8150\u3068\u6d44\u5316\u306b\u7528\u3044\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u5b88\u308a\u306e\u3001\u307e\u3063\u3059\u3050\u306a\u3001\u9999\u308a\u3067\u5fc3\u3092\u6674\u3089\u3059\u6a39\u3002\u6839\u306f\u6df1\u304f\u3001\u68a2\u306f\u5929\u306b\u2014\u2014\u5927\u5730\u306b\u7d50\u3070\u308c\u305f\u307e\u307e\u9ad8\u307f\u3078\u6607\u308b\u6559\u3048\u3002",mythPt:"O cedro \xe9 a \xe1rvore imortal das montanhas; nos cumes do Tauro e do L\xedbano vive mil anos. No mundo antigo era emblema de imortalidade, for\xe7a e do sagrado \u2014 o Templo de Salom\xe3o foi constru\xeddo da sua madeira, e na Epopeia de Gilgamesh o her\xf3i entra na floresta sagrada de cedros. A sua resina era usada no embalsamamento e na purifica\xe7\xe3o. Na Anat\xf3lia, \xe1rvore protetora, ereta, cujo aroma clareia a mente; raiz funda, copa no c\xe9u \u2014 a li\xe7\xe3o de se elevar permanecendo ligado \xe0 terra.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/C%C3%A8dre_du_Liban_Barouk_2005.jpg/330px-C%C3%A8dre_du_Liban_Barouk_2005.jpg"},{id:"plant-124",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3f",color:"#8FA968",name:"S\xf6\u011f\xfct",nameEn:"Willow",nameDe:"Weide",nameEs:"Sauce",nameFr:"Saule",nameJa:"\u67f3",namePt:"Salgueiro",origin:"Antik Yunan & T\xfcrk Mitolojisi",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Turkic Mythology",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & t\xfcrkische Mythologie",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y mitolog\xeda t\xfarquica",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et mythologie turque",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u30c6\u30e5\u30eb\u30af\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e mitologia t\xfarquica",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["zarafet","esneklik","yas","\u015fefkat","yenilenme"],propertiesEn:["grace","flexibility","mourning","tenderness","renewal"],propertiesDe:["Anmut","Biegsamkeit","Trauer","Zartheit","Erneuerung"],propertiesEs:["gracia","flexibilidad","duelo","ternura","renovaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["gr\xe2ce","souplesse","deuil","tendresse","renouveau"],propertiesJa:["\u512a\u7f8e","\u3057\u306a\u3084\u304b\u3055","\u54c0\u60bc","\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055","\u518d\u751f"],propertiesPt:["gra\xe7a","flexibilidade","luto","ternura","renova\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn r\xfczg\xe2ra s\xf6\u011f\xfct gibi e\u011fil; dallar\u0131n yere de\u011fse de k\xf6k\xfcn sa\u011flam kald\u0131k\xe7a k\u0131r\u0131lmazs\u0131n. S\xf6\u011f\xfct sana h\xfczn\xfcn de bir zarafeti oldu\u011funu, esnek bir kalbin her f\u0131rt\u0131nadan sonra yeniden ye\u015ferdi\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, bend to the wind like a willow; though your branches touch the ground, as long as your root stays firm you will not break. The willow whispers that grief, too, has a grace, and that a flexible heart greens again after every storm.",dailyMessageDe:"Beuge dich heute dem Wind wie eine Weide; auch wenn deine Zweige den Boden ber\xfchren, zerbrichst du nicht, solange deine Wurzel fest bleibt. Die Weide fl\xfcstert, dass auch die Trauer eine Anmut hat und dass ein biegsames Herz nach jedem Sturm wieder ergr\xfcnt.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, d\xf3blate al viento como un sauce; aunque tus ramas toquen el suelo, mientras tu ra\xedz siga firme no te romper\xe1s. El sauce susurra que el duelo tambi\xe9n tiene una gracia, y que un coraz\xf3n flexible reverdece tras cada tormenta.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, ploie au vent comme un saule ; m\xeame si tes branches touchent le sol, tant que ta racine reste ferme tu ne romps pas. Le saule murmure que le deuil aussi a une gr\xe2ce, et qu'un c\u0153ur souple reverdit apr\xe8s chaque temp\xeate.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u67f3\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u98a8\u306b\u3057\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u679d\u304c\u5730\u306b\u89e6\u308c\u3066\u3082\u3001\u6839\u304c\u3057\u3063\u304b\u308a\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u304b\u304e\u308a\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u6298\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002\u67f3\u306f\u3001\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u306b\u3082\u307e\u305f\u512a\u7f8e\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3001\u3057\u306a\u3084\u304b\u306a\u5fc3\u304c\u5d50\u306e\u305f\u3073\u306b\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u7dd1\u3065\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3092\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, curve-se ao vento como um salgueiro; ainda que os seus galhos toquem o ch\xe3o, enquanto a sua raiz permanecer firme voc\xea n\xe3o se quebrar\xe1. O salgueiro sussurra que o luto tamb\xe9m tem uma gra\xe7a, e que um cora\xe7\xe3o flex\xedvel reverdece ap\xf3s cada tempestade.",howToUse:"Bir s\xf6\u011f\xfct a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n alt\u0131nda durup sallanan dallar\u0131n\u0131n suya de\u011fi\u015fini seyrederek zarafet ve yenilenme niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. \u0130nce bir s\xf6\u011f\xfct dal\u0131n\u0131 bir \xe7elenk gibi \xf6rmek de \u015fefkat ve yas niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may stand beneath a willow and watch its swaying branches touch the water to accompany an intention of grace and renewal. Weaving a slender willow branch into a wreath is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of tenderness and mourning.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst unter einer Weide stehen und ihren schwingenden Zweigen zusehen, wie sie das Wasser ber\xfchren, um eine Absicht von Anmut und Erneuerung zu begleiten. Einen schlanken Weidenzweig zu einem Kranz zu flechten ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Zartheit und Trauer ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes detenerte bajo un sauce y mirar sus ramas que se mecen tocando el agua para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de gracia y renovaci\xf3n. Tejer una rama delgada de sauce en una corona es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de ternura y duelo.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux te tenir sous un saule et regarder ses branches qui se balancent toucher l'eau pour accompagner une intention de gr\xe2ce et de renouveau. Tresser une fine branche de saule en couronne est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de tendresse et de deuil.",howToUseJa:"\u67f3\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u4f47\u307f\u3001\u63fa\u308c\u308b\u679d\u304c\u6c34\u306b\u89e6\u308c\u308b\u306e\u3092\u773a\u3081\u3066\u3001\u512a\u7f8e\u3068\u518d\u751f\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u7d30\u3044\u67f3\u306e\u679d\u3092\u82b1\u8f2a\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u7de8\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3055\u3068\u54c0\u60bc\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode parar sob um salgueiro e observar os seus galhos que balan\xe7am tocando a \xe1gua para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de gra\xe7a e renova\xe7\xe3o. Tecer um ramo fino de salgueiro em uma coroa \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de ternura e luto.",affirmation:"R\xfczg\xe2ra s\xf6\u011f\xfct gibi e\u011filiyorum ama k\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131yorum, kalbim her f\u0131rt\u0131nadan sonra yeniden ye\u015feriyor.",affirmationEn:"I bend to the wind like a willow but do not break, and my heart greens again after every storm.",affirmationDe:"Ich beuge mich dem Wind wie eine Weide, doch ich zerbreche nicht, und mein Herz ergr\xfcnt nach jedem Sturm aufs Neue.",affirmationEs:"Me doblo al viento como un sauce pero no me rompo, y mi coraz\xf3n reverdece tras cada tormenta.",affirmationFr:"Je ploie au vent comme un saule mais ne romps pas, et mon c\u0153ur reverdit apr\xe8s chaque temp\xeate.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u67f3\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u98a8\u306b\u3057\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3082\u6298\u308c\u305a\u3001\u5fc3\u306f\u5d50\u306e\u305f\u3073\u306b\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u7dd1\u3065\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Curvo-me ao vento como um salgueiro mas n\xe3o me quebro, e o meu cora\xe7\xe3o reverdece ap\xf3s cada tempestade.",myth:"Do\u011fu k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde s\xf6\u011f\xfct di\u015fi zarafetini ve ilkbahar\u0131 temsil eder; Japon Ainular\u0131n\u0131n inan\u0131\u015f\u0131nda ilk insanlar\u0131n belkemi\u011fi s\xf6\u011f\xfct a\u011fac\u0131ndand\u0131r. Yunan mitolojisinde 'g\xfcn bat\u0131m\u0131' nymphalar\u0131 Hesperisler, tanr\u0131\xe7a Hera'n\u0131n alt\u0131n elmalar\u0131n\u0131 bir ejderhan\u0131n bek\xe7ili\u011finde korurken Herakles elmalar\u0131 \xe7al\u0131nca b\xfcy\xfck bir \xfcz\xfcnt\xfcye kap\u0131l\u0131r; tanr\u0131lar onlar\u0131 kavak, karaa\u011fa\xe7 ve s\xf6\u011f\xfct a\u011fa\xe7lar\u0131na d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcr. T\xfcrk k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde s\xf6\u011f\xfct, yi\u011fitlerin g\xf6lgesinde oturdu\u011fu kutlu bir a\u011fa\xe7t\u0131r; kutu bir insana girdi\u011finde o ki\u015fi \xe7ocuklar\u0131 seven, duygulu ve evine ba\u011fl\u0131 bir huy edinir, k\xfc\xe7\xfck ku\u015flar\u0131 bir anne gibi korudu\u011funa inan\u0131l\u0131r.",mythEn:"In Eastern culture, the willow represents feminine grace and the spring; in the belief of the Japanese Ainu, the spine of the first humans was made of willow. In Greek myth, the Hesperides, nymphs of the 'sunset,' guarded the golden apples of the goddess Hera under the watch of a dragon; when Heracles stole the apples, they fell into deep grief, and the gods turned them into poplar, elm, and willow trees. In Turkic culture, the willow is a blessed tree in whose shade heroes sit; when its blessing enters a person, that one takes on a nature that loves children, is tender and devoted to the home, and it is believed to protect small birds like a mother.",mythDe:"In der \xf6stlichen Kultur steht die Weide f\xfcr weibliche Anmut und den Fr\xfchling; im Glauben der japanischen Ainu war das R\xfcckgrat der ersten Menschen aus Weide. In der griechischen Mythologie h\xfcteten die Hesperiden, Nymphen des 'Sonnenuntergangs,' die goldenen \xc4pfel der G\xf6ttin Hera unter der Wache eines Drachen; als Herakles die \xc4pfel stahl, verfielen sie in tiefe Trauer, und die G\xf6tter verwandelten sie in Pappel, Ulme und Weide. In der t\xfcrkischen Kultur ist die Weide ein gesegneter Baum, in dessen Schatten Helden sitzen; wenn ihr Segen in einen Menschen eingeht, nimmt dieser ein Wesen an, das Kinder liebt, zart und dem Heim zugetan ist, und man glaubt, sie sch\xfctze kleine V\xf6gel wie eine Mutter.",mythEs:"En la cultura oriental, el sauce representa la gracia femenina y la primavera; en la creencia de los ainu japoneses, la columna vertebral de los primeros humanos era de sauce. En la mitolog\xeda griega, las Hesp\xe9rides, ninfas del 'ocaso', guardaban las manzanas de oro de la diosa Hera bajo la vigilancia de un drag\xf3n; cuando Heracles rob\xf3 las manzanas, cayeron en un hondo pesar, y los dioses las convirtieron en \xe1lamo, olmo y sauce. En la cultura t\xfarquica, el sauce es un \xe1rbol bendito a cuya sombra se sientan los h\xe9roes; cuando su bendici\xf3n entra en una persona, esta adopta un car\xe1cter que ama a los ni\xf1os, tierno y apegado al hogar, y se cree que protege a los pajarillos como una madre.",mythFr:"Dans la culture orientale, le saule repr\xe9sente la gr\xe2ce f\xe9minine et le printemps ; dans la croyance des A\xefnous du Japon, la colonne vert\xe9brale des premiers humains \xe9tait de saule. Dans la mythologie grecque, les Hesp\xe9rides, nymphes du 'couchant,' gardaient les pommes d'or de la d\xe9esse H\xe9ra sous la garde d'un dragon ; quand H\xe9racl\xe8s d\xe9roba les pommes, elles tomb\xe8rent dans un profond chagrin, et les dieux les chang\xe8rent en peuplier, orme et saule. Dans la culture turque, le saule est un arbre b\xe9ni \xe0 l'ombre duquel s'assoient les h\xe9ros ; quand sa b\xe9n\xe9diction entre en une personne, celle-ci prend un caract\xe8re qui aime les enfants, tendre et attach\xe9 au foyer, et l'on croit qu'il prot\xe8ge les petits oiseaux comme une m\xe8re.",mythJa:"\u6771\u6d0b\u306e\u6587\u5316\u3067\u306f\u3001\u67f3\u306f\u5973\u6027\u7684\u306a\u512a\u7f8e\u3068\u6625\u3092\u8868\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u30a2\u30a4\u30cc\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u6700\u521d\u306e\u4eba\u3005\u306e\u80cc\u9aa8\u306f\u67f3\u3067\u3067\u304d\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u300e\u65e5\u6ca1\u300f\u306e\u30cb\u30f3\u30d5\u3067\u3042\u308b\u30d8\u30b9\u30da\u30ea\u30c7\u30b9\u304c\u3001\u7adc\u306e\u898b\u5f35\u308a\u306e\u3082\u3068\u3067\u5973\u795e\u30d8\u30e9\u306e\u9ec4\u91d1\u306e\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3092\u5b88\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u30d8\u30e9\u30af\u30ec\u30b9\u304c\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3092\u76d7\u3080\u3068\u6df1\u3044\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u306b\u6c88\u307f\u3001\u795e\u3005\u306f\u5f7c\u5973\u305f\u3061\u3092\u30dd\u30d7\u30e9\u3001\u30cb\u30ec\u3001\u67f3\u306e\u6728\u306b\u5909\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30c6\u30e5\u30eb\u30af\u306e\u6587\u5316\u3067\u306f\u3001\u67f3\u306f\u82f1\u96c4\u305f\u3061\u304c\u305d\u306e\u9670\u306b\u5ea7\u308b\u795d\u798f\u3055\u308c\u305f\u6728\u3067\u3001\u305d\u306e\u795d\u798f\u304c\u4eba\u306b\u5165\u308b\u3068\u3001\u305d\u306e\u4eba\u306f\u5b50\u3069\u3082\u3092\u611b\u3057\u3001\u60c5\u306b\u7be4\u304f\u3001\u5bb6\u5ead\u3092\u5927\u5207\u306b\u3059\u308b\u6c17\u8cea\u3092\u5e2f\u3073\u3001\u5c0f\u9ce5\u305f\u3061\u3092\u6bcd\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u5b88\u308b\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na cultura oriental, o salgueiro representa a gra\xe7a feminina e a primavera; na cren\xe7a dos ainus do Jap\xe3o, a coluna vertebral dos primeiros humanos era de salgueiro. Na mitologia grega, as Hesp\xe9rides, ninfas do 'poente', guardavam as ma\xe7\xe3s de ouro da deusa Hera sob a vigil\xe2ncia de um drag\xe3o; quando H\xe9racles roubou as ma\xe7\xe3s, ca\xedram num profundo pesar, e os deuses as transformaram em choupo, olmo e salgueiro. Na cultura t\xfarquica, o salgueiro \xe9 uma \xe1rvore aben\xe7oada \xe0 sombra da qual se sentam os her\xf3is; quando a sua b\xean\xe7\xe3o entra numa pessoa, esta assume um car\xe1ter que ama as crian\xe7as, terno e apegado ao lar, e acredita-se que protege os passarinhos como uma m\xe3e.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Salix_alba_Morton.jpg/330px-Salix_alba_Morton.jpg"},{id:"plant-125",emoji:"\ud83c\udf38",color:"#6A5ACD",name:"S\xfcsen",nameEn:"Iris",nameDe:"Schwertlilie",nameEs:"Lirio",nameFr:"Iris",nameJa:"\u30a2\u30e4\u30e1",namePt:"\xcdris",origin:"Antik Yunan",originEn:"Ancient Greece",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland",originEs:"Antigua Grecia",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra de la Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra da Garganta",properties:["haber","umut","ba\u011f","ilham","arac\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["message","hope","bond","inspiration","mediation"],propertiesDe:["Botschaft","Hoffnung","Verbindung","Inspiration","Vermittlung"],propertiesEs:["mensaje","esperanza","v\xednculo","inspiraci\xf3n","mediaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["message","espoir","lien","inspiration","m\xe9diation"],propertiesJa:["\u4f1d\u8a00","\u5e0c\u671b","\u7d46","\u970a\u611f","\u4ef2\u7acb\u3061"],propertiesPt:["mensagem","esperan\xe7a","v\xednculo","inspira\xe7\xe3o","media\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xf6kle yer aras\u0131nda bir k\xf6pr\xfc ol; bir g\xf6kku\u015fa\u011f\u0131 nas\u0131l f\u0131rt\u0131nan\u0131n ard\u0131ndan umudu m\xfcjdelerse, senin s\xf6z\xfcn de birinin kalbine \u0131\u015f\u0131k ta\u015f\u0131yabilir. S\xfcsen sana iletmek istedi\u011fin haberin, nazik\xe7e s\xf6ylendi\u011finde bir ba\u011f kurdu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, be a bridge between sky and earth; just as a rainbow heralds hope after the storm, your word too can carry light into someone's heart. The iris whispers that the message you wish to deliver, spoken gently, forges a bond.",dailyMessageDe:"Sei heute eine Br\xfccke zwischen Himmel und Erde; so wie ein Regenbogen nach dem Sturm Hoffnung verk\xfcndet, kann auch dein Wort Licht in das Herz eines anderen tragen. Die Schwertlilie fl\xfcstert, dass die Botschaft, die du \xfcberbringen willst, sanft gesprochen, eine Verbindung kn\xfcpft.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, s\xe9 un puente entre el cielo y la tierra; as\xed como un arco\xedris anuncia la esperanza tras la tormenta, tu palabra tambi\xe9n puede llevar luz al coraz\xf3n de alguien. El lirio susurra que el mensaje que deseas entregar, dicho con dulzura, teje un v\xednculo.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, sois un pont entre le ciel et la terre ; de m\xeame qu'un arc-en-ciel annonce l'espoir apr\xe8s la temp\xeate, ta parole aussi peut porter la lumi\xe8re dans le c\u0153ur d'autrui. L'iris murmure que le message que tu veux transmettre, dit avec douceur, tisse un lien.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u5929\u3068\u5730\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u306e\u6a4b\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u8679\u304c\u5d50\u306e\u3042\u3068\u306b\u5e0c\u671b\u3092\u544a\u3052\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u3082\u307e\u305f\u3001\u8ab0\u304b\u306e\u5fc3\u306b\u5149\u3092\u904b\u3079\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a2\u30e4\u30e1\u306f\u3001\u4f1d\u3048\u305f\u3044\u8a00\u8449\u304c\u3001\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u8a9e\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u304d\u7d46\u3092\u7d50\u3076\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, seja uma ponte entre o c\xe9u e a terra; assim como um arco-\xedris anuncia a esperan\xe7a ap\xf3s a tempestade, a sua palavra tamb\xe9m pode levar luz ao cora\xe7\xe3o de algu\xe9m. A \xedris sussurra que a mensagem que voc\xea deseja transmitir, dita com delicadeza, tece um v\xednculo.",howToUse:"S\xfcsenin mor \xe7i\xe7eklerini bir vazoda seyrederek haber ve umut niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bir s\xfcsen \xe7i\xe7e\u011fini sevdi\u011fine sunmak ya da bir niyet mektubunun yan\u0131na koymak da ba\u011f ve arac\u0131l\u0131k niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may contemplate the iris's purple flowers in a vase to accompany an intention of message and hope. Offering an iris to someone you love or placing it beside a letter of intention is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of bond and mediation.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die violetten Bl\xfcten der Schwertlilie in einer Vase betrachten, um eine Absicht von Botschaft und Hoffnung zu begleiten. Eine Schwertlilie einem geliebten Menschen zu schenken oder sie neben einen Brief der Absicht zu legen ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Verbindung und Vermittlung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes contemplar las flores moradas del lirio en un jarr\xf3n para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de mensaje y esperanza. Ofrecer un lirio a alguien a quien amas o colocarlo junto a una carta de intenci\xf3n es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de v\xednculo y mediaci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux contempler les fleurs violettes de l'iris dans un vase pour accompagner une intention de message et d'espoir. Offrir un iris \xe0 un \xeatre aim\xe9 ou le poser pr\xe8s d'une lettre d'intention est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de lien et de m\xe9diation.",howToUseJa:"\u30a2\u30e4\u30e1\u306e\u7d2b\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u3067\u773a\u3081\u3066\u3001\u4f1d\u8a00\u3068\u5e0c\u671b\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a2\u30e4\u30e1\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u4eba\u306b\u8d08\u3063\u305f\u308a\u3001\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u624b\u7d19\u306e\u305d\u3070\u306b\u7f6e\u3044\u305f\u308a\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u7d46\u3068\u4ef2\u7acb\u3061\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode contemplar as flores roxas da \xedris em um vaso para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de mensagem e esperan\xe7a. Oferecer uma \xedris a algu\xe9m que voc\xea ama ou coloc\xe1-la ao lado de uma carta de inten\xe7\xe3o \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de v\xednculo e media\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"G\xf6kle yer aras\u0131nda bir k\xf6pr\xfc oluyorum, s\xf6zlerim nazik\xe7e bir ba\u011f kuruyor.",affirmationEn:"I become a bridge between sky and earth, and my words gently forge a bond.",affirmationDe:"Ich werde zur Br\xfccke zwischen Himmel und Erde, und meine Worte kn\xfcpfen sanft eine Verbindung.",affirmationEs:"Me vuelvo un puente entre el cielo y la tierra, y mis palabras tejen con dulzura un v\xednculo.",affirmationFr:"Je deviens un pont entre le ciel et la terre, et mes paroles tissent avec douceur un lien.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u5929\u3068\u5730\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u306e\u6a4b\u3068\u306a\u308a\u3001\u8a00\u8449\u304c\u3084\u3055\u3057\u304f\u7d46\u3092\u7d50\u3076\u3002",affirmationPt:"Torno-me uma ponte entre o c\xe9u e a terra, e as minhas palavras tecem com delicadeza um v\xednculo.",myth:"S\xfcsenin Latince ad\u0131 \u0130ris'tir; Yunan mitolojisinde \u0130ris g\xf6kku\u015fa\u011f\u0131n\u0131 temsil eder ve tanr\u0131larla insanlar aras\u0131nda haberle\u015fmeyi sa\u011flayan kanatl\u0131 bir habercidir. \xd6zellikle tanr\u0131 Zeus ile tanr\u0131\xe7a Hera'n\u0131n hizmetinde bulunur, hatta Hera'n\u0131n nedimesi say\u0131l\u0131r; tasvirlerinde g\xf6kku\u015fa\u011f\u0131 renginde bir t\xfcle sar\u0131nm\u0131\u015f kanatl\u0131 bir k\u0131z olarak g\xf6sterilir. Bu y\xfczden g\xf6kku\u015fa\u011f\u0131n\u0131n, tanr\u0131lar\u0131n sesini insanlara duyulur k\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131na inan\u0131l\u0131r. S\xfcsen \xe7i\xe7e\u011finin \xe7o\u011funlukla mezarl\u0131klarda yeti\u015fmesi de, belki onun \xf6lenlerle tanr\u0131lar aras\u0131ndaki haberle\u015fmeyi s\xfcrd\xfcrmek i\xe7in orada a\xe7t\u0131\u011f\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcncesine ba\u011flan\u0131r.",mythEn:"The Latin name of the iris is Iris; in Greek myth, Iris represents the rainbow and is the winged messenger who carries word between gods and humans. She serves especially the god Zeus and the goddess Hera, and is even counted as Hera's handmaiden; in her depictions she is shown as a winged maiden wrapped in a rainbow-colored veil. For this reason it is believed that the rainbow makes the voice of the gods audible to humans. That the iris flower most often grows in graveyards is linked, perhaps, to the thought that it blooms there to keep up the messaging between the dead and the gods.",mythDe:"Der lateinische Name der Schwertlilie ist Iris; in der griechischen Mythologie steht Iris f\xfcr den Regenbogen und ist die gefl\xfcgelte Botin, die Kunde zwischen G\xf6ttern und Menschen tr\xe4gt. Sie dient besonders dem Gott Zeus und der G\xf6ttin Hera und gilt sogar als Heras Dienerin; in ihren Darstellungen erscheint sie als gefl\xfcgeltes M\xe4dchen, in einen regenbogenfarbenen Schleier geh\xfcllt. Deshalb glaubt man, der Regenbogen mache die Stimme der G\xf6tter den Menschen h\xf6rbar. Dass die Schwertlilie am h\xe4ufigsten auf Friedh\xf6fen w\xe4chst, wird vielleicht mit dem Gedanken verbunden, dass sie dort bl\xfcht, um die Verst\xe4ndigung zwischen den Toten und den G\xf6ttern aufrechtzuerhalten.",mythEs:"El nombre latino del lirio es Iris; en la mitolog\xeda griega, Iris representa el arco\xedris y es la mensajera alada que lleva la palabra entre dioses y humanos. Sirve sobre todo al dios Zeus y a la diosa Hera, y hasta se la cuenta como doncella de Hera; en sus representaciones se la muestra como una joven alada envuelta en un velo del color del arco\xedris. Por eso se cree que el arco\xedris hace audible para los humanos la voz de los dioses. Que la flor del lirio crezca con m\xe1s frecuencia en los cementerios se vincula, quiz\xe1, con la idea de que florece all\xed para mantener la comunicaci\xf3n entre los muertos y los dioses.",mythFr:"Le nom latin de l'iris est Iris ; dans la mythologie grecque, Iris repr\xe9sente l'arc-en-ciel et est la messag\xe8re ail\xe9e qui porte la parole entre les dieux et les humains. Elle sert surtout le dieu Zeus et la d\xe9esse H\xe9ra, et est m\xeame compt\xe9e comme suivante d'H\xe9ra ; dans ses repr\xe9sentations, elle appara\xeet comme une jeune fille ail\xe9e envelopp\xe9e d'un voile aux couleurs de l'arc-en-ciel. C'est pourquoi l'on croit que l'arc-en-ciel rend audible aux humains la voix des dieux. Que la fleur d'iris pousse le plus souvent dans les cimeti\xe8res se rattache, peut-\xeatre, \xe0 l'id\xe9e qu'elle y fleurit pour entretenir la communication entre les morts et les dieux.",mythJa:"\u30a2\u30e4\u30e1\u306e\u30e9\u30c6\u30f3\u540d\u306f\u30a4\u30ea\u30b9\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30a4\u30ea\u30b9\u306f\u8679\u3092\u8868\u3057\u3001\u795e\u3005\u3068\u4eba\u9593\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u306b\u8a00\u8449\u3092\u904b\u3076\u7ffc\u3042\u308b\u4f7f\u8005\u3067\u3059\u3002\u3068\u304f\u306b\u795e\u30bc\u30a6\u30b9\u3068\u5973\u795e\u30d8\u30e9\u306b\u4ed5\u3048\u3001\u30d8\u30e9\u306e\u4f8d\u5973\u3068\u3082\u3055\u308c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u59ff\u306f\u8679\u8272\u306e\u30f4\u30a7\u30fc\u30eb\u3092\u307e\u3068\u3063\u305f\u7ffc\u3042\u308b\u4e59\u5973\u3068\u3057\u3066\u63cf\u304b\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u305d\u306e\u305f\u3081\u3001\u8679\u306f\u795e\u3005\u306e\u58f0\u3092\u4eba\u9593\u306b\u805e\u3053\u3048\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3059\u308b\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30a2\u30e4\u30e1\u306e\u82b1\u304c\u5893\u5730\u306b\u591a\u304f\u54b2\u304f\u306e\u3082\u3001\u304a\u305d\u3089\u304f\u3001\u6b7b\u8005\u3068\u795e\u3005\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u306e\u4f1d\u9054\u3092\u4fdd\u3064\u305f\u3081\u306b\u305d\u3053\u3067\u54b2\u304f\u3068\u3044\u3046\u8003\u3048\u306b\u7d50\u3073\u3064\u3051\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"O nome latino da \xedris \xe9 Iris; na mitologia grega, Iris representa o arco-\xedris e \xe9 a mensageira alada que leva a palavra entre deuses e humanos. Serve sobretudo ao deus Zeus e \xe0 deusa Hera, e \xe9 at\xe9 contada como dama de companhia de Hera; em suas representa\xe7\xf5es, aparece como uma jovem alada envolta num v\xe9u da cor do arco-\xedris. Por isso acredita-se que o arco-\xedris torna aud\xedvel aos humanos a voz dos deuses. Que a flor da \xedris cres\xe7a mais frequentemente nos cemit\xe9rios liga-se, talvez, \xe0 ideia de que ela floresce ali para manter a comunica\xe7\xe3o entre os mortos e os deuses.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg"},{id:"plant-126",emoji:"\ud83c\udf51",color:"#F6A192",name:"\u015eeftali",nameEn:"Peach",nameDe:"Pfirsich",nameEs:"Melocot\xf3n",nameFr:"P\xeache",nameJa:"\u6843",namePt:"P\xeassego",origin:"\xc7in & Japon Mitolojisi",originEn:"Chinese & Japanese Mythology",originDe:"Chinesische & japanische Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda china y japonesa",originFr:"Mythologie chinoise et japonaise",originJa:"\u4e2d\u56fd\u30fb\u65e5\u672c\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia chinesa e japonesa",element:"ate\u015f",elementEn:"fire",elementDe:"Feuer",elementEs:"fuego",elementFr:"feu",elementJa:"\u706b",elementPt:"fogo",chakra:"Sakral \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Sacral Chakra",chakraDe:"Sakralchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Sacro",chakraFr:"Chakra Sacr\xe9",chakraJa:"\u4ed9\u9aa8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Sacral",properties:["\xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck","koruma","gen\xe7lik","ar\u0131nma","tatl\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["immortality","protection","youth","cleansing","sweetness"],propertiesDe:["Unsterblichkeit","Schutz","Jugend","Reinigung","S\xfc\xdfe"],propertiesEs:["inmortalidad","protecci\xf3n","juventud","purificaci\xf3n","dulzura"],propertiesFr:["immortalit\xe9","protection","jeunesse","purification","douceur"],propertiesJa:["\u4e0d\u6b7b","\u5b88\u8b77","\u82e5\u3055","\u6d44\u5316","\u7518\u3055"],propertiesPt:["imortalidade","prote\xe7\xe3o","juventude","purifica\xe7\xe3o","do\xe7ura"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn seni karanl\u0131ktan ay\u0131racak tatl\u0131 bir g\xfcce g\xfcven; bazen en korkutucu g\xf6lgeler bile bir niyetle, bir cesaretle da\u011f\u0131l\u0131r. \u015eeftali sana i\xe7indeki tatl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n hem seni koruyan hem de seni tazeleyen bir arma\u011fan oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, trust in a sweet power that will set you apart from the dark; sometimes even the most frightening shadows scatter before an intention, a courage. The peach whispers that the sweetness within you is a gift that both protects and renews you.",dailyMessageDe:"Vertraue heute einer s\xfc\xdfen Kraft, die dich vom Dunkel scheidet; manchmal zerstreuen sich selbst die furchterregendsten Schatten vor einer Absicht, einem Mut. Der Pfirsich fl\xfcstert, dass die S\xfc\xdfe in dir ein Geschenk ist, das dich zugleich sch\xfctzt und erneuert.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, conf\xeda en un dulce poder que te apartar\xe1 de la oscuridad; a veces, hasta las sombras m\xe1s temibles se dispersan ante una intenci\xf3n, un valor. El melocot\xf3n susurra que la dulzura que llevas dentro es un don que a la vez te protege y te renueva.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, fie-toi \xe0 une douce puissance qui te s\xe9parera de l'obscurit\xe9 ; parfois, m\xeame les ombres les plus effrayantes se dissipent devant une intention, un courage. La p\xeache murmure que la douceur en toi est un don qui \xe0 la fois te prot\xe8ge et te renouvelle.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u95c7\u304b\u3089\u5206\u304b\u3064\u7518\u3044\u529b\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3068\u304d\u306b\u3001\u6700\u3082\u6050\u308d\u3057\u3044\u5f71\u3055\u3048\u3001\u4e00\u3064\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3001\u4e00\u3064\u306e\u52c7\u6c17\u306e\u524d\u306b\u6563\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u6843\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u5185\u306a\u308b\u7518\u3055\u304c\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3082\u3057\u3001\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u3082\u3059\u308b\u8d08\u308a\u3082\u306e\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, confie em um doce poder que o apartar\xe1 da escurid\xe3o; \xe0s vezes, at\xe9 as sombras mais assustadoras se dispersam diante de uma inten\xe7\xe3o, de uma coragem. O p\xeassego sussurra que a do\xe7ura dentro de voc\xea \xe9 um presente que ao mesmo tempo o protege e o renova.",howToUse:"Olgun bir \u015feftaliyi taze yiyerek gen\xe7lik ve tatl\u0131l\u0131k niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bir \u015feftali \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi dal\u0131n\u0131 bir vazoda tutmak ya da kap\u0131n\u0131n yak\u0131n\u0131nda bulundurmak da koruma ve ar\u0131nma niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may eat a ripe peach fresh to accompany an intention of youth and sweetness. Keeping a branch of peach blossom in a vase or near the door is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of protection and cleansing.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst einen reifen Pfirsich frisch essen, um eine Absicht von Jugend und S\xfc\xdfe zu begleiten. Einen Zweig Pfirsichbl\xfcte in einer Vase oder nahe der T\xfcr aufzubewahren ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Schutz und Reinigung ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes comer un melocot\xf3n maduro fresco para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de juventud y dulzura. Guardar una rama de flor de melocot\xf3n en un jarr\xf3n o cerca de la puerta es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de protecci\xf3n y purificaci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux manger une p\xeache m\xfbre fra\xeeche pour accompagner une intention de jeunesse et de douceur. Garder une branche de fleur de p\xeacher dans un vase ou pr\xe8s de la porte est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de protection et de purification.",howToUseJa:"\u719f\u3057\u305f\u6843\u3092\u751f\u306e\u307e\u307e\u98df\u3079\u3066\u3001\u82e5\u3055\u3068\u7518\u3055\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u6843\u306e\u82b1\u306e\u679d\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u306b\u633f\u3057\u305f\u308a\u3001\u6238\u53e3\u306e\u8fd1\u304f\u306b\u7f6e\u3044\u305f\u308a\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u5b88\u8b77\u3068\u6d44\u5316\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode comer um p\xeassego maduro fresco para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de juventude e do\xe7ura. Manter um ramo de flor de pessegueiro em um vaso ou perto da porta \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de prote\xe7\xe3o e purifica\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7imdeki tatl\u0131l\u0131k beni hem koruyor hem tazeliyor, karanl\u0131k g\xf6lgeler \xf6n\xfcmde da\u011f\u0131l\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"The sweetness within me both protects and renews me, and dark shadows scatter before me.",affirmationDe:"Die S\xfc\xdfe in mir sch\xfctzt und erneuert mich zugleich, und dunkle Schatten zerstreuen sich vor mir.",affirmationEs:"La dulzura en m\xed me protege y me renueva a la vez, y las sombras oscuras se dispersan ante m\xed.",affirmationFr:"La douceur en moi me prot\xe8ge et me renouvelle \xe0 la fois, et les ombres sombres se dissipent devant moi.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306e\u5185\u306a\u308b\u7518\u3055\u306f\u79c1\u3092\u5b88\u308a\u3082\u3057\u3001\u65b0\u305f\u306b\u3082\u3057\u3001\u6697\u3044\u5f71\u306f\u79c1\u306e\u524d\u3067\u6563\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"A do\xe7ura dentro de mim me protege e me renova ao mesmo tempo, e as sombras escuras se dispersam diante de mim.",myth:"\xc7in inanc\u0131nda bir ki\u015fi \xf6ld\xfc\u011f\xfcnde, \xf6b\xfcr d\xfcnyaya giden ruhu oradaki 'd\xfcnya a\u011fac\u0131'ndan bir \u015feftali yedi\u011finde \xfc\xe7 bin y\u0131l ya\u015fama hakk\u0131 kazan\u0131r. \xc7in mitolojisinde \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck pe\u015findeki yaramaz bir maymun, Bat\u0131n\u0131n krali\xe7esi Xi Wangmu'nun kutsal bah\xe7esindeki \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck \u015feftalilerini bek\xe7ilik ederken hepsini yiyerek \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz olur. Japon mitolojisinde ise ilksel ilah \u0130zanagi, \xf6len e\u015fi \u0130zanami'yi \xf6l\xfcler \xfclkesi Yomi'de g\xf6rmeye gider; oradan ka\xe7arken pe\u015fine d\xfc\u015fen k\xf6t\xfc g\xfc\xe7lere, ge\xe7itte yeti\u015fmi\u015f \xfc\xe7 \u015feftaliyi f\u0131rlatarak onlar\u0131 durdurur ve \u015feftaliye 'bana yard\u0131m etti\u011fin gibi, s\u0131k\u0131nt\u0131ya d\xfc\u015fen t\xfcm insanlara da yard\u0131m et' diye seslenir. B\xf6ylece Japon inan\u0131\u015f\u0131nda \u015feftali k\xf6t\xfc ruhlar\u0131 kovan kutsal bir meyve say\u0131l\u0131r.",mythEn:"In Chinese belief, when a person dies, their soul, journeying to the other world, gains the right to live three thousand years when it eats a peach from the 'world tree' there. In Chinese myth, a mischievous monkey in pursuit of immortality, while guarding the immortality peaches in the sacred garden of Xi Wangmu, Queen of the West, eats them all and becomes immortal. In Japanese myth, the primeval god Izanagi goes to see his dead wife Izanami in Yomi, the land of the dead; fleeing from there, he stops the evil powers that pursue him by hurling three peaches that grew at the pass, and calls to the peach, 'As you helped me, help all people who fall into hardship.' Thus in Japanese belief the peach is held to be a sacred fruit that drives away evil spirits.",mythDe:"Im chinesischen Glauben erlangt die Seele eines Verstorbenen auf ihrer Reise in die andere Welt das Recht, dreitausend Jahre zu leben, wenn sie dort einen Pfirsich vom 'Weltenbaum' isst. In der chinesischen Mythologie isst ein schelmischer Affe auf der Suche nach Unsterblichkeit, w\xe4hrend er die Unsterblichkeitspfirsiche im heiligen Garten der Xi Wangmu, der K\xf6nigin des Westens, bewacht, sie alle und wird unsterblich. In der japanischen Mythologie geht der Urgott Izanagi, um seine verstorbene Frau Izanami in Yomi, dem Land der Toten, zu sehen; auf der Flucht von dort h\xe4lt er die b\xf6sen M\xe4chte, die ihn verfolgen, auf, indem er drei Pfirsiche, die am Pass gewachsen waren, schleudert, und ruft dem Pfirsich zu: 'Wie du mir geholfen hast, hilf allen Menschen, die in Not geraten.' So gilt im japanischen Glauben der Pfirsich als heilige Frucht, die b\xf6se Geister vertreibt.",mythEs:"En la creencia china, cuando una persona muere, su alma, al viajar al otro mundo, obtiene el derecho de vivir tres mil a\xf1os cuando come all\xed un melocot\xf3n del '\xe1rbol del mundo'. En la mitolog\xeda china, un mono travieso en busca de la inmortalidad, mientras custodia los melocotones de la inmortalidad en el jard\xedn sagrado de Xi Wangmu, reina del Oeste, los come todos y se vuelve inmortal. En la mitolog\xeda japonesa, el dios primordial Izanagi va a ver a su esposa muerta Izanami en Yomi, la tierra de los muertos; al huir de all\xed, detiene a las potencias malignas que lo persiguen arrojando tres melocotones que crec\xedan en el paso, y le dice al melocot\xf3n: 'Como me ayudaste, ayuda tambi\xe9n a toda la gente que cae en la desgracia.' As\xed, en la creencia japonesa, el melocot\xf3n se tiene por un fruto sagrado que expulsa a los malos esp\xedritus.",mythFr:"Dans la croyance chinoise, lorsqu'une personne meurt, son \xe2me, en voyageant vers l'autre monde, gagne le droit de vivre trois mille ans quand elle y mange une p\xeache de l'\xab arbre du monde \xbb. Dans la mythologie chinoise, un singe espi\xe8gle en qu\xeate d'immortalit\xe9, alors qu'il garde les p\xeaches d'immortalit\xe9 dans le jardin sacr\xe9 de Xi Wangmu, reine de l'Ouest, les mange toutes et devient immortel. Dans la mythologie japonaise, le dieu primordial Izanagi va voir sa femme d\xe9funte Izanami \xe0 Yomi, le pays des morts ; fuyant de l\xe0, il arr\xeate les puissances mauvaises qui le poursuivent en lan\xe7ant trois p\xeaches qui avaient pouss\xe9 au col, et il dit \xe0 la p\xeache : \xab Comme tu m'as aid\xe9, aide aussi tous les hommes qui tombent dans le malheur. \xbb Ainsi, dans la croyance japonaise, la p\xeache est tenue pour un fruit sacr\xe9 qui chasse les mauvais esprits.",mythJa:"\u4e2d\u56fd\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u4eba\u304c\u6b7b\u306c\u3068\u3001\u3042\u306e\u4e16\u3078\u5411\u304b\u3046\u9b42\u306f\u3001\u305d\u3053\u306b\u3042\u308b\u300e\u4e16\u754c\u306e\u6a39\u300f\u306e\u6843\u3092\u98df\u3079\u308b\u3068\u4e09\u5343\u5e74\u751f\u304d\u308b\u6a29\u5229\u3092\u5f97\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e2d\u56fd\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u4e0d\u6b7b\u3092\u6c42\u3081\u308b\u3044\u305f\u305a\u3089\u306a\u733f\u304c\u3001\u897f\u306e\u5973\u738b\u897f\u738b\u6bcd\u306e\u8056\u306a\u308b\u5ead\u306e\u4e0d\u6b7b\u306e\u6843\u3092\u898b\u5f35\u308b\u3046\u3061\u306b\u3059\u3079\u3066\u98df\u3079\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u3001\u4e0d\u6b7b\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u65e5\u672c\u795e\u8a71\u3067\u306f\u3001\u539f\u521d\u306e\u795e\u30a4\u30b6\u30ca\u30ae\u304c\u3001\u6b7b\u3093\u3060\u59bb\u30a4\u30b6\u30ca\u30df\u3092\u6b7b\u8005\u306e\u56fd\u30e8\u30df\u306b\u4f1a\u3044\u306b\u884c\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u305d\u3053\u304b\u3089\u9003\u3052\u308b\u969b\u3001\u8ffd\u3063\u3066\u304f\u308b\u90aa\u60aa\u306a\u529b\u3092\u3001\u5742\u3067\u5b9f\u3063\u305f\u4e09\u3064\u306e\u6843\u3092\u6295\u3052\u3064\u3051\u3066\u9000\u3051\u3001\u6843\u306b\u300e\u79c1\u3092\u52a9\u3051\u305f\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u82e6\u3057\u307f\u306b\u9665\u308b\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u4eba\u3092\u3082\u52a9\u3051\u3088\u300f\u3068\u547c\u3073\u304b\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u4fe1\u4ef0\u3067\u306f\u3001\u6843\u306f\u60aa\u970a\u3092\u8ffd\u3044\u6255\u3046\u8056\u306a\u308b\u679c\u5b9f\u3068\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Na cren\xe7a chinesa, quando uma pessoa morre, a sua alma, ao viajar para o outro mundo, ganha o direito de viver tr\xeas mil anos quando come ali um p\xeassego da '\xe1rvore do mundo'. Na mitologia chinesa, um macaco travesso em busca da imortalidade, enquanto guarda os p\xeassegos da imortalidade no jardim sagrado de Xi Wangmu, rainha do Oeste, come-os todos e torna-se imortal. Na mitologia japonesa, o deus primordial Izanagi vai ver a sua esposa morta Izanami em Yomi, a terra dos mortos; ao fugir de l\xe1, det\xe9m as pot\xeancias malignas que o perseguem atirando tr\xeas p\xeassegos que cresceram no desfiladeiro, e diz ao p\xeassego: 'Assim como me ajudaste, ajuda tamb\xe9m todas as pessoas que caem na desgra\xe7a.' Assim, na cren\xe7a japonesa, o p\xeassego \xe9 tido como um fruto sagrado que afasta os maus esp\xedritos.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg"},{id:"plant-127",emoji:"\ud83c\udf33",color:"#5C7A4D",name:"\u015eim\u015fir",nameEn:"Boxwood",nameDe:"Buchsbaum",nameEs:"Boj",nameFr:"Buis",nameJa:"\u30c4\u30b2",namePt:"Buxo",origin:"\u0130ran Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"Persian Tradition",originDe:"Persische Tradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n persa",originFr:"Tradition persane",originJa:"\u30da\u30eb\u30b7\u30e3\u306e\u4f1d\u7d71",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o persa",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"K\xf6k \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Root Chakra",chakraDe:"Wurzelchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra Ra\xedz",chakraFr:"Chakra Racine",chakraJa:"\u30eb\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Raiz",properties:["kutsall\u0131k","dilek","s\xfcreklilik","koruma","sebat"],propertiesEn:["sacredness","wish","continuity","protection","steadfastness"],propertiesDe:["Heiligkeit","Wunsch","Best\xe4ndigkeit","Schutz","Standhaftigkeit"],propertiesEs:["sacralidad","deseo","continuidad","protecci\xf3n","firmeza"],propertiesFr:["sacralit\xe9","v\u0153u","continuit\xe9","protection","constance"],propertiesJa:["\u8056\u6027","\u9858\u3044","\u7d99\u7d9a","\u5b88\u8b77","\u5805\u5fcd"],propertiesPt:["sacralidade","desejo","continuidade","prote\xe7\xe3o","firmeza"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn bir dile\u011fini sessizce nazik bir niyet ipli\u011fine ba\u011fla; bazen kutsal olan, sab\u0131rla ve umutla beklenen k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir istektir. \u015eim\u015fir sana her mevsim ye\u015fil kalan bir dal\u0131n, s\xfcreklili\u011fin ve sars\u0131lmaz bir umudun simgesi oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, quietly tie one of your wishes to a gentle thread of intention; sometimes the sacred is a small desire awaited with patience and hope. Boxwood whispers that a branch staying green in every season is a symbol of continuity and of an unshakable hope.",dailyMessageDe:"Kn\xfcpfe heute still einen deiner W\xfcnsche an einen zarten Faden der Absicht; manchmal ist das Heilige ein kleiner Wunsch, der mit Geduld und Hoffnung erwartet wird. Der Buchsbaum fl\xfcstert, dass ein Zweig, der in jeder Jahreszeit gr\xfcn bleibt, ein Sinnbild der Best\xe4ndigkeit und einer unersch\xfctterlichen Hoffnung ist.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, ata en silencio uno de tus deseos a un tierno hilo de intenci\xf3n; a veces lo sagrado es un peque\xf1o anhelo aguardado con paciencia y esperanza. El boj susurra que una rama que permanece verde en toda estaci\xf3n es s\xedmbolo de continuidad y de una esperanza inquebrantable.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, noue en silence l'un de tes v\u0153ux \xe0 un tendre fil d'intention ; parfois le sacr\xe9 est un petit d\xe9sir attendu avec patience et espoir. Le buis murmure qu'un rameau qui reste vert en toute saison est le symbole de la continuit\xe9 et d'un espoir in\xe9branlable.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u3072\u3068\u3064\u306e\u9858\u3044\u3092\u3001\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u7cf8\u306b\u9759\u304b\u306b\u7d50\u3073\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u3068\u304d\u306b\u8056\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u306f\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u5e0c\u671b\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u5f85\u305f\u308c\u308b\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u671b\u307f\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30c4\u30b2\u306f\u3001\u3069\u306e\u5b63\u7bc0\u3082\u7dd1\u306e\u307e\u307e\u306e\u679d\u304c\u3001\u7d99\u7d9a\u3068\u63fa\u308b\u304c\u306c\u5e0c\u671b\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, amarre em sil\xeancio um dos seus desejos a um terno fio de inten\xe7\xe3o; \xe0s vezes o sagrado \xe9 um pequeno anseio aguardado com paci\xeancia e esperan\xe7a. O buxo sussurra que um ramo que permanece verde em toda esta\xe7\xe3o \xe9 s\xedmbolo de continuidade e de uma esperan\xe7a inabal\xe1vel.",howToUse:"Bir \u015fim\u015fir dal\u0131na ya da yak\u0131n\u0131ndaki bir a\u011faca renkli bir kuma\u015f par\xe7as\u0131 ba\u011flayarak dile\u011fini ve niyetini sembolik olarak iletebilirsin. Her mevsim ye\u015fil kalan \u015fim\u015firin yapraklar\u0131n\u0131 seyretmek de s\xfcreklilik ve koruma niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir and\u0131r.",howToUseEn:"You may tie a colorful piece of cloth to a boxwood branch or a nearby tree to convey your wish and intention symbolically. Contemplating the boxwood's leaves, which stay green in every season, is also a gentle moment honoring an intention of continuity and protection.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst ein buntes St\xfcck Stoff an einen Buchsbaumzweig oder einen nahen Baum binden, um deinen Wunsch und deine Absicht symbolisch zu \xfcbermitteln. Die Bl\xe4tter des Buchsbaums zu betrachten, die in jeder Jahreszeit gr\xfcn bleiben, ist ebenfalls ein zarter Augenblick, der eine Absicht von Best\xe4ndigkeit und Schutz ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes atar un trozo de tela de color a una rama de boj o a un \xe1rbol cercano para transmitir tu deseo e intenci\xf3n de forma simb\xf3lica. Contemplar las hojas del boj, que permanecen verdes en toda estaci\xf3n, es tambi\xe9n un momento tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de continuidad y protecci\xf3n.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux nouer un morceau d'\xe9toffe color\xe9e \xe0 un rameau de buis ou \xe0 un arbre voisin pour transmettre ton v\u0153u et ton intention de fa\xe7on symbolique. Contempler les feuilles du buis, qui restent vertes en toute saison, est aussi un instant tendre qui honore une intention de continuit\xe9 et de protection.",howToUseJa:"\u30c4\u30b2\u306e\u679d\u3084\u8fd1\u304f\u306e\u6728\u306b\u8272\u3068\u308a\u3069\u308a\u306e\u5e03\u304d\u308c\u3092\u7d50\u3093\u3067\u3001\u9858\u3044\u3068\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u306b\u4f1d\u3048\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3069\u306e\u5b63\u7bc0\u3082\u7dd1\u306e\u307e\u307e\u306e\u30c4\u30b2\u306e\u8449\u3092\u773a\u3081\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u7d99\u7d9a\u3068\u5b88\u8b77\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u3072\u3068\u3068\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode amarrar um peda\xe7o de tecido colorido a um ramo de buxo ou a uma \xe1rvore pr\xf3xima para transmitir o seu desejo e a sua inten\xe7\xe3o de forma simb\xf3lica. Contemplar as folhas do buxo, que permanecem verdes em toda esta\xe7\xe3o, \xe9 tamb\xe9m um momento terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de continuidade e prote\xe7\xe3o.",affirmation:"Dile\u011fimi nazik bir niyetle ba\u011fl\u0131yorum, umudum her mevsim ye\u015fil kal\u0131yor.",affirmationEn:"I tie my wish with a gentle intention, and my hope stays green in every season.",affirmationDe:"Ich kn\xfcpfe meinen Wunsch mit einer zarten Absicht, und meine Hoffnung bleibt in jeder Jahreszeit gr\xfcn.",affirmationEs:"Ato mi deseo con una tierna intenci\xf3n, y mi esperanza permanece verde en toda estaci\xf3n.",affirmationFr:"Je noue mon v\u0153u avec une tendre intention, et mon espoir reste vert en toute saison.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u9858\u3044\u3092\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u610f\u56f3\u3067\u7d50\u3073\u3001\u5e0c\u671b\u306f\u3069\u306e\u5b63\u7bc0\u3082\u7dd1\u306e\u307e\u307e\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Amarro o meu desejo com uma terna inten\xe7\xe3o, e a minha esperan\xe7a permanece verde em toda esta\xe7\xe3o.",myth:"\u0130ran k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde kutsal say\u0131lan \u015fim\u015fir (\u015fim\u015fad) a\u011fac\u0131, \xf6zellikle kutsal ziyaret yerlerine ve t\xfcrbelere dikilirdi. Her mevsim ye\u015fil kalan bu a\u011fac\u0131n, kendisine s\u0131\u011f\u0131nanlara yard\u0131m edece\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Bu y\xfczden insanlar dileklerini ve ihtiya\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 iletmek i\xe7in \u015fim\u015fir a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n dallar\u0131na renkli kuma\u015f par\xe7alar\u0131 ba\u011flarlard\u0131; her ba\u011flanan bez, sab\u0131rla ve umutla beklenen bir niyetin sessiz bir simgesiydi.",mythEn:"Held sacred in Persian culture, the boxwood (shimshad) tree was planted especially at holy places of pilgrimage and at shrines. This tree, which stays green in every season, was believed to help those who took refuge with it. For this reason people tied colorful pieces of cloth to the boxwood's branches to convey their wishes and needs; each cloth bound there was a silent symbol of an intention awaited with patience and hope.",mythDe:"Der in der persischen Kultur als heilig geltende Buchsbaum (Schimschad) wurde besonders an heiligen Wallfahrtsorten und an Schreinen gepflanzt. Man glaubte, dass dieser Baum, der in jeder Jahreszeit gr\xfcn bleibt, jenen helfe, die bei ihm Zuflucht suchten. Deshalb banden die Menschen bunte Stoffst\xfccke an die Zweige des Buchsbaums, um ihre W\xfcnsche und N\xf6te zu \xfcbermitteln; jedes dort gebundene Tuch war ein stilles Sinnbild einer mit Geduld und Hoffnung erwarteten Absicht.",mythEs:"Tenido por sagrado en la cultura persa, el boj (shimshad) se plantaba sobre todo en santos lugares de peregrinaci\xf3n y en santuarios. Se cre\xeda que este \xe1rbol, que permanece verde en toda estaci\xf3n, ayudaba a quienes se acog\xedan a \xe9l. Por ello la gente ataba trozos de tela de colores a las ramas del boj para transmitir sus deseos y necesidades; cada tela all\xed atada era un s\xedmbolo silencioso de una intenci\xf3n aguardada con paciencia y esperanza.",mythFr:"Tenu pour sacr\xe9 dans la culture persane, le buis (shimshad) \xe9tait plant\xe9 surtout aux saints lieux de p\xe8lerinage et aux sanctuaires. On croyait que cet arbre, qui reste vert en toute saison, aidait ceux qui se r\xe9fugiaient aupr\xe8s de lui. C'est pourquoi les gens nouaient des morceaux d'\xe9toffe color\xe9s aux rameaux du buis pour transmettre leurs v\u0153ux et leurs besoins ; chaque \xe9toffe nou\xe9e l\xe0 \xe9tait un symbole silencieux d'une intention attendue avec patience et espoir.",mythJa:"\u30da\u30eb\u30b7\u30e3\u306e\u6587\u5316\u3067\u8056\u306a\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3068\u3055\u308c\u305f\u30c4\u30b2\uff08\u30b7\u30e0\u30b7\u30e3\u30fc\u30c9\uff09\u306e\u6728\u306f\u3001\u3068\u304f\u306b\u8056\u306a\u308b\u5de1\u793c\u5730\u3084\u970a\u5edf\u306b\u690d\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3069\u306e\u5b63\u7bc0\u3082\u7dd1\u306e\u307e\u307e\u306e\u3053\u306e\u6728\u306f\u3001\u3059\u304c\u308b\u8005\u3092\u52a9\u3051\u308b\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u305d\u306e\u305f\u3081\u4eba\u3005\u306f\u3001\u9858\u3044\u3084\u6c42\u3081\u3092\u4f1d\u3048\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3001\u30c4\u30b2\u306e\u679d\u306b\u8272\u3068\u308a\u3069\u308a\u306e\u5e03\u304d\u308c\u3092\u7d50\u3073\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u305d\u3053\u306b\u7d50\u3070\u308c\u305f\u4e00\u679a\u3072\u3068\u3064\u3076\u306e\u5e03\u306f\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u5e0c\u671b\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u5f85\u305f\u308c\u308b\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u3001\u9759\u304b\u306a\u8c61\u5fb4\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002",mythPt:"Tido como sagrado na cultura persa, o buxo (shimshad) era plantado sobretudo em santos lugares de peregrina\xe7\xe3o e em santu\xe1rios. Acreditava-se que esta \xe1rvore, que permanece verde em toda esta\xe7\xe3o, ajudava aqueles que se refugiavam junto dela. Por isso as pessoas amarravam peda\xe7os de tecido colorido aos ramos do buxo para transmitir os seus desejos e necessidades; cada pano ali amarrado era um s\xedmbolo silencioso de uma inten\xe7\xe3o aguardada com paci\xeancia e esperan\xe7a.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Buxus_sempervirens.jpg/330px-Buxus_sempervirens.jpg"},{id:"plant-128",emoji:"\ud83c\udf43",color:"#7A6A4F",name:"T\xfct\xfcn",nameEn:"Tobacco",nameDe:"Tabak",nameEs:"Tabaco",nameFr:"Tabac",nameJa:"\u30bf\u30d0\u30b3",namePt:"Tabaco",origin:"K\u0131z\u0131lderili Mitolojisi",originEn:"Native American Mythology",originDe:"Indianische Mythologie",originEs:"Mitolog\xeda amerindia",originFr:"Mythologie am\xe9rindienne",originJa:"\u30cd\u30a4\u30c6\u30a3\u30d6\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u30f3\u795e\u8a71",originPt:"Mitologia amer\xedndia",element:"hava",elementEn:"air",elementDe:"Luft",elementEs:"aire",elementFr:"air",elementJa:"\u98a8",elementPt:"ar",chakra:"Bo\u011faz \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Throat Chakra",chakraDe:"Halschakra",chakraEs:"Chakra de la Garganta",chakraFr:"Chakra de la Gorge",chakraJa:"\u5589\u306e\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra da Garganta",properties:["bar\u0131\u015f","dua","ba\u011f","misafirperverlik","arac\u0131l\u0131k"],propertiesEn:["peace","prayer","bond","hospitality","mediation"],propertiesDe:["Frieden","Gebet","Verbindung","Gastfreundschaft","Vermittlung"],propertiesEs:["paz","oraci\xf3n","v\xednculo","hospitalidad","mediaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["paix","pri\xe8re","lien","hospitalit\xe9","m\xe9diation"],propertiesJa:["\u5e73\u548c","\u7948\u308a","\u7d46","\u3082\u3066\u306a\u3057","\u4ef2\u7acb\u3061"],propertiesPt:["paz","ora\xe7\xe3o","v\xednculo","hospitalidade","media\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn y\xfckselen bir dua gibi, i\xe7tenli\u011fini g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcne ta\u015f\u0131; bar\u0131\u015f \xe7o\u011fu zaman payla\u015f\u0131lan sessiz bir anla, bir bulu\u015fmayla ba\u015flar. T\xfct\xfcn sana iki kalbin aras\u0131ndaki k\xf6pr\xfcn\xfcn, samimi bir niyetle kurulabilece\u011fini f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, like a rising prayer, carry your sincerity to the sky; peace often begins with a shared moment of silence, a meeting. Tobacco whispers that the bridge between two hearts can be built with a sincere intention.",dailyMessageDe:"Trage heute, wie ein aufsteigendes Gebet, deine Aufrichtigkeit zum Himmel; Frieden beginnt oft mit einem geteilten Augenblick der Stille, einer Begegnung. Der Tabak fl\xfcstert, dass die Br\xfccke zwischen zwei Herzen mit einer aufrichtigen Absicht gebaut werden kann.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, como una oraci\xf3n que se eleva, lleva tu sinceridad al cielo; la paz suele comenzar con un momento compartido de silencio, un encuentro. El tabaco susurra que el puente entre dos corazones puede tenderse con una intenci\xf3n sincera.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, telle une pri\xe8re qui s'\xe9l\xe8ve, porte ta sinc\xe9rit\xe9 vers le ciel ; la paix commence souvent par un moment partag\xe9 de silence, une rencontre. Le tabac murmure que le pont entre deux c\u0153urs peut se b\xe2tir avec une intention sinc\xe8re.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u7acb\u3061\u306e\u307c\u308b\u7948\u308a\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u8aa0\u5b9f\u3055\u3092\u5929\u3078\u3068\u904b\u3073\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u5e73\u548c\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u5206\u304b\u3061\u5408\u3046\u6c88\u9ed9\u306e\u3072\u3068\u3068\u304d\u3001\u3072\u3068\u3064\u306e\u51fa\u4f1a\u3044\u304b\u3089\u59cb\u307e\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30bf\u30d0\u30b3\u306f\u3001\u4e8c\u3064\u306e\u5fc3\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u306e\u6a4b\u304c\u3001\u8aa0\u5b9f\u306a\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u3088\u3063\u3066\u67b6\u3051\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, como uma ora\xe7\xe3o que se eleva, leve a sua sinceridade ao c\xe9u; a paz muitas vezes come\xe7a com um momento partilhado de sil\xeancio, um encontro. O tabaco sussurra que a ponte entre dois cora\xe7\xf5es pode ser constru\xedda com uma inten\xe7\xe3o sincera.",howToUse:"Bir tutam kurutulmu\u015f t\xfct\xfcn yapra\u011f\u0131n\u0131 bir niyet ya da dua sembol\xfc olarak k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir kapta tutabilir, t\xf6rensel bir bulu\u015fmada bar\u0131\u015f niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bitki ba\u011f\u0131ml\u0131l\u0131k yap\u0131c\u0131 ve zararl\u0131 oldu\u011fundan kullan\u0131m\u0131 yaln\u0131zca sembolik ve t\xf6renseldir; i\xe7sel kullan\u0131m \xf6nerilmez.",howToUseEn:"You may keep a pinch of dried tobacco leaf in a small vessel as a symbol of intention or prayer, accompanying an intention of peace at a ceremonial meeting. Since the plant is addictive and harmful, its use is symbolic and ceremonial only; inner use is not advised.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst eine Prise getrocknetes Tabakblatt in einem kleinen Gef\xe4\xdf als Symbol der Absicht oder des Gebets aufbewahren und so eine Absicht des Friedens bei einer zeremoniellen Begegnung begleiten. Da die Pflanze s\xfcchtig macht und sch\xe4dlich ist, ist ihr Gebrauch nur symbolisch und zeremoniell; innere Anwendung wird nicht empfohlen.",howToUseEs:"Puedes guardar una pizca de hoja de tabaco seca en un peque\xf1o recipiente como s\xedmbolo de intenci\xf3n u oraci\xf3n, acompa\xf1ando una intenci\xf3n de paz en un encuentro ceremonial. Como la planta es adictiva y da\xf1ina, su uso es solo simb\xf3lico y ceremonial; no se aconseja el uso interno.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux garder une pinc\xe9e de feuille de tabac s\xe9ch\xe9e dans un petit r\xe9cipient comme symbole d'intention ou de pri\xe8re, accompagnant une intention de paix lors d'une rencontre c\xe9r\xe9monielle. Comme la plante cr\xe9e une d\xe9pendance et est nocive, son usage est seulement symbolique et c\xe9r\xe9moniel ; l'usage interne n'est pas conseill\xe9.",howToUseJa:"\u3072\u3068\u3064\u307e\u307f\u306e\u4e7e\u3044\u305f\u30bf\u30d0\u30b3\u306e\u8449\u3092\u3001\u610f\u56f3\u3084\u7948\u308a\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u5bb9\u308c\u7269\u306b\u4fdd\u3061\u3001\u5100\u793c\u7684\u306a\u96c6\u3044\u3067\u5e73\u548c\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3053\u306e\u690d\u7269\u306f\u4f9d\u5b58\u6027\u304c\u3042\u308a\u6709\u5bb3\u3067\u3042\u308b\u305f\u3081\u3001\u305d\u306e\u7528\u3044\u65b9\u306f\u8c61\u5fb4\u7684\u30fb\u5100\u793c\u7684\u306a\u3082\u306e\u306b\u9650\u3089\u308c\u3001\u5185\u670d\u306f\u52e7\u3081\u3089\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode guardar uma pitada de folha de tabaco seca em um pequeno recipiente como s\xedmbolo de inten\xe7\xe3o ou ora\xe7\xe3o, acompanhando uma inten\xe7\xe3o de paz em um encontro cerimonial. Como a planta \xe9 viciante e nociva, seu uso \xe9 apenas simb\xf3lico e cerimonial; o uso interno n\xe3o \xe9 aconselhado.",affirmation:"\u0130\xe7tenli\u011fimi bir dua gibi g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcne ta\u015f\u0131yorum, kalplerin aras\u0131nda bar\u0131\u015f k\xf6pr\xfcs\xfc kuruyorum.",affirmationEn:"I carry my sincerity to the sky like a prayer, and I build a bridge of peace between hearts.",affirmationDe:"Ich trage meine Aufrichtigkeit wie ein Gebet zum Himmel und baue eine Br\xfccke des Friedens zwischen den Herzen.",affirmationEs:"Llevo mi sinceridad al cielo como una oraci\xf3n, y tiendo un puente de paz entre los corazones.",affirmationFr:"Je porte ma sinc\xe9rit\xe9 au ciel comme une pri\xe8re, et je b\xe2tis un pont de paix entre les c\u0153urs.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u8aa0\u5b9f\u3055\u3092\u7948\u308a\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u5929\u3078\u904b\u3073\u3001\u5fc3\u3068\u5fc3\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u306b\u5e73\u548c\u306e\u6a4b\u3092\u67b6\u3051\u308b\u3002",affirmationPt:"Levo a minha sinceridade ao c\xe9u como uma ora\xe7\xe3o, e construo uma ponte de paz entre os cora\xe7\xf5es.",myth:"T\xfct\xfcn\xfcn kullan\u0131m\u0131 ilk olarak Amerikan yerlilerine aittir; b\xfcy\xfcc\xfc-\u015fifac\u0131lar t\xfct\xfcn \xe7ubu\u011funu (Calumet) ayinlerde kullan\u0131r, bu de\u011ferli arac\u0131 konuklar\u0131na sunarak misafirperverlik g\xf6sterirlerdi. Zamanla bu t\xfct\xfcn \xe7ubu\u011fu 'bar\u0131\u015f \xe7ubu\u011fu' olarak an\u0131ld\u0131 ve yerlilerle gelenler aras\u0131ndaki bar\u0131\u015f\u0131n simgesi oldu. Bir Kuzey Amerika s\xf6ylencesinde, uzun bir yolculuk s\u0131ras\u0131nda kalabal\u0131ktan ayr\u0131lan gen\xe7 bir kad\u0131nla bir adam tenha bir yerde sevi\u015fip evlenir; sonra ilk birle\u015ftikleri yerden ge\xe7erken tatl\u0131 bir koku al\u0131r ve orada bir bitkinin bitti\u011fini g\xf6r\xfcrler. Bu bitkinin a\u015fklar\u0131n\u0131n \xfcr\xfcn\xfc oldu\u011funa inan\u0131rlar; kuruyan yapraklar\u0131 yak\u0131nca koku daha da g\xfczelle\u015fir ve bu ota t\xfct\xfcn denir. T\xfct\xfcn\xfcn, o \xf6rnek \xe7ift gibi, insanlar aras\u0131nda bar\u0131\u015f\u0131 ve mutlulu\u011fu sa\u011flad\u0131\u011f\u0131na inan\u0131l\u0131r.",mythEn:"The use of tobacco belongs first to the native peoples of America; the medicine-healers used the tobacco pipe (Calumet) in their rites and showed hospitality by offering this precious instrument to their guests. In time this pipe came to be called the 'peace pipe' and became the symbol of peace between the natives and the newcomers. In a North American tale, during a long journey, a young woman and a man who slip away from the crowd make love in a secluded place and marry; later, passing by the place where they first joined, they catch a sweet scent and see a plant growing there. They believe this plant is the fruit of their love; when its dried leaves are burned, the scent grows even lovelier, and this herb is called tobacco. It is believed that tobacco, like that exemplary couple, brings about peace and happiness among people.",mythDe:"Der Gebrauch des Tabaks geh\xf6rt zuerst den Ureinwohnern Amerikas; die Medizinheiler verwendeten die Tabakpfeife (Calumet) in ihren Riten und erwiesen Gastfreundschaft, indem sie dieses kostbare Ger\xe4t ihren G\xe4sten darboten. Mit der Zeit wurde diese Pfeife 'Friedenspfeife' genannt und wurde zum Sinnbild des Friedens zwischen den Ureinwohnern und den Ank\xf6mmlingen. In einer nordamerikanischen Erz\xe4hlung lieben sich auf einer langen Reise eine junge Frau und ein Mann, die sich von der Menge entfernen, an einem abgelegenen Ort und heiraten; sp\xe4ter, als sie an dem Ort vorbeikommen, wo sie sich zuerst vereinten, nehmen sie einen s\xfc\xdfen Duft wahr und sehen dort eine Pflanze wachsen. Sie glauben, diese Pflanze sei die Frucht ihrer Liebe; wenn ihre getrockneten Bl\xe4tter verbrannt werden, wird der Duft noch lieblicher, und dieses Kraut wird Tabak genannt. Man glaubt, dass der Tabak, wie jenes vorbildliche Paar, Frieden und Gl\xfcck unter den Menschen stiftet.",mythEs:"El uso del tabaco pertenece primero a los pueblos nativos de Am\xe9rica; los hechiceros-sanadores usaban la pipa de tabaco (Calumet) en sus ritos y mostraban hospitalidad ofreciendo este precioso instrumento a sus hu\xe9spedes. Con el tiempo, esta pipa pas\xf3 a llamarse 'pipa de la paz' y se volvi\xf3 el s\xedmbolo de la paz entre los nativos y los reci\xe9n llegados. En un relato norteamericano, durante un largo viaje, una joven y un hombre que se apartan de la multitud hacen el amor en un lugar apartado y se casan; m\xe1s tarde, al pasar por el lugar donde se unieron por primera vez, perciben un dulce aroma y ven una planta que crece all\xed. Creen que esa planta es el fruto de su amor; cuando se queman sus hojas secas, el aroma se vuelve a\xfan m\xe1s bello, y esta hierba se llama tabaco. Se cree que el tabaco, como aquella pareja ejemplar, procura la paz y la felicidad entre las personas.",mythFr:"L'usage du tabac appartient d'abord aux peuples natifs d'Am\xe9rique ; les sorciers-gu\xe9risseurs employaient la pipe \xe0 tabac (Calumet) dans leurs rites et t\xe9moignaient de l'hospitalit\xe9 en offrant ce pr\xe9cieux instrument \xe0 leurs h\xf4tes. Avec le temps, cette pipe fut appel\xe9e la \xab pipe de la paix \xbb et devint le symbole de la paix entre les natifs et les nouveaux venus. Dans un r\xe9cit nord-am\xe9ricain, au cours d'un long voyage, une jeune femme et un homme qui s'\xe9loignent de la foule font l'amour dans un lieu retir\xe9 et se marient ; plus tard, en passant par l'endroit o\xf9 ils s'unirent pour la premi\xe8re fois, ils sentent un doux parfum et voient une plante y pousser. Ils croient que cette plante est le fruit de leur amour ; quand on br\xfble ses feuilles s\xe9ch\xe9es, le parfum devient encore plus suave, et cette herbe est appel\xe9e tabac. On croit que le tabac, comme ce couple exemplaire, instaure la paix et le bonheur parmi les hommes.",mythJa:"\u30bf\u30d0\u30b3\u306e\u4f7f\u7528\u306f\u3001\u307e\u305a\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u306e\u5148\u4f4f\u6c11\u306b\u5c5e\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u546a\u533b\u305f\u3061\u306f\u5100\u5f0f\u3067\u30bf\u30d0\u30b3\u306e\u30d1\u30a4\u30d7\uff08\u30ab\u30eb\u30e1\u30c3\u30c8\uff09\u3092\u7528\u3044\u3001\u3053\u306e\u8cb4\u91cd\u306a\u9053\u5177\u3092\u5ba2\u306b\u5dee\u3057\u51fa\u3057\u3066\u3082\u3066\u306a\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3084\u304c\u3066\u3053\u306e\u30d1\u30a4\u30d7\u306f\u300e\u5e73\u548c\u306e\u30d1\u30a4\u30d7\u300f\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u3001\u5148\u4f4f\u6c11\u3068\u6765\u8a2a\u8005\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u306e\u5e73\u548c\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u3042\u308b\u5317\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u306e\u7269\u8a9e\u3067\u306f\u3001\u9577\u3044\u65c5\u306e\u9014\u4e2d\u3001\u4eba\u6df7\u307f\u304b\u3089\u96e2\u308c\u305f\u82e5\u3044\u5973\u3068\u7537\u304c\u4eba\u76ee\u306b\u3064\u304b\u306c\u5834\u6240\u3067\u611b\u3092\u4ea4\u308f\u3057\u3001\u7d50\u5a5a\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u306e\u3061\u306b\u521d\u3081\u3066\u7d50\u3070\u308c\u305f\u5834\u6240\u3092\u901a\u308a\u304b\u304b\u308b\u3068\u3001\u7518\u3044\u9999\u308a\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u304d\u3001\u305d\u3053\u306b\u4e00\u672c\u306e\u8349\u304c\u751f\u3048\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u3092\u898b\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e8c\u4eba\u306f\u305d\u306e\u8349\u3092\u81ea\u5206\u305f\u3061\u306e\u611b\u306e\u5b9f\u308a\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e7e\u3044\u305f\u8449\u3092\u71c3\u3084\u3059\u3068\u9999\u308a\u306f\u3044\u3063\u305d\u3046\u7f8e\u3057\u304f\u306a\u308a\u3001\u3053\u306e\u8349\u306f\u30bf\u30d0\u30b3\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30bf\u30d0\u30b3\u306f\u3001\u3042\u306e\u624b\u672c\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306a\u592b\u5a66\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u4eba\u3005\u306e\u3042\u3044\u3060\u306b\u5e73\u548c\u3068\u5e78\u798f\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u3068\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"O uso do tabaco pertence primeiro aos povos nativos da Am\xe9rica; os feiticeiros-curandeiros usavam o cachimbo de tabaco (Calumet) em seus ritos e mostravam hospitalidade oferecendo este precioso instrumento aos seus convidados. Com o tempo, este cachimbo passou a ser chamado 'cachimbo da paz' e tornou-se o s\xedmbolo da paz entre os nativos e os rec\xe9m-chegados. Num relato norte-americano, durante uma longa viagem, uma jovem e um homem que se afastam da multid\xe3o fazem amor num lugar isolado e se casam; mais tarde, ao passar pelo lugar onde se uniram pela primeira vez, sentem um doce aroma e veem uma planta crescendo ali. Acreditam que essa planta \xe9 o fruto do seu amor; quando suas folhas secas s\xe3o queimadas, o aroma torna-se ainda mais belo, e esta erva \xe9 chamada tabaco. Acredita-se que o tabaco, como aquele casal exemplar, traz paz e felicidade entre as pessoas.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/DunhillLightFlake.jpg/330px-DunhillLightFlake.jpg"},{id:"plant-129",emoji:"\ud83d\udc99",color:"#4A90D9",name:"Unutma Beni \xc7i\xe7e\u011fi",nameEn:"Forget-me-not",nameDe:"Vergissmeinnicht",nameEs:"Nomeolvides",nameFr:"Myosotis",nameJa:"\u30ef\u30b9\u30ec\u30ca\u30b0\u30b5",namePt:"Mios\xf3tis",origin:"Avrupa Halk Gelene\u011fi",originEn:"European Folk Tradition",originDe:"Europ\xe4ische Volkstradition",originEs:"Tradici\xf3n popular europea",originFr:"Tradition populaire europ\xe9enne",originJa:"\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u306e\u6c11\u9593\u4f1d\u627f",originPt:"Tradi\xe7\xe3o popular europeia",element:"su",elementEn:"water",elementDe:"Wasser",elementEs:"agua",elementFr:"eau",elementJa:"\u6c34",elementPt:"\xe1gua",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["sad\u0131k a\u015fk","anma","ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k","fedak\xe2rl\u0131k","hat\u0131rlama"],propertiesEn:["faithful love","remembrance","devotion","sacrifice","memory"],propertiesDe:["treue Liebe","Erinnerung","Hingabe","Aufopferung","Ged\xe4chtnis"],propertiesEs:["amor fiel","memoria","devoci\xf3n","sacrificio","recuerdo"],propertiesFr:["amour fid\xe8le","souvenir","d\xe9votion","sacrifice","m\xe9moire"],propertiesJa:["\u8aa0\u5b9f\u306a\u611b","\u8ffd\u61b6","\u732e\u8eab","\u72a0\u7272","\u8a18\u61b6"],propertiesPt:["amor fiel","mem\xf3ria","devo\xe7\xe3o","sacrif\xedcio","lembran\xe7a"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xf6z\xfcn\xfc kama\u015ft\u0131ran hazinelerin ortas\u0131nda, en k\u0131ymetli \u015feyi unutma; ger\xe7ek de\u011fer \xe7o\u011fu zaman parlayanda de\u011fil, sana 'beni unutma' diyen sevgide sakl\u0131d\u0131r. Unutma Beni \xc7i\xe7e\u011fi sana sad\u0131k bir sevginin, her \u015feyden daha de\u011ferli oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, amid treasures that dazzle your eyes, do not forget the most precious thing; true worth often hides not in what glitters but in the love that says to you, 'forget me not.' The forget-me-not whispers that a faithful love is more precious than anything.",dailyMessageDe:"Vergiss heute inmitten von Sch\xe4tzen, die deine Augen blenden, das Kostbarste nicht; wahrer Wert verbirgt sich oft nicht im Gl\xe4nzenden, sondern in der Liebe, die zu dir sagt: 'Vergiss mein nicht.' Das Vergissmeinnicht fl\xfcstert, dass eine treue Liebe kostbarer ist als alles andere.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, entre tesoros que deslumbran tus ojos, no olvides lo m\xe1s precioso; el verdadero valor suele ocultarse no en lo que brilla, sino en el amor que te dice: 'no me olvides.' El nomeolvides susurra que un amor fiel es m\xe1s precioso que cualquier cosa.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, parmi les tr\xe9sors qui \xe9blouissent tes yeux, n'oublie pas le plus pr\xe9cieux ; la vraie valeur se cache souvent non dans ce qui brille, mais dans l'amour qui te dit : \xab ne m'oublie pas. \xbb Le myosotis murmure qu'un amour fid\xe8le est plus pr\xe9cieux que tout.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u76ee\u3092\u7729\u307e\u305b\u308b\u5b9d\u306e\u53ea\u4e2d\u3067\u3001\u6700\u3082\u5c0a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u3092\u5fd8\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002\u771f\u306e\u4fa1\u5024\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3070\u3057\u3070\u8f1d\u304f\u3082\u306e\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306b\u300e\u79c1\u3092\u5fd8\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3067\u300f\u3068\u8a9e\u308a\u304b\u3051\u308b\u611b\u306b\u96a0\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u30ef\u30b9\u30ec\u30ca\u30b0\u30b5\u306f\u3001\u8aa0\u5b9f\u306a\u611b\u304c\u4f55\u3088\u308a\u3082\u5c0a\u3044\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, em meio a tesouros que deslumbram os seus olhos, n\xe3o esque\xe7a a coisa mais preciosa; o verdadeiro valor muitas vezes se esconde n\xe3o no que brilha, mas no amor que lhe diz: 'n\xe3o me esque\xe7a.' O mios\xf3tis sussurra que um amor fiel \xe9 mais precioso do que qualquer coisa.",howToUse:"Unutma beni \xe7i\xe7e\u011finin k\xfc\xe7\xfck mavi \xe7i\xe7eklerini bir vazoda seyrederek anma ve sad\u0131k a\u015fk niyetine e\u015flik edebilirsin. Bir tutam bu \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi sevdi\u011fine sunmak ya da bir hat\u0131ra kitab\u0131n\u0131n aras\u0131nda kurutmak da ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k ve hat\u0131rlama niyetini onurland\u0131ran nazik bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may contemplate the forget-me-not's small blue flowers in a vase to accompany an intention of remembrance and faithful love. Offering a handful of these flowers to someone you love or pressing them in a keepsake book is also a gentle gesture honoring an intention of devotion and memory.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die kleinen blauen Bl\xfcten des Vergissmeinnichts in einer Vase betrachten, um eine Absicht von Erinnerung und treuer Liebe zu begleiten. Eine Handvoll dieser Bl\xfcten einem geliebten Menschen zu schenken oder sie in einem Erinnerungsbuch zu pressen ist ebenfalls eine zarte Geste, die eine Absicht von Hingabe und Ged\xe4chtnis ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes contemplar las peque\xf1as flores azules del nomeolvides en un jarr\xf3n para acompa\xf1ar una intenci\xf3n de memoria y amor fiel. Ofrecer un pu\xf1ado de estas flores a alguien a quien amas o prensarlas en un libro de recuerdos es tambi\xe9n un gesto tierno que honra una intenci\xf3n de devoci\xf3n y recuerdo.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux contempler les petites fleurs bleues du myosotis dans un vase pour accompagner une intention de souvenir et d'amour fid\xe8le. Offrir une poign\xe9e de ces fleurs \xe0 un \xeatre aim\xe9 ou les presser dans un livre-souvenir est aussi un geste tendre qui honore une intention de d\xe9votion et de m\xe9moire.",howToUseJa:"\u30ef\u30b9\u30ec\u30ca\u30b0\u30b5\u306e\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u9752\u3044\u82b1\u3092\u82b1\u74f6\u3067\u773a\u3081\u3066\u3001\u8ffd\u61b6\u3068\u8aa0\u5b9f\u306a\u611b\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306b\u5bc4\u308a\u6dfb\u308f\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3072\u3068\u3064\u304b\u307f\u306e\u3053\u306e\u82b1\u3092\u611b\u3059\u308b\u4eba\u306b\u8d08\u3063\u305f\u308a\u3001\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u306e\u672c\u306b\u306f\u3055\u3093\u3067\u62bc\u3057\u82b1\u306b\u3057\u305f\u308a\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u732e\u8eab\u3068\u8a18\u61b6\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode contemplar as pequenas flores azuis do mios\xf3tis em um vaso para acompanhar uma inten\xe7\xe3o de mem\xf3ria e amor fiel. Oferecer um punhado dessas flores a algu\xe9m que voc\xea ama ou prens\xe1-las em um livro de recorda\xe7\xf5es \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto terno que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de devo\xe7\xe3o e lembran\xe7a.",affirmation:"Parlayan\u0131n ortas\u0131nda en k\u0131ymetliyi unutmuyorum, sad\u0131k bir sevgiyi kalbimde ta\u015f\u0131yorum.",affirmationEn:"Amid all that glitters I do not forget the most precious, and I carry a faithful love in my heart.",affirmationDe:"Inmitten von allem, was gl\xe4nzt, vergesse ich das Kostbarste nicht, und ich trage eine treue Liebe in meinem Herzen.",affirmationEs:"En medio de todo lo que brilla no olvido lo m\xe1s precioso, y llevo un amor fiel en mi coraz\xf3n.",affirmationFr:"Au milieu de tout ce qui brille, je n'oublie pas le plus pr\xe9cieux, et je porte un amour fid\xe8le dans mon c\u0153ur.",affirmationJa:"\u8f1d\u304f\u3082\u306e\u3059\u3079\u3066\u306e\u53ea\u4e2d\u3067\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u6700\u3082\u5c0a\u3044\u3082\u306e\u3092\u5fd8\u308c\u305a\u3001\u8aa0\u5b9f\u306a\u611b\u3092\u5fc3\u306b\u62b1\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Em meio a tudo o que brilha, n\xe3o esque\xe7o o mais precioso, e carrego um amor fiel no meu cora\xe7\xe3o.",myth:"Bir halk s\xf6ylencesine g\xf6re da\u011fda gezen bir adam, yerde mavi bir \xe7i\xe7ek g\xf6r\xfcp kopar\u0131r ve \u015fapkas\u0131na takar; o anda \xf6n\xfcnde kocaman bir demir kap\u0131 aralan\u0131r. \u0130\xe7eride yakut, z\xfcmr\xfct, elmas y\u0131\u011f\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r; adam a\xe7 g\xf6zl\xfcl\xfckle ceplerini doldururken d\xfc\u015fen \u015fapkas\u0131n\u0131 fark etmez. Tam \xe7\u0131karken \u015fapkayla yere d\xfc\u015fen mavi \xe7i\xe7ek 'beni unutma' diye seslenir; ama adam d\xf6n\xfcp daha \xe7ok ta\u015f toplar ve kap\u0131 aniden kapan\u0131r, esrarengiz kap\u0131n\u0131n s\u0131rr\u0131 o \xe7i\xe7ekte kald\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\xe7in bir daha asla bulunamaz. Bir Avusturya s\xf6ylencesinde ise Tuna k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131ndaki iki sevgili ak\u0131nt\u0131ya kap\u0131lm\u0131\u015f mavi bir \xe7i\xe7ek g\xf6r\xfcr; gen\xe7 adam sevgilisi i\xe7in nehre atlay\u0131p \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi ona f\u0131rlat\u0131r ama kendisi sulara kap\u0131l\u0131rken son s\xf6z\xfc 'beni unutma' olur, ve \xe7i\xe7e\u011fe bu ad verilir.",mythEn:"According to a folk tale, a man walking in the mountains sees a blue flower on the ground, plucks it, and pins it to his hat; at that moment a huge iron door opens before him. Inside, rubies, emeralds, and diamonds are heaped up; as he greedily fills his pockets, he does not notice his hat that has fallen. Just as he is about to leave, the blue flower that fell with the hat calls out, 'forget me not'; but the man turns back to gather still more stones, and the door suddenly shuts, and because the secret of the mysterious door remained in that flower, it can never be found again. In an Austrian tale, two lovers by the Danube see a blue flower carried off by the current; the young man leaps into the river for his beloved and flings the flower to her, but as he himself is swept away, his last word is 'forget me not,' and so the flower is given this name.",mythDe:"Einem Volksm\xe4rchen nach sieht ein Mann, der im Gebirge wandert, eine blaue Blume am Boden, pfl\xfcckt sie und steckt sie an seinen Hut; in diesem Augenblick \xf6ffnet sich vor ihm eine riesige eiserne T\xfcr. Drinnen sind Rubine, Smaragde und Diamanten aufgeh\xe4uft; w\xe4hrend er gierig seine Taschen f\xfcllt, bemerkt er seinen Hut nicht, der herabgefallen ist. Gerade als er gehen will, ruft die blaue Blume, die mit dem Hut zu Boden fiel: 'Vergiss mein nicht'; doch der Mann kehrt um, noch mehr Steine zu sammeln, und die T\xfcr schlie\xdft sich pl\xf6tzlich, und weil das Geheimnis der geheimnisvollen T\xfcr in jener Blume blieb, kann sie nie wieder gefunden werden. In einer \xf6sterreichischen Erz\xe4hlung sehen zwei Liebende an der Donau eine blaue Blume, die die Str\xf6mung forttr\xe4gt; der junge Mann springt f\xfcr seine Geliebte in den Fluss und schleudert ihr die Blume zu, doch w\xe4hrend er selbst fortgerissen wird, ist sein letztes Wort 'Vergiss mein nicht', und so erh\xe4lt die Blume diesen Namen.",mythEs:"Seg\xfan un cuento popular, un hombre que pasea por las monta\xf1as ve una flor azul en el suelo, la arranca y la prende en su sombrero; en ese instante se abre ante \xe9l una enorme puerta de hierro. Dentro hay rub\xedes, esmeraldas y diamantes amontonados; mientras llena con avidez sus bolsillos, no advierte su sombrero, que ha ca\xeddo. Justo cuando va a salir, la flor azul que cay\xf3 con el sombrero exclama: 'no me olvides'; pero el hombre vuelve a recoger a\xfan m\xe1s piedras, y la puerta se cierra de golpe, y como el secreto de la misteriosa puerta qued\xf3 en aquella flor, nunca m\xe1s puede hallarse. En un relato austr\xedaco, dos amantes junto al Danubio ven una flor azul arrastrada por la corriente; el joven se lanza al r\xedo por su amada y le arroja la flor, pero mientras \xe9l mismo es arrastrado, su \xfaltima palabra es 'no me olvides', y as\xed se le da este nombre a la flor.",mythFr:"Selon un conte populaire, un homme qui se prom\xe8ne dans les montagnes voit une fleur bleue par terre, la cueille et la pique \xe0 son chapeau ; \xe0 cet instant, une \xe9norme porte de fer s'ouvre devant lui. \xc0 l'int\xe9rieur, des rubis, des \xe9meraudes et des diamants sont entass\xe9s ; tandis qu'il remplit avidement ses poches, il ne remarque pas son chapeau qui est tomb\xe9. Au moment o\xf9 il va sortir, la fleur bleue tomb\xe9e avec le chapeau s'\xe9crie : \xab ne m'oublie pas \xbb ; mais l'homme revient ramasser encore plus de pierres, et la porte se referme soudain, et parce que le secret de la porte myst\xe9rieuse est rest\xe9 dans cette fleur, on ne peut plus jamais la retrouver. Dans un r\xe9cit autrichien, deux amants au bord du Danube voient une fleur bleue emport\xe9e par le courant ; le jeune homme se jette dans le fleuve pour sa bien-aim\xe9e et lui lance la fleur, mais tandis qu'il est lui-m\xeame emport\xe9, son dernier mot est \xab ne m'oublie pas \xbb, et c'est ainsi que la fleur re\xe7oit ce nom.",mythJa:"\u3042\u308b\u6c11\u8a71\u306b\u3088\u308c\u3070\u3001\u5c71\u3092\u6b69\u304f\u7537\u304c\u5730\u9762\u306b\u9752\u3044\u82b1\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u3066\u6458\u307f\u3001\u5e3d\u5b50\u306b\u633f\u3059\u3068\u3001\u305d\u306e\u77ac\u9593\u3001\u76ee\u306e\u524d\u306b\u5de8\u5927\u306a\u9244\u306e\u6249\u304c\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e2d\u306b\u306f\u30eb\u30d3\u30fc\u3001\u30a8\u30e1\u30e9\u30eb\u30c9\u3001\u30c0\u30a4\u30e4\u30e2\u30f3\u30c9\u304c\u7a4d\u307f\u4e0a\u3052\u3089\u308c\u3001\u7537\u306f\u6b32\u6df1\u304f\u30dd\u30b1\u30c3\u30c8\u3092\u6e80\u305f\u3059\u3046\u3061\u3001\u843d\u3061\u305f\u5e3d\u5b50\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u304d\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002\u7acb\u3061\u53bb\u308d\u3046\u3068\u3057\u305f\u307e\u3055\u306b\u305d\u306e\u3068\u304d\u3001\u5e3d\u5b50\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u843d\u3061\u305f\u9752\u3044\u82b1\u304c\u300e\u79c1\u3092\u5fd8\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3067\u300f\u3068\u547c\u3073\u304b\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3051\u308c\u3069\u7537\u306f\u3082\u3063\u3068\u591a\u304f\u306e\u5b9d\u77f3\u3092\u62fe\u3044\u306b\u623b\u308a\u3001\u6249\u306f\u7a81\u7136\u9589\u3058\u3001\u8b0e\u306e\u6249\u306e\u79d8\u5bc6\u306f\u305d\u306e\u82b1\u306b\u6b8b\u3063\u305f\u305f\u3081\u3001\u4e8c\u5ea6\u3068\u898b\u3064\u3051\u3089\u308c\u306a\u304f\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3042\u308b\u30aa\u30fc\u30b9\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u306e\u7269\u8a9e\u3067\u306f\u3001\u30c9\u30ca\u30a6\u306e\u307b\u3068\u308a\u306e\u4e8c\u4eba\u306e\u604b\u4eba\u304c\u3001\u6d41\u308c\u306b\u3055\u3089\u308f\u308c\u308b\u9752\u3044\u82b1\u3092\u898b\u307e\u3059\u3002\u82e5\u8005\u306f\u604b\u4eba\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u5ddd\u306b\u98db\u3073\u8fbc\u307f\u3001\u82b1\u3092\u5f7c\u5973\u306b\u6295\u3052\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u81ea\u3089\u306f\u6d41\u3055\u308c\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3001\u305d\u306e\u6700\u5f8c\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u304c\u300e\u79c1\u3092\u5fd8\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3067\u300f\u3068\u306a\u308a\u3001\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u82b1\u306b\u3053\u306e\u540d\u304c\u4e0e\u3048\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",mythPt:"Segundo um conto popular, um homem que passeia nas montanhas v\xea uma flor azul no ch\xe3o, colhe-a e prende-a ao chap\xe9u; nesse instante, uma enorme porta de ferro se abre diante dele. Dentro, h\xe1 rubis, esmeraldas e diamantes amontoados; enquanto enche avidamente os bolsos, n\xe3o percebe o chap\xe9u que caiu. Justo quando vai sair, a flor azul que caiu com o chap\xe9u exclama: 'n\xe3o me esque\xe7a'; mas o homem volta para recolher ainda mais pedras, e a porta se fecha de repente, e porque o segredo da misteriosa porta ficou naquela flor, ela nunca mais pode ser encontrada. Num relato austr\xedaco, dois amantes \xe0 beira do Dan\xfabio veem uma flor azul levada pela correnteza; o jovem atira-se ao rio pela amada e lhe lan\xe7a a flor, mas enquanto ele pr\xf3prio \xe9 arrastado, a sua \xfaltima palavra \xe9 'n\xe3o me esque\xe7a', e assim a flor recebe esse nome.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Myosotis_arvensis_ois.JPG/330px-Myosotis_arvensis_ois.JPG"},{id:"plant-130",emoji:"\ud83e\uded2",color:"#6B7A3A",name:"Zeytin",nameEn:"Olive",nameDe:"Olive",nameEs:"Olivo",nameFr:"Olivier",nameJa:"\u30aa\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6",namePt:"Oliveira",origin:"Antik Yunan & Akdeniz",originEn:"Ancient Greece & Mediterranean",originDe:"Antikes Griechenland & Mittelmeerraum",originEs:"Antigua Grecia y Mediterr\xe1neo",originFr:"Gr\xe8ce antique et M\xe9diterran\xe9e",originJa:"\u53e4\u4ee3\u30ae\u30ea\u30b7\u30e3\u30fb\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77",originPt:"Gr\xe9cia Antiga e Mediterr\xe2neo",element:"toprak",elementEn:"earth",elementDe:"Erde",elementEs:"tierra",elementFr:"terre",elementJa:"\u5730",elementPt:"terra",chakra:"Kalp \xc7akra",chakraEn:"Heart Chakra",chakraDe:"Herzchakra",chakraEs:"Chakra del Coraz\xf3n",chakraFr:"Chakra du C\u0153ur",chakraJa:"\u30cf\u30fc\u30c8\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30e9",chakraPt:"Chakra Card\xedaco",properties:["bar\u0131\u015f","bilgelik","bereket","\xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck","uzla\u015fma"],propertiesEn:["peace","wisdom","abundance","immortality","reconciliation"],propertiesDe:["Frieden","Weisheit","F\xfclle","Unsterblichkeit","Vers\xf6hnung"],propertiesEs:["paz","sabidur\xeda","abundancia","inmortalidad","reconciliaci\xf3n"],propertiesFr:["paix","sagesse","abondance","immortalit\xe9","r\xe9conciliation"],propertiesJa:["\u5e73\u548c","\u53e1\u667a","\u8c4a\u7a63","\u4e0d\u6b7b","\u548c\u89e3"],propertiesPt:["paz","sabedoria","abund\xe2ncia","imortalidade","reconcilia\xe7\xe3o"],dailyMessage:"Bug\xfcn g\xfc\xe7 g\xf6sterisi yerine bilgece bir arma\u011fan sun; en kal\u0131c\u0131 zafer, y\u0131kmayan, besleyen ve bar\u0131\u015f getiren oland\u0131r. Zeytin sana yak\u0131lsan bile k\xfcllerinden yeniden filiz verebilece\u011fini, sabr\u0131n ve bar\u0131\u015f\u0131n \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz bir g\xfc\xe7 oldu\u011funu f\u0131s\u0131ldar.",dailyMessageEn:"Today, instead of a show of force, offer a wise gift; the most lasting victory is the one that does not destroy but nourishes and brings peace. The olive whispers that even if you are burned, you can sprout anew from your ashes, and that patience and peace are an immortal strength.",dailyMessageDe:"Biete heute statt einer Machtdemonstration ein weises Geschenk dar; der dauerhafteste Sieg ist jener, der nicht zerst\xf6rt, sondern n\xe4hrt und Frieden bringt. Die Olive fl\xfcstert, dass du, selbst wenn du verbrannt wirst, aus deiner Asche neu sprie\xdfen kannst und dass Geduld und Frieden eine unsterbliche Kraft sind.",dailyMessageEs:"Hoy, en lugar de un alarde de fuerza, ofrece un don sabio; la victoria m\xe1s duradera es la que no destruye, sino que nutre y trae paz. El olivo susurra que, aunque te quemen, puedes brotar de nuevo de tus cenizas, y que la paciencia y la paz son una fuerza inmortal.",dailyMessageFr:"Aujourd'hui, au lieu d'une d\xe9monstration de force, offre un don sage ; la victoire la plus durable est celle qui ne d\xe9truit pas mais nourrit et apporte la paix. L'olivier murmure que, m\xeame si tu es br\xfbl\xe9, tu peux rena\xeetre de tes cendres, et que la patience et la paix sont une force immortelle.",dailyMessageJa:"\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u529b\u306e\u8a87\u793a\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u3001\u8ce2\u3044\u8d08\u308a\u3082\u306e\u3092\u5dee\u3057\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002\u6700\u3082\u9577\u304f\u7d9a\u304f\u52dd\u5229\u306f\u3001\u58ca\u3055\u305a\u3001\u990a\u3044\u3001\u5e73\u548c\u3092\u3082\u305f\u3089\u3059\u3082\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002\u30aa\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6\u306f\u3001\u305f\u3068\u3048\u713c\u304b\u308c\u3066\u3082\u3001\u7070\u306e\u4e2d\u304b\u3089\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u82bd\u5439\u3051\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3001\u305d\u3057\u3066\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u5e73\u548c\u304c\u4e0d\u6b7b\u306e\u529b\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3068\u56c1\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",dailyMessagePt:"Hoje, em vez de uma demonstra\xe7\xe3o de for\xe7a, ofere\xe7a um presente s\xe1bio; a vit\xf3ria mais duradoura \xe9 a que n\xe3o destr\xf3i, mas nutre e traz paz. A oliveira sussurra que, mesmo que voc\xea seja queimado, pode brotar de novo das suas cinzas, e que a paci\xeancia e a paz s\xe3o uma for\xe7a imortal.",howToUse:"Zeytin meyvesini ya da zeytinya\u011f\u0131n\u0131 besleyici bir ikram olarak tadabilir, bir zeytin dal\u0131n\u0131 bar\u0131\u015f ve uzla\u015fma niyetinin simgesi olarak yan\u0131nda bulundurabilirsin. Bir damla zeytinya\u011f\u0131yla bir kandil yakmak da bilgelik ve bereket niyetini onurland\u0131ran eski bir jesttir.",howToUseEn:"You may enjoy the olive fruit or olive oil as a nourishing treat, and keep an olive branch by you as a symbol of an intention of peace and reconciliation. Lighting a lamp with a drop of olive oil is also an ancient gesture honoring an intention of wisdom and abundance.",howToUseDe:"Du kannst die Olivenfrucht oder das Oliven\xf6l als n\xe4hrende K\xf6stlichkeit genie\xdfen und einen Olivenzweig als Symbol einer Absicht von Frieden und Vers\xf6hnung bei dir behalten. Eine Lampe mit einem Tropfen Oliven\xf6l zu entz\xfcnden ist ebenfalls eine alte Geste, die eine Absicht von Weisheit und F\xfclle ehrt.",howToUseEs:"Puedes disfrutar el fruto del olivo o el aceite de oliva como un manjar nutritivo, y guardar junto a ti una rama de olivo como s\xedmbolo de una intenci\xf3n de paz y reconciliaci\xf3n. Encender una l\xe1mpara con una gota de aceite de oliva es tambi\xe9n un gesto antiguo que honra una intenci\xf3n de sabidur\xeda y abundancia.",howToUseFr:"Tu peux savourer le fruit de l'olivier ou l'huile d'olive comme une douceur nourrissante, et garder pr\xe8s de toi un rameau d'olivier comme symbole d'une intention de paix et de r\xe9conciliation. Allumer une lampe avec une goutte d'huile d'olive est aussi un geste ancien qui honore une intention de sagesse et d'abondance.",howToUseJa:"\u30aa\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6\u306e\u5b9f\u3084\u30aa\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6\u6cb9\u3092\u6ecb\u990a\u3042\u308b\u4e00\u54c1\u3068\u3057\u3066\u5473\u308f\u3044\u3001\u5e73\u548c\u3068\u548c\u89e3\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3001\u30aa\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6\u306e\u679d\u3092\u305d\u3070\u306b\u7f6e\u304f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e00\u6ef4\u306e\u30aa\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6\u6cb9\u3067\u706f\u3092\u3068\u3082\u3059\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3001\u53e1\u667a\u3068\u8c4a\u7a63\u306e\u610f\u56f3\u3092\u656c\u3046\u53e4\u3044\u884c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",howToUsePt:"Voc\xea pode apreciar o fruto da oliveira ou o azeite de oliva como uma guloseima nutritiva, e manter junto de si um ramo de oliveira como s\xedmbolo de uma inten\xe7\xe3o de paz e reconcilia\xe7\xe3o. Acender uma lamparina com uma gota de azeite \xe9 tamb\xe9m um gesto antigo que honra uma inten\xe7\xe3o de sabedoria e abund\xe2ncia.",affirmation:"G\xfc\xe7 g\xf6sterisi yerine bilgece bir arma\u011fan sunuyorum, k\xfcllerimden bile yeniden filiz veriyorum.",affirmationEn:"Instead of a show of force I offer a wise gift, and I sprout anew even from my ashes.",affirmationDe:"Statt einer Machtdemonstration biete ich ein weises Geschenk dar, und ich sprie\xdfe sogar aus meiner Asche neu.",affirmationEs:"En lugar de un alarde de fuerza ofrezco un don sabio, y broto de nuevo incluso de mis cenizas.",affirmationFr:"Au lieu d'une d\xe9monstration de force, j'offre un don sage, et je renais m\xeame de mes cendres.",affirmationJa:"\u79c1\u306f\u529b\u306e\u8a87\u793a\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u8ce2\u3044\u8d08\u308a\u3082\u306e\u3092\u5dee\u3057\u51fa\u3057\u3001\u7070\u306e\u4e2d\u304b\u3089\u3055\u3048\u3075\u305f\u305f\u3073\u82bd\u5439\u304f\u3002",affirmationPt:"Em vez de uma demonstra\xe7\xe3o de for\xe7a, ofere\xe7o um presente s\xe1bio, e broto de novo at\xe9 das minhas cinzas.",myth:"Zeytin, Anadolu ve Akdeniz'in \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz a\u011fac\u0131d\u0131r; binlerce y\u0131l ya\u015far, kesilse de k\xf6k\xfcnden yeniden filizlenir. Bar\u0131\u015f\u0131n, bereketin ve kal\u0131c\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n simgesidir \u2014 sava\u015f sonras\u0131 uzat\u0131lan zeytin dal\u0131 sulhun habercisidir. Antik \xe7a\u011fda Athena'n\u0131n arma\u011fan\u0131 say\u0131lan zeytin, kutsal kandilleri yakar, kazananlar\u0131n ba\u015f\u0131na ta\xe7 olurdu. Anadolu'da zeytinya\u011f\u0131 \u015fifan\u0131n, ayd\u0131nl\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve kutsaman\u0131n \xf6z\xfcd\xfcr; t\xfcrbelerde kandiller onunla yanar. Ya\u015fl\u0131 ama h\xe2l\xe2 meyve veren g\xf6vdesi, sabr\u0131n ve k\xf6kl\xfc bilgeli\u011fin dersidir.",mythEn:"The olive is the immortal tree of Anatolia and the Mediterranean; it lives for thousands of years and, though cut down, sprouts again from its root. It is the emblem of peace, abundance and permanence \u2014 the olive branch extended after war heralds reconciliation. In antiquity the gift of Athena, the olive lit sacred lamps and crowned victors. In Anatolia olive oil is the essence of healing, light and blessing; the lamps of shrines burn with it. Its old yet still-fruiting trunk is the lesson of patience and deep-rooted wisdom.",mythDe:"Der Olivenbaum ist der unsterbliche Baum Anatoliens und des Mittelmeers; er lebt Tausende von Jahren und treibt, selbst gef\xe4llt, aus der Wurzel neu aus. Er ist Sinnbild von Frieden, F\xfclle und Best\xe4ndigkeit \u2014 der nach dem Krieg gereichte \xd6lzweig k\xfcndet Vers\xf6hnung an. In der Antike Gabe der Athene, entz\xfcndete die Olive heilige Lampen und kr\xf6nte die Sieger. In Anatolien ist Oliven\xf6l die Essenz von Heilung, Licht und Segen; die Lampen der Schreine brennen damit. Sein alter, doch noch fruchtender Stamm lehrt Geduld und tief verwurzelte Weisheit.",mythEs:"El olivo es el \xe1rbol inmortal de Anatolia y el Mediterr\xe1neo; vive miles de a\xf1os y, aun talado, rebrota desde su ra\xedz. Es emblema de paz, abundancia y permanencia \u2014 la rama de olivo tendida tras la guerra anuncia la reconciliaci\xf3n. En la antig\xfcedad, don de Atenea, el olivo encend\xeda l\xe1mparas sagradas y coronaba a los vencedores. En Anatolia el aceite de oliva es la esencia de la sanaci\xf3n, la luz y la bendici\xf3n; con \xe9l arden las l\xe1mparas de los santuarios. Su tronco viejo pero a\xfan fruct\xedfero ense\xf1a la paciencia y la sabidur\xeda de ra\xedces profundas.",mythFr:"L'olivier est l'arbre immortel de l'Anatolie et de la M\xe9diterran\xe9e ; il vit des mill\xe9naires et, m\xeame abattu, repousse de sa racine. Il est l'embl\xe8me de la paix, de l'abondance et de la permanence \u2014 le rameau d'olivier tendu apr\xe8s la guerre annonce la r\xe9conciliation. Dans l'Antiquit\xe9, don d'Ath\xe9na, l'olivier allumait les lampes sacr\xe9es et couronnait les vainqueurs. En Anatolie, l'huile d'olive est l'essence de la gu\xe9rison, de la lumi\xe8re et de la b\xe9n\xe9diction ; les lampes des sanctuaires en br\xfblent. Son tronc vieux mais encore f\xe9cond enseigne la patience et la sagesse aux racines profondes.",mythJa:"\u30aa\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6\u306f\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3068\u5730\u4e2d\u6d77\u306e\u4e0d\u6b7b\u306e\u6a39\u3002\u4f55\u5343\u5e74\u3082\u751f\u304d\u3001\u5207\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3082\u6839\u304b\u3089\u518d\u3073\u82bd\u5439\u304f\u3002\u5e73\u548c\u3068\u8c4a\u7a63\u3068\u6c38\u7d9a\u306e\u8c61\u5fb4\u2014\u2014\u6226\u306e\u5f8c\u306b\u5dee\u3057\u51fa\u3055\u308c\u308b\u30aa\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6\u306e\u679d\u306f\u548c\u89e3\u306e\u544a\u3052\u3002\u53e4\u4ee3\u306b\u306f\u30a2\u30c6\u30ca\u306e\u8d08\u308a\u7269\u3068\u3055\u308c\u3001\u8056\u306a\u308b\u706f\u3092\u70b9\u3057\u3001\u52dd\u8005\u306e\u982d\u3092\u51a0\u3057\u305f\u3002\u30a2\u30ca\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u3067\u306f\u30aa\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6\u6cb9\u306f\u7652\u3057\u3068\u5149\u3068\u795d\u798f\u306e\u7cbe\u9ac4\u3067\u3042\u308a\u3001\u8056\u5edf\u306e\u706f\u306f\u3053\u308c\u3067\u71c3\u3048\u308b\u3002\u8001\u3044\u3066\u306a\u304a\u5b9f\u3092\u3064\u3051\u308b\u305d\u306e\u5e79\u306f\u3001\u5fcd\u8010\u3068\u6df1\u304f\u6839\u3056\u3057\u305f\u53e1\u667a\u306e\u6559\u3048\u3002",mythPt:"A oliveira \xe9 a \xe1rvore imortal da Anat\xf3lia e do Mediterr\xe2neo; vive milhares de anos e, mesmo cortada, rebenta de novo da raiz. \xc9 emblema de paz, abund\xe2ncia e perman\xeancia \u2014 o ramo de oliveira estendido ap\xf3s a guerra anuncia a reconcilia\xe7\xe3o. Na antiguidade, d\xe1diva de Atena, a oliveira acendia l\xe2mpadas sagradas e coroava os vencedores. Na Anat\xf3lia, o azeite \xe9 a ess\xeancia da cura, da luz e da b\xean\xe7\xe3o; com ele ardem as l\xe2mpadas dos santu\xe1rios. O seu tronco velho mas ainda frut\xedfero ensina a paci\xeancia e a sabedoria de ra\xedzes profundas.",imageUrl:"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Olivesfromjordan.jpg/330px-Olivesfromjordan.jpg"}]},731,[]);
__d(function(e,a,i,n,r,t,o){r.exports=[{id:"a001",name:"Bozkurt",emoji:"\ud83d\udc3a",element:"hava",symbolism:["liderlik","aile","koruma","i\xe7g\xfcd\xfc"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Canis_lupus_lupus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Bozkurt, T\xfcrk mitolojisinin kalbinde ya\u015fayan en kutsal rehber hayvand\u0131r; Ergenekon destan\u0131nda karanl\u0131k da\u011fdan \xe7\u0131k\u0131\u015f\u0131 yaln\u0131zca o m\xfcmk\xfcn k\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. G\xf6k T\xfcrk gelene\u011finde kurt, ata ruhlar\u0131n\u0131n bedenlenmi\u015f hali olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr \u2014 ulumas\u0131 d\xfcnyalar aras\u0131 bir mesaj, izi ise kutsal bir yol haritas\u0131d\u0131r. Orta Asya \u015famanizminde \u015faman c\xfcbbesine kurt postu dikilmesi, o g\xfcc\xfc beden \xfczerinde ta\u015f\u0131mak i\xe7indir. Kuzey Amerika yerli gelene\u011finde kurt, s\xfcr\xfc zekas\u0131 ve sesle ileti\u015fim kurma g\xfcc\xfcyle \xf6\u011fretmenin ve rehberli\u011fin en b\xfcy\xfck simgesidir. Norse mitolojisinde ise hem Fenrir'in s\u0131n\u0131rs\u0131z g\xfcc\xfc hem de Odin'in iki sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 kurdu Geri ve Freki, kutsal olanla vah\u015fi olan\u0131n ayr\u0131lmaz birli\u011fini temsil eder. Kurdun t\u0131bb\u0131 s\xfcr\xfc ba\u011f\u0131n\u0131n g\xfcc\xfcd\xfcr; hangi ili\u015fkilerin seni besleyip hangilerinin seni t\xfcketti\u011fini hissetme kapasitesidir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise s\xfcr\xfcye o kadar ba\u011flanmak ki kendi sesini kaybetmektir.",dailyMessage:"Bozkurt bug\xfcn sana bir soru soruyor: ger\xe7ek s\xfcr\xfcn kim? Etraf\u0131ndaki insanlardan hangisi seninle ayn\u0131 ritmi payla\u015f\u0131yor, hangisi yaln\u0131zca ayn\u0131 arazide dola\u015f\u0131yor \u2014 bu ikisi ayn\u0131 \u015fey de\u011fil. Kurt, biyolojik olarak s\xfcr\xfc olmadan hayatta kalamaz; ama yanl\u0131\u015f s\xfcr\xfcyle de tam olamaz, bunu i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcs\xfcyle bilir. \u0130\xe7g\xfcd\xfcn sana kimi sevdi\u011fini de\u011fil, kime g\xfcvendi\u011fini s\xf6yl\xfcyor \u2014 bu sesin fark\u0131nda m\u0131s\u0131n? Belki uzun s\xfcredir g\xf6rmezden geldi\u011fin bir ba\u011f var, ya da enerji \xe7eken bir ili\u015fki i\xe7inde s\u0131k\u0131\u015fm\u0131\u015f hissediyorsun. Bozkurt ne severek ne korkarak se\xe7im yapar \u2014 sadece ger\xe7e\u011fi hisseder ve hareket eder. Bug\xfcn kendi ululama sesine kulak ver: neye evet, neye hay\u0131r diyor? En zor ama en d\xfcr\xfcst cevap genellikle ilk gelendir. Sesini bul; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc ulumayan bir kurt zamanla yok olur.",guidance:"Bu ak\u015fam ya da sabah sessiz bir anda kendinize \u015funu sorun: 'Hayat\u0131mda en \xe7ok kime g\xfcveniyorum ve onunla ne kadar zaman ge\xe7iriyorum?' Cevab\u0131n\u0131z enerjinizi nereye yat\u0131rman\u0131z gerekti\u011fini g\xf6sterecek. Bir hafta boyunca her g\xfcn bu ki\u015fiyle bilin\xe7li bir \u015fekilde ba\u011flant\u0131 kurmay\u0131 deneyin \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir mesaj, bir telefon, ya da sessizce yan yana oturmak yeterli. Ger\xe7ek s\xfcr\xfcn\xfc bulduktan sonra i\xe7indeki kurt dinginle\u015fir.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Grey Wolf",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["leadership","family","protection","instinct"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Grey Wolf \u2014 Bozkurt, the sacred wolf of Turkic tradition \u2014 is the most sacred guide animal at the heart of Turkic mythology; in the Ergenekon legend, only the grey wolf could lead the Turkic people out of the dark mountain valley. In the Gokturk tradition, the wolf is seen as the embodied form of ancestral spirits \u2014 its howl a message between worlds, its track a sacred map. In Central Asian shamanism, wolf pelts were sewn onto the shaman's robe to carry that power on the body. In the Native American tradition, the wolf, with its pack intelligence and gift for vocal communication, is the greatest symbol of teaching and guidance. In Norse mythology, both Fenrir's boundless power and Odin's two warrior wolves, Geri and Freki, represent the inseparable unity of the sacred and the wild. The wolf's medicine is the strength of the pack bond \u2014 the capacity to feel which relationships nourish you and which drain you. Its shadow side is becoming so bound to the pack that you lose your own voice.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Grey Wolf asks you a question: who is your true pack? Of the people around you, who shares your rhythm, and who simply roams the same terrain \u2014 these are not the same thing. The wolf cannot biologically survive without a pack; yet with the wrong pack it cannot be whole either, and it knows this by instinct. Your instinct tells you not whom you love, but whom you trust \u2014 are you aware of that voice? Perhaps there is a bond you've long ignored, or you feel trapped in a relationship that drains you. The Bozkurt chooses neither out of love nor fear \u2014 it simply senses the truth and moves. Today, listen to your own howl: what is it saying yes to, what no? The hardest but most honest answer is usually the first one that comes. Find your voice; for a wolf that does not howl eventually disappears.",guidanceEn:"Tonight or tomorrow morning, in a quiet moment, ask yourself: 'Whom in my life do I trust most, and how much time do I spend with them?' Your answer will show you where to invest your energy. For one week, try to consciously connect with that person every day \u2014 a small message, a phone call, or simply sitting quietly side by side is enough. Once you find your true pack, the wolf within grows still."},{id:"a002",name:"Kartal",emoji:"\ud83e\udd85",element:"hava",symbolism:["\xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck","vizyon","g\xfc\xe7","y\xfcksek bak\u0131\u015f"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Aquila_chrysaetos_portrait.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kartal, Anadolu'nun en eski tanr\u0131sal simgelerinden biridir; Hitit panteonunda f\u0131rt\u0131na tanr\u0131s\u0131 Tarhunna'n\u0131n yan\u0131nda \xe7ift ba\u015fl\u0131 kartal olarak tasvir edilir ve g\xfcc\xfcn hem y\xfcksek hem geni\u015f g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfc temsil eder. S\xfcmer ve Akad mitolojisinde Anzu adl\u0131 kartal-aslan, ilahi g\xfc\xe7lerin sahibi olarak g\xf6klerde h\xfck\xfcm s\xfcrer. Kuzey Amerika'n\u0131n yerli gelene\u011finde kartal, B\xfcy\xfck Ruh'un d\xfcnyayla konu\u015fma arac\u0131d\u0131r; t\xfcy\xfc dua ta\u015f\u0131r, y\xfcksek u\xe7u\u015fu ise ruhun beden \xfcst\xfc \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc sembolize eder. M\u0131s\u0131r'da g\xfcne\u015f tanr\u0131s\u0131 Ra'n\u0131n ba\u015f\u0131 kartal ba\u015f\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 ayd\u0131nl\u0131k, hakikat ve ilahi yarg\u0131 bu ku\u015fta somutla\u015f\u0131r. Norse gelene\u011finde Odin'in oturdu\u011fu Yggdrasil a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131n tepesinde kartal bulunur; bilgeli\u011fi ve kozmik perspektifi simgeler. Kartal\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: herhangi bir konuya g\xf6m\xfclmeden \xf6nce y\xfcksek u\xe7u\u015fu hat\u0131rlayabilme kapasitesidir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise o kadar y\xfckse\u011fe \xe7\u0131kmak ki yery\xfcz\xfcndeki insanlar\u0131 ve g\xfcndelik ger\xe7e\u011fi unutmakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Kartal bug\xfcn seni durduruyor ve soruyor: ne kadar uza\u011f\u0131 g\xf6rebiliyorsun? Kartal, biyolojik olarak insan g\xf6z\xfcn\xfcn d\xf6rt ila sekiz kat\u0131 keskinli\u011fiyle g\xf6r\xfcr ve binlerce metre y\xfcksekten av\u0131n\u0131 se\xe7ebilir \u2014 bu yaln\u0131zca fiziksel de\u011fil, ruhsal bir mesajd\u0131r. \u015eu an ya\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131n durumu yak\u0131n mesafeden de\u011fil, y\u0131ll\u0131k perspektifle baksan nas\u0131l g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcrd\xfc? Bug\xfcn kafana tak\u0131lan o konu, be\u015f y\u0131l sonra h\xe2l\xe2 bu kadar b\xfcy\xfck m\xfc olacak? Sorunun i\xe7inde de\u011fil, \xfczerinde dur bir an. Etraf\u0131nda d\xf6nen g\xfcr\xfclt\xfcye, aceleye, bask\u0131ya kap\u0131lma \u2014 y\xfcksekten bakt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda as\u0131l \xf6ncelik nettir. Peki ger\xe7ekten nereye u\xe7mak istiyorsun, kimin beklentisi i\xe7in de\u011fil, kendi ruhun i\xe7in? Kartal bunu bilmeden kanatlar\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7maz. Bug\xfcn y\xfcksek bak\u0131\u015fa izin ver.",guidance:"Bir ka\u011f\u0131t al\u0131n ve \u015funu yaz\u0131n: 'Be\u015f y\u0131l sonra ne olmak istiyorum?' Ard\u0131ndan bug\xfcnk\xfc endi\u015felerinizi bu uzun perspektifle kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131r\u0131n; hangisi ger\xe7ekten \xf6nemli, hangisi ge\xe7ici g\xfcr\xfclt\xfc? Bu egzersizi haftada bir tekrarlay\u0131n \u2014 kartal\u0131n g\xf6z\xfcyle bakmay\u0131 al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k haline getirdik\xe7e g\xfcndelik karma\u015fa i\xe7inde y\xf6n\xfcn\xfcz\xfc kaybetmezsiniz. Perspektif, \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn en sessiz bi\xe7imidir.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Eagle",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["freedom","vision","power","higher perspective"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Eagle is one of Anatolia's most ancient divine symbols; in the Hittite pantheon it is depicted as the double-headed eagle beside the storm god Tarhunna, representing power that is at once high and wide of sight. In Sumerian and Akkadian mythology, the eagle-lion Anzu reigns in the heavens as the keeper of divine forces. In Native American tradition, the eagle is the Great Spirit's instrument of communion with the world; its feather carries prayer, and its high flight symbolizes the soul's freedom beyond the body. In Egypt, the sun god Ra is given an eagle's head \u2014 light, truth, and divine judgment embodied in this bird. In Norse tradition, an eagle sits atop Yggdrasil, Odin's tree, symbolizing wisdom and cosmic perspective. The eagle's medicine is the capacity to remember the high flight before sinking into any one matter. Its shadow side is rising so high that one forgets the people on the ground and the everyday truth.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Eagle stops you and asks: how far can you see? Biologically, the eagle's eyesight is four to eight times sharper than a human's, able to pick out prey from thousands of meters above \u2014 and this is not only physical but spiritual. If you looked at your current situation not from close range but with a five-year perspective, how would it appear? That thing weighing on your mind today \u2014 will it still feel this big five years from now? Stand for a moment not inside the problem but above it. Don't be swept up in the noise, urgency, and pressure around you \u2014 from above, what truly matters is clear. And where do you really want to fly \u2014 not for someone else's expectations, but for your own soul? The eagle never spreads its wings without knowing this. Today, allow yourself the higher view.",guidanceEn:"Take a piece of paper and write: 'Who do I want to be in five years?' Then compare today's worries against this longer perspective; which truly matter, and which are passing noise? Repeat this exercise once a week \u2014 as seeing through the eagle's eye becomes a habit, you will not lose your direction in daily chaos. Perspective is the quietest form of freedom."},{id:"a003",name:"At",emoji:"\ud83d\udc34",element:"toprak",symbolism:["\xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck","g\xfc\xe7","seyahat","ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Horses_at_waterhole.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"At, T\xfcrk ve Mo\u011fol bozk\u0131r gelene\u011finde neredeyse insan kadar kutsal bir varl\u0131kt\u0131r; sava\u015f\xe7\u0131n\u0131n ruhu at\u0131yla birlikte ta\u015f\u0131n\u0131r, iyi bir at \xf6l\xfcnce sahibiyle birlikte g\xf6m\xfcl\xfcrd\xfc. Orta Asya \u015famanizminde at, \u015faman\u0131n ruhsal yolculukta kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 ara\xe7t\u0131r \u2014 davulun ad\u0131 da 'at't\u0131r, davula vuruldu\u011funda \u015faman ruhu s\u0131rt\u0131nda \xf6teki alemlere gider. Kelt gelene\u011finde Epona tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 at formunda tasvir edilir; bereket, do\u011furganl\u0131k ve ge\xe7i\u015f t\xf6renlerinin koruyucusudur. Hindu mitolojisinde Hayagriva, at ba\u015fl\u0131 bilgelik tanr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; Ashvamedha kurban\u0131 ise kozmik g\xfcc\xfc yenileme rit\xfcelidir. Kuzey Amerika yerli gelene\u011finde 'b\xfcy\xfck k\xf6pek' olarak an\u0131lan at, \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck ve ruhun s\u0131n\u0131rs\u0131z hareket kapasitesini simgeler. At\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131 bedeni ve ruhu harekete ge\xe7irmektir \u2014 durgunlu\u011fu k\u0131rar, yeni ufuklara ta\u015f\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise dizginsiz enerjinin y\u0131k\u0131ma d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmesi, g\xfcc\xfcn y\xf6n\xfcn\xfc kaybetmesidir.",dailyMessage:"At bug\xfcn bedenini hat\u0131rl\u0131yor olman i\xe7in sana geliyor. Ruhu t\xfcm a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131yla oturan bir bedende tutamazs\u0131n \u2014 hareket, var olu\u015fun en ilkel dilidir. Atlar yo\u011fun stres alt\u0131nda bile bedenlerini titretirler, bu titreme birikmi\u015f gerginli\u011fi bo\u015faltman\u0131n do\u011fal yoludur; sen ne zamand\u0131r bedendeki gerilimi d\u0131\u015far\u0131 b\u0131rakmad\u0131n? Bug\xfcn fiziksel olarak bir \u015fey yap: ko\u015f, dans et, y\xfcr\xfc, y\xfcz \u2014 ama d\u0131\u015far\u0131 \xe7\u0131k ve hareket et. \u0130\xe7indeki enerji bast\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda anksiyete olur, serbest b\u0131rak\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda g\xfc\xe7 olur. Bu fark k\xfc\xe7\xfck de\u011fil. Peki seni hangi y\xf6ne \xe7ekiyor bu enerji \u2014 ne zaman en son i\xe7g\xfcd\xfclerine k\xf6r\xfc k\xf6r\xfcne g\xfcvendin? At, d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmeden ko\u015far; bazen tam da buna ihtiyac\u0131n vard\u0131r. Bug\xfcn a\u015f\u0131r\u0131 analiz etme, sadece hareket et.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn en az yirmi dakika a\xe7\u0131k havada, telefonsuz y\xfcr\xfcy\xfcn. Y\xfcr\xfcrken sizi en \xe7ok neyin heyecanland\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 \u2014 bir proje, bir hayal, bir insan \u2014 d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcn ve o d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceyle birlikte ad\u0131m at\u0131n. Hareket, d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceyi netle\u015ftirir; beden harekete ge\xe7ti\u011finde zihin de a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r. At bu s\u0131rr\u0131 binlerce y\u0131ld\u0131r ta\u015f\u0131yor.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Horse",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["freedom","power","travel","loyalty"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Turkic and Mongolian steppe tradition, the Horse is almost as sacred as a human being; the warrior's soul travels with his horse, and a good horse was buried with its owner at death. In Central Asian shamanism, the horse is the vehicle the shaman uses for spirit journeys \u2014 the drum itself is called 'the horse,' and when it is struck, the shaman's soul rides on its back to other worlds. In Celtic tradition, the goddess Epona is depicted in the form of a horse; she is the guardian of abundance, fertility, and rites of passage. In Hindu mythology, Hayagriva is the horse-headed god of wisdom; the Ashvamedha sacrifice is a ritual of renewing cosmic power. In Native American tradition the horse was called 'big dog' and symbolizes freedom and the soul's limitless capacity for movement. The horse's medicine is to set body and soul in motion \u2014 breaking stagnation, carrying you to new horizons. Its shadow side is unbridled energy becoming destruction, power losing its direction.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Horse comes to you so that you remember your body. You cannot hold the soul in a body weighed down by all its heaviness \u2014 movement is the most primal language of existence. Even under intense stress, horses tremble their bodies; this trembling is a natural way of releasing accumulated tension. How long has it been since you let the tension out of your body? Today, do something physical: run, dance, walk, swim \u2014 but get outside and move. Energy that is suppressed becomes anxiety; energy that is freed becomes power. The difference is not small. And in what direction is this energy pulling you \u2014 when did you last trust your instincts blindly? The horse runs without thinking; sometimes that is exactly what you need. Today, don't over-analyze, just move.",guidanceEn:"Today, walk outside for at least twenty minutes, phoneless. As you walk, think about what excites you most \u2014 a project, a dream, a person \u2014 and step in rhythm with that thought. Movement clears thought; when the body moves, the mind opens. The horse has carried this secret for thousands of years."},{id:"a004",name:"Turna",emoji:"\ud83d\udd4a\ufe0f",element:"hava",symbolism:["\xf6zlem","ruhsal yolculuk","hasret","sevgi"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Grus_grus_01.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Turna, Anadolu halk \u015fiirinin ve ozanl\u0131k gelene\u011finin en k\xf6kl\xfc imgelerinden biridir; Pir Sultan Abdal'dan A\u015f\u0131k Veysel'e pek \xe7ok ozan, turnan\u0131n kanatlar\u0131na \xf6zlem ve haber y\xfcklemi\u015ftir. Alevi-Bekta\u015fi gelene\u011finde turna semah d\xf6nme rit\xfcelinde kutsal bir ku\u015ftur \u2014 k\xfcmesi yani cemaati temsil eder, sema d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfc turnalar gibi g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcnde halka olur. Uzak Do\u011fu'da turna uzun \xf6mr\xfcn, bilgeli\u011fin ve asaletin simgesidir; Japon gelene\u011finde bin ka\u011f\u0131t turna katlamak dilek ger\xe7ekle\u015ftirir. Keltlerde turna ya da bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l, su ve kar\xe2n\u0131n ge\xe7i\u015f bek\xe7isidir; ruhsal d\xfcnyayla bu d\xfcnya aras\u0131nda arabuluculuk yapar. \u015eamanizmin pek \xe7ok kolunda g\xf6\xe7men ku\u015flar, ruhlar\u0131n ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131lar\u0131 ve evrensel haberciler olarak kutsan\u0131r. Turnan\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, \xf6zlemi hem ac\u0131ya hem g\xfcce d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrebilmektir \u2014 hasret, kalbin nereye ait oldu\u011funu g\xf6sterir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise ge\xe7mi\u015fe ya da eri\u015filemeyen \u015feye o kadar as\u0131lmak ki \u015fimdiki ana k\xf6r kalmakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Turna bug\xfcn kalbinde biriken bir \xf6zlemi y\xfczeye ta\u015f\u0131yor. Uzakta olan biri mi var, yoksa kendinin bir par\xe7as\u0131 m\u0131 \u2014 bir hayalin, bir h\xe2lin, bir sesin \xf6zlemi? Bu hasret seni zay\u0131flatm\u0131yor, aksine kalbin ger\xe7ekte ne istedi\u011fini net bir \u015fekilde g\xf6steriyor. Turna g\xf6\xe7 ederken y\xf6n hatas\u0131na d\xfc\u015fmez; binlerce kilometre \xf6tedeki ana yurdunu i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcyle bulur. Sen de o \xf6zlemin y\xf6n\xfcn\xfc biliyorsun. S\xf6ylemeden ge\xe7i\u015ftirdi\u011fin, i\xe7ine g\xf6md\xfc\u011f\xfcn \u015fey ne? Bug\xfcn onu dile getirmek, bir c\xfcmleyle bile olsa, i\xe7ini hem a\u011fr\u0131tacak hem hafifletecek. Hasreti bast\u0131rmak onu b\xfcy\xfct\xfcr; ifade etmek onu d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcr. Kalbinde hangi kanat \xe7\u0131rp\u0131n\u0131yor, hangi ufka do\u011fru?",guidance:"Bug\xfcn bir ka\u011f\u0131da \xf6zledi\u011finiz \u015feyi \u2014 bir ki\u015fiyi, bir h\xe2li, bir an\u0131 \u2014 \xfc\xe7 c\xfcmleyle yaz\u0131n. Ard\u0131ndan \u015funu sorun kendinize: 'Bu \xf6zlemin bana ne \xf6\u011fretmesi gerekiyor?' Yaz\u0131n\u0131n sonuna bir niyet ekleyin: bu \xf6zlemin enerjisini bug\xfcn yarat\u0131c\u0131 ya da ba\u011flant\u0131 kurucu bir eyleme nas\u0131l d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrebilirsiniz? Turna hasreti \u015fiire, d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfc ise \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011fe \xe7evirir.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Crane",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["longing","spiritual journey","yearning","love"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Crane (Turna) is one of the deepest-rooted images of Anatolian folk poetry and the ozan (bard) tradition; from Pir Sultan Abdal to Asik Veysel, many bards have loaded longing and tidings onto the crane's wings. In the Alevi-Bektashi tradition the crane is sacred in the semah whirling ritual \u2014 it represents the congregation, and the dancers form a circle in the sky like cranes. In the Far East the crane symbolizes longevity, wisdom, and nobility; in Japanese tradition folding a thousand paper cranes is said to grant a wish. Among the Celts, the crane or heron is the guardian of the passage between water and land, mediating between this world and the spirit world. In many branches of shamanism, migratory birds are blessed as carriers of souls and universal messengers. The crane's medicine is the ability to turn longing into both pain and strength \u2014 yearning shows the heart where it belongs. Its shadow side is clinging so tightly to the past or to the unreachable that one becomes blind to the present moment.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Crane brings to the surface a longing gathering in your heart. Is it someone far away, or a part of yourself \u2014 a dream, a state, a voice you miss? This yearning is not weakening you; on the contrary, it shows clearly what the heart truly wants. The crane never loses its way in migration; it finds its homeland thousands of kilometers away by instinct. You too know the direction of your longing. What is it that you brush aside without speaking, that you bury inside? Today, putting it into words, even a single sentence, will both ache and lighten your heart. Suppressed longing grows; expressed longing transforms. Which wing is fluttering in your heart, toward which horizon?",guidanceEn:"Today, write on a piece of paper, in three sentences, what you long for \u2014 a person, a state, a moment. Then ask yourself: 'What is this longing meant to teach me?' At the end, add an intention: how can you turn the energy of this longing today into a creative act or an act of connection? The crane turns yearning into poetry and the return journey into freedom."},{id:"a005",name:"H\xfcma Ku\u015fu",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8b",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["talih","kutsall\u0131k","y\xfcksek ruhsall\u0131k","\u015fans"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Persian_Simurgh.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"H\xfcma Ku\u015fu, \u0130ran ve Osmanl\u0131 saray \u015fiirinin en y\xfcce imgelerinden biridir; \xfczerine g\xf6lgesi d\xfc\u015fen ki\u015fi talihli olur, padi\u015fah olur, kutsan\u0131r \u2014 bu y\xfczden Osmanl\u0131'da 'h\xfcma-y\u0131 devlet' deyimi h\xfck\xfcmdar\u0131n baht\u0131na i\u015faret eder. Firdevsi'nin \u015eehname'sinde H\xfcma'ya benzetilen Simurg ise arif ruhun ula\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131 en y\xfcce varl\u0131\u011f\u0131 temsil eder; Attar'\u0131n Mant\u0131ku't-Tayr'\u0131nda ise Simurg, otuz ku\u015fun uzun yolculu\u011funun ard\u0131ndan ula\u015ft\u0131klar\u0131 kendi \xf6zleridir. M\u0131s\u0131r mitolojisinde Benu ku\u015fu, g\xfcne\u015fin yeniden do\u011fu\u015funu simgeler ve H\xfcma'n\u0131n k\xf6kenlerinden biri olarak kabul edilir. Hindu gelene\u011finde Garuda, tanr\u0131lar\u0131n g\xfcne\u015f kartal\u0131 olarak ya\u015fam\u0131 besleyen ilahi enerjiyi ta\u015f\u0131r. Japon mitolojisinde Ho-oo ad\u0131 verilen efsanevi ku\u015f, bar\u0131\u015f\u0131n ve h\xfck\xfcmdarl\u0131\u011f\u0131n habercisidir. H\xfcma'n\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131 nadir ve se\xe7ilmi\u015f anlara a\xe7\u0131k olma kapasitesidir \u2014 o anlar herkese g\xf6r\xfcnmez, yaln\u0131zca haz\u0131r y\xfcreklere. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise her \u015feyin d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan gelmesini beklemek, kendi i\xe7 \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6rmezden gelmektir.",dailyMessage:"H\xfcma bug\xfcn g\xf6lgesini \xfczerine d\xfc\u015f\xfcr\xfcyor \u2014 bu, her g\xfcnk\xfc bir ziyaret de\u011fil. Baz\u0131 anlar talih de\u011fil, fark etme \xe7a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; g\xf6zlerin a\xe7\u0131k, y\xfcre\u011fin haz\u0131rsa g\xf6r\xfcrs\xfcn. Hayat\u0131nda \u015fu an sana bir kap\u0131 aralan\u0131yor mu, bir davet geliyor mu, bir olas\u0131l\u0131k beliriyor mu? Bunu k\xfc\xe7\xfcmseme ya da 'hen\xfcz haz\u0131r de\u011filim' diye ge\xe7 b\u0131rakma. H\xfcma'n\u0131n g\xf6lgesi k\u0131sa s\xfcrer; ya o anda kar\u015f\u0131lars\u0131n ya ge\xe7er. Bekledi\u011fin an de\u011fil mi bu diye sorma; cevab\u0131 zaten biliyorsun. \u0130\xe7indeki haz\u0131rl\u0131k m\xfckemmel olmak zorunda de\u011fil, ger\xe7ek olmak zorunda. Kalbinin hangi kap\u0131y\u0131 \xe7almak istedi\u011fini bir d\xfc\u015f\xfcn. Bug\xfcn o kap\u0131y\u0131 bir ad\u0131m aral\u0131yabilirsin \u2014 sadece bir ad\u0131m yeterli.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn erteledi\u011finiz bir ad\u0131m\u0131 \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck de olsa \u2014 at\u0131n. Bir e-posta tasla\u011f\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6nderin, bir kursa kaydolun, bir insanla ileti\u015fime ge\xe7in. H\xfcma'n\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131 harekettir; talih, haz\u0131rl\u0131kl\u0131 y\xfcrekleri bulur ama hareketsiz bekleyenleri aramaz. At\u0131lan ad\u0131m, gelecek kap\u0131lar\u0131n anahtar\u0131n\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131r.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Huma Bird",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["fortune","sanctity","high spirituality","luck"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Huma Bird is one of the most exalted images of Persian and Ottoman court poetry; whoever the bird's shadow falls upon becomes fortunate, becomes a sovereign, becomes blessed \u2014 hence the Ottoman phrase 'huma-yi devlet,' pointing to the ruler's destiny. The Simurgh, often compared to the Huma in Firdawsi's Shahnameh, represents the highest being the seeker's soul can reach; in Attar's Mantiq al-Tayr, the Simurgh is in fact the very essence the thirty birds discover at the end of their long journey. In Egyptian mythology, the Bennu bird symbolizes the sun's rebirth and is considered one of the Huma's origins. In Hindu tradition, Garuda, the gods' solar eagle, carries the divine energy that nourishes life. In Japanese mythology, the legendary bird called Ho-oo is the herald of peace and just rule. The Huma's medicine is the capacity to remain open to rare and chosen moments \u2014 moments not visible to everyone, only to ready hearts. Its shadow side is to wait for everything to come from outside, ignoring one's own inner light.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Huma casts its shadow upon you \u2014 and this is not an everyday visit. Some moments are not luck but a call to notice; if your eyes are open and your heart is ready, you see. Right now is a door opening for you in your life, an invitation arriving, a possibility appearing? Do not belittle it or postpone it with 'I'm not ready yet.' The Huma's shadow is brief; either you meet it in that moment, or it passes. Don't ask whether this is the moment you've been waiting for; you already know the answer. The readiness within you does not have to be perfect, only real. Consider which door your heart wants to knock on. Today you can open that door by just one step \u2014 a single step is enough.",guidanceEn:"Today, take a step you have been postponing \u2014 however small. Send a draft email, sign up for a course, reach out to someone. The Huma's medicine is movement; fortune finds prepared hearts but does not seek those who wait without moving. The step you take carries the key to the doors yet to come."},{id:"a006",name:"Anka",emoji:"\ud83d\udd25",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["yeniden do\u011fu\u015f","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","\xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck","cesaret"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Phoenix_detail_from_Aberdeen_Bestiary.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Anka, hem T\xfcrk hem de \u0130ran-Arap mistik gelene\u011finde ruhsal d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn en b\xfcy\xfck simgesidir; Kaf da\u011f\u0131nda ya\u015far, d\xfcnyadan el \xe7ekmi\u015f arif bir varl\u0131kt\u0131r ve Simurg ile \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirilir. Yunan-Roma mitolojisindeki Anka Ku\u015fu (Phoenix), be\u015f y\xfcz y\u0131lda bir kendi yakt\u0131\u011f\u0131 ate\u015fte yanar ve k\xfcllerinden dirilerek \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfc\u011f\xfcn d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc tamamlar. M\u0131s\u0131r'da Benu ku\u015fu olarak kar\u015f\u0131m\u0131za \xe7\u0131kan bu sembol, Heliopolis tap\u0131na\u011f\u0131n\u0131n kutsal ta\u015f\u0131 benben'in \xfczerinde do\u011fan g\xfcne\u015fle \xf6zde\u015ftir \u2014 her sabah karanl\u0131ktan \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa ge\xe7i\u015fi temsil eder. \xc7in gelene\u011finde Feng Huang, d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfc\u011f\xfcn ve yeniden kurulu\u015fun simgesi olarak be\u015f erdemin birle\u015fimidir. Aztek mitolojisinde Quetzalcoatl, t\xfcyl\xfc y\u0131lan olarak hem t\xfckeni\u015f hem yenilenmeyi b\xfcnyesinde ta\u015f\u0131r. Ankan\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, her biti\u015f i\xe7inde gizlenmi\u015f do\u011fu\u015fu g\xf6rebilme kapasitesidir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise bu ate\u015fi sormadan dal\u0131p her\u015feyi yakma, yeniden do\u011fu\u015fu de\u011fil yaln\u0131zca y\u0131k\u0131m\u0131 se\xe7mektir.",dailyMessage:"Anka bug\xfcn sana yanman\u0131n ka\xe7\u0131n\u0131lmaz oldu\u011funu, ama bu ate\u015fin seni yok etmeyece\u011fini hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. \u0130\xe7inde bitti\u011fini hissetti\u011fin bir \u015fey var \u2014 bir d\xf6nem, bir ili\u015fki, bir kimlik, bir al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k. Bu biti\u015f seni korkutuyor olabilir; ama anka olmak i\xe7in \xf6nce yakmak gerekiyor. Elinde tuttu\u011fun, art\u0131k sana ait olmayan ne var? O eski hikaye \u2014 'ben b\xf6yleyim, hep b\xf6yle oldu' \u2014 k\xfcllerinde ne kadar yer kapl\u0131yor? D\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm ac\u0131s\u0131z de\u011fildir, ama ac\u0131 ile biti\u015f ayn\u0131 \u015fey de\u011fildir. Bug\xfcn k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir \u015feyi yakabilirsin: bir beklentiyi, bir \xf6fkeyi, bir rol maskesini. Ne b\u0131rak\u0131rsan o kadar hafiflersin. Yeni sen zaten k\xfcllerin alt\u0131nda haz\u0131r bekliyor.",guidance:"Bir ka\u011f\u0131da art\u0131k size uymayan \xfc\xe7 inanc\u0131, al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ya da rol\xfc yaz\u0131n. Ard\u0131ndan bu ka\u011f\u0131d\u0131 rit\xfcel bi\xe7imde \u2014 ger\xe7ekten yakabilirseniz g\xfcvenli bir ortamda, ya da sembolik olarak y\u0131rtarak \u2014 'b\u0131rak\u0131yorum' niyetiyle imha edin. Bu basit ama g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir bo\u015faltma rit\xfcelidir. Sembolik eylem, bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131 harekete ge\xe7irir \u2014 anka k\xfcllerinden bu y\xfczden do\u011far.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Anka (Phoenix)",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["rebirth","transformation","immortality","courage"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Anka, in both Turkic and Perso-Arabic mystical traditions, is the greatest symbol of spiritual transformation; it dwells on Mount Qaf, is an enlightened being who has withdrawn from the world, and is identified with the Simurgh. The Phoenix of Greek and Roman mythology burns once every five hundred years in fire of its own making and rises from its ashes to complete the cycle of immortality. In Egypt, this symbol appears as the Bennu bird, identified with the sun rising upon the sacred benben stone of Heliopolis \u2014 representing each morning's passage from darkness to light. In Chinese tradition, the Feng Huang is the symbol of righteousness and renewal, a union of the five virtues. In Aztec mythology, Quetzalcoatl, the feathered serpent, holds within itself both exhaustion and renewal. The Anka's medicine is the ability to see the birth hidden within every ending. Its shadow side is rushing into this fire without question, burning everything, choosing not rebirth but only destruction.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Anka reminds you that the burning is inevitable, but this fire will not destroy you. There is something within you that you feel is ending \u2014 a chapter, a relationship, an identity, a habit. This ending may frighten you; but to become the Anka, one must first burn. What are you still holding that no longer belongs to you? That old story \u2014 'this is how I am, this is how I've always been' \u2014 how much space does it occupy among your ashes? Transformation is not painless, but pain and ending are not the same thing. Today you can burn one small thing: an expectation, an anger, a role-mask. The more you release, the lighter you become. The new you is already waiting beneath the ashes.",guidanceEn:"Write on a piece of paper three beliefs, habits, or roles that no longer fit you. Then destroy this paper ritually \u2014 if you can safely burn it, do so, or symbolically tear it \u2014 with the intention 'I release this.' This is a simple but powerful releasing ritual. Symbolic action stirs the unconscious \u2014 this is why the phoenix is born from its ashes."},{id:"a007",name:"Geyik",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8c",element:"toprak",symbolism:["zarafet","\u015fefkat","yenilenme","sezgi"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Red_Deer_in_field.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Geyik, Orta Asya ve Sibirya \u015famanizminin en k\xf6kl\xfc ruhsal rehber hayvanlar\u0131ndan biridir; geyi\u011fin boynuzu d\xfcnyalar a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131 and\u0131r\u0131r \u2014 k\xf6kleriyle yeralt\u0131na, dallar\u0131yla g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcne uzanan bir kozmik haritad\u0131r. Altay ve Yakut \u015famanlar\u0131 geyik s\u0131rt\u0131nda \xf6teki alemlere yolculuk yapt\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131 anlat\u0131r; bu nedenle geyik hem rehber hem ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131 hem de koruyucudur. Kelt gelene\u011finde Cernunnos, boynuzlu bir tanr\u0131 olarak do\u011fan\u0131n d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc, \xf6l\xfcm ve yeniden do\u011fu\u015fu y\xf6netir; geyikler onun kutsal hayvanlar\u0131d\u0131r. Hindu mitolojisinde geyik, tanr\u0131\xe7a Saraswati'nin arac\u0131 olan nazikli\u011fin ve ilahi sezginin simgesidir. Kuzey Amerika Lakota gelene\u011finde geyik, \u015fefkat ve sevecen g\xfc\xe7 \xf6\u011fretisini ta\u015f\u0131r \u2014 sert de\u011fil, nazik ama sars\u0131lmaz. Geyi\u011fin t\u0131bb\u0131 zarafetle g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olmakt\u0131r; \u015fefkat, zay\u0131fl\u0131k de\u011fil derin bir g\xfc\xe7 bi\xe7imidir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise o kadar yumu\u015fak davranmak ki kendi s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 unutmak, ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131n bak\u0131\u015f\u0131nda donup kalmakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Geyik bug\xfcn sana \u015fefkatin ne kadar b\xfcy\xfck bir g\xfc\xe7 oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Her \u015feyi sertlikle, diren\xe7le, \xe7abayla \xe7\xf6zmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yorsun belki \u2014 ama geyik bize ba\u015fka bir yolu g\xf6steriyor. Nazik bir dokunu\u015f, bazen sert bir hamleden \xe7ok daha derin iz b\u0131rak\u0131r. Bu hem ba\u015fkalar\u0131na olan davran\u0131\u015f\u0131n hem de kendine olan sesinde ge\xe7erli. Kendine bug\xfcn nas\u0131l konu\u015fuyorsun \u2014 bir d\xfc\u015fman gibi mi, bir sevgili gibi mi? \u015eefkat g\xf6stermek, o an\u0131n ac\u0131s\u0131ndan ka\xe7mak de\u011fil; tam tersine onu d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrecek g\xfcce sahip olmakt\u0131r. Bug\xfcn kalbini dokunduran bir \u015feyin yan\u0131nda dur \u2014 a\u011fla, izin ver, hisset. Geyik g\xf6zlerini kapatmaz; g\xfczelli\u011fe ve ac\u0131ya e\u015fit bir \u015fekilde bakar. Yumu\u015fa, ama kaybolma.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn kendinize y\xf6nelik en az \xfc\xe7 \u015fefkatli c\xfcmle s\xf6yleyin \u2014 sesli olarak. 'Elimden gelenin en iyisini yap\u0131yorum', 'Bu s\xfcre\xe7 zor, buna izin var', 'De\u011ferliyim' gibi. Sesli dile getirmek, zihinsel onaydan daha derin bir etki yarat\u0131r. Bunu \xfc\xe7 g\xfcn boyunca tekrarlay\u0131n; geyi\u011fin nazikli\u011fi i\xe7inize sindi\u011finde d\u0131\u015far\u0131ya da akmaya ba\u015flar.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Red Deer",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["grace","compassion","renewal","intuition"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Deer is one of the deepest-rooted spirit guide animals in Central Asian and Siberian shamanism; its antlers evoke the World Tree \u2014 a cosmic map reaching with its roots into the underworld and its branches into the sky. Altai and Yakut shamans speak of journeying to other realms on the back of a deer; thus the deer is at once guide, carrier, and protector. In Celtic tradition, Cernunnos, the horned god, governs nature's cycle, death, and rebirth; deer are his sacred animals. In Hindu mythology, the deer is the symbol of the gentleness and divine intuition embodied in the goddess Saraswati's vehicle. In the Lakota tradition of North America, the deer carries the teaching of compassion and tender strength \u2014 not harsh, but gentle and unshakable. The deer's medicine is to be strong through grace; compassion is not weakness but a deep form of power. Its shadow side is being so soft that one forgets one's own boundaries, freezing under another's gaze.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Deer reminds you what a great power compassion is. Perhaps you are trying to solve everything with hardness, resistance, effort \u2014 but the deer shows us another way. A gentle touch sometimes leaves a far deeper mark than a sharp move. This applies both to how you treat others and how you speak to yourself. How are you speaking to yourself today \u2014 as an enemy, or as a beloved? To show compassion is not to flee the pain of the moment; it is to have the power to transform it. Today, stay beside what touches your heart \u2014 cry, allow it, feel it. The deer does not close its eyes; it looks upon beauty and pain equally. Soften, but do not disappear.",guidanceEn:"Today, say aloud at least three compassionate sentences to yourself \u2014 'I am doing my best,' 'This process is hard, and that's allowed,' 'I am worthy.' Speaking aloud creates a deeper effect than mental affirmation. Repeat this for three days; as the deer's gentleness settles inside, it begins to flow outward as well."},{id:"a008",name:"Bayku\u015f",emoji:"\ud83e\udd89",element:"hava",symbolism:["bilgelik","gizem","i\xe7g\xf6r\xfc","karanl\u0131kta g\xf6rme"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Bubo_bubo_sibiricus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Bayku\u015f, Anadolu'da \xe7ift de\u011ferli bir varl\u0131kt\u0131r; bir yanda Athena'n\u0131n kutsal ku\u015fu olarak Yunan-Roma k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnden miras bilgeli\u011fi simgeler, \xf6te yanda eski T\xfcrk ve Orta Asya halk inan\u0131\u015flar\u0131nda \xf6l\xfcm\xfcn ve ge\xe7i\u015fin habercisi say\u0131l\u0131r \u2014 bu dualite onun en derin \xf6zelli\u011fidir. S\xfcmer'de Lilith'in ku\u015fu olarak bilinir; gece, bilinmezlik ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcc\xfc karanl\u0131\u011f\u0131n koruyucusudur. Kelt Druid gelene\u011finde bayku\u015f, Cailleach'\u0131n (K\u0131\u015f Kad\u0131n\u0131'n\u0131n) kutsal hayvan\u0131d\u0131r; karanl\u0131kta g\xf6rmek, g\xf6r\xfcnmezi g\xf6rmek demektir. Hindu gelene\u011finde Lakshmi'nin arac\u0131 olan bayku\u015f, zenginli\u011fin ve i\xe7g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcn simgesidir \u2014 d\u0131\u015f parlakl\u0131k de\u011fil, i\xe7sel berrakl\u0131k zenginli\u011fidir. Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde Osun'un kutsal ku\u015flar\u0131 aras\u0131nda bayku\u015f yer al\u0131r; b\xfcy\xfc, d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm ve gizli bilginin ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r. Bayku\u015fun t\u0131bb\u0131 karanl\u0131kta bile g\xf6rme kapasitesidir \u2014 belirsizlik, korku ya da gece i\xe7inde bile y\xf6n\xfcn\xfc bulmak. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise o kadar \xe7ok analiz etmek ki hareketsiz kalmak, bilgiye sahip olmak ama onu kullanamamakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Bayku\u015f bug\xfcn sana herkesin g\xf6remedi\u011fi \u015feyi g\xf6rme g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Etraf\u0131ndaki ko\u015fturmacada, g\xfcr\xfclt\xfcde, performanslarda \u2014 ger\xe7ek ne? Bir durumda, bir insanda, bir karar s\xfcrecinde y\xfczey alt\u0131nda ne d\xf6n\xfcyor? Bayku\u015f karanl\u0131kta avlan\u0131r \xe7\xfcnk\xfc tam sessizlikte en ince sesi duyar; bu, dikkat ve sab\u0131r gerektiren bir sanatt\u0131r. Bug\xfcn konu\u015fmadan \xf6nce bir ad\u0131m daha dinle. Aceleyle verdi\u011fin cevaplar, bayku\u015fun g\xf6rece\u011fi \u015feyi gizler. Hakk\u0131nda i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcsel bir \u015fey hissetti\u011fin ama ak\u0131lla bast\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131n bir konu var m\u0131? O his ne diyor? Karanl\u0131ktan korkmak, orada ne oldu\u011funu asla \xf6\u011frenememek demektir \u2014 bayku\u015f bunu bize g\xf6sterir. Bug\xfcn en ince sese kulak ver.",guidance:"Bu gece ya da yar\u0131n sabah on dakika boyunca sadece oturun ve g\xf6zlemleme prati\u011fi yap\u0131n. Herhangi bir \u015feyi \u2014 bir durumu, bir ili\u015fkiyi, bir duyguyu \u2014 yarg\u0131lamadan, \xe7\xf6zmeden, yaln\u0131zca g\xf6zlemleyin. Zihin konu\u015ftu\u011funda onu not edin ama ona kat\u0131lmay\u0131n. Bayku\u015fun en b\xfcy\xfck g\xfcc\xfc, g\xf6rmeden \xf6nce dinlemektir. Bu on dakika i\xe7g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcz\xfc derinle\u015ftirir.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Owl",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["wisdom","mystery","insight","seeing in the dark"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Owl is a being of dual valence in Anatolia; on one side it symbolizes the wisdom inherited from the Greco-Roman culture as Athena's sacred bird, and on the other in old Turkic and Central Asian folk belief it was considered a herald of death and transition \u2014 and this duality is its deepest quality. In Sumer it is known as Lilith's bird; the guardian of night, the unknown, and transformative darkness. In Celtic Druid tradition, the owl is the sacred animal of the Cailleach (Winter Woman); to see in the dark is to see the invisible. In Hindu tradition, the owl is the vehicle of Lakshmi, symbolizing wealth and insight \u2014 wealth not of outer brilliance but of inner clarity. In the African Yoruba tradition, the owl is among Osun's sacred birds; the carrier of magic, transformation, and hidden knowledge. The owl's medicine is the capacity to see even in darkness \u2014 to find your direction even amid uncertainty, fear, or night. Its shadow side is to analyze so much that you remain motionless, to possess knowledge yet be unable to use it.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Owl reminds you of your power to see what others cannot. In the busyness, noise, and performances around you \u2014 what is the truth? In a situation, a person, a decision-making process, what is moving beneath the surface? The owl hunts in the dark because it hears the finest sound in total silence; this is an art that requires attention and patience. Today, listen for one more breath before you speak. Hasty answers conceal what the owl would see. Is there something you intuitively feel about a matter, but suppress with the mind? What is that intuition saying? To fear the dark is never to learn what is there \u2014 the owl shows us this. Today, listen for the finest sound.",guidanceEn:"Tonight or tomorrow morning, for ten minutes, simply sit and practice observing. Watch something \u2014 a situation, a relationship, an emotion \u2014 without judging, without solving, only observing. When the mind speaks, note it but do not join it. The owl's greatest power is to listen before seeing. These ten minutes deepen your insight."},{id:"a009",name:"Aslan",emoji:"\ud83e\udd81",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["cesaret","onur","kraliyet","g\xfc\xe7"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Lion_waiting_in_Namibia.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Aslan, Anadolu'nun en eski tanr\u0131sal koruyucu hayvanlar\u0131ndan biridir; Hitit tap\u0131naklar\u0131n\u0131n kap\u0131 s\xf6velerinde \xe7ift aslan fig\xfcrleri d\xfc\u015fman enerjileri ve k\xf6t\xfc ruhlar\u0131 uzak tutar. Mezopotamya'da \u0130\u015ftar/\u0130nanna, aslan s\u0131rt\u0131nda tasvir edilir \u2014 sava\u015f\u0131n, tutkun ve adaletin tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 olan \u0130nanna'n\u0131n g\xfcc\xfc aslan\u0131n bedeniyle somutla\u015f\u0131r. M\u0131s\u0131r'da sfenks ve sekhmet, aslan\u0131 tanr\u0131sal savunman\u0131n ve g\xfcne\u015fin ate\u015fiyle \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirir. Afrika Maasai gelene\u011finde aslan avlamak ergenlik t\xf6reninin merkezindedir; bu rit\xfcel, gencin kendi aslan\u0131n\u0131 \u2014 korkusunu \u2014 \xf6ld\xfcrmesi anlam\u0131na gelir. Hindu mitolojisinde Narasimha, aslan-insan bi\xe7imindeki Vi\u015fnu avatar\u0131d\u0131r; haks\u0131zl\u0131\u011fa kar\u015f\u0131 ilahi m\xfcdahaleyi temsil eder. Aslan\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, onurla var olmak ve korkuya ra\u011fmen durmakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise g\xfcc\xfcn kibire, koruyuculu\u011fun tahakk\xfcme d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmesi \u2014 s\xfcr\xfcy\xfc y\xf6netirken s\xfcr\xfcn\xfcn sesini bast\u0131rmakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Aslan bug\xfcn sana onurunu hat\u0131rlatmak i\xe7in geliyor. Bir yerde k\xfc\xe7\xfck d\xfc\u015f\xfcr\xfcld\xfcn, hakk\u0131n yendi ya da sessiz kalmay\u0131 se\xe7tin \u2014 bunu aslan hissetmez. Aslanlar korktuktan de\u011fil, korku varken de durmay\u0131 bilerek liderlik ederler. Sesini y\xfckseltmek, s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 \xe7izmek, itiraz etmek \u2014 bunlar sald\u0131rganl\u0131k de\u011fil, onurun korunmas\u0131d\u0131r. Vazge\xe7ti\u011finde ne kaybediyorsun ger\xe7ekten? Ve durdu\u011funda ne kazan\u0131yorsun, yaln\u0131zca sonu\xe7 de\u011fil, i\xe7inde ne hissediyorsun? Bazen en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc jest, 'hay\u0131r' demek ya da 'bu do\u011fru de\u011fil' demektir. Onur, d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan verilmez; i\xe7eriden ta\u015f\u0131n\u0131r. Bug\xfcn aslan gibi dur.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn bir s\u0131n\u0131r belirleyin \u2014 ufak da olsa. Bir iste\u011fi reddledin, bir durumu d\xfczelttiniz, ya da i\xe7inizden hep kabul etti\u011finiz bir durumu sesli olarak sorgulad\u0131n\u0131z. Bunu yaparken g\xf6zlemleyin: beden nas\u0131l hissediyor? Aslan gibi durman\u0131n nas\u0131l bir his oldu\u011funu tan\u0131d\u0131k\xe7a bunu daha b\xfcy\xfck alanlara da ta\u015f\u0131yabilirsiniz.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Lion",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["courage","honor","royalty","power"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Lion is one of Anatolia's most ancient divine protector animals; on the doorjambs of Hittite temples, paired lion figures kept enemy energies and evil spirits at bay. In Mesopotamia, Ishtar/Inanna is depicted on the back of a lion \u2014 the power of the goddess of war, passion, and justice embodied in the lion's body. In Egypt, the sphinx and Sekhmet identify the lion with divine defense and the fire of the sun. In African Maasai tradition, hunting a lion lies at the heart of the initiation ceremony; this ritual means the youth slays his own lion \u2014 his fear. In Hindu mythology, Narasimha is the lion-human avatar of Vishnu, representing divine intervention against injustice. The lion's medicine is to exist with honor and to stand even in the presence of fear. Its shadow side is power turning to arrogance, protectiveness turning to domination \u2014 silencing the very pack one leads.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Lion comes to remind you of your honor. Somewhere you were diminished, your rights trampled, or you chose to remain silent \u2014 the lion does not let this pass. Lions lead not by feeling no fear, but by knowing how to stand even when fear is present. Raising your voice, drawing a boundary, objecting \u2014 these are not aggression but the preservation of honor. What do you truly lose when you give in? And when you stand firm, what do you gain \u2014 not just the outcome, but what do you feel inside? Sometimes the strongest gesture is to say 'no' or 'this is not right.' Honor is not bestowed from outside; it is carried from within. Today, stand like a lion.",guidanceEn:"Today, set a boundary \u2014 however small. Refuse a request, correct a situation, or aloud question something you have always silently accepted. As you do this, observe: how does the body feel? As you become familiar with the feeling of standing like a lion, you can carry it into greater arenas as well."},{id:"a010",name:"Ay\u0131",emoji:"\ud83d\udc3b",element:"toprak",symbolism:["g\xfc\xe7","iyile\u015fme","sezgi","i\xe7e \xe7ekilme"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Brown_bear.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Ay\u0131, Orta Asya ve Sibirya \u015famanizminde \u015faman\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc yard\u0131mc\u0131 ruhlar\u0131ndan biridir; ay\u0131 postu giyen \u015faman iyile\u015fme rit\xfcellerinde onun g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc bedenine davet eder. Kuzey Anadolu ve Karadeniz k\u0131y\u0131lar\u0131nda Orta Asya'dan gelen ay\u0131 k\xfclt\xfcn\xfcn izleri ya\u015far; halk inan\u0131\u015f\u0131nda ay\u0131, orman\u0131n h\xe2kimi ve yaral\u0131 ruhlar\u0131n \u015fifac\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r. Kuzey Amerika'n\u0131n pek \xe7ok yerli gelene\u011finde ay\u0131, beden bilgeli\u011finin ve meditatif iyile\u015fmenin en b\xfcy\xfck \xf6\u011fretmenidir \u2014 k\u0131\u015f uykusu, i\xe7e \xe7ekilme ve yenilenme d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc temsil eder. Norse mitolojisinde berserkerler sava\u015fa ay\u0131 postunun ruhuyla girerdi; Odin'in kendisi ay\u0131yla \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirildi\u011fi d\xf6nemler olmu\u015ftur. Kelt gelene\u011finde di\u015fi ay\u0131, ana\xe7 g\xfcc\xfcn ve topra\u011f\u0131n koruyuculu\u011funun simgesidir. Ay\u0131n\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, \xe7ekilmenin zay\u0131fl\u0131k de\u011fil derin bir g\xfc\xe7 bi\xe7imi oldu\u011funu bilmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise o kadar i\xe7e \xe7ekilmek ki d\xfcnyayla ba\u011f\u0131 tamamen koparmak, yenilenmeyi izolasyona d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrmektir.",dailyMessage:"Ay\u0131 bug\xfcn seni ma\u011farana davet ediyor. D\u0131\u015f d\xfcnya ile yo\u011fun temas bazen ruhu t\xfcketir \u2014 bu bir zay\u0131fl\u0131k de\u011fil, biyolojik bir ger\xe7ek. Ay\u0131lar fizyolojik olarak k\u0131\u015f\u0131n metabolizmalar\u0131n\u0131 yava\u015flat\u0131r, beden \u0131s\u0131lar\u0131 d\xfc\u015fer, d\u0131\u015f uyaranlara kapat\u0131r ve bu s\xfcre\xe7ten her ilkbaharda daha g\xfc\xe7l\xfc, daha olgun \xe7\u0131karlar. Sen ne zamand\u0131r ger\xe7ekten dinlenmedin? Ne zamand\u0131r sadece var olmak i\xe7in zaman ay\u0131rd\u0131n \u2014 bir \u015fey \xfcretmek, kan\u0131tlamak, tamamlamak zorunda kalmadan? Uyku, sessizlik, yaln\u0131zl\u0131k \u2014 bunlar verimsizlik de\u011fil, gelecek g\xfcc\xfcn\xfcn tohumudur. Kendinle ba\u015f ba\u015fa kalmaktan korkmak, kendi i\xe7 sesinle y\xfczle\u015fmemek anlam\u0131na gelir. Bug\xfcn o korkuya de\u011fil, o davete kulak ver.",guidance:"Bu hafta en az bir bu\xe7uk saatlik 'ma\u011fara zaman\u0131' ayarlay\u0131n: telefon kapal\u0131, plan yok, \xfcretim yok. Sadece olun \u2014 bir kitap, sessizlik, yar\u0131m \u015fekerleme, ya da bo\u015f bir bak\u0131\u015f. Bu zaman\u0131 su\xe7luluk duymadan ge\xe7irin; ay\u0131n\u0131n bilgeli\u011fi, yenilenmek i\xe7in yeterince cesaretli olmakt\u0131r. Ma\u011faradan \xe7\u0131kt\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131zda i\xe7inizde ne kadar farkl\u0131 bir enerji oldu\u011funa \u015fa\u015f\u0131racaks\u0131n\u0131z.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Bear",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["strength","healing","intuition","withdrawal"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Bear is one of the shaman's most powerful helping spirits in Central Asian and Siberian shamanism; the shaman wearing the bear pelt invites that power into his body during healing rituals. Along the northern Anatolian and Black Sea coast, traces of the bear cult brought from Central Asia still live on; in folk belief, the bear is the master of the forest and the healer of wounded souls. In many Native American traditions, the bear is the greatest teacher of body wisdom and meditative healing \u2014 its hibernation represents the cycle of withdrawal and renewal. In Norse mythology, the berserkers entered battle with the spirit of the bear pelt; even Odin himself was at times identified with the bear. In Celtic tradition, the she-bear is the symbol of maternal strength and the guardianship of the earth. The bear's medicine is to know that withdrawal is not weakness but a deep form of strength. Its shadow side is withdrawing so far that the bond with the world is severed entirely, turning renewal into isolation.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Bear invites you into your cave. Intense contact with the outer world sometimes drains the soul \u2014 this is not a weakness but a biological truth. In winter, bears physiologically slow their metabolism, lower their body temperature, close themselves off from outer stimuli, and each spring emerge stronger, riper. How long has it been since you truly rested? When did you last give yourself time simply to be \u2014 without having to produce, prove, or complete anything? Sleep, silence, solitude \u2014 these are not unproductive; they are the seeds of your future strength. To fear being alone with yourself means refusing to face your own inner voice. Today, listen not to that fear but to that invitation.",guidanceEn:"This week, schedule at least an hour and a half of 'cave time': phone off, no plans, no production. Just be \u2014 a book, silence, a half-nap, or an empty gaze. Spend this time without guilt; the bear's wisdom is to be brave enough to renew yourself. When you emerge from the cave, you will be surprised at how different an energy you carry inside."},{id:"a011",name:"Tilki",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8a",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["zeka","uyum sa\u011flama","\xe7eviklik","strateji"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Fox_Vulpes_vulpes.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Tilki, T\xfcrk ve Orta Asya halk hikayelerinde her zaman en zeki karakterdir; Nasreddin Hoca f\u0131kralar\u0131na benzer bir zeka ile g\xfc\xe7l\xfcleri atlat\u0131r, g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcrde yenilir ama asl\u0131nda kazan\u0131r. \u015einto gelene\u011finde tilki (kitsune) en az dokuz kuyruklu oldu\u011funda neredeyse tanr\u0131sal bilgeli\u011fe ula\u015f\u0131r; tap\u0131nak koruyucusu ve ilahi habercisi olarak sayg\u0131 g\xf6r\xfcr. Kelt mitolojisinde tilki, orman\u0131n ak\u0131ll\u0131 k\u0131lavuzu ve gizli yollar\u0131n bilen ruhudur. Kuzey Amerika Trickster gelene\u011finde Coyote ve Tilki, insanlara cahilliklerini, kibirlerini ve kat\u0131l\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131 \u015fakalar ve tuzaklar arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla g\xf6sterir \u2014 bu \xf6\u011fretim ac\u0131 olabilir ama d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcc\xfcd\xfcr. M\u0131s\u0131r gelene\u011finde Anubis'in tilkiye benzeyen ba\u015f\u0131, ge\xe7i\u015f rit\xfcellerinde rehberlik g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc simgeler. Tilkinin t\u0131bb\u0131 uyum sa\u011flama ve \xe7evik d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmedir \u2014 ayn\u0131 anda hem g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr hem g\xf6r\xfcnmez olmak, hem ciddi hem oyunbaz olmak. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise zekan\u0131n manip\xfclasyona, \xe7evikli\u011fin g\xfcvensizli\u011fe d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmesidir.",dailyMessage:"Tilki bug\xfcn senden daha ak\u0131ll\u0131ca oynaman\u0131 istiyor \u2014 do\u011frudan de\u011fil, \xe7evik; sert de\u011fil, stratejik. Tilkinin en ilgin\xe7 \xf6zelliklerinden biri habitat\u0131na \xe7ok h\u0131zl\u0131 uyum sa\u011flamas\u0131d\u0131r; kentlerde bile hayatta kal\u0131r, \xe7\xfcnk\xfc kurallar\u0131 de\u011fil zemini okur. Sen de \u015fu an i\xe7inde bulundu\u011fun ortam\u0131 ger\xe7ekten okuyabiliyor musun \u2014 kim ne istiyor, ne zaman ne s\xf6ylenmeli, hangi kap\u0131 hangi anahtara a\xe7\u0131l\u0131yor? Bir durumu \xe7ok do\u011frudan ele ald\u0131\u011f\u0131nda ne oluyor, geri tepmiyor mu? Belki farkl\u0131 bir a\xe7\u0131dan yakla\u015fman\u0131n zaman\u0131. \xd6te yandan dikkat: zeka, d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfc\u011f\xfcn yerine ge\xe7mez. Tilkinin g\xf6lgesi zekay\u0131 ara\xe7salla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131p g\xfcven k\u0131rmas\u0131d\u0131r. Bug\xfcn hem ak\u0131ll\u0131 hem sahici ol.",guidance:"Tak\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir problem ya da ili\u015fki i\xe7in al\u0131\u015f\u0131lmad\u0131k bir \xe7\xf6z\xfcm yolu deneyin. Normalde ne yapard\u0131n\u0131z? \u015eimdi tam tersini ya da \xe7ok farkl\u0131 bir a\xe7\u0131y\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcn. Tilkinin zekas\u0131 yeni yollar\u0131 g\xf6rmek i\xe7in eski haritalar\u0131 bir kenara b\u0131rakmakla ba\u015flar. Bu egzersiz hem sorun \xe7\xf6zme kapasitenizisorguyu hem de esnekli\u011finizi g\xfc\xe7lendirir.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Fox",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["intelligence","adaptability","agility","strategy"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Turkic and Central Asian folktales, the Fox is always the cleverest character; with an intelligence akin to Nasreddin Hodja's, it outwits the powerful, appears to lose yet truly wins. In the Shinto tradition, the fox (kitsune) attains near-divine wisdom upon growing nine tails; it is revered as the temple guardian and divine messenger. In Celtic mythology, the fox is the clever guide of the forest and the spirit who knows the hidden paths. In the Native American Trickster tradition, Coyote and Fox reveal to humans their ignorance, arrogance, and rigidity through jokes and traps \u2014 this teaching may be painful but is transformative. In Egyptian tradition, the fox-like head of Anubis symbolizes the power of guidance in transition rituals. The fox's medicine is adaptability and agile thinking \u2014 being at once visible and invisible, at once serious and playful. Its shadow side is intelligence turning to manipulation, agility turning to untrustworthiness.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Fox wants you to play more cleverly \u2014 not directly, but agilely; not harshly, but strategically. One of the fox's most striking qualities is its rapid adaptation to its habitat; it survives even in cities, because it reads not the rules but the ground. Are you truly reading the environment you are in right now \u2014 who wants what, when something should be said, which door opens with which key? When you handle a situation too directly, doesn't it rebound? Perhaps it is time to approach from a different angle. At the same time, beware: intelligence does not substitute for honesty. The fox's shadow is to instrumentalize cleverness and break trust. Today, be both clever and true.",guidanceEn:"Try an unconventional solution for a problem or relationship you are stuck on. What would you normally do? Now consider the opposite, or a very different angle. The fox's intelligence begins with setting aside old maps to see new paths. This exercise strengthens both your problem-solving capacity and your flexibility."},{id:"a012",name:"Yunus",emoji:"\ud83d\udc2c",element:"su",symbolism:["ne\u015fe","oyun","zeka","topluluk"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Dolphin_ka_cropped.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Yunus, Ege ve Akdeniz k\u0131y\u0131lar\u0131nda \xe7ok eski \xe7a\u011flardan beri kutsal bir hayvan olarak ya\u015fam\u0131\u015ft\u0131r; Antik Yunan'da denizde bo\u011fulma tehlikesine kar\u015f\u0131 yunuslar\u0131n insanlar\u0131 k\u0131y\u0131ya ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131na dair efsaneler anlat\u0131l\u0131r ve Apollon bazen yunus formunda tezah\xfcr eder. Girit Minos uygarl\u0131\u011f\u0131nda yunus fresk resimlerinde \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn ve ya\u015fam sevincinin simgesidir. Keltlerin Deniz Tanr\u0131s\u0131 Manann\xe1n mac Lir'in kutsal hayvanlar\u0131 aras\u0131nda yunus yer al\u0131r; ne\u015fe ve derin bilgeli\u011fin bir arada bulunabilece\u011fini g\xf6sterir. Maori gelene\u011finde yunus, tanr\u0131lar\u0131n denizde rehberlik etmek i\xe7in g\xf6nderdi\u011fi kutsal varl\u0131klard\u0131r. Hindistan k\u0131y\u0131 k\xfclt\xfcrlerinde Gangetic yunus, kutsal Ganj nehrinin ruhsal koruyucusudur. Yunusun t\u0131bb\u0131 ne\u015feyi bilgelikle bir arada ta\u015f\u0131makt\u0131r \u2014 oyun, zekay\u0131 k\xf6relten de\u011fil, keskinle\u015ftiren bir enerjidir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise her \u015feyi oyuna \xe7evirip derinle\u015fmekten, durup hissetmekten ka\xe7makt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Yunus bug\xfcn sana hayat\u0131n a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 bir s\xfcre b\u0131rakman\u0131 s\xf6yl\xfcyor. Yunus bal\u0131klar\u0131 beyin kapasiteleri oran\u0131nda belki en y\xfcksek oyun davran\u0131\u015f\u0131na sahip memelilerden biridir \u2014 dalga s\xf6rf yaparlar, aynay\u0131 tan\u0131rlar, birbirleriyle \u015fark\u0131 s\xf6ylerler. Bu bir \xe7ocukluk kal\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131 de\u011fil, y\xfcksek zek\xe2n\u0131n i\u015faretidir. Ne zaman en son sadece e\u011flenmek i\xe7in bir \u015fey yapt\u0131n, bir amaca y\xf6nelik olmadan? Ne zaman g\xfcld\xfcn \u2014 ger\xe7ekten, zorlamadan? Ciddiyet bazen \xfcretkenli\u011fin de\u011fil t\xfckenmi\u015fli\u011fin i\u015faretidir. Bug\xfcn beynin en iyi \xe7al\u0131\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131 istiyorsan onu biraz oyuna b\u0131rak. Bir \u015feyi hafife almak, onu \xf6nemsememek de\u011fildir; bazen \xe7\xf6z\xfcm, s\u0131k\u0131 kavramay\u0131 b\u0131rakmaktan gelir.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn tamamen anlams\u0131z ve e\u011flenceli bir \u015fey yap\u0131n: \xe7izin, dans edin, \xe7ocuk\xe7a bir oyun oynay\u0131n, k\xf6p\xfckl\xfc su i\xe7erken sa\xe7ma bir \u015fark\u0131 s\xf6yleyin. S\xfcre: en az on be\u015f dakika, telefon kapal\u0131. Oyun, sinir sistemini yeniler ve yarat\u0131c\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceyi a\xe7ar \u2014 yunus bunu milyonlarca y\u0131ld\u0131r biliyor. Siz de bu gece biraz daha hafif uyursunuz.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Dolphin",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["joy","play","intelligence","community"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Dolphin has lived as a sacred animal along the Aegean and Mediterranean coasts since ancient times; in Ancient Greece, legends are told of dolphins carrying drowning humans to shore, and Apollo sometimes manifests in dolphin form. In Minoan Crete, the dolphin in fresco paintings is the symbol of freedom and the joy of life. The dolphin is among the sacred animals of the Celtic sea god Manannan mac Lir; it shows that joy and deep wisdom can dwell together. In Maori tradition, dolphins are sacred beings the gods send to guide travelers at sea. In Indian coastal cultures, the Gangetic dolphin is the spiritual guardian of the sacred Ganges River. The dolphin's medicine is to carry joy alongside wisdom \u2014 play is an energy that does not dull intelligence but sharpens it. Its shadow side is turning everything into play, fleeing from depth and from stopping to truly feel.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Dolphin tells you to set down the weight of life for a while. Dolphins are among the mammals with perhaps the highest level of play behavior relative to their brain capacity \u2014 they surf waves, recognize themselves in mirrors, sing with each other. This is not a residue of childhood but a sign of high intelligence. When did you last do something just to enjoy it, with no purpose? When did you laugh \u2014 truly, without effort? Seriousness is sometimes the sign not of productivity but of burnout. Today, if you want your brain to work at its best, let it play a little. Taking something lightly is not dismissing its importance; sometimes the solution comes from loosening your grip.",guidanceEn:"Today, do something entirely pointless and fun: draw, dance, play a childish game, sing a silly song while drinking sparkling water. Duration: at least fifteen minutes, phone off. Play renews the nervous system and opens creative thought \u2014 the dolphin has known this for millions of years. You'll sleep a little lighter tonight, too."},{id:"a013",name:"Kaplumba\u011fa",emoji:"\ud83d\udc22",element:"toprak",symbolism:["sab\u0131r","bilgelik","uzun \xf6m\xfcr","istikrar"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Galapagos_tortoise_Santa_Cruz_1.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kaplumba\u011fa, Anadolu halk mitolojisinde d\xfcnyan\u0131n ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131s\u0131 motifinin bir par\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r; pek \xe7ok k\xfclt\xfcrde d\xfcnya kaplumba\u011fan\u0131n s\u0131rt\u0131nda durur \u2014 bu inan\u0131\u015f Orta Asya, Hint ve Amerikan yerli geleneklerinde e\u015f zamanl\u0131 ortaya \xe7\u0131kar. Hindu kozmolojisinde Kurma, Vi\u015fnu'nun ikinci avatar\u0131d\u0131r; devlerin ve tanr\u0131lar\u0131n okyanusunun dibini kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131rmas\u0131nda destek olur, sab\u0131r ve dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n ilahi bi\xe7imidir. \xc7in gelene\u011finde kaplumba\u011fa d\xf6rt kutsal hayvan\u0131n birisi olup kuzeyinin ve k\u0131\u015f\u0131n koruyucusudur; kabu\u011fundaki desen fal ve kehanet arac\u0131 olarak da kullan\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. Kuzey Amerika Iroquois gelene\u011finde d\xfcnya 'b\xfcy\xfck kaplumba\u011fan\u0131n s\u0131rt\u0131'd\u0131r \u2014 topra\u011f\u0131, atalar\u0131, s\xfcreklilik ve dayan\u0131\u015fmay\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131r. Bat\u0131 Afrika gelene\u011finde kaplumba\u011fa, bilgeli\u011fi temsil eden trickster fig\xfcr\xfcd\xfcr; yava\u015f ama asla dur, az ama asla bo\u015f. Kaplumba\u011fan\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131 s\xfcregelen, \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc ilerleme ile i\xe7sel kaleyi korumakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise kabu\u011fun bir savunma de\u011fil, hapis haline geldi\u011fi and\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Kaplumba\u011fa bug\xfcn sana ritmin \xf6nemini hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Etraf\u0131ndaki ko\u015fturmacaya bak\u0131p geride kalm\u0131\u015f gibi hissedebilirsin \u2014 ama ger\xe7ekte mi \xf6yle? Kaplumba\u011falar d\xfcnyan\u0131n en eski canl\u0131 soylar\u0131ndan birini temsil eder; onlardan daha 'h\u0131zl\u0131' ya\u015fayan pek \xe7ok t\xfcr \xe7oktan t\xfckendi. S\xfcrd\xfcr\xfclebilirlik, h\u0131z de\u011fil ritim ve derinliktir. \u015eu an sa\u011flam att\u0131\u011f\u0131n her ad\u0131m, \xfcst\xfcne in\u015fa edebilece\u011fin bir zemin kurar. Peki sen ger\xe7ekten nereye gidiyorsun ve bu yol ger\xe7ekten sana ait mi? Bazen yava\u015flamak, yanl\u0131\u015f yolda h\u0131zl\u0131 gitmemek i\xe7indir. Sa\u011flam zemin \xfczerinde, kendi temponuzda, g\xf6zler net: bu kaplumba\u011fan\u0131n bilgeli\u011fidir.",guidance:"B\xfcy\xfck bir hedefinizi \xfc\xe7 ayl\u0131k k\xfc\xe7\xfck par\xe7alara b\xf6l\xfcn, ard\u0131ndan bu haftaki tek somut ad\u0131m\u0131 belirleyin. Yaln\u0131zca o ad\u0131ma odaklan\u0131n. Kaplumba\u011fa t\xfcm yolculu\u011fu ayn\u0131 anda d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmez; yaln\u0131zca \u015fu anki ad\u0131m\u0131n\u0131 bilir. Bu odak hem stresi azalt\u0131r hem de tutarl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 art\u0131r\u0131r \u2014 kademeli ilerleme, d\xfczenli yineleme ile g\xfcce d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Tortoise",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["patience","wisdom","longevity","stability"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Tortoise is part of the world-bearer motif in Anatolian folk mythology; in many cultures the world stands upon the back of a tortoise \u2014 this belief arises simultaneously in Central Asian, Indian, and Native American traditions. In Hindu cosmology, Kurma is Vishnu's second avatar; he supports the churning of the ocean by gods and demons and is the divine form of patience and endurance. In Chinese tradition, the tortoise is one of the four sacred animals, guardian of the north and of winter; the patterns on its shell were used for divination and oracular reading. In the Iroquois tradition of North America, the world is 'the back of the great turtle' \u2014 bearing the earth, the ancestors, continuity, and solidarity. In West African tradition, the tortoise is the trickster figure who represents wisdom; slow but never stopping, little but never empty. The tortoise's medicine is to advance continuously and measuredly while guarding the inner fortress. Its shadow side is the moment the shell turns from defense into prison.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Tortoise reminds you of the importance of rhythm. Looking at the rush around you, you may feel left behind \u2014 but is that really so? Tortoises represent one of the oldest living lineages on Earth; many faster-living species have long since gone extinct. Sustainability is not speed but rhythm and depth. Every solid step you take now builds a foundation you can build upon. So where are you truly going, and is this path truly yours? Sometimes slowing down is precisely so as not to rush down the wrong road. On solid ground, at your own pace, with clear eyes: this is the tortoise's wisdom.",guidanceEn:"Break a large goal into three-month pieces, then identify the single concrete step for this week. Focus only on that step. The tortoise does not think of the whole journey at once; it knows only its current step. This focus reduces stress and increases consistency \u2014 gradual progress, through regular repetition, becomes power."},{id:"a014",name:"Y\u0131lan",emoji:"\ud83d\udc0d",element:"su",symbolism:["d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","\u015fifa","yenilenme","bilgelik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Vipera_berus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Y\u0131lan, Anadolu'nun en eski tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Kibele'nin ve iyile\u015fme tanr\u0131s\u0131 Asklepios'un kutsal hayvan\u0131d\u0131r; Asklepios'un asas\u0131na sar\u0131lm\u0131\u015f y\u0131lan bug\xfcn h\xe2l\xe2 t\u0131bb\u0131n simgesidir. Eski Anadolu'da y\u0131lan evlerin koruyucusu say\u0131l\u0131r, ev y\u0131lan\u0131n\u0131 \xf6ld\xfcrmek u\u011fursuzluk getirir; bu inan\xe7lar Anadolu kadim tanr\u0131\xe7a k\xfclt\xfcnden miras kalm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. M\u0131s\u0131r'da Uraeus y\u0131lan\u0131, firavunun tac\u0131nda ilahi g\xfc\xe7 ve kral yetkisinin simgesidir; Wadjet, koruyucu tanr\u0131\xe7a olarak kobra formunda tasvir edilir. Hindu gelene\u011finde Kundalini enerjisi, omurgada uyuyan bir y\u0131lan olarak betimlenir; uyan\u0131\u015f\u0131 ruhsal d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn en y\xfcce bi\xe7imidir. Aztek mitolojisinde Quetzalcoatl, t\xfcyl\xfc y\u0131lan tanr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 topra\u011f\u0131 ve g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcn\xfc, maddeyi ve ruhu birle\u015ftirir. Y\u0131lan\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131 d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcmd\xfcr; eski derinin at\u0131lmas\u0131, kal\u0131plar\u0131n b\u0131rak\u0131lmas\u0131 ve do\u011fal yenilenme d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcne g\xfcvenmek. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcmden s\xfcrekli ka\xe7mak ya da her \u015feyi ayn\u0131 anda de\u011fi\u015ftirme d\xfcrt\xfcs\xfcyle ba\u015flay\u0131p hi\xe7birini tamamlamamakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Y\u0131lan bug\xfcn deri de\u011fi\u015ftirme zaman\u0131n\u0131n geldi\u011fini s\xf6yl\xfcyor. Y\u0131lanlar b\xfcy\xfcyebilmek i\xe7in derilerini b\xfct\xfcn\xfcyle atarlar \u2014 k\u0131smen de\u011fil, tamamen; ve bu s\xfcre\xe7 biyolojik olarak onlara y\xfck de\u011fil, rahatlama getirir. Elinde tuttu\u011fun, art\u0131k sana tam uymayan ne var? Bir inan\xe7: 'Ben sevgiye lay\u0131k de\u011filim', 'Ba\u015faramam', 'Hep b\xf6yle olacak.' Bu eski deriler art\u0131k dar geliyor, hissediyorsun bunu. Bir al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k, bir ili\u015fki kal\u0131b\u0131, bir self-image \u2014 bunlardan hangisi art\u0131k ger\xe7e\u011fi yans\u0131tm\u0131yor? B\u0131rakmak, kaybetmek de\u011fildir; daha do\u011fru bir benli\u011fe ge\xe7i\u015f kap\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r. Y\u0131lan ge\xe7mi\u015fine bakmaz, yeni derisinin i\xe7inde tam olarak mevcuttur. Bug\xfcn o ge\xe7i\u015f i\xe7in ne b\u0131rakabilirsin?",guidance:"Bir ka\u011f\u0131da 'art\u0131k bana uymayan \u015fey' olarak \xfc\xe7 inan\xe7 ya da al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k yaz\u0131n. Her birinin yan\u0131na 'bunun yerine ne se\xe7iyorum?' diye yeni bir c\xfcmle ekleyin. Bu pratik, bilin\xe7li d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn ba\u015flang\u0131c\u0131d\u0131r. Y\u0131lan derisi de\u011fi\u015ftirmeden \xf6nce i\xe7ten d\u0131\u015fa haz\u0131rlan\u0131r \u2014 siz de zihninizde haz\u0131rland\u0131k\xe7a ger\xe7ek de\u011fi\u015fim kendili\u011finden kolayla\u015f\u0131r.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Snake",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["transformation","healing","renewal","wisdom"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Snake is the sacred animal of Anatolia's most ancient goddess Cybele and of the healing god Asklepios; the serpent coiled around Asklepios's staff remains the symbol of medicine today. In ancient Anatolia, the snake was considered the guardian of the house, and to kill the household snake was to bring misfortune; these beliefs are inherited from Anatolia's ancient goddess cult. In Egypt, the Uraeus serpent on the pharaoh's crown is the symbol of divine power and royal authority; Wadjet, as the protective goddess, is depicted in the form of a cobra. In Hindu tradition, Kundalini energy is portrayed as a serpent asleep at the base of the spine; its awakening is the most exalted form of spiritual transformation. In Aztec mythology, Quetzalcoatl is the feathered serpent god \u2014 uniting earth and sky, matter and spirit. The snake's medicine is transformation; the shedding of old skin, the releasing of patterns, and trust in the natural cycle of renewal. Its shadow side is to flee transformation continually, or to attempt to change everything at once and finish nothing.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Snake tells you it is time to shed your skin. Snakes shed their skin entirely in order to grow \u2014 not partly, but completely; and this process biologically brings them not burden but relief. What are you holding that no longer fits you? A belief: 'I am not worthy of love,' 'I cannot succeed,' 'It will always be this way.' These old skins are growing tight \u2014 you can feel it. A habit, a relationship pattern, a self-image \u2014 which of these no longer reflects the truth? Letting go is not losing; it is the doorway to a truer self. The snake does not look back at its past; it is fully present inside its new skin. What can you release today to make that passage?",guidanceEn:"On a piece of paper, write three beliefs or habits as 'no longer fit me.' Beside each, add a new sentence: 'What do I choose instead?' This practice is the beginning of conscious transformation. The snake prepares from the inside out before it sheds \u2014 as you prepare in your mind, real change becomes effortless of itself."},{id:"a015",name:"Kelebek",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8b",element:"hava",symbolism:["d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","g\xfczellik","hafiflik","de\u011fi\u015fim"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Papillon_pourpre.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kelebek, T\xfcrk ve Anadolu halk k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde ruhun, \xf6zellikle de \xf6len sevdililerin ruhunun ziyareti olarak yorumlan\u0131r; aniden beliriveren bir kelebek, ge\xe7mi\u015f bir sevgiliyi ya da atay\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131r. Antik Yunan'da 'Psyche' hem kelebek hem de ruh anlam\u0131na gelir; Psyche ve Eros efsanesi, ruhun a\u015fk arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm yolculu\u011funu anlat\u0131r. Aztek gelene\u011finde Itzpapalotl, obsidyen kelebe\u011fi tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r; kurban ve yeniden do\u011fu\u015f rit\xfcellerinin koruyucusudur. \xc7in k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde kelebek \xe7ifti, a\u015fk\u0131n ve evlilik mutlulu\u011funun simgesidir; Zhuangzi'nin kelebek r\xfcyas\u0131 ise en \xfcnl\xfc kimlik-felsefe metinlerinden biridir. Kuzey Amerika Pueblo gelene\u011finde kelebek danslar\u0131, bahar\u0131n ve yenilenen do\u011fan\u0131n kutsal kar\u015f\u0131lanmas\u0131d\u0131r. Kelebe\u011fin t\u0131bb\u0131 kozas\u0131 i\xe7inde tam teslimiyetle ge\xe7irilen karanl\u0131k d\xf6nemin bir biti\u015f de\u011fil, derin bir d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm oldu\u011funu bilmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc tamamlamadan kozay\u0131 erken yaratmak \u2014 g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcrde haz\u0131r, i\xe7eride yar\u0131m kalmak.",dailyMessage:"Kelebek bug\xfcn sana d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn sessizce tamamland\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 m\xfcjdeliyor. O koza d\xf6neminde \u2014 karanl\u0131k, s\u0131k\u0131\u015fm\u0131\u015f, anlams\u0131z hissetti\u011fin g\xfcnlerde \u2014 asl\u0131nda her \u015feyi kaybetmiyordun; yeniden \u015fekilleniyordun. Kelebek larvas\u0131n\u0131n kozaya girdi\u011finde neredeyse eriyip s\u0131v\u0131la\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 biliyor musun? Eski yap\u0131 tamamen \xe7\xf6z\xfcl\xfcr, yeni yap\u0131 s\u0131f\u0131rdan in\u015fa olur \u2014 bu do\u011fan\u0131n en radikal d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm mucizesidir. Sen de o s\xfcre\xe7ten ge\xe7tin ya da h\xe2l\xe2 ge\xe7iyorsun. Eski sen art\u0131k yok \u2014 bu kay\u0131p de\u011fil, evrim. Yeni kanatlar\u0131n var; onlar\u0131 a\xe7maya izin vermek, kelebek olmay\u0131 tamamlamakt\u0131r. Peki hangi konuda h\xe2l\xe2 kozan\u0131n i\xe7inde bekliyorsun, ne seni \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa \xe7\u0131kmaktan al\u0131koyuyor?",guidance:"Bug\xfcn ya da bu hafta boyunca her sabah uyan\u0131nca bir c\xfcmle yaz\u0131n: 'Bug\xfcn kelebek olarak ne yapard\u0131m?' Bu soru sizi yeni kimli\u011finize ba\u011flar \u2014 eski al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131z\u0131n de\u011fil, d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfcz ki\u015finin perspektifinden hareket etmeye ba\u015flars\u0131n\u0131z. Kelebek, t\u0131rt\u0131l kafas\u0131yla u\xe7amaz; siz de eski zihin \xe7er\xe7evesiyle yeni hayat\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 ya\u015fayamazs\u0131n\u0131z.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Butterfly",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["transformation","beauty","lightness","change"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Turkic and Anatolian folk culture, the Butterfly is interpreted as the visitation of a soul, especially that of departed loved ones; a butterfly suddenly appearing reminds one of a past beloved or ancestor. In Ancient Greek, 'Psyche' means both butterfly and soul; the legend of Psyche and Eros tells of the soul's transformative journey through love. In Aztec tradition, Itzpapalotl is the obsidian butterfly goddess; guardian of sacrifice and rebirth rituals. In Chinese culture, the pair of butterflies symbolizes love and marital happiness; Zhuangzi's butterfly dream is among the most famous philosophical texts of identity. In the Pueblo tradition of North America, butterfly dances are the sacred welcoming of spring and renewed nature. The butterfly's medicine is to know that the dark period spent in surrender within the cocoon is not an ending but a deep transformation. Its shadow side is to leave the cocoon before transformation is complete \u2014 appearing ready, yet inwardly unfinished.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Butterfly announces that your transformation has been quietly completed. In that cocoon time \u2014 the days when you felt dark, stuck, meaningless \u2014 you were not really losing everything; you were being reshaped. Did you know that the butterfly larva, once inside the cocoon, nearly melts and liquefies? The old structure dissolves entirely, and a new one is built from scratch \u2014 this is nature's most radical miracle of transformation. You have passed through this, or are still passing through it. The old you is gone \u2014 this is not loss but evolution. You have new wings; to allow yourself to spread them is to complete the becoming of the butterfly. So in what matter are you still waiting inside the cocoon? What is keeping you from stepping into the light?",guidanceEn:"Today or all this week, write one sentence each morning upon waking: 'What would I do today as a butterfly?' This question connects you to your new identity \u2014 you begin to act from the perspective not of your old habits but of the person you have become. The butterfly cannot fly with the caterpillar's head; you cannot live your new life within the frame of the old mind."},{id:"a016",name:"Tavus",emoji:"\ud83e\udd9a",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["g\xfczellik","\xf6zg\xfcven","b\xfct\xfcnl\xfck","koruyuculuk"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Pavo_cristatus_Photograph_by_Shantanu_Kuveskar.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Tavus ku\u015fu, Osmanl\u0131 saray sembolizminde ve Do\u011fu Akdeniz k\xfclt\xfcrel belle\u011finde g\xfczelli\u011fin, koruman\u0131n ve cennetin simgesidir; \u0130slam ikonografisinde cennet bah\xe7esinin ku\u015fu olarak tasvir edilir, her g\xf6z\xfc ayr\u0131 bir ilahi bak\u0131\u015f\u0131 temsil eder. Hristiyanl\u0131k gelene\u011finde tavus t\xfcy\xfcndeki 'g\xf6z' motifi, her yerde haz\u0131r olan ilahi g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfc ve \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfc\u011f\xfc simgeler; Bizans kiliselerinde yayg\u0131n bir motiftir. Hindu gelene\u011finde Saraswati'nin ve Karttikeya'n\u0131n kutsal hayvan\u0131 olan tavus, bilgeli\u011fi, g\xfczelli\u011fi ve sava\u015f\u0131n koruyuculu\u011funu bir arada ta\u015f\u0131r. Yunan mitolojisinde Hera'n\u0131n kutsal ku\u015fu olan tavusun kuyru\u011fundaki g\xf6zler, y\xfcz g\xf6zl\xfc dev Argus'un Io'ya g\xf6zetiminden kalma iz olarak anlat\u0131l\u0131r. \xc7in gelene\u011finde tavus t\xfcy\xfc soylulu\u011fun, sadakatin ve koruman\u0131n simgesi olarak kullan\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. Tavusun t\u0131bb\u0131 \xf6zg\xfcn g\xfczelli\u011fi ve t\xfcm y\xf6nleri g\xf6rme kapasitesini i\xe7erir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise g\xf6steriyi i\xe7eri\u011fin yerine ge\xe7irmek, g\xf6r\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfcn i\xe7in de\u011fil g\xf6r\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfcn gibi i\xe7in ya\u015famakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Tavus bug\xfcn senden kuyru\u011funu a\xe7man\u0131 istiyor \u2014 ama g\xf6steri\u015f i\xe7in de\u011fil, b\xfct\xfcnl\xfck i\xe7in. Tavus kuyru\u011funu a\xe7mak biyolojik olarak enerji gerektiren, savunmas\u0131zl\u0131k i\xe7eren bir eylemdir; her t\xfcy bir mesaj ta\u015f\u0131r. Sen kim oldu\u011funu ne kadar g\xf6steriyorsun? Hangi yetene\u011fini, hangi d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceni, hangi taraf\u0131n\u0131 sakl\u0131yorsun \u2014 ve bu saklanman\u0131n as\u0131l nedeni ne? Korku mu, al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfcl\xfck m\xfc, yoksa yarg\u0131lanma kayg\u0131s\u0131 m\u0131? Ger\xe7ek g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcrl\xfck, ba\u015fkalar\u0131na da kendileri olma cesareti verir. Seninle ayn\u0131 t\xfcyleri ta\u015f\u0131yanlar \u2014 ayn\u0131 duyarl\u0131l\u0131klar\u0131, ayn\u0131 hayalleri \u2014 seni g\xf6r\xfcnce rahatlar. Bug\xfcn bir ad\u0131m daha g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr ol: d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceni payla\u015f, bir eserini g\xf6ster, sahici bir his ilet.",guidance:"Bu hafta bir \u015feyi payla\u015f\u0131n, normalde saklad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z \u2014 bir fikir, bir his, bir yarat\u0131m. Sosyal medyada, bir konu\u015fmada, ya da sadece bir insanla birebir. G\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr olmak pratik gerektirir. Tavus kuyru\u011funu bir kez a\xe7t\u0131ktan sonra kapamay\u0131 kolayca se\xe7emez; ve siz de bir kez ger\xe7ekten g\xf6r\xfcld\xfckten sonra saklanman\u0131n ne kadar gereksiz oldu\u011funu anlars\u0131n\u0131z.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Peacock",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["beauty","self-confidence","wholeness","protectiveness"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Peacock, in Ottoman court symbolism and in the cultural memory of the Eastern Mediterranean, is the symbol of beauty, protection, and paradise; in Islamic iconography it is depicted as the bird of the garden of paradise, each eye representing a separate divine gaze. In Christian tradition, the 'eye' motif on the peacock feather symbolizes the omnipresent divine vision and immortality; it is a common motif in Byzantine churches. In Hindu tradition, the peacock, the sacred animal of Saraswati and Karttikeya, carries together wisdom, beauty, and the protection of war. In Greek mythology, the eyes on the tail of Hera's sacred peacock are said to be traces of the hundred-eyed giant Argus, set to watch over Io. In Chinese tradition, the peacock feather has been used as a symbol of nobility, loyalty, and protection. The peacock's medicine is one's authentic beauty and the capacity to see from every angle. Its shadow side is letting display take the place of substance, living for how you appear rather than as who you are.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Peacock wants you to spread your tail \u2014 not for display, but for wholeness. Spreading the peacock's tail is biologically an act that requires energy and contains vulnerability; each feather carries a message. How much of who you are do you show? Which talent, which thought, which side of yourself are you hiding \u2014 and what is the real reason for hiding? Fear, modesty, or the worry of being judged? True visibility gives others the courage to be themselves, too. Those who carry the same feathers \u2014 the same sensitivities, the same dreams \u2014 feel relieved when they see you. Today, become a little more visible: share a thought, show a creation, transmit a genuine feeling.",guidanceEn:"This week, share something you usually hide \u2014 an idea, a feeling, a creation. On social media, in a conversation, or just one-on-one with a person. Being visible takes practice. Once the peacock spreads its tail, it cannot easily choose to close it again; once you are truly seen, you, too, will realize how needless hiding is."},{id:"a017",name:"Leylek",emoji:"\ud83e\udda2",element:"hava",symbolism:["u\u011fur","yenilik","bereket","aile"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/White_stork_Ciconia_ciconia.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Leylek, Anadolu halk k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde u\u011furun ve berekelin en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc simgelerinden biridir; leyle\u011fin kondu\u011fu evin bolluk ve huzur i\xe7inde olaca\u011f\u0131na inan\u0131l\u0131r, yuvas\u0131 y\u0131k\u0131lmaz. Lohusa anneye leylek yuvas\u0131 olan evden toprak getirilmesi dahi u\u011fur say\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. \u0130slam k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde leylek 'hac ku\u015fu' olarak da bilinir; Mekke'ye gidip geldi\u011fine inan\u0131lan bu ku\u015f, kutsal yolculu\u011fun ve ilahi koruman\u0131n simgesidir. Yunan mitolojisinde leylekler ebeveynlerine sadakatla bakan, onlara yiyecek getiren erdemli ku\u015flar olarak bilinir; bu davran\u0131\u015f, aile ba\u011flar\u0131n\u0131n ve minnetin simgesi olmu\u015ftur. Slav gelene\u011finde bahar leyle\u011finin geli\u015fi k\xf6yleri yeniden can kazanm\u0131\u015f bir d\xfcnyaya kar\u015f\u0131lar; \u015fans, bolluk ve do\u011furganl\u0131kla \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirilir. Afrika gelene\u011finde \xe7e\u015fitli leylek t\xfcrleri su ve bereketin koruyucusu olarak kutsan\u0131r. Leyle\u011fin t\u0131bb\u0131, iyili\u011fe a\xe7\u0131k kalmak ve bereket d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcne g\xfcvenmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise o kadar beklenti i\xe7inde ya\u015famak ki \u015fu an\u0131n k\xfc\xe7\xfck bereket i\u015faretlerini g\xf6rmemektir.",dailyMessage:"Leylek bug\xfcn iyi \u015feyler ta\u015f\u0131yor \u2014 ama kap\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7\u0131k tutman gerekiyor. Bereket her zaman b\xfcy\xfck patlamalarla gelmiyor; \xe7o\u011funlukla dikkat edilmesini bekleyen k\xfc\xe7\xfck dokunu\u015flarla geliyor. Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131nda olan k\xfc\xe7\xfck g\xfczelliklere bakt\u0131n m\u0131 \u2014 seni g\xfcld\xfcren bir \u015fey, beklenmedik yerde gelen bir nezaket, bir an birlik? Leylek biyolojik olarak binlerce kilometre ge\xe7i\u015f yapar ve tam zaman\u0131nda, tam do\u011fru yere iner \u2014 bu titizlikle planlanm\u0131\u015f de\u011fil, i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcseldir. Senin hayat\u0131nda da baz\u0131 \u015feyler tam zaman\u0131nda gelecek; ama bunu g\xf6rebilmek i\xe7in umudunu kaybetmemi\u015f olman, g\xf6zlerini a\xe7\u0131k tutman gerekiyor. Minnetle bakmak, berekat i\xe7in alan a\xe7ar. Bug\xfcn neye \u015f\xfckredebilirsin?",guidance:"Bu ak\u015fam uyumadan \xf6nce, bug\xfcn fark etti\u011finiz \xfc\xe7 k\xfc\xe7\xfck iyili\u011fi ya da g\xfczelli\u011fi yaz\u0131n. B\xfcy\xfck olaylar de\u011fil \u2014 minik anlar. Bunu yedi g\xfcn boyunca yap\u0131n. Ara\u015ft\u0131rmalar minnet prati\u011finin beynin pozitif uyaranlara a\xe7\u0131kl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 art\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6steriyor; leylek hep geliyordu, siz sadece onu g\xf6rmeyi \xf6\u011freniyorsunuz.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Stork",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["good fortune","newness","abundance","family"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Stork is one of the strongest symbols of good fortune and abundance in Anatolian folk culture; it is believed that the house upon which a stork settles will enjoy plenty and peace, and its nest is never destroyed. Even soil from a house with a stork's nest was considered lucky to bring to a new mother. In Islamic culture, the stork is also known as the 'pilgrim bird'; this bird, believed to journey to and from Mecca, symbolizes the sacred journey and divine protection. In Greek mythology, storks are virtuous birds who care loyally for their parents and bring them food; this behavior became a symbol of family bonds and gratitude. In Slavic tradition, the spring stork's arrival greets the villages as a world coming back to life; it is identified with luck, abundance, and fertility. In African tradition, various stork species are revered as guardians of water and fertility. The stork's medicine is to remain open to goodness and to trust the cycle of abundance. Its shadow side is to live so much in expectation that one fails to see the small signs of abundance in the present moment.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Stork brings good things \u2014 but you need to keep your door open. Abundance does not always come with great explosions; most often it comes through small touches awaiting your attention. Have you noticed the small beauties in your life today \u2014 something that made you smile, an unexpected kindness, a moment of togetherness? The stork biologically migrates thousands of kilometers and lands at the right time, in just the right place \u2014 this is not meticulous planning but instinct. Some things will come to your life at just the right time too; but in order to see this, you must not have lost hope, you must keep your eyes open. Looking with gratitude opens space for abundance. What can you be grateful for today?",guidanceEn:"Tonight before sleep, write down three small kindnesses or beauties you noticed today. Not great events \u2014 tiny moments. Do this for seven days. Research shows that a gratitude practice increases the brain's openness to positive stimuli; the stork was always coming, you are simply learning to see it."},{id:"a018",name:"\u015eahin",emoji:"\ud83e\udd85",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["h\u0131z","odak","kararl\u0131l\u0131k","hedef"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Falco_peregrinus_good.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"\u015eahin, Osmanl\u0131 saray\u0131nda ve T\xfcrk soylu gelene\u011finde y\xfczy\u0131llarca en prestiJli evcil av ku\u015fu olmu\u015f, sahibe stat\xfc ve keskin zeka kazand\u0131rm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r; \u015fahini e\u011fitmenin kendisi de bir sanat olarak g\xf6r\xfclm\xfc\u015ft\xfcr. M\u0131s\u0131r'da Horus, \u015fahin ba\u015fl\u0131 g\xfcne\u015f tanr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 her g\xfcn g\xfcne\u015fi g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcnde ta\u015f\u0131yan, ilahi adaletin ve krall\u0131\u011f\u0131n koruyucusudur; g\xf6z\xfc, 'Wadjet G\xf6z\xfc' olarak t\xfcm g\xf6zetim ve koruma ikonografisinin ba\u015f\u0131d\u0131r. Antik M\u0131s\u0131r'da Ra da \u015fahin formunda tasvir edilir. Kelt gelene\u011finde \u015fahin, ge\xe7mi\u015fin zincirlerini \xe7\xf6zme ve geni\u015f perspektifle bakma g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc simgeler. Aztek gelene\u011finde Huitzilopochtli'nin sava\u015f sembol\xfc \u015fahindir; g\xfcne\u015fi karanl\u0131ktan kurtarmak i\xe7in sava\u015fan g\xfc\xe7. Kuzey Amerika Lakota gelene\u011finde \u015fahin t\xfcy\xfc en kutsal hediyelerden biridir; netlik, odak ve ilahi ba\u011flant\u0131n\u0131n simgesidir. \u015eahinin t\u0131bb\u0131 odaklanm\u0131\u015f, keskin ve zamanl\u0131 harekettir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise o kadar odaklanmak ki periferik bilgiyi ve ili\u015fkisel ba\u011flant\u0131y\u0131 yitirmektir.",dailyMessage:"\u015eahin bug\xfcn tek bir \u015feye odaklanman\u0131 istiyor. \u015eahin Do\u011fa'n\u0131n en h\u0131zl\u0131 yarat\u0131klar\u0131ndan biridir \u2014 dal\u0131\u015f h\u0131z\u0131 saatte \xfc\xe7 y\xfcz kilometreyi a\u015fabilir. Ama bu h\u0131z, tek bir hedefe tam odaklanmadan m\xfcmk\xfcn olmaz; \u015fahin ayn\u0131 anda bir\xe7ok ava bakmaz. Bug\xfcn senin i\xe7in o tek \u015fey ne? Zihninde ayn\u0131 anda ka\xe7 tane '\xf6ncelik' var? Bunlar\u0131n hepsi ger\xe7ekten \xf6ncelikli mi, yoksa erteleme mi? Bir \u015feye odaklanmak, di\u011fer her \u015feyi sonraya b\u0131rakmak demektir \u2014 ve bu bir kay\u0131p de\u011fil, bir se\xe7im. Se\xe7im yapabilmek, g\xfcc\xfcn i\u015faretidir. Bug\xfcn o tek \u015feyi belirle; gerisi bekleyebilir.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn\xfcn g\xf6rev listesini yaz\u0131n ve en \xf6nemli \xfc\xe7 \u015feyi daireler i\xe7ine al\u0131n. Ard\u0131ndan bu \xfc\xe7ten yaln\u0131zca birine \u2014 en y\xfcksek etkiye sahip olana \u2014 \xf6ncelik verin ve geri kalanlar\u0131 yar\u0131na b\u0131rak\u0131n. \u015eahinin h\u0131z\u0131 odaktan gelir; siz de odakland\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131zda \u015fa\u015f\u0131rt\u0131c\u0131 bir etkinlikle ilerledi\u011finizi fark edeceksiniz.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Falcon",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["speed","focus","determination","purpose"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Falcon was for centuries the most prestigious hunting bird of the Ottoman court and the Turkic noble tradition, bringing its owner status and sharp wit; the very training of a falcon was considered an art. In Egypt, Horus is the falcon-headed sun god \u2014 the bearer of the sun across the sky each day, the guardian of divine justice and kingship; his eye, the 'Eye of Wadjet,' is the source of all surveillance and protection iconography. In Ancient Egypt, Ra too is depicted in falcon form. In Celtic tradition, the falcon symbolizes the power to dissolve the chains of the past and look from a wide perspective. In Aztec tradition, Huitzilopochtli's war symbol is the falcon; the power that fights to rescue the sun from darkness. In the Lakota tradition of North America, the falcon feather is among the most sacred gifts; the symbol of clarity, focus, and divine connection. The falcon's medicine is focused, sharp, and well-timed action. Its shadow side is becoming so focused that one loses peripheral information and relational connection.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Falcon asks you to focus on one thing. The falcon is among nature's fastest creatures \u2014 its dive speed can exceed three hundred kilometers per hour. But that speed is impossible without total focus on a single target; the falcon does not look at many prey at once. What is your one thing today? How many 'priorities' do you hold in your mind simultaneously? Are they all truly priorities, or is this procrastination? To focus on one thing is to leave everything else for later \u2014 and this is not loss but choice. To be able to choose is the sign of power. Today, identify that one thing; the rest can wait.",guidanceEn:"Write today's task list and circle the three most important. Then prioritize only one of those three \u2014 the one with the highest impact \u2014 and leave the rest for tomorrow. The falcon's speed comes from focus; when you focus, you will be amazed at how effectively you progress."},{id:"a019",name:"Pars",emoji:"\ud83d\udc06",element:"toprak",symbolism:["\xe7eviklik","g\xfc\xe7","yaln\u0131zl\u0131k","\xf6zg\xfcven"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Leopard_africa.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Pars ve leopar, Anadolu'nun en eski arkeolojik bulgular\u0131nda kar\u015f\u0131m\u0131za \xe7\u0131kar; \xc7atalh\xf6y\xfck'te bulunan ta\u015f fig\xfcrinlerde tanr\u0131\xe7a parslara e\u015flik eder ve bu g\xfc\xe7l\xfc birliktelik, di\u015fil g\xfcc\xfcn, sezginin ve vah\u015fi do\u011fan\u0131n kutsal birli\u011fini temsil eder. Hitit gelene\u011finde de leopar ve pars izleri, kraliyet t\xf6reni motiflerinde g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr. M\u0131s\u0131r'da Sekhmet'in sava\u015f bi\xe7imi leoparla \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirilir; \u015famanist t\xf6renlerinde pars postu giyen M\u0131s\u0131r rahipleri, tanr\u0131sal g\xfcce arac\u0131 olurlard\u0131. Afrika gelene\u011finde, \xf6zellikle Bat\u0131 Afrika Yoruba k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde leopar, sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 asaletin ve kontroll\xfc g\xfcc\xfcn simgesidir. Aztek panteonunda Tezcatlipoca'n\u0131n bir avatar\u0131 olan sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 pars, gece ve gizem g\xfcc\xfcn\xfcn ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r. Buda \xf6\u011fretilerinde kar leopar\u0131 zorlu da\u011f yollar\u0131nda yaln\u0131z y\xfcr\xfcyen dervi\u015f gibidir; yaln\u0131zl\u0131k, zay\u0131fl\u0131k de\u011fil \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfckt\xfcr. Pars\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131 kendi ba\u015f\u0131na g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olmak ve bu g\xfcc\xfc sessizce ta\u015f\u0131yabilmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise o kadar yaln\u0131z olmak ki ger\xe7ek ba\u011f\u0131n ortadan kalkt\u0131\u011f\u0131 bir tecrite d\xfc\u015fmektir.",dailyMessage:"Pars bug\xfcn sana kendi ba\u015f\u0131nal\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n bir g\xfc\xe7 oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Leoparlar do\u011fada a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131n iki kat\u0131n\u0131 a\u011faca ta\u015f\u0131yabilecek g\xfc\xe7te avc\u0131lard\u0131r ve bunu sessizce, tek ba\u015flar\u0131na yaparlar \u2014 onay beklemeden, alk\u0131\u015f aramadan. Sen ne zamand\u0131r ba\u015fkalar\u0131n\u0131n onay\u0131n\u0131 bekliyorsun bir ad\u0131m atmak i\xe7in? \u0130\xe7inde zaten bildi\u011fin, ama do\u011frulat\u0131lmas\u0131n\u0131 bekledi\u011fin bir karar var m\u0131? Peki bu do\u011frulama gelse de gelmese de do\u011fru olan de\u011fi\u015fiyor mu? Yaln\u0131z olmak yanl\u0131\u015f hissettirebilir \u2014 ama yaln\u0131zl\u0131k ile izolasyon farkl\u0131 \u015feylerdir. Yaln\u0131zl\u0131k kendi merkezinle ba\u011flant\u0131d\u0131r; izolasyon ise korkudan duvarlar \xf6rmektir. Bug\xfcn g\xfcvendi\u011fin sesi duy: i\xe7indeki o ince sesi. O pars sesine kulak ver.",guidance:"Bir karar var m\u0131 onaylanmas\u0131n\u0131 bekledi\u011finiz? Bug\xfcn bu karar\u0131, ba\u015fkas\u0131na dan\u0131\u015fmadan, kendiniz verin \u2014 sonra bir hafta o kararla ya\u015fay\u0131n. Pars\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131 deneyimle \xf6\u011frenilir; kendinize g\xfcvenme kapasitesi, kendinize g\xfcvenmeyi se\xe7tik\xe7e geli\u015fir. Karar m\xfckemmel olmak zorunda de\u011fil, sahici olmak zorunda.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Anatolian Leopard",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["agility","power","solitude","self-confidence"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Leopard (Pars) appears in Anatolia's earliest archaeological finds; in the stone figurines unearthed at Catalhoyuk the goddess is accompanied by leopards, and this powerful union represents the sacred unity of feminine power, intuition, and the wild. Traces of the leopard appear too in Hittite royal ceremonial motifs. In Egypt, Sekhmet's warrior aspect is identified with the leopard; Egyptian priests wearing leopard skins in shamanic ceremonies served as mediators of divine power. In African tradition, particularly in the West African Yoruba culture, the leopard is the symbol of warrior nobility and controlled power. In the Aztec pantheon, the warrior jaguar \u2014 an avatar of Tezcatlipoca \u2014 is the bearer of the powers of night and mystery. In Buddhist teachings, the snow leopard is like a dervish walking alone on difficult mountain paths; solitude is not weakness but freedom. The leopard's medicine is to be strong on one's own and to carry that strength quietly. Its shadow side is to be so alone that real connection disappears, falling into isolation.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Leopard reminds you that your aloneness is a strength. Leopards are predators powerful enough to carry twice their own weight up a tree, and they do this silently, alone \u2014 without waiting for approval, without seeking applause. How long have you been waiting for someone else's approval before taking a step? Is there a decision you already know within yourself, but are waiting to have validated? Does the truth change whether that validation comes or not? Being alone can feel wrong \u2014 but aloneness and isolation are different things. Aloneness is connection with your own center; isolation is building walls out of fear. Today, hear the voice you trust: that fine voice within. Listen to that leopard's voice.",guidanceEn:"Is there a decision you are waiting to have approved? Today, make that decision without consulting anyone \u2014 then live with it for a week. The leopard's medicine is learned through experience; the capacity to trust yourself grows as you choose to trust yourself. The decision does not have to be perfect, only authentic."},{id:"a020",name:"Ar\u0131",emoji:"\ud83d\udc1d",element:"toprak",symbolism:["\xe7al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k","topluluk","yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131k","bereket"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Bee_on_Sedum.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Ar\u0131, Anadolu'da Hristiyanl\u0131k \xf6ncesi d\xf6nemden bu yana kutsal bir varl\u0131kt\u0131r; Efes'teki Artemis k\xfclt\xfcnde tap\u0131nak ar\u0131lar\u0131 kutsal say\u0131lm\u0131\u015f, rahipler 'ar\u0131' anlam\u0131na gelen isimler ta\u015f\u0131m\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da ar\u0131, firavunun unvanlar\u0131 aras\u0131nda yer alm\u0131\u015f ve M\u0131s\u0131r'\u0131n b\xfct\xfcnle\u015fmesinin simgesi olmu\u015ftur. Yunan mitolojisinde ar\u0131lar Apollo'nun tap\u0131na\u011f\u0131na hizmet eden kutsal hayvanlar olup k\xe2hinlerin sesi onlar\u0131n sesiyle b\xfct\xfcnle\u015fir. Kuzey Amerika Maya gelene\u011finde Ah Muzen Cab, ar\u0131lar\u0131n ve bal\u0131n tanr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; uzun ya\u015fam ve bolluk ayinlerinin merkezindedir. Hint gelene\u011finde Kamadeva'n\u0131n oku ar\u0131lardan yap\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r; a\u015fk, g\xfczellik ve yarat\u0131m\u0131n en derin tatl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 simgeler. Celtic gelene\u011finde ar\u0131, iki d\xfcnya aras\u0131nda mesaj ta\u015f\u0131yan kutsal habercidir \u2014 do\u011fumlar, \xf6l\xfcmler, d\xfc\u011f\xfcnler ar\u0131lara bildirilirdi. Ar\u0131n\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, bireysel \xe7abay\u0131 kolektif bir bereketle birle\u015ftirme kapasitesidir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise kovan u\u011fruna bireyin yok olmas\u0131, ya da tam tersine kolektiviteden kopup yaln\u0131z ve verimsiz kalmakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"Ar\u0131 bug\xfcn emek ile bereket aras\u0131ndaki o gizli ba\u011f\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Bir ar\u0131 g\xfcnde be\u015f y\xfczden fazla \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi ziyaret eder ve t\xfcm hayat\u0131 boyunca yaln\u0131zca bir \xe7ay ka\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131 bal \xfcretir \u2014 ama binlerce ar\u0131 bir arada muazzam bir bol \xfcr\xfcn yarat\u0131r. K\xfc\xe7\xfck, tutarl\u0131, sistematik ad\u0131mlar birikiyor \u2014 bunu g\xf6r\xfcyor musun? \u015eu an u\u011fra\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n \u015feyin sonu\xe7lar\u0131 yava\u015f g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyor olabilir, ama birikimi gizlidir. Ne ekiyorsun, nas\u0131l bak\u0131yorsun, ne kadar sab\u0131r ta\u015f\u0131yorsun? Ar\u0131 asla atlamaz: her ad\u0131m atar, her \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi b\xfcy\xfck bir g\xf6rev gibi de\u011fil k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir ad\u0131m gibi g\xf6r\xfcr. Bug\xfcn hangi k\xfc\xe7\xfck ad\u0131m\u0131 atmay\u0131 erteliyorsun? O ad\u0131m, i\xe7inde gizlenen bir bereketin kap\u0131s\u0131 olabilir.",guidance:"B\xfcy\xfck hedefinize giden bir 'g\xfcnl\xfck ar\u0131 ad\u0131m\u0131' belirleyin \u2014 her g\xfcn tekrarlayabilece\u011finiz, k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama tutarl\u0131 bir eylem. Bunu en az yirmi bir g\xfcn yap\u0131n. Ar\u0131 ritmi \u015f\xf6yledir: d\xfczenli, kararl\u0131 ve mevsimin gereklerine uyumlu. Yirmi birinci g\xfcnde geriye bak\u0131n ve ne kadar ilerledti\u011finizi g\xf6r\xfcn; bal bu sab\u0131rla yap\u0131l\u0131r.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Bee",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["industriousness","community","creativity","abundance"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Bee has been a sacred being in Anatolia since pre-Christian times; in the cult of Artemis at Ephesus, temple bees were considered sacred, and the priests bore names meaning 'bee.' In ancient Egypt, the bee figured among the pharaoh's titles and became a symbol of Egypt's unification. In Greek mythology, bees were the sacred animals serving Apollo's temple, the voice of the oracles intertwined with theirs. In the Mayan tradition of North America, Ah Muzen Cab is the god of bees and honey; central to long-life and abundance rites. In Indian tradition, Kamadeva's arrows are made of bees; symbolizing the deepest sweetness of love, beauty, and creation. In Celtic tradition, the bee is the sacred messenger carrying tidings between the two worlds \u2014 births, deaths, and weddings were announced to the bees. The bee's medicine is the capacity to weave individual effort into collective abundance. Its shadow side is the individual disappearing for the hive's sake, or conversely cutting oneself off from the collective and becoming lonely and unproductive.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Bee reminds you of the secret bond between labor and abundance. A single bee visits more than five hundred flowers a day and produces only a teaspoon of honey in its lifetime \u2014 but thousands of bees together create an immense harvest. Small, consistent, systematic steps accumulate \u2014 do you see this? The fruits of what you are working on now may appear slow, but the accumulation is hidden. What are you sowing, how are you tending it, how much patience are you holding? The bee never skips: it takes every step, treats every flower not as a great task but as a small step. Which small step are you postponing today? That step may be the door to a hidden abundance within you.",guidanceEn:"Choose a 'daily bee step' toward your big goal \u2014 a small but consistent action you can repeat every day. Do this for at least twenty-one days. The bee's rhythm is regular, steady, and attuned to the season's needs. On the twenty-first day, look back and see how far you have come; honey is made with this patience."},{id:"a021",name:"K\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7",emoji:"\ud83d\udc26",element:"hava",symbolism:["\xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck","yolculuk","umut","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Hirundo_rustica_-_Radujevac.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"K\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7, Anadolu'da bahar\u0131n ve umudun en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc habercisidir; halk inan\u0131\u015f\u0131na g\xf6re k\u0131rlang\u0131c\u0131n kondu\u011fu eve bereket gelir, yuvas\u0131 y\u0131k\u0131lamaz \u2014 onu inciten u\u011fursuzluk getirir. T\xfcrk halk \u015fiirinde k\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7, \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn ve yurt sevgisinin simgesidir; s\xfcrg\xfcndeki \u015fairin bile en \xe7ok \xf6zledi\u011fi k\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7 sesidir. Antik Yunan'da k\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7 Aphrodite'nin kutsal ku\u015fuydu; sevginin, yeniden bulu\u015fman\u0131n ve ge\xe7i\u015flerin habercisidir. M\u0131s\u0131r mitolojisinde k\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7, Osiris'in ruhunun ald\u0131\u011f\u0131 bi\xe7imlerden biridir; \xf6l\xfcmden yeniden do\u011fu\u015fu simgeleyen bu ku\u015f, g\xfcne\u015fin her sabah tekrar do\u011fmas\u0131na e\u015flik eder. Japon Haiku gelene\u011finde k\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7, an'\u0131n g\xfczelli\u011fini ve ge\xe7icili\u011fini en ince bi\xe7imde yakalar. Kelt gelene\u011finde g\xf6\xe7men ku\u015flar ruhlar\u0131n ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; k\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7lar \xf6zellikle atalarla ba\u011flant\u0131 kurman\u0131n simgesidir. K\u0131rlang\u0131c\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131 yeniden ba\u015flama cesareti ve eski a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131klar\u0131 b\u0131rakmakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise hi\xe7bir yerde durmamak, s\xfcrekli hareket ederek ger\xe7ek bir yere ait olmaktan ka\xe7\u0131nmakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"K\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7 bug\xfcn sana yeni bir d\xf6nemin kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n araland\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 s\xf6yl\xfcyor. \u0130\xe7inde hissetti\u011fin o k\xfc\xe7\xfck k\u0131p\u0131rdanma \u2014 o merak, o umut, o 'belki' \u2014 \xf6nemsiz de\u011fil. K\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7lar G\xfcney Afrika'dan Orta Avrupa'ya kadar binlerce kilometre g\xf6\xe7 eder ve \u015fa\u015f\u0131rt\u0131c\u0131 bir do\u011frulukla tam geri d\xf6nerler \u2014 bu sadece i\xe7g\xfcd\xfc de\u011fil, g\xfcven ve cesaret de gerektirir. Yeni bir \u015fey ba\u015flatmak i\xe7in m\xfckemmel zaman\u0131 bekliyorsun belki \u2014 ama k\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7 bahar\u0131 beklemez; bahar\u0131 o getirir. Bug\xfcn k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7 yapabilirsin: bir ad\u0131m, bir deneme, bir davet. Ertelemek, o olas\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n i\xe7indeki enerjiyi yava\u015f yava\u015f eritir. Peki ne zamand\u0131r ba\u015flamay\u0131 bekliyorsun ve bu bekleme sana ne kat\u0131yor?",guidance:"Bug\xfcn ya da bu hafta i\xe7inde erteledi\u011finiz bir ba\u015flang\u0131c\u0131 yap\u0131n \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck olsun, ama ger\xe7ek olsun. Bir kurs kayd\u0131, bir sayfa yazma, bir aleti elinize alma, bir mesaj g\xf6nderme. K\u0131rlang\u0131\xe7 t\u0131bb\u0131 harekette gizlidir; ilk kanat vuru\u015fu, t\xfcm g\xf6\xe7\xfc m\xfcmk\xfcn k\u0131lar.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Swallow",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["freedom","journey","hope","return"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Swallow is in Anatolia the strongest herald of spring and hope; folk belief holds that the house upon which a swallow settles is blessed with abundance and that its nest must never be disturbed \u2014 to harm one brings misfortune. In Turkish folk poetry, the swallow is the symbol of freedom and the love of homeland; even an exiled poet most longs for the song of the swallow. In Ancient Greece, the swallow was Aphrodite's sacred bird; the herald of love, reunion, and passages. In Egyptian mythology, the swallow is one of the forms taken by the soul of Osiris; this bird, symbolizing rebirth from death, accompanies the sun rising again each morning. In Japanese haiku tradition, the swallow captures most finely the beauty and transience of the moment. In Celtic tradition, migratory birds are carriers of souls; swallows especially are the symbol of connection with the ancestors. The swallow's medicine is the courage to begin again and to release old weights. Its shadow side is never to settle anywhere, to keep moving so as never to belong to a real place.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Swallow tells you the door to a new chapter is opening. That small stirring you feel inside \u2014 that curiosity, that hope, that 'maybe' \u2014 is not trivial. Swallows migrate thousands of kilometers from South Africa to Central Europe and return with astonishing precision to the exact same place \u2014 this requires not only instinct but trust and courage. Perhaps you are waiting for the perfect time to begin something new \u2014 but the swallow does not wait for spring; it brings the spring. Today you can make a small beginning: a step, an attempt, an invitation. Postponing slowly erodes the energy held within that possibility. So how long have you been waiting to begin, and what is this waiting giving you?",guidanceEn:"Today, or this week, make a beginning you have been postponing \u2014 small, but real. A course registration, a page of writing, picking up an instrument, sending a message. The swallow's medicine is hidden in movement; the first wingbeat is what makes the whole migration possible."},{id:"a022",name:"G\xfcvercin",emoji:"\ud83d\udd4a\ufe0f",element:"su",symbolism:["bar\u0131\u015f","sevgi","mesaj","uyum"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Rock_dove_Columba_livia.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"G\xfcvercin, Anadolu'nun en eski tanr\u0131\xe7a imgelerinden biridir; \u0130\u015ftar, Afrodit ve Ven\xfcs'\xfcn kutsal ku\u015fu olarak sevginin, bereketin ve huzurun simgesidir \u2014 bu ba\u011f be\u015f bin y\u0131l\u0131 a\u015fk\u0131n bir ge\xe7mi\u015fe sahiptir. \u0130brahimi geleneklerde g\xfcvercin ilahi mesaj\u0131n ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; Hz. Nuh'a dal\u0131 getiren g\xfcvercin, tufan sonras\u0131nda d\xfcnyan\u0131n yeniden ya\u015fanabilir oldu\u011funu m\xfcjdeler. Hristiyanl\u0131kta Kutsal Ruh'un sembol\xfc olan beyaz g\xfcvercin, vaftiz t\xf6renlerinin ve ruhsal feyzin i\u015faretidir. Hint gelene\u011finde g\xfcvercin Kama'n\u0131n (a\u015fk tanr\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n) kutsal hayvanlar\u0131ndan biridir; \xe7iftle\u015fme ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve sadakat ile \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirilir. Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde g\xfcvercin bar\u0131\u015f\u0131n ve toplumsal uyumun simgesidir. S\xfcmer mitolojisinde \u0130nanna'n\u0131n g\xfcvercinleri sevgi tap\u0131naklar\u0131nda u\xe7ar. G\xfcvercinin t\u0131bb\u0131, \xe7at\u0131\u015fman\u0131n ortas\u0131nda bar\u0131\u015f\u0131 se\xe7me ve affetmenin \xf6zg\xfcrle\u015ftirici g\xfcc\xfcd\xfcr. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise her \xe7at\u0131\u015fmadan ka\xe7mak, bar\u0131\u015f ad\u0131na kendi ger\xe7e\u011fini bast\u0131rmakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"G\xfcvercin bug\xfcn bar\u0131\u015fa davet ediyor \u2014 ama bu, her \u015feyi kabullenmek de\u011fil. Ger\xe7ek bar\u0131\u015f, bir ili\u015fkide, bir durumda ya da kendi i\xe7inde \xe7at\u0131\u015fmay\u0131 g\xf6rmezden gelmek de\u011fil; onu d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrmektir. G\xfcvercinlerin \xe7ift olarak y\u0131llar boyu ayn\u0131 yuva b\xf6lgesine sad\u0131k kald\u0131klar\u0131 bilinir \u2014 bu fedakarl\u0131k de\u011fil, derinlik tercihidir. \u015eu an kimin ya da neyin ile bir gerginlik ya\u015f\u0131yorsun? Bu gerginli\u011fi \xe7\xf6zmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131rken kaybetmekten korktu\u011fun \u015fey ne \u2014 hakkl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 m\u0131, konumunu mu, yoksa ba\u015fka bir \u015feyi mi? Affetmek, hak vermek de\u011fildir; kendini \xf6zg\xfcr k\u0131lmakt\u0131r. Bug\xfcn k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir bar\u0131\u015f ad\u0131m\u0131 atmak nas\u0131l hissettirir?",guidance:"K\xfcsk\xfcn ya da gergin oldu\u011funuz biriyle ileti\u015fime ge\xe7in \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck, ama samimi bir jest yap\u0131n: bir mesaj, bir soru, ya da sadece bir kabul. Bar\u0131\u015f\u0131 in\u015fa etmek bir kez yap\u0131lan b\xfcy\xfck bir hareketten de\u011fil, k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama tutarl\u0131 dokunu\u015flardan olu\u015fur. G\xfcvercin bunu biliyor; siz de biliyordunuz zaten.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Dove",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["peace","love","message","harmony"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Dove is one of Anatolia's most ancient goddess images; as the sacred bird of Ishtar, Aphrodite, and Venus, it is the symbol of love, abundance, and peace \u2014 a bond spanning more than five thousand years. In the Abrahamic traditions, the dove is the bearer of divine messages; the dove bringing the branch to the Prophet Noah heralds that the world is once again habitable after the flood. In Christianity, the white dove, symbol of the Holy Spirit, is the sign of baptism and spiritual grace. In Hindu tradition, the dove is among the sacred animals of Kama, the god of love; identified with mating loyalty and faithfulness. In the African Yoruba tradition, the dove is the symbol of peace and social harmony. In Sumerian mythology, Inanna's doves fly in the temples of love. The dove's medicine is choosing peace in the midst of conflict and the freeing power of forgiveness. Its shadow side is fleeing every conflict, suppressing one's own truth in the name of peace.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Dove invites you to peace \u2014 but this is not the same as accepting everything. True peace is not ignoring the conflict in a relationship, a situation, or within yourself; it is transforming it. Doves are known to remain loyal in pairs to the same nesting territory for years \u2014 this is not self-sacrifice but a choice for depth. With whom or what are you currently in tension? In trying to resolve this tension, what are you afraid of losing \u2014 your rightness, your position, or something else? Forgiving is not granting agreement; it is freeing yourself. How does it feel today to take one small step toward peace?",guidanceEn:"Reach out to someone with whom you are estranged or tense \u2014 make a small but sincere gesture: a message, a question, or simply an acknowledgment. Building peace is made not of one grand action but of small, consistent touches. The dove knows this; you knew it too."},{id:"a023",name:"B\xfclb\xfcl",emoji:"\ud83c\udfb5",element:"hava",symbolism:["sevgi","\u015fiir","hasret","g\xfczellik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Luscinia_megarhynchos_Marek_Szczepanek.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"B\xfclb\xfcl, T\xfcrk Divan edebiyat\u0131n\u0131n ve tasavvuf \u015fiirinin en merkezi imgesidir; g\xfcl ile b\xfclb\xfcl ili\u015fkisi, \xe2\u015f\u0131k ile sevgili, insan ile ilahi aras\u0131ndaki kavu\u015fulamayan ama vazge\xe7ilemeyen \xf6zlemi simgeler. Fuzuli, \u015eeyh Galip ve Yunus Emre'nin \u015fiirlerinde b\xfclb\xfcl, y\xfcre\u011fin sesinini bulmak i\xe7in ac\u0131y\u0131 bile dile getirme cesaretini temsil eder. Haf\u0131z'\u0131n Fars\xe7a \u015fiirinde b\xfclb\xfcl, ilahi hakikatin mecazi a\u015fk\u0131 i\xe7inde \u015fark\u0131 s\xf6yleyen ariftir. \u0130ran gelene\u011finde 'b\xfclb\xfcl-i g\xfcl' imgesi, ruhun yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015ftan gelen \xf6zlemini anlat\u0131r. \xc7in gelene\u011finde b\xfclb\xfcl, aldat\u0131c\u0131 g\xfczellikle asl\u0131nda saf sesin kar\u015f\u0131la\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131 anlatan masallarda yer al\u0131r; Hans Christian Andersen'in b\xfclb\xfcl hikayesi bu simgeyi Do\u011fu'dan Bat\u0131'ya ta\u015f\u0131m\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. Kelt gelene\u011finde ard\u0131\xe7 ku\u015flar\u0131 ve b\xfclb\xfcllere benzer \xf6ten ku\u015flar, \xf6teki d\xfcnyadan gelen m\xfczi\u011fi temsil eder. B\xfclb\xfcl\xfcn t\u0131bb\u0131, ac\u0131y\u0131 g\xfczelli\u011fe d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrebilme ve i\xe7sel sesi d\u0131\u015fa ta\u015f\u0131ma kapasitesidir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise o kadar derin \xf6zlemde ya\u015famak ki \u015fimdiki an\u0131n ger\xe7ek g\xfczelli\u011fini ka\xe7\u0131rmakt\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"B\xfclb\xfcl bug\xfcn sana s\xf6ylemedi\u011fin \u015feyi s\xf6ylemeni istiyor. \u0130\xe7inde biriken duygu, d\xfc\u015f\xfcnce, s\xf6z \u2014 onu susturmak onu \xe7\xf6zm\xfcyor, aksine o enerji i\xe7inde birikmeye devam ediyor. B\xfclb\xfcl karanl\u0131k gecelerde bile \u015fark\u0131 s\xf6yler; onun sesi, duyulsun ya da duyulmas\u0131n, asla i\xe7erde tutulmaz. Hangi s\xf6z\xfc hapsediyorsun? Kime s\xf6ylemen gereken ama erteledi\u011fin ne var? Bir mektup bile olsa, g\xf6nderilmeyecek bir mektup bile, s\xf6ylenmemi\u015f olan\u0131 dile getirmenin arac\u0131 olabilir. \u0130fade olmadan bir duygu donar; ifadeyle d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr. Bug\xfcn bir kelime, bir \u015fark\u0131, bir \xe7izim \u2014 hangi bi\xe7imiyle olursa olsun, sesini ver.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn s\xf6ylemedi\u011finiz bir \u015feyi yaz\u0131n \u2014 g\xf6nderebilece\u011finiz ya da g\xf6nderemeyece\u011finiz bir mektup olarak. Adresleyin, duyguyu dile getirin, sonunu ba\u011flay\u0131n. G\xf6ndermek zorunda de\u011filsiniz; ama yazmak, i\xe7inizdeki sesin \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc kazanmas\u0131d\u0131r. B\xfclb\xfcl bu y\xfczden gecenin ortas\u0131nda bile \u015fark\u0131 s\xf6yler: \xe7\xfcnk\xfc tutmak, onu \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcr.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Nightingale",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["love","poetry","longing","beauty"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Nightingale is the central image of Turkish Divan literature and Sufi poetry; the relationship between the rose and the nightingale symbolizes the unreachable yet inescapable longing between lover and beloved, between human and divine. In the poetry of Fuzuli, Sheikh Galip, and Yunus Emre, the nightingale represents the courage even to give voice to pain in order to find the heart's voice. In Hafez's Persian poetry, the nightingale is the gnostic who sings of divine truth within the metaphor of love. In Persian tradition, the image of the 'nightingale of the rose' tells of the soul's longing from its creation. In Chinese tradition, the nightingale features in tales of pure song meeting deceptive beauty; Hans Christian Andersen's nightingale story carried this symbol from East to West. In Celtic tradition, thrushes and birds whose song resembles the nightingale's represent music from the otherworld. The nightingale's medicine is the capacity to turn pain into beauty and to carry the inner voice outward. Its shadow side is to live so deeply in longing that one misses the real beauty of the present moment.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Nightingale wants you to say what you have not said. The feeling, thought, or word accumulating within you \u2014 silencing it does not resolve it; that energy keeps gathering inside. The nightingale sings even on the darkest nights; its voice, whether heard or not, is never kept inside. What word are you imprisoning? What is it that you should say to someone but keep postponing? Even a letter \u2014 even an unsent letter \u2014 can be a means of voicing what has gone unsaid. Without expression, a feeling freezes; with expression, it transforms. Today, a word, a song, a drawing \u2014 in whatever form, give your voice.",guidanceEn:"Today, write down something you have not said \u2014 as a letter you may or may not send. Address it, name the feeling, finish it. You do not have to send it; but writing it is your inner voice claiming its freedom. This is why the nightingale sings even in the middle of the night: because holding it in would kill it."},{id:"a024",name:"Kaplan",emoji:"\ud83d\udc2f",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["g\xfc\xe7","tutku","cesaret","kontrol"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Tiger_in_Ranthambhore.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kaplan, eski T\xfcrk destanlar\u0131nda pars ve kaplan motiflerinin i\xe7 i\xe7e ge\xe7ti\u011fi kutsal bir sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 imgesidir; T\xfcrk boylar\u0131n\u0131n sava\u015f sancaklar\u0131nda ve destanlarda kaplan benzetmeleri s\u0131k\xe7a yer al\u0131r. Hindu panteonunda Durga, kaplan s\u0131rt\u0131nda sava\u015fa kat\u0131lan tanr\u0131\xe7ad\u0131r \u2014 bu g\xfc\xe7, di\u015fil enerjinin d\xfczensizli\u011fe kar\u015f\u0131 bilin\xe7li ve kontroll\xfc sava\u015f\u0131n\u0131 simgeler. \xc7in astrolojisinde kaplan, koruyucu ve g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir i\u015farettir; Asya k\xfclt\xfcrlerinde d\xf6rt \xf6nemli efsanevi hayvan\u0131n beyaz kaplan\u0131, bat\u0131 y\xf6n\xfcn\xfcn ve sonbahar\u0131n h\xe2kimidir. Aztek gelene\u011finde Tepeyollotl, da\u011f\u0131n kalbi olan kaplan tanr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; karanl\u0131\u011f\u0131n, yank\u0131n\u0131n ve i\xe7sel g\xfc\xe7lerin simgesidir. \u015einto gelene\u011finde kaplan, k\xf6t\xfc ruhlar\u0131 ve hastal\u0131klar\u0131 defeden koruyucu hayvan olarak tap\u0131nak kap\u0131lar\u0131nda tasvir edilir. Kuzey Amerika yerli gelene\u011finde kaplan ve benzer b\xfcy\xfck kediler, sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 ruhun ve kontrol\xfcll\xfc g\xfcc\xfcn \xf6\u011fretmenidir. Kaplan\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131 tutkuyu kontroll\xfc bir g\xfcce d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise bu g\xfcc\xfcn kendini de \xe7evresini de yakacak kontrols\xfcz bir enerjiye d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmesidir.",dailyMessage:"Kaplan bug\xfcn i\xe7indeki tutkuyu uyand\u0131r\u0131yor \u2014 ama bu uyar\u0131 ayn\u0131 zamanda bir kontrol sorusu. Kaplan avland\u0131\u011f\u0131nda biyolojik olarak inan\u0131lmaz bir odak ve sab\u0131r g\xf6sterir; saatlerce bekler, an\u0131 \xf6l\xe7er, sonra hareket eder \u2014 ama bu hareket kontrols\xfcz de\u011fil, tam tersine m\xfckemmel zamanl\u0131d\u0131r. Sen hangi tutku ya da enerjiyi ta\u015f\u0131yorsun \u015fu an \u2014 \xf6fke, h\u0131rs, sevgi, heyecan? Bu enerji seni ta\u015f\u0131yabilir ya da yakabilir; fark, y\xf6nde ve bilincinde. Bast\u0131rma onu, \xe7\xfcnk\xfc bast\u0131r\u0131lan enerji bilin\xe7sizce patlar. Ama b\u0131rak o enerji sana hizmet etsin, etraf\u0131n\u0131 tahrip etmesin. Bug\xfcn bu g\xfc\xe7l\xfc hissi bir amaca nas\u0131l ba\u011flars\u0131n?",guidance:"Yo\u011fun bir duygu ya da enerji hissediyorsan\u0131z \u2014 \xf6fke, tutku, hayal k\u0131r\u0131kl\u0131\u011f\u0131 \u2014 onu fiziksel bir kanala y\xf6nlendirin: egzersiz, dans, yazma ya da yarat\u0131c\u0131 bir proje. Bu, duyguyu bast\u0131rmak de\u011fil, onu d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrmektir. Kaplan enerjisi bo\u015fta b\u0131rak\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda kendini da\u011f\u0131t\u0131r; y\xf6nlendirildi\u011finde en b\xfcy\xfck ba\u015far\u0131lar\u0131n itici g\xfcc\xfc olur.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Tiger",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["strength","passion","courage","control"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the old Turkic epics, the Tiger is a sacred warrior image in which leopard and tiger motifs are interwoven; tiger comparisons appear often on the war banners and in the epics of Turkic peoples. In the Hindu pantheon, Durga is the goddess who rides into battle on the back of a tiger \u2014 this power symbolizes the feminine energy's conscious, controlled war against disorder. In Chinese astrology, the tiger is a protective and powerful sign; among the four important mythical animals of Asian cultures, the White Tiger is the master of the west and of autumn. In Aztec tradition, Tepeyollotl, the tiger god, is the heart of the mountain; the symbol of darkness, echo, and inner forces. In the Shinto tradition, the tiger is depicted at temple gates as a protector animal that wards off evil spirits and disease. In the Native American tradition, the tiger and similar great cats are the teachers of the warrior spirit and controlled power. The tiger's medicine is to turn passion into controlled power. Its shadow side is that this power becomes uncontrolled energy that burns the self and its surroundings alike.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Tiger awakens the passion within you \u2014 but this awakening is also a question of control. When hunting, the tiger biologically shows incredible focus and patience; it waits for hours, measures the moment, then moves \u2014 but this movement is not uncontrolled; on the contrary, it is perfectly timed. What passion or energy are you carrying right now \u2014 anger, ambition, love, excitement? This energy can carry you or it can burn you; the difference lies in direction and in awareness. Do not suppress it, because suppressed energy explodes unconsciously. But let this energy serve you, not devastate your surroundings. Today, how can you bind this powerful feeling to a purpose?",guidanceEn:"If you are feeling an intense emotion or energy \u2014 anger, passion, disappointment \u2014 channel it into a physical outlet: exercise, dance, writing, or a creative project. This is not suppressing the feeling but transforming it. Tiger energy, left idle, scatters itself; directed, it becomes the driving force of the greatest accomplishments."},{id:"a025",name:"K\xf6pek",emoji:"\ud83d\udc15",element:"toprak",symbolism:["sadakat","koruma","sevgi","g\xfcven"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/YellowLabradorLooking_new.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"K\xf6pek, insanl\u0131\u011f\u0131n en eski yol arkada\u015f\u0131 olarak Anadolu'da \xe7oban\u0131n ve evin en sad\u0131k koruyucusudur; \xc7oban k\xf6pe\u011fi gelene\u011fi Orta Asya'dan Anadolu'ya uzanan bir s\xfcreklilik ta\u015f\u0131r. Antik Yunan'da Hekate'nin kutsal hayvan\u0131 olan k\xf6pek, s\u0131n\u0131r kap\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131n ve ge\xe7i\u015f rit\xfcellerinin bek\xe7isidir. M\u0131s\u0131r'da Anubis, \xe7akal-k\xf6pek ba\u015fl\u0131 tanr\u0131 olarak \xf6l\xfclerin ruhlar\u0131n\u0131 \xf6teki d\xfcnyaya g\xfcvenle ta\u015f\u0131r; sadakatin ve rehberli\u011fin en eski tanr\u0131sal bi\xe7imidir. Aztek gelene\u011finde Xolotl, \xe7\u0131plak k\xf6pek tanr\u0131s\u0131 olarak ruhlar\u0131 \xf6l\xfcm yolculu\u011funda e\u015flik eder ve \xf6teki d\xfcnyaya g\xfcvenle ula\u015ft\u0131r\u0131r. Kelt gelene\u011finde k\xf6pekler iyile\u015fme ve koruma g\xfc\xe7leriyle bilinir; su kaynaklar\u0131n\u0131n yan\u0131ndaki tap\u0131naklarda k\xf6pek fig\xfcrinleri bulunmu\u015ftur. \u0130slami gelenekte Hz. Ashab-\u0131 Kehf'in k\xf6pe\u011fi, sadakatin ve ilahi koruma alt\u0131nda uyku halinin simgesi olarak kutsalla\u015fm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. K\xf6pe\u011fin t\u0131bb\u0131 ko\u015fulsuz ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131k ve ger\xe7ek g\xfcven in\u015fas\u0131d\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc ise s\u0131n\u0131r tan\u0131maks\u0131z\u0131n herkese boyun e\u011fmek, s\xfcr\xfc i\xe7inde kendi sesini b\xfct\xfcn\xfcyle kaybetmektir.",dailyMessage:"K\xf6pek bug\xfcn sana g\xfcvenin ne kadar nadir ve de\u011ferli bir \u015fey oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. K\xf6pekler sizi sabah uyand\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131zda sanki aylar ge\xe7mi\u015f gibi kar\u015f\u0131lar \u2014 bu abart\u0131 de\u011fil, tam varl\u0131k halidir; ge\xe7mi\u015f k\u0131rg\u0131nl\u0131klar\u0131, gelecek kayg\u0131lar\u0131 olmadan tam \u015fu an sevinir ve ba\u011flan\u0131r. Sen kim i\xe7in bu kadar tam varolusun? Kim sana g\xfcveniyor ve sen o ki\u015fiye ger\xe7ekten ne kadar g\xfcvenilirsin \u2014 s\xf6ylediklerinde mi, duygusal varl\u0131\u011f\u0131nda m\u0131? G\xfcvenilirlik b\xfcy\xfck jestlerle de\u011fil, k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama tutarl\u0131 ad\u0131mlarla in\u015fa edilir: s\xf6z\xfcn\xfc tutmak, orada olmak, haz\u0131r bulunmak. Bug\xfcn kimin yan\u0131nda durman gerekiyor \u2014 fiziksel ya da duygusal olarak? Bir mesaj, bir ziyaret, sadece 'buraday\u0131m' demek yeterli olabilir.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn g\xfcvendi\u011finiz ya da g\xfcvenilmesini istedi\u011finiz bir ki\u015fiye somut, tutarl\u0131 bir jest yap\u0131n: verdi\u011finiz bir s\xf6z\xfc tutun, bir iste\u011fine cevap verin ya da sadece 'seni d\xfc\u015f\xfcnd\xfcm' deyin. K\xf6pe\u011fin bilgeli\u011fi \u015fimdi ve burada olmakt\u0131r; bu an ge\xe7ince o g\xfcven f\u0131rsat\u0131 da ge\xe7er. G\xfcven, g\xfcnl\xfck k\xfc\xe7\xfck do\u011frularla in\u015fa edilir.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Dog",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["loyalty","protection","love","trust"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Dog, humanity's oldest companion, is in Anatolia the most loyal guardian of the shepherd and the home; the tradition of the shepherd's dog carries an unbroken continuity from Central Asia to Anatolia. In Ancient Greece, the dog, sacred animal of Hecate, is the keeper of threshold gates and passage rituals. In Egypt, Anubis, the jackal-headed god, carries the souls of the dead safely to the other world; the most ancient divine form of loyalty and guidance. In the Aztec tradition, Xolotl, the hairless dog god, accompanies souls on the death journey and brings them safely to the otherworld. In Celtic tradition, dogs are known for their powers of healing and protection; dog figurines have been found in temples beside water sources. In the Islamic tradition, the dog of the People of the Cave (Ashab al-Kahf) has been sanctified as the symbol of loyalty and of sleep under divine protection. The dog's medicine is unconditional devotion and the building of true trust. Its shadow side is to submit to everyone without keeping any boundary, losing one's voice entirely within the pack.",dailyMessageEn:"Today the Dog reminds you how rare and precious a thing trust is. Dogs greet you in the morning as if months had passed \u2014 this is not exaggeration but the state of full presence; they rejoice and bond in the very now, without past grievances or future worries. For whom are you this fully present? Who trusts you, and how trustworthy are you really to that person \u2014 in what you say, or in your emotional presence? Trustworthiness is built not by grand gestures but by small, consistent steps: keeping your word, being there, being available. By whose side do you need to stand today \u2014 physically or emotionally? A message, a visit, simply saying 'I am here' may be enough.",guidanceEn:"Today, make a concrete, consistent gesture to someone you trust or whose trust you want to earn: keep a promise you have given, respond to a request of theirs, or simply say 'I was thinking of you.' The dog's wisdom is to be here and now; once this moment passes, so does the opportunity for trust. Trust is built through small, daily acts of truth."},{id:"a026",name:"\xc7ita",emoji:"\ud83d\udc3e",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["h\u0131z","odak","f\u0131rsat","kararl\u0131l\u0131k"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Gepard_Kruger.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"\xc7ita, Osmanl\u0131 saraylar\u0131nda sultanlar\u0131n av orta\u011f\u0131yd\u0131; e\u011fitilmi\u015f \xe7ita g\xf6zleri ba\u011fl\u0131 at \xfczerinde ta\u015f\u0131n\u0131r, av\u0131n tam an\u0131nda serbest b\u0131rak\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131 \u2014 bu bir g\xfcven ve zamanlama sanat\u0131yd\u0131. Anadolu k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde \xe7ita gibi h\u0131zl\u0131 hareket etmek erdemin de\u011fil, f\u0131rsat\u0131 koklayan bilgeli\u011fin g\xf6stergesi say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Afrika gelene\u011finde \xe7ita, g\xfcne\u015fin \xe7ocu\u011fu ve topra\u011f\u0131n en h\u0131zl\u0131 ruhudur; Maasai sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131 \xe7ita postunu ta\u015f\u0131yarak onun odak g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc bedenlerine \xe7ekerdi. Aztek mitolojisinde h\u0131zla hareket eden g\xfcne\u015f \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n yery\xfcz\xfcndeki temsilcisi olan \xe7ita, an\u0131n tanr\u0131s\u0131yla ili\u015fkilendirilirdi. Hindu gelene\u011finde \xe7ita imgesi, dharman\u0131n yerine getirilmesinde teredd\xfcts\xfcz hareketle ba\u011flant\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 do\u011fru eylem, do\u011fru anda, tek ad\u0131mda. \xc7itan\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o kadar h\u0131zl\u0131 ko\u015far ki uzun mesafelerde t\xfckenebilir; kapasitesinin s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6rmeden hep daha fazlas\u0131na uzanmak yorgunluktan de\u011fil, yan\u0131lsamadan kaynaklan\u0131r.",dailyMessage:"\xc7ita bug\xfcn sana \u015funu soruyor: Neyi bekliyorsun, ger\xe7ekten? \xc7ita d\xfcnyan\u0131n en h\u0131zl\u0131 kara hayvan\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 ama bu h\u0131z rastgele de\u011fil, sab\u0131rla se\xe7ilmi\u015f tek bir ana adam\u0131\u015f odaklanman\u0131n \xfcr\xfcn\xfcd\xfcr; av\u0131n\u0131 dakikalarca izler, sonra y\xfcz metre mesafede s\u0131f\u0131r teredd\xfctle harekete ge\xe7er. Sen de belki \xe7ok uzun s\xfcredir izliyorsun. Analiz bitti, harita \xe7izildi, risk hesapland\u0131 \u2014 \u015fimdi i\xe7inde hangi ses h\xe2l\xe2 'biraz daha bekle' diyor? Ve o ses ger\xe7ekten sa\u011fduyudan m\u0131, yoksa korkudan m\u0131 geliyor? \xc7ita bir f\u0131rsat\u0131 ka\xe7\u0131r\u0131rsa ikinci bir \u015fans aramaz; dinlenir, yeniden odaklan\u0131r ve ba\u015fka bir an i\xe7in haz\u0131r olur. Bug\xfcn ka\xe7mas\u0131na izin verme. \u015eu an harekete ge\xe7meni gerektiren o tek \u015fey nedir \u2014 onu yap, sadece onu.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn i\xe7inde erteledi\u011fin ama 'biliyorum ne yapmam gerekti\u011fini' dedi\u011fin bir eylem se\xe7. Bunu be\u015f dakika i\xe7inde ba\u015flat \u2014 m\xfckemmel de\u011fil, sadece ba\u015fla. \xc7itan\u0131n g\xfcc\xfc m\xfckemmel ko\u015fu\u015fta de\u011fil, teredd\xfcts\xfcz ilk ad\u0131mdad\u0131r; o ilk ad\u0131m at\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda momentum seni ta\u015f\u0131r.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Cheetah",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["speed","focus","opportunity","decisiveness"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The cheetah was the hunting companion of Ottoman sultans; trained cheetahs were carried blindfolded on horseback and released at the precise moment of pursuit \u2014 an art of trust and timing. In Anatolian culture, moving as swiftly as a cheetah was considered not a sign of virtue but of a wisdom that scents opportunity. In African tradition, the cheetah is the child of the sun and the swiftest spirit of the earth; Maasai warriors wore cheetah pelts to draw its focused power into their bodies. In Aztec mythology, the cheetah was associated with the deity of the present moment, representing swift-moving sunlight upon the earth. In Hindu tradition, the cheetah's image is linked to acting without hesitation in the fulfillment of dharma \u2014 right action, at the right moment, in a single step. The shadow side of the cheetah: it runs so fast it can exhaust itself over long distances; reaching always for more without seeing the limit of one's capacity arises not from fatigue but from illusion.",dailyMessageEn:"Cheetah asks you today: What are you really waiting for? The cheetah is the fastest land animal in the world \u2014 but this speed is not random; it is the fruit of focus devoted to a single moment, patiently chosen. It watches its prey for minutes, then moves with zero hesitation from a hundred meters away. Perhaps you have been watching too long as well. The analysis is done, the map is drawn, the risk is calculated \u2014 what voice within still whispers 'wait a little longer'? And does that voice come from true discernment, or from fear? If a cheetah misses an opportunity, it does not chase a second chance; it rests, refocuses, and prepares for another moment. Do not let this one slip away. What is the one thing that needs your action right now \u2014 do that, only that.",guidanceEn:"Choose one action you have been postponing today but about which you can say, 'I know what I need to do.' Begin it within five minutes \u2014 not perfectly, just begin. The cheetah's power lies not in flawless running but in the first step taken without hesitation; once that step is made, momentum carries you."},{id:"a027",name:"Ejderha",emoji:"\ud83d\udc09",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","g\xfc\xe7","ate\u015f","mistisizm"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Chinese_dragon.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Orta Asya T\xfcrk ve Mo\u011fol kozmolojisinde ejderha, yerin ve g\xf6\u011f\xfcn aras\u0131nda ya\u015fayan b\xfcy\xfck g\xfc\xe7 olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr; Yer-Su ruhlar\u0131n\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfcs\xfc ejderhaya benzer bi\xe7imde betimlenir ve \u015famanlar onunla m\xfczakere ederek ya\u011fmur, bereket ve zafer dilerdi. Anadolu halk anlat\u0131s\u0131nda y\u0131lan-ejder s\u0131kl\u0131kla su kaynaklar\u0131n\u0131 korur; k\xf6y\xfcn suyuna sahip \xe7\u0131kan bu yarat\u0131k k\xf6t\xfc de\u011fil, kadim bir ahde sad\u0131k koruyucudur. \xc7in mitolojisinde ejderha y\u0131k\u0131c\u0131 de\u011fil, d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcc\xfcd\xfcr \u2014 g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcn\xfcn be\u015f ejderhas\u0131 be\u015f y\xf6n\xfc y\xf6netir ve imparator ejderhan\u0131n torunuydu; bu y\xfczden g\xfcc\xfcn ve bilgeli\u011fin en y\xfcce sembol\xfcd\xfcr. Kelt gelene\u011finde ise ejder, ley hatlar\u0131n\u0131n \u2014 yery\xfcz\xfcn\xfcn enerji damarlar\u0131n\u0131n \u2014 tam \xfczerinde ya\u015far ve bu noktalar\u0131 korur; onunla uyum i\xe7inde olmak, yerin gizli g\xfcc\xfcne eri\u015fmek demektir. Hindu mitolojisinde Vritra adl\u0131 y\u0131lan-ejder, sular\u0131n \xf6n\xfcn\xfc t\u0131kayarak kurakl\u0131\u011fa sebep olur; \u0130ndra onu \xf6ld\xfcrerek nehirleri serbest b\u0131rak\u0131r \u2014 bast\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131\u015f g\xfcc\xfcn serbest b\u0131rak\u0131lmas\u0131n\u0131n kozmik metaforu. Ejderhan\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: i\xe7indeki g\xfcc\xfc o kadar bast\u0131rmak ki ate\u015f i\xe7e d\xf6ner ve seni yakar.",dailyMessage:"Ejderha bug\xfcn sana \u015funu s\xf6yl\xfcyor: Uzun s\xfcredir benden \xe7ok daha k\xfc\xe7\xfck g\xf6r\xfcnmeyi se\xe7iyorsun. \u0130\xe7inde ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n o ate\u015f \u2014 o tutku, o vizyon, o \xf6fke bile \u2014 ger\xe7ek. Onu '\xe7ok b\xfcy\xfck', '\xe7ok iddial\u0131', 'kabul g\xf6rmez' diye s\xf6n\xfcmleyip durma. \u015eu an hayat\u0131nda ger\xe7ek potansiyelini gizledi\u011fin bir alan var m\u0131? Kendine sorman gereken soru \u015fu: Bu b\xfcy\xfckl\xfc\u011f\xfc kim i\xe7in sakl\u0131yorum? Ejderhalar da\u011flar\u0131n ard\u0131nda ya\u015far \xe7\xfcnk\xfc k\xfc\xe7\xfck mek\xe2nlara s\u0131\u011fmazlar \u2014 belki sen de bulundu\u011fun alan\u0131 b\xfcy\xfctmen gerekiyor. Ate\u015fini yakarken ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131 yakmak zorunda de\u011filsin; g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olmak ile zulmetmek aras\u0131nda da\u011flar kadar fark var. Bug\xfcn o ate\u015fi d\xfcnyaya d\xfcr\xfcst\xe7e g\xf6ster.",guidance:"Bir ka\u011f\u0131da 'ger\xe7ekten istedi\u011fim ama \xe7ok b\xfcy\xfck diye bast\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131m \u015fey' diye ba\u015flayan bir c\xfcmle yaz ve sonunu tamamla \u2014 sans\xfcrs\xfcz, kimseye g\xf6stermeden. Bu ate\u015fe isim koymak, onu kontrol etmenin ilk ad\u0131m\u0131d\u0131r. Sonra o ka\u011f\u0131d\u0131 bir hafta boyunca yan\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Dragon",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["transformation","power","fire","mysticism"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Central Asian Turkic and Mongolian cosmology, the dragon is seen as the great power dwelling between earth and sky; the most potent of the Yer-Su spirits is depicted in dragon-like form, and shamans negotiated with it for rain, abundance, and victory. In Anatolian folk narrative, the serpent-dragon often guards water sources; this creature protecting the village's water is not evil but an ancient guardian faithful to a primordial covenant. In Chinese mythology, the dragon is not destructive but transformative \u2014 the five dragons of the heavens govern the five directions, and the emperor was the dragon's descendant; thus it is the supreme symbol of power and wisdom. In Celtic tradition, the dragon dwells directly upon the ley lines \u2014 the energy veins of the earth \u2014 and guards these points; to be in harmony with it is to access the earth's hidden power. In Hindu mythology, the serpent-dragon Vritra blocks the waters and causes drought; Indra slays it to release the rivers \u2014 a cosmic metaphor for the liberation of suppressed power. The shadow side of the dragon: suppressing the power within so deeply that the fire turns inward and burns you.",dailyMessageEn:"Dragon tells you today: For too long you have chosen to appear smaller than you are. The fire you carry within \u2014 that passion, that vision, even that anger \u2014 is real. Do not keep dimming it with labels like 'too big,' 'too ambitious,' 'unacceptable.' Is there an area in your life right now where you are hiding your true potential? The question to ask yourself is this: For whom am I saving this greatness? Dragons dwell beyond the mountains because they do not fit in small spaces \u2014 perhaps you too need to expand the space you inhabit. To burn your fire, you need not burn another; there is a mountain's worth of difference between being powerful and being cruel. Today, show that fire honestly to the world.",guidanceEn:"On a piece of paper, write a sentence beginning 'What I truly want but have suppressed because it feels too big...' and complete it \u2014 uncensored, for no one's eyes but yours. Naming this fire is the first step in mastering it. Then carry that paper with you for a week."},{id:"a028",name:"Karakulak",emoji:"\ud83d\udc31",element:"hava",symbolism:["\xe7eviklik","gizem","ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131zl\u0131k","sezgi"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Caracal.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Karakulak, Anadolu ve Orta Asya bozk\u0131rlar\u0131nda h\xfck\xfcmdarlara adanm\u0131\u015f av hayvanlar\u0131ndan biri olarak bilinir; y\xfcksek s\u0131\xe7rama g\xfcc\xfc ve benzersiz h\u0131z\u0131yla sahadaki en \xe7evik avc\u0131 say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131, padi\u015fah \xe7ad\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 s\xfcsleyen motiflerde s\u0131kl\u0131kla yer al\u0131rd\u0131. \u015eamanist gelenekte karakulak kulaklar\u0131 \u2014 o uzun siyah p\xfcsk\xfcll\xfc kulaklar \u2014 ruhlar\u0131n f\u0131s\u0131lt\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 yakalayan antenler olarak yorumlan\u0131r; \u015faman s\u0131radan insan\u0131n duyamad\u0131\u011f\u0131 frekanslara bu kulaklar arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla eri\u015fir. M\u0131s\u0131r mitolojisinde kedi ailesinin t\xfcm \xfcyeleri \u0130sis ve Bastet ile ba\u011flant\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r; karakula\u011f\u0131n ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve gece g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfc, bilin\xe7alt\u0131ndan gelen sezginin sembolleri olarak okunur. Kelt gelene\u011finde gece avc\u0131lar\u0131, \xd6teki D\xfcnya ile s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n incelmesi s\u0131ras\u0131nda g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr h\xe2le gelir \u2014 karakulak gibi sessiz ve g\xf6r\xfcnmez av, ruhsal \xe2lemle \xf6rt\xfc\u015fen bir bilin\xe7 h\xe2linin metaforudur. Afrika savanas\u0131nda karakulak, g\xf6zlendi\u011fini hi\xe7 hissettirmeden g\xf6zlemler; bu nitelik Bat\u0131 Afrika bilgeli\u011finde 'konu\u015fmadan anlamak' olarak kutsan\u0131r. Karakula\u011f\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o denli ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131z olmak ki k\xf6pr\xfcler kuramamak, her ba\u011f\u0131 tehdit olarak hissetmek.",dailyMessage:"Karakulak bug\xfcn sana sessizli\u011fin i\xe7indeki g\xfcc\xfc hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Bu hayvan av\u0131n\u0131 yakalamadan \xf6nce saatlerce hi\xe7 k\u0131p\u0131rdamaz; kulaklar\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131lt\u0131y\u0131, titre\u015fimi, r\xfczg\xe2r\u0131n i\xe7indeki mesaj\u0131 okur \u2014 sonra hareket eder. Sen ne zaman son kez ger\xe7ekten dinledin? Yaln\u0131zca s\xf6yleneni de\u011fil, s\xf6ylenmeyeni? Etraf\u0131ndaki her \u015feyi a\xe7\u0131klamak, her d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceni payla\u015fmak, her bo\u015flu\u011fu doldurmak zorunda de\u011filsin. Susman\u0131n kendisi bir bilgi bi\xe7imidir. Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131nda sana bir \u015fey f\u0131s\u0131ldayan ama g\xfcr\xfclt\xfcn\xfcn alt\u0131nda kalan bir ses var m\u0131? Karakulak gibi ol: g\xf6zlemle, hisset, bekle \u2014 sonra tek ve kesin bir hamleyle hareket et. Ger\xe7ek sezgi sessizli\u011fin i\xe7inde do\u011far.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn en az yirmi dakika kendinle sessiz kal \u2014 telefon yok, m\xfczik yok, konu\u015fma yok. Sadece g\xf6zlemle: bedeninde ne hissediyorsun, zihninde hangi d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceler kendili\u011finden y\xfczeliyor? Karakulak meditasyonu budur: duymak i\xe7in \xf6nce susturmak.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Caracal",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["agility","mystery","independence","intuition"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The caracal is known as one of the hunting animals dedicated to rulers across the Anatolian and Central Asian steppes; with its remarkable leaping power and unmatched speed, it was considered the most agile hunter in the field, often featured in motifs adorning the sultan's tents. In shamanic tradition, the caracal's ears \u2014 those long, black-tufted ears \u2014 are interpreted as antennae catching the whispers of spirits; the shaman accesses frequencies inaudible to ordinary humans through these ears. In Egyptian mythology, all members of the feline family are linked to Isis and Bastet; the caracal's independence and night vision are read as symbols of intuition arising from the unconscious. In Celtic tradition, night hunters become visible during the thinning of the veil between worlds \u2014 silent and unseen prey like the caracal is a metaphor for a state of consciousness overlapping with the spirit realm. In the African savanna, the caracal observes without ever letting itself be felt as observer; this quality is honored in West African wisdom as 'understanding without speaking.' The shadow side of the caracal: being so independent that one cannot build bridges, sensing every bond as a threat.",dailyMessageEn:"Caracal reminds you today of the power within silence. This animal does not move for hours before catching its prey; its ears read the whisper, the vibration, the message within the wind \u2014 then it moves. When did you last truly listen? Not only to what is said, but to what goes unsaid? You do not have to explain everything around you, share every thought, fill every silence. Silence itself is a form of knowing. Today, is there a voice whispering something to you in your life, but buried beneath the noise? Be like the caracal: observe, feel, wait \u2014 then move with a single, decisive stroke. True intuition is born within silence.",guidanceEn:"Spend at least twenty minutes alone with yourself today in silence \u2014 no phone, no music, no conversation. Just observe: what do you feel in your body, what thoughts surface on their own? This is caracal meditation: to hear, one must first silence."},{id:"a029",name:"Maral",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8c",element:"toprak",symbolism:["y\xfccelik","g\xfczellik","onur","bolluk"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Cervus_elaphus_maral.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Maral, T\xfcrk ve Altay mitolojisinin en kutsal hayvanlar\u0131ndan biridir; Geyik Ana ya da Maral Ana olarak bilinen bu varl\u0131k, \u015faman\u0131n yolculu\u011funda rehber ruh olarak kar\u015f\u0131s\u0131na \xe7\u0131kar ve onu g\xf6ksel \xe2leme ta\u015f\u0131r. Orta Asya hal\u0131lar\u0131nda, Paz\u0131r\u0131k kurganlar\u0131nda ve kaya resimlerinde maral motifi, ruhun y\xfckselmesini ve kutsal g\xfczelli\u011fi simgeler. Anadolu T\xfcrk halk \u015fiirinde maral, ula\u015f\u0131lamaz sevgiliyle \xf6zde\u015fle\u015fir; Divan \u015fiirinde 'ahuyu and\u0131r\u0131r y\xfcr\xfcy\xfc\u015f\xfcn' dizesi g\xfczelli\u011fi ve vakar\u0131 birlikte anlat\u0131r. Kelt mitolojisinde Cernunnos'un kutsal geyi\u011fi orman\u0131n efendisi ve d\xf6ng\xfcn\xfcn koruyucusudur \u2014 boynuzlar\u0131n her y\u0131l d\xfc\u015f\xfcp yeniden bitmesi, \xf6l\xfcm ve yeniden do\u011fumun kesintisiz d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc temsil eder. Kuzey Amerika yerlilerinde geyik, \u015fefkatin ve nazik uyumun \xf6\u011fretmenidir; sava\u015f\xe7\u0131n\u0131n y\xfcre\u011fine \u015fefkat katan ruh hayvan\u0131 olarak se\xe7ilir. Norse mitolojisinde Yggdrasil'in dallar\u0131nda ya\u015fayan d\xf6rt kutsal geyik, zaman\u0131n d\xf6rt boyutunu otlatarak t\xfcketir \u2014 bu imgede geyik zaman\u0131n kendisini ta\u015f\u0131r. Maral\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: y\xfcceli\u011fe o kadar odaklanmak ki yere basmay\u0131 unutmak, hayalperestli\u011fin ger\xe7eklikten kopmas\u0131.",dailyMessage:"Maral bug\xfcn sana y\xfcksekli\u011fi hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor \u2014 ama ger\xe7ek y\xfckseklik ne demek? Bu hayvan da\u011flarda ya\u015far; hem y\xfcksekte hem de zemindedir, hem g\xf6rkemliyken hem de tehlikeyi anl\u0131k sezer. 'Ger\xe7ek\xe7i ol' diyen sesler bazen ba\u015fkalar\u0131n\u0131n kendi s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 sana giydirme giri\u015fimidir \u2014 evrenin s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131 de\u011fil. Bug\xfcn \u015funu sor kendine: En \xe7ok k\u0131s\u0131tlamay\u0131 nereden al\u0131yorum, d\xfcnyadan m\u0131 yoksa kendi kafamdan m\u0131? Maral boynuzlar\u0131 her y\u0131l d\xf6k\xfcl\xfcr ve yeniden b\xfcy\xfcr \u2014 kaybetti\u011fini sand\u0131\u011f\u0131n g\xfc\xe7 d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfcn bir par\xe7as\u0131, kal\u0131c\u0131 bir son de\u011fil. Hayalin k\xfc\xe7\xfck geliyorsa, b\xfcy\xfctmenin zaman\u0131 gelmi\u015f demektir. Y\u0131ld\u0131zlara uzanmak seni yerden koparmaz; seni seni yapan k\xf6klerinden enerji alarak yukar\u0131ya ula\u015fmakt\u0131r as\u0131l.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn bir ka\u011f\u0131da 'be\u015f y\u0131l i\xe7inde nas\u0131l bir hayat istiyorum' sorusunu cevapla \u2014 sans\xfcrs\xfcz, mant\u0131k s\xfczgecinden ge\xe7irmeden, yaln\u0131zca kalbin cevab\u0131yla. Sonra bu vizyondan geriye do\u011fru y\xfcr\xfc: bu ay ne yapman gerekir? Maral vizyonu b\xfcy\xfck tutar, ad\u0131mlar\u0131 kararl\u0131 atar.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Maral Deer",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["majesty","beauty","honor","abundance"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Maral is one of the most sacred animals in Turkic and Altai mythology; known as Geyik Ana or Maral Ana (Deer Mother), this being appears in the shaman's journey as a guiding spirit and carries them to the celestial realm. In Central Asian carpets, Pazyryk burial mounds, and rock paintings, the Maral motif symbolizes the soul's ascent and sacred beauty. In Anatolian Turkic folk poetry, the Maral is identified with the unreachable beloved; in Divan poetry, the line 'your walk recalls the doe' expresses beauty and dignity together. In Celtic mythology, Cernunnos's sacred stag is lord of the forest and guardian of the cycle \u2014 antlers falling and growing back each year represent the unbroken cycle of death and rebirth. Among North American natives, the deer is the teacher of compassion and gentle harmony; it is chosen as the spirit animal that brings tenderness to the warrior's heart. In Norse mythology, four sacred deer dwelling in the branches of Yggdrasil graze on the four dimensions of time \u2014 in this image the deer carries time itself. The shadow side of the Maral: being so focused on the heights that one forgets to touch the ground, where dreaminess severs from reality.",dailyMessageEn:"Maral reminds you today of altitude \u2014 but what does true altitude mean? This animal lives in the mountains; it is both high and grounded, both magnificent and instantly attuned to danger. Voices that say 'be realistic' are sometimes others' attempts to drape their own limits over you \u2014 not the limits of the universe. Today ask yourself: Where do I receive the most restriction, from the world or from my own mind? The Maral's antlers shed each year and grow anew \u2014 what you thought you lost is part of a cycle of power, not a permanent ending. If your dream feels small, the time has come to make it larger. Reaching for the stars does not uproot you from the earth; the true ascent draws energy from the roots that make you who you are.",guidanceEn:"Today, answer on paper: 'What kind of life do I want five years from now?' \u2014 uncensored, unfiltered by logic, only the heart's answer. Then walk backward from that vision: what must you do this month? The Maral keeps the vision vast and the steps steady."},{id:"a030",name:"Timsah",emoji:"\ud83d\udc0a",element:"su",symbolism:["sab\u0131r","adaptasyon","hayatta kalma","g\xfc\xe7"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Crocodylus_niloticus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Timsah, Mezopotamya ve Anadolu'nun antik \xe7a\u011flar\u0131nda sular\u0131n gizemli efendisi olarak bilinirdi; F\u0131rat ve Dicle nehirlerinde ya\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131na inan\u0131lan bu yarat\u0131k, suyun hem verici hem de y\u0131k\u0131c\u0131 g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc birden ta\u015f\u0131yan kutsal bir varl\u0131kt\u0131. M\u0131s\u0131r mitolojisinde Sobek, timsah ba\u015fl\u0131 tanr\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 hem Nil'in bereketinin hem de sava\u015f g\xfcc\xfcn\xfcn simgesi; firavunlar\u0131n onu sayg\u0131yla besledi\u011fi tap\u0131naklar Nil kenar\u0131nda in\u015fa edilmi\u015fti. Aztek mitolojisinde Cipactli adl\u0131 timsah benzeri yarat\u0131k, d\xfcnyan\u0131n \xfczerine kuruldu\u011fu ilk varl\u0131kt\u0131r \u2014 yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7 noktas\u0131, varolu\u015fun zemini. Kuzey Avustralya yerli k\xfclt\xfcrlerinde timsah, R\xfcya Zaman\u0131'n\u0131n en eski koruyucusu olup atalar bilgisini nesilden nesile ta\u015f\u0131r. Afrika gelene\u011finde timsah, sab\u0131rla bekleyen g\xfcc\xfc temsil eder \u2014 nehir k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131nda hareketsiz yatan beden, h\u0131zl\u0131 nehir ak\u0131\u015f\u0131ndan daha b\xfcy\xfck bir enerjiye sahiptir \xe7\xfcnk\xfc zaman\u0131 bilgece kullan\u0131r. Timsah\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: sab\u0131rtan ataleti, stratejiden uzla\u015fmac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131, beklemeyi gerekli cesareti ertelemek i\xe7in kullanmak.",dailyMessage:"Timsah bug\xfcn sana sab\u0131r ile hareketsizlik aras\u0131ndaki ince \xe7izgiyi g\xf6steriyor. Bu hayvan saatlerce nehrin k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131nda hareketsiz yatar \u2014 bu uyku de\u011fil, yo\u011fun bir fark\u0131ndal\u0131k h\xe2lidir; kalp at\u0131\u015f\u0131 yava\u015flar, solunum derinle\u015fir, b\xfct\xfcn dikkat bir noktaya toplan\u0131r. Peki sen \u015fu an ger\xe7ekten stratejik mi bekliyorsun, yoksa harekete ge\xe7mekten ka\xe7\u0131nmak i\xe7in bekliyormu\u015f gibi mi yap\u0131yorsun? Bu soruya d\xfcr\xfcst\xe7e cevap ver. Hayat\u0131nda \u015fu an do\u011fru zaman\u0131 kollamay\u0131 gerektiren bir durum varsa, sezgine g\xfcven \u2014 ger\xe7ek sab\u0131r i\xe7i huzurludur, kayg\u0131l\u0131 de\u011fil. Do\u011fru an geldi\u011finde timsah yar\u0131m saniyede suyun y\xfcz\xfcne f\u0131rlar; o teredd\xfct yoktur, o hesaplama yoktur \u2014 haz\u0131rl\u0131k o anda i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcye d\xf6n\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015ft\xfcr. Seni haz\u0131rl\u0131kl\u0131 tutan nedir?",guidance:"Hayat\u0131nda \u015fu an 'beklemekte oldu\u011fun' bir \u015feyi listele ve her biri i\xe7in \u015funu yaz: 'Bu strateji mi, yoksa erteleme mi?' Cevap i\xe7ten gelsin. Strateji olanlar i\xe7in bir 'devreye giri\u015f sinyali' belirle \u2014 hangi ko\u015ful ger\xe7ekle\u015fti\u011finde harekete ge\xe7eceksin? Bu netlik, sab\u0131rla eylemi bir arada tutar.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Crocodile",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["patience","adaptation","survival","power"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the ancient ages of Mesopotamia and Anatolia, the crocodile was known as the mysterious lord of waters; this creature, believed to live in the Euphrates and Tigris, was a sacred being carrying both the giving and the destructive power of water. In Egyptian mythology, Sobek is the crocodile-headed god \u2014 symbol of both the Nile's abundance and the power of war; pharaohs built temples along the Nile where he was fed with reverence. In Aztec mythology, the crocodile-like being called Cipactli is the primordial creature upon whom the world was founded \u2014 the starting point of creation, the ground of existence. In Northern Australian Aboriginal cultures, the crocodile is the oldest guardian of the Dreaming, carrying ancestral knowledge from generation to generation. In African tradition, the crocodile represents power waiting in patience \u2014 its body lying motionless on the riverbank holds greater energy than the swift current because it uses time wisely. The shadow side of the crocodile: turning patience into inertia, strategy into compromise, using waiting to postpone the courage that is needed.",dailyMessageEn:"Crocodile shows you today the fine line between patience and stillness. This animal lies motionless by the river for hours \u2014 this is not sleep but a state of intense awareness; the heart slows, breath deepens, all attention gathers to a single point. So, are you truly waiting strategically right now, or only pretending to wait to avoid acting? Answer this honestly. If a situation in your life requires you to watch for the right moment, trust your intuition \u2014 true patience is inwardly peaceful, not anxious. When the right moment comes, the crocodile lunges to the surface in half a second; there is no hesitation, no calculation \u2014 preparation has become instinct in that moment. What is keeping you ready?",guidanceEn:"List the things you are currently 'waiting on' in your life and write next to each: 'Is this strategy, or is this avoidance?' Let the answer come from within. For those that are truly strategy, define an 'activation signal' \u2014 what condition must arise before you act? This clarity holds patience and action together."},{id:"a031",name:"Kartal Bayku\u015fu",emoji:"\ud83e\udd85",element:"hava",symbolism:["bilgelik","g\xfc\xe7","gece","derin s\u0131r"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Bubo_bubo_sibiricus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kartal Bayku\u015f, Orta Asya ve Sibirya \u015famanizminde en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc ruh yolculu\u011fu ku\u015fudur; \u015faman t\xf6renlerinde kartal bayku\u015f t\xfcy\xfc ba\u015fl\u0131\u011fa, davula ve kost\xfcme dikilir \xe7\xfcnk\xfc bu t\xfcyler \xfc\xe7 \xe2lem aras\u0131ndaki ge\xe7i\u015fe arac\u0131l\u0131k eder. Anadolu halk inan\u0131\u015f\u0131nda kartal bayku\u015fu r\xfcyada g\xf6rmek, atalar\u0131n bir mesaj g\xf6nderdi\u011finin i\u015fareti say\u0131l\u0131r ve \u015fabah\u0131na kadar bu mesaj\u0131n anlam\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcl\xfcr. Antik Yunan'da Athena'n\u0131n kutsal ku\u015fu olan bayku\u015f, bilgelik tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6z\xfc mesabesindeydi \u2014 karan\u0131n ve g\xfcnd\xfcz\xfcn \xf6tesini g\xf6rmek, g\xf6r\xfcnmeyen ger\xe7e\u011fi sezebilmek onun arma\u011fan\u0131d\u0131r. Aztek gelene\u011finde Miktlantek\xfchtli, \xf6l\xfcler tanr\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n yan\u0131nda kartal bayku\u015f bulunur ve bu varl\u0131k iki d\xfcnya aras\u0131ndaki habercili\u011fi \xfcstlenir. Kelt mitolojisinde bayku\u015f, yeralt\u0131 d\xfcnyas\u0131n\u0131n ve ge\xe7i\u015fin sesi olup \xf6l\xfcm de\u011fil d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm haberini getirir. Norse anlat\u0131lar\u0131nda bilgeli\u011fin sembolleri olan ku\u015flar, Odin'in g\xf6zleri gibi g\xf6r\xfcnmez ger\xe7ekleri aktar\u0131r. Kartal Bayku\u015funun g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131n sesine o kadar dalmak ki g\xfcndelik ger\xe7eklikle ba\u011f\u0131 koparmak, sezgiyi ger\xe7eklikten ay\u0131rt edemez olmak.",dailyMessage:"Kartal Bayku\u015fu bug\xfcn bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131n kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 aral\u0131yor ve sana \u015funu soruyor: Son g\xfcnlerde sana s\xfcrekli tekrarlanan bir g\xf6r\xfcnt\xfc, bir say\u0131, bir r\xfcya motifi ya da 'tesad\xfcfen' kar\u015f\u0131na \xe7\u0131kan bir sembol var m\u0131? Bu hayvan geceyi g\xf6r\xfcr \xe7\xfcnk\xfc \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa ihtiya\xe7 duymaz \u2014 i\xe7 \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131yla y\xf6nlenir. Sesin olmad\u0131\u011f\u0131 sessizli\u011fe git; oradan gelen mesaj, d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan gelen her tavsiyeden daha do\u011frudur. R\xfcyalar\u0131n son zamanlarda yo\u011funla\u015ft\u0131 m\u0131, ya da uyurken \xe7\xf6z\xfclemeyen bir \u015feyin cevab\u0131yla uyand\u0131n m\u0131? Bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131 konu\u015fuyor. Kartal Bayku\u015fu seni bu derin sesin yan\u0131na g\xf6t\xfcrmek istiyor \u2014 ama bunun i\xe7in \xf6nce ak\u0131l g\xfcr\xfclt\xfcs\xfcn\xfc susturmak gerekiyor. Bu gece yatarken 'g\xf6rmem gereken nedir?' diye sor ve sabah ilk anda ne geldi\u011fini not al.",guidance:"Bir hafta boyunca her sabah uyand\u0131\u011f\u0131nda, telefona bakmadan \xf6nce, akl\u0131na gelen ilk \xfc\xe7 \u015feyi bir deftere yaz \u2014 r\xfcya kal\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131, sezgiler, kelimeler, imgeler. Bu pratik bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131yla bilin\xe7li bir diyalog kurar ve zamanla i\xe7 rehberli\u011fin sesi netle\u015fir. Kartal Bayku\u015fu geceyi ayd\u0131nlatmaz \u2014 ama onu okur.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Eagle Owl",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["wisdom","power","night","deep mystery"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Eagle Owl is the most powerful spirit-journey bird in Central Asian and Siberian shamanism; in shamanic ceremonies, eagle owl feathers are sewn into the headdress, drum, and costume because these feathers mediate passage between the three realms. In Anatolian folk belief, seeing an eagle owl in a dream is taken as a sign that the ancestors have sent a message, and one ponders its meaning until dawn. In ancient Greece, the owl \u2014 sacred bird of Athena \u2014 was the very eye of the goddess of wisdom; seeing beyond darkness and daylight, sensing the unseen truth, is its gift. In Aztec tradition, the eagle owl accompanies Mictlantecuhtli, god of the dead, and serves as messenger between the two worlds. In Celtic mythology, the owl is the voice of the underworld and the threshold, bringing not death but transformation. In Norse narratives, birds as symbols of wisdom \u2014 like Odin's eyes \u2014 convey unseen truths. The shadow side of the Eagle Owl: plunging so deeply into the unconscious that one severs ties with daily reality, no longer able to distinguish intuition from fact.",dailyMessageEn:"Eagle Owl opens the door of the unconscious today and asks: In recent days, has an image, a number, a dream motif, or a symbol that 'coincidentally' appeared been recurring for you? This animal sees the night because it needs no light \u2014 it is guided by inner light. Go to the silence where there is no sound; the message that arises there is truer than any counsel from outside. Have your dreams intensified lately, or have you woken with the answer to something you could not solve while awake? The unconscious is speaking. Eagle Owl wants to lead you to this deep voice \u2014 but to do so, the noise of the mind must first be hushed. Tonight, as you lie down, ask 'what do I need to see?' and note the first thing that comes in the morning.",guidanceEn:"For a week, each morning upon waking \u2014 before looking at your phone \u2014 write the first three things that come to mind in a notebook: dream fragments, intuitions, words, images. This practice builds a conscious dialogue with the unconscious, and over time the voice of inner guidance becomes clear. Eagle Owl does not illuminate the night \u2014 it reads it."},{id:"a032",name:"Bo\u011fa",emoji:"\ud83d\udc02",element:"toprak",symbolism:["g\xfc\xe7","istikrar","azim","bereket"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Cattle.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Bo\u011fa, Anadolu'nun en eski kutsal hayvan\u0131d\u0131r; \xc7atalh\xf6y\xfck'te bulunan yedi bin y\u0131ll\u0131k tap\u0131nak duvarlar\u0131na kaz\u0131nan bo\u011fa ba\u015flar\u0131, bu co\u011frafyada k\xf6kl\xfc bir g\xfc\xe7 ve bereket k\xfclt\xfcn\xfcn ilk izleridir. Hitit panteonunda Tesup, f\u0131rt\u0131na tanr\u0131s\u0131 ve tanr\u0131lar\u0131n kral\u0131, iki kutsal bo\u011fan\u0131n \xfczerinde durur \u2014 g\xfcc\xfcn ve g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcn\xfcn efendisi. Mezopotamya'da Enlil, bo\u011fa sesi gibi g\xfcrl\xfcyor olarak anlat\u0131l\u0131r; S\xfcmer metinlerinde bo\u011fa, tar\u0131m medeniyetinin bel kemi\u011fi ve ya\u015fam enerjisinin simgesidir. M\u0131s\u0131r'da Apis bo\u011fas\u0131, Ptah tanr\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n ruhunun bedenlenmi\u015f h\xe2liydi ve \xf6l\xfcm\xfcnde b\xfcy\xfck yas tutulurdu; yeniden do\u011facak Apis bo\u011fas\u0131n\u0131n kutsal nitelikleri oldu\u011fu d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcl\xfcrd\xfc. Hint mitolojisinde Nandi, \u015eiva'n\u0131n kutsal bo\u011fas\u0131 ve tap\u0131nak bek\xe7isidir; tap\u0131na\u011fa girmeden \xf6nce Nandi'nin kula\u011f\u0131na s\xf6ylenen dilekler do\u011frudan \u015eiva'ya ula\u015f\u0131r. Kelt gelene\u011finde kutsal bo\u011fa kurban\u0131, topra\u011f\u0131n bereketini ve korumas\u0131n\u0131 sa\u011flayan y\u0131l\u0131n en \xf6nemli t\xf6renlerindendi. Bo\u011fan\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: inat\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n kararl\u0131l\u0131kla kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131lmas\u0131, de\u011fi\u015fime kap\u0131lar\u0131 tamamen kapamak.",dailyMessage:"Bo\u011fa bug\xfcn sana kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n ger\xe7ek g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Bu hayvan binlerce kiloluk bir g\xfc\xe7t\xfcr ama sa\xe7ma sapan her \u015feye do\u011fru ko\u015fmaz \u2014 y\xf6n\xfcn\xfc se\xe7er, yerini bilir, enerji harcamadan \xf6nce de\u011ferlendirir. Hayat\u0131nda \u015fu an engel gibi g\xf6r\xfcnen \u015fey seni ger\xe7ekten mi durduruyor, yoksa sen mi duraksad\u0131n? Duvar ger\xe7ekse bile sab\u0131rla ve g\xfc\xe7le ona kar\u015f\u0131 durmak onu a\u015f\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131r. Bug\xfcn seni en \xe7ok hangi bask\u0131 zay\u0131flatmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor ve sen ona nas\u0131l cevap veriyorsun? Bo\u011fa ba\u015f\u0131n\u0131 e\u011fmez \u2014 ama bu onun zay\u0131fl\u0131\u011f\u0131 de\u011fil, bilgeli\u011fidir; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc hangi sava\u015f\u0131n de\u011ferli oldu\u011funu bilir. Senin i\xe7in de\u011ferli olan sava\u015f hangisi? Ona adanm\u0131\u015f enerjin var m\u0131?",guidance:"Bu hafta boyunca her g\xfcn ona bir ad\u0131m at: kar\u015f\u0131nda duran o engeli \u2014 ili\u015fki, proje, karar, birikim \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama somut bir eylemle ge\xe7meye \xe7al\u0131\u015f. B\xfcy\xfck kararl\u0131l\u0131k b\xfcy\xfck jestlerle de\u011fil, k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama s\xfcrekli ad\u0131mlarla g\xf6sterilir. Bo\u011fan\u0131n g\xfcc\xfc s\xfcratte de\u011fil, a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131ndad\u0131r.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Bull",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["strength","stability","perseverance","abundance"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The bull is Anatolia's most ancient sacred animal; the bull heads carved upon the seven-thousand-year-old temple walls of \xc7atalh\xf6y\xfck are the earliest traces of a deeply rooted cult of strength and abundance in this geography. In the Hittite pantheon, Teshub, storm god and king of the gods, stands upon two sacred bulls \u2014 lord of power and sky. In Mesopotamia, Enlil is described as thundering like the bull's voice; in Sumerian texts, the bull is the backbone of agricultural civilization and the symbol of life-energy. In Egypt, the Apis bull was the embodied soul of the god Ptah, and great mourning followed its death; the reincarnated Apis bull was believed to bear sacred qualities. In Hindu mythology, Nandi is Shiva's sacred bull and temple guardian; wishes whispered into Nandi's ear before entering the temple reach Shiva directly. In Celtic tradition, the sacred bull sacrifice was among the year's most important ceremonies, ensuring the earth's fertility and protection. The shadow side of the bull: confusing stubbornness with determination, closing the doors to change entirely.",dailyMessageEn:"Bull reminds you today of the true power of your resolve. This animal is a force of thousands of kilograms but does not charge toward everything foolishly \u2014 it chooses its direction, knows its ground, evaluates before spending energy. Is the obstacle that appears before you in your life really stopping you, or did you pause? Even if the wall is real, standing against it with patience and strength erodes it. What pressure is most trying to weaken you today, and how do you respond? The bull does not bow its head \u2014 but this is not its weakness; it is its wisdom, for it knows which battle is worthy. Which battle is worthy for you? Have you devoted energy to it?",guidanceEn:"This week, take one step toward it each day: try to pass the obstacle before you \u2014 a relationship, project, decision, savings \u2014 with a small but concrete action. Great determination is shown not by grand gestures but by small, continuous steps. The bull's strength lies not in speed but in weight."},{id:"a033",name:"Kar\u0131nca",emoji:"\ud83d\udc1c",element:"toprak",symbolism:["sab\u0131r","topluluk","azim","organizasyon"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Ant.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kar\u0131nca, T\xfcrk halk k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde sabr\u0131n ve \xe7al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131\u011f\u0131n efsanevi sembol\xfcd\xfcr; 'Bir kar\u0131nca bir kayay\u0131 deler, sabr\u0131 varsa' atas\xf6z\xfc, bu k\xfc\xe7\xfck yarat\u0131\u011fa atfedilen metaforik g\xfcc\xfc \xf6zetler. Anadolu folklorunda kar\u0131nca yuvas\u0131 \xfczerine bas\u0131l\u0131rsa ya\u011fmur ya\u011faca\u011f\u0131na inan\u0131l\u0131r \u2014 kar\u0131ncalar topra\u011f\u0131n nabz\u0131n\u0131 tutan, do\u011fan\u0131n mesaj\u0131n\u0131 okuyan rehberler olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr. Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da Khepri adl\u0131 g\xfcne\u015f tanr\u0131s\u0131 b\xf6cek formunda canlan\u0131r ve k\xfc\xe7\xfcc\xfck yarat\u0131klar\u0131n b\xfcy\xfck g\xfc\xe7leri ta\u015f\u0131yabilece\u011fi inanc\u0131n\u0131 do\u011frular; kar\u0131nca bu gelene\u011fin yerel temsilcisidir. Kuzey Amerika Hopi gelene\u011finde Kar\u0131nca \u0130nsanlar (Ant People), k\u0131yametten \xf6nce insanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 yeralt\u0131na \xe7ekip hayatta tutan kutsal varl\u0131klard\u0131r \u2014 topluluk zekas\u0131 ve \xf6ng\xf6r\xfc onlar\u0131n en b\xfcy\xfck arma\u011fan\u0131d\u0131r. S\xfcleyman Peygamber'in kar\u0131ncaya sayg\u0131 duydu\u011fu anlat\u0131s\u0131 Kur'an'da da ge\xe7er; Neml suresinde kar\u0131ncalar aralar\u0131nda konu\u015fan, toplumlar\u0131n\u0131 \xf6rg\xfctleyen, \xf6ng\xf6r\xfcl\xfc varl\u0131klar olarak tasvir edilir. Hinduizm'de karma \xf6\u011fretisi kar\u0131nca imgesiyle s\u0131kl\u0131kla \xf6rneklenir: k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama birikmekte olan eylemler, sonunda devasa yap\u0131lar in\u015fa eder. Kar\u0131ncan\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: yaln\u0131zca sistem i\xe7inde \xe7al\u0131\u015fmak, sorgulamamak, kendi k\xfc\xe7\xfck g\xf6revinin \xf6tesini g\xf6rmemek.",dailyMessage:"Kar\u0131nca bug\xfcn sana b\xfcy\xfck sonu\xe7lar\u0131n nas\u0131l do\u011fdu\u011funu g\xf6steriyor: ta\u015f\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131n \xfcst\xfcne. Bu k\xfc\xe7\xfck yarat\u0131k kendi a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n elli kat\u0131n\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yabilir \u2014 bunu biliyor muydun? Beyin b\xfcy\xfckl\xfc\u011f\xfcyle orant\u0131s\u0131z bir \u015fekilde karma\u015f\u0131k toplumlar in\u015fa eder, tah\u0131l depolar, yollar a\xe7ar, k\xf6pr\xfcler kurar. Sen de \u015fu an b\xfcy\xfck bir hedefe bak\u0131p ezilmi\u015f hissediyorsan, kar\u0131nca gibi d\xfc\u015f\xfcn: bug\xfcn sadece bir ta\u015f. Yar\u0131n bir tane daha. Ama sistematik ol \u2014 rastgele enerjin da\u011f\u0131t\u0131lmas\u0131n. Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131nda en \xe7ok birikimini par\xe7alayan \u015fey nedir? O par\xe7alanman\u0131n \xfczerine d\xfczenli ve k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir eylem koy. Kar\u0131ncalar asla durmaz \u2014 ama asla da ko\u015fmaz; ritimle y\xfcr\xfcrler.",guidance:"B\xfcy\xfck hedefinizi k\xfc\xe7\xfck haftal\u0131k g\xf6revlere b\xf6l\xfcn ve bu haftan\u0131n tek g\xf6revini bug\xfcn belirleyin. Bunu bir ka\u011f\u0131da yaz\u0131n ve g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr bir yere yap\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131n. Kar\u0131nca verimlili\u011finin s\u0131rr\u0131, hedefi her zaman g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr tutmakt\u0131r \u2014 bu zihinsel oda\u011f\u0131 sabit k\u0131lar ve her k\xfc\xe7\xfck ad\u0131m\u0131 anlaml\u0131 yapar.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Ant",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["patience","community","perseverance","organization"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The ant is the legendary symbol of patience and industriousness in Turkic folk culture; the proverb 'An ant can pierce a rock, if it has patience' sums up the metaphoric power attributed to this small creature. In Anatolian folklore, it is believed that rain will fall if one steps on an anthill \u2014 ants are seen as guides who feel the earth's pulse and read nature's messages. In ancient Egypt, the sun god Khepri appears in insect form, affirming the belief that tiny beings can carry great powers; the ant is the local representative of this tradition. In the Hopi tradition of North America, the Ant People are sacred beings who pulled humanity underground before apocalypse and kept them alive \u2014 communal intelligence and foresight are their greatest gifts. The narrative of the Prophet Solomon's respect for the ant is also recounted in the Qur'an; in Surat An-Naml, ants are described as beings who speak among themselves, organize their society, and foresee. In Hinduism, the doctrine of karma is often illustrated through the ant image: small but accumulating actions ultimately build immense structures. The shadow side of the ant: working only within the system, not questioning, seeing nothing beyond one's small task.",dailyMessageEn:"Ant shows you today how great results are born: stone upon stone. This small creature can carry fifty times its own weight \u2014 did you know? Disproportionate to its brain size, it builds complex societies, stores grain, opens roads, builds bridges. If you are looking at a great goal right now and feel crushed, think like the ant: today, just one stone. Tomorrow, one more. But be systematic \u2014 do not scatter your energy at random. What is most fragmenting your accumulation in life today? Place a regular, small action over that fragmentation. Ants never stop \u2014 but they never run either; they walk with rhythm.",guidanceEn:"Break your great goal into small weekly tasks and decide today on this week's single task. Write it on a piece of paper and post it where it is visible. The secret of ant efficiency is to keep the goal always visible \u2014 this anchors mental focus and makes every small step meaningful."},{id:"a034",name:"Hac Leyle\u011fi",emoji:"\ud83d\udd4a\ufe0f",element:"hava",symbolism:["hac","yolculuk","manevi ar\u0131nma","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/White_stork_Ciconia_ciconia.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Hac Leyle\u011fi, T\xfcrk ve \u0130slam k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde yery\xfcz\xfcn\xfcn kutsal topraklar\u0131na her y\u0131l d\xfczenli yolculuk yapan bir varl\u0131k olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr; halk aras\u0131nda 'hac'a giden ku\u015f' olarak bilinir ve onun ge\xe7i\u015fi hay\u0131rl\u0131 kabul edilir. Anadolu'da leylek evlere yuva kurdu\u011funda o eve bereket ve koruma geldi\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131r; onu \xfcrk\xfctmek ya da yuvaya zarar vermek u\u011fursuzluk say\u0131l\u0131r. Antik M\u0131s\u0131r'da ibis ve leylek formundaki ruh ku\u015fu Ba, \xf6len ki\u015finin ruhunun serbest dola\u015f\u0131m\u0131n\u0131 temsil eder; bu imgede ku\u015fun g\xf6\xe7\xfc ruhun \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcd\xfcr. Kelt gelene\u011finde g\xf6\xe7 eden ku\u015flar, \xd6teki D\xfcnya'ya ge\xe7i\u015f kap\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131n bek\xe7ileridir; onlar\u0131n izledi\u011fi yollar, ley hatlar\u0131yla \xe7ak\u0131\u015f\u0131r ve kutsal co\u011frafyan\u0131n haritas\u0131n\u0131 \xe7izer. Hinduizm'de Hamsa \u2014 hem ku\u011fu hem hac ku\u015fu \u2014 ruhun maddi olandan manevi olana yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131 yolculu\u011fun simgesidir; 'ben kimim?' sorusunu soran ruhun her nefeste yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\xe7 yolculu\u011fu temsil eder. Japon gelene\u011finde Tsuru (turna), y\u0131lda bir kez cennetle yery\xfcz\xfc aras\u0131nda gidip gelen el\xe7idir \u2014 dua ve ar\u0131nman\u0131n kanatl\u0131 sembol\xfc. Hac Leyle\u011finin g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: d\u0131\u015fsal yolculu\u011fa o kadar odaklanmak ki i\xe7 yolculu\u011fu unutmak, co\u011frafyay\u0131 ar\u0131nman\u0131n yerine koymak.",dailyMessage:"Hac Leyle\u011fi bug\xfcn sana bir yolculu\u011fa \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131yor \u2014 ama bu mutlaka co\u011frafi bir mesafe de\u011fil. Ruhun \u015fu an nereye gitmek istiyor? Uzun s\xfcredir yapmak istedi\u011fin ama erteledi\u011fin bir ar\u0131nma, bir y\xfczle\u015fme, bir d\xf6n\xfc\u015f var m\u0131? Leyle\u011fin her y\u0131l binlerce kilometre u\xe7mas\u0131 yaln\u0131zca g\xf6\xe7 i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcs\xfc de\u011fil \u2014 ruhsal bir haf\u0131za, bir \xe7ekim, bir eve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f \xf6zlemidir. Sen de i\xe7inde b\xf6yle bir \xe7ekimi hissediyor musun? Belki bir ili\u015fkide kapanmam\u0131\u015f bir hesap, belki seninle bar\u0131\u015fmak istedi\u011fin bir ge\xe7mi\u015f, belki uzun zamand\u0131r gitmedi\u011fin bir i\xe7 sessizlik. Bug\xfcn o yolculu\u011fa bir ad\u0131m at. Hacca gitmek i\xe7in y\u0131llarca haz\u0131rlan\u0131l\u0131r \u2014 ama i\xe7 yolculu\u011fu ba\u015flatmak i\xe7in tek bir niyet yeterlidir.",guidance:"Bu hafta sessiz bir yerde, belki do\u011fada ya da bir mum \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131nda, \u015fu soruyu kendine sor ve cevab\u0131n\u0131 yaz: 'Ruhsal olarak nereye d\xf6nmek istiyorum?' Bu sorunun cevab\u0131, ger\xe7ek yolculu\u011funun haritas\u0131d\u0131r. Sonra o yolculu\u011fa bug\xfcn atabilece\u011fin en k\xfc\xe7\xfck ad\u0131m\u0131 belirle ve yap.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Pilgrim Stork",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["pilgrimage","journey","spiritual purification","return"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Pilgrim Stork is seen in Turkic and Islamic culture as a being making regular yearly journeys to the sacred lands of the earth; it is known among folk as 'the bird that goes on the Hajj,' and its passage is considered auspicious. In Anatolia, when a stork builds its nest upon a home, that home is believed to receive blessing and protection; frightening it or harming its nest is considered ill-omened. In ancient Egypt, the soul-bird Ba in the form of ibis and stork represents the free wandering of the deceased's soul; in this image, the bird's migration is the soul's freedom. In Celtic tradition, migratory birds are guardians of the gateways to the Otherworld; the paths they travel coincide with ley lines and chart the map of sacred geography. In Hinduism, the Hamsa \u2014 both swan and pilgrim bird \u2014 symbolizes the soul's journey from the material to the spiritual; it represents the inner journey the soul makes with each breath, asking 'who am I?' In Japanese tradition, the Tsuru (crane) is the messenger that travels once a year between heaven and earth \u2014 winged symbol of prayer and purification. The shadow side of the Pilgrim Stork: focusing so much on the outer journey that one forgets the inner journey, mistaking geography for purification.",dailyMessageEn:"Pilgrim Stork calls you to a journey today \u2014 but not necessarily a geographic one. Where does your soul wish to go right now? Is there a purification, a reckoning, a return you have long wished to make but kept postponing? The stork flying thousands of kilometers each year is not only migratory instinct \u2014 it is spiritual memory, an attraction, a longing for home. Do you feel such a pull within you? Perhaps an unfinished account in a relationship, perhaps a past you wish to make peace with, perhaps an inner silence you have long avoided. Take one step toward that journey today. Years are spent preparing for the Hajj \u2014 but to begin the inner journey, a single intention is enough.",guidanceEn:"This week, in a quiet place \u2014 perhaps in nature or by candlelight \u2014 ask yourself this question and write the answer: 'Where do I want to return, spiritually?' The answer is the map of your true journey. Then identify the smallest step you can take today toward that journey, and take it."},{id:"a035",name:"\xd6rdek",emoji:"\ud83e\udd86",element:"su",symbolism:["uyum","duygusal denge","berrakl\u0131k","rahatl\u0131k"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Anas_platyrhynchos_male_female_quadrat.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"\xd6rdek, Anadolu ve T\xfcrk halk k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde g\xf6l\xfcn sahibi ve suyun koruyucu ruhu olarak anlat\u0131l\u0131r; g\xf6l kenar\u0131nda \xf6rdek g\xf6rmek su ruhlar\u0131n\u0131n bar\u0131\u015f\u0131k oldu\u011funun ve o suyun i\xe7ilip kullan\u0131labilece\u011finin i\u015fareti say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. \u015eamanist gelenekte su ku\u015flar\u0131, \xfc\xe7 \xe2lemin \u2014 g\xf6k, yery\xfcz\xfc ve yeralt\u0131 sular\u0131 \u2014 birden i\xe7inden ge\xe7en arac\u0131 varl\u0131klard\u0131r; \xf6rdek hem u\xe7ar hem y\xfczer hem de dalar. Kelt mitolojisinde su ku\u015flar\u0131 \xf6zellikle \xf6rdek ve ku\u011fu, ilahi habercilerdir; anlat\u0131mlarda \xf6rdekler \xe7o\u011funlukla tanr\u0131lar\u0131n k\u0131l\u0131k de\u011fi\u015ftirmi\u015f halleridir. Japon Shinto gelene\u011finde kamo (\xf6rdek), tanr\u0131sal varl\u0131klar\u0131n beraber u\xe7tu\u011fu kutsal ku\u015ftur ve onu g\xf6zlemlemek i\xe7 huzuru getirir. Kuzey Amerika yerlilerinde \xf6rdek, duygusal berrakl\u0131\u011f\u0131n \xf6\u011fretmenidir \u2014 su y\xfczeyinde rahat y\xfczebilmek, derin sularda dalabilmek ve gerekti\u011finde havalanabilmek, her ko\u015fula uyum sa\u011flayan esnek bilincin imgesidir. \xc7in gelene\u011finde mandarin \xf6rde\u011fi \xe7ift olarak betimlenir ve uyumlu birlikteli\u011fin simgesidir. \xd6rde\u011fin g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: esnekli\u011fin tutars\u0131zl\u0131\u011fa d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmesi, her ortamda y\xfczmek isterken hi\xe7birinde k\xf6kl\xfc olamamak.",dailyMessage:"\xd6rdek bug\xfcn sana \xe7ok boyutlu olman\u0131n bir g\xfc\xe7 oldu\u011funu s\xf6yl\xfcyor. Su y\xfczeyinde rahat\xe7a y\xfczer, gerekti\u011finde derin sulara dalar, istedi\u011finde g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcne a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r \u2014 ama bunu yaparken hep o zarif, sakin g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcm\xfc korur. Peki, sen farkl\u0131 hayatlar\u0131n\u0131 \u2014 i\u015f hayat\u0131, aile, i\xe7 d\xfcnya, sosyal kimlik \u2014 nas\u0131l dengeliyorsun? Bunlar aras\u0131nda \xe7at\u0131\u015fma hissediyor musun, yoksa her biri seni sensen yapan farkl\u0131 bir katman m\u0131? \xd6rdek t\xfcyleri suyun i\xe7ine girmez \u2014 her ortamda bulunur ama ortam onu d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcremez. Sen de \xe7evrene uyum sa\u011flarken \xf6z\xfcn\xfc kaybetmeden duruyor musun? Bu ince fark, y\xfczeyde y\xfczmek ile i\xe7inde erimek aras\u0131ndad\u0131r.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn i\xe7inde en rahat hissetti\u011finiz ortam\u0131 ve en zorlay\u0131c\u0131 hissetti\u011finiz ortam\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcn. \u0130kincisinde kendinize dair ne kaybediyorsunuz? Bunu bir c\xfcmleyle yaz\u0131n. Sonra bu c\xfcmleyi bir k\u0131lavuz olarak ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131n: 'Nerede olursam olay\u0131m, \u015funu koruyaca\u011f\u0131m.' \xd6rdek t\xfcyleri gibi koruyucu bir kaplama bu olacak.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Duck",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["harmony","emotional balance","clarity","ease"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The duck is told of as the lake's keeper and the protective spirit of water in Anatolian and Turkic folk culture; seeing a duck at the lake's edge was taken as a sign that the water spirits were at peace and that the water was safe to drink and use. In shamanic tradition, water birds are mediator beings traversing the three realms \u2014 sky, earth, and the waters beneath the earth; the duck flies, swims, and dives. In Celtic mythology, water birds \u2014 especially duck and swan \u2014 are divine messengers; in many tales, ducks are gods in disguise. In Japanese Shinto tradition, the kamo (duck) is a sacred bird in whose company divine beings fly, and observing it brings inner peace. Among North American natives, the duck is the teacher of emotional clarity \u2014 being able to swim with ease at the surface, dive into deep waters, and take flight when needed is the image of a flexible consciousness adapting to all conditions. In Chinese tradition, mandarin ducks are depicted as a pair and symbolize harmonious union. The shadow side of the duck: flexibility becoming inconsistency, wanting to swim in every environment yet rooting in none.",dailyMessageEn:"Duck tells you today that being multidimensional is a strength. It swims easily on the surface, dives into deep waters when needed, takes to the sky when it wishes \u2014 yet always maintains that graceful, calm appearance. So, how do you balance your different lives \u2014 work, family, inner world, social identity? Do you feel conflict among them, or is each a different layer that makes you who you are? The duck's feathers do not let water in \u2014 it is present in every environment, but the environment cannot transform it. Are you adapting to your surroundings without losing your essence? This subtle distinction lies between swimming on the surface and dissolving within.",guidanceEn:"Think today of the environment in which you feel most at ease and the one in which you feel most challenged. What part of yourself do you lose in the second? Write it in one sentence. Then carry that sentence as a guide: 'Wherever I am, I will protect this.' Let it be a protective coating, like the duck's feathers."},{id:"a036",name:"Kuzgun",emoji:"\ud83d\udc26\u200d\u2b1b",element:"hava",symbolism:["s\u0131r","kehanet","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","bilin\xe7"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Common_raven_(Corvus_corax).jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kuzgun, T\xfcrk \u015famanizminde en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc \xf6teki d\xfcnya habercilerinden biridir; Sibirya \u015famanlar\u0131n\u0131n t\xf6renlerinde kuzgun t\xfcy\xfc ve kuzgun maskesi, ruhlar\u0131n d\xfcnyas\u0131na ge\xe7i\u015fi kolayla\u015ft\u0131rmak i\xe7in kullan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Anadolu halk inanc\u0131nda kuzgunun \xf6tt\xfc\u011f\xfc y\xf6ne bakmak, gizli haberleri ya da yakla\u015fan de\u011fi\u015fimi g\xf6rebilece\u011fine inan\u0131lan bir i\u015faret say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Norse mitolojisinde Odin'in iki kuzgunu Huginn (d\xfc\u015f\xfcnce) ve Muninn (bellek), her g\xfcn d\xfcnyan\u0131n d\xf6rt bir yan\u0131na u\xe7ar ve ak\u015fam Odin'in omzuna konup her \u015feyi f\u0131s\u0131ldar; bu imgede kuzgun bilen varl\u0131\u011f\u0131n g\xf6z\xfc ve kula\u011f\u0131d\u0131r. Kelt gelene\u011finde Morrigan, sava\u015f tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131, kuzgun formunu al\u0131r ve kehanette bulunur; kuzgunlar\u0131n \xfc\xe7 kez \xe7a\u011f\u0131rmas\u0131 d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn e\u015fi\u011fini haber verir. Kuzey Amerika yerlilerinde Kuzgun Yarat\u0131c\u0131, g\xfcne\u015fi \xe7alarak d\xfcnyaya \u0131\u015f\u0131k getiren trickster \u2014 hem aldat\u0131c\u0131 hem kurtar\u0131c\u0131, hem g\xf6lge hem ayd\u0131nl\u0131k. \xc7in ve Japon geleneklerinde \xfc\xe7 bacakl\u0131 g\xfcne\u015f kuzgunu, g\xf6ksel habercinin ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn simgesidir. Kuzgunun g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: gizemin i\xe7ine o kadar \xe7ekilmek ki somut ger\xe7eklikle ba\u011f\u0131 koparmak, mesajlar\u0131 paranoyayla yorumlamak.",dailyMessage:"Kuzgun bug\xfcn sana evrenin seninle konu\u015ftu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor \u2014 ama yaln\u0131zca dinleyenler i\u015fitir. Son g\xfcnlerde tekrar eden bir say\u0131, bir renk, bir isim ya da yaln\u0131zca tesad\xfcf deyip ge\xe7ti\u011fin ama i\xe7ini k\u0131p\u0131rdatan bir an var m\u0131? Kuzgun semboller diliyle konu\u015fur \xe7\xfcnk\xfc do\u011frudan s\xf6z bazen yanl\u0131\u015f anla\u015f\u0131l\u0131r \u2014 imgeler, sezgiler, r\xfcyalar, aniden akl\u0131na gelen bir \u015fark\u0131 s\xf6z\xfc, hepsi mesaj ta\u015f\u0131yabilir. Frekans\u0131n\u0131 bu kanala ayarla. Ama dikkat: kuzgunun g\xfcc\xfc mesajlar\u0131 g\xf6rmekte de\u011fil, onlar\u0131 do\u011fru yorumlamaktad\u0131r. Panikle de\u011fil, merakla bak. \u015eu an hayat\u0131nda anlamland\u0131ramad\u0131\u011f\u0131n ama \xfczerine d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmeden ge\xe7emedi\u011fin bir \u015fey var m\u0131? Belki cevap orada.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn bir sembol defteri ba\u015flat\u0131n: Dikkatinizi \xe7eken her tekrarlayan \u015feyi \u2014 say\u0131, renk, hayvan, kelime \u2014 not edin ve yan\u0131na o andaki duygusal halinizi yaz\u0131n. Bir ay sonra bakt\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131zda \xf6r\xfcnt\xfcler ortaya \xe7\u0131kacak. Kuzgun kehaneti anl\u0131k de\u011fil, birikimledir.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Raven",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["mystery","prophecy","transformation","consciousness"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The raven is one of the most powerful otherworldly messengers in Turkic shamanism; in Siberian shamans' ceremonies, raven feathers and raven masks were used to ease passage into the spirit world. In Anatolian folk belief, looking in the direction of the raven's call was considered a sign by which one might glimpse hidden news or approaching change. In Norse mythology, Odin's two ravens Huginn (thought) and Muninn (memory) fly daily across the four corners of the world and at evening land upon Odin's shoulder, whispering everything; in this image, the raven is the eye and ear of the knowing being. In Celtic tradition, Morrigan, the war goddess, takes the form of a raven and prophesies; ravens calling three times announce the threshold of transformation. Among North American natives, Raven the Creator is the trickster who stole the sun and brought light to the world \u2014 both deceiver and savior, both shadow and light. In Chinese and Japanese traditions, the three-legged sun raven is symbol of the celestial messenger and of transformation. The shadow side of the raven: withdrawing so deeply into mystery that one severs from concrete reality, interpreting messages with paranoia.",dailyMessageEn:"Raven reminds you today that the universe is speaking to you \u2014 but only those who listen will hear. In recent days, has there been a recurring number, color, name, or a moment you dismissed as coincidence that nonetheless stirred something within you? Raven speaks through the language of symbols because direct speech is sometimes misunderstood \u2014 images, intuitions, dreams, a lyric that suddenly comes to mind, all can carry messages. Tune yourself to this channel. But beware: the raven's power lies not in seeing messages but in interpreting them rightly. Look with curiosity, not panic. Is there something in your life right now that you cannot quite make sense of but cannot stop reflecting on? Perhaps the answer is there.",guidanceEn:"Begin a symbol journal today: note each recurring thing that catches your attention \u2014 number, color, animal, word \u2014 and write your emotional state at that moment beside it. When you look back after a month, patterns will emerge. Raven's prophecy is not instantaneous but cumulative."},{id:"a037",name:"Ak Kelebek",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8b",element:"hava",symbolism:["ruh","\xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck","g\xfczellik","de\u011fi\u015fim"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Pieris_brassicae.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Ak Kelebek, Anadolu ve T\xfcrk halk gelene\u011finde ruhun \xf6zg\xfcr h\xe2li olarak yorumlan\u0131r; \xf6len birinin ard\u0131ndan gelen beyaz kelebek, onun ruhunun huzurla ayr\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n i\u015fareti say\u0131l\u0131r. Divan \u015fiirinde kelebek a\u015fk\u0131n ate\u015fine ko\u015fan, yanmay\u0131 g\xf6ze alan ruhun imgesidir \u2014 'pervane gibi' d\xf6nd\xfc\u011f\xfcm\xfcz \u015fey bizi hem yak\u0131p hem ayd\u0131nlat\u0131r. Antik Yunan'da Psykhe s\xf6zc\xfc\u011f\xfc hem 'ruh' hem 'kelebek' anlam\u0131na gelir; Psykhe'nin kelebek kanatl\u0131 tasviri, ruhun \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfcn ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn\xfcn en eski g\xf6rsel metaforudur. Aztek mitolojisinde sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 ruhlar\u0131 kelebek ve sinekku\u015fu formunda g\xfcne\u015fin etraf\u0131nda dans eder; Quetzalpallin ad\u0131 verilen bu kutsal kelebekler \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz sava\u015fanlar\u0131n simgesidir. Japon k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde kelebe\u011fi g\xf6rmek, sevilen bir yak\u0131n\u0131n ruhunun ziyaret\xe7isi olarak de\u011ferlendirilir. \xc7in gelene\u011finde ise \xe7ift kelebek imgesi mutlulu\u011fun ve ne\u015fenin, tek kelebek ise ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn sembol\xfcd\xfcr. Ak Kelebe\u011fin g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: hafifli\u011fi s\u0131\u011fl\u0131kla kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131rmak, a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve k\xf6kl\xfcl\xfc\u011f\xfc y\xfck olarak g\xf6rmek, s\xfcrekli y\xfczeyde kal\u0131p derinle\u015fememek.",dailyMessage:"Ak Kelebek bug\xfcn sana hafiflik sorusunu soruyor: Bu a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yabilirsin \u2014 ama ta\u015f\u0131mak zorunda m\u0131s\u0131n? Kelebek t\u0131rt\u0131l h\xe2lindeyken ger\xe7ek anlamda \xf6l\xfcr koza i\xe7inde; tam olarak \xe7\xf6z\xfcl\xfcr, her \u015feyi b\u0131rak\u0131r ve o karanl\u0131kta bamba\u015fka bir varl\u0131\u011fa d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr. Bu bir metafor de\u011fil, biyolojik bir ger\xe7ek. Peki sen \u015fu an neyin i\xe7inde \xe7\xf6z\xfcl\xfcyorsun? Hangi eski form \u2014 eski inan\xe7, eski ili\u015fki \xf6r\xfcnt\xfcs\xfc, eski kimlik \u2014 senin ger\xe7ek d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcne yer a\xe7mak i\xe7in gitmek istiyor? Bug\xfcn ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n d\xfc\u015f\xfcnceler aras\u0131nda hangileri seni y\xfckseltiyor, hangileri yere \xe7ekiyor? En az bir tanesini bug\xfcn bilin\xe7le b\u0131rak \u2014 bir d\xfc\u015f\xfcnce, bir kayg\u0131, bir ge\xe7mi\u015fe ait \xf6fke. Sadece bir tane. Hafiflik birden gelmiyor; bir b\u0131rak\u0131\u015fla ba\u015fl\u0131yor.",guidance:"Bu ak\u015fam oturun ve bir ka\u011f\u0131da \u015fu an ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z d\xfc\u015f\xfcncelerden birini yaz\u0131n \u2014 \xfczerinize y\xfck olan, sizi geriye \xe7eken. Ka\u011f\u0131d\u0131 katlay\u0131n ve bir mum yak\u0131n. Ka\u011f\u0131d\u0131 ate\u015fe yakla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131n ya da sembolik olarak \xe7\xf6pe at\u0131n ve \u015funu s\xf6yleyin: 'Bu benim de\u011fil, bunu b\u0131rak\u0131yorum.' Ak Kelebek rit\xfceli bu \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama bilin\xe7li b\u0131rak\u0131\u015f.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"White Butterfly",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["soul","freedom","beauty","change"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The White Butterfly is interpreted in Anatolian and Turkic folk tradition as the free state of the soul; a white butterfly that comes after a death is taken as a sign that the soul has departed in peace. In Divan poetry, the butterfly is the image of the soul that runs toward the fire of love, willing to be consumed \u2014 what we 'circle like a moth' both burns and illuminates us. In ancient Greek, the word Psyche means both 'soul' and 'butterfly'; the depiction of Psyche with butterfly wings is the oldest visual metaphor for the soul's freedom and transformation. In Aztec mythology, the souls of warriors dance around the sun in butterfly and hummingbird form; these sacred butterflies called Quetzalpapalotl symbolize immortal warriors. In Japanese culture, seeing a butterfly is regarded as the visit of a beloved one's soul. In Chinese tradition, the image of two butterflies symbolizes happiness and joy, while a lone butterfly symbolizes independence and freedom. The shadow side of the White Butterfly: confusing lightness with shallowness, seeing weight and rootedness as burden, remaining always on the surface and unable to deepen.",dailyMessageEn:"White Butterfly asks you today the question of lightness: You can carry this weight \u2014 but must you? The butterfly truly dies in the chrysalis stage; it fully dissolves, releases everything, and in that darkness becomes a wholly different being. This is not a metaphor but biological reality. So, what are you dissolving in right now? Which old form \u2014 old belief, old relational pattern, old identity \u2014 wishes to leave to make room for your true transformation? Among the thoughts you carry today, which lift you and which drag you down? Release at least one consciously today \u2014 a thought, a worry, an old anger. Just one. Lightness does not come all at once; it begins with a single letting-go.",guidanceEn:"This evening, sit and write on a piece of paper one of the thoughts you are carrying \u2014 one that weighs on you, that pulls you back. Fold the paper and light a candle. Hold it near the flame or symbolically discard it and say: 'This is not mine, I release it.' This is the White Butterfly ritual \u2014 small but conscious release."},{id:"a038",name:"Deve",emoji:"\ud83d\udc2a",element:"toprak",symbolism:["dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k","sab\u0131r","kaynak","yolculuk"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Camelus_dromedarius_Egpyt.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Deve, \u0130pek Yolu medeniyetinin omurgas\u0131d\u0131r; y\xfczy\u0131llar boyunca Anadolu \xfczerinden ge\xe7en kervanlarla bilgi, k\xfclt\xfcr, baharat ve kuma\u015f\u0131n ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131s\u0131 olan bu hayvan, yolculu\u011fun kendisinin canl\u0131 sembol\xfc olmu\u015ftur. T\xfcrk ve Arap k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde deve yaln\u0131zca i\u015f hayvan\u0131 de\u011fil, sayg\u0131n bir yol arkada\u015f\u0131d\u0131r; \u015fair Fuzuli deve \xe7\xf6lden ge\xe7erken g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcne bakan g\xf6zlerinden s\xf6z eder \u2014 uza\u011fa bakmak, geni\u015f ufuk g\xf6rmek deve bilgeli\u011finin \xf6z\xfcd\xfcr. \u0130slam gelene\u011finde deve kutsal hayvanlar aras\u0131nda say\u0131l\u0131r; Hz. Peygamber'in devesi Kasva bir\xe7ok \xf6nemli karar\u0131 y\xf6nlendirmi\u015ftir ve deve ya\u011f\u0131z\u0131 Kadir Gecesi konu\u015ftu\u011funa inan\u0131l\u0131r. Kuzey Afrika Tuareg gelene\u011finde deve, \xe7\xf6l\xfcn mabedindeki en kutsal varl\u0131kt\u0131r \u2014 sahibinin hayat\u0131n\u0131 bilir, sezgiyle y\xf6nelir, gerekti\u011finde susturulmu\u015f bir bilgelikle y\xfcr\xfcr. Mo\u011fol \u015famanizminde deve, topra\u011f\u0131n ruhunu ta\u015f\u0131yan ve uzun yolculuklara refakat eden ruh hayvan\u0131d\u0131r. Tibet gelene\u011finde hayat\u0131n uzun ve zorlu yolculu\u011fu deve imgesiyle simgelenir; sabr\u0131n ve i\xe7sel kayna\u011f\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc metaforudur. Devenin g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: inatla y\xfcklenmek, s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 bilmemek ya da tersine durmak i\xe7in zorluklar\u0131 bahane etmek.",dailyMessage:"Deve bug\xfcn sana uzun yolda oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Ve bunu \u015fefkatle s\xf6yl\xfcyor \xe7\xfcnk\xfc o da biliyor: \xc7\xf6l ger\xe7ek, s\u0131cakl\u0131k ger\xe7ek, y\xfck a\u011f\u0131r. Ama i\xe7inde o kambur var \u2014 senin enerji depon, senin rezervin, kimsenin g\xf6remedi\u011fi o i\xe7 kaynak. T\xfckenmi\u015flik hissediyorsun belki, ya da bu yolun ne kadar s\xfcrece\u011fini merak ediyorsun. Deve b\xfct\xfcn g\xfcn y\xfcr\xfcr, su i\xe7mez, \u015fikayet etmez \u2014 \xe7\xfcnk\xfc yolunun sonunda ne oldu\u011funu biliyor gibidir. Sen \u015fu an y\xfcr\xfcd\xfc\u011f\xfcn yolun sonunda ne g\xf6r\xfcyorsun? O vizyon seni ta\u015f\u0131yor mu, yoksa bulan\u0131k m\u0131? Bitkinlik ge\xe7icidir, pes etmek kal\u0131c\u0131. \u0130\xe7indeki rezerve el at \u2014 o su orada, deponun i\xe7inde.",guidance:"Bu hafta enerjinizi t\xfcketen bir \u015feyi listeleyin ve her birinin yan\u0131na \u015funu yaz\u0131n: 'Bu zorunlu mu, yoksa kald\u0131rabilece\u011fim biri var m\u0131?' Deve y\xfck\xfcn\xfc payla\u015fmay\u0131 bilir \u2014 kervan hayvan\u0131d\u0131r, yaln\u0131z de\u011fildir. Hangi y\xfck\xfc b\u0131rakabilirsiniz ya da birine devredebilirsiniz? O bo\u015falan alan, yolculu\u011fun geri kalan\u0131 i\xe7in size g\xfc\xe7 verecek.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Camel",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["endurance","patience","resource","journey"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The camel is the backbone of Silk Road civilization; this animal, which carried knowledge, culture, spices, and fabric through caravans crossing Anatolia for centuries, has become the living symbol of the journey itself. In Turkic and Arab cultures, the camel is not merely a working animal but a revered traveling companion; the poet Fuzuli speaks of the camel crossing the desert and lifting its eyes to the sky \u2014 to look far, to see the wide horizon, is the essence of camel wisdom. In Islamic tradition, the camel is counted among the sacred animals; the Prophet's camel Qaswa guided many important decisions, and it is believed that the camel speaks on the Night of Power. In North African Tuareg tradition, the camel is the most sacred being in the temple of the desert \u2014 it knows the life of its owner, finds direction by intuition, and walks when needed with a silenced wisdom. In Mongolian shamanism, the camel is the spirit animal that carries the soul of the earth and accompanies long journeys. In Tibetan tradition, the long and arduous journey of life is symbolized by the camel image; it is the most powerful metaphor for patience and inner resource. The shadow side of the camel: stubbornly bearing burdens, not knowing one's limit, or conversely using difficulty as an excuse to stop.",dailyMessageEn:"Camel reminds you today that you are on a long road. And it says this with compassion because it too knows: the desert is real, the heat is real, the load is heavy. But within you is that hump \u2014 your reservoir of energy, your store, the inner resource no one sees. Perhaps you feel depleted, or wonder how long this road will continue. The camel walks all day, drinks no water, does not complain \u2014 because it seems to know what lies at the journey's end. What do you see at the end of the road you walk? Does that vision carry you, or is it blurry? Exhaustion is temporary; giving up is permanent. Reach into your reserve \u2014 the water is there, within the store.",guidanceEn:"This week, list one thing that drains your energy and write next to each: 'Is this essential, or is there someone who can carry it with me?' The camel knows how to share its load \u2014 it is a caravan animal, not a solitary one. Which burden can you set down or pass on? The space freed will fuel the rest of your journey."},{id:"a039",name:"Bal\u0131k",emoji:"\ud83d\udc1f",element:"su",symbolism:["bereket","bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131","ak\u0131\u015f","\xe7o\u011falma"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Atlantic_cod.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Bal\u0131k, Anadolu ve Mezopotamya k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde suyun ve sezginin en derin sembol\xfcd\xfcr; S\xfcmer'in bal\u0131k tanr\u0131s\u0131 Enki hem tatl\u0131 sular\u0131n hem de gizemli bilginin efendisiydi \u2014 onun havuzundaki bal\u0131klar kutsal bilgeli\u011fi ta\u015f\u0131rd\u0131. Anadolu halk k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde bal\u0131k motifi bereket ve \xe7o\u011falma anlam\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131r, gelinlere ve \xe7ocuk sahibi olmak isteyenlere bal\u0131k fig\xfcrleri hediye edilirdi. H\u0131ristiyanl\u0131k'ta bal\u0131k simgesi (Ikhthys) hem inanc\u0131n gizli i\u015fareti hem de ruhsal suyun i\xe7inde ya\u015fayan \xf6z\xfcn imgesidir. Japon k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde Koi bal\u0131\u011f\u0131, zorluklar\u0131 a\u015farak nehri yukar\u0131 t\u0131rmanan, azmin ve ruhsal olgunla\u015fman\u0131n simgesidir; \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfc\u011f\xfcn ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn i\u015fareti. Hindu gelene\u011finde Manu'nun bal\u0131\u011f\u0131 Matsya, tufandan \xf6nce uyard\u0131 ve kurtulu\u015fa \xf6nc\xfcl\xfck etti \u2014 sezgisel uyar\u0131n\u0131n ve ilahi koruman\u0131n sembol\xfc. K\u0131z\u0131lderili geleneklerinde Somon, b\xfcy\xfck d\xf6ng\xfcn\xfcn, do\u011fuma d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcn ve i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcsel bilginin habercisidir \u2014 geri d\xf6ner, k\xf6k\xfcne d\xf6ner, sonra yeniden ba\u015flar. Bal\u0131\u011f\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131na o kadar dalmak ki g\xfcndelik hayatla temas kurmak g\xfc\xe7le\u015fmek, sezgiyle ger\xe7ekli\u011fi kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131rmak.",dailyMessage:"Bal\u0131k bug\xfcn seni derinlere \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131yor \u2014 ama bu derinlik kayg\u0131 verici de\u011fil, ayd\u0131nlat\u0131c\u0131. Suyun y\xfczeyinden g\xf6r\xfclenler ger\xe7e\u011fin yaln\u0131zca bir katman\u0131d\u0131r; as\u0131l olan a\u015fa\u011f\u0131da y\xfczer, derinlikte sakl\u0131d\u0131r. \u015eu an hayat\u0131nda \xe7ok y\xfczeysel de\u011ferlendirdi\u011fin ama sezginin seni ba\u015fka bir \u015feye i\u015faret etti\u011fi bir durum var m\u0131? O belirsiz his, o a\xe7\u0131klamas\u0131 olmayan \xe7ekim ya da itim \u2014 bu bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131ndan gelen bir haritad\u0131r. Mant\u0131k her zaman en h\u0131zl\u0131 yol de\u011fil; bazen i\xe7g\xfcd\xfc seni devreden \xe7\u0131kar\u0131r ve do\u011fru y\xf6n\xfc g\xf6sterir. Sezgine g\xfcvenmekte zorland\u0131\u011f\u0131n son bir an hat\u0131rl\u0131yor musun? Ve o sezgi hakl\u0131 \xe7\u0131kt\u0131 m\u0131? Bal\u0131\u011f\u0131n dersini al: suya gir, derine dal, i\xe7eriden bak.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn i\xe7inde mant\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z\u0131n 'evet' dedi\u011fi ama i\xe7inizin 'hay\u0131r' dedi\u011fi ya da tam tersini ya\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir durumu d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcn. Bir ka\u011f\u0131da \u015funu yaz\u0131n: 'Sezgim bana ne s\xf6yl\xfcyor?' ve cevab\u0131 sans\xfcrs\xfczce yaz\u0131n. Bu pratik bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131yla bilin\xe7li bir k\xf6pr\xfc kurar ve zamanla g\xfcvenilir bir i\xe7 pusula geli\u015ftirirsiniz.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Fish",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["abundance","unconscious","flow","multiplication"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The fish is the deepest symbol of water and intuition in Anatolian and Mesopotamian culture; the Sumerian fish god Enki was lord of both fresh waters and mysterious knowledge \u2014 the fish in his pools carried sacred wisdom. In Anatolian folk culture, the fish motif carries the meaning of abundance and multiplication, and figures of fish were given as gifts to brides and those wishing to have children. In Christianity, the fish symbol (Ichthys) is both a secret sign of faith and an image of the essence dwelling within spiritual water. In Japanese culture, the Koi fish, which climbs upstream overcoming obstacles, symbolizes perseverance and spiritual maturation; it is the sign of immortality and transformation. In Hindu tradition, Manu's fish Matsya warned before the flood and led to salvation \u2014 symbol of intuitive warning and divine protection. In Native American traditions, the Salmon is herald of the great cycle, of return to one's birth, and of instinctual knowledge \u2014 it returns, returns to its root, then begins again. The shadow side of the fish: plunging so deeply into the unconscious that it becomes difficult to maintain contact with daily life, confusing intuition with reality.",dailyMessageEn:"Fish calls you to the depths today \u2014 but this depth is not anxious, it is illuminating. What is seen from the water's surface is only one layer of truth; the essential swims below, hidden in the deep. Is there a situation in your life right now that you have evaluated too superficially, while your intuition points you toward something else? That vague feeling, that pull or repulsion you cannot explain \u2014 this is a map from the unconscious. Logic is not always the fastest way; sometimes instinct bypasses the circuit and shows the right direction. Do you remember the last time you struggled to trust your intuition? And did that intuition prove right? Take the fish's lesson: enter the water, dive deep, look from within.",guidanceEn:"Think today of a situation where your logic said 'yes' but your inner self said 'no' \u2014 or the opposite. On a paper, write: 'What is my intuition telling me?' and write the answer uncensored. This practice builds a conscious bridge with the unconscious, and over time you develop a reliable inner compass."},{id:"a040",name:"Horoz",emoji:"\ud83d\udc13",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["uyan\u0131\u015f","yeni g\xfcn","cesaret","d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfck"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Rooster.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Horoz, Anadolu'da g\xfcne\u015fin ve sabah\u0131n kutsal habercisidir; k\xf6y k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde horozun \xf6tmesi yaln\u0131zca zaman de\u011fil, gecenin biti\u011fi ve karanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 yenen \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131n bildirisidir. T\xfcrk halk inan\u0131\u015f\u0131nda horozun \xf6t\xfc\u015f\xfc cinleri ve k\xf6t\xfc ruhlar\u0131 kovalar; bu y\xfczden 'horoz \xf6tt\xfc' s\xf6z\xfc hem ger\xe7ek bir sesi hem de koruyucu bir kapan\u0131\u015f\u0131 anlat\u0131r. Antik \u0130ran Zerd\xfc\u015ft gelene\u011finde horoz kutsal hayvanlar aras\u0131nda en \xf6nemlilerinden biridir; Sraosha adl\u0131 adanma mele\u011finin sesi horozun sesi olarak belirir ve karanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 deler. Japon Shinto gelene\u011finde Niwatori (horoz) g\xfcne\u015f tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Amaterasu'yu ma\u011faras\u0131ndan \xe7\u0131karmak i\xe7in \xf6ten ku\u015ftur \u2014 \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131n olmad\u0131\u011f\u0131 yerde onun sesi ayd\u0131nl\u0131\u011f\u0131 geri \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131r. Antik Yunan'da horoz Asklepios'un kutsal hayvan\u0131d\u0131r; iyile\u015fme tanr\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n tap\u0131naklar\u0131nda horoz kurban edilir \xe7\xfcnk\xfc g\xfcndo\u011fumunun getirdi\u011fi yenileni\u015f, hastal\u0131\u011f\u0131n biti\u015fini simgeler. \xc7in k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde horoz on iki hayvan aras\u0131ndad\u0131r ve cesareti, g\xfcveni ve a\xe7\u0131k s\xf6zl\xfcl\xfc\u011f\xfc temsil eder. Horozun g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: ba\u011f\u0131ran ama dinlemeyen, ba\u015flayan ama s\xfcrd\xfcremeyen, enerjisini gece rezervine koymak yerine ilk anda t\xfcketen.",dailyMessage:"Horoz bug\xfcn sana \u015funu s\xf6yl\xfcyor: G\xfcne\u015f \xe7oktan do\u011fdu. Sesin \xe7\u0131kmas\u0131, uyan\u0131\u015f i\xe7in i\u015faret vermesi, o ilk sesi \xe7\u0131karmas\u0131 gerekiyor. Hayat\u0131nda ne kadar s\xfcredir bekliyorsun \u2014 o proje, o konu\u015fma, o ad\u0131m, o karar \u2014 haz\u0131r m\u0131s\u0131n ger\xe7ekten? Yoksa 'm\xfckemmel zaman' gelsin diye mi duraks\u0131yorsun? Horoz m\xfckemmel sabah\u0131 beklemez; sabah\u0131 oldu\u011funu ilan eder ve sabah\u0131 var eder. Bu ilan yetki beklemiyor, onay beklemiyor, \u015fartlar\u0131n tam olgunla\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131 beklemiyor. Bug\xfcn sen ne ilan etmek istiyorsun? K\xfc\xe7\xfck ya da b\xfcy\xfck, \xf6zel ya da kamusal \u2014 bir ses \xe7\u0131kar. \u0130lk ad\u0131m\u0131n enerjisini ta\u015f\u0131; geri kalan\u0131 o momentumun i\xe7inde \u015fekillenir.",guidance:"Bu sabah ya da \xf6\u011fleden \xf6nce, erteledi\u011finiz en \xf6nemli \u015feye on dakika ay\u0131r\u0131n. Sadece ba\u015flay\u0131n \u2014 bitirmek zorunda de\u011filsiniz. Horoz b\xfct\xfcn g\xfcn\xfc \xf6tmez; sadece ba\u015flang\u0131c\u0131 ilan eder. O ilk on dakika, b\xfcy\xfck bir \u015feyin kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7ar.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Rooster",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["awakening","new day","courage","honesty"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The rooster is the sacred herald of the sun and the morning in Anatolia; in village culture, the rooster's crow is not only time but the proclamation that night has ended and light has conquered the darkness. In Turkic folk belief, the rooster's crow drives away jinn and evil spirits; thus the phrase 'the rooster has crowed' expresses both a real sound and a protective closure. In ancient Persian Zoroastrian tradition, the rooster is among the most important of sacred animals; the voice of the angel of devotion Sraosha is manifested as the rooster's voice, piercing the darkness. In Japanese Shinto tradition, Niwatori (rooster) is the bird that crowed to draw the sun goddess Amaterasu from her cave \u2014 where there is no light, his voice calls the brightness back. In ancient Greece, the rooster was sacred to Asclepius; roosters were sacrificed in the temples of the god of healing because the renewal brought by sunrise symbolizes the end of illness. In Chinese culture, the rooster is among the twelve animals and represents courage, confidence, and frankness. The shadow side of the rooster: one who shouts but does not listen, who begins but cannot sustain, who exhausts his energy in the first moment rather than placing it in the night reserve.",dailyMessageEn:"Rooster tells you today: The sun has long since risen. Your voice must come forth, signal the awakening, make that first sound. How long have you been waiting in your life \u2014 that project, that conversation, that step, that decision \u2014 are you truly ready? Or are you pausing for the 'perfect time'? The rooster does not wait for the perfect morning; he proclaims that it is morning and makes morning happen. This proclamation does not wait for permission, does not wait for approval, does not wait for conditions to fully ripen. What do you wish to proclaim today? Small or large, private or public \u2014 make a sound. Carry the energy of the first step; the rest will take shape within that momentum.",guidanceEn:"This morning or before noon, give ten minutes to the most important thing you have been postponing. Just begin \u2014 you do not have to finish. The rooster does not crow all day; it only proclaims the beginning. Those first ten minutes open the door to something great."},{id:"a041",name:"Tav\u015fan",emoji:"\ud83d\udc07",element:"su",symbolism:["do\u011furganl\u0131k","ay d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc","h\u0131zl\u0131 zeka","ka\xe7\u0131nma"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Oryctolagus_cuniculus_Tasmania_2.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Tav\u015fan, Anadolu ve T\xfcrk halk gelene\u011finde zekas\u0131yla nam salm\u0131\u015f, g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olan\u0131 bile alt eden bir kahraman olarak masallarda s\u0131k\xe7a yer al\u0131r; 'tav\u015fan tilkiyi kand\u0131rd\u0131' motifi, g\xfc\xe7ten de\u011fil zekadan gelen zafer anlat\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r. Anadolu'da tav\u015fan\u0131 \xf6ld\xfcrmek u\u011fursuz say\u0131l\u0131r, yolda kar\u015f\u0131la\u015fmak ise bir karar a\u015famas\u0131nda farkl\u0131 bir yol se\xe7meye i\u015faret eder. M\u0131s\u0131r mitolojisinde Ay tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 \u0130sis'in kutsal hayvan\u0131 aras\u0131nda tav\u015fan say\u0131l\u0131r; Ay'\u0131n b\xfcy\xfcy\xfcp k\xfc\xe7\xfcld\xfc\u011f\xfc gibi tav\u015fan\u0131n d\xf6ng\xfcsel \xfcremesi, do\u011fan\u0131n ritmiyle \xf6zde\u015fle\u015fir. Mezoamerika yerli gelene\u011finde Ay'\u0131n y\xfcz\xfcndeki leke tav\u015fan olarak yorumlan\u0131r \u2014 Mayan sanat yap\u0131tlar\u0131nda bu tav\u015fan simgesi \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfc\u011f\xfcn ve Ay d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfcn imgesidir. Kelt mitolojisinde beyaz tav\u015fan ya da yabani tav\u015fan \xd6teki D\xfcnya'n\u0131n el\xe7isidir; onu kovalamak b\xfcy\xfcl\xfc bir yolculu\u011fun ba\u015flang\u0131c\u0131d\u0131r. \xc7in gelene\u011finde Jade Tav\u015fan Ay'da ya\u015far ve \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck iksiri haz\u0131rlar \u2014 uzun \xf6m\xfcr ve bereketin simgesi. Tav\u015fan\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: korkudan ka\xe7mak, tehlikeyi o kadar erken sezinleyip hareketsiz kalmak ki f\u0131rsat da ka\xe7mak.",dailyMessage:"Tav\u015fan bug\xfcn sana k\u0131vrakl\u0131k ve Ay enerjisi hakk\u0131nda bir \u015fey s\xf6yl\xfcyor. Bu hayvan, d\xfcnyan\u0131n en keskin reflekslerine sahiptir \u2014 herhangi bir y\xf6nde s\u0131f\u0131rdan h\u0131zlanabilir ve an\u0131nda de\u011fi\u015ftirebilir y\xf6n\xfcn\xfc. Ama bu tepki korkudan de\u011fil, sezgiden gelir \u2014 tehlikeyi koklayan burun, t\xfcm v\xfccuda mesaj\u0131 iletir. Sen \u015fu an h\u0131zl\u0131 karar vermeyi gerektiren bir durumda m\u0131s\u0131n? \u0130\xe7 ses ne diyor \u2014 ka\xe7mak m\u0131 istiyor, yoksa farkl\u0131 bir y\xf6ne mi s\u0131\xe7ramak? Bu ikisi farkl\u0131 \u015feyler. Tav\u015fan zekas\u0131 belirsizli\u011fi sevmez: se\xe7enekleri h\u0131zla de\u011ferlendirir ve en iyi rotaya girer. Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131nda bu netli\u011fe ihtiya\xe7 duydu\u011fun bir alan var \u2014 ona bak.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn bir karar vermeniz gereken ama s\xfcrekli erteledi\u011finiz \u015feyi ka\u011f\u0131da yaz\u0131n. Sonra h\u0131zla iki s\xfctun yap\u0131n: 'Yaparsam ne olur' ve 'Yapmazsam ne olur'. Tav\u015fan zihni ile karar verin \u2014 uzun analiz de\u011fil, sezgi destekli h\u0131z. \u0130lk s\xfctun sizi daha m\u0131 heyecanland\u0131r\u0131yor, yoksa korkutuyor mu? Cevap orada.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Rabbit",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["fertility","moon cycle","quick wit","evasion"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The rabbit appears frequently in Anatolian and Turkic folk tradition as a hero famed for its cleverness, defeating even the strong; the motif 'the rabbit tricked the fox' is the narrative of victory through wit rather than force. In Anatolia, killing a rabbit is considered ill-omened, and crossing one's path is taken as a sign to choose a different course at a decision point. In Egyptian mythology, the rabbit is counted among the sacred animals of the moon goddess Isis; like the waxing and waning of the moon, the rabbit's cyclical breeding is identified with the rhythm of nature. In Mesoamerican native tradition, the mark on the moon's face is interpreted as a rabbit \u2014 in Mayan artworks, this rabbit symbol is the image of immortality and the moon cycle. In Celtic mythology, the white rabbit or wild hare is the messenger of the Otherworld; chasing it is the beginning of a magical journey. In Chinese tradition, the Jade Rabbit lives on the moon and prepares the elixir of immortality \u2014 symbol of longevity and abundance. The shadow side of the rabbit: fleeing from fear, sensing danger so early that one freezes and thereby misses the opportunity.",dailyMessageEn:"Rabbit tells you something today about agility and moon energy. This animal has the sharpest reflexes in the world \u2014 it can accelerate in any direction from zero and instantly change course. But this reaction comes not from fear but from intuition \u2014 the nose that scents danger relays the message to the whole body. Are you in a situation right now requiring a quick decision? What does the inner voice say \u2014 does it want to flee, or to leap in a different direction? These two are different things. Rabbit intelligence dislikes uncertainty: it rapidly evaluates options and chooses the best route. There is an area in your life today where you need this clarity \u2014 look at it.",guidanceEn:"Write today on paper a decision you must make but have been postponing. Then quickly make two columns: 'If I do it, what happens' and 'If I don't, what happens.' Decide with the rabbit's mind \u2014 not long analysis but intuition-backed speed. Does the first column excite you more, or frighten you? The answer is there."},{id:"a042",name:"Akrep",emoji:"\ud83e\udd82",element:"toprak",symbolism:["d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","savunma","tutku","\xf6l\xfcm-yenido\u011fum"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Centruroides_vittatus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Akrep, Anadolu co\u011frafyas\u0131nda hem ger\xe7ek tehlikenin hem de gizemli g\xfcc\xfcn simgesidir; Anadolu'nun g\xfcneyindeki k\xf6y gelene\u011finde akrep \u0131s\u0131r\u0131\u011f\u0131 s\u0131radan bir olay de\u011fil, ki\u015finin 'akreple s\u0131nanmas\u0131' olarak yorumlan\u0131r ve hayatta kalan\u0131n g\xfcc\xfc artt\u0131\u011f\u0131na inan\u0131l\u0131r. Divan \u015fiirinde akrep sevgilinin kirpi\u011fine ya da bak\u0131\u015f\u0131na benzetilir \u2014 can alan ama vazge\xe7ilemeyen bir g\xfc\xe7. Antik M\u0131s\u0131r'da Serket ya da Selket adl\u0131 tanr\u0131\xe7a akrep ba\u015fl\u0131d\u0131r; \xf6l\xfcleri koruyan, zehri ilaca \xe7eviren ikili do\u011fan\u0131n tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r. Mezopotamya'da 'Akrep \u0130nsanlar' Tiamat'\u0131n sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 yar\u0131 insan yar\u0131 akrep bu varl\u0131klar d\xfcnyan\u0131n kap\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131 korur ve yaln\u0131zca hak edenler ge\xe7ebilir. Aztek mitolojisinde Citlaltlachtli adl\u0131 akrep tanr\u0131s\u0131, Ay'\u0131n d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc denetler ve \xf6l\xfcm-yenido\u011fum sarmal\u0131n\u0131 temsil eder. Bat\u0131 Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm enerjisi ile \xe7ok benzer bi\xe7imde, akrep imgesi \xf6lmeden d\xf6n\xfc\u015febilmenin g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc simgeler. Akrebin g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: savunmay\u0131 sald\u0131r\u0131ya d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrmek, zehri gereksiz yere kullanmak, her ili\u015fkiyi tehdit olarak g\xf6rmek.",dailyMessage:"Akrep bug\xfcn sana derin bir hakikati f\u0131s\u0131ld\u0131yor: \u015eu an i\xe7inde bir \u015fey \xf6l\xfcyor \u2014 ve bu iyi bir haber. Eski bir kal\u0131p, eski bir inan\xe7, eski bir ili\u015fki dinami\u011fi ya da ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n a\u011f\u0131r bir kimlik sona eriyor. Buna direnme. Akrep, d\xfcnyan\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc zehrini ta\u015f\u0131r ama ayn\u0131 zamanda d\xfcnyan\u0131n en k\xf6kl\xfc d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm enerjisini de bar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131r \u2014 \xf6l\xfcm ve yeniden do\u011fum onun do\u011fas\u0131d\u0131r. S\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 koruma konusunda bug\xfcn bir test ya\u015f\u0131yor musun? Biri ya da bir durum seni a\u015ft\u0131rmaya, s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 ge\xe7meye, seni k\xfc\xe7\xfcltmeye mi \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor? Zehrini esirgeme \u2014 ama bunu patlayarak de\u011fil, netlikle yap. 'Hay\u0131r' demek \u015fiddet de\u011fildir; kendinle kurdu\u011fun en kutsal anla\u015fman\u0131n ifadesidir.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn i\xe7inde birine ya da bir duruma 'hay\u0131r' demeniz gereken ama 'evet' dedi\u011finiz bir \u015feyi d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcn. O s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131 bu hafta i\xe7inde netle\u015ftirin \u2014 bir mesajla, bir konu\u015fmayla ya da yaln\u0131zca kendi i\xe7inizde bir kararla. S\u0131n\u0131rlar k\u0131r\u0131lganl\u0131ktan de\u011fil, \xf6zde\u011ferden \xe7izildi\u011finde ger\xe7ek g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc g\xf6sterir. Akrep b\xf6yle korur.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Scorpion",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["transformation","defense","passion","death-rebirth"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The scorpion is the symbol of both real danger and mysterious power in Anatolian geography; in the village tradition of southern Anatolia, a scorpion sting is not an ordinary event but is interpreted as one's 'trial by scorpion,' and the survivor is believed to grow stronger. In Divan poetry, the scorpion is compared to the beloved's eyelash or gaze \u2014 a force that kills yet cannot be renounced. In ancient Egypt, the goddess Serket or Selket is scorpion-headed; she is the goddess of dual nature who protects the dead and turns poison into medicine. In Mesopotamia, the 'Scorpion Men' are warriors of Tiamat \u2014 these half-human, half-scorpion beings guard the gates of the world, and only the worthy may pass. In Aztec mythology, the scorpion god Citlaltlachtli oversees the moon's cycle and represents the death-rebirth spiral. In the West African Yoruba tradition, similarly to transformative energy, the scorpion image symbolizes the power to transform without dying. The shadow side of the scorpion: turning defense into attack, using poison needlessly, seeing every relationship as a threat.",dailyMessageEn:"Scorpion whispers a deep truth to you today: Something within you is dying right now \u2014 and this is good news. An old pattern, an old belief, an old relational dynamic, or a heavy identity you have carried is ending. Do not resist. Scorpion carries the most potent poison in the world but also harbors the world's most rooted transformation energy \u2014 death and rebirth are its nature. Are you facing a test of your boundaries today? Is someone or some situation trying to overstep, cross your line, diminish you? Do not withhold your poison \u2014 but use it not by exploding but with clarity. Saying 'no' is not violence; it is the expression of the most sacred covenant you have made with yourself.",guidanceEn:"Think today of someone or something to whom you should have said 'no' but said 'yes.' Clarify that boundary this week \u2014 by a message, a conversation, or simply by a decision within yourself. Boundaries show their true power when drawn not from fragility but from self-worth. This is how the scorpion protects."},{id:"a043",name:"Kurba\u011fa",emoji:"\ud83d\udc38",element:"su",symbolism:["d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","ya\u011fmur","temizlenme","ge\xe7i\u015f"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Atelopus_zeteki1.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kurba\u011fa, Anadolu k\xf6y k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde ya\u011fmurun habercisi ve bereketin simgesidir; 'Kurba\u011fa \xf6tt\xfc m\xfc, ya\u011fmur yak\u0131nd\u0131r' s\xf6z\xfc hem meteorolojik bir ger\xe7ek hem de do\u011fan\u0131n dilini okuman\u0131n bir bi\xe7imidir. Eski Anadolu inan\u0131\u015f\u0131nda kurba\u011fa sesi duyuldu\u011funda \xe7ift\xe7i, ekine su verecek g\xfcnlerin yakla\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hisseder \u2014 bu bir g\xfcven, bir m\xfcjdedir. M\u0131s\u0131r mitolojisinde Heket adl\u0131 kurba\u011fa tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131, do\u011fum ve yenido\u011fumun koruyucusudur; do\u011fum s\u0131ras\u0131nda lohusan\u0131n yan\u0131nda Heket'in fig\xfcr\xfc tutulur \xe7\xfcnk\xfc bu ge\xe7i\u015fi y\xf6netti\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Aztek gelene\u011finde Tlaltecuhtli, yery\xfcz\xfc tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r ve kurba\u011fa formunda betimlen\u0131r \u2014 yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n ve d\xf6ng\xfcn\xfcn yery\xfcz\xfc bedenleni\u015fi. Kelt mitolojisinde kurba\u011fa hem su hem toprak varl\u0131\u011f\u0131 olarak iki d\xfcnya aras\u0131nda k\xf6pr\xfcd\xfcr; kutsal su kaynaklar\u0131na kurba\u011fa sunmas\u0131 b\u0131rakmak y\xfczy\u0131llarca s\xfcrd\xfcr\xfclm\xfc\u015ft\xfcr. Japon k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde Kaeru hem 'kurba\u011fa' hem 'geri d\xf6nmek' anlam\u0131na gelir \u2014 eve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f, k\xf6klerine d\xf6n\xfc\u015f, \xf6z\xfcne d\xf6n\xfc\u015f simgesidir. Kurba\u011fan\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: eri\u015fteki ge\xe7ici h\xe2le tak\u0131l\u0131p kalmak, d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcme direnmek, kuyunun dibinden ba\u015fka bir yer olmad\u0131\u011f\u0131na inanmak.",dailyMessage:"Kurba\u011fa bug\xfcn sana \u015funu s\xf6yl\xfcyor: \u015eark\u0131 s\xf6yleme vakti. Kurba\u011fan\u0131n \xf6t\xfc\u015f\xfc yaln\u0131zca bir ses de\u011fil \u2014 e\u015fini \xe7a\u011f\u0131rmak, topra\u011fa m\xfcjde vermek, suyun gelmekte oldu\u011funu ilan etmektir. Sen de uzun s\xfcredir sessiz mi oldun? Bir \u015feyin de\u011fi\u015fti\u011fini, bir \u015feyin sonland\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ya da bir \u015feyin yeniden ba\u015flad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hen\xfcz seslendirmedin mi? Kurba\u011fa \xfc\xe7 formda var olur: yumurta, iriba\u015f, kurba\u011fa. Her biri bir \xf6ncekinden tamamen farkl\u0131 \u2014 suyu b\u0131rak\u0131p karaya \xe7\u0131kmak, solunga\xe7lar\u0131 b\u0131rak\u0131p akci\u011ferle nefes almak. Bu kadar k\xf6kl\xfc bir d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcmden ge\xe7iyorsun belki de. Hangi eski formunu b\u0131rakmaya haz\u0131rs\u0131n? Ve bu yeni sesi \xe7\u0131karmak i\xe7in haz\u0131r m\u0131s\u0131n?",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn i\xe7inde eski bir al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131\u011f\u0131, inanc\u0131 ya da kal\u0131b\u0131 \u2014 art\u0131k size hizmet etmeyen birini \u2014 bilin\xe7le b\u0131rak\u0131n. Bunu yaparken sesli s\xf6yleyin: 'Bunu b\u0131rak\u0131yorum.' Kurba\u011fan\u0131n sesli \xf6t\xfc\u015f\xfc, de\u011fi\u015fimin aktar\u0131lmas\u0131d\u0131r. Sessiz kararlar bazen hayatta kalmaz \u2014 sesli niyet k\xf6k salar.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Frog",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["transformation","rain","cleansing","transition"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The frog is the herald of rain and the symbol of abundance in Anatolian village culture; the saying 'When the frog croaks, rain is near' is both a meteorological truth and a way of reading nature's language. In ancient Anatolian belief, when the frog's voice is heard, the farmer senses the days of watering the crop are approaching \u2014 this is an assurance, a glad tiding. In Egyptian mythology, the frog goddess Heket is the guardian of birth and rebirth; her figure was held beside the woman in labor because she was believed to govern this passage. In Aztec tradition, Tlaltecuhtli, goddess of the earth, is depicted in frog form \u2014 the earthly embodiment of creation and the cycle. In Celtic mythology, the frog, as a creature of both water and earth, is a bridge between two worlds; the practice of leaving frog offerings at sacred springs continued for centuries. In Japanese culture, Kaeru means both 'frog' and 'to return' \u2014 symbol of returning home, returning to one's roots, returning to one's essence. The shadow side of the frog: clinging to the transient state at the threshold, resisting transformation, believing there is no place but the bottom of the well.",dailyMessageEn:"Frog tells you today: It is time to sing. The frog's croak is not just a sound \u2014 it is calling a mate, heralding the earth, proclaiming that water is coming. Have you too been silent too long? Have you not yet voiced that something has changed, ended, or begun anew? The frog exists in three forms: egg, tadpole, frog. Each is wholly different from the last \u2014 leaving the water for land, leaving gills for lungs. Perhaps you too are passing through such a profound transformation. Which old form are you ready to release? And are you ready to make this new sound?",guidanceEn:"Today, consciously release an old habit, belief, or pattern that no longer serves you. As you do so, say it aloud: 'I let this go.' The frog's vocal croak is the transmission of change. Silent decisions sometimes do not survive \u2014 voiced intention takes root."},{id:"a044",name:"Karga",emoji:"\ud83d\udc26\u200d\u2b1b",element:"hava",symbolism:["zeka","haberci","mistik","uyum"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Corvus_corone_2_(Marek_Szczepanek).jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Karga, T\xfcrk halk gelene\u011finde hem u\u011fursuz hem bilge bir haberci olarak iki kutuplu bir yer tutar; 'Karga ka\u011f\u0131n\u0131 medh eyler' atas\xf6z\xfc \xf6znel k\xf6rl\xfc\u011f\xfc anlatmak i\xe7in kullan\u0131l\u0131r, ama \xf6te yandan karga sesi k\xf6ylerde yakla\u015fan tehlikenin ya da misafirin habercisi say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Anadolu'da bir kargan\u0131n pencereye konmas\u0131, ev sahibinin yak\u0131nda haber alaca\u011f\u0131na yorumlan\u0131r. Sibirya \u015famanizminde karga, hem trickster hem de bilge olarak iki y\xfczl\xfc bir g\xfc\xe7 ta\u015f\u0131r; \u015faman rit\xfcellerinde karga t\xfcy\xfc habercili\u011fin ve mesaj iletiminin simgesidir. Norse mitolojisinde ise Odin'in kuzgun-kargar\u0131ms\u0131 ku\u015flar\u0131 Huginn ve Muninn, bilgi ve haf\u0131zan\u0131n tanr\u0131sal temsilcileridir \u2014 karga ailesi d\xfc\u015f\xfcncenin kanatlanmas\u0131d\u0131r. Kuzey Amerika yerlilerinde Karga, ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7larda \u0131\u015f\u0131k olmayan d\xfcnyaya ate\u015fi ve g\xfcne\u015fi getiren yarat\u0131c\u0131 trickster'd\u0131r; onun zekas\u0131 kural tan\u0131maz ama sonu\xe7ta hep daha b\xfcy\xfck bir iyili\u011fe hizmet eder. Japonya'da Yatagarasu, \xfc\xe7 bacakl\u0131 kutsal karga, g\xfcne\u015fin sava\u015f\xe7\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n rehberidir \u2014 tanr\u0131sal irade ve strateji onun simgesidir. Kargan\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: zekan\u0131n kibre d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmesi, her \u015feyi biliyor olmak, dinlemek yerine hep konu\u015fmak.",dailyMessage:"Karga bug\xfcn sana zekan\u0131 kullanman\u0131 s\xf6yl\xfcyor \u2014 ama nas\u0131l kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 da soruyor. Bu hayvan ara\xe7 kullanmay\u0131 \xf6\u011frenir, sorun \xe7\xf6zer, birbirini uyar\u0131r, kolektif haf\u0131za ta\u015f\u0131r. Tek ba\u015f\u0131na de\u011fil, s\xfcr\xfcyle ak\u0131ll\u0131d\u0131r. \u015eu an \xf6n\xfcndeki bir zorluk seni bunalt\u0131yorsa, bunu yaln\u0131z \xe7\xf6zmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor musun? Karga hi\xe7 yaln\u0131z avlanmaz \u2014 etraf\u0131ndaki a\u011fa g\xfcvenir. Bug\xfcn kimi arayabilirsin, kimin bilgisinden yararlanabilirsin, kimin deneyiminden ders \xe7\u0131karabilirsin? Zeka bazen bilmemektir \u2014 bilmeyeni bilmek, sormay\u0131 becermek, cevab\u0131 aramak. \xd6n\xfcndeki bariyer g\xfc\xe7 gerektirmiyor, ustal\u0131k gerektiriyor. Ustal\u0131k i\xe7in bazen ara\xe7 gerekir, bazen dost.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn \xe7\xf6zmekte zorland\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir konuda g\xfcvendi\u011finiz birine dan\u0131\u015f\u0131n \u2014 ya da konuyla ilgili bir kitap, makale, podcast aray\u0131n. Karga her nesilde biriktirilen bilgiyi aktar\u0131r; sizin jenerasyon birikimleriniz zaten etraf\u0131n\u0131zda. Onlara el at\u0131n.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Crow",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["intelligence","messenger","mystic","harmony"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The crow holds a bipolar place in Turkic folk tradition as both an ill-omened and a wise messenger; the proverb 'The crow praises its own chick' is used to describe subjective blindness, but on the other hand the crow's call was considered in villages the herald of approaching danger or of a guest. In Anatolia, a crow landing on the window is interpreted as a sign that the homeowner will soon receive news. In Siberian shamanism, the crow bears a two-faced power as both trickster and sage; in shamanic rituals, the crow feather is the symbol of messaging and message transmission. In Norse mythology, Odin's raven-crow-like birds Huginn and Muninn are divine representatives of knowledge and memory \u2014 the corvid family is the winging of thought. Among North American natives, Crow is the creative trickster who brought fire and the sun to a world that originally had no light; its intelligence is irreverent but ultimately serves a greater good. In Japan, Yatagarasu, the three-legged sacred crow, is the guide of the sun warrior \u2014 divine will and strategy are his symbols. The shadow side of the crow: intelligence turning into arrogance, knowing everything, speaking always instead of listening.",dailyMessageEn:"Crow tells you today to use your intelligence \u2014 but also asks how you are using it. This animal learns to use tools, solves problems, warns its kin, carries collective memory. It is wise not alone but with the flock. If a challenge before you is overwhelming, are you trying to solve it alone? Crow never hunts alone \u2014 it trusts the web around it. Whom can you call today, whose knowledge can you draw upon, whose experience can you learn from? Intelligence is sometimes not knowing \u2014 to know one's not-knowing, to be skilled at asking, to seek the answer. The barrier before you does not require strength, it requires craft. Craft sometimes requires tools, sometimes a friend.",guidanceEn:"Today, consult someone you trust about a matter you are struggling to resolve \u2014 or seek a book, article, or podcast on the subject. Crow transmits the knowledge accumulated through each generation; the accumulations of your generation are already around you. Reach out to them."},{id:"a045",name:"Sincap",emoji:"\ud83d\udc3f\ufe0f",element:"hava",symbolism:["birikim","haz\u0131rl\u0131k","ne\u015fe","\xe7eviklik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Sciurus_vulgaris_qtl1.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Sincap, Anadolu ormanlar\u0131nda \xe7ocukluk masallar\u0131n\u0131n ve halk hikayelerinin sevimli bilgesidir; 'K\u0131\u015f gelmeden haz\u0131rla' \xf6\u011f\xfcd\xfcn\xfcn canl\u0131 simgesi olarak orman k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde derin bir yeri vard\u0131r. Topra\u011fa g\xf6md\xfc\u011f\xfc pek \xe7ok f\u0131st\u0131\u011f\u0131 unuttu\u011fu i\xe7in asl\u0131nda orman\u0131n en b\xfcy\xfck a\u011fa\xe7 diktirenidir \u2014 bilmeden b\xfcy\xfck iyilikler yapar bu \xf6zelli\u011fi, beklenmedik hay\u0131rseverli\u011fin metaforu. Norse mitolojisinde Ratatosk adl\u0131 sincap, d\xfcnya a\u011fac\u0131 Yggdrasil boyunca ko\u015farak kartal ile y\u0131lan aras\u0131nda mesaj ta\u015f\u0131r \u2014 hem haberci hem de kavga k\xf6r\xfckleyen, bilginin ta\u015f\u0131nmas\u0131n\u0131n iki y\xf6nl\xfc do\u011fas\u0131n\u0131 simgeler. Kelt gelene\u011finde sincap, c\xf6mertli\u011fin ve ileriye haz\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131n koruyucusudur; sonbahar ayinlerinde sincap imgeleri \xf6ne \xe7\u0131kar ve gelecek ku\u015faklara haz\u0131rl\u0131k anlam\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131r. Kuzey Amerika yerli anlat\u0131m\u0131nda sincap, '\u0130yi \u015eeyler Biriktir' \xf6\u011fretmeninin ta kendisidir; yaln\u0131zca besin de\u011fil, iyilik, s\xf6z ve niyet biriktirmeyi \xf6\u011fretir. Japon halk k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde sincap enerjisi ve ne\u015fesi, ya\u015fam\u0131n aktif taraf\u0131n\u0131 simgeler \u2014 her a\u011fa\xe7tan a\u011faca atlamak yeni olas\u0131l\u0131klara a\xe7\u0131k olmakt\u0131r. Sincab\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o kadar fazla biriktirmek ki kullanmamak, birikim kayg\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n ne\u015feyi ezmesi.",dailyMessage:"Sincap bug\xfcn sana haz\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131n ne\u015feli bir eylem oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Gelece\u011fi d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmek endi\u015feyle de\u011fil, merakla yap\u0131labilir \u2014 'nas\u0131l koruyaca\u011f\u0131m' yerine 'nas\u0131l b\xfcy\xfctece\u011fim' sorusu sormak, sincab\u0131n tarz\u0131d\u0131r. Bu hayvan k\u0131\u015f i\xe7in haz\u0131rlan\u0131r ama bunu \u015fark\u0131 s\xf6yleyerek yapar; her daldan dala atlay\u0131\u015f\u0131 bir oyun, her f\u0131st\u0131k g\xf6m\xfc\u015f\xfc bir umut tohumu. \u015eu an hayat\u0131nda uzun vadeli d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmekte zorland\u0131\u011f\u0131n bir alan var m\u0131 \u2014 para, sa\u011fl\u0131k, ili\u015fki, kariyer? Orada k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama anlaml\u0131 bir \u015fey biriktirmeye ba\u015flamak i\xe7in bug\xfcn ne yapabilirsin? Ve bunu yaparken kayg\u0131y\u0131 de\u011fil, \xf6ng\xf6r\xfcy\xfc yak\u0131t olarak kullanabilir misin?",guidance:"Bu hafta i\xe7inde k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama d\xfczenli bir birikim al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ba\u015flat\u0131n: G\xfcnde be\u015f dakika okumak, haftada bir kendinize k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir miktar para ay\u0131rmak, her g\xfcn bir dakika nefes egzersizi yapmak. Sincab\u0131n g\xfcc\xfc miktarda de\u011fil, d\xfczenliliktedir. K\xfc\xe7\xfck ama istikrarl\u0131 birikim, zamanla \u015fa\u015f\u0131rt\u0131c\u0131 sonu\xe7lar do\u011furur.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Squirrel",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["accumulation","preparation","joy","agility"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The squirrel is the beloved sage of childhood tales and folk stories in Anatolian forests; it holds a deep place in forest culture as the living symbol of the counsel 'prepare before winter comes.' Because it forgets many of the nuts it buries in the ground, it is actually the greatest tree-planter of the forest \u2014 unwittingly it does great good, a metaphor for unexpected kindness. In Norse mythology, the squirrel Ratatoskr runs along the world tree Yggdrasil carrying messages between the eagle and the serpent \u2014 both messenger and instigator, symbolizing the two-way nature of knowledge transmission. In Celtic tradition, the squirrel is the guardian of generosity and forward preparation; squirrel imagery appears prominently in autumn rites and carries the meaning of preparation for future generations. In North American native narrative, the squirrel is the teacher of 'Accumulate Good Things' \u2014 it teaches the gathering not only of food but of kindness, words, and intentions. In Japanese folk culture, the squirrel's energy and joy symbolize the active side of life \u2014 leaping from tree to tree is to be open to new possibilities. The shadow side of the squirrel: accumulating so much that one does not use it, the anxiety of accumulation crushing joy.",dailyMessageEn:"Squirrel reminds you today that preparation is a joyful act. Thinking of the future can be done not with worry but with curiosity \u2014 asking 'how will I grow it' rather than 'how will I protect it' is the squirrel's way. This animal prepares for winter but does so while singing; each leap from branch to branch is a play, each buried nut a seed of hope. Is there an area in your life right now where you struggle to think long-term \u2014 money, health, relationship, career? What can you do today to begin accumulating something small but meaningful there? And as you do, can you use foresight rather than anxiety as fuel?",guidanceEn:"This week, begin a small but regular accumulation habit: reading five minutes a day, setting aside a small amount of money each week, doing one minute of breathing exercise each day. The squirrel's power lies not in quantity but in regularity. Small but steady accumulation, over time, yields surprising results."},{id:"a046",name:"Yarasa",emoji:"\ud83e\udd87",element:"hava",symbolism:["ge\xe7i\u015f","sezgi","korku-y\xfczle\u015fme","yeniden do\u011fum"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Common_pipistrelle_(Pipistrellus_pipistrellus)_(8389169597).jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Yarasa, Anadolu ve T\xfcrk halk k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde karanl\u0131\u011f\u0131n gizemli sakini olarak hem \xe7ekinilen hem de b\xfcy\xfcl\xfc bulunan bir varl\u0131kt\u0131r; ma\u011faralarda ya\u015famas\u0131 onu yeralt\u0131 ile yery\xfcz\xfc aras\u0131ndaki s\u0131n\u0131r b\xf6lgesinin bek\xe7isi yapar. Baz\u0131 Orta Asya gelene\u011finde yarasa derisi \u015faman kost\xfcmlerine dikilir \xe7\xfcnk\xfc yarasa g\xf6r\xfcnmeyeni 'duyar' \u2014 ekolokasyon g\xfcc\xfc, ruhsal \xe2lemdeki alg\u0131 kapasitesinin metaforudur. \xc7in k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde yarasa (Fu) mutlulu\u011fun ve \u015fans\u0131n sembol\xfcd\xfcr; be\u015f yarasa fig\xfcr\xfc be\u015f nimeti temsil eder \u2014 uzun \xf6m\xfcr, zenginlik, sa\u011fl\u0131k, erdem ve huzurlu \xf6l\xfcm. Aztek mitolojisinde Camazotz adl\u0131 yarasa tanr\u0131s\u0131, yeralt\u0131 d\xfcnyas\u0131n\u0131n haberini ta\u015f\u0131r ve kurbanlar\u0131n ba\u015f\u0131n\u0131 kopar\u0131r \u2014 \xf6l\xfcmle hesapla\u015fman\u0131n en \xe7arp\u0131c\u0131 imgelerinden biridir. Mayan gelene\u011finde yarasa, yeniden do\u011fumun ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn kutsal simgesidir; ma\u011faradan \xe7\u0131kan yarasa, \xf6teki d\xfcnyadan gelen bilginin bu d\xfcnyaya ta\u015f\u0131nmas\u0131d\u0131r. Kelt anlat\u0131m\u0131nda ise yarasa, g\xfcnbat\u0131m\u0131nda a\u015fikar olan \u015feyin d\xfc\u015f\xfcncelerde nas\u0131l kayboldu\u011funu g\xf6sterir \u2014 bilin\xe7 ve bilin\xe7d\u0131\u015f\u0131 aras\u0131ndaki alacakaranl\u0131k varl\u0131\u011f\u0131. Yarasan\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: karanl\u0131\u011fa o kadar al\u0131\u015fmak ki \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa \xe7\u0131kamamak, bilinmeyen ter\xf6rden donup kalmak.",dailyMessage:"Yarasa bug\xfcn seni bir e\u015fi\u011fe davet ediyor \u2014 karanl\u0131k bir alana, bilinmeyene do\u011fru. Bu \xe7a\u011fr\u0131 korkutucu gelebilir, ama \u015funu bil: Yarasa karanl\u0131kta g\xf6rmez, karanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\u015fitir. G\xf6zlerinden de\u011fil, titre\u015fimlerinden \xf6\u011frenir. Peki sen \u015fu an hayat\u0131nda neye karanl\u0131k diyorsun \u2014 ama asl\u0131nda sadece hen\xfcz tan\u0131\u015fmad\u0131\u011f\u0131n bir alan? Ses \xe7\u0131kar ve yank\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 dinle. Korku genellikle ger\xe7ek tehlikeden de\u011fil, bilinmezden gelir. Bir e\u015fiktesin: eski sen bu ma\u011faran\u0131n i\xe7inde kalmak istiyor, yeni sen \xe7\u0131kmak istiyor. Bu ge\xe7i\u015f ac\u0131s\u0131z olmaz \u2014 ama zorunludur. Yarasa do\u011far ve an\u0131nda u\xe7may\u0131 \xf6\u011frenir. Sen de haz\u0131r oldu\u011fundan daha haz\u0131rs\u0131n.",guidance:"Bu hafta i\xe7inde en \xe7ok korktu\u011funuz ama i\xe7ten i\xe7e merak etti\u011finiz bir \u015feye k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir ad\u0131m at\u0131n \u2014 bunu ara\u015ft\u0131rmak, birine sormak ya da sessizce g\xf6z atmak olabilir. Yarasa korkunun i\xe7inden ge\xe7erek yol bulur; ayn\u0131 \u015fekilde siz de bir ad\u0131m atarak korkunuzun ger\xe7ek boyutunu ke\u015ffedeceksiniz. \xc7o\u011fu zaman d\xfc\u015f\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfczden \xe7ok daha k\xfc\xe7\xfckt\xfcr.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Bat",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["transition","intuition","facing fear","rebirth"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The bat is the mysterious dweller of darkness in Anatolian and Turkic folk culture, both feared and considered magical; living in caves makes it the keeper of the borderland between the underworld and earth. In some Central Asian traditions, bat skin is sewn into shamanic costumes because the bat 'hears' the unseen \u2014 its echolocation is a metaphor for perceptive capacity in the spiritual realm. In Chinese culture, the bat (Fu) is the symbol of happiness and luck; the figure of five bats represents the five blessings \u2014 long life, wealth, health, virtue, and peaceful death. In Aztec mythology, the bat god Camazotz carries the news of the underworld and severs the heads of sacrifices \u2014 one of the most striking images of reckoning with death. In Mayan tradition, the bat is the sacred symbol of rebirth and transformation; emerging from the cave, the bat carries knowledge from the other world into this one. In Celtic narrative, the bat shows how that which is revealed at sunset becomes lost in thought \u2014 the twilight being between consciousness and the unconscious. The shadow side of the bat: becoming so accustomed to darkness that one cannot emerge into the light, freezing in the terror of the unknown.",dailyMessageEn:"Bat invites you today to a threshold \u2014 to a dark area, toward the unknown. This call may feel frightening, but know this: Bat does not see in the darkness, it hears the darkness. It learns not from its eyes but from its vibrations. What in your life are you calling dark \u2014 but is actually only an area you have not yet met? Make a sound and listen to its echo. Fear usually comes not from real danger but from the unknown. You are at a threshold: the old self wishes to remain in this cave, the new self wishes to emerge. This passage will not be painless \u2014 but it is necessary. The bat is born and immediately learns to fly. You too are more ready than you know.",guidanceEn:"This week, take a small step toward something you most fear yet secretly are curious about \u2014 researching it, asking someone, or quietly looking it over. The bat finds its way through fear; in the same way, you will discover the true size of your fear by taking a step. Most often, it is far smaller than you imagined."},{id:"a047",name:"Yenge\xe7",emoji:"\ud83e\udd80",element:"su",symbolism:["s\u0131n\u0131r","ev","duygu","geri \xe7ekilme"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/CallinectesSapidusOregon.JPG&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Yenge\xe7, Ege ve Akdeniz k\u0131y\u0131lar\u0131nda ya\u015fayan Anadolu halklar\u0131 i\xe7in hem besin hem de sembol olarak k\xf6kl\xfc bir yere sahiptir; k\u0131y\u0131 gelene\u011finde yenge\xe7 yan y\xfcr\xfcy\xfc\u015f\xfc, sezgisel ve dolamba\xe7l\u0131 ilerlemenin, direkt olmayan ama etkili bir yolun imgesidir. Anadolu Rum ve Laz k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde ay d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcne ba\u011fl\u0131 deniz hayvanlar\u0131 kutsald\u0131r ve yenge\xe7 bu d\xf6ng\xfcn\xfcn en belirgin temsilcisidir. Antik M\u0131s\u0131r'da Skarabeus'un yenge\xe7 e\u015fde\u011feri, yeniden do\u011fum ve d\xf6ng\xfcn\xfcn sembol\xfcd\xfcr; kabuk de\u011fi\u015ftirmek ruhun ar\u0131nmas\u0131 olarak yorumlan\u0131r. Mezopotamya astrolojisinde Yenge\xe7 burcu, ana\xe7 suyun, annenin korumas\u0131n\u0131n ve duygusal derinli\u011fin simgesidir; bu bur\xe7 Ay'la y\xf6netilir ve Ay kadar de\u011fi\u015fken ve derin oldu\u011fu d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcl\xfcr. Kelt gelene\u011finde deniz hayvanlar\u0131, \xd6teki D\xfcnya'n\u0131n deniz alt\u0131nda bulundu\u011fu inanc\u0131yla ba\u011flant\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r; yenge\xe7 evini s\u0131rt\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131yarak her yerde g\xfcvenli alan yarat\u0131r. Kuzey Amerika yerli k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde denizy\u0131ld\u0131z\u0131 ve yenge\xe7 gibi hayvanlar, hassasiyetin ve s\u0131n\u0131r koruyuculu\u011funun \xf6\u011fretmenleridir. Yenge\xe7in g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: kabu\u011fun i\xe7ine o kadar \xe7ekilmek ki b\xfcy\xfcmek i\xe7in gerekli savunmas\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ya\u015fayamamak.",dailyMessage:"Yenge\xe7 bug\xfcn sana duygusal g\xfcvenli\u011fin ne demek oldu\u011funu soruyor. Bu hayvan k\u0131\u015fk\u0131rt\u0131lmadan sald\u0131rmaz \u2014 ama k\u0131\u015fk\u0131rt\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda pen\xe7eleri g\xfc\xe7l\xfcd\xfcr. Ve evini s\u0131rt\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131r; nerede olursa olsun, i\xe7i g\xfcvende. Sen \u015fu an i\xe7ini nerede g\xfcvende hissediyorsun? O alan ger\xe7ekten korunuyor mu? Birileri bu alan\u0131 ihlal ediyor mu \u2014 izniniz olmadan, s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 g\xf6rmezden gelerek? Geri \xe7ekilmek zay\u0131fl\u0131k de\u011fildir. Kabu\u011funa girmek, toparlanmak, biraz sessizlikte kalmak \u2014 bunlar dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n bir par\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r. Pen\xe7elerini ne zaman kullanman gerekiyor, ne zaman kabu\u011funda kalman? Bu fark\u0131 bug\xfcn i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcnle tart\u0131\u015fman\u0131 istiyor Yenge\xe7.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn ya da bu hafta i\xe7inde hayat\u0131n\u0131zda bir 'hay\u0131r' prati\u011fi yap\u0131n: Sizi yorgunla\u015ft\u0131ran, t\xfcketen ama 'ay\u0131p olur' diye kabul etti\u011finiz bir daveti, iste\u011fi ya da y\xfck\xfcml\xfcl\xfc\u011f\xfc nazik\xe7e reddedin. Yenge\xe7 pen\xe7esi nettir \u2014 ama zarif. S\u0131n\u0131r koymak, ili\u015fkiyi bitirmek de\u011fil, onu s\xfcrd\xfcr\xfclebilir k\u0131lmakt\u0131r.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Crab",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["boundary","home","emotion","withdrawal"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The crab holds a deep place for the Anatolian peoples living along the Aegean and Mediterranean coasts, both as nourishment and symbol; in coastal tradition, the crab's sideways walk is the image of intuitive, winding progress \u2014 an indirect yet effective path. In Anatolian Greek and Laz cultures, sea creatures linked to the moon cycle are sacred, and the crab is the most prominent representative of this cycle. In ancient Egypt, the crab's equivalent of the Scarabeus is the symbol of rebirth and the cycle; shedding the shell is interpreted as the soul's purification. In Mesopotamian astrology, the sign of Cancer is the symbol of nurturing water, mother's protection, and emotional depth; this sign is ruled by the moon and is considered as variable and deep as the moon. In Celtic tradition, sea creatures are linked to the belief that the Otherworld lies beneath the sea; the crab, carrying its home on its back, creates safe space wherever it goes. In North American native culture, animals like the starfish and crab are teachers of sensitivity and boundary-keeping. The shadow side of the crab: withdrawing so deeply into the shell that one cannot live the vulnerability needed for growth.",dailyMessageEn:"Crab asks you today what emotional safety means. This animal does not attack unprovoked \u2014 but when provoked, its claws are strong. And it carries its home on its back; wherever it is, its inside is safe. Where do you feel safe within yourself right now? Is that space truly being protected? Is someone violating it \u2014 without your permission, ignoring your boundaries? Withdrawing is not weakness. Going into your shell, gathering yourself, staying a while in silence \u2014 these are part of resilience. When must you use your claws, and when must you stay in your shell? Crab wants you to discern this difference with your instinct today.",guidanceEn:"This day or this week, practice a 'no' in your life: gently decline an invitation, request, or obligation you accepted out of social pressure that depletes you. The crab's claw is clear \u2014 but graceful. Setting a boundary does not end the relationship; it makes it sustainable."},{id:"a048",name:"Fil",emoji:"\ud83d\udc18",element:"toprak",symbolism:["bellek","bilgelik","\u015fefkat","g\xfc\xe7"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/African_Bush_Elephant.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Fil, Anadolu'da do\u011fal ya\u015fam hayvan\u0131 olmasa da Mevlana'n\u0131n Mesnevi'sinde en derin hikayelerin birini ta\u015f\u0131r: Karanl\u0131k odadaki fil, herkesin yaln\u0131zca dokundu\u011fu k\u0131sm\u0131 tarif eder \u2014 biri 's\xfctun', di\u011feri 'yelpaze', di\u011feri 'duvar' der. Hakikat par\xe7alara b\xf6l\xfcn\xfcr ama fil tektir. Hint mitolojisinde Ganesha, fil ba\u015fl\u0131 tanr\u0131, ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7lar\u0131n, bilgeli\u011fin ve engellerin a\u015f\u0131lmas\u0131n\u0131n koruyucusudur; herhangi bir yeni giri\u015fimde \xf6nce Ganesha'ya dua edilir. Budizm'de beyaz fil, ayd\u0131nlanman\u0131n sembol\xfcd\xfcr; Buda'n\u0131n do\u011fumundan \xf6nce annesinin r\xfcyas\u0131nda beyaz bir fil g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfc rivayet edilir. Afrika gelene\u011finde fil toplulu\u011fun haf\u0131zas\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 en ya\u015fl\u0131 di\u015fi, suyun yerini, \xf6l\xfcm\xfcn oldu\u011fu alanlar\u0131, ge\xe7mi\u015fin izlerini ta\u015f\u0131r; o olmadan s\xfcr\xfc yolunu kaybeder. Kelt mitolojisinde mamut imgesi, k\u0131\u015f ge\xe7irmeyi bilen ve \xf6l\xfcm so\u011fu\u011funda bile ya\u015famaya devam eden dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n simgesidir. Taoizm'de fil, a\u011f\u0131r ama sessiz, g\xfc\xe7l\xfc ama nazik bir y\xfcr\xfcy\xfc\u015fle 'eylemsiz eylem'in prati\u011fini \xf6\u011fretir. Filin g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: haf\u0131zan\u0131n kine d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmesi, ba\u011f\u0131\u015flamadan anmak, ge\xe7mi\u015fi bir kalkan gibi ta\u015f\u0131mak.",dailyMessage:"Fil bug\xfcn sana iki \u015feyi ayn\u0131 anda hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor: Hem b\xfcy\xfckl\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc hem de hassasiyetini. Bu hayvan tonlarca a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131yla hassas bir \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi ezmeden ge\xe7ebilir \u2014 \xe7\xfcnk\xfc her ad\u0131m\u0131n a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n fark\u0131ndad\u0131r. Sen \u015fu an ne kadar dikkatli y\xfcr\xfcyorsun? Ge\xe7mi\u015ften hangi dersi h\xe2l\xe2 ta\u015f\u0131yorsun ve bu ders seni mi ayd\u0131nlat\u0131yor, yoksa senin i\xe7in mi karar veriyor? Fil affeder ama unutmaz \u2014 bu dengeyi kendi hayat\u0131nda nas\u0131l kuruyorsun? Bir ili\u015fkide, bir ge\xe7mi\u015f k\u0131r\u0131lmada ya da kendi kendinle olan bir hesapta bu denge nerede duruyor? B\xfcy\xfck varl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011frenip sonra yava\u015f\xe7a, dikkatle, sars\u0131lmaz bir huzurla hareket et. Her ad\u0131m\u0131n \xf6nemli.",guidance:"Ge\xe7mi\u015fte ya\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z ve h\xe2l\xe2 ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir deneyimi d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcn. Bir ka\u011f\u0131da \u015funlar\u0131 yaz\u0131n: 'Bu bana ne \xf6\u011fretti?' ve 'Bunu art\u0131k b\u0131rakmak i\xe7in neye ihtiyac\u0131m var?' Fil bilgeli\u011fi dersi \xf6\u011frenir ama y\xfck\xfc ta\u015f\u0131maz. Bu pratik, haf\u0131zay\u0131 g\xfcce d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrmenin ilk ad\u0131m\u0131d\u0131r.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Elephant",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["memory","wisdom","compassion","strength"],anatolianMeaningEn:"Although not a native animal of Anatolia, the elephant bears one of the deepest stories in Rumi's Mathnawi: the elephant in the dark room, where each person describes only the part they have touched \u2014 one says 'pillar,' another 'fan,' another 'wall.' Truth is divided into pieces, but the elephant is one. In Hindu mythology, Ganesha, the elephant-headed god, is the guardian of beginnings, wisdom, and the overcoming of obstacles; before any new undertaking, one prays first to Ganesha. In Buddhism, the white elephant is the symbol of enlightenment; it is told that before Buddha's birth, his mother saw a white elephant in her dream. In African tradition, the elephant is the memory of the community \u2014 the oldest female carries the location of water, the places of death, the traces of the past; without her, the herd loses its way. In Celtic mythology, the mammoth image is the symbol of endurance, knowing how to weather winter and continuing to live even in the cold of death. In Taoism, the elephant teaches the practice of 'effortless action' with a heavy yet silent, strong yet gentle walk. The shadow side of the elephant: memory turning into resentment, remembering without forgiving, carrying the past like a shield.",dailyMessageEn:"Elephant reminds you today of two things simultaneously: both your greatness and your sensitivity. This animal can pass over a delicate flower without crushing it despite its many tons \u2014 because it is aware of the weight of each step. How carefully are you walking right now? Which lesson from the past are you still carrying, and does that lesson illuminate you or decide for you? The elephant forgives but does not forget \u2014 how do you build this balance in your own life? In a relationship, in a past wound, or in an account you keep with yourself, where does this balance stand? Learn your great presence, then move slowly, carefully, with unshakable peace. Every step matters.",guidanceEn:"Think of an experience from the past that you still carry. Write on a piece of paper: 'What did this teach me?' and 'What do I need to finally release this?' Elephant wisdom learns the lesson but does not carry the burden. This practice is the first step in turning memory into strength."},{id:"a049",name:"Va\u015fak",emoji:"\ud83d\udc08\u200d\u2b1b",element:"toprak",symbolism:["s\u0131r saklama","keskin g\xf6r\xfc","yaln\u0131zl\u0131k","kadim bilgi"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Lynx_lynx2.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Va\u015fak, Anadolu ormanlar\u0131n\u0131n en az g\xf6r\xfclen, en az anla\u015f\u0131lan ama en derin s\u0131rlar\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yan avc\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; Karadeniz ve Do\u011fu Anadolu da\u011flar\u0131nda iz b\u0131rakan bu hayvan, k\xf6y k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde \xe7o\u011funlukla efsane boyutunda kal\u0131r \u2014 g\xf6renler \xe7ok azd\u0131r ama varl\u0131\u011f\u0131na herkes inan\u0131r. \u015eamanist gelenekte va\u015fak, gizli bilginin ve s\u0131rr\u0131n koruyucusudur; onu r\xfcyada g\xf6rmek, hen\xfcz bilinmeyen ama yakla\u015fan bir ger\xe7e\u011fi haber verir. Kuzey Amerika yerli gelene\u011finde Va\u015fak, 'S\u0131rlar\u0131n Bek\xe7isi'dir \u2014 onun enerjisiyle \xe7al\u0131\u015fan biri, s\xf6ylenmeyeni duyar, g\xf6sterilmeyeni g\xf6r\xfcr; dedikodu ve y\xfczeysel bilgiyle ilgilenmez, ger\xe7e\u011fi arar. Kelt mitolojisinde s\u0131n\u0131r varl\u0131klar\u0131 \u2014 g\xf6r\xfcnmez d\xfcnyayla g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr d\xfcnya aras\u0131nda ya\u015fayanlar \u2014 kediler ve vah\u015fi kedilerdir; va\u015fak bu ailenin en kudretli \xfcyesidir. \u0130skandinav gelene\u011finde Freya'n\u0131n arabas\u0131n\u0131 \xe7eken iki b\xfcy\xfck kedi va\u015fa\u011fa benzer; onlar g\xfc\xe7 ve ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131n tanr\u0131sal temsilcileridir. Tibet'te yaln\u0131z ya\u015fayan g\xfc\xe7l\xfc kedi t\xfcrleri, meditasyon ustalar\u0131n\u0131n hayvan sembolleriyle ili\u015fkilendirilir \u2014 yaln\u0131zl\u0131k bilgeli\u011fin okulu, sessizlik ger\xe7e\u011fin dilidir. Va\u015fa\u011f\u0131n g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: yaln\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\xe7e kapanmaya \xe7evirmek, bildi\u011fini payla\u015fmamak ve b\xf6ylece d\xfcnyayla k\xf6pr\xfcy\xfc koparmak.",dailyMessage:"Va\u015fak bug\xfcn sana g\xf6rmedi\u011finin g\xf6r\xfclmedi\u011fi bir hakikati hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Bu hayvan g\xf6r\xfcnmeden g\xf6zlemler; av\u0131n\u0131 saatlerce izler, sessizce yakla\u015f\u0131r, tam zaman\u0131nda harekete ge\xe7er. Sen etraf\u0131nda olmakta oldu\u011funun ka\xe7\u0131n\u0131 ger\xe7ekten g\xf6r\xfcyorsun? S\xf6ylenmeyenler, saklan\u0131lanlar, y\xfczeyin alt\u0131nda akan ger\xe7ekler \u2014 bug\xfcn bunlara dikkat et. Va\u015fak enerjisi sana bir \u015feyi s\xf6yl\xfcyor: Herkesin g\xf6remedi\u011fini g\xf6r\xfcyorsun, herkesin anlayamad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 anl\u0131yorsun. Bu bir y\xfck olabilir \u2014 ya da bir g\xfc\xe7. Ama bu g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfc yaln\u0131zca korkuyla ta\u015f\u0131ma; onu bilgelikle ta\u015f\u0131. Baz\u0131 \u015feyleri bilmek i\xe7in konu\u015fmak gerekmez. Sessizli\u011fin i\xe7inde bu netli\u011fi koru.",guidance:"Bu hafta boyunca bir g\xf6zlem prati\u011fi yap\u0131n: G\xfcnde bir kez, etraf\u0131n\u0131zda s\xf6ylenmeden akan bir ger\xe7e\u011fi \u2014 bir ili\u015fkide, bir ortamda, kendinizde \u2014 fark edin ve bunu bir deftere not edin. Va\u015fak g\xfcc\xfc birikmektedir; g\xf6zlemledik\xe7e g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcz derinle\u015fir ve zamanla sizi \xe7ok \xf6tesine g\xf6t\xfcrecek bir i\xe7g\xf6r\xfc kap\u0131s\u0131 a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Lynx",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["keeping secrets","keen sight","solitude","ancient knowledge"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The lynx is the least seen, least understood, yet deepest secret-bearing hunter of the Anatolian forests; this animal leaving its tracks in the Black Sea and Eastern Anatolian mountains often remains in the realm of legend in village culture \u2014 those who have seen it are very few, but everyone believes in its existence. In shamanic tradition, the lynx is the guardian of hidden knowledge and secret; seeing it in a dream foretells an as-yet-unknown but approaching truth. In North American native tradition, Lynx is the 'Keeper of Secrets' \u2014 one who works with its energy hears what is unsaid, sees what is not shown; it is not concerned with gossip or surface knowledge, it seeks truth. In Celtic mythology, boundary beings \u2014 those living between the unseen and seen world \u2014 are cats and wild cats; the lynx is the most powerful member of this family. In Scandinavian tradition, the two great cats pulling Freya's chariot resemble lynxes; they are divine representatives of strength and independence. In Tibet, solitary powerful cat species are associated with the animal symbols of meditation masters \u2014 solitude is the school of wisdom, silence is the language of truth. The shadow side of the lynx: turning solitude into withdrawal, not sharing what one knows and thus severing the bridge with the world.",dailyMessageEn:"Lynx reminds you today of a truth that the unseen of you is not unseen. This animal observes without being seen; it watches its prey for hours, approaches silently, acts at the exact moment. How much of what is happening around you do you truly see? The unsaid, the hidden, the truths flowing beneath the surface \u2014 pay attention to these today. Lynx energy tells you something: You see what others cannot see, you understand what others cannot grasp. This may be a burden \u2014 or it may be a power. But do not carry this sight with fear alone; carry it with wisdom. To know certain things, one need not speak. Within your silence, preserve this clarity.",guidanceEn:"Practice an observation exercise throughout this week: once a day, notice a truth flowing unspoken around you \u2014 in a relationship, an environment, in yourself \u2014 and note it in a journal. Lynx power accumulates; as you observe, your sight deepens, and over time a door of insight far beyond opens."},{id:"a050",name:"\xd6r\xfcmcek",emoji:"\ud83d\udd77\ufe0f",element:"hava",symbolism:["dokuma","kader","yarat\u0131m","sab\u0131r"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/European_garden_spider_(Araneus_diadematus).jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"\xd6r\xfcmcek, \u0130slam gelene\u011finde \xf6zel ve kutsal bir yere sahiptir; Hz. Muhammed Mekke'den Medine'ye hicret ederken s\u0131\u011f\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131 Sevr ma\u011faras\u0131n\u0131n giri\u015fini bir \xf6r\xfcmcek a\u011f\u0131yla kaplam\u0131\u015f ve bu a\u011f d\xfc\u015fmanlar\u0131 geri \xe7evirmi\u015ftir. Bu anlat\u0131 \xf6r\xfcmce\u011fi koruman\u0131n ve ilahi yard\u0131m\u0131n simgesi haline getirir \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir varl\u0131\u011f\u0131n b\xfcy\xfck tarihi de\u011fi\u015ftirmesi. Anadolu halk k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde \xf6r\xfcmcek \xf6ld\xfcrmek u\u011fursuz say\u0131l\u0131r; '\xf6r\xfcmce\u011fi \xf6ld\xfcrme, evine bereket gelir' s\xf6z\xfc yayg\u0131nd\u0131r. Afrika Akan gelene\u011finde Anansi, d\xfcnyalar\u0131n en ak\u0131ll\u0131 yarat\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve hikayelerin ilk sahibi olan \xf6r\xfcmcek tanr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; onun hikayeleri olmadan d\xfcnya manalar\u0131 yitirirdi \u2014 yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131k ve dili o tutar. Kuzey Amerika Navajo gelene\u011finde \xd6r\xfcmcek Kad\u0131n (Spider Woman), ilk dokuyan ve insanlara hem sanat\u0131 hem de varolu\u015fun anlam\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011fretendir; hayat\u0131n a\u011f\u0131 onun elindedir. Hint mitolojisinde Maya \u2014 ill\xfczyon \u2014 bir a\u011f metaforuyla anlat\u0131l\u0131r; a\u011f ger\xe7ekmi\u015f gibi g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr ama dokuyan ger\xe7ektir. Japon gelene\u011finde Jor\u014dgumo adl\u0131 \xf6r\xfcmcek varl\u0131k, d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn ve gizli g\xfcc\xfcn simgesidir. \xd6r\xfcmce\u011fin g\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: a\u011fa o kadar g\xfcvenmek ki a\u011f\u0131n d\u0131\u015f\u0131nda bir ya\u015fam hayal edememek, kendi yaratt\u0131\u011f\u0131n tuza\u011fa d\xfc\u015fmek.",dailyMessage:"\xd6r\xfcmcek bug\xfcn sana \u015funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor: Hayat\u0131n\u0131n a\u011f\u0131n\u0131 sen \xf6r\xfcyorsun. Her karar bir iplik, her ili\u015fki bir d\xfc\u011f\xfcm, her niyet bir ba\u011flant\u0131 noktas\u0131. Ama a\u011f\u0131 \xf6rerken merkeze d\xf6nd\xfc\u011f\xfcnde \u2014 tam ortada durdu\u011funda \u2014 orada kim var? D\xfc\u015f\xfcncelerin mi, korkular\u0131n m\u0131, tutkular\u0131n m\u0131? \xd6r\xfcmcek merkezden \xf6rmeye ba\u015flar; kendi \xf6z\xfcnden d\u0131\u015far\u0131ya do\u011fru geni\u015fler. Bug\xfcn sen hangi merkezden \xf6r\xfcyorsun? E\u011fer a\u011f\u0131n kar\u0131\u015f\u0131ksa, korkuyla m\u0131 yoksa g\xfc\xe7le mi \xf6r\xfcld\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc sor kendine. Bir iplik kopsa \xf6r\xfcmcek paniklemez \u2014 onar\u0131r, yeniden ba\u011flar ve \xf6rmeye devam eder. Hayat\u0131nda hangi iplik koptu ve sen onu hen\xfcz onarmad\u0131n? Onarmak i\xe7in bug\xfcn k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir ad\u0131m at.",guidance:"Bu hafta yarat\u0131c\u0131 bir eylem ger\xe7ekle\u015ftirin: Yazmak, \xe7izmek, pi\u015firmek, bir \u015fey in\u015fa etmek, bir plan tasarlamak \u2014 ne olursa olsun elinizle ve zihninizle bir \u015fey yarat\u0131n. \xd6r\xfcmcek a\u011f\u0131n\u0131 her g\xfcn yeniler; siz de yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 bir al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k haline getirin. K\xfc\xe7\xfck ama d\xfczenli yarat\u0131m, zamanla hayat\u0131n\u0131z\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc a\u011f\u0131n\u0131 kurar.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Spider",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["weaving","fate","creation","patience"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The spider holds a special and sacred place in Islamic tradition; when the Prophet Muhammad emigrated from Mecca to Medina, the entrance of the cave of Thawr where he took shelter was covered by a spider's web, and this web turned the enemies back. This narrative makes the spider a symbol of protection and divine aid \u2014 a small but powerful being changing great history. In Anatolian folk culture, killing a spider is considered ill-omened; the saying 'do not kill the spider, abundance comes to your home' is widespread. In African Akan tradition, Anansi is the wisest creature in the worlds and the spider god who first owned stories; without his stories the world would lose its meanings \u2014 he holds creativity and language. In North American Navajo tradition, Spider Woman is the first weaver and the one who taught humanity both art and the meaning of existence; the web of life is in her hands. In Hindu mythology, Maya \u2014 illusion \u2014 is told through the metaphor of a web; the web seems real, but the weaver is real. In Japanese tradition, the spider being called Jor\u014dgumo is the symbol of transformation and hidden power. The shadow side of the spider: trusting the web so much that one cannot imagine a life outside it, falling into the trap one has spun.",dailyMessageEn:"Spider reminds you today: You are weaving the web of your life. Every decision is a thread, every relationship a knot, every intention a point of connection. But as you weave, when you return to the center \u2014 when you stand exactly at the middle \u2014 who is there? Your thoughts, your fears, your passions? Spider begins to weave from the center; it expands outward from its own essence. From what center are you weaving today? If your web is tangled, ask yourself whether it was woven with fear or with power. If a thread breaks, the spider does not panic \u2014 it repairs, reconnects, and continues weaving. Which thread has broken in your life that you have not yet mended? Take a small step today to repair it.",guidanceEn:"Carry out a creative act this week: writing, drawing, cooking, building something, designing a plan \u2014 whatever it is, create something with your hands and mind. The spider renews its web each day; make your creativity a habit. Small but regular creation, over time, builds the most powerful web of your life."},{id:"a051",name:"Ku\u011fu",emoji:"\ud83e\udda2",element:"su",symbolism:["d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","safl\u0131k","incelik","ruh yolculu\u011fu"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Mute_swan_Vrhnika.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"T\xfcrk ve Altay \u015famanizminde ku\u011fu, \u015faman\u0131n g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfc yolculu\u011funun kutsal arac\u0131d\u0131r; beyaz kanatlar\u0131 alt d\xfcnya ile \xfcst d\xfcnya aras\u0131ndaki ge\xe7i\u015fi simgeler, ulumas\u0131 ise ruhlar\u0131n sesini ta\u015f\u0131r. Kazak ve K\u0131rg\u0131z destanlar\u0131nda ku\u011fu k\u0131z motifi \u2014 bir insan bedene b\xfcr\xfcnm\xfc\u015f g\xf6k ruhudur; kanatlar\u0131 \xe7al\u0131n\u0131rsa d\xfcnyaya ba\u011flan\u0131r, geri al\u0131rsa u\xe7ar gider. Kelt gelene\u011finde Caer \u0130ormeith efsanesinde ku\u011fu, tanr\u0131lar\u0131n a\u015fk dilidir \u2014 her iki y\u0131lda bir insan ile ku\u011fu formu aras\u0131nda d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm ge\xe7irir, bu da ruhun asla tek bir bi\xe7imde kalmamas\u0131 gerekti\u011fini \xf6\u011fretir. Norse mitolojisinde Valk\xfcr sava\u015f tanr\u0131\xe7alar\u0131 ku\u011fu bi\xe7imine b\xfcr\xfcnerek g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfcnde u\xe7arlard\u0131; \xf6l\xfc sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131n ruhlar\u0131n\u0131 Valhalla'ya ta\u015f\u0131yan kutsal haberci. Hint gelene\u011finde Hamsa \u2014 kutsal ku\u011fu \u2014 Brahma'n\u0131n binitidir ve saf bilgeli\u011fin simgesidir; s\xfct ile suyu birbirinden ay\u0131rabildi\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131r, t\u0131pk\u0131 bilgenin ger\xe7e\u011fi yanl\u0131\u015ftan ay\u0131rmas\u0131 gibi. Ku\u011funun t\u0131bb\u0131: y\xfczeyde zarifken suda g\xfc\xe7l\xfc kanatlarla k\xfcrek \xe7ekmektir \u2014 g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr g\xfczellik, g\xf6r\xfcnmez eme\u011fin meyvesidir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: safl\u0131k tak\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131, ger\xe7ek duygular\u0131 bast\u0131rmak ve her \u015feyi g\xfczel g\xf6stermek u\u011fruna i\xe7teki karanl\u0131ktan ka\xe7mak.",dailyMessage:"Ku\u011fu bug\xfcn seni i\xe7eriden d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmeye, yaln\u0131zca d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan de\u011fil derinden de\u011fi\u015fmeye \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131yor. Bu ku\u015fun suda hareketi bir s\u0131rra benzer: y\xfczeyde kusursuz bir s\xfcz\xfc\u015f g\xf6r\xfcrs\xfcn, ama suyun alt\u0131nda kanatlar h\u0131zla, durmaks\u0131z\u0131n \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r \u2014 hi\xe7 kimse o \xe7abay\u0131 g\xf6rmez. Sen de belki \u015fu an b\xf6ylesin: d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan sakin g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyorsun ama i\xe7inde b\xfcy\xfck bir d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm sanc\u0131s\u0131 var. Bu sanc\u0131y\u0131 saklamana gerek yok; d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc sahici k\u0131lmak i\xe7in \xf6nce onu kabul etmek gerekir. Kendine sor: ka\xe7 zamand\u0131r g\xfc\xe7l\xfc g\xf6r\xfcnmek i\xe7in zay\u0131fl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 gizliyorsun? Hangi d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm sanc\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 utanarak i\xe7inde sakl\u0131yorsun, oysa o sanc\u0131 tam da seni b\xfcy\xfcten \u015fey? Ku\u011fu bir sabah suya bakt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \xe7irkin \xf6rdek yavrulu\u011funu g\xf6rmez art\u0131k \u2014 ama o d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm birden olmaz, her k\xfcrek \xe7al\u0131\u015fta, her bekleyi\u015fte ger\xe7ekle\u015fir. Bug\xfcn zarafetini s\xfcrd\xfcrmek i\xe7in g\xf6sterdi\u011fin gizli \xe7abay\u0131 onurland\u0131r; o emek, senin ger\xe7ek g\xfczelli\u011findir.",guidance:"Bu ak\u015fam bir k\xe2\u011f\u0131t al\u0131n ve \u015fu soruyu yaz\u0131n: 'D\u0131\u015far\u0131dan g\xfczel g\xf6stermek i\xe7in i\xe7eriden ne \xf6d\xfcyorum?' Cevaplar\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 yarg\u0131lamadan, sadece g\xf6rerek yaz\u0131n. Sonra bu listedeki en a\u011f\u0131r olan\u0131 se\xe7in ve yar\u0131n, yaln\u0131zca bir ki\u015fiye ya da yaln\u0131zca kendinize, ger\xe7e\u011fi s\xf6yleyin. Sahici d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm, g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcrde de\u011fil \u2014 i\xe7te ba\u015flar.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Swan",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["transformation","purity","grace","soul journey"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Turkic and Altai shamanism, the swan is the sacred vehicle of the shaman's sky journey; its white wings symbolize the passage between the lower and upper worlds, and its call carries the voices of souls. In Kazakh and Kyrgyz epics, the swan-maiden motif appears as a sky spirit clothed in human form; if her wings are stolen she is bound to earth, if returned she flies away. In Celtic tradition, the legend of Caer Iormeith presents the swan as the love language of the gods, shifting every other year between human and swan form, teaching that the soul must never remain in a single shape. In Norse mythology, the Valkyries took swan form to fly across the sky, sacred messengers carrying fallen warriors' souls to Valhalla. In Hindu tradition the Hamsa, the sacred swan, is the mount of Brahma and the symbol of pure wisdom; it is said to separate milk from water just as the sage separates truth from falsehood. The swan's medicine is to row with powerful wings beneath the water while remaining graceful above; visible beauty is the fruit of invisible labor. Its shadow side is an obsession with purity, suppressing real feelings and fleeing the inner darkness in order to keep everything looking beautiful.",dailyMessageEn:"The Swan calls you today to transform from within, not merely on the surface but at the deepest layer. This bird's movement on water is like a secret: above, you see a flawless glide, but beneath the surface the wings work tirelessly, ceaselessly, and no one sees that effort. Perhaps you are like this right now: calm on the outside but with a great labor of transformation unfolding inside you. You do not need to hide this labor; to make transformation real, you must first acknowledge it. Ask yourself: how long have you been concealing your weakness in order to appear strong? Which pain of becoming are you hiding in shame, when that very pain is what is growing you? One morning the swan looks at the water and no longer sees an ugly duckling, but that transformation does not arrive all at once; it happens with every stroke, every patient wait. Today, honor the hidden effort behind your grace; that labor is your true beauty.",guidanceEn:"Tonight take a piece of paper and write this question: 'What am I paying inside in order to look beautiful outside?' Write your answers without judgment, simply by seeing them. Then choose the heaviest item on the list and tomorrow, to one person or to yourself alone, speak the truth. Real transformation does not begin where it shows; it begins within."},{id:"a052",name:"Kondor",emoji:"\ud83e\udd85",element:"hava",symbolism:["\xfcst d\xfcnya","ata ruhlar\u0131","\xf6l\xfcm k\xf6pr\xfcs\xfc","\xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Condor_California_Gymnogyps_californianus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"And Da\u011flar\u0131 \u015famanizminin en kutsal ku\u015fu olan kondor, Quechua gelene\u011finde Apuchin \u2014 da\u011f ruhlar\u0131n\u0131n habercisi \u2014 olarak bilinir; \xf6l\xfclerin ruhlar\u0131n\u0131 \xfcst d\xfcnyaya ta\u015f\u0131r ve ya\u015fayanlarla atalar aras\u0131nda k\xf6pr\xfc kurar. \u0130nka kozmolojisinde \xfc\xe7 d\xfcnya \xfc\xe7l\xfcs\xfc \u2014 Hanan Pacha (yukar\u0131 d\xfcnya), Kay Pacha (bu d\xfcnya) ve Ukhu Pacha (alt d\xfcnya) \u2014 aras\u0131ndaki ge\xe7i\u015fi sa\u011flayan varl\u0131k olarak kondora kutsal kozmik arabulucu rol\xfc verilmi\u015ftir. Kuzey Amerika B\xfcy\xfck Ova halklar\u0131n\u0131n baz\u0131lar\u0131nda kondor ile kartal i\xe7 i\xe7e ge\xe7er; her ikisi de g\xfcne\u015fe en yak\u0131n u\xe7abilen, dolay\u0131s\u0131yla ilahi mesajlar\u0131 en do\u011fru ta\u015f\u0131yan ku\u015flar olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr. Aztek gelene\u011finde ise \xf6l\xfc yiyen ku\u015flar \u2014 zopilote/kondor \u2014 temizleyici tanr\u0131sal varl\u0131klard\u0131r; \xf6l\xfcm\xfc tamamlayan, d\xf6ng\xfcy\xfc kapatan kutsal ellerdir. Afrika Maasai gelene\u011finde kartal ve kondor gibi b\xfcy\xfck kanatlar, atalarla konu\u015fma yetisini simgeler \u2014 dua y\xfcksekten u\xe7an ku\u015fla birlikte tanr\u0131ya iletilir. Kondorun t\u0131bb\u0131: y\xfcksekten bakan g\xf6z, k\xfc\xe7\xfck kay\u0131plar\u0131n birer ge\xe7i\u015f noktas\u0131 oldu\u011funu g\xf6r\xfcr; ac\u0131 da b\xfcy\xfck kanatlarla ta\u015f\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131nda u\xe7u\u015fa d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: \xf6lm\xfc\u015f olan\u0131 b\u0131rakmay\u0131 reddederek ge\xe7mi\u015fin \xfczerinde s\xfcz\xfclmeye devam etmek.",dailyMessage:"Kondor bug\xfcn seni y\xfcksek bir perspektiften hayat\u0131na bakmaya davet ediyor \u2014 kaybetti\u011fin, geride b\u0131rakt\u0131\u011f\u0131n ya da bitmesine \xfcz\xfcld\xfc\u011f\xfcn bir \u015fey var, bunu biliyorum. Ama kondorun g\xf6z\xfcnden bak\u0131nca, o nokta bir sona de\u011fil bir ge\xe7i\u015f kap\u0131s\u0131na benziyor. Bu ku\u015fun kanatlar\u0131 o denli geni\u015ftir ki tek bir hava ak\u0131m\u0131yla saatlerce s\xfcz\xfcl\xfcr; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc y\xfcksekli\u011fin kendisi onu ta\u015f\u0131r. Sen de bu anda, ta en y\xfcksekten bakabilirsen, g\xf6receksin ki ac\u0131n seni k\xfc\xe7\xfcltm\xfcyor \u2014 aksine bir \u015feyin d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc tamaml\u0131yor. Atalar\u0131ndan gelen bir g\xfc\xe7 var i\xe7inde; bilmiyorsan bile, o g\xfc\xe7 senin damarlar\u0131nda ya\u015f\u0131yor. Bug\xfcn kendin i\xe7in \u015funu sor: Hangi kayb\u0131n ya da biti\u015fin i\xe7inde asl\u0131nda bir \xf6zg\xfcrle\u015fme gizli? Kondor \xf6lm\xfc\u015f olan\u0131 yemekle ya\u015fam\u0131 besler \u2014 ac\u0131 da b\xf6yle bir t\u0131pt\u0131r, b\u0131rakabilirsen d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr. Bug\xfcn ge\xe7mi\u015finle ban\u015f yap ve ona minnetini s\xf6yle; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc seni buraya o getirdi.",guidance:"Bir mektup yaz\u0131n \u2014 b\u0131rakmaya haz\u0131r oldu\u011funuz bir \u015feye, bir ili\u015fkiye, bir d\xf6nemin sonuna ya da bir hayal k\u0131r\u0131kl\u0131\u011f\u0131na. \xdc\xe7 paragraf: \xf6nce ona ne bor\xe7lusunuz, sonra ne \xf6\u011fretti\u011fi, son olarak da ona veda. Mektubu y\xfcksek bir yere koyun \u2014 bir raf, bir da\u011f, hatta katlay\u0131p r\xfczg\xe2ra b\u0131rak\u0131n. Kondor gibi, y\xfcksekten veda edilir.",rarity:"legendary",nameEn:"Andean Condor",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["upper world","ancestor spirits","bridge of death","freedom"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The most sacred bird of Andean shamanism, the condor is known in Quechua tradition as Apuchin, the messenger of the mountain spirits; it carries the souls of the dead to the upper world and bridges the living with the ancestors. In Incan cosmology the condor is the sacred cosmic mediator that allows passage among the three worlds: Hanan Pacha (the upper world), Kay Pacha (this world), and Ukhu Pacha (the lower world). In some Great Plains traditions of North America, condor and eagle merge; both are seen as the birds that fly closest to the sun and therefore carry divine messages most truly. In Aztec tradition the corpse-eating birds, zopilote and condor, are cleansing divine beings; they are the sacred hands that complete death and close the cycle. In African Maasai tradition the great wings of eagle and condor symbolize the capacity to speak with ancestors; prayer ascends to the divine alongside the high-flying bird. The condor's medicine: the eye that looks from on high sees that small losses are doorways of passage; even pain, when carried on great wings, becomes flight. Its shadow side is to refuse to release what has died, continuing to soar above the past instead of letting it go.",dailyMessageEn:"The condor invites you today to look at your life from a high vantage. I know there is something you have lost, left behind, or grieved the ending of. But seen through the condor's eyes, that point is not an end but a doorway of passage. This bird's wings are so wide it can glide for hours on a single current of air, because the height itself carries it. If, in this moment, you can look from the very highest point, you will see that your pain is not diminishing you; rather, it is completing the cycle of something. There is a strength within you that comes from your ancestors; even if you do not know it, that strength lives in your blood. Today, ask yourself: within which loss or ending is a hidden liberation? The condor nourishes life by consuming what has died; pain is such a medicine too, transforming when released. Make peace with your past today and offer it your gratitude, for it has brought you here.",guidanceEn:"Write a letter to something you are ready to release: a relationship, the end of an era, or a disappointment. Three paragraphs: first what you owe it, then what it taught you, and finally your farewell. Place the letter somewhere high, a shelf, a mountain, or fold it and release it to the wind. Like the condor, farewells are spoken from on high."},{id:"a053",name:"Somon",emoji:"\ud83d\udc1f",element:"su",symbolism:["k\xf6ke d\xf6n\xfc\u015f","bilgelik","azim","i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcsel y\xf6n"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Pacific_salmon.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kelt gelene\u011finde somon, bilgeli\u011fin kayna\u011f\u0131nda ya\u015fayan kutsal bal\u0131kt\u0131r; \u0130rlanda mitolojisinde bilginin f\u0131nd\u0131klar\u0131ndan beslenen Fintan adl\u0131 somon, onu yiyen ki\u015fiye t\xfcm evrenin s\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 aktar\u0131r. Druidlerin ruhani merkezindeki kaynakta y\xfczen bu bal\u0131k, eri\u015filmez bilgeli\u011fin simgesidir \u2014 onu bulmak i\xe7in \xf6nce i\xe7inden ge\xe7mek gerekir. Norse gelene\u011finde Loki bir somonun bi\xe7imine b\xfcr\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfcnde tanr\u0131lar taraf\u0131ndan yakalan\u0131r; somon hem ka\xe7\u0131\u015f kurnazl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hem de sonunda bulunan ger\xe7e\u011fi simgeler. Kuzey Amerika k\u0131y\u0131 halklar\u0131nda \u2014 Haida, Tlingit ve di\u011ferleri \u2014 somon kutsald\u0131r \xe7\xfcnk\xfc y\u0131lda bir geri d\xf6ner; bu d\xf6n\xfc\u015f, \xf6l\xfcp dirilmenin, k\xf6ke ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve topluma sunulan ya\u015fam\u0131n simgesidir. Japon gelene\u011finde somon, azmin ve \xe7aban\u0131n \xf6d\xfcl\xfcn\xfc temsil eder \u2014 en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc nehir ak\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 a\u015fan bal\u0131k, yumurtalar\u0131n\u0131 en g\xfcvenli yerde b\u0131rakabilir. Sibirya \u015famanizminde ise \u015faman ruhlar\u0131n\u0131n su bi\xe7iminde tezah\xfcr etti\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131r ve somon bu ruhlar\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc arac\u0131s\u0131 say\u0131l\u0131r. Somonun t\u0131bb\u0131: do\u011fdu\u011fun yeri, \xf6z\xfcn\xfc, k\xf6klerin nerede oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlayarak ilerlemek \u2014 ne kadar uza\u011fa gidersen git, geri d\xf6nme yolu i\xe7inde yaz\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: ak\u0131nt\u0131ya kar\u015f\u0131 y\xfczmeyi al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k haline getirip ac\u0131y\u0131 liyakat kan\u0131t\u0131 saymak \u2014 zorluk her zaman do\u011fru yol de\u011fildir.",dailyMessage:"Somon bug\xfcn sana zorlu yolun anlam\u0131n\u0131 soruyor. \u015eu an ak\u0131nt\u0131ya kar\u015f\u0131 y\xfcz\xfcyor olabilirsin \u2014 her \u015fey daha a\u011f\u0131r, her ad\u0131m daha yorucu hissediliyor. Ama somon bunu bir hata oldu\u011fu i\xe7in yapm\u0131yor; do\u011fdu\u011fu yere d\xf6n\xfcyor \xe7\xfcnk\xfc yumurtalar\u0131n\u0131 orada b\u0131rakmas\u0131 gerekiyor, en g\xfcvenli, en ger\xe7ek yerde. Senin de bu yorucu yolculu\u011funun bir k\xf6k\xfc var: nereden geliyorsun, ne i\xe7in y\xfcz\xfcyorsun? Bu soruyu kendin i\xe7in net yan\u0131tlayabiliyor musun? Bazen k\xf6k\xfcmuzu kaybetti\u011fimizde enerjimiz de da\u011f\u0131l\u0131yor \u2014 ger\xe7ek motivasyon, i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcsel y\xf6nelim o k\xf6k\xfc hat\u0131rlad\u0131\u011f\u0131nda geri geliyor. Bug\xfcn seni yoran \u015feyin alt\u0131nda hangi derin bir 'neden' yat\u0131yor? Somon i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcyle bilir nereye d\xf6nece\u011fini; senin i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcn seni nereye \xe7ekiyor? Yorgunlu\u011funa ra\u011fmen bir ad\u0131m daha at \u2014 ama bu sefer neyin i\xe7in att\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 bil.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn be\u015f dakika g\xf6zlerinizi kapat\u0131n ve \u015fu soruyu sorun: 'Beni ba\u015flatan, ger\xe7ekten \xf6nem verdi\u011fim \u015fey neydi?' Cevab\u0131 yarg\u0131lamadan hissedin. Sonra bunu bir yere yaz\u0131n ve bu haftan\u0131n ba\u015f\u0131nda g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr bir yere as\u0131n. Somonun g\xfcc\xfc ak\u0131nt\u0131ya kar\u015f\u0131 y\xfczmekten de\u011fil, nereye gitti\u011fini bilmesinden gelir.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Salmon",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["return to source","wisdom","perseverance","instinctual direction"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Celtic tradition the salmon is the sacred fish that lives at the source of wisdom; in Irish mythology, Fintan the salmon, fed by the nuts of knowledge, transfers all the secrets of the universe to whoever eats him. Swimming in the spring at the spiritual center of the Druids, this fish symbolizes inaccessible wisdom, found only by passing through one's own depths. In Norse tradition Loki takes the form of a salmon and is caught by the gods; the salmon represents both the cunning of escape and the truth finally discovered. Among the coastal peoples of North America, the Haida, Tlingit, and others, the salmon is sacred because it returns once a year; this return symbolizes dying and rising, devotion to one's roots, and a life offered to community. In Japanese tradition the salmon represents the reward of perseverance and effort; the fish that overcomes the strongest river current can lay its eggs in the safest place. In Siberian shamanism, the spirits of shamans are believed to manifest in watery forms, and the salmon is held to be the most powerful vessel of these spirits. The salmon's medicine: to remember where you were born, your essence, where your roots lie, while moving forward. No matter how far you go, the way back is written inside you. Its shadow side is to make swimming against the current a habit and treat suffering as proof of worth; hardship is not always the right path.",dailyMessageEn:"The Salmon asks you today about the meaning of the difficult road. You may be swimming against the current right now, everything feels heavier, every step more tiring. But the salmon does not do this because it is mistaken; it returns to its birthplace because it must lay its eggs there, in the safest, most authentic place. Your wearying journey has a root too: where are you coming from, what are you swimming toward? Can you answer this question clearly for yourself? Sometimes when we lose our root our energy scatters, and real motivation, instinctual orientation, returns when we remember it. Today, beneath what tires you, what deep 'why' lies waiting? The salmon knows by instinct where to return; what is your instinct drawing you toward? Take one more step despite the tiredness, but this time know what you are stepping for.",guidanceEn:"Close your eyes for five minutes today and ask: 'What started me on this path, what did I truly care about?' Feel the answer without judgment. Then write it somewhere and hang it where you can see it at the start of this week. The salmon's strength comes not from swimming against the current but from knowing where it is going."},{id:"a054",name:"Sinek Ku\u015fu",emoji:"\ud83c\udf3a",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["ne\u015fe","hafiflik","sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 ruhu","an'da ya\u015fam"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Rufous_Hummingbird.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Aztek gelene\u011finde d\xfc\u015fen sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131n ruhlar\u0131 sinek ku\u015funa \u2014 huitzilin'e \u2014 d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcrd\xfc; bu nedenle sinek ku\u015fu en b\xfcy\xfck sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 cesaretinin k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir bedendeki tezah\xfcr\xfcd\xfcr. Sava\u015f tanr\u0131s\u0131 Huitzilopochtli'nin ad\u0131 da bu ku\u015ftan gelir \u2014 g\xfcne\u015f sava\u015f\xe7\u0131s\u0131, k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama korkusuz. And \u015famanizminde sinek ku\u015fu, a\u015fk ve iyile\u015fmenin habercisidir; onu g\xf6rmek, kalbin ne\u015feye a\xe7\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n i\u015faretidir. Kuzey Amerika Pueblo gelene\u011finde sinek ku\u015fu ya\u011fmur duas\u0131nda kullan\u0131l\u0131r \u2014 en k\xfc\xe7\xfck, en \xe7evik varl\u0131k, bulutlarla konu\u015fma yetisine sahiptir. Meksika halk gelene\u011finde sinek ku\u015fu b\xfcy\xfcde \xf6nemli bir yer tutar; \xf6zellikle a\u015fk b\xfcy\xfclerinde ve kalp a\xe7ma rit\xfcellerinde bu ku\u015fun t\xfcyleri ya da imgesi kullan\u0131l\u0131r. Japon haiku gelene\u011finde de sinek ku\u015fu an\u0131n i\xe7inde tam ya\u015faman\u0131n simgesidir \u2014 bir \xe7i\xe7ekten di\u011ferine ge\xe7i\u015fi saf varl\u0131kla yapar, ge\xe7mi\u015fi ya da gelece\u011fi d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmeden. Sinek ku\u015funun t\u0131bb\u0131: kanatlar\u0131n\u0131 dakikada seksen kez \xe7\u0131rparak havada sabit durabilir; bu muazzam enerji harcamas\u0131, an\u0131n tam ortas\u0131nda olmak i\xe7in katlan\u0131lan kutsal \xe7abad\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: s\xfcrekli hareket halinde olmak, bir yerde konaklamay\u0131, derinle\u015fmeyi, k\xf6kl\xfc olmay\u0131 reddedebilmek.",dailyMessage:"Sinek Ku\u015fu bug\xfcn sana boyutundan ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131z g\xfc\xe7 dersi veriyor. Bu k\xfc\xe7\xfck yarat\u0131k, v\xfccudundaki a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131n iki kat\u0131 kadar nektar ta\u015f\u0131yabilir \u2014 sanki her \u015fey imk\xe2ns\u0131z g\xf6r\xfcnse de bir yol bulur. \u015eu anda seni b\xfcy\xfck ve a\u011f\u0131r g\xf6r\xfcnen bir y\xfck var m\u0131? Belki bir sorun, bir karar, bir belirsizlik. Sinek Ku\u015fu o y\xfck\xfcn ger\xe7ekte ne kadar b\xfcy\xfck oldu\u011funu de\u011fil, senin ona nas\u0131l yakla\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 sorgular. Bug\xfcn hangi a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131mak yerine onun etraf\u0131nda zarif bir dans edebilirsin? Bir de \u015funu sor kendine: ne\u015feni son ald\u0131\u011f\u0131n yer nereydi ve o andan bu yana ne kadar zaman ge\xe7ti? K\xfc\xe7\xfck bir an bile yeter \u2014 tek bir \xe7i\xe7e\u011fin nektar\u0131, sinek ku\u015funu g\xfcnlerce besler. Hafifli\u011fi se\xe7mek, ciddiyetsizlik de\u011fildir; tam tersine, a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131 gereksiz yere ta\u015f\u0131may\u0131 b\u0131rakmakt\u0131r.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn bilerek k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir sevin\xe7 an\u0131 yarat\u0131n: bir \xe7i\xe7e\u011fe bak\u0131n, sevdi\u011finiz bir m\xfczi\u011fi \xfc\xe7 dakika boyunca sadece m\xfczi\u011fe odaklanarak dinleyin ya da bir \xe7ocu\u011fun oyununu sessizce izleyin. Bu k\xfc\xe7\xfck an, i\xe7inizi bo\u015faltmaya de\u011fil doldurmaya yarar. Sinek ku\u015fu her \xe7i\xe7e\u011fi tam olarak ziyaret eder \u2014 siz de bu k\xfc\xe7\xfck an\u0131 tam olarak ya\u015fay\u0131n.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Hummingbird",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["joy","lightness","warrior spirit","presence in the moment"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Aztec tradition the souls of fallen warriors transformed into hummingbirds, huitzilin; the hummingbird is therefore the greatest warrior courage manifest in a tiny body. The name of the war god Huitzilopochtli comes from this bird: the sun warrior, small but fearless. In Andean shamanism the hummingbird is the messenger of love and healing; to see one is a sign that the heart is opening to joy. In Pueblo tradition of North America the hummingbird is invoked in rain prayers; the smallest, swiftest being holds the power to speak with the clouds. In Mexican folk tradition the hummingbird holds an important place in magic, especially in love spells and heart-opening rituals where its feathers or image are used. In the Japanese haiku tradition the hummingbird is a symbol of fully inhabiting the moment; it moves from flower to flower in pure presence, untroubled by past or future. The hummingbird's medicine: by beating its wings eighty times per second, it holds itself still in the air; this immense expenditure of energy is the sacred effort required to be fully at the center of the moment. Its shadow side is constant motion, the inability to settle, deepen, or take root anywhere.",dailyMessageEn:"The Hummingbird teaches you today about strength independent of size. This tiny creature can carry nectar twice its body weight; though everything looks impossible, it finds a way. Is there a burden that feels large and heavy to you right now? Perhaps a problem, a decision, a piece of uncertainty. The Hummingbird does not question how large that burden truly is but how you approach it. Today, around which weight could you weave a graceful dance instead of carrying it? And ask yourself: where did you last receive joy, and how long has it been since then? A single small moment is enough; the nectar of one flower nourishes the hummingbird for days. To choose lightness is not to be unserious; it is, on the contrary, to stop carrying unnecessary weight.",guidanceEn:"Today deliberately create a small moment of delight: gaze at a flower, listen to a piece of music you love for three minutes with full attention, or quietly watch a child play. This small moment serves to fill you, not to empty you. The hummingbird visits each flower fully; you too live this small moment fully."},{id:"a055",name:"Yaban Domuzu",emoji:"\ud83d\udc17",element:"toprak",symbolism:["ham g\xfc\xe7","cesaret","sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 y\xfcrek","toprak ba\u011f\u0131"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Wild_Boar_Facing_Viewer.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kelt mitolojisinde yaban domuzu Twrch Trwyth, kahramanlar\u0131n avlad\u0131\u011f\u0131 en tehlikeli ve kutsal yarat\u0131kt\u0131r \u2014 Arthur'un destan\u0131nda ona ula\u015fmak neredeyse imk\xe2ns\u0131z bir cesareti gerektirir. \u0130rlanda'n\u0131n en b\xfcy\xfck kahramanlar\u0131 domuz avc\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131nda s\u0131nanm\u0131\u015f, sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 ruhunu bu hayvan\u0131n kar\u015f\u0131s\u0131nda kan\u0131tlam\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. Norse mitolojisinde Freyr'in kutsal domuzu Gullinbursti alt\u0131n k\u0131llar\u0131 olan ve karanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ayd\u0131nlatan bir yarat\u0131kt\u0131r; bereket, liderlik ve sava\u015f\xe7\u0131l\u0131k \xfc\xe7l\xfcs\xfcn\xfc bir arada ta\u015f\u0131r. Yunan gelene\u011finde Kalydon domuzu tanr\u0131\xe7a Artemis'in gazab\u0131yla g\xf6nderilmi\u015f ilahi bir g\xfc\xe7t\xfcr; onu avlamak, \xf6l\xfcml\xfcn\xfcn tanr\u0131sal s\u0131navdan ge\xe7mesi anlam\u0131na gelir. Hint gelene\u011finde Varaha \u2014 Vishnu'nun domuz bi\xe7imi \u2014 yeri okyanusun dibinden kurtar\u0131r; ham g\xfc\xe7 ile koruyucu sevginin b\xfct\xfcnle\u015fti\u011fi ilahi tezah\xfcrd\xfcr. \xc7in takviminde domuz y\u0131l\u0131nda do\u011fanlar cesur, d\xfcr\xfcst ve enerjik say\u0131l\u0131r; \xc7in halk gelene\u011finde domuz topra\u011f\u0131 seven, bereketle ve bollukla \xf6zde\u015fle\u015fen bir hayvand\u0131r. Yaban domuzunun t\u0131bb\u0131: geri ad\u0131m atmaz, etraf\u0131ndan dola\u015fmaz, g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfc yoldan ge\xe7er \u2014 bu do\u011frudan, korkusuz hareket bi\xe7imi as\u0131l g\xfc\xe7t\xfcr. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: her \u015feyi kafa kafaya \xe7\xf6zmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015fmak; zaman zaman dolayl\u0131 yolun ya da dinlenmenin daha ak\u0131ll\u0131ca oldu\u011funu g\xf6rmemek.",dailyMessage:"Yaban Domuzu bug\xfcn seni do\u011frudan, korkusuz bir eyleme \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131yor. Uzun s\xfcredir etraf\u0131ndan dola\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n, erteledi\u011fin, \xfczerine d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcp yine bekledi\u011fin bir \u015fey var. Belki bir konu\u015fma, bir karar, bir s\u0131n\u0131r ya da bir ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7. Domuz o konu hakk\u0131nda sana \u015funu diyor: a\u015f\u0131r\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmek, bazen korkuya verilen en \u015f\u0131k isimdir. Elbette haz\u0131rl\u0131k \xf6nemlidir, ama bir noktadan sonra haz\u0131rlanmak bitmez \u2014 harekete ge\xe7mek gerekir. \u0130\xe7inde o g\xfc\xe7 zaten var. Bunu sana kan\u0131tlamam gerekmiyor; sen de biliyorsun. Bug\xfcn tam olarak neyin \xf6n\xfcnde duraks\u0131yorsun? O duraksaman\u0131n alt\u0131nda ne yat\u0131yor \u2014 ger\xe7ek bir tehlike mi, yoksa al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k haline gelmi\u015f bir \xe7ekinme mi? Yaban domuzu, kendisinden on kat b\xfcy\xfck bir aslana bile geri \xe7ekilmez \u2014 \xe7\xfcnk\xfc g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan de\u011fil i\xe7eriden al\u0131r. Bug\xfcn o g\xfcc\xfc kendin i\xe7in kullan.",guidance:"Uzun s\xfcredir erteledi\u011finiz bir eylemi yar\u0131m saate s\u0131\u011fd\u0131r\u0131n: o mesaj\u0131 g\xf6nderin, o konu\u015fmay\u0131 yap\u0131n, o ilk ad\u0131m\u0131 at\u0131n. Zaman say\u0131n \u2014 30 dakika, tam 30 dakika. Harekete ge\xe7menin g\xfcc\xfc, m\xfckemmel ko\u015fullar\u0131 beklemekten de\u011fil, \u015fu an ba\u015flamaktan gelir. Yaban domuzu m\xfckemmel zemini beklemez; oradaki zeminde ilerler.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Wild Boar",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["raw power","courage","warrior heart","earth bond"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Celtic mythology the wild boar Twrch Trwyth is the most dangerous and sacred creature hunted by heroes; in the Arthurian legend, reaching him requires almost impossible courage. The greatest heroes of Ireland were tested in the boar hunt, proving their warrior spirit before this animal. In Norse mythology Freyr's sacred boar Gullinbursti has golden bristles and illuminates the darkness; he carries the triad of fertility, leadership, and martial power. In Greek tradition the Calydonian Boar is a divine force sent by the wrath of Artemis; to hunt it is for the mortal to pass through a divine trial. In Hindu tradition Varaha, the boar form of Vishnu, rescues the earth from the depths of the ocean: the divine manifestation in which raw strength and protective love are united. In the Chinese calendar those born in the Year of the Pig are considered brave, honest, and energetic; in Chinese folk tradition the pig is an animal that loves the earth and is identified with fertility and abundance. The wild boar's medicine: it does not step back, does not circle around, but moves through the path it sees. This direct, fearless movement is true strength. Its shadow side is trying to meet everything head-on, failing to see that at times the indirect way or rest is wiser.",dailyMessageEn:"The Wild Boar calls you today to direct, fearless action. There is something you have been circling, postponing, thinking over and waiting on for a long time. Perhaps a conversation, a decision, a boundary or a beginning. The Boar says to you about that matter: overthinking is sometimes the most elegant name we give to fear. Of course preparation is important, but past a certain point preparation never ends; you must act. That strength is already inside you. I do not need to prove it to you; you know it already. Today, what exactly are you pausing before? What lies beneath that hesitation, real danger, or a flinching that has become habit? The wild boar does not retreat even from a lion ten times its size, because its power comes from within, not without. Today, use that power for yourself.",guidanceEn:"Fit a long-postponed action into thirty minutes: send that message, have that conversation, take that first step. Time yourself, exactly thirty minutes. The power of acting comes not from waiting for perfect conditions but from beginning now. The wild boar does not wait for ideal ground; it advances on the ground it stands on."},{id:"a056",name:"Kedi",emoji:"\ud83d\udc31",element:"hava",symbolism:["ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131zl\u0131k","gece sezgisi","b\xfcy\xfc","\xf6z-g\xfcven"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Cat_August_2010-4.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da Bastet \u2014 kedi ba\u015fl\u0131 tanr\u0131\xe7a \u2014 evin, \xe7ocuklar\u0131n ve di\u015fil g\xfcc\xfcn koruyucusuydu; g\xfcne\u015fin \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 gecenin i\xe7ine ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve bu sayede karanl\u0131kta g\xfcvenli\u011fi sa\u011flad\u0131\u011f\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcl\xfcrd\xfc. M\u0131s\u0131r'da bir kediyi \xf6ld\xfcrmek \xf6l\xfcm cezas\u0131yla sonu\xe7lan\u0131rd\u0131 \u2014 bu, kedinin ruhani stat\xfcs\xfcn\xfcn ne denli derin oldu\u011funu g\xf6sterir. Kelt gelene\u011finde kedi, Faerie d\xfcnyas\u0131na \u2014 g\xf6r\xfcnmez alemlere \u2014 a\xe7\u0131lan kap\u0131n\u0131n bek\xe7isidir; \xf6zellikle siyah kedi her iki d\xfcnyan\u0131n aras\u0131nda serbest\xe7e dola\u015fabilir. Slav halk gelene\u011finde 'ev kedisi' (domovoi'nin arkada\u015f\u0131) evin ruhunu korur; kedi bir eve ilk girdi\u011finde onun y\xfcr\xfcd\xfc\u011f\xfc yer, evin en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc enerji noktas\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6sterir. Japon gelene\u011finde maneki-neko \u2014 davet eden kedi \u2014 bolluk ve \u015fans\u0131 \xe7eker; bir pen\xe7esini kald\u0131rm\u0131\u015f bu fig\xfcr, pasif g\xf6r\xfcn\xfc\u015f\xfcn ard\u0131ndaki aktif davet enerjisini simgeler. Norse mitolojisinde a\u015fk tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Freya'n\u0131n arabas\u0131 iki dev kedi taraf\u0131ndan \xe7ekilir; bu da kedinin hem g\xfczellik hem de ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131z di\u015fil g\xfcc\xfc temsil etti\u011fini g\xf6sterir. Kedinin t\u0131bb\u0131: kendi ritmine ve i\xe7 sesine g\xfcvenmek \u2014 ne zaman yakla\u015faca\u011f\u0131n\u0131, ne zaman uzak duraca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcyle bilmek. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131zl\u0131k ad\u0131na ger\xe7ek yak\u0131nl\u0131ktan, savunmas\u0131zl\u0131ktan ve ba\u011flanmaktan ka\xe7\u0131nmak.",dailyMessage:"Kedi bug\xfcn sana ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131n ger\xe7ek anlam\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Bu hayvan ne zorlanarak sevilir ne de korku y\xfcz\xfcnden yan\u0131nda kal\u0131r \u2014 istedi\u011finde gelir, istemedi\u011finde \xe7ekilir. Ve bu y\xfczden bir kedi sana geldi\u011finde, o an\u0131n de\u011feri vard\u0131r \xe7\xfcnk\xfc ger\xe7ektir. Peki sen? Ka\xe7 zamand\u0131r beklentilere, sosyal bask\u0131lara, ba\u015fkalar\u0131n\u0131 hayal k\u0131r\u0131kl\u0131\u011f\u0131na u\u011fratmama korkusuna g\xf6re hareket ediyorsun? Hangi 'evet' asl\u0131nda i\xe7inde 'hay\u0131r' olan bir kelime? Kedi hi\xe7 sahte evet demez \u2014 bu onun en b\xfcy\xfck g\xfcc\xfcd\xfcr. Sezgin bug\xfcn sana ne s\xf6yl\xfcyor, ama akl\u0131n bunu susturuyor mu? Belki bir insan, bir ortam ya da bir al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k var ki sana enerji vermiyor ama oradan ayr\u0131lam\u0131yorsun. Kedi gibi ol: zarif ama net. Bug\xfcn bir \u015feyi i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcyle se\xe7 \u2014 a\xe7\u0131klamak ya da \xf6z\xfcr dilemek zorunda de\u011filsin.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn bir karar\u0131 ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131n onay\u0131n\u0131 almadan verin. K\xfc\xe7\xfck bir \u015fey olabilir \u2014 ne yiyece\u011finiz, nereye gidece\u011finiz, ne dinleyece\u011finiz. Bu k\xfc\xe7\xfck prati\u011fin amac\u0131, i\xe7inizden gelen sesi tan\u0131may\u0131 \xf6\u011frenmek. Her g\xfcn bir k\xfc\xe7\xfck 'kendi sesim' karar\u0131 alarak ba\u015flay\u0131n; zamanla daha b\xfcy\xfck konularda da o sese g\xfcvenebileceksiniz.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Cat",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["independence","night intuition","magic","self-trust"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In ancient Egypt Bastet, the cat-headed goddess, was the protector of the home, of children, and of feminine power; it was thought that she carried the light of the sun into the night, ensuring safety in the darkness. To kill a cat in Egypt was punishable by death, a sign of how deep the cat's spiritual status ran. In Celtic tradition the cat is the keeper of the door to the Faerie realm, the unseen worlds; the black cat especially can move freely between both worlds. In Slavic folk tradition the household cat (companion of the domovoi) protects the spirit of the home; the place a cat first walks when entering a house reveals its strongest energy point. In Japanese tradition the maneki-neko, the beckoning cat, draws abundance and luck; with one paw raised, this figure symbolizes the active invitation hidden behind a passive appearance. In Norse mythology the chariot of the love goddess Freya is drawn by two giant cats, showing that the cat embodies both beauty and independent feminine power. The cat's medicine: trusting your own rhythm and inner voice, knowing by instinct when to draw close and when to keep distance. Its shadow side is avoiding real intimacy, vulnerability, and attachment in the name of independence.",dailyMessageEn:"The Cat reminds you today of the true meaning of independence. This animal is neither loved through force nor stays by fear; she comes when she wishes, withdraws when she does not. And so when a cat comes to you, that moment has value because it is true. And you? How long have you been moving according to expectations, social pressure, the fear of disappointing others? Which of your 'yes' answers is actually a 'no' on the inside? A cat never says a false yes; this is her greatest strength. What is your intuition telling you today that your mind is silencing? Perhaps there is a person, a setting, or a habit that gives you no energy and yet you cannot leave it. Be like the cat: graceful but clear. Today choose something by instinct; you do not need to explain or apologize.",guidanceEn:"Make a decision today without asking for anyone's approval. It can be small: what you will eat, where you will go, what you will listen to. The aim of this small practice is to learn to recognize the voice that comes from within. Begin each day by making one small 'my-own-voice' decision; in time you will trust that voice on greater matters too."},{id:"a057",name:"Yusuf\xe7uk",emoji:"\ud83e\udee7",element:"su",symbolism:["ill\xfczyon","\u0131\u015f\u0131k d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc","\xe7evik zihin","an bilinci"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Blue_dragonfly_-_Aeshna_cyanea.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Japon gelene\u011finde yusuf\xe7uk \u2014 tombo \u2014 g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 simgesidir; Japonya'n\u0131n eski ad\u0131 Akitsushima, 'yusuf\xe7uk adas\u0131' anlam\u0131na gelir. Samuray k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde yusuf\xe7uk geri gidemedi\u011fi i\xe7in yaln\u0131zca ileri bakar \u2014 bu \xf6zelli\u011fi, asla geri \xe7ekilmeyecek olan sava\u015f\xe7\u0131n\u0131n ruhunu temsil eder. Kuzey Amerika Navajo gelene\u011finde yusuf\xe7uk, safl\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve mutlulu\u011fun simgesidir; ruhsal temizlik t\xf6renlerinde bu hayvan\u0131n imgesi kullan\u0131l\u0131r. Hint gelene\u011finde yusuf\xe7uklar\u0131n kanatlar\u0131 \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131 k\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131nda ortaya \xe7\u0131kan renk de\u011fi\u015fimi, Maya ill\xfczyonunu \u2014 var olmayan \u015feyleri ger\xe7ekmi\u015f gibi g\xf6rme e\u011filimini \u2014 simgeler. Aztek gelene\u011finde ise yusuf\xe7uk, b\xfcy\xfcc\xfclerin ve \u015famanlar\u0131n ruhsal ara\u015ft\u0131rma ara\xe7lar\u0131ndan biridir; su ile havan\u0131n birle\u015fim noktas\u0131nda u\xe7arak iki elementin bilgeli\u011fini ta\u015f\u0131r. Kelt gelene\u011finde yusuf\xe7uk, Faerie d\xfcnyas\u0131na ait bir varl\u0131k olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr \u2014 onlar\u0131 g\xf6ren ki\u015fi, g\xf6r\xfcnmez alemlere bir anl\u0131\u011f\u0131na ba\u011flanm\u0131\u015f demektir. Yusuf\xe7u\u011fun t\u0131bb\u0131: \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131n a\xe7\u0131s\u0131na g\xf6re renk de\u011fi\u015ftirmek \u2014 ger\xe7ekli\u011fin tek bir perspektifi yoktur, bak\u0131\u015f a\xe7\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 de\u011fi\u015ftirmek her \u015feyi d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcr. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: \xe7ok fazla perspektife kayarak hi\xe7birinde karar verememek; ill\xfczyon k\u0131rarken ger\xe7e\u011fi de ka\xe7\u0131rmak.",dailyMessage:"Yusuf\xe7uk bug\xfcn sana \u015funu soruyor: o durumu ger\xe7ekten g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfcn gibi mi g\xf6r\xfcyorsun, yoksa sana \xf6yle mi g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyor? Bu k\xfc\xe7\xfck, \xe7evik varl\u0131k kanatlar\u0131yla \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131 k\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131nda onlarca farkl\u0131 renk ortaya \xe7\u0131kar \u2014 oysa kanat tek renktir. Bak\u0131\u015f a\xe7\u0131s\u0131 her \u015feyi de\u011fi\u015ftirir. \u015eu an zor gelen, a\u011f\u0131r hissettiren bir durum varsa, bir ad\u0131m geri \xe7ekil ve sorun: ba\u015fka birinin g\xf6z\xfcnden bu nas\u0131l g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcrd\xfc? Hangi yorumu ger\xe7ek mi san\u0131yorsun, oysa o sadece bir yorum? Bazen bir durumu oldu\u011fundan b\xfcy\xfck, bazen de oldu\u011fundan k\xfc\xe7\xfck g\xf6r\xfcr\xfcz \u2014 her ikisi de bizi yan\u0131lt\u0131r. Yusuf\xe7uk su ile havan\u0131n birle\u015fim noktas\u0131nda ya\u015far; sen de bu anda duygu ile d\xfc\u015f\xfcncenin tam ortas\u0131nda bir yerde duruyorsun. Bug\xfcn sadece g\xf6zlemle \u2014 yarg\u0131lamadan, \xe7\xf6z\xfcm aramadan. Ne g\xf6r\xfcyorsun?",guidance:"Bug\xfcn zor gelen bir durumu bir k\xe2\u011f\u0131da yaz\u0131n. Sonra onu bir arkada\u015f\u0131n, bir \xe7ocu\u011fun ve bir ya\u015fl\u0131 bilgenin nas\u0131l g\xf6rece\u011fini hayal edin \u2014 her birinin yorumunu birka\xe7 c\xfcmleyle yaz\u0131n. Bu \xfc\xe7 perspektif, durumun ill\xfczyon katmanlar\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7ar. Yusuf\xe7u\u011fun bilgeli\u011fi, tek bir a\xe7\u0131dan bakmay\u0131 b\u0131rakmakt\u0131r.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Dragonfly",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["illusion","transformation of light","agile mind","moment awareness"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Japanese tradition the dragonfly, tombo, is a powerful warrior symbol; one of Japan's ancient names, Akitsushima, means 'island of dragonflies.' In samurai culture the dragonfly cannot move backward, only forward, a quality that represents the spirit of the warrior who will never retreat. In Navajo tradition of North America the dragonfly symbolizes purity and happiness; its image is used in rites of spiritual cleansing. In Hindu tradition the shift of color produced when light refracts through the dragonfly's wings symbolizes the illusion of Maya, the tendency to see what does not exist as if it were real. In Aztec tradition the dragonfly is one of the spiritual investigative tools of sorcerers and shamans; flying at the meeting point of water and air, it carries the wisdom of both elements. In Celtic tradition the dragonfly is regarded as a being of the Faerie realm; whoever sees one has been briefly connected to the unseen worlds. The dragonfly's medicine: to change color with the angle of the light. Reality has no single perspective; changing your viewpoint transforms everything. Its shadow side is slipping into too many perspectives so that you can decide on none; breaking illusions while also missing the truth.",dailyMessageEn:"The Dragonfly asks you today: are you really seeing that situation as it is, or as it appears to you? When this small, agile creature refracts light through its wings, dozens of different colors emerge, yet the wing is a single color. Perspective changes everything. If there is a situation that feels hard or heavy right now, step back and ask: how would this look through someone else's eyes? Which interpretation are you taking as reality when it is only one interpretation? Sometimes we see a situation as larger than it is, sometimes as smaller, and both mislead us. The dragonfly lives at the meeting point of water and air; you too stand somewhere in the middle of feeling and thought right now. Today, simply observe, without judging, without seeking solutions. What do you see?",guidanceEn:"Write a difficult situation on a piece of paper today. Then imagine how a friend, a child, and an elder sage would each see it; write each one's interpretation in a few sentences. These three perspectives open the layers of illusion around the situation. The wisdom of the dragonfly is to stop looking from a single angle."},{id:"a058",name:"H\xfcdh\xfcd",emoji:"\ud83d\udc26",element:"hava",symbolism:["ilahi rehber","ruhsal mesaj","bilge yolcu","sadakat"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Upupa_epops_close.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kur'an-\u0131 Kerim'in 27. suresi olan Neml'de H\xfcdh\xfcd, S\xfcleyman Peygamber ile Sebe Melikesi aras\u0131nda ger\xe7e\u011fi ta\u015f\u0131yan el\xe7idir \u2014 gizli olan\u0131 g\xf6rm\xfc\u015f, uzak mesafeden ger\xe7e\u011fi getirmi\u015ftir. Bu anlat\u0131, H\xfcdh\xfcd'\xfc yaln\u0131zca bir ku\u015f de\u011fil, ilahi bilginin arac\u0131s\u0131 yapan sembolik bir derinli\u011fe ta\u015f\u0131r. 12. y\xfczy\u0131l Sufi \u015fairi Ferid\xfcddin Attar'\u0131n Mant\u0131k-ut Tayr'\u0131nda \u2014 Ku\u015flar\u0131n Dili'nde \u2014 H\xfcdh\xfcd, t\xfcm ku\u015flar\u0131 Anka ku\u015funu aramaya yani ruhun Tanr\u0131'ya olan yolculu\u011funa rehberlik eden bilgedir. Her ku\u015fun korkusunu, engelini ve bahanesini dinleyip cevaplar: bu, ruhsal yolculu\u011fun bilge \xf6\u011fretmenidir. M\u0131s\u0131r gelene\u011finde H\xfcdh\xfcd, \xf6l\xfclerin ruhlar\u0131n\u0131 \xf6teki d\xfcnyaya ta\u015f\u0131yan Tehuti \u2014 Thoth \u2014 ile ba\u011flant\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r; bilgelik ve ge\xe7i\u015f ku\u015fudur. Orta Do\u011fu halk gelene\u011finde H\xfcdh\xfcd'\xfcn ba\u015f\u0131ndaki ta\xe7, ona verilen ruhani otoritenin i\u015faretidir \u2014 o, s\u0131radan ku\u015flar aras\u0131nda krald\u0131r. Yahudi Kabbalah gelene\u011finde ise H\xfcdh\xfcd, S\xfcleyman'\u0131n hikmeti ve mistik bilgisiyle \xf6zde\u015fle\u015fir. H\xfcdh\xfcd\xfcn t\u0131bb\u0131: uzak mesafeden ger\xe7e\u011fi ta\u015f\u0131yabilmek \u2014 i\xe7imizdeki o ince sesle ba\u011flant\u0131 kurmak ve o sesi cesurca dile getirmek. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: ger\xe7e\u011fi bilip bildi\u011fini s\xf6ylememek; sahte bir al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfcl\xfck ya da korku ad\u0131na i\xe7sel bilgeli\u011fi susturmak.",dailyMessage:"H\xfcdh\xfcd bug\xfcn sana \xe7ok \xf6zel bir mesaj getiriyor \u2014 ama o mesaj d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan de\u011fil, ta i\xe7inden geliyor. Uzun s\xfcredir bildi\u011fin ama g\xf6rmezden geldi\u011fin, hissetti\u011fin ama kabul etmekten ka\xe7\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131n bir ger\xe7ek var. Belki bir ili\u015fki hakk\u0131nda, bir karar hakk\u0131nda ya da kendinle ilgili bir \u015fey hakk\u0131nda. O ses bu sabah biraz daha y\xfcksek konu\u015fuyor. H\xfcdh\xfcd S\xfcleyman'a ger\xe7e\u011fi s\xf6ylemekten korkmad\u0131 \u2014 uzak diyarlardan, tehlikeli yollardan ge\xe7erek o haberi ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131. Sen kime ya da neye o haberi ta\u015f\u0131maktan ka\xe7\u0131n\u0131yorsun? Belki kendinize bile s\xf6ylemeyi erteledi\u011finiz bir ger\xe7ek var. Bug\xfcn o sesi susturmak yerine, ona k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir alan a\xe7. Bir k\xe2\u011f\u0131da ya da kalbinde, sadece kendine, onu yazabilir ya da seslendirebilirsin. Ger\xe7ek, ta\u015f\u0131nmay\u0131 bekliyor.",guidance:"Bu g\xfcn i\xe7inde on dakika sessiz oturun ve \u015fu soruyu sorun: 'Ne biliyorum ama s\xf6ylemiyorum ya da kabul etmiyorum?' Cevab\u0131 yarg\u0131lamadan, sadece dinleyin. Sonra o ger\xe7e\u011fi bir k\xe2\u011f\u0131da kendinize bir mektup olarak yaz\u0131n. H\xfcdh\xfcd'\xfcn g\xfcc\xfc, ger\xe7e\u011fi ta\u015f\u0131makt\u0131r; sizin g\xfcc\xfcn\xfcz onu \xf6nce kendinizde tutmaya ba\u015flamakt\u0131r.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Hoopoe",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["divine guide","spiritual message","wise traveler","loyalty"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the 27th Surah of the Quran, An-Naml, the Hoopoe is the messenger who carries truth between the Prophet Solomon and the Queen of Sheba; he has seen what was hidden and brought truth from afar. This narrative lifts the Hoopoe into a symbolic depth, making him not merely a bird but the bearer of divine knowledge. In the 12th-century Sufi poet Farid ud-Din Attar's Mantiq-ut-Tayr (The Conference of the Birds), the Hoopoe is the sage who guides all the birds in their search for the Simurgh, that is, the journey of the soul to God. He listens to each bird's fear, obstacle, and excuse and answers them: this is the wise teacher of the spiritual journey. In Egyptian tradition the Hoopoe is connected with Thoth (Tehuti), who carries the souls of the dead to the next world; he is the bird of wisdom and transition. In Middle Eastern folk tradition the crown on the Hoopoe's head is the sign of the spiritual authority granted to him; among ordinary birds, he is king. In the Jewish Kabbalistic tradition the Hoopoe is identified with Solomon's wisdom and mystical knowledge. The Hoopoe's medicine: to carry truth across distances, to connect with that fine voice inside us and to speak it courageously. Its shadow side is to know the truth and not speak it; to silence one's inner wisdom under the guise of false humility or fear.",dailyMessageEn:"The Hoopoe brings you a very special message today, but that message comes not from outside but from your deepest interior. There is a truth you have long known and ignored, felt and avoided acknowledging. Perhaps about a relationship, a decision, or something about yourself. That voice is speaking a little louder this morning. The Hoopoe did not fear telling Solomon the truth; he carried that news from distant lands across dangerous roads. To whom, or to what, are you avoiding carrying that news? Perhaps there is a truth you have been postponing telling even yourself. Today, instead of silencing that voice, give it a small space. On paper, or in your heart, only to yourself, you can write it or speak it. Truth waits to be carried.",guidanceEn:"Sit in silence for ten minutes today and ask: 'What do I know that I am not saying or acknowledging?' Listen to the answer without judgment. Then write that truth as a letter to yourself. The Hoopoe's strength is to carry truth; yours is to begin by holding it within yourself."},{id:"a059",name:"Akbaba",emoji:"\ud83e\udd85",element:"hava",symbolism:["ar\u0131nma","d\xf6ng\xfc","\xf6l\xfcm\xfc kucaklama","yenilenme"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Gyps_africanus_(Ruppell%27s_vulture).jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da akbaba, \xdcst M\u0131s\u0131r'\u0131n koruyucu tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Nekhbet olarak tap\u0131n\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131 \u2014 firavunlar\u0131n tac\u0131n\u0131 s\xfcsleyen bu kutsal ku\u015f, annelik g\xfcc\xfcn\xfcn, koruyuculu\u011fun ve d\xf6ng\xfcn\xfcn simgesiydi. M\u0131s\u0131r'da akbaban\u0131n yaln\u0131zca di\u015fi do\u011fdu\u011funa ve r\xfczg\xe2rdan d\xf6llenerek \xfcredi\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131; bu inan\xe7 onu saf di\u015fil g\xfcc\xfcn, bakire annenin sembol\xfc yap\u0131yordu. Aztek gelene\u011finde akbaba \u2014 zopilote \u2014 tanr\u0131\xe7a Coatlicue ile ili\u015fkilendirilir; \xf6l\xfc eti yemesi, topra\u011f\u0131 temizlemesi ve ya\u015fam d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc tamamlamas\u0131 nedeniyle kutsal bir varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Kuzey Amerika gelene\u011finde akbaba, B\xfcy\xfck Temizleyici olarak tan\u0131mlan\u0131r \u2014 k\xf6t\xfc kokuya kar\u015f\u0131 direnci ve \xf6l\xfcm\xfc d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrme kapasitesi ile g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir t\u0131ba sahiptir. Afrika Zulu gelene\u011finde akbaba b\xfcy\xfck mesafeleri g\xf6rebilen sezgisiyle, kayna\u011f\u0131 uzaktan sezerek oraya u\xe7mas\u0131yla bilinir \u2014 bu, uzak g\xf6r\xfc\u015fl\xfcl\xfc\u011f\xfcn ve i\xe7sel bilincin simgesidir. Tibet B\xf6n gelene\u011finde \u2014 g\xf6k g\xf6m\xfcs\xfc gelene\u011finde \u2014 akbabalar \xf6l\xfc bedenini alarak ruhu \xf6zg\xfcrle\u015ftirir; bu nedenle \xf6l\xfcm s\xfcreci kutsal ve temiz bir yolculuktur. Akbaban\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: sona erenleri \xe7\xf6z\xfcme kavu\u015fturmak, d\xf6ng\xfcy\xfc tamamlamak, kirliyi temize \xe7evirmek \u2014 \xf6l\xfcm i\xe7inde gizli olan ya\u015fam enerjisini g\xf6rmek. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: yaln\u0131zca sona erenleri beklemek; tamamlanmay\u0131 beklemenin i\xe7inde pasif bir t\xfckenmeye kap\u0131lmak.",dailyMessage:"Akbaba bug\xfcn sana cesur ama gerekli bir soruyu soruyor: i\xe7inde, hayat\u0131nda, ili\u015fkilerinde ya da d\xfc\u015f\xfcncelerinde \u2014 art\u0131k i\u015flevi kalmam\u0131\u015f, ama tutunmaya devam etti\u011fin ne var? Akbaba \xf6l\xfc eti yiyen bir ku\u015f de\u011fildir; o, d\xf6ng\xfcn\xfcn tamamlanmas\u0131na izin veren kutsal bir temizlik\xe7idir. Topra\u011f\u0131 besler, d\xf6ng\xfcy\xfc kapat\u0131r, ya\u015fam\u0131n devam etmesini sa\u011flar \u2014 t\xfcm bunlar\u0131 ba\u015fkalar\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6remedi\u011fi bir \u015fey g\xf6rme kapasitesiyle yapar. Sen bug\xfcn o kapasiteni kullanabilir misin? Hangi al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131\u011f\u0131n, hangi hik\xe2yen, hangi rol\xfcn art\u0131k seni beslemedi\u011fini g\xf6r\xfcyorsun? Sona ermek ac\u0131 verebilir \u2014 ama akbabay\u0131 izlersen anlar\u0131s\u0131n: o sona erenden yeni bir ya\u015fam do\u011far. Bug\xfcn bir \u015feyin bitmesine, kapanmas\u0131na ya da de\u011fi\u015fmesine izin ver. Bu, yenilgiye de\u011fil, d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcme ad\u0131m atmakt\u0131r.",guidance:"Bir temizleme rit\xfceli yap\u0131n: fiziksel bir alan\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 \u2014 odan\u0131z\u0131, \xe7antan\u0131z\u0131, bilgisayar\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 \u2014 temizleyin ve bu s\xfcre\xe7te zihinsel olarak da ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z gereksiz y\xfck\xfc b\u0131rakt\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 hayal edin. Her at\u0131lan nesneyle birlikte i\xe7inizden ge\xe7irdi\u011finiz bir d\xfc\u015f\xfcnce, bir \xf6fke ya da bir beklenti de gitsin. Akbaba sembolik temizleme yapar; siz de fiziksel temizlikle ruhsal d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm ba\u015flatabilirsiniz.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Vulture",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["purification","cycle","embracing death","renewal"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In ancient Egypt the vulture was worshipped as Nekhbet, protective goddess of Upper Egypt; this sacred bird crowning the pharaohs was the symbol of motherhood's power, of protection, and of the cycle. In Egypt it was believed that all vultures were born female and conceived from the wind; this belief made the vulture a symbol of pure feminine power, the virgin mother. In Aztec tradition the vulture, zopilote, is associated with the goddess Coatlicue; because it eats the dead, cleanses the earth, and completes the cycle of life, it is a sacred being. In North American tradition the vulture is called the Great Purifier, with strong medicine in its resistance to foul scent and its capacity to transform death. In African Zulu tradition the vulture is known for the intuition with which it sees over great distances, sensing the source from far away and flying there: this symbolizes far-sightedness and inner awareness. In the Tibetan B\xf6n tradition, in sky burial, vultures take the dead body and release the soul; thus the process of death becomes a sacred and clean journey. The vulture's medicine: to bring resolution to what has ended, to complete the cycle, to turn impurity into purity, to see the hidden life energy within death. Its shadow side is to wait only for endings, to fall into a passive depletion within waiting for completion.",dailyMessageEn:"The Vulture asks you a brave but necessary question today: within yourself, in your life, your relationships, or your thoughts, what no longer serves a function yet you still hold to? The vulture is not a bird that eats death; it is the sacred cleanser that allows the cycle to complete. It nourishes the earth, closes the cycle, allows life to continue, all by means of a capacity to see what others cannot see. Can you use that capacity today? Which habit, which story, which role do you see no longer feeding you? Endings can be painful, but if you watch the vulture you will understand: a new life rises from what has ended. Today let something end, close, or change. This is a step not into defeat but into transformation.",guidanceEn:"Carry out a cleansing ritual: clean a physical space, your room, your bag, your computer, and imagine that you are mentally releasing the unnecessary load you carry. With each discarded object, let a thought, an anger, or an expectation leave with it. The vulture performs symbolic cleansing; you too can begin spiritual transformation through physical cleansing."},{id:"a060",name:"Jaguar",emoji:"\ud83d\udc06",element:"toprak",symbolism:["gece g\xfcne\u015fi","\u015faman d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc","alt d\xfcnya","g\xfc\xe7"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Jaguar_at_the_San_Diego_Zoo_1.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Aztek uygarl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc \u015faman hayvan\u0131 olan jaguar, Tecuani olarak bilinen ve gece g\xfcne\u015fini \u2014 yer alt\u0131ndaki karanl\u0131\u011fa yolculuk eden g\xfcne\u015fi \u2014 temsil eden kutsal varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Maya Popol Vuh'unda Hunahpu ve Xbalanque \u2014 kahraman ikizler \u2014 Jaguar Tanr\u0131s\u0131'n\u0131n yard\u0131m\u0131yla \xf6l\xfcm d\xfcnyas\u0131ndan geri d\xf6nerler; jaguar hem tehlike hem de kurtulu\u015fun anahtar\u0131d\u0131r. Azteklerde Jaguar Sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131 \u2014 Ocelotl \u2014 ordunun en se\xe7kin ve en korkusuz sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131yd\u0131; jaguar postu giydiklerinde o hayvan\u0131n g\xfcc\xfcne b\xfcr\xfcnd\xfcklerine inan\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. G\xfcney Amerika Amazonyas\u0131 \u015famanizminde \u015faman yaguarete \u2014 jaguar \u2014 bi\xe7imine b\xfcr\xfcnerek alt d\xfcnyaya iner, hasta ruhlar\u0131 bulur ve geri getirir. Bu d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm, bilginin karanl\u0131kta aranmas\u0131 gerekti\u011fini \xf6\u011fretir. Peru Quechua gelene\u011finde jaguar, U\xe7ku \u2014 derin bilgi \u2014 ile ili\u015fkilendirilir; g\xf6rmek i\xe7in karanl\u0131\u011fa ihtiya\xe7 duyulur. Afrika ve G\xfcneydo\u011fu Asya gelene\u011finde benzer b\xfcy\xfck kediler \u2014 leopar, kaplan \u2014 de gece g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfc nedeniyle karanl\u0131kta yol g\xf6steren ruhsal rehberler olarak kabul edilir. Jaguar\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: karanl\u0131ktan korkmadan i\xe7ine girmek; g\xf6zlerini kapsaml\u0131 a\xe7arak g\xf6r\xfcnmeyeni g\xf6rmek ve g\xfc\xe7 kayna\u011f\u0131n\u0131 tam da en \xe7ok korkulan yerden \xe7\u0131karmak. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olmak ad\u0131na savunmas\u0131zl\u0131ktan tamamen koparak g\xf6lgede yaln\u0131z kalmak.",dailyMessage:"Jaguar bug\xfcn seni karanl\u0131\u011fa \u2014 kordu\u011fun, ka\xe7\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131n o i\xe7 mek\xe2nlara \u2014 davet ediyor. Bu b\xfcy\xfck kedi, av\u0131n\u0131 g\xfcnd\xfcz de\u011fil gece yakalar; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc g\xf6zleri karanl\u0131kta alt\u0131 kat daha iyi g\xf6r\xfcr. Sen de fark etmiyor musun: en b\xfcy\xfck g\xfc\xe7 kaynaklar\u0131n\u0131n tam da en \xe7ok korktu\u011fun yerlerde gizli oldu\u011funu? Uzun s\xfcredir ka\xe7\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131n, \xfczerine d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmekten \xe7ekindi\u011fin bir \u015fey var. Belki bir duygu, bir an\u0131, bir ger\xe7ek ya da bir y\xfczle\u015fme. Jaguar avlan\u0131rken ko\u015fmaz \u2014 sab\u0131rla, sessizce, ad\u0131m ad\u0131m yakla\u015f\u0131r. Bu a\u011f\u0131rl\u0131kl\u0131, kararl\u0131 sessizlik, g\xfcc\xfcn ta kendisidir. Bug\xfcn i\xe7indeki karanl\u0131kta ne g\xf6r\xfcyorsun? G\xf6zlerini kapat\u0131p o karanl\u0131\u011fa bakabilir misin \u2014 ka\xe7madan, \xe7\xf6zmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015fmadan, sadece orada olarak? Jaguar bilir ki karanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 tan\u0131mak, onu yenmenin tek yoludur.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn g\xf6zlerinizi kapat\u0131n ve i\xe7inizde en \xe7ok ka\xe7\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir duyguyu veya konuyu hissedin. Ona bir \u015fekil verin \u2014 bir renk, bir doku, bir ses. Ard\u0131ndan hayal edin ki Jaguar gibi sessizce ona yakla\u015f\u0131yorsunuz. Onu \xe7\xf6zmeyeceksiniz \u2014 sadece yan\u0131na oturacaks\u0131n\u0131z. Be\u015f dakika boyunca o duyguyla birlikte olmak, onu y\u0131llar boyunca ka\xe7\u0131nmaktan daha \xe7ok \u015fey \xf6\u011fretir.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Jaguar",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["night sun","shamanic transformation","lower world","power"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The most powerful shamanic animal of the Aztec civilization, the jaguar is known as Tecuani, the sacred being who represents the night sun, the sun that travels into the underground darkness. In the Mayan Popol Vuh, the hero twins Hunahpu and Xbalanque return from the world of death with the help of the Jaguar God; the jaguar is both the danger and the key to salvation. Among the Aztecs the Jaguar Warriors (Ocelotl) were the most select and fearless soldiers; when they wore the jaguar pelt they were believed to take on the animal's power. In the shamanism of the Amazon of South America the shaman shifts into the form of the yaguarete, the jaguar, to descend into the lower world, find sick souls, and bring them back. This transformation teaches that knowledge must be sought in the dark. In the Quechua tradition of Peru the jaguar is associated with Uchu, deep knowledge; one needs darkness in order to see. In African and Southeast Asian traditions similar great cats, leopards and tigers, are also accepted as spirit guides leading through the dark thanks to their night sight. The jaguar's medicine: to enter the darkness without fear; to open wide your eyes and see the unseen, drawing the source of power from precisely the place most feared. Its shadow side is to cut yourself off completely from vulnerability in the name of strength and remain alone in the shadow.",dailyMessageEn:"The Jaguar invites you today into the darkness, the inner spaces you fear and avoid. This great cat catches its prey not by day but by night, because its eyes see six times better in darkness. Have you not noticed: that your greatest sources of strength are hidden in the very places you most fear? There is something you have long avoided, hesitated to dwell on. Perhaps an emotion, a memory, a truth, or a confrontation. The jaguar does not run while hunting; it approaches with patience, silence, step by step. This weighted, resolute silence is power itself. What do you see in the darkness inside you today? Can you close your eyes and look at that darkness without fleeing, without trying to fix, simply being there? The jaguar knows that to know the darkness is the only way to overcome it.",guidanceEn:"Close your eyes today and feel the emotion or topic you most avoid. Give it a shape, a color, a texture, a sound. Then imagine that, like the Jaguar, you approach it in silence. You will not solve it; you will simply sit beside it. Five minutes of being with that emotion teaches more than years of avoiding it."},{id:"a061",name:"Kobra",emoji:"\ud83d\udc0d",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["ilahi koruma","kundalini","kral i\u015fareti","gizli g\xfc\xe7"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Ophiophagus_hannah_2.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da kobra \u2014 uraeus \u2014 firavunlar\u0131n ba\u015fl\u0131\u011f\u0131na i\u015flenmi\u015f, ilahi iktidar\u0131n ve koruyucu g\xfcc\xfcn simgesiydi. Wadjet tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 kobra bi\xe7imindeydi ve M\u0131s\u0131r'\u0131n alt Deltas\u0131'n\u0131 koruyan kutsal ate\u015f g\xf6z\xfcyd\xfc; d\xfc\u015fmanlar\u0131 yakan, firavunu koruyan bu varl\u0131k, g\xfcc\xfcn en saf bi\xe7imini temsil eder. Hint gelene\u011finde Naga \u2014 kobra \u2014 Kundalini enerjisinin somutla\u015fm\u0131\u015f halidir; omurgan\u0131n dibinde uyuyan bu y\u0131lan uyan\u0131nca bilin\xe7 her \xe7akray\u0131 a\u015farak ta\xe7 \xe7akraya ula\u015f\u0131r ve ayd\u0131nlanma ger\xe7ekle\u015fir. Shiva'n\u0131n boynuna sar\u0131lm\u0131\u015f kobra, \xf6l\xfcm\xfc ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc kucaklaman\u0131n simgesidir \u2014 o enerjinin kontrol alt\u0131nda tutulmas\u0131 de\u011fil, onunla dans edilmesidir. Yunan gelene\u011finde Asklepios'un asas\u0131na sar\u0131lm\u0131\u015f y\u0131lan, iyile\u015fmenin simgesidir; zehirli olan\u0131n ayn\u0131 zamanda iyile\u015ftirici oldu\u011funu g\xf6sterir. Aztek gelene\u011finde Quetzalcoatl \u2014 T\xfcyl\xfc Y\u0131lan \u2014 yarat\u0131c\u0131 ilahi g\xfcc\xfcn en b\xfcy\xfck simgesidir; y\u0131lan topra\u011fa ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcme, kanatlar ise \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011fe ve y\xfckseli\u015fe kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131k gelir. Mezoamerika, \xc7in ve Afrika geleneklerinde kobra ya da b\xfcy\xfck y\u0131lanlar her zaman gizli bilginin ve koruyucu g\xfcc\xfcn sahibi olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr. Kobran\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: i\xe7indeki uyuyan g\xfcc\xfc tan\u0131mak; o g\xfcc\xfcn ba\u015fkalar\u0131n\u0131 yaralamak i\xe7in de\u011fil, kendini ve sevdiklerini korumak i\xe7in var oldu\u011funu bilmek. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc bilin\xe7sizce ya da \xf6fkeyle kullanmak; s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131 netlik yerine \xf6fkeyle koymak.",dailyMessage:"Kobra bug\xfcn i\xe7inde uyuyan o g\xfcc\xfc uyand\u0131r\u0131yor. Bunu d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan hissetmiyorsun belki \u2014 ama i\xe7inde, uzun s\xfcredir bast\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131\u015f, beklemeye al\u0131nm\u0131\u015f, '\u015fimdi de\u011fil, sonra' denilmi\u015f bir enerji var. O enerji sald\u0131rmak i\xe7in de\u011fil, seni korumak i\xe7in var. Bug\xfcn hangi s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 net \xe7izmedi\u011fin i\xe7in kendini k\xfc\xe7\xfck hissediyorsun? Kobra, sald\u0131rmadan \xf6nce dik durur \u2014 bu bir uyar\u0131d\u0131r, bir g\xfc\xe7 g\xf6sterisidir, sava\u015fa de\u011fil kendi alan\u0131n\u0131 korumaya \xe7a\u011fr\u0131d\u0131r. Sen de bu anda, bir durumda, bir ili\u015fkide ya da kendi i\xe7inde, o dik duru\u015fa ihtiya\xe7 duyuyor olabilirsin. Kendine sor: neye 'hay\u0131r' demekten korkuyorsun? O 'hay\u0131r'\u0131n alt\u0131nda ne var \u2014 utan\xe7 m\u0131, ret korkusu mu, sevilmeme kayg\u0131s\u0131 m\u0131? Kobra \xf6z\xfcr dilemez; s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131 ger\xe7ektir. Bug\xfcn sen de kendi ger\xe7e\u011finde dur.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn, hayat\u0131n\u0131zdaki bir durumda s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 netle\u015ftirin. Bunu s\xf6ylemek zorunda de\u011filsiniz \u2014 \xf6nce i\xe7inizde net olun. Bir k\xe2\u011f\u0131da \u015funu yaz\u0131n: 'Bu konuda kabul edebileceklerim \u015funlar; kabul edemeyeceklerim \u015funlar.' S\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131 netle\u015ftirmek, kar\u015f\u0131ya sald\u0131rmak de\u011fildir \u2014 kendinize sad\u0131k olmakt\u0131r. Kobran\u0131n g\xfcc\xfc sald\u0131r\u0131dan de\u011fil, netlikten gelir.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Cobra",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["divine protection","kundalini","royal sign","hidden power"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In ancient Egypt the cobra, the uraeus, was the symbol of divine sovereignty and protective power, worked into the pharaohs' headdress. The goddess Wadjet was in cobra form, the sacred eye of fire guarding Lower Egypt; this being who burned enemies and guarded the pharaoh embodies the purest form of power. In Hindu tradition the Naga, the cobra, is the embodiment of Kundalini energy; when this serpent sleeping at the base of the spine awakens, consciousness passes through every chakra and reaches the crown, and enlightenment occurs. The cobra coiled around Shiva's neck symbolizes the embrace of death and transformation; that energy is not to be controlled but to be danced with. In Greek tradition the serpent coiled around the staff of Asclepius is the symbol of healing; it shows that the poisonous is also the healing. In Aztec tradition Quetzalcoatl, the Feathered Serpent, is the greatest symbol of creative divine power; the serpent corresponds to earth and transformation, the feathers to freedom and ascension. In Mesoamerican, Chinese, and African traditions the cobra or great serpents are always seen as possessors of hidden knowledge and protective power. The cobra's medicine: to recognize the sleeping power within you, knowing that it exists not to harm others but to protect yourself and those you love. Its shadow side is using your power unconsciously or in anger; setting boundaries with anger rather than clarity.",dailyMessageEn:"The Cobra awakens within you the sleeping power today. You may not feel it from outside, but inside you there is an energy long suppressed, placed on hold, told 'not now, later.' That energy exists not to attack but to protect you. Today, which boundary you have not drawn clearly is making you feel small? The cobra rises tall before striking; this is a warning, a display of strength, a call not to battle but to protect its own space. Right now, in some situation, in a relationship, or within yourself, you may need that upright stance. Ask yourself: what are you afraid to say 'no' to? What is beneath that 'no', shame, fear of rejection, anxiety about being unloved? The cobra does not apologize; the boundary is real. Today, stand in your own truth.",guidanceEn:"Today, clarify your boundary in one situation in your life. You do not have to speak it; first be clear inside. Write on paper: 'In this matter, what I can accept is this; what I cannot accept is this.' Clarifying boundaries is not attacking the other; it is being faithful to yourself. The cobra's power comes not from attack but from clarity."},{id:"a062",name:"Puma",emoji:"\ud83e\udd81",element:"toprak",symbolism:["sessiz liderlik","yaln\u0131z g\xfc\xe7","gizli cesaret","sab\u0131rl\u0131 eylem"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Mountain_Lion_-_Puma_concolor.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kuzey Amerika Quechua ve Andean gelene\u011finde puma \u2014 puma ya da singa \u2014 toprak ile g\xfcc\xfcn, yerle g\xf6kle aras\u0131ndaki dengeyi koruyan kutsal efendidir. \u0130nka \xfc\xe7 d\xfcnya sembolizminde puma bu d\xfcnyay\u0131 \u2014 Kay Pacha'y\u0131 \u2014 temsil eder; y\u0131lan alt d\xfcnyay\u0131, kondor ise \xfcst d\xfcnyay\u0131. Puma, tam olarak \u015fu an\u0131n hayvan\u0131d\u0131r: ne ge\xe7mi\u015fte ne gelecekte, tam burada. Aztek gelene\u011finde Ocelotl \u2014 b\xfcy\xfck kedi sava\u015f\xe7\u0131s\u0131 \u2014 sessiz ve g\xf6r\xfcnmez hareketiyle d\xfc\u015fman\u0131n yak\u0131n\u0131na kadar sokulur; bu sessiz g\xfc\xe7, hayk\u0131rmaktan \xe7ok daha etkilidir. Kuzey Amerika Cherokee gelene\u011finde puma kutsal bir rehberdir; onun izini g\xf6rmek, do\u011fru yolda oldu\u011funun i\u015fareti say\u0131l\u0131r. Peru halk gelene\u011finde puma da\u011f\u0131n ruhuyla konu\u015fur \u2014 y\xfcksekte, sessizde, yaln\u0131z ya\u015fayan bu hayvan, kalabal\u0131\u011fa de\u011fil derinli\u011fe aittir. Japonya'da kaplan \u2014 pumaya yak\u0131n e\u015fde\u011fer \u2014 sessiz bekleyi\u015f ve tek hamlede kesin eylem ile \xf6zde\u015fle\u015fir; bu Zen anlay\u0131\u015f\u0131nda da kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131k bulur: hareketten \xf6nce gelen derin sessizlik. Puman\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: kendini kan\u0131tlama ihtiyac\u0131 duymadan g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olmak; otoriteyi d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan de\u011fil i\xe7eriden ta\u015f\u0131mak. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: yaln\u0131zl\u0131\u011fa o kadar al\u0131\u015fmak ki yard\u0131m istemeyi, destek almay\u0131 ya da g\xfcven in\u015fa etmeyi unutmak.",dailyMessage:"Puma bug\xfcn sessizli\u011finin g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor. Hi\xe7bir \u015feyi hayk\u0131rarak kan\u0131tlamak zorunda de\u011filsin; en derin g\xfc\xe7, en sessiz harekette sakl\u0131d\u0131r. Bu b\xfcy\xfck kedi av\u0131n\u0131 uzaktan saatlerce izler, sab\u0131rla bekler ve tam an geldi\u011finde tek bir hamleyle hareket eder \u2014 ne erkenden ne gecikmeli. Sen de belki \u015fu an bir \u015feyi hakl\u0131 \xe7\u0131karmak, ba\u015fkalar\u0131na anlatmak, onaylatmak i\xe7in \xe7abal\u0131yorsun. Puma bunu asla yapmaz. Peki sen neden yap\u0131yorsun? \u0130\xe7indeki o sessiz bilgelik, hayat\u0131n\u0131n hangi alan\u0131nda h\xe2l\xe2 kendine g\xfcvenmeni bekliyor? Belki bir karar var ki \xe7oktan verildi ama h\xe2l\xe2 ba\u015fkalar\u0131na sormaya devam ediyorsun. Belki bir \u015feyi yapma hakk\u0131n var ve onu talep etmeni bekliyor. Bug\xfcn kendi i\xe7sel otoritene geri d\xf6n; o ses her zaman oradayd\u0131.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn bir konuda ba\u015fkas\u0131na sormadan kendi karar\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 verin. B\xfcy\xfck bir \u015fey olmas\u0131na gerek yok: ne yiyece\u011finiz, nas\u0131l ge\xe7irece\u011finiz, neye \xf6ncelik verece\u011finiz. Karar\u0131n ard\u0131ndan i\xe7inizden gelen sesle konu\u015fun: bu karar sizi nas\u0131l hissettirdi? Puman\u0131n \xf6\u011fretisi \u015fudur: liderlik d\u0131\u015far\u0131ya de\u011fil, \xf6nce i\xe7eriye yap\u0131lan bir yolculukla ba\u015flar.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Puma / Cougar",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["quiet leadership","solitary power","hidden courage","patient action"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the Quechua and Andean traditions of South America the puma (or singa) is the sacred lord who preserves the balance between earth and power, between ground and sky. In the Incan symbolism of the three worlds the puma represents this world, Kay Pacha; the serpent the lower world, and the condor the upper world. The puma is the animal of the present moment: not in the past, not in the future, but right here. In Aztec tradition the Ocelotl, the great cat warrior, with silent and unseen movement closes the distance to the enemy; this silent strength is far more effective than shouting. In the Cherokee tradition of North America the puma is a sacred guide; to see its tracks is a sign of being on the right path. In Peruvian folk tradition the puma speaks with the spirit of the mountain; this animal living high, in silence, alone, belongs not to the crowd but to depth. In Japan the tiger, the puma's near equivalent, is identified with silent waiting and decisive action in a single stroke; this resonates with the Zen understanding too: the deep silence that precedes motion. The puma's medicine: to be powerful without needing to prove yourself; to carry authority from within rather than from without. Its shadow side is becoming so accustomed to solitude that you forget how to ask for help, to receive support, or to build trust.",dailyMessageEn:"The Puma reminds you today of the strength of your silence. You do not need to prove anything by shouting; the deepest power is hidden in the quietest motion. This great cat watches its prey from afar for hours, waits in patience, and when the exact moment comes acts in a single motion, neither too soon nor too late. Perhaps right now you are exerting yourself to justify something, to explain it to others, to seek their approval. The puma never does this. Why do you? Where in your life is that quiet inner wisdom still waiting for you to trust it? Perhaps there is a decision already made that you keep asking others about. Perhaps there is a thing you have the right to do, and it is waiting for you to claim it. Today, return to your own inner authority; that voice was always there.",guidanceEn:"Make a decision today without asking anyone. It does not have to be a big thing: what to eat, how to spend a moment, what to prioritize. After deciding, speak with the voice that arises within: how did this decision make you feel? The puma's teaching: leadership begins not as a journey outward but as a journey first made inward."},{id:"a063",name:"Su Samuru",emoji:"\ud83e\udda6",element:"su",symbolism:["oyun","kad\u0131n bilgeli\u011fi","\u015fans","ak\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Lontra_canadensis.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kuzey Amerika yerli geleneklerinde \u2014 \xf6zellikle Great Lakes b\xf6lgesinin halklar\u0131nda \u2014 su samuru kad\u0131n bilgeli\u011finin, ne\u015fenin ve suyun kutsal arma\u011fan\u0131n\u0131n simgesidir; bu hayvan nehirlerde oynarken g\xf6rmek, o g\xfcn\xfcn bereketli ge\xe7ece\u011fine i\u015faret say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Kelt gelene\u011finde su samuru \u2014 dobhar-ch\xfa \u2014 su ile toprak aras\u0131nda ya\u015fayan mistik bir varl\u0131kt\u0131r; ger\xe7ekli\u011fin iki katman\u0131 aras\u0131nda \xf6zg\xfcrce ge\xe7i\u015f yapabilen, \u015fekil de\u011fi\u015ftirebilen b\xfcy\xfcl\xfc yarat\u0131k. Slav ve \u0130skandinav folklorunda su ruhlar\u0131 \u2014 rusalka, nixie \u2014 ile ili\u015fkilendirilen su samurunun oyunculu\u011fu, do\u011fan\u0131n ne\u015fe dilinin ta kendisidir; nehirler g\xfcler, hayat akar. Japon gelene\u011finde su samurunun birbirine tak\u0131l\u0131p yuvarlanmas\u0131 ve birlikte kaymas\u0131, uyum i\xe7inde ne\u015fenin simgesidir; bunu izlemek bile \u015fans getirir. \xc7in gelene\u011finde su samurunun keskin zek\xe2s\u0131 ve bal\u0131k tutma ustal\u0131\u011f\u0131, pratik zekan\u0131n oyunla bir arada olabilece\u011fini g\xf6sterir \u2014 \xe7al\u0131\u015fmak ile e\u011flenmek ayn\u0131 \u015fey olabilir. Su samurununun t\u0131bb\u0131: her \u015feyi \xe7ok ciddiye alman\u0131n kimi zaman ger\xe7e\u011fi bulan\u0131kla\u015ft\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6rmek; oyunun kendisi bir bilgelik bi\xe7imidir ve \xf6\u011frenmeyi kolayla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: sorumlulu\u011fu hafife al\u0131p her \u015feyi oyuna d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrerek ger\xe7ek zorluklar\u0131n \xfczerinden ge\xe7mek.",dailyMessage:"Su Samuru bug\xfcn sana hafifli\u011fi hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor \u2014 ve bu, ciddiyetsizlik de\u011fil, bir denge \xe7a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r. Bu hayvan, suyun en h\u0131zl\u0131 ve so\u011fuk b\xf6l\xfcmlerinde dahi oyun oynar; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc ne\u015fe, ko\u015fullara g\xf6re a\xe7\u0131lan bir \u015fey de\u011fildir, her ko\u015fulda i\xe7inde ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n bir \u015feydir. Peki sen? Ka\xe7 zamand\u0131r 'her \u015fey d\xfczelince e\u011flenece\u011fim, o i\u015f bitince rahatlar\u0131m, \u015fu sorun \xe7\xf6z\xfcl\xfcnce g\xfclece\u011fim' diyorsun? Su samuru beklemez. \u015eu an nehirde \u2014 hayat\u0131n tam ortas\u0131nda \u2014 oyun oynar. Bug\xfcn neyle e\u011flenebilirsin? Sadece bir \u015fey: bir yemek, bir \u015fark\u0131, bir g\xfcl\xfc\u015fme, bir an\u0131. Bug\xfcn hayat\u0131nda en \xe7ok y\xfck gibi hissettiren \u015fey nedir \u2014 ve o y\xfck\xfc onbe\u015f dakika kenara b\u0131raksan ne olur? Hi\xe7bir \u015fey de\u011fi\u015fmez, ama sen de\u011fi\u015firsin: biraz daha hafiflersin, biraz daha kendine d\xf6nersin.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn bilin\xe7li olarak bir \u015feyi oyunla yap\u0131n: e\u011fer \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yorsan\u0131z, en yarat\u0131c\u0131 yakla\u015f\u0131mla; e\u011fer temizliyorsan\u0131z, sevdi\u011finiz m\xfczikle; e\u011fer biriyle konu\u015fuyorsan\u0131z, g\xfcl\xfc\u015fmeyi \xf6nce gelen yap\u0131n. Su samuru bize \u015funu \xf6\u011fretir: zihni rahatlatmak i\xe7in izin gerekmiyor. Ne\u015fe, bir \xf6d\xfcl de\u011fil \u2014 bir pratiktir.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Otter",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["play","feminine wisdom","luck","fluidity"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Native American traditions, especially among the peoples of the Great Lakes region, the otter is the symbol of feminine wisdom, joy, and the sacred gift of water; to see this animal playing in the rivers was a sign that the day would be abundant. In Celtic tradition the otter (dobhar-ch\xfa) is a mystical being living between water and earth, a magical creature able to pass freely between the two layers of reality and to change shape. In Slavic and Scandinavian folklore the otter, associated with water spirits (rusalka, nixie), is the very language of nature's joy; the rivers laugh, life flows. In Japanese tradition otters tumbling and sliding together symbolize joy in harmony; even watching them brings luck. In Chinese tradition the otter's sharp intelligence and mastery of fishing show that practical intelligence can coexist with play; working and enjoying can be one and the same. The otter's medicine: to see that taking everything too seriously sometimes blurs the truth; play itself is a form of wisdom and makes learning easier. Its shadow side is treating responsibility too lightly and turning everything into play so as to skip over real difficulties.",dailyMessageEn:"The Otter reminds you today of lightness, and this is not unseriousness but a call to balance. This animal plays even in the fastest and coldest parts of the water, because joy is not something that opens according to conditions but something you carry within regardless of them. And you? How long have you been saying 'when things settle I will enjoy, when that job is done I will rest, when that problem is solved I will laugh'? The otter does not wait. Right now, in the river, in the very middle of life, she plays. What can you enjoy today? Just one thing: a meal, a song, a laugh, a memory. What feels heaviest in your life today, and what would happen if you set that weight down for fifteen minutes? Nothing changes, but you do: a little lighter, a little more returned to yourself.",guidanceEn:"Today do one thing consciously with play: if you are working, with the most creative approach; if you are cleaning, with music you love; if you are talking with someone, put laughter first. The otter teaches: you do not need permission to ease the mind. Joy is not a reward; it is a practice."},{id:"a064",name:"Bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l",emoji:"\ud83e\udda2",element:"su",symbolism:["sab\u0131r","odak","\xf6z-belirlenim","derinlik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Great_Blue_Heron-27527-2.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da Bennu ku\u015fu \u2014 yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n ba\u015flang\u0131c\u0131nda su \xfczerindeki ilk tepede duran ve g\xfcne\u015fi ilk kez \xe7a\u011f\u0131ran kutsal varl\u0131k \u2014 bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131la benzetilir; bu nedenle bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l, yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n, yenilenen her g\xfcn\xfcn ve derin oda\u011f\u0131n simgesidir. \xc7in gelene\u011finde bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l sabr\u0131n ve uzun vadeli bak\u0131\u015f a\xe7\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n simgesidir; bal\u0131k tutarken saatlerce hareketsiz beklemesi, meditasyonun canl\u0131 bedenleni\u015fi gibidir. Kelt gelene\u011finde Ardea \u2014 b\xfcy\xfck bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l \u2014 \xf6z-belirlenim ve yaln\u0131z g\xfcc\xfcn simgesidir; s\xfcr\xfcyle de\u011fil yaln\u0131z ya\u015far, kendi ritmiyle beslenir, kimsenin onay\u0131na ihtiya\xe7 duymaz. Bu \xf6zellik, kalabal\u0131\u011fa ra\u011fmen kendi yolundan gitme cesaretini simgeler. Japon geleneksel sanat\u0131nda bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l zarif ve sessiz varl\u0131\u011f\u0131yla bilgeli\u011fin imgesi olarak tekrar tekrar kullan\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r; en k\xfc\xe7\xfck hareketi bile b\xfcy\xfck bir kas\u0131tla yap\u0131l\u0131r. Kuzey Amerika gelene\u011finde bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l, se\xe7ici olmay\u0131 \xf6\u011fretir \u2014 hangi bal\u0131\u011f\u0131 avlayaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 dikkatle se\xe7er, hepsine ayn\u0131 anda sald\u0131rmaz. Bu, odaklanman\u0131n ve \xf6nceliklendirmenin en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc t\u0131bb\u0131d\u0131r. Bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: do\u011fru an\u0131 bekleyebilmek ve o an geldi\u011finde teredd\xfcts\xfcz hareket etmek \u2014 sab\u0131r ile kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n bir arada bulunmas\u0131. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: beklemenin i\xe7inde donup kalmak; sab\u0131r ad\u0131na hareketi s\xfcresiz ertelemek.",dailyMessage:"Bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l bug\xfcn seni derin, keskin bir odaklanmaya davet ediyor. Bu ku\u015f av\u0131n\u0131 ararken saatlerce k\u0131p\u0131rdamaz \u2014 r\xfczg\xe2r eser, sular dalgalan\u0131r, ku\u015flar \xe7\u0131\u011fl\u0131k atar, o hareket etmez. \xc7\xfcnk\xfc o tam olarak ne arad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 bilir ve o an\u0131 bekler. Sen bu anda ka\xe7 tane farkl\u0131 y\xf6ne birden bak\u0131yorsun? Ka\xe7 d\xfc\u015f\xfcnce, ka\xe7 kayg\u0131, ka\xe7 \xf6ncelik ayn\u0131 anda zihnini me\u015fgul ediyor? Bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l bize \u015funu \xf6\u011fretiyor: her \u015feyi ayn\u0131 anda yapmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015fmak, hi\xe7birini yapmamakla e\u015fde\u011ferdir. Bug\xfcn sadece bir \u015feyi se\xe7. Bir konuya, bir g\xf6reve, bir ili\u015fkiye ya da bir i\xe7sel soruya tam dikkatini ver. O bal\u0131k gelecek \u2014 ama sen de orada, tam uyan\u0131k, tam haz\u0131r olmak zorundas\u0131n. Bu sabah i\xe7in sana bir soru: 'Benim i\xe7in \u015fu an en \xf6nemli olan tek \u015fey nedir?'",guidance:"Bug\xfcn 'tek \u015fey' prati\u011fi yap\u0131n: g\xfcn boyunca yapaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131z i\u015flerin bir listesini \xe7\u0131kar\u0131n, sonra o listeden yaln\u0131zca EN \xf6nemli olan\u0131 daire i\xe7ine al\u0131n. G\xfcn i\xe7inde zihniniz da\u011f\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda, o daireye bak\u0131n ve geri d\xf6n\xfcn. Bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131l y\xfcz bal\u0131\u011f\u0131 de\u011fil, do\u011fru bal\u0131\u011f\u0131 avlar. Siz de bug\xfcn do\u011fru \u015feyi se\xe7in.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Heron",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["patience","focus","self-determination","depth"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In ancient Egypt the Bennu bird, the sacred being standing on the first mound rising from the waters at the beginning of creation and calling forth the sun for the first time, was likened to the heron; therefore the heron symbolizes creation, the renewed beginning of each day, and deep focus. In Chinese tradition the heron symbolizes patience and the long view; standing motionless for hours while fishing, it is meditation made flesh. In Celtic tradition the Ardea, the great heron, symbolizes self-determination and solitary power; not in flocks but alone, feeding by its own rhythm, needing no one's approval. This quality symbolizes the courage to go your own way despite the crowd. In Japanese traditional art the heron, with its graceful and silent presence, has been used again and again as an image of wisdom; even its smallest movement is done with great intent. In North American tradition the heron teaches selectivity; it chooses carefully which fish to catch and does not strike at all of them at once. This is the most powerful medicine of focus and prioritization. The heron's medicine: to wait for the right moment and to act without hesitation when it arrives, patience and resolve together. Its shadow side is freezing within the waiting; postponing action indefinitely in the name of patience.",dailyMessageEn:"The Heron invites you today into a deep, sharp focus. This bird, while seeking its prey, will not stir for hours; the wind blows, the waters ripple, birds cry out, and it does not move. Because it knows exactly what it is looking for and waits for that moment. How many different directions are you looking at right now? How many thoughts, anxieties, priorities are crowding your mind at once? The heron teaches: to try to do everything at once is equivalent to doing none. Today, choose only one thing. Give your full attention to one topic, one task, one relationship, or one inner question. That fish will come, but you must also be there, fully awake, fully ready. A question for this morning: 'What is the single most important thing for me right now?'",guidanceEn:"Today, practice the 'one thing': make a list of what you have to do today, then circle only the MOST important one. When your mind scatters during the day, look at that circle and return. The heron does not catch a hundred fish; it catches the right one. You too, choose the right thing today."},{id:"a065",name:"\xc7akal",emoji:"\ud83d\udc15",element:"toprak",symbolism:["trickster \xf6\u011fretici","s\u0131n\u0131r y\xfcr\xfcy\xfcc\xfcs\xfc","ge\xe7i\u015f rehberi","g\xf6lge bilgeli\u011fi"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Golden_jackal_Canis_aureus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da Anubis \u2014 \xe7akal ba\u015fl\u0131 \xf6l\xfcm tanr\u0131s\u0131 \u2014 ruhlar\u0131 \xf6l\xfcm sonras\u0131nda tartarak \xf6teki d\xfcnyaya ge\xe7i\u015f izni verirdi; kalbi t\xfcyden a\u011f\u0131r olan ruhlar ge\xe7emezdi. \xc7akal burada en \xf6nemli i\u015flevi \xfcstlenir: ger\xe7e\u011fi tartmak, g\xf6r\xfcnmeyeni g\xf6rmek, s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131 i\u015faret etmek. Kuzey Amerika \u015faman gelene\u011finde Coyote \u2014 \xe7akal\u0131n kuzey kolu \u2014 en b\xfcy\xfck trickster \xf6\u011fretmendir; hata yapt\u0131r\u0131r, g\xfcld\xfcr\xfcr, t\xf6kezletir, ama her t\xf6kezlemenin i\xe7inde derin bir ders b\u0131rak\u0131r. Onun \xf6\u011fretisi sahneden de\u011fil, ya\u015fanm\u0131\u015f anlardan ge\xe7er. Meksika ve Aztek gelene\u011finde Coyote, d\xfcnya yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131n \xf6nemli fig\xfcrlerinden biridir; tanr\u0131lar\u0131n hata yapmas\u0131na da izin veren, m\xfckemmeliyet\xe7ili\u011fi k\u0131ran kutsal denge noktas\u0131d\u0131r. Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde Eshu/Elegba \u2014 yol a\u011f\u0131zlar\u0131n\u0131n bek\xe7isi \u2014 \xe7akal\u0131n kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131d\u0131r; her ba\u015flang\u0131c\u0131, her ge\xe7i\u015fi izler, beklenmedik dersleri o getirir. Anadolu halk inanc\u0131nda \xe7akal\u0131n ulumas \u0131 geceyi i\u015faret eder ve kimi b\xf6lgelerde 'yolu de\u011fi\u015ftir' uyar\u0131s\u0131 olarak yorumlan\u0131r. \xc7akal\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: beklenmedik anlarda gelen dersi fark etmek, kendi hatalar\u0131na g\xfclebilmek ve g\xfcl\xfc\u015f\xfcn i\xe7indeki mesaj\u0131 ka\xe7\u0131rmamak. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: her \u015feyi ders olarak g\xf6rerek yorulmak; ya da tersine, dersler gelirken yaln\u0131zca g\xfclerek \xfcst\xfcnden ge\xe7mek.",dailyMessage:"\xc7akal bug\xfcn sana beklenmedik bir yerden bir ders geldi\u011fini haber veriyor. Belki d\xfcn sinir eden bir durum, belki k\xfc\xe7\xfck g\xf6r\xfcnen bir engel, belki g\xfcld\xfc\u011f\xfcn ya da k\xfc\xe7\xfcmsedi\u011fin bir \u015fey \u2014 i\u015fte tam oraya bak. Trickster \xf6\u011fretmenler hi\xe7bir zaman ders kitab\u0131ndan gelmiyor; onlar hayat\u0131n en garip anlar\u0131na saklan\u0131yorlar. \u015eu an hayat\u0131nda seni en \xe7ok \u015fa\u015f\u0131rtan ya da rahats\u0131z eden \u015fey nedir? O rahats\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131n i\xe7inde ne sakl\u0131? \xc7akal g\xfcld\xfcr\xfcrken de \xf6\u011fretir \u2014 ama sen bunu fark etmek i\xe7in g\xfclmenin ortas\u0131nda bir anl\u0131k durup bakabilmek zorundas\u0131n. Bug\xfcn kaybetti\u011fin, mah\xe7up kald\u0131\u011f\u0131n ya da 'yanl\u0131\u015f yapt\u0131m' dedi\u011fin bir \u015feyi hat\u0131rla: o an\u0131n i\xe7inde ne \xf6\u011frendin? Belki hen\xfcz fark etmedin. \xc7akal sab\u0131rl\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 ders anla\u015f\u0131lana kadar farkl\u0131 bi\xe7imlerde gelir.",guidance:"Bu hafta i\xe7inde sizi en \xe7ok rahats\u0131z eden ya da sinir eden bir durumu se\xe7in ve \u015fu soruyu sorun: 'Bu bana ne \xf6\u011fretmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor?' Cevab\u0131 hemen bulmak zorunda de\u011filsiniz \u2014 sadece soruyu a\xe7\u0131k b\u0131rak\u0131n. \xc7akal bize \u015funu \xf6\u011fretiyor: merak, \xf6fkeden \xe7ok daha iyi bir \xf6\u011fretmen tercihidir. Bir not defterine bu soruyu yaz\u0131n ve \xfc\xe7 g\xfcn sonra tekrar bak\u0131n.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Jackal",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["trickster teacher","boundary walker","guide of transitions","shadow wisdom"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In ancient Egypt Anubis, the jackal-headed god of death, weighed souls after death and granted them passage to the next world; souls heavier than a feather could not pass. Here the jackal performs the most important function: to weigh truth, to see the unseen, to mark the boundary. In the North American shamanic tradition Coyote, the jackal's northern cousin, is the greatest trickster teacher; he makes you err, he makes you laugh, he makes you stumble, but within every stumbling he leaves a deep lesson. His teaching comes not from the stage but from lived moments. In Mexican and Aztec tradition Coyote is one of the important figures in the creation of the world; the sacred balance point that permits even the gods to make mistakes and breaks perfectionism. In the Yoruba tradition of Africa Eshu/Elegba, the keeper of the crossroads, is the jackal's counterpart; he watches every beginning, every transition, and brings the unexpected lessons. In Anatolian folk belief the jackal's howling marks the night and in some regions is interpreted as a warning to 'change your path.' The jackal's medicine: to notice the lesson that comes in unexpected moments, to be able to laugh at your own mistakes, and not to miss the message inside the laughter. Its shadow side is exhausting yourself by treating everything as a lesson, or conversely, only laughing your way past the lessons as they come.",dailyMessageEn:"The Jackal brings you news today: a lesson has arrived from an unexpected place. Perhaps a situation that annoyed you yesterday, a seemingly small obstacle, something you laughed at or dismissed, look there. Trickster teachers never come from a textbook; they hide in life's strangest moments. What in your life right now surprises or disturbs you most? What is hidden within that disturbance? The Jackal teaches even while making you laugh, but to notice this you must be able to pause in the middle of laughing and look. Today, remember something you lost, were embarrassed by, or said 'I did wrong' about: what did you learn in that moment? You may not yet have noticed. The Jackal is patient; the lesson returns in different forms until it is understood.",guidanceEn:"Choose a situation this week that annoyed or angered you most and ask: 'What is this trying to teach me?' You do not need to find the answer immediately; just leave the question open. The Jackal teaches: curiosity is a better choice of teacher than anger. Write this question in a notebook and look again three days later."},{id:"a066",name:"Ketsal Ku\u015fu",emoji:"\ud83e\udd9a",element:"hava",symbolism:["\xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck","kutsal g\xfczellik","ilahi renk","esaret kabul etmeme"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Pharomachrus_mocinno.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Aztek ve Maya uygarl\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131n en kutsal ku\u015fu olan Ketsal, Quetzalcoatl'\u0131n \u2014 T\xfcyl\xfc Y\u0131lan Tanr\u0131s\u0131'n\u0131n \u2014 \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck ve bilgelik y\xf6n\xfcn\xfc simgeler; bu ku\u015fun parlak k\u0131rm\u0131z\u0131-ye\u015fil t\xfcyleri, firavunlar\u0131n ve Aztek h\xfck\xfcmdarlar\u0131n\u0131n ta\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 s\xfcslerdi. Ketsal esir al\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131nda ya\u015famay\u0131 reddeder ya da \xe7ok k\u0131sa s\xfcrede \xf6l\xfcrd\xfc \u2014 bu \xf6zellik, \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn ya\u015fam\u0131n kendisinden daha de\u011ferli oldu\u011funun kutsal kan\u0131t\u0131 say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. Maya mitolojisinde ye\u015fil ve k\u0131rm\u0131z\u0131n\u0131n birlikteli\u011fi \u2014 orman ve kan \u2014 ya\u015fam ile \xf6l\xfcm\xfcn, b\xfcy\xfcme ile kurban\u0131n b\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc simgeler; g\xfczellik hi\xe7bir zaman bedelsiz de\u011fildir. G\xfcney Amerika And geleneklerinde Ketsal, Hana Pacha \u2014 \xfcst d\xfcnya \u2014 ile ba\u011flant\u0131l\u0131 ilahi bir habercidir; onu g\xf6rmek b\xfcy\xfck bir \u015fans ve ilahi l\xfctuf say\u0131l\u0131r. Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde Oshun'un tavus t\xfcyleri ve Ketsal'\u0131n t\xfcyleri benzer bi\xe7imde ilahi g\xfczellik ve \xf6zg\xfcr a\u015fk enerjisini simgeler. Hindu gelene\u011finde Krishna'n\u0131n tavus t\xfcyl\xfc tac\u0131 Ketsal'\u0131n t\xfcyleriyle ayn\u0131 ruhani mesaj\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131r: kutsal g\xfczellik, \xf6zg\xfcr bir ruhun i\u015faretidir. Ketsal'\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfc hi\xe7bir konfora, g\xfcvenli\u011fe ya da be\u011fenilme iste\u011fine feda etmemek. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck ad\u0131na her t\xfcrl\xfc ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131ktan, sorumluluktan ya da k\xf6k salmaktan ka\xe7\u0131nmak.",dailyMessage:"Ketsal Ku\u015fu bug\xfcn sana soruyor: hangi kafeste ya\u015f\u0131yorsun? \xc7o\u011fu kafes demir parmakl\u0131klardan de\u011fil, inan\xe7lardan yap\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r: 'Bunu yapamam', 'Bu benim hakk\u0131m de\u011fil', 'Ba\u015fkalar\u0131 ne der', 'Zaten b\xf6yle gidecek' \u2014 bunlar\u0131n hepsi birer parmakl\u0131kt\u0131r. Ketsal esir al\u0131nd\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \xf6l\xfcr \u2014 \xe7\xfcnk\xfc \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfcks\xfcz ya\u015fam, onun i\xe7in ya\u015fam de\u011fildir. Peki sen hangi ko\u015fullar alt\u0131nda ger\xe7ek anlamda '\xf6zg\xfcr' hissediyorsun? Ve o \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfc \u015fu an ka\xe7 \xf6l\xe7\xfcde ya\u015f\u0131yorsun? Belki d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan her \u015fey yolunda g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyor ama i\xe7inde bir s\u0131k\u0131\u015fm\u0131\u015fl\u0131k var, bir bask\u0131, bir 'ben daha fazlas\u0131n\u0131 hak ederim ama s\xf6yleyemiyorum' sesi. Bug\xfcn o sesin ne s\xf6yledi\u011fini dinle. \xd6zg\xfcrl\xfck bir yere ka\xe7mak de\u011fildir \u2014 i\xe7indeki ger\xe7e\u011fe sad\u0131k kalmakt\u0131r. Bug\xfcn o sadakate k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir ad\u0131m at.",guidance:"Bir k\xe2\u011f\u0131da \u015fu soruya cevap verin: 'E\u011fer kimsenin g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfc \xf6nemli olmasayd\u0131, hayat\u0131mda ne farkl\u0131 olurdu?' Bu cevab\u0131n i\xe7inde \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfcz\xfc bulabilirsiniz. Sonra bu cevaptan bir ad\u0131m\u0131 se\xe7in \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck, ama ger\xe7ek. Ketsal'\u0131n t\xfcyleri tek tek b\xfcy\xfcr; \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck de tek tek, bilin\xe7li se\xe7imlerle in\u015fa edilir.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Quetzal",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["freedom","sacred beauty","divine color","refusal of captivity"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The most sacred bird of the Aztec and Mayan civilizations, the Quetzal symbolizes the freedom and wisdom aspect of Quetzalcoatl, the Feathered Serpent god; the bird's brilliant red and green feathers adorned the crowns of pharaohs and Aztec rulers. When captured, the Quetzal refuses to live or dies very quickly; this quality was considered sacred proof that freedom is more valuable than life itself. In Mayan mythology the union of green and red, forest and blood, symbolizes the wholeness of life and death, growth and sacrifice; beauty is never without cost. In the Andean traditions of South America the Quetzal is a divine messenger connected with Hana Pacha, the upper world; to see it is considered great luck and divine grace. In the Yoruba tradition of Africa, Oshun's peacock feathers and the feathers of the Quetzal similarly symbolize divine beauty and the energy of free love. In Hindu tradition the peacock-feather crown of Krishna carries the same spiritual message as the Quetzal's feathers: sacred beauty is the sign of a free soul. The Quetzal's medicine: not to sacrifice freedom for any comfort, security, or desire to be liked. Its shadow side is avoiding all attachment, responsibility, or rootedness in the name of freedom.",dailyMessageEn:"The Quetzal asks you today: in which cage are you living? Most cages are made not of iron bars but of beliefs: 'I cannot do this,' 'This is not my right,' 'What will others say,' 'It will be like this anyway,' each one a bar. When captured, the Quetzal dies, because a life without freedom is, for him, no life. Under what conditions do you feel truly 'free'? And to what degree are you living that freedom right now? Perhaps everything looks fine from the outside but inside there is a constriction, a pressure, a voice saying 'I deserve more but cannot say it.' Listen today to what that voice is saying. Freedom is not running away to a place; it is staying faithful to the truth inside you. Take a small step toward that faithfulness today.",guidanceEn:"Answer this question on paper: 'If no one's opinion mattered, what would be different in my life?' Within that answer you can find your freedom. Then choose one step from that answer, small but real. The Quetzal's feathers grow one by one; freedom too is built through one conscious choice after another."},{id:"a067",name:"Maymun",emoji:"\ud83d\udc12",element:"hava",symbolism:["zeka","yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131k","oyuncu zihin","esneklik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Rhesus_Macaque,_Galta,_Rajasthan,_India.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Hint gelene\u011finin en b\xfcy\xfck maymun tanr\u0131s\u0131 Hanuman \u2014 Rama'ya sonsuz ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131kla hizmet eden ve imk\xe2ns\u0131z\u0131 ba\u015faran kahraman \u2014 g\xfc\xe7l\xfc zek\xe2, al\xe7akg\xf6n\xfcll\xfc hizmet ve s\u0131n\u0131rs\u0131z enerjinin simgesidir; da\u011f\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yabilir, okyanuslar\u0131 a\u015fabilir, ama kendini daima Rama'n\u0131n kula\u011f\u0131nda g\xf6r\xfcr. \xc7in takviminde maymun y\u0131l\u0131, en zeki, en uyumlu ve en yarat\u0131c\u0131 ruhu simgeler \u2014 bu ruhlar ko\u015fullar\u0131 de\u011fi\u015ftirme yetenekleriyle \xf6ne \xe7\u0131kar. Aztek gelene\u011finde Ozomatli \u2014 maymun tanr\u0131s\u0131 \u2014 zanaat, dans ve sanat\u0131n koruyucusudur; yarat\u0131c\u0131 ifadenin kutsal patronudur. Japon k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde \xfc\xe7 maymun \u2014 g\xf6rmezden gel, duymadan gel, konu\u015fmadan gel \u2014 bir bilgelik sistemi olu\u015fturur; dikkat se\xe7icili\u011finin ve zihinsel huzurun simgesidir. Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde Eshu'nun \xe7aresiz ama zeki yard\u0131mc\u0131s\u0131 maymun, h\u0131zl\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcnme ve uyum sa\u011flama kapasitesinin simgesidir. Kuzey Amerika baz\u0131 geleneklerinde ise s\xf6z\xfcn ve sembolik dilin ustas\u0131 olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr. Maymunun t\u0131bb\u0131: zihni esnek tutmak, al\u0131\u015f\u0131lagelen \xe7\xf6z\xfcm yollar\u0131n\u0131n \xf6tesine ge\xe7mek ve her durumun i\xe7inde yarat\u0131c\u0131 bir alternatif aramak. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: zihni \xe7ok aktif tutmak, a\u015f\u0131r\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmek, bir daldan di\u011ferine atlayarak asla bir yerde derinle\u015fememek.",dailyMessage:"Maymun bug\xfcn zihnini esnetmeye ve oynatmaya davet ediyor. Bir problemin \xf6n\xfcnde duruyorsun ve al\u0131\u015f\u0131ld\u0131k yoldan \xe7\xf6zmek ya \xe7al\u0131\u015fm\u0131yor ya da seni t\u0131k\u0131yor. Ama maymun hi\xe7bir zaman tek bir a\u011fac\u0131n dal\u0131na ba\u011fl\u0131 kalmaz \u2014 \xe7\xfcnk\xfc etraf\u0131nda her yanda tutunacak dal vard\u0131r. Senin probleminin de birden fazla \xe7\xf6z\xfcm yolu var. Bug\xfcn \u015funu dene: o sorunu \u015fimdiye kadar hi\xe7 d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmedi\u011fin bir a\xe7\u0131dan bak. Be\u015f ya\u015f\u0131ndaki bir \xe7ocuk nas\u0131l \xe7\xf6zerdi? Ya da ayn\u0131 sorunu tamamen tersine \xe7evirsen ne olur? Maymun yanl\u0131\u015f yap-sil-tekrar mekanizmas\u0131yla \xf6\u011frenir; ilk deneme m\xfckemmel olmak zorunda de\u011fil. Bug\xfcn yanl\u0131\u015f yapma iznini kendinize verin \u2014 \xe7\xfcnk\xfc o 'yanl\u0131\u015f' i\xe7inde do\u011fru yol sakl\u0131 olabilir. Zihnin ne kadar geni\u015f oynayabilir?",guidance:"Tak\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir problemi bug\xfcn k\xe2\u011f\u0131da \xe7izin \u2014 s\xf6zc\xfckle de\u011fil, \u015fekillerle. Sonra etraf\u0131na \xfc\xe7 farkl\u0131 \xe7\xf6z\xfcm yolu \xe7izin. En sa\xe7ma olan\u0131n\u0131 bile yaz\u0131n. Maymun gibi oynay\u0131n: m\xfckemmeliyet\xe7ili\u011fi b\u0131rak\u0131n, olas\u0131l\u0131klar\u0131 serbest b\u0131rak\u0131n. Yarat\u0131c\u0131 zihin, d\xfczeni bozdu\u011funuzda ortaya \xe7\u0131kar.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Monkey",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["intelligence","creativity","playful mind","flexibility"],anatolianMeaningEn:"Hanuman, the greatest monkey god of Hindu tradition, the hero who serves Rama with endless devotion and accomplishes the impossible, is the symbol of strong intelligence, humble service, and boundless energy; he can carry a mountain, cross oceans, yet always sees himself by Rama's ear. In the Chinese calendar the Year of the Monkey symbolizes the smartest, most adaptable, and most creative soul; these spirits stand out for their ability to alter conditions. In Aztec tradition Ozomatli, the monkey god, is the protector of craft, dance, and the arts; the sacred patron of creative expression. In Japanese culture the three monkeys, see no evil, hear no evil, speak no evil, form a system of wisdom; they symbolize the selectivity of attention and the mind's peace. In the Yoruba tradition of Africa Eshu's resourceful and clever helper, the monkey, symbolizes the capacity for swift thinking and adaptation. In some North American traditions he is seen as a master of speech and symbolic language. The monkey's medicine: to keep the mind flexible, to move beyond habitual solutions, and to seek a creative alternative within every situation. Its shadow side is keeping the mind too active, overthinking, leaping from one branch to another and never being able to deepen anywhere.",dailyMessageEn:"The Monkey invites you today to stretch and play with your mind. You stand before a problem and solving it the familiar way is either not working or blocking you. But the monkey is never bound to a single branch of a single tree; there are branches everywhere around it. Your problem too has more than one solution. Try this today: look at the problem from an angle you have never considered. How would a five-year-old solve it? Or what would happen if you reversed the problem entirely? The monkey learns by trial-error-retry; the first attempt does not have to be perfect. Today, give yourself permission to be wrong, because inside that 'wrong' the right path may be hidden. How widely can your mind play?",guidanceEn:"Draw a problem you are stuck on today on paper, with shapes rather than words. Then draw three different solutions around it. Include even the most absurd. Play like a monkey: let go of perfectionism, release possibilities. Creative mind appears when you disrupt order."},{id:"a068",name:"Papa\u011fan",emoji:"\ud83e\udd9c",element:"hava",symbolism:["ileti\u015fim","haf\u0131za","\xf6\u011fretici ses","do\u011fruluk"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Tanimbar_Cockatoo.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Mevl\xe2n\xe2 Cel\xe2leddin Rumi'nin Mesnevi'sinde papa\u011fan, kafese hapsedilmi\u015f insan ruhunun \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011fe hasretini dile getirir \u2014 kendi orijinal sesini arayan, yank\u0131lanmayan bir hakikati aramak yerine tekrara hapsolan varl\u0131\u011f\u0131n simgesidir. Sufi gelene\u011finde papa\u011fan hem tehlikeyi hem de kurtulu\u015fu simgeler: taklit eden zihir, ilahi sesi bast\u0131r\u0131r; ama taklidin fark\u0131na varan bilin\xe7, ger\xe7ek sese d\xf6ner. Hint gelene\u011finde papa\u011fan \u2014 Kamadeva'n\u0131n binitidir \u2014 a\u015fk\u0131n, tutkunun ve duygular\u0131n ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; bu g\xfczel ye\u015fil ku\u015f hem ilhami hem de obsesyonu simgeler. And \u015famanizminde papa\u011fan orman\u0131n bilgesi, renklerin konu\u015fan dilidir; orada ya\u015fanan her \u015feyi kaydeder, geri yans\u0131t\u0131r. Orta Amerika ve Afrika gelene\u011finde renkli ku\u015flar, ileti\u015fimin ve topluluk ba\u011f\u0131n\u0131n simgesidir; onlar\u0131n sesi, kolektif akl\u0131n a\u011fz\u0131ndan \xe7\u0131kan bilgeliktir. Aztek gelene\u011finde papa\u011fan g\xfcne\u015f ile ili\u015fkilidir \u2014 parlak renkleri g\xfcne\u015fin ate\u015fini yans\u0131t\u0131r ve bu \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131n sesle bulu\u015ftu\u011fu yerde kutsal ileti\u015fim do\u011far. Papa\u011fan\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: yans\u0131tma g\xfcc\xfc \u2014 ba\u015fkas\u0131na s\xf6yledi\u011fimizi kendi kulaklar\u0131m\u0131zla duymak ve kendi \xf6\u011f\xfctlerimize uymak. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: kendi sesi olmadan ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131 taklit etmek; s\xf6zc\xfcklerin anlam\u0131n\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131madan tekrar etmek.",dailyMessage:"Papa\u011fan bug\xfcn sana bir ayna tutuyor \u2014 ve bu aynada kendi sesini duyacaks\u0131n. Son zamanlarda birine ne s\xf6yledin? Hangi tavsiyeyi, hangi ger\xe7e\u011fi, hangi cesaretlendirmeyi aktard\u0131n? \u015eimdi bir saniye dur: o tavsiyeyi sen kendine veriyor musun? Papa\u011fan ilgin\xe7 bir paradoks ta\u015f\u0131r: en iyi taklit\xe7idir, ama bir noktada o taklit ger\xe7ek sese d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr \u2014 yeterince tekrar edince s\xf6zc\xfckler anlam kazan\u0131r. Belki sana da \u015fimdi bu ger\xe7ek: kendinize s\xfcrekli \xf6\u011f\xfctledi\u011finiz ama hi\xe7 uygulamad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z \u015fey nedir? Sabah kalk\u0131n, g\xfcne g\xfczel ba\u015flay\u0131n, kendi de\u011ferlerinize sad\u0131k olun \u2014 bunlar\u0131 s\xf6yl\xfcyorsunuz ba\u015fkas\u0131na, peki ya kendinize? Bug\xfcn o tavsiyeyi bir g\xfcn, sadece bir g\xfcn i\xe7in kendinize uygulay\u0131n. Papa\u011fan\u0131n sesi en g\xfczel, g\xf6n\xfclden geldi\u011finde \xe7\u0131kar.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn kendinize en s\u0131k verdi\u011finiz tavsiyeyi yaz\u0131n. Sonra bu tavsiyeyi hayat\u0131n\u0131za nas\u0131l uygulayabilece\u011finize dair \xfc\xe7 somut ad\u0131m belirleyin. Yar\u0131n sabah bu listeye bak\u0131n. Papa\u011fan bize \u015funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131r: s\xf6ylemek, bilmek demektir; yapmak ise anlamak.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Parrot",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["communication","memory","instructive voice","truthfulness"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Mevlana Jalaluddin Rumi's Masnavi, the parrot voices the longing of the human soul trapped in a cage for its freedom; he is the symbol of the being who searches for his own original voice and, instead of seeking a truth without echo, becomes imprisoned in repetition. In the Sufi tradition the parrot symbolizes both danger and deliverance: the imitating mind drowns out the divine voice, but the awareness that recognizes the imitation returns to the true voice. In Hindu tradition the parrot is the mount of Kamadeva, the carrier of love, passion, and emotion; this beautiful green bird symbolizes both inspiration and obsession. In Andean shamanism the parrot is the sage of the forest, the speaking tongue of colors; it records and reflects back everything that occurs there. In Central American and African traditions colorful birds symbolize communication and community bonding; their voice is the wisdom that issues from the mouth of the collective mind. In Aztec tradition the parrot is connected with the sun; its bright colors reflect the sun's fire, and where this light meets voice, sacred communication is born. The parrot's medicine: the power of reflection, hearing with our own ears what we say to another and following our own counsel. Its shadow side is imitating others without one's own voice; repeating words without carrying their meaning.",dailyMessageEn:"The Parrot holds up a mirror to you today, and in this mirror you will hear your own voice. What have you said to someone recently? Which piece of advice, which truth, which encouragement did you offer? Pause now for a second: are you giving that advice to yourself? The parrot carries a curious paradox: it is the best mimic, yet at a certain point that mimicry turns into a true voice; through enough repetition the words gain meaning. Perhaps this is now true for you: what do you constantly counsel yourself but never practice? Rise in the morning, begin the day well, stay faithful to your own values, you say these things to others, but what about to yourself? Today, apply that advice to yourself for one day, only one day. The parrot's voice is most beautiful when it comes from the heart.",guidanceEn:"Write down the advice you most often give yourself today. Then identify three concrete steps for applying this advice to your life. Look at this list tomorrow morning. The parrot reminds us: saying is knowing; doing is understanding."},{id:"a069",name:"Bizon",emoji:"\ud83e\uddac",element:"toprak",symbolism:["kutsal bereket","minnettarl\u0131k","topluluk","g\xfc\xe7"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/American_bison_k5680-1.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kuzey Amerika Lakota, Cheyenne ve Sioux geleneklerinde Bizon \u2014 Tatanka \u2014 kutsal bereketin ve b\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfcn simgesidir; bu hayvan \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcld\xfc\u011f\xfcnde hi\xe7bir par\xe7as\u0131 ziyan edilmez, her \u015feyi bir ba\u011f\u0131\u015f olarak kabul edilir. B\xfcy\xfck Bizon Ruhu \u2014 Wakan Tanka'n\u0131n bir tezah\xfcr\xfc olarak \u2014 t\xfcm ya\u015fayan varl\u0131klar\u0131n birbirine ba\u011fl\u0131 oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlatan en b\xfcy\xfck \xf6\u011fretmendir. Kuzey Amerika gelene\u011finde Beyaz Bizon \u0130ne\u011fi'nin \u2014 White Buffalo Calf Woman'\u0131n \u2014 geli\u015fiyle yeni bir \xe7a\u011f\u0131n a\xe7\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131na ve insanlar\u0131n minnettarl\u0131k yoluna d\xf6nece\u011fine inan\u0131l\u0131r. Keltlerin kutsal inek-\xf6k\xfcz gelene\u011fiyle bizonun g\xfcc\xfc \xf6rt\xfc\u015f\xfcr; her ikisi de topra\u011f\u0131n bereketi, topluluk ve c\xf6mertlik ruhunu simgeler. Tibet B\xf6n gelene\u011finde yak \u2014 kutsal inek gibi \u2014 hem beslenmeyi hem de ruhsal g\xfcc\xfc tek bedende ta\u015f\u0131r; kutsall\u0131k ve pratik hizmet ayn\u0131 varl\u0131kta bir arada bulunur. Hint gelene\u011finde kutsal inek t\xfcm bereketi sembolize eder; ine\u011fe zarar vermek t\xfcm bollu\u011fun kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 kapatmak anlam\u0131na gelir. Bizonun t\u0131bb\u0131: sahip olunan her \u015feyi ba\u011f\u0131\u015f olarak g\xf6rmek; minnettarl\u0131k, bereketini art\u0131rman\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc yoludur. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o kadar verimli ve g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olmak ki kendi ihtiya\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 ihmal etmek; s\xfcr\xfc i\xe7in her \u015feyi feda ederken kendini t\xfcketmek.",dailyMessage:"Bizon bug\xfcn seni derin bir minnettarl\u0131\u011fa davet ediyor \u2014 ama bu s\u0131radan, g\xf6rev gibi hissedilen bir \u015f\xfck\xfcr de\u011fil. Lakota gelene\u011finde bizon \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcld\xfckten sonra her par\xe7as\u0131 i\xe7in ayr\u0131 ayr\u0131 dua edilirdi \u2014 kemi\u011fi, derisi, eti, i\xe7i, hi\xe7biri bo\u015fa gitmezdi. Bu, varl\u0131\u011f\u0131n b\xfct\xfcn\xfcyle kabul edilmesiydi. Sen bug\xfcn hayat\u0131nda neye bu dikkati ve \u015f\xfckr\xfc veriyorsun? Zorluklar, engeller, kay\u0131plar bile \u2014 bunlar da seni bir \u015fekilde beslemi\u015ftir, g\xfc\xe7lendirmi\u015ftir, d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrm\xfc\u015ft\xfcr. Bug\xfcn zorluklar\u0131na bile minnettar olabilir misin? Bu soruyla otur bir s\xfcre. Bizonun b\xfcy\xfckl\xfc\u011f\xfc yaln\u0131zca fiziksel de\u011fildir \u2014 o b\xfcy\xfckl\xfck, verdi\u011fi arma\u011fan\u0131n tamam\u0131nda gizlidir. Senin de verdi\u011fin, ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n, payla\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n \u015feylerin tamam\u0131 bir arma\u011fand\u0131r. Bug\xfcn bunu fark eden bir an yarat.",guidance:"Bu ak\u015fam k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir rit\xfcel yap\u0131n: bug\xfcn hayat\u0131n\u0131za dokunan \xfc\xe7 \u015feye \u2014 b\xfcy\xfck ya da k\xfc\xe7\xfck, g\xfczel ya da zor \u2014 i\xe7ten bir te\u015fekk\xfcr edin. Bunlar\u0131 sesli s\xf6yleyin ya da yaz\u0131n. Minnettarl\u0131k prati\u011fi beynin reward sistemini aktive eder ve bak\u0131\u015f a\xe7\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 ger\xe7ekten de\u011fi\u015ftirir. Bizon her g\xfcn\xfc ba\u011f\u0131\u015f olarak g\xf6r\xfcr; siz de bug\xfcn \xf6yle yap\u0131n.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Bison",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["sacred abundance","gratitude","community","strength"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the Lakota, Cheyenne, and Sioux traditions of North America the Bison, Tatanka, is the symbol of sacred abundance and wholeness; when this animal is killed no part of it is wasted, every part is accepted as a gift. The Great Bison Spirit, as a manifestation of Wakan Tanka, is the greatest teacher reminding us that all living beings are interconnected. In North American tradition it is believed that with the arrival of the White Buffalo Calf Woman a new age opens and people return to the path of gratitude. The strength of the bison overlaps with the Celtic tradition of the sacred cow-ox; both symbolize the fertility of the earth, community, and the spirit of generosity. In the Tibetan B\xf6n tradition the yak, like the sacred cow, carries nourishment and spiritual strength in one body; sanctity and practical service coexist in the same being. In Hindu tradition the sacred cow symbolizes all abundance; to harm a cow is to close the door to all plenty. The bison's medicine: to see everything you possess as a gift; gratitude is the strongest way to increase abundance. Its shadow side is being so productive and strong that you neglect your own needs, sacrificing everything for the herd while exhausting yourself.",dailyMessageEn:"The Bison invites you today into deep gratitude, and this is not an ordinary, dutiful thanks. In Lakota tradition after the bison was killed, a separate prayer was offered for each part, the bone, the hide, the meat, the inside; none went to waste. This was the acceptance of a being in its wholeness. To what do you give this attention and gratitude in your life today? Difficulties, obstacles, even losses, these too have nourished, strengthened, and transformed you in some way. Can you be grateful even for your difficulties today? Sit with this question a while. The bison's greatness is not only physical; that greatness is hidden in the completeness of the gift it offers. Everything you give, carry, and share is also a gift in its wholeness. Today, create a moment in which you notice this.",guidanceEn:"Perform a small ritual this evening: offer heartfelt thanks to three things, great or small, beautiful or hard, that touched your life today. Speak them aloud or write them. The practice of gratitude activates the brain's reward system and truly changes your perspective. The bison sees each day as a gift; do the same today."},{id:"a070",name:"Kanguru",emoji:"\ud83e\udd98",element:"toprak",symbolism:["ileri at\u0131l\u0131\u015f","yolculuk","s\u0131\xe7rama cesareti","ana\xe7 g\xfc\xe7"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Kangaroo_Australia_filtered.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Avustralya Aborijin R\xfcya Zaman\u0131 \u2014 Dreamtime \u2014 gelene\u011finde kanguru en kutsal Totem hayvanlardan biridir; onun geri gitememesi, yaln\u0131zca ileri atlayabilmesi, ileriye bak\u0131\u015f\u0131n, de\u011fi\u015fimin ve yolculu\u011fun kutsal i\u015fareti say\u0131l\u0131r. Kanguru hareketini arka bacaklar\u0131 ve kuyru\u011fuyla sa\u011flar; \xfc\xe7 destek noktas\u0131 onu kararl\u0131 ve g\xfc\xe7l\xfc k\u0131lar \u2014 bu, denge i\xe7inde ilerlemenin simgesidir. Aborijin anlat\u0131mlar\u0131nda kanguru, Ata ruhlar\u0131n\u0131n yery\xfcz\xfcndeki tezah\xfcrlerinden biridir; toprak \xfczerinde b\u0131rakt\u0131\u011f\u0131 izler, R\xfcya Yollar\u0131'n\u0131n bir par\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r. And \u015famanizminde buna yak\u0131n hayvan Vicu\xf1a'd\u0131r \u2014 kutsal ilerlemenin ve ana\xe7l\u0131\u011f\u0131n simgesi olan bu hayvan, yavrular\u0131n\u0131 karn\u0131nda ya da yan\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131yarak b\xfcy\xfcterek toplum i\xe7in \xf6\u011fretmenlik yapar. Maori gelene\u011finde (Yeni Zelanda) ileriye bakma ve ge\xe7mi\u015ften ders alarak yeni bir yol a\xe7ma en \xf6nemli erdemler aras\u0131ndad\u0131r; kanguru bu anlay\u0131\u015f\u0131n hayvan bedeni gibidir. Afrika Zulu gelene\u011finde g\xfc\xe7l\xfc atlayan hayvanlar, engellerini a\u015fan, s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131 ge\xe7en ruhlar olarak sayg\u0131 g\xf6r\xfcr. Kangurunun t\u0131bb\u0131: ge\xe7mi\u015fe d\xf6nme yetene\u011finin yoklu\u011fu bir k\u0131s\u0131tlama de\u011fil, ileri gitme zorunlulu\u011funun kutsal arma\u011fan\u0131d\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o denli h\u0131zl\u0131 ileriye atlamak ki k\xf6kleri unutmak; her zaman hareket etmek ama asla yerle\u015fememek.",dailyMessage:"Kanguru bug\xfcn sana yaln\u0131zca bir y\xf6n oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor: ileri. Bu \xf6yle s\u0131radan bir ilerleme de\u011fil \u2014 ge\xe7mi\u015fe fiziksel olarak d\xf6nememe zorunlulu\u011funu bilin\xe7li bir se\xe7ime d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrm\xfc\u015f bir varl\u0131\u011f\u0131n hareketi. Sen bu anda ge\xe7mi\u015fte tutunmaya, orada bir \u015feyleri yeniden \xe7\xf6zmeye, orada kalm\u0131\u015f bir hasreti ya da pi\u015fmanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131maya \xe7abal\u0131yor olabilirsin. Peki o ge\xe7mi\u015f seni bug\xfcn besliyor mu, yoksa sadece a\u011f\u0131rla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131yor mu? Kanguru yavrusunu karn\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131r \u2014 bir \u015feyleri ta\u015f\u0131mak normaldir, ama zaman\u0131 gelince b\u0131rakmak da gereklidir. \u015eu an hangi ge\xe7mi\u015fi karn\u0131nda ta\u015f\u0131maya devam ediyorsun ki art\u0131k b\xfcy\xfcd\xfc ve seni t\u0131k\u0131yor? O s\u0131\xe7ramay\u0131 yapman i\xe7in ger\xe7ekte neye ihtiyac\u0131n var? Bug\xfcn o ad\u0131m\u0131 atmak i\xe7in haz\u0131r oldu\u011funu hisset.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn tamamlanmam\u0131\u015f b\u0131rakt\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir \u015feyi bitirin \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir g\xf6rev, bir konu\u015fma ya da bir karar. Bitirme eylemi, zihnin 'bitmemi\u015f d\xf6ng\xfcler'inden kurtulmas\u0131n\u0131 sa\u011flar ve yeni ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7lar i\xe7in alan a\xe7ar. Kanguru gibi, kuyru\u011funuzu sabit tutun, arka bacaklar\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 haz\u0131rlay\u0131n ve atlay\u0131n.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Kangaroo",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["forward leap","journey","courage to leap","maternal strength"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the Dreamtime tradition of the Australian Aborigines the kangaroo is one of the most sacred totem animals; its inability to move backward, its capacity only to leap forward, is the sacred sign of looking forward, of change, of the journey. The kangaroo's movement is supported by its hind legs and tail; three points of support make it stable and strong, symbolizing advancing within balance. In Aboriginal narratives the kangaroo is one of the earthly manifestations of the Ancestor spirits; the tracks it leaves on the earth are part of the Dreaming Tracks. In Andean shamanism the closest animal is the Vicu\xf1a, symbol of sacred forward movement and motherhood; this animal teaches the community by raising its young while carrying them in its belly or beside it. In Maori tradition (New Zealand) looking forward and opening a new path through lessons of the past is among the highest virtues; the kangaroo is the animal body of this understanding. In African Zulu tradition strongly leaping animals are honored as spirits that overcome obstacles and cross boundaries. The kangaroo's medicine: the absence of the ability to go back is not a constraint but the sacred gift of the necessity to go forward. Its shadow side is leaping forward so quickly that you forget your roots; always moving but never settling.",dailyMessageEn:"The Kangaroo reminds you today that there is only one direction: forward. This is not ordinary progress; it is the movement of a being that has transformed the inability to physically return to the past into a conscious choice. Right now, you may be striving to hold onto the past, to resolve something there again, to carry a longing or regret that has stayed there. Is that past nourishing you today or only weighing you down? The kangaroo carries her young in her belly; carrying something is normal, but when the time comes it is necessary to let go. Which past are you still carrying in your belly that has now outgrown the space and is blocking you? What do you truly need in order to make that leap? Today, sense that you are ready to take that step.",guidanceEn:"Finish today something you left unfinished: a small task, a conversation, or a decision. The act of completion releases the mind from 'unfinished loops' and makes room for new beginnings. Like the kangaroo, steady your tail, ready your hind legs, and leap."},{id:"a071",name:"Ren Geyi\u011fi",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8c",element:"toprak",symbolism:["\u015faman arac\u0131","kozmik yolculuk","ata ba\u011flant\u0131s\u0131","rehberlik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Rangifer_tarandus_-_Wrangel_Island.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Sibirya ve Altay \u015famanizminde ren geyi\u011fi, \u015faman\u0131n \xfc\xe7 d\xfcnya aras\u0131ndaki kozmik yolculu\u011funun kutsal binitidir; \u015faman davuluna ren derisi gerilir ve bu ses, o yolculu\u011fun kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7ar. Altay destanlar\u0131nda kahraman d\xfcnyan\u0131n d\xf6rt k\xf6\u015fesine ren geyi\u011finin s\u0131rt\u0131nda gider \u2014 hayvan, d\xfcnyalar aras\u0131 otoyolun kutsal arac\u0131d\u0131r. Sami gelene\u011finde \u2014 Kuzey \u0130skandinav halklar\u0131n\u0131n en eski geleneklerinden biri \u2014 ren geyi\u011fi hem fiziksel hem ruhsal beslenmenin kayna\u011f\u0131d\u0131r; noaidi (\u015faman) bu hayvan\u0131n ruhsal rehberli\u011fiyle \xf6teki d\xfcnyaya yolculuk yapar. Norse mitolojisinde Yggdrasil'i \u2014 evrenin a\u011fac\u0131n\u0131 \u2014 kemiren d\xf6rt geyik, zaman\u0131n d\xf6rt boyutunu simgeler; geyik, evrensel bilginin ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131c\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r. Kelt gelene\u011finde Cernunnos \u2014 boynuzlu tanr\u0131 \u2014 geyikle \xf6zde\u015fle\u015fir ve her iki d\xfcnyan\u0131n aras\u0131ndaki s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131 temsil eder; o s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131 ge\xe7ebilmek, derin bilgelikle m\xfcmk\xfcnd\xfcr. Kuzey Amerika Anishinaabe gelene\u011finde geyik zarafet ve sezginin simgesidir; onun do\u011fada sessizce hareket etmesi, \xe7evrenin her sesini dinleyerek ya\u015famas\u0131n\u0131n sonucudur. Ren Geyi\u011finin t\u0131bb\u0131: atalardan gelen bilgeli\u011fi ta\u015f\u0131mak ve o bilgeli\u011fi kozmik yolculukta rehber yapmak; ge\xe7mi\u015fin sesini dinleyerek \u015fimdinin yolunu bulmak. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: ata bilgeli\u011fine o kadar yaslanmak ki kendi ki\u015fisel ke\u015ffinin kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 kapatmak.",dailyMessage:"Ren Geyi\u011fi bug\xfcn seni bilmedi\u011fin bir yere g\xf6t\xfcrmeye haz\u0131r \u2014 ve o yolda rehberin atalar\u0131ndan gelen, i\xe7inde sakl\u0131 bir bilgeliktir. Bu bilgeli\u011fi bir kitapta ya da \xf6\u011fretmende aramana gerek yok; o senin damarlar\u0131nda, sezginde, v\xfccudunun haf\u0131zas\u0131nda ya\u015f\u0131yor. Bug\xfcn i\xe7g\xfcd\xfclerine tam olarak kulak verdin mi? Bir \u015feyden uzak durma hissi, ya da tam tersine bir \u015feye do\u011fru g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir \xe7ekilme \u2014 o sinyaller rastgele de\u011fildir. Ren geyi\u011fi karanl\u0131kta bile yolu bulur \xe7\xfcnk\xfc i\xe7sel bir pusulayla hareket eder; sen de b\xf6yle bir pusulayla do\u011fuyorsun. \u015eu an hayat\u0131nda hangi konuda i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcn bir \u015fey s\xf6yl\xfcyor ama akl\u0131n onu susturuyor? Bug\xfcn o sese biraz daha fazla g\xfcvenmeyi dene \u2014 bir ad\u0131m, k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama ger\xe7ek. Nereden geldi\u011fini bilmek, nereye gitti\u011fini anlamana yard\u0131mc\u0131 olur.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn sessiz bir yerde oturun ve atalara ya da ge\xe7mi\u015fe bir ba\u011flant\u0131 kurun: bir foto\u011frafa bak\u0131n, sevdi\u011finiz biri hakk\u0131nda bir an\u0131y\u0131 hat\u0131rlay\u0131n ya da onlar\u0131n size s\xf6yledi\u011fi bir s\xf6z\xfc hat\u0131rlay\u0131n. Sonra \u015funu sorun: 'O ki\u015fi bug\xfcn bana ne derdi?' Bu cevap, i\xe7inizdeki ata bilgeli\u011finin sesidir. Ren Geyi\u011finin \xf6\u011fretisi: yolculuk daha \xf6nce yap\u0131lm\u0131\u015f; siz sadece kendi versiyonunuzu ya\u015f\u0131yorsunuz.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Reindeer",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["shamanic vehicle","cosmic journey","ancestor connection","guidance"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Siberian and Altai shamanism the reindeer is the sacred mount of the shaman's cosmic journey among the three worlds; reindeer hide is stretched over the shaman's drum, and that sound opens the doors of that journey. In Altai epics the hero travels to the four corners of the world on the back of the reindeer; the animal is the sacred vehicle of the highway between worlds. In Sami tradition, one of the most ancient traditions of the Northern Scandinavian peoples, the reindeer is the source of both physical and spiritual nourishment; the noaidi (shaman) journeys to the other world through this animal's spiritual guidance. In Norse mythology the four stags that gnaw Yggdrasil, the world tree, symbolize the four dimensions of time; the stag is the carrier of universal knowledge. In Celtic tradition Cernunnos, the horned god, is identified with the stag and represents the boundary between the two worlds; the ability to cross that boundary is possible with deep wisdom. In the Anishinaabe tradition of North America the deer is the symbol of grace and intuition; its silent movement through nature is the result of living by listening to every sound of the environment. The reindeer's medicine: to carry ancestral wisdom and make that wisdom your guide in the cosmic journey; to find the way of the present by listening to the voice of the past. Its shadow side is leaning so heavily on ancestral wisdom that you close the door to your own personal discovery.",dailyMessageEn:"The Reindeer is ready to carry you today to a place you do not know, and on that road your guide is a wisdom from your ancestors hidden inside you. You do not need to seek this wisdom in a book or a teacher; it lives in your blood, your intuition, the memory of your body. Today, did you fully listen to your instincts? The sense of staying away from something, or on the contrary a strong pull toward something, those signals are not random. The reindeer finds its path even in darkness because it moves by an inner compass; you too are born with such a compass. In which area of your life right now is your instinct saying something while your mind silences it? Today, try trusting that voice a little more, a small but real step. Knowing where you come from helps you understand where you are going.",guidanceEn:"Sit in a quiet place today and make a connection to your ancestors or your past: look at a photograph, remember a memory of someone you loved, or recall a word they said to you. Then ask: 'What would that person say to me today?' This answer is the voice of the ancestral wisdom inside you. The Reindeer's teaching: the journey has been traveled before; you are simply living your own version."},{id:"a072",name:"Kirpi",emoji:"\ud83e\udd94",element:"toprak",symbolism:["savunma","i\xe7g\xf6zlem","yava\u015f bilgelik","dikkatli ad\u0131m"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Erinaceus_europaeus_LC0119.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Anadolu halk gelene\u011finde kirpi \u015feytan\u0131 ve k\xf6t\xfc ruhu def eden bir koruyucu olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr; evlere yak\u0131n ya\u015famas\u0131 onun ev ruhlar\u0131yla akraba oldu\u011funa i\u015faret eder. \u0130ran edebiyat\u0131nda zek\xe2s\u0131yla g\xfc\xe7l\xfc d\xfc\u015fmanlar\u0131n\u0131 alt eden k\xfc\xe7\xfck kahraman olarak yer alan kirpi, ufak bedenin i\xe7indeki muazzam zek\xe2n\u0131n simgesidir. Slav folklorunda kirpi \u2014 hedgehog \u2014 mevsim ge\xe7i\u015flerinin habercisidir; bahar\u0131n geli\u015fini ya da k\u0131\u015f\u0131n sertli\u011fini \xf6ng\xf6rebilir, bu nedenle do\u011fa\xfcst\xfc bir sezgiyle donat\u0131lm\u0131\u015f say\u0131l\u0131r. Kelt gelene\u011finde kirpi topra\u011f\u0131n ve gece sezgisinin bilgesidir; dikenlerinin kendisi bile bir \xf6\u011freti ta\u015f\u0131r: kim yakla\u015fabilir, kim yakla\u015famaz \u2014 bunu v\xfccudu otomatik olarak belirler. Roma gelene\u011finde kirpi meyveler ta\u015f\u0131yan bir varl\u0131k olarak bilinir \u2014 bir me\u015fe palamudu s\u0131rt\u0131na alarak evi besler; k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama \xe7al\u0131\u015fkan, sessiz ama verimli. Kuzey Afrika Berberi gelene\u011finde kirpi b\xfcy\xfcye kar\u015f\u0131 koruyucu bir g\xfcce sahiptir ve nazardan koruyan muska olarak kullan\u0131l\u0131r. Kirpinin t\u0131bb\u0131: kendi s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 ve ihtiya\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 dikenler gibi net ta\u015f\u0131mak; kim oldu\u011funu, ne istedi\u011fini ve neye izin verece\u011fini bilmek. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: savunma mekanizmas\u0131 o kadar aktif olmak ki ger\xe7ek yak\u0131nla\u015fmay\u0131 da engellemek, sevgiyi bile uzakta tutmak.",dailyMessage:"Kirpi bug\xfcn seni yava\u015flamaya ve dikkatli ad\u0131m atmaya davet ediyor. Bu k\xfc\xe7\xfck hayvan tela\u015fla hareket etmez \u2014 geceyi yava\u015f\xe7a ke\u015ffeder, durup dinler, geri \xe7ekilir ve devam eder. Sezgisi her ad\u0131m\u0131n\u0131 y\xf6nlendirir. Sen bu anda ka\xe7 tane uyar\u0131 sinyalini g\xf6rmezden geliyorsun \xe7\xfcnk\xfc h\u0131zl\u0131 ilerlemek istiyorsun? Kirpinin dikenler bir sald\u0131r\u0131 arac\u0131 de\u011fildir \u2014 sadece bir 'buraya kadar' s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131d\u0131r. Senin de b\xf6yle s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n var, ama onlar\u0131 net ifade ediyor musun? Bug\xfcn kendine sor: hangi ili\u015fkide, hangi durumda ya da hangi y\xfck\xfcml\xfcl\xfckte 'hay\u0131r' demek istiyorsun ama demiyorsun? Dikenlerin bir i\u015flevi var \u2014 i\xe7ini korumak. Bu koruma sa\u011fl\u0131kl\u0131; onu su\xe7luluk duymadan ta\u015f\u0131yabilirsin. Bug\xfcn bir \u015feye hay\u0131r demeden \xf6nce i\xe7inde nas\u0131l hissetti\u011fine bak \u2014 cevap zaten orada.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn h\u0131zl\u0131 cevap vermek yerine, birinin size bir \u015fey sordu\u011funda 'D\xfc\u015f\xfcneyim' deyin. Bu k\xfc\xe7\xfck duraklama, sizi i\xe7inizle temasa ge\xe7irir. Kirpi dikenlerini an\u0131nda \xe7\u0131karmaz \u2014 gelen tehdidin ger\xe7ek mi oldu\u011funu \xf6nce hisseder. Siz de bug\xfcn bir kez, reflekslerinizden de\u011fil bilin\xe7li bir se\xe7imden hareket edin.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Hedgehog",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["defense","introspection","slow wisdom","careful step"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Anatolian folk tradition the hedgehog is seen as a protector that wards off the devil and evil spirits; its living near homes points to its kinship with the household spirits. In Persian literature the hedgehog appears as the little hero who defeats stronger enemies with cleverness, the symbol of immense intelligence within a tiny body. In Slavic folklore the hedgehog is the herald of seasonal change; it can foresee the arrival of spring or the harshness of winter and is therefore endowed with a supernatural intuition. In Celtic tradition the hedgehog is the sage of earth and night intuition; its very spines carry a teaching, who may approach and who may not, its body decides automatically. In Roman tradition the hedgehog is known as a fruit-bearer, taking an acorn on its back to feed the home; small but industrious, silent but productive. In the Berber tradition of North Africa the hedgehog has a protective power against magic and is used as an amulet against the evil eye. The hedgehog's medicine: to carry your boundaries and needs as clearly as your spines, to know who you are, what you want, and what you will allow. Its shadow side is having defenses so active that you also block genuine closeness, keeping even love at a distance.",dailyMessageEn:"The Hedgehog invites you today to slow down and step carefully. This small animal does not move in haste; it explores the night slowly, pauses to listen, withdraws, and continues. Its intuition guides every step. How many warning signals are you ignoring right now because you want to move quickly? The hedgehog's spines are not a tool of attack; they are simply a 'this far' boundary. You have such boundaries too, but are you expressing them clearly? Ask yourself today: in which relationship, situation, or obligation do you want to say 'no' but are not? Spines have a function: to protect what is inside. This protection is healthy; you can carry it without guilt. Today, before saying yes to something, look at how you feel inside; the answer is already there.",guidanceEn:"Instead of answering quickly today, when someone asks you something, say 'Let me think.' This small pause puts you in contact with yourself. The hedgehog does not raise its spines instantly; it first senses whether the incoming threat is real. You too, just once today, move from a conscious choice rather than from reflex."},{id:"a073",name:"Kertenkele",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8e",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["r\xfcya","g\xfcne\u015f enerjisi","h\u0131zl\u0131 adaptasyon","yeniden do\u011fu\u015f"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Green_iguana_on_a_tree.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kuzey Amerika Pueblo ve Navajo geleneklerinde kertenkele \u2014 \xf6zellikle Gila canavar\u0131 ve iguana \u2014 r\xfcya d\xfcnyas\u0131n\u0131n bek\xe7isidir; g\xfcne\u015fte \u0131s\u0131narak g\xfc\xe7 toplayan bu varl\u0131k, gece ve g\xfcnd\xfcz aras\u0131ndaki ge\xe7i\u015fin simgesidir. And \u015famanizminde kertenkele g\xfcne\u015fin s\u0131cakl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 do\u011frudan kana i\u015fleyen bir varl\u0131k olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr; bu nedenle ya\u015fam enerjisini harekete ge\xe7irmenin ve i\xe7sel \u0131s\u0131y\u0131 uyand\u0131rman\u0131n simgesidir. M\u0131s\u0131r hiyeroglif gelene\u011finde kertenkele bol ve bereketle \xf6zde\u015fle\u015fir \u2014 'kertenkele' hiyeroglifu 'y\xfczlerce kat' anlam\u0131na da gelir. Aztek gelene\u011finde Cipactli \u2014 yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n ilk canavar\u0131 \u2014 kertenkele bi\xe7imindedir; yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131k ve k\xf6kenle do\u011frudan ba\u011flant\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r. Aborijin gelene\u011finde monitor kertenkele \u2014 goanna \u2014 topra\u011f\u0131n bilgisine eri\u015fimi temsil eder; onu izlemek, yerin s\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6rmektir. Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde baz\u0131 kertenkele t\xfcrleri de\u011fi\u015fim ve uyum sa\u011flaman\u0131n ustas\u0131 olarak kabul edilir; bu h\u0131z, bilgeli\u011fin bir bi\xe7imidir. Kertenkele'nin t\u0131bb\u0131: g\xfcne\u015f enerjisini \u2014 yarat\u0131c\u0131, \u0131s\u0131t\u0131c\u0131, canland\u0131r\u0131c\u0131 g\xfcc\xfc \u2014 bilin\xe7li emmek; r\xfcyalar\u0131n i\xe7indeki mesaj\u0131 g\xfcnl\xfck hayata ta\u015f\u0131mak. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: uyum o kadar h\u0131zl\u0131 olmak ki kendi \xf6zg\xfcn rengi kaybolabilmek; her ortama uyum sa\u011flarken kim oldu\u011funu unutmak.",dailyMessage:"Kertenkele bug\xfcn sana r\xfcyalar\u0131n\u0131 ciddiye almay\u0131 s\xf6yl\xfcyor \u2014 hem gece g\xf6rd\xfcklerini hem de uyan\u0131kken i\xe7inde ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n o derin \xf6zlemleri. Bu hayvan g\xfcne\u015fte \u0131s\u0131n\u0131rken yaln\u0131zca bedenini \u0131s\u0131tm\u0131yor; sinir sistemini, d\xfc\u015f\xfcncesini, tepkilerini ayarl\u0131yor. Sen de bug\xfcn hangi 'g\xfcne\u015f' sana enerji veriyor \u2014 hangi d\xfc\u015f\xfcnce, hangi ki\u015fi, hangi eylem seni canland\u0131r\u0131yor? R\xfcyalar o d\xfc\u015f\xfcncelerin y\xfczd\xfc\u011f\xfc havuzdan bilgi getirir; geceleri zihnin \xe7\xf6zd\xfc\u011f\xfc \u015feyleri g\xfcnd\xfcz hayat\u0131na sunmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r. Bu gece uyumadan \xf6nce bir soru sor kendine \u2014 yar\u0131n sabah ilk akl\u0131na gelen cevab\u0131 not et. Kertenkele ayn\u0131 zamanda h\u0131zl\u0131 uyum sa\u011flar; \u015fu an de\u011fi\u015fen bir ko\u015ful varsa onu direnmek yerine zarif bir esneklikle kucakla. Diren\xe7 enerjini t\xfcketir; ak\u0131\u015f seni ta\u015f\u0131r.",guidance:"Bu gece uyumadan \xf6nce bir k\xe2\u011f\u0131da \u015fu soruyu yaz\u0131n: 'Bu anda \xe7\xf6zmek istedi\u011fim ya da anlamak istedi\u011fim \u015fey nedir?' K\xe2\u011f\u0131d\u0131 yast\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z\u0131n alt\u0131na koyun. Sabah uyand\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131zda akl\u0131n\u0131za ilk gelen \u015feyi \u2014 bir g\xf6r\xfcnt\xfc, bir his, bir c\xfcmle \u2014 hemen yaz\u0131n. Kertenkele g\xfcne\u015f enerjisini do\u011frudan al\u0131r; siz de bilin\xe7alt\u0131 enerjisini bu pratikle do\u011frudan \xe7ekebilirsiniz.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Lizard",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["dream","solar energy","swift adaptation","rebirth"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the Pueblo and Navajo traditions of North America the lizard, especially the Gila monster and the iguana, is the keeper of the dream world; gathering strength by warming in the sun, this being symbolizes the transition between night and day. In Andean shamanism the lizard is regarded as a being that directly imprints the sun's warmth into the blood; it symbolizes the activation of life energy and the awakening of inner heat. In Egyptian hieroglyphic tradition the lizard is identified with plenty and fertility; the 'lizard' glyph also carries the meaning of 'hundredfold.' In Aztec tradition Cipactli, the first monster of creation, has the form of a lizard; it is directly connected with creativity and origin. In Aboriginal tradition the monitor lizard, the goanna, represents access to the wisdom of the earth; to watch it is to see the secrets of the ground. In the Yoruba tradition of Africa certain lizard species are accepted as masters of change and adaptation; this speed is a form of wisdom. The lizard's medicine: to consciously absorb solar energy, the creative, warming, vitalizing force, and to bring the message inside dreams into daily life. Its shadow side is adapting so quickly that you may lose your own original color; conforming to every environment while forgetting who you are.",dailyMessageEn:"The Lizard tells you today to take your dreams seriously, both the ones you see by night and the deep longings you carry while waking. While warming in the sun this animal warms not only its body; it adjusts its nervous system, its thought, its reactions. Which 'sun' gives you energy today, which thought, which person, which action enlivens you? Dreams carry information from the pool in which those thoughts swim; they try to present to your daytime life what your mind has resolved at night. Tonight before sleeping, ask yourself a question and write down the answer that first comes in the morning. The lizard also adapts swiftly; if there is a condition changing right now, embrace it with graceful flexibility rather than resisting. Resistance depletes your energy; flow carries you.",guidanceEn:"Tonight before sleeping, write on a piece of paper: 'What is it I want to resolve or understand at this time?' Place the paper under your pillow. When you wake, write immediately the first thing that comes to mind, an image, a sensation, a sentence. The lizard takes solar energy directly; you too can draw on subconscious energy directly through this practice."},{id:"a074",name:"Ko\xe7",emoji:"\ud83d\udc0f",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["ilahi yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131k","\xf6nc\xfc liderlik","g\xfcne\u015f g\xfcc\xfc","kararl\u0131l\u0131k"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Ovis_ammon_-_Barbary_sheep.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da ba\u015f tanr\u0131 Amun-Ra ko\xe7 ba\u015fl\u0131 olarak tasvir edilirdi; ko\xe7, yarat\u0131c\u0131 g\xfcc\xfcn, g\xfcne\u015fin ve evrensel ilkenin somutla\u015fmas\u0131yd\u0131. Amun tap\u0131naklar\u0131nda ko\xe7 heykellerinin dizildi\u011fi yollar \u2014 sphinx gibi \u2014 ilahi g\xfcce giden kutsal ge\xe7i\u015fi simgeliyordu. Yunan mitolojisinde alt\u0131n postlu ko\xe7 \u2014 Chrysomallus \u2014 Argonautlar\u0131n destan\u0131n\u0131 ba\u015flat\u0131r; bu hayvan hem kutsall\u0131\u011f\u0131 hem de imk\xe2ns\u0131z yolculu\u011fun fitilini ate\u015fleyen cesareti simgeler. Hint gelene\u011finde ate\u015f tanr\u0131s\u0131 Agni'nin binitidir ko\xe7; bu da ko\xe7u ate\u015fin, yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve ilk k\u0131v\u0131lc\u0131m\u0131n simgesi yapar. Eski Ahit'te ko\xe7 fedak\xe2rl\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve yenilenmenin simgesidir \u2014 \u0130brahim'in o\u011flunun yerine sunulan ko\xe7, yeni bir d\xf6nemi ba\u015flatan kutsal giri\u015ftir. Zerd\xfc\u015ft gelene\u011finde ko\xe7 g\xfcne\u015f enerjisiyle ba\u011flant\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r; bahar\u0131n geli\u015fini, Nevruz'u ve yeniden do\u011fu\u015fu simgeler. Anadolu'da h\xe2l\xe2 ya\u015fayan Nevruz rit\xfcellerinde ko\xe7 bu yenilenme enerjisinin canl\u0131 simgesidir. Ko\xe7un t\u0131bb\u0131: d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmeden \xf6nce hareket etme cesareti; kafay\u0131 koyup ge\xe7me g\xfcc\xfc, \xf6nc\xfc olma ve yolu a\xe7ma yetisi. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: \xe7ok h\u0131zl\u0131 hareket edip geri d\xf6n\xfclmez hatalar\u0131n i\xe7ine dalmak; \xf6nce kafa, sonra beyin gibi davranmak.",dailyMessage:"Ko\xe7 bug\xfcn seni ba\u015flatmaya \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131yor. Bu hayvan kafas\u0131n\u0131 bir hedefe koyar ve oraya gider \u2014 teredd\xfct etmez, sormaz, beklemez. D\xfc\u015f\xfcncelerin \xe7ok uzun s\xfcredir d\xf6ng\xfcde; analiz paralizi ya\u015f\u0131yorsun: her \u015feyi o kadar \xe7ok d\xfc\u015f\xfcnd\xfcn ki art\u0131k hareket edemez hale geldin. Ama ko\xe7 biliyor ki ilk ad\u0131m at\u0131lmadan yol a\xe7\u0131lmaz. M\xfckemmel haz\u0131rl\u0131k beklentisi, en b\xfcy\xfck ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7 engelidir. Bug\xfcn hangi \u015feyi \xe7ok uzun zamand\u0131r haz\u0131rlan\u0131yorsun? O haz\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131n sonu gelmeyecek \xe7\xfcnk\xfc m\xfckemmel an hi\xe7bir zaman gelmez. Ko\xe7 bahar\u0131 beklemez, bahar\u0131 ba\u015flat\u0131r. Sen de bug\xfcn, tam olarak \u015fu anda, o ilk ad\u0131m\u0131 at. Sonras\u0131 seni d\xfczelter; ama ba\u015flamadan d\xfczelme olmaz. \u0130lk hareket cesareti, di\u011fer t\xfcm cesaretlerin anas\u0131d\u0131r.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn \xe7ok uzun s\xfcredir erteledi\u011finiz bir \u015feyin ilk ad\u0131m\u0131n\u0131 at\u0131n \u2014 sadece ilk ad\u0131m\u0131. Tam bir plan yapman\u0131za gerek yok; sadece hareket edin. Be\u015f dakika bile yeter: o e-postay\u0131 a\xe7\u0131n, o k\xe2\u011f\u0131d\u0131 masadan kald\u0131r\u0131n, o kayd\u0131 ba\u015flat\u0131n. Ko\xe7 gibi, kafan\u0131z\u0131 koyun ve ge\xe7in. Hareket momentum yarat\u0131r; momentum ise kendi yolunu a\xe7ar.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Ram",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["divine creativity","pioneer leadership","solar power","resolve"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In ancient Egypt the chief god Amun-Ra was depicted with a ram's head; the ram was the embodiment of creative power, the sun, and the universal principle. In the temples of Amun the avenues lined with ram statues, like sphinxes, symbolized the sacred passage to divine power. In Greek mythology the golden-fleeced ram Chrysomallus begins the saga of the Argonauts; this animal symbolizes both sanctity and the courage that ignites the impossible journey. In Hindu tradition the ram is the mount of the fire god Agni, which makes it the symbol of fire, creativity, and the first spark. In the Old Testament the ram is the symbol of sacrifice and renewal; the ram offered in place of Abraham's son is the sacred initiation of a new era. In the Zoroastrian tradition the ram is connected with solar energy; it symbolizes the coming of spring, Nevruz, and rebirth. In the Nevruz rituals still alive in Anatolia, the ram is the living symbol of this renewing energy. The ram's medicine: the courage to act before thinking; the strength to lower the head and pass through, the capacity to be a pioneer and to open the way. Its shadow side is moving too quickly into irreversible mistakes; acting head first and brain second.",dailyMessageEn:"The Ram calls you today to begin. This animal lowers its head toward a target and goes there; it does not hesitate, does not ask, does not wait. Your thoughts have been in a loop too long; you are experiencing analysis paralysis: you have considered everything so much you can no longer act. But the ram knows that without the first step no road opens. Expecting perfect preparation is the greatest obstacle to beginning. Today, what have you been preparing for far too long? That preparation will never end because the perfect moment never comes. The ram does not wait for spring; the ram begins spring. Today, exactly right now, take that first step. The next steps will straighten themselves; but without beginning there is no straightening. The courage of the first move is the mother of all other courage.",guidanceEn:"Today, take the first step of something you have been postponing for too long, only the first step. You do not need a full plan; just move. Even five minutes is enough: open that email, lift that paper from the desk, start that recording. Like the ram, lower your head and pass through. Movement creates momentum; momentum opens its own road."},{id:"a075",name:"Koi Bal\u0131\u011f\u0131",emoji:"\ud83d\udc20",element:"su",symbolism:["d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm azmi","bereket","kararl\u0131l\u0131k","a\u015fma"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Koi-karp.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"\xc7in gelene\u011finde koi bal\u0131\u011f\u0131 \u2014 li yu \u2014 \u015felaleden yukar\u0131 \xe7\u0131karak ejderhaya d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcr; bu efsane Longmen \u015eelalesi'nden kaynaklan\u0131r ve azmin, kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve imk\xe2ns\u0131z\u0131 ba\u015farman\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc sembol\xfcd\xfcr. \xc7in Budizm'inde koi'nin \u015felaleden \xe7\u0131k\u0131\u015f\u0131, ayd\u0131nlanmaya giden yolun zorlu\u011funu simgeler; o diren\xe7 sayesinde ger\xe7ek d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm m\xfcmk\xfcnd\xfcr. Japon k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde koi \u2014 nishikigoi \u2014 hem g\xfczelli\u011fin hem de g\xfc\xe7l\xfc iradenin simgesidir; samuray aileleri koi havuzlar\u0131 yapar, bu bal\u0131klar\u0131 sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 ruhunun simgesi olarak yeti\u015ftirir. Koi bal\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n rengi bile anlam ta\u015f\u0131r: k\u0131rm\u0131z\u0131 enerji ve sevgiyi, beyaz safl\u0131\u011f\u0131, siyah de\u011fi\u015fimi, alt\u0131n rengi servet ve bollu\u011fu simgeler. Japon Koi Festivali'nde \u2014 Kodomo no Hi \u2014 \xe7ocuklar i\xe7in koi bayra\u011f\u0131 as\u0131l\u0131r; bu bayraklar hayat\u0131n ak\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131na direnerek y\xfckselen cesur ruhu simgeler. Sufi gelene\u011finde bal\u0131k su i\xe7inde Tanr\u0131'y\u0131 arar \u2014 oysa su Tanr\u0131'n\u0131n ta kendisidir; koi'nin bu aray\u0131\u015f\u0131, arad\u0131\u011f\u0131n \u015feyin zaten i\xe7inde oldu\u011funun metaforudur. Koi bal\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131: zorluk kar\u015f\u0131s\u0131nda pes etmemek, tam da d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm an\u0131nda vazge\xe7meme cesaretini g\xf6stermek \u2014 \xe7\xfcnk\xfc \u015felale tam ge\xe7ilmeden ejderha olunmaz. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: inatla ak\u0131nt\u0131ya kar\u015f\u0131 y\xfczmeye devam ederken hangi ak\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131n ger\xe7ekten a\u015f\u0131lmaya de\u011fer oldu\u011funu g\xf6rmemek.",dailyMessage:"Koi bug\xfcn sana \u015funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor: en zor an genellikle tam vazge\xe7mek istedi\u011fin and\u0131r \u2014 ama o an ayn\u0131 zamanda d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn en yak\u0131n oldu\u011fu and\u0131r. \u015eelaleden ge\xe7meye \xe7al\u0131\u015fan koi bin kez d\xfc\u015fer, s\xfcr\xfcklenir, geri d\xf6ner. Ama b\u0131rakmaz. Ve bir g\xfcn a\u015far \u2014 o a\u015fma an\u0131nda sadece bal\u0131k de\u011fil, ejderha olur. Sen \u015fu an o \u015felalenin tam \xf6n\xfcndesin. Bu uzun s\xfcredir s\xfcrd\xfcrd\xfc\u011f\xfcn, yorucu gelen, 'biraz daha' dedi\u011fin \u015fey: nedir? B\u0131rakmak istedi\u011fin an, belki de en yak\u0131n oldu\u011fun and\u0131r. Koi ak\u0131nt\u0131ya kar\u015f\u0131 y\xfczerken sormak istedi\u011fim soru \u015fu: o zorluk seni ne \xf6\u011fretiyor? Hangi kas bu diren\xe7le g\xfc\xe7leniyor? Ejderha olmak i\xe7in \u015felaleden ge\xe7mek \u015fartt\u0131r \u2014 kolayl\u0131kla ge\xe7ilen bir hayat seni d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrmez. Bug\xfcn bir ad\u0131m daha at.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn b\u0131rakmak istedi\u011finiz ama b\u0131rakmaman\u0131z gereken o \u015feye bir g\xfcn daha verin \u2014 sadece bir g\xfcn. Sonra yeniden de\u011ferlendirin. Koi'nin \xf6\u011fretisi: d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm anl\u0131k de\u011fil, birikimli bir s\xfcre\xe7tir. K\xfc\xe7\xfck bir kazan\u0131m defteri tutun: her g\xfcn 'bug\xfcn ne kadar ilerledi' sorusunu yan\u0131tlay\u0131n. Birikimin fark\u0131na varmak, devam etmenin en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc yak\u0131t\u0131d\u0131r.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Koi Fish",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["perseverance in transformation","abundance","resolve","surpassing"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Chinese tradition the koi fish (li yu) ascends the waterfall and becomes a dragon; this legend originates at the Longmen Falls and is the most powerful symbol of perseverance, resolve, and accomplishing the impossible. In Chinese Buddhism the koi's ascent of the waterfall symbolizes the difficulty of the path to enlightenment; through that endurance true transformation becomes possible. In Japanese culture koi (nishikigoi) symbolizes both beauty and strong will; samurai families built koi ponds, raising these fish as symbols of warrior spirit. Even the koi's color carries meaning: red symbolizes energy and love, white purity, black change, golden wealth and abundance. At the Japanese Koi Festival, Kodomo no Hi, koi flags are hung for the children; these flags symbolize the brave soul rising against the current of life. In Sufi tradition the fish seeks God within the water, yet the water is God itself; the koi's seeking is a metaphor for the truth that what you seek is already inside you. The koi's medicine: not to give up in the face of difficulty, showing the courage not to abandon hope precisely at the moment of transformation, for one does not become a dragon without crossing the falls. Its shadow side is stubbornly continuing to swim against every current without seeing which currents are truly worth surpassing.",dailyMessageEn:"The Koi reminds you today: the hardest moment is usually exactly the one in which you want to give up, but that moment is also when transformation is closest. The koi trying to pass the waterfall falls a thousand times, is swept back, returns. But it does not let go. And one day it surpasses; in that moment of surpassing it becomes not just a fish but a dragon. You are right now standing before that waterfall. What is the thing you have long sustained, that feels exhausting, that you keep saying 'a little more' to? The moment you want to release may also be the moment you are closest. As the koi swims against the current, the question I want to ask is: what is this hardship teaching you? Which muscle grows stronger through this resistance? To become a dragon one must cross the waterfall; a life easily passed does not transform you. Take one more step today.",guidanceEn:"Today, give that thing you want to release but must not release one more day, just one day. Then reevaluate. The koi's teaching: transformation is not instant but cumulative. Keep a small notebook of gains: each day answer 'how far did I get today?' Noticing the accumulation is the strongest fuel for continuing."},{id:"a076",name:"Bukalemun",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8e",element:"hava",symbolism:["uyum","ba\u011flam okuma","gizlenme bilgeli\u011fi","denge"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Chamaeleo_chamaeleon_-_1.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Anadolu halk inan\u0131\u015flar\u0131nda bukalemun, gizlenme sanat\u0131n\u0131n ustas\u0131 olarak hem hayranl\u0131k hem de \u015f\xfcpheyle kar\u015f\u0131lan\u0131r; renk de\u011fi\u015ftirme yetene\u011fi kimi zaman kurnazl\u0131\u011f\u0131n, kimi zaman ise ortama duyarl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n i\u015fareti say\u0131l\u0131r. Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde bukalemun, yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n ilk an\u0131nda kamelyan\u0131n dokuz farkl\u0131 deri giydi\u011fi ve her birinde farkl\u0131 bir bilgelik edindi\u011fi anlat\u0131l\u0131r; bu y\xfczden \u015famanlar onu ba\u011flam okuyan b\xfcy\xfck bilge olarak anar. Hint mitolojisinde Maya \u2014 yan\u0131lsama tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 \u2014 bazen bukalemun bi\xe7iminde tecelli eder; g\xf6r\xfcnenin ard\u0131ndaki ger\xe7e\u011fi kavrayanlar\u0131 \xf6d\xfcllendirir. M\u0131s\u0131r hiyeroglif gelene\u011finde ise iki g\xf6z ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131z hareket eden bu yarat\u0131k, e\u015f zamanl\u0131 iki bak\u0131\u015f a\xe7\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 simgeler: ge\xe7mi\u015f ile gelece\u011fi ayn\u0131 anda g\xf6rmek. Kelt druid \xf6\u011fretilerinde bukalemun, do\u011fan\u0131n diliyle konu\u015fan ve \xe7evresini okuyarak hayatta kalan bilge fig\xfcrd\xfcr. Bukalemunun t\u0131bb\u0131, uyumun bir zay\u0131fl\u0131k de\u011fil, derin bir zek\xe2 bi\xe7imi oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlat\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: s\xfcrekli de\u011fi\u015fmekten as\u0131l rengi, as\u0131l y\xfcz\xfc unutmak \u2014 \xe7evreye \xf6ylesine uyum sa\u011flamak ki kendin kalamamak.",dailyMessage:"Bukalemun bug\xfcn sana \xe7ok ince bir soruyu sormak i\xe7in geldi: uyum mu sa\u011fl\u0131yorsun, yoksa kayboluyor musun? Bu ikisi aras\u0131ndaki fark bazen sadece bir his kal\u0131nl\u0131\u011f\u0131 kadard\u0131r. Bukalemun iki g\xf6z\xfcn\xfc birbirinden ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131z hareket ettirir \u2014 biri her zaman ileriye, biri arkaya bakar; hi\xe7bir zaman t\xfcm\xfcyle ba\u011flam\u0131n\u0131 yitirmez. Sen bug\xfcn hangi ortamda olursan ol, bir g\xf6z\xfcn\xfc daima kendine \xe7evirebilir misin? Belki bir toplant\u0131da, bir ili\u015fkide ya da bir konu\u015fmada fark\u0131nda olmadan renk de\u011fi\u015ftirdin \u2014 bu bazen sa\u011fl\u0131kl\u0131d\u0131r. Ama fark etmeden yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda, sonras\u0131nda yorgun hissediyorsan, bu bir mesajd\u0131r. Bug\xfcn biri sana bir \u015fey s\xf6yledi\u011finde ya da bir ortama girdi\u011finde i\xe7inden ge\xe7en ilk ses neydi, onu duyabildin mi? Uyum bir sanatt\u0131r; ama sanat\xe7\u0131, tuvalinin kim oldu\u011funu asla unutmaz.",guidance:"Bu ak\u015fam birka\xe7 dakika ay\u0131r\u0131n ve \u015funu yaz\u0131n: Bug\xfcn kim i\xe7in kim oldum? Cevab\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 yarg\u0131lamadan okuyun. Haftada bir bu soruyu sormak, yava\u015f yava\u015f uyum ile kay\u0131p aras\u0131ndaki fark\u0131 hissetmenizi sa\u011flar \u2014 bu ayr\u0131m\u0131 fark etmek, \xf6z\xfcn\xfcz\xfc koruman\u0131n en pratik yoludur.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Chameleon",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["adaptation","context reading","wisdom of concealment","balance"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Anatolian folk belief, the chameleon is regarded with both admiration and suspicion as a master of the art of concealment; its color-changing ability is sometimes seen as a sign of cunning and sometimes as sensitivity to environment. In the African Yoruba tradition it is told that at the first moment of creation the chameleon wore nine different skins, gaining a different wisdom in each one; for this reason shamans honor it as the great sage who reads context. In Hindu mythology, Maya \u2014 the goddess of illusion \u2014 at times manifests in chameleon form, rewarding those who perceive the truth behind appearances. In the Egyptian hieroglyphic tradition, this creature whose two eyes move independently symbolizes simultaneous double vision: seeing past and future at the same time. In Celtic druid teachings the chameleon is the wise figure who speaks the language of nature and survives by reading its surroundings. The medicine of the chameleon reminds us that adaptation is not weakness but a deep form of intelligence. Its shadow side: changing so constantly that you forget your true color, your true face \u2014 adapting to your surroundings so completely that you can no longer remain yourself.",dailyMessageEn:"Chameleon has come today to ask you a very subtle question: are you adapting, or are you disappearing? The difference between the two is sometimes only as thick as a feeling. The chameleon moves its two eyes independently \u2014 one always looking forward, one looking back; it never wholly loses its context. Wherever you find yourself today, can you keep one eye always turned toward yourself? Perhaps in a meeting, in a relationship, or in a conversation, you changed color without noticing \u2014 sometimes this is healthy. But when you do it unconsciously and feel tired afterward, that is a message. When someone said something to you today or you entered an environment, could you still hear the first voice that rose within you? Adaptation is an art; but the artist never forgets whose canvas they are.",guidanceEn:"This evening, take a few minutes and write: Who was I for whom today? Read your answer without judgment. Asking yourself this question once a week will slowly help you sense the difference between adaptation and loss \u2014 noticing that distinction is the most practical way to protect your essence."},{id:"a077",name:"Porsuk",emoji:"\ud83e\udda1",element:"toprak",symbolism:["k\xf6k bilgeli\u011fi","toprak koruyucusu","inat\xe7\u0131 cesaret","derine inme"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Badger-badger.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Anadolu'da porsuk, da\u011f k\xf6ylerinde yer bilen hayvan olarak an\u0131l\u0131r; topra\u011f\u0131n alt\u0131n\u0131 bilen, derinlerde ne oldu\u011funu hisseden kadim bir varl\u0131k say\u0131l\u0131r. Kelt gelene\u011finde porsuk, a\u011fa\xe7lar\u0131n k\xf6klerinde ve topra\u011f\u0131n alt\u0131nda ya\u015fayan bilgeli\u011fin koruyucusudur \u2014 orman bilgesinin en yak\u0131n yolda\u015f\u0131 olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr. Norse mitolojisinde Midgard'\u0131n derinliklerinde ya\u015fayan porsuk, D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131 Yggdrasil'in k\xf6klerini bilen ve koruyan g\xfc\xe7l\xfc ruh hayvanlar\u0131ndan biridir. Kuzey Amerika K\u0131z\u0131lderili gelene\u011finde porsuk, inat\xe7\u0131 sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 ruhunun simgesidir \u2014 \xfc\xe7 kat\u0131 b\xfcy\xfckl\xfc\u011f\xfcndeki hayvanlara bile geri ad\u0131m atmaz; cesaret g\xf6stergesi olarak sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lara porsuk di\u015fi tak\u0131l\u0131r. Slav \u015famanizminde ise porsuk, topra\u011f\u0131n i\xe7inden ata ruhlar\u0131yla ileti\u015fim kuran ara varl\u0131kt\u0131r; yuvas\u0131n\u0131n derinli\u011fi, bilgeli\u011finin derinli\u011fiyle e\u015fde\u011fer tutulur. Porsukun t\u0131bb\u0131, y\xfczeyin alt\u0131na inme cesareti ve kendi ma\u011faras\u0131n\u0131 savunma kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131d\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o kadar derine inmek ki y\xfczeye bir daha \xe7\u0131kamamak \u2014 inat\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n esnekli\u011fi yutmas\u0131.",dailyMessage:"Porsuk bug\xfcn sana bir \u015fey kaz\u0131may\u0131 teklif ediyor \u2014 bir sorunun, bir ili\u015fkinin, bir duygunun y\xfczeyi de\u011fil, zeminine. Ger\xe7ek porsuk bir engelle kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131nda etraf\u0131ndan dola\u015fmaz; do\u011frudan alt\u0131ndan ge\xe7er. Bug\xfcn seni zorlayan o durum var ya \u2014 y\xfczeyde ne g\xf6r\xfcyorsun, ama alt\u0131nda ne yat\u0131yor? Belki \xf6fkenin alt\u0131nda yaral\u0131 bir beklenti var, belki yorgunlu\u011fun alt\u0131nda uzun s\xfcredir ertelenmi\u015f bir ihtiya\xe7. Porsuk kendi yuvas\u0131n\u0131 kimseye b\u0131rakmaz \u2014 senin korunmas\u0131 gereken bir i\xe7 alan\u0131n var m\u0131? Bug\xfcn ona izin vermeden giren var m\u0131? \u0130nat\xe7\u0131 cesaret bazen hay\u0131r demek, bazen de as\u0131l meseleyi ad\u0131yla \xe7a\u011f\u0131rmakt\u0131r. Bu ak\u015fam kendine sor: Bug\xfcn asl\u0131nda neyden bahsediyordum, ger\xe7ekte ne hissediyordum? Zemini buldu\u011funda, in\u015fa da oradan ba\u015flar.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn ya da bu hafta, sizi zorlayan bir konuyu bir ka\u011f\u0131da yaz\u0131n ve ard\u0131ndan Bunun alt\u0131nda ne var? sorusunu \xfc\xe7 kez tekrarlay\u0131n \u2014 her seferinde bir \xf6nceki cevab\u0131n alt\u0131na bak\u0131n. Bu y\xf6ntem, ger\xe7ek meseleyi y\xfczeye \xe7\u0131karmak i\xe7in kullan\u0131lan basit ama g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir \xf6z-sorgulama tekni\u011fidir; k\xf6k bulundu\u011funda \xe7\xf6z\xfcm de netle\u015fir.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Badger",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["root wisdom","guardian of the earth","stubborn courage","going deep"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Anatolia the badger is known in mountain villages as the animal that knows the ground; it is considered an ancient being who knows what lies beneath the earth and senses what stirs in the depths. In the Celtic tradition the badger is the guardian of the wisdom that lives in the roots of trees and beneath the soil \u2014 seen as the closest companion of the forest sage. In Norse mythology the badger who lives in the depths of Midgard is one of the powerful spirit animals who knows and protects the roots of the World Tree Yggdrasil. In the Native American traditions of North America the badger is the symbol of the stubborn warrior spirit \u2014 it does not retreat even before animals three times its size; badger teeth were worn by warriors as a mark of courage. In Slavic shamanism the badger is the in-between being who communicates with ancestor spirits from within the earth; the depth of its den is held equivalent to the depth of its wisdom. The medicine of the badger is the courage to descend beneath the surface and the determination to defend one's own cave. Its shadow side: descending so deep that one can never rise to the surface again \u2014 stubbornness swallowing flexibility.",dailyMessageEn:"Badger is offering you something to dig today \u2014 not the surface of a problem, a relationship, or an emotion, but its ground. When a real badger meets an obstacle, it does not go around it; it goes directly underneath. That situation that is pressing you today \u2014 what do you see on the surface, and what lies beneath? Perhaps beneath the anger is a wounded expectation, perhaps beneath the exhaustion is a long-postponed need. Badger does not surrender its den to anyone \u2014 do you have an inner space that needs protecting? Has someone entered it today without permission? Stubborn courage is sometimes saying no, and sometimes calling the real matter by its true name. This evening ask yourself: What was I really talking about today, what was I truly feeling? When you find the ground, that is where construction begins.",guidanceEn:"Today or this week, write down on paper a matter that is troubling you, then repeat the question What lies beneath this? three times \u2014 each time looking beneath the previous answer. This method is a simple but powerful self-inquiry technique used to bring the real issue to the surface; when the root is found, the solution becomes clear."},{id:"a078",name:"Kunduz",emoji:"\ud83e\uddab",element:"toprak",symbolism:["yarat\u0131c\u0131 in\u015fa","topluluk","azim","pratik bilgelik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/American_Beaver.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Anadolu ve Orta Asya T\xfcrk gelene\u011finde kunduz, su m\xfchendisi ve ev kurucusu olarak sayg\u0131 g\xf6r\xfcr; Altay \u015famanizminde kunduzun kurdu\u011fu baraj, d\xfcnya ile \xf6teki d\xfcnya aras\u0131ndaki bilin\xe7li s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131 simgeler. Kuzey Amerika Cree ve Ojibwe gelene\u011finde kunduz, yedi ku\u015fak ilerisi d\xfc\u015f\xfcnerek in\u015fa eden hikmet varl\u0131\u011f\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 bir a\u011fac\u0131 kesmeden \xf6nce onun \xe7evresine bakmas\u0131, uzun vadeli d\xfc\u015f\xfcncenin \xf6rne\u011fidir. Slav halk inan\u0131\u015flar\u0131nda kunduz evin koruyucu ruhudur; bir evin yak\u0131n\u0131na kunduz yuva kurarsa o ev bereketli ve sa\u011flam say\u0131l\u0131r. Japon Shinto gelene\u011finde su kenar\u0131nda in\u015fa eden her yarat\u0131k gibi kunduz da kami \u2014 kutsal ruh \u2014 ta\u015f\u0131yan varl\u0131k olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr; akarsuyu de\u011fi\u015ftirme g\xfcc\xfc onu yarat\u0131c\u0131 tanr\u0131sal varl\u0131k k\u0131lar. Kelt gelene\u011finde kunduz, topluluk i\xe7in fedak\xe2rl\u0131k eden ve birlikte in\u015fa etmenin g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc temsil eden kutsal hayvand\u0131r. Kunduzun t\u0131bb\u0131, hayal ile eylemi birle\u015ftirme yetene\u011fi ve topluluk i\xe7in somut de\u011fer \xfcretme g\xfcc\xfcd\xfcr. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o kadar me\u015fgul olmak ki dinlemeyi, akmay\u0131, suyun do\u011fal seyrini engellemeyi fark etmemek.",dailyMessage:"Kunduz bug\xfcn seni bir \u015fey in\u015fa etmeye \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131yor \u2014 ama planlara, hayallere de\u011fil, ger\xe7ek bir ta\u015f koymaya. Kunduz baraj\u0131n\u0131 bir gece i\xe7inde bitirmez; her g\xfcn bir dal, her g\xfcn bir \xe7amur katman\u0131. Zihnindeki o b\xfcy\xfck proje, o ili\u015fki, o de\u011fi\u015fim \u2014 bug\xfcn ona bir tu\u011fla koyabilir misin? K\xfc\xe7\xfck g\xf6r\xfcnebilir, anlams\u0131z bile gelebilir; ama kunduzun b\xfcy\xfck s\u0131rr\u0131 \u015fudur: her dal, sonraki i\xe7in zemin haz\u0131rlar. Bug\xfcn ne in\u015fa etmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yorsun ve o binada senin d\u0131\u015f\u0131nda kimin de yeri var? \xc7\xfcnk\xfc kunduz yaln\u0131z in\u015fa etmez \u2014 ailesiyle, s\xfcr\xfcs\xfcyle \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r. Bug\xfcn biri sana yard\u0131m teklif ettiyse kabul et; sen de birine yard\u0131m edebilirsen uzanabilirsin. \u0130n\u015fa etmek, yaln\u0131z olmak zorunda de\u011fil.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn \xfczerinde \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir projeye veya hedefe dair tek somut bir eylem belirleyin \u2014 \xe7ok k\xfc\xe7\xfck, \xe7ok basit bir \u015fey. Bunu bir yere yaz\u0131n ve g\xfcn bitmeden yap\u0131n. Ara\u015ft\u0131rmalar, k\xfc\xe7\xfck tamamlanm\u0131\u015f eylemlerin beyne ilerliyorum sinyali verdi\u011fini ve motivasyonu s\xfcrd\xfcrd\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc g\xf6steriyor; b\xfcy\xfck hedefler k\xfc\xe7\xfck tu\u011flalarla ger\xe7ek olur.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Beaver",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["creative building","community","perseverance","practical wisdom"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Anatolian and Central Asian Turkic tradition the beaver is honored as the water engineer and home builder; in Altai shamanism the dam built by the beaver symbolizes the conscious boundary between this world and the otherworld. In the Cree and Ojibwe traditions of North America the beaver is the being of wisdom who builds with seven generations in mind \u2014 its habit of surveying a tree's surroundings before felling it is an example of long-term thinking. In Slavic folk belief the beaver is the protective spirit of the home; if a beaver builds its lodge near a house, that house is considered abundant and sound. In the Japanese Shinto tradition every creature that builds by water \u2014 including the beaver \u2014 is seen as a being carrying kami, sacred spirit; its power to alter a stream makes it a creative, godlike presence. In the Celtic tradition the beaver is the sacred animal that sacrifices for the community and represents the strength of building together. The medicine of the beaver is the ability to unite vision with action and the power to produce tangible value for community. Its shadow side: becoming so busy that one forgets to listen, to flow, or to notice when one is damming the natural current of water.",dailyMessageEn:"Beaver calls you today to build something \u2014 not plans, not dreams, but to lay an actual stone. Beaver does not finish its dam in one night; one branch a day, one layer of mud a day. That great project, that relationship, that change in your mind \u2014 can you place a single brick on it today? It may seem small, even meaningless; but the great secret of the beaver is this: every branch prepares the ground for the next. What are you trying to build today, and who besides you has a place in that structure? For the beaver does not build alone \u2014 it works with its family, its colony. If someone offered you help today, accept it; if you can offer help to someone, extend it. Building does not have to be lonely.",guidanceEn:"Decide on one tangible action today for a project or goal you are working on \u2014 something very small, very simple. Write it down somewhere and do it before the day ends. Research shows that small completed actions signal to the brain I am moving forward and sustain motivation; great goals become real through small bricks."},{id:"a079",name:"Guguk Ku\u015fu",emoji:"\ud83d\udc26",element:"hava",symbolism:["zaman bilinci","d\xf6ng\xfc sesi","ruh \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131c\u0131","de\u011fi\u015fim i\u015fareti"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Cuculus_canorus_vogelartinfo_chris_romeiks_D7C8243_cropped.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"T\xfcrk ve Altay \u015famanizminde guguk ku\u015funun sesi ruhun \xe7a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 \u015faman transa ge\xe7erken guguk sesini kullan\u0131r, \xe7\xfcnk\xfc bu ses iki d\xfcnya aras\u0131ndaki kap\u0131y\u0131 a\xe7ar. Anadolu halk inan\u0131\u015f\u0131nda guguk sesi ilkbaharda ilk duyuldu\u011funda cebindeki paran\u0131n say\u0131s\u0131 o y\u0131l ka\xe7 kez \xe7o\u011falaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 s\xf6yler; zaman ve bollukla derin bir ba\u011f\u0131 vard\u0131r. Slav folklorunda guguk ku\u015fu \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz bilge kad\u0131n Baba Yaga'n\u0131n habercisidir \u2014 ka\xe7 y\u0131l \xf6m\xfcr kald\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 sayan mistik bir varl\u0131k olarak kutsal korku i\xe7inde dinlenir. Kelt druid gelene\u011finde guguk sesi, yeni bir mevsiMin, yeni bir d\xf6ng\xfcn\xfcn ba\u015flad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n bildirisiydi; do\u011fan\u0131n takvimini i\u015fiten tek ku\u015ftu. M\u0131s\u0131r hiyeroglif gelene\u011finde zaman d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc temsil eden Netem-Netem isimli ku\u015f, guguk ku\u015fuyla \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirilir \u2014 tekrar eden d\xf6ng\xfclerin bilgesiydi. Hindu mitolojisinde ise guguk ku\u015fu Kama'n\u0131n, a\u015fk ve arzu tanr\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n kutsal habercisidir; bahar geldi\u011finde \xf6ter ve kalpleri uyand\u0131r\u0131r. Guguk ku\u015funun t\u0131bb\u0131, zaman\u0131n fark\u0131nda olmak ve her d\xf6ng\xfcn\xfcn getirdi\u011fi mesaj\u0131 duymakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: zaman\u0131n ge\xe7ti\u011fini fark etmek ama hep ertelemek \u2014 say\u0131lan anlar\u0131n bo\u015fa ge\xe7mesini seyretmek.",dailyMessage:"Guguk Ku\u015fu bug\xfcn sana bir \u015feyi nazik\xe7e ama kararl\u0131l\u0131kla hat\u0131rlatmak i\xe7in geldi: zaman ger\xe7ekten ge\xe7iyor. Bu korku de\u011fil \u2014 bir davet, bir hat\u0131rlatma. Guguk ku\u015fu y\u0131l\u0131n belli haftalar\u0131nda \xf6ter, sonra susar; her sesinin bir zaman\u0131 vard\u0131r. Sende de susmadan \xf6nce s\xf6ylenmesi gereken bir \u015fey var m\u0131? Yap\u0131lmay\u0131 bekleyen bir ad\u0131m, a\xe7\u0131lmay\u0131 bekleyen bir kap\u0131, verilmey\u0131 bekleyen bir karar? Bug\xfcn kendine d\xfcr\xfcst\xe7e sor: Ka\xe7 mevsimdir ayn\u0131 yerde bekliyorum? Ertelemek bazen koruyucudur; ama bir noktadan sonra erteleme, korkuya hizmet etmeye ba\u015flar. Guguk ku\u015fu ne \xf6z\xfcr diler ne a\xe7\u0131klar \u2014 zaman\u0131 gelince \xf6ter. Bug\xfcn zaman\u0131 gelen o \u015feyin sesi sen misin?",guidance:"Bu hafta erteledi\u011finiz en \xf6nemli bir \u015feyi se\xe7in ve ona dair be\u015f dakikal\u0131k bir eylem belirleyin \u2014 sadece be\u015f dakika. Zamanlay\u0131c\u0131 kurun ve o eylemi yap\u0131n. Beyin b\xfcy\xfck g\xf6revleri ertelemeye, k\xfc\xe7\xfck ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7lar\u0131 ise kabul etmeye meyillidir; bir kez ba\u015fland\u0131\u011f\u0131nda devam etmek \xe7o\u011fu zaman kendili\u011finden gelir.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Cuckoo",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["awareness of time","voice of the cycle","spirit caller","sign of change"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Turkic and Altai shamanism the cuckoo's call is the calling of the soul \u2014 the shaman uses the cuckoo's voice when entering trance, for this sound opens the door between two worlds. In Anatolian folk belief, when the cuckoo is first heard in spring, the number of coins in your pocket is said to foretell how many times your abundance will multiply that year; it has a deep bond with time and prosperity. In Slavic folklore the cuckoo is the herald of the immortal wise woman Baba Yaga \u2014 listened to with sacred awe as a mystical being who counts how many years of life remain. In Celtic druid tradition the cuckoo's call announced that a new season, a new cycle had begun; it was the only bird that heard nature's calendar. In the Egyptian hieroglyphic tradition the bird Netem-Netem, who represents the cycle of time, is identified with the cuckoo \u2014 the sage of recurring cycles. In Hindu mythology the cuckoo is the sacred messenger of Kama, god of love and desire; it sings when spring comes and awakens hearts. The medicine of the cuckoo is to be aware of time and to hear the message each cycle brings. Its shadow side: noticing the passing of time but always postponing \u2014 watching the counted moments slip away.",dailyMessageEn:"Cuckoo has come today to remind you, gently but firmly, of one thing: time is really passing. This is not a fear \u2014 it is an invitation, a reminder. The cuckoo sings only in certain weeks of the year, then falls silent; every voice has its season. Is there something within you that must be spoken before silence falls? A step waiting to be taken, a door waiting to be opened, a decision waiting to be made? Ask yourself honestly today: How many seasons have I been waiting in the same place? Postponement is sometimes protective; but past a certain point, it begins to serve fear. The cuckoo neither apologizes nor explains \u2014 when its time comes, it sings. Are you the voice of that thing whose time has come today?",guidanceEn:"This week, choose the most important thing you have been postponing and define a five-minute action toward it \u2014 only five minutes. Set a timer and do that action. The brain tends to postpone large tasks but accepts small beginnings; once you have begun, continuing often comes naturally."},{id:"a080",name:"Saksa\u011fan",emoji:"\ud83d\udc26\u200d\u2b1b",element:"hava",symbolism:["haberci","ikili do\u011fa","zeka","denge"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Pica_pica_pica_portrait.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Anadolu halk gelene\u011finde saksa\u011fan, siyah-beyaz rengiyle hem u\u011fur hem u\u011fursuzluk ta\u015f\u0131yan \xe7ift do\u011fal\u0131 bir ku\u015ftur \u2014 tek g\xf6r\xfclmesi k\xf6t\xfc haber, \xe7ift g\xf6r\xfclmesi iyi haber say\u0131l\u0131r; bu nedenle saksa\u011fan geldi, haber var denir. \xc7in mitolojisinde saksa\u011fan sevin\xe7 ku\u015fudur \u2014 \xc7ince ad\u0131 Xi Que do\u011frudan mutluluk ku\u015fu anlam\u0131na gelir; evliliklerde, kutlamalarda ve yeni ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7larda kutlu say\u0131l\u0131r. Kelt gelene\u011finde saksa\u011fan, iki d\xfcnya aras\u0131ndaki k\xf6pr\xfcd\xfcr \u2014 g\xfcnd\xfcz ile gece, \xf6l\xfcm ile ya\u015fam, g\xf6r\xfcnen ile g\xf6r\xfcnmez aras\u0131nda gidip gelen bilge habercidir. Slav \u015famanizminde saksa\u011fan t\xfcyleri, iki yanl\u0131 bir \u015feyi sembolize etmek i\xe7in rit\xfcellerde kullan\u0131l\u0131r; ikili ger\xe7e\u011fi kavraman\u0131n arac\u0131d\u0131r. \u0130skandinav folklorunda saksa\u011fan, Odin'in habercisi olarak gizli bilgileri ta\u015f\u0131r ve karanl\u0131k ile ayd\u0131nl\u0131k aras\u0131ndaki dengeyi korur. Saksa\u011fan\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, z\u0131tl\u0131klar\u0131n bir arada var olabilece\u011fini kabul etmek ve tek tarafl\u0131 yarg\u0131lamaktan vazge\xe7mektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: s\xfcrekli iki taraf\u0131 g\xf6rmekten karar veremez hale gelmek \u2014 dengeyi s\xfcrd\xfcr\xfcrken hareketsiz kalmak.",dailyMessage:"Saksa\u011fan bug\xfcn seni iki tarafl\u0131 bir ger\xe7e\u011fin \xf6n\xfcnde durmaya davet ediyor. Bir kanat siyah, bir kanat beyaz \u2014 ve bu ku\u015f tek renkte u\xe7amaz. Bug\xfcn hakk\u0131nda yarg\u0131da bulundu\u011fun bir ki\u015fi ya da durum var m\u0131? G\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfcn yaln\u0131zca bir kanat olabilir. Saksa\u011fan inan\u0131lmaz derecede zeki bir ku\u015ftur; aynay\u0131 tan\u0131yan, kendini fark eden az say\u0131da hayvandan biridir. Kendini tan\u0131mak, kendi karanl\u0131k ve ayd\u0131nl\u0131k taraflar\u0131n\u0131 ayn\u0131 anda g\xf6rebilmek demektir. Bug\xfcn bir duruma ya da insana bakt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda sadece bir rengi mi g\xf6r\xfcyorsun? \xd6te taraf\u0131 g\xf6rmek seni hakl\u0131 \xe7\u0131karmaz, ama daha eksiksiz bir ger\xe7e\u011fe g\xf6t\xfcr\xfcr. Hangi taraf\u0131 g\xf6rmezden geliyorsun?",guidance:"Bug\xfcn sizi zorlayan bir ki\u015fi veya durumu d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcn ve \u015funu yaz\u0131n: Bu konuda hakl\u0131 oldu\u011fumu d\xfc\u015f\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfcm \u015feyler... ve Bu konuda yan\u0131l\u0131yor olabilece\u011fim \u015feyler... Her iki listeyi de ger\xe7ek niyetle doldurun. Bu egzersiz, yarg\u0131 yerine anlay\u0131\u015fa ge\xe7i\u015f i\xe7in g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir ara\xe7t\u0131r \u2014 saksa\u011fan\u0131n her iki kanad\u0131na bakmay\u0131 \xf6\u011fretir.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Magpie",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["messenger","dual nature","intelligence","balance"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Anatolian folk tradition the magpie, with its black-and-white plumage, is a dual-natured bird carrying both good and ill fortune \u2014 seeing one alone is bad news, seeing two is good news; this is why people say the magpie has come, there is news. In Chinese mythology the magpie is the bird of joy \u2014 its Chinese name Xi Que literally means bird of happiness; it is regarded as auspicious at weddings, celebrations, and new beginnings. In Celtic tradition the magpie is the bridge between two worlds \u2014 the wise messenger who moves between day and night, death and life, the seen and the unseen. In Slavic shamanism magpie feathers are used in rituals to symbolize that which has two sides; it is the instrument for grasping dual reality. In Scandinavian folklore the magpie is Odin's messenger, carrying hidden knowledge and preserving the balance between darkness and light. The medicine of the magpie is to accept that opposites can coexist and to release one-sided judgment. Its shadow side: constantly seeing both sides to the point of being unable to decide \u2014 remaining motionless while sustaining balance.",dailyMessageEn:"Magpie invites you today to stand before a two-sided truth. One wing black, one wing white \u2014 and this bird cannot fly in a single color. Is there a person or situation you have been judging today? What you see may be only one wing. The magpie is an astonishingly intelligent bird; it is one of the few animals that recognizes itself in a mirror. To know oneself is to be able to see one's dark and light sides at the same time. When you look at a situation or a person today, are you seeing only one color? Seeing the other side will not prove you right, but it will lead you to a fuller truth. Which side are you ignoring?",guidanceEn:"Think of a person or situation that is troubling you today and write: Things I believe I am right about in this... and Things I might be wrong about in this... Fill both lists with genuine intention. This exercise is a powerful tool for moving from judgment to understanding \u2014 it teaches you to look at both wings of the magpie."},{id:"a081",name:"Simurg",emoji:"\u2728",element:"hava",symbolism:["kolektif bilgelik","ilahi hakikat","a\u015fk\u0131n","birlik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Simurgh_on_a_13th_century_Persian_plate.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"\u0130ran ve T\xfcrk tasavvuf gelene\u011finin en derin sembollerinden olan Simurg, Ferid\xfcddin Attar'\u0131n 12. y\xfczy\u0131lda kaleme ald\u0131\u011f\u0131 Mant\u0131k-ut Tayr'da otuz ku\u015fun a\u015farak ula\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve i\xe7inde kendilerini g\xf6rd\xfckleri kutsal varl\u0131kt\u0131r; Si otuz, murg ku\u015f demektir \u2014 kolektif bilincin doruk noktas\u0131. Divan \u015fiirinde Simurg, ula\u015f\u0131lmaz olan ilahi g\xfczelli\u011fin, a\u015fk\u0131n bilgeli\u011fin ve tamamlanm\u0131\u015fl\u0131\u011f\u0131n simgesidir; H\xfcma ku\u015fu ile \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ferek g\xf6\u011fe y\xfckselen ve d\xfc\u015fmeyen \xf6zg\xfcr ruhun arketipidir. Pers mitolojisinde Simurg, Demavend Da\u011f\u0131'n\u0131n zirvesinde ya\u015fayan ve binlerce y\u0131ll\u0131k bilgeli\u011fi b\xfcnyesinde ta\u015f\u0131yan efsanevi varl\u0131kt\u0131r \u2014 Zal'\u0131 yeti\u015ftirmi\u015f, R\xfcstem'in do\u011fumuna tan\u0131kl\u0131k etmi\u015ftir. Hint Garuda gelene\u011fiyle paralel olarak Simurg da ilahi ile insani aras\u0131ndaki k\xf6pr\xfcy\xfc temsil eder; her iki kanat ayn\u0131 anda iki d\xfcnyaya uzan\u0131r. \xc7in mitolojisindeki Fenghuang gibi Simurg da hem y\xfckselen hem de t\xfcm \xf6\u011fretileri kendi bedeninde bar\u0131nd\u0131ran bilge varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Simurg'un t\u0131bb\u0131, en derin ger\xe7e\u011fi hat\u0131rlat\u0131r: arayan ile aranan ayn\u0131 varl\u0131kt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: i\xe7sel bilgeli\u011fi g\xf6rmezden gelip onu d\u0131\u015far\u0131da aramaya devam etmek \u2014 yolculu\u011fu as\u0131l hedefin kendisinden uzakla\u015fmak i\xe7in kullanmak.",dailyMessage:"Simurg bug\xfcn sana en b\xfcy\xfck s\u0131rr\u0131 f\u0131s\u0131ld\u0131yor: sen zaten oradas\u0131n. Otuz ku\u015f Simurg'u aramak i\xe7in yedi vadi a\u015ft\u0131 \u2014 gurur, a\u015fk, bilgi, kanaat, tevhid, hayret ve hi\xe7lik vadilerinden ge\xe7ti. Ve Simurg'a ula\u015ft\u0131klar\u0131nda aynay\u0131 g\xf6rd\xfcler: Simurg onlard\u0131. Bug\xfcn neyi d\u0131\u015far\u0131da ar\u0131yorsun? Onay\u0131, huzuru, anlam\u0131, sevgiyi \u2014 hangisi? Ve i\xe7ine bakt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda, o \u015feyin bir k\u0131v\u0131lc\u0131m\u0131 zaten orada de\u011fil mi? Belki tam parlakl\u0131kta de\u011fil, belki biraz tozu var; ama s\xf6nmemi\u015f. Simurg'un \xe7a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131 bu de\u011fil: Git bul. Simurg'un \xe7a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131: Dur, i\xe7ine bak. Bug\xfcn bir an i\xe7in d\u0131\u015far\u0131ya uzanan eli geri \xe7ek ve kendine sor: Arad\u0131\u011f\u0131m \u015feyden zaten neye sahibim?",guidance:"On dakika sessiz bir yere oturun ve \u015fu soruyu i\xe7inizde ta\u015f\u0131y\u0131n: Ba\u015fkas\u0131ndan bekledi\u011fim ya da d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan arad\u0131\u011f\u0131m en \xf6nemli \u015feyi, bug\xfcn kendime nas\u0131l verebilirim? Hemen cevap aramay\u0131n \u2014 sadece soruyu tutun. Simurg meditasyonu, i\xe7sel kaynakla ba\u011flant\u0131 kurmak i\xe7in en eski tekniklerden biridir; cevap genellikle sessizli\u011fin i\xe7inden gelir.",rarity:"legendary",nameEn:"Simurgh",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["collective wisdom","divine truth","transcendence","unity"],anatolianMeaningEn:"Among the deepest symbols of Iranian and Turkic mystical tradition, the Simurgh is the sacred being which, in Farid ud-Din Attar's twelfth-century Conference of the Birds (Mantiq ut-Tayr), the thirty birds finally reach only to see themselves within it; Si means thirty, murg means bird \u2014 the very peak of collective consciousness. In Divan poetry the Simurgh is the symbol of the unattainable divine beauty, transcendent wisdom, and completion; identified with the Huma bird, it is the archetype of the free soul that ascends to heaven and never falls. In Persian mythology the Simurgh is the legendary being who dwells on the summit of Mount Damavand and carries millennia of wisdom \u2014 it raised Zal and witnessed the birth of Rostam. In parallel with the Hindu Garuda tradition, the Simurgh represents the bridge between the divine and the human; both wings reach simultaneously into two worlds. Like the Fenghuang of Chinese mythology, the Simurgh is the wise being who ascends and contains all teachings within its own body. The medicine of the Simurgh recalls the deepest truth: seeker and sought are one and the same being. Its shadow side: ignoring inner wisdom and continuing to seek it outside \u2014 using the journey to move away from the destination itself.",dailyMessageEn:"Simurgh whispers the greatest secret to you today: you are already there. The thirty birds crossed seven valleys in search of the Simurgh \u2014 the valleys of pride, love, knowledge, contentment, unity, wonder, and nothingness. And when they reached the Simurgh they saw a mirror: the Simurgh was them. What are you searching for outside today? Approval, peace, meaning, love \u2014 which one? And when you look within, is a spark of that thing not already there? Perhaps not at full brightness, perhaps a little dusty; but not extinguished. The Simurgh's call is not Go and find. The Simurgh's call is Stop, look within. Today, for a single moment, draw back the hand reaching outward and ask yourself: Of what I am searching for, what do I already possess?",guidanceEn:"Sit in a quiet place for ten minutes and carry this question within you: How can I give myself today the most important thing I have been expecting from others or seeking outside? Do not search immediately for an answer \u2014 just hold the question. The Simurgh meditation is one of the oldest techniques for connecting with inner resources; the answer usually arises from silence."},{id:"a082",name:"Garuda",emoji:"\ud83d\udd25",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["ilahi ara\xe7","\xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck","g\xfcne\u015f g\xfcc\xfc","iyili\u011fin savunucusu"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Garuda_Indonesia.svg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Hindu ve Budist mitolojisinin en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc tanr\u0131sal varl\u0131klar\u0131ndan Garuda, tanr\u0131 Vishnu'nun kutsal bine\u011fi ve zehrin \u2014 yani cehaletin ve k\xf6t\xfcl\xfc\u011f\xfcn \u2014 yok edicisidir; kartal ba\u015f\u0131, insan g\xf6vdesi ve alt\u0131n kanatlar\u0131yla hem hayvansal hem tanr\u0131sal g\xfcc\xfc birle\u015ftirir. Bali ve Endonezya \u015faman gelene\u011finde Garuda, toplumun koruyucu ruhudur \u2014 k\xf6y t\xf6renlerinde dev Garuda maskeleri giyilir ve bu g\xfc\xe7 bedende ya\u015fat\u0131l\u0131r. Tayland ulusal sembol\xfc olan Garuda, krali otoriteyi ve iyili\u011fi koruma g\xf6revini temsil eder; adalet y\xfcr\xfct\xfcc\xfclerinin \xfczerinde Garuda imgesi ta\u015f\u0131mas\u0131 bu kutsal koruyuculu\u011fun simgesidir. Japon Budizminde Karura ad\u0131yla an\u0131lan Garuda, ate\u015f \xfcfleyen kutsal ku\u015f olarak bilgeli\u011fin ve g\xfcc\xfcn koruyucusudur. Aztek gelene\u011findeki kartal sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 arketipiyle paralel olan Garuda da g\xfcne\u015fin g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc yere indiren ve karanl\u0131\u011fa kar\u015f\u0131 sava\u015fan \u0131\u015f\u0131k sava\u015f\xe7\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r. Garuda'n\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, g\xfcne\u015f enerjisiyle hareket etmek \u2014 korkudan de\u011fil, do\u011fru oldu\u011funa inand\u0131\u011f\u0131n \u015fey i\xe7in aya\u011fa kalkmakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o kadar emin olmak ki ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131n ger\xe7e\u011fini duymay\u0131 b\u0131rakmak \u2014 koruyuculu\u011fun dogmatizme d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmesi.",dailyMessage:"Garuda bug\xfcn seni bir \u015fey i\xe7in aya\u011fa kalkmaya \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131yor. G\xfcne\u015fin g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc ta\u015f\u0131yan bu varl\u0131k ne korkudan ne de \xf6fkeden u\xe7ar \u2014 a\xe7\u0131k bir ama\xe7la, net bir do\u011frulukla hareket eder. Bug\xfcn g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfcn ama sessiz kald\u0131\u011f\u0131n bir haks\u0131zl\u0131k ya da yanl\u0131\u015fl\u0131k var m\u0131? Belki k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir \u015fey: birinin \xfczerine y\u0131k\u0131lan bir su\xe7lama, g\xf6rmezden gelinen bir ihtiya\xe7, s\xf6ylenmesi gereken bir ger\xe7ek. Garuda'n\u0131n zehri yok etmesi bir metafordur \u2014 zehir bazen s\xf6ylenmemi\u015f ger\xe7eklerdir, i\xe7ine d\xf6k\xfclen \xf6fkedir, su g\xf6t\xfcrmez adaletsizliktir. Ama dikkat et: Garuda g\xfcne\u015f gibi yakar, k\xf6r\xfc k\xf6r\xfcne de\u011fil, bir amaca hizmet ederek. Bug\xfcn sesini y\xfckseltirken seni y\xf6nlendiren his ne \u2014 do\u011fruluk mu, \xf6fke mi? \u0130kisi bazen i\xe7 i\xe7e ge\xe7er; fark\u0131 bilmek, g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc yerinde kullanmakt\u0131r.",guidance:"Bug\xfcn dile getirmek isteyip erteledi\u011finiz bir \u015fey varsa, \xf6nce \u015funu yaz\u0131n: Bu konuda ne hissediyorum, ne s\xf6ylemek istiyorum ve amac\u0131m ne? Bu \xfc\xe7 soruyu yan\u0131tlad\u0131ktan sonra konu\u015fun ya da yaz\u0131n. Garuda eylemsiz u\xe7maz \u2014 netlik, cesaretle birle\u015fti\u011finde g\xfc\xe7 olur.",rarity:"legendary",nameEn:"Garuda",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["divine vehicle","freedom","solar power","defender of the good"],anatolianMeaningEn:"One of the most powerful divine beings in Hindu and Buddhist mythology, Garuda is the sacred mount of the god Vishnu and the destroyer of poison \u2014 of ignorance and evil; with eagle head, human body, and golden wings, it unites animal and divine power. In Balinese and Indonesian shamanic tradition, Garuda is the guardian spirit of the community \u2014 great Garuda masks are worn in village rituals and this power is brought to life in the body. As the national symbol of Thailand, Garuda represents royal authority and the duty to protect the good; the bearing of the Garuda image by enforcers of justice is the sign of this sacred guardianship. Known as Karura in Japanese Buddhism, Garuda is the sacred bird that breathes fire, the protector of wisdom and strength. Paralleling the eagle-warrior archetype of the Aztec tradition, Garuda is the warrior of light who brings down the power of the sun and battles against the darkness. The medicine of Garuda is to move with solar energy \u2014 to rise up not out of fear, but for what you believe to be right. Its shadow side: being so certain that you stop hearing another's truth \u2014 guardianship turning into dogmatism.",dailyMessageEn:"Garuda calls you today to rise up for something. This being who carries the sun's power flies neither from fear nor from anger \u2014 it moves with clear purpose and crisp rightness. Is there an injustice or wrongness you have witnessed today and remained silent about? Perhaps something small: a blame heaped on someone, an overlooked need, a truth that needs to be spoken. Garuda's destruction of poison is a metaphor \u2014 poison is sometimes the unspoken truth, the anger turned inward, the unmistakable injustice. But take care: Garuda burns like the sun, not blindly, but in service of purpose. When you raise your voice today, what is guiding you \u2014 rightness, or anger? The two sometimes interweave; knowing the difference is what places your power where it belongs.",guidanceEn:"If there is something you have been wanting to speak but have postponed, first write: What am I feeling about this, what do I want to say, and what is my intention? After answering these three questions, speak or write. Garuda does not fly without aim \u2014 clarity, joined with courage, becomes power."},{id:"a083",name:"Ke\xe7i",emoji:"\ud83d\udc10",element:"toprak",symbolism:["yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131k","da\u011f \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfc","sarp yol","canl\u0131l\u0131k"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Capra_caucasica_Eichwald,_1831.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Anadolu'da ke\xe7i, en eski evcil hayvanlardan biri olarak neolitik d\xf6nemden bu yana bereketin, canl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n ve direncin simgesi olmu\u015ftur; G\xf6bekli Tepe'de ke\xe7i fig\xfcrlerinin bulunmas\u0131, bu kutsal ba\u011f\u0131n ne kadar derin k\xf6klere sahip oldu\u011funu g\xf6sterir. Yunan mitolojisinde Pan tanr\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n kutsal hayvan\u0131 olan ke\xe7i hem m\xfczi\u011fin hem yabani do\u011fan\u0131n hem de bereketli yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n simgesidir; Olimpos'taki tanr\u0131lar Zeus'u Amalthea isimli kutsal ke\xe7inin s\xfct\xfcyle beslediler \u2014 bu y\xfczden ke\xe7i, tanr\u0131lar\u0131n anas\u0131d\u0131r. Norse mitolojisinde Thor'un arabas\u0131 iki ke\xe7i taraf\u0131ndan \xe7ekilir: Tanngrisnir ve Tanngnj\xf3str \u2014 her sabah kesilip her ak\u015fam yeniden dirilirler; sonsuz yenileni\u015f ve dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n simgesidir. Kelt gelene\u011finde ke\xe7i, yorulmadan en sarp kayal\u0131klar\u0131 t\u0131rmanan ve imk\xe2ns\u0131za ula\u015fan cesur ruhun arketipidir \u2014 Kelt sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131 ke\xe7i sembol\xfcn\xfc kalkanlar\u0131na i\u015flerdi. \xc7in astrolojisinde ke\xe7i y\u0131l\u0131nda do\u011fanlar, yarat\u0131c\u0131, sezgisel ve kendi yolunu bulan ki\u015filer olarak tan\u0131mlan\u0131r. Ke\xe7inin t\u0131bb\u0131, en sarp zeminlerde bile yol bulmak, engeli bir basamak olarak kullanmakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: inat\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n esnekli\u011fi engellemesi \u2014 her zeminde z\u0131plamak ama hi\xe7birinde k\xf6k salamamak.",dailyMessage:"Ke\xe7i bug\xfcn seni dik bir yamac\u0131n \xf6n\xfcnde durduruyor ve \u015funu s\xf6yl\xfcyor: bu yolun ba\u015fka bir \xe7\u0131k\u0131\u015f\u0131 var. Ke\xe7iler kayal\u0131klara t\u0131rman\u0131rken di\u011fer hayvanlar\u0131n g\xf6remedi\u011fi \xe7atlaklar\u0131, k\xfc\xe7\xfck \xe7\u0131k\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131, gizli basamaklar\u0131 kullan\u0131r. O imk\xe2ns\u0131z gibi g\xf6r\xfcnen durum \u2014 belki bir ili\u015fki, belki bir proje, belki bir karar \u2014 sende de bak\u0131lmam\u0131\u015f bir a\xe7\u0131s\u0131 var. Bug\xfcn ayn\u0131 kap\u0131y\u0131 tekrar tekrar \xe7almay\u0131 b\u0131rak\u0131p etraf\u0131na bakabilir misin? Belki bir pencere a\xe7\u0131k, belki arka kap\u0131, belki hi\xe7 fark etmedi\u011fin bir yol. Ke\xe7inin \xf6\u011fretisi \u015fu: t\u0131rmanmay\u0131 b\u0131rakmak ile farkl\u0131 bir rota denemek farkl\u0131 \u015feylerdir. Vazge\xe7me \u2014 ama ayn\u0131 yolu da b\u0131rakabilirsin. Bug\xfcn kendine sor: Bu problemin benim daha \xf6nce g\xf6rmedi\u011fim hangi y\xf6n\xfc var?",guidance:"T\u0131kand\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir konuyu bir ka\u011f\u0131da yaz\u0131n ve ard\u0131ndan en az \xfc\xe7 farkl\u0131 \xe7\xf6z\xfcm yolu listeleyin \u2014 bunlardan biri mutlaka al\u0131\u015f\u0131lmad\u0131k olsun. Ke\xe7i, al\u0131\u015f\u0131lmad\u0131k yolda y\xfcr\xfcr; beyin de tan\u0131d\u0131k rotalar\u0131n d\u0131\u015f\u0131na \xe7\u0131kt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda yarat\u0131c\u0131 \xe7\xf6z\xfcmler \xfcretmeye ba\u015flar. En beklenmedik \xe7\xf6z\xfcm bazen en i\u015fe yarayan\u0131d\u0131r.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Goat",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["creativity","mountain freedom","the steep path","vitality"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Anatolia the goat, one of the oldest domesticated animals, has been a symbol of abundance, vitality, and endurance since the Neolithic era; the presence of goat figures at G\xf6bekli Tepe shows how deeply rooted this sacred bond is. In Greek mythology the goat, sacred animal of the god Pan, is the symbol of music, wild nature, and fertile creativity; the gods of Olympus nursed Zeus with the milk of the sacred goat Amalthea \u2014 for this reason the goat is mother of the gods. In Norse mythology Thor's chariot is drawn by two goats: Tanngrisnir and Tanngnj\xf3str \u2014 slain each morning and reborn each evening; they are the symbol of eternal renewal and endurance. In Celtic tradition the goat is the archetype of the courageous soul that, without tiring, climbs the steepest cliffs and reaches the impossible \u2014 Celtic warriors etched the goat symbol on their shields. In Chinese astrology, those born in the year of the goat are described as creative, intuitive people who find their own way. The medicine of the goat is to find a path even on the steepest ground and to use obstacles as steps. Its shadow side: when stubbornness blocks flexibility \u2014 leaping on every ground but never taking root in any.",dailyMessageEn:"Goat stops you today before a sheer slope and says: this road has another way out. When goats climb cliffs, they use cracks, small ledges, and hidden steps that other animals cannot see. That seemingly impossible situation \u2014 perhaps a relationship, a project, a decision \u2014 also has an angle you have not yet examined. Can you stop knocking on the same door over and over today and look around? Perhaps a window is open, perhaps a back door, perhaps a path you have never noticed. The teaching of the goat is this: stopping climbing and trying a different route are different things. Do not give up \u2014 but you can release the same path. Ask yourself today: What aspect of this problem have I not seen before?",guidanceEn:"Write down on a paper an issue where you feel stuck and then list at least three different ways out \u2014 let one of them be unconventional. The goat walks the unconventional path; the brain too begins to produce creative solutions when it leaves familiar routes. The most unexpected solution is sometimes the one that works best."},{id:"a084",name:"\u0130bis",emoji:"\ud83e\udda2",element:"hava",symbolism:["bilgelik","kutsal yaz\u0131","ilahi ileti\u015fim","g\xf6zlem"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Ibis_ibis_1.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'\u0131n en b\xfcy\xfck bilgelik tanr\u0131s\u0131 Thoth, ibis ba\u015fl\u0131 bir tanr\u0131 olarak tasvir edilir \u2014 yaz\u0131n\u0131n, matemati\u011fin, astronominin, b\xfcy\xfcn\xfcn ve t\xfcm bilimlerin ilahi koruyucusudur; ibis bu nedenle bilginin kutsal cisimle\u015fmesi olarak tap\u0131nak bah\xe7elerinde ya\u015fat\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. \u0130bis, Nil sular\u0131n\u0131n y\xfckselmesini \xf6nceden hisseder ve y\xfcksek yerlere \xe7ekilirdi \u2014 bu g\xf6zlem yetene\u011fi ona gelece\u011fi bilen ku\u015f unvan\u0131n\u0131 kazand\u0131rd\u0131; M\u0131s\u0131rl\u0131lar onu kutsal bir hava tahminleyici olarak g\xf6rd\xfcler. Antik Yunan'da Hermes, Thoth'un kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 olarak ileti\u015fim ve bilgelik tanr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; bu ba\u011flant\u0131 arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla ibis, Bat\u0131 ezoterizminde bilginin ve ileti\u015fimin simgesi h\xe2line geldi. Afrika \u015faman gelene\u011finde ibis, derine inen gagas\u0131yla \xe7amurun i\xe7indeki ger\xe7e\u011fi \xe7\u0131karan varl\u0131kt\u0131r \u2014 g\xf6r\xfcnmeyeni g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr k\u0131lan bilgedir. Japonya'da ibis ulusal ku\u015f stat\xfcs\xfcndedir ve safl\u0131k, titizlik ile sessiz g\xf6zlemin simgesi olarak kabul edilir. \u0130bis'in t\u0131bb\u0131, g\xf6zlemleyerek \xf6\u011frenmek ve y\xfczeyin alt\u0131ndaki ger\xe7e\u011fi sab\u0131rla aramakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o kadar \xe7ok bilgi biriktirmek ki bilgeli\u011fi eylemden koparmak \u2014 s\xfcrekli analiz ederken hareketsiz kalmak.",dailyMessage:"\u0130bis bug\xfcn seni bilginin en eski bi\xe7imine davet ediyor: sessiz g\xf6zlem. Thoth her \u015feyi yazmadan \xf6nce g\xf6zlemledi, her s\xf6z\xfc s\xf6ylemeden \xf6nce d\xfc\u015f\xfcnd\xfc. Bug\xfcn bir duruma ya da bir ili\u015fkiye hemen tepki verme \u2014 \xf6nce g\xf6zlemle. Gagas\u0131n\u0131 \xe7amura dald\u0131rarak avlanan ibis, sab\u0131rs\u0131zca dal\u0131p \xe7\u0131kan bir bal\u0131k\xe7\u0131 de\u011fildir; bekler, hisseder, sonra hareket eder. Bug\xfcn sana bir soru ya da sorun sunuldu\u011funda, ilk tepkini vermeden \xf6nce bir nefes al ve sor: Burada hen\xfcz g\xf6rmedi\u011fim ne var? Bazen en de\u011ferli bilgiler konu\u015fmalar\u0131n aras\u0131ndaki sessizlikte, kelimeler yerine tonlarda, y\xfczlerin de\u011fil ellerin hareketinde gizlidir. Bug\xfcn neye ger\xe7ekten dikkat ettin?",guidance:"Bu hafta bir konu\u015fmada ya da toplant\u0131da kas\u0131tl\u0131 olarak g\xf6zlemci rol\xfcn\xfc \xfcstlenin: konu\u015fmaktan \xe7ok dinleyin, not al\u0131n, yarg\u0131lamadan kay\u0131t yap\u0131n. Sonras\u0131nda \u015funu yaz\u0131n: Bug\xfcn fark etti\u011fim ama normalde atlayaca\u011f\u0131m \u015fey neydi? \u0130bis gibi derin g\xf6zlem, bilgi ile bilgeli\u011fi birle\u015ftiren k\xf6pr\xfcd\xfcr.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Ibis",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["wisdom","sacred writing","divine communication","observation"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The greatest wisdom god of ancient Egypt, Thoth, is depicted as an ibis-headed deity \u2014 the divine guardian of writing, mathematics, astronomy, magic, and all the sciences; for this reason the ibis was kept as the sacred embodiment of knowledge in temple gardens. The ibis sensed in advance the rising of the Nile waters and withdrew to higher ground \u2014 this gift of observation earned it the title of the bird that knows the future; the Egyptians regarded it as a sacred forecaster of weather. In ancient Greece, Hermes \u2014 the counterpart of Thoth \u2014 is the god of communication and wisdom; through this connection the ibis became the symbol of knowledge and communication in Western esotericism. In African shamanic tradition the ibis, with its deep-probing beak, is the being who draws truth from the mud \u2014 the sage who makes the unseen seen. In Japan the ibis holds the status of national bird and is regarded as the symbol of purity, meticulousness, and silent observation. The medicine of the ibis is to learn by observing and to seek with patience the truth beneath the surface. Its shadow side: gathering so much information that wisdom becomes severed from action \u2014 remaining motionless while perpetually analyzing.",dailyMessageEn:"Ibis invites you today to the most ancient form of knowing: silent observation. Thoth observed before he wrote anything, considered before he spoke any word. Today do not react immediately to a situation or a relationship \u2014 first observe. The ibis, hunting by dipping its beak into the mud, is not a fisher who plunges in impatiently; it waits, senses, then moves. When a question or problem is offered to you today, take a breath before your first reaction and ask: What is here that I have not yet seen? Sometimes the most valuable knowledge is hidden in the silences between words, in tones rather than words, in the movement of hands rather than faces. What did you truly pay attention to today?",guidanceEn:"This week, deliberately take on the role of observer in a conversation or a meeting: listen more than you speak, take notes, record without judgment. Afterward write: What did I notice today that I would normally have skipped? Like the ibis, deep observation is the bridge that unites knowledge with wisdom."},{id:"a085",name:"\u0130skarabe",emoji:"\ud83e\udeb2",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["yeniden do\u011fu\u015f","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","u\u011fur","g\xfcne\u015f enerjisi"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Scarabaeus_sacer_2.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc sembollerinden biri olan iskarabe b\xf6ce\u011fi, g\xfcbre yuvarlayan skarabeus t\xfcr\xfcnden esinlenerek g\xfcne\u015f tanr\u0131s\u0131 Khepri ile \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirildi \u2014 Khepri yuvarlamak anlam\u0131na gelir ve her sabah ufuktan yuvarlanan g\xfcne\u015f bu b\xf6ce\u011fin imgesiyle anlat\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131. \u0130skarabe m\xfch\xfcrleri M\u0131s\u0131r mumyalar\u0131n\u0131n kalp b\xf6lgesine yerle\u015ftirilirdi; ahiret yolculu\u011funda kalbi koruyan ve yeniden do\u011fu\u015fu g\xfcvence alt\u0131na alan kutsal t\u0131ls\u0131m. Anadolu'da skarabeus fig\xfcrleri Hitit, Frig ve Lidya uygarl\u0131klar\u0131nda da bulunan kutsal sembollerdir \u2014 M\u0131s\u0131r'dan Anadolu'ya ge\xe7en bu g\xfc\xe7 imgesi, evrenselden yerel bir d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm bilgeli\u011fine d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc. \xc7in ve Japon k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcnde b\xf6cek d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcmleri \u2014 \xf6zellikle pupa ve ergin a\u015famas\u0131 \u2014 yeniden do\u011fu\u015fun ve manevi d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn g\xfc\xe7l\xfc simgeleridir. Aztek gelene\u011finde g\xfcne\u015fin her g\xfcn yeniden do\u011fmas\u0131, G\xfcne\u015f Ta\u015f\u0131'nda anlat\u0131l\u0131r ve benzer bi\xe7imde yeniden ba\u015flaman\u0131n kozmik d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcne i\u015faret eder. \u0130skarabenin t\u0131bb\u0131, her g\xfcn\xfcn s\u0131f\u0131rdan ba\u015flaman\u0131n m\xfcmk\xfcn oldu\u011funu hat\u0131rlatmak ve d\xfcn\xfcn y\xfck\xfcn\xfc bug\xfcne ta\u015f\u0131may\u0131 reddetmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: s\xfcrekli yeniden ba\u015flamak ama hi\xe7bir \u015feyi tamamlamamak \u2014 de\u011fi\u015fim ill\xfczyonunda tamamlanmay\u0131 ertelemek.",dailyMessage:"\u0130skarabe bug\xfcn sana g\xfcne\u015fin en b\xfcy\xfck s\u0131rr\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor: her sabah ger\xe7ekten yeni bir g\xfcne\u015f do\u011far. Ayn\u0131 g\xfcne\u015f de\u011fil \u2014 d\xfcn geceye batan g\xfcne\u015f geri gelmez; sabah ufukta g\xf6r\xfcnen yeni bir ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7t\u0131r. D\xfcn\xfcn yorgunlu\u011funu, utanc\u0131n\u0131, h\xfcsran\u0131n\u0131 bu g\xfcne ta\u015f\u0131man zorunlu de\u011fil. \u0130skarabe topra\u011f\u0131n i\xe7inde karanl\u0131kta yuvarlana yuvarlana ilerler ve bir g\xfcn \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa \xe7\u0131kar \u2014 bu s\xfcre\xe7 \xe7irkin, zor, pis g\xf6r\xfcnebilir; ama sonunda kanatlar a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r. Sende de \u015fu an topra\u011f\u0131n alt\u0131nda olan bir \u015fey var m\u0131 \u2014 bir s\xfcre\xe7, bir zorluk, bir d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm? Bitti gibi hissettiren o \u015fey belki bitmemi\u015ftir, belki hen\xfcz \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa \xe7\u0131kmam\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. Ve bug\xfcn, \u015fu anda, hangi d\xfcn\xfcn y\xfck\xfcn\xfc b\u0131rakabilirsin?",guidance:"Her sabah uyan\u0131nca, yataktan kalkmadan \xf6nce otuz saniye \u015funu hissedin: Bu g\xfcn d\xfcndenden farkl\u0131. Ben de d\xfcndekinden farkl\u0131y\u0131m. Ard\u0131ndan b\u0131rakmak istedi\u011finiz bir \u015feyi \u2014 bir duygu, bir d\xfc\u015f\xfcnce, bir al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k \u2014 i\xe7inizde ad\u0131yla fark edin ve Bu g\xfcn onu ta\u015f\u0131m\u0131yorum deyin. \u0130skarabe rit\xfceli, g\xfcn\xfc temiz bir zihinle a\xe7man\u0131n kadim ve g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir yoludur.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Scarab",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["rebirth","transformation","good fortune","solar energy"],anatolianMeaningEn:"One of the most powerful symbols of ancient Egypt, the scarab beetle \u2014 inspired by the dung-rolling Scarabaeus sacer \u2014 was identified with the sun god Khepri; Khepri means to roll, and the sun rolling up over the horizon each morning was told through this beetle's image. Scarab amulets were placed over the heart of Egyptian mummies; a sacred talisman protecting the heart on the journey through the afterlife and securing rebirth. In Anatolia scarab figures are also sacred symbols found in Hittite, Phrygian, and Lydian civilizations \u2014 this image of power, passing from Egypt to Anatolia, transformed from a universal to a local wisdom of transformation. In Chinese and Japanese culture insect transformations \u2014 particularly the pupa and adult stages \u2014 are powerful symbols of rebirth and spiritual transformation. In Aztec tradition the daily rebirth of the sun, told on the Sun Stone, points in a similar way to the cosmic cycle of beginning again. The medicine of the scarab is to remember that each day can truly begin from zero and to refuse to carry yesterday's burden into today. Its shadow side: continually starting again but completing nothing \u2014 postponing fulfillment in the illusion of change.",dailyMessageEn:"Scarab reminds you today of the sun's greatest secret: every morning a truly new sun rises. Not the same sun \u2014 the sun that set last night does not return; what appears on the horizon at dawn is a new beginning. You are not obliged to carry yesterday's tiredness, shame, or disappointment into today. The scarab rolls and rolls in darkness beneath the earth and one day emerges into light \u2014 this process may look ugly, hard, dirty; but in the end the wings open. Is there something currently beneath the soil for you \u2014 a process, a difficulty, a transformation? What feels finished may not be finished, may not yet have emerged into light. And today, right now, which of yesterday's burdens can you set down?",guidanceEn:"Each morning when you wake, before rising from bed, feel this for thirty seconds: This day is different from yesterday. And I am different from the one I was yesterday. Then notice something within you that you wish to release \u2014 an emotion, a thought, a habit \u2014 and say I do not carry it today. The scarab ritual is an ancient and powerful way to open the day with a clean mind."},{id:"a086",name:"Piton",emoji:"\ud83d\udc0d",element:"toprak",symbolism:["ata ruhu","kutsal koruyucu","bereket","toprak ba\u011flant\u0131s\u0131"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Python_molurus_molurus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Bat\u0131 Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde piton, Tanr\u0131 Olodumare'nin en kutsal tezah\xfcrlerinden biridir \u2014 k\xf6ylerin etraf\u0131nda ya\u015fayan pitonlar ata ruhlar\u0131n\u0131n bedenlenmi\u015f hali olarak korunur, onlara zarar vermek a\u011f\u0131r bir tabu say\u0131l\u0131r. Benin ve Fon halk\u0131n\u0131n Vodun gelene\u011finde Dan Ayido Hwedo \u2014 g\xf6kku\u015fa\u011f\u0131 y\u0131lan\u0131 \u2014 tanr\u0131sal bir piton olarak d\xfcnyay\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yan, ge\xe7i\u015fleri ve d\xf6ng\xfcleri y\xf6neten kozmik varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Avustralya Aborijin R\xfcya Zaman\u0131'nda G\xf6kku\u015fa\u011f\u0131 Y\u0131lan\u0131, yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n en temel varl\u0131\u011f\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 nehirleri, da\u011flar\u0131, ya\u015fam\u0131n kendisini bi\xe7imlendiren kutsal piton. Hint mitolojisinde Ananta Shesha, evrenin okyanus \xfczerinde k\u0131vr\u0131lan devasa kutsal y\u0131lan\u0131d\u0131r; Vishnu onun \xfczerinde uyur ve bu g\xf6r\xfcnt\xfc kozmik denge ile ata bilgeli\u011fini simgeler. Orta Amerika Maya gelene\u011finde t\xfcyl\xfc y\u0131lan Kukulk\xe1n, yerin ve g\xf6\u011f\xfcn bir arada dans\u0131n\u0131 temsil eder \u2014 ata ruhlar\u0131yla canl\u0131lar aras\u0131ndaki k\xf6pr\xfc. Pitonun t\u0131bb\u0131, seni besleyen ve koruyan g\xf6r\xfcnmez d\xfczeni fark etmek ve ata bilgeli\u011fine sayg\u0131 g\xf6stermektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: k\xf6klerine o kadar ba\u011fl\u0131 kalmak ki de\u011fi\u015fime kapal\u0131 hale gelmek \u2014 ge\xe7mi\u015fi onurland\u0131rmak ile onda s\u0131k\u0131\u015f\u0131p kalmak aras\u0131ndaki fark\u0131 yitirmek.",dailyMessage:"Piton bug\xfcn seni k\xf6klerine davet ediyor. K\xf6kler g\xf6r\xfcnmez, alt\u0131nda; ama a\u011fac\u0131 tutan onlard\u0131r. Seni bug\xfcne ta\u015f\u0131yan, ayakta tutan o g\xf6r\xfcnmez d\xfczeni \u2014 ailen, gelene\u011fin, bu topra\u011f\u0131n, seni seven insanlar\u0131n \u2014 bug\xfcn bir an i\xe7in fark et. Bazen en k\xfc\xe7\xfck minnetten en b\xfcy\xfck g\xfc\xe7 do\u011far. Piton yava\u015f hareket eder ama bask\u0131s\u0131 tart\u0131\u015f\u0131lmazd\u0131r \u2014 o g\xfcc\xfc topraktan al\u0131r. Sen de bug\xfcn enerjini yenilemek istiyorsan, kayna\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rlaman yeterli olabilir. Seni bug\xfcne ta\u015f\u0131yan bir insan var m\u0131 \u2014 h\xe2l\xe2 hayatta ya da art\u0131k de\u011fil \u2014 ona i\xe7ten bir te\u015fekk\xfcr hissedebilir misin? O ba\u011flant\u0131, seni ta\u015f\u0131yan g\xf6r\xfcnmez bir g\xfc\xe7t\xfcr.",guidance:"Bu hafta i\xe7inde bir atan\u0131z\u0131, bir \xf6\u011fretmeninizi ya da sizi \u015fekillendiren bir ki\u015fiyi d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcn ve ona dair k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir eylem ger\xe7ekle\u015ftirin: bir foto\u011frafa bak\u0131n, bir an\u0131y\u0131 yaz\u0131n, ya da m\xfcmk\xfcnse o ki\u015fiyi aray\u0131n. Ata ba\u011flant\u0131s\u0131, k\xf6klenme ve kimlik g\xfc\xe7lendirme prati\u011finin en kadim ve etkin bi\xe7imidir; k\xf6kl\xfc a\u011fa\xe7lar f\u0131rt\u0131nada daha sa\u011flam durur.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Python",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["ancestor spirit","sacred protector","fertility","earth connection"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the West African Yoruba tradition the python is one of the holiest manifestations of God Olodumare \u2014 pythons living around villages are protected as the embodied form of ancestor spirits, and harming them is considered a grave taboo. In the Vodun tradition of the Benin and Fon peoples, Dan Ayido Hwedo \u2014 the rainbow serpent \u2014 is a divine python, a cosmic being who carries the world and governs passages and cycles. In Australian Aboriginal Dreamtime the Rainbow Serpent is the most fundamental being of creation \u2014 a sacred python who shaped the rivers, mountains, and life itself. In Hindu mythology Ananta Shesha is the immense sacred serpent coiled upon the cosmic ocean; Vishnu sleeps upon him, and this image symbolizes cosmic balance and ancestral wisdom. In the Mayan tradition of Central America Kukulk\xe1n, the feathered serpent, represents the joined dance of earth and sky \u2014 the bridge between ancestor spirits and the living. The medicine of the python is to notice the invisible order that feeds and protects you and to honor ancestral wisdom. Its shadow side: clinging so tightly to one's roots that one closes off to change \u2014 losing the distinction between honoring the past and being stuck in it.",dailyMessageEn:"Python invites you to your roots today. Roots are unseen, beneath; but they are what hold the tree. For a single moment today, notice the invisible order that has carried you to this day \u2014 your family, your tradition, this land, the people who love you. Sometimes the smallest gratitude births the greatest power. Python moves slowly but its grip is indisputable \u2014 it draws this power from the earth. If you wish to renew your energy today, remembering your source may be enough. Is there a person who carried you to this day \u2014 still alive or no longer \u2014 for whom you can feel sincere thanks? That connection is an invisible force that carries you.",guidanceEn:"This week, think of an ancestor, a teacher, or a person who shaped you, and perform a small act in their honor: look at a photograph, write a memory, or if possible call that person. The connection to ancestors is the most ancient and effective practice of rootedness and identity strengthening; trees with deep roots stand firmer in the storm."},{id:"a087",name:"Albatros",emoji:"\ud83d\udd4a\ufe0f",element:"hava",symbolism:["sonsuz yolculuk","okyanus \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfc","dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k","g\xfcven"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Diomedea_exulans_-_SE_Tasmania.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Kelt denizcilerinin kutsal koruyucu ku\u015fu olan albatros, \xf6ld\xfcr\xfclmesi en a\u011f\u0131r denizci tabusuydu \u2014 bir albatrosu \xf6ld\xfcrmek, kendi felaketini davet etmekti. Samuel Taylor Coleridge'in Ya\u015fl\u0131 Denizcinin Masal\u0131 \u015fiirinde albatros \xf6ld\xfcrme imgesi bu yasa\u011f\u0131 edebiyata ta\u015f\u0131m\u0131\u015f ve evrensel bir simge haline getirmi\u015ftir. Maori gelene\u011finde albatros, \xf6lm\xfc\u015f denizcilerin ruhlar\u0131n\u0131 bar\u0131nd\u0131ran kutsal ku\u015ftur; okyanusun \xfczerinde s\xfcz\xfclen onlar\u0131n ruhlar\u0131, gidenlerin geri d\xf6nece\u011fini m\xfcjdeler. Polinezya \u015famanizminde albatros, r\xfczg\xe2r\u0131 o kadar iyi tan\u0131r ki kanat \xe7\u0131rpmadan y\xfczlerce kilometre u\xe7ar \u2014 do\u011fan\u0131n g\xfcc\xfcne teslim olman\u0131n ve onunla dans etmenin ustal\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 temsil eder. Norse mitolojisinde denizin sonsuzlu\u011funu a\u015fan varl\u0131klar, Odin'in mesajc\u0131lar\u0131 say\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131; albatros bu kategoride tanr\u0131sal postac\u0131 olarak an\u0131l\u0131r. Japonya'da ise albatros Shinto gelene\u011finde okyanus kamisi olarak derin bir sayg\u0131yla kar\u015f\u0131lan\u0131r. Albatrosun t\u0131bb\u0131, uzun soluklu bir yolculu\u011fa g\xfcvenle devam etmek ve hem ge\xe7mi\u015fe hem gelece\u011fe dair kayg\u0131y\u0131 b\u0131rakmakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: yolculu\u011fu o kadar sevmek ki bir yere ait olmay\u0131, k\xf6k salmay\u0131 istememek.",dailyMessage:"Albatros bug\xfcn sana sonsuz ufuktan bir mesaj getiriyor: yol, var\u0131\u015f noktas\u0131 kadar kutsal. Bu ku\u015f kanat \xe7\u0131rpmadan okyanusun \xfczerinde s\xfcz\xfcl\xfcr \u2014 r\xfczg\xe2r\u0131 diren\xe7 de\u011fil, ortak olarak kullan\u0131r. Sen de bug\xfcn hayat\u0131n\u0131n i\xe7indeki r\xfczg\xe2rlar\u0131 d\xfc\u015f\xfcn: seni zorlayan ama belki de ta\u015f\u0131yan g\xfc\xe7ler. Onlara direnmek yerine onlarla s\xfcz\xfclmeyi deneyebilir misin? Uzun s\xfcredir devam eden bir yolculukta m\u0131s\u0131n \u2014 bir ili\u015fki, bir proje, bir iyile\u015fme s\xfcreci? Var\u0131\u015f neresi bilmiyorsun, biti\u015fi g\xf6r\xfcnm\xfcyor; ama albatros da her g\xfcn nereye ula\u015faca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 bilmez. Sadece u\xe7ar. Yolun ortas\u0131nda olmak, kaybolmu\u015f olmak de\u011fildir. Bug\xfcn hangi yolun ortadas\u0131n ve onu terk etmeden, durup nefes almana izin var m\u0131?",guidance:"Bug\xfcn y\xfcr\xfcy\xfc\u015fe \xe7\u0131k\u0131n \u2014 hedefe de\u011fil, yola odaklanarak. Bir yere varmak i\xe7in de\u011fil, y\xfcr\xfcmenin kendisi i\xe7in. Y\xfcr\xfcrken etraf\u0131n\u0131zdaki tek bir \u015feyi \u2014 bir ses, bir koku, bir renk \u2014 tam dikkatinizle fark edin. Albatros meditasyonu budur: \u015fu andaki yolda tam olarak bulunmak. Bu pratik, hedef odakl\u0131 zihnin dengelenmesine ve \u015fimdiki ana d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcne yard\u0131mc\u0131 olur.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Albatross",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["endless journey","ocean freedom","endurance","trust"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The sacred protector bird of Celtic sailors, the albatross \u2014 to kill one was the gravest of seafaring taboos; killing an albatross was to summon one's own disaster. Samuel Taylor Coleridge's poem The Rime of the Ancient Mariner carried this prohibition into literature and made the killing of an albatross a universal symbol. In Maori tradition the albatross is the sacred bird that houses the souls of deceased sailors; their souls soaring over the ocean bring word that the departed will return. In Polynesian shamanism the albatross knows the wind so well that it can fly hundreds of kilometers without a single beat of its wings \u2014 embodying the mastery of surrendering to and dancing with the force of nature. In Norse mythology beings who crossed the vastness of the sea were counted as Odin's messengers; the albatross is honored in this category as a divine courier. In Japan the albatross is received in the Shinto tradition with deep reverence as an ocean kami. The medicine of the albatross is to continue a long journey with trust and to release anxiety about both past and future. Its shadow side: loving the journey so much that one refuses to belong anywhere, refuses to take root.",dailyMessageEn:"Albatross brings you a message today from the endless horizon: the path is as sacred as the destination. This bird soars over the ocean without flapping its wings \u2014 it uses the wind not as resistance but as partner. Think today of the winds within your own life: the forces that press you yet perhaps also carry you. Instead of resisting them, can you try to soar with them? Are you on a journey that has been going on for a long time \u2014 a relationship, a project, a process of healing? You do not know where you will arrive, the end is not visible; but the albatross too does not know every day where it will land. It simply flies. Being in the middle of the road does not mean being lost. Which path are you in the middle of today, and do you allow yourself, without leaving it, to pause and breathe?",guidanceEn:"Take a walk today \u2014 focusing not on a destination but on the path itself. Not to reach somewhere, but for the sake of walking. As you walk, notice one thing around you \u2014 a sound, a scent, a color \u2014 with your full attention. This is the albatross meditation: being fully present on the path of the moment. This practice helps balance the goal-oriented mind and returns you to the present."},{id:"a088",name:"Flamingo",emoji:"\ud83e\udda9",element:"su",symbolism:["zarafet","topluluk dengesi","denge","renklilik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Greater_flamingo_Phoenicopterus_ruber_roseus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Akdeniz havzas\u0131nda antik \xe7a\u011flardan bu yana g\xf6r\xfclen flamingo, M\u0131s\u0131r hiyeroglif gelene\u011finde Ra \u2014 g\xfcne\u015f \u2014 ile ili\u015fkilendirilir; pembe-k\u0131z\u0131l rengi g\xfcne\u015fin ufuktaki yans\u0131mas\u0131 olarak kutsal say\u0131l\u0131r. Afrika \u015faman gelene\u011finde flamingo, su ile ate\u015fin bulu\u015ftu\u011fu liminal alanda duran denge varl\u0131\u011f\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 s\u0131\u011f sularda tek ayak \xfczerinde saatlerce durabilmesi, g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr bir huzuru simgeler. G\xfcney Amerika And gelene\u011finde flamingolar, anda ta\u015f\u0131nan kutsal enerji ak\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr h\xe2lidir \u2014 b\xfcy\xfck s\xfcr\xfcler halinde u\xe7malar\u0131, kolektif ruhun bireysel bedende ger\xe7ekle\u015fmesini simgeler. Hint mitolojisinde flamingo, Hamsa ku\u015fu ile \xf6zde\u015fle\u015ftirilir \u2014 su ile topra\u011f\u0131 ay\u0131rt eden, s\xfct\xfc sudan s\xfczen, hakikati yan\u0131lsamadan ay\u0131ran bilge varl\u0131k. Antik Roma'da nadirlik ve l\xfcks olarak g\xf6r\xfclmesine kar\u015f\u0131n bu ku\u015f M\u0131s\u0131r ve Fenike geleneklerinde kutsall\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 korumu\u015ftur. Flamingonun t\u0131bb\u0131, kalabal\u0131k i\xe7inde denge bulmak ve kendi merkezini korurken toplulukla birlikte s\xfcz\xfclebilmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: g\xf6r\xfcnt\xfcye o kadar \xf6nem vermek ki ger\xe7ek dengeyi kaybetmek \u2014 d\u0131\u015f zarafet i\xe7sel huzurun yerini tutamaz.",dailyMessage:"Flamingo bug\xfcn sana tek ayak \xfczerinde durman\u0131n s\u0131rr\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011fretiyor: denge, dura\u011fanl\u0131ktan de\u011fil, s\xfcrekli k\xfc\xe7\xfck ayarlamalardan gelir. Flamingo asl\u0131nda her an hafif\xe7e sallan\u0131r \u2014 ama bu sallant\u0131 onu d\xfc\u015f\xfcrmez, ta\u015f\u0131r. Hayat\u0131nda \u015fu an dengelemeye \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n ne var? \u0130\u015f ve dinlenme, vermek ve almak, yaln\u0131zl\u0131k ve birliktelik \u2014 hangisi seni zoruyor? Flamingonun en b\xfcy\xfck s\u0131rr\u0131 pembe rengi: bu renk yediklerinden gelir, i\xe7sel beslenmenin d\u0131\u015fa yans\u0131mas\u0131d\u0131r. Sen de bug\xfcn i\xe7ini ne ile besliyorsun, ve bu d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcyor mu? Kalabal\u0131k i\xe7inde kendi merkezini bulmak bir sanatt\u0131r \u2014 ne kayboluyor ne de kat\u0131la\u015f\u0131yor olmak. Bug\xfcn bir topluluk i\xe7indeyken kendini nas\u0131l hissediyorsun?",guidance:"Bu hafta her sabah iki dakika tek ayak \xfczerinde durmay\u0131 deneyin \u2014 ger\xe7ekten. D\xfc\u015f\xfcnce f\u0131rt\u0131nas\u0131 ya\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131zda ya da bunald\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131zda bu egzersizi yap\u0131n. Fiziksel denge ile zihinsel denge birbirini besler; beyin denge tutarken \u015fimdiye odaklanmak zorunda kal\u0131r ve bu, k\u0131sa s\xfcreli de olsa kayg\u0131y\u0131 s\u0131f\u0131rlar.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Flamingo",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["grace","community balance","equilibrium","color and vibrancy"],anatolianMeaningEn:"Seen in the Mediterranean basin since antiquity, the flamingo is in the Egyptian hieroglyphic tradition associated with Ra \u2014 the sun; its pink-red color is held sacred as the reflection of the sun on the horizon. In African shamanic tradition the flamingo is the being of balance who stands in the liminal zone where water and fire meet \u2014 its ability to stand on a single leg in shallow water for hours symbolizes a visible serenity. In the Andean tradition of South America flamingos are the visible form of the sacred energy flow carried in the Andes \u2014 their flight in great flocks symbolizes the realization of the collective soul through individual bodies. In Hindu mythology the flamingo is identified with the Hamsa bird \u2014 the wise being who distinguishes water from earth, strains milk from water, separates truth from illusion. While considered a rarity and luxury in ancient Rome, this bird retained its sacredness in Egyptian and Phoenician traditions. The medicine of the flamingo is to find balance amid the crowd and to be able to glide together with the community while protecting one's own center. Its shadow side: caring so much for appearance that one loses true balance \u2014 outer grace cannot replace inner peace.",dailyMessageEn:"Flamingo teaches you today the secret of standing on one leg: balance comes not from stillness but from constant small adjustments. The flamingo actually sways lightly at every moment \u2014 but this swaying does not topple it, it carries it. What are you trying to balance in your life right now? Work and rest, giving and receiving, solitude and togetherness \u2014 which one is pressing on you? The flamingo's greatest secret is its pink color: this color comes from what it eats, the outer reflection of inner nourishment. What are you feeding your inside with today, and does it show on the outside? Finding your own center amid a crowd is an art \u2014 being neither lost nor hardened. How do you feel today when you are within a community?",guidanceEn:"This week try standing on one leg for two minutes each morning \u2014 really. Do this exercise when you experience a storm of thoughts or feel overwhelmed. Physical balance and mental balance feed each other; while the brain holds balance it is forced to focus on the present, and this resets anxiety even briefly."},{id:"a089",name:"Manta Vatoz",emoji:"\ud83c\udf0a",element:"su",symbolism:["su u\xe7u\u015fu","derinlik yolculu\u011fu","\xf6zg\xfcr ruh","sezgi"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Manta_birostris-Thailand4.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Polinezya okyanus\xe7uluk gelene\u011finde manta vatoz, g\xf6r\xfcnmez okyanus ak\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131 hisseden ve onlar\u0131 yol haritas\u0131 olarak kullanan kutsal deniz varl\u0131\u011f\u0131d\u0131r; Polinezya denizcileri bu varl\u0131\u011f\u0131 derinin f\u0131s\u0131lday\u0131c\u0131s\u0131 olarak g\xf6r\xfcrd\xfc. And \u015famanizminde manta vatoz iki d\xfcnya aras\u0131ndaki k\xf6pr\xfcd\xfcr \u2014 y\xfczey ile derin, bilin\xe7 ile bilin\xe7alt\u0131, g\xfcnd\xfcz ile gece aras\u0131nda gidip gelen bilge rehber. Japon Shinto gelene\u011finde okyanus varl\u0131klar\u0131 Ry\u016bjin'in sakinleri olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr; manta gibi b\xfcy\xfck ve zarif deniz varl\u0131klar\u0131 denizin tanr\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n el\xe7ileri kabul edilir. Aztek deniz mitolojisinde ilkel deniz yarat\u0131klar\u0131 ve onlardan do\u011fan denizin kutsal sakinleri, manta gibi varl\u0131klarla sembolik ba\u011flar ta\u015f\u0131r; bilinmeyenin derinliklerini simgelerler. Hawaii gelene\u011finde manta, iyi \u015fans ve koruyucu ruh olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr \u2014 bir manta suyun alt\u0131nda sizi izliyorsa, ata ruhunuz yan\u0131n\u0131zdad\u0131r. Manta vatoz'un t\u0131bb\u0131, g\xf6r\xfcnmez ak\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131 hissetmek ve sezgiyle hareket etmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: y\xfczeyde ne oldu\u011funu g\xf6rmezden gelerek derine o kadar dalmak ki pratik ger\xe7eklikten kopulmak.",dailyMessage:"Manta Vatoz bug\xfcn sana su alt\u0131ndaki ak\u0131nt\u0131lara dikkat etmeni s\xf6yl\xfcyor. Y\xfczeyde her \u015fey sakin g\xf6r\xfcnebilir \u2014 ama derin ak\u0131nt\u0131lar hi\xe7 durmaz. Bir ili\u015fkinde, bir projede, kendi i\xe7inde y\xfczeyin alt\u0131nda ne oluyor? Manta dev kanatlar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7\u0131rpmadan s\xfcz\xfcl\xfcr \u2014 g\xfc\xe7 harcamaz, ak\u0131nt\u0131yla dans eder. Sen de bug\xfcn var olan bir g\xfc\xe7le sava\u015fmak yerine onu hissetmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015fabilir misin? Belki bir durum seni s\xfcrekli zoruyor ve nedeni anla\u015f\u0131lam\u0131yor \u2014 belki y\xfczeyin alt\u0131nda anla\u015f\u0131lmay\u0131 bekleyen bir ak\u0131nt\u0131 var. Bug\xfcn sezgine g\xfcven: mant\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n d\u0131\u015flad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcn zaten biliyor olabilir. Ne hissediyorsun \u2014 bunu kelimelerle de\u011fil, i\xe7inden s\xf6yler misin?",guidance:"Bu ak\u015fam oturun ve g\xf6zlerinizi kapat\u0131n. Bir ili\u015fkinizi ya da durumunuzu d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfcn ve kendinize sorun: Bu konuda i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcm bana ne s\xf6yl\xfcyor, ama ben onu duymazdan m\u0131 geliyorum? On dakika bu soruyla kal\u0131n \u2014 cevab\u0131 zorlamay\u0131n, sadece suyun alt\u0131ndaki ak\u0131nt\u0131y\u0131 hissedin. Sezgi, bast\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131\u015f bilgi denen \u015feydir; ona alan a\xe7mak onu duyman\u0131n en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc yoludur.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Manta Ray",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["flight through water","journey into depth","free spirit","intuition"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the Polynesian seafaring tradition the manta ray is the sacred sea being who senses unseen ocean currents and uses them as a map; Polynesian sailors regarded this being as the whisperer of the deep. In Andean shamanism the manta ray is the bridge between two worlds \u2014 the wise guide who moves between surface and depth, consciousness and unconsciousness, day and night. In Japanese Shinto tradition ocean beings are seen as inhabitants of Ry\u016bjin; large and graceful sea beings like the manta are accepted as emissaries of the sea god. In Aztec sea mythology the primordial sea creatures and the sacred inhabitants of the sea that arose from them carry symbolic bonds with beings such as the manta; they symbolize the depths of the unknown. In Hawaiian tradition the manta is seen as good fortune and a protective spirit \u2014 if a manta is watching you beneath the water, your ancestor spirit is beside you. The medicine of the manta ray is to sense the invisible currents and to move by intuition. Its shadow side: diving so deep that you ignore what is happening on the surface \u2014 becoming severed from practical reality.",dailyMessageEn:"Manta Ray asks you today to pay attention to the currents beneath the water. On the surface everything may look calm \u2014 but the deep currents never stop. In a relationship, in a project, within yourself, what is happening beneath the surface? Manta glides without flapping its great wings \u2014 it does not spend force, it dances with the current. Today, instead of fighting an existing force, can you try to feel it? Perhaps a situation has been pressing on you constantly and you cannot understand why \u2014 perhaps beneath the surface a current is waiting to be understood. Trust your intuition today: what your mind dismisses, your instinct may already know. What are you feeling \u2014 can you say it not in words, but from within?",guidanceEn:"This evening sit and close your eyes. Think of one of your relationships or situations and ask: What is my instinct telling me about this, but which I am pretending not to hear? Stay with this question for ten minutes \u2014 do not force the answer, just feel the current beneath the water. Intuition is what we call suppressed knowing; opening space for it is the most powerful way to hear it."},{id:"a090",name:"Yele Kurdu",emoji:"\ud83d\udc3a",element:"toprak",symbolism:["yaln\u0131z ama g\xfc\xe7l\xfc","\xf6zg\xfcn yol","k\xf6pr\xfc kurucu","And ruhu"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Maned_wolf2.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"G\xfcney Amerika'n\u0131n And ve Pampa ovalar\u0131n\u0131n kutsal hayvan\u0131 olan Yele Kurdu, ne tam bir kurt ne tam bir tilkidir \u2014 kendi ba\u015f\u0131na bir cins olu\u015fturur ve bu benzersizli\u011fi onu spirit\xfcel olarak \xe7ok g\xfc\xe7l\xfc k\u0131lar. Brezilya ve Arjantin yerli \u015faman gelene\u011finde Yele Kurdu, arazi s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 koruyan ve ge\xe7i\u015fleri denetleyen kutsal bek\xe7idir \u2014 bir yerden di\u011ferine ge\xe7erken ona sayg\u0131 g\xf6sterilmesi gerekir. Guaran\xed mitolojisinde Yele Kurdu, orman ruhunun habercisidir ve karanl\u0131kla ayd\u0131nl\u0131k aras\u0131ndaki dengeyi temsil eder. And \u015famanizminde uzun bacakl\u0131 yap\u0131s\u0131 k\xf6pr\xfc kurucu olarak yorumlan\u0131r: yeri ile g\xf6\u011f\xfc, ge\xe7mi\u015fi ile gelece\u011fi, yaln\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ile toplulu\u011fu birbirine ba\u011flar. Guaran\xed gelene\u011finde ise Yele Kurdu'nun havlamas\u0131, tehlikeden koruyan ve toplulu\u011fu uyaran bir kutsal ses olarak sayg\u0131yla dinlenir. Yele Kurdu'nun t\u0131bb\u0131, kendi kategorisini yaratmak ve ba\u015fka kimseyle k\u0131yaslanmaya gerek duymadan \xf6zg\xfcn olmakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: \xf6zg\xfcnl\xfc\u011fe o kadar tutunmak ki toplulu\u011fa kat\u0131lmay\u0131 reddetmek \u2014 yaln\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131 kimlik olarak benimsemek.",dailyMessage:"Yele Kurdu bug\xfcn sana \u015funu s\xf6yl\xfcyor: sen kendi t\xfcr\xfcn\xfcn tek \xfcyesisin \u2014 ve bu bir sorun de\u011fil, bir arma\u011fan. Kurt kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131rmalar\u0131na dayanamaz; tilki benzetmelerine. O yaln\u0131zca Yele Kurdu'dur. Sen de bug\xfcn kendinle k\u0131yaslad\u0131\u011f\u0131n insanlar\u0131 bir an i\xe7in paranteze al. Onlar\u0131n yolu onlar\u0131nd\u0131r \u2014 s\u0131\xe7ray\u0131\u015flar\u0131, ba\u015far\u0131lar\u0131, tempolar\u0131, ritmileri. Senin yolun senindir ve belki ba\u015fka kimsenin yoluna benzemiyor \u2014 bu, kayboldu\u011fun anlam\u0131na gelmiyor. \xd6zg\xfcn olmak, yaln\u0131z olmak demek de\u011fildir; ama kendi \xe7izginde y\xfcr\xfcmek, bazen yaln\u0131z ad\u0131mlar atmay\u0131 gerektirir. Bug\xfcn kendine sor: Hangi k\u0131yaslamay\u0131 b\u0131rak\u0131rsam, kendime daha \xe7ok yer a\xe7ar\u0131m?",guidance:"Bu hafta boyunca ba\u015fkalar\u0131yla bilin\xe7li olarak k\u0131yaslamay\u0131 b\u0131rakmak i\xe7in \u015fu egzersizi yap\u0131n: kendinizi biriyle k\u0131yaslad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 fark etti\u011finiz her an, hemen \u015funu sorun: Benim kendi yolumda bug\xfcn att\u0131\u011f\u0131m ad\u0131m ne? Bu soruyu cevaplamak sizi d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan i\xe7eriye, k\u0131yastan kendi yolunuza geri getirir. Yele Kurdu uzun vadeli bir pratikle geli\u015fir.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Maned Wolf",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["solitary yet strong","original path","bridge builder","Andean spirit"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The sacred animal of the Andean and pampas plains of South America, the Maned Wolf is neither truly a wolf nor truly a fox \u2014 it forms its own genus, and this uniqueness makes it spiritually very powerful. In the indigenous shamanic traditions of Brazil and Argentina the Maned Wolf is the sacred keeper who guards boundaries of land and oversees passages \u2014 one must show it respect when crossing from one place to another. In Guaran\xed mythology the Maned Wolf is the herald of the forest spirit and represents the balance between darkness and light. In Andean shamanism its long-legged form is interpreted as bridge-builder: it joins earth to sky, past to future, solitude to community. In the Guaran\xed tradition the Maned Wolf's bark is listened to with reverence as a sacred voice that protects from danger and warns the community. The medicine of the Maned Wolf is to create one's own category and to be original without needing to be compared to anyone else. Its shadow side: holding so tightly to originality that one refuses to join community \u2014 embracing solitude as identity.",dailyMessageEn:"Maned Wolf says this to you today: you are the only member of your own kind \u2014 and this is not a problem, it is a gift. The Maned Wolf cannot bear wolf comparisons; nor fox likenesses. It is only the Maned Wolf. Today, for a moment, set aside the people with whom you have been comparing yourself. Their paths are theirs \u2014 their leaps, their successes, their tempos, their rhythms. Your path is yours and perhaps resembles no one else's \u2014 this does not mean you are lost. To be original is not to be alone; but walking your own line sometimes requires solitary steps. Ask yourself today: Which comparison would I have to release to make more room for myself?",guidanceEn:"Throughout this week, to consciously release comparison with others, practice this: the moment you notice you are comparing yourself with someone, immediately ask: What step did I take today on my own path? Answering this question brings you from outside to inside, from comparison back to your own way. The Maned Wolf grows through a long-term practice."},{id:"a091",name:"Ate\u015f Ku\u015fu",emoji:"\ud83d\udd25",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["arzu ate\u015fi","ilham","pe\u015finden ko\u015fmay\u0131 hak etmek","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Zhar-Ptitsa.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Slav mitolojisinin en b\xfcy\xfcleyici varl\u0131\u011f\u0131 Zhar-Ptitsa \u2014 Ate\u015f Ku\u015fu \u2014 pe\u015finden ko\u015fulmadan durulmas\u0131 imk\xe2ns\u0131z ama yakalanmas\u0131 da neredeyse m\xfcmk\xfcn olmayan kutsal bir arma\u011fand\u0131r; masallarda onu yakalamak kahraman\u0131n hayat\u0131n\u0131 sonsuza dek de\u011fi\u015ftirir. T\xfcrk ve \u0130ran tasavvufundaki Z\xfcmr\xfcd-\xfc Anka ve H\xfcma ku\u015fu, Ate\u015f Ku\u015fu'nun karde\u015f sembolleridir \u2014 her ikisi de ilham\u0131n, d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn ve ula\u015f\u0131lmas\u0131 zor ama vazge\xe7ilmez arzunun simgesidir. Hindu Garuda gelene\u011finde ate\u015f ve \u0131\u015f\u0131k ta\u015f\u0131yan ku\u015f fig\xfcr\xfc, ilahi ilham\u0131n cisimle\u015fmi\u015f halidir \u2014 sanat\xe7\u0131lar\u0131n, \u015fairlerin ve bilgelerin ruh hayvan\u0131d\u0131r. Aztek mitolojisinde Quetzalcoatl \u2014 t\xfcyl\xfc y\u0131lan tanr\u0131s\u0131 \u2014 ate\u015f ve \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131 birle\u015ftirerek yarat\u0131c\u0131 d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn arketipini temsil eder; Ate\u015f Ku\u015fu ile payla\u015f\u0131lan bu ilham motifi evrenseldir. Macar halk masallar\u0131nda T\u0171zmad\xe1r \u2014 Ate\u015f Ku\u015fu \u2014 masal\u0131n kahraman\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131nayan, onu de\u011fi\u015ftiren, bitmez t\xfckenmez bir aray\u0131\u015f\u0131n nesnesidir. Kelt gelene\u011finde ise \u0131\u015f\u0131k ku\u015flar\u0131, druidlerin g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfc kehanet sembolleridir. Ate\u015f Ku\u015fu'nun t\u0131bb\u0131, bast\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131\u015f arzunun serbest b\u0131rak\u0131lmas\u0131 ve ilham\u0131n pe\u015finden gitme cesareti. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: arzunun ate\u015finde yanarak bitmeden ya\u015famamak \u2014 hayallerin prati\u011fi ele ge\xe7irmesi.",dailyMessage:"Ate\u015f Ku\u015fu bug\xfcn i\xe7inde bir \u0131\u015f\u0131k alevlendiriyor \u2014 o uzun s\xfcredir bast\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131n, ger\xe7ek\xe7i de\u011fil dedi\u011fin, utanarak ya da korkarak bir kenara koydu\u011fun arzu. Onu bug\xfcn g\xf6rmezden gelme. Ate\u015f, yakmak i\xe7in de\u011fil \u0131s\u0131tmak i\xe7in vard\u0131r \u2014 ayd\u0131nlatmak, y\xf6nlendirmek, enerji vermek i\xe7in. Bir arzu, seni yanl\u0131\u015f bir yere \xe7ekmiyorsa seni do\u011fru yere ta\u015f\u0131yan bir pusuladan ba\u015fka bir \u015fey de\u011fildir. Bug\xfcn ger\xe7ek\xe7i olal\u0131m sesini bir an i\xe7in k\u0131s ve \u015funu sor: Bu arzum bende neden bu kadar \u0131srar ediyor? Ne anlatmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor? Ate\u015f Ku\u015fu masallar\u0131n\u0131n kahraman\u0131 onu yakalayanlar de\u011fil, pe\u015finden cesaretle ko\u015fanlard\u0131r. Sen bug\xfcn bir ad\u0131m atmaya cesaret edebilir misin?",guidance:"Bir ka\u011f\u0131da E\u011fer ba\u015far\u0131s\u0131z olamayaca\u011f\u0131m\u0131 bilseydim ne yapard\u0131m? sorusunu yan\u0131tlay\u0131n. Cevab\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 okuyun ve ard\u0131ndan bu arzunun i\xe7inde bir hafta, bir ay, bir y\u0131l i\xe7inde at\u0131labilecek k\xfc\xe7\xfcc\xfck bir ad\u0131m belirleyin. Ate\u015f Ku\u015fu'nu yakalamak b\xfcy\xfck bir hamleyle de\u011fil, cesaretle at\u0131lan k\xfc\xe7\xfck ad\u0131mlarla ba\u015flar.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Firebird",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["fire of desire","inspiration","earning the chase","transformation"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The most enchanting being of Slavic mythology, Zhar-Ptitsa \u2014 the Firebird \u2014 is a sacred gift impossible not to pursue but nearly impossible to catch; in folktales, catching it changes the hero's life forever. The Z\xfcmr\xfcd-\xfc Anka and Huma bird of Turkic and Iranian Sufism are sibling symbols of the Firebird \u2014 all of them embodiments of inspiration, transformation, and a desire that is hard to reach yet indispensable. In the Hindu Garuda tradition the figure of the bird that carries fire and light is the embodied form of divine inspiration \u2014 the spirit animal of artists, poets, and sages. In Aztec mythology Quetzalcoatl \u2014 the feathered serpent god \u2014 uniting fire and light, represents the archetype of creative transformation; this motif of inspiration shared with the Firebird is universal. In Hungarian folktales T\u0171zmad\xe1r \u2014 the Firebird \u2014 is the object of an endless quest that tests and transforms the hero. In Celtic tradition birds of light are the prophetic symbols seen by druids. The medicine of the Firebird is the release of suppressed desire and the courage to follow inspiration. Its shadow side: burning in the fire of desire without ever living it to fulfillment \u2014 letting dreams overtake practice.",dailyMessageEn:"Firebird kindles a light within you today \u2014 that desire you have long suppressed, called unrealistic, set aside in shame or fear. Do not ignore it today. Fire exists not to burn but to warm \u2014 to illuminate, to guide, to give energy. A desire, if it is not pulling you toward the wrong place, is nothing other than a compass carrying you toward the right one. Today, for a moment, turn down the voice that says be realistic and ask: Why does this desire insist so strongly in me? What is it trying to tell me? In Firebird tales the hero is not the one who catches it but the one who pursues it with courage. Can you dare to take one step today?",guidanceEn:"On a sheet of paper, answer the question What would I do if I knew I could not fail? Read your answer and then determine within this desire one tiny step that could be taken within a week, a month, a year. Catching the Firebird begins not with a great leap but with small steps taken in courage."},{id:"a092",name:"Deve Ku\u015fu",emoji:"\ud83e\udd9a",element:"toprak",symbolism:["ger\xe7e\u011fe y\xfczle\u015fme","yerden g\xfc\xe7","h\u0131z","pratik g\xfc\xe7"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Ostrich_Struthio_camelus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da deve ku\u015fu t\xfcy\xfc, hakikat tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Maat'\u0131n sembol\xfcyd\xfc \u2014 \xd6l\xfcler Kitab\u0131'nda \xf6len ki\u015finin kalbi bu t\xfcyle tart\u0131l\u0131r, e\u011fer t\xfcyden hafifse cennet kap\u0131s\u0131 a\xe7\u0131l\u0131rd\u0131; bu y\xfczden deve ku\u015fu, ger\xe7ek ve d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfc\u011f\xfcn \xf6l\xe7\xfcs\xfc say\u0131l\u0131r. Afrika \u015faman gelene\u011finde deve ku\u015fu, kendi g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc kendi yolunda kullanan varl\u0131\u011f\u0131n arketipidir \u2014 u\xe7amaz ama karadan kimse ona yeti\u015femez; her varl\u0131\u011f\u0131n kendi \xf6zg\xfcn g\xfcc\xfcn\xfcn oldu\u011funu \xf6\u011fretir. Kuzey Amerika K\u0131z\u0131lderili inan\u0131\u015flar\u0131nda yerde g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olan\u0131n hik\xe2yesi, toprak ruhlar\u0131yla ba\u011flant\u0131y\u0131 simgeler; ka\xe7mak yerine ko\u015fan deve ku\u015fu, yerden g\xfc\xe7 alan sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 ruhun imgesidir. Maori gelene\u011finde Moa \u2014 nesli t\xfckenmi\u015f dev ku\u015f \u2014 ve deve ku\u015fuyla akrabal\u0131\u011f\u0131 bilinen \xf6teki y\xfcr\xfcyen ku\u015flar, yerden g\xfc\xe7 alman\u0131n ve u\xe7mayan ama g\xfc\xe7l\xfc olman\u0131n simgesidir. Zulu gelene\u011finde ise deve ku\u015fu t\xfcyleri ba\u015fl\u0131kta kullan\u0131l\u0131r ve sava\u015f\xe7\u0131n\u0131n h\u0131z\u0131n\u0131, yerden gelen g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc simgeler. Deve ku\u015funun t\u0131bb\u0131, ba\u015fkalar\u0131n\u0131n alan\u0131nda de\u011fil kendi \xf6zg\xfcn alan\u0131nda parlamak ve yerden ald\u0131\u011f\u0131 g\xfc\xe7le hareket etmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: ba\u015fkalar\u0131n\u0131n u\xe7u\u015funa bakarak kendi ko\u015fusunu k\xfc\xe7\xfcmsemek \u2014 kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131rma tuza\u011f\u0131na d\xfc\u015fmek.",dailyMessage:"Deve Ku\u015fu bug\xfcn sana ba\u015fka bir g\xfc\xe7 bi\xe7imi sunuyor. Herkes gibi u\xe7man gerekmiyor; ama kendi alan\u0131nda kimse seninle rekabet edemez. Deve ku\u015fu 70 kilometre h\u0131z yapar, tek tekme ile aslan \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcr, on be\u015f kiloyu sindirir \u2014 kendi boyutunda tart\u0131\u015f\u0131lmaz bir g\xfc\xe7. Sen de bug\xfcn ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131n oyun alan\u0131nda onlarla yar\u0131\u015fmay\u0131 b\u0131rakabilir misin? Bug\xfcn kendi ger\xe7ek g\xfc\xe7 alan\u0131n ne \u2014 d\xfc\u015f\xfcnmeden, k\u0131yaslamadan s\xf6ylesen ne olurdu? Belki empat\u0131n, belki yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n, belki sadakatin, belki sabr\u0131n. Ve bu g\xfcn o g\xfc\xe7 alan\u0131nda k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir ad\u0131m atmak m\xfcmk\xfcn m\xfc? Maat'\u0131n terazisinde \xf6l\xe7\xfclen kalp gibi, bug\xfcn kalbine bak: d\xfcr\xfcst m\xfc oldu\u011funa, ger\xe7e\u011fe mi hizmet etti\u011fine.",guidance:"G\xfc\xe7l\xfc y\xf6nlerinizi fark etmek i\xe7in \u015funu yap\u0131n: g\xfcvendi\u011finiz \xfc\xe7 ki\u015fiye sorun: Bende en \xe7ok ne var? Cevaplar\u0131n\u0131 not al\u0131n. Sonra bu hafta bu g\xfc\xe7lerden birini bilin\xe7li olarak kullan\u0131n. Deve ku\u015fu kendi g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc miras olarak almam\u0131\u015ft\u0131r; her ko\u015fuda yeniden ke\u015ffeder. Sizin g\xfc\xe7leriniz de tan\u0131nd\u0131k\xe7a b\xfcy\xfcr.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Ostrich",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["facing truth","power from the ground","speed","practical strength"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In ancient Egypt the ostrich feather was the symbol of Maat, the goddess of truth \u2014 in the Book of the Dead the heart of the deceased was weighed against this feather, and if the heart was lighter than the feather, the gate of paradise opened; for this reason the ostrich is held as the measure of truth and honesty. In African shamanic tradition the ostrich is the archetype of the being who uses its own power in its own way \u2014 it cannot fly, but on land no one can overtake it; it teaches that every being has its own unique strength. In Native American beliefs of North America the story of the one who is mighty on the ground symbolizes connection with earth spirits; the ostrich, which runs rather than flees, is the image of the warrior spirit drawing strength from the earth. In Maori tradition the Moa \u2014 the extinct giant bird \u2014 and other walking birds known to be kin to the ostrich are symbols of drawing power from the ground and of being flightless yet strong. In Zulu tradition ostrich feathers are used in headdresses, symbolizing the warrior's speed and the power that comes from the earth. The medicine of the ostrich is to shine not in another's domain but in one's own original field, and to move with the strength drawn from the ground. Its shadow side: looking at others' flight and belittling one's own running \u2014 falling into the trap of comparison.",dailyMessageEn:"Ostrich offers you a different form of power today. You do not need to fly like everyone else; but in your own field, no one can rival you. The ostrich runs at 70 kilometers per hour, kills a lion with a single kick, digests fifteen kilos \u2014 an undeniable power in its own dimension. Can you stop today competing with others on their playing field? What is your real field of strength today \u2014 what would it be if you said it without thinking, without comparing? Perhaps your empathy, perhaps your creativity, perhaps your loyalty, perhaps your patience. And is it possible today to take a small step within that field? Like the heart weighed on Maat's scale, look at your heart today: is it being honest, is it serving truth?",guidanceEn:"To recognize your strengths, do this: ask three people you trust, What do you see most in me? Note their answers. Then this week, consciously use one of these strengths. The ostrich did not inherit its strength; it rediscovers it in every run. Your strengths too grow as they are recognized."},{id:"a093",name:"Kilin",emoji:"\ud83e\udd84",element:"ate\u015f",symbolism:["kutsal \u015fans","nadir do\u011fu\u015f","d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfck","ilahi i\u015faret"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Qilin_Ming_Dynasty_painting.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"\xc7in, Japon ve Kore mitolojisinin en kutsal efsanevi varl\u0131\u011f\u0131 olan Kilin, yaln\u0131zca erdemli bir h\xfck\xfcmdar tahtta oldu\u011funda ya da b\xfcy\xfck bir bilgenin do\u011fumunda g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr; Konf\xfc\xe7y\xfcs'\xfcn do\u011fumundan \xf6nce bir Kilin'in belirdi\u011fi s\xf6ylenir. Japonya'da Kirin, hem zarafet hem g\xfc\xe7 hem de saf iyili\u011fin simgesidir \u2014 bu y\xfczden en \xfcnl\xfc Japon bira markas\u0131 bu ismi ta\u015f\u0131r; m\xfckemmellik ve uzun \xf6mr\xfc temsil eder. T\xfcrk ve \u0130slam ezoterizmindeki Buraq \u2014 Peygamber'in mirac\u0131nda kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 kutsal binek \u2014 ile Kilin aras\u0131nda kavramsal bir paralellik kurulur: her ikisi de tanr\u0131sal yolculukta kullan\u0131lan, d\xfcnyalar\u0131 a\u015fan kutsal varl\u0131klard\u0131r. Kore Goryeo gelene\u011finde Kilin, sava\u015f\u0131n bitmesi ve bar\u0131\u015f\u0131n gelmesi \xf6ncesinde g\xf6r\xfclen simgedir; u\u011fruna gelinen bar\u0131\u015f\u0131n habercisi olarak sayg\u0131yla an\u0131l\u0131r. Afrika Bat\u0131 gelene\u011finde z\xfcrafa \u2014 Kilin'in ger\xe7ek hayattaki kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 olarak zaman zaman g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr \u2014 de benzer \u015fekilde iki d\xfcnyay\u0131 bir arada g\xf6ren kutsal varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Kilin'in t\u0131bb\u0131, nadir olan\u0131 fark etmek, s\u0131radan i\xe7indeki erdemin i\u015faretini g\xf6rmek ve kutsal anlar\u0131 onurland\u0131rmakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o kadar nadir ve m\xfckemmel olmay\u0131 beklemek ki hi\xe7bir \u015feyi yeterince kutsal g\xf6rmemek \u2014 ideal beklentisi ger\xe7ek an\u0131n g\xfczelli\u011fini \xf6rtebilir.",dailyMessage:"Kilin bug\xfcn sana nadir bir an ya\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hat\u0131rlatmak i\xe7in geldi. Bu an \u2014 tam bu an \u2014 tekrar etmeyecek. Belki s\u0131radan g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyor: bir kahvenin kokusu, bir bak\u0131\u015f\u0131n s\u0131cakl\u0131\u011f\u0131, bir sessizli\u011fin kalitesi. Ama Kilin yaln\u0131zca b\xfcy\xfck anlarda de\u011fil, erdemin g\xf6r\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfc her yerde belirir \u2014 b\xfcy\xfck jestlerde de\u011fil, k\xfc\xe7\xfck d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfcklerde. Bug\xfcn etraf\u0131nda birinin yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131 k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama ger\xe7ek bir iyilik var m\u0131? Ya da senin yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131n, fark etmeden ge\xe7i\u015ftirdi\u011fin bir erdemin var m\u0131? Kilin seninle ayn\u0131 \u015feyi ar\u0131yor: hakiki, saf, bozulmam\u0131\u015f bir an. Ve o an, her g\xfcn i\xe7inde bir yerde gizlenmi\u015f durumda. Bug\xfcn onu aramaya \xe7\u0131kabilir misin?",guidance:"Bu hafta her g\xfcn ak\u015fam \u015funu not edin: Bug\xfcn kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131m ya da ya\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131m en hakiki, en saf an ne oldu? Bir haftal\u0131k notlar\u0131 okuyun \u2014 b\xfcy\xfck olaylar de\u011fil, k\xfc\xe7\xfck ger\xe7ekler. Kilin prati\u011fi, s\u0131radan olan\u0131n i\xe7indeki nadirli\u011fi g\xf6rme kapasitesini geli\u015ftirmek i\xe7in kullan\u0131lan bir minnet ve fark\u0131ndal\u0131k egzersizidir.",rarity:"legendary",nameEn:"Qilin",elementEn:"fire",symbolismEn:["sacred fortune","rare appearance","honesty","divine sign"],anatolianMeaningEn:"The Qilin, one of the most sacred legendary beings of Chinese, Japanese, and Korean mythology, appears only when a virtuous ruler is on the throne or at the birth of a great sage; it is said that a Qilin appeared before the birth of Confucius. In Japan the Kirin is the symbol of grace, strength, and pure goodness \u2014 for which reason the most famous Japanese beer bears this name; it represents excellence and long life. A conceptual parallel is drawn between the Qilin and the Buraq of Turkic and Islamic esotericism \u2014 the sacred mount used by the Prophet during his ascension: both are sacred beings used in divine journeys, transcending worlds. In the Korean Goryeo tradition the Qilin is the symbol seen before the end of war and the coming of peace; it is honored as the herald of the peace for which one yearns. In West African tradition the giraffe \u2014 sometimes seen as the real-world counterpart of the Qilin \u2014 is similarly a sacred being who sees two worlds at once. The medicine of the Qilin is to notice what is rare, to see the sign of virtue within the ordinary, and to honor sacred moments. Its shadow side: waiting for something so rare and perfect that one finds nothing sacred enough \u2014 the expectation of the ideal can hide the beauty of the present moment.",dailyMessageEn:"Qilin has come today to remind you that you are living a rare moment. This moment \u2014 exactly this moment \u2014 will not repeat. It may look ordinary: the scent of a coffee, the warmth of a glance, the quality of a silence. But Qilin appears not only in great moments but wherever virtue shows itself \u2014 not in grand gestures, but in small honesties. Is there a small but real kindness around you today that someone has done? Or a virtue of your own that you have brushed past without noticing? The Qilin is seeking the same thing you are: an authentic, pure, unspoiled moment. And that moment is hidden somewhere within every day. Can you go out to find it today?",guidanceEn:"Each evening this week note: What was the most authentic, most pure moment I encountered or lived today? Read through a week's notes \u2014 not great events, but small truths. The Qilin practice is a gratitude and awareness exercise used to develop the capacity to see rarity within the ordinary."},{id:"a094",name:"Su Ayg\u0131r\u0131",emoji:"\ud83e\udd9b",element:"su",symbolism:["do\u011fum g\xfcc\xfc","di\u015fil g\xfc\xe7","sular koruyucusu","ana\xe7 cesaret"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Hippopotamus_in_Botswana.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Eski M\u0131s\u0131r'da hamile kad\u0131nlar\u0131n ve do\u011fumun kutsal koruyucusu Taweret, su ayg\u0131r\u0131 ba\u015fl\u0131 bir tanr\u0131\xe7ayd\u0131 \u2014 do\u011fum sanc\u0131lar\u0131nda kad\u0131nlar\u0131n yan\u0131nda olan, k\xf6t\xfcl\xfc\u011f\xfc uzakla\u015ft\u0131ran ve yeni hayat\u0131 koruma alt\u0131na alan kutsal di\u015fi g\xfc\xe7. Nil'in sahibi olarak an\u0131lan su ayg\u0131r\u0131, hayat veren suyu ve tehlikeyi bir arada ta\u015f\u0131r \u2014 bereketin ve tehlikenin ayn\u0131 bedende birle\u015fimi, do\u011fan\u0131n en d\xfcr\xfcst imgesidir. Afrika Zulu ve Xhosa gelene\u011finde su ayg\u0131r\u0131, nehirlerin ve g\xf6llerin koruyucu ruhudur \u2014 suyun i\xe7ine giren ve \xe7\u0131kan, iki d\xfcnyan\u0131n sahibi olan g\xfc\xe7l\xfc ata varl\u0131k. Bat\u0131 Afrika Yoruba gelene\u011finde ise su ayg\u0131r\u0131 Olokun \u2014 derin denizin tanr\u0131s\u0131 \u2014 ile ili\u015fkilendirilir; derin sular hem bilinmeyeni hem de kozmik di\u015fil g\xfcc\xfc simgeler. Kelt gelene\u011finde each uisce \u2014 su at\u0131 \u2014 efsanesinde b\xfcy\xfck su varl\u0131klar\u0131 hem tehlikeli hem de kutsal addedilir; ana\xe7 ve koruyucu g\xfc\xe7 olarak sayg\u0131yla an\u0131l\u0131r. Su ayg\u0131r\u0131n\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, koruyucu g\xfcc\xfc \u2014 hem sevgiyle besleyici hem de gerekti\u011finde sert \u2014 tam anlam\u0131yla kullanmakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: koruyuculu\u011fun kontrole d\xf6n\xfc\u015fmesi \u2014 sevenin s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131 i\xe7inde hapsetmesi.",dailyMessage:"Su Ayg\u0131r\u0131 bug\xfcn sende derin bir g\xfcc\xfc uyand\u0131r\u0131yor: ana\xe7 cesaret. Bu g\xfc\xe7 cinsiyetle de\u011fil, se\xe7imle ilgilidir \u2014 ister kad\u0131n ister erkek ol, bu se\xe7imi yapabilirsin. Su ayg\u0131r\u0131 d\xfcnyan\u0131n en tehlikeli b\xfcy\xfck memelilerinden biri olarak bilinir, ama bu tehlike sald\u0131rganl\u0131ktan de\u011fil, korumadan gelir \u2014 yavrusunu tehdit alt\u0131nda hissederse ne yapaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 bilir. Bug\xfcn kimi ya da neyi korumak istiyorsun? Bir ili\u015fki, bir de\u011fer, bir insan, bir yarat\u0131c\u0131 proje \u2014 neyin s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131na tecav\xfcz edildi ve sen hen\xfcz harekete ge\xe7medin? Besleyici g\xfc\xe7 ile koruyucu g\xfc\xe7 ayn\u0131 kaynaktan gelir: derin sevgi. Ama sevginin sesi bazen yumu\u015fak, bazen sert olur. Bug\xfcn sesin hangisi olmay\u0131 gerektiriyor?",guidance:"Koruman\u0131z gereken ama hen\xfcz koruyamad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z bir \u015fey varsa, bug\xfcn k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama somut bir s\u0131n\u0131r belirleyin: Bu konuda \u015fundan sonra \u015f\xf6yle davranaca\u011f\u0131m. Bunu yaz\u0131n. S\u0131n\u0131r belirlemek sevgisizlik de\u011fil, sevginin en derin bi\xe7imidir \u2014 su ayg\u0131r\u0131 s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 bilir, bu y\xfczden i\xe7indekiler g\xfcvende olur.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Hippopotamus",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["the power of birth","feminine strength","guardian of waters","maternal courage"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In ancient Egypt Taweret, the sacred protector of pregnant women and of birth, was a hippopotamus-headed goddess \u2014 the sacred feminine power who stood beside women in their birth pangs, drove away evil, and placed new life under protection. Known as the master of the Nile, the hippopotamus carries both the life-giving water and danger together \u2014 the union of abundance and danger in the same body is one of nature's most honest images. In the African Zulu and Xhosa traditions the hippopotamus is the protective spirit of rivers and lakes \u2014 a powerful ancestral being who enters and leaves the water, master of two worlds. In the West African Yoruba tradition the hippopotamus is associated with Olokun \u2014 god of the deep sea; deep waters symbolize both the unknown and cosmic feminine power. In Celtic tradition the legend of the each uisce \u2014 water horse \u2014 holds large water beings as both dangerous and sacred; they are honored as maternal and protective powers. The medicine of the hippopotamus is to use protective power \u2014 both lovingly nourishing and, when necessary, firm \u2014 in its fullness. Its shadow side: guardianship turning into control \u2014 the lover imprisoning within their own boundaries.",dailyMessageEn:"Hippopotamus awakens a deep power within you today: maternal courage. This power has to do not with gender but with choice \u2014 whether woman or man, you can make this choice. The hippopotamus is known as one of the most dangerous large mammals in the world, but this danger comes not from aggression but from protection \u2014 when it feels its young threatened, it knows what to do. Whom or what do you wish to protect today? A relationship, a value, a person, a creative project \u2014 whose boundary has been violated while you have not yet acted? Nourishing power and protective power come from the same source: deep love. But the voice of love is sometimes soft, sometimes firm. Which does your voice need to be today?",guidanceEn:"If there is something you must protect but have not yet been able to, set today a small but tangible boundary: From now on in this matter I will behave like this. Write it down. Setting boundaries is not lovelessness; it is the deepest form of love \u2014 the hippopotamus knows its boundary, and that is why those within it are safe."},{id:"a095",name:"Anakonda",emoji:"\ud83d\udc0d",element:"su",symbolism:["kozmik y\u0131lan","su bilgeli\u011fi","d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm","Orta D\xfcnya"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Eunectes_murinus_2.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Amazonia ve And \u015famanizminin en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc ruh hayvanlar\u0131ndan anakonda, b\xfcy\xfck nehirlerin \u2014 Amazonas, Orinoko \u2014 kozmik ruhunun cisimle\u015fmi\u015f halidir; Guaran\xed ve Tup\xed gelene\u011finde Sucuriju Gigante olarak an\u0131lan dev su y\u0131lan\u0131, d\xfcnyan\u0131n d\xfczenini koruyan kozmik varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Amazon yerlileri i\xe7in anakonda salt bir hayvan de\u011fil, suyun ve ya\u015fam\u0131n ilk atas\u0131, Orta D\xfcnya'n\u0131n hakimidir \u2014 nehirlerin yata\u011f\u0131n\u0131 onun devasa g\xf6vdesi olu\u015fturmu\u015ftur. Azteklerin t\xfcyl\xfc y\u0131lan\u0131 Quetzalcoatl ile anakondan\u0131n su y\u0131lan\u0131 arketipi aras\u0131nda derin bir paralel vard\u0131r: her ikisi de d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc, yeniden do\u011fu\u015fu ve yarat\u0131c\u0131 kozmik g\xfcc\xfc simgeler. Hint mitolojisindeki Naga \u2014 kutsal y\u0131lan tanr\u0131s\u0131 \u2014 ve anakonda aras\u0131nda da kavramsal ba\u011flar kurulabilir; her ikisi de suyun, bilgeli\u011fin ve d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfcn koruyucusudur. Afrika Voodoo gelene\u011finde Damballah Wedo \u2014 g\xf6kku\u015fa\u011f\u0131 y\u0131lan\u0131 \u2014 anakondayla \xf6zde\u015fle\u015fen kozmik y\u0131lan tanr\u0131s\u0131d\u0131r; hayat\u0131n d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc ve sonsuz d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc y\xf6netir. Anakondal\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, yava\u015f ama derin ve kararl\u0131 bir d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm g\xfcc\xfcd\xfcr. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: o kadar sarmak ki nefes ald\u0131rmamak \u2014 d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc zorlamak.",dailyMessage:"Anakonda bug\xfcn sana yava\u015f ama ka\xe7\u0131n\u0131lmaz bir ger\xe7e\u011fi hat\u0131rlat\u0131yor: d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm bazen bask\u0131 alt\u0131nda ger\xe7ekle\u015fir. Bu ac\u0131 verici olabilir \u2014 ama anakondan\u0131n sarmas\u0131 k\u0131rmaz, d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcr. Hayat\u0131nda \u015fu an s\u0131k\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131\u015f gibi hissetti\u011fin bir yer var m\u0131? Bir ili\u015fki, bir durum, bir s\xfcre\xe7 seni zorluyor, k\xf6\u015feye s\u0131k\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131yor gibi g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyor? Anakonda'n\u0131n mesaj\u0131: bask\u0131 bir son de\u011fil, bir ba\u015flang\u0131c\u0131n ko\u015fuludur. Eski h\xfccre y\u0131rt\u0131lmadan yeni h\xfccre olu\u015famaz. Bug\xfcn direndi\u011fin \u015fey, belki tam anlam\u0131yla kucaklanmay\u0131 bekliyor. Sarmak ile bo\u011fulmak aras\u0131ndaki fark \u015fudur: birinde nefes kesilir, di\u011ferinde yenilenir. Bug\xfcn neye direniyor, neye teslim olabilirsin?",guidance:"Kendinizi direniyor oldu\u011funuz bir durumu se\xe7in ve be\u015f dakika boyunca \u015funu yaz\u0131n: Bu durum bana ne \xf6\u011fretmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor? Bu bask\u0131n\u0131n i\xe7inde ne d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcyor? Yazmay\u0131 bitirdi\u011finizde geri okuyun \u2014 anakonda gibi, i\xe7inizdeki d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc ad\u0131yla \xe7a\u011f\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131zda o s\xfcre\xe7 h\u0131zlan\u0131r ve g\xfc\xe7 kazan\u0131r.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Anaconda",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["cosmic serpent","water wisdom","transformation","the Middle World"],anatolianMeaningEn:"One of the most powerful spirit animals of Amazonian and Andean shamanism, the anaconda is the embodied form of the cosmic spirit of the great rivers \u2014 the Amazonas, the Orinoco; in Guaran\xed and Tup\xed tradition it is honored as Sucuriju Gigante, the giant water serpent, a cosmic being who preserves the order of the world. For Amazonian indigenous peoples the anaconda is not merely an animal but the first ancestor of water and life, the ruler of the Middle World \u2014 the beds of the rivers were formed by its enormous body. There is a deep parallel between the Aztec feathered serpent Quetzalcoatl and the water-serpent archetype of the anaconda: both symbolize transformation, rebirth, and creative cosmic power. Conceptual links can also be drawn between the Hindu Naga \u2014 the sacred serpent god \u2014 and the anaconda; both are guardians of water, wisdom, and transformation. In the African Vodou tradition Damballah Wedo \u2014 the rainbow serpent \u2014 is identified with the anaconda as the cosmic serpent god; he governs the cycle of life and endless transformation. The medicine of the anaconda is a slow yet deep and resolute power of transformation. Its shadow side: coiling so tightly that no breath is allowed \u2014 forcing transformation.",dailyMessageEn:"Anaconda reminds you today of a slow but inevitable truth: transformation sometimes takes place under pressure. This can be painful \u2014 but the anaconda's coil does not break, it transforms. Is there a place in your life right now where you feel constricted? Is a relationship, a situation, a process pressing you, seeming to back you into a corner? The anaconda's message: pressure is not an end but the condition of a beginning. The new cell cannot form without the old cell tearing. What you are resisting today may be waiting to be fully embraced. The difference between being held and being smothered is this: in one, breath stops; in the other, breath is renewed. What are you resisting, and what can you surrender to today?",guidanceEn:"Choose a situation you are resisting and write for five minutes: What is this situation trying to teach me? What is transforming within this pressure? When you have finished writing, read it back \u2014 like the anaconda, when you call the transformation within you by its name, the process gains speed and strength."},{id:"a096",name:"Tukan",emoji:"\ud83e\udd9c",element:"hava",symbolism:["renklilik","yarat\u0131c\u0131 ileti\u015fim","tropik bilgelik","bereket"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Ramphastos_toco_-Brazil-8.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Orta ve G\xfcney Amerika'n\u0131n tropikal ormanlar\u0131nda ya\u015fayan tukan, Amazonia \u015faman gelene\u011finde orman\u0131n renk b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcs\xfc olarak an\u0131l\u0131r \u2014 gagas\u0131n\u0131n b\xfcy\xfckl\xfc\u011f\xfc ve renklerinin ihti\u015fam\u0131, hayat\u0131n bollu\u011funu ve kutlanmas\u0131n\u0131 simgeler. Guaran\xed \u015famanizmine g\xf6re tukan, orman\u0131n sesini ta\u015f\u0131r \u2014 gagas\u0131ndan \xe7\u0131kan sesler ruhlar\u0131n dilindedir ve \u015faman ayinlerinde tukan \xe7a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131 yap\u0131l\u0131r. Azteklerin Xochipilli \u2014 \xe7i\xe7ek ve m\xfczik tanr\u0131s\u0131 \u2014 k\xfclt\xfcnde renkli ku\u015flar hayat\u0131n kutlamas\u0131n\u0131 simgeler ve tukan t\xfcyleri Aztek ba\u015f s\xfcslerinde kutsal bir unsur olarak kullan\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. Karayip ve Amazonia yerli gelene\u011finde tukan t\xfcyleri hem sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131n hem \u015famanlar\u0131n kutsal s\xfcs\xfcd\xfcr \u2014 renk, g\xfc\xe7 ve ileti\u015fimi bir arada ta\u015f\u0131yan varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Kuzeybat\u0131 Amazonia Tukano halk\u0131 \u2014 ad\u0131n\u0131 bu ku\u015ftan al\u0131r \u2014 tukana \xf6zel bir ruhsal \xf6nem atfeder; klan totemlerinde ve orman rit\xfcellerinde merkezi bir yer tutar. Afrika kabile s\xfcs gelene\u011finde parlak renkler, toplulu\u011fun kimli\u011fini ve g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc d\u0131\u015fa vurman\u0131n kutsal bir yoludur. Tukan\u0131n t\u0131bb\u0131, hayat\u0131 renkleriyle kutlamak ve ileti\u015fimin g\xfczelli\u011fini yarat\u0131c\u0131 bir ifade bi\xe7imi olarak kullanmakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: d\u0131\u015far\u0131dan g\xf6steri\u015fli olmak ama i\xe7ten bo\u015f olmak \u2014 rengin derinli\u011fi yoksa sadece g\xfcr\xfclt\xfcd\xfcr.",dailyMessage:"Tukan bug\xfcn sana hayat\u0131n\u0131 biraz daha renkli ve dolu ya\u015famaya davet ediyor. Bu basit bir kendini iyi hissettir \xe7a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131 de\u011fil; tukan renksiz ya\u015fayamaz \u2014 renkler onun dilidir, varl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n par\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r. Sen de bug\xfcn kendi renklerini ne kadar kullan\u0131yorsun? Yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n, mizah\u0131n, ne\u015fen, merak\u0131n \u2014 bunlar senden ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131n i\xe7in de\u011fil, senin ger\xe7ek do\u011fan\u0131n sesleridir. Belki uzun s\xfcredir ciddi olmak, verimli olmak, makul olmak ad\u0131na bu renkleri bast\u0131rd\u0131n. Tukan gagas\u0131n\u0131n b\xfcy\xfckl\xfc\u011f\xfc onu zorlamaz \u2014 o oldu\u011fu \u015feyin en b\xfcy\xfck versiyonu olarak ta\u015f\u0131r onu. Bug\xfcn kendinizin en b\xfcy\xfck ve en renkli versiyonu i\xe7in ne yapabilirsiniz?",guidance:"Bug\xfcn s\u0131radan bir \u015feyi biraz daha g\xfczel yap\u0131n: yedi\u011finiz bir \u015feyi bir k\xe2seye koyun, masa \xf6rt\xfcs\xfc serin, bir \u015fark\u0131 s\xf6yleyin, bir renk ekleyin ortam\u0131n\u0131za. K\xfc\xe7\xfck ama ger\xe7ek. Tukan rituali budur: hayat\u0131 her g\xfcn k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir g\xfczellikle kutlamak \u2014 bu birikerek b\xfcy\xfcr ve i\xe7sel ne\u015feyi besler.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Toucan",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["vibrant color","creative communication","tropical wisdom","abundance"],anatolianMeaningEn:"Living in the tropical forests of Central and South America, the toucan is honored in the Amazonian shamanic tradition as the color-sorcerer of the forest \u2014 the great size of its beak and the splendor of its colors symbolize the abundance and celebration of life. According to Guaran\xed shamanism the toucan carries the voice of the forest \u2014 the sounds from its beak are in the language of spirits, and during shamanic rituals the toucan's call is invoked. In the Aztec cult of Xochipilli \u2014 god of flowers and music \u2014 colorful birds symbolize the celebration of life, and toucan feathers were used as a sacred element in Aztec headdresses. In the Caribbean and Amazonian indigenous traditions toucan feathers are the sacred adornment of both warriors and shamans \u2014 a being that carries color, strength, and communication together. The Tukano people of the northwest Amazon \u2014 who take their name from this bird \u2014 attribute special spiritual importance to the toucan; it holds a central place in clan totems and forest rituals. In African tribal adornment tradition bright colors are a sacred way of expressing the identity and strength of a community. The medicine of the toucan is to celebrate life with its colors and to use the beauty of communication as a creative form of expression. Its shadow side: appearing showy on the outside while being empty within \u2014 if color has no depth, it is only noise.",dailyMessageEn:"Toucan invites you today to live your life a little more colorfully and fully. This is not a simple feel good summons; the toucan cannot live without color \u2014 colors are its language, part of its being. How much do you use your own colors today? Your creativity, your humor, your joy, your curiosity \u2014 these are not voices for anyone else but for the voice of your true nature. Perhaps for a long time, in the name of being serious, being productive, being reasonable, you have suppressed these colors. The toucan's great beak does not burden it \u2014 it carries it as the largest version of what it is. What can you do today for the largest and most colorful version of yourself?",guidanceEn:"Today, make something ordinary a little more beautiful: serve something you are eating on a nice plate, lay a cloth on the table, sing a song, add a color to your environment. Small but real. This is the toucan ritual: celebrating life each day with a small beauty \u2014 it accumulates, grows, and feeds inner joy."},{id:"a097",name:"Dingo",emoji:"\ud83d\udc15",element:"toprak",symbolism:["yabani \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck","saf i\xe7g\xfcd\xfc","ehlile\u015fmemi\u015f ruh","sadakat"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Dingo_Noosa.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Avustralya Aborijin R\xfcya Zaman\u0131 gelene\u011finde dingo, insan ile vah\u015fi do\u011fa aras\u0131ndaki k\xf6pr\xfcd\xfcr \u2014 evcille\u015ftirilmi\u015f ama tam anlam\u0131yla evcil olmayan, vah\u015fi ama yaln\u0131z da olmayan bu varl\u0131k, iki d\xfcnya aras\u0131ndaki s\u0131n\u0131rda ya\u015far. R\xfcya Zaman\u0131 anlat\u0131lar\u0131nda dingo, insanlara yolu g\xf6steren, s\xfcr\xfcy\xfc koruyan ve saf i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcyle hareket eden kutsal yolda\u015ft\u0131r \u2014 ne kaybeder ne de kaybettirir. Kelt gelene\u011findeki hound \u2014 kutsal k\xf6pek arketipi \u2014 ile dingo aras\u0131nda paralel bir ba\u011f kurulabilir: her ikisi de sadakati ve saf i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcy\xfc temsil eden, ama hi\xe7bir zaman tam anlam\u0131yla ehlile\u015ftirilemeyen g\xfc\xe7l\xfc ruhu simgeler. Japonya Shinto gelene\u011finde ormanlarda ya\u015fayan k\xf6pek benzeri tanr\u0131 fig\xfcrleri, do\u011fan\u0131n ruhuna yak\u0131n olan ve insanlara yol g\xf6steren kutsal hayvan imgelerini temsil eder. Mayan k\xf6pek tanr\u0131s\u0131 ve And \u015famanl\u0131\u011f\u0131ndaki kutsal k\xf6pek fig\xfcrleri de dingoyla evrensel anlat\u0131da bulu\u015fur: saf i\xe7g\xfcd\xfc, bilinmeyende yol g\xf6sterme. Dingonun t\u0131bb\u0131, t\xfcm sosyal kalabal\u0131ktan s\u0131yr\u0131larak en ham, en saf, en ger\xe7ek iste\u011fi duymakt\u0131r. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: vah\u015fili\u011fi \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfck sanarak sorumluluktan ka\xe7mak \u2014 s\xfcr\xfcden ayr\u0131lmak ile kendinden kopman\u0131n fark\u0131n\u0131 yitirmek.",dailyMessage:"Dingo bug\xfcn seni en ger\xe7ek i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcne davet ediyor \u2014 o sosyal beklentilerin, kurallar\u0131n, yap\u0131lmas\u0131 gerekenler listesinin d\u0131\u015f\u0131nda kalan ham sese. Dingo ne y\xfczde y\xfcz evcil ne y\xfczde y\xfcz vah\u015fidir \u2014 o bu ikisi aras\u0131nda dengeyi bilin\xe7sizce, sezgisel olarak korur. Sen de bug\xfcn bir an i\xe7in sosyal filtreyi kald\u0131r: ger\xe7ekten ne istiyorsun, ger\xe7ekten ne hissediyorsun? O ilk cevap, en yarg\u0131s\u0131z an \u2014 onu dinle. Belki o ses seni \u015fa\u015f\u0131rt\u0131r, belki rahats\u0131z eder. Ama o ses senin en ger\xe7ek par\xe7andan geliyor. Dingo izlerini takip eder \u2014 nereden geldi\u011fini bilir. Bug\xfcn kendi izlerini takip edebilir misin?",guidance:"Bug\xfcn on dakika tamamen yaln\u0131z kal\u0131n \u2014 telefonsuz, beklentisiz. Ve kendinize sorun: \u015eu an ger\xe7ekten ne istiyorum? \u0130lk cevab\u0131 not al\u0131n, onu mant\u0131kla de\u011ferlendirmeyin. Dingo prati\u011fi, i\xe7g\xfcd\xfcye kulak vermenin en saf bi\xe7imidir; bu soruyu d\xfczenli sormak, otantik ya\u015fam\u0131n temelini olu\u015fturur.",rarity:"common",nameEn:"Dingo",elementEn:"earth",symbolismEn:["wild freedom","pure instinct","untamed spirit","loyalty"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In the Australian Aboriginal Dreamtime tradition the dingo is the bridge between humanity and wild nature \u2014 domesticated yet not fully tame, wild yet not solitary, this being lives on the boundary between two worlds. In Dreamtime narratives the dingo is the sacred companion who shows people the way, guards the flock, and moves by pure instinct \u2014 neither lost nor causing loss. A parallel connection can be drawn between the Celtic hound \u2014 the sacred dog archetype \u2014 and the dingo: both symbolize loyalty and pure instinct, the powerful spirit that can never be fully domesticated. In the Japanese Shinto tradition the dog-like deity figures who dwell in the forests represent sacred animal images that are close to nature's spirit and show humans the way. The Mayan dog god and the sacred dog figures of Andean shamanism also meet the dingo in a universal narrative: pure instinct, guidance through the unknown. The medicine of the dingo is, sloughing off all the social crowd, to hear the rawest, purest, most genuine longing. Its shadow side: mistaking wildness for freedom and escaping responsibility \u2014 losing the distinction between leaving the pack and breaking off from oneself.",dailyMessageEn:"Dingo invites you today to your truest instinct \u2014 that raw voice that remains outside the social expectations, the rules, the list of shoulds. The dingo is neither a hundred percent tame nor a hundred percent wild \u2014 it preserves the balance between the two unconsciously, intuitively. Today, for a moment, lift the social filter: what do you really want, what do you really feel? That first answer, the most non-judgmental moment \u2014 listen to it. Perhaps that voice surprises you, perhaps it discomforts you. But that voice comes from your most genuine part. The dingo follows its tracks \u2014 it knows where it came from. Can you follow your own tracks today?",guidanceEn:"Spend ten minutes today completely alone \u2014 no phone, no expectations. And ask yourself: What do I truly want right now? Note the first answer without judging it with logic. The dingo practice is the purest form of listening to instinct; asking this question regularly forms the foundation of an authentic life."},{id:"a098",name:"Platipus",emoji:"\ud83e\udd86",element:"su",symbolism:["\xe7ift do\u011fa","benzersizlik","s\u0131n\u0131fland\u0131r\u0131lamaz g\xfczellik","merak"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Platypus.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Avustralya Aborijin R\xfcya Zaman\u0131'nda platipus, farkl\u0131 d\xfcnyalar\u0131n s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131nda ya\u015fayan kutsal varl\u0131kt\u0131r \u2014 hem karada hem suda, hem memeli hem yumurtlayan, hem zehirli hem zarars\u0131z \u2014 t\xfcm bu \xe7eli\u015fkiler bir arada. Bu nedenle platipus, ikili ger\xe7e\u011fin ve s\u0131n\u0131r a\u015fman\u0131n sembol\xfcd\xfcr. R\xfcya Zaman\u0131'n\u0131n yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f anlat\u0131lar\u0131ndan birinde platipus, \xf6rdek ile su s\u0131\xe7an\u0131n\u0131n birle\u015fiminden do\u011far \u2014 iki farkl\u0131 d\xfcnyan\u0131n bar\u0131\u015fma an\u0131 olarak kutlan\u0131r. \xc7in Taoizm'inde Yin-Yang sembol\xfc gibi platipus da z\u0131tlar\u0131n bir arada var olu\u015funu ve bu \xe7eli\u015fkili birle\u015fimin b\xfct\xfcnl\xfck yaratt\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011fretir. Hint felsefi gelene\u011finde Advaita \u2014 ikili\u011fin \xf6tesi \u2014 kavram\u0131yla platipus'un ikili do\u011fas\u0131 paralel d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfclebilir: g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcrde iki \u015fey, \xf6z\xfcnde bir. Japon Zen gelene\u011finde mu \u2014 s\u0131n\u0131fland\u0131r\u0131lamaz olan, ne evet ne hay\u0131r \u2014 kavram\u0131 platipus'un evrensel anlat\u0131s\u0131yla bulu\u015fur; tan\u0131m\u0131n d\u0131\u015f\u0131nda kalan varl\u0131k, tan\u0131m\u0131n kendisini sorgulatan varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Celtic \u015faman gelene\u011finde ise bi\xe7im de\u011fi\u015ftiren shapeshifter arketipi, platipus'un \xe7ok kimlikli yap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 yans\u0131t\u0131r. Platipusun t\u0131bb\u0131, tan\u0131mlanmay\u0131 reddetmek ve kendi \xe7eli\u015fkili g\xfczelli\u011fini b\xfct\xfcnl\xfck olarak kabul etmektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: her yere biraz ait olmak ama hi\xe7bir yere tam olarak ait olamamak \u2014 k\xf6ks\xfczl\xfck hissi.",dailyMessage:"Platipus bug\xfcn sana \xe7ok \xf6nemli bir \u015feyi s\xf6yl\xfcyor: kendini bir kategoriye, bir etikete, bir kal\u0131ba sokmak zorunda de\u011filsin. Bilim insanlar\u0131 platipusu ilk g\xf6rd\xfcklerinde sahte sand\u0131lar \u2014 b\xf6yle bir \u015fey olamazd\u0131. Ama o vard\u0131. Hem memeli hem yumurtlayan, hem ku\u015f gagal\u0131 hem memeli v\xfccutlu. Ve var olmaya devam etti, s\u0131n\u0131fland\u0131rma bitmeden. Sen de belki hem-hemsin: hem introvert hem ekstrover, hem hassas hem g\xfc\xe7l\xfc, hem geleneksel hem \xf6zg\xfcr. Bunlar \xe7eli\u015fki de\u011fil, senin b\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfcn. Bug\xfcn kendine hangi etiketi zorla yap\u0131\u015ft\u0131rmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yorsun? Ve o etiketi bir anl\u0131\u011f\u0131na b\u0131rak\u0131p sadece var olmaya izin verseydin ne olurdu?",guidance:"Kendinizi tan\u0131mlamak i\xe7in kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z \xfc\xe7 etiketi yaz\u0131n. Sonra her birinin yan\u0131na \u015funu sorun: Bu etiket beni tam m\u0131 tan\u0131ml\u0131yor, yoksa sadece bir par\xe7am\u0131 m\u0131? Platipus egzersizi, kimlik kat\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 gev\u015fetmek ve daha geni\u015f bir \xf6z-kabule yer a\xe7mak i\xe7in kullan\u0131lan g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir \xf6z-sorgulama prati\u011fidir.",rarity:"rare",nameEn:"Platypus",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["dual nature","uniqueness","unclassifiable beauty","curiosity"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Australian Aboriginal Dreamtime the platypus is the sacred being who lives on the boundary of different worlds \u2014 both on land and in water, both mammal and egg-laying, both venomous and harmless \u2014 all these contradictions held together. For this reason the platypus is the symbol of dual reality and boundary-crossing. In one Dreamtime creation narrative the platypus is born of the union of duck and water rat \u2014 celebrated as the moment of reconciliation between two different worlds. Like the Yin-Yang symbol of Chinese Taoism, the platypus teaches the coexistence of opposites and that this contradictory union creates wholeness. In the Hindu philosophical tradition the concept of Advaita \u2014 beyond duality \u2014 can be considered in parallel with the platypus's dual nature: two things in appearance, one in essence. In the Japanese Zen tradition the concept of mu \u2014 that which cannot be classified, neither yes nor no \u2014 meets the universal narrative of the platypus; the being that lies outside definition is the being that calls definition itself into question. In Celtic shamanic tradition the shapeshifter archetype mirrors the multi-identified structure of the platypus. The medicine of the platypus is to refuse to be defined and to accept one's own contradictory beauty as wholeness. Its shadow side: belonging a little to every place but never fully to any \u2014 a feeling of rootlessness.",dailyMessageEn:"Platypus is telling you something very important today: you do not need to fit yourself into a category, a label, a mold. When scientists first saw the platypus, they thought it was a hoax \u2014 such a thing could not exist. But it existed. Both mammal and egg-laying, with the bill of a bird and the body of a mammal. And it kept on existing, while classification was still pending. Perhaps you too are both: both introvert and extrovert, both sensitive and strong, both traditional and free. These are not contradictions but your wholeness. Which label are you forcing on yourself today? And what if, for a moment, you released that label and gave yourself permission simply to be?",guidanceEn:"Write three labels you use to define yourself. Then beside each ask: Does this label fully define me, or only a part of me? The platypus exercise is a powerful self-inquiry practice used to loosen identity rigidity and open space for a wider self-acceptance."},{id:"a099",name:"Dalg\u0131\xe7 Ku\u015fu",emoji:"\ud83d\udc26",element:"su",symbolism:["r\xfcya","bilin\xe7alt\u0131 sesi","i\xe7sel \xe7\u0131\u011fl\u0131k","derinlik"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/Common_loon.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"Sibirya \u015famanizminde dalg\u0131\xe7 ku\u015funun tuhaf ve yank\u0131lanan \xe7\u0131\u011fl\u0131\u011f\u0131, \xf6teki d\xfcnyan\u0131n sesinin bu d\xfcnyaya s\u0131zmas\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 \u015famanlar transa ge\xe7erken dalg\u0131\xe7 \xe7\u0131\u011fl\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 taklit eder ve bu ses iki d\xfcnya aras\u0131ndaki kap\u0131y\u0131 aralar. Kuzey Amerika B\xfcy\xfck G\xf6ller halklar\u0131ndan Ojibwe ve Cree gelene\u011finde dalg\u0131\xe7 ku\u015fu, r\xfcyalar\u0131n ve bilin\xe7alt\u0131n\u0131n kutsal habercisidir \u2014 onun sesini geceleri duymak, ata ruhlar\u0131ndan bir mesaj almak anlam\u0131na gelir. \u0130skandinav folklorunda ve \xf6zellikle Finlandiya-Karelya \u015fiir gelene\u011finde dalg\u0131\xe7 ku\u015fu, Kalevala destan\u0131yla ba\u011flant\u0131l\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n ba\u015flang\u0131c\u0131nda suya dalan kutsal ku\u015f, yumurtas\u0131ndan d\xfcnyay\u0131 yaratan b\xfcy\xfck varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Kuzey Avrupa Sami gelene\u011finde dalg\u0131\xe7 ku\u015fu, gece d\xfcnyas\u0131 ile g\xfcnd\xfcz d\xfcnyas\u0131 aras\u0131nda gidip gelen ruh rehberidir \u2014 karanl\u0131k sulardan \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011fa \xe7\u0131kar ve bu yolculu\u011fu bilen yold\u0131r. \u0130nuit gelene\u011finde dalg\u0131\xe7 ku\u015fu, denizin ve kar\u0131n aras\u0131nda k\xf6pr\xfc kuran, so\u011fu\u011fun ruhunu ta\u015f\u0131yan kutsal varl\u0131kt\u0131r. Dalg\u0131\xe7 ku\u015funun t\u0131bb\u0131, bilin\xe7alt\u0131ndan gelen mesajlara kulak vermek ve i\xe7 sesin duyulmas\u0131na izin vermektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: bilin\xe7alt\u0131n\u0131n derinliklerine o kadar dalmak ki y\xfczeye \xe7\u0131kmak istemez hale gelmek.",dailyMessage:"Dalg\u0131\xe7 Ku\u015fu bug\xfcn seni i\xe7indeki en derin ve en tuhaf sese do\u011fru y\xf6nlendiriyor. Bu ses bazen r\xfcyalarda gelir, bazen ani bir his olarak, bazen mant\u0131kla a\xe7\u0131klanamayan bir bilme an\u0131nda. Onu bast\u0131r\u0131yor musun? Dalg\u0131\xe7 ku\u015fu suyun alt\u0131nda ve \xfcst\xfcnde e\u015fit derecede ustal\u0131kla hareket eder \u2014 bilin\xe7 ile bilin\xe7alt\u0131 aras\u0131nda bir \xe7eli\u015fki g\xf6rmez. Sen de bug\xfcn akl\u0131n\u0131n mant\u0131kl\u0131 de\u011fil dedi\u011fi ama i\xe7inin ama do\u011fru dedi\u011fi bir \u015fey var m\u0131? R\xfcyan, bir tak\u0131nt\u0131n, s\xfcrekli d\xf6nen bir d\xfc\u015f\xfcnce \u2014 bunlar bilin\xe7alt\u0131n\u0131n sesi olabilir, duyulmak isteyebilir. Onun tuhaf, g\xfczel \xe7\u0131\u011fl\u0131\u011f\u0131 gibi, i\xe7indeki ses de bu d\xfcnyaya \xe7\u0131kmak istiyor. Bug\xfcn ona k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir kap\u0131 a\xe7abilir misin?",guidance:"Bu gece yatmadan \xf6nce defterinizi yast\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131z\u0131n yan\u0131na koyun. Sabah uyand\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131zda \u2014 telefona bakmadan, konu\u015fmadan \u2014 g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfcz ya da hissetti\u011finiz \u015feyi hemen yaz\u0131n. R\xfcya g\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfc tutmak, bilin\xe7alt\u0131 mesajlar\u0131n\u0131 yakalamak i\xe7in en kadim ve kan\u0131tlanm\u0131\u015f y\xf6ntemlerden biridir. Dalg\u0131\xe7 ku\u015fu bunu sular alt\u0131nda yapar; siz k\xe2\u011f\u0131t \xfczerinde.",rarity:"uncommon",nameEn:"Loon",elementEn:"water",symbolismEn:["dream","voice of the unconscious","inner cry","depth"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Siberian shamanism the loon's strange and reverberating cry is the voice of the otherworld leaking into this world \u2014 shamans imitate the loon's cry as they enter trance, and this sound opens the door between two realms. In the Great Lakes traditions of the Ojibwe and Cree peoples of North America the loon is the sacred messenger of dreams and the unconscious \u2014 to hear its call at night is to receive a message from the ancestor spirits. In Scandinavian folklore, and particularly in the Finnish-Karelian Kalevala poetic tradition, the loon is the sacred bird that dives into the water at the beginning of creation; from its egg the world is born. In the S\xe1mi tradition of northern Europe the loon is the soul guide who passes between the world of night and the world of day \u2014 emerging from dark waters into light, knowing this journey. In Inuit tradition the loon is the sacred being that builds a bridge between sea and land, carrying the spirit of the cold. The medicine of the loon is to listen to messages from the unconscious and to allow the inner voice to be heard. Its shadow side: diving so deeply into the depths of the unconscious that one no longer wishes to surface.",dailyMessageEn:"Loon turns you today toward the deepest and strangest voice within you. This voice sometimes comes in dreams, sometimes as a sudden sensation, sometimes in a knowing that logic cannot explain. Are you suppressing it? The loon moves with equal mastery beneath and above the water \u2014 it sees no contradiction between conscious and unconscious. Is there something today that your mind says is illogical but your inside says is right? A dream, an obsession, a thought that keeps returning \u2014 these may be the voice of the unconscious, wanting to be heard. Like its strange, beautiful cry, the voice within you also wants to emerge into this world. Can you open a small door for it today?",guidanceEn:"Tonight, before you sleep, place your notebook by your pillow. When you wake in the morning \u2014 without looking at your phone, without speaking \u2014 immediately write down what you saw or felt. Keeping a dream journal is one of the most ancient and proven methods for catching unconscious messages. The loon does this beneath the water; you do it on paper."},{id:"a100",name:"Beyaz Geyik",emoji:"\ud83e\udd8c",element:"hava",symbolism:["kutsal belirti","d\xf6n\xfcm noktas\u0131","ilahi \xe7a\u011fr\u0131","nadir an"],imageUrl:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:FilePath/White_deer_-_The_Art_of_White_Deer.jpg&width=300",anatolianMeaning:"T\xfcrk ve Anadolu gelene\u011finde beyaz geyik, Tanr\u0131'n\u0131n ya da kutsal bir g\xfcc\xfcn el\xe7isi olarak g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr \u2014 Anadolu'daki pek \xe7ok kurulu\u015f efsanesinde beyaz bir geyi\u011fin pe\u015finden gidilerek yeni \u015fehirlerin kuruldu\u011fu anlat\u0131l\u0131r; Bursa, Konya ve Sivas'\u0131n kurulu\u015f hik\xe2yeleri bu kutsal izde y\xfcr\xfcmekle ba\u015flar. Kelt mitolojisinde S\xeddhe'nin beyaz geyi\u011fi, \xf6l\xfcml\xfc d\xfcnyadan Ebedi Arazi'ye \xe7a\u011fr\u0131d\u0131r \u2014 bir beyaz geyik g\xf6rmek \xf6l\xfcml\xfcye senin zaman\u0131n geldi, d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm kap\u0131nda mesaj\u0131n\u0131 verir; Arthur efsanelerinde kutsal av, beyaz geyi\u011fi kovalamakla ba\u015flar. Kuzey Amerika Lakota gelene\u011finde Beyaz Bufalo'nun karde\u015f sembol\xfc olan beyaz hayvan, yeni bir \xe7a\u011f\u0131n, yeni bir anla\u015fman\u0131n ve kutsal bar\u0131\u015f\u0131n i\u015faretidir. \xc7in mitolojisinde beyaz geyik, \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfc\u011f\xfcn ve ilahi bilgeli\u011fin simgesidir \u2014 Tao bilgelerinin bine\u011fi olarak g\xf6sterilir ve ya\u015fam\u0131n d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfc a\u015fm\u0131\u015f ruhu temsil eder. Slav gelene\u011finde beyaz geyik, orman tanr\u0131lar\u0131ndan gelen mesaj\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yan el\xe7idir \u2014 onu g\xf6ren \u015fans de\u011fil sorumluluk kazan\u0131r: art\u0131k farkl\u0131 bir g\xf6zle g\xf6rmek zorundad\u0131r. Japon Shinto gelene\u011finde ise beyaz geyik, tanr\u0131sal mesajlar\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yan kutsal varl\u0131k olarak sayg\u0131 g\xf6r\xfcr. Beyaz Geyik'in t\u0131bb\u0131, kutsal d\xf6n\xfcm noktalar\u0131n\u0131 fark etmek ve hayat\u0131n ilahi \xe7a\u011fr\u0131lar\u0131na g\xf6zleri a\xe7\u0131k yan\u0131t vermektir. G\xf6lge y\xf6n\xfc: her \u015feyde i\u015faret aramak ve s\u0131radan olan\u0131 g\xf6rmezden gelmek \u2014 kutsal her yerde, ama g\xf6z\xfcn ona bakmay\u0131 \xf6\u011frenmesi gerekir.",dailyMessage:"Beyaz Geyik bug\xfcn sana bir \u015feyi duyuruyor: sen bir d\xf6n\xfcm noktas\u0131ndas\u0131n. Belki bunu zaten hissediyordun \u2014 ya da hen\xfcz tam ad\u0131n\u0131 koyamam\u0131\u015ft\u0131n. Bir \u015fey bitmek \xfczere ya da ba\u015flamak \xfczere \u2014 ya da ikisi birden. Kelt gelene\u011finde beyaz geyik pe\u015finden gidilmesi ama asla avlanmamas\u0131 gereken varl\u0131kt\u0131r; o seni bir yere \xe7ekiyor ama ona sahip olamazs\u0131n \u2014 o bir \xe7a\u011fr\u0131d\u0131r, bir ganimet de\u011fil. Bug\xfcn seni \xe7eken o ses nereye g\xf6t\xfcr\xfcyor? Kalbinin seni \xe7ekti\u011fi y\xf6n, mant\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n \xe7ok riskli ya da \xe7ok erken dedi\u011fi yer olabilir. Ama beyaz geyik beklemez; o an\u0131n i\xe7indedir. Bug\xfcn o \xe7a\u011fr\u0131y\u0131 duyuyor musun? Ve ona bir ad\u0131m atmaya cesaret edebilir misin?",guidance:"Sessiz bir anda oturun ve kendinize sorun: Kalbim beni \u015fu an nereye \xe7ekiyor? Bu soruyu mant\u0131kla de\u011fil, g\xf6\u011fs\xfcn\xfczle cevaplay\u0131n. Cevab\u0131 not al\u0131n. Ard\u0131ndan bu y\xf6nde bug\xfcn at\u0131labilecek tek somut bir ad\u0131m belirleyin \u2014 k\xfc\xe7\xfck olsun, ama ger\xe7ek olsun. Beyaz Geyik nadir g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr; ama g\xf6r\xfcnd\xfc\u011f\xfcnde harekete ge\xe7ilmesi i\xe7in gelmektedir.",rarity:"legendary",nameEn:"White Stag",elementEn:"air",symbolismEn:["sacred sign","turning point","divine calling","rare moment"],anatolianMeaningEn:"In Turkic and Anatolian tradition the white stag is seen as the messenger of God or of a sacred power \u2014 in many founding legends of Anatolia, new cities are established by following a white stag; the founding stories of Bursa, Konya, and Sivas begin with the walking of this sacred trail. In Celtic mythology the white stag of the S\xeddhe is the call from the mortal world to the Eternal Land \u2014 to see a white stag is to be told your time has come, transformation is at your door; the sacred hunt of the Arthurian legends begins with the chase of the white stag. In the Lakota tradition of North America the white animal \u2014 sibling symbol of the White Buffalo \u2014 is the sign of a new age, a new covenant, and a sacred peace. In Chinese mythology the white stag is the symbol of immortality and divine wisdom \u2014 shown as the mount of Taoist sages and representing the soul that has transcended the cycle of life. In Slavic tradition the white stag is the messenger who carries word from the forest gods \u2014 the one who sees it gains not luck but responsibility: from now on they must see with different eyes. In the Japanese Shinto tradition the white stag is honored as the sacred being who carries divine messages. The medicine of the White Stag is to notice sacred turning points and to answer life's divine callings with open eyes. Its shadow side: searching for signs in everything and ignoring what is ordinary \u2014 the sacred is everywhere, but the eye must learn to look at it.",dailyMessageEn:"White Stag announces something to you today: you are at a turning point. Perhaps you were already sensing this \u2014 or perhaps you had not yet been able to name it. Something is about to end or about to begin \u2014 or both at once. In the Celtic tradition the white stag is the being to be followed but never hunted; it draws you somewhere, but you cannot possess it \u2014 it is a calling, not a prize. Where is the voice drawing you today taking you? The direction your heart pulls you may be the place your mind calls too risky or too early. But the white stag does not wait; it is within the moment. Can you hear that call today? And can you find the courage to take a step toward it?",guidanceEn:"Sit in a quiet moment and ask yourself: Where is my heart drawing me right now? Answer this question not with your mind but with your chest. Note the answer. Then determine one tangible step in this direction that can be taken today \u2014 let it be small, but let it be real. The White Stag appears rarely; but when it appears, it has come so that one will move."}]},732,[]);
